('Gen.5.28', 'BSB', 'When Lamech was 182 years old, he had a son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.5.29', 'BSB', 'And he named him Noah, saying, “May this one comfort us in the labor and toil of our hands caused by the ground that the LORD has cursed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.5.30', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Noah, Lamech lived 595 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.5.31', 'BSB', 'So Lamech lived a total of 777 years, and then he died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.5.32', 'BSB', 'After Noah was 500 years old, he became the father of Shem, Ham, and Japheth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.1', 'BSB', 'Now when men began to multiply on the face of the earth and daughters were born to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.2', 'BSB', 'the sons of God saw that the daughters of men were beautiful, and they took as wives whomever they chose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.3', 'BSB', 'So the LORD said, “My Spirit will not contend with man forever, for he is mortal; his days shall be 120 years.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.4', 'BSB', 'The Nephilim were on the earth in those days—and afterward as well—when the sons of God had relations with the daughters of men. And they bore them children who became the mighty men of old, men of renown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.5', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD saw that the wickedness of man was great upon the earth, and that every inclination of the thoughts of his heart was altogether evil all the time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.6', 'BSB', 'And the LORD regretted that He had made man on the earth, and He was grieved in His heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.7', 'BSB', 'So the LORD said, “I will blot out man, whom I have created, from the face of the earth—every man and beast and crawling creature and bird of the air—for I am grieved that I have made them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.8', 'BSB', 'Noah, however, found favor in the eyes of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.9', 'BSB', 'This is the account of Noah. Noah was a righteous man, blameless in his generation; Noah walked with God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.10', 'BSB', 'And Noah had three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.11', 'BSB', 'Now the earth was corrupt in the sight of God, and full of violence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.12', 'BSB', 'And God looked upon the earth and saw that it was corrupt; for all living creatures on the earth had corrupted their ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.13', 'BSB', 'Then God said to Noah, “The end of all living creatures has come before Me, because through them the earth is full of violence. Now behold, I will destroy both them and the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.14', 'BSB', 'Make for yourself an ark of gopher wood; make rooms in the ark and coat it with pitch inside and out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.15', 'BSB', 'And this is how you are to build it: The ark is to be 300 cubits long, 50 cubits wide, and 30 cubits high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.16', 'BSB', 'You are to make a roof for the ark, finish its walls a cubit from the top, place a door in the side of the ark, and build lower, middle, and upper decks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.17', 'BSB', 'And behold, I will bring floodwaters upon the earth to destroy every creature under the heavens that has the breath of life. Everything on the earth will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.18', 'BSB', 'But I will establish My covenant with you, and you will enter the ark—you and your sons and your wife and your sons’ wives with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.19', 'BSB', 'And you are to bring two of every living creature into the ark—male and female—to keep them alive with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.20', 'BSB', 'Two of every kind of bird and animal and crawling creature will come to you to be kept alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.21', 'BSB', 'You are also to take for yourself every kind of food that is eaten and gather it as food for yourselves and for the animals.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.6.22', 'BSB', 'So Noah did everything precisely as God had commanded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Noah, “Go into the ark, you and all your family, because I have found you righteous in this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.2', 'BSB', 'You are to take with you seven pairs of every kind of clean animal, a male and its mate; a pair of every kind of unclean animal, a male and its mate;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.3', 'BSB', 'and seven pairs of every kind of bird of the air, male and female, to preserve their offspring on the face of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.4', 'BSB', 'For seven days from now I will send rain on the earth for forty days and forty nights, and I will wipe from the face of the earth every living thing I have made.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.5', 'BSB', 'And Noah did all that the LORD had commanded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.6', 'BSB', 'Now Noah was 600 years old when the floodwaters came upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.7', 'BSB', 'And Noah and his wife, with his sons and their wives, entered the ark to escape the waters of the flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.8', 'BSB', 'The clean and unclean animals, the birds, and everything that crawls along the ground', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.9', 'BSB', 'came to Noah to enter the ark, two by two, male and female, as God had commanded Noah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.10', 'BSB', 'And after seven days the floodwaters came upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.11', 'BSB', 'In the six hundredth year of Noah’s life, on the seventeenth day of the second month, all the fountains of the great deep burst forth, and the floodgates of the heavens were opened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.12', 'BSB', 'And the rain fell upon the earth for forty days and forty nights.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.13', 'BSB', 'On that very day Noah entered the ark, along with his sons Shem, Ham, and Japheth, and his wife, and the three wives of his sons—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.14', 'BSB', 'they and every kind of wild animal, livestock, crawling creature, bird, and winged creature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.15', 'BSB', 'They came to Noah to enter the ark, two by two of every creature with the breath of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.16', 'BSB', 'And they entered, the male and female of every living thing, as God had commanded Noah. Then the LORD shut him in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.17', 'BSB', 'For forty days the flood kept coming on the earth, and the waters rose and lifted the ark high above the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.18', 'BSB', 'So the waters continued to surge and rise greatly on the earth, and the ark floated on the surface of the waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.19', 'BSB', 'Finally, the waters completely inundated the earth, so that all the high mountains under all the heavens were covered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.20', 'BSB', 'The waters rose and covered the mountaintops to a depth of fifteen cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.21', 'BSB', 'And every living thing that moved upon the earth perished—birds, livestock, animals, every creature that swarms upon the earth, and all mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.22', 'BSB', 'Of all that was on dry land, everything that had the breath of life in its nostrils died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.23', 'BSB', 'And every living thing on the face of the earth was destroyed—man and livestock, crawling creatures and birds of the air; they were blotted out from the earth, and only Noah and those with him in the ark remained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.7.24', 'BSB', 'And the waters prevailed upon the earth for 150 days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.1', 'BSB', 'But God remembered Noah and all the animals and livestock that were with him in the ark. And God sent a wind over the earth, and the waters began to subside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.2', 'BSB', 'The springs of the deep and the floodgates of the heavens were closed, and the rain from the sky was restrained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.3', 'BSB', 'The waters receded steadily from the earth, and after 150 days the waters had gone down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.4', 'BSB', 'On the seventeenth day of the seventh month, the ark came to rest on the mountains of Ararat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.5', 'BSB', 'And the waters continued to recede until the tenth month, and on the first day of the tenth month the tops of the mountains became visible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.6', 'BSB', 'After forty days Noah opened the window he had made in the ark', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.7', 'BSB', 'and sent out a raven. It kept flying back and forth until the waters had dried up from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.8', 'BSB', 'Then Noah sent out a dove to see if the waters had receded from the surface of the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.9', 'BSB', 'But the dove found no place to rest her foot, and she returned to him in the ark, because the waters were still covering the surface of all the earth. So he reached out his hand and brought her back inside the ark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.10', 'BSB', 'Noah waited seven more days and again sent out the dove from the ark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.11', 'BSB', 'And behold, the dove returned to him in the evening with a freshly plucked olive leaf in her beak. So Noah knew that the waters had receded from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.12', 'BSB', 'And Noah waited seven more days and sent out the dove again, but this time she did not return to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.13', 'BSB', 'In Noah’s six hundred and first year, on the first day of the first month, the waters had dried up from the earth. So Noah removed the covering from the ark and saw that the surface of the ground was dry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.14', 'BSB', 'By the twenty-seventh day of the second month, the earth was fully dry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.15', 'BSB', 'Then God said to Noah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.16', 'BSB', '“Come out of the ark, you and your wife, along with your sons and their wives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.17', 'BSB', 'Bring out all the living creatures that are with you—birds, livestock, and everything that crawls upon the ground—so that they can spread out over the earth and be fruitful and multiply upon it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.18', 'BSB', 'So Noah came out, along with his sons and his wife and his sons’ wives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.19', 'BSB', 'Every living creature, every creeping thing, and every bird—everything that moves upon the earth—came out of the ark, kind by kind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.20', 'BSB', 'Then Noah built an altar to the LORD. And taking from every kind of clean animal and clean bird, he offered burnt offerings on the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.21', 'BSB', 'When the LORD smelled the pleasing aroma, He said in His heart, “Never again will I curse the ground because of man, even though every inclination of his heart is evil from his youth. And never again will I destroy all living creatures as I have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.8.22', 'BSB', 'As long as the earth endures, seedtime and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter, day and night shall never cease.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.1', 'BSB', 'And God blessed Noah and his sons and said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply and fill the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.2', 'BSB', 'The fear and dread of you will fall on every living creature on the earth, every bird of the air, every creature that crawls on the ground, and all the fish of the sea. They are delivered into your hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.3', 'BSB', 'Everything that lives and moves will be food for you; just as I gave you the green plants, I now give you all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.4', 'BSB', 'But you must not eat meat with its lifeblood still in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.5', 'BSB', 'And surely I will require the life of any man or beast by whose hand your lifeblood is shed. I will demand an accounting from anyone who takes the life of his fellow man:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.6', 'BSB', 'Whoever sheds the blood of man, by man his blood will be shed; for in His own image God has made mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.7', 'BSB', 'But as for you, be fruitful and multiply; spread out across the earth and multiply upon it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.8', 'BSB', 'Then God said to Noah and his sons with him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.9', 'BSB', '“Behold, I now establish My covenant with you and your descendants after you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.10', 'BSB', 'and with every living creature that was with you—the birds, the livestock, and every beast of the earth—every living thing that came out of the ark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.11', 'BSB', 'And I establish My covenant with you: Never again will all life be cut off by the waters of a flood; never again will there be a flood to destroy the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.12', 'BSB', 'And God said, “This is the sign of the covenant I am making between Me and you and every living creature with you, a covenant for all generations to come:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.13', 'BSB', 'I have set My rainbow in the clouds, and it will be a sign of the covenant between Me and the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.14', 'BSB', 'Whenever I form clouds over the earth and the rainbow appears in the clouds,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.15', 'BSB', 'I will remember My covenant between Me and you and every living creature of every kind. Never again will the waters become a flood to destroy all life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.16', 'BSB', 'And whenever the rainbow appears in the clouds, I will see it and remember the everlasting covenant between God and every living creature of every kind that is on the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.17', 'BSB', 'So God said to Noah, “This is the sign of the covenant that I have established between Me and every creature on the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.18', 'BSB', 'The sons of Noah who came out of the ark were Shem, Ham, and Japheth. And Ham was the father of Canaan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.19', 'BSB', 'These three were the sons of Noah, and from them the whole earth was populated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.20', 'BSB', 'Now Noah, a man of the soil, proceeded to plant a vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.21', 'BSB', 'But when he drank some of its wine, he became drunk and uncovered himself inside his tent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.22', 'BSB', 'And Ham, the father of Canaan, saw his father’s nakedness and told his two brothers outside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.23', 'BSB', 'Then Shem and Japheth took a garment and placed it across their shoulders, and walking backward, they covered their father’s nakedness. Their faces were turned away so that they did not see their father’s nakedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.24', 'BSB', 'When Noah awoke from his drunkenness and learned what his youngest son had done to him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.25', 'BSB', 'he said, “Cursed be Canaan! A servant of servants shall he be to his brothers.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.26', 'BSB', 'He also declared: “Blessed be the LORD, the God of Shem! May Canaan be the servant of Shem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.27', 'BSB', 'May God expand the territory of Japheth; may he dwell in the tents of Shem, and may Canaan be his servant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.28', 'BSB', 'After the flood, Noah lived 350 years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.9.29', 'BSB', 'So Noah lived a total of 950 years, and then he died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.1', 'BSB', 'This is the account of Noah’s sons Shem, Ham, and Japheth, who also had sons after the flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.2', 'BSB', 'The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.3', 'BSB', 'The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.4', 'BSB', 'And the sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, the Kittites, and the Rodanites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.5', 'BSB', 'From these, the maritime peoples separated into their territories, according to their languages, by clans within their nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.6', 'BSB', 'The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.7', 'BSB', 'The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. And the sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.8', 'BSB', 'Cush was the father of Nimrod, who began to be a mighty one on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.9', 'BSB', 'He was a mighty hunter before the LORD; so it is said, “Like Nimrod, a mighty hunter before the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.10', 'BSB', 'His kingdom began in Babylon, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.11', 'BSB', 'From that land he went forth into Assyria, where he built Nineveh, Rehoboth-Ir, Calah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.12', 'BSB', 'and Resen, which is between Nineveh and the great city of Calah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.13', 'BSB', 'Mizraim was the father of the Ludites, the Anamites, the Lehabites, the Naphtuhites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.14', 'BSB', 'the Pathrusites, the Casluhites (from whom the Philistines came), and the Caphtorites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.15', 'BSB', 'And Canaan was the father of Sidon his firstborn, and of the Hittites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.16', 'BSB', 'the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.17', 'BSB', 'the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.18', 'BSB', 'the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites. Later the Canaanite clans were scattered,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.19', 'BSB', 'and the borders of Canaan extended from Sidon toward Gerar as far as Gaza, and then toward Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim, as far as Lasha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.20', 'BSB', 'These are the sons of Ham according to their clans, languages, lands, and nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.21', 'BSB', 'And sons were also born to Shem, the older brother of Japheth; Shem was the forefather of all the sons of Eber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.22', 'BSB', 'The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arphaxad, Lud, and Aram.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.23', 'BSB', 'The sons of Aram: Uz, Hul, Gether, and Mash.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.24', 'BSB', 'Arphaxad was the father of Shelah, and Shelah was the father of Eber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.25', 'BSB', 'Two sons were born to Eber: One was named Peleg, because in his days the earth was divided, and his brother was named Joktan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.26', 'BSB', 'And Joktan was the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.27', 'BSB', 'Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.28', 'BSB', 'Obal, Abimael, Sheba,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.29', 'BSB', 'Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were sons of Joktan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.30', 'BSB', 'Their territory extended from Mesha to Sephar, in the eastern hill country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.31', 'BSB', 'These are the sons of Shem, according to their clans, languages, lands, and nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.10.32', 'BSB', 'All these are the clans of Noah’s sons, according to their generations and nations. From these the nations of the earth spread out after the flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.1', 'BSB', 'Now the whole world had one language and a common form of speech.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.2', 'BSB', 'And as people journeyed eastward, they found a plain in the land of Shinar and settled there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.3', 'BSB', 'And they said to one another, “Come, let us make bricks and bake them thoroughly.” So they used brick instead of stone, and tar instead of mortar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.4', 'BSB', '“Come,” they said, “let us build for ourselves a city with a tower that reaches to the heavens, that we may make a name for ourselves and not be scattered over the face of all the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.5', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD came down to see the city and the tower that the sons of men were building.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.6', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said, “If they have begun to do this as one people speaking the same language, then nothing they devise will be beyond them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.7', 'BSB', 'Come, let Us go down and confuse their language, so that they will not understand one another’s speech.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.8', 'BSB', 'So the LORD scattered them from there over the face of all the earth, and they stopped building the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.9', 'BSB', 'That is why it is called Babel, for there the LORD confused the language of the whole world, and from that place the LORD scattered them over the face of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.10', 'BSB', 'This is the account of Shem. Two years after the flood, when Shem was 100 years old, he became the father of Arphaxad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.11', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Arphaxad, Shem lived 500 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.12', 'BSB', 'When Arphaxad was 35 years old, he became the father of Shelah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.13', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Shelah, Arphaxad lived 403 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.14', 'BSB', 'When Shelah was 30 years old, he became the father of Eber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.15', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Eber, Shelah lived 403 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.16', 'BSB', 'When Eber was 34 years old, he became the father of Peleg.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.17', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Peleg, Eber lived 430 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.18', 'BSB', 'When Peleg was 30 years old, he became the father of Reu.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.19', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Reu, Peleg lived 209 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.20', 'BSB', 'When Reu was 32 years old, he became the father of Serug.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.21', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Serug, Reu lived 207 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.22', 'BSB', 'When Serug was 30 years old, he became the father of Nahor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.23', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Nahor, Serug lived 200 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.24', 'BSB', 'When Nahor was 29 years old, he became the father of Terah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.25', 'BSB', 'And after he had become the father of Terah, Nahor lived 119 years and had other sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.26', 'BSB', 'When Terah was 70 years old, he became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.27', 'BSB', 'This is the account of Terah. Terah became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran. And Haran became the father of Lot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.28', 'BSB', 'During his father Terah’s lifetime, Haran died in his native land, in Ur of the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.29', 'BSB', 'And Abram and Nahor took wives for themselves. Abram’s wife was named Sarai, and Nahor’s wife was named Milcah; she was the daughter of Haran, who was the father of both Milcah and Iscah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.30', 'BSB', 'But Sarai was barren; she had no children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.31', 'BSB', 'And Terah took his son Abram, his grandson Lot son of Haran, and his daughter-in-law Sarai the wife of Abram, and they set out from Ur of the Chaldeans for the land of Canaan. But when they arrived in Haran, they settled there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.11.32', 'BSB', 'Terah lived 205 years, and he died in Haran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Abram, “Leave your country, your kindred, and your father’s household, and go to the land I will show you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.2', 'BSB', 'I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, so that you will be a blessing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
