('Gen.12.4', 'BSB', 'So Abram departed, as the LORD had directed him, and Lot went with him. Abram was seventy-five years old when he left Haran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.5', 'BSB', 'And Abram took his wife Sarai, his nephew Lot, and all the possessions and people they had acquired in Haran, and set out for the land of Canaan. When they came to the land of Canaan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.6', 'BSB', 'Abram traveled through the land as far as the site of the Oak of Moreh at Shechem. And at that time the Canaanites were in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.7', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD appeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the LORD, who had appeared to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.8', 'BSB', 'From there Abram moved on to the hill country east of Bethel and pitched his tent, with Bethel to the west and Ai to the east. There he built an altar to the LORD, and he called on the name of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.9', 'BSB', 'And Abram journeyed on toward the Negev.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.10', 'BSB', 'Now there was a famine in the land. So Abram went down to Egypt to live there for a while because the famine was severe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.11', 'BSB', 'As he was about to enter Egypt, he said to his wife Sarai, “Look, I know that you are a beautiful woman,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.12', 'BSB', 'and when the Egyptians see you, they will say, ‘This is his wife.’ Then they will kill me but will let you live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.13', 'BSB', 'Please say you are my sister, so that I will be treated well for your sake, and on account of you my life will be spared.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.14', 'BSB', 'So when Abram entered Egypt, the Egyptians saw that the woman was very beautiful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.15', 'BSB', 'When Pharaoh’s officials saw Sarai, they commended her to him, and she was taken into the palace of Pharaoh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.16', 'BSB', 'He treated Abram well on her account, and Abram acquired sheep and cattle, male and female donkeys, menservants and maidservants, and camels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.17', 'BSB', 'The LORD, however, afflicted Pharaoh and his household with severe plagues because of Abram’s wife Sarai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.18', 'BSB', 'So Pharaoh summoned Abram and asked, “What have you done to me? Why didn’t you tell me she was your wife?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.19', 'BSB', 'Why did you say, ‘She is my sister,’ so that I took her as my wife? Now then, here is your wife. Take her and go!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.12.20', 'BSB', 'Then Pharaoh gave his men orders concerning Abram, and they sent him away with his wife and all his possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.1', 'BSB', 'So Abram went up out of Egypt into the Negev—he and his wife and all his possessions—and Lot was with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.2', 'BSB', 'And Abram had become extremely wealthy in livestock and silver and gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.3', 'BSB', 'From the Negev he journeyed from place to place toward Bethel, until he came to the place between Bethel and Ai where his tent had formerly been pitched,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.4', 'BSB', 'to the site where he had built the altar. And there Abram called on the name of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.5', 'BSB', 'Now Lot, who was traveling with Abram, also had flocks and herds and tents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.6', 'BSB', 'But the land was unable to support both of them while they stayed together, for they had so many possessions that they were unable to coexist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.7', 'BSB', 'And there was discord between the herdsmen of Abram and the herdsmen of Lot. At that time the Canaanites and the Perizzites were also living in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.8', 'BSB', 'So Abram said to Lot, “Please let there be no contention between you and me, or between your herdsmen and my herdsmen. After all, we are brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.9', 'BSB', 'Is not the whole land before you? Now separate yourself from me. If you go to the left, I will go to the right; if you go to the right, I will go to the left.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.10', 'BSB', 'And Lot looked out and saw that the whole plain of the Jordan, all the way to Zoar, was well watered like the garden of the LORD, like the land of Egypt. (This was before the LORD destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.11', 'BSB', 'So Lot chose the whole plain of the Jordan for himself and set out toward the east. And Abram and Lot parted company.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.12', 'BSB', 'Abram lived in the land of Canaan, but Lot settled in the cities of the plain and pitched his tent toward Sodom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.13', 'BSB', 'But the men of Sodom were wicked, sinning greatly against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.14', 'BSB', 'After Lot had departed, the LORD said to Abram, “Now lift up your eyes from the place where you are, and look to the north and south and east and west,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.15', 'BSB', 'for all the land that you see, I will give to you and your offspring forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.16', 'BSB', 'I will make your offspring like the dust of the earth, so that if one could count the dust of the earth, then your offspring could be counted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.17', 'BSB', 'Get up and walk around the land, through its length and breadth, for I will give it to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.13.18', 'BSB', 'So Abram moved his tent and went to live near the Oaks of Mamre at Hebron, where he built an altar to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gen.14.1', 'BSB', 'In those days Amraphel king of Shinar, Arioch king of Ellasar, Chedorlaomer king of Elam, and Tidal king of Goiim', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
