('Num.7.83', 'BSB', 'and a peace offering of two oxen, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Ahira son of Enan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.84', 'BSB', 'So these were the offerings from the leaders of Israel for the dedication of the altar when it was anointed: twelve silver platters, twelve silver bowls, and twelve gold dishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.85', 'BSB', 'Each silver platter weighed a hundred and thirty shekels, and each silver bowl seventy shekels. The total weight of the silver articles was two thousand four hundred shekels, according to the sanctuary shekel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.86', 'BSB', 'The twelve gold dishes filled with incense weighed ten shekels each, according to the sanctuary shekel. The total weight of the gold dishes was a hundred and twenty shekels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.87', 'BSB', 'All the livestock for the burnt offering totaled twelve bulls, twelve rams, and twelve male lambs a year old—together with their grain offerings—and twelve male goats for the sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.88', 'BSB', 'All the livestock sacrificed for the peace offering totaled twenty-four bulls, sixty rams, sixty male goats, and sixty male lambs a year old. This was the dedication offering for the altar after it was anointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.7.89', 'BSB', 'When Moses entered the Tent of Meeting to speak with the LORD, he heard the voice speaking to him from between the two cherubim above the mercy seat on the ark of the Testimony. Thus the LORD spoke to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.2', 'BSB', '“Speak to Aaron and tell him: ‘When you set up the seven lamps, they are to light the area in front of the lampstand.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.3', 'BSB', 'And Aaron did so; he set up the lamps facing toward the front of the lampstand, just as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.4', 'BSB', 'This is how the lampstand was constructed: it was made of hammered gold from its base to its blossoms, fashioned according to the pattern the LORD had shown Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.5', 'BSB', 'Again the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.6', 'BSB', '“Take the Levites from among the Israelites and make them ceremonially clean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.7', 'BSB', 'This is what you must do to cleanse them: Sprinkle them with the water of purification. Have them shave their whole bodies and wash their clothes, and so purify themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.8', 'BSB', 'Then have them take a young bull with its grain offering of fine flour mixed with oil, and you are to take a second young bull for a sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.9', 'BSB', 'Bring the Levites before the Tent of Meeting and assemble the whole congregation of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.10', 'BSB', 'You are to present the Levites before the LORD and have the Israelites lay their hands upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.11', 'BSB', 'Aaron is to present the Levites before the LORD as a wave offering from the sons of Israel, so that they may perform the service of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.12', 'BSB', 'And the Levites are to lay their hands on the heads of the bulls, and offer to the LORD one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering, to make atonement for the Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.13', 'BSB', 'You are to have the Levites stand before Aaron and his sons and then present them before the LORD as a wave offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.14', 'BSB', 'In this way you shall separate the Levites from the rest of the Israelites, and the Levites will belong to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.15', 'BSB', 'After you have cleansed them and presented them as a wave offering, they may come to serve at the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.16', 'BSB', 'For the Levites have been wholly given to Me from among the sons of Israel. I have taken them for Myself in place of all who come first from the womb, the firstborn of all the sons of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.17', 'BSB', 'For every firstborn male in Israel is Mine, both man and beast. I set them apart for Myself on the day I struck down all the firstborn in the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.18', 'BSB', 'But I have taken the Levites in place of all the firstborn among the sons of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.19', 'BSB', 'And I have given the Levites as a gift to Aaron and his sons from among the Israelites, to perform the service for the Israelites at the Tent of Meeting and to make atonement on their behalf, so that no plague will come against the Israelites when they approach the sanctuary.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.20', 'BSB', 'So Moses, Aaron, and the whole congregation of Israel did with the Levites everything that the LORD had commanded Moses they should do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.21', 'BSB', 'The Levites purified themselves and washed their clothes, and Aaron presented them as a wave offering before the LORD. Aaron also made atonement for them to cleanse them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.22', 'BSB', 'After that, the Levites came to perform their service at the Tent of Meeting in the presence of Aaron and his sons. Thus they did with the Levites just as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.23', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.24', 'BSB', '“This applies to the Levites: Men twenty-five years of age or older shall enter to perform the service in the work at the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.25', 'BSB', 'But at the age of fifty, they must retire from performing the work and no longer serve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.8.26', 'BSB', 'After that, they may assist their brothers in fulfilling their duties at the Tent of Meeting, but they themselves are not to do the work. This is how you are to assign responsibilities to the Levites.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.1', 'BSB', 'In the first month of the second year after Israel had come out of the land of Egypt, the LORD spoke to Moses in the Wilderness of Sinai:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.2', 'BSB', '“The Israelites are to observe the Passover at its appointed time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.3', 'BSB', 'You are to observe it at the appointed time, at twilight on the fourteenth day of this month, in accordance with its statutes and ordinances.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.4', 'BSB', 'So Moses told the Israelites to observe the Passover,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.5', 'BSB', 'and they did so in the Wilderness of Sinai, at twilight on the fourteenth day of the first month. The Israelites did everything just as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.6', 'BSB', 'But there were some men who were unclean due to a dead body, so they could not observe the Passover on that day. And they came before Moses and Aaron that same day', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.7', 'BSB', 'and said to Moses, “We are unclean because of a dead body, but why should we be excluded from presenting the LORD’s offering with the other Israelites at the appointed time?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.8', 'BSB', '“Wait here until I find out what the LORD commands concerning you,” Moses replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.9', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.10', 'BSB', '“Tell the Israelites: ‘When any one of you or your descendants is unclean because of a dead body, or is away on a journey, he may still observe the Passover to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.11', 'BSB', 'Such people are to observe it at twilight on the fourteenth day of the second month. They are to eat the lamb, together with unleavened bread and bitter herbs;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.12', 'BSB', 'they may not leave any of it until morning or break any of its bones. They must observe the Passover according to all its statutes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.13', 'BSB', 'But if a man who is ceremonially clean and is not on a journey still fails to observe the Passover, he must be cut off from his people, because he did not present the LORD’s offering at its appointed time. That man will bear the consequences of his sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.14', 'BSB', 'If a foreigner dwelling among you wants to observe the Passover to the LORD, he is to do so according to the Passover statute and its ordinances. You are to apply the same statute to both the foreigner and the native of the land.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.15', 'BSB', 'On the day that the tabernacle, the Tent of the Testimony, was set up, the cloud covered it and appeared like fire above the tabernacle from evening until morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.16', 'BSB', 'It remained that way continually; the cloud would cover the tabernacle by day, and at night it would appear like fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.17', 'BSB', 'Whenever the cloud was lifted from above the Tent, the Israelites would set out, and wherever the cloud settled, there the Israelites would camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.18', 'BSB', 'At the LORD’s command the Israelites set out, and at the LORD’s command they camped. As long as the cloud remained over the tabernacle, they remained encamped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.19', 'BSB', 'Even when the cloud lingered over the tabernacle for many days, the Israelites kept the LORD’s charge and did not set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.20', 'BSB', 'Sometimes the cloud remained over the tabernacle for only a few days, and they would camp at the LORD’s command and set out at the LORD’s command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.21', 'BSB', 'Sometimes the cloud remained only from evening until morning, and when it lifted in the morning, they would set out. Whether it was by day or by night, when the cloud was taken up, they would set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.22', 'BSB', 'Whether the cloud lingered for two days, a month, or longer, the Israelites camped and did not set out as long as the cloud remained over the tabernacle; but when it was lifted, they would set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.9.23', 'BSB', 'They camped at the LORD’s command, and they set out at the LORD’s command; they carried out the LORD’s charge according to His command through Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.2', 'BSB', '“Make two trumpets of hammered silver to be used for calling the congregation and for having the camps set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.3', 'BSB', 'When both are sounded, the whole congregation is to assemble before you at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.4', 'BSB', 'But if only one is sounded, then the leaders, the heads of the clans of Israel, are to gather before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.5', 'BSB', 'When you sound short blasts, the camps that lie on the east side are to set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.6', 'BSB', 'When you sound the short blasts a second time, the camps that lie on the south side are to set out. The blasts are to signal them to set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.7', 'BSB', 'To convene the assembly, you are to sound long blasts, not short ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.8', 'BSB', 'The sons of Aaron, the priests, are to sound the trumpets. This shall be a permanent statute for you and the generations to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.9', 'BSB', 'When you enter into battle in your land against an adversary who attacks you, sound short blasts on the trumpets, and you will be remembered before the LORD your God and saved from your enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.10', 'BSB', 'And on your joyous occasions, your appointed feasts, and the beginning of each month, you are to blow the trumpets over your burnt offerings and fellowship offerings to serve as a reminder for you before your God. I am the LORD your God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.11', 'BSB', 'On the twentieth day of the second month of the second year, the cloud was lifted from above the tabernacle of the Testimony,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.12', 'BSB', 'and the Israelites set out from the Wilderness of Sinai, traveling from place to place until the cloud settled in the Wilderness of Paran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.13', 'BSB', 'They set out this first time according to the LORD’s command through Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.14', 'BSB', 'First, the divisions of the camp of Judah set out under their standard, with Nahshon son of Amminadab in command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.15', 'BSB', 'Nethanel son of Zuar was over the division of the tribe of Issachar,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.16', 'BSB', 'and Eliab son of Helon was over the division of the tribe of Zebulun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.17', 'BSB', 'Then the tabernacle was taken down, and the Gershonites and the Merarites set out, transporting it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.18', 'BSB', 'Then the divisions of the camp of Reuben set out under their standard, with Elizur son of Shedeur in command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.19', 'BSB', 'Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai was over the division of the tribe of Simeon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.20', 'BSB', 'and Eliasaph son of Deuel was over the division of the tribe of Gad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.21', 'BSB', 'Then the Kohathites set out, transporting the holy objects; the tabernacle was to be set up before their arrival.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.22', 'BSB', 'Next, the divisions of the camp of Ephraim set out under their standard, with Elishama son of Ammihud in command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.23', 'BSB', 'Gamaliel son of Pedahzur was over the division of the tribe of Manasseh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.24', 'BSB', 'and Abidan son of Gideoni was over the division of the tribe of Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.25', 'BSB', 'Finally, the divisions of the camp of Dan set out under their standard, serving as the rear guard for all units, with Ahiezer son of Ammishaddai in command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.26', 'BSB', 'Pagiel son of Ocran was over the division of the tribe of Asher,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.27', 'BSB', 'and Ahira son of Enan was over the division of the tribe of Naphtali.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.28', 'BSB', 'This was the order of march for the Israelite divisions as they set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.29', 'BSB', 'Then Moses said to Hobab, the son of Moses’ father-in-law Reuel the Midianite, “We are setting out for the place of which the LORD said: ‘I will give it to you.’ Come with us, and we will treat you well, for the LORD has promised good things to Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.30', 'BSB', '“I will not go,” Hobab replied. “Instead, I am going back to my own land and my own people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.31', 'BSB', '“Please do not leave us,” Moses said, “since you know where we should camp in the wilderness, and you can serve as our eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.32', 'BSB', 'If you come with us, we will share with you whatever good things the LORD gives us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.33', 'BSB', 'So they set out on a three-day journey from the mountain of the LORD, with the ark of the covenant of the LORD traveling ahead of them for those three days to seek a resting place for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.34', 'BSB', 'And the cloud of the LORD was over them by day when they set out from the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.35', 'BSB', 'Whenever the ark set out, Moses would say, “Rise up, O LORD! May Your enemies be scattered; may those who hate You flee before You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.10.36', 'BSB', 'And when it came to rest, he would say: “Return, O LORD, to the countless thousands of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.1', 'BSB', 'Soon the people began to complain about their hardship in the hearing of the LORD, and when He heard them, His anger was kindled, and fire from the LORD blazed among them and consumed the outskirts of the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.2', 'BSB', 'And the people cried out to Moses, and he prayed to the LORD, and the fire died down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.3', 'BSB', 'So that place was called Taberah, because the fire of the LORD had burned among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.4', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the rabble among them had a strong craving for other food, and again the Israelites wept and said, “Who will feed us meat?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.5', 'BSB', 'We remember the fish we ate freely in Egypt, along with the cucumbers, melons, leeks, onions, and garlic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.6', 'BSB', 'But now our appetite is gone; there is nothing to see but this manna!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.7', 'BSB', 'Now the manna resembled coriander seed, and its appearance was like that of gum resin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.8', 'BSB', 'The people walked around and gathered it, ground it on a handmill or crushed it in a mortar, then boiled it in a cooking pot or shaped it into cakes. It tasted like pastry baked with fine oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.9', 'BSB', 'When the dew fell on the camp at night, the manna would fall with it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.10', 'BSB', 'Then Moses heard the people of family after family weeping at the entrances to their tents, and the anger of the LORD was kindled greatly, and Moses was also displeased.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.11', 'BSB', 'So Moses asked the LORD, “Why have You brought this trouble on Your servant? Why have I not found favor in Your sight, that You have laid upon me the burden of all these people?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.12', 'BSB', 'Did I conceive all these people? Did I give them birth, so that You should tell me, ‘Carry them in your bosom, as a nurse carries an infant,’ to the land that You swore to give their fathers?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.13', 'BSB', 'Where can I get meat for all these people? For they keep crying out to me, ‘Give us meat to eat!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.14', 'BSB', 'I cannot carry all these people by myself; it is too burdensome for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.15', 'BSB', 'If this is how You are going to treat me, please kill me right now—if I have found favor in Your eyes—and let me not see my own wretchedness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.16', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses, “Bring Me seventy of the elders of Israel known to you as leaders and officers of the people. Bring them to the Tent of Meeting and have them stand there with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.17', 'BSB', 'And I will come down and speak with you there, and I will take some of the Spirit that is on you and put that Spirit on them. They will help you bear the burden of the people, so that you do not have to bear it by yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.18', 'BSB', 'And say to the people: Consecrate yourselves for tomorrow, and you will eat meat, because you have cried out in the hearing of the LORD, saying: ‘Who will feed us meat? For we were better off in Egypt!’ Therefore the LORD will give you meat, and you will eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.19', 'BSB', 'You will eat it not for one or two days, nor for five or ten or twenty days,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.20', 'BSB', 'but for a whole month—until it comes out of your nostrils and makes you nauseous—because you have rejected the LORD, who is among you, and have cried out before Him, saying, ‘Why did we ever leave Egypt?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.21', 'BSB', 'But Moses replied, “Here I am among 600,000 men on foot, yet You say, ‘I will give them meat, and they will eat for a month.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.22', 'BSB', 'If all our flocks and herds were slaughtered for them, would they have enough? Or if all the fish in the sea were caught for them, would they have enough?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.23', 'BSB', 'The LORD answered Moses, “Is the LORD’s arm too short? Now you will see whether or not My word will come to pass.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.24', 'BSB', 'So Moses went out and relayed to the people the words of the LORD, and he gathered seventy of the elders of the people and had them stand around the tent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.25', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD came down in the cloud and spoke to him, and He took some of the Spirit that was on Moses and placed that Spirit on the seventy elders. As the Spirit rested on them, they prophesied—but they never did so again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.26', 'BSB', 'Two men, however, had remained in the camp—one named Eldad and the other Medad—and the Spirit rested on them. They were among those listed, but they had not gone out to the tent, and they prophesied in the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.27', 'BSB', 'A young man ran and reported to Moses, “Eldad and Medad are prophesying in the camp.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.28', 'BSB', 'Joshua son of Nun, the attendant to Moses since youth, spoke up and said, “Moses, my lord, stop them!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.29', 'BSB', 'But Moses replied, “Are you jealous on my account? I wish that all the LORD’s people were prophets and that the LORD would place His Spirit on them!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.30', 'BSB', 'Then Moses returned to the camp, along with the elders of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.31', 'BSB', 'Now a wind sent by the LORD came up, drove in quail from the sea, and brought them near the camp, about two cubits above the surface of the ground, for a day’s journey in every direction around the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.32', 'BSB', 'All that day and night, and all the next day, the people stayed up gathering the quail. No one gathered less than ten homers, and they spread them out all around the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.33', 'BSB', 'But while the meat was still between their teeth, before it was chewed, the anger of the LORD burned against the people, and the LORD struck them with a severe plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.34', 'BSB', 'So they called that place Kibroth-hattaavah, because there they buried the people who had craved other food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.11.35', 'BSB', 'From Kibroth-hattaavah the people moved on to Hazeroth, where they remained for some time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.1', 'BSB', 'Then Miriam and Aaron criticized Moses because of the Cushite woman he had married, for he had taken a Cushite wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.2', 'BSB', '“Does the LORD speak only through Moses?” they said. “Does He not also speak through us?” And the LORD heard this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.3', 'BSB', 'Now Moses was a very humble man, more so than any man on the face of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.4', 'BSB', 'And suddenly the LORD said to Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, “You three, come out to the Tent of Meeting.” So the three went out,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.5', 'BSB', 'and the LORD came down in a pillar of cloud, stood at the entrance to the Tent, and summoned Aaron and Miriam. When both of them had stepped forward,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.6', 'BSB', 'He said, “Hear now My words: If there is a prophet among you, I, the LORD, will reveal Myself to him in a vision; I will speak to him in a dream.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.7', 'BSB', 'But this is not so with My servant Moses; he is faithful in all My house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.8', 'BSB', 'I speak with him face to face, clearly and not in riddles; he sees the form of the LORD. Why then were you unafraid to speak against My servant Moses?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.9', 'BSB', 'So the anger of the LORD burned against them, and He departed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.10', 'BSB', 'As the cloud lifted from above the Tent, suddenly Miriam became leprous, white as snow. Aaron turned toward her, saw that she was leprous,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.11', 'BSB', 'and said to Moses, “My lord, please do not hold against us this sin we have so foolishly committed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.12', 'BSB', 'Please do not let her be like a stillborn infant whose flesh is half consumed when he comes out of his mother’s womb.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.13', 'BSB', 'So Moses cried out to the LORD, “O God, please heal her!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.14', 'BSB', 'But the LORD answered Moses, “If her father had but spit in her face, would she not have been in disgrace for seven days? Let her be confined outside the camp for seven days; after that she may be brought back in.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.15', 'BSB', 'So Miriam was confined outside the camp for seven days, and the people did not move on until she was brought in again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.12.16', 'BSB', 'After that, the people set out from Hazeroth and camped in the Wilderness of Paran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.1', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.2', 'BSB', '“Send out for yourself men to spy out the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the Israelites. From each of their fathers’ tribes send one man who is a leader among them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.3', 'BSB', 'So at the consent of the LORD, Moses sent them out from the Wilderness of Paran. All the men were leaders of the Israelites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.4', 'BSB', 'and these were their names: From the tribe of Reuben, Shammua son of Zaccur;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.5', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Simeon, Shaphat son of Hori;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.6', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Judah, Caleb son of Jephunneh;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.7', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Issachar, Igal son of Joseph;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.8', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Ephraim, Hoshea son of Nun;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.9', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Benjamin, Palti son of Raphu;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.10', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Zebulun, Gaddiel son of Sodi;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.11', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Manasseh (a tribe of Joseph), Gaddi son of Susi;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.12', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Dan, Ammiel son of Gemalli;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.13', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Asher, Sethur son of Michael;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.14', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Naphtali, Nahbi son of Vophsi;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.15', 'BSB', 'and from the tribe of Gad, Geuel son of Machi.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.16', 'BSB', 'These were the names of the men Moses sent to spy out the land; and Moses gave to Hoshea son of Nun the name Joshua.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.17', 'BSB', 'When Moses sent them to spy out the land of Canaan, he told them, “Go up through the Negev and into the hill country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.18', 'BSB', 'See what the land is like and whether its people are strong or weak, few or many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.19', 'BSB', 'Is the land where they live good or bad? Are the cities where they dwell open camps or fortifications?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.20', 'BSB', 'Is the soil fertile or unproductive? Are there trees in it or not? Be courageous, and bring back some of the fruit of the land.” (It was the season for the first ripe grapes.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.21', 'BSB', 'So they went up and spied out the land from the Wilderness of Zin as far as Rehob, toward Lebo-hamath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.22', 'BSB', 'They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the descendants of Anak, dwelled. It had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.23', 'BSB', 'When they came to the Valley of Eshcol, they cut down a branch with a single cluster of grapes, which they carried on a pole between two men. They also took some pomegranates and figs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.24', 'BSB', 'Because of the cluster of grapes the Israelites cut there, that place was called the Valley of Eshcol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.25', 'BSB', 'After forty days the men returned from spying out the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.26', 'BSB', 'and they went back to Moses, Aaron, and the whole congregation of Israel in the Wilderness of Paran at Kadesh. They brought back a report for the whole congregation and showed them the fruit of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.27', 'BSB', 'And they gave this account to Moses: “We went into the land to which you sent us, and indeed, it is flowing with milk and honey. Here is some of its fruit!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.28', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, the people living in the land are strong, and the cities are large and fortified. We even saw the descendants of Anak there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.29', 'BSB', 'The Amalekites live in the land of the Negev; the Hittites, Jebusites, and Amorites live in the hill country; and the Canaanites live by the sea and along the Jordan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.30', 'BSB', 'Then Caleb quieted the people before Moses and said, “We must go up and take possession of the land, for we can certainly conquer it!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.31', 'BSB', 'But the men who had gone up with him replied, “We cannot go up against the people, for they are stronger than we are!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.32', 'BSB', 'So they gave the Israelites a bad report about the land that they had spied out: “The land we explored devours its inhabitants, and all the people we saw there are great in stature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.13.33', 'BSB', 'We even saw the Nephilim there—the descendants of Anak that come from the Nephilim! We seemed like grasshoppers in our own sight, and we must have seemed the same to them!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.1', 'BSB', 'Then the whole congregation lifted up their voices and cried out, and that night the people wept.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.2', 'BSB', 'All the Israelites grumbled against Moses and Aaron, and the whole congregation said to them, “If only we had died in the land of Egypt, or if only we had died in this wilderness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.3', 'BSB', 'Why is the LORD bringing us into this land to fall by the sword? Our wives and children will become plunder. Would it not be better for us to go back to Egypt?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.4', 'BSB', 'So they said to one another, “Let us appoint a leader and return to Egypt.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.5', 'BSB', 'Then Moses and Aaron fell facedown before the whole assembly of the congregation of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.6', 'BSB', 'Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh, who were among those who had spied out the land, tore their clothes', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.7', 'BSB', 'and said to the whole congregation of Israel, “The land we passed through and explored is an exceedingly good land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.8', 'BSB', 'If the LORD delights in us, He will bring us into this land, a land flowing with milk and honey, and He will give it to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.9', 'BSB', 'Only do not rebel against the LORD, and do not be afraid of the people of the land, for they will be like bread for us. Their protection has been removed, and the LORD is with us. Do not be afraid of them!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.10', 'BSB', 'But the whole congregation threatened to stone Joshua and Caleb. Then the glory of the LORD appeared to all the Israelites at the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.11', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses, “How long will this people treat Me with contempt? How long will they refuse to believe in Me, despite all the signs I have performed among them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.12', 'BSB', 'I will strike them with a plague and destroy them—and I will make you into a nation greater and mightier than they are.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.13', 'BSB', 'But Moses said to the LORD, “The Egyptians will hear of it, for by Your strength You brought this people from among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.14', 'BSB', 'And they will tell it to the inhabitants of this land. They have already heard that You, O LORD, are in the midst of this people, that You, O LORD, have been seen face to face, that Your cloud stands over them, and that You go before them in a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.15', 'BSB', 'If You kill this people as one man, the nations who have heard of Your fame will say,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.16', 'BSB', '‘Because the LORD was unable to bring this people into the land He swore to give them, He has slaughtered them in the wilderness.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.17', 'BSB', 'So now I pray, may the power of my Lord be magnified, just as You have declared:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.18', 'BSB', '‘The LORD is slow to anger and abounding in loving devotion, forgiving iniquity and transgression. Yet He will by no means leave the guilty unpunished; He will visit the iniquity of the fathers upon their children to the third and fourth generation.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.19', 'BSB', 'Pardon, I pray, the iniquity of this people, in keeping with the greatness of Your loving devotion, just as You have forgiven them ever since they left Egypt.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.20', 'BSB', '“I have pardoned them as you requested,” the LORD replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.21', 'BSB', '“Yet as surely as I live and as surely as the whole earth is filled with the glory of the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.22', 'BSB', 'not one of the men who have seen My glory and the signs I performed in Egypt and in the wilderness—yet have tested Me and disobeyed Me these ten times—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.23', 'BSB', 'not one will ever see the land that I swore to give their fathers. None of those who have treated Me with contempt will see it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.24', 'BSB', 'But because My servant Caleb has a different spirit and has followed Me wholeheartedly, I will bring him into the land he has entered, and his descendants will inherit it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.25', 'BSB', 'Now since the Amalekites and Canaanites are living in the valleys, turn back tomorrow and head for the wilderness along the route to the Red Sea.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.26', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses and Aaron,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.27', 'BSB', '“How long will this wicked congregation grumble against Me? I have heard the complaints that the Israelites are making against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.28', 'BSB', 'So tell them: As surely as I live, declares the LORD, I will do to you exactly as I heard you say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.29', 'BSB', 'Your bodies will fall in this wilderness—all who were numbered in the census, everyone twenty years of age or older—because you have grumbled against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.30', 'BSB', 'Surely none of you will enter the land in which I swore to settle you, except Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.31', 'BSB', 'But I will bring your children, whom you said would become plunder, into the land you have rejected—and they will enjoy it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.32', 'BSB', 'As for you, however, your bodies will fall in this wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.33', 'BSB', 'Your children will be shepherds in the wilderness for forty years, and they will suffer for your unfaithfulness until the last of your bodies lies in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.34', 'BSB', 'In keeping with the forty days you spied out the land, you shall bear your guilt forty years—a year for each day—and you will experience My alienation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.35', 'BSB', 'I, the LORD, have spoken, and I will surely do these things to this entire wicked congregation, which has conspired against Me. They will meet their end in the wilderness, and there they will die.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.36', 'BSB', 'So the men Moses had sent to spy out the land, who had returned and made the whole congregation grumble against him by bringing out a bad report about the land—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.37', 'BSB', 'those men who had brought out the bad report about the land—were struck down by a plague before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.38', 'BSB', 'Of those men who had gone to spy out the land, only Joshua son of Nun and Caleb son of Jephunneh remained alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.39', 'BSB', 'And when Moses relayed these words to all the Israelites, the people mourned bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.40', 'BSB', 'Early the next morning they got up and went up toward the ridge of the hill country. “We have indeed sinned,” they said, “but we will go to the place the LORD has promised.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.41', 'BSB', 'But Moses said, “Why are you transgressing the commandment of the LORD? This will not succeed!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.42', 'BSB', 'Do not go up, lest you be struck down by your enemies, because the LORD is not among you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.43', 'BSB', 'For there the Amalekites and Canaanites will face you, and you will fall by the sword. Because you have turned away from the LORD, He will not be with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.44', 'BSB', 'But they dared to go up to the ridge of the hill country, though neither Moses nor the ark of the covenant of the LORD moved from the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.14.45', 'BSB', 'Then the Amalekites and Canaanites who lived in that part of the hill country came down, attacked them, and routed them all the way to Hormah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.2', 'BSB', '“Speak to the Israelites and tell them: After you enter the land that I am giving you as a home', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.3', 'BSB', 'and you present an offering made by fire to the LORD from the herd or flock to produce a pleasing aroma to the LORD—either a burnt offering or a sacrifice, for a special vow or freewill offering or appointed feast—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.4', 'BSB', 'then the one presenting his offering to the LORD shall also present a grain offering of a tenth of an ephah of fine flour mixed with a quarter hin of olive oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.5', 'BSB', 'With the burnt offering or sacrifice of each lamb, you are to prepare a quarter hin of wine as a drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.6', 'BSB', 'With a ram you are to prepare a grain offering of two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with a third of a hin of olive oil,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.7', 'BSB', 'and a third of a hin of wine as a drink offering, a pleasing aroma to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.8', 'BSB', 'When you prepare a young bull as a burnt offering or sacrifice to fulfill a vow or as a peace offering to the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.9', 'BSB', 'present with the bull a grain offering of three-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with half a hin of olive oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.10', 'BSB', 'Also present half a hin of wine as a drink offering. It is an offering made by fire, a pleasing aroma to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.11', 'BSB', 'This is to be done for each bull, ram, lamb, or goat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.12', 'BSB', 'This is how you must prepare each one, no matter how many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.13', 'BSB', 'Everyone who is native-born shall prepare these things in this way when he presents an offering made by fire as a pleasing aroma to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.14', 'BSB', 'And for the generations to come, if a foreigner residing with you or someone else among you wants to prepare an offering made by fire as a pleasing aroma to the LORD, he is to do exactly as you do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.15', 'BSB', 'The assembly is to have the same statute both for you and for the foreign resident; it is a permanent statute for the generations to come. You and the foreigner shall be the same before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.16', 'BSB', 'The same law and the same ordinance will apply both to you and to the foreigner residing with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.17', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.18', 'BSB', '“Speak to the Israelites and tell them: When you enter the land to which I am bringing you', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.19', 'BSB', 'and you eat the food of the land, you shall lift up an offering to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.20', 'BSB', 'From the first of your dough, you are to lift up a cake as a contribution; offer it just like an offering from the threshing floor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.21', 'BSB', 'Throughout your generations, you are to give the LORD an offering from the first of your dough.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.22', 'BSB', 'Now if you stray unintentionally and do not obey all these commandments that the LORD has spoken to Moses—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.23', 'BSB', 'all that the LORD has commanded you through Moses from the day the LORD gave them and continuing through the generations to come—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.24', 'BSB', 'and if it was done unintentionally without the knowledge of the congregation, then the whole congregation is to prepare one young bull as a burnt offering, a pleasing aroma to the LORD, with its grain offering and drink offering according to the regulation, and one male goat as a sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.25', 'BSB', 'The priest is to make atonement for the whole congregation of Israel, so that they may be forgiven; for the sin was unintentional and they have brought to the LORD an offering made by fire and a sin offering, presented before the LORD for their unintentional sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.26', 'BSB', 'Then the whole congregation of Israel and the foreigners residing among them will be forgiven, since it happened to all the people unintentionally.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.27', 'BSB', 'Also, if one person sins unintentionally, he is to present a year-old female goat as a sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.28', 'BSB', 'And the priest shall make atonement before the LORD on behalf of the person who erred by sinning unintentionally; and when atonement has been made for him, he will be forgiven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.29', 'BSB', 'You shall have the same law for the one who acts in error, whether he is a native-born Israelite or a foreigner residing among you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.30', 'BSB', 'But the person who sins defiantly, whether a native or foreigner, blasphemes the LORD. That person shall be cut off from among his people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.31', 'BSB', 'He shall certainly be cut off, because he has despised the word of the LORD and broken His commandment; his guilt remains on him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.32', 'BSB', 'While the Israelites were in the wilderness, a man was found gathering wood on the Sabbath day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.33', 'BSB', 'Those who found the man gathering wood brought him to Moses, Aaron, and the whole congregation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.34', 'BSB', 'and because it had not been declared what should be done to him, they placed him in custody.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.35', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses, “The man must surely be put to death. The whole congregation is to stone him outside the camp.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.36', 'BSB', 'So the whole congregation took the man outside the camp and stoned him to death, as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.37', 'BSB', 'Later, the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.38', 'BSB', '“Speak to the Israelites and tell them that throughout the generations to come they are to make for themselves tassels for the corners of their garments, with a blue cord on each tassel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.39', 'BSB', 'These will serve as tassels for you to look at, so that you may remember all the commandments of the LORD, that you may obey them and not prostitute yourselves by following your own heart and your own eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.40', 'BSB', 'Then you will remember and obey all My commandments, and you will be holy to your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.15.41', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD your God who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be your God. I am the LORD your God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.1', 'BSB', 'Now Korah son of Izhar, the son of Kohath son of Levi, along with some Reubenites—Dathan and Abiram, sons of Eliab, and On son of Peleth—conducted', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.2', 'BSB', 'a rebellion against Moses, along with 250 men of Israel renowned as leaders of the congregation and representatives in the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.3', 'BSB', 'They came together against Moses and Aaron and told them, “You have taken too much upon yourselves! For everyone in the entire congregation is holy, and the LORD is in their midst. Why then do you exalt yourselves above the assembly of the LORD?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.4', 'BSB', 'When Moses heard this, he fell facedown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.5', 'BSB', 'Then he said to Korah and all his followers, “Tomorrow morning the LORD will reveal who belongs to Him and who is holy, and He will bring that person near to Himself. The one He chooses, He will bring near to Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.6', 'BSB', 'You, Korah, and all your followers are to do as follows: Take censers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.7', 'BSB', 'and tomorrow you are to place fire and incense in them in the presence of the LORD. Then the man the LORD chooses will be the one who is holy. It is you sons of Levi who have taken too much upon yourselves!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.8', 'BSB', 'Moses also said to Korah, “Now listen, you sons of Levi!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.9', 'BSB', 'Is it not enough for you that the God of Israel has separated you from the congregation of Israel and brought you near to Himself to perform the work at the LORD’s tabernacle, and to stand before the congregation to minister to them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.10', 'BSB', 'He has brought you near, you and all your fellow Levites, but you are seeking the priesthood as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore, it is you and all your followers who have conspired against the LORD! As for Aaron, who is he that you should grumble against him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.12', 'BSB', 'Then Moses summoned Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, but they said, “We will not come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.13', 'BSB', 'Is it not enough that you have brought us up out of a land flowing with milk and honey to kill us in the wilderness? Must you also appoint yourself as ruler over us?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.14', 'BSB', 'Moreover, you have not brought us into a land flowing with milk and honey or given us an inheritance of fields and vineyards. Will you gouge out the eyes of these men? No, we will not come!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.15', 'BSB', 'Then Moses became very angry and said to the LORD, “Do not regard their offering. I have not taken one donkey from them or mistreated a single one of them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.16', 'BSB', 'And Moses said to Korah, “You and all your followers are to appear before the LORD tomorrow—you and they and Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.17', 'BSB', 'Each man is to take his censer, place incense in it, and present it before the LORD—250 censers. You and Aaron are to present your censers as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.18', 'BSB', 'So each man took his censer, put fire and incense in it, and stood with Moses and Aaron at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.19', 'BSB', 'When Korah had gathered his whole assembly against them at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, the glory of the LORD appeared to the whole congregation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.20', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses and Aaron,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.21', 'BSB', '“Separate yourselves from this congregation so that I may consume them in an instant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.22', 'BSB', 'But Moses and Aaron fell facedown and said, “O God, the God of the spirits of all flesh, when one man sins, will You be angry with the whole congregation?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.23', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.24', 'BSB', '“Tell the congregation to move away from the dwellings of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.25', 'BSB', 'So Moses got up and went to Dathan and Abiram, and the elders of Israel followed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.26', 'BSB', 'And he warned the congregation, “Move away now from the tents of these wicked men. Do not touch anything that belongs to them, or you will be swept away because of all their sins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.27', 'BSB', 'So they moved away from the dwellings of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram. Meanwhile, Dathan and Abiram had come out and stood at the entrances to their tents with their wives and children and infants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.28', 'BSB', 'Then Moses said, “This is how you will know that the LORD has sent me to do all these things, for it was not my own doing:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.29', 'BSB', 'If these men die a natural death, or if they suffer the fate of all men, then the LORD has not sent me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.30', 'BSB', 'But if the LORD brings about something unprecedented, and the earth opens its mouth and swallows them and all that belongs to them so that they go down alive into Sheol, then you will know that these men have treated the LORD with contempt.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.31', 'BSB', 'As soon as Moses had finished saying all this, the ground beneath them split open,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.32', 'BSB', 'and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them and their households—all Korah’s men and all their possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.33', 'BSB', 'They went down alive into Sheol with all they owned. The earth closed over them, and they vanished from the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.34', 'BSB', 'At their cries, all the people of Israel who were around them fled, saying, “The earth may swallow us too!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.35', 'BSB', 'And fire came forth from the LORD and consumed the 250 men who were offering the incense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.36', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.37', 'BSB', '“Tell Eleazar son of Aaron the priest to remove the censers from the flames and to scatter the coals far away, because the censers are holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.38', 'BSB', 'As for the censers of those who sinned at the cost of their own lives, hammer them into sheets to overlay the altar, for these were presented before the LORD, and so have become holy. They will serve as a sign to the Israelites.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.39', 'BSB', 'So Eleazar the priest took the bronze censers brought by those who had been burned up, and he had them hammered out to overlay the altar,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.40', 'BSB', 'just as the LORD commanded him through Moses. This was to be a reminder to the Israelites that no outsider who is not a descendant of Aaron should approach to offer incense before the LORD, lest he become like Korah and his followers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.41', 'BSB', 'The next day the whole congregation of Israel grumbled against Moses and Aaron, saying, “You have killed the LORD’s people!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.42', 'BSB', 'But when the congregation gathered against them, Moses and Aaron turned toward the Tent of Meeting, and suddenly the cloud covered it and the glory of the LORD appeared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.43', 'BSB', 'Then Moses and Aaron went to the front of the Tent of Meeting,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.44', 'BSB', 'and the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.45', 'BSB', '“Get away from this congregation so that I may consume them in an instant.” And Moses and Aaron fell facedown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.46', 'BSB', 'Moses said to Aaron, “Take your censer, place fire from the altar in it, and add incense. Go quickly to the congregation and make atonement for them, because wrath has come out from the LORD; the plague has begun.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.47', 'BSB', 'So Aaron took the censer as Moses had ordered and ran into the midst of the assembly. And seeing that the plague had begun among the people, he offered the incense and made atonement for the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.48', 'BSB', 'He stood between the living and the dead, and the plague was halted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.49', 'BSB', 'But those who died from the plague numbered 14,700, in addition to those who had died on account of Korah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.16.50', 'BSB', 'Then Aaron returned to Moses at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, since the plague had been halted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.1', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.2', 'BSB', '“Speak to the Israelites and take from them twelve staffs, one from the leader of each tribe. Write each man’s name on his staff,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.3', 'BSB', 'and write Aaron’s name on the staff of Levi, because there must be one staff for the head of each tribe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.4', 'BSB', 'Place the staffs in the Tent of Meeting in front of the Testimony, where I meet with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.5', 'BSB', 'The staff belonging to the man I choose will sprout, and I will rid Myself of the constant grumbling of the Israelites against you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.6', 'BSB', 'So Moses spoke to the Israelites, and each of their leaders gave him a staff—one for each of the leaders of their tribes, twelve staffs in all. And Aaron’s staff was among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.7', 'BSB', 'Then Moses placed the staffs before the LORD in the Tent of the Testimony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.8', 'BSB', 'The next day Moses entered the Tent of the Testimony and saw that Aaron’s staff, representing the house of Levi, had sprouted, put forth buds, blossomed, and produced almonds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.9', 'BSB', 'Then Moses brought out all the staffs from the LORD’s presence to all the Israelites. They saw them, and each man took his own staff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.10', 'BSB', 'The LORD said to Moses, “Put Aaron’s staff back in front of the Testimony, to be kept as a sign for the rebellious, so that you may put an end to their grumbling against Me, lest they die.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.11', 'BSB', 'So Moses did as the LORD had commanded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.12', 'BSB', 'Then the Israelites declared to Moses, “Look, we are perishing! We are lost; we are all lost!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.17.13', 'BSB', 'Anyone who comes near the tabernacle of the LORD will die. Are we all going to perish?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.1', 'BSB', 'So the LORD said to Aaron, “You and your sons and your father’s house must bear the iniquity involving the sanctuary. And you and your sons alone must bear the iniquity involving your priesthood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.2', 'BSB', 'But bring with you also your brothers from the tribe of Levi, the tribe of your father, that they may join you and assist you and your sons before the Tent of the Testimony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.3', 'BSB', 'And they shall attend to your duties and to all the duties of the Tent; but they must not come near to the furnishings of the sanctuary or the altar, or both they and you will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.4', 'BSB', 'They are to join you and attend to the duties of the Tent of Meeting, doing all the work at the Tent; but no outsider may come near you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.5', 'BSB', 'And you shall attend to the duties of the sanctuary and of the altar, so that wrath may not fall on the Israelites again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.6', 'BSB', 'Behold, I Myself have selected your fellow Levites from the Israelites as a gift to you, dedicated to the LORD to perform the service for the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.7', 'BSB', 'But only you and your sons shall attend to your priesthood for everything concerning the altar and what is inside the veil, and you are to perform that service. I am giving you the work of the priesthood as a gift, but any outsider who comes near the sanctuary must be put to death.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.8', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Aaron, “Behold, I have put you in charge of My offerings. As for all the sacred offerings of the Israelites, I have given them to you and your sons as a portion and a permanent statute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.9', 'BSB', 'A portion of the most holy offerings reserved from the fire will be yours. From all the offerings they render to Me as most holy offerings, whether grain offerings or sin offerings or guilt offerings, that part belongs to you and your sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.10', 'BSB', 'You are to eat it as a most holy offering, and every male may eat it. You shall regard it as holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.11', 'BSB', 'And this is yours as well: the offering of their gifts, along with all the wave offerings of the Israelites. I have given this to you and your sons and daughters as a permanent statute. Every ceremonially clean person in your household may eat it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.12', 'BSB', 'I give you all the freshest olive oil and all the finest new wine and grain that the Israelites give to the LORD as their firstfruits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.13', 'BSB', 'The firstfruits of everything in their land that they bring to the LORD will belong to you. Every ceremonially clean person in your household may eat them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.14', 'BSB', 'Every devoted thing in Israel belongs to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.15', 'BSB', 'The firstborn of every womb, whether man or beast, that is offered to the LORD belongs to you. But you must surely redeem every firstborn son and every firstborn male of unclean animals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.16', 'BSB', 'You are to pay the redemption price for a month-old male according to your valuation: five shekels of silver, according to the sanctuary shekel, which is twenty gerahs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.17', 'BSB', 'But you must not redeem the firstborn of an ox, a sheep, or a goat; they are holy. You are to sprinkle their blood on the altar and burn their fat as an offering made by fire, a pleasing aroma to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.18', 'BSB', 'And their meat belongs to you, just as the breast and right thigh of the wave offering belong to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.19', 'BSB', 'All the holy offerings that the Israelites present to the LORD I give to you and to your sons and daughters as a permanent statute. It is a permanent covenant of salt before the LORD for you and your offspring.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.20', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Aaron, “You will have no inheritance in their land, nor will you have any portion among them. I am your portion and your inheritance among the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.21', 'BSB', 'Behold, I have given to the Levites all the tithes in Israel as an inheritance in return for the work they do, the service of the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.22', 'BSB', 'No longer may the Israelites come near to the Tent of Meeting, or they will incur guilt and die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.23', 'BSB', 'The Levites are to perform the work of the Tent of Meeting, and they must bear their iniquity. This is a permanent statute for the generations to come. The Levites will not receive an inheritance among the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.24', 'BSB', 'For I have given to the Levites as their inheritance the tithe that the Israelites present to the LORD as a contribution. That is why I told them that they would not receive an inheritance among the Israelites.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.25', 'BSB', 'And the LORD instructed Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.26', 'BSB', '“Speak to the Levites and tell them: ‘When you receive from the Israelites the tithe that I have given you as your inheritance, you must present part of it as an offering to the LORD—a tithe of the tithe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.27', 'BSB', 'Your offering will be reckoned to you as grain from the threshing floor or juice from the winepress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.28', 'BSB', 'So you are to present an offering to the LORD from all the tithes you receive from the Israelites, and from these you are to give the LORD’s offering to Aaron the priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.29', 'BSB', 'You must present the offering due the LORD from all the best of every gift, the holiest part of it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.30', 'BSB', 'Therefore say to the Levites, ‘When you have presented the best part, it will be reckoned to you as the produce of the threshing floor or winepress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.31', 'BSB', 'And you and your households may eat the rest of it anywhere; it is the compensation for your work at the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.18.32', 'BSB', 'Once you have presented the best part of it, you will not incur guilt because of it. But you must not defile the sacred offerings of the Israelites, or else you will die.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses and Aaron,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.2', 'BSB', '“This is the statute of the law that the LORD has commanded: Instruct the Israelites to bring you an unblemished red heifer that has no defect and has never been placed under a yoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.3', 'BSB', 'Give it to Eleazar the priest, and he will have it brought outside the camp and slaughtered in his presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.4', 'BSB', 'Eleazar the priest is to take some of its blood on his finger and sprinkle it seven times toward the front of the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.5', 'BSB', 'Then the heifer must be burned in his sight. Its hide, its flesh, and its blood are to be burned, along with its dung.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.6', 'BSB', 'The priest is to take cedar wood, hyssop, and scarlet wool and throw them onto the burning heifer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.7', 'BSB', 'Then the priest must wash his clothes and bathe his body in water; after that he may enter the camp, but he will be ceremonially unclean until evening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.8', 'BSB', 'The one who burned the heifer must also wash his clothes and bathe his body in water, and he too will be ceremonially unclean until evening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.9', 'BSB', 'Then a man who is ceremonially clean is to gather up the ashes of the heifer and store them in a ceremonially clean place outside the camp. They must be kept by the congregation of Israel for preparing the water of purification; this is for purification from sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.10', 'BSB', 'The man who has gathered up the ashes of the heifer must also wash his clothes, and he will be ceremonially unclean until evening. This is a permanent statute for the Israelites and for the foreigner residing among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.11', 'BSB', 'Whoever touches any dead body will be unclean for seven days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.12', 'BSB', 'He must purify himself with the water on the third day and on the seventh day; then he will be clean. But if he does not purify himself on the third and seventh days, he will not be clean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.13', 'BSB', 'Anyone who touches a human corpse and fails to purify himself defiles the tabernacle of the LORD. That person must be cut off from Israel. He remains unclean, because the water of purification has not been sprinkled on him, and his uncleanness is still on him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.14', 'BSB', 'This is the law when a person dies in a tent: Everyone who enters the tent and everyone already in the tent will be unclean for seven days,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.15', 'BSB', 'and any open container without a lid fastened on it is unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.16', 'BSB', 'Anyone in the open field who touches someone who has been killed by the sword or has died of natural causes, or anyone who touches a human bone or a grave, will be unclean for seven days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.17', 'BSB', 'For the purification of the unclean person, take some of the ashes of the burnt sin offering, put them in a jar, and pour fresh water over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.18', 'BSB', 'Then a man who is ceremonially clean is to take some hyssop, dip it in the water, and sprinkle the tent, all the furnishings, and the people who were there. He is also to sprinkle the one who touched a bone, a grave, or a person who has died or been slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.19', 'BSB', 'The man who is ceremonially clean is to sprinkle the unclean person on the third day and on the seventh day. After he purifies the unclean person on the seventh day, the one being cleansed must wash his clothes and bathe in water, and that evening he will be clean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.20', 'BSB', 'But if a person who is unclean does not purify himself, he will be cut off from the assembly, because he has defiled the sanctuary of the LORD. The water of purification has not been sprinkled on him; he is unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.21', 'BSB', 'This is a permanent statute for the people: The one who sprinkles the water of purification must wash his clothes, and whoever touches the water of purification will be unclean until evening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.19.22', 'BSB', 'Anything the unclean person touches will become unclean, and anyone who touches it will be unclean until evening.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.1', 'BSB', 'In the first month, the whole congregation of Israel entered the Wilderness of Zin and stayed in Kadesh. There Miriam died and was buried.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.2', 'BSB', 'Now there was no water for the congregation, so they gathered against Moses and Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.3', 'BSB', 'The people quarreled with Moses and said, “If only we had perished with our brothers before the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.4', 'BSB', 'Why have you brought the LORD’s assembly into this wilderness for us and our livestock to die here?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.5', 'BSB', 'Why have you led us up out of Egypt to bring us to this wretched place? It is not a place of grain, figs, vines, or pomegranates—and there is no water to drink!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.6', 'BSB', 'Then Moses and Aaron went from the presence of the assembly to the entrance to the Tent of Meeting. They fell facedown, and the glory of the LORD appeared to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.7', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.8', 'BSB', '“Take the staff and assemble the congregation. You and your brother Aaron are to speak to the rock while they watch, and it will pour out its water. You will bring out water from the rock and provide drink for the congregation and their livestock.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.9', 'BSB', 'So Moses took the staff from the LORD’s presence, just as he had been commanded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.10', 'BSB', 'Then Moses and Aaron gathered the assembly in front of the rock, and Moses said to them, “Listen now, you rebels, must we bring you water out of this rock?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.11', 'BSB', 'Then Moses raised his hand and struck the rock twice with his staff, so that a great amount of water gushed out, and the congregation and their livestock were able to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.12', 'BSB', 'But the LORD said to Moses and Aaron, “Because you did not trust Me to show My holiness in the sight of the Israelites, you will not bring this assembly into the land that I have given them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.13', 'BSB', 'These were the waters of Meribah, where the Israelites quarreled with the LORD, and He showed His holiness among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.14', 'BSB', 'From Kadesh, Moses sent messengers to tell the king of Edom, “This is what your brother Israel says: You know all the hardship that has befallen us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.15', 'BSB', 'how our fathers went down to Egypt, where we lived many years. The Egyptians mistreated us and our fathers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.16', 'BSB', 'and when we cried out to the LORD, He heard our voice, sent an angel, and brought us out of Egypt. Now look, we are in Kadesh, a city on the edge of your territory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.17', 'BSB', 'Please let us pass through your land. We will not cut through any field or vineyard, or drink water from any well. We will stay on the King’s Highway; we will not turn to the right or to the left until we have passed through your territory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.18', 'BSB', 'But Edom answered, “You may not travel through our land, or we will come out and confront you with the sword.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.19', 'BSB', '“We will stay on the main road,” the Israelites replied, “and if we or our herds drink your water, we will pay for it. There will be no problem; only let us pass through on foot.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.20', 'BSB', 'But Edom insisted, “You may not pass through.” And they came out to confront the Israelites with a large army and a strong hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.21', 'BSB', 'So Edom refused to allow Israel to pass through their territory, and Israel turned away from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.22', 'BSB', 'After they had set out from Kadesh, the whole congregation of Israel came to Mount Hor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.23', 'BSB', 'And at Mount Hor, near the border of the land of Edom, the LORD said to Moses and Aaron,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.24', 'BSB', '“Aaron will be gathered to his people; he will not enter the land that I have given the Israelites, because both of you rebelled against My command at the waters of Meribah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.25', 'BSB', 'Take Aaron and his son Eleazar and bring them up Mount Hor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.26', 'BSB', 'Remove Aaron’s priestly garments and put them on his son Eleazar. Aaron will be gathered to his people and will die there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.27', 'BSB', 'So Moses did as the LORD had commanded, and they climbed Mount Hor in the sight of the whole congregation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.28', 'BSB', 'After Moses had removed Aaron’s garments and put them on his son Eleazar, Aaron died there on top of the mountain. Then Moses and Eleazar came down from the mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.20.29', 'BSB', 'When the whole congregation saw that Aaron had died, the entire house of Israel mourned for him thirty days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.1', 'BSB', 'When the Canaanite king of Arad, who lived in the Negev, heard that Israel was coming along the road to Atharim, he attacked Israel and captured some prisoners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.2', 'BSB', 'So Israel made a vow to the LORD: “If You will deliver this people into our hands, we will devote their cities to destruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.3', 'BSB', 'And the LORD heard Israel’s plea and delivered up the Canaanites. Israel devoted them and their cities to destruction; so they named the place Hormah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.4', 'BSB', 'Then they set out from Mount Hor along the route to the Red Sea, in order to bypass the land of Edom. But the people grew impatient on the journey', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.5', 'BSB', 'and spoke against God and against Moses: “Why have you led us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? There is no bread or water, and we detest this wretched food!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.6', 'BSB', 'So the LORD sent venomous snakes among the people, and many of the Israelites were bitten and died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.7', 'BSB', 'Then the people came to Moses and said, “We have sinned by speaking against the LORD and against you. Intercede with the LORD so He will take the snakes away from us.” So Moses interceded for the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.8', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses, “Make a fiery serpent and mount it on a pole. When anyone who is bitten looks at it, he will live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.9', 'BSB', 'So Moses made a bronze snake and mounted it on a pole. If anyone who was bitten looked at the bronze snake, he would live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.10', 'BSB', 'Then the Israelites set out and camped at Oboth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.11', 'BSB', 'They journeyed from Oboth and camped at Iye-abarim in the wilderness opposite Moab to the east.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.12', 'BSB', 'From there they set out and camped in the Valley of Zered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.13', 'BSB', 'From there they moved on and camped on the other side of the Arnon, in the wilderness that extends into the Amorite territory. Now the Arnon is the border between the Moabites and the Amorites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore it is stated in the Book of the Wars of the LORD: “Waheb in Suphah and the wadis of the Arnon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.15', 'BSB', 'even the slopes of the wadis that extend to the site of Ar and lie along the border of Moab.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.16', 'BSB', 'From there they went on to Beer, the well where the LORD said to Moses, “Gather the people so that I may give them water.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.17', 'BSB', 'Then Israel sang this song: “Spring up, O well, all of you sing to it!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.18', 'BSB', 'The princes dug the well; the nobles of the people hollowed it out with their scepters and with their staffs.” From the wilderness the Israelites went on to Mattanah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.19', 'BSB', 'and from Mattanah to Nahaliel, and from Nahaliel to Bamoth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.20', 'BSB', 'and from Bamoth to the valley in Moab where the top of Pisgah overlooks the wasteland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.21', 'BSB', 'Then Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.22', 'BSB', '“Let us pass through your land. We will not cut through any field or vineyard, or drink water from any well. We will stay on the King’s Highway until we have passed through your territory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.23', 'BSB', 'But Sihon would not let Israel pass through his territory. Instead, he gathered his whole army and went out to confront Israel in the wilderness. When he came to Jahaz, he fought against Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.24', 'BSB', 'And Israel put him to the sword and took possession of his land, from the Arnon to the Jabbok—but only up to the border of the Ammonites, because it was fortified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.25', 'BSB', 'Israel captured all the cities of the Amorites and occupied them, including Heshbon and all its villages.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.26', 'BSB', 'Heshbon was the city of Sihon king of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab and taken all his land as far as the Arnon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.27', 'BSB', 'That is why the poets say: “Come to Heshbon, let it be rebuilt; let the city of Sihon be restored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.28', 'BSB', 'For a fire went out from Heshbon, a blaze from the city of Sihon. It consumed Ar of Moab, the rulers of Arnon’s heights.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.29', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, O Moab! You are destroyed, O people of Chemosh! He gave up his sons as refugees, and his daughters into captivity to Sihon king of the Amorites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.30', 'BSB', 'But we have overthrown them; Heshbon is destroyed as far as Dibon. We demolished them as far as Nophah, which reaches to Medeba.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.31', 'BSB', 'So Israel lived in the land of the Amorites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.32', 'BSB', 'After Moses had sent spies to Jazer, Israel captured its villages and drove out the Amorites who were there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.33', 'BSB', 'Then they turned and went up the road to Bashan, and Og king of Bashan and his whole army came out to meet them in battle at Edrei.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.34', 'BSB', 'But the LORD said to Moses, “Do not fear him, for I have delivered him into your hand, along with all his people and his land. Do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.21.35', 'BSB', 'So they struck down Og, along with his sons and his whole army, until no remnant was left. And they took possession of his land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.1', 'BSB', 'Then the Israelites traveled on and camped in the plains of Moab near the Jordan, across from Jericho.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.2', 'BSB', 'Now Balak son of Zippor saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.3', 'BSB', 'and Moab was terrified of the people because they were numerous. Indeed, Moab dreaded the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.4', 'BSB', 'So the Moabites said to the elders of Midian, “This horde will devour everything around us, as an ox licks up the grass of the field.” Since Balak son of Zippor was king of Moab at that time,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.5', 'BSB', 'he sent messengers to Balaam son of Beor at Pethor, which is by the Euphrates in the land of his people. “Behold, a people has come out of Egypt,” said Balak. “They cover the face of the land and have settled next to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.6', 'BSB', 'So please come now and put a curse on this people, because they are too mighty for me. Perhaps I may be able to defeat them and drive them out of the land; for I know that those you bless are blessed, and those you curse are cursed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.7', 'BSB', 'The elders of Moab and Midian departed with the fees for divination in hand. They came to Balaam and relayed to him the words of Balak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.8', 'BSB', '“Spend the night here,” Balaam replied, “and I will give you the answer that the LORD speaks to me.” So the princes of Moab stayed with Balaam.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.9', 'BSB', 'Then God came to Balaam and asked, “Who are these men with you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.10', 'BSB', 'And Balaam said to God, “Balak son of Zippor, king of Moab, sent me this message:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.11', 'BSB', '‘Behold, a people has come out of Egypt, and they cover the face of the land. Now come and put a curse on them for me. Perhaps I may be able to fight against them and drive them away.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.12', 'BSB', 'But God said to Balaam, “Do not go with them. You are not to curse this people, for they are blessed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.13', 'BSB', 'So Balaam got up the next morning and said to Balak’s princes, “Go back to your homeland, because the LORD has refused to let me go with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.14', 'BSB', 'And the princes of Moab arose, returned to Balak, and said, “Balaam refused to come with us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.15', 'BSB', 'Then Balak sent other princes, more numerous and more distinguished than the first messengers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.16', 'BSB', 'They came to Balaam and said, “This is what Balak son of Zippor says: ‘Please let nothing hinder you from coming to me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.17', 'BSB', 'for I will honor you richly and do whatever you say. So please come and put a curse on this people for me!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.18', 'BSB', 'But Balaam replied to the servants of Balak, “If Balak were to give me his house full of silver and gold, I could not do anything small or great to go beyond the command of the LORD my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.19', 'BSB', 'So now, please stay here overnight as the others did, that I may find out what else the LORD has to tell me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.20', 'BSB', 'That night God came to Balaam and said, “Since these men have come to summon you, get up and go with them, but you must only do what I tell you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.21', 'BSB', 'So in the morning Balaam got up, saddled his donkey, and went with the princes of Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.22', 'BSB', 'Then God’s anger was kindled because Balaam was going along, and the angel of the LORD stood in the road to oppose him. Balaam was riding his donkey, and his two servants were with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.23', 'BSB', 'When the donkey saw the angel of the LORD standing in the road with a drawn sword in his hand, she turned off the path and went into a field. So Balaam beat her to return her to the path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.24', 'BSB', 'Then the angel of the LORD stood in a narrow passage between two vineyards, with walls on either side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.25', 'BSB', 'And the donkey saw the angel of the LORD and pressed herself against the wall, crushing Balaam’s foot against it. So he beat her once again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.26', 'BSB', 'And the angel of the LORD moved on ahead and stood in a narrow place where there was no room to turn to the right or left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.27', 'BSB', 'When the donkey saw the angel of the LORD, she lay down under Balaam, and he became furious and beat her with his staff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.28', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD opened the donkey’s mouth, and she said to Balaam, “What have I done to you that you have beaten me these three times?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.29', 'BSB', 'Balaam answered the donkey, “You have made a fool of me! If I had a sword in my hand, I would kill you right now!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.30', 'BSB', 'But the donkey said to Balaam, “Am I not the donkey you have ridden all your life until today? Have I ever treated you this way before?” “No,” he replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.31', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD opened Balaam’s eyes, and he saw the angel of the LORD standing in the road with a drawn sword in his hand. And Balaam bowed low and fell facedown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.32', 'BSB', 'The angel of the LORD asked him, “Why have you beaten your donkey these three times? Behold, I have come out to oppose you, because your way is perverse before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.33', 'BSB', 'The donkey saw me and turned away from me these three times. If she had not turned away, then by now I would surely have killed you and let her live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.34', 'BSB', '“I have sinned,” Balaam said to the angel of the LORD, “for I did not realize that you were standing in the road to confront me. And now, if this is displeasing in your sight, I will go back home.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.35', 'BSB', 'But the angel of the LORD said to Balaam, “Go with the men, but you are to speak only what I tell you.” So Balaam went with the princes of Balak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.36', 'BSB', 'When Balak heard that Balaam was coming, he went out to meet him at the Moabite city on the Arnon border, at the edge of his territory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.37', 'BSB', 'And he said to Balaam, “Did I not send you an urgent summons? Why did you not come to me? Am I really not able to richly reward you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.38', 'BSB', '“See, I have come to you,” Balaam replied, “but can I say just anything? I must speak only the word that God puts in my mouth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.39', 'BSB', 'So Balaam accompanied Balak, and they came to Kiriath-huzoth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.40', 'BSB', 'Balak sacrificed cattle and sheep, and he gave portions to Balaam and the princes who were with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.22.41', 'BSB', 'The next morning, Balak took Balaam and brought him up to Bamoth-baal. From there he could see the outskirts of the camp of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.1', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam said to Balak, “Build for me seven altars here, and prepare for me seven bulls and seven rams.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.2', 'BSB', 'So Balak did as Balaam had instructed, and Balak and Balaam offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.3', 'BSB', '“Stay here by your burnt offering while I am gone,” Balaam said to Balak. “Perhaps the LORD will meet with me. And whatever He reveals to me, I will tell you.” So Balaam went off to a barren height,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.4', 'BSB', 'and God met with him. “I have set up seven altars,” Balaam said, “and on each altar I have offered a bull and a ram.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.5', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD put a message in Balaam’s mouth, saying, “Return to Balak and give him this message.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.6', 'BSB', 'So he returned to Balak, who was standing there beside his burnt offering, with all the princes of Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.7', 'BSB', 'And Balaam lifted up an oracle, saying: “Balak brought me from Aram, the king of Moab from the mountains of the east. ‘Come,’ he said, ‘put a curse on Jacob for me; come and denounce Israel!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.8', 'BSB', 'How can I curse what God has not cursed? How can I denounce what the LORD has not denounced?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.9', 'BSB', 'For I see them from atop the rocky cliffs, and I watch them from the hills. Behold, a people dwelling apart, not reckoning themselves among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.10', 'BSB', 'Who can count the dust of Jacob or number even a fourth of Israel? Let me die the death of the righteous; let my end be like theirs!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.11', 'BSB', 'Then Balak said to Balaam, “What have you done to me? I brought you here to curse my enemies, and behold, you have only blessed them!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.12', 'BSB', 'But Balaam replied, “Should I not speak exactly what the LORD puts in my mouth?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.13', 'BSB', 'Then Balak said to him, “Please come with me to another place where you can see them. You will only see the outskirts of their camp—not all of them. And from there, curse them for me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.14', 'BSB', 'So Balak took him to the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah, where he built seven altars and offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.15', 'BSB', 'Balaam said to Balak, “Stay here beside your burnt offering while I meet the LORD over there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.16', 'BSB', 'And the LORD met with Balaam and put a message in his mouth, saying, “Return to Balak and speak what I tell you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.17', 'BSB', 'So he returned to Balak, who was standing there by his burnt offering with the princes of Moab. “What did the LORD say?” Balak asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.18', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam lifted up an oracle, saying: “Arise, O Balak, and listen; give ear to me, O son of Zippor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.19', 'BSB', 'God is not a man, that He should lie, or a son of man, that He should change His mind. Does He speak and not act? Does He promise and not fulfill?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.20', 'BSB', 'I have indeed received a command to bless; He has blessed, and I cannot change it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.21', 'BSB', 'He considers no disaster for Jacob; He sees no trouble for Israel. The LORD their God is with them, and the shout of the King is among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.22', 'BSB', 'God brought them out of Egypt with strength like a wild ox.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.23', 'BSB', 'For there is no spell against Jacob and no divination against Israel. It will now be said of Jacob and Israel, ‘What great things God has done!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.24', 'BSB', 'Behold, the people rise like a lioness; they rouse themselves like a lion, not resting until they devour their prey and drink the blood of the slain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.25', 'BSB', 'Now Balak said to Balaam, “Then neither curse them at all nor bless them at all!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.26', 'BSB', 'But Balaam replied, “Did I not tell you that whatever the LORD says, I must do?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.27', 'BSB', '“Please come,” said Balak, “I will take you to another place. Perhaps it will please God that you curse them for me from there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.28', 'BSB', 'And Balak took Balaam to the top of Peor, which overlooks the wasteland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.29', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam said, “Build for me seven altars here, and prepare for me seven bulls and seven rams.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.23.30', 'BSB', 'So Balak did as Balaam had instructed, and he offered a bull and a ram on each altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.1', 'BSB', 'And when Balaam saw that it pleased the LORD to bless Israel, he did not resort to sorcery as on previous occasions, but he turned his face toward the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.2', 'BSB', 'When Balaam looked up and saw Israel encamped tribe by tribe, the Spirit of God came upon him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.3', 'BSB', 'and he lifted up an oracle, saying: “This is the prophecy of Balaam son of Beor, the prophecy of a man whose eyes are open,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.4', 'BSB', 'the prophecy of one who hears the words of God, who sees a vision from the Almighty, who bows down with eyes wide open:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.5', 'BSB', 'How lovely are your tents, O Jacob, your dwellings, O Israel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.6', 'BSB', 'They spread out like palm groves, like gardens beside a stream, like aloes the LORD has planted, like cedars beside the waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.7', 'BSB', 'Water will flow from his buckets, and his seed will have abundant water. His king will be greater than Agag, and his kingdom will be exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.8', 'BSB', 'God brought him out of Egypt with strength like a wild ox, to devour hostile nations and crush their bones, to pierce them with arrows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.9', 'BSB', 'He crouches, he lies down like a lion; like a lioness, who dares to rouse him? Blessed are those who bless you and cursed are those who curse you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.10', 'BSB', 'Then Balak’s anger burned against Balaam, and he struck his hands together and said to Balaam, “I summoned you to curse my enemies, but behold, you have persisted in blessing them these three times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore, flee at once to your home! I said I would richly reward you, but instead the LORD has denied your reward.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.12', 'BSB', 'Balaam answered Balak, “Did I not already tell the messengers you sent me', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.13', 'BSB', 'that even if Balak were to give me his house full of silver and gold, I could not do anything of my own accord, good or bad, to go beyond the command of the LORD? I will speak whatever the LORD says.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.14', 'BSB', 'Now I am going back to my people, but come, let me warn you what this people will do to your people in the days to come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.15', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam lifted up an oracle, saying, “This is the prophecy of Balaam son of Beor, the prophecy of a man whose eyes are open,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.16', 'BSB', 'the prophecy of one who hears the words of God, who has knowledge from the Most High, who sees a vision from the Almighty, who bows down with eyes wide open:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.17', 'BSB', 'I see him, but not now; I behold him, but not near. A star will come forth from Jacob, and a scepter will arise from Israel. He will crush the skulls of Moab and strike down all the sons of Sheth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.18', 'BSB', 'Edom will become a possession, as will Seir, his enemy; but Israel will perform with valor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.19', 'BSB', 'A ruler will come from Jacob and destroy the survivors of the city.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.20', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam saw Amalek and lifted up an oracle, saying: “Amalek was first among the nations, but his end is destruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.21', 'BSB', 'Next he saw the Kenites and lifted up an oracle, saying: “Your dwelling place is secure, and your nest is set in a cliff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.22', 'BSB', 'Yet Kain will be destroyed when Asshur takes you captive.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.23', 'BSB', 'Once more Balaam lifted up an oracle, saying: “Ah, who can live unless God has ordained it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.24', 'BSB', 'Ships will come from the coasts of Cyprus; they will subdue Asshur and Eber, but they too will perish forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.24.25', 'BSB', 'Then Balaam arose and returned to his homeland, and Balak also went on his way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.1', 'BSB', 'While Israel was staying in Shittim, the men began to indulge in sexual immorality with the daughters of Moab,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.2', 'BSB', 'who also invited them to the sacrifices for their gods. And the people ate and bowed down to these gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.3', 'BSB', 'So Israel joined in worshiping Baal of Peor, and the anger of the LORD burned against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.4', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses, “Take all the leaders of the people and execute them in broad daylight before the LORD, so that His fierce anger may turn away from Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.5', 'BSB', 'So Moses told the judges of Israel, “Each of you must kill all of his men who have joined in worshiping Baal of Peor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.6', 'BSB', 'Just then an Israelite man brought to his family a Midianite woman in the sight of Moses and the whole congregation of Israel while they were weeping at the entrance to the Tent of Meeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.7', 'BSB', 'On seeing this, Phinehas son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, got up from the assembly, took a spear in his hand,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.8', 'BSB', 'followed the Israelite into his tent, and drove the spear through both of them—through the Israelite and on through the belly of the woman. So the plague against the Israelites was halted,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.9', 'BSB', 'but those who died in the plague numbered 24,000.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.10', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.11', 'BSB', '“Phinehas son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, has turned My wrath away from the Israelites; for he was zealous for My sake among them, so that I did not consume the Israelites in My zeal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.12', 'BSB', 'Declare, therefore, that I am granting him My covenant of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.13', 'BSB', 'It will be a covenant of permanent priesthood for him and his descendants, because he was zealous for his God and made atonement for the Israelites.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.14', 'BSB', 'The name of the Israelite who was slain with the Midianite woman was Zimri son of Salu, the leader of a Simeonite family.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.15', 'BSB', 'And the name of the slain Midianite woman was Cozbi, the daughter of Zur, a tribal chief of a Midianite family.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.16', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.17', 'BSB', '“Attack the Midianites and strike them dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.25.18', 'BSB', 'For they assailed you deceitfully when they seduced you in the matter of Peor and their sister Cozbi, the daughter of the Midianite leader, the woman who was killed on the day the plague came because of Peor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.1', 'BSB', 'After the plague had ended, the LORD said to Moses and Eleazar son of Aaron the priest,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.2', 'BSB', '“Take a census of the whole congregation of Israel by the houses of their fathers—all those twenty years of age or older who can serve in the army of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.3', 'BSB', 'So on the plains of Moab by the Jordan, across from Jericho, Moses and Eleazar the priest issued the instruction,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.4', 'BSB', '“Take a census of the men twenty years of age or older, as the LORD has commanded Moses.” And these were the Israelites who came out of the land of Egypt:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.5', 'BSB', 'Reuben was the firstborn of Israel. These were the descendants of Reuben: The Hanochite clan from Hanoch, the Palluite clan from Pallu,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.6', 'BSB', 'the Hezronite clan from Hezron, and the Carmite clan from Carmi.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.7', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Reuben, and their registration numbered 43,730.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.8', 'BSB', 'Now the son of Pallu was Eliab,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.9', 'BSB', 'and the sons of Eliab were Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram. It was Dathan and Abiram, chosen by the congregation, who fought against Moses and Aaron with the followers of Korah who rebelled against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.10', 'BSB', 'And the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them along with Korah, whose followers died when the fire consumed 250 men. They serve as a warning sign.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.11', 'BSB', 'However, the line of Korah did not die out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.12', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Simeon by their clans: The Nemuelite clan from Nemuel, the Jaminite clan from Jamin, the Jachinite clan from Jachin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.13', 'BSB', 'the Zerahite clan from Zerah, and the Shaulite clan from Shaul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.14', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Simeon, and there were 22,200 men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.15', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Gad by their clans: The Zephonite clan from Zephon, the Haggite clan from Haggi, the Shunite clan from Shuni,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.16', 'BSB', 'the Oznite clan from Ozni, the Erite clan from Eri,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.17', 'BSB', 'the Arodite clan from Arod, and the Arelite clan from Areli.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.18', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Gad, and their registration numbered 40,500.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.19', 'BSB', 'The sons of Judah were Er and Onan, but they died in the land of Canaan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.20', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Judah by their clans: The Shelanite clan from Shelah, the Perezite clan from Perez, and the Zerahite clan from Zerah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.21', 'BSB', 'And these were the descendants of Perez: the Hezronite clan from Hezron and the Hamulite clan from Hamul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.22', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Judah, and their registration numbered 76,500.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.23', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Issachar by their clans: The Tolaite clan from Tola, the Punite clan from Puvah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.24', 'BSB', 'the Jashubite clan from Jashub, and the Shimronite clan from Shimron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.25', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Issachar, and their registration numbered 64,300.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.26', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Zebulun by their clans: The Seredite clan from Sered, the Elonite clan from Elon, and the Jahleelite clan from Jahleel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.27', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Zebulun, and their registration numbered 60,500.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.28', 'BSB', 'The descendants of Joseph included the clans of Manasseh and Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.29', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Manasseh: The Machirite clan from Machir, the father of Gilead, and the Gileadite clan from Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.30', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Gilead: the Iezerite clan from Iezer, the Helekite clan from Helek,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.31', 'BSB', 'the Asrielite clan from Asriel, the Shechemite clan from Shechem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.32', 'BSB', 'the Shemidaite clan from Shemida, and the Hepherite clan from Hepher.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.33', 'BSB', 'Now Zelophehad son of Hepher had no sons but only daughters. The names of his daughters were Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.34', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Manasseh, and their registration numbered 52,700.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.35', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Ephraim by their clans: The Shuthelahite clan from Shuthelah, the Becherite clan from Becher, and the Tahanite clan from Tahan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.36', 'BSB', 'And the descendants of Shuthelah were the Eranite clan from Eran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.37', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Ephraim, and their registration numbered 32,500. These clans were the descendants of Joseph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.38', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Benjamin by their clans: The Belaite clan from Bela, the Ashbelite clan from Ashbel, the Ahiramite clan from Ahiram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.39', 'BSB', 'the Shuphamite clan from Shupham, and the Huphamite clan from Hupham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.40', 'BSB', 'And the descendants of Bela from Ard and Naaman were the Ardite clan from Ard and the Naamite clan from Naaman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.41', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Benjamin, and their registration numbered 45,600.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.42', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Dan by their clans: The Shuhamite clan from Shuham. These were the clans of Dan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.43', 'BSB', 'All of them were Shuhamite clans, and their registration numbered 64,400.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.44', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Asher by their clans: The Imnite clan from Imnah, the Ishvite clan from Ishvi, and the Beriite clan from Beriah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.45', 'BSB', 'And these were the descendants of Beriah: the Heberite clan from Heber and the Malchielite clan from Malchiel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.46', 'BSB', 'And the name of Asher’s daughter was Serah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.47', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Asher, and their registration numbered 53,400.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.48', 'BSB', 'These were the descendants of Naphtali by their clans: The Jahzeelite clan from Jahzeel, the Gunite clan from Guni,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.49', 'BSB', 'the Jezerite clan from Jezer, and the Shillemite clan from Shillem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.50', 'BSB', 'These were the clans of Naphtali, and their registration numbered 45,400.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.51', 'BSB', 'These men of Israel numbered 601,730 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.52', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.53', 'BSB', '“The land is to be divided among the tribes as an inheritance, according to the number of names.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.54', 'BSB', 'Increase the inheritance for a large tribe and decrease it for a small one; each tribe is to receive its inheritance according to the number of those registered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.55', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the land must be divided by lot; they shall receive their inheritance according to the names of the tribes of their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.56', 'BSB', 'Each inheritance is to be divided by lot among the larger and smaller tribes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.57', 'BSB', 'Now these were the Levites numbered by their clans: The Gershonite clan from Gershon, the Kohathite clan from Kohath, and the Merarite clan from Merari.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.58', 'BSB', 'These were the families of the Levites: The Libnite clan, the Hebronite clan, the Mahlite clan, the Mushite clan, and the Korahite clan. Now Kohath was the father of Amram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.59', 'BSB', 'and Amram’s wife was named Jochebed. She was also a daughter of Levi, born to Levi in Egypt. To Amram she bore Aaron, Moses, and their sister Miriam.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.60', 'BSB', 'Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar were born to Aaron,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.61', 'BSB', 'but Nadab and Abihu died when they offered unauthorized fire before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.62', 'BSB', 'The registration of the Levites totaled 23,000, every male a month old or more; they were not numbered among the other Israelites, because no inheritance was given to them among the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.63', 'BSB', 'These were the ones numbered by Moses and Eleazar the priest when they counted the Israelites on the plains of Moab by the Jordan, across from Jericho.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.64', 'BSB', 'Among all these, however, there was not one who had been numbered by Moses and Aaron the priest when they counted the Israelites in the Wilderness of Sinai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.26.65', 'BSB', 'For the LORD had told them that they would surely die in the wilderness. Not one was left except Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.1', 'BSB', 'Now the daughters of Zelophehad son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, belonged to the clans of Manasseh son of Joseph. These were the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah. They approached', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.2', 'BSB', 'the entrance to the Tent of Meeting, stood before Moses, Eleazar the priest, the leaders, and the whole congregation, and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.3', 'BSB', '“Our father died in the wilderness, but he was not among the followers of Korah who gathered together against the LORD. Instead, he died because of his own sin, and he had no sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.4', 'BSB', 'Why should the name of our father disappear from his clan because he had no sons? Give us property among our father’s brothers.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.5', 'BSB', 'So Moses brought their case before the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.6', 'BSB', 'and the LORD answered him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.7', 'BSB', '“The daughters of Zelophehad speak correctly. You certainly must give them property as an inheritance among their father’s brothers, and transfer their father’s inheritance to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.8', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, you shall say to the Israelites, ‘If a man dies and leaves no son, you are to transfer his inheritance to his daughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.9', 'BSB', 'If he has no daughter, give his inheritance to his brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.10', 'BSB', 'If he has no brothers, give his inheritance to his father’s brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.11', 'BSB', 'And if his father has no brothers, give his inheritance to the next of kin from his clan, that he may take possession of it. This is to be a statutory ordinance for the Israelites, as the LORD has commanded Moses.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.12', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses, “Go up this mountain of the Abarim range and see the land that I have given the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.13', 'BSB', 'After you have seen it, you too will be gathered to your people, as your brother Aaron was;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.14', 'BSB', 'for when the congregation contended in the Wilderness of Zin, both of you rebelled against My command to show My holiness in their sight regarding the waters.” Those were the waters of Meribah in Kadesh, in the Wilderness of Zin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.15', 'BSB', 'So Moses appealed to the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.16', 'BSB', '“May the LORD, the God of the spirits of all flesh, appoint a man over the congregation', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.17', 'BSB', 'who will go out and come in before them, and who will lead them out and bring them in, so that the congregation of the LORD will not be like sheep without a shepherd.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.18', 'BSB', 'And the LORD replied to Moses, “Take Joshua son of Nun, a man with the Spirit in him, and lay your hands on him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.19', 'BSB', 'Have him stand before Eleazar the priest and the whole congregation, and commission him in their sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.20', 'BSB', 'Confer on him some of your authority, so that the whole congregation of Israel will obey him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.21', 'BSB', 'He shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who will seek counsel for him before the LORD by the judgment of the Urim. At his command, he and all the Israelites with him—the entire congregation—will go out and come in.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.22', 'BSB', 'Moses did as the LORD had commanded him. He took Joshua, had him stand before Eleazar the priest and the whole congregation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.27.23', 'BSB', 'and laid his hands on him and commissioned him, as the LORD had instructed through Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.2', 'BSB', '“Command the Israelites and say to them: See that you present to Me at its appointed time the food for My offerings by fire, as a pleasing aroma to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.3', 'BSB', 'And tell them that this is the offering made by fire you are to present to the LORD as a regular burnt offering each day: two unblemished year-old male lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.4', 'BSB', 'Offer one lamb in the morning and the other at twilight,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.5', 'BSB', 'along with a tenth of an ephah of fine flour as a grain offering, mixed with a quarter hin of oil from pressed olives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.6', 'BSB', 'This is a regular burnt offering established at Mount Sinai as a pleasing aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.7', 'BSB', 'The drink offering accompanying each lamb shall be a quarter hin. Pour out the offering of fermented drink to the LORD in the sanctuary area.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.8', 'BSB', 'And offer the second lamb at twilight, with the same grain offering and drink offering as in the morning. It is an offering made by fire, a pleasing aroma to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.9', 'BSB', 'On the Sabbath day, present two unblemished year-old male lambs, accompanied by a grain offering of two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil, as well as a drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.10', 'BSB', 'This is the burnt offering for every Sabbath, in addition to the regular burnt offering and its drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.11', 'BSB', 'At the beginning of every month, you are to present to the LORD a burnt offering of two young bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.12', 'BSB', 'along with three-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil as a grain offering with each bull, two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil as a grain offering with the ram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.13', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil as a grain offering with each lamb. This is a burnt offering, a pleasing aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.14', 'BSB', 'Their drink offerings shall be half a hin of wine with each bull, a third of a hin with the ram, and a quarter hin with each lamb. This is the monthly burnt offering to be made at each new moon throughout the year.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.15', 'BSB', 'In addition to the regular burnt offering with its drink offering, one male goat is to be presented to the LORD as a sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.16', 'BSB', 'The fourteenth day of the first month is the LORD’s Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.17', 'BSB', 'On the fifteenth day of this month, there shall be a feast; for seven days unleavened bread is to be eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.18', 'BSB', 'On the first day there is to be a sacred assembly; you must not do any regular work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.19', 'BSB', 'Present to the LORD an offering made by fire, a burnt offering of two young bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old, all unblemished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.20', 'BSB', 'The grain offering shall consist of fine flour mixed with oil; offer three-tenths of an ephah with each bull, two-tenths of an ephah with the ram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.21', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah with each of the seven lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.22', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering to make atonement for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.23', 'BSB', 'You are to present these in addition to the regular morning burnt offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.24', 'BSB', 'Offer the same food each day for seven days as an offering made by fire, a pleasing aroma to the LORD. It is to be offered with its drink offering and the regular burnt offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.25', 'BSB', 'On the seventh day you shall hold a sacred assembly; you must not do any regular work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.26', 'BSB', 'On the day of firstfruits, when you present an offering of new grain to the LORD during the Feast of Weeks, you are to hold a sacred assembly; you must not do any regular work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.27', 'BSB', 'Present a burnt offering of two young bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old as a pleasing aroma to the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.28', 'BSB', 'together with their grain offerings of fine flour mixed with oil—three-tenths of an ephah with each bull, two-tenths of an ephah with the ram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.29', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah with each of the seven lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.30', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat to make atonement for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.28.31', 'BSB', 'Offer them with their drink offerings in addition to the regular burnt offering and its grain offering. The animals must be unblemished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.1', 'BSB', '“On the first day of the seventh month, you are to hold a sacred assembly, and you must not do any regular work. This will be a day for you to sound the trumpets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.2', 'BSB', 'As a pleasing aroma to the LORD, you are to present a burnt offering of one young bull, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.3', 'BSB', 'together with their grain offerings of fine flour mixed with oil—three-tenths of an ephah with the bull, two-tenths of an ephah with the ram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.4', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah with each of the seven male lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.5', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering to make atonement for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.6', 'BSB', 'These are in addition to the monthly and daily burnt offerings with their prescribed grain offerings and drink offerings. They are a pleasing aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.7', 'BSB', 'On the tenth day of this seventh month, you are to hold a sacred assembly, and you shall humble yourselves; you must not do any work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.8', 'BSB', 'Present as a pleasing aroma to the LORD a burnt offering of one young bull, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.9', 'BSB', 'together with their grain offerings of fine flour mixed with oil—three-tenths of an ephah with the bull, two-tenths of an ephah with the ram,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.10', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah with each of the seven lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.11', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the sin offering of atonement and the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.12', 'BSB', 'On the fifteenth day of the seventh month, you are to hold a sacred assembly; you must not do any regular work, and you shall observe a feast to the LORD for seven days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.13', 'BSB', 'As a pleasing aroma to the LORD, you are to present an offering made by fire, a burnt offering of thirteen young bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.14', 'BSB', 'along with the grain offering of three-tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil with each of the thirteen bulls, two-tenths of an ephah with each of the two rams,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.15', 'BSB', 'and a tenth of an ephah with each of the fourteen lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.16', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.17', 'BSB', 'On the second day you are to present twelve young bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.18', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.19', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.20', 'BSB', 'On the third day you are to present eleven bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.21', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.22', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.23', 'BSB', 'On the fourth day you are to present ten bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.24', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.25', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.26', 'BSB', 'On the fifth day you are to present nine bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.27', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.28', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.29', 'BSB', 'On the sixth day you are to present eight bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.30', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.31', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.32', 'BSB', 'On the seventh day you are to present seven bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.33', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.34', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.35', 'BSB', 'On the eighth day you are to hold a solemn assembly; you must not do any regular work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.36', 'BSB', 'As a pleasing aroma to the LORD, you are to present an offering made by fire, a burnt offering of one bull, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old, all unblemished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.37', 'BSB', 'along with the grain and drink offerings for the bulls, rams, and lambs, according to the number prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.38', 'BSB', 'Include one male goat as a sin offering, in addition to the regular burnt offering with its grain offering and drink offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.39', 'BSB', 'You are to present these offerings to the LORD at your appointed times, in addition to your vow and freewill offerings, whether burnt offerings, grain offerings, drink offerings, or peace offerings.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.29.40', 'BSB', 'So Moses spoke all this to the Israelites just as the LORD had commanded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.1', 'BSB', 'Then Moses said to the heads of the tribes of Israel, “This is what the LORD has commanded:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.2', 'BSB', 'If a man makes a vow to the LORD or swears an oath to obligate himself by a pledge, he must not break his word; he must do everything he has promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.3', 'BSB', 'And if a woman in her father’s house during her youth makes a vow to the LORD or obligates herself by a pledge,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.4', 'BSB', 'and her father hears about her vow or pledge but says nothing to her, then all the vows or pledges by which she has bound herself shall stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.5', 'BSB', 'But if her father prohibits her on the day he hears about it, then none of the vows or pledges by which she has bound herself shall stand. The LORD will absolve her because her father has prohibited her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.6', 'BSB', 'If a woman marries while under a vow or rash promise by which she has bound herself,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.7', 'BSB', 'and her husband hears of it but says nothing to her on that day, then the vows or pledges by which she has bound herself shall stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.8', 'BSB', 'But if her husband prohibits her when he hears of it, he nullifies the vow that binds her or the rash promise she has made, and the LORD will absolve her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.9', 'BSB', 'Every vow a widow or divorced woman pledges to fulfill is binding on her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.10', 'BSB', 'If a woman in her husband’s house has made a vow or put herself under an obligation with an oath,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.11', 'BSB', 'and her husband hears of it but says nothing to her and does not prohibit her, then all the vows or pledges by which she has bound herself shall stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.12', 'BSB', 'But if her husband nullifies them on the day he hears of them, then nothing that came from her lips, whether her vows or pledges, shall stand. Her husband has nullified them, and the LORD will absolve her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.13', 'BSB', 'Her husband may confirm or nullify any vow or any sworn pledge to deny herself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.14', 'BSB', 'But if her husband says nothing to her from day to day, then he confirms all the vows and pledges that bind her. He has confirmed them, because he said nothing to her on the day he heard about them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.15', 'BSB', 'But if he nullifies them after he hears of them, then he will bear her iniquity.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.30.16', 'BSB', 'These are the statutes that the LORD commanded Moses concerning the relationship between a man and his wife, and between a father and a young daughter still in his home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.1', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.2', 'BSB', '“Take vengeance on the Midianites for the Israelites. After that, you will be gathered to your people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.3', 'BSB', 'So Moses told the people, “Arm some of your men for war, that they may go against the Midianites and execute the LORD’s vengeance on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.4', 'BSB', 'Send into battle a thousand men from each tribe of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.5', 'BSB', 'So a thousand men were recruited from each tribe of Israel—twelve thousand armed for war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.6', 'BSB', 'And Moses sent the thousand from each tribe into battle, along with Phinehas son of Eleazar the priest, who took with him the vessels of the sanctuary and the trumpets for signaling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.7', 'BSB', 'Then they waged war against Midian, as the LORD had commanded Moses, and they killed every male.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.8', 'BSB', 'Among the slain were Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba—the five kings of Midian. They also killed Balaam son of Beor with the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.9', 'BSB', 'The Israelites captured the Midianite women and their children, and they plundered all their herds, flocks, and goods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.10', 'BSB', 'Then they burned all the cities where the Midianites had lived, as well as all their encampments,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.11', 'BSB', 'and carried away all the plunder and spoils, both people and animals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.12', 'BSB', 'They brought the captives, spoils, and plunder to Moses, to Eleazar the priest, and to the congregation of Israel at the camp on the plains of Moab, by the Jordan across from Jericho.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.13', 'BSB', 'And Moses, Eleazar the priest, and all the leaders of the congregation went to meet them outside the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.14', 'BSB', 'But Moses was angry with the officers of the army—the commanders of thousands and commanders of hundreds—who were returning from the battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.15', 'BSB', '“Have you spared all the women?” he asked them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.16', 'BSB', '“Look, these women caused the sons of Israel, through the counsel of Balaam, to turn unfaithfully against the LORD at Peor, so that the plague struck the congregation of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.17', 'BSB', 'So now, kill all the boys, as well as every woman who has had relations with a man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.18', 'BSB', 'but spare for yourselves every girl who has never had relations with a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.19', 'BSB', 'All of you who have killed a person or touched the dead are to remain outside the camp for seven days. On the third day and the seventh day you are to purify both yourselves and your captives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.20', 'BSB', 'And purify every garment and leather good, everything made of goat’s hair, and every article of wood.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.21', 'BSB', 'Then Eleazar the priest said to the soldiers who had gone into battle, “This is the statute of the law which the LORD has commanded Moses:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.22', 'BSB', 'Only the gold, silver, bronze, iron, tin, and lead—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.23', 'BSB', 'everything that can withstand the fire—must be put through the fire, and it will be clean. But it must still be purified with the water of purification. And everything that cannot withstand the fire must pass through the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.24', 'BSB', 'On the seventh day you are to wash your clothes, and you will be clean. After that you may enter the camp.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.25', 'BSB', 'The LORD said to Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.26', 'BSB', '“You and Eleazar the priest and the family heads of the congregation are to take a count of what was captured, both of man and beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.27', 'BSB', 'Then divide the captives between the troops who went out to battle and the rest of the congregation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.28', 'BSB', 'Set aside a tribute for the LORD from what belongs to the soldiers who went into battle: one out of every five hundred, whether persons, cattle, donkeys, or sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.29', 'BSB', 'Take it from their half and give it to Eleazar the priest as an offering to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.30', 'BSB', 'From the Israelites’ half, take one out of every fifty, whether persons, cattle, donkeys, sheep, or other animals, and give them to the Levites who keep charge of the tabernacle of the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.31', 'BSB', 'So Moses and Eleazar the priest did as the LORD had commanded Moses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.32', 'BSB', 'and this plunder remained from the spoils the soldiers had taken: 675,000 sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.33', 'BSB', '72,000 cattle,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.34', 'BSB', '61,000 donkeys,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.35', 'BSB', 'and 32,000 women who had not slept with a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.36', 'BSB', 'This was the half portion for those who had gone to war: 337,500 sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.37', 'BSB', 'including a tribute to the LORD of 675,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.38', 'BSB', '36,000 cattle, including a tribute to the LORD of 72,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.39', 'BSB', '30,500 donkeys, including a tribute to the LORD of 61,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.40', 'BSB', 'and 16,000 people, including a tribute to the LORD of 32.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.41', 'BSB', 'Moses gave the tribute to Eleazar the priest as an offering for the LORD, as the LORD had commanded Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.42', 'BSB', 'From the Israelites’ half, which Moses had set apart from the men who had gone to war,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.43', 'BSB', 'this half belonged to the congregation: 337,500 sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.44', 'BSB', '36,000 cattle,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.45', 'BSB', '30,500 donkeys,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.46', 'BSB', 'and 16,000 people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.47', 'BSB', 'From the Israelites’ half, Moses took one out of every fifty persons and animals and gave them to the Levites who kept charge of the tabernacle of the LORD, as the LORD had commanded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.48', 'BSB', 'Then the officers who were over the units of the army—the commanders of thousands and of hundreds—approached Moses', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.49', 'BSB', 'and said, “Your servants have counted the soldiers under our command, and not one of us is missing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.50', 'BSB', 'So we have brought to the LORD an offering of the gold articles each man acquired—armlets, bracelets, rings, earrings, and necklaces—to make atonement for ourselves before the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.51', 'BSB', 'So Moses and Eleazar the priest received from them all the articles made out of gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.52', 'BSB', 'All the gold that the commanders of thousands and of hundreds presented as an offering to the LORD weighed 16,750 shekels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.53', 'BSB', 'Each of the soldiers had taken plunder for himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.31.54', 'BSB', 'And Moses and Eleazar the priest received the gold from the commanders of thousands and of hundreds and brought it into the Tent of Meeting as a memorial for the Israelites before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.1', 'BSB', 'Now the Reubenites and Gadites, who had very large herds and flocks, surveyed the lands of Jazer and Gilead, and they saw that the region was suitable for livestock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.2', 'BSB', 'So the Gadites and Reubenites came to Moses, Eleazar the priest, and the leaders of the congregation, and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.3', 'BSB', '“Ataroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.4', 'BSB', 'which the LORD conquered before the congregation of Israel, are suitable for livestock—and your servants have livestock.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.5', 'BSB', '“If we have found favor in your sight,” they said, “let this land be given to your servants as a possession. Do not make us cross the Jordan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.6', 'BSB', 'But Moses asked the Gadites and Reubenites, “Shall your brothers go to war while you sit here?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.7', 'BSB', 'Why are you discouraging the Israelites from crossing into the land that the LORD has given them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.8', 'BSB', 'This is what your fathers did when I sent them from Kadesh-barnea to inspect the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.9', 'BSB', 'For when your fathers went up to the Valley of Eshcol and saw the land, they discouraged the Israelites from entering the land that the LORD had given them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.10', 'BSB', 'So the anger of the LORD was kindled that day, and He swore an oath, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.11', 'BSB', '‘Because they did not follow Me wholeheartedly, not one of the men twenty years of age or older who came out of Egypt will see the land that I swore to give Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.12', 'BSB', 'not one except Caleb son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite and Joshua son of Nun—because they did follow the LORD wholeheartedly.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.13', 'BSB', 'The anger of the LORD burned against Israel, and He made them wander in the wilderness forty years, until the whole generation who had done evil in His sight was gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.14', 'BSB', 'Now behold, you, a brood of sinners, have risen up in place of your fathers to further stoke the burning anger of the LORD against Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.15', 'BSB', 'For if you turn away from following Him, He will once again leave this people in the wilderness, and you will be the cause of their destruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.16', 'BSB', 'Then the Gadites and Reubenites approached Moses and said, “We want to build sheepfolds here for our livestock and cities for our little ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.17', 'BSB', 'But we will arm ourselves and be ready to go ahead of the Israelites until we have brought them into their place. Meanwhile, our little ones will remain in the fortified cities for protection from the inhabitants of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.18', 'BSB', 'We will not return to our homes until every Israelite has taken possession of his inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.19', 'BSB', 'Yet we will not have an inheritance with them across the Jordan and beyond, because our inheritance has come to us on the east side of the Jordan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.20', 'BSB', 'Moses replied, “If you will do this—if you will arm yourselves before the LORD for battle,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.21', 'BSB', 'and if every one of your armed men crosses the Jordan before the LORD, until He has driven His enemies out before Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.22', 'BSB', 'then when the land is subdued before the LORD, you may return and be free of obligation to the LORD and to Israel. And this land will belong to you as a possession before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.23', 'BSB', 'But if you do not do this, you will certainly sin against the LORD—and be assured that your sin will find you out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.24', 'BSB', 'Build cities for your little ones and folds for your flocks, but do what you have promised.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.25', 'BSB', 'The Gadites and Reubenites said to Moses, “Your servants will do just as our lord commands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.26', 'BSB', 'Our children, our wives, our livestock, and all our animals will remain here in the cities of Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.27', 'BSB', 'But your servants are equipped for war, and every man will cross over to the battle before the LORD, just as our lord says.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.28', 'BSB', 'So Moses gave orders about them to Eleazar the priest, to Joshua son of Nun, and to the family leaders of the tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.29', 'BSB', 'And Moses said to them, “If the Gadites and Reubenites cross the Jordan with you, with every man armed for battle before the LORD, and the land is subdued before you, then you are to give them the land of Gilead as a possession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.30', 'BSB', 'But if they do not arm themselves and go across with you, then they must accept their possession among you in the land of Canaan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.31', 'BSB', 'The Gadites and Reubenites replied, “As the LORD has spoken to your servants, so we will do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.32', 'BSB', 'We will cross over into the land of Canaan armed before the LORD, that we may have our inheritance on this side of the Jordan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.33', 'BSB', 'So Moses gave to the Gadites, to the Reubenites, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh son of Joseph the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites and the kingdom of Og king of Bashan—the land including its cities and the territory surrounding them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.34', 'BSB', 'And the Gadites built up Dibon, Ataroth, Aroer,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.35', 'BSB', 'Atroth-shophan, Jazer, Jogbehah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.36', 'BSB', 'Beth-nimrah, and Beth-haran as fortified cities, and they built folds for their flocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.37', 'BSB', 'The Reubenites built up Heshbon, Elealeh, Kiriathaim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.38', 'BSB', 'as well as Nebo and Baal-meon (whose names were changed), and Sibmah. And they renamed the cities they rebuilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.39', 'BSB', 'The descendants of Machir son of Manasseh went to Gilead, captured it, and drove out the Amorites who were there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.40', 'BSB', 'So Moses gave Gilead to the clan of Machir son of Manasseh, and they settled there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.41', 'BSB', 'Jair, a descendant of Manasseh, went and captured their villages and called them Havvoth-jair.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.32.42', 'BSB', 'And Nobah went and captured Kenath and its villages and called it Nobah, after his own name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.1', 'BSB', 'These are the journeys of the Israelites when they came out of the land of Egypt by their divisions under the leadership of Moses and Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.2', 'BSB', 'At the LORD’s command, Moses recorded the stages of their journey. These are the stages listed by their starting points:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.3', 'BSB', 'On the fifteenth day of the first month, on the day after the Passover, the Israelites set out from Rameses. They marched out defiantly in full view of all the Egyptians,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.4', 'BSB', 'who were burying all their firstborn, whom the LORD had struck down among them; for the LORD had executed judgment against their gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.5', 'BSB', 'The Israelites set out from Rameses and camped at Succoth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.6', 'BSB', 'They set out from Succoth and camped at Etham, on the edge of the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.7', 'BSB', 'They set out from Etham and turned back to Pi-hahiroth, opposite Baal-zephon, and they camped near Migdol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.8', 'BSB', 'They set out from Pi-hahiroth and crossed through the sea, into the wilderness, and they journeyed three days into the Wilderness of Etham and camped at Marah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.9', 'BSB', 'They set out from Marah and came to Elim, where there were twelve springs and seventy palm trees, and they camped there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.10', 'BSB', 'They set out from Elim and camped by the Red Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.11', 'BSB', 'They set out from the Red Sea and camped in the Desert of Sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.12', 'BSB', 'They set out from the Desert of Sin and camped at Dophkah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.13', 'BSB', 'They set out from Dophkah and camped at Alush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.14', 'BSB', 'They set out from Alush and camped at Rephidim, where there was no water for the people to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.15', 'BSB', 'They set out from Rephidim and camped in the Wilderness of Sinai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.16', 'BSB', 'They set out from the Wilderness of Sinai and camped at Kibroth-hattaavah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Num.33.17', 'BSB', 'They set out from Kibroth-hattaavah and camped at Hazeroth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
