('Ezra.2.36', 'BSB', 'The priests: The descendants of Jedaiah (through the house of Jeshua), 973;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.37', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Immer, 1,052;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.38', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Pashhur, 1,247;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.39', 'BSB', 'and the descendants of Harim, 1,017.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.40', 'BSB', 'The Levites: the descendants of Jeshua and Kadmiel (through the line of Hodaviah ), 74.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.41', 'BSB', 'The singers: the descendants of Asaph, 128.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.42', 'BSB', 'The gatekeepers: the descendants of Shallum, the descendants of Ater, the descendants of Talmon, the descendants of Akkub, the descendants of Hatita, and the descendants of Shobai, 139 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.43', 'BSB', 'The temple servants: the descendants of Ziha, the descendants of Hasupha, the descendants of Tabbaoth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.44', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Keros, the descendants of Siaha, the descendants of Padon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.45', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Lebanah, the descendants of Hagabah, the descendants of Akkub,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.46', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Hagab, the descendants of Shalmai, the descendants of Hanan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.47', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Giddel, the descendants of Gahar, the descendants of Reaiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.48', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Rezin, the descendants of Nekoda, the descendants of Gazzam,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.49', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Uzza, the descendants of Paseah, the descendants of Besai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.50', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Asnah, the descendants of Meunim, the descendants of Nephusim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.51', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Bakbuk, the descendants of Hakupha, the descendants of Harhur,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.52', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Bazluth, the descendants of Mehida, the descendants of Harsha,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.53', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Barkos, the descendants of Sisera, the descendants of Temah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.54', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Neziah, and the descendants of Hatipha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.55', 'BSB', 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Sophereth, the descendants of Peruda,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.56', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.57', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Ami.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.58', 'BSB', 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.59', 'BSB', 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer, but could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.60', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 652 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.61', 'BSB', 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.62', 'BSB', 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.63', 'BSB', 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.64', 'BSB', 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.65', 'BSB', 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 200 male and female singers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.66', 'BSB', 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.67', 'BSB', '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.68', 'BSB', 'When they arrived at the house of the LORD in Jerusalem, some of the heads of the families gave freewill offerings to rebuild the house of God on its original site.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.69', 'BSB', 'According to their ability, they gave to the treasury for this work 61,000 darics of gold, 5,000 minas of silver, and 100 priestly garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.2.70', 'BSB', 'So the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, along with some of the people, settled in their own towns; and the rest of the Israelites settled in their towns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.1', 'BSB', 'By the seventh month, the Israelites had settled in their towns, and the people assembled as one man in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.2', 'BSB', 'Then Jeshua son of Jozadak and his fellow priests, along with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and his associates, began to build the altar of the God of Israel to sacrifice burnt offerings on it, as it is written in the Law of Moses the man of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.3', 'BSB', 'They set up the altar on its foundation and sacrificed burnt offerings on it to the LORD—both the morning and evening burnt offerings—even though they feared the people of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.4', 'BSB', 'They also celebrated the Feast of Tabernacles in accordance with what is written, and they offered burnt offerings daily based on the number prescribed for each day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.5', 'BSB', 'After that, they presented the regular burnt offerings and those for New Moons and for all the appointed sacred feasts of the LORD, as well as all the freewill offerings brought to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.6', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the seventh month, the Israelites began to offer burnt offerings to the LORD, although the foundation of the temple of the LORD had not been laid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.7', 'BSB', 'They gave money to the masons and carpenters, and food and drink and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar logs from Lebanon to Joppa by sea, as authorized by Cyrus king of Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.8', 'BSB', 'In the second month of the second year after they had arrived at the house of God in Jerusalem, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, Jeshua son of Jozadak, and the rest of their associates including the priests, the Levites, and all who had returned to Jerusalem from the captivity, began the work. They appointed Levites twenty years of age or older to supervise the construction of the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.9', 'BSB', 'So Jeshua and his sons and brothers, Kadmiel and his sons (descendants of Yehudah), and the sons of Henadad and their sons and brothers—all Levites—joined together to supervise those working on the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.10', 'BSB', 'When the builders had laid the foundation of the temple of the LORD, the priests in their apparel with trumpets, and the Levites (the sons of Asaph) with cymbals, took their positions to praise the LORD, as David king of Israel had prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.11', 'BSB', 'And they sang responsively with praise and thanksgiving to the LORD: “For He is good; for His loving devotion to Israel endures forever.” Then all the people gave a great shout of praise to the LORD, because the foundation of the house of the LORD had been laid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.12', 'BSB', 'But many of the older priests, Levites, and family heads who had seen the first temple wept loudly when they saw the foundation of this temple. Still, many others shouted joyfully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.3.13', 'BSB', 'The people could not distinguish the shouts of joy from the sound of weeping, because the people were making so much noise. And the sound was heard from afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.1', 'BSB', 'When the enemies of Judah and Benjamin heard that the exiles were building a temple for the LORD, the God of Israel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.2', 'BSB', 'they approached Zerubbabel and the heads of the families, saying, “Let us build with you because, like you, we seek your God and have been sacrificing to Him since the time of King Esar-haddon of Assyria, who brought us here.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.3', 'BSB', 'But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the other heads of the families of Israel replied, “You have no part with us in building a house for our God, since we alone must build it for the LORD, the God of Israel, as Cyrus king of Persia has commanded us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.4', 'BSB', 'Then the people of the land set out to discourage the people of Judah and make them afraid to build.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.5', 'BSB', 'They hired counselors against them to frustrate their plans throughout the reign of Cyrus king of Persia and down to the reign of Darius king of Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.6', 'BSB', 'At the beginning of the reign of Xerxes, an accusation was lodged against the people of Judah and Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.7', 'BSB', 'And in the days of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his associates wrote a letter to Artaxerxes. It was written in Aramaic and then translated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.8', 'BSB', 'Rehum the commander and Shimshai the scribe wrote the letter against Jerusalem to King Artaxerxes as follows:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.9', 'BSB', 'From Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their associates—the judges and officials over Tripolis, Persia, Erech and Babylon, the Elamites of Susa,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.10', 'BSB', 'and the rest of the peoples whom the great and honorable Ashurbanipal deported and settled in the cities of Samaria and elsewhere west of the Euphrates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.11', 'BSB', '(This is the text of the letter they sent to him.) To King Artaxerxes, From your servants, the men west of the Euphrates:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.12', 'BSB', 'Let it be known to the king that the Jews who came from you to us have returned to Jerusalem. And they are rebuilding that rebellious and wicked city, restoring its walls, and repairing its foundations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.13', 'BSB', 'Let it now be known to the king that if that city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, they will not pay tribute, duty, or toll, and the royal treasury will suffer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.14', 'BSB', 'Now because we are in the service of the palace and it is not fitting for us to allow the king to be dishonored, we have sent to inform the king', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.15', 'BSB', 'that a search should be made of the record books of your fathers. In these books you will discover and verify that the city is a rebellious city, harmful to kings and provinces, inciting sedition from ancient times. That is why this city was destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.16', 'BSB', 'We advise the king that if this city is rebuilt and its walls are restored, you will have no dominion west of the Euphrates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.17', 'BSB', 'Then the king sent this reply: To Rehum the commander, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of your associates living in Samaria and elsewhere in the region west of the Euphrates: Greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.18', 'BSB', 'The letter you sent us has been translated and read in my presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.19', 'BSB', 'I issued a decree, and a search was conducted. It was discovered that this city has revolted against kings from ancient times, engaging in rebellion and sedition.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.20', 'BSB', 'And mighty kings have ruled over Jerusalem and exercised authority over the whole region west of the Euphrates; and tribute, duty, and toll were paid to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.21', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, issue an order for these men to stop, so that this city will not be rebuilt until I so order.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.22', 'BSB', 'See that you do not neglect this matter. Why allow this threat to increase and the royal interests to suffer?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.23', 'BSB', 'When the text of the letter from King Artaxerxes was read to Rehum, Shimshai the scribe, and their associates, they went immediately to the Jews in Jerusalem and forcibly stopped them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.4.24', 'BSB', 'Thus the construction of the house of God in Jerusalem ceased, and it remained at a standstill until the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.1', 'BSB', 'Later, the prophets Haggai and Zechariah son of Iddo prophesied to the Jews in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, who was over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.2', 'BSB', 'Then Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and Jeshua son of Jozadak rose up and began to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. And the prophets of God were with them, helping them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.3', 'BSB', 'At that time Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates went to the Jews and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.4', 'BSB', 'They also asked, “What are the names of the men who are constructing this building?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.5', 'BSB', 'But the eye of their God was on the elders of the Jews, so that they were not stopped until a report was sent to Darius and written instructions about this matter were returned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.6', 'BSB', 'This is the text of the letter that Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates, the officials in the region, sent to King Darius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.7', 'BSB', 'The report they sent him read as follows: To King Darius: All peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.8', 'BSB', 'Let it be known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God. The people are rebuilding it with large stones, and placing timbers in the walls. This work is being carried out diligently and is prospering in their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.9', 'BSB', 'So we questioned the elders and asked, “Who authorized you to rebuild this temple and restore this structure?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.10', 'BSB', 'We also asked for their names, so that we could write down the names of their leaders for your information.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.11', 'BSB', 'And this is the answer they returned: “We are servants of the God of heaven and earth, and we are rebuilding the temple that was built many years ago, which a great king of Israel built and completed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.12', 'BSB', 'But since our fathers angered the God of heaven, He delivered them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the Chaldean who destroyed this temple and carried away the people to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.13', 'BSB', 'In his first year, however, Cyrus king of Babylon issued a decree to rebuild this house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.14', 'BSB', 'He also removed from the temple of Babylon the gold and silver articles belonging to the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar had taken and carried there from the temple in Jerusalem. King Cyrus gave these articles to a man named Sheshbazzar, whom he appointed governor', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.15', 'BSB', 'and instructed, ‘Take these articles, put them in the temple in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be rebuilt on its original site.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.16', 'BSB', 'So this Sheshbazzar came and laid the foundation of the house of God in Jerusalem, and from that time until now it has been under construction, but it has not yet been completed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.5.17', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, if it pleases the king, let a search be made of the royal archives in Babylon to see if King Cyrus did indeed issue a decree to rebuild the house of God in Jerusalem. Then let the king send us his decision in this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.1', 'BSB', 'Thus King Darius ordered a search of the archives stored in the treasury of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.2', 'BSB', 'And a scroll was found in the fortress of Ecbatana, in the province of Media, with the following written on it: Memorandum:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.3', 'BSB', 'In the first year of King Cyrus, he issued a decree concerning the house of God in Jerusalem: Let the house be rebuilt as a place for offering sacrifices, and let its foundations be firmly laid. It is to be sixty cubits high and sixty cubits wide,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.4', 'BSB', 'with three layers of cut stones and one of timbers. The costs are to be paid from the royal treasury.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.5', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, the gold and silver articles of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took from the temple in Jerusalem and carried to Babylon, must also be returned to the temple in Jerusalem and deposited in the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore Darius decreed: To Tattenai governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and your associates and officials in the region: You must stay away from that place!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.7', 'BSB', 'Leave this work on the house of God alone. Let the governor and elders of the Jews rebuild this house of God on its original site.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.8', 'BSB', 'I hereby decree what you must do for these elders of the Jews who are rebuilding this house of God: The cost is to be paid in full to these men from the royal treasury out of the taxes of the provinces west of the Euphrates, so that the work will not be hindered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.9', 'BSB', 'Whatever is needed—young bulls, rams, and lambs for burnt offerings to the God of heaven, as well as wheat, salt, wine, and oil, as requested by the priests in Jerusalem—must be given to them daily without fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.10', 'BSB', 'Then they will be able to offer sacrifices of a sweet aroma to the God of heaven and to pray for the lives of the king and his sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.11', 'BSB', 'I also decree that if any man interferes with this directive, a beam is to be torn from his house and raised up, and he is to be impaled on it. And his own house shall be made a pile of rubble for this offense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.12', 'BSB', 'May God, who has caused His Name to dwell there, overthrow any king or people who lifts a hand to alter this decree or to destroy this house of God in Jerusalem. I, Darius, have issued the decree. Let it be carried out with diligence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.13', 'BSB', 'In response, Tattenai the governor of the region west of the Euphrates, Shethar-bozenai, and their associates diligently carried out what King Darius had decreed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.14', 'BSB', 'So the Jewish elders built and prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah son of Iddo. They finished building according to the command of the God of Israel and the decrees of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes, kings of Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.15', 'BSB', 'And this temple was completed on the third day of the month of Adar, in the sixth year of the reign of King Darius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.16', 'BSB', 'Then the people of Israel—the priests, the Levites, and the rest of the exiles—celebrated the dedication of the house of God with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.17', 'BSB', 'For the dedication of the house of God they offered a hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs, and a sin offering for all Israel of twelve male goats, one for each tribe of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.18', 'BSB', 'They also appointed the priests by their divisions and the Levites by their groups to the service of God in Jerusalem, according to what is written in the Book of Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.19', 'BSB', 'On the fourteenth day of the first month, the exiles kept the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.20', 'BSB', 'All the priests and Levites had purified themselves and were ceremonially clean. And the Levites slaughtered the Passover lamb for all the exiles, for their priestly brothers, and for themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.21', 'BSB', 'The Israelites who had returned from exile ate it, together with all who had separated themselves from the uncleanness of the peoples of the land to seek the LORD, the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.6.22', 'BSB', 'For seven days they kept the Feast of Unleavened Bread with joy, because the LORD had made them joyful and turned the heart of the king of Assyria toward them to strengthen their hands in the work on the house of the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.1', 'BSB', 'Many years later, during the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.2', 'BSB', 'the son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.3', 'BSB', 'the son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.4', 'BSB', 'the son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.5', 'BSB', 'the son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.6', 'BSB', 'this Ezra came up from Babylon. He was a scribe skilled in the Law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given. The king had granted Ezra all his requests, for the hand of the LORD his God was upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.7', 'BSB', 'So in the seventh year of King Artaxerxes, he went up to Jerusalem with some of the Israelites, including priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, and temple servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.8', 'BSB', 'Ezra arrived in Jerusalem in the fifth month of the seventh year of the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.9', 'BSB', 'He had begun the journey from Babylon on the first day of the first month, and he arrived in Jerusalem on the first day of the fifth month, for the gracious hand of his God was upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.10', 'BSB', 'For Ezra had set his heart to study the Law of the LORD, to practice it, and to teach its statutes and ordinances in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.11', 'BSB', 'This is the text of the letter King Artaxerxes had given to Ezra the priest and scribe, an expert in the commandments and statutes of the LORD to Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.12', 'BSB', 'Artaxerxes, king of kings. To Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven: Greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.13', 'BSB', 'I hereby decree that any volunteers among the Israelites in my kingdom, including the priests and Levites, may go up with you to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.14', 'BSB', 'You are sent by the king and his seven counselors to evaluate Judah and Jerusalem according to the Law of your God, which is in your hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.15', 'BSB', 'Moreover, you are to take with you the silver and gold that the king and his counselors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose dwelling is in Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.16', 'BSB', 'together with all the silver and gold you may find in all the province of Babylon, as well as the freewill offerings of the people and priests to the house of their God in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.17', 'BSB', 'With this money, therefore, you are to buy as many bulls, rams, and lambs as needed, together with their grain offerings and drink offerings, and offer them on the altar at the house of your God in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.18', 'BSB', 'You and your brothers may do whatever seems best with the rest of the silver and gold, according to the will of your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.19', 'BSB', 'You must deliver to the God of Jerusalem all the articles given to you for the service of the house of your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.20', 'BSB', 'And if anything else is needed for the house of your God that you may have occasion to supply, you may pay for it from the royal treasury.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.21', 'BSB', 'I, King Artaxerxes, decree to all the treasurers west of the Euphrates: Whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the Law of the God of heaven, may require of you, it must be provided promptly,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.22', 'BSB', 'up to a hundred talents of silver, a hundred cors of wheat, a hundred baths of wine, a hundred baths of olive oil, and salt without limit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.23', 'BSB', 'Whatever is commanded by the God of heaven must be done diligently for His house. For why should wrath fall on the realm of the king and his sons?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.24', 'BSB', 'And be advised that you have no authority to impose tribute, duty, or toll on any of the priests, Levites, singers, doorkeepers, temple servants, or other servants of this house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.25', 'BSB', 'And you, Ezra, according to the wisdom of your God which you possess, are to appoint magistrates and judges to judge all the people west of the Euphrates—all who know the laws of your God. And you are to teach these laws to anyone who does not know them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.26', 'BSB', 'If anyone does not keep the law of your God and the law of the king, let a strict judgment be executed against him, whether death, banishment, confiscation of property, or imprisonment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.27', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put into the heart of the king to so honor the house of the LORD in Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.7.28', 'BSB', 'and who has shown me favor before the king, his counselors, and all his powerful officials. And because the hand of the LORD my God was upon me, I took courage and gathered the leaders of Israel to return with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.1', 'BSB', 'These are the family heads and genealogical records of those who returned with me from Babylon during the reign of King Artaxerxes:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.2', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Phinehas, Gershom; from the descendants of Ithamar, Daniel; from the descendants of David, Hattush', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.3', 'BSB', 'of the descendants of Shecaniah; from the descendants of Parosh, Zechariah, and with him were registered 150 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.4', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Pahath-Moab, Eliehoenai son of Zerahiah, and with him 200 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.5', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Zattu, Shecaniah son of Jahaziel, and with him 300 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.6', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Adin, Ebed son of Jonathan, and with him 50 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.7', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Elam, Jeshaiah son of Athaliah, and with him 70 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.8', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Shephatiah, Zebadiah son of Michael, and with him 80 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.9', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Joab, Obadiah son of Jehiel, and with him 218 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.10', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Bani, Shelomith son of Josiphiah, and with him 160 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.11', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Bebai, Zechariah son of Bebai, and with him 28 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.12', 'BSB', 'from the descendants of Azgad, Johanan son of Hakkatan, and with him 110 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.13', 'BSB', 'from the later descendants of Adonikam, these were their names: Eliphelet, Jeiel, and Shemaiah, and with them 60 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.14', 'BSB', 'and from the descendants of Bigvai, both Uthai and Zaccur, and with them 70 men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.15', 'BSB', 'Now I assembled these exiles at the canal that flows to Ahava, and we camped there three days. And when I searched among the people and priests, I found no Levites there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.16', 'BSB', 'Then I summoned the leaders: Eliezer, Ariel, Shemaiah, Elnathan, Jarib, Elnathan, Nathan, Zechariah, and Meshullam, as well as the teachers Joiarib and Elnathan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.17', 'BSB', 'And I sent them to Iddo, the leader at Casiphia, with a message for him and his kinsmen, the temple servants at Casiphia, that they should bring to us ministers for the house of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.18', 'BSB', 'And since the gracious hand of our God was upon us, they brought us Sherebiah—a man of insight from the descendants of Mahli son of Levi, the son of Israel—along with his sons and brothers, 18 men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.19', 'BSB', 'also Hashabiah, together with Jeshaiah, from the descendants of Merari, and his brothers and their sons, 20 men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.20', 'BSB', 'They also brought 220 of the temple servants, all designated by name. David and the officials had appointed them to assist the Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.21', 'BSB', 'And there by the Ahava Canal I proclaimed a fast, so that we might humble ourselves before our God and ask Him for a safe journey for us and our children, with all our possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.22', 'BSB', 'For I was ashamed to ask the king for an escort of soldiers and horsemen to protect us from our enemies on the road, since we had told him, “The hand of our God is gracious to all who seek Him, but His great anger is against all who forsake Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.23', 'BSB', 'So we fasted and petitioned our God about this, and He granted our request.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.24', 'BSB', 'Then I set apart twelve of the leading priests, together with Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.25', 'BSB', 'and I weighed out to them the contribution of silver and gold and the articles that the king, his counselors, his leaders, and all the Israelites there had offered for the house of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.26', 'BSB', 'I weighed out into their hands 650 talents of silver, articles of silver weighing 100 talents, 100 talents of gold,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.27', 'BSB', '20 gold bowls valued at 1,000 darics, and two articles of fine polished bronze, as precious as gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.28', 'BSB', 'Then I told them, “You are holy to the LORD, and these articles are holy. The silver and gold are a freewill offering to the LORD, the God of your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.29', 'BSB', 'Guard them carefully until you weigh them out in the chambers of the house of the LORD in Jerusalem before the leading priests, Levites, and heads of the Israelite families.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.30', 'BSB', 'So the priests and Levites took charge of the silver and gold and sacred articles that had been weighed out to be taken to the house of our God in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.31', 'BSB', 'On the twelfth day of the first month we set out from the Ahava Canal to go to Jerusalem, and the hand of our God was upon us to protect us from the hands of the enemies and bandits along the way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.32', 'BSB', 'So we arrived at Jerusalem and rested there for three days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.33', 'BSB', 'On the fourth day, in the house of our God, we weighed out the silver and gold and sacred articles into the hand of Meremoth son of Uriah, the priest. Eleazar son of Phinehas was with him, along with the Levites Jozabad son of Jeshua and Noadiah son of Binnui.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.34', 'BSB', 'Everything was verified by number and weight, and the total weight was recorded at that time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.35', 'BSB', 'Then the exiles who had returned from captivity sacrificed burnt offerings to the God of Israel: 12 bulls for all Israel, 96 rams, 77 lambs, and a sin offering of 12 male goats. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.8.36', 'BSB', 'They also delivered the king’s edicts to the royal satraps and governors of the region west of the Euphrates, who proceeded to assist the people and the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.1', 'BSB', 'After these things had been accomplished, the leaders approached me and said, “The people of Israel, including the priests and Levites, have not kept themselves separate from the surrounding peoples whose abominations are like those of the Canaanites, Hittites, Perizzites, Jebusites, Ammonites, Moabites, Egyptians, and Amorites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.2', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the Israelites have taken some of their daughters as wives for themselves and their sons, so that the holy seed has been mixed with the people of the land. And the leaders and officials have taken the lead in this unfaithfulness!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.3', 'BSB', 'When I heard this report, I tore my tunic and cloak, pulled out some hair from my head and beard, and sat down in horror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.4', 'BSB', 'Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel gathered around me because of the unfaithfulness of the exiles, while I sat there in horror until the evening offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.5', 'BSB', 'At the evening offering, I got up from my humiliation with my tunic and cloak torn, and I fell on my knees, spread out my hands to the LORD my God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.6', 'BSB', 'and said: “O my God, I am ashamed and embarrassed to lift up my face to You, my God, because our iniquities are higher than our heads, and our guilt has reached the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.7', 'BSB', 'From the days of our fathers to this day, our guilt has been great. Because of our iniquities, we and our kings and priests have been delivered into the hands of the kings of the earth and put to the sword and captivity, to pillage and humiliation, as we are this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.8', 'BSB', 'But now, for a brief moment, grace has come from the LORD our God to preserve for us a remnant and to give us a stake in His holy place. Even in our bondage, our God has given us new life and light to our eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.9', 'BSB', 'Though we are slaves, our God has not forsaken us in our bondage, but He has extended to us grace in the sight of the kings of Persia, giving us new life to rebuild the house of our God and repair its ruins, and giving us a wall of protection in Judah and Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.10', 'BSB', 'And now, our God, what can we say after this? For we have forsaken the commandments', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.11', 'BSB', 'that You gave through Your servants the prophets, saying: ‘The land that you are entering to possess is a land polluted by the impurity of its peoples and the abominations with which they have filled it from end to end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.12', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, do not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters for your sons. Never seek their peace or prosperity, so that you may be strong and may eat the good things of the land, leaving it as an inheritance to your sons forever.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.13', 'BSB', 'After all that has come upon us because of our evil deeds and our great guilt (though You, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserve and have given us such a remnant as this),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.14', 'BSB', 'shall we again break Your commandments and intermarry with the peoples who commit these abominations? Would You not become so angry with us as to wipe us out, leaving no remnant or survivor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.9.15', 'BSB', 'O LORD, God of Israel, You are righteous! For we remain this day as a remnant. Here we are before You in our guilt, though because of it no one can stand before You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.1', 'BSB', 'While Ezra prayed and made this confession, weeping and falling facedown before the house of God, a very large assembly of Israelites—men, women, and children—gathered around him, and the people wept bitterly as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.2', 'BSB', 'Then Shecaniah son of Jehiel, an Elamite, said to Ezra: “We have been unfaithful to our God by marrying foreign women from the people of the land, yet in spite of this, there is hope for Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.3', 'BSB', 'So now let us make a covenant before our God to send away all the foreign wives and their children, according to the counsel of my lord and of those who tremble at the command of our God. Let it be done according to the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.4', 'BSB', 'Get up, for this matter is your responsibility, and we will support you. Be strong and take action!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.5', 'BSB', 'So Ezra got up and made the leading priests, Levites, and all Israel take an oath to do what had been said. And they took the oath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.6', 'BSB', 'Then Ezra withdrew from before the house of God and walked to the chamber of Jehohanan son of Eliashib. And while he stayed there, he ate no food and drank no water, because he was mourning over the unfaithfulness of the exiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.7', 'BSB', 'And a proclamation was issued throughout Judah and Jerusalem that all the exiles should gather at Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.8', 'BSB', 'Whoever failed to appear within three days would forfeit all his property, according to the counsel of the leaders and elders, and would himself be expelled from the assembly of the exiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.9', 'BSB', 'So within the three days, all the men of Judah and Benjamin assembled in Jerusalem, and on the twentieth day of the ninth month, all the people sat in the square at the house of God, trembling regarding this matter and because of the heavy rain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.10', 'BSB', 'Then Ezra the priest stood up and said to them, “You have been unfaithful by marrying foreign women, adding to the guilt of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.11', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, make a confession to the LORD, the God of your fathers, and do His will. Separate yourselves from the people of the land and from your foreign wives.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.12', 'BSB', 'And the whole assembly responded in a loud voice: “Truly we must do as you say!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.13', 'BSB', 'But there are many people here, and it is the rainy season. We are not able to stay out in the open. Nor is this the work of one or two days, for we have transgressed greatly in this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.14', 'BSB', 'Let our leaders represent the whole assembly. Then let everyone in our towns who has married a foreign woman come at an appointed time, together with the elders and judges of each town, until the fierce anger of our God in this matter is turned away from us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.15', 'BSB', '(Only Jonathan son of Asahel and Jahzeiah son of Tikvah, supported by Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite, opposed this plan.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.16', 'BSB', 'So the exiles did as proposed. Ezra the priest selected men who were family heads, each of them identified by name, to represent their families. On the first day of the tenth month they launched the investigation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.17', 'BSB', 'and by the first day of the first month they had dealt with all the men who had married foreign women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.18', 'BSB', 'Among the descendants of the priests who had married foreign women were found these descendants of Jeshua son of Jozadak and his brothers: Maaseiah, Eliezer, Jarib, and Gedaliah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.19', 'BSB', 'They pledged to send their wives away, and for their guilt they presented a ram from the flock as a guilt offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.20', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Immer: Hanani and Zebadiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.21', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Harim: Maaseiah, Elijah, Shemaiah, Jehiel, and Uzziah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.22', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Pashhur: Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethanel, Jozabad, and Elasah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.23', 'BSB', 'Among the Levites: Jozabad, Shimei, Kelaiah (that is, Kelita), Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.24', 'BSB', 'From the singers: Eliashib. From the gatekeepers: Shallum, Telem, and Uri.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.25', 'BSB', 'And among the other Israelites, from the descendants of Parosh: Ramiah, Izziah, Malchijah, Mijamin, Eleazar, Malchijah, and Benaiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.26', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Elam: Mattaniah, Zechariah, Jehiel, Abdi, Jeremoth, and Elijah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.27', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Zattu: Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, Jeremoth, Zabad, and Aziza.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.28', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Bebai: Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and Athlai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.29', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Bani: Meshullam, Malluch, Adaiah, Jashub, Sheal, and Jeremoth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.30', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Pahath-moab: Adna, Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezalel, Binnui, and Manasseh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.31', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Harim: Eliezer, Isshijah, Malchijah, Shemaiah, Shimeon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.32', 'BSB', 'Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.33', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Hashum: Mattenai, Mattattah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.34', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Bani: Maadai, Amram, Uel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.35', 'BSB', 'Benaiah, Bedeiah, Cheluhi,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.36', 'BSB', 'Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.37', 'BSB', 'Mattaniah, Mattenai, and Jaasu.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.38', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Binnui: Shimei,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.39', 'BSB', 'Shelemiah, Nathan, Adaiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.40', 'BSB', 'Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.41', 'BSB', 'Azarel, Shelemiah, Shemariah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.42', 'BSB', 'Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.43', 'BSB', 'And from the descendants of Nebo: Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Jaddai, Joel, and Benaiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezra.10.44', 'BSB', 'All these men had married foreign women, and some of them had children by these wives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of Nehemiah son of Hacaliah: In the month of Chislev, in the twentieth year, while I was in the citadel of Susa,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.2', 'BSB', 'Hanani, one of my brothers, arrived with men from Judah. So I questioned them about the remnant of the Jews who had survived the exile, and also about Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.3', 'BSB', 'And they told me, “The remnant who survived the exile are there in the province, in great trouble and disgrace. The wall of Jerusalem is broken down, and its gates are burned with fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.4', 'BSB', 'When I heard these words, I sat down and wept. I mourned for days, fasting and praying before the God of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.5', 'BSB', 'Then I said: “O LORD, God of heaven, the great and awesome God who keeps His covenant of loving devotion with those who love Him and keep His commandments,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.6', 'BSB', 'let Your eyes be open and Your ears attentive to hear the prayer that I, Your servant, now pray before You day and night for Your servants, the Israelites. I confess the sins that we Israelites have committed against You. Both I and my father’s house have sinned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.7', 'BSB', 'We have behaved corruptly against You and have not kept the commandments, statutes, and ordinances that You gave Your servant Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.8', 'BSB', 'Remember, I pray, the word that You commanded Your servant Moses when You said, ‘If you are unfaithful, I will scatter you among the nations,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.9', 'BSB', 'but if you return to Me and keep and practice My commandments, then even if your exiles have been banished to the farthest horizon, I will gather them from there and bring them to the place I have chosen as a dwelling for My Name.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.10', 'BSB', 'They are Your servants and Your people. You redeemed them by Your great power and mighty hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.1.11', 'BSB', 'O Lord, may Your ear be attentive to my prayer and to the prayers of Your servants who delight to revere Your name. Give Your servant success this day, I pray, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.” (At that time I was the cupbearer to the king.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.1', 'BSB', 'Now in the month of Nisan, in the twentieth year of King Artaxerxes, when wine was set before him, I took the wine and gave it to the king. I had never been sad in his presence,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.2', 'BSB', 'so the king said to me, “Why is your face sad, though you are not ill? This could only be sadness of the heart.” I was overwhelmed with fear', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.3', 'BSB', 'and replied to the king, “May the king live forever! Why should I not be sad when the city where my fathers are buried lies in ruins, and its gates have been destroyed by fire?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.4', 'BSB', '“What is your request?” replied the king. So I prayed to the God of heaven', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.5', 'BSB', 'and answered the king, “If it pleases the king, and if your servant has found favor in your sight, I ask that you send me to Judah, to the city where my fathers are buried, so that I may rebuild it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.6', 'BSB', 'Then the king, with the queen seated beside him, asked me, “How long will your journey take, and when will you return?” So it pleased the king to send me, and I set a time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.7', 'BSB', 'I also said to him, “If it pleases the king, may letters be given to me for the governors west of the Euphrates, so that they will grant me safe passage until I reach Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.8', 'BSB', 'And may I have a letter to Asaph, keeper of the king’s forest, so that he will give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel to the temple, for the city wall, and for the house I will occupy.” And because the gracious hand of my God was upon me, the king granted my requests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.9', 'BSB', 'Then I went to the governors west of the Euphrates and gave them the king’s letters. The king had also sent army officers and cavalry with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.10', 'BSB', 'But when Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite official heard about this, they were deeply disturbed that someone had come to seek the well-being of the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.11', 'BSB', 'After I had arrived in Jerusalem and had been there three days,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.12', 'BSB', 'I set out at night with a few men. I did not tell anyone what my God had laid on my heart to do for Jerusalem. The only animal with me was the one on which I was riding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.13', 'BSB', 'So I went out at night through the Valley Gate toward the Well of the Serpent and the Dung Gate, and I inspected the walls of Jerusalem that had been broken down and the gates that had been destroyed by fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.14', 'BSB', 'Then I went on to the Fountain Gate and the King’s Pool, but there was no room for the animal under me to get through;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.15', 'BSB', 'so I went up the valley by night and inspected the wall. Then I headed back and reentered through the Valley Gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.16', 'BSB', 'The officials did not know where I had gone or what I was doing, for I had not yet told the Jews or priests or nobles or officials or any other workers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.17', 'BSB', 'Then I said to them, “You see the trouble we are in. Jerusalem lies in ruins, and its gates have been burned down. Come, let us rebuild the wall of Jerusalem, so that we will no longer be a disgrace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.18', 'BSB', 'I also told them about the gracious hand of my God upon me, and what the king had said to me. “Let us start rebuilding,” they replied, and they set their hands to this good work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.19', 'BSB', 'But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite official, and Geshem the Arab heard about this, they mocked us and ridiculed us, saying, “What is this you are doing? Are you rebelling against the king?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.2.20', 'BSB', 'So I answered them and said, “The God of heaven is the One who will grant us success. We, His servants, will start rebuilding, but you have no portion, right, or claim in Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.1', 'BSB', 'At the Sheep Gate, Eliashib the high priest and his fellow priests began rebuilding. They dedicated it and installed its doors. After building as far as the Tower of the Hundred and the Tower of Hananel, they dedicated the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.2', 'BSB', 'The men of Jericho built next to Eliashib, and Zaccur son of Imri built next to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.3', 'BSB', 'The Fish Gate was rebuilt by the sons of Hassenaah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.4', 'BSB', 'Next to them, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, made repairs. Next to him, Meshullam son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel, made repairs; and next to him, Zadok son of Baana made repairs as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.5', 'BSB', 'Next to him, the Tekoites made repairs, but their nobles did not put their shoulders to the work under their supervisors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.6', 'BSB', 'The Jeshanah Gate was repaired by Joiada son of Paseah and Meshullam son of Besodeiah. They laid its beams and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.7', 'BSB', 'Next to them, repairs were made by Melatiah the Gibeonite, Jadon the Meronothite, and the men of Gibeon and Mizpah, who were under the authority of the governor of the region west of the Euphrates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.8', 'BSB', 'Next to them, Uzziel son of Harhaiah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs, and next to him, Hananiah son of the perfumer made repairs. They fortified Jerusalem as far as the Broad Wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.9', 'BSB', 'Next to them, Rephaiah son of Hur, ruler of a half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.10', 'BSB', 'next to him, Jedaiah son of Harumaph made repairs across from his house; and next to him, Hattush son of Hashabneiah made repairs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.11', 'BSB', 'Malchijah son of Harim and Hasshub son of Pahath-moab repaired another section, as well as the Tower of the Ovens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.12', 'BSB', 'And next to them, Shallum son of Hallohesh, ruler of the other half-district of Jerusalem, made repairs, with the help of his daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.13', 'BSB', 'The Valley Gate was repaired by Hanun and the residents of Zanoah. They rebuilt it, installed its doors, bolts, and bars, and repaired a thousand cubits of the wall as far as the Dung Gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.14', 'BSB', 'The Dung Gate was repaired by Malchijah son of Rechab, ruler of the district of Beth-haccherem. He rebuilt it and installed its doors, bolts, and bars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.15', 'BSB', 'The Fountain Gate was repaired by Shallun son of Col-hozeh, ruler of the district of Mizpah. He rebuilt it, roofed it, and installed its doors, bolts, and bars. He also repaired the wall of the Pool of Shelah near the king’s garden, as far as the stairs that descend from the City of David.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.16', 'BSB', 'Beyond him, Nehemiah son of Azbuk, ruler of a half-district of Beth-zur, made repairs up to a point opposite the tombs of David, as far as the artificial pool and the House of the Mighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.17', 'BSB', 'Next to him, the Levites made repairs under Rehum son of Bani, and next to him, Hashabiah, ruler of a half-district of Keilah, made repairs for his district.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.18', 'BSB', 'Next to him, their countrymen made repairs under Binnui son of Henadad, ruler of the other half-district of Keilah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.19', 'BSB', 'And next to him, Ezer son of Jeshua, ruler of Mizpah, repaired another section opposite the Ascent to the Armory, near the angle in the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.20', 'BSB', 'Next to him, Baruch son of Zabbai diligently repaired another section, from the angle to the doorway of the house of Eliashib the high priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.21', 'BSB', 'Next to him, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, repaired another section, from the doorway of the house of Eliashib to the end of the house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.22', 'BSB', 'And next to him, the priests from the surrounding area made repairs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.23', 'BSB', 'Beyond them, Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs in front of their house, and next to them, Azariah son of Maaseiah, the son of Ananiah, made repairs beside his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.24', 'BSB', 'After him, Binnui son of Henadad repaired another section, from the house of Azariah to the angle and the corner,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.25', 'BSB', 'and Palal son of Uzai made repairs opposite the angle and the tower that juts out from the upper palace of the king near the courtyard of the guard. Next to him, Pedaiah son of Parosh', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.26', 'BSB', 'and the temple servants living on the hill of Ophel made repairs opposite the Water Gate toward the east and the tower that juts out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.27', 'BSB', 'And next to them, the Tekoites repaired another section, from a point opposite the great tower that juts out to the wall of Ophel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.28', 'BSB', 'Above the Horse Gate, each of the priests made repairs in front of his own house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.29', 'BSB', 'Next to them, Zadok son of Immer made repairs opposite his house, and next to him, Shemaiah son of Shecaniah, the guard of the East Gate, made repairs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.30', 'BSB', 'Next to him, Hananiah son of Shelemiah, as well as Hanun the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another section. Next to them, Meshullam son of Berechiah made repairs opposite his own quarters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.31', 'BSB', 'Next to him, Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs as far as the house of the temple servants and the merchants, opposite the Inspection Gate, and as far as the upper room above the corner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.3.32', 'BSB', 'And between the upper room above the corner and the Sheep Gate, the goldsmiths and merchants made repairs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.1', 'BSB', 'Now when Sanballat heard that we were rebuilding the wall, he was furious and filled with indignation. He ridiculed the Jews', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.2', 'BSB', 'before his associates and the army of Samaria, saying, “What are these feeble Jews doing? Can they restore the wall by themselves? Will they offer sacrifices? Will they complete it in a day? Can they bring these burnt stones back to life from the mounds of rubble?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.3', 'BSB', 'Then Tobiah the Ammonite, who was beside him, said, “If even a fox were to climb up on what they are building, it would break down their wall of stones!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.4', 'BSB', 'Hear us, O God, for we are despised. Turn their scorn back upon their own heads, and let them be taken as plunder to a land of captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.5', 'BSB', 'Do not cover up their iniquity or let their sin be blotted out from Your sight, for they have provoked the builders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.6', 'BSB', 'So we rebuilt the wall until all of it was joined together up to half its height, for the people had a mind to work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.7', 'BSB', 'When Sanballat and Tobiah, together with the Arabs, Ammonites, and Ashdodites, heard that the repair to the walls of Jerusalem was progressing and that the gaps were being closed, they were furious,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.8', 'BSB', 'and all of them conspired to come and fight against Jerusalem and create a hindrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.9', 'BSB', 'So we prayed to our God and posted a guard against them day and night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.10', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the people of Judah said: “The strength of the laborer fails, and there is so much rubble that we will never be able to rebuild the wall.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.11', 'BSB', 'And our enemies said, “Before they know or see a thing, we will come into their midst, kill them, and put an end to the work.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.12', 'BSB', 'At that time the Jews who lived nearby came and told us ten times over, “Wherever you turn, they will attack us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.13', 'BSB', 'So I stationed men behind the lowest sections of the wall, at the vulnerable areas. I stationed them by families with their swords, spears, and bows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.14', 'BSB', 'After I had made an inspection, I stood up and said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people, “Do not be afraid of them. Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your brothers, your sons and your daughters, your wives and your homes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.15', 'BSB', 'When our enemies heard that we were aware of their scheme and that God had frustrated it, each of us returned to his own work on the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.16', 'BSB', 'And from that day on, half of my servants did the work while the other half held spears, shields, bows, and armor. The officers stationed themselves behind all the people of Judah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.17', 'BSB', 'who were rebuilding the wall. The laborers who carried materials worked with one hand and held a weapon with the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.18', 'BSB', 'And each of the builders worked with his sword strapped at his side. But the trumpeter stayed beside me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.19', 'BSB', 'Then I said to the nobles, the officials, and the rest of the people: “The work is great and extensive, and we are spread out far from one another along the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.20', 'BSB', 'Wherever you hear the sound of the horn, rally to us there. Our God will fight for us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.21', 'BSB', 'So we continued the work, while half of the men held spears from the break of dawn until the stars came out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.22', 'BSB', 'At that time I also said to the people, “Let every man and his servant spend the night inside Jerusalem, so that they can stand guard by night and work by day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.4.23', 'BSB', 'So neither I nor my brothers nor my servants nor the guards with me changed out of our clothes; each carried his weapon, even to go for water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.1', 'BSB', 'About that time there was a great outcry from the people and their wives against their fellow Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.2', 'BSB', 'Some were saying, “We and our sons and daughters are numerous. We must get grain in order to eat and stay alive.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.3', 'BSB', 'Others were saying, “We are mortgaging our fields, our vineyards, and our homes to get grain during the famine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.4', 'BSB', 'Still others were saying, “We have borrowed money to pay the king’s tax on our fields and vineyards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.5', 'BSB', 'We and our children are just like our countrymen and their children, yet we are subjecting our sons and daughters to slavery. Some of our daughters are already enslaved, but we are powerless to redeem them because our fields and vineyards belong to others.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.6', 'BSB', 'When I heard their outcry and these complaints, I became extremely angry,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.7', 'BSB', 'and after serious thought I rebuked the nobles and officials, saying, “You are exacting usury from your own brothers!” So I called a large assembly against them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.8', 'BSB', 'and said, “We have done our best to buy back our Jewish brothers who were sold to foreigners, but now you are selling your own brothers, that they may be sold back to us!” But they remained silent, for they could find nothing to say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.9', 'BSB', 'So I continued, “What you are doing is not right. Shouldn’t you walk in the fear of our God to avoid the reproach of our foreign enemies?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.10', 'BSB', 'I, as well as my brothers and my servants, have been lending the people money and grain. Please, let us stop this usury.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.11', 'BSB', 'Please restore to them immediately their fields, vineyards, olive groves, and houses, along with the percentage of the money, grain, new wine, and oil that you have been assessing them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.12', 'BSB', '“We will restore it,” they replied, “and will require nothing more from them. We will do as you say.” So I summoned the priests and required of the nobles and officials an oath that they would do what they had promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.13', 'BSB', 'I also shook out the folds of my robe and said, “May God likewise shake out of His house and possession every man who does not keep this promise. May such a man be shaken out and have nothing!” The whole assembly said, “Amen,” and they praised the LORD. And the people did as they had promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.14', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, from the day King Artaxerxes appointed me to be their governor in the land of Judah, from his twentieth year until his thirty-second year (twelve years total), neither I nor my brothers ate the food allotted to the governor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.15', 'BSB', 'The governors before me had heavily burdened the people, taking from them bread and wine plus forty shekels of silver. Their servants also oppressed the people, but I did not do this because of my fear of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.16', 'BSB', 'Instead, I devoted myself to the construction of the wall, and all my servants were gathered there for the work; we did not acquire any land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.17', 'BSB', 'There were 150 Jews and officials at my table, besides the guests from the surrounding nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.18', 'BSB', 'Each day one ox, six choice sheep, and some fowl were prepared for me, and once every ten days an abundance of all kinds of wine was provided. But I did not demand the food allotted to the governor, because the burden on the people was so heavy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.5.19', 'BSB', 'Remember me favorably, O my God, for all that I have done for this people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.1', 'BSB', 'When Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arab, and the rest of our enemies heard that I had rebuilt the wall and not a gap was left—though to that time I had not yet installed the doors in the gates—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.2', 'BSB', 'Sanballat and Geshem sent me this message: “Come, let us meet together in one of the villages on the plain of Ono.” But they were planning to harm me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.3', 'BSB', 'So I sent messengers to them, saying, “I am doing a great work and cannot come down. Why should the work stop while I leave it to go down to you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.4', 'BSB', 'Four times they sent me the same message, and each time I gave the same reply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.5', 'BSB', 'The fifth time, Sanballat sent me this same message by his young servant, who had in his hand an unsealed letter', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.6', 'BSB', 'that read: “It is reported among the nations—and Geshem agrees—that you and the Jews are plotting to revolt, and this is why you are building the wall. According to these reports, you are to become their king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.7', 'BSB', 'and you have even appointed prophets in Jerusalem to proclaim on your behalf: ‘There is a king in Judah.’ Soon these rumors will reach the ears of the king. So come, let us confer together.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.8', 'BSB', 'Then I sent him this reply: “There is nothing to these rumors you are spreading; you are inventing them in your own mind.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.9', 'BSB', 'For they were all trying to frighten us, saying, “Their hands will be weakened in the work, and it will never be finished.” But now, my God, strengthen my hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.10', 'BSB', 'Later, I went to the house of Shemaiah son of Delaiah, the son of Mehetabel, who was confined to his house. He said: “Let us meet at the house of God inside the temple. Let us shut the temple doors because they are coming to kill you— by night they are coming to kill you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.11', 'BSB', 'But I replied, “Should a man like me run away? Should one like me go into the temple to save his own life? I will not go!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.12', 'BSB', 'I realized that God had not sent him, but that he had uttered this prophecy against me because Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.13', 'BSB', 'He had been hired to intimidate me so that I would sin by doing as he suggested, so they could give me a bad name in order to discredit me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.14', 'BSB', 'O my God, remember Tobiah and Sanballat for what they have done, and also Noadiah the prophetess and the other prophets who tried to intimidate me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.15', 'BSB', 'So the wall was completed in fifty-two days, on the twenty-fifth of Elul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.16', 'BSB', 'When all our enemies heard about this, all the surrounding nations were afraid and disheartened, for they realized that this task had been accomplished by our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.17', 'BSB', 'Also in those days, the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and Tobiah’s letters came back to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.18', 'BSB', 'For many in Judah were bound by oath to him, since he was a son-in-law of Shecaniah son of Arah, and his son Jehohanan had married the daughter of Meshullam son of Berechiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.6.19', 'BSB', 'Moreover, these nobles kept reporting to me Tobiah’s good deeds, and they relayed my words to him. And Tobiah sent letters to intimidate me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.1', 'BSB', 'When the wall had been rebuilt and I had set the doors in place, the gatekeepers, singers, and Levites were appointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.2', 'BSB', 'Then I put my brother Hanani in charge of Jerusalem, along with Hananiah the commander of the fortress, because he was a faithful man who feared God more than most.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.3', 'BSB', 'And I told them, “Do not open the gates of Jerusalem until the sun is hot. While the guards are on duty, keep the doors shut and securely fastened. And appoint the residents of Jerusalem as guards, some at their posts and some at their own homes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.4', 'BSB', 'Now the city was large and spacious, but there were few people in it, and the houses had not yet been rebuilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.5', 'BSB', 'Then my God put it into my heart to assemble the nobles, the officials, and the people to be enrolled by genealogy. I found the genealogical register of those who had first returned, and I found the following written in it:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.6', 'BSB', 'These are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.7', 'BSB', 'accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.8', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Parosh, 2,172;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
