('Neh.7.57', 'BSB', 'The descendants of the servants of Solomon: the descendants of Sotai, the descendants of Sophereth, the descendants of Perida,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.58', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Jaala, the descendants of Darkon, the descendants of Giddel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.59', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Shephatiah, the descendants of Hattil, the descendants of Pochereth-hazzebaim, and the descendants of Amon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.60', 'BSB', 'The temple servants and descendants of the servants of Solomon numbered 392 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.61', 'BSB', 'The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer, but could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.62', 'BSB', 'the descendants of Delaiah, the descendants of Tobiah, and the descendants of Nekoda, 642 in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.63', 'BSB', 'And from among the priests: the descendants of Hobaiah, the descendants of Hakkoz, and the descendants of Barzillai (who had married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and was called by their name).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.64', 'BSB', 'These men searched for their family records, but they could not find them and so were excluded from the priesthood as unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.65', 'BSB', 'The governor ordered them not to eat the most holy things until there was a priest to consult the Urim and Thummim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.66', 'BSB', 'The whole assembly numbered 42,360,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.67', 'BSB', 'in addition to their 7,337 menservants and maidservants, as well as their 245 male and female singers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.68', 'BSB', 'They had 736 horses, 245 mules,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.69', 'BSB', '435 camels, and 6,720 donkeys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.70', 'BSB', 'Some of the heads of the families contributed to the project. The governor gave to the treasury 1,000 darics of gold, 50 bowls, and 530 priestly garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.71', 'BSB', 'And some of the heads of the families gave to the treasury for the project 20,000 darics of gold and 2,200 minas of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.72', 'BSB', 'The rest of the people gave a total of 20,000 darics of gold, 2,000 minas of silver, and 67 priestly garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.7.73', 'BSB', 'So the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, and temple servants, along with some of the people and the rest of the Israelites, settled in their own towns. And by the seventh month the Israelites had settled in their towns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.1', 'BSB', 'At that time all the people gathered together in the square before the Water Gate, and they asked Ezra the scribe to bring out the Book of the Law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded for Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.2', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the seventh month, Ezra the priest brought the Law before the assembly of men and women and all who could listen and understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.3', 'BSB', 'So Ezra read it aloud from daybreak until noon as he faced the square before the Water Gate, in front of the men and women and those who could understand. And all the people listened attentively to the Book of the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.4', 'BSB', 'Ezra the scribe stood on a high wooden platform built for this occasion. At his right side stood Mattithiah, Shema, Anaiah, Uriah, Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, and at his left were Pedaiah, Mishael, Malchijah, Hashum, Hash-baddanah, Zechariah, and Meshullam.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.5', 'BSB', 'Ezra opened the book in full view of all the people, since he was standing above them all, and as he opened it, all the people stood up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.6', 'BSB', 'Then Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God, and with their hands uplifted, all the people said, “Amen, Amen!” Then they bowed down and worshiped the LORD with their faces to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.7', 'BSB', 'The Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, and Pelaiah—instructed the people in the Law as they stood in their places.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.8', 'BSB', 'So they read from the Book of the Law of God, explaining it and giving insight, so that the people could understand what was being read.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.9', 'BSB', 'Nehemiah the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who were instructing the people said to all of them, “This day is holy to the LORD your God. Do not mourn or weep.” For all the people were weeping as they heard the words of the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.10', 'BSB', 'Then Nehemiah told them, “Go and eat what is rich, drink what is sweet, and send out portions to those who have nothing prepared, since today is holy to our Lord. Do not grieve, for the joy of the LORD is your strength.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.11', 'BSB', 'And the Levites calmed all the people, saying, “Be still, since today is holy. Do not grieve.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.12', 'BSB', 'Then all the people began to eat and drink, to send out portions, and to rejoice greatly, because they understood the words that had been made known to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.13', 'BSB', 'On the second day of the month, the heads of all the families, along with the priests and Levites, gathered around Ezra the scribe to study the words of the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.14', 'BSB', 'And they found written in the Law, which the LORD had commanded through Moses, that the Israelites were to dwell in booths during the feast of the seventh month.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.15', 'BSB', 'So they proclaimed this message and spread it throughout their towns and in Jerusalem, saying, “Go out to the hill country and bring back branches of olive, wild olive, myrtle, palm, and other leafy trees, to make booths, as it is written.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.16', 'BSB', 'And the people went out, brought back branches, and made booths on their own rooftops, in their courtyards, in the court of the house of God, and in the squares by the Water Gate and by the Gate of Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.17', 'BSB', 'The whole assembly who had returned from exile made booths and lived in them. From the days of Joshua son of Nun until that day, the Israelites had not celebrated like this. And there was great rejoicing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.8.18', 'BSB', 'Day after day, from the first day to the last, Ezra read from the Book of the Law of God. The Israelites kept the feast for seven days, and on the eighth day they held an assembly, according to the ordinance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.1', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-fourth day of the same month, the Israelites gathered together, fasting and wearing sackcloth, with dust on their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.2', 'BSB', 'Those of Israelite descent separated themselves from all the foreigners, and they stood and confessed their sins and the iniquities of their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.3', 'BSB', 'While they stood in their places, they read from the Book of the Law of the LORD their God for a quarter of the day, and they spent another quarter of the day in confession and worship of the LORD their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.4', 'BSB', 'And the Levites—Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani—stood on the raised platform and cried out in a loud voice to the LORD their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.5', 'BSB', 'Then the Levites—Jeshua, Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah—said, “Stand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting: Blessed be Your glorious name, and may it be exalted above all blessing and praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.6', 'BSB', 'You alone are the LORD. You created the heavens, the highest heavens with all their host, the earth and all that is on it, the seas and all that is in them. You give life to all things, and the host of heaven worships You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.7', 'BSB', 'You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, who brought him out of Ur of the Chaldeans and gave him the name Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.8', 'BSB', 'You found his heart faithful before You, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanites and Hittites, of the Amorites and Perizzites, of the Jebusites and Girgashites— to give it to his descendants. You have kept Your promise, because You are righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.9', 'BSB', 'You saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt; You heard their cry at the Red Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.10', 'BSB', 'You performed signs and wonders against Pharaoh, all his officials, and all the people of his land, for You knew they had acted with arrogance against our fathers. You made a name for Yourself that endures to this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.11', 'BSB', 'You divided the sea before them, and they crossed through it on dry ground. You hurled their pursuers into the depths like a stone into raging waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.12', 'BSB', 'You led them with a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night, to light for them the way in which they should travel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.13', 'BSB', 'You came down on Mount Sinai and spoke with them from heaven. You gave them just ordinances, true laws, and good statutes and commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.14', 'BSB', 'You revealed to them Your holy Sabbath and gave them commandments and statutes and laws through Your servant Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.15', 'BSB', 'In their hunger You gave them bread from heaven; in their thirst You brought them water from the rock. You told them to go in and possess the land which You had sworn to give them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.16', 'BSB', 'But they and our fathers became arrogant and stiff-necked and did not obey Your commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.17', 'BSB', 'They refused to listen and failed to remember the wonders You performed among them. They stiffened their necks and appointed a leader to return them to their bondage in Egypt. But You are a forgiving God, gracious and compassionate, slow to anger and rich in loving devotion, and You did not forsake them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.18', 'BSB', 'Even when they cast for themselves an image of a calf and said, ‘This is your God who brought you up out of Egypt,’ and when they committed terrible blasphemies,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.19', 'BSB', 'You in Your great compassion did not forsake them in the wilderness. By day the pillar of cloud never turned away from guiding them on their path; and by the night the pillar of fire illuminated the way they should go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.20', 'BSB', 'You gave Your good Spirit to instruct them. You did not withhold Your manna from their mouths, and You gave them water for their thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.21', 'BSB', 'For forty years You sustained them in the wilderness, so that they lacked nothing. Their clothes did not wear out and their feet did not swell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.22', 'BSB', 'You gave them kingdoms and peoples and allotted to them every corner of the land. So they took the land of Sihon king of Heshbon and of Og king of Bashan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.23', 'BSB', 'You multiplied their descendants like the stars of heaven and brought them to the land You had told their fathers to enter and possess.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.24', 'BSB', 'So their descendants went in and possessed the land; You subdued before them the Canaanites dwelling in the land. You delivered into their hands the kings and peoples of the land, to do with them as they wished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.25', 'BSB', 'They captured fortified cities and fertile land and took houses full of all goods, wells already dug, vineyards, olive groves, and fruit trees in abundance. So they ate and were filled; they grew fat and delighted in Your great goodness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.26', 'BSB', 'But they were disobedient and rebelled against You; they flung Your law behind their backs. They killed Your prophets, who had admonished them to return to You. They committed terrible blasphemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.27', 'BSB', 'So You delivered them into the hands of enemies who oppressed them, and in their time of distress they cried out to You. From heaven You heard them, and in Your great compassion You gave them deliverers who saved them from the hands of their enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.28', 'BSB', 'But as soon as they had rest, they again did evil in Your sight. So You abandoned them to the hands of their enemies, who had dominion over them. When they cried out to You again, You heard from heaven, and You delivered them many times in Your compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.29', 'BSB', 'You admonished them to turn back to Your law, but they were arrogant and disobeyed Your commandments. They sinned against Your ordinances, by which a man will live if he practices them. They stubbornly shrugged their shoulders; they stiffened their necks and would not obey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.30', 'BSB', 'You were patient with them for many years, and Your Spirit admonished them through Your prophets. Yet they would not listen, so You gave them into the hands of the neighboring peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.31', 'BSB', 'But in Your great compassion, You did not put an end to them; nor did You forsake them, for You are a gracious and compassionate God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.32', 'BSB', 'So now, our God, the great and mighty and awesome God who keeps His gracious covenant, do not view lightly all the hardship that has come upon us, and upon our kings and leaders, our priests and prophets, our ancestors and all Your people, from the days of the kings of Assyria until today.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.33', 'BSB', 'You are just in all that has befallen us, because You have acted faithfully, while we have acted wickedly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.34', 'BSB', 'Our kings and leaders and priests and fathers did not obey Your law or listen to Your commandments and warnings that You gave them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.35', 'BSB', 'For even while they were in their kingdom, with the abundant goodness that You had given them, and in the spacious and fertile land that You had set before them, they would not serve You or turn from their wicked ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.36', 'BSB', 'So here we are today as slaves in the land You gave our fathers to enjoy its fruit and goodness— here we are as slaves!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.37', 'BSB', 'Its abundant harvest goes to the kings You have set over us because of our sins. And they rule over our bodies and our livestock as they please. We are in great distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.9.38', 'BSB', 'In view of all this, we make a binding agreement, putting it in writing and sealing it with the names of our leaders, Levites, and priests.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.1', 'BSB', 'Now these were the ones who sealed the document: Nehemiah the governor, son of Hacaliah, and also Zedekiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.2', 'BSB', 'Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.3', 'BSB', 'Pashhur, Amariah, Malchijah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.4', 'BSB', 'Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.5', 'BSB', 'Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.6', 'BSB', 'Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.7', 'BSB', 'Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.8', 'BSB', 'Maaziah, Bilgai, and Shemaiah. These were the priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.9', 'BSB', 'The Levites: Jeshua son of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of Henadad, Kadmiel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.10', 'BSB', 'and their associates: Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.11', 'BSB', 'Mica, Rehob, Hashabiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.12', 'BSB', 'Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.13', 'BSB', 'Hodiah, Bani, and Beninu.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.14', 'BSB', 'And the leaders of the people: Parosh, Pahath-moab, Elam, Zattu, Bani,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.15', 'BSB', 'Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.16', 'BSB', 'Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.17', 'BSB', 'Ater, Hezekiah, Azzur,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.18', 'BSB', 'Hodiah, Hashum, Bezai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.19', 'BSB', 'Hariph, Anathoth, Nebai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.20', 'BSB', 'Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.21', 'BSB', 'Meshezabel, Zadok, Jaddua,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.22', 'BSB', 'Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.23', 'BSB', 'Hoshea, Hananiah, Hasshub,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.24', 'BSB', 'Hallohesh, Pilha, Shobek,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.25', 'BSB', 'Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.26', 'BSB', 'Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.27', 'BSB', 'Malluch, Harim, and Baanah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.28', 'BSB', '“The rest of the people—the priests, Levites, gatekeepers, singers, temple servants, and all who had separated themselves from the people of the land to obey the Law of God—along with their wives and all their sons and daughters who are able to understand,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.29', 'BSB', 'hereby join with their noble brothers and commit themselves with a sworn oath to follow the Law of God given through His servant Moses and to carefully obey all the commandments, ordinances, and statutes of the LORD our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.30', 'BSB', 'We will not give our daughters in marriage to the people of the land, and we will not take their daughters for our sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.31', 'BSB', 'When the people of the land bring merchandise or any kind of grain to sell on the Sabbath day, we will not buy from them on a Sabbath or holy day. Every seventh year we will let the fields lie fallow, and will cancel every debt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.32', 'BSB', 'We also place ourselves under the obligation to contribute a third of a shekel yearly for the service of the house of our God:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.33', 'BSB', 'for the showbread, for the regular grain offerings and burnt offerings, for the Sabbath offerings, for the New Moons and appointed feasts, for the holy offerings, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the duties of the house of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.34', 'BSB', 'We have cast lots among the priests, Levites, and people for the donation of wood by our families at the appointed times each year. They are to bring it to the house of our God to burn on the altar of the LORD our God, as it is written in the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.35', 'BSB', 'We will also bring the firstfruits of our land and of every fruit tree to the house of the LORD year by year.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.36', 'BSB', 'And we will bring the firstborn of our sons and our livestock, as it is written in the Law, and will bring the firstborn of our herds and flocks to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.37', 'BSB', 'Moreover, we will bring to the priests at the storerooms of the house of our God the firstfruits of our dough, of our grain offerings, of the fruit of all our trees, and of our new wine and oil. A tenth of our produce belongs to the Levites, so that they shall receive tithes in all the towns where we labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.38', 'BSB', 'A priest of Aaron’s line is to accompany the Levites when they collect the tenth, and the Levites are to bring a tenth of these tithes to the storerooms of the treasury in the house of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.10.39', 'BSB', 'For the Israelites and the Levites are to bring the contributions of grain, new wine, and oil to the storerooms where the articles of the sanctuary are kept and where the ministering priests, the gatekeepers, and the singers stay. Thus we will not neglect the house of our God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.1', 'BSB', 'Now the leaders of the people settled in Jerusalem, and the rest of the people cast lots to bring one out of ten to live in the holy city of Jerusalem, while the remaining nine were to dwell in their own towns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.2', 'BSB', 'And the people blessed all the men who volunteered to live in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.3', 'BSB', 'These are the heads of the provinces who settled in Jerusalem. (In the villages of Judah, however, each lived on his own property in their towns—the Israelites, priests, Levites, temple servants, and descendants of Solomon’s servants—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.4', 'BSB', 'while some of the descendants of Judah and Benjamin settled in Jerusalem.) From the descendants of Judah: Athaiah son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalalel, a descendant of Perez;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.5', 'BSB', 'and Maaseiah son of Baruch, the son of Col-hozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, a descendant of Shelah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.6', 'BSB', 'The descendants of Perez who settled in Jerusalem totaled 468 men of valor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.7', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of Benjamin: Sallu son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jeshaiah;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.8', 'BSB', 'and his followers Gabbai and Sallai—928 men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.9', 'BSB', 'Joel son of Zichri was the officer over them, and Judah son of Hassenuah was over the Second District of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.10', 'BSB', 'From the priests: Jedaiah son of Joiarib; Jachin;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.11', 'BSB', 'Seraiah son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the chief official of the house of God;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.12', 'BSB', 'and their associates who did the work at the temple—822 men; Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.13', 'BSB', 'and his associates, the leaders of families—242 men; Amashai son of Azarel, the son of Ahzai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.14', 'BSB', 'and his associates —128 mighty men of valor. Zabdiel son of Haggedolim was their overseer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.15', 'BSB', 'From the Levites: Shemaiah son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.16', 'BSB', 'Shabbethai and Jozabad, two leaders of the Levites, who supervised the work outside the house of God;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.17', 'BSB', 'Mattaniah son of Mica, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, who led in thanksgiving and prayer; Bakbukiah, second among his associates; and Abda son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.18', 'BSB', 'The Levites in the holy city totaled 284.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.19', 'BSB', 'And the gatekeepers: Akkub, Talmon, and their associates, who kept watch at the gates—172 men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.20', 'BSB', 'The rest of the Israelites, with the priests and Levites, were in all the villages of Judah, each on his own inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.21', 'BSB', 'The temple servants lived on the hill of Ophel, with Ziha and Gishpa over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.22', 'BSB', 'Now the overseer of the Levites in Jerusalem was Uzzi son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Mica. He was one of Asaph’s descendants, who were the singers in charge of the service of the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.23', 'BSB', 'For there was a command from the king concerning the singers, an ordinance regulating their daily activities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.24', 'BSB', 'Pethahiah son of Meshezabel, a descendant of Zerah son of Judah, was the king’s agent in every matter concerning the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.25', 'BSB', 'As for the villages with their fields, some of the people of Judah lived in Kiriath-arba, Dibon, Jekabzeel, and their villages;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.26', 'BSB', 'in Jeshua, Moladah, and Beth-pelet;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.27', 'BSB', 'in Hazar-shual; in Beersheba and its villages;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.28', 'BSB', 'in Ziklag; in Meconah and its villages;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.29', 'BSB', 'in En-rimmon, Zorah, Jarmuth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.30', 'BSB', 'Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages; in Lachish and its fields; and in Azekah and its villages. So they settled from Beersheba all the way to the Valley of Hinnom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.31', 'BSB', 'The descendants of Benjamin from Geba lived in Michmash, Aija, and Bethel with its villages;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.32', 'BSB', 'in Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.33', 'BSB', 'Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.34', 'BSB', 'Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.35', 'BSB', 'Lod, and Ono; and in the Valley of the Craftsmen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.11.36', 'BSB', 'And some divisions of the Levites of Judah settled in Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.1', 'BSB', 'Now these are the priests and Levites who went up with Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and with Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.2', 'BSB', 'Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.3', 'BSB', 'Shecaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.4', 'BSB', 'Iddo, Ginnethon, Abijah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.5', 'BSB', 'Mijamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.6', 'BSB', 'Shemaiah, Joiarib, Jedaiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.7', 'BSB', 'Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, and Jedaiah. These were the leaders of the priests and their associates in the days of Jeshua.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.8', 'BSB', 'The Levites were Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, and Mattaniah, who, with his associates, led the songs of thanksgiving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.9', 'BSB', 'Bakbukiah and Unni, their associates, stood across from them in the services.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.10', 'BSB', 'Jeshua was the father of Joiakim, Joiakim was the father of Eliashib, Eliashib was the father of Joiada,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.11', 'BSB', 'Joiada was the father of Jonathan, and Jonathan was the father of Jaddua.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.12', 'BSB', 'In the days of Joiakim, these were the heads of the priestly families: of the family of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.13', 'BSB', 'of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.14', 'BSB', 'of Malluchi, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.15', 'BSB', 'of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.16', 'BSB', 'of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.17', 'BSB', 'of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin and of Moadiah, Piltai;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.18', 'BSB', 'of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jonathan;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.19', 'BSB', 'of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.20', 'BSB', 'of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.21', 'BSB', 'of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; and of Jedaiah, Nethanel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.22', 'BSB', 'In the days of Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan, and Jaddua, during the reign of Darius the Persian, the heads of the families of the Levites and priests were recorded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.23', 'BSB', 'As for the descendants of Levi, the family heads up to the days of Johanan son of Eliashib were recorded in the Book of the Chronicles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.24', 'BSB', 'The leaders of the Levites were Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua son of Kadmiel, along with their associates, who stood across from them to give praise and thanksgiving as one section alternated with the other, as prescribed by David the man of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.25', 'BSB', 'Mattaniah, Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, and Akkub were gatekeepers who guarded the storerooms at the gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.26', 'BSB', 'They served in the days of Joiakim son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor and Ezra the priest and scribe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.27', 'BSB', 'At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, the Levites were sought out from all their homes and brought to Jerusalem to celebrate the joyous dedication with thanksgiving and singing, accompanied by cymbals, harps, and lyres.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.28', 'BSB', 'The singers were also assembled from the region around Jerusalem, from the villages of the Netophathites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.29', 'BSB', 'from Beth-gilgal, and from the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for they had built villages for themselves around Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.30', 'BSB', 'After the priests and Levites had purified themselves, they purified the people, the gates, and the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.31', 'BSB', 'Then I brought the leaders of Judah up on the wall, and I appointed two great thanksgiving choirs. One was to proceed along the top of the wall to the right, toward the Dung Gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.32', 'BSB', 'Hoshaiah and half the leaders of Judah followed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.33', 'BSB', 'along with Azariah, Ezra, Meshullam,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.34', 'BSB', 'Judah, Benjamin, Shemaiah, Jeremiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.35', 'BSB', 'and some of the priests with trumpets, and also Zechariah son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.36', 'BSB', 'and his associates—Shemaiah, Azarel, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethanel, Judah, and Hanani—with the musical instruments prescribed by David the man of God. Ezra the scribe led the procession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.37', 'BSB', 'At the Fountain Gate they climbed the steps of the City of David on the ascent to the wall and passed above the house of David to the Water Gate on the east.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.38', 'BSB', 'The second thanksgiving choir proceeded to the left, and I followed it with half the people along the top of the wall, past the Tower of the Ovens to the Broad Wall,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.39', 'BSB', 'over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate, the Fish Gate, the Tower of Hananel, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.40', 'BSB', 'The two thanksgiving choirs then stood in the house of God, as did I, along with the half of the officials accompanying me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.41', 'BSB', 'as well as the priests with their trumpets—Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.42', 'BSB', 'and also Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. Then the choirs sang out under the direction of Jezrahiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.43', 'BSB', 'On that day they offered great sacrifices, rejoicing because God had given them great joy. The women and children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard from afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.44', 'BSB', 'And on that same day men were appointed over the rooms that housed the supplies, contributions, firstfruits, and tithes. The portions specified by the Law for the priests and Levites were gathered into these storerooms from the fields of the villages, because Judah rejoiced over the priests and Levites who were serving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.45', 'BSB', 'They performed the service of their God and the service of purification, along with the singers and gatekeepers, as David and his son Solomon had prescribed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.46', 'BSB', 'For long ago, in the days of David and Asaph, there were directors for the singers and for the songs of praise and thanksgiving to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.12.47', 'BSB', 'So in the days of Zerubbabel and Nehemiah, all Israel contributed the daily portions for the singers and gatekeepers. They also set aside daily portions for the Levites, and the Levites set aside daily portions for the descendants of Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.1', 'BSB', 'At that time the Book of Moses was read aloud in the hearing of the people, and in it they found the passage stating that no Ammonite or Moabite should ever enter the assembly of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.2', 'BSB', 'because they had not met the Israelites with food and water, but had hired Balaam to call down a curse against them (although our God had turned the curse into a blessing).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.3', 'BSB', 'As soon as the people heard this law, they excluded from Israel all of foreign descent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.4', 'BSB', 'Now before this, Eliashib the priest, a relative of Tobiah, had been put in charge of the storerooms of the house of our God', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.5', 'BSB', 'and had prepared for Tobiah a large room where they had previously stored the grain offerings, the frankincense, the temple articles, and the tithes of grain, new wine, and oil prescribed for the Levites, singers, and gatekeepers, along with the contributions for the priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.6', 'BSB', 'While all this was happening, I was not in Jerusalem, because I had returned to Artaxerxes king of Babylon in the thirty-second year of his reign. Some time later I obtained leave from the king', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.7', 'BSB', 'to return to Jerusalem. Then I discovered the evil that Eliashib had done on behalf of Tobiah by providing him a room in the courts of the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.8', 'BSB', 'And I was greatly displeased and threw all of Tobiah’s household goods out of the room.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.9', 'BSB', 'Then I ordered that the rooms be purified, and I had the articles of the house of God restored to them, along with the grain offerings and frankincense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.10', 'BSB', 'I also learned that because the portions for the Levites had not been given to them, all the Levites and singers responsible for performing the service had gone back to their own fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.11', 'BSB', 'So I rebuked the officials and asked, “Why has the house of God been neglected?” Then I gathered the Levites and singers together and stationed them at their posts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.12', 'BSB', 'and all Judah brought a tenth of the grain, new wine, and oil into the storerooms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.13', 'BSB', 'I appointed as treasurers over the storerooms Shelemiah the priest, Zadok the scribe, and Pedaiah of the Levites, with Hanan son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah, to assist them, because they were considered trustworthy. They were responsible for distributing the supplies to their fellow Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.14', 'BSB', 'Remember me for this, O my God, and do not blot out my deeds of loving devotion for the house of my God and for its services.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.15', 'BSB', 'In those days I saw people in Judah treading winepresses on the Sabbath and bringing in grain and loading it on donkeys, along with wine, grapes, and figs. All kinds of goods were being brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them against selling food on that day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.16', 'BSB', 'Additionally, men of Tyre who lived there were importing fish and all kinds of merchandise and selling them on the Sabbath to the people of Judah in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.17', 'BSB', 'Then I rebuked the nobles of Judah and asked, “What is this evil you are doing—profaning the Sabbath day?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.18', 'BSB', 'Did not your forefathers do the same things, so that our God brought all this disaster on us and on this city? And now you are rekindling His wrath against Israel by profaning the Sabbath!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.19', 'BSB', 'When the evening shadows began to fall on the gates of Jerusalem, just before the Sabbath, I ordered that the gates be shut and not opened until after the Sabbath. I posted some of my servants at the gates so that no load could enter on the Sabbath day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.20', 'BSB', 'Once or twice, the merchants and those who sell all kinds of goods camped outside Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.21', 'BSB', 'but I warned them, “Why are you camping in front of the wall? If you do it again, I will lay hands on you.” From that time on, they did not return on the Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.22', 'BSB', 'Then I instructed the Levites to purify themselves and guard the gates in order to keep the Sabbath day holy. Remember me for this as well, O my God, and show me mercy according to Your abundant loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.23', 'BSB', 'In those days I also saw Jews who had married women from Ashdod, Ammon, and Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.24', 'BSB', 'Half of their children spoke the language of Ashdod or of the other peoples, but could not speak the language of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.25', 'BSB', 'I rebuked them and called down curses on them. I beat some of these men and pulled out their hair. Then I made them take an oath before God and said, “You must not give your daughters in marriage to their sons or take their daughters as wives for your sons or for yourselves!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.26', 'BSB', 'Did not King Solomon of Israel sin in matters like this? There was not a king like him among many nations, and he was loved by his God, who made him king over all Israel—yet foreign women drew him into sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.27', 'BSB', 'Must we now hear that you too are doing all this terrible evil and acting unfaithfully against our God by marrying foreign women?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.28', 'BSB', 'Even one of the sons of Jehoiada son of Eliashib the high priest had become a son-in-law to Sanballat the Horonite. Therefore I drove him away from me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.29', 'BSB', 'Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.30', 'BSB', 'Thus I purified the priests and Levites from everything foreign, and I assigned specific duties to each of the priests and Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Neh.13.31', 'BSB', 'I also arranged for contributions of wood at the appointed times, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, with favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is what happened in the days of Xerxes, who reigned over 127 provinces from India to Cush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.2', 'BSB', 'In those days King Xerxes sat on his royal throne in the citadel of Susa.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.3', 'BSB', 'In the third year of his reign, Xerxes held a feast for all his officials and servants. The military leaders of Persia and Media were there, along with the nobles and princes of the provinces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.4', 'BSB', 'And for a full 180 days he displayed the glorious riches of his kingdom and the magnificent splendor of his greatness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.5', 'BSB', 'At the end of this time, in the garden court of the royal palace, the king held a seven-day feast for all the people in the citadel of Susa, from the least to the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.6', 'BSB', 'Hangings of white and blue linen were fastened with cords of fine white and purple material to silver rings on the marble pillars. Gold and silver couches were arranged on a mosaic pavement of porphyry, marble, mother-of-pearl, and other costly stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.7', 'BSB', 'Beverages were served in an array of goblets of gold, each with a different design, and the royal wine flowed freely, according to the king’s bounty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.8', 'BSB', 'By order of the king, no limit was placed on the drinking, and every official of his household was to serve each man whatever he desired.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.9', 'BSB', 'Queen Vashti also gave a banquet for the women in the royal palace of King Xerxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.10', 'BSB', 'On the seventh day, when the king’s heart was merry with wine, he ordered the seven eunuchs who served him—Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, Abagtha, Zethar, and Carkas—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.11', 'BSB', 'to bring Queen Vashti before him, wearing her royal crown, to display her beauty to the people and officials. For she was beautiful to behold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.12', 'BSB', 'Queen Vashti, however, refused to come at the king’s command brought by his eunuchs. And the king became furious, and his anger burned within him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.13', 'BSB', 'Then the king consulted the wise men who knew the times, for it was customary for him to confer with the experts in law and justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.14', 'BSB', 'His closest advisors were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media who had personal access to the king and ranked highest in the kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.15', 'BSB', '“According to law,” he asked, “what should be done with Queen Vashti, since she refused to obey the command of King Xerxes delivered by the eunuchs?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.16', 'BSB', 'And in the presence of the king and his princes, Memucan replied, “Queen Vashti has wronged not only the king, but all the princes and the peoples in all the provinces of King Xerxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.17', 'BSB', 'For the conduct of the queen will become known to all women, causing them to despise their husbands and say, ‘King Xerxes ordered Queen Vashti to be brought before him, but she did not come.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.18', 'BSB', 'This very day the noble women of Persia and Media who have heard about the queen’s conduct will say the same thing to all the king’s officials, resulting in much contempt and wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.19', 'BSB', 'So if it pleases the king, let him issue a royal decree, and let it be recorded in the laws of Persia and Media so that it cannot be repealed, that Vashti shall never again enter the presence of King Xerxes, and that her royal position shall be given to a woman better than she.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.20', 'BSB', 'The edict the king issues will be heard throughout his vast kingdom—and so all women, from the least to the greatest, will honor their husbands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.21', 'BSB', 'The king and his princes were pleased with this counsel; so the king did as Memucan had advised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.1.22', 'BSB', 'He sent letters to all the provinces of the kingdom, to each province in its own script and to each people in their own language, proclaiming that every man should be master of his own household.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.1', 'BSB', 'Some time later, when the anger of King Xerxes had subsided, he remembered Vashti and what she had done, and what had been decreed against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.2', 'BSB', 'Then the king’s attendants proposed, “Let a search be made for beautiful young virgins for the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.3', 'BSB', 'and let the king appoint commissioners in each province of his kingdom to assemble all the beautiful young women into the harem at the citadel of Susa. Let them be placed under the care of Hegai, the king’s eunuch in charge of the women, and let them be given beauty treatments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.4', 'BSB', 'Then let the young woman who pleases the king become queen in place of Vashti.” This suggestion pleased the king, and he acted accordingly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.5', 'BSB', 'Now there was at the citadel of Susa a Jewish man from the tribe of Benjamin named Mordecai son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.6', 'BSB', 'He had been carried into exile from Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon among those taken captive with Jeconiah king of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.7', 'BSB', 'And Mordecai had brought up Hadassah (that is, Esther), the daughter of his uncle, because she did not have a father or mother. The young woman was lovely in form and appearance, and when her father and mother had died, Mordecai had taken her in as his own daughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.8', 'BSB', 'When the king’s command and edict had been proclaimed, many young women gathered at the citadel of Susa under the care of Hegai. Esther was also taken to the palace and placed under the care of Hegai, the custodian of the women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.9', 'BSB', 'And the young woman pleased him and obtained his favor, so he quickly provided her with beauty treatments and the special diet. He assigned to her seven select maidservants from the palace and transferred her with them to the best place in the harem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.10', 'BSB', 'Esther did not reveal her people or her lineage, because Mordecai had instructed her not to do so.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.11', 'BSB', 'And every day Mordecai would walk back and forth in front of the court of the harem to learn about Esther’s welfare and what was happening to her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.12', 'BSB', 'In the twelve months before her turn to go to King Xerxes, the harem regulation required each young woman to receive beauty treatments with oil of myrrh for six months, and then with perfumes and cosmetics for another six months.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.13', 'BSB', 'When the young woman would go to the king, she was given whatever she requested to take with her from the harem to the king’s palace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.14', 'BSB', 'She would go there in the evening, and in the morning she would return to a second harem under the care of Shaashgaz, the king’s eunuch in charge of the concubines. She would not return to the king unless he delighted in her and summoned her by name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.15', 'BSB', 'Now Esther was the daughter of Abihail, the uncle from whom Mordecai had adopted her as his own daughter. And when it was her turn to go to the king, she did not ask for anything except what Hegai, the king’s trusted official in charge of the harem, had advised. And Esther found favor in the eyes of everyone who saw her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.16', 'BSB', 'She was taken to King Xerxes in the royal palace in the tenth month, the month of Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.17', 'BSB', 'And the king loved Esther more than all the other women, and she found grace and favor in his sight more than all of the other virgins. So he placed the royal crown upon her head and made her queen in place of Vashti.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.18', 'BSB', 'Then the king held a great banquet, Esther’s banquet, for all his officials and servants. He proclaimed a tax holiday in the provinces and gave gifts worthy of the king’s bounty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.19', 'BSB', 'When the virgins were assembled a second time, Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.20', 'BSB', 'Esther still had not revealed her lineage or her people, just as Mordecai had instructed. She obeyed Mordecai’s command, as she had done under his care.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.21', 'BSB', 'In those days, while Mordecai was sitting at the king’s gate, Bigthan and Teresh, two of the king’s eunuchs who guarded the entrance, grew angry and conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.22', 'BSB', 'When Mordecai learned of the plot, he reported it to Queen Esther, and she informed the king on Mordecai’s behalf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.2.23', 'BSB', 'After the report had been investigated and verified, both officials were hanged on the gallows. And all this was recorded in the Book of the Chronicles in the presence of the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.1', 'BSB', 'After these events, King Xerxes honored Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, elevating him to a position above all the princes who were with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.2', 'BSB', 'All the royal servants at the king’s gate bowed down and paid homage to Haman, because the king had commanded that this be done for him. But Mordecai would not bow down or pay homage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.3', 'BSB', 'Then the royal servants at the king’s gate asked Mordecai, “Why do you disobey the command of the king?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.4', 'BSB', 'Day after day they warned him, but he would not comply. So they reported it to Haman to see whether Mordecai’s behavior would be tolerated, since he had told them he was a Jew.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.5', 'BSB', 'When Haman saw that Mordecai would not bow down or pay him homage, he was filled with rage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.6', 'BSB', 'And when he learned the identity of Mordecai’s people, he scorned the notion of laying hands on Mordecai alone. Instead, he sought to destroy all of Mordecai’s people, the Jews, throughout the kingdom of Xerxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.7', 'BSB', 'In the twelfth year of King Xerxes, in the first month, the month of Nisan, the Pur (that is, the lot) was cast before Haman to determine a day and month. And the lot fell on the twelfth month, the month of Adar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.8', 'BSB', 'Then Haman informed King Xerxes, “There is a certain people scattered and dispersed among the peoples of every province of your kingdom. Their laws are different from everyone else’s, and they do not obey the king’s laws. So it is not in the king’s best interest to tolerate them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.9', 'BSB', 'If it pleases the king, let a decree be issued to destroy them, and I will deposit ten thousand talents of silver into the royal treasury to pay those who carry it out.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.10', 'BSB', 'So the king removed the signet ring from his finger and gave it to Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.11', 'BSB', '“Keep your money,” said the king to Haman. “These people are given to you to do with them as you please.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.12', 'BSB', 'On the thirteenth day of the first month, the royal scribes were summoned and the order was written exactly as Haman commanded the royal satraps, the governors of each province, and the officials of each people, in the script of each province and the language of every people. It was written in the name of King Xerxes and sealed with the royal signet ring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.13', 'BSB', 'And the letters were sent by couriers to each of the royal provinces with the order to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the Jews—young and old, women and children—and to plunder their possessions on a single day, the thirteenth day of Adar, the twelfth month.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.14', 'BSB', 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that they would be ready on that day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.3.15', 'BSB', 'The couriers left, spurred on by the king’s command, and the edict was issued in the citadel of Susa. Then the king and Haman sat down to drink, but the city of Susa was in confusion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.1', 'BSB', 'When Mordecai learned of all that had happened, he tore his clothes, put on sackcloth and ashes, and went out into the middle of the city, wailing loudly and bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.2', 'BSB', 'But he went only as far as the king’s gate, because the law prohibited anyone wearing sackcloth from entering that gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.3', 'BSB', 'In every province to which the king’s command and edict came, there was great mourning among the Jews. They fasted, wept, and lamented, and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.4', 'BSB', 'When Esther’s maidens and eunuchs came and told her about Mordecai, the queen was overcome with distress. She sent clothes for Mordecai to wear instead of his sackcloth, but he would not accept them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.5', 'BSB', 'Then Esther summoned Hathach, one of the king’s eunuchs appointed to her, and she dispatched him to Mordecai to learn what was troubling him and why.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.6', 'BSB', 'So Hathach went out to Mordecai in the city square in front of the king’s gate,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.7', 'BSB', 'and Mordecai told him all that had happened to him, including the exact amount of money that Haman had promised to pay into the royal treasury in order to destroy the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.8', 'BSB', 'Mordecai also gave Hathach a copy of the written decree issued in Susa for the destruction of the Jews, to show and explain to Esther, urging her to approach the king, implore his favor, and plead before him for her people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.9', 'BSB', 'So Hathach went back and relayed Mordecai’s response to Esther.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.10', 'BSB', 'Then Esther spoke to Hathach and instructed him to tell Mordecai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.11', 'BSB', '“All the royal officials and the people of the king’s provinces know that one law applies to every man or woman who approaches the king in the inner court without being summoned—that he be put to death. Only if the king extends the gold scepter may that person live. But I have not been summoned to appear before the king for the past thirty days.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.12', 'BSB', 'When Esther’s words were relayed to Mordecai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.13', 'BSB', 'he sent back to her this reply: “Do not imagine that because you are in the king’s palace you alone will escape the fate of all the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.14', 'BSB', 'For if you remain silent at this time, relief and deliverance for the Jews will arise from another place, but you and your father’s house will perish. And who knows if perhaps you have come to the kingdom for such a time as this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.15', 'BSB', 'Then Esther sent this reply to Mordecai:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.16', 'BSB', '“Go and assemble all the Jews who can be found in Susa, and fast for me. Do not eat or drink for three days, night or day, and I and my maidens will fast as you do. After that, I will go to the king, even though it is against the law. And if I perish, I perish!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.4.17', 'BSB', 'So Mordecai went and did all that Esther had instructed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.1', 'BSB', 'On the third day, Esther put on her royal attire and stood in the inner court of the palace across from the king’s quarters. The king was sitting on his royal throne in the royal courtroom, facing the entrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.2', 'BSB', 'As soon as the king saw Queen Esther standing in the court, she found favor in his sight. The king extended the gold scepter in his hand toward Esther, and she approached and touched the tip of the scepter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.3', 'BSB', '“What is it, Queen Esther?” the king inquired. “What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be given to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.4', 'BSB', '“If it pleases the king,” Esther replied, “may the king and Haman come today to the banquet I have prepared for the king.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.5', 'BSB', '“Hurry,” commanded the king, “and bring Haman, so we can do as Esther has requested.” So the king and Haman went to the banquet that Esther had prepared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.6', 'BSB', 'And as they drank their wine, the king said to Esther, “What is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.7', 'BSB', 'Esther replied, “This is my petition and my request:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.8', 'BSB', 'If I have found favor in the sight of the king, and if it pleases the king to grant my petition and fulfill my request, may the king and Haman come tomorrow to the banquet I will prepare for them. Then I will answer the king’s question.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.9', 'BSB', 'That day Haman went out full of joy and glad of heart. At the king’s gate, however, he saw Mordecai, who did not rise or tremble in fear at his presence. And Haman was filled with rage toward Mordecai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.10', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, Haman restrained himself and went home. And calling for his friends and his wife Zeresh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.11', 'BSB', 'Haman recounted to them his glorious wealth, his many sons, and all the ways the king had honored and promoted him over the other officials and servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.12', 'BSB', '“What is more,” Haman added, “Queen Esther invited no one but me to join the king at the banquet she prepared, and I am invited back tomorrow along with the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.13', 'BSB', 'Yet none of this satisfies me as long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.5.14', 'BSB', 'His wife Zeresh and all his friends told him, “Have them build a gallows fifty cubits high, and ask the king in the morning to have Mordecai hanged on it. Then go to the banquet with the king and enjoy yourself.” The advice pleased Haman, and he had the gallows constructed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.1', 'BSB', 'That night sleep escaped the king; so he ordered the Book of Records, the Chronicles, to be brought in and read to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.2', 'BSB', 'And there it was found recorded that Mordecai had exposed Bigthana and Teresh, two of the eunuchs who guarded the king’s entrance, when they had conspired to assassinate King Xerxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.3', 'BSB', 'The king inquired, “What honor or dignity has been bestowed on Mordecai for this act?” “Nothing has been done for him,” replied the king’s attendants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.4', 'BSB', '“Who is in the court?” the king asked. Now Haman had just entered the outer court of the palace to ask the king to hang Mordecai on the gallows he had prepared for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.5', 'BSB', 'So the king’s attendants answered him, “Haman is there, standing in the court.” “Bring him in,” ordered the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.6', 'BSB', 'Haman entered, and the king asked him, “What should be done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor?” Now Haman thought to himself, “Whom would the king be delighted to honor more than me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.7', 'BSB', 'And Haman told the king, “For the man whom the king is delighted to honor,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.8', 'BSB', 'have them bring a royal robe that the king himself has worn and a horse on which the king himself has ridden—one with a royal crest placed on its head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.9', 'BSB', 'Let the robe and the horse be entrusted to one of the king’s most noble princes. Let them array the man the king wants to honor and parade him on the horse through the city square, proclaiming before him, ‘This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.10', 'BSB', '“Hurry,” said the king to Haman, “and do just as you proposed. Take the robe and the horse to Mordecai the Jew, who is sitting at the king’s gate. Do not neglect anything that you have suggested.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.11', 'BSB', 'So Haman took the robe and the horse, arrayed Mordecai, and paraded him through the city square, crying out before him, “This is what is done for the man whom the king is delighted to honor!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.12', 'BSB', 'Then Mordecai returned to the king’s gate. But Haman rushed home, with his head covered in grief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.13', 'BSB', 'Haman told his wife Zeresh and all his friends everything that had happened. His advisers and his wife Zeresh said to him, “Since Mordecai, before whom your downfall has begun, is Jewish, you will not prevail against him—for surely you will fall before him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.6.14', 'BSB', 'While they were still speaking with Haman, the king’s eunuchs arrived and rushed him to the banquet that Esther had prepared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.1', 'BSB', 'So the king and Haman went to dine with Esther the queen,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.2', 'BSB', 'and as they drank their wine on that second day, the king asked once more, “Queen Esther, what is your petition? It will be given to you. What is your request? Even up to half the kingdom, it will be fulfilled.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.3', 'BSB', 'Queen Esther replied, “If I have found favor in your sight, O king, and if it pleases the king, grant me my life as my petition, and the lives of my people as my request.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.4', 'BSB', 'For my people and I have been sold out to destruction, death, and annihilation. If we had merely been sold as menservants and maidservants, I would have remained silent, because no such distress would justify burdening the king.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.5', 'BSB', 'Then King Xerxes spoke up and asked Queen Esther, “Who is this, and where is the one who would devise such a scheme?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.6', 'BSB', 'Esther replied, “The adversary and enemy is this wicked man—Haman!” And Haman stood in terror before the king and queen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.7', 'BSB', 'In his fury, the king arose from drinking his wine and went to the palace garden, while Haman stayed behind to beg Queen Esther for his life, for he realized that the king was planning a terrible fate for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.8', 'BSB', 'Just as the king returned from the palace garden to the banquet hall, Haman was falling on the couch where Esther was reclining. The king exclaimed, “Would he actually assault the queen while I am in the palace?” As soon as the words had left the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.9', 'BSB', 'Then Harbonah, one of the eunuchs attending the king, said: “There is a gallows fifty cubits high at Haman’s house. He had it built for Mordecai, who gave the report that saved the king.” “Hang him on it!” declared the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.7.10', 'BSB', 'So they hanged Haman on the gallows he had prepared for Mordecai. Then the fury of the king subsided.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.1', 'BSB', 'That same day King Xerxes awarded Queen Esther the estate of Haman, the enemy of the Jews. And Mordecai entered the king’s presence because Esther had revealed his relation to her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.2', 'BSB', 'The king removed the signet ring he had recovered from Haman and presented it to Mordecai. And Esther appointed Mordecai over the estate of Haman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.3', 'BSB', 'And once again, Esther addressed the king. She fell at his feet weeping and begged him to revoke the evil scheme of Haman the Agagite, which he had devised against the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.4', 'BSB', 'The king extended the gold scepter toward Esther, and she arose and stood before the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.5', 'BSB', '“If it pleases the king,” she said, “and if I have found favor in his sight, and the matter seems proper to the king, and I am pleasing in his sight, may an order be written to revoke the letters that the scheming Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, wrote to destroy the Jews in all the king’s provinces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.6', 'BSB', 'For how could I bear to see the disaster that would befall my people? How could I bear to see the destruction of my kindred?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.7', 'BSB', 'So King Xerxes said to Esther the Queen and Mordecai the Jew, “Behold, I have given Haman’s estate to Esther, and he was hanged on the gallows because he attacked the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.8', 'BSB', 'Now you may write in the king’s name as you please regarding the Jews, and seal it with the royal signet ring. For a decree that is written in the name of the king and sealed with the royal signet ring cannot be revoked.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.9', 'BSB', 'At once the royal scribes were summoned, and on the twenty-third day of the third month (the month of Sivan ), they recorded all of Mordecai’s orders to the Jews and to the satraps, governors, and princes of the 127 provinces from India to Cush —writing to each province in its own script, to every people in their own language, and to the Jews in their own script and language.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.10', 'BSB', 'Mordecai wrote in the name of King Xerxes and sealed it with the royal signet ring. He sent the documents by mounted couriers riding on swift horses bred from the royal mares.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.11', 'BSB', 'By these letters the king permitted the Jews in each and every city the right to assemble and defend themselves, to destroy, kill, and annihilate all the forces of any people or province hostile to them, including women and children, and to plunder their possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.12', 'BSB', 'The single day appointed throughout all the provinces of King Xerxes was the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.13', 'BSB', 'A copy of the text of the edict was to be issued in every province and published to all the people, so that the Jews would be ready on that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.14', 'BSB', 'The couriers rode out in haste on their royal horses, pressed on by the command of the king. And the edict was also issued in the citadel of Susa.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.15', 'BSB', 'Mordecai went out from the presence of the king in royal garments of blue and white, with a large gold crown and a purple robe of fine linen. And the city of Susa shouted and rejoiced.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.16', 'BSB', 'For the Jews it was a time of light and gladness, of joy and honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.8.17', 'BSB', 'In every province and every city, wherever the king’s edict and decree reached, there was joy and gladness among the Jews, with feasting and celebrating. And many of the people of the land themselves became Jews, because the fear of the Jews had fallen upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.1', 'BSB', 'On the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, the month of Adar, the king’s command and edict were to be executed. On this day the enemies of the Jews had hoped to overpower them, but their plan was overturned and the Jews overpowered those who hated them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.2', 'BSB', 'In each of the provinces of King Xerxes, the Jews assembled in their cities to attack those who sought to harm them. No man could withstand them, because the fear of them had fallen upon all peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.3', 'BSB', 'And all the officials of the provinces, the satraps, the governors, and the king’s administrators helped the Jews, because the fear of Mordecai had fallen upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.4', 'BSB', 'For Mordecai exercised great power in the palace, and his fame spread throughout the provinces as he became more and more powerful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.5', 'BSB', 'The Jews put all their enemies to the sword, killing and destroying them, and they did as they pleased to those who hated them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.6', 'BSB', 'In the citadel of Susa, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.7', 'BSB', 'including Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.8', 'BSB', 'Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.9', 'BSB', 'Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vaizatha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.10', 'BSB', 'They killed these ten sons of Haman son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.11', 'BSB', 'On that day the number of those killed in the citadel of Susa was reported to the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.12', 'BSB', 'who said to Queen Esther, “In the citadel of Susa the Jews have killed and destroyed five hundred men, including Haman’s ten sons. What have they done in the rest of the royal provinces? Now what is your petition? It will be given to you. And what further do you request? It will be fulfilled.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.13', 'BSB', 'Esther replied, “If it pleases the king, may the Jews in Susa also have tomorrow to carry out today’s edict, and may the bodies of Haman’s ten sons be hanged on the gallows.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.14', 'BSB', 'So the king commanded that this be done. An edict was issued in Susa, and they hanged the ten sons of Haman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.15', 'BSB', 'On the fourteenth day of the month of Adar, the Jews in Susa came together again and put to death three hundred men there, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.16', 'BSB', 'The rest of the Jews in the royal provinces also assembled to defend themselves and rid themselves of their enemies. They killed 75,000 who hated them, but they did not lay a hand on the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.17', 'BSB', 'This was done on the thirteenth day of the month of Adar, and on the fourteenth day they rested, making it a day of feasting and joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.18', 'BSB', 'The Jews in Susa, however, had assembled on the thirteenth and the fourteenth days of the month. So they rested on the fifteenth day, making it a day of feasting and joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.19', 'BSB', 'This is why the rural Jews, who live in the villages, observe the fourteenth day of the month of Adar as a day of joy and feasting. It is a holiday for sending gifts to one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.20', 'BSB', 'Mordecai recorded these events and sent letters to all the Jews in all the provinces of King Xerxes, both near and far,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.21', 'BSB', 'to establish among them an annual celebration on the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month of Adar', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.22', 'BSB', 'as the days on which the Jews gained rest from their enemies and the month in which their sorrow turned to joy and their mourning into a holiday. He wrote that these were to be days of feasting and joy, of sending gifts to one another and to the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.23', 'BSB', 'So the Jews agreed to continue the custom they had started, as Mordecai had written to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.24', 'BSB', 'For Haman son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had plotted against the Jews to destroy them and had cast the Pur (that is, the lot) to crush and destroy them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.25', 'BSB', 'But when it came before the king, he commanded by letter that the wicked scheme which Haman had devised against the Jews should come back upon his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.26', 'BSB', 'Therefore these days are called Purim, from the word Pur. Because of all the instructions in this letter, and because of all they had seen and experienced,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.27', 'BSB', 'the Jews bound themselves to establish the custom that they and their descendants and all who join them should not fail to celebrate these two days at the appointed time each and every year, according to their regulation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.28', 'BSB', 'These days should be remembered and celebrated by every generation, family, province, and city, so that these days of Purim should not fail to be observed among the Jews, nor should the memory of them fade from their descendants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.29', 'BSB', 'So Queen Esther daughter of Abihail, along with Mordecai the Jew, wrote with full authority to confirm this second letter concerning Purim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.30', 'BSB', 'And Mordecai sent letters with words of peace and truth to all the Jews in the 127 provinces of the kingdom of Xerxes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.31', 'BSB', 'in order to confirm these days of Purim at their appointed time, just as Mordecai the Jew and Queen Esther had established them and had committed themselves and their descendants to the times of fasting and lamentation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.9.32', 'BSB', 'So Esther’s decree confirmed these regulations about Purim, which were written into the record.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.10.1', 'BSB', 'Now King Xerxes imposed tribute throughout the land, even to its farthest shores.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.10.2', 'BSB', 'And all of Mordecai’s powerful and magnificent accomplishments, together with the full account of the greatness to which the king had raised him, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Media and Persia?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Esth.10.3', 'BSB', 'For Mordecai the Jew was second only to King Xerxes, preeminent among the Jews and highly favored by his many kinsmen, seeking the good of his people and speaking peace to all his countrymen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.1', 'BSB', 'There was a man in the land of Uz whose name was Job. And this man was blameless and upright, fearing God and shunning evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.2', 'BSB', 'He had seven sons and three daughters,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.3', 'BSB', 'and he owned 7,000 sheep, 3,000 camels, 500 yoke of oxen, 500 female donkeys, and a very large number of servants. Job was the greatest man of all the people of the East.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.4', 'BSB', 'Job’s sons would take turns holding feasts in their homes, and they would invite their three sisters to eat and drink with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.5', 'BSB', 'And when the days of feasting were over, Job would send for his children to purify them, rising early in the morning to offer burnt offerings for all of them. For Job thought, “Perhaps my children have sinned and cursed God in their hearts.” This was Job’s regular practice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.6', 'BSB', 'One day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.7', 'BSB', '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.8', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.9', 'BSB', 'Satan answered the LORD, “Does Job fear God for nothing?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.10', 'BSB', 'Have You not placed a hedge on every side around him and his household and all that he owns? You have blessed the work of his hands, and his possessions have increased in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.11', 'BSB', 'But stretch out Your hand and strike all that he has, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.12', 'BSB', '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “Everything he has is in your hands, but you must not lay a hand on the man himself.” Then Satan went out from the presence of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.13', 'BSB', 'One day, while Job’s sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.14', 'BSB', 'a messenger came and reported to Job: “While the oxen were plowing and the donkeys were grazing nearby,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.15', 'BSB', 'the Sabeans swooped down and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.16', 'BSB', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The fire of God fell from heaven. It burned and consumed the sheep and the servants, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.17', 'BSB', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “The Chaldeans formed three bands, raided the camels, and took them away. They put the servants to the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.18', 'BSB', 'While he was still speaking, another messenger came and reported: “Your sons and daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother’s house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.19', 'BSB', 'when suddenly a mighty wind swept in from the desert and struck the four corners of the house. It collapsed on the young people and they are dead, and I alone have escaped to tell you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.20', 'BSB', 'Then Job stood up, tore his robe, and shaved his head. He fell to the ground and worshiped,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.21', 'BSB', 'saying: “Naked I came from my mother’s womb, and naked I will return. The LORD gave, and the LORD has taken away. Blessed be the name of the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.1.22', 'BSB', 'In all this, Job did not sin or charge God with wrongdoing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.1', 'BSB', 'On another day the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan also came with them to present himself before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.2', 'BSB', '“Where have you come from?” said the LORD to Satan. “From roaming through the earth,” he replied, “and walking back and forth in it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.3', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Satan, “Have you considered My servant Job? For there is no one on earth like him, a man who is blameless and upright, who fears God and shuns evil. He still retains his integrity, even though you incited Me against him to ruin him without cause.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.4', 'BSB', '“Skin for skin!” Satan replied. “A man will give up all he owns in exchange for his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.5', 'BSB', 'But stretch out Your hand and strike his flesh and bones, and he will surely curse You to Your face.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.6', 'BSB', '“Very well,” said the LORD to Satan. “He is in your hands, but you must spare his life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.7', 'BSB', 'So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD and infected Job with terrible boils from the soles of his feet to the crown of his head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.8', 'BSB', 'And Job took a piece of broken pottery to scrape himself as he sat among the ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.9', 'BSB', 'Then Job’s wife said to him, “Do you still retain your integrity? Curse God and die!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.10', 'BSB', '“You speak as a foolish woman speaks,” he told her. “Should we accept from God only good and not adversity?” In all this, Job did not sin in what he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.11', 'BSB', 'Now when Job’s three friends—Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite—heard about all this adversity that had come upon him, each of them came from his home, and they met together to go and sympathize with Job and comfort him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.12', 'BSB', 'When they lifted up their eyes from afar, they could barely recognize Job. They began to weep aloud, and each man tore his robe and threw dust in the air over his head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.2.13', 'BSB', 'Then they sat on the ground with him for seven days and seven nights, but no one spoke a word to him because they saw how intense his suffering was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.1', 'BSB', 'After this, Job opened his mouth and cursed the day of his birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.2', 'BSB', 'And this is what he said:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.3', 'BSB', '“May the day of my birth perish, and the night it was said, ‘A boy is conceived.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.4', 'BSB', 'If only that day had turned to darkness! May God above disregard it; may no light shine upon it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.5', 'BSB', 'May darkness and gloom reclaim it, and a cloud settle over it; may the blackness of the day overwhelm it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.6', 'BSB', 'If only darkness had taken that night away! May it not appear among the days of the year; may it never be entered in any of the months.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, may that night be barren; may no joyful voice come into it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.8', 'BSB', 'May it be cursed by those who curse the day — those prepared to rouse Leviathan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.9', 'BSB', 'May its morning stars grow dark; may it wait in vain for daylight; may it not see the breaking of dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.10', 'BSB', 'For that night did not shut the doors of the womb to hide the sorrow from my eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.11', 'BSB', 'Why did I not perish at birth; why did I not die as I came from the womb?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.12', 'BSB', 'Why were there knees to receive me, and breasts that I should be nursed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.13', 'BSB', 'For now I would be lying down in peace; I would be asleep and at rest', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.14', 'BSB', 'with kings and counselors of the earth, who built for themselves cities now in ruins,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.15', 'BSB', 'or with princes who had gold, who filled their houses with silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.16', 'BSB', 'Or why was I not hidden like a stillborn child, like an infant who never sees daylight?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.17', 'BSB', 'There the wicked cease from raging, and there the weary find rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.18', 'BSB', 'The captives enjoy their ease; they do not hear the voice of the oppressor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.19', 'BSB', 'Both small and great are there, and the slave is freed from his master.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.20', 'BSB', 'Why is light given to the miserable, and life to the bitter of soul,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.21', 'BSB', 'who long for death that does not come, and search for it like hidden treasure,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.22', 'BSB', 'who rejoice and greatly exult when they can find the grave?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.23', 'BSB', 'Why is life given to a man whose way is hidden, whom God has hedged in?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.24', 'BSB', 'I sigh when food is put before me, and my groans pour out like water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.25', 'BSB', 'For the thing I feared has overtaken me, and what I dreaded has befallen me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.3.26', 'BSB', 'I am not at ease or quiet; I have no rest, for trouble has come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.1', 'BSB', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.2', 'BSB', '“If one ventures a word with you, will you be wearied? Yet who can keep from speaking?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.3', 'BSB', 'Surely you have instructed many, and have strengthened their feeble hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.4', 'BSB', 'Your words have steadied those who stumbled; you have braced the knees that were buckling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.5', 'BSB', 'But now trouble has come upon you, and you are weary. It strikes you, and you are dismayed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.6', 'BSB', 'Is your reverence not your confidence, and the uprightness of your ways your hope?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.7', 'BSB', 'Consider now, I plead: Who, being innocent, has ever perished? Or where have the upright been destroyed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.8', 'BSB', 'As I have observed, those who plow iniquity and those who sow trouble reap the same.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.9', 'BSB', 'By the breath of God they perish, and by the blast of His anger they are consumed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.10', 'BSB', 'The lion may roar, and the fierce lion may growl, yet the teeth of the young lions are broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.11', 'BSB', 'The old lion perishes for lack of prey, and the cubs of the lioness are scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.12', 'BSB', 'Now a word came to me secretly; my ears caught a whisper of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.13', 'BSB', 'In disquieting visions in the night, when deep sleep falls on men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.14', 'BSB', 'fear and trembling came over me and made all my bones shudder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.15', 'BSB', 'Then a spirit glided past my face, and the hair on my body bristled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.16', 'BSB', 'It stood still, but I could not discern its appearance; a form loomed before my eyes, and I heard a whispering voice:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.17', 'BSB', '‘Can a mortal be more righteous than God, or a man more pure than his Maker?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.18', 'BSB', 'If God puts no trust in His servants, and He charges His angels with error,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.19', 'BSB', 'how much more those who dwell in houses of clay, whose foundations are in the dust, who can be crushed like a moth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.20', 'BSB', 'They are smashed to pieces from dawn to dusk; unnoticed, they perish forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.4.21', 'BSB', 'Are not their tent cords pulled up, so that they die without wisdom?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.1', 'BSB', '“Call out if you please, but who will answer? To which of the holy ones will you turn?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.2', 'BSB', 'For resentment kills a fool, and envy slays the simple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.3', 'BSB', 'I have seen a fool taking root, but suddenly his house was cursed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.4', 'BSB', 'His sons are far from safety, crushed in court without a defender.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.5', 'BSB', 'The hungry consume his harvest, taking it even from the thorns, and the thirsty pant after his wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.6', 'BSB', 'For distress does not spring from the dust, and trouble does not sprout from the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.7', 'BSB', 'Yet man is born to trouble as surely as sparks fly upward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.8', 'BSB', 'However, if I were you, I would appeal to God and lay my cause before Him—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.9', 'BSB', 'the One who does great and unsearchable things, wonders without number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.10', 'BSB', 'He gives rain to the earth and sends water upon the fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.11', 'BSB', 'He sets the lowly on high, so that mourners are lifted to safety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.12', 'BSB', 'He thwarts the schemes of the crafty, so that their hands find no success.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.13', 'BSB', 'He catches the wise in their craftiness, and sweeps away the plans of the cunning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.14', 'BSB', 'They encounter darkness by day and grope at noon as in the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.15', 'BSB', 'He saves the needy from the sword in their mouth and from the clutches of the powerful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.16', 'BSB', 'So the poor have hope, and injustice shuts its mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.17', 'BSB', 'Blessed indeed is the man whom God corrects; so do not despise the discipline of the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.18', 'BSB', 'For He wounds, but He also binds; He strikes, but His hands also heal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.19', 'BSB', 'He will rescue you from six calamities; no harm will touch you in seven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.20', 'BSB', 'In famine He will redeem you from death, and in battle from the stroke of the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.21', 'BSB', 'You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue, and will not fear havoc when it comes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.22', 'BSB', 'You will laugh at destruction and famine, and need not fear the beasts of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.23', 'BSB', 'For you will have a covenant with the stones of the field, and the wild animals will be at peace with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.24', 'BSB', 'You will know that your tent is secure, and find nothing amiss when inspecting your home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.25', 'BSB', 'You will know that your offspring will be many, your descendants like the grass of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.26', 'BSB', 'You will come to the grave in full vigor, like a sheaf of grain gathered in season.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.5.27', 'BSB', 'Indeed, we have investigated, and it is true! So hear it and know for yourself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.2', 'BSB', '“If only my grief could be weighed and placed with my calamity on the scales.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.3', 'BSB', 'For then it would outweigh the sand of the seas— no wonder my words have been rash.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.4', 'BSB', 'For the arrows of the Almighty have pierced me; my spirit drinks in their poison; the terrors of God are arrayed against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.5', 'BSB', 'Does a wild donkey bray over fresh grass, or an ox low over its fodder?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.6', 'BSB', 'Is tasteless food eaten without salt, or is there flavor in the white of an egg?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.7', 'BSB', 'My soul refuses to touch them; they are loathsome food to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.8', 'BSB', 'If only my request were granted and God would fulfill my hope:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.9', 'BSB', 'that God would be willing to crush me, to unleash His hand and cut me off!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.10', 'BSB', 'It still brings me comfort, and joy through unrelenting pain, that I have not denied the words of the Holy One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.11', 'BSB', 'What strength do I have, that I should still hope? What is my future, that I should be patient?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.12', 'BSB', 'Is my strength like that of stone, or my flesh made of bronze?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.13', 'BSB', 'Is there any help within me now that success is driven from me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.14', 'BSB', 'A despairing man should have the kindness of his friend, even if he forsakes the fear of the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.15', 'BSB', 'But my brothers are as faithless as wadis, as seasonal streams that overflow,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.16', 'BSB', 'darkened because of the ice and the inflow of melting snow,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.17', 'BSB', 'but ceasing in the dry season and vanishing from their channels in the heat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.18', 'BSB', 'Caravans turn aside from their routes; they go into the wasteland and perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.19', 'BSB', 'The caravans of Tema look for water; the travelers of Sheba hope to find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.20', 'BSB', 'They are confounded because they had hoped; their arrival brings disappointment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.21', 'BSB', 'For now you are of no help; you see terror, and you are afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.22', 'BSB', 'Have I ever said, ‘Give me something; offer me a bribe from your wealth;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.23', 'BSB', 'deliver me from the hand of the enemy; redeem me from the grasp of the ruthless’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.24', 'BSB', 'Teach me, and I will be silent. Help me understand how I have erred.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.25', 'BSB', 'How painful are honest words! But what does your argument prove?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.26', 'BSB', 'Do you intend to correct my words, and treat as wind my cry of despair?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.27', 'BSB', 'You would even cast lots for an orphan and barter away your friend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.28', 'BSB', 'But now, please look at me. Would I lie to your face?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.29', 'BSB', 'Reconsider; do not be unjust. Reconsider, for my righteousness is at stake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.6.30', 'BSB', 'Is there iniquity on my tongue? Can my mouth not discern malice?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.1', 'BSB', '“Is not man consigned to labor on earth? Are not his days like those of a hired hand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.2', 'BSB', 'Like a slave he longs for shade; like a hireling he waits for his wages.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.3', 'BSB', 'So I am allotted months of futility, and nights of misery are appointed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.4', 'BSB', 'When I lie down I think: ‘When will I get up?’ But the night drags on, and I toss and turn until dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.5', 'BSB', 'My flesh is clothed with worms and encrusted with dirt; my skin is cracked and festering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.6', 'BSB', 'My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle; they come to an end without hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.7', 'BSB', 'Remember that my life is but a breath. My eyes will never again see happiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.8', 'BSB', 'The eye that beholds me will no longer see me. You will look for me, but I will be no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.9', 'BSB', 'As a cloud vanishes and is gone, so he who goes down to Sheol does not come back up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.10', 'BSB', 'He never returns to his house; his place remembers him no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will not restrain my mouth; I will speak in the anguish of my spirit; I will complain in the bitterness of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.12', 'BSB', 'Am I the sea, or the monster of the deep, that You must keep me under guard?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.13', 'BSB', 'When I think my bed will comfort me and my couch will ease my complaint,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.14', 'BSB', 'then You frighten me with dreams and terrify me with visions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.15', 'BSB', 'so that I would prefer strangling and death over my life in this body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.16', 'BSB', 'I loathe my life! I would not live forever. Leave me alone, for my days are but a breath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.17', 'BSB', 'What is man that You should exalt him, that You should set Your heart upon him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.18', 'BSB', 'that You attend to him every morning, and test him every moment?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.19', 'BSB', 'Will You never look away from me, or leave me alone to swallow my spittle?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.20', 'BSB', 'If I have sinned, what have I done to You, O watcher of mankind? Why have You made me Your target, so that I am a burden to You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.7.21', 'BSB', 'Why do You not pardon my transgression and take away my iniquity? For soon I will lie down in the dust; You will seek me, but I will be no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.1', 'BSB', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.2', 'BSB', '“How long will you go on saying such things? The words of your mouth are a blustering wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.3', 'BSB', 'Does God pervert justice? Does the Almighty pervert what is right?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.4', 'BSB', 'When your children sinned against Him, He gave them over to their rebellion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.5', 'BSB', 'But if you would earnestly seek God and ask the Almighty for mercy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.6', 'BSB', 'if you are pure and upright, even now He will rouse Himself on your behalf and restore your righteous estate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.7', 'BSB', 'Though your beginnings were modest, your latter days will flourish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.8', 'BSB', 'Please inquire of past generations and consider the discoveries of their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.9', 'BSB', 'For we were born yesterday and know nothing; our days on earth are but a shadow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.10', 'BSB', 'Will they not teach you and tell you, and speak from their understanding?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.11', 'BSB', 'Does papyrus grow where there is no marsh? Do reeds flourish without water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.12', 'BSB', 'While the shoots are still uncut, they dry up quicker than grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.13', 'BSB', 'Such is the destiny of all who forget God; so the hope of the godless will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.14', 'BSB', 'His confidence is fragile; his security is in a spider’s web.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.15', 'BSB', 'He leans on his web, but it gives way; he holds fast, but it does not endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.16', 'BSB', 'He is a well-watered plant in the sunshine, spreading its shoots over the garden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.17', 'BSB', 'His roots wrap around the rock heap; he looks for a home among the stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.18', 'BSB', 'If he is uprooted from his place, it will disown him, saying, ‘I never saw you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.19', 'BSB', 'Surely this is the joy of his way; yet others will spring from the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.20', 'BSB', 'Behold, God does not reject the blameless, nor will He strengthen the hand of evildoers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.21', 'BSB', 'He will yet fill your mouth with laughter, and your lips with a shout of joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.8.22', 'BSB', 'Your enemies will be clothed in shame, and the tent of the wicked will be no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.2', 'BSB', '“Yes, I know that it is so, but how can a mortal be righteous before God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.3', 'BSB', 'If one wished to contend with God, he could not answer Him one time out of a thousand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.4', 'BSB', 'God is wise in heart and mighty in strength. Who has resisted Him and prospered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.5', 'BSB', 'He moves mountains without their knowledge and overturns them in His anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.6', 'BSB', 'He shakes the earth from its place, so that its foundations tremble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.7', 'BSB', 'He commands the sun not to shine; He seals off the stars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.8', 'BSB', 'He alone stretches out the heavens and treads on the waves of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.9', 'BSB', 'He is the Maker of the Bear and Orion, of the Pleiades and the constellations of the south.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.10', 'BSB', 'He does great things beyond searching out, and wonders without number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.11', 'BSB', 'Were He to pass by me, I would not see Him; were He to move, I would not recognize Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.12', 'BSB', 'If He takes away, who can stop Him? Who dares to ask Him, ‘What are You doing?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.13', 'BSB', 'God does not restrain His anger; the helpers of Rahab cower beneath Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.14', 'BSB', 'How then can I answer Him or choose my arguments against Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.15', 'BSB', 'For even if I were right, I could not answer. I could only beg my Judge for mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.16', 'BSB', 'If I summoned Him and He answered me, I do not believe He would listen to my voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.17', 'BSB', 'For He would crush me with a tempest and multiply my wounds without cause.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.18', 'BSB', 'He does not let me catch my breath, but overwhelms me with bitterness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.19', 'BSB', 'If it is a matter of strength, He is indeed mighty! If it is a matter of justice, who can summon Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.20', 'BSB', 'Even if I were righteous, my mouth would condemn me; if I were blameless, it would declare me guilty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.21', 'BSB', 'Though I am blameless, I have no concern for myself; I despise my own life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.22', 'BSB', 'It is all the same, and so I say, ‘He destroys both the blameless and the wicked.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.23', 'BSB', 'When the scourge brings sudden death, He mocks the despair of the innocent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.24', 'BSB', 'The earth is given into the hand of the wicked; He blindfolds its judges. If it is not He, then who is it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.25', 'BSB', 'My days are swifter than a runner; they flee without seeing good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.26', 'BSB', 'They sweep by like boats of papyrus, like an eagle swooping down on its prey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.27', 'BSB', 'If I were to say, ‘I will forget my complaint and change my expression and smile,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.28', 'BSB', 'I would still dread all my sufferings; I know that You will not acquit me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.29', 'BSB', 'Since I am already found guilty, why should I labor in vain?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.30', 'BSB', 'If I should wash myself with snow and cleanse my hands with lye,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.31', 'BSB', 'then You would plunge me into the pit, and even my own clothes would despise me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.32', 'BSB', 'For He is not a man like me, that I can answer Him, that we can take each other to court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.33', 'BSB', 'Nor is there a mediator between us, to lay his hand upon us both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.34', 'BSB', 'Let Him remove His rod from me, so that His terror will no longer frighten me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.9.35', 'BSB', 'Then I would speak without fear of Him. But as it is, I am on my own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.1', 'BSB', '“I loathe my own life; I will express my complaint and speak in the bitterness of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.2', 'BSB', 'I will say to God: Do not condemn me! Let me know why You prosecute me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.3', 'BSB', 'Does it please You to oppress me, to reject the work of Your hands and favor the schemes of the wicked?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.4', 'BSB', 'Do You have eyes of flesh? Do You see as man sees?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.5', 'BSB', 'Are Your days like those of a mortal, or Your years like those of a man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.6', 'BSB', 'that You should seek my iniquity and search out my sin—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.7', 'BSB', 'though You know that I am not guilty, and there is no deliverance from Your hand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.8', 'BSB', 'Your hands shaped me and altogether formed me. Would You now turn and destroy me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.9', 'BSB', 'Please remember that You molded me like clay. Would You now return me to dust?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.10', 'BSB', 'Did You not pour me out like milk, and curdle me like cheese?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.11', 'BSB', 'You clothed me with skin and flesh, and knit me together with bones and sinews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.12', 'BSB', 'You have granted me life and loving devotion, and Your care has preserved my spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.13', 'BSB', 'Yet You concealed these things in Your heart, and I know that this was in Your mind:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.14', 'BSB', 'If I sinned, You would take note, and would not acquit me of my iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.15', 'BSB', 'If I am guilty, woe to me! And even if I am righteous, I cannot lift my head. I am full of shame and aware of my affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.16', 'BSB', 'Should I hold my head high, You would hunt me like a lion, and again display Your power against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.17', 'BSB', 'You produce new witnesses against me and multiply Your anger toward me. Hardships assault me in wave after wave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.18', 'BSB', 'Why then did You bring me from the womb? Oh, that I had died, and no eye had seen me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.19', 'BSB', 'If only I had never come to be, but had been carried from the womb to the grave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.20', 'BSB', 'Are my days not few? Withdraw from me, that I may have a little comfort,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.21', 'BSB', 'before I go—never to return— to a land of darkness and gloom,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.10.22', 'BSB', 'to a land of utter darkness, of deep shadow and disorder, where even the light is like darkness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.1', 'BSB', 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.2', 'BSB', '“Should this stream of words go unanswered and such a speaker be vindicated?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.3', 'BSB', 'Should your babbling put others to silence? Will you scoff without rebuke?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.4', 'BSB', 'You have said, ‘My doctrine is sound, and I am pure in Your sight.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.5', 'BSB', 'But if only God would speak and open His lips against you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.6', 'BSB', 'and disclose to you the secrets of wisdom, for true wisdom has two sides. Know then that God exacts from you less than your iniquity deserves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.7', 'BSB', 'Can you fathom the deep things of God or discover the limits of the Almighty?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.8', 'BSB', 'They are higher than the heavens—what can you do? They are deeper than Sheol—what can you know?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.9', 'BSB', 'Their measure is longer than the earth and wider than the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.10', 'BSB', 'If He comes along to imprison you, or convenes a court, who can stop Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.11', 'BSB', 'Surely He knows the deceit of men. If He sees iniquity, does He not take note?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.12', 'BSB', 'But a witless man can no more become wise than the colt of a wild donkey can be born a man!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.13', 'BSB', 'As for you, if you direct your heart and lift up your hands to Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.14', 'BSB', 'if you put away the iniquity in your hand, and allow no injustice to dwell in your tents,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.15', 'BSB', 'then indeed you will lift up your face without shame; you will stand firm and unafraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.16', 'BSB', 'For you will forget your misery, recalling it only as waters gone by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.17', 'BSB', 'Your life will be brighter than noonday; its darkness will be like the morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.18', 'BSB', 'You will be secure, because there is hope, and you will look around and lie down in safety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.19', 'BSB', 'You will lie down without fear, and many will court your favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.11.20', 'BSB', 'But the eyes of the wicked will fail, and escape will elude them; they will hope for their last breath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.2', 'BSB', '“Truly then you are the people with whom wisdom itself will die!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.3', 'BSB', 'But I also have a mind; I am not inferior to you. Who does not know such things as these?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.4', 'BSB', 'I am a laughingstock to my friends, though I called on God, and He answered. The righteous and upright man is a laughingstock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.5', 'BSB', 'The one at ease scorns misfortune as the fate of those whose feet are slipping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.6', 'BSB', 'The tents of robbers are safe, and those who provoke God are secure— those who carry their god in their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.7', 'BSB', 'But ask the animals, and they will instruct you; ask the birds of the air, and they will tell you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.8', 'BSB', 'Or speak to the earth, and it will teach you; let the fish of the sea inform you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.9', 'BSB', 'Which of all these does not know that the hand of the LORD has done this?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.10', 'BSB', 'The life of every living thing is in His hand, as well as the breath of all mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.11', 'BSB', 'Does not the ear test words as the tongue tastes its food?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.12', 'BSB', 'Wisdom is found with the elderly, and understanding comes with long life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.13', 'BSB', 'Wisdom and strength belong to God; counsel and understanding are His.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.14', 'BSB', 'What He tears down cannot be rebuilt; the man He imprisons cannot be released.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.15', 'BSB', 'If He holds back the waters, they dry up, and if He releases them, they overwhelm the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.16', 'BSB', 'True wisdom and power belong to Him. The deceived and the deceiver are His.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.17', 'BSB', 'He leads counselors away barefoot and makes fools of judges.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.18', 'BSB', 'He loosens the bonds placed by kings and fastens a belt around their waists.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.19', 'BSB', 'He leads priests away barefoot and overthrows the established.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.20', 'BSB', 'He deprives the trusted of speech and takes away the discernment of elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.21', 'BSB', 'He pours out contempt on nobles and disarms the mighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.22', 'BSB', 'He reveals the deep things of darkness and brings deep shadows into light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.23', 'BSB', 'He makes nations great and destroys them; He enlarges nations, then disperses them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.24', 'BSB', 'He deprives the earth’s leaders of reason and makes them wander in a trackless wasteland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.12.25', 'BSB', 'They grope in the darkness without light; He makes them stagger like drunkards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.1', 'BSB', '“Indeed, my eyes have seen all this; my ears have heard and understood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.2', 'BSB', 'What you know, I also know; I am not inferior to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.3', 'BSB', 'Yet I desire to speak to the Almighty and argue my case before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.4', 'BSB', 'You, however, smear with lies; you are all worthless physicians.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.5', 'BSB', 'If only you would remain silent; for that would be your wisdom!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.6', 'BSB', 'Hear now my argument, and listen to the plea of my lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.7', 'BSB', 'Will you speak wickedly on God’s behalf or speak deceitfully for Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.8', 'BSB', 'Would you show Him partiality or argue in His defense?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.9', 'BSB', 'Would it be well when He examined you? Could you deceive Him like a man?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.10', 'BSB', 'Surely He would rebuke you if you secretly showed partiality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.11', 'BSB', 'Would His majesty not terrify you? Would the dread of Him not fall upon you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.12', 'BSB', 'Your maxims are proverbs of ashes; your defenses are defenses of clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.13', 'BSB', 'Be silent, and I will speak. Then let come to me what may.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.14', 'BSB', 'Why do I put myself at risk and take my life in my own hands?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.15', 'BSB', 'Though He slay me, I will hope in Him. I will still defend my ways to His face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.16', 'BSB', 'Moreover, this will be my salvation, for no godless man can appear before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.17', 'BSB', 'Listen carefully to my words; let my declaration ring in your ears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.18', 'BSB', 'Behold, now that I have prepared my case, I know that I will be vindicated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.19', 'BSB', 'Can anyone indict me? If so, I will be silent and die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.20', 'BSB', 'Only grant these two things to me, so that I need not hide from You:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.21', 'BSB', 'Withdraw Your hand from me, and do not let Your terror frighten me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.22', 'BSB', 'Then call me, and I will answer, or let me speak, and You can reply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.23', 'BSB', 'How many are my iniquities and sins? Reveal to me my transgression and sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.24', 'BSB', 'Why do You hide Your face and consider me as Your enemy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.25', 'BSB', 'Would You frighten a windblown leaf? Would You chase after dry chaff?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.26', 'BSB', 'For You record bitter accusations against me and bequeath to me the iniquities of my youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.27', 'BSB', 'You put my feet in the stocks and stand watch over all my paths; You set a limit for the soles of my feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.13.28', 'BSB', 'So man wastes away like something rotten, like a moth-eaten garment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.1', 'BSB', '“Man, who is born of woman, is short of days and full of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.2', 'BSB', 'Like a flower, he comes forth, then withers away; like a fleeting shadow, he does not endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.3', 'BSB', 'Do You open Your eyes to one like this? Will You bring him into judgment before You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.4', 'BSB', 'Who can bring out clean from unclean? No one!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.5', 'BSB', 'Since his days are determined and the number of his months is with You, and since You have set limits that he cannot exceed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.6', 'BSB', 'look away from him and let him rest, so he can enjoy his day as a hired hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.7', 'BSB', 'For there is hope for a tree: If it is cut down, it will sprout again, and its tender shoots will not fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.8', 'BSB', 'If its roots grow old in the ground and its stump dies in the soil,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.9', 'BSB', 'at the scent of water it will bud and put forth twigs like a sapling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.10', 'BSB', 'But a man dies and is laid low; he breathes his last, and where is he?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.11', 'BSB', 'As water disappears from the sea and a river becomes parched and dry,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.12', 'BSB', 'so a man lies down and does not rise. Until the heavens are no more, he will not be awakened or roused from sleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.13', 'BSB', 'If only You would hide me in Sheol and conceal me until Your anger has passed! If only You would appoint a time for me and then remember me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.14', 'BSB', 'When a man dies, will he live again? All the days of my hard service I will wait, until my renewal comes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.15', 'BSB', 'You will call, and I will answer; You will desire the work of Your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.16', 'BSB', 'For then You would count my steps, but would not keep track of my sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.17', 'BSB', 'My transgression would be sealed in a bag, and You would cover over my iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.18', 'BSB', 'But as a mountain erodes and crumbles and a rock is dislodged from its place,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.19', 'BSB', 'as water wears away the stones and torrents wash away the soil, so You destroy a man’s hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.20', 'BSB', 'You forever overpower him, and he passes on; You change his countenance and send him away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.21', 'BSB', 'If his sons receive honor, he does not know it; if they are brought low, he is unaware.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.14.22', 'BSB', 'He feels only the pain of his own body and mourns only for himself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.2', 'BSB', '“Does a wise man answer with empty counsel or fill his belly with the hot east wind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.3', 'BSB', 'Should he argue with useless words or speeches that serve no purpose?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.4', 'BSB', 'But you even undermine the fear of God and hinder meditation before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.5', 'BSB', 'For your iniquity instructs your mouth, and you choose the language of the crafty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.6', 'BSB', 'Your own mouth, not mine, condemns you; your own lips testify against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.7', 'BSB', 'Were you the first man ever born? Were you brought forth before the hills?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.8', 'BSB', 'Do you listen in on the council of God or limit wisdom to yourself?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.9', 'BSB', 'What do you know that we do not? What do you understand that is not clear to us?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.10', 'BSB', 'Both the gray-haired and the aged are on our side— men much older than your father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.11', 'BSB', 'Are the consolations of God not enough for you, even words spoken gently to you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.12', 'BSB', 'Why has your heart carried you away, and why do your eyes flash,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.13', 'BSB', 'as you turn your spirit against God and pour such words from your mouth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.14', 'BSB', 'What is man, that he should be pure, or one born of woman, that he should be righteous?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.15', 'BSB', 'If God puts no trust in His holy ones, if even the heavens are not pure in His eyes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.16', 'BSB', 'how much less man, who is vile and corrupt, who drinks injustice like water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.17', 'BSB', 'Listen to me and I will inform you. I will describe what I have seen,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.18', 'BSB', 'what was declared by wise men and was not concealed from their fathers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.19', 'BSB', 'to whom alone the land was given when no foreigner passed among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.20', 'BSB', 'A wicked man writhes in pain all his days; only a few years are reserved for the ruthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.21', 'BSB', 'Sounds of terror fill his ears; in his prosperity the destroyer attacks him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.22', 'BSB', 'He despairs of his return from darkness; he is marked for the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.23', 'BSB', 'He wanders about as food for vultures; he knows the day of darkness is at hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.24', 'BSB', 'Distress and anguish terrify him, overwhelming him like a king poised to attack.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.25', 'BSB', 'For he has stretched out his hand against God and has vaunted himself against the Almighty,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.26', 'BSB', 'rushing headlong at Him with a thick, studded shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.27', 'BSB', 'Though his face is covered with fat and his waistline bulges with flesh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.28', 'BSB', 'he will dwell in ruined cities, in abandoned houses destined to become rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.29', 'BSB', 'He will no longer be rich; his wealth will not endure. His possessions will not overspread the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.30', 'BSB', 'He will not escape from the darkness; the flame will wither his shoots, and the breath of God’s mouth will carry him away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.31', 'BSB', 'Let him not deceive himself with trust in emptiness, for emptiness will be his reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.32', 'BSB', 'It will be paid in full before his time, and his branch will not flourish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.33', 'BSB', 'He will be like a vine stripped of its unripe grapes, like an olive tree that sheds its blossoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.34', 'BSB', 'For the company of the godless will be barren, and fire will consume the tents of bribery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.15.35', 'BSB', 'They conceive trouble and give birth to evil; their womb is pregnant with deceit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.2', 'BSB', '“I have heard many things like these; miserable comforters are you all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.3', 'BSB', 'Is there no end to your long-winded speeches? What provokes you to continue testifying?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.4', 'BSB', 'I could also speak like you if you were in my place; I could heap up words against you and shake my head at you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.5', 'BSB', 'But I would encourage you with my mouth, and the consolation of my lips would bring relief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.6', 'BSB', 'Even if I speak, my pain is not relieved, and if I hold back, how will it go away?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.7', 'BSB', 'Surely He has now exhausted me; You have devastated all my family.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.8', 'BSB', 'You have bound me, and it has become a witness; my frailty rises up and testifies against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.9', 'BSB', 'His anger has torn me and opposed me; He gnashes His teeth at me. My adversary pierces me with His eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.10', 'BSB', 'They open their mouths against me and strike my cheeks with contempt; they join together against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.11', 'BSB', 'God has delivered me to unjust men; He has thrown me to the clutches of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.12', 'BSB', 'I was at ease, but He shattered me; He seized me by the neck and crushed me. He has set me up as His target;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.13', 'BSB', 'His archers surround me. He pierces my kidneys without mercy and spills my gall on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.14', 'BSB', 'He breaks me with wound upon wound; He rushes me like a mighty warrior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.15', 'BSB', 'I have sewn sackcloth over my skin; I have buried my horn in the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.16', 'BSB', 'My face is red with weeping, and deep shadows ring my eyes;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.17', 'BSB', 'yet my hands are free of violence and my prayer is pure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.18', 'BSB', 'O earth, do not cover my blood; may my cry for help never be laid to rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.19', 'BSB', 'Even now my witness is in heaven, and my advocate is on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.20', 'BSB', 'My friends are my scoffers as my eyes pour out tears to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.21', 'BSB', 'Oh, that a man might plead with God as he pleads with his neighbor!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.16.22', 'BSB', 'For when only a few years are past I will go the way of no return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.1', 'BSB', '“My spirit is broken; my days are extinguished; the grave awaits me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.2', 'BSB', 'Surely mockers surround me, and my eyes must gaze at their rebellion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.3', 'BSB', 'Give me, I pray, the pledge You demand. Who else will be my guarantor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.4', 'BSB', 'You have closed their minds to understanding; therefore You will not exalt them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.5', 'BSB', 'If a man denounces his friends for a price, the eyes of his children will fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.6', 'BSB', 'He has made me a byword among the people, a man in whose face they spit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.7', 'BSB', 'My eyes have grown dim with grief, and my whole body is but a shadow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.8', 'BSB', 'The upright are appalled at this, and the innocent are stirred against the godless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.9', 'BSB', 'Yet a righteous one holds to his way, and the one with clean hands grows stronger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.10', 'BSB', 'But come back and try again, all of you. For I will not find a wise man among you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.11', 'BSB', 'My days have passed; my plans are broken off— even the desires of my heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.12', 'BSB', 'They have turned night into day, making light seem near in the face of darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.13', 'BSB', 'If I look for Sheol as my home, if I spread out my bed in darkness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.14', 'BSB', 'and say to corruption, ‘You are my father,’ and to the worm, ‘My mother,’ or ‘My sister,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.15', 'BSB', 'where then is my hope? Who can see any hope for me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.17.16', 'BSB', 'Will it go down to the gates of Sheol? Will we go down together into the dust?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.1', 'BSB', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.2', 'BSB', '“How long until you end these speeches? Show some sense, and then we can talk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.3', 'BSB', 'Why are we regarded as cattle, as stupid in your sight?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.4', 'BSB', 'You who tear yourself in anger— should the earth be forsaken on your account, or the rocks be moved from their place?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.5', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the lamp of the wicked is extinguished; the flame of his fire does not glow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.6', 'BSB', 'The light in his tent grows dark, and the lamp beside him goes out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.7', 'BSB', 'His vigorous stride is shortened, and his own schemes trip him up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.8', 'BSB', 'For his own feet lead him into a net, and he wanders into its mesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.9', 'BSB', 'A trap seizes his heel; a snare grips him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.10', 'BSB', 'A noose is hidden in the ground, and a trap lies in his path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.11', 'BSB', 'Terrors frighten him on every side and harass his every step.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.12', 'BSB', 'His strength is depleted, and calamity is ready at his side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.13', 'BSB', 'It devours patches of his skin; the firstborn of death devours his limbs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.14', 'BSB', 'He is torn from the shelter of his tent and is marched off to the king of terrors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.15', 'BSB', 'Fire resides in his tent; burning sulfur rains down on his dwelling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.16', 'BSB', 'The roots beneath him dry up, and the branches above him wither away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.17', 'BSB', 'The memory of him perishes from the earth, and he has no name in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.18', 'BSB', 'He is driven from light into darkness and is chased from the inhabited world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.19', 'BSB', 'He has no offspring or posterity among his people, no survivor where he once lived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.20', 'BSB', 'Those in the west are appalled at his fate, while those in the east tremble in horror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.18.21', 'BSB', 'Surely such is the dwelling of the wicked and the place of one who does not know God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.2', 'BSB', '“How long will you torment me and crush me with your words?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.3', 'BSB', 'Ten times now you have reproached me; you shamelessly mistreat me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.4', 'BSB', 'Even if I have truly gone astray, my error concerns me alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.5', 'BSB', 'If indeed you would exalt yourselves above me and use my disgrace against me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.6', 'BSB', 'then understand that it is God who has wronged me and drawn His net around me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.7', 'BSB', 'Though I cry out, ‘Violence!’ I get no response; though I call for help, there is no justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.8', 'BSB', 'He has blocked my way so I cannot pass; He has veiled my paths with darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.9', 'BSB', 'He has stripped me of my honor and removed the crown from my head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.10', 'BSB', 'He tears me down on every side until I am gone; He uproots my hope like a tree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.11', 'BSB', 'His anger burns against me, and He counts me among His enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.12', 'BSB', 'His troops advance together; they construct a ramp against me and encamp around my tent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.13', 'BSB', 'He has removed my brothers from me; my acquaintances have abandoned me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.14', 'BSB', 'My kinsmen have failed me, and my friends have forgotten me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.15', 'BSB', 'My guests and maidservants count me as a stranger; I am a foreigner in their sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.16', 'BSB', 'I call for my servant, but he does not answer, though I implore him with my own mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.17', 'BSB', 'My breath is repulsive to my wife, and I am loathsome to my own family.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.18', 'BSB', 'Even little boys scorn me; when I appear, they deride me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.19', 'BSB', 'All my best friends despise me, and those I love have turned against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.20', 'BSB', 'My skin and flesh cling to my bones; I have escaped by the skin of my teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.21', 'BSB', 'Have pity on me, my friends, have pity, for the hand of God has struck me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.22', 'BSB', 'Why do you persecute me as God does? Will you never get enough of my flesh?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.23', 'BSB', 'I wish that my words were recorded and inscribed in a book,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.24', 'BSB', 'by an iron stylus on lead, or chiseled in stone forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.25', 'BSB', 'But I know that my Redeemer lives, and in the end He will stand upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.26', 'BSB', 'Even after my skin has been destroyed, yet in my flesh I will see God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.27', 'BSB', 'I will see Him for myself; my eyes will behold Him, and not as a stranger. How my heart yearns within me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.28', 'BSB', 'If you say, ‘Let us persecute him, since the root of the matter lies with him,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.19.29', 'BSB', 'then you should fear the sword yourselves, because wrath brings punishment by the sword, so that you may know there is a judgment.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.1', 'BSB', 'Then Zophar the Naamathite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.2', 'BSB', '“So my anxious thoughts compel me to answer, because of the turmoil within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.3', 'BSB', 'I have heard a rebuke that insults me, and my understanding prompts a reply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.4', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that from antiquity, since man was placed on the earth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.5', 'BSB', 'the triumph of the wicked has been brief and the joy of the godless momentary?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.6', 'BSB', 'Though his arrogance reaches the heavens, and his head touches the clouds,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.7', 'BSB', 'he will perish forever, like his own dung; those who had seen him will ask, ‘Where is he?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.8', 'BSB', 'He will fly away like a dream, never to be found; he will be chased away like a vision in the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.9', 'BSB', 'The eye that saw him will see him no more, and his place will no longer behold him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.10', 'BSB', 'His sons will seek the favor of the poor, for his own hands must return his wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.11', 'BSB', 'The youthful vigor that fills his bones will lie down with him in the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.12', 'BSB', 'Though evil is sweet in his mouth and he conceals it under his tongue,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.13', 'BSB', 'though he cannot bear to let it go and keeps it in his mouth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.14', 'BSB', 'yet in his stomach his food sours into the venom of cobras within him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.15', 'BSB', 'He swallows wealth but vomits it out; God will force it from his stomach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.16', 'BSB', 'He will suck the poison of cobras; the fangs of a viper will kill him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.17', 'BSB', 'He will not enjoy the streams, the rivers flowing with honey and cream.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.18', 'BSB', 'He must return the fruit of his labor without consuming it; he cannot enjoy the profits of his trading.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.19', 'BSB', 'For he has oppressed and forsaken the poor; he has seized houses he did not build.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.20', 'BSB', 'Because his appetite is never satisfied, he cannot escape with his treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.21', 'BSB', 'Nothing is left for him to consume; thus his prosperity will not endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.22', 'BSB', 'In the midst of his plenty, he will be distressed; the full force of misery will come upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.23', 'BSB', 'When he has filled his stomach, God will vent His fury upon him, raining it down on him as he eats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.24', 'BSB', 'Though he flees from an iron weapon, a bronze-tipped arrow will pierce him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.25', 'BSB', 'It is drawn out of his back, the gleaming point from his liver. Terrors come over him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.26', 'BSB', 'Total darkness is reserved for his treasures. A fire unfanned will consume him and devour what is left in his tent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.27', 'BSB', 'The heavens will expose his iniquity, and the earth will rise up against him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.28', 'BSB', 'The possessions of his house will be removed, flowing away on the day of God’s wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.20.29', 'BSB', 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God, the inheritance God has appointed him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.2', 'BSB', '“Listen carefully to my words; let this be your consolation to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.3', 'BSB', 'Bear with me while I speak; then, after I have spoken, you may go on mocking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.4', 'BSB', 'Is my complaint against a man? Then why should I not be impatient?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.5', 'BSB', 'Look at me and be appalled; put your hand over your mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.6', 'BSB', 'When I remember, terror takes hold, and my body trembles in horror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.7', 'BSB', 'Why do the wicked live on, growing old and increasing in power?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.8', 'BSB', 'Their descendants are established around them, and their offspring before their eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.9', 'BSB', 'Their homes are safe from fear; no rod of punishment from God is upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.10', 'BSB', 'Their bulls breed without fail; their cows bear calves and do not miscarry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.11', 'BSB', 'They send forth their little ones like a flock; their children skip about,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.12', 'BSB', 'singing to the tambourine and lyre and making merry at the sound of the flute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.13', 'BSB', 'They spend their days in prosperity and go down to Sheol in peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.14', 'BSB', 'Yet they say to God: ‘Leave us alone! For we have no desire to know Your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.15', 'BSB', 'Who is the Almighty, that we should serve Him, and what would we gain if we pray to Him?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.16', 'BSB', 'Still, their prosperity is not in their own hands, so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.17', 'BSB', 'How often is the lamp of the wicked put out? Does disaster come upon them? Does God, in His anger, apportion destruction?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.18', 'BSB', 'Are they like straw before the wind, like chaff swept away by a storm?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.19', 'BSB', 'It is said that God lays up one’s punishment for his children. Let God repay the man himself, so he will know it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.20', 'BSB', 'Let his eyes see his own destruction; let him drink for himself the wrath of the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.21', 'BSB', 'For what does he care about his household after him, when the number of his months has run out?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.22', 'BSB', 'Can anyone teach knowledge to God, since He judges those on high?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.23', 'BSB', 'One man dies full of vigor, completely secure and at ease.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.24', 'BSB', 'His body is well nourished, and his bones are rich with marrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.25', 'BSB', 'Yet another man dies in the bitterness of his soul, having never tasted prosperity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.26', 'BSB', 'But together they lie down in the dust, and worms cover them both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.27', 'BSB', 'Behold, I know your thoughts full well, the schemes by which you would wrong me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.28', 'BSB', 'For you say, ‘Where now is the nobleman’s house, and where are the tents in which the wicked dwell?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.29', 'BSB', 'Have you never asked those who travel the roads? Do you not accept their reports?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.30', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the evil man is spared from the day of calamity, delivered from the day of wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.31', 'BSB', 'Who denounces his behavior to his face? Who repays him for what he has done?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.32', 'BSB', 'He is carried to the grave, and watch is kept over his tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.33', 'BSB', 'The clods of the valley are sweet to him; everyone follows behind him, and those before him are without number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.21.34', 'BSB', 'So how can you comfort me with empty words? For your answers remain full of falsehood.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.1', 'BSB', 'Then Eliphaz the Temanite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.2', 'BSB', '“Can a man be of use to God? Can even a wise man benefit Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.3', 'BSB', 'Does it delight the Almighty that you are righteous? Does He profit if your ways are blameless?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.4', 'BSB', 'Is it for your reverence that He rebukes you and enters into judgment against you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.5', 'BSB', 'Is not your wickedness great? Are not your iniquities endless?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.6', 'BSB', 'For you needlessly demanded security from your brothers and deprived the naked of their clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.7', 'BSB', 'You gave no water to the weary and withheld food from the famished,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.8', 'BSB', 'while the land belonged to a mighty man, and a man of honor lived on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.9', 'BSB', 'You sent widows away empty-handed, and the strength of the fatherless was crushed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore snares surround you, and sudden peril terrifies you;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.11', 'BSB', 'it is so dark you cannot see, and a flood of water covers you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.12', 'BSB', 'Is not God as high as the heavens? Look at the highest stars, how lofty they are!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.13', 'BSB', 'Yet you say: ‘What does God know? Does He judge through thick darkness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.14', 'BSB', 'Thick clouds veil Him so He does not see us as He traverses the vault of heaven.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.15', 'BSB', 'Will you stay on the ancient path that wicked men have trod?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.16', 'BSB', 'They were snatched away before their time, and their foundations were swept away by a flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.17', 'BSB', 'They said to God, ‘Depart from us. What can the Almighty do to us?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.18', 'BSB', 'But it was He who filled their houses with good things; so I stay far from the counsel of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.19', 'BSB', 'The righteous see it and are glad; the innocent mock them:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.20', 'BSB', '‘Surely our foes are destroyed, and fire has consumed their excess.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.21', 'BSB', 'Reconcile now and be at peace with Him; thereby good will come to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.22', 'BSB', 'Receive instruction from His mouth, and lay up His words in your heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.23', 'BSB', 'If you return to the Almighty, you will be restored. If you remove injustice from your tents', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.24', 'BSB', 'and consign your gold to the dust and the gold of Ophir to the stones of the ravines,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.25', 'BSB', 'then the Almighty will be your gold and the finest silver for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.26', 'BSB', 'Surely then you will delight in the Almighty and lift up your face to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.27', 'BSB', 'You will pray to Him, and He will hear you, and you will fulfill your vows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.28', 'BSB', 'Your decisions will be carried out, and light will shine on your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.29', 'BSB', 'When men are brought low and you say, ‘Lift them up!’ then He will save the lowly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.22.30', 'BSB', 'He will deliver even one who is not innocent, rescuing him through the cleanness of your hands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.2', 'BSB', '“Even today my complaint is bitter. His hand is heavy despite my groaning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.3', 'BSB', 'If only I knew where to find Him, so that I could go to His seat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.4', 'BSB', 'I would plead my case before Him and fill my mouth with arguments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.5', 'BSB', 'I would learn how He would answer, and consider what He would say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.6', 'BSB', 'Would He contend with me in His great power? No, He would certainly take note of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.7', 'BSB', 'Then an upright man could reason with Him, and I would be delivered forever from my Judge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.8', 'BSB', 'If I go east, He is not there, and if I go west, I cannot find Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.9', 'BSB', 'When He is at work in the north, I cannot behold Him; when He turns to the south, I cannot see Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.10', 'BSB', 'Yet He knows the way I have taken; when He has tested me, I will come forth as gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.11', 'BSB', 'My feet have followed in His tracks; I have kept His way without turning aside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.12', 'BSB', 'I have not departed from the command of His lips; I have treasured the words of His mouth more than my daily bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.13', 'BSB', 'But He is unchangeable, and who can oppose Him? He does what He desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.14', 'BSB', 'For He carries out His decree against me, and He has many such plans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore I am terrified in His presence; when I consider this, I fear Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.16', 'BSB', 'God has made my heart faint; the Almighty has terrified me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.23.17', 'BSB', 'Yet I am not silenced by the darkness, by the thick darkness that covers my face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.1', 'BSB', '“Why does the Almighty not reserve times for judgment? Why may those who know Him never see His days?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.2', 'BSB', 'Men move boundary stones; they pasture stolen flocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.3', 'BSB', 'They drive away the donkey of the fatherless and take the widow’s ox in pledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.4', 'BSB', 'They push the needy off the road and force all the poor of the land into hiding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.5', 'BSB', 'Indeed, like wild donkeys in the desert, the poor go to work foraging for food; the wasteland is food for their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.6', 'BSB', 'They gather fodder in the fields and glean the vineyards of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.7', 'BSB', 'Without clothing, they spend the night naked; they have no covering against the cold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.8', 'BSB', 'Drenched by mountain rains, they huddle against the rocks for want of shelter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.9', 'BSB', 'The fatherless infant is snatched from the breast; the nursing child of the poor is seized for a debt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.10', 'BSB', 'Without clothing, they wander about naked. They carry the sheaves, but still go hungry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.11', 'BSB', 'They crush olives within their walls; they tread the winepresses, but go thirsty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.12', 'BSB', 'From the city, men groan, and the souls of the wounded cry out, yet God charges no one with wrongdoing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.13', 'BSB', 'Then there are those who rebel against the light, not knowing its ways or staying on its paths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.14', 'BSB', 'When daylight is gone, the murderer rises to kill the poor and needy; in the night he is like a thief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.15', 'BSB', 'The eye of the adulterer watches for twilight. Thinking, ‘No eye will see me,’ he covers his face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.16', 'BSB', 'In the dark they dig through houses; by day they shut themselves in, never to experience the light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.17', 'BSB', 'For to them, deep darkness is their morning; surely they are friends with the terrors of darkness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.18', 'BSB', 'They are but foam on the surface of the water; their portion of the land is cursed, so that no one turns toward their vineyards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.19', 'BSB', 'As drought and heat consume the melting snow, so Sheol steals those who have sinned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.20', 'BSB', 'The womb forgets them; the worm feeds on them; they are remembered no more. So injustice is like a broken tree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.21', 'BSB', 'They prey on the barren and childless, and show no kindness to the widow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.22', 'BSB', 'Yet by His power, God drags away the mighty; though rising up, they have no assurance of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.23', 'BSB', 'He gives them a sense of security, but His eyes are on their ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.24', 'BSB', 'They are exalted for a moment, then they are gone; they are brought low and gathered up like all others; they are cut off like heads of grain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.24.25', 'BSB', 'If this is not so, then who can prove me a liar and reduce my words to nothing?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.1', 'BSB', 'Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.2', 'BSB', '“Dominion and awe belong to God; He establishes harmony in the heights of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.3', 'BSB', 'Can His troops be numbered? On whom does His light not rise?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.4', 'BSB', 'How then can a man be just before God? How can one born of woman be pure?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.5', 'BSB', 'If even the moon does not shine, and the stars are not pure in His sight,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.25.6', 'BSB', 'how much less man, who is but a maggot, and the son of man, who is but a worm!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.2', 'BSB', '“How you have helped the powerless and saved the arm that is feeble!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.3', 'BSB', 'How you have counseled the unwise and provided fully sound insight!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.4', 'BSB', 'To whom have you uttered these words? And whose spirit spoke through you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.5', 'BSB', 'The dead tremble— those beneath the waters and those who dwell in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.6', 'BSB', 'Sheol is naked before God, and Abaddon has no covering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.7', 'BSB', 'He stretches out the north over empty space; He hangs the earth upon nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.8', 'BSB', 'He wraps up the waters in His clouds, yet the clouds do not burst under their own weight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.9', 'BSB', 'He covers the face of the full moon, spreading over it His cloud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.10', 'BSB', 'He has inscribed a horizon on the face of the waters at the boundary between light and darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.11', 'BSB', 'The foundations of heaven quake, astounded at His rebuke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.12', 'BSB', 'By His power He stirred the sea; by His understanding He shattered Rahab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.13', 'BSB', 'By His breath the skies were cleared; His hand pierced the fleeing serpent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.26.14', 'BSB', 'Indeed, these are but the fringes of His ways; how faint is the whisper we hear of Him! Who then can understand the thunder of His power?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.1', 'BSB', 'Job continued his discourse:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.2', 'BSB', '“As surely as God lives, who has deprived me of justice— the Almighty, who has embittered my soul—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.3', 'BSB', 'as long as my breath is still within me and the breath of God remains in my nostrils,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.4', 'BSB', 'my lips will not speak wickedness, and my tongue will not utter deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.5', 'BSB', 'I will never say that you are right; I will maintain my integrity until I die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.6', 'BSB', 'I will cling to my righteousness and never let go. As long as I live, my conscience will not accuse me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.7', 'BSB', 'May my enemy be like the wicked and my opponent like the unjust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.8', 'BSB', 'For what is the hope of the godless when he is cut off, when God takes away his life?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.9', 'BSB', 'Will God hear his cry when distress comes upon him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.10', 'BSB', 'Will he delight in the Almighty? Will he call upon God at all times?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.11', 'BSB', 'I will instruct you in the power of God. I will not conceal the ways of the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.12', 'BSB', 'Surely all of you have seen it for yourselves. Why then do you keep up this empty talk?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.13', 'BSB', 'This is the wicked man’s portion from God— the heritage the ruthless receive from the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.14', 'BSB', 'Though his sons are many, they are destined for the sword; and his offspring will never have enough food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.15', 'BSB', 'His survivors will be buried by the plague, and their widows will not weep for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.16', 'BSB', 'Though he heaps up silver like dust and piles up a wardrobe like clay,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.17', 'BSB', 'what he lays up, the righteous will wear, and his silver will be divided by the innocent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.18', 'BSB', 'The house he built is like a moth’s cocoon, like a hut set up by a watchman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.19', 'BSB', 'He lies down wealthy, but will do so no more; when he opens his eyes, all is gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.20', 'BSB', 'Terrors overtake him like a flood; a tempest sweeps him away in the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.21', 'BSB', 'The east wind carries him away, and he is gone; it sweeps him out of his place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.22', 'BSB', 'It hurls itself against him without mercy as he flees headlong from its power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.27.23', 'BSB', 'It claps its hands at him and hisses him out of his place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.1', 'BSB', '“Surely there is a mine for silver and a place where gold is refined.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.2', 'BSB', 'Iron is taken from the earth, and copper is smelted from ore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.3', 'BSB', 'Man puts an end to the darkness; he probes the farthest recesses for ore in deepest darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.4', 'BSB', 'Far from human habitation he cuts a shaft in places forgotten by the foot of man. Far from men he dangles and sways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.5', 'BSB', 'Food may come from the earth, but from below it is transformed as by fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.6', 'BSB', 'Its rocks are the source of sapphires, containing flecks of gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.7', 'BSB', 'No bird of prey knows that path; no falcon’s eye has seen it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.8', 'BSB', 'Proud beasts have never trodden it; no lion has ever prowled over it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.9', 'BSB', 'The miner strikes the flint; he overturns mountains at their base.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.10', 'BSB', 'He hews out channels in the rocks, and his eyes spot every treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.11', 'BSB', 'He stops up the sources of the streams to bring what is hidden to light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.12', 'BSB', 'But where can wisdom be found, and where does understanding dwell?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.13', 'BSB', 'No man can know its value, nor is it found in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.14', 'BSB', 'The ocean depths say, ‘It is not in me,’ while the sea declares, ‘It is not with me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.15', 'BSB', 'It cannot be bought with gold, nor can its price be weighed out in silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.16', 'BSB', 'It cannot be valued in the gold of Ophir, in precious onyx or sapphire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.17', 'BSB', 'Neither gold nor crystal can compare to it, nor jewels of fine gold be exchanged for it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.18', 'BSB', 'Coral and quartz are unworthy of mention; the price of wisdom is beyond rubies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.19', 'BSB', 'Topaz from Cush cannot compare to it, nor can it be valued in pure gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.20', 'BSB', 'From where then does wisdom come, and where does understanding dwell?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.21', 'BSB', 'It is hidden from the eyes of every living thing and concealed from the birds of the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.22', 'BSB', 'Abaddon and Death say, ‘We have heard a rumor about it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.23', 'BSB', 'But God understands its way, and He knows its place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.24', 'BSB', 'For He looks to the ends of the earth and sees everything under the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.25', 'BSB', 'When God fixed the weight of the wind and measured out the waters,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.26', 'BSB', 'when He set a limit for the rain and a path for the thunderbolt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.27', 'BSB', 'then He looked at wisdom and appraised it; He established it and searched it out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.28.28', 'BSB', 'And He said to man, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom, and to turn away from evil is understanding.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.1', 'BSB', 'And Job continued his discourse:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.2', 'BSB', '“How I long for the months gone by, for the days when God watched over me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.3', 'BSB', 'when His lamp shone above my head, and by His light I walked through the darkness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.4', 'BSB', 'when I was in my prime, when the friendship of God rested on my tent,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.5', 'BSB', 'when the Almighty was still with me and my children were around me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.6', 'BSB', 'when my steps were bathed in cream and the rock poured out for me streams of oil!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.7', 'BSB', 'When I went out to the city gate and took my seat in the public square,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.8', 'BSB', 'the young men saw me and withdrew, and the old men rose to their feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.9', 'BSB', 'The princes refrained from speaking and covered their mouths with their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.10', 'BSB', 'The voices of the nobles were hushed, and their tongues stuck to the roofs of their mouths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.11', 'BSB', 'For those who heard me called me blessed, and those who saw me commended me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.12', 'BSB', 'because I rescued the poor who cried out and the fatherless who had no helper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.13', 'BSB', 'The dying man blessed me, and I made the widow’s heart sing for joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.14', 'BSB', 'I put on righteousness, and it clothed me; justice was my robe and my turban.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.15', 'BSB', 'I served as eyes to the blind and as feet to the lame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.16', 'BSB', 'I was a father to the needy, and I took up the case of the stranger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.17', 'BSB', 'I shattered the fangs of the unjust and snatched the prey from his teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.18', 'BSB', 'So I thought: ‘I will die in my nest and multiply my days as the sand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.19', 'BSB', 'My roots will spread out to the waters, and the dew will rest nightly on my branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.20', 'BSB', 'My glory is ever new within me, and my bow is renewed in my hand.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.21', 'BSB', 'Men listened to me with expectation, waiting silently for my counsel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.22', 'BSB', 'After my words, they spoke no more; my speech settled on them like dew.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.23', 'BSB', 'They waited for me as for rain and drank in my words like spring showers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.24', 'BSB', 'If I smiled at them, they did not believe it; the light of my countenance was precious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.29.25', 'BSB', 'I chose their course and presided as chief. So I dwelt as a king among his troops, as a comforter of the mourners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.1', 'BSB', '“But now they mock me, men younger than I am, whose fathers I would have refused to entrust with my sheep dogs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.2', 'BSB', 'What use to me was the strength of their hands, since their vigor had left them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.3', 'BSB', 'Gaunt from poverty and hunger, they gnawed the dry land, and the desolate wasteland by night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.4', 'BSB', 'They plucked mallow among the shrubs, and the roots of the broom tree were their food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.5', 'BSB', 'They were banished from among men, shouted down like thieves,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.6', 'BSB', 'so that they lived on the slopes of the wadis, among the rocks and in holes in the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.7', 'BSB', 'They cried out among the shrubs and huddled beneath the nettles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.8', 'BSB', 'A senseless and nameless brood, they were driven off the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.9', 'BSB', 'And now they mock me in song; I have become a byword among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.10', 'BSB', 'They abhor me and keep far from me; they do not hesitate to spit in my face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.11', 'BSB', 'Because God has unstrung my bow and afflicted me, they have cast off restraint in my presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.12', 'BSB', 'The rabble arises at my right; they lay snares for my feet and build siege ramps against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.13', 'BSB', 'They tear up my path; they profit from my destruction, with no one to restrain them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.14', 'BSB', 'They advance as through a wide breach; through the ruins they keep rolling in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.15', 'BSB', 'Terrors are turned loose against me; they drive away my dignity as by the wind, and my prosperity has passed like a cloud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.16', 'BSB', 'And now my soul is poured out within me; days of affliction grip me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.17', 'BSB', 'Night pierces my bones, and my gnawing pains never rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.18', 'BSB', 'With great force He grasps my garment; He seizes me by the collar of my tunic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.19', 'BSB', 'He throws me into the mud, and I have become like dust and ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.20', 'BSB', 'I cry out to You for help, but You do not answer; when I stand up, You merely look at me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.21', 'BSB', 'You have ruthlessly turned on me; You oppose me with Your strong hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.22', 'BSB', 'You snatch me up into the wind and drive me before it; You toss me about in the storm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.23', 'BSB', 'Yes, I know that You will bring me down to death, to the place appointed for all the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.24', 'BSB', 'Yet no one stretches out his hand to a ruined man when he cries for help in his distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.25', 'BSB', 'Have I not wept for those in trouble? Has my soul not grieved for the needy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.26', 'BSB', 'But when I hoped for good, evil came; when I looked for light, darkness fell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.27', 'BSB', 'I am churning within and cannot rest; days of affliction confront me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.28', 'BSB', 'I go about blackened, but not by the sun. I stand up in the assembly and cry for help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.29', 'BSB', 'I have become a brother of jackals, a companion of ostriches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.30', 'BSB', 'My skin grows black and peels, and my bones burn with fever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.30.31', 'BSB', 'My harp is tuned to mourning and my flute to the sound of weeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.1', 'BSB', '“I have made a covenant with my eyes. How then could I gaze with desire at a virgin?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.2', 'BSB', 'For what is the allotment of God from above, or the heritage from the Almighty on high?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.3', 'BSB', 'Does not disaster come to the unjust and calamity to the workers of iniquity?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.4', 'BSB', 'Does He not see my ways and count my every step?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.5', 'BSB', 'If I have walked in falsehood or my foot has rushed to deceit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.6', 'BSB', 'let God weigh me with honest scales, that He may know my integrity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.7', 'BSB', 'If my steps have turned from the path, if my heart has followed my eyes, or if impurity has stuck to my hands,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.8', 'BSB', 'then may another eat what I have sown, and may my crops be uprooted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.9', 'BSB', 'If my heart has been enticed by my neighbor’s wife, or I have lurked at his door,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.10', 'BSB', 'then may my own wife grind grain for another, and may other men sleep with her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.11', 'BSB', 'For that would be a heinous crime, an iniquity to be judged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.12', 'BSB', 'For it is a fire that burns down to Abaddon; it would root out my entire harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.13', 'BSB', 'If I have rejected the cause of my manservant or maidservant when they made a complaint against me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.14', 'BSB', 'what will I do when God rises to judge? How will I answer when called to account?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.15', 'BSB', 'Did not He who made me in the womb also make them? Did not the same One form us in the womb?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.16', 'BSB', 'If I have denied the desires of the poor or allowed the widow’s eyes to fail,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.17', 'BSB', 'if I have eaten my morsel alone, not sharing it with the fatherless—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.18', 'BSB', 'though from my youth I reared him as would a father, and from my mother’s womb I guided the widow—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.19', 'BSB', 'if I have seen one perish for lack of clothing, or a needy man without a cloak,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.20', 'BSB', 'if his heart has not blessed me for warming him with the fleece of my sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.21', 'BSB', 'if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless because I saw that I had support in the gate,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.22', 'BSB', 'then may my arm fall from my shoulder and be torn from its socket.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.23', 'BSB', 'For calamity from God terrifies me, and His splendor I cannot overpower.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.24', 'BSB', 'If I have put my trust in gold or called pure gold my security,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.25', 'BSB', 'if I have rejoiced in my great wealth because my hand had gained so much,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.26', 'BSB', 'if I have beheld the sun in its radiance or the moon moving in splendor,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.27', 'BSB', 'so that my heart was secretly enticed and my hand threw a kiss from my mouth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.28', 'BSB', 'this would also be an iniquity to be judged, for I would have denied God on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.29', 'BSB', 'If I have rejoiced in my enemy’s ruin, or exulted when evil befell him—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.30', 'BSB', 'I have not allowed my mouth to sin by asking for his life with a curse—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.31', 'BSB', 'if the men of my house have not said, ‘Who is there who has not had his fill?’—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.32', 'BSB', 'but no stranger had to lodge on the street, for my door has been open to the traveler—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.33', 'BSB', 'if I have covered my transgressions like Adam by hiding my guilt in my heart,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.34', 'BSB', 'because I greatly feared the crowds and the contempt of the clans terrified me, so that I kept silent and would not go outside—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.35', 'BSB', '(Oh, that I had one to hear me! Here is my signature. Let the Almighty answer me; let my accuser compose an indictment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.36', 'BSB', 'Surely I would carry it on my shoulder and wear it like a crown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.37', 'BSB', 'I would give account of all my steps; I would approach Him like a prince.)—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.38', 'BSB', 'if my land cries out against me and its furrows weep together,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.39', 'BSB', 'if I have devoured its produce without payment or broken the spirit of its tenants,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.31.40', 'BSB', 'then let briers grow instead of wheat and stinkweed instead of barley.” Thus conclude the words of Job.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.1', 'BSB', 'So these three men stopped answering Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.2', 'BSB', 'This kindled the anger of Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite, of the family of Ram. He burned with anger against Job for justifying himself rather than God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.3', 'BSB', 'and he burned with anger against Job’s three friends because they had failed to refute Job, and yet had condemned him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.4', 'BSB', 'Now Elihu had waited to speak to Job because the others were older than he.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.5', 'BSB', 'But when he saw that the three men had no further reply, his anger was kindled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.6', 'BSB', 'So Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite declared: “I am young in years, while you are old; that is why I was timid and afraid to tell you what I know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.7', 'BSB', 'I thought that age should speak, and many years should teach wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.8', 'BSB', 'But there is a spirit in a man, the breath of the Almighty, that gives him understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.9', 'BSB', 'It is not only the old who are wise, or the elderly who understand justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore I say, ‘Listen to me; I too will declare what I know.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.11', 'BSB', 'Indeed, I waited while you spoke; I listened to your reasoning; as you searched for words,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.12', 'BSB', 'I paid you full attention. But no one proved Job wrong; not one of you rebutted his arguments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.13', 'BSB', 'So do not claim, ‘We have found wisdom; let God, not man, refute him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.14', 'BSB', 'But Job has not directed his words against me, and I will not answer him with your arguments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.15', 'BSB', 'Job’s friends are dismayed, with no more to say; words have escaped them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.16', 'BSB', 'Must I wait, now that they are silent, now that they stand and no longer reply?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.17', 'BSB', 'I too will answer; yes, I will declare what I know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.18', 'BSB', 'For I am full of words, and my spirit within me compels me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, my belly is like unvented wine; it is about to burst like a new wineskin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.20', 'BSB', 'I must speak and find relief; I must open my lips and respond.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.21', 'BSB', 'I will be partial to no one, nor will I flatter any man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.32.22', 'BSB', 'For I do not know how to flatter, or my Maker would remove me in an instant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.1', 'BSB', '“But now, O Job, hear my speech, and listen to all my words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.2', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will open my mouth; my address is on the tip of my tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.3', 'BSB', 'My words are from an upright heart, and my lips speak sincerely what I know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.4', 'BSB', 'The Spirit of God has made me, and the breath of the Almighty gives me life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.5', 'BSB', 'Refute me if you can; prepare your case and confront me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.6', 'BSB', 'I am just like you before God; I was also formed from clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.7', 'BSB', 'Surely no fear of me should terrify you; nor will my hand be heavy upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.8', 'BSB', 'Surely you have spoken in my hearing, and I have heard these very words:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.9', 'BSB', '‘I am pure, without transgression; I am clean, with no iniquity in me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.10', 'BSB', 'Yet God finds occasions against me; He counts me as His enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.11', 'BSB', 'He puts my feet in the stocks; He watches over all my paths.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.12', 'BSB', 'Behold, you are not right in this matter. I will answer you, for God is greater than man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.13', 'BSB', 'Why do you complain to Him that He answers nothing a man asks?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.14', 'BSB', 'For God speaks in one way and in another, yet no one notices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.15', 'BSB', 'In a dream, in a vision in the night, when deep sleep falls upon men as they slumber on their beds,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.16', 'BSB', 'He opens their ears and terrifies them with warnings', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.17', 'BSB', 'to turn a man from wrongdoing and keep him from pride,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.18', 'BSB', 'to preserve his soul from the Pit and his life from perishing by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.19', 'BSB', 'A man is also chastened on his bed with pain and constant distress in his bones,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.20', 'BSB', 'so that he detests his bread, and his soul loathes his favorite food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.21', 'BSB', 'His flesh wastes away from sight, and his hidden bones protrude.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.22', 'BSB', 'He draws near to the Pit, and his life to the messengers of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.23', 'BSB', 'Yet if there is a messenger on his side, one mediator in a thousand, to tell a man what is right for him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.24', 'BSB', 'to be gracious to him and say, ‘Spare him from going down to the Pit; I have found his ransom,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.25', 'BSB', 'then his flesh is refreshed like a child’s; he returns to the days of his youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.26', 'BSB', 'He prays to God and finds favor; he sees God’s face and shouts for joy, and God restores His righteousness to that man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.27', 'BSB', 'Then he sings before men with these words: ‘I have sinned and perverted what was right; yet I did not get what I deserved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.28', 'BSB', 'He redeemed my soul from going down to the Pit, and I will live to see the light.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.29', 'BSB', 'Behold, all these things God does to a man, two or even three times,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.30', 'BSB', 'to bring back his soul from the Pit, that he may be enlightened with the light of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.31', 'BSB', 'Pay attention, Job, and listen to me; be silent, and I will speak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.32', 'BSB', 'But if you have something to say, answer me; speak up, for I would like to vindicate you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.33.33', 'BSB', 'But if not, then listen to me; be quiet, and I will teach you wisdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.1', 'BSB', 'Then Elihu continued:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.2', 'BSB', '“Hear my words, O wise men; give ear to me, O men of learning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.3', 'BSB', 'For the ear tests words as the mouth tastes food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.4', 'BSB', 'Let us choose for ourselves what is right; let us learn together what is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.5', 'BSB', 'For Job has declared, ‘I am righteous, yet God has deprived me of justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.6', 'BSB', 'Would I lie about my case? My wound is incurable, though I am without transgression.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.7', 'BSB', 'What man is like Job, who drinks up derision like water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.8', 'BSB', 'He keeps company with evildoers and walks with wicked men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.9', 'BSB', 'For he has said, ‘It profits a man nothing that he should delight in God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore listen to me, O men of understanding. Far be it from God to do wrong, and from the Almighty to act unjustly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.11', 'BSB', 'For according to a man’s deeds He repays him; according to a man’s ways He brings consequences.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.12', 'BSB', 'Indeed, it is true that God does not act wickedly, and the Almighty does not pervert justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.13', 'BSB', 'Who gave Him charge over the earth? Who appointed Him over the whole world?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.14', 'BSB', 'If He were to set His heart to it and withdraw His Spirit and breath,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.15', 'BSB', 'all flesh would perish together and mankind would return to the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.16', 'BSB', 'If you have understanding, hear this; listen to my words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.17', 'BSB', 'Could one who hates justice govern? Will you condemn the just and mighty One,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.18', 'BSB', 'who says to kings, ‘You are worthless!’ and to nobles, ‘You are wicked,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.19', 'BSB', 'who is not partial to princes and does not favor rich over poor? For they are all the work of His hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.20', 'BSB', 'They die in an instant, in the middle of the night. The people convulse and pass away; the mighty are removed without human hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.21', 'BSB', 'For His eyes are on the ways of a man, and He sees his every step.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.22', 'BSB', 'There is no darkness or deep shadow where the workers of iniquity can hide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.23', 'BSB', 'For God need not examine a man further or have him approach for judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.24', 'BSB', 'He shatters the mighty without inquiry and sets up others in their place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore, He recognizes their deeds; He overthrows them in the night and they are crushed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.26', 'BSB', 'He strikes them for their wickedness in full view,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.27', 'BSB', 'because they turned aside from Him and had no regard for any of His ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.28', 'BSB', 'They caused the cry of the poor to come before Him, and He heard the outcry of the afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.29', 'BSB', 'But when He remains silent, who can condemn Him? When He hides His face, who can see Him? Yet He watches over both man and nation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.30', 'BSB', 'that godless men should not rule or lay snares for the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.31', 'BSB', 'Suppose someone says to God, ‘I have endured my punishment; I will offend no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.32', 'BSB', 'Teach me what I cannot see; if I have done wrong, I will not do it again.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.33', 'BSB', 'Should God repay you on your own terms when you have disavowed His? You must choose, not I; so tell me what you know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.34', 'BSB', 'Men of understanding will declare to me, and the wise men who hear me will say:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.35', 'BSB', '‘Job speaks without knowledge; his words lack insight.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.36', 'BSB', 'If only Job were tried to the utmost for answering like a wicked man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.34.37', 'BSB', 'For he adds rebellion to his sin; he claps his hands among us and multiplies his words against God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.1', 'BSB', 'And Elihu went on to say:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.2', 'BSB', '“Do you think this is just? You say, ‘I am more righteous than God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.3', 'BSB', 'For you ask, ‘What does it profit me, and what benefit do I gain apart from sin?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.4', 'BSB', 'I will reply to you and to your friends as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.5', 'BSB', 'Look to the heavens and see; gaze at the clouds high above you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.6', 'BSB', 'If you sin, what do you accomplish against Him? If you multiply your transgressions, what do you do to Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.7', 'BSB', 'If you are righteous, what do you give Him, or what does He receive from your hand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.8', 'BSB', 'Your wickedness affects only a man like yourself, and your righteousness only a son of man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.9', 'BSB', 'Men cry out under great oppression; they plead for relief from the arm of the mighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.10', 'BSB', 'But no one asks, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives us songs in the night,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.11', 'BSB', 'who teaches us more than the beasts of the earth and makes us wiser than the birds of the air?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.12', 'BSB', 'There they cry out, but He does not answer, because of the pride of evil men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.13', 'BSB', 'Surely God does not listen to empty pleas, and the Almighty does not take note of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.14', 'BSB', 'How much less, then, when you say that you do not see Him, that your case is before Him and you must wait for Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.15', 'BSB', 'and further, that in His anger He has not punished or taken much notice of folly!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.35.16', 'BSB', 'So Job opens his mouth in vain and multiplies words without knowledge.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.1', 'BSB', 'And Elihu continued:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.2', 'BSB', '“Bear with me a little longer, and I will show you that there is more to be said on God’s behalf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.3', 'BSB', 'I get my knowledge from afar, and I will ascribe justice to my Maker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.4', 'BSB', 'For truly my words are free of falsehood; one perfect in knowledge is with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.5', 'BSB', 'Indeed, God is mighty, but He despises no one; He is mighty in strength of understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.6', 'BSB', 'He does not keep the wicked alive, but He grants justice to the afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.7', 'BSB', 'He does not take His eyes off the righteous, but He enthrones them with kings and exalts them forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.8', 'BSB', 'And if men are bound with chains, caught in cords of affliction,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.9', 'BSB', 'then He tells them their deeds and how arrogantly they have transgressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.10', 'BSB', 'He opens their ears to correction and commands that they turn from iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.11', 'BSB', 'If they obey and serve Him, then they end their days in prosperity and their years in happiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.12', 'BSB', 'But if they do not obey, then they perish by the sword and die without knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.13', 'BSB', 'The godless in heart harbor resentment; even when He binds them, they do not cry for help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.14', 'BSB', 'They die in their youth, among the male shrine prostitutes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.15', 'BSB', 'God rescues the afflicted by their affliction and opens their ears in oppression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.16', 'BSB', 'Indeed, He drew you from the jaws of distress to a spacious and broad place, to a table full of richness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.17', 'BSB', 'But now you are laden with the judgment due the wicked; judgment and justice have seized you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.18', 'BSB', 'Be careful that no one lures you with riches; do not let a large bribe lead you astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.19', 'BSB', 'Can your wealth or all your mighty effort keep you from distress?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.20', 'BSB', 'Do not long for the night, when people vanish from their homes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.21', 'BSB', 'Be careful not to turn to iniquity, for this you have preferred to affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.22', 'BSB', 'Behold, God is exalted in His power. Who is a teacher like Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.23', 'BSB', 'Who has appointed His way for Him, or told Him, ‘You have done wrong’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.24', 'BSB', 'Remember to magnify His work, which men have praised in song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.25', 'BSB', 'All mankind has seen it; men behold it from afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.26', 'BSB', 'Indeed, God is great—beyond our knowledge; the number of His years is unsearchable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.27', 'BSB', 'For He draws up drops of water which distill the rain from the mist,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.28', 'BSB', 'which the clouds pour out and shower abundantly on mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.29', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, who can understand how the clouds spread out, how the thunder roars from His pavilion?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.30', 'BSB', 'See how He scatters His lightning around Him and covers the depths of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.31', 'BSB', 'For by these He judges the nations and provides food in abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.32', 'BSB', 'He fills His hands with lightning and commands it to strike its mark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.36.33', 'BSB', 'The thunder declares His presence; even the cattle regard the rising storm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.1', 'BSB', '“At this my heart also pounds and leaps from its place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.2', 'BSB', 'Listen closely to the thunder of His voice and the rumbling that comes from His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.3', 'BSB', 'He unleashes His lightning beneath the whole sky and sends it to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.4', 'BSB', 'Then there comes a roaring sound; He thunders with His majestic voice. He does not restrain the lightning when His voice resounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.5', 'BSB', 'God thunders wondrously with His voice; He does great things we cannot comprehend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.6', 'BSB', 'For He says to the snow, ‘Fall on the earth,’ and to the gentle rain, ‘Pour out a mighty downpour.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.7', 'BSB', 'He seals up the hand of every man, so that all men may know His work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.8', 'BSB', 'The wild animals enter their lairs; they settle down in their dens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.9', 'BSB', 'The tempest comes from its chamber, and the cold from the driving north winds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.10', 'BSB', 'By the breath of God the ice is formed and the watery expanses are frozen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.11', 'BSB', 'He loads the clouds with moisture; He scatters His lightning through them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.12', 'BSB', 'They swirl about, whirling at His direction, accomplishing all that He commands over the face of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.13', 'BSB', 'Whether for punishment or for His land, He accomplishes this in His loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.14', 'BSB', 'Listen to this, O Job; stand still and consider the wonders of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.15', 'BSB', 'Do you know how God dispatches the clouds or makes the lightning flash?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.16', 'BSB', 'Do you understand how the clouds float, those wonders of Him who is perfect in knowledge?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.17', 'BSB', 'You whose clothes get hot when the land lies hushed under the south wind,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.18', 'BSB', 'can you, like Him, spread out the skies to reflect the heat like a mirror of bronze?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.19', 'BSB', 'Teach us what we should say to Him; we cannot draw up our case when our faces are in darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.20', 'BSB', 'Should He be told that I want to speak? Would a man ask to be swallowed up?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.21', 'BSB', 'Now no one can gaze at the sun when it is bright in the skies after the wind has swept them clean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.22', 'BSB', 'Out of the north He comes in golden splendor; awesome majesty surrounds Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.23', 'BSB', 'The Almighty is beyond our reach; He is exalted in power! In His justice and great righteousness He does not oppress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.37.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore, men fear Him, for He is not partial to the wise in heart.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.2', 'BSB', '“Who is this who obscures My counsel by words without knowledge?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.3', 'BSB', 'Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.4', 'BSB', 'Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Tell Me, if you have understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.5', 'BSB', 'Who fixed its measurements? Surely you know! Or who stretched a measuring line across it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.6', 'BSB', 'On what were its foundations set, or who laid its cornerstone,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.7', 'BSB', 'while the morning stars sang together and all the sons of God shouted for joy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.8', 'BSB', 'Who enclosed the sea behind doors when it burst forth from the womb,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.9', 'BSB', 'when I made the clouds its garment and thick darkness its blanket,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.10', 'BSB', 'when I fixed its boundaries and set in place its bars and doors,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.11', 'BSB', 'and I declared: ‘You may come this far, but no farther; here your proud waves must stop’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.12', 'BSB', 'In your days, have you commanded the morning or assigned the dawn its place,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.13', 'BSB', 'that it might spread to the ends of the earth and shake the wicked out of it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.14', 'BSB', 'The earth takes shape like clay under a seal; its hills stand out like the folds of a garment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.15', 'BSB', 'Light is withheld from the wicked, and their upraised arm is broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.16', 'BSB', 'Have you journeyed to the vents of the sea or walked in the trenches of the deep?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.17', 'BSB', 'Have the gates of death been revealed to you? Have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.18', 'BSB', 'Have you surveyed the extent of the earth? Tell Me, if you know all this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.19', 'BSB', 'Where is the way to the home of light? Do you know where darkness resides,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.20', 'BSB', 'so you can lead it back to its border? Do you know the paths to its home?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.21', 'BSB', 'Surely you know, for you were already born! And the number of your days is great!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.22', 'BSB', 'Have you entered the storehouses of snow or observed the storehouses of hail,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.23', 'BSB', 'which I hold in reserve for times of trouble, for the day of war and battle?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.24', 'BSB', 'In which direction is the lightning dispersed, or the east wind scattered over the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.25', 'BSB', 'Who cuts a channel for the flood or clears a path for the thunderbolt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.26', 'BSB', 'to bring rain on a barren land, on a desert where no man lives,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.27', 'BSB', 'to satisfy the parched wasteland and make it sprout with tender grass?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.28', 'BSB', 'Does the rain have a father? Who has begotten the drops of dew?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.29', 'BSB', 'From whose womb does the ice emerge? Who gives birth to the frost from heaven,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.30', 'BSB', 'when the waters become hard as stone and the surface of the deep is frozen?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.31', 'BSB', 'Can you bind the chains of the Pleiades or loosen the belt of Orion?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.32', 'BSB', 'Can you bring forth the constellations in their seasons or lead out the Bear and her cubs?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.33', 'BSB', 'Do you know the laws of the heavens? Can you set their dominion over the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.34', 'BSB', 'Can you command the clouds so that a flood of water covers you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.35', 'BSB', 'Can you send the lightning bolts on their way? Do they report to you, ‘Here we are’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.36', 'BSB', 'Who has put wisdom in the heart or given understanding to the mind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.37', 'BSB', 'Who has the wisdom to count the clouds? Or who can tilt the water jars of the heavens', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.38', 'BSB', 'when the dust hardens into a mass and the clods of earth stick together?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.39', 'BSB', 'Can you hunt the prey for a lioness or satisfy the hunger of young lions', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.40', 'BSB', 'when they crouch in their dens and lie in wait in the thicket?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.38.41', 'BSB', 'Who provides food for the raven when its young cry out to God as they wander about for lack of food?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.1', 'BSB', '“Do you know when mountain goats give birth? Have you watched the doe bear her fawn?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.2', 'BSB', 'Can you count the months they are pregnant? Do you know the time they give birth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.3', 'BSB', 'They crouch down and bring forth their young; they deliver their newborn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.4', 'BSB', 'Their young ones thrive and grow up in the open field; they leave and do not return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.5', 'BSB', 'Who set the wild donkey free? Who released the swift donkey from the harness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.6', 'BSB', 'I made the wilderness his home and the salt flats his dwelling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.7', 'BSB', 'He scorns the tumult of the city and never hears the shouts of a driver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.8', 'BSB', 'He roams the mountains for pasture, searching for any green thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.9', 'BSB', 'Will the wild ox consent to serve you? Will he stay by your manger at night?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.10', 'BSB', 'Can you hold him to the furrow with a harness? Will he plow the valleys behind you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.11', 'BSB', 'Can you rely on his great strength? Will you leave your hard work to him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.12', 'BSB', 'Can you trust him to bring in your grain and gather it to your threshing floor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.13', 'BSB', 'The wings of the ostrich flap joyfully, but cannot match the pinions and feathers of the stork.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.14', 'BSB', 'For she leaves her eggs on the ground and lets them warm in the sand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.15', 'BSB', 'She forgets that a foot may crush them, or a wild animal may trample them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.16', 'BSB', 'She treats her young harshly, as if not her own, with no concern that her labor was in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.17', 'BSB', 'For God has deprived her of wisdom; He has not endowed her with understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.18', 'BSB', 'Yet when she proudly spreads her wings, she laughs at the horse and its rider.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.19', 'BSB', 'Do you give strength to the horse or adorn his neck with a mane?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.20', 'BSB', 'Do you make him leap like a locust, striking terror with his proud snorting?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.21', 'BSB', 'He paws in the valley and rejoices in his strength; he charges into battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.22', 'BSB', 'He laughs at fear, frightened of nothing; he does not turn back from the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.23', 'BSB', 'A quiver rattles at his side, along with a flashing spear and lance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.24', 'BSB', 'Trembling with excitement, he devours the distance; he cannot stand still when the ram’s horn sounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.25', 'BSB', 'At the blast of the horn, he snorts with fervor. He catches the scent of battle from afar— the shouts of captains and the cry of war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.26', 'BSB', 'Does the hawk take flight by your understanding and spread his wings toward the south?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.27', 'BSB', 'Does the eagle soar at your command and make his nest on high?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.28', 'BSB', 'He dwells on a cliff and lodges there; his stronghold is on a rocky crag.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.29', 'BSB', 'From there he spies out food; his eyes see it from afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.39.30', 'BSB', 'His young ones feast on blood; and where the slain are, there he is.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.1', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Job:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.2', 'BSB', '“Will the faultfinder contend with the Almighty? Let him who argues with God give an answer.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.3', 'BSB', 'Then Job answered the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.4', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am insignificant. How can I reply to You? I place my hand over my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.5', 'BSB', 'I have spoken once, but I have no answer— twice, but I have nothing to add.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.6', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind and said:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.7', 'BSB', '“Now brace yourself like a man; I will question you, and you shall inform Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.8', 'BSB', 'Would you really annul My justice? Would you condemn Me to justify yourself?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.9', 'BSB', 'Do you have an arm like God’s? Can you thunder with a voice like His?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.10', 'BSB', 'Then adorn yourself with majesty and splendor, and clothe yourself with honor and glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.11', 'BSB', 'Unleash the fury of your wrath; look on every proud man and bring him low.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.12', 'BSB', 'Look on every proud man and humble him; trample the wicked where they stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.13', 'BSB', 'Bury them together in the dust; imprison them in the grave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.14', 'BSB', 'Then I will confess to you that your own right hand can save you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.15', 'BSB', 'Look at Behemoth, which I made along with you. He feeds on grass like an ox.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.16', 'BSB', 'See the strength of his loins and the power in the muscles of his belly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.17', 'BSB', 'His tail sways like a cedar; the sinews of his thighs are tightly knit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.18', 'BSB', 'His bones are tubes of bronze; his limbs are rods of iron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.19', 'BSB', 'He is the foremost of God’s works; only his Maker can draw the sword against him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.20', 'BSB', 'The hills yield him their produce, while all the beasts of the field play nearby.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.21', 'BSB', 'He lies under the lotus plants, hidden among the reeds of the marsh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.22', 'BSB', 'The lotus plants conceal him in their shade; the willows of the brook surround him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.23', 'BSB', 'Though the river rages, Behemoth is unafraid; he remains secure, though the Jordan surges to his mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.40.24', 'BSB', 'Can anyone capture him as he looks on, or pierce his nose with a snare?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.1', 'BSB', '“Can you pull in Leviathan with a hook or tie down his tongue with a rope?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.2', 'BSB', 'Can you put a cord through his nose or pierce his jaw with a hook?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.3', 'BSB', 'Will he beg you for mercy or speak to you softly?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.4', 'BSB', 'Will he make a covenant with you to take him as a slave for life?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.5', 'BSB', 'Can you pet him like a bird or put him on a leash for your maidens?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.6', 'BSB', 'Will traders barter for him or divide him among the merchants?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.7', 'BSB', 'Can you fill his hide with harpoons or his head with fishing spears?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.8', 'BSB', 'If you lay a hand on him, you will remember the battle and never repeat it!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.9', 'BSB', 'Surely hope of overcoming him is false. Is not the sight of him overwhelming?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.10', 'BSB', 'No one is so fierce as to rouse Leviathan. Then who is able to stand against Me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.11', 'BSB', 'Who has given to Me that I should repay him? Everything under heaven is Mine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.12', 'BSB', 'I cannot keep silent about his limbs, his power and graceful form.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.13', 'BSB', 'Who can strip off his outer coat? Who can approach him with a bridle?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.14', 'BSB', 'Who can open his jaws, ringed by his fearsome teeth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.15', 'BSB', 'His rows of scales are his pride, tightly sealed together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.16', 'BSB', 'One scale is so near to another that no air can pass between them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.17', 'BSB', 'They are joined to one another; they clasp and cannot be separated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.18', 'BSB', 'His snorting flashes with light, and his eyes are like the rays of dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.19', 'BSB', 'Firebrands stream from his mouth; fiery sparks shoot forth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.20', 'BSB', 'Smoke billows from his nostrils as from a boiling pot over burning reeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.21', 'BSB', 'His breath sets coals ablaze, and flames pour from his mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.22', 'BSB', 'Strength resides in his neck, and dismay leaps before him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.23', 'BSB', 'The folds of his flesh are tightly joined; they are firm and immovable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.24', 'BSB', 'His chest is as hard as a rock, as hard as a lower millstone!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.25', 'BSB', 'When Leviathan rises up, the mighty are terrified; they withdraw before his thrashing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.26', 'BSB', 'The sword that reaches him has no effect, nor does the spear or dart or arrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.27', 'BSB', 'He regards iron as straw and bronze as rotten wood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.28', 'BSB', 'No arrow can make him flee; slingstones become like chaff to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.29', 'BSB', 'A club is regarded as straw, and he laughs at the sound of the lance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.30', 'BSB', 'His undersides are jagged potsherds, spreading out the mud like a threshing sledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.31', 'BSB', 'He makes the depths seethe like a cauldron; he makes the sea like a jar of ointment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.32', 'BSB', 'He leaves a glistening wake behind him; one would think the deep had white hair!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.33', 'BSB', 'Nothing on earth is his equal— a creature devoid of fear!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.41.34', 'BSB', 'He looks down on all the haughty; he is king over all the proud.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.1', 'BSB', 'Then Job replied to the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.2', 'BSB', '“I know that You can do all things and that no plan of Yours can be thwarted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.3', 'BSB', 'You asked, ‘Who is this who conceals My counsel without knowledge?’ Surely I spoke of things I did not understand, things too wonderful for me to know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.4', 'BSB', 'You said, ‘Listen now, and I will speak. I will question you, and you shall inform Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.5', 'BSB', 'My ears had heard of You, but now my eyes have seen You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore I retract my words, and I repent in dust and ashes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.7', 'BSB', 'After the LORD had spoken these words to Job, He said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My wrath is kindled against you and your two friends. For you have not spoken about Me accurately, as My servant Job has.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.8', 'BSB', 'So now, take seven bulls and seven rams, go to My servant Job, and sacrifice a burnt offering for yourselves. Then My servant Job will pray for you, for I will accept his prayer and not deal with you according to your folly. For you have not spoken accurately about Me, as My servant Job has.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.9', 'BSB', 'So Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite went and did as the LORD had told them; and the LORD accepted Job’s request.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.10', 'BSB', 'After Job had prayed for his friends, the LORD restored his prosperity and doubled his former possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.11', 'BSB', 'All his brothers and sisters and prior acquaintances came and dined with him in his house. They consoled him and comforted him over all the adversity that the LORD had brought upon him. And each one gave him a piece of silver and a gold ring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.12', 'BSB', 'So the LORD blessed Job’s latter days more than his first. He owned 14,000 sheep, 6,000 camels, 1,000 yoke of oxen, and 1,000 female donkeys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.13', 'BSB', 'And he also had seven sons and three daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.14', 'BSB', 'He named his first daughter Jemimah, his second Keziah, and his third Keren-happuch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.15', 'BSB', 'No women as beautiful as Job’s daughters could be found in all the land, and their father granted them an inheritance among their brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.16', 'BSB', 'After this, Job lived 140 years and saw his children and their children to the fourth generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Job.42.17', 'BSB', 'And so Job died, old and full of years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.1', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, or set foot on the path of sinners, or sit in the seat of mockers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.2', 'BSB', 'But his delight is in the Law of the LORD, and on His law he meditates day and night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.3', 'BSB', 'He is like a tree planted by streams of water, yielding its fruit in season, whose leaf does not wither, and who prospers in all he does.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.4', 'BSB', 'Not so the wicked! For they are like chaff driven off by the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore the wicked will not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the assembly of the righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.1.6', 'BSB', 'For the LORD guards the path of the righteous, but the way of the wicked will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.1', 'BSB', 'Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.2', 'BSB', 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together, against the LORD and against His Anointed One:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.3', 'BSB', '“Let us break Their chains and cast away Their cords.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.4', 'BSB', 'The One enthroned in heaven laughs; the Lord taunts them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.5', 'BSB', 'Then He rebukes them in His anger, and terrifies them in His fury:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.6', 'BSB', '“I have installed My King on Zion, upon My holy mountain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.7', 'BSB', 'I will proclaim the decree spoken to Me by the LORD: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.8', 'BSB', 'Ask Me, and I will make the nations Your inheritance, the ends of the earth Your possession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.9', 'BSB', 'You will break them with an iron scepter; You will shatter them like pottery.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore be wise, O kings; be admonished, O judges of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.11', 'BSB', 'Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.2.12', 'BSB', 'Kiss the Son, lest He be angry and you perish in your rebellion, when His wrath ignites in an instant. Blessed are all who take refuge in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, how my foes have increased! How many rise up against me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.2', 'BSB', 'Many say of me, “God will not deliver him.” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.3', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, and the One who lifts my head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.4', 'BSB', 'To the LORD I cry aloud, and He answers me from His holy mountain. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.5', 'BSB', 'I lie down and sleep; I wake again, for the LORD sustains me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.6', 'BSB', 'I will not fear the myriads set against me on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.7', 'BSB', 'Arise, O LORD! Save me, O my God! Strike all my enemies on the jaw; break the teeth of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.3.8', 'BSB', 'Salvation belongs to the LORD; may Your blessing be on Your people. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.1', 'BSB', 'Answer me when I call, O God of my righteousness! You have relieved my distress; show me grace and hear my prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.2', 'BSB', 'How long, O men, will my honor be maligned? How long will you love vanity and seek after lies? Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.3', 'BSB', 'Know that the LORD has set apart the godly for Himself; the LORD hears when I call to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.4', 'BSB', 'Be angry, yet do not sin; on your bed, search your heart and be still. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.5', 'BSB', 'Offer the sacrifices of the righteous and trust in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.6', 'BSB', 'Many ask, “Who can show us the good?” Shine the light of Your face upon us, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.7', 'BSB', 'You have filled my heart with more joy than when grain and new wine abound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.4.8', 'BSB', 'I will lie down and sleep in peace, for You alone, O LORD, make me dwell in safety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.1', 'BSB', 'Give ear to my words, O LORD; consider my groaning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.2', 'BSB', 'Attend to the sound of my cry, my King and my God, for to You I pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.3', 'BSB', 'In the morning, O LORD, You hear my voice; at daybreak I lay my plea before You and wait in expectation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.4', 'BSB', 'For You are not a God who delights in wickedness; no evil can dwell with You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.5', 'BSB', 'The boastful cannot stand in Your presence; You hate all workers of iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.6', 'BSB', 'You destroy those who tell lies; the LORD abhors the man of bloodshed and deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.7', 'BSB', 'But I will enter Your house by the abundance of Your loving devotion; in reverence I will bow down toward Your holy temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.8', 'BSB', 'Lead me, O LORD, in Your righteousness because of my enemies; make straight Your way before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.9', 'BSB', 'For not a word they speak can be trusted; destruction lies within them. Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.10', 'BSB', 'Declare them guilty, O God; let them fall by their own devices. Drive them out for their many transgressions, for they have rebelled against You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.11', 'BSB', 'But let all who take refuge in You rejoice; let them ever shout for joy. May You shelter them, that those who love Your name may rejoice in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.5.12', 'BSB', 'For surely You, O LORD, bless the righteous; You surround them with the shield of Your favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.2', 'BSB', 'Be merciful to me, O LORD, for I am frail; heal me, O LORD, for my bones are in agony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.3', 'BSB', 'My soul is deeply distressed. How long, O LORD, how long?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.4', 'BSB', 'Turn, O LORD, and deliver my soul; save me because of Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.5', 'BSB', 'For there is no mention of You in death; who can praise You from Sheol?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.6', 'BSB', 'I am weary from groaning; all night I flood my bed with weeping and drench my couch with tears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.7', 'BSB', 'My eyes fail from grief; they grow dim because of all my foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.8', 'BSB', 'Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity, for the LORD has heard my weeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.9', 'BSB', 'The LORD has heard my cry for mercy; the LORD accepts my prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.6.10', 'BSB', 'All my enemies will be ashamed and dismayed; they will turn back in sudden disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD my God, I take refuge in You; save me and deliver me from all my pursuers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.2', 'BSB', 'or they will shred my soul like a lion and tear me to pieces with no one to rescue me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.3', 'BSB', 'O LORD my God, if I have done this, if injustice is on my hands,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.4', 'BSB', 'if I have rewarded my ally with evil, if I have plundered my foe without cause,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.5', 'BSB', 'then may my enemy pursue me and overtake me; may he trample me to the ground and leave my honor in the dust. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.6', 'BSB', 'Arise, O LORD, in Your anger; rise up against the fury of my enemies. Awake, my God, and ordain judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.7', 'BSB', 'Let the assembled peoples gather around You; take Your seat over them on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD judges the peoples; vindicate me, O LORD, according to my righteousness and integrity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.9', 'BSB', 'Put an end to the evil of the wicked, but establish the righteous, O righteous God who searches hearts and minds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.10', 'BSB', 'My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.11', 'BSB', 'God is a righteous judge and a God who feels indignation each day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.12', 'BSB', 'If one does not repent, God will sharpen His sword; He has bent and strung His bow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.13', 'BSB', 'He has prepared His deadly weapons; He ordains His arrows with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.14', 'BSB', 'Behold, the wicked man travails with evil; he conceives trouble and births falsehood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.15', 'BSB', 'He has dug a hole and hollowed it out; he has fallen into a pit of his own making.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.16', 'BSB', 'His trouble recoils on himself, and his violence falls on his own head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.7.17', 'BSB', 'I will thank the LORD for His righteousness and sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth! You have set Your glory above the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.2', 'BSB', 'From the mouths of children and infants You have ordained praise on account of Your adversaries, to silence the enemy and avenger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.3', 'BSB', 'When I behold Your heavens, the work of Your fingers, the moon and the stars, which You have set in place—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.4', 'BSB', 'what is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.5', 'BSB', 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.6', 'BSB', 'You made him ruler of the works of Your hands; You have placed everything under his feet:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.7', 'BSB', 'all sheep and oxen, and even the beasts of the field,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.8', 'BSB', 'the birds of the air and the fish of the sea, all that swim the paths of the seas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.8.9', 'BSB', 'O LORD, our Lord, how majestic is Your name in all the earth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.1', 'BSB', 'I will give thanks to the LORD with all my heart; I will recount all Your wonders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.2', 'BSB', 'I will be glad and rejoice in You; I will sing praise to Your name, O Most High.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.3', 'BSB', 'When my enemies retreat, they stumble and perish before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.4', 'BSB', 'For You have upheld my just cause; You sit on Your throne judging righteously.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.5', 'BSB', 'You have rebuked the nations; You have destroyed the wicked; You have erased their name forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.6', 'BSB', 'The enemy has come to eternal ruin, and You have uprooted their cities; the very memory of them has vanished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.7', 'BSB', 'But the LORD abides forever; He has established His throne for judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.8', 'BSB', 'He judges the world with justice; He governs the people with equity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.9', 'BSB', 'The LORD is a refuge for the oppressed, a stronghold in times of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.10', 'BSB', 'Those who know Your name trust in You, for You, O LORD, have not forsaken those who seek You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.11', 'BSB', 'Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion; proclaim His deeds among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.12', 'BSB', 'For the Avenger of bloodshed remembers; He does not ignore the cry of the afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.13', 'BSB', 'Be merciful to me, O LORD; see how my enemies afflict me! Lift me up from the gates of death,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.14', 'BSB', 'that I may declare all Your praises— that within the gates of Daughter Zion I may rejoice in Your salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.15', 'BSB', 'The nations have fallen into a pit of their making; their feet are caught in the net they have hidden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.16', 'BSB', 'The LORD is known by the justice He brings; the wicked are ensnared by the work of their hands. Higgaion Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.17', 'BSB', 'The wicked will return to Sheol— all the nations who forget God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.18', 'BSB', 'For the needy will not always be forgotten; nor the hope of the oppressed forever dashed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.19', 'BSB', 'Rise up, O LORD, do not let man prevail; let the nations be judged in Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.9.20', 'BSB', 'Lay terror upon them, O LORD; let the nations know they are but men. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.1', 'BSB', 'Why, O LORD, do You stand far off? Why do You hide in times of trouble?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.2', 'BSB', 'In pride the wicked pursue the needy; let them be caught in the schemes they devise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.3', 'BSB', 'For the wicked man boasts in the cravings of his heart; he blesses the greedy and reviles the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.4', 'BSB', 'In his pride the wicked man does not seek Him; in all his schemes there is no God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.5', 'BSB', 'He is secure in his ways at all times; Your lofty judgments are far from him; he sneers at all his foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.6', 'BSB', 'He says to himself, “I will not be moved; from age to age I am free of distress.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.7', 'BSB', 'His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and violence; trouble and malice are under his tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.8', 'BSB', 'He lies in wait near the villages; in ambush he slays the innocent; his eyes watch in stealth for the helpless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.9', 'BSB', 'He lies in wait like a lion in a thicket; he lurks to seize the oppressed; he catches the lowly in his net.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.10', 'BSB', 'They are crushed and beaten down; the hapless fall prey to his strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.11', 'BSB', 'He says to himself, “God has forgotten; He hides His face and never sees.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.12', 'BSB', 'Arise, O LORD! Lift up Your hand, O God! Do not forget the helpless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.13', 'BSB', 'Why has the wicked man renounced God? He says to himself, “You will never call me to account.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.14', 'BSB', 'But You have regarded trouble and grief; You see to repay it by Your hand. The victim entrusts himself to You; You are the helper of the fatherless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.15', 'BSB', 'Break the arm of the wicked and evildoer; call him to account for his wickedness until none is left to be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.16', 'BSB', 'The LORD is King forever and ever; the nations perish from His land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.17', 'BSB', 'You have heard, O LORD, the desire of the humble; You will strengthen their hearts. You will incline Your ear,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.10.18', 'BSB', 'to vindicate the fatherless and oppressed, that the men of the earth may strike terror no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.1', 'BSB', 'In the LORD I take refuge. How then can you say to me: “Flee like a bird to your mountain!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.2', 'BSB', 'For behold, the wicked bend their bows. They set their arrow on the string to shoot from the shadows at the upright in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.3', 'BSB', 'If the foundations are destroyed, what can the righteous do?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.4', 'BSB', 'The LORD is in His holy temple; the LORD is on His heavenly throne. His eyes are watching closely; they examine the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD tests the righteous and the wicked; His soul hates the lover of violence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.6', 'BSB', 'On the wicked He will rain down fiery coals and sulfur; a scorching wind will be their portion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.11.7', 'BSB', 'For the LORD is righteous; He loves justice. The upright will see His face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.1', 'BSB', 'Help, O LORD, for the godly are no more; the faithful have vanished from among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.2', 'BSB', 'They lie to one another; they speak with flattering lips and a double heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.3', 'BSB', 'May the LORD cut off all flattering lips and every boastful tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.4', 'BSB', 'They say, “With our tongues we will prevail. We own our lips—who can be our master?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.5', 'BSB', '“For the cause of the oppressed and for the groaning of the needy, I will now arise,” says the LORD. “I will bring safety to him who yearns.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.6', 'BSB', 'The words of the LORD are flawless, like silver refined in a furnace, like gold purified sevenfold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.7', 'BSB', 'You, O LORD, will keep us; You will forever guard us from this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.12.8', 'BSB', 'The wicked wander freely, and vileness is exalted among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.1', 'BSB', 'How long, O LORD? Will You forget me forever? How long will You hide Your face from me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.2', 'BSB', 'How long must I wrestle in my soul, with sorrow in my heart each day? How long will my enemy dominate me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.3', 'BSB', 'Consider me and respond, O LORD my God. Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in death,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.4', 'BSB', 'lest my enemy say, “I have overcome him,” and my foes rejoice when I fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.5', 'BSB', 'But I have trusted in Your loving devotion; my heart will rejoice in Your salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.13.6', 'BSB', 'I will sing to the LORD, for He has been good to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.1', 'BSB', 'The fool says in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt; their acts are vile. There is no one who does good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD looks down from heaven upon the sons of men to see if any understand, if any seek God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.3', 'BSB', 'All have turned away, they have together become corrupt; there is no one who does good, not even one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.4', 'BSB', 'Will the workers of iniquity never learn? They devour my people like bread; they refuse to call upon the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.5', 'BSB', 'There they are, overwhelmed with dread, for God is in the company of the righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.6', 'BSB', 'You sinners frustrate the plans of the oppressed, yet the LORD is their shelter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.14.7', 'BSB', 'Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come from Zion! When the LORD restores His captive people, let Jacob rejoice, let Israel be glad!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.15.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, who may abide in Your tent? Who may dwell on Your holy mountain?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.15.2', 'BSB', 'He who walks with integrity and practices righteousness, who speaks the truth from his heart,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.15.3', 'BSB', 'who has no slander on his tongue, who does no harm to his neighbor, who casts no scorn on his friend,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.15.4', 'BSB', 'who despises the vile but honors those who fear the LORD, who does not revise a costly oath,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.15.5', 'BSB', 'who lends his money without interest and refuses a bribe against the innocent. He who does these things will never be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.1', 'BSB', 'Preserve me, O God, for in You I take refuge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.2', 'BSB', 'I said to the LORD, “You are my Lord; apart from You I have no good thing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.3', 'BSB', 'As for the saints in the land, they are the excellence in whom all my delight resides.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.4', 'BSB', 'Sorrows will multiply to those who chase other gods. I will not pour out their libations of blood, or speak their names with my lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD is my chosen portion and my cup; You have made my lot secure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.6', 'BSB', 'The lines of my boundary have fallen in pleasant places; surely my inheritance is delightful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.7', 'BSB', 'I will bless the LORD who counsels me; even at night my conscience instructs me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.8', 'BSB', 'I have set the LORD always before me. Because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will dwell securely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.10', 'BSB', 'For You will not abandon my soul to Sheol, nor will You let Your Holy One see decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.16.11', 'BSB', 'You have made known to me the path of life; You will fill me with joy in Your presence, with eternal pleasures at Your right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.1', 'BSB', 'Hear, O LORD, my righteous plea; listen to my cry. Give ear to my prayer— it comes from lips free of deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.2', 'BSB', 'May my vindication come from Your presence; may Your eyes see what is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.3', 'BSB', 'You have tried my heart; You have visited me in the night. You have tested me and found no evil; I have resolved not to sin with my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.4', 'BSB', 'As for the deeds of men— by the word of Your lips I have avoided the ways of the violent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.5', 'BSB', 'My steps have held to Your paths; my feet have not slipped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.6', 'BSB', 'I call on You, O God, for You will answer me. Incline Your ear to me; hear my words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.7', 'BSB', 'Show the wonders of Your loving devotion, You who save by Your right hand those who seek refuge from their foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.8', 'BSB', 'Keep me as the apple of Your eye; hide me in the shadow of Your wings', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.9', 'BSB', 'from the wicked who assail me, from my mortal enemies who surround me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.10', 'BSB', 'They have closed their callous hearts; their mouths speak with arrogance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.11', 'BSB', 'They have tracked us down, and now surround us; their eyes are set to cast us to the ground,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.12', 'BSB', 'like a lion greedy for prey, like a young lion lurking in ambush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.13', 'BSB', 'Arise, O LORD, confront them! Bring them to their knees; deliver me from the wicked by Your sword,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.14', 'BSB', 'from such men, O LORD, by Your hand— from men of the world whose portion is in this life. May You fill the bellies of Your treasured ones and satisfy their sons, so they leave their abundance to their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.17.15', 'BSB', 'As for me, I will behold Your face in righteousness; when I awake, I will be satisfied in Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.1', 'BSB', 'I love You, O LORD, my strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer. My God is my rock, in whom I take refuge, my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my stronghold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.3', 'BSB', 'I will call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised; so shall I be saved from my enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.4', 'BSB', 'The cords of death encompassed me; the torrents of chaos overwhelmed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.5', 'BSB', 'The cords of Sheol entangled me; the snares of death confronted me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.6', 'BSB', 'In my distress I called upon the LORD; I cried to my God for help. From His temple He heard my voice, and my cry for His help reached His ears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.7', 'BSB', 'Then the earth shook and quaked, and the foundations of the mountains trembled; they were shaken because He burned with anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.8', 'BSB', 'Smoke rose from His nostrils, and consuming fire came from His mouth; glowing coals blazed forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.9', 'BSB', 'He parted the heavens and came down with dark clouds beneath His feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.10', 'BSB', 'He mounted a cherub and flew; He soared on the wings of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.11', 'BSB', 'He made darkness His hiding place, and storm clouds a canopy around Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.12', 'BSB', 'From the brightness of His presence His clouds advanced— hailstones and coals of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.13', 'BSB', 'The LORD thundered from heaven; the voice of the Most High resounded— hailstones and coals of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.14', 'BSB', 'He shot His arrows and scattered the foes; He hurled lightning and routed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.15', 'BSB', 'The channels of the sea appeared, and the foundations of the world were exposed, at Your rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of Your nostrils.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.16', 'BSB', 'He reached down from on high and took hold of me; He drew me out of deep waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.17', 'BSB', 'He rescued me from my powerful enemy, from foes too mighty for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.18', 'BSB', 'They confronted me in my day of calamity, but the LORD was my support.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.19', 'BSB', 'He brought me out into the open; He rescued me because He delighted in me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.20', 'BSB', 'The LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness; He has repaid me according to the cleanness of my hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.21', 'BSB', 'For I have kept the ways of the LORD and have not wickedly departed from my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.22', 'BSB', 'For all His ordinances are before me; I have not disregarded His statutes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.23', 'BSB', 'And I have been blameless before Him and kept myself from iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.24', 'BSB', 'So the LORD has repaid me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in His sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.25', 'BSB', 'To the faithful You show Yourself faithful, to the blameless You show Yourself blameless;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.26', 'BSB', 'to the pure You show Yourself pure, but to the crooked You show Yourself shrewd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.27', 'BSB', 'For You save an afflicted people, but You humble those with haughty eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.28', 'BSB', 'For You, O LORD, light my lamp; my God lights up my darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.29', 'BSB', 'For in You I can charge an army, and with my God I can scale a wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.30', 'BSB', 'As for God, His way is perfect; the word of the LORD is flawless. He is a shield to all who take refuge in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.31', 'BSB', 'For who is God besides the LORD? And who is the Rock except our God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.32', 'BSB', 'It is God who arms me with strength and makes my way clear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.33', 'BSB', 'He makes my feet like those of a deer and stations me upon the heights.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.34', 'BSB', 'He trains my hands for battle; my arms can bend a bow of bronze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.35', 'BSB', 'You have given me Your shield of salvation; Your right hand upholds me, and Your gentleness exalts me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.36', 'BSB', 'You broaden the path beneath me so that my ankles do not give way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.37', 'BSB', 'I pursued my enemies and overtook them; I did not turn back until they were consumed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.38', 'BSB', 'I crushed them so they could not rise; they have fallen under my feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.39', 'BSB', 'You have armed me with strength for battle; You have subdued my foes beneath me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.40', 'BSB', 'You have made my enemies retreat before me; I put an end to those who hated me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.41', 'BSB', 'They cried for help, but there was no one to save them— to the LORD, but He did not answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.42', 'BSB', 'I ground them as dust in the face of the wind; I trampled them like mud in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.43', 'BSB', 'You have delivered me from the strife of the people; You have made me the head of nations; a people I had not known shall serve me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.44', 'BSB', 'When they hear me, they obey me; foreigners cower before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.45', 'BSB', 'Foreigners lose heart and come trembling from their strongholds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.46', 'BSB', 'The LORD lives, and blessed be my Rock! And may the God of my salvation be exalted—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.47', 'BSB', 'the God who avenges me and subdues nations beneath me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.48', 'BSB', 'who delivers me from my enemies. You exalt me above my foes; You rescue me from violent men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.49', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will praise You, O LORD, among the nations; I will sing praises to Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.18.50', 'BSB', 'Great salvation He brings to His king. He shows loving devotion to His anointed, to David and his descendants forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.1', 'BSB', 'The heavens declare the glory of God; the skies proclaim the work of His hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.2', 'BSB', 'Day after day they pour forth speech; night after night they reveal knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.3', 'BSB', 'Without speech or language, without a sound to be heard,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.4', 'BSB', 'their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world. In the heavens He has pitched a tent for the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.5', 'BSB', 'Like a bridegroom emerging from his chamber, like a champion rejoicing to run his course,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.6', 'BSB', 'it rises at one end of the heavens and runs its circuit to the other; nothing is deprived of its warmth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.7', 'BSB', 'The Law of the LORD is perfect, reviving the soul; the testimony of the LORD is trustworthy, making wise the simple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.8', 'BSB', 'The precepts of the LORD are right, bringing joy to the heart; the commandments of the LORD are radiant, giving light to the eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.9', 'BSB', 'The fear of the LORD is pure, enduring forever; the judgments of the LORD are true, being altogether righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.10', 'BSB', 'They are more precious than gold, than much pure gold; they are sweeter than honey, than honey from the comb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.11', 'BSB', 'By them indeed Your servant is warned; in keeping them is great reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.12', 'BSB', 'Who can discern his own errors? Cleanse me from my hidden faults.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.13', 'BSB', 'Keep Your servant also from willful sins; may they not rule over me. Then I will be blameless and cleansed of great transgression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.19.14', 'BSB', 'May the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be pleasing in Your sight, O LORD, my Rock and my Redeemer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.1', 'BSB', 'May the LORD answer you in the day of trouble; may the name of the God of Jacob protect you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.2', 'BSB', 'May He send you help from the sanctuary and sustain you from Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.3', 'BSB', 'May He remember all your gifts and look favorably on your burnt offerings. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.4', 'BSB', 'May He give you the desires of your heart and make all your plans succeed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.5', 'BSB', 'May we shout for joy at your victory and raise a banner in the name of our God. May the LORD grant all your petitions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.6', 'BSB', 'Now I know that the LORD saves His anointed; He answers him from His holy heaven with the saving power of His right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.7', 'BSB', 'Some trust in chariots and others in horses, but we trust in the name of the LORD our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.8', 'BSB', 'They collapse and fall, but we rise up and stand firm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.20.9', 'BSB', 'O LORD, save the king. Answer us on the day we call.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, the king rejoices in Your strength. How greatly he exults in Your salvation!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.2', 'BSB', 'You have granted his heart’s desire and have not withheld the request of his lips. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.3', 'BSB', 'For You welcomed him with rich blessings; You placed on his head a crown of pure gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.4', 'BSB', 'He asked You for life, and You granted it— length of days, forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.5', 'BSB', 'Great is his glory in Your salvation; You bestow on him splendor and majesty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.6', 'BSB', 'For You grant him blessings forever; You cheer him with joy in Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.7', 'BSB', 'For the king trusts in the LORD; through the loving devotion of the Most High, he will not be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.8', 'BSB', 'Your hand will apprehend all Your enemies; Your right hand will seize those who hate You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.9', 'BSB', 'You will place them in a fiery furnace at the time of Your appearing. In His wrath the LORD will engulf them, and the fire will consume them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.10', 'BSB', 'You will wipe their descendants from the earth, and their offspring from the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.11', 'BSB', 'Though they intend You harm, the schemes they devise will not prevail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.12', 'BSB', 'For You will put them to flight when Your bow is trained upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.21.13', 'BSB', 'Be exalted, O LORD, in Your strength; we will sing and praise Your power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.1', 'BSB', 'My God, my God, why have You forsaken me? Why are You so far from saving me, so far from my words of groaning?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.2', 'BSB', 'I cry out by day, O my God, but You do not answer, and by night, but I have no rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.3', 'BSB', 'Yet You are holy, enthroned on the praises of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.4', 'BSB', 'In You our fathers trusted; they trusted and You delivered them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.5', 'BSB', 'They cried out to You and were set free; they trusted in You and were not disappointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.6', 'BSB', 'But I am a worm and not a man, scorned by men and despised by the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.7', 'BSB', 'All who see me mock me; they sneer and shake their heads:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.8', 'BSB', '“He trusts in the LORD, let the LORD deliver him; let the LORD rescue him, since He delights in him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.9', 'BSB', 'Yet You brought me forth from the womb; You made me secure at my mother’s breast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.10', 'BSB', 'From birth I was cast upon You; from my mother’s womb You have been my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.11', 'BSB', 'Be not far from me, for trouble is near and there is no one to help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.12', 'BSB', 'Many bulls surround me; strong bulls of Bashan encircle me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.13', 'BSB', 'They open their jaws against me like lions that roar and maul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.14', 'BSB', 'I am poured out like water, and all my bones are disjointed. My heart is like wax; it melts away within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.15', 'BSB', 'My strength is dried up like a potsherd, and my tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth. You lay me in the dust of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.16', 'BSB', 'For dogs surround me; a band of evil men encircles me; they have pierced my hands and feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.17', 'BSB', 'I can count all my bones; they stare and gloat over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.18', 'BSB', 'They divide my garments among them and cast lots for my clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.19', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, be not far off; O my Strength, come quickly to help me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.20', 'BSB', 'Deliver my soul from the sword, my precious life from the power of wild dogs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.21', 'BSB', 'Save me from the mouth of the lion; at the horns of the wild oxen You have answered me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.22', 'BSB', 'I will proclaim Your name to my brothers; I will praise You in the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.23', 'BSB', 'You who fear the LORD, praise Him! All descendants of Jacob, honor Him! All offspring of Israel, revere Him!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.24', 'BSB', 'For He has not despised or detested the torment of the afflicted. He has not hidden His face from him, but has attended to his cry for help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.25', 'BSB', 'My praise for You resounds in the great assembly; I will fulfill my vows before those who fear You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.26', 'BSB', 'The poor will eat and be satisfied; those who seek the LORD will praise Him. May your hearts live forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.27', 'BSB', 'All the ends of the earth will remember and turn to the LORD. All the families of the nations will bow down before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.28', 'BSB', 'For dominion belongs to the LORD and He rules over the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.29', 'BSB', 'All the rich of the earth will feast and worship; all who go down to the dust will kneel before Him— even those unable to preserve their lives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.30', 'BSB', 'Posterity will serve Him; they will declare the Lord to a new generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.22.31', 'BSB', 'They will come and proclaim His righteousness to a people yet unborn— all that He has done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.2', 'BSB', 'He makes me lie down in green pastures; He leads me beside quiet waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.3', 'BSB', 'He restores my soul; He guides me in the paths of righteousness for the sake of His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.4', 'BSB', 'Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for You are with me; Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.5', 'BSB', 'You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies. You anoint my head with oil; my cup overflows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.23.6', 'BSB', 'Surely goodness and mercy will follow me all the days of my life, and I will dwell in the house of the LORD forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.1', 'BSB', 'The earth is the LORD’s, and the fullness thereof, the world and all who dwell therein.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.2', 'BSB', 'For He has founded it upon the seas and established it upon the waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.3', 'BSB', 'Who may ascend the hill of the LORD? Who may stand in His holy place?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.4', 'BSB', 'He who has clean hands and a pure heart, who does not lift up his soul to an idol or swear deceitfully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.5', 'BSB', 'He will receive blessing from the LORD and vindication from the God of his salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.6', 'BSB', 'Such is the generation of those who seek Him, who seek Your face, O God of Jacob. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.7', 'BSB', 'Lift up your heads, O gates! Be lifted up, O ancient doors, that the King of Glory may enter!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.8', 'BSB', 'Who is this King of Glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.9', 'BSB', 'Lift up your heads, O gates! Be lifted up, O ancient doors, that the King of Glory may enter!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.24.10', 'BSB', 'Who is He, this King of Glory? The LORD of Hosts— He is the King of Glory. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.1', 'BSB', 'To You, O LORD, I lift up my soul;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.2', 'BSB', 'in You, my God, I trust. Do not let me be put to shame; do not let my enemies exult over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.3', 'BSB', 'Surely none who wait for You will be put to shame; but those who are faithless without cause will be disgraced.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.4', 'BSB', 'Show me Your ways, O LORD; teach me Your paths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.5', 'BSB', 'Guide me in Your truth and teach me, for You are the God of my salvation; all day long I wait for You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.6', 'BSB', 'Remember, O LORD, Your compassion and loving devotion, for they are from age to age.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.7', 'BSB', 'Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my rebellious acts; remember me according to Your loving devotion, because of Your goodness, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.8', 'BSB', 'Good and upright is the LORD; therefore He shows sinners the way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.9', 'BSB', 'He guides the humble in what is right and teaches them His way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.10', 'BSB', 'All the LORD’s ways are loving and faithful to those who keep His covenant and His decrees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.11', 'BSB', 'For the sake of Your name, O LORD, forgive my iniquity, for it is great.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.12', 'BSB', 'Who is the man who fears the LORD? He will instruct him in the path chosen for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.13', 'BSB', 'His soul will dwell in prosperity, and his descendants will inherit the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD confides in those who fear Him, and reveals His covenant to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.15', 'BSB', 'My eyes are always on the LORD, for He will free my feet from the mesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.16', 'BSB', 'Turn to me and be gracious, for I am lonely and afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.17', 'BSB', 'The troubles of my heart increase; free me from my distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.18', 'BSB', 'Consider my affliction and trouble, and take away all my sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.19', 'BSB', 'Consider my enemies, for they are many, and they hate me with vicious hatred.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.20', 'BSB', 'Guard my soul and deliver me; let me not be put to shame, for I take refuge in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.21', 'BSB', 'May integrity and uprightness preserve me, because I wait for You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.25.22', 'BSB', 'Redeem Israel, O God, from all its distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.1', 'BSB', 'Vindicate me, O LORD! For I have walked with integrity; I have trusted in the LORD without wavering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.2', 'BSB', 'Test me, O LORD, and try me; examine my heart and mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.3', 'BSB', 'For Your loving devotion is before my eyes, and I have walked in Your truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.4', 'BSB', 'I do not sit with deceitful men, nor keep company with hypocrites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.5', 'BSB', 'I hate the mob of evildoers, and refuse to sit with the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.6', 'BSB', 'I wash my hands in innocence that I may go about Your altar, O LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.7', 'BSB', 'to raise my voice in thanksgiving and declare all Your wonderful works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.8', 'BSB', 'O LORD, I love the house where You dwell, the place where Your glory resides.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.9', 'BSB', 'Do not take my soul away with sinners, or my life with men of bloodshed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.10', 'BSB', 'in whose hands are wicked schemes, whose right hands are full of bribes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.11', 'BSB', 'But I will walk with integrity; redeem me and be merciful to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.26.12', 'BSB', 'My feet stand on level ground; in the congregations I will bless the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD is my light and my salvation— whom shall I fear? The LORD is the stronghold of my life— whom shall I dread?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.2', 'BSB', 'When the wicked came upon me to devour my flesh, my enemies and foes stumbled and fell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.3', 'BSB', 'Though an army encamps around me, my heart will not fear; though a war breaks out against me, I will keep my trust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.4', 'BSB', 'One thing I have asked of the LORD; this is what I desire: to dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to gaze on the beauty of the LORD and seek Him in His temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.5', 'BSB', 'For in the day of trouble He will hide me in His shelter; He will conceal me under the cover of His tent; He will set me high upon a rock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.6', 'BSB', 'Then my head will be held high above my enemies around me. At His tabernacle I will offer sacrifices with shouts of joy; I will sing and make music to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.7', 'BSB', 'Hear, O LORD, my voice when I call; be merciful and answer me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.8', 'BSB', 'My heart said, “Seek His face.” Your face, O LORD, I will seek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.9', 'BSB', 'Hide not Your face from me, nor turn away Your servant in anger. You have been my helper; do not leave me or forsake me, O God of my salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.10', 'BSB', 'Though my father and mother forsake me, the LORD will receive me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.11', 'BSB', 'Teach me Your way, O LORD, and lead me on a level path, because of my oppressors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.12', 'BSB', 'Do not hand me over to the will of my foes, for false witnesses rise up against me, breathing out violence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.13', 'BSB', 'Still I am certain to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.27.14', 'BSB', 'Wait patiently for the LORD; be strong and courageous. Wait patiently for the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.1', 'BSB', 'To You, O LORD, I call; be not deaf to me, O my Rock. For if You remain silent, I will be like those descending to the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.2', 'BSB', 'Hear my cry for mercy when I call to You for help, when I lift up my hands toward Your holy sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.3', 'BSB', 'Do not drag me away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, who speak peace to their neighbors while malice is in their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.4', 'BSB', 'Repay them according to their deeds and for their works of evil. Repay them for what their hands have done; bring back on them what they deserve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.5', 'BSB', 'Since they show no regard for the works of the LORD or what His hands have done, He will tear them down and never rebuild them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.6', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD, for He has heard my cry for mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.7', 'BSB', 'The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusts in Him, and I am helped. Therefore my heart rejoices, and I give thanks to Him with my song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD is the strength of His people, a stronghold of salvation for His anointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.28.9', 'BSB', 'Save Your people and bless Your inheritance; shepherd them and carry them forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.1', 'BSB', 'Ascribe to the LORD, O heavenly beings, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.2', 'BSB', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.3', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD is over the waters; the God of glory thunders; the LORD is heard over many waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.4', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD is powerful; the voice of the LORD is majestic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.5', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD breaks the cedars; the LORD shatters the cedars of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.6', 'BSB', 'He makes Lebanon skip like a calf, and Sirion like a young wild ox.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.7', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD strikes with flames of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.8', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD shakes the wilderness; the LORD shakes the Wilderness of Kadesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.9', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD twists the oaks and strips the forests bare. And in His temple all cry, “Glory!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.10', 'BSB', 'The LORD sits enthroned over the flood; the LORD is enthroned as King forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.29.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD gives His people strength; the LORD blesses His people with peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.1', 'BSB', 'I will exalt You, O LORD, for You have lifted me up and have not allowed my foes to rejoice over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.2', 'BSB', 'O LORD my God, I cried to You for help, and You healed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.3', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You pulled me up from Sheol; You spared me from descending into the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.4', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD, O you His saints, and praise His holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.5', 'BSB', 'For His anger is fleeting, but His favor lasts a lifetime. Weeping may stay the night, but joy comes in the morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.6', 'BSB', 'In prosperity I said, “I will never be shaken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.7', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You favored me; You made my mountain stand strong. When You hid Your face, I was dismayed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.8', 'BSB', 'To You, O LORD, I called, and I begged my Lord for mercy:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.9', 'BSB', '“What gain is there in my bloodshed, in my descent to the Pit? Will the dust praise You? Will it proclaim Your faithfulness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.10', 'BSB', 'Hear me, O LORD, and have mercy; O LORD, be my helper.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.11', 'BSB', 'You turned my mourning into dancing; You peeled off my sackcloth and clothed me with joy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.30.12', 'BSB', 'that my heart may sing Your praises and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.1', 'BSB', 'In You, O LORD, I have taken refuge; let me never be put to shame; save me by Your righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.2', 'BSB', 'Incline Your ear to me; come quickly to my rescue. Be my rock of refuge, the stronghold of my deliverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.3', 'BSB', 'For You are my rock and my fortress; lead me and guide me for the sake of Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.4', 'BSB', 'You free me from the net laid out for me, for You are my refuge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.5', 'BSB', 'Into Your hands I commit my spirit; You have redeemed me, O LORD, God of truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.6', 'BSB', 'I hate those who cling to worthless idols, but in the LORD I trust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.7', 'BSB', 'I will be glad and rejoice in Your loving devotion, for You have seen my affliction; You have known the anguish of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.8', 'BSB', 'You have not delivered me to the enemy; You have set my feet in the open.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.9', 'BSB', 'Be merciful to me, O LORD, for I am in distress; my eyes fail from sorrow, my soul and body as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.10', 'BSB', 'For my life is consumed with grief and my years with groaning; my iniquity has drained my strength, and my bones are wasting away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.11', 'BSB', 'Among all my enemies I am a disgrace, and among my neighbors even more. I am dreaded by my friends— they flee when they see me on the street.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.12', 'BSB', 'I am forgotten like a dead man, out of mind. I am like a broken vessel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.13', 'BSB', 'For I hear the slander of many; there is terror on every side. They conspire against me and plot to take my life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.14', 'BSB', 'But I trust in You, O LORD; I say, “You are my God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.15', 'BSB', 'My times are in Your hands; deliver me from my enemies and from those who pursue me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.16', 'BSB', 'Make Your face shine on Your servant; save me by Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.17', 'BSB', 'O LORD, let me not be ashamed, for I have called on You. Let the wicked be put to shame; let them lie silent in Sheol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.18', 'BSB', 'May lying lips be silenced— lips that speak with arrogance against the righteous, full of pride and contempt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.19', 'BSB', 'How great is Your goodness which You have laid up for those who fear You, which You have bestowed before the sons of men on those who take refuge in You!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.20', 'BSB', 'You hide them in the secret place of Your presence from the schemes of men. You conceal them in Your shelter from accusing tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.21', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD, for He has shown me His loving devotion in a city under siege.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.22', 'BSB', 'In my alarm I said, “I am cut off from Your sight!” But You heard my plea for mercy when I called to You for help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.23', 'BSB', 'Love the LORD, all His saints. The LORD preserves the faithful, but fully repays the arrogant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.31.24', 'BSB', 'Be strong and courageous, all you who hope in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.1', 'BSB', 'Blessed is he whose transgressions are forgiven, whose sins are covered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.2', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man whose iniquity the LORD does not count against him, in whose spirit there is no deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.3', 'BSB', 'When I kept silent, my bones became brittle from my groaning all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.4', 'BSB', 'For day and night Your hand was heavy upon me; my strength was drained as in the summer heat. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.5', 'BSB', 'Then I acknowledged my sin to You and did not hide my iniquity. I said, “I will confess my transgressions to the LORD,” and You forgave the guilt of my sin. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore let all the godly pray to You while You may be found. Surely when great waters rise, they will not come near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.7', 'BSB', 'You are my hiding place. You protect me from trouble; You surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.8', 'BSB', 'I will instruct you and teach you the way you should go; I will give you counsel and watch over you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.9', 'BSB', 'Do not be like the horse or mule, which have no understanding; they must be controlled with bit and bridle to make them come to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.10', 'BSB', 'Many are the sorrows of the wicked, but loving devotion surrounds him who trusts in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.32.11', 'BSB', 'Be glad in the LORD and rejoice, O righteous ones; shout for joy, all you upright in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.1', 'BSB', 'Rejoice in the LORD, O righteous ones; it is fitting for the upright to praise Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.2', 'BSB', 'Praise the LORD with the harp; make music to Him with ten strings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.3', 'BSB', 'Sing to Him a new song; play skillfully with a shout of joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.4', 'BSB', 'For the word of the LORD is upright, and all His work is trustworthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD loves righteousness and justice; the earth is full of His loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.6', 'BSB', 'By the word of the LORD the heavens were made, and all the stars by the breath of His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.7', 'BSB', 'He piles up the waters of the sea; He puts the depths into storehouses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.8', 'BSB', 'Let all the earth fear the LORD; let all the people of the world revere Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.9', 'BSB', 'For He spoke, and it came to be; He commanded, and it stood firm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.10', 'BSB', 'The LORD frustrates the plans of the nations; He thwarts the devices of the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.11', 'BSB', 'The counsel of the LORD stands forever, the purposes of His heart to all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.12', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD, the people He has chosen as His inheritance!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.13', 'BSB', 'The LORD looks down from heaven; He sees all the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.14', 'BSB', 'From His dwelling place He gazes on all who inhabit the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.15', 'BSB', 'He shapes the hearts of each; He considers all their works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.16', 'BSB', 'No king is saved by his vast army; no warrior is delivered by his great strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.17', 'BSB', 'A horse is a vain hope for salvation; even its great strength cannot save.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.18', 'BSB', 'Surely the eyes of the LORD are on those who fear Him, on those whose hope is in His loving devotion', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.19', 'BSB', 'to deliver them from death and keep them alive in famine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.20', 'BSB', 'Our soul waits for the LORD; He is our help and our shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.21', 'BSB', 'For our hearts rejoice in Him, since we trust in His holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.33.22', 'BSB', 'May Your loving devotion rest on us, O LORD, as we put our hope in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.1', 'BSB', 'I will bless the LORD at all times; His praise will always be on my lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.2', 'BSB', 'My soul boasts in the LORD; let the oppressed hear and rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.3', 'BSB', 'Magnify the LORD with me; let us exalt His name together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.4', 'BSB', 'I sought the LORD, and He answered me; He delivered me from all my fears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.5', 'BSB', 'Those who look to Him are radiant with joy; their faces shall never be ashamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.6', 'BSB', 'This poor man called out, and the LORD heard him; He saved him from all his troubles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.7', 'BSB', 'The angel of the LORD encamps around those who fear Him, and he delivers them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.8', 'BSB', 'Taste and see that the LORD is good; blessed is the man who takes refuge in Him!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.9', 'BSB', 'Fear the LORD, you His saints, for those who fear Him lack nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.10', 'BSB', 'Young lions go lacking and hungry, but those who seek the LORD lack no good thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.11', 'BSB', 'Come, children, listen to me; I will teach you the fear of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.12', 'BSB', 'Who is the man who delights in life, who desires to see good days?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.13', 'BSB', 'Keep your tongue from evil and your lips from deceitful speech.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.14', 'BSB', 'Turn away from evil and do good; seek peace and pursue it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.15', 'BSB', 'The eyes of the LORD are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their cry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.16', 'BSB', 'But the face of the LORD is against those who do evil, to wipe out all memory of them from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.17', 'BSB', 'The righteous cry out, and the LORD hears; He delivers them from all their troubles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.18', 'BSB', 'The LORD is near to the brokenhearted; He saves the contrite in spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.19', 'BSB', 'Many are the afflictions of the righteous, but the LORD delivers him from them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.20', 'BSB', 'He protects all his bones; not one of them will be broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.21', 'BSB', 'Evil will slay the wicked, and the haters of the righteous will be condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.34.22', 'BSB', 'The LORD redeems His servants, and none who take refuge in Him will be condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.1', 'BSB', 'Contend with my opponents, O LORD; fight against those who fight against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.2', 'BSB', 'Take up Your shield and buckler; arise and come to my aid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.3', 'BSB', 'Draw the spear and javelin against my pursuers; say to my soul: “I am your salvation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.4', 'BSB', 'May those who seek my life be disgraced and put to shame; may those who plan to harm me be driven back and confounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.5', 'BSB', 'May they be like chaff in the wind, as the angel of the LORD drives them away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.6', 'BSB', 'May their path be dark and slick, as the angel of the LORD pursues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.7', 'BSB', 'For without cause they laid their net for me; without reason they dug a pit for my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.8', 'BSB', 'May ruin befall them by surprise; may the net they hid ensnare them; may they fall into the hazard they created.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.9', 'BSB', 'Then my soul will rejoice in the LORD and exult in His salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.10', 'BSB', 'All my bones will exclaim, “Who is like You, O LORD, who delivers the afflicted from the aggressor, the poor and needy from the robber?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.11', 'BSB', 'Hostile witnesses come forward; they make charges I know nothing about.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.12', 'BSB', 'They repay me evil for good, to the bereavement of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.13', 'BSB', 'Yet when they were ill, I put on sackcloth; I humbled myself with fasting, but my prayers returned unanswered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.14', 'BSB', 'I paced about as for my friend or brother; I was bowed down with grief, like one mourning for his mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.15', 'BSB', 'But when I stumbled, they assembled in glee; they gathered together against me. Assailants I did not know slandered me without ceasing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.16', 'BSB', 'Like godless jesters at a feast, they gnashed their teeth at me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.17', 'BSB', 'How long, O Lord, will You look on? Rescue my soul from their ravages, my precious life from these lions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.18', 'BSB', 'Then I will give You thanks in the great assembly; I will praise You among many people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.19', 'BSB', 'Let not my enemies gloat over me without cause, nor those who hate me without reason wink in malice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.20', 'BSB', 'For they do not speak peace, but they devise deceitful schemes against those who live quietly in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.21', 'BSB', 'They gape at me and say, “Aha, aha! Our eyes have seen!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.22', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You have seen it; be not silent. O Lord, be not far from me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.23', 'BSB', 'Awake and rise to my defense, to my cause, my God and my Lord!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.24', 'BSB', 'Vindicate me by Your righteousness, O LORD my God, and do not let them gloat over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.25', 'BSB', 'Let them not say in their hearts, “Aha, just what we wanted!” Let them not say, “We have swallowed him up!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.26', 'BSB', 'May those who gloat in my distress be ashamed and confounded; may those who exalt themselves over me be clothed in shame and reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.27', 'BSB', 'May those who favor my vindication shout for joy and gladness; may they always say, “Exalted be the LORD who delights in His servant’s well-being.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.35.28', 'BSB', 'Then my tongue will proclaim Your righteousness and Your praises all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.1', 'BSB', 'An oracle is in my heart regarding the transgression of the wicked man: There is no fear of God before his eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.2', 'BSB', 'For his eyes are too full of conceit to detect or hate his own sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.3', 'BSB', 'The words of his mouth are wicked and deceitful; he has ceased to be wise and well-doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.4', 'BSB', 'Even on his bed he plots wickedness; he sets himself on a path that is not good; he fails to reject evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.5', 'BSB', 'Your loving devotion, O LORD, reaches to the heavens, Your faithfulness to the clouds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.6', 'BSB', 'Your righteousness is like the highest mountains; Your judgments are like the deepest sea. O LORD, You preserve man and beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.7', 'BSB', 'How precious is Your loving devotion, O God, that the children of men take refuge in the shadow of Your wings!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.8', 'BSB', 'They feast on the abundance of Your house, and You give them drink from Your river of delights.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.9', 'BSB', 'For with You is the fountain of life; in Your light we see light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.10', 'BSB', 'Extend Your loving devotion to those who know You, and Your righteousness to the upright in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.11', 'BSB', 'Let not the foot of the proud come against me, nor the hand of the wicked drive me away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.36.12', 'BSB', 'There the evildoers lie fallen, thrown down and unable to rise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.1', 'BSB', 'Do not fret over those who do evil; do not envy those who do wrong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.2', 'BSB', 'For they wither quickly like grass and wilt like tender plants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.3', 'BSB', 'Trust in the LORD and do good; dwell in the land and cultivate faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.4', 'BSB', 'Delight yourself in the LORD, and He will give you the desires of your heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.5', 'BSB', 'Commit your way to the LORD; trust in Him, and He will do it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.6', 'BSB', 'He will bring forth your righteousness like the dawn, your justice like the noonday sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.7', 'BSB', 'Be still before the LORD and wait patiently for Him; do not fret when men prosper in their ways, when they carry out wicked schemes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.8', 'BSB', 'Refrain from anger and abandon wrath; do not fret—it can only bring harm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.9', 'BSB', 'For the evildoers will be cut off, but those who hope in the LORD will inherit the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.10', 'BSB', 'Yet a little while, and the wicked will be no more; though you look for them, they will not be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.11', 'BSB', 'But the meek will inherit the land and delight in abundant prosperity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.12', 'BSB', 'The wicked scheme against the righteous and gnash their teeth at them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.13', 'BSB', 'but the Lord laughs, seeing that their day is coming.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.14', 'BSB', 'The wicked have drawn the sword and bent the bow to bring down the poor and needy, to slay those whose ways are upright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.15', 'BSB', 'But their swords will pierce their own hearts, and their bows will be broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.16', 'BSB', 'Better is the little of the righteous than the abundance of many who are wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.17', 'BSB', 'For the arms of the wicked will be broken, but the LORD upholds the righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.18', 'BSB', 'The LORD knows the days of the blameless, and their inheritance will last forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.19', 'BSB', 'In the time of evil they will not be ashamed, and in the days of famine they will be satisfied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.20', 'BSB', 'But the wicked and enemies of the LORD will perish like the glory of the fields. They will vanish; like smoke they will fade away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.21', 'BSB', 'The wicked borrow and do not repay, but the righteous are gracious and giving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.22', 'BSB', 'Surely those He blesses will inherit the land, but the cursed will be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.23', 'BSB', 'The steps of a man are ordered by the LORD who takes delight in his journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.24', 'BSB', 'Though he falls, he will not be overwhelmed, for the LORD is holding his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.25', 'BSB', 'I once was young and now am old, yet never have I seen the righteous abandoned or their children begging for bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.26', 'BSB', 'They are ever generous and quick to lend, and their children are a blessing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.27', 'BSB', 'Turn away from evil and do good, so that you will abide forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.28', 'BSB', 'For the LORD loves justice and will not forsake His saints. They are preserved forever, but the offspring of the wicked will be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.29', 'BSB', 'The righteous will inherit the land and dwell in it forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.30', 'BSB', 'The mouth of the righteous man utters wisdom, and his tongue speaks justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.31', 'BSB', 'The law of his God is in his heart; his steps do not falter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.32', 'BSB', 'Though the wicked lie in wait for the righteous, and seek to slay them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.33', 'BSB', 'the LORD will not leave them in their power or let them be condemned under judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.34', 'BSB', 'Wait for the LORD and keep His way, and He will raise you up to inherit the land. When the wicked are cut off, you will see it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.35', 'BSB', 'I have seen a wicked, ruthless man flourishing like a well-rooted native tree,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.36', 'BSB', 'yet he passed away and was no more; though I searched, he could not be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.37', 'BSB', 'Consider the blameless and observe the upright, for posterity awaits the man of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.38', 'BSB', 'But the transgressors will all be destroyed; the future of the wicked will be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.39', 'BSB', 'The salvation of the righteous is from the LORD; He is their stronghold in time of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.37.40', 'BSB', 'The LORD helps and delivers them; He rescues and saves them from the wicked, because they take refuge in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.2', 'BSB', 'For Your arrows have pierced me deeply, and Your hand has pressed down on me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.3', 'BSB', 'There is no soundness in my body because of Your anger; there is no rest in my bones because of my sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.4', 'BSB', 'For my iniquities have overwhelmed me; they are a burden too heavy to bear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.5', 'BSB', 'My wounds are foul and festering because of my sinful folly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.6', 'BSB', 'I am bent and brought low; all day long I go about mourning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.7', 'BSB', 'For my loins are full of burning pain, and no soundness remains in my body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.8', 'BSB', 'I am numb and badly crushed; I groan in anguish of heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.9', 'BSB', 'O Lord, my every desire is before You; my groaning is not hidden from You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.10', 'BSB', 'My heart pounds, my strength fails, and even the light of my eyes has faded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.11', 'BSB', 'My beloved and friends shun my disease, and my kinsmen stand at a distance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.12', 'BSB', 'Those who seek my life lay snares; those who wish me harm speak destruction, plotting deceit all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.13', 'BSB', 'But like a deaf man, I do not hear; and like a mute man, I do not open my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.14', 'BSB', 'I am like a man who cannot hear, whose mouth offers no reply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.15', 'BSB', 'I wait for You, O LORD; You will answer, O Lord my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.16', 'BSB', 'For I said, “Let them not gloat over me— those who taunt me when my foot slips.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.17', 'BSB', 'For I am ready to fall, and my pain is ever with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.18', 'BSB', 'Yes, I confess my iniquity; I am troubled by my sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.19', 'BSB', 'Many are my enemies without cause, and many hate me without reason.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.20', 'BSB', 'Those who repay my good with evil attack me for pursuing the good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.21', 'BSB', 'Do not forsake me, O LORD; be not far from me, O my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.38.22', 'BSB', 'Come quickly to help me, O Lord my Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.1', 'BSB', 'I said, “I will watch my ways so that I will not sin with my tongue; I will guard my mouth with a muzzle as long as the wicked are present.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.2', 'BSB', 'I was speechless and still; I remained silent, even from speaking good, and my sorrow was stirred.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.3', 'BSB', 'My heart grew hot within me; as I mused, the fire burned. Then I spoke with my tongue:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.4', 'BSB', '“Show me, O LORD, my end and the measure of my days. Let me know how fleeting my life is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.5', 'BSB', 'You, indeed, have made my days as handbreadths, and my lifetime as nothing before You. Truly each man at his best exists as but a breath. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.6', 'BSB', 'Surely every man goes about like a phantom; surely he bustles in vain; he heaps up riches not knowing who will haul them away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.7', 'BSB', 'And now, O Lord, for what do I wait? My hope is in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.8', 'BSB', 'Deliver me from all my transgressions; do not make me the reproach of fools.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.9', 'BSB', 'I have become mute; I do not open my mouth because of what You have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.10', 'BSB', 'Remove Your scourge from me; I am perishing by the force of Your hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.11', 'BSB', 'You discipline and correct a man for his iniquity, consuming like a moth what he holds dear; surely each man is but a vapor. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.12', 'BSB', 'Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear to my cry for help; do not be deaf to my weeping. For I am a foreigner dwelling with You, a stranger like all my fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.39.13', 'BSB', 'Turn Your gaze away from me, that I may again be cheered before I depart and am no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.1', 'BSB', 'I waited patiently for the LORD; He inclined to me and heard my cry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.2', 'BSB', 'He lifted me up from the pit of despair, out of the miry clay; He set my feet upon a rock, and made my footsteps firm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.3', 'BSB', 'He put a new song in my mouth, a hymn of praise to our God. Many will see and fear and put their trust in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.4', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man who has made the LORD his trust, who has not turned to the proud, nor to those who lapse into falsehood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.5', 'BSB', 'Many, O LORD my God, are the wonders You have done, and the plans You have for us— none can compare to You— if I proclaim and declare them, they are more than I can count.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.6', 'BSB', 'Sacrifice and offering You did not desire, but my ears You have opened. Burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not require.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.7', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “Here I am, I have come— it is written about me in the scroll:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.8', 'BSB', 'I delight to do Your will, O my God; Your law is within my heart.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.9', 'BSB', 'I proclaim righteousness in the great assembly; behold, I do not seal my lips, as You, O LORD, do know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.10', 'BSB', 'I have not covered up Your righteousness in my heart; I have declared Your faithfulness and salvation; I have not concealed Your loving devotion and faithfulness from the great assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.11', 'BSB', 'O LORD, do not withhold Your mercy from me; Your loving devotion and faithfulness will always guard me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.12', 'BSB', 'For evils without number surround me; my sins have overtaken me, so that I cannot see. They are more than the hairs of my head, and my heart has failed within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.13', 'BSB', 'Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me; hurry, O LORD, to help me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.14', 'BSB', 'May those who seek my life be ashamed and confounded; may those who wish me harm be repelled and humiliated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.15', 'BSB', 'May those who say to me, “Aha, aha!” be appalled at their own shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.16', 'BSB', 'May all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You; may those who love Your salvation always say, “The LORD be magnified!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.40.17', 'BSB', 'But I am poor and needy; may the Lord think of me. You are my helper and deliverer; O my God, do not delay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.1', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the one who cares for the poor; the LORD will deliver him in the day of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD will protect and preserve him; He will bless him in the land and refuse to surrender him to the will of his foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.3', 'BSB', 'The LORD will sustain him on his bed of illness and restore him from his bed of sickness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.4', 'BSB', 'I said, “O LORD, be gracious to me; heal me, for I have sinned against You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.5', 'BSB', 'My enemies say with malice: “When will he die and be forgotten?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.6', 'BSB', 'My visitor speaks falsehood; he gathers slander in his heart; he goes out and spreads it abroad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.7', 'BSB', 'All who hate me whisper against me; they imagine the worst for me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.8', 'BSB', '“A vile disease has been poured into him; he will never get up from where he lies!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.9', 'BSB', 'Even my close friend whom I trusted, the one who shared my bread, has lifted up his heel against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.10', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, be gracious to me and raise me up, that I may repay them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.11', 'BSB', 'By this I know that You delight in me, for my enemy does not triumph over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.12', 'BSB', 'In my integrity You uphold me and set me in Your presence forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.41.13', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting. Amen and Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.1', 'BSB', 'As the deer pants for streams of water, so my soul longs after You, O God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.2', 'BSB', 'My soul thirsts for God, the living God. When shall I come and appear in God’s presence?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.3', 'BSB', 'My tears have been my food both day and night, while men ask me all day long, “Where is your God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.4', 'BSB', 'These things come to mind as I pour out my soul: how I walked with the multitude, leading the procession to the house of God with shouts of joy and praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.5', 'BSB', 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him for the salvation of His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.6', 'BSB', 'O my God, my soul despairs within me. Therefore I remember You from the land of Jordan and the peaks of Hermon— even from Mount Mizar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.7', 'BSB', 'Deep calls to deep in the roar of Your waterfalls; all Your breakers and waves have rolled over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD decrees His loving devotion by day, and at night His song is with me as a prayer to the God of my life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.9', 'BSB', 'I say to God my Rock, “Why have You forgotten me? Why must I walk in sorrow because of the enemy’s oppression?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.10', 'BSB', 'Like the crushing of my bones, my enemies taunt me, while they say to me all day long, “Where is your God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.42.11', 'BSB', 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him, my Savior and my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.43.1', 'BSB', 'Vindicate me, O God, and plead my case against an ungodly nation; deliver me from deceitful and unjust men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.43.2', 'BSB', 'For You are the God of my refuge. Why have You rejected me? Why must I walk in sorrow because of the enemy’s oppression?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.43.3', 'BSB', 'Send out Your light and Your truth; let them lead me. Let them bring me to Your holy mountain, and to the place where You dwell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.43.4', 'BSB', 'Then I will go to the altar of God, to God, my greatest joy. I will praise You with the harp, O God, my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.43.5', 'BSB', 'Why are you downcast, O my soul? Why the unease within me? Put your hope in God, for I will yet praise Him, my Savior and my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.1', 'BSB', 'We have heard with our ears, O God; our fathers have told us the work You did in their days, in the days of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.2', 'BSB', 'With Your hand You drove out the nations and planted our fathers there; You crushed the peoples and cast them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.3', 'BSB', 'For it was not by their sword that they took the land; their arm did not bring them victory. It was by Your right hand, Your arm, and the light of Your face, because You favored them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.4', 'BSB', 'You are my King, O God, who ordains victories for Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.5', 'BSB', 'Through You we repel our foes; through Your name we trample our enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.6', 'BSB', 'For I do not trust in my bow, nor does my sword save me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.7', 'BSB', 'For You save us from our enemies; You put those who hate us to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.8', 'BSB', 'In God we have boasted all day long, and Your name we will praise forever. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.9', 'BSB', 'But You have rejected and humbled us; You no longer go forth with our armies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.10', 'BSB', 'You have made us retreat from the foe, and those who hate us have plundered us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.11', 'BSB', 'You have given us up as sheep to be devoured; You have scattered us among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.12', 'BSB', 'You sell Your people for nothing; no profit do You gain from their sale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.13', 'BSB', 'You have made us a reproach to our neighbors, a mockery and derision to those around us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.14', 'BSB', 'You have made us a byword among the nations, a laughingstock among the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.15', 'BSB', 'All day long my disgrace is before me, and shame has covered my face,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.16', 'BSB', 'at the voice of the scorner and reviler, because of the enemy, bent on revenge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.17', 'BSB', 'All this has come upon us, though we have not forgotten You or betrayed Your covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.18', 'BSB', 'Our hearts have not turned back; our steps have not strayed from Your path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.19', 'BSB', 'But You have crushed us in the lair of jackals; You have covered us with deepest darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.20', 'BSB', 'If we had forgotten the name of our God or spread out our hands to a foreign god,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.21', 'BSB', 'would not God have discovered, since He knows the secrets of the heart?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.22', 'BSB', 'Yet for Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.23', 'BSB', 'Wake up, O Lord! Why are You sleeping? Arise! Do not reject us forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.24', 'BSB', 'Why do You hide Your face and forget our affliction and oppression?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.25', 'BSB', 'For our soul has sunk to the dust; our bodies cling to the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.44.26', 'BSB', 'Rise up; be our help! Redeem us on account of Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.1', 'BSB', 'My heart is stirred by a noble theme as I recite my verses to the king; my tongue is the pen of a skillful writer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.2', 'BSB', 'You are the most handsome of men; grace has anointed your lips, since God has blessed you forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.3', 'BSB', 'Strap your sword at your side, O mighty warrior; appear in your majesty and splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.4', 'BSB', 'In your splendor ride forth in victory on behalf of truth and humility and justice; may your right hand show your awesome deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.5', 'BSB', 'Your arrows pierce the hearts of the king’s foes; the nations fall beneath your feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.6', 'BSB', 'Your throne, O God, endures forever and ever, and justice is the scepter of Your kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.7', 'BSB', 'You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; therefore God, your God, has anointed you above your companions with the oil of joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.8', 'BSB', 'All your garments are fragrant with myrrh and aloes and cassia; from palaces of ivory the harps make you glad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.9', 'BSB', 'The daughters of kings are among your honored women; the queen stands at your right hand, adorned with the gold of Ophir.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.10', 'BSB', 'Listen, O daughter! Consider and incline your ear: Forget your people and your father’s house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.11', 'BSB', 'and the king will desire your beauty; bow to him, for he is your lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.12', 'BSB', 'The Daughter of Tyre will come with a gift; men of wealth will seek your favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.13', 'BSB', 'All glorious is the princess in her chamber; her gown is embroidered with gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.14', 'BSB', 'In colorful garments she is led to the king; her virgin companions are brought before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.15', 'BSB', 'They are led in with joy and gladness; they enter the palace of the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.16', 'BSB', 'Your sons will succeed your fathers; you will make them princes throughout the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.45.17', 'BSB', 'I will commemorate your name through all generations; therefore the nations will praise you forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.1', 'BSB', 'God is our refuge and strength, an ever-present help in times of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.2', 'BSB', 'Therefore we will not fear, though the earth is transformed and the mountains are toppled into the depths of the seas,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.3', 'BSB', 'though their waters roar and foam and the mountains quake in the surge. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.4', 'BSB', 'There is a river whose streams delight the city of God, the holy place where the Most High dwells.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.5', 'BSB', 'God is within her; she will not be moved. God will help her when morning dawns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.6', 'BSB', 'Nations rage, kingdoms crumble; the earth melts when He lifts His voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.7', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our fortress. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.8', 'BSB', 'Come, see the works of the LORD, who brings devastation upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.9', 'BSB', 'He makes wars to cease throughout the earth; He breaks the bow and shatters the spear; He burns the shields in the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.10', 'BSB', '“Be still and know that I am God; I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted over the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.46.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our fortress. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.1', 'BSB', 'Clap your hands, all you peoples; shout unto God with a voice of triumph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.2', 'BSB', 'How awesome is the LORD Most High, the great King over all the earth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.3', 'BSB', 'He subdues nations beneath us, and peoples under our feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.4', 'BSB', 'He chooses our inheritance for us, the pride of Jacob, whom He loves. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.5', 'BSB', 'God has ascended amid shouts of joy, the LORD with the sound of the horn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.6', 'BSB', 'Sing praises to God, sing praises; sing praises to our King, sing praises!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.7', 'BSB', 'For God is King of all the earth; sing profound praises to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.8', 'BSB', 'God reigns over the nations; God is seated on His holy throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.47.9', 'BSB', 'The nobles of the nations have assembled as the people of the God of Abraham; for the shields of the earth belong to God; He is highly exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.1', 'BSB', 'Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, His holy mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.2', 'BSB', 'Beautiful in loftiness, the joy of all the earth, like the peaks of Zaphon is Mount Zion, the city of the great King.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.3', 'BSB', 'God is in her citadels; He has shown Himself to be a fortress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.4', 'BSB', 'For behold, the kings assembled; they all advanced together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.5', 'BSB', 'They saw and were astounded; they fled in terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.6', 'BSB', 'Trembling seized them there, anguish like a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.7', 'BSB', 'With a wind from the east You wrecked the ships of Tarshish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.8', 'BSB', 'As we have heard, so we have seen in the city of the LORD of Hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish her forever. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.9', 'BSB', 'Within Your temple, O God, we contemplate Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.10', 'BSB', 'Your name, O God, like Your praise, reaches to the ends of the earth; Your right hand is full of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.11', 'BSB', 'Mount Zion is glad, the daughters of Judah rejoice, on account of Your judgments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.12', 'BSB', 'March around Zion, encircle her, count her towers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.13', 'BSB', 'consider her ramparts, tour her citadels, that you may tell the next generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.48.14', 'BSB', 'For this God is our God forever and ever; He will be our guide even till death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.1', 'BSB', 'Hear this, all you peoples; listen, all inhabitants of the world,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.2', 'BSB', 'both low and high, rich and poor alike.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.3', 'BSB', 'My mouth will impart wisdom, and the meditation of my heart will bring understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.4', 'BSB', 'I will incline my ear to a proverb; I will express my riddle with the harp:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.5', 'BSB', 'Why should I fear in times of trouble, when wicked usurpers surround me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.6', 'BSB', 'They trust in their wealth and boast in their great riches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.7', 'BSB', 'No man can possibly redeem his brother or pay his ransom to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.8', 'BSB', 'For the redemption of his soul is costly, and never can payment suffice,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.9', 'BSB', 'that he should live on forever and not see decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.10', 'BSB', 'For it is clear that wise men die, and the foolish and the senseless both perish and leave their wealth to others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.11', 'BSB', 'Their graves are their eternal homes— their dwellings for endless generations— even though their lands were their namesakes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.12', 'BSB', 'But a man, despite his wealth, cannot endure; he is like the beasts that perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.13', 'BSB', 'This is the fate of the self-confident and their followers who endorse their sayings. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.14', 'BSB', 'Like sheep they are destined for Sheol. Death will be their shepherd. The upright will rule them in the morning, and their form will decay in Sheol, far from their lofty abode.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.15', 'BSB', 'But God will redeem my life from Sheol, for He will surely take me to Himself. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.16', 'BSB', 'Do not be amazed when a man grows rich, when the splendor of his house increases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.17', 'BSB', 'For when he dies, he will carry nothing away; his abundance will not follow him down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.18', 'BSB', 'Though in his lifetime he blesses his soul— and men praise you when you prosper—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.19', 'BSB', 'he will join the generation of his fathers, who will never see the light of day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.49.20', 'BSB', 'A man who has riches without understanding is like the beasts that perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.1', 'BSB', 'The Mighty One, God the LORD, speaks and summons the earth from where the sun rises to where it sets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.2', 'BSB', 'From Zion, perfect in beauty, God shines forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.3', 'BSB', 'Our God approaches and will not be silent! Consuming fire precedes Him, and a tempest rages around Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.4', 'BSB', 'He summons the heavens above, and the earth, that He may judge His people:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.5', 'BSB', '“Gather to Me My saints, who made a covenant with Me by sacrifice.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.6', 'BSB', 'And the heavens proclaim His righteousness, for God Himself is Judge. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.7', 'BSB', '“Hear, O My people, and I will speak, O Israel, and I will testify against you: I am God, your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.8', 'BSB', 'I do not rebuke you for your sacrifices, and your burnt offerings are ever before Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.9', 'BSB', 'I have no need for a bull from your stall or goats from your pens,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.10', 'BSB', 'for every beast of the forest is Mine— the cattle on a thousand hills.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.11', 'BSB', 'I know every bird in the mountains, and the creatures of the field are Mine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.12', 'BSB', 'If I were hungry, I would not tell you, for the world is Mine, and the fullness thereof.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.13', 'BSB', 'Do I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.14', 'BSB', 'Sacrifice a thank offering to God, and fulfill your vows to the Most High.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.15', 'BSB', 'Call upon Me in the day of trouble; I will deliver you, and you will honor Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.16', 'BSB', 'To the wicked, however, God says, “What right have you to recite My statutes and to bear My covenant on your lips?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.17', 'BSB', 'For you hate My instruction and cast My words behind you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.18', 'BSB', 'When you see a thief, you befriend him, and throw in your lot with adulterers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.19', 'BSB', 'You unleash your mouth for evil and unharness your tongue for deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.20', 'BSB', 'You sit and malign your brother; you slander your own mother’s son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.21', 'BSB', 'You have done these things, and I kept silent; you thought I was just like you. But now I rebuke you and accuse you to your face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.22', 'BSB', 'Now consider this, you who forget God, lest I tear you to pieces, with no one to rescue you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.50.23', 'BSB', 'He who sacrifices a thank offering honors Me, and to him who rights his way, I will show the salvation of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.1', 'BSB', 'Have mercy on me, O God, according to Your loving devotion; according to Your great compassion, blot out my transgressions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.2', 'BSB', 'Wash me clean of my iniquity and cleanse me from my sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.3', 'BSB', 'For I know my transgressions, and my sin is always before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.4', 'BSB', 'Against You, You only, have I sinned and done what is evil in Your sight, so that You may be proved right when You speak and blameless when You judge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.5', 'BSB', 'Surely I was brought forth in iniquity; I was sinful when my mother conceived me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.6', 'BSB', 'Surely You desire truth in the inmost being; You teach me wisdom in the inmost place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.7', 'BSB', 'Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean; wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.8', 'BSB', 'Let me hear joy and gladness; let the bones You have crushed rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.9', 'BSB', 'Hide Your face from my sins and blot out all my iniquities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.10', 'BSB', 'Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.11', 'BSB', 'Cast me not away from Your presence; take not Your Holy Spirit from me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.12', 'BSB', 'Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, and sustain me with a willing spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.13', 'BSB', 'Then I will teach transgressors Your ways, and sinners will return to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.14', 'BSB', 'Deliver me from bloodguilt, O God, the God of my salvation, and my tongue will sing of Your righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.15', 'BSB', 'O Lord, open my lips, and my mouth will declare Your praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.16', 'BSB', 'For You do not delight in sacrifice, or I would bring it; You take no pleasure in burnt offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.17', 'BSB', 'The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit; a broken and a contrite heart, O God, You will not despise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.18', 'BSB', 'In Your good pleasure, cause Zion to prosper; build up the walls of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.51.19', 'BSB', 'Then You will delight in righteous sacrifices, in whole burnt offerings; then bulls will be offered on Your altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.1', 'BSB', 'Why do you boast of evil, O mighty man? The loving devotion of God endures all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.2', 'BSB', 'Your tongue devises destruction like a sharpened razor, O worker of deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.3', 'BSB', 'You love evil more than good, falsehood more than speaking truth. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.4', 'BSB', 'You love every word that devours, O deceitful tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.5', 'BSB', 'Surely God will bring you down to everlasting ruin; He will snatch you up and tear you away from your tent; He will uproot you from the land of the living. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.6', 'BSB', 'The righteous will see and fear; they will mock the evildoer, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.7', 'BSB', '“Look at the man who did not make God his refuge, but trusted in the abundance of his wealth and strengthened himself by destruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.8', 'BSB', 'But I am like an olive tree flourishing in the house of God; I trust in the loving devotion of God forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.52.9', 'BSB', 'I will praise You forever, because You have done it. I will wait on Your name— for it is good— in the presence of Your saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.1', 'BSB', 'The fool says in his heart, “There is no God.” They are corrupt; their ways are vile. There is no one who does good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.2', 'BSB', 'God looks down from heaven upon the sons of men to see if any understand, if any seek God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.3', 'BSB', 'All have turned away, they have together become corrupt; there is no one who does good, not even one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.4', 'BSB', 'Will the workers of iniquity never learn? They devour my people like bread; they refuse to call upon God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.5', 'BSB', 'There they are, overwhelmed with dread, where there was nothing to fear. For God has scattered the bones of those who besieged you. You put them to shame, for God has despised them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.53.6', 'BSB', 'Oh, that the salvation of Israel would come from Zion! When God restores His captive people, let Jacob rejoice, let Israel be glad!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.1', 'BSB', 'Save me, O God, by Your name, and vindicate me by Your might!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.2', 'BSB', 'Hear my prayer, O God; listen to the words of my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.3', 'BSB', 'For strangers rise up against me, and ruthless men seek my life— men with no regard for God. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.4', 'BSB', 'Surely God is my helper; the Lord is the sustainer of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.5', 'BSB', 'He will reward my enemies with evil. In Your faithfulness, destroy them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.6', 'BSB', 'Freely I will sacrifice to You; I will praise Your name, O LORD, for it is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.54.7', 'BSB', 'For He has delivered me from every trouble, and my eyes have stared down my foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.1', 'BSB', 'Listen to my prayer, O God, and do not ignore my plea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.2', 'BSB', 'Attend to me and answer me. I am restless in my complaint, and distraught', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.3', 'BSB', 'at the voice of the enemy, at the pressure of the wicked. For they release disaster upon me and revile me in their anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.4', 'BSB', 'My heart murmurs within me, and the terrors of death assail me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.5', 'BSB', 'Fear and trembling grip me, and horror has overwhelmed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.6', 'BSB', 'I said, “Oh, that I had wings like a dove! I would fly away and find rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.7', 'BSB', 'How far away I would flee! In the wilderness I would remain. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.8', 'BSB', 'I would hurry to my shelter, far from this raging tempest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.9', 'BSB', 'O Lord, confuse and confound their speech, for I see violence and strife in the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.10', 'BSB', 'Day and night they encircle the walls, while malice and trouble lie within.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.11', 'BSB', 'Destruction is within; oppression and deceit never leave the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.12', 'BSB', 'For it is not an enemy who insults me; that I could endure. It is not a foe who rises against me; from him I could hide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.13', 'BSB', 'But it is you, a man like myself, my companion and close friend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.14', 'BSB', 'We shared sweet fellowship together; we walked with the crowd into the house of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.15', 'BSB', 'Let death seize them by surprise; let them go down to Sheol alive, for evil is with them in their homes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.16', 'BSB', 'But I call to God, and the LORD saves me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.17', 'BSB', 'Morning, noon, and night, I cry out in distress, and He hears my voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.18', 'BSB', 'He redeems my soul in peace from the battle waged against me, even though many oppose me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.19', 'BSB', 'God will hear and humiliate them— the One enthroned for the ages— Selah because they do not change and they have no fear of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.20', 'BSB', 'My companion attacks his friends; he violates his covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.21', 'BSB', 'His speech is smooth as butter, but war is in his heart. His words are softer than oil, yet they are swords unsheathed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.22', 'BSB', 'Cast your burden upon the LORD and He will sustain you; He will never let the righteous be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.55.23', 'BSB', 'But You, O God, will bring them down to the Pit of destruction; men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days. But I will trust in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.1', 'BSB', 'Be merciful to me, O God, for men are hounding me; all day they press their attack.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.2', 'BSB', 'My enemies pursue me all day long, for many proudly assail me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.3', 'BSB', 'When I am afraid, I put my trust in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.4', 'BSB', 'In God, whose word I praise— in God I trust. I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.5', 'BSB', 'All day long they twist my words; all their thoughts are on my demise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.6', 'BSB', 'They conspire, they lurk, they watch my steps while they wait to take my life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.7', 'BSB', 'In spite of such sin, will they escape? In Your anger, O God, cast down the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.8', 'BSB', 'You have taken account of my wanderings. Put my tears in Your bottle— are they not in Your book?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.9', 'BSB', 'Then my enemies will retreat on the day I cry for help. By this I will know that God is on my side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.10', 'BSB', 'In God, whose word I praise, in the LORD, whose word I praise,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.11', 'BSB', 'in God I trust; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.12', 'BSB', 'Your vows are upon me, O God; I will render thank offerings to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.56.13', 'BSB', 'For You have delivered my soul from death, and my feet from stumbling, that I may walk before God in the light of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.1', 'BSB', 'Have mercy on me, O God, have mercy, for in You my soul takes refuge. In the shadow of Your wings I will take shelter until the danger has passed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.2', 'BSB', 'I cry out to God Most High, to God who fulfills His purpose for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.3', 'BSB', 'He reaches down from heaven and saves me; He rebukes those who trample me. Selah God sends forth His loving devotion and His truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.4', 'BSB', 'My soul is among the lions; I lie down with ravenous beasts— with men whose teeth are spears and arrows, whose tongues are sharp swords.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.5', 'BSB', 'Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.6', 'BSB', 'They spread a net for my feet; my soul was despondent. They dug a pit before me, but they themselves have fallen into it! Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.7', 'BSB', 'My heart is steadfast, O God, my heart is steadfast. I will sing and make music.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.8', 'BSB', 'Awake, my glory! Awake, O harp and lyre! I will awaken the dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.9', 'BSB', 'I will praise You, O Lord, among the nations; I will sing Your praises among the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.10', 'BSB', 'For Your loving devotion reaches to the heavens, and Your faithfulness to the clouds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.57.11', 'BSB', 'Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.1', 'BSB', 'Do you indeed speak justly, O rulers? Do you judge uprightly, O sons of men?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.2', 'BSB', 'No, in your hearts you devise injustice; with your hands you mete out violence on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.3', 'BSB', 'The wicked are estranged from the womb; the liars go astray from birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.4', 'BSB', 'Their venom is like the venom of a snake, like a cobra that shuts its ears,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.5', 'BSB', 'refusing to hear the tune of the charmer who skillfully weaves his spell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.6', 'BSB', 'O God, shatter their teeth in their mouths; O LORD, tear out the fangs of the lions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.7', 'BSB', 'May they vanish like water that runs off; when they draw the bow, may their arrows be blunted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.8', 'BSB', 'Like a slug that dissolves in its slime, like a woman’s stillborn child, may they never see the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.9', 'BSB', 'Before your pots can feel the burning thorns— whether green or dry— He will sweep them away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.10', 'BSB', 'The righteous will rejoice when they see they are avenged; they will wash their feet in the blood of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.58.11', 'BSB', 'Then men will say, “There is surely a reward for the righteous! There is surely a God who judges the earth!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.1', 'BSB', 'Deliver me from my enemies, O my God; protect me from those who rise against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.2', 'BSB', 'Deliver me from workers of iniquity, and save me from men of bloodshed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.3', 'BSB', 'See how they lie in wait for me. Fierce men conspire against me for no transgression or sin of my own, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.4', 'BSB', 'For no fault of my own, they move swiftly to attack me. Arise to help me, and take notice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.5', 'BSB', 'O LORD God of Hosts, the God of Israel, rouse Yourself to punish all the nations; show no mercy to the wicked traitors. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.6', 'BSB', 'They return in the evening, snarling like dogs and prowling around the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.7', 'BSB', 'See what they spew from their mouths— sharp words from their lips: “For who can hear us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.8', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, laugh at them; You scoff at all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.9', 'BSB', 'I will keep watch for You, O my strength, because You, O God, are my fortress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.10', 'BSB', 'My God of loving devotion will come to meet me; God will let me stare down my foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.11', 'BSB', 'Do not kill them, or my people will forget. Scatter them by Your power, and bring them down, O Lord, our shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.12', 'BSB', 'By the sins of their mouths and the words of their lips, let them be trapped in their pride, in the curses and lies they utter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.13', 'BSB', 'Consume them in wrath; consume them till they are no more, so it may be known to the ends of the earth that God rules over Jacob. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.14', 'BSB', 'They return in the evening, snarling like dogs and prowling around the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.15', 'BSB', 'They scavenge for food, and growl if they are not satisfied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.16', 'BSB', 'But I will sing of Your strength and proclaim Your loving devotion in the morning. For You are my fortress, my refuge in times of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.59.17', 'BSB', 'To You, O my strength, I sing praises, for You, O God, are my fortress, my God of loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.1', 'BSB', 'You have rejected us, O God; You have broken us; You have been angry; restore us!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.2', 'BSB', 'You have shaken the land and torn it open. Heal its fractures, for it is quaking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.3', 'BSB', 'You have shown Your people hardship; we are staggered from the wine You made us drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.4', 'BSB', 'You have raised a banner for those who fear You, that they may flee the bow. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.5', 'BSB', 'Respond and save us with Your right hand, that Your beloved may be delivered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.6', 'BSB', 'God has spoken from His sanctuary: “I will triumph! I will parcel out Shechem and apportion the Valley of Succoth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.7', 'BSB', 'Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine; Ephraim is My helmet, Judah is My scepter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.8', 'BSB', 'Moab is My washbasin; upon Edom I toss My sandal; over Philistia I shout in triumph.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.9', 'BSB', 'Who will bring me to the fortified city? Who will lead me to Edom?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.10', 'BSB', 'Have You not rejected us, O God? Will You no longer march out, O God, with our armies?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.11', 'BSB', 'Give us aid against the enemy, for the help of man is worthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.60.12', 'BSB', 'With God we will perform with valor, and He will trample our enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.1', 'BSB', 'Hear my cry, O God; attend to my prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.2', 'BSB', 'From the ends of the earth I call out to You whenever my heart is faint. Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.3', 'BSB', 'For You have been my refuge, a tower of strength against the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.4', 'BSB', 'Let me dwell in Your tent forever and take refuge in the shelter of Your wings. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.5', 'BSB', 'For You have heard my vows, O God; You have given me the inheritance reserved for those who fear Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.6', 'BSB', 'Increase the days of the king’s life; may his years span many generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.7', 'BSB', 'May he sit enthroned in God’s presence forever; appoint Your loving devotion and Your faithfulness to guard him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.61.8', 'BSB', 'Then I will ever sing praise to Your name and fulfill my vows day by day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.1', 'BSB', 'In God alone my soul finds rest; my salvation comes from Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.2', 'BSB', 'He alone is my rock and my salvation. He is my fortress; I will never be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.3', 'BSB', 'How long will you threaten a man? Will all of you throw him down like a leaning wall or a tottering fence?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.4', 'BSB', 'They fully intend to cast him down from his lofty perch; they delight in lies; with their mouths they bless, but inwardly they curse. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.5', 'BSB', 'Rest in God alone, O my soul, for my hope comes from Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.6', 'BSB', 'He alone is my rock and my salvation; He is my fortress; I will not be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.7', 'BSB', 'My salvation and my honor rest on God, my strong rock; my refuge is in God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.8', 'BSB', 'Trust in Him at all times, O people; pour out your hearts before Him. God is our refuge. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.9', 'BSB', 'Lowborn men are but a vapor, the exalted but a lie. Weighed on the scale, they go up; together they are but a vapor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.10', 'BSB', 'Place no trust in extortion, or false hope in stolen goods. If your riches increase, do not set your heart upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.11', 'BSB', 'God has spoken once; I have heard this twice: that power belongs to God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.62.12', 'BSB', 'and loving devotion to You, O Lord. For You will repay each man according to his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.1', 'BSB', 'O God, You are my God. Earnestly I seek You; my soul thirsts for You. My body yearns for You in a dry and weary land without water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.2', 'BSB', 'So I have seen You in the sanctuary and beheld Your power and glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.3', 'BSB', 'Because Your loving devotion is better than life, my lips will glorify You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.4', 'BSB', 'So I will bless You as long as I live; in Your name I will lift my hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.5', 'BSB', 'My soul is satisfied as with the richest of foods; with joyful lips my mouth will praise You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.6', 'BSB', 'When I remember You on my bed, I think of You through the watches of the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.7', 'BSB', 'For You are my help; I will sing for joy in the shadow of Your wings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.8', 'BSB', 'My soul clings to You; Your right hand upholds me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.9', 'BSB', 'But those who seek my life to destroy it will go into the depths of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.10', 'BSB', 'They will fall to the power of the sword; they will become a portion for foxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.63.11', 'BSB', 'But the king will rejoice in God; all who swear by Him will exult, for the mouths of liars will be shut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.1', 'BSB', 'Hear, O God, my voice of complaint; preserve my life from dread of the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.2', 'BSB', 'Hide me from the scheming of the wicked, from the mob of workers of iniquity,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.3', 'BSB', 'who sharpen their tongues like swords and aim their bitter words like arrows,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.4', 'BSB', 'ambushing the innocent in seclusion, shooting suddenly, without fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.5', 'BSB', 'They hold fast to their evil purpose; they speak of hiding their snares. “Who will see them?” they say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.6', 'BSB', 'They devise injustice and say, “We have perfected a secret plan.” For the inner man and the heart are mysterious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.7', 'BSB', 'But God will shoot them with arrows; suddenly they will be wounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.8', 'BSB', 'They will be made to stumble, their own tongues turned against them. All who see will shake their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.9', 'BSB', 'Then all mankind will fear and proclaim the work of God; so they will ponder what He has done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.64.10', 'BSB', 'Let the righteous rejoice in the LORD and take refuge in Him; let all the upright in heart exult.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.1', 'BSB', 'Praise awaits You, O God, in Zion; to You our vows will be fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.2', 'BSB', 'O You who listen to prayer, all people will come to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.3', 'BSB', 'When iniquities prevail against me, You atone for our transgressions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.4', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the one You choose and bring near to dwell in Your courts! We are filled with the goodness of Your house, the holiness of Your temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.5', 'BSB', 'With awesome deeds of righteousness You answer us, O God of our salvation, the hope of all the ends of the earth and of the farthest seas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.6', 'BSB', 'You formed the mountains by Your power, having girded Yourself with might.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.7', 'BSB', 'You stilled the roaring of the seas, the pounding of their waves, and the tumult of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.8', 'BSB', 'Those who live far away fear Your wonders; You make the dawn and sunset shout for joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.9', 'BSB', 'You attend to the earth and water it; with abundance You enrich it. The streams of God are full of water, for You prepare our grain by providing for the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.10', 'BSB', 'You soak its furrows and level its ridges; You soften it with showers and bless its growth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.11', 'BSB', 'You crown the year with Your bounty, and Your paths overflow with plenty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.12', 'BSB', 'The pastures of the wilderness overflow; the hills are robed with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.65.13', 'BSB', 'The pastures are clothed with flocks, and the valleys are decked with grain. They shout in triumph; indeed, they sing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.1', 'BSB', 'Make a joyful noise to God, all the earth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.2', 'BSB', 'Sing the glory of His name; make His praise glorious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.3', 'BSB', 'Say to God, “How awesome are Your deeds! So great is Your power that Your enemies cower before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.4', 'BSB', 'All the earth bows down to You; they sing praise to You; they sing praise to Your name.” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.5', 'BSB', 'Come and see the works of God; how awesome are His deeds toward mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.6', 'BSB', 'He turned the sea into dry land; they passed through the waters on foot; there we rejoiced in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.7', 'BSB', 'He rules forever by His power; His eyes watch the nations. Do not let the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.8', 'BSB', 'Bless our God, O peoples; let the sound of His praise be heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.9', 'BSB', 'He preserves our lives and keeps our feet from slipping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.10', 'BSB', 'For You, O God, have tested us; You have refined us like silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.11', 'BSB', 'You led us into the net; You laid burdens on our backs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.12', 'BSB', 'You let men ride over our heads; we went through fire and water, but You brought us into abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.13', 'BSB', 'I will enter Your house with burnt offerings; I will fulfill my vows to You—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.14', 'BSB', 'the vows that my lips promised and my mouth spoke in my distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.15', 'BSB', 'I will offer You fatlings as burnt offerings, with the fragrant smoke of rams; I will offer bulls and goats. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.16', 'BSB', 'Come and listen, all you who fear God, and I will declare what He has done for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.17', 'BSB', 'I cried out to Him with my mouth and praised Him with my tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.18', 'BSB', 'If I had cherished iniquity in my heart, the Lord would not have listened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.19', 'BSB', 'But God has surely heard; He has attended to the sound of my prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.66.20', 'BSB', 'Blessed be God, who has not rejected my prayer or withheld from me His loving devotion!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.1', 'BSB', 'May God be gracious to us and bless us, and cause His face to shine upon us, Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.2', 'BSB', 'that Your ways may be known on earth, Your salvation among all nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.3', 'BSB', 'Let the peoples praise You, O God; let all the peoples praise You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.4', 'BSB', 'Let the nations be glad and sing for joy, for You judge the peoples justly and lead the nations of the earth. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.5', 'BSB', 'Let the peoples praise You, O God; let all the peoples praise You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.6', 'BSB', 'The earth has yielded its harvest; God, our God, blesses us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.67.7', 'BSB', 'God blesses us, that all the ends of the earth shall fear Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.1', 'BSB', 'God arises. His enemies are scattered, and those who hate Him flee His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.2', 'BSB', 'As smoke is blown away, You will drive them out; as wax melts before the fire, the wicked will perish in the presence of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.3', 'BSB', 'But the righteous will be glad and rejoice before God; they will celebrate with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.4', 'BSB', 'Sing to God! Sing praises to His name. Exalt Him who rides on the clouds — His name is the LORD— and rejoice before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.5', 'BSB', 'A father of the fatherless, and a defender of the widows, is God in His holy habitation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.6', 'BSB', 'God settles the lonely in families; He leads the prisoners out to prosperity, but the rebellious dwell in a sun-scorched land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.7', 'BSB', 'O God, when You went out before Your people, when You marched through the wasteland, Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.8', 'BSB', 'the earth shook and the heavens poured down rain before God, the One on Sinai, before God, the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.9', 'BSB', 'You sent abundant rain, O God; You refreshed Your weary inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.10', 'BSB', 'Your flock settled therein; O God, from Your bounty You provided for the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.11', 'BSB', 'The Lord gives the command; a great company of women proclaim it:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.12', 'BSB', '“Kings and their armies flee in haste; she who waits at home divides the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.13', 'BSB', 'Though you lie down among the sheepfolds, the wings of the dove are covered with silver, and her feathers with shimmering gold.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.14', 'BSB', 'When the Almighty scattered the kings in the land, it was like the snow falling on Zalmon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.15', 'BSB', 'A mountain of God is Mount Bashan; a mountain of many peaks is Mount Bashan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.16', 'BSB', 'Why do you gaze in envy, O mountains of many peaks? This is the mountain God chose for His dwelling, where the LORD will surely dwell forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.17', 'BSB', 'The chariots of God are tens of thousands— thousands of thousands are they; the Lord is in His sanctuary as He was at Sinai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.18', 'BSB', 'You have ascended on high; You have led captives away. You have received gifts from men, even from the rebellious, that the LORD God may dwell there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.19', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the Lord, who daily bears our burden, the God of our salvation. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.20', 'BSB', 'Our God is a God of deliverance; the Lord GOD is our rescuer from death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.21', 'BSB', 'Surely God will crush the heads of His enemies, the hairy crowns of those who persist in guilty ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.22', 'BSB', 'The Lord said, “I will retrieve them from Bashan, I will bring them up from the depths of the sea,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.23', 'BSB', 'that your foot may be dipped in the blood of your foes— the tongues of your dogs in the same.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.24', 'BSB', 'They have seen Your procession, O God— the march of my God and King into the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.25', 'BSB', 'The singers lead the way, the musicians follow after, among the maidens playing tambourines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.26', 'BSB', 'Bless God in the great congregation; bless the LORD from the fountain of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.27', 'BSB', 'There is Benjamin, the youngest, ruling them, the princes of Judah in their company, the princes of Zebulun and of Naphtali.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.28', 'BSB', 'Summon Your power, O God; show Your strength, O God, which You have exerted on our behalf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.29', 'BSB', 'Because of Your temple at Jerusalem kings will bring You gifts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.30', 'BSB', 'Rebuke the beast in the reeds, the herd of bulls among the calves of the nations, until it submits, bringing bars of silver. Scatter the nations who delight in war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.31', 'BSB', 'Envoys will arrive from Egypt; Cush will stretch out her hands to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.32', 'BSB', 'Sing to God, O kingdoms of the earth; sing praises to the Lord— Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.33', 'BSB', 'to Him who rides upon the highest heavens of old; behold, His mighty voice resounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.34', 'BSB', 'Ascribe the power to God, whose majesty is over Israel, whose strength is in the skies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.68.35', 'BSB', 'O God, You are awesome in Your sanctuary; the God of Israel Himself gives strength and power to His people. Blessed be God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.1', 'BSB', 'Save me, O God, for the waters are up to my neck.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.2', 'BSB', 'I have sunk into the miry depths, where there is no footing; I have drifted into deep waters, where the flood engulfs me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.3', 'BSB', 'I am weary from my crying; my throat is parched. My eyes fail, looking for my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.4', 'BSB', 'Those who hate me without cause outnumber the hairs of my head; many are those who would destroy me— my enemies for no reason. Though I did not steal, I must repay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.5', 'BSB', 'You know my folly, O God, and my guilt is not hidden from You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.6', 'BSB', 'May those who hope in You not be ashamed through me, O Lord GOD of Hosts; may those who seek You not be dishonored through me, O God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.7', 'BSB', 'For I have endured scorn for Your sake, and shame has covered my face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.8', 'BSB', 'I have become a stranger to my brothers and a foreigner to my mother’s sons,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.9', 'BSB', 'because zeal for Your house has consumed me, and the insults of those who insult You have fallen on me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.10', 'BSB', 'I wept and fasted, but it brought me reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.11', 'BSB', 'I made sackcloth my clothing, and I was sport to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.12', 'BSB', 'Those who sit at the gate mock me, and I am the song of drunkards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.13', 'BSB', 'But my prayer to You, O LORD, is for a time of favor. In Your abundant loving devotion, O God, answer me with Your sure salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.14', 'BSB', 'Rescue me from the mire and do not let me sink; deliver me from my foes and out of the deep waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.15', 'BSB', 'Do not let the floods engulf me or the depths swallow me up; let not the Pit close its mouth over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.16', 'BSB', 'Answer me, O LORD, for Your loving devotion is good; turn to me in keeping with Your great compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.17', 'BSB', 'Hide not Your face from Your servant, for I am in distress. Answer me quickly!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.18', 'BSB', 'Draw near to my soul and redeem me; ransom me because of my foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.19', 'BSB', 'You know my reproach, my shame and disgrace. All my adversaries are before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.20', 'BSB', 'Insults have broken my heart, and I am in despair. I looked for sympathy, but there was none, for comforters, but I found no one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.21', 'BSB', 'They poisoned my food with gall and gave me vinegar to quench my thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.22', 'BSB', 'May their table become a snare; may it be a retribution and a trap.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.23', 'BSB', 'May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.24', 'BSB', 'Pour out Your wrath upon them, and let Your burning anger overtake them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.25', 'BSB', 'May their place be deserted; let there be no one to dwell in their tents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.26', 'BSB', 'For they persecute the one You struck and recount the pain of those You wounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.27', 'BSB', 'Add iniquity to their iniquity; let them not share in Your righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.28', 'BSB', 'May they be blotted out of the Book of Life and not listed with the righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.29', 'BSB', 'But I am in pain and distress; let Your salvation protect me, O God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.30', 'BSB', 'I will praise God’s name in song and exalt Him with thanksgiving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.31', 'BSB', 'And this will please the LORD more than an ox, more than a bull with horns and hooves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.32', 'BSB', 'The humble will see and rejoice. You who seek God, let your hearts be revived!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.33', 'BSB', 'For the LORD listens to the needy and does not despise His captive people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.34', 'BSB', 'Let heaven and earth praise Him, the seas and everything that moves in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.35', 'BSB', 'For God will save Zion and rebuild the cities of Judah, that they may dwell there and possess it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.69.36', 'BSB', 'The descendants of His servants will inherit it, and those who love His name will settle in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.70.1', 'BSB', 'Make haste, O God, to deliver me! Hurry, O LORD, to help me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.70.2', 'BSB', 'May those who seek my life be ashamed and confounded; may those who wish me harm be repelled and humiliated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.70.3', 'BSB', 'May those who say, “Aha, aha!” retreat because of their shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.70.4', 'BSB', 'May all who seek You rejoice and be glad in You; may those who love Your salvation always say, “Let God be magnified!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.70.5', 'BSB', 'But I am poor and needy; hurry to me, O God. You are my help and my deliverer; O LORD, do not delay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.1', 'BSB', 'In You, O LORD, I have taken refuge; let me never be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.2', 'BSB', 'In Your justice, rescue and deliver me; incline Your ear and save me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.3', 'BSB', 'Be my rock of refuge, where I can always go. Give the command to save me, for You are my rock and my fortress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.4', 'BSB', 'Deliver me, O my God, from the hand of the wicked, from the grasp of the unjust and ruthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.5', 'BSB', 'For You are my hope, O Lord GOD, my confidence from my youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.6', 'BSB', 'I have leaned on You since birth; You pulled me from my mother’s womb. My praise is always for You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.7', 'BSB', 'I have become a portent to many, but You are my strong refuge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.8', 'BSB', 'My mouth is filled with Your praise and with Your splendor all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.9', 'BSB', 'Do not discard me in my old age; do not forsake me when my strength fails.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.10', 'BSB', 'For my enemies speak against me, and those who lie in wait for my life conspire,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.11', 'BSB', 'saying, “God has forsaken him; pursue him and seize him, for there is no one to rescue him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.12', 'BSB', 'Be not far from me, O God. Hurry, O my God, to help me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.13', 'BSB', 'May the accusers of my soul be ashamed and consumed; may those who seek my harm be covered with scorn and disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.14', 'BSB', 'But I will always hope and will praise You more and more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.15', 'BSB', 'My mouth will declare Your righteousness and Your salvation all day long, though I cannot know their full measure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.16', 'BSB', 'I will enter in the strength of the Lord GOD; I will proclaim Your righteousness—Yours alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.17', 'BSB', 'O God, You have taught me from my youth, and to this day I proclaim Your marvelous deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.18', 'BSB', 'Even when I am old and gray, do not forsake me, O God, until I proclaim Your power to the next generation, Your might to all who are to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.19', 'BSB', 'Your righteousness reaches to the heavens, O God, You who have done great things. Who, O God, is like You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.20', 'BSB', 'Though You have shown me many troubles and misfortunes, You will revive me once again. Even from the depths of the earth You will bring me back up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.21', 'BSB', 'You will increase my honor and comfort me once again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.22', 'BSB', 'So I will praise You with the harp for Your faithfulness, O my God; I will sing praise to You with the lyre, O Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.23', 'BSB', 'When I sing praise to You my lips will shout for joy, along with my soul, which You have redeemed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.71.24', 'BSB', 'My tongue will indeed proclaim Your righteousness all day long, for those who seek my harm are disgraced and confounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.1', 'BSB', 'Endow the king with Your justice, O God, and the son of the king with Your righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.2', 'BSB', 'May he judge Your people with righteousness and Your afflicted with justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.3', 'BSB', 'May the mountains bring peace to the people, and the hills bring righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.4', 'BSB', 'May he vindicate the afflicted among the people; may he save the children of the needy and crush the oppressor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.5', 'BSB', 'May they fear him as long as the sun shines, as long as the moon remains, through all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.6', 'BSB', 'May he be like rain that falls on freshly cut grass, like spring showers that water the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.7', 'BSB', 'May the righteous flourish in his days and prosperity abound, until the moon is no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.8', 'BSB', 'May he rule from sea to sea, and from the Euphrates to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.9', 'BSB', 'May the nomads bow before him, and his enemies lick the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.10', 'BSB', 'May the kings of Tarshish and distant shores bring tribute; may the kings of Sheba and Seba offer gifts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.11', 'BSB', 'May all kings bow down to him and all nations serve him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.12', 'BSB', 'For he will deliver the needy who cry out and the afflicted who have no helper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.13', 'BSB', 'He will take pity on the poor and needy and save the lives of the oppressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.14', 'BSB', 'He will redeem them from oppression and violence, for their blood is precious in his sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.15', 'BSB', 'Long may he live! May gold from Sheba be given him. May people ever pray for him; may they bless him all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.16', 'BSB', 'May there be an abundance of grain in the land; may it sway atop the hills. May its fruit trees flourish like the forests of Lebanon, and its people like the grass of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.17', 'BSB', 'May his name endure forever; may his name continue as long as the sun shines. In him may all nations be blessed; may they call him blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.18', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD God, the God of Israel, who alone does marvelous deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.19', 'BSB', 'And blessed be His glorious name forever; may all the earth be filled with His glory. Amen and amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.72.20', 'BSB', 'Thus conclude the prayers of David son of Jesse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.1', 'BSB', 'Surely God is good to Israel, to those who are pure in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.2', 'BSB', 'But as for me, my feet had almost stumbled; my steps had nearly slipped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.3', 'BSB', 'For I envied the arrogant when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.4', 'BSB', 'They have no struggle in their death; their bodies are well-fed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.5', 'BSB', 'They are free of the burdens others carry; they are not afflicted like other men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore pride is their necklace; a garment of violence covers them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.7', 'BSB', 'From their prosperity proceeds iniquity; the imaginations of their hearts run wild.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.8', 'BSB', 'They mock and speak with malice; with arrogance they threaten oppression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.9', 'BSB', 'They set their mouths against the heavens, and their tongues strut across the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.10', 'BSB', 'So their people return to this place and drink up waters in abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.11', 'BSB', 'The wicked say, “How can God know? Does the Most High have knowledge?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.12', 'BSB', 'Behold, these are the wicked— always carefree as they increase their wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.13', 'BSB', 'Surely in vain I have kept my heart pure; in innocence I have washed my hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.14', 'BSB', 'For I am afflicted all day long and punished every morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.15', 'BSB', 'If I had said, “I will speak this way,” then I would have betrayed Your children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.16', 'BSB', 'When I tried to understand all this, it was troublesome in my sight', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.17', 'BSB', 'until I entered God’s sanctuary; then I discerned their end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.18', 'BSB', 'Surely You set them on slick ground; You cast them down into ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.19', 'BSB', 'How suddenly they are laid waste, completely swept away by terrors!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.20', 'BSB', 'Like one waking from a dream, so You, O Lord, awaken and despise their form.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.21', 'BSB', 'When my heart was grieved and I was pierced within,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.22', 'BSB', 'I was senseless and ignorant; I was a brute beast before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.23', 'BSB', 'Yet I am always with You; You hold my right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.24', 'BSB', 'You guide me with Your counsel, and later receive me in glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.25', 'BSB', 'Whom have I in heaven but You? And on earth I desire no one besides You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.26', 'BSB', 'My flesh and my heart may fail, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.27', 'BSB', 'Those far from You will surely perish; You destroy all who are unfaithful to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.73.28', 'BSB', 'But as for me, it is good to draw near to God. I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may proclaim all Your works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.1', 'BSB', 'Why have You rejected us forever, O God? Why does Your anger smolder against the sheep of Your pasture?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.2', 'BSB', 'Remember Your congregation, which You purchased long ago and redeemed as the tribe of Your inheritance— Mount Zion where You dwell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.3', 'BSB', 'Turn Your steps to the everlasting ruins, to everything in the sanctuary the enemy has destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.4', 'BSB', 'Your foes have roared within Your meeting place; they have unfurled their banners as signs,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.5', 'BSB', 'like men wielding axes in a thicket of trees', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.6', 'BSB', 'and smashing all the carvings with hatchets and picks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.7', 'BSB', 'They have burned Your sanctuary to the ground; they have defiled the dwelling place of Your Name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.8', 'BSB', 'They said in their hearts, “We will crush them completely.” They burned down every place where God met us in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.9', 'BSB', 'There are no signs for us to see. There is no longer any prophet. And none of us knows how long this will last.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.10', 'BSB', 'How long, O God, will the enemy taunt You? Will the foe revile Your name forever?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.11', 'BSB', 'Why do You withdraw Your strong right hand? Stretch it out to destroy them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.12', 'BSB', 'Yet God is my King from ancient times, working salvation on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.13', 'BSB', 'You divided the sea by Your strength; You smashed the heads of the dragons of the sea;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.14', 'BSB', 'You crushed the heads of Leviathan; You fed him to the creatures of the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.15', 'BSB', 'You broke open the fountain and the flood; You dried up the ever-flowing rivers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.16', 'BSB', 'The day is Yours, and also the night; You established the moon and the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.17', 'BSB', 'You set all the boundaries of the earth; You made the summer and winter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.18', 'BSB', 'Remember how the enemy has mocked You, O LORD, how a foolish people has spurned Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.19', 'BSB', 'Do not deliver the soul of Your dove to beasts; do not forget the lives of Your afflicted forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.20', 'BSB', 'Consider Your covenant, for haunts of violence fill the dark places of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.21', 'BSB', 'Do not let the oppressed retreat in shame; may the poor and needy praise Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.22', 'BSB', 'Rise up, O God; defend Your cause! Remember how the fool mocks You all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.74.23', 'BSB', 'Do not disregard the clamor of Your adversaries, the uproar of Your enemies that ascends continually.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.1', 'BSB', 'We give thanks to You, O God; we give thanks, for Your Name is near. The people declare Your wondrous works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.2', 'BSB', '“When I choose a time, I will judge fairly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.3', 'BSB', 'When the earth and all its dwellers quake, it is I who bear up its pillars. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.4', 'BSB', 'I say to the proud, ‘Do not boast,’ and to the wicked, ‘Do not lift up your horn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.5', 'BSB', 'Do not lift up your horn against heaven or speak with an outstretched neck.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.6', 'BSB', 'For exaltation comes neither from east nor west, nor out of the desert,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.7', 'BSB', 'but it is God who judges; He brings down one and exalts another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.8', 'BSB', 'For a cup is in the hand of the LORD, full of foaming wine mixed with spices. He pours from His cup, and all the wicked of the earth drink it down to the dregs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.9', 'BSB', 'But I will proclaim Him forever; I will sing praise to the God of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.75.10', 'BSB', '“All the horns of the wicked I will cut off, but the horns of the righteous will be exalted.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.1', 'BSB', 'God is known in Judah; His name is great in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.2', 'BSB', 'His tent is in Salem, His dwelling place in Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.3', 'BSB', 'There He shattered the flaming arrows, the shield and sword and weapons of war. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.4', 'BSB', 'You are resplendent with light, more majestic than mountains filled with game.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.5', 'BSB', 'The valiant lie plundered; they sleep their last sleep. No men of might could lift a hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.6', 'BSB', 'At Your rebuke, O God of Jacob, both horse and rider lie stunned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.7', 'BSB', 'You alone are to be feared. When You are angry, who can stand before You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.8', 'BSB', 'From heaven You pronounced judgment, and the earth feared and was still', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.9', 'BSB', 'when God rose up to judge, to save all the lowly of the earth. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.10', 'BSB', 'Even the wrath of man shall praise You; with the survivors of wrath You will clothe Yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.11', 'BSB', 'Make and fulfill your vows to the LORD your God; let all the neighboring lands bring tribute to Him who is to be feared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.76.12', 'BSB', 'He breaks the spirits of princes; He is feared by the kings of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.1', 'BSB', 'I cried out to God; I cried aloud to God to hear me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.2', 'BSB', 'In the day of trouble I sought the Lord; through the night my outstretched hands did not grow weary; my soul refused to be comforted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.3', 'BSB', 'I remembered You, O God, and I groaned; I mused and my spirit grew faint. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.4', 'BSB', 'You have kept my eyes from closing; I am too troubled to speak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.5', 'BSB', 'I considered the days of old, the years long in the past.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.6', 'BSB', 'At night I remembered my song; in my heart I mused, and my spirit pondered:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.7', 'BSB', '“Will the Lord spurn us forever and never show His favor again?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.8', 'BSB', 'Is His loving devotion gone forever? Has His promise failed for all time?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.9', 'BSB', 'Has God forgotten to be gracious? Has His anger shut off His compassion?” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.10', 'BSB', 'So I said, “I am grieved that the right hand of the Most High has changed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.11', 'BSB', 'I will remember the works of the LORD; yes, I will remember Your wonders of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.12', 'BSB', 'I will reflect on all You have done and ponder Your mighty deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.13', 'BSB', 'Your way, O God, is holy. What god is so great as our God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.14', 'BSB', 'You are the God who works wonders; You display Your strength among the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.15', 'BSB', 'With power You redeemed Your people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.16', 'BSB', 'The waters saw You, O God; the waters saw You and swirled; even the depths were shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.17', 'BSB', 'The clouds poured down water; the skies resounded with thunder; Your arrows flashed back and forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.18', 'BSB', 'Your thunder resounded in the whirlwind; the lightning lit up the world; the earth trembled and quaked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.19', 'BSB', 'Your path led through the sea, Your way through the mighty waters, but Your footprints were not to be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.77.20', 'BSB', 'You led Your people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.1', 'BSB', 'Give ear, O my people, to my instruction; listen to the words of my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.2', 'BSB', 'I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things hidden from the beginning,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.3', 'BSB', 'that we have heard and known and our fathers have relayed to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.4', 'BSB', 'We will not hide them from their children, but will declare to the next generation the praises of the LORD and His might, and the wonders He has performed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.5', 'BSB', 'For He established a testimony in Jacob and appointed a law in Israel, which He commanded our fathers to teach to their children,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.6', 'BSB', 'that the coming generation would know them— even children yet to be born— to arise and tell their own children', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.7', 'BSB', 'that they should put their confidence in God, not forgetting His works, but keeping His commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.8', 'BSB', 'Then they will not be like their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation, whose heart was not loyal, whose spirit was not faithful to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.9', 'BSB', 'The archers of Ephraim turned back on the day of battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.10', 'BSB', 'They failed to keep God’s covenant and refused to live by His law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.11', 'BSB', 'They forgot what He had done, the wonders He had shown them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.12', 'BSB', 'He worked wonders before their fathers in the land of Egypt, in the region of Zoan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.13', 'BSB', 'He split the sea and brought them through; He set the waters upright like a wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.14', 'BSB', 'He led them with a cloud by day and with a light of fire all night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.15', 'BSB', 'He split the rocks in the wilderness and gave them drink as abundant as the seas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.16', 'BSB', 'He brought streams from the stone and made water flow down like rivers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.17', 'BSB', 'But they continued to sin against Him, rebelling in the desert against the Most High.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.18', 'BSB', 'They willfully tested God by demanding the food they craved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.19', 'BSB', 'They spoke against God, saying, “Can God really prepare a table in the wilderness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.20', 'BSB', 'When He struck the rock, water gushed out and torrents raged. But can He also give bread or supply His people with meat?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore the LORD heard and was filled with wrath; so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and His anger flared against Israel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.22', 'BSB', 'because they did not believe God or rely on His salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.23', 'BSB', 'Yet He commanded the clouds above and opened the doors of the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.24', 'BSB', 'He rained down manna for them to eat; He gave them grain from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.25', 'BSB', 'Man ate the bread of angels; He sent them food in abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.26', 'BSB', 'He stirred the east wind from the heavens and drove the south wind by His might.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.27', 'BSB', 'He rained meat on them like dust, and winged birds like the sand of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.28', 'BSB', 'He felled them in the midst of their camp, all around their dwellings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.29', 'BSB', 'So they ate and were well filled, for He gave them what they craved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.30', 'BSB', 'Yet before they had filled their desire, with the food still in their mouths,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.31', 'BSB', 'God’s anger flared against them, and He put to death their strongest and subdued the young men of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.32', 'BSB', 'In spite of all this, they kept on sinning; despite His wonderful works, they did not believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.33', 'BSB', 'So He ended their days in futility, and their years in sudden terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.34', 'BSB', 'When He slew them, they would seek Him; they repented and searched for God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.35', 'BSB', 'And they remembered that God was their Rock, that God Most High was their Redeemer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.36', 'BSB', 'But they deceived Him with their mouths, and lied to Him with their tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.37', 'BSB', 'Their hearts were disloyal to Him, and they were unfaithful to His covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.38', 'BSB', 'And yet He was compassionate; He forgave their iniquity and did not destroy them. He often restrained His anger and did not unleash His full wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.39', 'BSB', 'He remembered that they were but flesh, a passing breeze that does not return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.40', 'BSB', 'How often they disobeyed Him in the wilderness and grieved Him in the desert!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.41', 'BSB', 'Again and again they tested God and provoked the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.42', 'BSB', 'They did not remember His power — the day He redeemed them from the adversary,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.43', 'BSB', 'when He performed His signs in Egypt and His wonders in the fields of Zoan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.44', 'BSB', 'He turned their rivers to blood, and from their streams they could not drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.45', 'BSB', 'He sent swarms of flies that devoured them, and frogs that devastated them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.46', 'BSB', 'He gave their crops to the grasshopper, the fruit of their labor to the locust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.47', 'BSB', 'He killed their vines with hailstones and their sycamore-figs with sleet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.48', 'BSB', 'He abandoned their cattle to the hail and their livestock to bolts of lightning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.49', 'BSB', 'He unleashed His fury against them, wrath, indignation, and calamity— a band of destroying angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.50', 'BSB', 'He cleared a path for His anger; He did not spare them from death but delivered their lives to the plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.51', 'BSB', 'He struck all the firstborn of Egypt, the virility in the tents of Ham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.52', 'BSB', 'He led out His people like sheep and guided them like a flock in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.53', 'BSB', 'He led them safely, so they did not fear, but the sea engulfed their enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.54', 'BSB', 'He brought them to His holy land, to the mountain His right hand had acquired.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.55', 'BSB', 'He drove out nations before them and apportioned their inheritance; He settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.56', 'BSB', 'But they tested and disobeyed God Most High, for they did not keep His decrees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.57', 'BSB', 'They turned back and were faithless like their fathers, twisted like a faulty bow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.58', 'BSB', 'They enraged Him with their high places and provoked His jealousy with their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.59', 'BSB', 'On hearing it, God was furious and rejected Israel completely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.60', 'BSB', 'He abandoned the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent He had pitched among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.61', 'BSB', 'He delivered His strength to captivity, and His splendor to the hand of the adversary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.62', 'BSB', 'He surrendered His people to the sword because He was enraged by His heritage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.63', 'BSB', 'Fire consumed His young men, and their maidens were left without wedding songs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.64', 'BSB', 'His priests fell by the sword, but their widows could not lament.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.65', 'BSB', 'Then the Lord awoke as from sleep, like a mighty warrior overcome by wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.66', 'BSB', 'He beat back His foes; He put them to everlasting shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.67', 'BSB', 'He rejected the tent of Joseph and refused the tribe of Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.68', 'BSB', 'But He chose the tribe of Judah, Mount Zion, which He loved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.69', 'BSB', 'He built His sanctuary like the heights, like the earth He has established forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.70', 'BSB', 'He chose David His servant and took him from the sheepfolds;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.71', 'BSB', 'from tending the ewes He brought him to be shepherd of His people Jacob, of Israel His inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.78.72', 'BSB', 'So David shepherded them with integrity of heart and guided them with skillful hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.1', 'BSB', 'The nations, O God, have invaded Your inheritance; they have defiled Your holy temple and reduced Jerusalem to rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.2', 'BSB', 'They have given the corpses of Your servants as food to the birds of the air, the flesh of Your saints to the beasts of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.3', 'BSB', 'They have poured out their blood like water all around Jerusalem, and there is no one to bury the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.4', 'BSB', 'We have become a reproach to our neighbors, a scorn and derision to those around us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.5', 'BSB', 'How long, O LORD? Will You be angry forever? Will Your jealousy burn like fire?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.6', 'BSB', 'Pour out Your wrath on the nations that do not acknowledge You, on the kingdoms that refuse to call on Your name,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.7', 'BSB', 'for they have devoured Jacob and devastated his homeland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.8', 'BSB', 'Do not hold past sins against us; let Your compassion come quickly, for we are brought low.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.9', 'BSB', 'Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of Your name; deliver us and atone for our sins, for the sake of Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.10', 'BSB', 'Why should the nations ask, “Where is their God?” Before our eyes, make known among the nations Your vengeance for the bloodshed of Your servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.11', 'BSB', 'May the groans of the captives reach You; by the strength of Your arm preserve those condemned to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.12', 'BSB', 'Pay back into the laps of our neighbors sevenfold the reproach they hurled at You, O Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.79.13', 'BSB', 'Then we Your people, the sheep of Your pasture, will thank You forever; from generation to generation we will declare Your praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.1', 'BSB', 'Hear us, O Shepherd of Israel, who leads Joseph like a flock; You who sit enthroned between the cherubim, shine forth', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.2', 'BSB', 'before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh. Rally Your mighty power and come to save us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.3', 'BSB', 'Restore us, O God, and cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.4', 'BSB', 'O LORD God of Hosts, how long will Your anger smolder against the prayers of Your people?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.5', 'BSB', 'You fed them with the bread of tears and made them drink the full measure of their tears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.6', 'BSB', 'You make us contend with our neighbors; our enemies mock us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.7', 'BSB', 'Restore us, O God of Hosts, and cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.8', 'BSB', 'You uprooted a vine from Egypt; You drove out the nations and transplanted it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.9', 'BSB', 'You cleared the ground for it, and it took root and filled the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.10', 'BSB', 'The mountains were covered by its shade, and the mighty cedars with its branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.11', 'BSB', 'It sent out its branches to the Sea, and its shoots toward the River.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.12', 'BSB', 'Why have You broken down its walls, so that all who pass by pick its fruit?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.13', 'BSB', 'The boar from the forest ravages it, and the creatures of the field feed upon it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.14', 'BSB', 'Return, O God of Hosts, we pray! Look down from heaven and see! Attend to this vine—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.15', 'BSB', 'the root Your right hand has planted, the son You have raised up for Yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.16', 'BSB', 'Your vine has been cut down and burned; they perish at the rebuke of Your countenance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.17', 'BSB', 'Let Your hand be upon the man at Your right hand, on the son of man You have raised up for Yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.18', 'BSB', 'Then we will not turn away from You; revive us, and we will call on Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.80.19', 'BSB', 'Restore us, O LORD God of Hosts; cause Your face to shine upon us, that we may be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.1', 'BSB', 'Sing for joy to God our strength; make a joyful noise to the God of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.2', 'BSB', 'Lift up a song, strike the tambourine, play the sweet-sounding harp and lyre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.3', 'BSB', 'Sound the ram’s horn at the New Moon, and at the full moon on the day of our Feast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.4', 'BSB', 'For this is a statute for Israel, an ordinance of the God of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.5', 'BSB', 'He ordained it as a testimony for Joseph when he went out over the land of Egypt, where I heard an unfamiliar language:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.6', 'BSB', '“I relieved his shoulder of the burden; his hands were freed from the basket.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.7', 'BSB', 'You called out in distress, and I rescued you; I answered you from the cloud of thunder; I tested you at the waters of Meribah. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.8', 'BSB', 'Hear, O My people, and I will warn you: O Israel, if only you would listen to Me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.9', 'BSB', 'There must be no strange god among you, nor shall you bow to a foreign god.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.10', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD your God, who brought you up out of Egypt. Open wide your mouth, and I will fill it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.11', 'BSB', 'But My people would not listen to Me, and Israel would not obey Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.12', 'BSB', 'So I gave them up to their stubborn hearts to follow their own devices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.13', 'BSB', 'If only My people would listen to Me, if Israel would follow My ways,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.14', 'BSB', 'how soon I would subdue their enemies and turn My hand against their foes!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.15', 'BSB', 'Those who hate the LORD would feign obedience, and their doom would last forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.81.16', 'BSB', 'But I would feed you the finest wheat; with honey from the rock I would satisfy you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.1', 'BSB', 'God presides in the divine assembly; He renders judgment among the gods:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.2', 'BSB', '“How long will you judge unjustly and show partiality to the wicked? Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.3', 'BSB', 'Defend the cause of the weak and fatherless; uphold the rights of the afflicted and oppressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.4', 'BSB', 'Rescue the weak and needy; save them from the hand of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.5', 'BSB', 'They do not know or understand; they wander in the darkness; all the foundations of the earth are shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.6', 'BSB', 'I have said, ‘You are gods; you are all sons of the Most High.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.7', 'BSB', 'But like mortals you will die, and like rulers you will fall.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.82.8', 'BSB', 'Arise, O God, judge the earth, for all the nations are Your inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.1', 'BSB', 'O God, be not silent; be not speechless; be not still, O God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.2', 'BSB', 'See how Your enemies rage, how Your foes have reared their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.3', 'BSB', 'With cunning they scheme against Your people and conspire against those You cherish,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.4', 'BSB', 'saying, “Come, let us erase them as a nation; may the name of Israel be remembered no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.5', 'BSB', 'For with one mind they plot together, they form an alliance against You—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.6', 'BSB', 'the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, of Moab and the Hagrites,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.7', 'BSB', 'of Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek, of Philistia with the people of Tyre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.8', 'BSB', 'Even Assyria has joined them, lending strength to the sons of Lot. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.9', 'BSB', 'Do to them as You did to Midian, as to Sisera and Jabin at the River Kishon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.10', 'BSB', 'who perished at Endor and became like dung on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.11', 'BSB', 'Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, and all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.12', 'BSB', 'who said, “Let us possess for ourselves the pastures of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.13', 'BSB', 'Make them like tumbleweed, O my God, like chaff before the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.14', 'BSB', 'As fire consumes a forest, as a flame sets the mountains ablaze,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.15', 'BSB', 'so pursue them with Your tempest, and terrify them with Your storm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.16', 'BSB', 'Cover their faces with shame, that they may seek Your name, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.17', 'BSB', 'May they be ever ashamed and terrified; may they perish in disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.83.18', 'BSB', 'May they know that You alone, whose name is the LORD, are Most High over all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.1', 'BSB', 'How lovely is Your dwelling place, O LORD of Hosts!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.2', 'BSB', 'My soul longs, even faints, for the courts of the LORD; my heart and my flesh cry out for the living God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.3', 'BSB', 'Even the sparrow has found a home, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she places her young near Your altars, O LORD of Hosts, my King and my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.4', 'BSB', 'How blessed are those who dwell in Your house! They are ever praising You. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.5', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those whose strength is in You, whose hearts are set on pilgrimage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.6', 'BSB', 'As they pass through the Valley of Baca, they make it a place of springs; even the autumn rain covers it with pools.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.7', 'BSB', 'They go from strength to strength, until each appears before God in Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.8', 'BSB', 'O LORD God of Hosts, hear my prayer; give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.9', 'BSB', 'Take notice of our shield, O God, and look with favor on the face of Your anointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.10', 'BSB', 'For better is one day in Your courts than a thousand elsewhere. I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God than dwell in the tents of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.11', 'BSB', 'For the LORD God is a sun and a shield; the LORD gives grace and glory; He withholds no good thing from those who walk with integrity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.84.12', 'BSB', 'O LORD of Hosts, how blessed is the man who trusts in You!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.1', 'BSB', 'You showed favor to Your land, O LORD; You restored Jacob from captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.2', 'BSB', 'You forgave the iniquity of Your people; You covered all their sin. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.3', 'BSB', 'You withheld all Your fury; You turned from Your burning anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.4', 'BSB', 'Restore us, O God of our salvation, and put away Your displeasure toward us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.5', 'BSB', 'Will You be angry with us forever? Will You draw out Your anger to all generations?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.6', 'BSB', 'Will You not revive us again, that Your people may rejoice in You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.7', 'BSB', 'Show us Your loving devotion, O LORD, and grant us Your salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.8', 'BSB', 'I will listen to what God the LORD will say; for He will surely speak peace to His people and His saints; He will not let them return to folly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.9', 'BSB', 'Surely His salvation is near to those who fear Him, that His glory may dwell in our land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.10', 'BSB', 'Loving devotion and faithfulness have joined together; righteousness and peace have kissed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.11', 'BSB', 'Faithfulness sprouts from the earth, and righteousness looks down from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.12', 'BSB', 'The LORD will indeed provide what is good, and our land will yield its increase.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.85.13', 'BSB', 'Righteousness will go before Him to prepare the way for His steps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.1', 'BSB', 'Incline Your ear, O LORD, and answer me, for I am poor and needy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.2', 'BSB', 'Preserve my soul, for I am godly. You are my God; save Your servant who trusts in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.3', 'BSB', 'Be merciful to me, O Lord, for I call to You all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.4', 'BSB', 'Bring joy to Your servant, for to You, O Lord, I lift up my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.5', 'BSB', 'For You, O Lord, are kind and forgiving, rich in loving devotion to all who call on You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.6', 'BSB', 'Hear my prayer, O LORD, and attend to my plea for mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.7', 'BSB', 'In the day of my distress I call on You, because You answer me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.8', 'BSB', 'O Lord, there is none like You among the gods, nor any works like Yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.9', 'BSB', 'All the nations You have made will come and bow before You, O Lord, and they will glorify Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.10', 'BSB', 'For You are great and perform wonders; You alone are God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.11', 'BSB', 'Teach me Your way, O LORD, that I may walk in Your truth. Give me an undivided heart, that I may fear Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.12', 'BSB', 'I will praise You, O Lord my God, with all my heart; I will glorify Your name forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.13', 'BSB', 'For great is Your loving devotion to me; You have delivered me from the depths of Sheol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.14', 'BSB', 'The arrogant rise against me, O God; a band of ruthless men seeks my life, with no regard for You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.15', 'BSB', 'But You, O Lord, are a compassionate and gracious God, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion and faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.16', 'BSB', 'Turn to me and have mercy; grant Your strength to Your servant; save the son of Your maidservant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.86.17', 'BSB', 'Show me a sign of Your goodness, that my enemies may see and be ashamed; for You, O LORD, have helped me and comforted me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.1', 'BSB', 'He has founded His city on the holy mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.3', 'BSB', 'Glorious things are ascribed to you, O city of God. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.4', 'BSB', '“I will mention Rahab and Babylon among those who know Me— along with Philistia, Tyre, and Cush — when I say, ‘This one was born in Zion.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.5', 'BSB', 'And it will be said of Zion: “This one and that one were born in her, and the Most High Himself will establish her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.6', 'BSB', 'The LORD will record in the register of the peoples: “This one was born in Zion.” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.87.7', 'BSB', 'Singers and pipers will proclaim, “All my springs of joy are in You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, the God of my salvation, day and night I cry out before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.2', 'BSB', 'May my prayer come before You; incline Your ear to my cry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.3', 'BSB', 'For my soul is full of troubles, and my life draws near to Sheol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.4', 'BSB', 'I am counted among those descending to the Pit. I am like a man without strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.5', 'BSB', 'I am forsaken among the dead, like the slain who lie in the grave, whom You remember no more, who are cut off from Your care.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.6', 'BSB', 'You have laid me in the lowest Pit, in the darkest of the depths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.7', 'BSB', 'Your wrath weighs heavily upon me; all Your waves have submerged me. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.8', 'BSB', 'You have removed my friends from me; You have made me repulsive to them; I am confined and cannot escape.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.9', 'BSB', 'My eyes grow dim with grief. I call to You daily, O LORD; I spread out my hands to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.10', 'BSB', 'Do You work wonders for the dead? Do departed spirits rise up to praise You? Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.11', 'BSB', 'Can Your loving devotion be proclaimed in the grave, Your faithfulness in Abaddon?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.12', 'BSB', 'Will Your wonders be known in the darkness, or Your righteousness in the land of oblivion?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.13', 'BSB', 'But to You, O LORD, I cry for help; in the morning my prayer comes before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.14', 'BSB', 'Why, O LORD, do You reject me? Why do You hide Your face from me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.15', 'BSB', 'From my youth I was afflicted and near death. I have borne Your terrors; I am in despair.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.16', 'BSB', 'Your wrath has swept over me; Your terrors have destroyed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.17', 'BSB', 'All day long they engulf me like water; they enclose me on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.88.18', 'BSB', 'You have removed my beloved and my friend; darkness is my closest companion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.1', 'BSB', 'I will sing of the loving devotion of the LORD forever; with my mouth I will proclaim Your faithfulness to all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.2', 'BSB', 'For I have said, “Loving devotion is built up forever; in the heavens You establish Your faithfulness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.3', 'BSB', 'You said, “I have made a covenant with My chosen one, I have sworn to David My servant:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.4', 'BSB', '‘I will establish your offspring forever and build up your throne for all generations.’” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.5', 'BSB', 'The heavens praise Your wonders, O LORD— Your faithfulness as well— in the assembly of the holy ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.6', 'BSB', 'For who in the skies can compare with the LORD? Who among the heavenly beings is like the LORD?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.7', 'BSB', 'In the council of the holy ones, God is greatly feared, and awesome above all who surround Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.8', 'BSB', 'O LORD God of Hosts, who is like You? O mighty LORD, Your faithfulness surrounds You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.9', 'BSB', 'You rule the raging sea; when its waves mount up, You still them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.10', 'BSB', 'You crushed Rahab like a carcass; You scattered Your enemies with Your mighty arm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.11', 'BSB', 'The heavens are Yours, and also the earth. The earth and its fullness You founded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.12', 'BSB', 'North and south You created; Tabor and Hermon shout for joy at Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.13', 'BSB', 'Mighty is Your arm; strong is Your hand. Your right hand is exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.14', 'BSB', 'Righteousness and justice are the foundation of Your throne; loving devotion and faithfulness go before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.15', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who know the joyful sound, who walk, O LORD, in the light of Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.16', 'BSB', 'They rejoice in Your name all day long, and in Your righteousness they exult.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.17', 'BSB', 'For You are the glory of their strength, and by Your favor our horn is exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.18', 'BSB', 'Surely our shield belongs to the LORD, and our king to the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.19', 'BSB', 'You once spoke in a vision; to Your godly ones You said, “I have bestowed help on a warrior; I have exalted one chosen from the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.20', 'BSB', 'I have found My servant David; with My sacred oil I have anointed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.21', 'BSB', 'My hand will sustain him; surely My arm will strengthen him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.22', 'BSB', 'No enemy will exact tribute; no wicked man will oppress him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.23', 'BSB', 'I will crush his foes before him and strike down those who hate him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.24', 'BSB', 'My faithfulness and loving devotion will be with him, and through My name his horn will be exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.25', 'BSB', 'I will set his hand over the sea, and his right hand upon the rivers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.26', 'BSB', 'He will call to Me, ‘You are my Father, my God, the Rock of my salvation.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.27', 'BSB', 'I will indeed appoint him as My firstborn, the highest of the kings of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.28', 'BSB', 'I will forever preserve My loving devotion for him, and My covenant with him will stand fast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.29', 'BSB', 'I will establish his line forever, his throne as long as the heavens endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.30', 'BSB', 'If his sons forsake My law and do not walk in My judgments,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.31', 'BSB', 'if they violate My statutes and fail to keep My commandments,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.32', 'BSB', 'I will attend to their transgression with the rod, and to their iniquity with stripes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.33', 'BSB', 'But I will not withdraw My loving devotion from him, nor ever betray My faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.34', 'BSB', 'I will not violate My covenant or alter the utterance of My lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.35', 'BSB', 'Once and for all I have sworn by My holiness— I will not lie to David—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.36', 'BSB', 'his offspring shall endure forever, and his throne before Me like the sun,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.37', 'BSB', 'like the moon, established forever, a faithful witness in the sky.” Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.38', 'BSB', 'Now, however, You have spurned and rejected him; You are enraged by Your anointed one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.39', 'BSB', 'You have renounced the covenant with Your servant and sullied his crown in the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.40', 'BSB', 'You have broken down all his walls; You have reduced his strongholds to rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.41', 'BSB', 'All who pass by plunder him; he has become a reproach to his neighbors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.42', 'BSB', 'You have exalted the right hand of his foes; You have made all his enemies rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.43', 'BSB', 'You have bent the edge of his sword and have not sustained him in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.44', 'BSB', 'You have ended his splendor and cast his throne to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.45', 'BSB', 'You have cut short the days of his youth; You have covered him with shame. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.46', 'BSB', 'How long, O LORD? Will You hide Yourself forever? Will Your wrath keep burning like fire?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.47', 'BSB', 'Remember the briefness of my lifespan! For what futility You have created all men!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.48', 'BSB', 'What man can live and never see death? Can he deliver his soul from the power of Sheol? Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.49', 'BSB', 'Where, O Lord, is Your loving devotion of old, which You faithfully swore to David?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.50', 'BSB', 'Remember, O Lord, the reproach of Your servants, which I bear in my heart from so many people—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.51', 'BSB', 'how Your enemies have taunted, O LORD, and have mocked every step of Your anointed one!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.89.52', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD forever! Amen and amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.1', 'BSB', 'Lord, You have been our dwelling place through all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.2', 'BSB', 'Before the mountains were born or You brought forth the earth and the world, from everlasting to everlasting You are God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.3', 'BSB', 'You return man to dust, saying, “Return, O sons of mortals.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.4', 'BSB', 'For in Your sight a thousand years are but a day that passes, or a watch of the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.5', 'BSB', 'You whisk them away in their sleep; they are like the new grass of the morning—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.6', 'BSB', 'in the morning it springs up new, but by evening it fades and withers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.7', 'BSB', 'For we are consumed by Your anger and terrified by Your wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.8', 'BSB', 'You have set our iniquities before You, our secret sins in the light of Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.9', 'BSB', 'For all our days decline in Your fury; we finish our years with a sigh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.10', 'BSB', 'The length of our days is seventy years— or eighty if we are strong— yet their pride is but labor and sorrow, for they quickly pass, and we fly away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.11', 'BSB', 'Who knows the power of Your anger? Your wrath matches the fear You are due.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.12', 'BSB', 'So teach us to number our days, that we may present a heart of wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.13', 'BSB', 'Return, O LORD! How long will it be? Have compassion on Your servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.14', 'BSB', 'Satisfy us in the morning with Your loving devotion, that we may sing for joy and be glad all our days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.15', 'BSB', 'Make us glad for as many days as You have afflicted us, for as many years as we have seen evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.16', 'BSB', 'May Your work be shown to Your servants, and Your splendor to their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.90.17', 'BSB', 'May the favor of the Lord our God rest upon us; establish for us the work of our hands— yes, establish the work of our hands!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.1', 'BSB', 'He who dwells in the shelter of the Most High will abide in the shadow of the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.2', 'BSB', 'I will say to the LORD, “You are my refuge and my fortress, my God, in whom I trust.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.3', 'BSB', 'Surely He will deliver you from the snare of the fowler, and from the deadly plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.4', 'BSB', 'He will cover you with His feathers; under His wings you will find refuge; His faithfulness is a shield and rampart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.5', 'BSB', 'You will not fear the terror of the night, nor the arrow that flies by day,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.6', 'BSB', 'nor the pestilence that stalks in the darkness, nor the calamity that destroys at noon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.7', 'BSB', 'Though a thousand may fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand, no harm will come near you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.8', 'BSB', 'You will only see it with your eyes and witness the punishment of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.9', 'BSB', 'Because you have made the LORD your dwelling— my refuge, the Most High—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.10', 'BSB', 'no evil will befall you, no plague will approach your tent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.11', 'BSB', 'For He will command His angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.12', 'BSB', 'They will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.13', 'BSB', 'You will tread on the lion and cobra; you will trample the young lion and serpent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.14', 'BSB', '“Because he loves Me, I will deliver him; because he knows My name, I will protect him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.15', 'BSB', 'When he calls out to Me, I will answer him; I will be with him in trouble. I will deliver him and honor him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.91.16', 'BSB', 'With long life I will satisfy him and show him My salvation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.1', 'BSB', 'It is good to praise the LORD, and to sing praises to Your name, O Most High,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.2', 'BSB', 'to proclaim Your loving devotion in the morning and Your faithfulness at night', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.3', 'BSB', 'with the ten-stringed harp and the melody of the lyre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.4', 'BSB', 'For You, O LORD, have made me glad by Your deeds; I sing for joy at the works of Your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.5', 'BSB', 'How great are Your works, O LORD, how deep are Your thoughts!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.6', 'BSB', 'A senseless man does not know, and a fool does not understand,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.7', 'BSB', 'that though the wicked sprout like grass, and all evildoers flourish, they will be forever destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.8', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, are exalted forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.9', 'BSB', 'For surely Your enemies, O LORD, surely Your enemies will perish; all evildoers will be scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.10', 'BSB', 'But You have exalted my horn like that of a wild ox; with fine oil I have been anointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.11', 'BSB', 'My eyes see the downfall of my enemies; my ears hear the wailing of my wicked foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.12', 'BSB', 'The righteous will flourish like a palm tree, and grow like a cedar in Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.13', 'BSB', 'Planted in the house of the LORD, they will flourish in the courts of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.14', 'BSB', 'In old age they will still bear fruit; healthy and green they will remain,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.92.15', 'BSB', 'to proclaim, “The LORD is upright; He is my Rock, and in Him there is no unrighteousness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.93.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD reigns! He is robed in majesty; the LORD has clothed and armed Himself with strength. The world indeed is firmly established; it cannot be moved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.93.2', 'BSB', 'Your throne was established long ago; You are from all eternity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.93.3', 'BSB', 'The floodwaters have risen, O LORD; the rivers have raised their voice; the seas lift up their pounding waves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.93.4', 'BSB', 'Above the roar of many waters— the mighty breakers of the sea— the LORD on high is majestic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.93.5', 'BSB', 'Your testimonies are fully confirmed; holiness adorns Your house, O LORD, for all the days to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, God of vengeance, O God of vengeance, shine forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.2', 'BSB', 'Rise up, O Judge of the earth; render a reward to the proud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.3', 'BSB', 'How long will the wicked, O LORD, how long will the wicked exult?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.4', 'BSB', 'They pour out arrogant words; all workers of iniquity boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.5', 'BSB', 'They crush Your people, O LORD; they oppress Your heritage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.6', 'BSB', 'They kill the widow and the foreigner; they murder the fatherless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.7', 'BSB', 'They say, “The LORD does not see; the God of Jacob pays no heed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.8', 'BSB', 'Take notice, O senseless among the people! O fools, when will you be wise?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.9', 'BSB', 'He who affixed the ear, can He not hear? He who formed the eye, can He not see?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.10', 'BSB', 'He who admonishes the nations, does He not discipline? He who teaches man, does He lack knowledge?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD knows the thoughts of man, that they are futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.12', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man You discipline, O LORD, and teach from Your law,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.13', 'BSB', 'to grant him relief from days of trouble, until a pit is dug for the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.14', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will not forsake His people; He will never abandon His heritage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.15', 'BSB', 'Surely judgment will again be righteous, and all the upright in heart will follow it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.16', 'BSB', 'Who will rise up for me against the wicked? Who will stand for me against the workers of iniquity?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.17', 'BSB', 'Unless the LORD had been my helper, I would soon have dwelt in the abode of silence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.18', 'BSB', 'If I say, “My foot is slipping,” Your loving devotion, O LORD, supports me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.19', 'BSB', 'When anxiety overwhelms me, Your consolation delights my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.20', 'BSB', 'Can a corrupt throne be Your ally— one devising mischief by decree?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.21', 'BSB', 'They band together against the righteous and condemn the innocent to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.22', 'BSB', 'But the LORD has been my stronghold, and my God is my rock of refuge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.94.23', 'BSB', 'He will bring upon them their own iniquity and destroy them for their wickedness. The LORD our God will destroy them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.1', 'BSB', 'Come, let us sing for joy to the LORD; let us shout to the Rock of our salvation!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.2', 'BSB', 'Let us enter His presence with thanksgiving; let us make a joyful noise to Him in song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.3', 'BSB', 'For the LORD is a great God, a great King above all gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.4', 'BSB', 'In His hand are the depths of the earth, and the mountain peaks belong to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.5', 'BSB', 'The sea is His, for He made it, and His hands formed the dry land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.6', 'BSB', 'O come, let us worship and bow down; let us kneel before the LORD our Maker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.7', 'BSB', 'For He is our God, and we are the people of His pasture, the sheep under His care. Today, if you hear His voice,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.8', 'BSB', 'do not harden your hearts as you did at Meribah, in the day at Massah in the wilderness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.9', 'BSB', 'where your fathers tested and tried Me, though they had seen My work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.10', 'BSB', 'For forty years I was angry with that generation, and I said, “They are a people whose hearts go astray, and they have not known My ways.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.95.11', 'BSB', 'So I swore on oath in My anger, “They shall never enter My rest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.1', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD a new song; sing to the LORD, all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.2', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD, bless His name; proclaim His salvation day after day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.3', 'BSB', 'Declare His glory among the nations, His wonderful deeds among all peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.4', 'BSB', 'For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; He is to be feared above all gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.5', 'BSB', 'For all the gods of the nations are idols, but it is the LORD who made the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.6', 'BSB', 'Splendor and majesty are before Him; strength and beauty fill His sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.7', 'BSB', 'Ascribe to the LORD, O families of the nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.8', 'BSB', 'Ascribe to the LORD the glory due His name; bring an offering and enter His courts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.9', 'BSB', 'Worship the LORD in the splendor of His holiness; tremble before Him, all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.10', 'BSB', 'Declare among the nations: “The LORD reigns!” The world is firmly established; it cannot be moved; He will judge the peoples with equity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.11', 'BSB', 'Let the heavens be glad and the earth rejoice; let the sea resound, and all that fills it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.12', 'BSB', 'Let the fields exult, and all that is in them. Then all the trees of the forest will sing for joy', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.96.13', 'BSB', 'before the LORD, for He is coming— He is coming to judge the earth. He will judge the world in righteousness and the peoples in His faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD reigns, let the earth rejoice; let the distant shores be glad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.2', 'BSB', 'Clouds and darkness surround Him; righteousness and justice are His throne’s foundation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.3', 'BSB', 'Fire goes before Him and consumes His foes on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.4', 'BSB', 'His lightning illuminates the world; the earth sees and trembles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.5', 'BSB', 'The mountains melt like wax at the presence of the LORD, before the Lord of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.6', 'BSB', 'The heavens proclaim His righteousness; all the peoples see His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.7', 'BSB', 'All worshipers of images are put to shame— those who boast in idols. Worship Him, all you gods!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.8', 'BSB', 'Zion hears and rejoices, and the towns of Judah exult because of Your judgments, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.9', 'BSB', 'For You, O LORD, are Most High over all the earth; You are exalted far above all gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.10', 'BSB', 'Hate evil, O you who love the LORD! He preserves the souls of His saints; He delivers them from the hand of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.11', 'BSB', 'Light shines on the righteous, gladness on the upright in heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.97.12', 'BSB', 'Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous ones, and praise His holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.1', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD a new song, for He has done wonders; His right hand and holy arm have gained Him the victory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD has proclaimed His salvation and revealed His righteousness to the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.3', 'BSB', 'He has remembered His love and faithfulness to the house of Israel; all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.4', 'BSB', 'Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth; break forth—let your cry ring out, and sing praises!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.5', 'BSB', 'Sing praises to the LORD with the lyre, in melodious song with the harp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.6', 'BSB', 'With trumpets and the blast of the ram’s horn shout for joy before the LORD, the King.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.7', 'BSB', 'Let the sea resound, and all that fills it, the world, and all who dwell in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.8', 'BSB', 'Let the rivers clap their hands, let the mountains sing together for joy', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.98.9', 'BSB', 'before the LORD, for He comes to judge the earth. He will judge the world with righteousness and the peoples with equity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD reigns; let the nations tremble! He is enthroned above the cherubim; let the earth quake!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.2', 'BSB', 'Great is the LORD in Zion; He is exalted above all the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.3', 'BSB', 'Let them praise Your great and awesome name— He is holy!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.4', 'BSB', 'The mighty King loves justice. You have established equity; You have exercised justice and righteousness in Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.5', 'BSB', 'Exalt the LORD our God, and worship at His footstool; He is holy!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.6', 'BSB', 'Moses and Aaron were among His priests; Samuel was among those who called on His name. They called to the LORD and He answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.7', 'BSB', 'He spoke to them from the pillar of cloud; they kept His decrees and the statutes He gave them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.8', 'BSB', 'O LORD our God, You answered them. You were a forgiving God to them, yet an avenger of their misdeeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.99.9', 'BSB', 'Exalt the LORD our God and worship at His holy mountain, for the LORD our God is holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.100.1', 'BSB', 'Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.100.2', 'BSB', 'Serve the LORD with gladness; come into His presence with joyful songs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.100.3', 'BSB', 'Know that the LORD is God. It is He who made us, and we are His; we are His people, and the sheep of His pasture.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.100.4', 'BSB', 'Enter His gates with thanksgiving and His courts with praise; give thanks to Him and bless His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.100.5', 'BSB', 'For the LORD is good, and His loving devotion endures forever; His faithfulness continues to all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.1', 'BSB', 'I will sing of Your loving devotion and justice; to You, O LORD, I will sing praises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.2', 'BSB', 'I will ponder the way that is blameless— when will You come to me? I will walk in my house with integrity of heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.3', 'BSB', 'I will set no worthless thing before my eyes. I hate the work of those who fall away; it shall not cling to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.4', 'BSB', 'A perverse heart shall depart from me; I will know nothing of evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.5', 'BSB', 'Whoever slanders his neighbor in secret, I will put to silence; the one with haughty eyes and a proud heart, I will not endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.6', 'BSB', 'My eyes favor the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me; he who walks in the way of integrity shall minister to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.7', 'BSB', 'No one who practices deceit shall dwell in my house; no one who tells lies shall stand in my presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.101.8', 'BSB', 'Every morning I will remove all the wicked of the land, that I may cut off every evildoer from the city of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.1', 'BSB', 'Hear my prayer, O LORD; let my cry for help come before You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.2', 'BSB', 'Do not hide Your face from me in my day of distress. Incline Your ear to me; answer me quickly when I call.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.3', 'BSB', 'For my days vanish like smoke, and my bones burn like glowing embers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.4', 'BSB', 'My heart is afflicted, and withered like grass; I even forget to eat my bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.5', 'BSB', 'Through my loud groaning my flesh clings to my bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.6', 'BSB', 'I am like a desert owl, like an owl among the ruins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.7', 'BSB', 'I lie awake; I am like a lone bird on a housetop.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.8', 'BSB', 'All day long my enemies taunt me; they ridicule me and curse me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.9', 'BSB', 'For I have eaten ashes like bread and mixed my drink with tears', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.10', 'BSB', 'because of Your indignation and wrath, for You have picked me up and cast me aside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.11', 'BSB', 'My days are like lengthening shadows, and I wither away like grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.12', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, sit enthroned forever; Your renown endures to all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.13', 'BSB', 'You will rise up and have compassion on Zion, for it is time to show her favor— the appointed time has come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.14', 'BSB', 'For Your servants delight in her stones and take pity on her dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.15', 'BSB', 'So the nations will fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth will fear Your glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.16', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will rebuild Zion; He has appeared in His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.17', 'BSB', 'He will turn toward the prayer of the destitute; He will not despise their prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.18', 'BSB', 'Let this be written for the generation to come, so that a people not yet created may praise the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.19', 'BSB', 'For He looked down from the heights of His sanctuary; the LORD gazed out from heaven to earth', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.20', 'BSB', 'to hear a prisoner’s groaning, to release those condemned to death,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.21', 'BSB', 'that they may proclaim the name of the LORD in Zion and praise Him in Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.22', 'BSB', 'when peoples and kingdoms assemble to serve the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.23', 'BSB', 'He has broken my strength on the way; He has cut short my days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.24', 'BSB', 'I say: “O my God, do not take me in the midst of my days! Your years go on through all generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.25', 'BSB', 'In the beginning You laid the foundations of the earth, and the heavens are the work of Your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.26', 'BSB', 'They will perish, but You remain; they will all wear out like a garment. Like clothing You will change them, and they will be passed on.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.27', 'BSB', 'But You remain the same, and Your years will never end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.102.28', 'BSB', 'The children of Your servants will dwell securely, and their descendants will be established before You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.1', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, O my soul; all that is within me, bless His holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.2', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, O my soul, and do not forget all His kind deeds—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.3', 'BSB', 'He who forgives all your iniquities and heals all your diseases,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.4', 'BSB', 'who redeems your life from the Pit and crowns you with loving devotion and compassion,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.5', 'BSB', 'who satisfies you with good things, so that your youth is renewed like the eagle’s.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.6', 'BSB', 'The LORD executes righteousness and justice for all the oppressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.7', 'BSB', 'He made known His ways to Moses, His deeds to the people of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD is compassionate and gracious, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.9', 'BSB', 'He will not always accuse us, nor harbor His anger forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.10', 'BSB', 'He has not dealt with us according to our sins or repaid us according to our iniquities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.11', 'BSB', 'For as high as the heavens are above the earth, so great is His loving devotion for those who fear Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.12', 'BSB', 'As far as the east is from the west, so far has He removed our transgressions from us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.13', 'BSB', 'As a father has compassion on his children, so the LORD has compassion on those who fear Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.14', 'BSB', 'For He knows our frame; He is mindful that we are dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.15', 'BSB', 'As for man, his days are like grass— he blooms like a flower of the field;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.16', 'BSB', 'when the wind passes over, it vanishes, and its place remembers it no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.17', 'BSB', 'But from everlasting to everlasting the loving devotion of the LORD extends to those who fear Him, and His righteousness to their children’s children—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.18', 'BSB', 'to those who keep His covenant and remember to obey His precepts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.19', 'BSB', 'The LORD has established His throne in heaven, and His kingdom rules over all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.20', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, all His angels mighty in strength who carry out His word, who hearken to the voice of His command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.21', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, all His hosts, you servants who do His will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.103.22', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, all His works in all places of His dominion. Bless the LORD, O my soul!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.1', 'BSB', 'Bless the LORD, O my soul! O LORD my God, You are very great; You are clothed with splendor and majesty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.2', 'BSB', 'He wraps Himself in light as with a garment; He stretches out the heavens like a tent,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.3', 'BSB', 'laying the beams of His chambers in the waters above, making the clouds His chariot, walking on the wings of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.4', 'BSB', 'He makes the winds His messengers, flames of fire His servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.5', 'BSB', 'He set the earth on its foundations, never to be moved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.6', 'BSB', 'You covered it with the deep like a garment; the waters stood above the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.7', 'BSB', 'At Your rebuke the waters fled; at the sound of Your thunder they hurried away—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.8', 'BSB', 'the mountains rose and the valleys sank to the place You assigned for them—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.9', 'BSB', 'You set a boundary they cannot cross, that they may never again cover the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.10', 'BSB', 'He sends forth springs in the valleys; they flow between the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.11', 'BSB', 'They give drink to every beast of the field; the wild donkeys quench their thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.12', 'BSB', 'The birds of the air nest beside the springs; they sing among the branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.13', 'BSB', 'He waters the mountains from His chambers; the earth is satisfied by the fruit of His works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.14', 'BSB', 'He makes the grass grow for the livestock and provides crops for man to cultivate, bringing forth food from the earth:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.15', 'BSB', 'wine that gladdens the heart of man, oil that makes his face to shine, and bread that sustains his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.16', 'BSB', 'The trees of the LORD have their fill, the cedars of Lebanon that He planted,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.17', 'BSB', 'where the birds build their nests; the stork makes her home in the cypresses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.18', 'BSB', 'The high mountains are for the wild goats, the cliffs a refuge for the rock badgers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.19', 'BSB', 'He made the moon to mark the seasons; the sun knows when to set.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.20', 'BSB', 'You bring darkness, and it becomes night, when all the beasts of the forest prowl.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.21', 'BSB', 'The young lions roar for their prey and seek their food from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.22', 'BSB', 'The sun rises, and they withdraw; they lie down in their dens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.23', 'BSB', 'Man goes forth to his work and to his labor until evening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.24', 'BSB', 'How many are Your works, O LORD! In wisdom You have made them all; the earth is full of Your creatures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.25', 'BSB', 'Here is the sea, vast and wide, teeming with creatures beyond number, living things both great and small.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.26', 'BSB', 'There the ships pass, and Leviathan, which You formed to frolic there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.27', 'BSB', 'All creatures look to You to give them their food in due season.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.28', 'BSB', 'When You give it to them, they gather it up; when You open Your hand, they are satisfied with good things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.29', 'BSB', 'When You hide Your face, they are terrified; when You take away their breath, they die and return to dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.30', 'BSB', 'When You send Your Spirit, they are created, and You renew the face of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.31', 'BSB', 'May the glory of the LORD endure forever; may the LORD rejoice in His works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.32', 'BSB', 'He looks on the earth, and it trembles; He touches the mountains, and they smolder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.33', 'BSB', 'I will sing to the LORD all my life; I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.34', 'BSB', 'May my meditation be pleasing to Him, for I rejoice in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.104.35', 'BSB', 'May sinners vanish from the earth and the wicked be no more. Bless the LORD, O my soul. Hallelujah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.1', 'BSB', 'Give thanks to the LORD, call upon His name; make known His deeds among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.2', 'BSB', 'Sing to Him, sing praises to Him; tell of all His wonders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.3', 'BSB', 'Glory in His holy name; let the hearts of those who seek the LORD rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.4', 'BSB', 'Seek out the LORD and His strength; seek His face always.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.5', 'BSB', 'Remember the wonders He has done, His marvels, and the judgments He has pronounced,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.6', 'BSB', 'O offspring of His servant Abraham, O sons of Jacob, His chosen ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.7', 'BSB', 'He is the LORD our God; His judgments carry throughout the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.8', 'BSB', 'He remembers His covenant forever, the word He ordained for a thousand generations—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.9', 'BSB', 'the covenant He made with Abraham, and the oath He swore to Isaac.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.10', 'BSB', 'He confirmed it to Jacob as a decree, to Israel as an everlasting covenant:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.11', 'BSB', '“I will give you the land of Canaan as the portion of your inheritance.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.12', 'BSB', 'When they were few in number, few indeed, and strangers in the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.13', 'BSB', 'they wandered from nation to nation, from one kingdom to another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.14', 'BSB', 'He let no man oppress them; He rebuked kings on their behalf:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.15', 'BSB', '“Do not touch My anointed ones! Do no harm to My prophets!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.16', 'BSB', 'He called down famine on the land and cut off all their supplies of food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.17', 'BSB', 'He sent a man before them— Joseph, sold as a slave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.18', 'BSB', 'They bruised his feet with shackles and placed his neck in irons,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.19', 'BSB', 'until his prediction came true and the word of the LORD proved him right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.20', 'BSB', 'The king sent and released him; the ruler of peoples set him free.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.21', 'BSB', 'He made him master of his household, ruler over all his substance,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.22', 'BSB', 'to instruct his princes as he pleased and teach his elders wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.23', 'BSB', 'Then Israel entered Egypt; Jacob dwelt in the land of Ham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.24', 'BSB', 'And the LORD made His people very fruitful, more numerous than their foes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.25', 'BSB', 'whose hearts He turned to hate His people, to conspire against His servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.26', 'BSB', 'He sent Moses His servant, and Aaron, whom He had chosen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.27', 'BSB', 'They performed His miraculous signs among them, and wonders in the land of Ham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.28', 'BSB', 'He sent darkness, and it became dark— yet they defied His words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.29', 'BSB', 'He turned their waters to blood and caused their fish to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.30', 'BSB', 'Their land teemed with frogs, even in their royal chambers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.31', 'BSB', 'He spoke, and insects swarmed— gnats throughout their country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.32', 'BSB', 'He gave them hail for rain, with lightning throughout their land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.33', 'BSB', 'He struck their vines and fig trees and shattered the trees of their country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.34', 'BSB', 'He spoke, and the locusts came— young locusts without number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.35', 'BSB', 'They devoured every plant in their land and consumed the produce of their soil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.36', 'BSB', 'Then He struck all the firstborn in their land, the firstfruits of all their vigor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.37', 'BSB', 'He brought Israel out with silver and gold, and none among His tribes stumbled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.38', 'BSB', 'Egypt was glad when they departed, for the dread of Israel had fallen on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.39', 'BSB', 'He spread a cloud as a covering and a fire to light up the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.40', 'BSB', 'They asked, and He brought quail and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.41', 'BSB', 'He opened a rock, and water gushed out; it flowed like a river in the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.42', 'BSB', 'For He remembered His holy promise to Abraham His servant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.43', 'BSB', 'He brought forth His people with rejoicing, His chosen with shouts of joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.44', 'BSB', 'He gave them the lands of the nations, that they might inherit the fruit of others’ labor,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.105.45', 'BSB', 'that they might keep His statutes and obey His laws. Hallelujah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.1', 'BSB', 'Hallelujah! Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.2', 'BSB', 'Who can describe the mighty acts of the LORD or fully proclaim His praise?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.3', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who uphold justice, who practice righteousness at all times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.4', 'BSB', 'Remember me, O LORD, in Your favor to Your people; visit me with Your salvation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.5', 'BSB', 'that I may see the prosperity of Your chosen ones, and rejoice in the gladness of Your nation, and give glory with Your inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.6', 'BSB', 'We have sinned like our fathers; we have done wrong and acted wickedly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.7', 'BSB', 'Our fathers in Egypt did not grasp Your wonders or remember Your abundant kindness; but they rebelled by the sea, there at the Red Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.8', 'BSB', 'Yet He saved them for the sake of His name, to make His power known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.9', 'BSB', 'He rebuked the Red Sea, and it dried up; He led them through the depths as through a desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.10', 'BSB', 'He saved them from the hand that hated them; He redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.11', 'BSB', 'The waters covered their foes; not one of them remained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.12', 'BSB', 'Then they believed His promises and sang His praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.13', 'BSB', 'Yet they soon forgot His works and failed to wait for His counsel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.14', 'BSB', 'They craved intensely in the wilderness and tested God in the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.15', 'BSB', 'So He granted their request, but sent a wasting disease upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.16', 'BSB', 'In the camp they envied Moses, as well as Aaron, the holy one of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.17', 'BSB', 'The earth opened up and swallowed Dathan; it covered the assembly of Abiram.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.18', 'BSB', 'Then fire blazed through their company; flames consumed the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.19', 'BSB', 'At Horeb they made a calf and worshiped a molten image.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.20', 'BSB', 'They exchanged their Glory for the image of a grass-eating ox.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.21', 'BSB', 'They forgot God their Savior, who did great things in Egypt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.22', 'BSB', 'wondrous works in the land of Ham, and awesome deeds by the Red Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.23', 'BSB', 'So He said He would destroy them— had not Moses His chosen one stood before Him in the breach to divert His wrath from destroying them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.24', 'BSB', 'They despised the pleasant land; they did not believe His promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.25', 'BSB', 'They grumbled in their tents and did not listen to the voice of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.26', 'BSB', 'So He raised His hand and swore to cast them down in the wilderness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.27', 'BSB', 'to disperse their offspring among the nations and scatter them throughout the lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.28', 'BSB', 'They yoked themselves to Baal of Peor and ate sacrifices offered to lifeless gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.29', 'BSB', 'So they provoked the LORD to anger with their deeds, and a plague broke out among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.30', 'BSB', 'But Phinehas stood and intervened, and the plague was restrained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.31', 'BSB', 'It was credited to him as righteousness for endless generations to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.32', 'BSB', 'At the waters of Meribah they angered the LORD, and trouble came to Moses because of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.33', 'BSB', 'For they rebelled against His Spirit, and Moses spoke rashly with his lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.34', 'BSB', 'They did not destroy the peoples as the LORD had commanded them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.35', 'BSB', 'but they mingled with the nations and adopted their customs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.36', 'BSB', 'They worshiped their idols, which became a snare to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.37', 'BSB', 'They sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.38', 'BSB', 'They shed innocent blood— the blood of their sons and daughters, whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan, and the land was polluted with blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.39', 'BSB', 'They defiled themselves by their actions and prostituted themselves by their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.40', 'BSB', 'So the anger of the LORD burned against His people, and He abhorred His own inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.41', 'BSB', 'He delivered them into the hand of the nations, and those who hated them ruled over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.42', 'BSB', 'Their enemies oppressed them, and subdued them under their hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.43', 'BSB', 'Many times He rescued them, but they were bent on rebellion and sank down in their iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.44', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless He heard their cry; He took note of their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.45', 'BSB', 'And He remembered His covenant with them, and relented by the abundance of His loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.46', 'BSB', 'He made them objects of compassion to all who held them captive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.47', 'BSB', 'Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from the nations, that we may give thanks to Your holy name, that we may glory in Your praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.106.48', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting. Let all the people say, “Amen!” Hallelujah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.1', 'BSB', 'Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.2', 'BSB', 'Let the redeemed of the LORD say so, whom He has redeemed from the hand of the enemy', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.3', 'BSB', 'and gathered from the lands, from east and west, from north and south.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.4', 'BSB', 'Some wandered in desert wastelands, finding no path to a city in which to dwell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.5', 'BSB', 'They were hungry and thirsty; their soul fainted within them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.6', 'BSB', 'Then they cried out to the LORD in their trouble, and He delivered them from their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.7', 'BSB', 'He led them on a straight path to reach a city where they could live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.8', 'BSB', 'Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion and His wonders to the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.9', 'BSB', 'For He satisfies the thirsty and fills the hungry with good things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.10', 'BSB', 'Some sat in darkness and in the shadow of death, prisoners in affliction and chains,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.11', 'BSB', 'because they rebelled against the words of God and despised the counsel of the Most High.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.12', 'BSB', 'He humbled their hearts with hard labor; they stumbled, and there was no one to help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.13', 'BSB', 'Then they cried out to the LORD in their trouble, and He saved them from their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.14', 'BSB', 'He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death and broke away their chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.15', 'BSB', 'Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion and His wonders to the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.16', 'BSB', 'For He has broken down the gates of bronze and cut through the bars of iron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.17', 'BSB', 'Fools, in their rebellious ways, and through their iniquities, suffered affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.18', 'BSB', 'They loathed all food and drew near to the gates of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.19', 'BSB', 'Then they cried out to the LORD in their trouble, and He saved them from their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.20', 'BSB', 'He sent forth His word and healed them; He rescued them from the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.21', 'BSB', 'Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion and His wonders to the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.22', 'BSB', 'Let them offer sacrifices of thanksgiving and declare His works with rejoicing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.23', 'BSB', 'Others went out to sea in ships, conducting trade on the mighty waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.24', 'BSB', 'They saw the works of the LORD, and His wonders in the deep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.25', 'BSB', 'For He spoke and raised a tempest that lifted the waves of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.26', 'BSB', 'They mounted up to the heavens, then sunk to the depths; their courage melted in their anguish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.27', 'BSB', 'They reeled and staggered like drunkards, and all their skill was useless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.28', 'BSB', 'Then they cried out to the LORD in their trouble, and He brought them out of their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.29', 'BSB', 'He calmed the storm to a whisper, and the waves of the sea were hushed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.30', 'BSB', 'They rejoiced in the silence, and He guided them to the harbor they desired.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.31', 'BSB', 'Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion and His wonders to the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.32', 'BSB', 'Let them exalt Him in the assembly of the people and praise Him in the council of the elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.33', 'BSB', 'He turns rivers into deserts, springs of water into thirsty ground,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.34', 'BSB', 'and fruitful land into fields of salt, because of the wickedness of its dwellers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.35', 'BSB', 'He turns a desert into pools of water and a dry land into flowing springs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.36', 'BSB', 'He causes the hungry to settle there, that they may establish a city in which to dwell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.37', 'BSB', 'They sow fields and plant vineyards that yield a fruitful harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.38', 'BSB', 'He blesses them, and they multiply greatly; He does not let their herds diminish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.39', 'BSB', 'When they are decreased and humbled by oppression, evil, and sorrow,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.40', 'BSB', 'He pours out contempt on the nobles and makes them wander in a trackless wasteland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.41', 'BSB', 'But He lifts the needy from affliction and increases their families like flocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.42', 'BSB', 'The upright see and rejoice, and all iniquity shuts its mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.107.43', 'BSB', 'Let him who is wise pay heed to these things and consider the loving devotion of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.1', 'BSB', 'My heart is steadfast, O God; I will sing and make music with all my being.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.2', 'BSB', 'Awake, O harp and lyre! I will awaken the dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.3', 'BSB', 'I will praise You, O LORD, among the nations; I will sing Your praises among the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.4', 'BSB', 'For Your loving devotion extends beyond the heavens, and Your faithfulness reaches to the clouds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.5', 'BSB', 'Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.6', 'BSB', 'Respond and save us with Your right hand, that Your beloved may be delivered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.7', 'BSB', 'God has spoken from His sanctuary: “I will triumph! I will parcel out Shechem and apportion the Valley of Succoth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.8', 'BSB', 'Gilead is Mine, and Manasseh is Mine; Ephraim is My helmet, Judah is My scepter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.9', 'BSB', 'Moab is My washbasin; upon Edom I toss My sandal; over Philistia I shout in triumph.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.10', 'BSB', 'Who will bring me to the fortified city? Who will lead me to Edom?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.11', 'BSB', 'Have You not rejected us, O God? Will You no longer march out, O God, with our armies?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.12', 'BSB', 'Give us aid against the enemy, for the help of man is worthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.108.13', 'BSB', 'With God we will perform with valor, and He will trample our enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.1', 'BSB', 'O God of my praise, be not silent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.2', 'BSB', 'For wicked and deceitful mouths open against me; they speak against me with lying tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.3', 'BSB', 'They surround me with hateful words and attack me without cause.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.4', 'BSB', 'In return for my love they accuse me, but I am a man of prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.5', 'BSB', 'They repay me evil for good, and hatred for my love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.6', 'BSB', 'Set over him a wicked man; let an accuser stand at his right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.7', 'BSB', 'When he is tried, let him be found guilty, and may his prayer be regarded as sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.8', 'BSB', 'May his days be few; may another take his position.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.9', 'BSB', 'May his children be fatherless and his wife a widow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.10', 'BSB', 'May his children wander as beggars, seeking sustenance far from their ruined homes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.11', 'BSB', 'May the creditor seize all he owns, and strangers plunder the fruits of his labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.12', 'BSB', 'May there be no one to extend kindness to him, and no one to favor his fatherless children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.13', 'BSB', 'May his descendants be cut off; may their name be blotted out from the next generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.14', 'BSB', 'May the iniquity of his fathers be remembered before the LORD, and the sin of his mother never be blotted out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.15', 'BSB', 'May their sins always remain before the LORD, that He may cut off their memory from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.16', 'BSB', 'For he never thought to show kindness, but pursued the poor and needy and brokenhearted, even to their death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.17', 'BSB', 'The cursing that he loved, may it fall on him; the blessing in which he refused to delight, may it be far from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.18', 'BSB', 'The cursing that he wore like a coat, may it soak into his body like water, and into his bones like oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.19', 'BSB', 'May it be like a robe wrapped about him, like a belt tied forever around him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.20', 'BSB', 'May this be the LORD’s reward to my accusers, to those who speak evil against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.21', 'BSB', 'But You, O GOD, the Lord, deal kindly with me for the sake of Your name; deliver me by the goodness of Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.22', 'BSB', 'For I am poor and needy; my heart is wounded within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.23', 'BSB', 'I am fading away like a lengthening shadow; I am shaken off like a locust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.24', 'BSB', 'My knees are weak from fasting, and my body grows lean and gaunt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.25', 'BSB', 'I am an object of scorn to my accusers; when they see me, they shake their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.26', 'BSB', 'Help me, O LORD my God; save me according to Your loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.27', 'BSB', 'Let them know that this is Your hand, that You, O LORD, have done it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.28', 'BSB', 'Though they curse, You will bless. When they rise up, they will be put to shame, but Your servant will rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.29', 'BSB', 'May my accusers be clothed with disgrace; may they wear their shame like a robe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.30', 'BSB', 'With my mouth I will thank the LORD profusely; I will praise Him in the presence of many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.109.31', 'BSB', 'For He stands at the right hand of the needy one, to save him from the condemners of his soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.1', 'BSB', 'The LORD said to my Lord: “Sit at My right hand until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD extends Your mighty scepter from Zion: “Rule in the midst of Your enemies.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.3', 'BSB', 'Your people shall be willing on Your day of battle. Arrayed in holy splendor, from the womb of the dawn, to You belongs the dew of Your youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.4', 'BSB', 'The LORD has sworn and will not change His mind: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.5', 'BSB', 'The Lord is at Your right hand; He will crush kings in the day of His wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.6', 'BSB', 'He will judge the nations, heaping up the dead; He will crush the leaders far and wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.110.7', 'BSB', 'He will drink from the brook by the road; therefore He will lift up His head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.1', 'BSB', 'Hallelujah! I will give thanks to the LORD with all my heart in the council of the upright and in the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.2', 'BSB', 'Great are the works of the LORD; they are pondered by all who delight in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.3', 'BSB', 'Splendid and majestic is His work; His righteousness endures forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.4', 'BSB', 'He has caused His wonders to be remembered; the LORD is gracious and compassionate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.5', 'BSB', 'He provides food for those who fear Him; He remembers His covenant forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.6', 'BSB', 'He has shown His people the power of His works by giving them the inheritance of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.7', 'BSB', 'The works of His hands are truth and justice; all His precepts are trustworthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.8', 'BSB', 'They are upheld forever and ever, enacted in truth and uprightness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.9', 'BSB', 'He has sent redemption to His people; He has ordained His covenant forever; holy and awesome is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.111.10', 'BSB', 'The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom; all who follow His precepts gain rich understanding. His praise endures forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.1', 'BSB', 'Hallelujah! Blessed is the man who fears the LORD, who greatly delights in His commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.2', 'BSB', 'His descendants will be mighty in the land; the generation of the upright will be blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.3', 'BSB', 'Wealth and riches are in his house, and his righteousness endures forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.4', 'BSB', 'Light dawns in the darkness for the upright— for the gracious, compassionate, and righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.5', 'BSB', 'It is well with the man who is generous and lends freely, whose affairs are guided by justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.6', 'BSB', 'Surely he will never be shaken; the righteous man will be remembered forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.7', 'BSB', 'He does not fear bad news; his heart is steadfast, trusting in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.8', 'BSB', 'His heart is assured; he does not fear, until he looks in triumph on his foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.9', 'BSB', 'He has scattered abroad his gifts to the poor; his righteousness endures forever; his horn will be lifted high in honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.112.10', 'BSB', 'The wicked man will see and be grieved; he will gnash his teeth and waste away; the desires of the wicked will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.1', 'BSB', 'Hallelujah! Give praise, O servants of the LORD; praise the name of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.2', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the name of the LORD both now and forevermore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.3', 'BSB', 'From where the sun rises to where it sets, the name of the LORD is praised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.4', 'BSB', 'The LORD is exalted over all the nations, His glory above the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.5', 'BSB', 'Who is like the LORD our God, the One enthroned on high?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.6', 'BSB', 'He humbles Himself to behold the heavens and the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.7', 'BSB', 'He raises the poor from the dust and lifts the needy from the dump', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.8', 'BSB', 'to seat them with nobles, with the princes of His people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.113.9', 'BSB', 'He settles the barren woman in her home as a joyful mother to her children. Hallelujah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.1', 'BSB', 'When Israel departed from Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of foreign tongue,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.2', 'BSB', 'Judah became God’s sanctuary, and Israel His dominion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.3', 'BSB', 'The sea observed and fled; the Jordan turned back;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.4', 'BSB', 'the mountains skipped like rams, the hills like lambs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.5', 'BSB', 'Why was it, O sea, that you fled, O Jordan, that you turned back,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.6', 'BSB', 'O mountains, that you skipped like rams, O hills, like lambs?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.7', 'BSB', 'Tremble, O earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.114.8', 'BSB', 'who turned the rock into a pool, the flint into a fountain of water!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.1', 'BSB', 'Not to us, O LORD, not to us, but to Your name be the glory, because of Your loving devotion, because of Your faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.2', 'BSB', 'Why should the nations say, “Where is their God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.3', 'BSB', 'Our God is in heaven; He does as He pleases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.4', 'BSB', 'Their idols are silver and gold, made by the hands of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.5', 'BSB', 'They have mouths, but cannot speak; they have eyes, but cannot see;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.6', 'BSB', 'they have ears, but cannot hear; they have noses, but cannot smell;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.7', 'BSB', 'they have hands, but cannot feel; they have feet, but cannot walk; they cannot even clear their throats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.8', 'BSB', 'Those who make them become like them, as do all who trust in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.9', 'BSB', 'O Israel, trust in the LORD! He is their help and shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.10', 'BSB', 'O house of Aaron, trust in the LORD! He is their help and shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.11', 'BSB', 'You who fear the LORD, trust in the LORD! He is their help and shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.12', 'BSB', 'The LORD is mindful of us; He will bless us. He will bless the house of Israel; He will bless the house of Aaron;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.13', 'BSB', 'He will bless those who fear the LORD— small and great alike.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.14', 'BSB', 'May the LORD give you increase, both you and your children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.15', 'BSB', 'May you be blessed by the LORD, the Maker of heaven and earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.16', 'BSB', 'The highest heavens belong to the LORD, but the earth He has given to mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.17', 'BSB', 'It is not the dead who praise the LORD, nor any who descend into silence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.115.18', 'BSB', 'But it is we who will bless the LORD, both now and forevermore. Hallelujah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.116.1', 'BSB', 'I love the LORD, for He has heard my voice— my appeal for mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.116.2', 'BSB', 'Because He has inclined His ear to me, I will call on Him as long as I live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.116.3', 'BSB', 'The ropes of death entangled me; the anguish of Sheol overcame me; I was confronted by trouble and sorrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ps.116.4', 'BSB', 'Then I called on the name of the LORD: “O LORD, deliver my soul!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
