('Prov.18.24', 'BSB', 'A man of many companions may come to ruin, but there is a friend who stays closer than a brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.1', 'BSB', 'Better a poor man who walks with integrity than a fool whose lips are perverse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.2', 'BSB', 'Even zeal is no good without knowledge, and he who hurries his footsteps misses the mark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.3', 'BSB', 'A man’s own folly subverts his way, yet his heart rages against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.4', 'BSB', 'Wealth attracts many friends, but a poor man is deserted by his friend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.5', 'BSB', 'A false witness will not go unpunished, and one who utters lies will not escape.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.6', 'BSB', 'Many seek the favor of the prince, and everyone is a friend of the gift giver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.7', 'BSB', 'All the brothers of a poor man hate him— how much more do his friends avoid him! He may pursue them with pleading, but they are nowhere to be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.8', 'BSB', 'He who acquires wisdom loves himself; one who safeguards understanding will find success.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.9', 'BSB', 'A false witness will not go unpunished, and one who pours out lies will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.10', 'BSB', 'Luxury is unseemly for a fool— how much worse for a slave to rule over princes!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.11', 'BSB', 'A man’s insight gives him patience, and his virtue is to overlook an offense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.12', 'BSB', 'A king’s rage is like the roar of a lion, but his favor is like dew on the grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.13', 'BSB', 'A foolish son is his father’s ruin, and a quarrelsome wife is like a constant dripping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.14', 'BSB', 'Houses and wealth are inherited from fathers, but a prudent wife is from the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.15', 'BSB', 'Laziness brings on deep sleep, and an idle soul will suffer hunger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.16', 'BSB', 'He who keeps a commandment preserves his soul, but he who is careless in his ways will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.17', 'BSB', 'Kindness to the poor is a loan to the LORD, and He will repay the lender.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.18', 'BSB', 'Discipline your son, for in that there is hope; do not be party to his death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.19', 'BSB', 'A man of great anger must pay the penalty; if you rescue him, you will have to do so again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.20', 'BSB', 'Listen to counsel and accept discipline, that you may be wise the rest of your days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.21', 'BSB', 'Many plans are in a man’s heart, but the purpose of the LORD will prevail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.22', 'BSB', 'The desire of a man is loving devotion; better to be poor than a liar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.23', 'BSB', 'The fear of the LORD leads to life, that one may rest content, without visitation from harm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.24', 'BSB', 'The slacker buries his hand in the dish; he will not even bring it back to his mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.25', 'BSB', 'Strike a mocker, and the simple will beware; rebuke the discerning man, and he will gain knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.26', 'BSB', 'He who assaults his father or evicts his mother is a son who brings shame and disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.27', 'BSB', 'If you cease to hear instruction, my son, you will stray from the words of knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.28', 'BSB', 'A corrupt witness mocks justice, and a wicked mouth swallows iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.19.29', 'BSB', 'Judgments are prepared for mockers, and beatings for the backs of fools.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.1', 'BSB', 'Wine is a mocker, strong drink is a brawler, and whoever is led astray by them is not wise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.2', 'BSB', 'The terror of a king is like the roar of a lion; whoever provokes him forfeits his own life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.3', 'BSB', 'It is honorable for a man to resolve a dispute, but any fool will quarrel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.4', 'BSB', 'The slacker does not plow in season; at harvest time he looks, but nothing is there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.5', 'BSB', 'The intentions of a man’s heart are deep waters, but a man of understanding draws them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.6', 'BSB', 'Many a man proclaims his loving devotion, but who can find a trustworthy man?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.7', 'BSB', 'The righteous man walks with integrity; blessed are his children after him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.8', 'BSB', 'A king who sits on a throne to judge sifts out all evil with his eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.9', 'BSB', 'Who can say, “I have kept my heart pure; I am cleansed from my sin”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.10', 'BSB', 'Differing weights and unequal measures — both are detestable to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.11', 'BSB', 'Even a young man is known by his actions— whether his conduct is pure and upright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.12', 'BSB', 'Ears that hear and eyes that see— the LORD has made them both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.13', 'BSB', 'Do not love sleep, or you will grow poor; open your eyes, and you will have plenty of food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.14', 'BSB', '“Worthless, worthless!” says the buyer, but on the way out, he gloats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.15', 'BSB', 'There is an abundance of gold and rubies, but lips of knowledge are a rare treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.16', 'BSB', 'Take the garment of the one who posts security for a stranger; get collateral if it is for a foreigner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.17', 'BSB', 'Food gained by fraud is sweet to a man, but later his mouth is full of gravel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.18', 'BSB', 'Set plans by consultation, and wage war under sound guidance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.19', 'BSB', 'He who reveals secrets is a constant gossip; avoid the one who babbles with his lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.20', 'BSB', 'Whoever curses his father or mother, his lamp will be extinguished in deepest darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.21', 'BSB', 'An inheritance gained quickly will not be blessed in the end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.22', 'BSB', 'Do not say, “I will avenge this evil!” Wait on the LORD, and He will save you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.23', 'BSB', 'Unequal weights are detestable to the LORD, and dishonest scales are no good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.24', 'BSB', 'A man’s steps are from the LORD, so how can anyone understand his own way?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.25', 'BSB', 'It is a trap for a man to dedicate something rashly, only later to reconsider his vows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.26', 'BSB', 'A wise king separates out the wicked and drives the threshing wheel over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.27', 'BSB', 'The spirit of a man is the lamp of the LORD, searching out his inmost being.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.28', 'BSB', 'Loving devotion and faithfulness preserve a king; by these he maintains his throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.29', 'BSB', 'The glory of young men is their strength, and gray hair is the splendor of the old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.20.30', 'BSB', 'Lashes and wounds scour evil, and beatings cleanse the inmost parts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.1', 'BSB', 'The king’s heart is a waterway in the hand of the LORD; He directs it where He pleases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.2', 'BSB', 'All a man’s ways seem right to him, but the LORD weighs the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.3', 'BSB', 'To do righteousness and justice is more desirable to the LORD than sacrifice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.4', 'BSB', 'Haughty eyes and a proud heart— the guides of the wicked—are sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.5', 'BSB', 'The plans of the diligent bring plenty, as surely as haste leads to poverty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.6', 'BSB', 'Making a fortune by a lying tongue is a vanishing mist, a deadly pursuit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.7', 'BSB', 'The violence of the wicked will sweep them away because they refuse to do what is just.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.8', 'BSB', 'The way of a guilty man is crooked, but the conduct of the innocent is upright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.9', 'BSB', 'Better to live on a corner of the roof than to share a house with a quarrelsome wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.10', 'BSB', 'The soul of the wicked man craves evil; his neighbor finds no favor in his eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.11', 'BSB', 'When a mocker is punished, the simple gain wisdom; and when a wise man is instructed, he acquires knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.12', 'BSB', 'The Righteous One considers the house of the wicked and brings the wicked to ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.13', 'BSB', 'Whoever shuts his ears to the cry of the poor, he too shall cry out and receive no answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.14', 'BSB', 'A gift in secret soothes anger, and a covert bribe pacifies great wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.15', 'BSB', 'Justice executed is a joy to the righteous, but a terror to the workers of iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.16', 'BSB', 'The man who strays from the path of understanding will rest in the assembly of the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.17', 'BSB', 'He who loves pleasure will become poor; the one who loves wine and oil will never be rich.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.18', 'BSB', 'The wicked become a ransom for the righteous, and the faithless for the upright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.19', 'BSB', 'Better to live in the desert than with a contentious and ill-tempered wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.20', 'BSB', 'Precious treasures and oil are in the dwelling of the wise, but a foolish man consumes them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.21', 'BSB', 'He who pursues righteousness and loving devotion finds life, righteousness, and honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.22', 'BSB', 'A wise man scales the city of the mighty and pulls down the stronghold in which they trust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.23', 'BSB', 'He who guards his mouth and tongue keeps his soul from distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.24', 'BSB', 'Mocker is the name of the proud and arrogant man— of him who acts with excessive pride.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.25', 'BSB', 'The craving of the slacker kills him because his hands refuse to work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.26', 'BSB', 'All day long he covets more, but the righteous give without restraint.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.27', 'BSB', 'The sacrifice of the wicked is detestable— how much more so when brought with ill intent!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.28', 'BSB', 'A lying witness will perish, but the man who listens to truth will speak forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.29', 'BSB', 'A wicked man hardens his face, but the upright man makes his way sure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.30', 'BSB', 'There is no wisdom, no understanding, no counsel that can prevail against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.21.31', 'BSB', 'A horse is prepared for the day of battle, but victory is of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.1', 'BSB', 'A good name is more desirable than great riches; favor is better than silver and gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.2', 'BSB', 'The rich and the poor have this in common: The LORD is Maker of them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.3', 'BSB', 'The prudent see danger and take cover, but the simple keep going and suffer the consequences.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.4', 'BSB', 'The rewards of humility and the fear of the LORD are wealth and honor and life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.5', 'BSB', 'Thorns and snares lie on the path of the perverse; he who guards his soul stays far from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.6', 'BSB', 'Train up a child in the way he should go, and when he is old he will not depart from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.7', 'BSB', 'The rich rule over the poor, and the borrower is slave to the lender.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.8', 'BSB', 'He who sows injustice will reap disaster, and the rod of his fury will be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.9', 'BSB', 'A generous man will be blessed, for he shares his bread with the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.10', 'BSB', 'Drive out the mocker, and conflict will depart; even quarreling and insults will cease.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.11', 'BSB', 'He who loves a pure heart and gracious lips will have the king for a friend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.12', 'BSB', 'The LORD’s eyes keep watch over knowledge, but He frustrates the words of the faithless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.13', 'BSB', 'The slacker says, “There is a lion outside! I will be slain in the streets!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.14', 'BSB', 'The mouth of an adulteress is a deep pit; he who is under the wrath of the LORD will fall into it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.15', 'BSB', 'Foolishness is bound up in the heart of a child, but the rod of discipline drives it far from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.16', 'BSB', 'Oppressing the poor to enrich oneself or giving gifts to the rich will surely lead to poverty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.17', 'BSB', 'Incline your ear and hear the words of the wise— apply your mind to my knowledge—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.18', 'BSB', 'for it is pleasing when you keep them within you and they are constantly on your lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.19', 'BSB', 'So that your trust may be in the LORD, I instruct you today—yes, you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.20', 'BSB', 'Have I not written for you thirty sayings about counsel and knowledge,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.21', 'BSB', 'to show you true and reliable words, that you may soundly answer those who sent you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.22', 'BSB', 'Do not rob a poor man because he is poor, and do not crush the afflicted at the gate,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.23', 'BSB', 'for the LORD will take up their case and will plunder those who rob them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.24', 'BSB', 'Do not make friends with an angry man, and do not associate with a hot-tempered man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.25', 'BSB', 'or you may learn his ways and entangle yourself in a snare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.26', 'BSB', 'Do not be one who gives pledges, who puts up security for debts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.27', 'BSB', 'If you have nothing with which to pay, why should your bed be taken from under you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.28', 'BSB', 'Do not move an ancient boundary stone which your fathers have placed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.22.29', 'BSB', 'Do you see a man skilled in his work? He will be stationed in the presence of kings; he will not stand before obscure men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.1', 'BSB', 'When you sit down to dine with a ruler, consider carefully what is set before you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.2', 'BSB', 'and put a knife to your throat if you possess a great appetite.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.3', 'BSB', 'Do not crave his delicacies, for that food is deceptive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.4', 'BSB', 'Do not wear yourself out to get rich; be wise enough to restrain yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.5', 'BSB', 'When you glance at wealth, it disappears, for it makes wings for itself and flies like an eagle to the sky.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.6', 'BSB', 'Do not eat the bread of a stingy man, and do not crave his delicacies;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.7', 'BSB', 'for he is keeping track, inwardly counting the cost. “Eat and drink,” he says to you, but his heart is not with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.8', 'BSB', 'You will vomit up what little you have eaten and waste your pleasant words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.9', 'BSB', 'Do not speak to a fool, for he will despise the wisdom of your words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.10', 'BSB', 'Do not move an ancient boundary stone or encroach on the fields of the fatherless,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.11', 'BSB', 'for their Redeemer is strong; He will take up their case against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.12', 'BSB', 'Apply your heart to instruction and your ears to words of knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.13', 'BSB', 'Do not withhold discipline from a child; although you strike him with a rod, he will not die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.14', 'BSB', 'Strike him with a rod, and you will deliver his soul from Sheol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.15', 'BSB', 'My son, if your heart is wise, my own heart will indeed rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.16', 'BSB', 'My inmost being will rejoice when your lips speak what is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.17', 'BSB', 'Do not let your heart envy sinners, but always continue in the fear of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.18', 'BSB', 'For surely there is a future, and your hope will not be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.19', 'BSB', 'Listen, my son, and be wise, and guide your heart on the right course.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.20', 'BSB', 'Do not join those who drink too much wine or gorge themselves on meat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.21', 'BSB', 'For the drunkard and the glutton will come to poverty, and drowsiness will clothe them in rags.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.22', 'BSB', 'Listen to your father who gave you life, and do not despise your mother when she is old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.23', 'BSB', 'Invest in truth and never sell it— in wisdom and instruction and understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.24', 'BSB', 'The father of a righteous man will greatly rejoice, and he who fathers a wise son will delight in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.25', 'BSB', 'May your father and mother be glad, and may she who gave you birth rejoice!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.26', 'BSB', 'My son, give me your heart, and let your eyes delight in my ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.27', 'BSB', 'For a prostitute is a deep pit, and an adulteress is a narrow well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.28', 'BSB', 'Like a robber she lies in wait and multiplies the faithless among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.29', 'BSB', 'Who has woe? Who has sorrow? Who has contentions? Who has complaints? Who has needless wounds? Who has bloodshot eyes?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.30', 'BSB', 'Those who linger over wine, who go to taste mixed drinks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.31', 'BSB', 'Do not gaze at wine while it is red, when it sparkles in the cup and goes down smoothly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.32', 'BSB', 'In the end it bites like a snake and stings like a viper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.33', 'BSB', 'Your eyes will see strange things, and your mind will utter perversities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.34', 'BSB', 'You will be like one sleeping on the high seas or lying on the top of a mast:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.23.35', 'BSB', '“They struck me, but I feel no pain! They beat me, but I did not know it! When can I wake up to search for another drink?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.1', 'BSB', 'Do not envy wicked men or desire their company;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.2', 'BSB', 'for their hearts devise violence, and their lips declare trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.3', 'BSB', 'By wisdom a house is built and by understanding it is established;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.4', 'BSB', 'through knowledge its rooms are filled with every precious and beautiful treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.5', 'BSB', 'A wise man is strong, and a man of knowledge enhances his strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.6', 'BSB', 'Only with sound guidance should you wage war, and victory lies in a multitude of counselors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.7', 'BSB', 'Wisdom is too high for a fool; he does not open his mouth in the meeting place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.8', 'BSB', 'He who plots evil will be called a schemer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.9', 'BSB', 'A foolish scheme is sin, and a mocker is detestable to men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.10', 'BSB', 'If you faint in the day of distress, how small is your strength!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.11', 'BSB', 'Rescue those being led away to death, and restrain those stumbling toward the slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.12', 'BSB', 'If you say, “Behold, we did not know about this,” does not He who weighs hearts consider it? Does not the One who guards your life know? Will He not repay a man according to his deeds?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.13', 'BSB', 'Eat honey, my son, for it is good, and the honeycomb is sweet to your taste.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.14', 'BSB', 'Know therefore that wisdom is sweet to your soul. If you find it, there is a future for you, and your hope will never be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.15', 'BSB', 'Do not lie in wait, O wicked man, near the dwelling of the righteous; do not destroy his resting place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.16', 'BSB', 'For though a righteous man may fall seven times, he still gets up; but the wicked stumble in bad times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.17', 'BSB', 'Do not gloat when your enemy falls, and do not let your heart rejoice when he stumbles,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.18', 'BSB', 'or the LORD will see and disapprove, and turn His wrath away from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.19', 'BSB', 'Do not fret over evildoers, and do not be envious of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.20', 'BSB', 'For the evil man has no future; the lamp of the wicked will be extinguished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.21', 'BSB', 'My son, fear the LORD and the king, and do not associate with the rebellious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.22', 'BSB', 'For they will bring sudden destruction. Who knows what ruin they can bring?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.23', 'BSB', 'These also are sayings of the wise: To show partiality in judgment is not good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.24', 'BSB', 'Whoever tells the guilty, “You are innocent”— peoples will curse him, and nations will denounce him;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.25', 'BSB', 'but it will go well with those who convict the guilty, and rich blessing will come upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.26', 'BSB', 'An honest answer given is like a kiss on the lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.27', 'BSB', 'Complete your outdoor work and prepare your field; after that, you may build your house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.28', 'BSB', 'Do not testify against your neighbor without cause, and do not deceive with your lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.29', 'BSB', 'Do not say, “I will do to him as he has done to me; I will repay the man according to his work.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.30', 'BSB', 'I went past the field of a slacker and by the vineyard of a man lacking judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.31', 'BSB', 'Thorns had grown up everywhere, thistles had covered the ground, and the stone wall was broken down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.32', 'BSB', 'I observed and took it to heart; I looked and received instruction:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.33', 'BSB', 'A little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to rest,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.24.34', 'BSB', 'and poverty will come upon you like a robber, and need like a bandit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.1', 'BSB', 'These are additional proverbs of Solomon, which were copied by the men of Hezekiah king of Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.2', 'BSB', 'It is the glory of God to conceal a matter and the glory of kings to search it out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.3', 'BSB', 'As the heavens are high and the earth is deep, so the hearts of kings cannot be searched.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.4', 'BSB', 'Remove the dross from the silver, and a vessel for a silversmith will come forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.5', 'BSB', 'Remove the wicked from the king’s presence, and his throne will be established in righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.6', 'BSB', 'Do not exalt yourself in the presence of the king, and do not stand in the place of great men;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.7', 'BSB', 'for it is better that he says to you, “Come up here!” than that you should be demoted in the presence of the prince. Even what you have seen with your own eyes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.8', 'BSB', 'do not bring hastily to court. Otherwise, what will you do in the end when your neighbor puts you to shame?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.9', 'BSB', 'Argue your case with your neighbor without betraying another’s confidence,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.10', 'BSB', 'lest the one who hears may disgrace you, and your infamy never go away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.11', 'BSB', 'A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in settings of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.12', 'BSB', 'Like an earring of gold or an ornament of fine gold is a wise man’s rebuke to a listening ear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.13', 'BSB', 'Like the cold of snow in the time of harvest is a trustworthy messenger to those who send him; he refreshes the soul of his masters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.14', 'BSB', 'Like clouds and wind without rain is the man who boasts of gifts never given.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.15', 'BSB', 'Through patience a ruler can be persuaded, and a gentle tongue can break a bone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.16', 'BSB', 'If you find honey, eat just what you need, lest you have too much and vomit it up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.17', 'BSB', 'Seldom set foot in your neighbor’s house, lest he grow weary and hate you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.18', 'BSB', 'Like a club or sword or sharp arrow is a man who bears false witness against his neighbor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.19', 'BSB', 'Like a broken tooth or a foot out of joint is confidence in a faithless man in time of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.20', 'BSB', 'Like one who removes a garment on a cold day or vinegar poured on a wound is one who sings songs to a heavy heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.21', 'BSB', 'If your enemy is hungry, give him food to eat, and if he is thirsty, give him water to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.22', 'BSB', 'For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head, and the LORD will reward you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.23', 'BSB', 'As the north wind brings forth rain, so a backbiting tongue brings angry looks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.24', 'BSB', 'Better to live on a corner of the roof than to share a house with a quarrelsome wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.25', 'BSB', 'Like cold water to a weary soul is good news from a distant land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.26', 'BSB', 'Like a muddied spring or a polluted well is a righteous man who gives way to the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.27', 'BSB', 'It is not good to eat too much honey or to search out one’s own glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.25.28', 'BSB', 'Like a city whose walls are broken down is a man who does not control his temper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.1', 'BSB', 'Like snow in summer and rain at harvest, honor does not befit a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.2', 'BSB', 'Like a fluttering sparrow or darting swallow, an undeserved curse does not come to rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.3', 'BSB', 'A whip for the horse, a bridle for the donkey, and a rod for the backs of fools!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.4', 'BSB', 'Do not answer a fool according to his folly, or you yourself will be like him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.5', 'BSB', 'Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he become wise in his own eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.6', 'BSB', 'Like cutting off one’s own feet or drinking violence is the sending of a message by the hand of a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.7', 'BSB', 'Like lame legs hanging limp is a proverb in the mouth of a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.8', 'BSB', 'Like binding a stone into a sling is the giving of honor to a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.9', 'BSB', 'Like a thorn that falls into the hand of a drunkard is a proverb in the mouth of a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.10', 'BSB', 'Like an archer who wounds at random is he who hires a fool or passerby.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.11', 'BSB', 'As a dog returns to its vomit, so a fool repeats his folly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.12', 'BSB', 'Do you see a man who is wise in his own eyes? There is more hope for a fool than for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.13', 'BSB', 'The slacker says, “A lion is in the road! A fierce lion roams the public square!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.14', 'BSB', 'As a door turns on its hinges, so the slacker turns on his bed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.15', 'BSB', 'The slacker buries his hand in the dish; it wearies him to bring it back to his mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.16', 'BSB', 'The slacker is wiser in his own eyes than seven men who answer discreetly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.17', 'BSB', 'Like one who grabs a dog by the ears is a passerby who meddles in a quarrel not his own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.18', 'BSB', 'Like a madman shooting firebrands and deadly arrows,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.19', 'BSB', 'so is the man who deceives his neighbor and says, “I was only joking!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.20', 'BSB', 'Without wood, a fire goes out; without gossip, a conflict ceases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.21', 'BSB', 'Like charcoal for embers and wood for fire, so is a quarrelsome man for kindling strife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.22', 'BSB', 'The words of a gossip are like choice morsels that go down into the inmost being.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.23', 'BSB', 'Like glaze covering an earthen vessel are burning lips and a wicked heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.24', 'BSB', 'A hateful man disguises himself with his speech, but he lays up deceit in his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.25', 'BSB', 'When he speaks graciously, do not believe him, for seven abominations fill his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.26', 'BSB', 'Though his hatred is concealed by deception, his wickedness will be exposed in the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.27', 'BSB', 'He who digs a pit will fall into it, and he who rolls a stone will have it roll back on him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.26.28', 'BSB', 'A lying tongue hates those it crushes, and a flattering mouth causes ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.1', 'BSB', 'Do not boast about tomorrow, for you do not know what a day may bring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.2', 'BSB', 'Let another praise you, and not your own mouth— a stranger, and not your own lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.3', 'BSB', 'A stone is heavy and sand is a burden, but aggravation from a fool outweighs them both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.4', 'BSB', 'Wrath is cruel and anger is like a flood, but who can withstand jealousy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.5', 'BSB', 'Better an open rebuke than love that is concealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.6', 'BSB', 'The wounds of a friend are faithful, but the kisses of an enemy are deceitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.7', 'BSB', 'The soul that is full loathes honey, but to a hungry soul, any bitter thing is sweet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.8', 'BSB', 'Like a bird that strays from its nest is a man who wanders from his home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.9', 'BSB', 'Oil and incense bring joy to the heart, and the sweetness of a friend is counsel to the soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.10', 'BSB', 'Do not forsake your friend or your father’s friend, and do not go to your brother’s house in the day of your calamity; better a neighbor nearby than a brother far away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.11', 'BSB', 'Be wise, my son, and bring joy to my heart, so that I can answer him who taunts me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.12', 'BSB', 'The prudent see danger and take cover; but the simple keep going and pay the penalty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.13', 'BSB', 'Take the garment of him who posts security for a stranger; get collateral if it is for a foreigner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.14', 'BSB', 'If one blesses his neighbor with a loud voice early in the morning, it will be counted to him as a curse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.15', 'BSB', 'A constant dripping on a rainy day and a contentious woman are alike—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.16', 'BSB', 'restraining her is like holding back the wind or grasping oil with one’s right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.17', 'BSB', 'As iron sharpens iron, so one man sharpens another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.18', 'BSB', 'Whoever tends a fig tree will eat its fruit, and he who looks after his master will be honored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.19', 'BSB', 'As water reflects the face, so the heart reflects the true man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.20', 'BSB', 'Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied; so the eyes of man are never satisfied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.21', 'BSB', 'A crucible for silver and a furnace for gold, but a man is tested by the praise accorded him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.22', 'BSB', 'Though you grind a fool like grain with mortar and a pestle, yet his folly will not depart from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.23', 'BSB', 'Be sure to know the state of your flocks, and pay close attention to your herds;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.24', 'BSB', 'for riches are not forever, nor does a crown endure to every generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.25', 'BSB', 'When hay is removed and new growth appears and the grain from the hills is gathered,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.26', 'BSB', 'the lambs will provide you with clothing, and the goats with the price of a field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.27.27', 'BSB', 'You will have plenty of goats’ milk to feed you— food for your household and nourishment for your maidservants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.1', 'BSB', 'The wicked flee when no one pursues, but the righteous are as bold as a lion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.2', 'BSB', 'A land in rebellion has many rulers, but a man of understanding and knowledge maintains order.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.3', 'BSB', 'A destitute leader who oppresses the poor is like a driving rain that leaves no food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.4', 'BSB', 'Those who forsake the law praise the wicked, but those who keep the law resist them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.5', 'BSB', 'Evil men do not understand justice, but those who seek the LORD comprehend fully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.6', 'BSB', 'Better a poor man who walks with integrity than a rich man whose ways are perverse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.7', 'BSB', 'A discerning son keeps the law, but a companion of gluttons disgraces his father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.8', 'BSB', 'He who increases his wealth by interest and usury lays it up for one who is kind to the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.9', 'BSB', 'Whoever turns his ear away from hearing the law, even his prayer is detestable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.10', 'BSB', 'He who leads the upright along the path of evil will fall into his own pit, but the blameless will inherit what is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.11', 'BSB', 'A rich man is wise in his own eyes, but a poor man with discernment sees through him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.12', 'BSB', 'When the righteous triumph, there is great glory, but when the wicked rise, men hide themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.13', 'BSB', 'He who conceals his sins will not prosper, but whoever confesses and renounces them will find mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.14', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man who is always reverent, but he who hardens his heart falls into trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.15', 'BSB', 'Like a roaring lion or a charging bear is a wicked ruler over a helpless people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.16', 'BSB', 'A leader who lacks judgment is also a great oppressor, but he who hates dishonest profit will prolong his days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.17', 'BSB', 'A man burdened by bloodguilt will flee into the Pit; let no one support him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.18', 'BSB', 'He who walks with integrity will be kept safe, but whoever is perverse in his ways will suddenly fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.19', 'BSB', 'The one who works his land will have plenty of food, but whoever chases fantasies will have his fill of poverty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.20', 'BSB', 'A faithful man will abound with blessings, but one eager to be rich will not go unpunished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.21', 'BSB', 'To show partiality is not good, yet a man will do wrong for a piece of bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.22', 'BSB', 'A stingy man hastens after wealth and does not know that poverty awaits him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.23', 'BSB', 'He who rebukes a man will later find more favor than one who flatters with his tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.24', 'BSB', 'He who robs his father or mother, saying, “It is not wrong,” is a companion to the man who destroys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.25', 'BSB', 'A greedy man stirs up strife, but he who trusts in the LORD will prosper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.26', 'BSB', 'He who trusts in himself is a fool, but one who walks in wisdom will be safe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.27', 'BSB', 'Whoever gives to the poor will not be in need, but he who hides his eyes will receive many curses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.28.28', 'BSB', 'When the wicked come to power, people hide themselves; but when they perish, the righteous flourish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.1', 'BSB', 'A man who remains stiff-necked after much reproof will suddenly be shattered beyond recovery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.2', 'BSB', 'When the righteous flourish, the people rejoice, but when the wicked rule, the people groan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.3', 'BSB', 'A man who loves wisdom brings joy to his father, but a companion of prostitutes squanders his wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.4', 'BSB', 'By justice a king brings stability to the land, but a man who exacts tribute demolishes it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.5', 'BSB', 'A man who flatters his neighbor spreads a net for his feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.6', 'BSB', 'An evil man is caught by his own sin, but a righteous one sings and rejoices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.7', 'BSB', 'The righteous consider the cause of the poor, but the wicked have no regard for such concerns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.8', 'BSB', 'Mockers inflame a city, but the wise turn away anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.9', 'BSB', 'If a wise man goes to court with a fool, there will be raving and laughing with no resolution.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.10', 'BSB', 'Men of bloodshed hate a blameless man, but the upright care for his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.11', 'BSB', 'A fool vents all his anger, but a wise man holds it back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.12', 'BSB', 'If a ruler listens to lies, all his officials will be wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.13', 'BSB', 'The poor man and the oppressor have this in common: The LORD gives light to the eyes of both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.14', 'BSB', 'A king who judges the poor with fairness— his throne will be established forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.15', 'BSB', 'A rod of correction imparts wisdom, but a child left to himself disgraces his mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.16', 'BSB', 'When the wicked thrive, rebellion increases; but the righteous will see their downfall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.17', 'BSB', 'Discipline your son, and he will give you rest; he will bring delight to your soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.18', 'BSB', 'Where there is no vision, the people cast off restraint; but blessed is he who keeps the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.19', 'BSB', 'A servant cannot be corrected by words alone; though he understands, he will not respond.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.20', 'BSB', 'Do you see a man who speaks in haste? There is more hope for a fool than for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.21', 'BSB', 'A servant pampered from his youth will bring grief in the end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.22', 'BSB', 'An angry man stirs up dissension, and a hot-tempered man abounds in transgression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.23', 'BSB', 'A man’s pride will bring him low, but a humble spirit will obtain honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.24', 'BSB', 'A partner to a thief hates his own soul; he receives the oath, but does not testify.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.25', 'BSB', 'The fear of man is a snare, but whoever trusts in the LORD is set securely on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.26', 'BSB', 'Many seek the ruler’s favor, but a man receives justice from the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.29.27', 'BSB', 'An unjust man is detestable to the righteous, and one whose way is upright is detestable to the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of Agur son of Jakeh—the burden that this man declared to Ithiel: “I am weary, O God, and worn out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.2', 'BSB', 'Surely I am the most ignorant of men, and I lack the understanding of a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.3', 'BSB', 'I have not learned wisdom, and I have no knowledge of the Holy One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.4', 'BSB', 'Who has ascended to heaven and come down? Who has gathered the wind in His hands? Who has bound up the waters in His cloak? Who has established all the ends of the earth? What is His name, and what is the name of His Son— surely you know!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.5', 'BSB', 'Every word of God is flawless; He is a shield to those who take refuge in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.6', 'BSB', 'Do not add to His words, lest He rebuke you and prove you a liar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.7', 'BSB', 'Two things I ask of You— do not refuse me before I die:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.8', 'BSB', 'Keep falsehood and deceitful words far from me. Give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with the bread that is my portion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.9', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, I may have too much and deny You, saying, ‘Who is the LORD?’ Or I may become poor and steal, profaning the name of my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.10', 'BSB', 'Do not slander a servant to his master, or he will curse you, and you will bear the guilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.11', 'BSB', 'There is a generation of those who curse their fathers and do not bless their mothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.12', 'BSB', 'There is a generation of those who are pure in their own eyes and yet unwashed of their filth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.13', 'BSB', 'There is a generation—how haughty are their eyes and pretentious are their glances—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.14', 'BSB', 'there is a generation whose teeth are swords and whose jaws are knives, devouring the oppressed from the earth and the needy from among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.15', 'BSB', 'The leech has two daughters: Give and Give. There are three things that are never satisfied, four that never say, ‘Enough!’:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.16', 'BSB', 'Sheol, the barren womb, land never satisfied with water, and fire that never says, ‘Enough!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.17', 'BSB', 'As for the eye that mocks a father and scorns obedience to a mother, may the ravens of the valley pluck it out and young vultures devour it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.18', 'BSB', 'There are three things too wonderful for me, four that I cannot understand:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.19', 'BSB', 'the way of an eagle in the sky, the way of a snake on a rock, the way of a ship at sea, and the way of a man with a maiden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.20', 'BSB', 'This is the way of an adulteress: She eats and wipes her mouth and says, ‘I have done nothing wrong.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.21', 'BSB', 'Under three things the earth trembles, under four it cannot bear up:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.22', 'BSB', 'a servant who becomes king, a fool who is filled with food,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.23', 'BSB', 'an unloved woman who marries, and a maidservant who supplants her mistress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.24', 'BSB', 'Four things on earth are small, yet they are exceedingly wise:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.25', 'BSB', 'The ants are creatures of little strength, yet they store up their food in the summer;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.26', 'BSB', 'the rock badgers are creatures of little power, yet they make their homes in the rocks;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.27', 'BSB', 'the locusts have no king, yet they all advance in formation;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.28', 'BSB', 'and the lizard can be caught in one’s hands, yet it is found in the palaces of kings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.29', 'BSB', 'There are three things that are stately in their stride, and four that are impressive in their walk:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.30', 'BSB', 'a lion, mighty among beasts, refusing to retreat before anything;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.31', 'BSB', 'a strutting rooster; a he-goat; and a king with his army around him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.32', 'BSB', 'If you have foolishly exalted yourself or if you have plotted evil, put your hand over your mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.30.33', 'BSB', 'For as the churning of milk yields butter, and the twisting of the nose draws blood, so the stirring of anger brings forth strife.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of King Lemuel—the burden that his mother taught him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.2', 'BSB', 'What shall I say, O my son? What, O son of my womb? What, O son of my vows?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.3', 'BSB', 'Do not spend your strength on women or your vigor on those who ruin kings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.4', 'BSB', 'It is not for kings, O Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine, or for rulers to crave strong drink,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.5', 'BSB', 'lest they drink and forget what is decreed, depriving all the oppressed of justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.6', 'BSB', 'Give strong drink to one who is perishing, and wine to the bitter in soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.7', 'BSB', 'Let him drink and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.8', 'BSB', 'Open your mouth for those with no voice, for the cause of all the dispossessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.9', 'BSB', 'Open your mouth, judge righteously, and defend the cause of the poor and needy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.10', 'BSB', 'A wife of noble character, who can find? She is far more precious than rubies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.11', 'BSB', 'The heart of her husband trusts in her, and he lacks nothing of value.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.12', 'BSB', 'She brings him good and not harm all the days of her life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.13', 'BSB', 'She selects wool and flax and works with eager hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.14', 'BSB', 'She is like the merchant ships, bringing her food from afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.15', 'BSB', 'She rises while it is still night to provide food for her household and portions for her maidservants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.16', 'BSB', 'She appraises a field and buys it; from her earnings she plants a vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.17', 'BSB', 'She girds herself with strength and shows that her arms are strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.18', 'BSB', 'She sees that her gain is good, and her lamp is not extinguished at night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.19', 'BSB', 'She stretches out her hands to the distaff and grasps the spindle with her fingers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.20', 'BSB', 'She opens her arms to the poor and reaches out her hands to the needy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.21', 'BSB', 'When it snows, she has no fear for her household, for they are all clothed in scarlet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.22', 'BSB', 'She makes coverings for her bed; her clothing is fine linen and purple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.23', 'BSB', 'Her husband is known at the city gate, where he sits among the elders of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.24', 'BSB', 'She makes linen garments and sells them; she delivers sashes to the merchants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.25', 'BSB', 'Strength and honor are her clothing, and she can laugh at the days to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.26', 'BSB', 'She opens her mouth with wisdom, and faithful instruction is on her tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.27', 'BSB', 'She watches over the affairs of her household and does not eat the bread of idleness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.28', 'BSB', 'Her children rise up and call her blessed; her husband praises her as well:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.29', 'BSB', '“Many daughters have done noble things, but you surpass them all!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.30', 'BSB', 'Charm is deceptive and beauty is fleeting, but a woman who fears the LORD is to be praised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Prov.31.31', 'BSB', 'Give her the fruit of her hands, and let her works praise her at the gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of the Teacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.2', 'BSB', '“Futility of futilities,” says the Teacher, “futility of futilities! Everything is futile!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.3', 'BSB', 'What does a man gain from all his labor, at which he toils under the sun?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.4', 'BSB', 'Generations come and generations go, but the earth remains forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.5', 'BSB', 'The sun rises and the sun sets; it hurries back to where it rises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.6', 'BSB', 'The wind blows southward, then turns northward; round and round it swirls, ever returning on its course.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.7', 'BSB', 'All the rivers flow into the sea, yet the sea is never full; to the place from which the streams come, there again they flow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.8', 'BSB', 'All things are wearisome, more than one can describe; the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear content with hearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.9', 'BSB', 'What has been will be again, and what has been done will be done again; there is nothing new under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.10', 'BSB', 'Is there a case where one can say, “Look, this is new”? It has already existed in the ages before us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.11', 'BSB', 'There is no remembrance of those who came before, and those yet to come will not be remembered by those who follow after.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.12', 'BSB', 'I, the Teacher, was king over Israel in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.13', 'BSB', 'And I set my mind to seek and explore by wisdom all that is done under heaven. What a heavy burden God has laid upon the sons of men to occupy them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.14', 'BSB', 'I have seen all the things that are done under the sun, and have found them all to be futile, a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.15', 'BSB', 'What is crooked cannot be straightened, and what is lacking cannot be counted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.16', 'BSB', 'I said to myself, “Behold, I have grown and increased in wisdom beyond all those before me who were over Jerusalem, and my mind has observed a wealth of wisdom and knowledge.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.17', 'BSB', 'So I set my mind to know wisdom and madness and folly; I learned that this, too, is a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.1.18', 'BSB', 'For with much wisdom comes much sorrow, and as knowledge grows, grief increases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.1', 'BSB', 'I said to myself, “Come now, I will test you with pleasure; enjoy what is good!” But it proved to be futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.2', 'BSB', 'I said of laughter, “It is folly,” and of pleasure, “What does it accomplish?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.3', 'BSB', 'I sought to cheer my body with wine and to embrace folly—my mind still guiding me with wisdom—until I could see what was worthwhile for men to do under heaven during the few days of their lives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.4', 'BSB', 'I expanded my pursuits. I built houses and planted vineyards for myself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.5', 'BSB', 'I made gardens and parks for myself, where I planted all kinds of fruit trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.6', 'BSB', 'I built reservoirs to water my groves of flourishing trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.7', 'BSB', 'I acquired menservants and maidservants, and servants were born in my house. I also owned more herds and flocks than anyone in Jerusalem before me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.8', 'BSB', 'and I accumulated for myself silver and gold and the treasure of kings and provinces. I gathered to myself male and female singers, and the delights of the sons of men—many concubines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.9', 'BSB', 'So I became great and surpassed all in Jerusalem who had preceded me; and my wisdom remained with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.10', 'BSB', 'Anything my eyes desired, I did not deny myself. I refused my heart no pleasure. For my heart took delight in all my work, and this was the reward for all my labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.11', 'BSB', 'Yet when I considered all the works that my hands had accomplished and what I had toiled to achieve, I found everything to be futile, a pursuit of the wind; there was nothing to be gained under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.12', 'BSB', 'Then I turned to consider wisdom and madness and folly; for what more can the king’s successor do than what has already been accomplished?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.13', 'BSB', 'And I saw that wisdom exceeds folly, just as light exceeds darkness:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.14', 'BSB', 'The wise man has eyes in his head, but the fool walks in darkness. Yet I also came to realize that one fate overcomes them both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.15', 'BSB', 'So I said to myself, “The fate of the fool will also befall me. What then have I gained by being wise?” And I said to myself that this too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.16', 'BSB', 'For there is no lasting remembrance of the wise, just as with the fool, seeing that both will be forgotten in the days to come. Alas, the wise man will die just like the fool!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.17', 'BSB', 'So I hated life, because the work that is done under the sun was grievous to me. For everything is futile and a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.18', 'BSB', 'I hated all for which I had toiled under the sun, because I must leave it to the man who comes after me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.19', 'BSB', 'And who knows whether that man will be wise or foolish? Yet he will take over all the labor at which I have worked skillfully under the sun. This too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.20', 'BSB', 'So my heart began to despair over all the labor that I had done under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.21', 'BSB', 'When there is a man who has labored with wisdom, knowledge, and skill, and he must give his portion to a man who has not worked for it, this too is futile and a great evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.22', 'BSB', 'For what does a man get for all the toil and striving with which he labors under the sun?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.23', 'BSB', 'Indeed, all his days are filled with grief, and his task is sorrowful; even at night, his mind does not rest. This too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.24', 'BSB', 'Nothing is better for a man than to eat and drink and enjoy his work. I have also seen that this is from the hand of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.25', 'BSB', 'For apart from Him, who can eat and who can find enjoyment?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.2.26', 'BSB', 'To the man who is pleasing in His sight, He gives wisdom and knowledge and joy, but to the sinner He assigns the task of gathering and accumulating that which he will hand over to one who pleases God. This too is futile and a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.1', 'BSB', 'To everything there is a season, and a time for every purpose under heaven:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.2', 'BSB', 'a time to be born and a time to die, a time to plant and a time to uproot,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.3', 'BSB', 'a time to kill and a time to heal, a time to break down and a time to build,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.4', 'BSB', 'a time to weep and a time to laugh, a time to mourn and a time to dance,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.5', 'BSB', 'a time to cast away stones and a time to gather stones together, a time to embrace and a time to refrain from embracing,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.6', 'BSB', 'a time to search and a time to count as lost, a time to keep and a time to discard,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.7', 'BSB', 'a time to tear and a time to mend, a time to be silent and a time to speak,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.8', 'BSB', 'a time to love and a time to hate, a time for war and a time for peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.9', 'BSB', 'What does the worker gain from his toil?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.10', 'BSB', 'I have seen the burden that God has laid upon the sons of men to occupy them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.11', 'BSB', 'He has made everything beautiful in its time. He has also set eternity in the hearts of men, yet they cannot fathom the work that God has done from beginning to end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.12', 'BSB', 'I know that there is nothing better for them than to rejoice and do good while they live,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.13', 'BSB', 'and also that every man should eat and drink and find satisfaction in all his labor—this is the gift of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.14', 'BSB', 'I know that everything God does endures forever; nothing can be added to it or taken from it. God does it so that they should fear Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.15', 'BSB', 'What exists has already been, and what will be has already been, for God will call to account what has passed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.16', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, I saw under the sun that in the place of judgment there is wickedness, and in the place of righteousness there is wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.17', 'BSB', 'I said in my heart, “God will judge the righteous and the wicked, since there is a time for every activity and every deed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.18', 'BSB', 'I said to myself, “As for the sons of men, God tests them so that they may see for themselves that they are but beasts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.19', 'BSB', 'For the fates of both men and beasts are the same: As one dies, so dies the other—they all have the same breath. Man has no advantage over the animals, since everything is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.20', 'BSB', 'All go to one place; all come from dust, and all return to dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.21', 'BSB', 'Who knows if the spirit of man rises upward and the spirit of the animal descends into the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.3.22', 'BSB', 'I have seen that there is nothing better for a man than to enjoy his work, because that is his lot. For who can bring him to see what will come after him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.1', 'BSB', 'Again I looked, and I considered all the oppression taking place under the sun. I saw the tears of the oppressed, and they had no comforter; the power lay in the hands of their oppressors, and there was no comforter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.2', 'BSB', 'So I admired the dead, who had already died, above the living, who are still alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.3', 'BSB', 'But better than both is he who has not yet existed, who has not seen the evil that is done under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.4', 'BSB', 'I saw that all labor and success spring from a man’s envy of his neighbor. This too is futile and a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.5', 'BSB', 'The fool folds his hands and consumes his own flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.6', 'BSB', 'Better one handful with tranquility than two handfuls with toil and pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.7', 'BSB', 'Again, I saw futility under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.8', 'BSB', 'There is a man all alone, without even a son or brother. And though there is no end to his labor, his eyes are still not content with his wealth: “For whom do I toil and bereave my soul of enjoyment?” This too is futile—a miserable task.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.9', 'BSB', 'Two are better than one, because they have a good return for their labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.10', 'BSB', 'For if one falls down, his companion can lift him up; but pity the one who falls without another to help him up!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.11', 'BSB', 'Again, if two lie down together, they will keep warm; but how can one keep warm alone?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.12', 'BSB', 'And though one may be overpowered, two can resist. Moreover, a cord of three strands is not quickly broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.13', 'BSB', 'Better is a poor but wise youth than an old but foolish king who no longer knows how to take a warning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.14', 'BSB', 'For the youth has come from the prison to the kingship, though he was born poor in his own kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.15', 'BSB', 'I saw that all who lived and walked under the sun followed this second one, the youth who succeeded the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.4.16', 'BSB', 'There is no limit to all the people who were before them. Yet the successor will not be celebrated by those who come even later. This too is futile and a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.1', 'BSB', 'Guard your steps when you go to the house of God. Draw near to listen rather than to offer the sacrifice of fools, who do not know that they do wrong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.2', 'BSB', 'Do not be quick to speak, and do not be hasty in your heart to utter a word before God. After all, God is in heaven and you are on earth. So let your words be few.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.3', 'BSB', 'As a dream comes through many cares, so the speech of a fool comes with many words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.4', 'BSB', 'When you make a vow to God, do not delay in fulfilling it, because He takes no pleasure in fools. Fulfill your vow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.5', 'BSB', 'It is better not to vow than to make a vow and not fulfill it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.6', 'BSB', 'Do not let your mouth cause your flesh to sin, and do not tell the messenger that your vow was a mistake. Why should God be angry with your words and destroy the work of your hands?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.7', 'BSB', 'For as many dreams bring futility, so do many words. Therefore, fear God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.8', 'BSB', 'If you see the oppression of the poor and the denial of justice and righteousness in the province, do not be astonished at the matter; for one official is watched by a superior, and others higher still are over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.9', 'BSB', 'The produce of the earth is taken by all; the king himself profits from the fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.10', 'BSB', 'He who loves money is never satisfied by money, and he who loves wealth is never satisfied by income. This too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.11', 'BSB', 'When good things increase, so do those who consume them; what then is the profit to the owner, except to behold them with his eyes?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.12', 'BSB', 'The sleep of the worker is sweet, whether he eats little or much, but the abundance of the rich man permits him no sleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.13', 'BSB', 'There is a grievous evil I have seen under the sun: wealth hoarded to the harm of its owner,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.14', 'BSB', 'or wealth lost in a failed venture, so when that man has a son there is nothing to pass on.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.15', 'BSB', 'As a man came from his mother’s womb, so he will depart again, naked as he arrived. He takes nothing for his labor to carry in his hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.16', 'BSB', 'This too is a grievous evil: Exactly as a man is born, so he will depart. What does he gain as he toils for the wind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.17', 'BSB', 'Moreover, all his days he eats in darkness, with much sorrow, sickness, and anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.18', 'BSB', 'Here is what I have seen to be good and fitting: to eat and drink, and to find satisfaction in all the labor one does under the sun during the few days of life that God has given him—for this is his lot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.19', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, God has given riches and wealth to every man, and He has enabled him to enjoy them, to accept his lot, and to rejoice in his labor. This is a gift from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.5.20', 'BSB', 'For a man seldom considers the days of his life, because God keeps him occupied with the joy of his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.1', 'BSB', 'There is another evil I have seen under the sun, and it weighs heavily upon mankind:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.2', 'BSB', 'God gives a man riches, wealth, and honor, so that he lacks nothing his heart desires; but God does not allow him to enjoy them. Instead, a stranger will enjoy them. This is futile and a grievous affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.3', 'BSB', 'A man may father a hundred children and live for many years; yet no matter how long he lives, if he is unsatisfied with his prosperity and does not even receive a proper burial, I say that a stillborn child is better off than he.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.4', 'BSB', 'For a stillborn child enters in futility and departs in darkness, and his name is shrouded in obscurity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.5', 'BSB', 'The child, though neither seeing the sun nor knowing anything, has more rest than that man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.6', 'BSB', 'even if he lives a thousand years twice over but fails to enjoy his prosperity. Do not all go to the same place?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.7', 'BSB', 'All a man’s labor is for his mouth, yet his appetite is never satisfied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.8', 'BSB', 'What advantage, then, has the wise man over the fool? What gain comes to the poor man who knows how to conduct himself before others?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.9', 'BSB', 'Better what the eye can see than the wandering of desire. This too is futile and a pursuit of the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.10', 'BSB', 'Whatever exists was named long ago, and what happens to a man is foreknown; but he cannot contend with one stronger than he.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.11', 'BSB', 'For the more words, the more futility—and how does that profit anyone?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.6.12', 'BSB', 'For who knows what is good for a man during the few days in which he passes through his fleeting life like a shadow? Who can tell a man what will come after him under the sun?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.1', 'BSB', 'A good name is better than fine perfume, and one’s day of death is better than his day of birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.2', 'BSB', 'It is better to enter a house of mourning than a house of feasting, since death is the end of every man, and the living should take this to heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.3', 'BSB', 'Sorrow is better than laughter, for a sad countenance is good for the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.4', 'BSB', 'The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning, but the heart of fools is in the house of pleasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.5', 'BSB', 'It is better to heed a wise man’s rebuke than to listen to the song of fools.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.6', 'BSB', 'For like the crackling of thorns under the pot, so is the laughter of the fool. This too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.7', 'BSB', 'Surely extortion turns a wise man into a fool, and a bribe corrupts the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.8', 'BSB', 'The end of a matter is better than the beginning, and a patient spirit is better than a proud one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.9', 'BSB', 'Do not be quickly provoked in your spirit, for anger settles in the lap of a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.10', 'BSB', 'Do not say, “Why were the old days better than these?” For it is unwise of you to ask about this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.11', 'BSB', 'Wisdom, like an inheritance, is good, and it benefits those who see the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.12', 'BSB', 'For wisdom, like money, is a shelter, and the advantage of knowledge is that wisdom preserves the life of its owner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.13', 'BSB', 'Consider the work of God: Who can straighten what He has bent?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.14', 'BSB', 'In the day of prosperity, be joyful, but in the day of adversity, consider this: God has made one of these along with the other, so that a man cannot discover anything that will come after him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.15', 'BSB', 'In my futile life I have seen both of these: A righteous man perishing in his righteousness, and a wicked man living long in his wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.16', 'BSB', 'Do not be overly righteous, and do not make yourself too wise. Why should you destroy yourself?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.17', 'BSB', 'Do not be excessively wicked, and do not be a fool. Why should you die before your time?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.18', 'BSB', 'It is good to grasp the one and not let the other slip from your hand. For he who fears God will follow both warnings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.19', 'BSB', 'Wisdom makes the wise man stronger than ten rulers in a city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.20', 'BSB', 'Surely there is no righteous man on earth who does good and never sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.21', 'BSB', 'Do not pay attention to every word that is spoken, or you may hear your servant cursing you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.22', 'BSB', 'For you know in your heart that many times you yourself have cursed others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.23', 'BSB', 'All this I tested by wisdom, saying, “I resolve to be wise.” But it was beyond me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.24', 'BSB', 'What exists is out of reach and very deep. Who can fathom it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.25', 'BSB', 'I directed my mind to understand, to explore, to search out wisdom and explanations, and to understand the stupidity of wickedness and the folly of madness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.26', 'BSB', 'And I find more bitter than death the woman who is a snare, whose heart is a net, and whose hands are chains. The man who pleases God escapes her, but the sinner is ensnared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.27', 'BSB', '“Behold,” says the Teacher, “I have discovered this by adding one thing to another to find an explanation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.28', 'BSB', 'While my soul was still searching but not finding, among a thousand I have found one upright man, but among all these I have not found one such woman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.7.29', 'BSB', 'Only this have I found: I have discovered that God made men upright, but they have sought out many schemes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.1', 'BSB', 'Who is like the wise man? Who knows the interpretation of a matter? A man’s wisdom brightens his face, and the sternness of his face is changed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.2', 'BSB', 'Keep the king’s command, I say, because of your oath before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.3', 'BSB', 'Do not hasten to leave his presence, and do not persist in a bad cause, for he will do whatever he pleases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.4', 'BSB', 'For the king’s word is supreme, and who can say to him, “What are you doing?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.5', 'BSB', 'Whoever keeps his command will come to no harm, and a wise heart knows the right time and procedure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.6', 'BSB', 'For there is a right time and procedure to every purpose, though a man’s misery weighs heavily upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.7', 'BSB', 'Since no one knows what will happen, who can tell him what is to come?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.8', 'BSB', 'As no man has power over the wind to contain it, so no one has authority over his day of death. As no one can be discharged in wartime, so wickedness will not release those who practice it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.9', 'BSB', 'All this I have seen, applying my mind to every deed that is done under the sun; there is a time when one man lords it over another to his own detriment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.10', 'BSB', 'Then too, I saw the burial of the wicked who used to go in and out of the holy place, and they were praised in the city where they had done so. This too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.11', 'BSB', 'When the sentence for a crime is not speedily executed, the hearts of men become fully set on doing evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.12', 'BSB', 'Although a sinner does evil a hundred times and still lives long, yet I also know that it will go well with those who fear God, who are reverent in His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.13', 'BSB', 'Yet because the wicked do not fear God, it will not go well with them, and their days will not lengthen like a shadow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.14', 'BSB', 'There is a futility that is done on the earth: There are righteous men who get what the actions of the wicked deserve, and there are wicked men who get what the actions of the righteous deserve. I say that this too is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.15', 'BSB', 'So I commended the enjoyment of life, because there is nothing better for a man under the sun than to eat and drink and be merry. For this joy will accompany him in his labor during the days of his life that God gives him under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.16', 'BSB', 'When I applied my mind to know wisdom and to observe the task that one performs on the earth—though his eyes do not see sleep in the day or even in the night—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.8.17', 'BSB', 'I saw every work of God, and that a man is unable to comprehend the work that is done under the sun. Despite his efforts to search it out, he cannot find its meaning; even if the wise man claims to know, he is unable to comprehend.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.1', 'BSB', 'So I took all this to heart and concluded that the righteous and the wise, as well as their deeds, are in God’s hands. Man does not know what lies ahead, whether love or hate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.2', 'BSB', 'It is the same for all: There is a common fate for the righteous and the wicked, for the good and the bad, for the clean and the unclean, for the one who sacrifices and the one who does not. As it is for the good, so it is for the sinner; as it is for the one who makes a vow, so it is for the one who refuses to take a vow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.3', 'BSB', 'This is an evil in everything that is done under the sun: There is one fate for everyone. Furthermore, the hearts of men are full of evil and madness while they are alive, and afterward they join the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.4', 'BSB', 'There is hope, however, for anyone who is among the living; for even a live dog is better than a dead lion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.5', 'BSB', 'For the living know that they will die, but the dead know nothing. They have no further reward, because the memory of them is forgotten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.6', 'BSB', 'Their love, their hate, and their envy have already vanished, and they will never again have a share in all that is done under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.7', 'BSB', 'Go, eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a cheerful heart, for God has already approved your works:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.8', 'BSB', 'Let your garments always be white, and never spare the oil for your head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.9', 'BSB', 'Enjoy life with your beloved wife all the days of the fleeting life that God has given you under the sun—all your fleeting days. For this is your portion in life and in your labor under the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.10', 'BSB', 'Whatever you find to do with your hands, do it with all your might, for in Sheol, where you are going, there is no work or planning or knowledge or wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.11', 'BSB', 'I saw something else under the sun: The race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong; neither is the bread to the wise, nor the wealth to the intelligent, nor the favor to the skillful. For time and chance happen to all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.12', 'BSB', 'For surely no man knows his time: Like fish caught in a cruel net or birds trapped in a snare, so men are ensnared in an evil time that suddenly falls upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.13', 'BSB', 'I have also seen this wisdom under the sun, and it was great to me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.14', 'BSB', 'There was a small city with few men. A mighty king came against it, surrounded it, and built large siege ramps against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.15', 'BSB', 'Now a poor wise man was found in the city, and he saved the city by his wisdom. Yet no one remembered that poor man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.16', 'BSB', 'And I said, “Wisdom is better than strength, but the wisdom of the poor man is despised, and his words are not heeded.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.17', 'BSB', 'The calm words of the wise are heeded over the shouts of a ruler among fools.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.9.18', 'BSB', 'Wisdom is better than weapons of war, but one sinner destroys much good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.1', 'BSB', 'As dead flies bring a stench to the perfumer’s oil, so a little folly outweighs wisdom and honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.2', 'BSB', 'A wise man’s heart inclines to the right, but the heart of a fool to the left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.3', 'BSB', 'Even as the fool walks along the road, his sense is lacking, and he shows everyone that he is a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.4', 'BSB', 'If the ruler’s temper flares against you, do not abandon your post, for calmness lays great offenses to rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.5', 'BSB', 'There is an evil I have seen under the sun— an error that proceeds from the ruler:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.6', 'BSB', 'Folly is appointed to great heights, but the rich sit in lowly positions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.7', 'BSB', 'I have seen slaves on horseback, while princes go on foot like slaves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.8', 'BSB', 'He who digs a pit may fall into it, and he who breaches a wall may be bitten by a snake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.9', 'BSB', 'The one who quarries stones may be injured by them, and he who splits logs endangers himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.10', 'BSB', 'If the axe is dull and the blade unsharpened, more strength must be exerted, but skill produces success.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.11', 'BSB', 'If the snake bites before it is charmed, there is no profit for the charmer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.12', 'BSB', 'The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious, but the lips of a fool consume him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.13', 'BSB', 'The beginning of his talk is folly, and the end of his speech is evil madness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.14', 'BSB', 'Yet the fool multiplies words. No one knows what is coming, and who can tell him what will come after him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.15', 'BSB', 'The toil of a fool wearies him, for he does not know the way to the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.16', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, O land whose king is a youth, and whose princes feast in the morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.17', 'BSB', 'Blessed are you, O land whose king is a son of nobles, and whose princes feast at the proper time— for strength and not for drunkenness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.18', 'BSB', 'Through laziness the roof caves in, and in the hands of the idle, the house leaks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.19', 'BSB', 'A feast is prepared for laughter, and wine makes life merry, but money is the answer for everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.10.20', 'BSB', 'Do not curse the king even in your thoughts, or curse the rich even in your bedroom, for a bird of the air may carry your words, and a winged creature may report your speech.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.1', 'BSB', 'Cast your bread upon the waters, for after many days you will find it again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.2', 'BSB', 'Divide your portion among seven, or even eight, for you do not know what disaster may befall the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.3', 'BSB', 'If the clouds are full, they will pour out rain upon the earth; whether a tree falls to the south or to the north, in the place where it falls, there it will lie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.4', 'BSB', 'He who watches the wind will fail to sow, and he who observes the clouds will fail to reap.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.5', 'BSB', 'As you do not know the path of the wind, or how the bones are formed in a mother’s womb, so you cannot understand the work of God, the Maker of all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.6', 'BSB', 'Sow your seed in the morning, and do not rest your hands in the evening, for you do not know which will succeed, whether this or that, or if both will equally prosper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.7', 'BSB', 'Light is sweet, and it pleases the eyes to see the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.8', 'BSB', 'So if a man lives many years, let him rejoice in them all. But let him remember the days of darkness, for they will be many. Everything to come is futile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.9', 'BSB', 'Rejoice, O young man, while you are young, and let your heart be glad in the days of your youth. Walk in the ways of your heart and in the sight of your eyes, but know that for all these things God will bring you to judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.11.10', 'BSB', 'So banish sorrow from your heart, and cast off pain from your body, for youth and vigor are fleeting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.1', 'BSB', 'Remember your Creator in the days of your youth, before the days of adversity come and the years approach of which you will say, “I find no pleasure in them,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.2', 'BSB', 'before the light of the sun, moon, and stars is darkened, and the clouds return after the rain,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.3', 'BSB', 'on the day the keepers of the house tremble and the strong men stoop, when those grinding cease because they are few and those watching through windows see dimly,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.4', 'BSB', 'when the doors to the street are shut and the sound of the mill fades away, when one rises at the sound of a bird and all the daughters of song grow faint,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.5', 'BSB', 'when men fear the heights and dangers of the road, when the almond tree blossoms, the grasshopper loses its spring, and the caper berry shrivels— for then man goes to his eternal home and mourners walk the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.6', 'BSB', 'Remember Him before the silver cord is snapped and the golden bowl is crushed, before the pitcher is shattered at the spring and the wheel is broken at the well,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.7', 'BSB', 'before the dust returns to the ground from which it came and the spirit returns to God who gave it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.8', 'BSB', '“Futility of futilities,” says the Teacher. “Everything is futile!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.9', 'BSB', 'Not only was the Teacher wise, but he also taught the people knowledge; he pondered, searched out, and arranged many proverbs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.10', 'BSB', 'The Teacher searched to find delightful sayings and to record accurate words of truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.11', 'BSB', 'The words of the wise are like goads, and the anthologies of the masters are like firmly embedded nails driven by a single Shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.12', 'BSB', 'And by these, my son, be further warned: There is no end to the making of many books, and much study wearies the body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.13', 'BSB', 'When all has been heard, the conclusion of the matter is this: Fear God and keep His commandments, because this is the whole duty of man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eccl.12.14', 'BSB', 'For God will bring every deed into judgment, along with every hidden thing, whether good or evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is Solomon’s Song of Songs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.2', 'BSB', 'Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth! For your love is more delightful than wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.3', 'BSB', 'The fragrance of your perfume is pleasing; your name is like perfume poured out. No wonder the maidens adore you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.4', 'BSB', 'Take me away with you—let us hurry! May the king bring me to his chambers. We will rejoice and delight in you; we will praise your love more than wine. It is only right that they adore you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.5', 'BSB', 'I am dark, yet lovely, O daughters of Jerusalem, like the tents of Kedar, like the curtains of Solomon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.6', 'BSB', 'Do not stare because I am dark, for the sun has gazed upon me. My mother’s sons were angry with me; they made me a keeper of the vineyards, but my own vineyard I have neglected.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.7', 'BSB', 'Tell me, O one I love, where do you pasture your sheep? Where do you rest them at midday? Why should I be like a veiled woman beside the flocks of your companions?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.8', 'BSB', 'If you do not know, O fairest of women, follow the tracks of the flock, and graze your young goats near the tents of the shepherds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.9', 'BSB', 'I compare you, my darling, to a mare among Pharaoh’s chariots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.10', 'BSB', 'Your cheeks are beautiful with ornaments, your neck with strings of jewels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.11', 'BSB', 'We will make you ornaments of gold, studded with beads of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.12', 'BSB', 'While the king was at his table, my perfume spread its fragrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.13', 'BSB', 'My beloved is to me a sachet of myrrh resting between my breasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.14', 'BSB', 'My beloved is to me a cluster of henna blossoms in the vineyards of En-gedi.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.15', 'BSB', 'How beautiful you are, my darling! Oh, how very beautiful! Your eyes are like doves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.16', 'BSB', 'How handsome you are, my beloved! Oh, how delightful! The soft grass is our bed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.1.17', 'BSB', 'The beams of our house are cedars; our rafters are fragrant firs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.1', 'BSB', 'I am a rose of Sharon, a lily of the valley.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.2', 'BSB', 'Like a lily among the thorns is my darling among the maidens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.3', 'BSB', 'Like an apricot tree among the trees of the forest is my beloved among the young men. I delight to sit in his shade, and his fruit is sweet to my taste.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.4', 'BSB', 'He has brought me to the house of wine, and his banner over me is love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.5', 'BSB', 'Sustain me with raisins; refresh me with apples, for I am faint with love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.6', 'BSB', 'His left hand is under my head, and his right arm embraces me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.7', 'BSB', 'O daughters of Jerusalem, I adjure you by the gazelles and does of the field: Do not arouse or awaken love until the time is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.8', 'BSB', 'Listen! My beloved approaches. Look! Here he comes, leaping across the mountains, bounding over the hills.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.9', 'BSB', 'My beloved is like a gazelle or a young stag. Look, he stands behind our wall, gazing through the windows, peering through the lattice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.10', 'BSB', 'My beloved calls to me, “Arise, my darling. Come away with me, my beautiful one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.11', 'BSB', 'For now the winter is past; the rain is over and gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.12', 'BSB', 'The flowers have appeared in the countryside; the season of singing has come, and the cooing of turtledoves is heard in our land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.13', 'BSB', 'The fig tree ripens its figs; the blossoming vines spread their fragrance. Arise, come away, my darling; come away with me, my beautiful one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.14', 'BSB', 'O my dove in the clefts of the rock, in the crevices of the cliff, let me see your face, let me hear your voice; for your voice is sweet, and your countenance is lovely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.15', 'BSB', 'Catch for us the foxes— the little foxes that ruin the vineyards— for our vineyards are in bloom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.16', 'BSB', 'My beloved is mine and I am his; he pastures his flock among the lilies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.2.17', 'BSB', 'Before the day breaks and shadows flee, turn, my beloved, and be like a gazelle or a young stag on the mountains of Bether.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.1', 'BSB', 'On my bed at night I sought the one I love; I sought him, but did not find him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.2', 'BSB', 'I will arise now and go about the city, through the streets and squares. I will seek the one I love. So I sought him but did not find him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.3', 'BSB', 'I encountered the watchmen on their rounds of the city: “Have you seen the one I love?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.4', 'BSB', 'I had just passed them when I found the one I love. I held him and would not let go until I had brought him to my mother’s house, to the chamber of the one who conceived me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.5', 'BSB', 'O daughters of Jerusalem, I adjure you by the gazelles and does of the field: Do not arouse or awaken love until the time is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.6', 'BSB', 'Who is this coming up from the wilderness like a column of smoke, scented with myrrh and frankincense from all the spices of the merchant?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, it is Solomon’s carriage, escorted by sixty of the mightiest men of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.8', 'BSB', 'All are skilled with the sword, experienced in warfare. Each has his sword at his side prepared for the terror of the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.9', 'BSB', 'King Solomon has made his carriage out of the timber of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.10', 'BSB', 'He has made its posts of silver, its base of gold, its seat of purple fabric. Its interior is inlaid with love by the daughters of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.3.11', 'BSB', 'Come out, O daughters of Zion, and gaze at King Solomon, wearing the crown his mother bestowed on the day of his wedding— the day of his heart’s rejoicing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.1', 'BSB', 'How beautiful you are, my darling— how very beautiful! Your eyes are like doves behind your veil. Your hair is like a flock of goats streaming down Mount Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.2', 'BSB', 'Your teeth are like a flock of newly shorn sheep coming up from the washing; each has its twin, and not one of them is lost.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.3', 'BSB', 'Your lips are like a scarlet ribbon, and your mouth is lovely. Your brow behind your veil is like a slice of pomegranate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.4', 'BSB', 'Your neck is like the tower of David, built with rows of stones; on it hang a thousand shields, all of them shields of warriors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.5', 'BSB', 'Your breasts are like two fawns, twins of a gazelle grazing among the lilies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.6', 'BSB', 'Before the day breaks and the shadows flee, I will make my way to the mountain of myrrh and to the hill of frankincense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.7', 'BSB', 'You are altogether beautiful, my darling; in you there is no flaw.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.8', 'BSB', 'Come with me from Lebanon, my bride, come with me from Lebanon! Descend from the peak of Amana, from the summits of Senir and Hermon, from the dens of the lions, from the mountains of the leopards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.9', 'BSB', 'You have captured my heart, my sister, my bride; you have stolen my heart with one glance of your eyes, with one jewel of your neck.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.10', 'BSB', 'How delightful is your love, my sister, my bride! Your love is much better than wine, and the fragrance of your perfume than all spices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.11', 'BSB', 'Your lips, my bride, drip sweetness like the honeycomb; honey and milk are under your tongue, and the fragrance of your garments is like the aroma of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.12', 'BSB', 'My sister, my bride, you are a garden locked up, a spring enclosed, a fountain sealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.13', 'BSB', 'Your branches are an orchard of pomegranates with the choicest of fruits, with henna and nard,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.14', 'BSB', 'with nard and saffron, with calamus and cinnamon, with every kind of frankincense tree, with myrrh and aloes, with all the finest spices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.15', 'BSB', 'You are a garden spring, a well of fresh water flowing down from Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.4.16', 'BSB', 'Awake, O north wind, and come, O south wind. Breathe on my garden and spread the fragrance of its spices. Let my beloved come into his garden and taste its choicest fruits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.1', 'BSB', 'I have come to my garden, my sister, my bride; I have gathered my myrrh with my spice. I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk. Eat, O friends, and drink; drink freely, O beloved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.2', 'BSB', 'I sleep, but my heart is awake. A sound! My beloved is knocking: “Open to me, my sister, my darling, my dove, my flawless one. My head is drenched with dew, my hair with the dampness of the night.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.3', 'BSB', 'I have taken off my robe— must I put it back on? I have washed my feet— must I soil them again?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.4', 'BSB', 'My beloved put his hand to the latch; my heart pounded for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.5', 'BSB', 'I rose up to open for my beloved. My hands dripped with myrrh, my fingers with flowing myrrh on the handles of the bolt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.6', 'BSB', 'I opened for my beloved, but he had turned and gone. My heart sank at his departure. I sought him, but did not find him. I called, but he did not answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.7', 'BSB', 'I encountered the watchmen on their rounds of the city. They beat me and bruised me; they took away my cloak, those guardians of the walls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.8', 'BSB', 'O daughters of Jerusalem, I adjure you, if you find my beloved, tell him I am sick with love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.9', 'BSB', 'How is your beloved better than others, O most beautiful among women? How is your beloved better than another, that you charge us so?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.10', 'BSB', 'My beloved is dazzling and ruddy, outstanding among ten thousand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.11', 'BSB', 'His head is purest gold; his hair is wavy and black as a raven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.12', 'BSB', 'His eyes are like doves beside the streams of water, bathed in milk and mounted like jewels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.13', 'BSB', 'His cheeks are like beds of spice, towers of perfume. His lips are like lilies, dripping with flowing myrrh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.14', 'BSB', 'His arms are rods of gold set with beryl. His body is an ivory panel bedecked with sapphires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.15', 'BSB', 'His legs are pillars of marble set on bases of pure gold. His appearance is like Lebanon, as majestic as the cedars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.5.16', 'BSB', 'His mouth is most sweet; he is altogether lovely. This is my beloved, and this is my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.1', 'BSB', 'Where has your beloved gone, O most beautiful among women? Which way has he turned? We will seek him with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.2', 'BSB', 'My beloved has gone down to his garden, to the beds of spices, to pasture his flock in the gardens and to gather lilies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.3', 'BSB', 'I belong to my beloved and he belongs to me; he pastures his flock among the lilies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.4', 'BSB', 'You are as beautiful, my darling, as Tirzah, as lovely as Jerusalem, as majestic as troops with banners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.5', 'BSB', 'Turn your eyes away from me, for they have overcome me. Your hair is like a flock of goats streaming down from Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.6', 'BSB', 'Your teeth are like a flock of sheep coming up from the washing; each has its twin, and not one of them is lost.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.7', 'BSB', 'Your brow behind your veil is like a slice of pomegranate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.8', 'BSB', 'There are sixty queens and eighty concubines, and maidens without number,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.9', 'BSB', 'but my dove, my perfect one, is unique, the favorite of the mother who bore her. The maidens see her and call her blessed; the queens and concubines sing her praises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.10', 'BSB', 'Who is this who shines like the dawn, as fair as the moon, as bright as the sun, as majestic as the stars in procession?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.11', 'BSB', 'I went down to the walnut grove to see the blossoms of the valley, to see if the vines were budding or the pomegranates were in bloom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.12', 'BSB', 'Before I realized it, my desire had set me among the royal chariots of my people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.6.13', 'BSB', 'Come back, come back, O Shulammite! Come back, come back, that we may gaze upon you. Why do you look at the Shulammite, as on the dance of Mahanaim?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.1', 'BSB', 'How beautiful are your sandaled feet, O daughter of the prince! The curves of your thighs are like jewels, the handiwork of a master.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.2', 'BSB', 'Your navel is a rounded goblet; it never lacks blended wine. Your waist is a mound of wheat encircled by the lilies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.3', 'BSB', 'Your breasts are like two fawns, twins of a gazelle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.4', 'BSB', 'Your neck is like a tower made of ivory; your eyes are like the pools of Heshbon by the gate of Bath-rabbim; your nose is like the tower of Lebanon, facing toward Damascus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.5', 'BSB', 'Your head crowns you like Mount Carmel, the hair of your head like purple threads; the king is captured in your tresses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.6', 'BSB', 'How fair and pleasant you are, O love, with your delights!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.7', 'BSB', 'Your stature is like a palm tree; your breasts are clusters of fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.8', 'BSB', 'I said, “I will climb the palm tree; I will take hold of its fruit.” May your breasts be like clusters of the vine, the fragrance of your breath like apples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.9', 'BSB', 'and your mouth like the finest wine. May it flow smoothly to my beloved, gliding gently over lips and teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.10', 'BSB', 'I belong to my beloved, and his desire is for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.11', 'BSB', 'Come, my beloved, let us go to the countryside; let us spend the night among the wildflowers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.12', 'BSB', 'Let us go early to the vineyards to see if the vine has budded, if the blossom has opened, if the pomegranates are in bloom— there I will give you my love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.7.13', 'BSB', 'The mandrakes send forth a fragrance, and at our door is every delicacy, new as well as old, that I have treasured up for you, my beloved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.1', 'BSB', 'O that you were to me like a brother who nursed at my mother’s breasts! If I found you outdoors, I would kiss you, and no one would despise me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.2', 'BSB', 'I would lead you and bring you to the house of my mother who taught me. I would give you spiced wine to drink, the nectar of my pomegranates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.3', 'BSB', 'His left hand is under my head, and his right arm embraces me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.4', 'BSB', 'O daughters of Jerusalem, I adjure you: Do not arouse or awaken love until the time is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.5', 'BSB', 'Who is this coming up from the wilderness, leaning on her beloved? I roused you under the apple tree; there your mother conceived you; there she travailed and brought you forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.6', 'BSB', 'Set me as a seal over your heart, as a seal upon your arm. For love is as strong as death, its jealousy as unrelenting as Sheol. Its sparks are fiery flames, the fiercest blaze of all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.7', 'BSB', 'Mighty waters cannot quench love; rivers cannot sweep it away. If a man were to give all the wealth of his house for love, his offer would be utterly scorned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.8', 'BSB', 'We have a little sister, and her breasts are not yet grown. What shall we do for our sister on the day she is spoken for?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.9', 'BSB', 'If she is a wall, we will build a tower of silver to protect her. If she is a door, we will enclose her with panels of cedar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.10', 'BSB', 'I am a wall, and my breasts are like towers. So I have become in his eyes like one who brings peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.11', 'BSB', 'Solomon had a vineyard in Baal-hamon. He leased it to the tenants. For its fruit, each was to bring a thousand shekels of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.12', 'BSB', 'But my own vineyard is mine to give; the thousand shekels are for you, O Solomon, and two hundred are for those who tend its fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.13', 'BSB', 'You who dwell in the gardens, my companions are listening for your voice. Let me hear it!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Song.8.14', 'BSB', 'Come away, my beloved, and be like a gazelle or a young stag on the mountains of spices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the vision concerning Judah and Jerusalem that Isaiah son of Amoz saw during the reigns of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.2', 'BSB', 'Listen, O heavens, and give ear, O earth, for the LORD has spoken: “I have raised children and brought them up, but they have rebelled against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.3', 'BSB', 'The ox knows its owner, and the donkey its master’s manger, but Israel does not know; My people do not understand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.4', 'BSB', 'Alas, O sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a brood of evildoers, children of depravity! They have forsaken the LORD; they have despised the Holy One of Israel and turned their backs on Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.5', 'BSB', 'Why do you want more beatings? Why do you keep rebelling? Your head has a massive wound, and your whole heart is afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.6', 'BSB', 'From the sole of your foot to the top of your head, there is no soundness— only wounds and welts and festering sores neither cleansed nor bandaged nor soothed with oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.7', 'BSB', 'Your land is desolate; your cities are burned with fire. Foreigners devour your fields before you— a desolation demolished by strangers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.8', 'BSB', 'And the Daughter of Zion is abandoned like a shelter in a vineyard, like a shack in a cucumber field, like a city besieged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.9', 'BSB', 'Unless the LORD of Hosts had left us a few survivors, we would have become like Sodom, we would have resembled Gomorrah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.10', 'BSB', 'Hear the word of the LORD, you rulers of Sodom; listen to the instruction of our God, you people of Gomorrah!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.11', 'BSB', '“What good to Me is your multitude of sacrifices?” says the LORD. “I am full from the burnt offerings of rams and the fat of well-fed cattle; I take no delight in the blood of bulls and lambs and goats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.12', 'BSB', 'When you come to appear before Me, who has required this of you— this trampling of My courts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.13', 'BSB', 'Bring your worthless offerings no more; your incense is detestable to Me— your New Moons, Sabbaths, and convocations. I cannot endure iniquity in a solemn assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.14', 'BSB', 'I hate your New Moons and your appointed feasts. They have become a burden to Me; I am weary of bearing them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.15', 'BSB', 'When you spread out your hands in prayer, I will hide My eyes from you; even though you multiply your prayers, I will not listen. Your hands are covered with blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.16', 'BSB', 'Wash and cleanse yourselves. Remove your evil deeds from My sight. Stop doing evil!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.17', 'BSB', 'Learn to do right; seek justice and correct the oppressor. Defend the fatherless and plead the case of the widow.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.18', 'BSB', '“Come now, let us reason together,” says the LORD. “Though your sins are like scarlet, they will be as white as snow; though they are as red as crimson, they will become like wool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.19', 'BSB', 'If you are willing and obedient, you will eat the best of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.20', 'BSB', 'But if you resist and rebel, you will be devoured by the sword.” For the mouth of the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.21', 'BSB', 'See how the faithful city has become a harlot! She once was full of justice; righteousness resided within her, but now only murderers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.22', 'BSB', 'Your silver has become dross; your fine wine is diluted with water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.23', 'BSB', 'Your rulers are rebels, friends of thieves. They all love bribes and chasing after rewards. They do not defend the fatherless, and the plea of the widow never comes before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore the Lord GOD of Hosts, the Mighty One of Israel, declares: “Ah, I will be relieved of My foes and avenge Myself on My enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.25', 'BSB', 'I will turn My hand against you; I will thoroughly purge your dross; I will remove all your impurities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.26', 'BSB', 'I will restore your judges as at first, and your counselors as at the beginning. After that you will be called the City of Righteousness, the Faithful City.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.27', 'BSB', 'Zion will be redeemed with justice, her repentant ones with righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.28', 'BSB', 'But rebels and sinners will together be shattered, and those who forsake the LORD will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.29', 'BSB', 'Surely you will be ashamed of the sacred oaks in which you have delighted; you will be embarrassed by the gardens that you have chosen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.30', 'BSB', 'For you will become like an oak whose leaves are withered, like a garden without water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.1.31', 'BSB', 'The strong man will become tinder and his work will be a spark; both will burn together, with no one to quench the flames.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.1', 'BSB', 'This is the message that was revealed to Isaiah son of Amoz concerning Judah and Jerusalem:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.2', 'BSB', 'In the last days the mountain of the house of the LORD will be established as the chief of the mountains; it will be raised above the hills, and all nations will stream to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.3', 'BSB', 'And many peoples will come and say: “Come, let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob. He will teach us His ways so that we may walk in His paths.” For the law will go forth from Zion, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.4', 'BSB', 'Then He will judge between the nations and arbitrate for many peoples. They will beat their swords into plowshares and their spears into pruning hooks. Nation will no longer take up the sword against nation, nor train anymore for war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.5', 'BSB', 'Come, O house of Jacob, let us walk in the light of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.6', 'BSB', 'For You have abandoned Your people, the house of Jacob, because they are filled with influences from the east; they are soothsayers like the Philistines; they strike hands with the children of foreigners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.7', 'BSB', 'Their land is full of silver and gold, with no limit to their treasures; their land is full of horses, with no limit to their chariots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.8', 'BSB', 'Their land is full of idols; they bow down to the work of their hands, to what their fingers have made.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.9', 'BSB', 'So mankind is brought low, and man is humbled— do not forgive them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.10', 'BSB', 'Go into the rocks and hide in the dust from the terror of the LORD and the splendor of His majesty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.11', 'BSB', 'The proud look of man will be humbled, and the loftiness of men brought low; the LORD alone will be exalted in that day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.12', 'BSB', 'For the Day of the LORD of Hosts will come against all the proud and lofty, against all that is exalted— it will be humbled—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.13', 'BSB', 'against all the cedars of Lebanon, lofty and lifted up, against all the oaks of Bashan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.14', 'BSB', 'against all the tall mountains, against all the high hills,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.15', 'BSB', 'against every high tower, against every fortified wall,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.16', 'BSB', 'against every ship of Tarshish, and against every stately vessel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.17', 'BSB', 'So the pride of man will be brought low, and the loftiness of men will be humbled; the LORD alone will be exalted in that day,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.18', 'BSB', 'and the idols will vanish completely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.19', 'BSB', 'Men will flee to caves in the rocks and holes in the ground, away from the terror of the LORD and from the splendor of His majesty, when He rises to shake the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.20', 'BSB', 'In that day men will cast away to the moles and bats their idols of silver and gold— the idols they made to worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.21', 'BSB', 'They will flee to caverns in the rocks and crevices in the cliffs, away from the terror of the LORD and from the splendor of His majesty, when He rises to shake the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.2.22', 'BSB', 'Put no more trust in man, who has only the breath in his nostrils. Of what account is he?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.1', 'BSB', 'For behold, the Lord GOD of Hosts is about to remove from Jerusalem and Judah both supply and support: the whole supply of food and water,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.2', 'BSB', 'the mighty man and the warrior, the judge and the prophet, the soothsayer and the elder,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.3', 'BSB', 'the commander of fifty and the dignitary, the counselor, the cunning magician, and the clever enchanter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.4', 'BSB', '“I will make mere lads their leaders, and children will rule over them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.5', 'BSB', 'The people will oppress one another, man against man, neighbor against neighbor; the young will rise up against the old, and the base against the honorable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.6', 'BSB', 'A man will seize his brother within his father’s house: “You have a cloak—you be our leader! Take charge of this heap of rubble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.7', 'BSB', 'On that day he will cry aloud: “I am not a healer. I have no food or clothing in my house. Do not make me leader of the people!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.8', 'BSB', 'For Jerusalem has stumbled and Judah has fallen because they spoke and acted against the LORD, defying His glorious presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.9', 'BSB', 'The expression on their faces testifies against them, and like Sodom they flaunt their sin; they do not conceal it. Woe to them, for they have brought disaster upon themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.10', 'BSB', 'Tell the righteous it will be well with them, for they will enjoy the fruit of their labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.11', 'BSB', 'Woe to the wicked; disaster is upon them! For they will be repaid with what their hands have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.12', 'BSB', 'Youths oppress My people, and women rule over them. O My people, your guides mislead you; they turn you from your paths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.13', 'BSB', 'The LORD arises to contend; He stands to judge the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD brings this charge against the elders and leaders of His people: “You have devoured the vineyard; the plunder of the poor is in your houses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.15', 'BSB', 'Why do you crush My people and grind the faces of the poor?” declares the Lord GOD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.16', 'BSB', 'The LORD also says: “Because the daughters of Zion are haughty— walking with heads held high and wanton eyes, prancing and skipping as they go, jingling the bracelets on their ankles—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.17', 'BSB', 'the Lord will bring sores on the heads of the daughters of Zion, and the LORD will make their foreheads bare.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.18', 'BSB', 'In that day the Lord will take away their finery: their anklets and headbands and crescents;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.19', 'BSB', 'their pendants, bracelets, and veils;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.20', 'BSB', 'their headdresses, ankle chains, and sashes; their perfume bottles and charms;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.21', 'BSB', 'their signet rings and nose rings;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.22', 'BSB', 'their festive robes, capes, cloaks, and purses;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.23', 'BSB', 'and their mirrors, linen garments, tiaras, and shawls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.24', 'BSB', 'Instead of fragrance there will be a stench; instead of a belt, a rope; instead of styled hair, baldness; instead of fine clothing, sackcloth; instead of beauty, shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.25', 'BSB', 'Your men will fall by the sword, and your warriors in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.3.26', 'BSB', 'And the gates of Zion will lament and mourn; destitute, she will sit on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.1', 'BSB', 'In that day seven women will take hold of one man and say, “We will eat our own bread and provide our own clothes. Just let us be called by your name. Take away our disgrace!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.2', 'BSB', 'On that day the Branch of the LORD will be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the land will be the pride and glory of Israel’s survivors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.3', 'BSB', 'Whoever remains in Zion and whoever is left in Jerusalem will be called holy— all in Jerusalem who are recorded among the living—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.4', 'BSB', 'when the Lord has washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion and cleansed the bloodstains from the heart of Jerusalem by a spirit of judgment and a spirit of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.5', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD will create over all of Mount Zion and over her assemblies a cloud of smoke by day and a glowing flame of fire by night. For over all the glory there will be a canopy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.4.6', 'BSB', 'a shelter to give shade from the heat by day, and a refuge and hiding place from the storm and the rain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.1', 'BSB', 'I will sing for my beloved a song of his vineyard: My beloved had a vineyard on a very fertile hill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.2', 'BSB', 'He dug it up and cleared the stones and planted the finest vines. He built a watchtower in the middle and dug out a winepress as well. He waited for the vineyard to yield good grapes, but the fruit it produced was sour!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.3', 'BSB', '“And now, O dwellers of Jerusalem and men of Judah, I exhort you to judge between Me and My vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.4', 'BSB', 'What more could I have done for My vineyard than I already did for it? Why, when I expected sweet grapes, did it bring forth sour fruit?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.5', 'BSB', 'Now I will tell you what I am about to do to My vineyard: I will take away its hedge, and it will be consumed; I will tear down its wall, and it will be trampled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.6', 'BSB', 'I will make it a wasteland, neither pruned nor cultivated, and thorns and briers will grow up. I will command the clouds that rain shall not fall on it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.7', 'BSB', 'For the vineyard of the LORD of Hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah are the plant of His delight. He looked for justice, but saw bloodshed; for righteousness, but heard a cry of distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.8', 'BSB', 'Woe to you who add house to house and join field to field until no place is left and you live alone in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.9', 'BSB', 'I heard the LORD of Hosts declare: “Surely many houses will become desolate, great mansions left unoccupied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.10', 'BSB', 'For ten acres of vineyard will yield but a bath of wine, and a homer of seed only an ephah of grain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.11', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who rise early in the morning in pursuit of strong drink, who linger into the evening, to be inflamed by wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.12', 'BSB', 'At their feasts are the lyre and harp, tambourines and flutes and wine. They disregard the actions of the LORD and fail to see the work of His hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore My people will go into exile for their lack of understanding; their dignitaries are starving and their masses are parched with thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore Sheol enlarges its throat and opens wide its enormous jaws, and down go Zion’s nobles and masses, her revelers and carousers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.15', 'BSB', 'So mankind will be brought low, and each man humbled; the arrogant will lower their eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.16', 'BSB', 'But the LORD of Hosts will be exalted by His justice, and the holy God will show Himself holy in righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.17', 'BSB', 'Lambs will graze as in their own pastures, and strangers will feed in the ruins of the wealthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.18', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who draw iniquity with cords of deceit and pull sin along with cart ropes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.19', 'BSB', 'to those who say, “Let Him hurry and hasten His work so that we may see it! Let the plan of the Holy One of Israel come so that we may know it!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.20', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who call evil good and good evil, who turn darkness to light and light to darkness, who replace bitter with sweet and sweet with bitter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.21', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who are wise in their own eyes and clever in their own sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.22', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who are heroes in drinking wine and champions in mixing beer,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.23', 'BSB', 'who acquit the guilty for a bribe and deprive the innocent of justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as a tongue of fire consumes the straw, and as dry grass shrivels in the flame, so their roots will decay and their blossoms will blow away like dust; for they have rejected the instruction of the LORD of Hosts and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore the anger of the LORD burns against His people; His hand is raised against them to strike them down. The mountains quake, and the corpses lay like refuse in the streets. Despite all this, His anger is not turned away; His hand is still upraised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.26', 'BSB', 'He lifts a banner for the distant nations and whistles for those at the ends of the earth. Behold—how speedily and swiftly they come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.27', 'BSB', 'None of them grows weary or stumbles; no one slumbers or sleeps. No belt is loose and no sandal strap is broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.28', 'BSB', 'Their arrows are sharpened, and all their bows are strung. The hooves of their horses are like flint; their chariot wheels are like a whirlwind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.29', 'BSB', 'Their roaring is like that of a lion; they roar like young lions. They growl and seize their prey; they carry it away from deliverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.5.30', 'BSB', 'In that day they will roar over it, like the roaring of the sea. If one looks over the land, he will see darkness and distress; even the light will be obscured by clouds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.1', 'BSB', 'In the year that King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord seated on a throne, high and exalted; and the train of His robe filled the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.2', 'BSB', 'Above Him stood seraphim, each having six wings: With two wings they covered their faces, with two they covered their feet, and with two they were flying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.3', 'BSB', 'And they were calling out to one another: “Holy, holy, holy is the LORD of Hosts; all the earth is full of His glory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.4', 'BSB', 'At the sound of their voices the doorposts and thresholds shook, and the temple was filled with smoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.5', 'BSB', 'Then I said: “Woe is me, for I am ruined, because I am a man of unclean lips dwelling among a people of unclean lips; for my eyes have seen the King, the LORD of Hosts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.6', 'BSB', 'Then one of the seraphim flew to me, and in his hand was a glowing coal that he had taken with tongs from the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.7', 'BSB', 'And with it he touched my mouth and said: “Now that this has touched your lips, your iniquity is removed and your sin is atoned for.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.8', 'BSB', 'Then I heard the voice of the Lord saying: “Whom shall I send? Who will go for Us?” And I said: “Here am I. Send me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.9', 'BSB', 'And He replied: “Go and tell this people, ‘Be ever hearing, but never understanding; be ever seeing, but never perceiving.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.10', 'BSB', 'Make the hearts of this people calloused; deafen their ears and close their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn and be healed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.11', 'BSB', 'Then I asked: “How long, O Lord?” And He replied: “Until the cities lie ruined and without inhabitant, until the houses are left unoccupied and the land is desolate and ravaged,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.12', 'BSB', 'until the LORD has driven men far away and the land is utterly forsaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.6.13', 'BSB', 'And though a tenth remains in the land, it will be burned again. As the terebinth and oak leave stumps when felled, so the holy seed will be a stump in the land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.1', 'BSB', 'Now in the days that Ahaz son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, was king of Judah, Rezin king of Aram marched up to wage war against Jerusalem. He was accompanied by Pekah son of Remaliah the king of Israel, but he could not overpower the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.2', 'BSB', 'When it was reported to the house of David that Aram was in league with Ephraim, the hearts of Ahaz and his people trembled like trees in the forest shaken by the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.3', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Isaiah, “Go out with your son Shear-jashub to meet Ahaz at the end of the aqueduct that feeds the upper pool, on the road to the Launderer’s Field,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.4', 'BSB', 'and say to him: Calm down and be quiet. Do not be afraid or disheartened over these two smoldering stubs of firewood—over the fierce anger of Rezin and Aram and of the son of Remaliah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.5', 'BSB', 'For Aram, along with Ephraim and the son of Remaliah, has plotted your ruin, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.6', 'BSB', '‘Let us invade Judah, terrorize it, and divide it among ourselves. Then we can install the son of Tabeal over it as king.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.7', 'BSB', 'But this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘It will not arise; it will not happen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.8', 'BSB', 'For the head of Aram is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin. Within sixty-five years Ephraim will be shattered as a people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.9', 'BSB', 'The head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is the son of Remaliah. If you do not stand firm in your faith, then you will not stand at all.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.10', 'BSB', 'Again the LORD spoke to Ahaz, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.11', 'BSB', '“Ask for a sign from the LORD your God, whether from the depths of Sheol or the heights of heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.12', 'BSB', 'But Ahaz replied, “I will not ask; I will not test the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.13', 'BSB', 'Then Isaiah said, “Hear now, O house of David! Is it not enough to try the patience of men? Will you try the patience of my God as well?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore the Lord Himself will give you a sign: Behold, the virgin will be with child and will give birth to a son, and will call Him Immanuel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.15', 'BSB', 'By the time He knows enough to reject evil and choose good, He will be eating curds and honey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.16', 'BSB', 'For before the boy knows enough to reject evil and choose good, the land of the two kings you dread will be laid waste.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.17', 'BSB', 'The LORD will bring on you and on your people and on the house of your father a time unlike any since the day Ephraim separated from Judah—He will bring the king of Assyria.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.18', 'BSB', 'On that day the LORD will whistle to the flies at the farthest streams of the Nile and to the bees in the land of Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.19', 'BSB', 'And they will all come and settle in the steep ravines and clefts of the rocks, in all the thornbushes and watering holes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.20', 'BSB', 'On that day the Lord will use a razor hired from beyond the Euphrates —the king of Assyria—to shave your head and the hair of your legs, and to remove your beard as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.21', 'BSB', 'On that day a man will raise a young cow and two sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.22', 'BSB', 'and from the abundance of milk they give, he will eat curds; for all who remain in the land will eat curds and honey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.23', 'BSB', 'And on that day, in every place that had a thousand vines worth a thousand shekels of silver, only briers and thorns will be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.24', 'BSB', 'Men will go there with bow and arrow, for the land will be covered with briers and thorns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.7.25', 'BSB', 'For fear of the briers and thorns, you will no longer traverse the hills once tilled by the hoe; they will become places for oxen to graze and sheep to trample.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Take a large scroll and write on it with an ordinary stylus: Maher-shalal-hash-baz.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.2', 'BSB', 'And I will appoint for Myself trustworthy witnesses—Uriah the priest and Zechariah son of Jeberekiah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.3', 'BSB', 'And I had relations with the prophetess, and she conceived and gave birth to a son. The LORD said to me, “Name him Maher-shalal-hash-baz.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.4', 'BSB', 'For before the boy knows how to cry ‘Father’ or ‘Mother,’ the wealth of Damascus and the plunder of Samaria will be carried off by the king of Assyria.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.5', 'BSB', 'And the LORD spoke to me further:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.6', 'BSB', '“Because this people has rejected the gently flowing waters of Shiloah and rejoiced in Rezin and the son of Remaliah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.7', 'BSB', 'the Lord will surely bring against them the mighty floodwaters of the Euphrates — the king of Assyria and all his pomp. It will overflow its channels and overrun its banks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.8', 'BSB', 'It will pour into Judah, swirling and sweeping over it, reaching up to the neck; its spreading streams will cover your entire land, O Immanuel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.9', 'BSB', 'Huddle together, O peoples, and be shattered; pay attention, all you distant lands; prepare for battle, and be shattered; prepare for battle, and be shattered!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.10', 'BSB', 'Devise a plan, but it will be thwarted; state a proposal, but it will not happen. For God is with us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.11', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD has spoken to me with a strong hand, instructing me not to walk in the way of this people:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.12', 'BSB', '“Do not call conspiracy everything these people regard as conspiracy. Do not fear what they fear; do not live in dread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.13', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts is the One you shall regard as holy. Only He should be feared; only He should be dreaded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.14', 'BSB', 'And He will be a sanctuary— but to both houses of Israel a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense, to the dwellers of Jerusalem a trap and a snare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.15', 'BSB', 'Many will stumble over these; they will fall and be broken; they will be ensnared and captured.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.16', 'BSB', 'Bind up the testimony and seal the law among my disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.17', 'BSB', 'I will wait for the LORD, who is hiding His face from the house of Jacob. I will put my trust in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.18', 'BSB', 'Here am I, and the children the LORD has given me as signs and symbols in Israel from the LORD of Hosts, who dwells on Mount Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.19', 'BSB', 'When men tell you to consult the spirits of the dead and the spiritists who whisper and mutter, shouldn’t a people consult their God instead? Why consult the dead on behalf of the living?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.20', 'BSB', 'To the law and to the testimony! If they do not speak according to this word, they have no light of dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.21', 'BSB', 'They will roam the land, dejected and hungry. When they are famished, they will become enraged; and looking upward, they will curse their king and their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.8.22', 'BSB', 'Then they will look to the earth and see only distress and darkness and the gloom of anguish. And they will be driven into utter darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.1', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, there will be no more gloom for those in distress. In the past He humbled the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali, but in the future He will honor the Way of the Sea, beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the nations:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.2', 'BSB', 'The people walking in darkness have seen a great light; on those living in the land of the shadow of death, a light has dawned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.3', 'BSB', 'You have enlarged the nation and increased its joy. The people rejoice before You as they rejoice at harvest time, as men rejoice in dividing the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.4', 'BSB', 'For as in the day of Midian You have shattered the yoke of their burden, the bar across their shoulders, and the rod of their oppressor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.5', 'BSB', 'For every trampling boot of battle and every garment rolled in blood will be burned as fuel for the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.6', 'BSB', 'For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given, and the government will be upon His shoulders. And He will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.7', 'BSB', 'Of the increase of His government and peace there will be no end. He will reign on the throne of David and over his kingdom, to establish and sustain it with justice and righteousness from that time and forevermore. The zeal of the LORD of Hosts will accomplish this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.8', 'BSB', 'The Lord has sent a message against Jacob, and it has fallen upon Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.9', 'BSB', 'All the people will know it— Ephraim and the dwellers of Samaria. With pride and arrogance of heart they will say:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.10', 'BSB', '“The bricks have fallen, but we will rebuild with finished stone; the sycamores have been felled, but we will replace them with cedars.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD has raised up the foes of Rezin against him and joined his enemies together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.12', 'BSB', 'Aram from the east and Philistia from the west have devoured Israel with open mouths. Despite all this, His anger is not turned away; His hand is still upraised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.13', 'BSB', 'But the people did not return to Him who struck them; they did not seek the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.14', 'BSB', 'So the LORD will cut off Israel’s head and tail, both palm branch and reed in a single day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.15', 'BSB', 'The head is the elder and honorable man, and the tail is the prophet who teaches lies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.16', 'BSB', 'For those who guide this people mislead them, and those they mislead are swallowed up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore the Lord takes no pleasure in their young men; He has no compassion on their fatherless and widows. For every one of them is godless and wicked, and every mouth speaks folly. Despite all this, His anger is not turned away; His hand is still upraised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.18', 'BSB', 'For wickedness burns like a fire that consumes the thorns and briers and kindles the forest thickets which roll upward in billows of smoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.19', 'BSB', 'By the wrath of the LORD of Hosts the land is scorched, and the people are fuel for the fire. No man even spares his brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.20', 'BSB', 'They carve out what is on the right, but they are still hungry; they eat what is on the left, but they are still not satisfied. Each one devours the flesh of his own offspring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.9.21', 'BSB', 'Manasseh devours Ephraim, and Ephraim Manasseh; together they turn against Judah. Despite all this, His anger is not turned away; His hand is still upraised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who enact unjust statutes and issue oppressive decrees,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.2', 'BSB', 'to deprive the poor of fair treatment and withhold justice from the oppressed of My people, to make widows their prey and orphans their plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.3', 'BSB', 'What will you do on the day of reckoning when devastation comes from afar? To whom will you flee for help? Where will you leave your wealth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.4', 'BSB', 'Nothing will remain but to crouch among the captives or fall among the slain. Despite all this, His anger is not turned away; His hand is still upraised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.5', 'BSB', 'Woe to Assyria, the rod of My anger; the staff in their hands is My wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.6', 'BSB', 'I will send him against a godless nation; I will dispatch him against a people destined for My rage, to take spoils and seize plunder, and to trample them down like clay in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.7', 'BSB', 'But this is not his intention; this is not his plan. For it is in his heart to destroy and cut off many nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.8', 'BSB', '“Are not all my commanders kings?” he says.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.9', 'BSB', '“Is not Calno like Carchemish? Is not Hamath like Arpad? Is not Samaria like Damascus?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.10', 'BSB', 'As my hand seized the idolatrous kingdoms whose images surpassed those of Jerusalem and Samaria,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.11', 'BSB', 'and as I have done to Samaria and its idols, will I not also do to Jerusalem and her idols?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.12', 'BSB', 'So when the Lord has completed all His work against Mount Zion and Jerusalem, He will say, “I will punish the king of Assyria for the fruit of his arrogant heart and the proud look in his eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.13', 'BSB', 'For he says: ‘By the strength of my hand I have done this, and by my wisdom, for I am clever. I have removed the boundaries of nations and plundered their treasures; like a mighty one I subdued their rulers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.14', 'BSB', 'My hand reached as into a nest to seize the wealth of the nations. Like one gathering abandoned eggs, I gathered all the earth. No wing fluttered, no beak opened or chirped.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.15', 'BSB', 'Does an axe raise itself above the one who swings it? Does a saw boast over him who saws with it? It would be like a rod waving the one who lifts it, or a staff lifting him who is not wood!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore the Lord GOD of Hosts will send a wasting disease among Assyria’s stout warriors, and under his pomp will be kindled a fire like a burning flame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.17', 'BSB', 'And the Light of Israel will become a fire, and its Holy One a flame. In a single day it will burn and devour Assyria’s thorns and thistles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.18', 'BSB', 'The splendor of its forests and orchards, both soul and body, it will completely destroy, as a sickness consumes a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.19', 'BSB', 'The remaining trees of its forests will be so few that a child could count them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.20', 'BSB', 'On that day the remnant of Israel and the survivors of the house of Jacob will no longer depend on him who struck them, but they will truly rely on the LORD, the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.21', 'BSB', 'A remnant will return —a remnant of Jacob— to the Mighty God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.22', 'BSB', 'Though your people, O Israel, be like the sand of the sea, only a remnant will return. Destruction has been decreed, overflowing with righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.23', 'BSB', 'For the Lord GOD of Hosts will carry out the destruction decreed upon the whole land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD of Hosts says: “O My people who dwell in Zion, do not fear Assyria, who strikes you with a rod and lifts his staff against you as the Egyptians did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.25', 'BSB', 'For in just a little while My fury against you will subside, and My anger will turn to their destruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.26', 'BSB', 'And the LORD of Hosts will brandish a whip against them, as when He struck Midian at the rock of Oreb. He will raise His staff over the sea, as He did in Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.27', 'BSB', 'On that day the burden will be lifted from your shoulders, and the yoke from your neck. The yoke will be broken because your neck will be too large.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.28', 'BSB', 'Assyria has entered Aiath and passed through Migron, storing their supplies at Michmash.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.29', 'BSB', 'They have crossed at the ford: “We will spend the night at Geba.” Ramah trembles; Gibeah of Saul flees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.30', 'BSB', 'Cry aloud, O Daughter of Gallim! Listen, O Laishah! O wretched Anathoth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.31', 'BSB', 'Madmenah flees; the people of Gebim take refuge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.32', 'BSB', 'Yet today they will halt at Nob, shaking a fist at the mount of Daughter Zion, at the hill of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.33', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Lord GOD of Hosts will lop off the branches with terrifying power. The tall trees will be cut down, the lofty ones will be felled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.10.34', 'BSB', 'He will clear the forest thickets with an axe, and Lebanon will fall before the Mighty One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.1', 'BSB', 'Then a shoot will spring up from the stump of Jesse, and a Branch from his roots will bear fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.2', 'BSB', 'The Spirit of the LORD will rest on Him— the Spirit of wisdom and understanding, the Spirit of counsel and strength, the Spirit of knowledge and fear of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.3', 'BSB', 'And He will delight in the fear of the LORD. He will not judge by what His eyes see, and He will not decide by what His ears hear,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.4', 'BSB', 'but with righteousness He will judge the poor, and with equity He will decide for the lowly of the earth. He will strike the earth with the rod of His mouth and slay the wicked with the breath of His lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.5', 'BSB', 'Righteousness will be the belt around His hips, and faithfulness the sash around His waist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.6', 'BSB', 'The wolf will live with the lamb, and the leopard will lie down with the goat; the calf and young lion and fatling will be together, and a little child will lead them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.7', 'BSB', 'The cow will graze with the bear, their young will lie down together, and the lion will eat straw like the ox.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.8', 'BSB', 'The infant will play by the cobra’s den, and the toddler will reach into the viper’s nest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.9', 'BSB', 'They will neither harm nor destroy on all My holy mountain, for the earth will be full of the knowledge of the LORD as the sea is full of water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.10', 'BSB', 'On that day the Root of Jesse will stand as a banner for the peoples. The nations will seek Him, and His place of rest will be glorious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.11', 'BSB', 'On that day the Lord will extend His hand a second time to recover the remnant of His people from Assyria, from Egypt, from Pathros, from Cush, from Elam, from Shinar, from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.12', 'BSB', 'He will raise a banner for the nations and gather the exiles of Israel; He will collect the scattered of Judah from the four corners of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.13', 'BSB', 'Then the jealousy of Ephraim will depart, and the adversaries of Judah will be cut off. Ephraim will no longer envy Judah, nor will Judah harass Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.14', 'BSB', 'They will swoop down on the slopes of the Philistines to the west; together they will plunder the sons of the east. They will lay their hands on Edom and Moab, and the Ammonites will be subject to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.15', 'BSB', 'The LORD will devote to destruction the gulf of the Sea of Egypt; with a scorching wind He will sweep His hand over the Euphrates. He will split it into seven streams for men to cross with dry sandals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.11.16', 'BSB', 'There will be a highway for the remnant of His people who remain from Assyria, as there was for Israel when they came up from the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.1', 'BSB', 'In that day you will say: “O LORD, I will praise You. Although You were angry with me, Your anger has turned away, and You have comforted me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.2', 'BSB', 'Surely God is my salvation; I will trust and not be afraid. For the LORD GOD is my strength and my song, and He also has become my salvation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.3', 'BSB', 'With joy you will draw water from the springs of salvation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.4', 'BSB', 'and on that day you will say: “Give praise to the LORD; proclaim His name! Make His works known among the peoples; declare that His name is exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.5', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD, for He has done glorious things. Let this be known in all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.12.6', 'BSB', 'Cry out and sing, O citizen of Zion, for great among you is the Holy One of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Babylon that Isaiah son of Amoz received:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.2', 'BSB', 'Raise a banner on a barren hilltop; call aloud to them. Wave your hand, that they may enter the gates of the nobles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.3', 'BSB', 'I have commanded My sanctified ones; I have even summoned My warriors to execute My wrath and exult in My triumph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.4', 'BSB', 'Listen, a tumult on the mountains, like that of a great multitude! Listen, an uproar among the kingdoms, like nations gathered together! The LORD of Hosts is mobilizing an army for war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.5', 'BSB', 'They are coming from faraway lands, from the ends of the heavens— the LORD and the weapons of His wrath— to destroy the whole country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.6', 'BSB', 'Wail, for the Day of the LORD is near; it will come as destruction from the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore all hands will fall limp, and every man’s heart will melt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.8', 'BSB', 'Terror, pain, and anguish will seize them; they will writhe like a woman in labor. They will look at one another, their faces flushed with fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.9', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Day of the LORD is coming— cruel, with fury and burning anger— to make the earth a desolation and to destroy the sinners within it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.10', 'BSB', 'For the stars of heaven and their constellations will not give their light. The rising sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.11', 'BSB', 'I will punish the world for its evil and the wicked for their iniquity. I will end the haughtiness of the arrogant and lay low the pride of the ruthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.12', 'BSB', 'I will make man scarcer than pure gold, and mankind rarer than the gold of Ophir.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will make the heavens tremble, and the earth will be shaken from its place at the wrath of the LORD of Hosts on the day of His burning anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.14', 'BSB', 'Like a hunted gazelle, like a sheep without a shepherd, each will return to his own people, each will flee to his native land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.15', 'BSB', 'Whoever is caught will be stabbed, and whoever is captured will die by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.16', 'BSB', 'Their infants will be dashed to pieces before their eyes, their houses will be looted, and their wives will be ravished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.17', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will stir up against them the Medes, who have no regard for silver and no desire for gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.18', 'BSB', 'Their bows will dash young men to pieces; they will have no mercy on the fruit of the womb; they will not look with pity on the children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.19', 'BSB', 'And Babylon, the jewel of the kingdoms, the glory of the pride of the Chaldeans, will be overthrown by God like Sodom and Gomorrah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.20', 'BSB', 'She will never be inhabited or settled from generation to generation; no nomad will pitch his tent there, no shepherd will rest his flock there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.21', 'BSB', 'But desert creatures will lie down there, and howling creatures will fill her houses. Ostriches will dwell there, and wild goats will leap about.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.13.22', 'BSB', 'Hyenas will howl in her fortresses and jackals in her luxurious palaces. Babylon’s time is at hand, and her days will not be prolonged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.1', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will have compassion on Jacob; once again He will choose Israel and settle them in their own land. The foreigner will join them and unite with the house of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.2', 'BSB', 'The nations will escort Israel and bring it to its homeland. Then the house of Israel will possess the nations as menservants and maidservants in the LORD’s land. They will make captives of their captors and rule over their oppressors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.3', 'BSB', 'On the day that the LORD gives you rest from your pain and torment, and from the hard labor into which you were forced,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.4', 'BSB', 'you will sing this song of contempt against the king of Babylon: How the oppressor has ceased, and how his fury has ended!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD has broken the staff of the wicked, the scepter of the rulers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.6', 'BSB', 'It struck the peoples in anger with unceasing blows; it subdued the nations in rage with relentless persecution.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.7', 'BSB', 'All the earth is at peace and at rest; they break out in song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.8', 'BSB', 'Even the cypresses and cedars of Lebanon exult over you: “Since you have been laid low, no woodcutter comes against us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.9', 'BSB', 'Sheol beneath is eager to meet you upon your arrival. It stirs the spirits of the dead to greet you— all the rulers of the earth. It makes all the kings of the nations rise from their thrones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.10', 'BSB', 'They will all respond to you, saying, “You too have become weak, as we are; you have become like us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.11', 'BSB', 'Your pomp has been brought down to Sheol, along with the music of your harps. Maggots are your bed and worms your blanket.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.12', 'BSB', 'How you have fallen from heaven, O day star, son of the dawn! You have been cut down to the ground, O destroyer of nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.13', 'BSB', 'You said in your heart: “I will ascend to the heavens; I will raise my throne above the stars of God. I will sit on the mount of assembly, in the far reaches of the north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.14', 'BSB', 'I will ascend above the tops of the clouds; I will make myself like the Most High.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.15', 'BSB', 'But you will be brought down to Sheol, to the lowest depths of the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.16', 'BSB', 'Those who see you will stare; they will ponder your fate: “Is this the man who shook the earth and made the kingdoms tremble,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.17', 'BSB', 'who turned the world into a desert and destroyed its cities, who refused to let the captives return to their homes?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.18', 'BSB', 'All the kings of the nations lie in state, each in his own tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.19', 'BSB', 'But you are cast out of your grave like a rejected branch, covered by those slain with the sword, and dumped into a rocky pit like a carcass trampled underfoot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.20', 'BSB', 'You will not join them in burial, since you have destroyed your land and slaughtered your own people. The offspring of the wicked will never again be mentioned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.21', 'BSB', 'Prepare a place to slaughter his sons for the iniquities of their forefathers. They will never rise up to possess a land or cover the earth with their cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.22', 'BSB', '“I will rise up against them,” declares the LORD of Hosts. “I will cut off from Babylon her name and her remnant, her offspring and her posterity,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.23', 'BSB', '“I will make her a place for owls and for swamplands; I will sweep her away with the broom of destruction,” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.24', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts has sworn: “Surely, as I have planned, so will it be; as I have purposed, so will it stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.25', 'BSB', 'I will break Assyria in My land; I will trample him on My mountain. His yoke will be taken off My people, and his burden removed from their shoulders.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.26', 'BSB', 'This is the plan devised for the whole earth, and this is the hand stretched out over all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.27', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts has purposed, and who can thwart Him? His hand is outstretched, so who can turn it back?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.28', 'BSB', 'In the year that King Ahaz died, this burden was received:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.29', 'BSB', 'Do not rejoice, all you Philistines, that the rod that struck you is broken. For a viper will spring from the root of the snake, and a flying serpent from its egg.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.30', 'BSB', 'Then the firstborn of the poor will find pasture, and the needy will lie down in safety, but I will kill your root by famine, and your remnant will be slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.31', 'BSB', 'Wail, O gate! Cry out, O city! Melt away, all you Philistines! For a cloud of smoke comes from the north, and there are no stragglers in its ranks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.14.32', 'BSB', 'What answer will be given to the envoys of that nation? “The LORD has founded Zion, where His afflicted people will find refuge.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Moab: Ar in Moab is ruined, destroyed in a night! Kir in Moab is devastated, destroyed in a night!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.2', 'BSB', 'Dibon goes up to its temple to weep at its high places. Moab wails over Nebo, as well as over Medeba. Every head is shaved, every beard is cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.3', 'BSB', 'In its streets they wear sackcloth; on the rooftops and in the public squares they all wail, falling down weeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.4', 'BSB', 'Heshbon and Elealeh cry out; their voices are heard as far as Jahaz. Therefore the soldiers of Moab cry out; their souls tremble within.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.5', 'BSB', 'My heart cries out over Moab; her fugitives flee as far as Zoar, as far as Eglath-shelishiyah. With weeping they ascend the slope of Luhith; they lament their destruction on the road to Horonaim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.6', 'BSB', 'The waters of Nimrim are dried up, and the grass is withered; the vegetation is gone, and the greenery is no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.7', 'BSB', 'So they carry their wealth and belongings over the Brook of the Willows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.8', 'BSB', 'For their outcry echoes to the border of Moab. Their wailing reaches Eglaim; it is heard in Beer-elim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.15.9', 'BSB', 'The waters of Dimon are full of blood, but I will bring more upon Dimon— a lion upon the fugitives of Moab and upon the remnant of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.1', 'BSB', 'Send the tribute lambs to the ruler of the land, from Sela in the desert to the mount of Daughter Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.2', 'BSB', 'Like fluttering birds pushed out of the nest, so are the daughters of Moab at the fords of the Arnon:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.3', 'BSB', '“Give us counsel; render a decision. Shelter us at noonday with shade as dark as night. Hide the refugees; do not betray the one who flees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.4', 'BSB', 'Let my fugitives stay with you; be a refuge for Moab from the destroyer.” When the oppressor has gone, destruction has ceased, and the oppressors have vanished from the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.5', 'BSB', 'in loving devotion a throne will be established in the tent of David. A judge seeking justice and hastening righteousness will sit on it in faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.6', 'BSB', 'We have heard of Moab’s pomposity, his exceeding pride and conceit, his overflowing arrogance. But his boasting is empty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore let Moab wail; let them wail together for Moab. Moan for the raisin cakes of Kir-hareseth, you who are utterly stricken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.8', 'BSB', 'For the fields of Heshbon have withered, along with the grapevines of Sibmah. The rulers of the nations have trampled its choicest vines, which had reached as far as Jazer and spread toward the desert. Their shoots had spread out and passed over the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.9', 'BSB', 'So I weep with Jazer for the vines of Sibmah; I drench Heshbon and Elealeh with my tears. Triumphant shouts have fallen silent over your summer fruit and your harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.10', 'BSB', 'Joy and gladness are removed from the orchard; no one sings or shouts in the vineyards. No one tramples the grapes in the winepresses; I have put an end to the cheering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore my heart laments for Moab like a harp, my inmost being for Kir-heres.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.12', 'BSB', 'When Moab appears on the high place, when he wearies himself and enters his sanctuary to pray, it will do him no good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.13', 'BSB', 'This is the message that the LORD spoke earlier concerning Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.16.14', 'BSB', 'And now the LORD says, “In three years, as a hired worker counts the years, Moab’s splendor will become an object of contempt, with all her many people. And those who are left will be few and feeble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Damascus: “Behold, Damascus is no longer a city; it has become a heap of ruins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.2', 'BSB', 'The cities of Aroer are forsaken; they will be left to the flocks, which will lie down with no one to fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.3', 'BSB', 'The fortress will disappear from Ephraim, and the sovereignty from Damascus. The remnant of Aram will be like the splendor of the Israelites,” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.4', 'BSB', '“In that day the splendor of Jacob will fade, and the fat of his body will waste away,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.5', 'BSB', 'as the reaper gathers the standing grain and harvests the ears with his arm, as one gleans heads of grain in the Valley of Rephaim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.6', 'BSB', 'Yet gleanings will remain, like an olive tree that has been beaten— two or three berries atop the tree, four or five on its fruitful branches,” declares the LORD, the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.7', 'BSB', 'In that day men will look to their Maker and turn their eyes to the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.8', 'BSB', 'They will not look to the altars they have fashioned with their hands or to the Asherahs and incense altars they have made with their fingers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.9', 'BSB', 'In that day their strong cities will be like forsaken thickets and summits, abandoned to the Israelites and to utter desolation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.10', 'BSB', 'For you have forgotten the God of your salvation and failed to remember the Rock of your refuge. Therefore, though you cultivate delightful plots and set out cuttings from exotic vines—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.11', 'BSB', 'though on the day you plant you make them grow, and on that morning you help your seed sprout— yet the harvest will vanish on the day of disease and incurable pain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.12', 'BSB', 'Alas, the tumult of many peoples; they rage like the roaring seas and clamoring nations; they rumble like the crashing of mighty waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.13', 'BSB', 'The nations rage like the rush of many waters. He rebukes them, and they flee far away, driven before the wind like chaff on the hills, like tumbleweeds before a gale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.17.14', 'BSB', 'In the evening, there is sudden terror! Before morning, they are no more! This is the portion of those who loot us and the lot of those who plunder us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to the land of whirring wings, along the rivers of Cush,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.2', 'BSB', 'which sends couriers by sea, in papyrus vessels on the waters. Go, swift messengers, to a people tall and smooth-skinned, to a people widely feared, to a powerful nation of strange speech, whose land is divided by rivers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.3', 'BSB', 'All you people of the world and dwellers of the earth, when a banner is raised on the mountains, you will see it; when a ram’s horn sounds, you will hear it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD has told me: “I will quietly look on from My dwelling place, like shimmering heat in the sunshine, like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.5', 'BSB', 'For before the harvest, when the blossom is gone and the flower becomes a ripening grape, He will cut off the shoots with a pruning knife and remove and discard the branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.6', 'BSB', 'They will all be left to the mountain birds of prey, and to the beasts of the land. The birds will feed on them in summer, and all the wild animals in winter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.18.7', 'BSB', 'At that time gifts will be brought to the LORD of Hosts— from a people tall and smooth-skinned, from a people widely feared, from a powerful nation of strange speech, whose land is divided by rivers— to Mount Zion, the place of the Name of the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Egypt: Behold, the LORD rides on a swift cloud; He is coming to Egypt. The idols of Egypt will tremble before Him, and the hearts of the Egyptians will melt within them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.2', 'BSB', '“So I will incite Egyptian against Egyptian; brother will fight against brother, neighbor against neighbor, city against city, and kingdom against kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.3', 'BSB', 'Then the spirit of the Egyptians will be emptied out from among them, and I will frustrate their plans, so that they will resort to idols and spirits of the dead, to mediums and spiritists.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.4', 'BSB', 'I will deliver the Egyptians into the hands of harsh masters, and a fierce king will rule over them,” declares the Lord GOD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.5', 'BSB', 'The waters of the Nile will dry up, and the riverbed will be parched and empty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.6', 'BSB', 'The canals will stink; the streams of Egypt will trickle and dry up; the reeds and rushes will wither.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.7', 'BSB', 'The bulrushes by the Nile, by the mouth of the river, and all the fields sown along the Nile, will wither, blow away, and be no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.8', 'BSB', 'Then the fishermen will mourn, all who cast a hook into the Nile will lament, and those who spread nets on the waters will pine away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.9', 'BSB', 'The workers in flax will be dismayed, and the weavers of fine linen will turn pale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.10', 'BSB', 'The workers in cloth will be dejected, and all the hired workers will be sick at heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.11', 'BSB', 'The princes of Zoan are mere fools; Pharaoh’s wise counselors give senseless advice. How can you say to Pharaoh, “I am one of the wise, a son of eastern kings”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.12', 'BSB', 'Where are your wise men now? Let them tell you and reveal what the LORD of Hosts has planned against Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.13', 'BSB', 'The princes of Zoan have become fools; the princes of Memphis are deceived. The cornerstones of her tribes have led Egypt astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD has poured into her a spirit of confusion. Egypt has been led astray in all she does, as a drunkard staggers through his own vomit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.15', 'BSB', 'There is nothing Egypt can do— head or tail, palm or reed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.16', 'BSB', 'In that day the Egyptians will be like women. They will tremble with fear beneath the uplifted hand of the LORD of Hosts, when He brandishes it against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.17', 'BSB', 'The land of Judah will bring terror to Egypt; whenever Judah is mentioned, Egypt will tremble over what the LORD of Hosts has planned against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.18', 'BSB', 'In that day five cities in the land of Egypt will speak the language of Canaan and swear allegiance to the LORD of Hosts. One of them will be called the City of the Sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.19', 'BSB', 'In that day there will be an altar to the LORD in the center of the land of Egypt, and a pillar to the LORD near her border.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.20', 'BSB', 'It will be a sign and a witness to the LORD of Hosts in the land of Egypt. When they cry out to the LORD because of their oppressors, He will send them a savior and defender to rescue them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.21', 'BSB', 'The LORD will make Himself known to Egypt, and on that day Egypt will acknowledge the LORD. They will worship with sacrifices and offerings; they will make vows to the LORD and fulfill them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.22', 'BSB', 'And the LORD will strike Egypt with a plague; He will strike them but heal them. They will turn to the LORD, and He will hear their prayers and heal them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.23', 'BSB', 'In that day there will be a highway from Egypt to Assyria. The Assyrians will go to Egypt, and the Egyptians to Assyria. The Egyptians and Assyrians will worship together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.24', 'BSB', 'In that day Israel will join a three-party alliance with Egypt and Assyria—a blessing upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.19.25', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts will bless them, saying, “Blessed be Egypt My people, Assyria My handiwork, and Israel My inheritance.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.1', 'BSB', 'Before the year that the chief commander, sent by Sargon king of Assyria, came to Ashdod and attacked and captured it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.2', 'BSB', 'the LORD had already spoken through Isaiah son of Amoz, saying, “Go, remove the sackcloth from your waist and the sandals from your feet.” And Isaiah did so, walking around naked and barefoot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.3', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said, “Just as My servant Isaiah has gone naked and barefoot for three years as a sign and omen against Egypt and Cush,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.4', 'BSB', 'so the king of Assyria will lead away the captives of Egypt and the exiles of Cush, young and old alike, naked and barefoot, with bared buttocks—to Egypt’s shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.5', 'BSB', 'Those who made Cush their hope and Egypt their boast will be dismayed and ashamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.20.6', 'BSB', 'And on that day the dwellers of this coastland will say, ‘See what has happened to our source of hope, those to whom we fled for help and deliverance from the king of Assyria! How then can we escape?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against the Desert by the Sea: Like whirlwinds sweeping through the Negev, an invader comes from the desert, from a land of terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.2', 'BSB', 'A dire vision is declared to me: “The traitor still betrays, and the destroyer still destroys. Go up, O Elam! Lay siege, O Media! I will put an end to all her groaning.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore my body is filled with anguish. Pain grips me, like the pains of a woman in labor. I am bewildered to hear, I am dismayed to see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.4', 'BSB', 'My heart falters; fear makes me tremble. The twilight of my desire has turned to horror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.5', 'BSB', 'They prepare a table, they lay out a carpet, they eat, they drink! Rise up, O princes, oil the shields!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord says to me: “Go, post a lookout and have him report what he sees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.7', 'BSB', 'When he sees chariots with teams of horsemen, riders on donkeys, riders on camels, he must be alert, fully alert.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.8', 'BSB', 'Then the lookout shouted: “Day after day, my lord, I stand on the watchtower; night after night I stay at my post.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.9', 'BSB', 'Look, here come the riders, horsemen in pairs.” And one answered, saying: “Fallen, fallen is Babylon! All the images of her gods lie shattered on the ground!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.10', 'BSB', 'O my people, crushed on the threshing floor, I tell you what I have heard from the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.11', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Dumah: One calls to me from Seir, “Watchman, what is left of the night? Watchman, what is left of the night?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.12', 'BSB', 'The watchman replies, “Morning has come, but also the night. If you would inquire, then inquire. Come back yet again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.13', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Arabia: In the thickets of Arabia you must lodge, O caravans of Dedanites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.14', 'BSB', 'Bring water for the thirsty, O dwellers of Tema; meet the refugees with food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.15', 'BSB', 'For they flee from the sword— the sword that is drawn— from the bow that is bent, and from the stress of battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.16', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord says to me: “Within one year, as a hired worker would count it, all the glory of Kedar will be gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.21.17', 'BSB', 'The remaining archers, the warriors of Kedar, will be few.” For the LORD, the God of Israel, has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against the Valley of Vision: What ails you now, that you have all gone up to the rooftops,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.2', 'BSB', 'O city of commotion, O town of revelry? Your slain did not die by the sword, nor were they killed in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.3', 'BSB', 'All your rulers have fled together, captured without a bow. All your fugitives were captured together, having fled to a distant place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore I said, “Turn away from me, let me weep bitterly! Do not try to console me over the destruction of the daughter of my people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.5', 'BSB', 'For the Lord GOD of Hosts has set a day of tumult and trampling and confusion in the Valley of Vision— of breaking down the walls and crying to the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.6', 'BSB', 'Elam takes up a quiver, with chariots and horsemen, and Kir uncovers the shield.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.7', 'BSB', 'Your choicest valleys are full of chariots, and horsemen are posted at the gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.8', 'BSB', 'He has uncovered the defenses of Judah. On that day you looked to the weapons in the House of the Forest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.9', 'BSB', 'You saw that there were many breaches in the walls of the City of David. You collected water from the lower pool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.10', 'BSB', 'You counted the houses of Jerusalem and tore them down to strengthen the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.11', 'BSB', 'You built a reservoir between the walls for the waters of the ancient pool, but you did not look to the One who made it, or consider Him who planned it long ago.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.12', 'BSB', 'On that day the Lord GOD of Hosts called for weeping and wailing, for shaven heads and the wearing of sackcloth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.13', 'BSB', 'But look, there is joy and gladness, butchering of cattle and slaughtering of sheep, eating of meat and drinking of wine: “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts has revealed in my hearing: “Until your dying day, this sin of yours will never be atoned for,” says the Lord GOD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD of Hosts says: “Go, say to Shebna, the steward in charge of the palace:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.16', 'BSB', 'What are you doing here, and who authorized you to carve out a tomb for yourself here—to chisel your tomb in the height and cut your resting place in the rock?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.17', 'BSB', 'Look, O mighty man! The LORD is about to shake you violently. He will take hold of you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.18', 'BSB', 'roll you into a ball, and sling you into a wide land. There you will die, and there your glorious chariots will remain—a disgrace to the house of your master.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.19', 'BSB', 'I will remove you from office, and you will be ousted from your position.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.20', 'BSB', 'On that day I will summon My servant, Eliakim son of Hilkiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.21', 'BSB', 'I will clothe him with your robe and tie your sash around him. I will put your authority in his hand, and he will be a father to the dwellers of Jerusalem and to the house of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.22', 'BSB', 'I will place on his shoulder the key to the house of David. What he opens no one can shut, and what he shuts no one can open.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.23', 'BSB', 'I will drive him like a peg into a firm place, and he will be a throne of glory for the house of his father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.24', 'BSB', 'So they will hang on him the whole burden of his father’s house: the descendants and the offshoots—all the lesser vessels, from bowls to every kind of jar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.22.25', 'BSB', 'In that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, the peg driven into a firm place will give way; it will be sheared off and fall, and the load upon it will be cut down.” Indeed, the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Tyre: Wail, O ships of Tarshish, for Tyre is laid waste, without house or harbor. Word has reached them from the land of Cyprus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.2', 'BSB', 'Be silent, O dwellers of the coastland, you merchants of Sidon, whose traders have crossed the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.3', 'BSB', 'On the great waters came the grain of Shihor; the harvest of the Nile was the revenue of Tyre; she was the merchant of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.4', 'BSB', 'Be ashamed, O Sidon, the stronghold of the sea, for the sea has spoken: “I have not been in labor or given birth. I have not raised young men or brought up young women.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.5', 'BSB', 'When the report reaches Egypt, they will writhe in agony over the news of Tyre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.6', 'BSB', 'Cross over to Tarshish; wail, O inhabitants of the coastland!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.7', 'BSB', 'Is this your jubilant city, whose origin is from antiquity, whose feet have taken her to settle far away?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.8', 'BSB', 'Who planned this against Tyre, the bestower of crowns, whose traders are princes, whose merchants are renowned on the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.9', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts planned it, to defile all its glorious beauty, to disgrace all the renowned of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.10', 'BSB', 'Cultivate your land like the Nile, O Daughter of Tarshish; there is no longer a harbor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD has stretched out His hand over the sea; He has made kingdoms tremble. He has given a command that the strongholds of Canaan be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.12', 'BSB', 'He said, “You shall rejoice no more, O oppressed Virgin Daughter of Sidon. Get up and cross over to Cyprus— even there you will find no rest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.13', 'BSB', 'Look at the land of the Chaldeans — a people now of no account. The Assyrians destined it for the desert creatures; they set up their siege towers and stripped its palaces. They brought it to ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.14', 'BSB', 'Wail, O ships of Tarshish, for your harbor has been destroyed!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.15', 'BSB', 'At that time Tyre will be forgotten for seventy years—the span of a king’s life. But at the end of seventy years, it will happen to Tyre as in the song of the harlot:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.16', 'BSB', '“Take up your harp, stroll through the city, O forgotten harlot. Make sweet melody, sing many a song, so you will be remembered.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.17', 'BSB', 'And at the end of seventy years, the LORD will restore Tyre. Then she will return to hire as a prostitute and sell herself to all the kingdoms on the face of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.23.18', 'BSB', 'Yet her profits and wages will be set apart to the LORD; they will not be stored or saved, for her profit will go to those who live before the LORD, for abundant food and fine clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.1', 'BSB', 'Behold, the LORD lays waste the earth and leaves it in ruins. He will twist its surface and scatter its inhabitants—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.2', 'BSB', 'people and priest alike, servant and master, maid and mistress, buyer and seller, lender and borrower, creditor and debtor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.3', 'BSB', 'The earth will be utterly laid waste and thoroughly plundered. For the LORD has spoken this word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.4', 'BSB', 'The earth mourns and withers; the world languishes and fades; the exalted of the earth waste away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.5', 'BSB', 'The earth is defiled by its people; they have transgressed the laws; they have overstepped the decrees and broken the everlasting covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore a curse has consumed the earth, and its inhabitants must bear the guilt; the earth’s dwellers have been burned, and only a few survive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.7', 'BSB', 'The new wine dries up, the vine withers. All the merrymakers now groan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.8', 'BSB', 'The joyful tambourines have ceased; the noise of revelers has stopped; the joyful harp is silent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.9', 'BSB', 'They no longer sing and drink wine; strong drink is bitter to those who consume it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.10', 'BSB', 'The city of chaos is shattered; every house is closed to entry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.11', 'BSB', 'In the streets they cry out for wine. All joy turns to gloom; rejoicing is exiled from the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.12', 'BSB', 'The city is left in ruins; its gate is reduced to rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.13', 'BSB', 'So will it be on the earth and among the nations, like a harvested olive tree, like a gleaning after a grape harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.14', 'BSB', 'They raise their voices, they shout for joy; from the west they proclaim the majesty of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore glorify the LORD in the east. Extol the name of the LORD, the God of Israel in the islands of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.16', 'BSB', 'From the ends of the earth we hear singing: “Glory to the Righteous One.” But I said, “I am wasting away! I am wasting away! Woe is me.” The treacherous betray; the treacherous deal in treachery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.17', 'BSB', 'Terror and pit and snare await you, O dweller of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.18', 'BSB', 'Whoever flees the sound of panic will fall into the pit, and whoever climbs from the pit will be caught in the snare. For the windows of heaven are open, and the foundations of the earth are shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.19', 'BSB', 'The earth is utterly broken apart, the earth is split open, the earth is shaken violently.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.20', 'BSB', 'The earth staggers like a drunkard and sways like a shack. Earth’s rebellion weighs it down, and it falls, never to rise again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.21', 'BSB', 'In that day the LORD will punish the host of heaven above and the kings of the earth below.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.22', 'BSB', 'They will be gathered together like prisoners in a pit. They will be confined to a dungeon and punished after many days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.24.23', 'BSB', 'The moon will be confounded and the sun will be ashamed; for the LORD of Hosts will reign on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem, and before His elders with great glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.1', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You are my God! I will exalt You; I will praise Your name. For You have worked wonders— plans formed long ago— in perfect faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.2', 'BSB', 'Indeed, You have made the city a heap of rubble, the fortified town a ruin. The fortress of strangers is a city no more; it will never be rebuilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore, a strong people will honor You. The cities of ruthless nations will revere You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.4', 'BSB', 'For You have been a refuge for the poor, a stronghold for the needy in distress, a refuge from the storm, a shade from the heat. For the breath of the ruthless is like rain against a wall,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.5', 'BSB', 'like heat in a dry land. You subdue the uproar of foreigners. As the shade of a cloud cools the heat, so the song of the ruthless is silenced.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.6', 'BSB', 'On this mountain the LORD of Hosts will prepare a banquet for all the peoples, a feast of aged wine, of choice meat, of finely aged wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.7', 'BSB', 'On this mountain He will swallow up the shroud that enfolds all peoples, the sheet that covers all nations;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.8', 'BSB', 'He will swallow up death forever. The Lord GOD will wipe away the tears from every face and remove the disgrace of His people from the whole earth. For the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.9', 'BSB', 'And in that day it will be said, “Surely this is our God; we have waited for Him, and He has saved us. This is the LORD for whom we have waited. Let us rejoice and be glad in His salvation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.10', 'BSB', 'For the hand of the LORD will rest on this mountain. But Moab will be trampled in his place as straw is trodden into the dung pile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.11', 'BSB', 'He will spread out his hands within it, as a swimmer spreads his arms to swim. His pride will be brought low, despite the skill of his hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.25.12', 'BSB', 'The high-walled fortress will be brought down, cast to the ground, into the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.1', 'BSB', 'In that day this song will be sung in the land of Judah: We have a strong city; salvation is established as its walls and ramparts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.2', 'BSB', 'Open the gates so a righteous nation may enter— one that remains faithful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.3', 'BSB', 'You will keep in perfect peace the steadfast of mind, because he trusts in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.4', 'BSB', 'Trust in the LORD forever, because GOD the LORD is the Rock eternal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.5', 'BSB', 'For He has humbled those who dwell on high; He lays the lofty city low. He brings it down to the ground; He casts it into the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.6', 'BSB', 'Feet trample it down— the feet of the oppressed, the steps of the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.7', 'BSB', 'The path of the righteous is level; You clear a straight path for the upright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.8', 'BSB', 'Yes, we wait for You, O LORD; we walk in the path of Your judgments. Your name and renown are the desire of our souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.9', 'BSB', 'My soul longs for You in the night; indeed, my spirit seeks You at dawn. For when Your judgments come upon the earth, the people of the world learn righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.10', 'BSB', 'Though grace is shown to the wicked man, he does not learn righteousness. In the land of righteousness he acts unjustly and fails to see the majesty of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.11', 'BSB', 'O LORD, Your hand is upraised, but they do not see it. They will see Your zeal for Your people and be put to shame. The fire set for Your enemies will consume them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.12', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You will establish peace for us. For all that we have accomplished, You have done for us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.13', 'BSB', 'O LORD our God, other lords besides You have had dominion, but Your name alone do we confess.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.14', 'BSB', 'The dead will not live; the departed spirits will not rise. Therefore You have punished and destroyed them; You have wiped out all memory of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.15', 'BSB', 'You have enlarged the nation, O LORD; You have enlarged the nation. You have gained glory for Yourself; You have extended all the borders of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.16', 'BSB', 'O LORD, they sought You in their distress; when You disciplined them, they poured out a quiet prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.17', 'BSB', 'As a woman with child about to give birth writhes and cries out in pain, so were we in Your presence, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.18', 'BSB', 'We were with child; we writhed in pain; but we gave birth to wind. We have given no salvation to the earth, nor brought any life into the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.19', 'BSB', 'Your dead will live; their bodies will rise. Awake and sing, you who dwell in the dust! For your dew is like the dew of the morning, and the earth will bring forth her dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.20', 'BSB', 'Go, my people, enter your rooms and shut your doors behind you. Hide yourselves a little while until the wrath has passed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.26.21', 'BSB', 'For behold, the LORD is coming out of His dwelling to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity. The earth will reveal her bloodshed and will no longer conceal her slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.1', 'BSB', 'In that day the LORD will take His sharp, great, and mighty sword, and bring judgment on Leviathan the fleeing serpent —Leviathan the coiling serpent—and He will slay the dragon of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.2', 'BSB', 'In that day: “Sing about a fruitful vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.3', 'BSB', 'I, the LORD, am its keeper; I water it continually. I guard it night and day so no one can disturb it;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.4', 'BSB', 'I am not angry. If only thorns and briers confronted Me, I would march and trample them, I would burn them to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.5', 'BSB', 'Or let them lay claim to My protection; let them make peace with Me— yes, let them make peace with Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.6', 'BSB', 'In the days to come, Jacob will take root. Israel will bud and blossom and fill the whole world with fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.7', 'BSB', 'Has the LORD struck Israel as He struck her oppressors? Was she killed like those who slayed her?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.8', 'BSB', 'By warfare and exile You contended with her and removed her with a fierce wind, as on the day the east wind blows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore Jacob’s guilt will be atoned for, and the full fruit of the removal of his sin will be this: When he makes all the altar stones like crushed bits of chalk, no Asherah poles or incense altars will remain standing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.10', 'BSB', 'For the fortified city lies deserted— a homestead abandoned, a wilderness forsaken. There the calves graze, and there they lie down; they strip its branches bare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.11', 'BSB', 'When its limbs are dry, they are broken off. Women come and use them for kindling; for this is a people without understanding. Therefore their Maker has no compassion on them, and their Creator shows them no favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.12', 'BSB', 'In that day the LORD will thresh from the flowing Euphrates to the Wadi of Egypt, and you, O Israelites, will be gathered one by one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.27.13', 'BSB', 'And in that day a great ram’s horn will sound, and those who were perishing in Assyria will come forth with those who were exiles in Egypt. And they will worship the LORD on the holy mountain in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to the majestic crown of Ephraim’s drunkards, to the fading flower of his glorious splendor, set on the summit above the fertile valley, the pride of those overcome by wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.2', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Lord has one who is strong and mighty. Like a hailstorm or destructive tempest, like a driving rain or flooding downpour, he will smash that crown to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.3', 'BSB', 'The majestic crown of Ephraim’s drunkards will be trampled underfoot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.4', 'BSB', 'The fading flower of his beautiful splendor, set on the summit above the fertile valley, will be like a ripe fig before the summer harvest: Whoever sees it will take it in his hand and swallow it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.5', 'BSB', 'On that day the LORD of Hosts will be a crown of glory, a diadem of splendor to the remnant of His people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.6', 'BSB', 'a spirit of justice to him who sits in judgment, and a strength to those who repel the onslaught at the gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.7', 'BSB', 'These also stagger from wine and stumble from strong drink: Priests and prophets reel from strong drink and are befuddled by wine. They stumble because of strong drink, muddled in their visions and stumbling in their judgments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.8', 'BSB', 'For all their tables are covered with vomit; there is not a place without filth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.9', 'BSB', 'Whom is He trying to teach? To whom is He explaining His message? To infants just weaned from milk? To babies removed from the breast?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.10', 'BSB', 'For they hear: “Order on order, order on order, line on line, line on line; a little here, a little there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.11', 'BSB', 'Indeed, with mocking lips and foreign tongues, He will speak to this people', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.12', 'BSB', 'to whom He has said: “This is the place of rest, let the weary rest; this is the place of repose.” But they would not listen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.13', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD to them will become: “Order on order, order on order, line on line, line on line; a little here, a little there,” so that they will go stumbling backward and will be injured, ensnared, and captured.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore hear the word of the LORD, O scoffers who rule this people in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.15', 'BSB', 'For you said, “We have made a covenant with death; we have fashioned an agreement with Sheol. When the overwhelming scourge passes through it will not touch us, because we have made lies our refuge and falsehood our hiding place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.16', 'BSB', 'So this is what the Lord GOD says: “See, I lay a stone in Zion, a tested stone, a precious cornerstone, a sure foundation; the one who believes will never be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.17', 'BSB', 'I will make justice the measuring line and righteousness the level. Hail will sweep away your refuge of lies, and water will flood your hiding place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.18', 'BSB', 'Your covenant with death will be dissolved, and your agreement with Sheol will not stand. When the overwhelming scourge passes through, you will be trampled by it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.19', 'BSB', 'As often as it passes through, it will carry you away; it will sweep through morning after morning, by day and by night.” The understanding of this message will bring sheer terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.20', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the bed is too short to stretch out on, and the blanket too small to wrap around you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.21', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will rise up as at Mount Perazim. He will rouse Himself as in the Valley of Gibeon, to do His work, His strange work, and to perform His task, His disturbing task.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.22', 'BSB', 'So now, do not mock, or your shackles will become heavier. Indeed, I have heard from the Lord GOD of Hosts a decree of destruction against the whole land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.23', 'BSB', 'Listen and hear my voice. Pay attention and hear what I say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.24', 'BSB', 'Does the plowman plow for planting every day? Does he continuously loosen and harrow the soil?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.25', 'BSB', 'When he has leveled its surface, does he not sow caraway and scatter cumin? He plants wheat in rows and barley in plots, and rye within its border.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.26', 'BSB', 'For his God instructs and teaches him properly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.27', 'BSB', 'Surely caraway is not threshed with a sledge, and the wheel of a cart is not rolled over the cumin. But caraway is beaten out with a stick, and cumin with a rod.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.28', 'BSB', 'Grain for bread must be ground, but it is not endlessly threshed. Though the wheels of the cart roll over it, the horses do not crush it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.28.29', 'BSB', 'This also comes from the LORD of Hosts, who is wonderful in counsel and excellent in wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, O Ariel, the city of Ariel where David camped! Year upon year let your festivals recur.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.2', 'BSB', 'And I will constrain Ariel, and there will be mourning and lamentation; she will be like an altar hearth before Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.3', 'BSB', 'I will camp in a circle around you; I will besiege you with towers and set up siege works against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.4', 'BSB', 'You will be brought low, you will speak from the ground, and out of the dust your words will be muffled. Your voice will be like a spirit from the ground; your speech will whisper out of the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.5', 'BSB', 'But your many foes will be like fine dust, the multitude of the ruthless like blowing chaff. Then suddenly, in an instant,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.6', 'BSB', 'you will be visited by the LORD of Hosts with thunder and earthquake and loud noise, with windstorm and tempest and consuming flame of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.7', 'BSB', 'All the many nations going out to battle against Ariel— even all who war against her, laying siege and attacking her— will be like a dream, like a vision in the night,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.8', 'BSB', 'as when a hungry man dreams he is eating, then awakens still hungry; as when a thirsty man dreams he is drinking, then awakens faint and parched. So will it be for all the many nations who go to battle against Mount Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.9', 'BSB', 'Stop and be astonished; blind yourselves and be sightless; be drunk, but not with wine; stagger, but not from strong drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.10', 'BSB', 'For the LORD has poured out on you a spirit of deep sleep. He has shut your eyes, O prophets; He has covered your heads, O seers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.11', 'BSB', 'And the entire vision will be to you like the words sealed in a scroll. If it is handed to someone to read, he will say, “I cannot, because it is sealed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.12', 'BSB', 'Or if the scroll is handed to one unable to read, he will say, “I cannot read.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore the Lord said: “These people draw near to Me with their mouths and honor Me with their lips, but their hearts are far from Me. Their worship of Me is but rules taught by men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will again confound these people with wonder upon wonder. The wisdom of the wise will vanish, and the intelligence of the intelligent will be hidden.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.15', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who dig deep to hide their plans from the LORD. In darkness they do their works and say, “Who sees us, and who will know?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.16', 'BSB', 'You have turned things upside down, as if the potter were regarded as clay. Shall what is formed say to him who formed it, “He did not make me”? Can the pottery say of the potter, “He has no understanding”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.17', 'BSB', 'In a very short time, will not Lebanon become an orchard, and the orchard seem like a forest?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.18', 'BSB', 'On that day the deaf will hear the words of the scroll, and out of the deep darkness the eyes of the blind will see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.19', 'BSB', 'The humble will increase their joy in the LORD, and the poor among men will rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.20', 'BSB', 'For the ruthless will vanish, the mockers will disappear, and all who look for evil will be cut down—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.21', 'BSB', 'those who indict a man with a word, who ensnare the mediator at the gate, and who with false charges deprive the innocent of justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.22', 'BSB', 'Therefore the LORD who redeemed Abraham says of the house of Jacob: “No longer will Jacob be ashamed and no more will his face grow pale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.23', 'BSB', 'For when he sees his children around him, the work of My hands, they will honor My name, they will sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and they will stand in awe of the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.29.24', 'BSB', 'Then the wayward in spirit will come to understanding, and those who grumble will accept instruction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.1', 'BSB', '“Woe to the rebellious children,” declares the LORD, “to those who carry out a plan that is not Mine, who form an alliance, but against My will, heaping up sin upon sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.2', 'BSB', 'They set out to go down to Egypt without asking My advice, to seek shelter under Pharaoh’s protection and take refuge in Egypt’s shade.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.3', 'BSB', 'But Pharaoh’s protection will become your shame, and the refuge of Egypt’s shade your disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.4', 'BSB', 'For though their princes are at Zoan and their envoys have arrived in Hanes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.5', 'BSB', 'everyone will be put to shame because of a people useless to them. They cannot be of help; they are good for nothing but shame and reproach.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.6', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against the beasts of the Negev: Through a land of hardship and distress, of lioness and lion, of viper and flying serpent, they carry their wealth on the backs of donkeys and their treasures on the humps of camels, to a people of no profit to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.7', 'BSB', 'Egypt’s help is futile and empty; therefore I have called her Rahab Who Sits Still.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.8', 'BSB', 'Go now, write it on a tablet in their presence and inscribe it on a scroll; it will be for the days to come, a witness forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.9', 'BSB', 'These are rebellious people, deceitful children, children unwilling to obey the LORD’s instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.10', 'BSB', 'They say to the seers, “Stop seeing visions!” and to the prophets, “Do not prophesy to us the truth! Speak to us pleasant words; prophesy illusions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.11', 'BSB', 'Get out of the way; turn off the road. Rid us of the Holy One of Israel!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Holy One of Israel says: “Because you have rejected this message, trusting in oppression and relying on deceit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.13', 'BSB', 'this iniquity of yours is like a breach about to fail, a bulge in a high wall, whose collapse will come suddenly— in an instant!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.14', 'BSB', 'It will break in pieces like a potter’s jar, shattered so that no fragment can be found. Not a shard will be found in the dust large enough to scoop the coals from a hearth or to skim the water from a cistern.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.15', 'BSB', 'For the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel, has said: “By repentance and rest you would be saved; your strength would lie in quiet confidence— but you were not willing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.16', 'BSB', '“No,” you say, “we will flee on horses.” Therefore you will flee! “We will ride swift horses,” but your pursuers will be faster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.17', 'BSB', 'A thousand will flee at the threat of one; at the threat of five you will all flee, until you are left alone like a pole on a mountaintop, like a banner on a hill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore the LORD longs to be gracious to you; therefore He rises to show you compassion, for the LORD is a just God. Blessed are all who wait for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.19', 'BSB', 'O people in Zion who dwell in Jerusalem, you will weep no more. He will surely be gracious when you cry for help; when He hears, He will answer you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.20', 'BSB', 'The Lord will give you the bread of adversity and the water of affliction, but your Teacher will no longer hide Himself—with your own eyes you will see Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.21', 'BSB', 'And whether you turn to the right or to the left, your ears will hear this command behind you: “This is the way. Walk in it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.22', 'BSB', 'So you will desecrate your silver-plated idols and your gold-plated images. You will throw them away like menstrual cloths, saying to them, “Be gone!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.23', 'BSB', 'Then He will send rain for the seed that you have sown in the ground, and the food that comes from your land will be rich and plentiful. On that day your cattle will graze in open pastures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.24', 'BSB', 'The oxen and donkeys that work the ground will eat salted fodder, winnowed with shovel and pitchfork.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.25', 'BSB', 'And from every high mountain and every raised hill, streams of water will flow in the day of great slaughter, when the towers fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.26', 'BSB', 'The light of the moon will be as bright as the sun, and the light of the sun will be seven times brighter—like the light of seven days—on the day that the LORD binds up the brokenness of His people and heals the wounds He has inflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.27', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Name of the LORD comes from afar, with burning anger and dense smoke. His lips are full of fury, and His tongue is like a consuming fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.28', 'BSB', 'His breath is like a rushing torrent that rises to the neck. He comes to sift the nations in a sieve of destruction; He bridles the jaws of the peoples to lead them astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.29', 'BSB', 'You will sing as on the night of a holy festival, and your heart will rejoice like one who walks to the music of a flute, going up to the mountain of the LORD, to the Rock of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.30', 'BSB', 'And the LORD will cause His majestic voice to be heard and His mighty arm to be revealed, striking in angry wrath with a flame of consuming fire, and with cloudburst, storm, and hailstones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.31', 'BSB', 'For Assyria will be shattered at the voice of the LORD; He will strike them with His scepter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.32', 'BSB', 'And with every stroke of the rod of punishment that the LORD brings down on them, the tambourines and lyres will sound as He battles with weapons brandished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.30.33', 'BSB', 'For Topheth has long been prepared; it has been made ready for the king. Its funeral pyre is deep and wide, with plenty of fire and wood. The breath of the LORD, like a torrent of burning sulfur, sets it ablaze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who go down to Egypt for help, who rely on horses, who trust in their abundance of chariots and in their multitude of horsemen. They do not look to the Holy One of Israel; they do not seek the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.2', 'BSB', 'Yet He too is wise and brings disaster; He does not call back His words. He will rise up against the house of the wicked and against the allies of evildoers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.3', 'BSB', 'But the Egyptians are men, not God; their horses are flesh, not spirit. When the LORD stretches out His hand, the helper will stumble, and the one he helps will fall; both will perish together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD has said to me: “Like a lion roaring or a young lion over its prey— and though a band of shepherds is called out against it, it is not terrified by their shouting or subdued by their clamor— so the LORD of Hosts will come down to do battle on Mount Zion and its heights.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.5', 'BSB', 'Like birds hovering overhead, so the LORD of Hosts will protect Jerusalem. He will shield it and deliver it; He will pass over it and preserve it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.6', 'BSB', 'Return to the One against whom you have so blatantly rebelled, O children of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.7', 'BSB', 'For on that day, every one of you will reject the idols of silver and gold that your own hands have sinfully made.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.8', 'BSB', '“Then Assyria will fall, but not by the sword of man; a sword will devour them, but not one made by mortals. They will flee before the sword, and their young men will be put to forced labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.31.9', 'BSB', 'Their rock will pass away for fear, and their princes will panic at the sight of the battle standard,” declares the LORD, whose fire is in Zion, whose furnace is in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.1', 'BSB', 'Behold, a king will reign in righteousness, and princes will rule with justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.2', 'BSB', 'Each will be like a shelter from the wind, a refuge from the storm, like streams of water in a dry land, like the shadow of a great rock in an arid land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.3', 'BSB', 'Then the eyes of those who see will no longer be closed, and the ears of those who hear will listen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.4', 'BSB', 'The mind of the rash will know and understand, and the stammering tongue will speak clearly and fluently.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.5', 'BSB', 'No longer will a fool be called noble, nor a scoundrel be respected.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.6', 'BSB', 'For a fool speaks foolishness; his mind plots iniquity. He practices ungodliness and speaks falsely about the LORD; he leaves the hungry empty and deprives the thirsty of drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.7', 'BSB', 'The weapons of the scoundrel are destructive; he hatches plots to destroy the poor with lies, even when the plea of the needy is just.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.8', 'BSB', 'But a noble man makes honorable plans; he stands up for worthy causes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.9', 'BSB', 'Stand up, you complacent women; listen to me. Give ear to my word, you overconfident daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.10', 'BSB', 'In a little more than a year you will tremble, O secure ones. For the grape harvest will fail and the fruit harvest will not arrive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.11', 'BSB', 'Shudder, you ladies of leisure; tremble, you daughters of complacency. Strip yourselves bare and put sackcloth around your waists.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.12', 'BSB', 'Beat your breasts for the pleasant fields, for the fruitful vines,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.13', 'BSB', 'and for the land of my people, overgrown with thorns and briers— even for every house of merriment in this city of revelry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.14', 'BSB', 'For the palace will be forsaken, the busy city abandoned. The hill and the watchtower will become caves forever— the delight of wild donkeys and a pasture for flocks—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.15', 'BSB', 'until the Spirit is poured out upon us from on high. Then the desert will be an orchard, and the orchard will seem like a forest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.16', 'BSB', 'Then justice will inhabit the wilderness, and righteousness will dwell in the fertile field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.17', 'BSB', 'The work of righteousness will be peace; the service of righteousness will be quiet confidence forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.18', 'BSB', 'Then my people will dwell in a peaceful place, in safe and secure places of rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.19', 'BSB', 'But hail will level the forest, and the city will sink to the depths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.32.20', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who sow beside abundant waters, who let the ox and donkey range freely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, O destroyer never destroyed, O traitor never betrayed! When you have finished destroying, you will be destroyed. When you have finished betraying, you will be betrayed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.2', 'BSB', 'O LORD, be gracious to us! We wait for You. Be our strength every morning and our salvation in time of trouble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.3', 'BSB', 'The peoples flee the thunder of Your voice; the nations scatter when You rise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.4', 'BSB', 'Your spoil, O nations, is gathered as by locusts; like a swarm of locusts men sweep over it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD is exalted, for He dwells on high; He has filled Zion with justice and righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.6', 'BSB', 'He will be the sure foundation for your times, a storehouse of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge. The fear of the LORD is Zion’s treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, their valiant ones cry aloud in the streets; the envoys of peace weep bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.8', 'BSB', 'The highways are deserted; travel has ceased. The treaty has been broken, the witnesses are despised, and human life is disregarded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.9', 'BSB', 'The land mourns and languishes; Lebanon is ashamed and decayed. Sharon is like a desert; Bashan and Carmel shake off their leaves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.10', 'BSB', '“Now I will arise,” says the LORD. “Now I will lift Myself up. Now I will be exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.11', 'BSB', 'You conceive chaff; you give birth to stubble. Your breath is a fire that will consume you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.12', 'BSB', 'The peoples will be burned to ashes, like thorns cut down and set ablaze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.13', 'BSB', 'You who are far off, hear what I have done; you who are near, acknowledge My might.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.14', 'BSB', 'The sinners in Zion are afraid; trembling grips the ungodly: “Who of us can dwell with a consuming fire? Who of us can dwell with everlasting flames?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.15', 'BSB', 'He who walks righteously and speaks with sincerity, who refuses gain from extortion, whose hand never takes a bribe, who stops his ears against murderous plots and shuts his eyes tightly against evil—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.16', 'BSB', 'he will dwell on the heights; the mountain fortress will be his refuge; his food will be provided and his water assured.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.17', 'BSB', 'Your eyes will see the King in His beauty and behold a land that stretches afar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.18', 'BSB', 'Your mind will ponder the former terror: “Where is he who tallies? Where is he who weighs? Where is he who counts the towers?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.19', 'BSB', 'You will no longer see the insolent, a people whose speech is unintelligible, who stammer in a language you cannot understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.20', 'BSB', 'Look upon Zion, the city of our appointed feasts. Your eyes will see Jerusalem, a peaceful pasture, a tent that does not wander; its tent pegs will not be pulled up, nor will any of its cords be broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.21', 'BSB', 'But there the Majestic One, our LORD, will be for us a place of rivers and wide canals, where no galley with oars will row, and no majestic vessel will pass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.22', 'BSB', 'For the LORD is our Judge, the LORD is our lawgiver, the LORD is our King. It is He who will save us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.23', 'BSB', 'Your ropes are slack; they cannot secure the mast or spread the sail. Then an abundance of spoils will be divided, and even the lame will carry off plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.33.24', 'BSB', 'And no resident of Zion will say, “I am sick.” The people who dwell there will be forgiven of iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.1', 'BSB', 'Come near, O nations, to listen; pay attention, O peoples. Let the earth hear, and all that fills it, the world and all that springs from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD is angry with all the nations and furious with all their armies. He will devote them to destruction; He will give them over to slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.3', 'BSB', 'Their slain will be left unburied, and the stench of their corpses will rise; the mountains will flow with their blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.4', 'BSB', 'All the stars of heaven will be dissolved. The skies will be rolled up like a scroll, and all their stars will fall like withered leaves from the vine, like foliage from the fig tree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.5', 'BSB', 'When My sword has drunk its fill in the heavens, then it will come down upon Edom, upon the people I have devoted to destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.6', 'BSB', 'The sword of the LORD is bathed in blood. It drips with fat— with the blood of lambs and goats, with the fat of the kidneys of rams. For the LORD has a sacrifice in Bozrah, a great slaughter in the land of Edom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.7', 'BSB', 'And the wild oxen will fall with them, the young bulls with the strong ones. Their land will be drenched with blood, and their soil will be soaked with fat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.8', 'BSB', 'For the LORD has a day of vengeance, a year of recompense for the cause of Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.9', 'BSB', 'Edom’s streams will be turned to tar, and her soil to sulfur; her land will become a blazing pitch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.10', 'BSB', 'It will not be quenched—day or night. Its smoke will ascend forever. From generation to generation it will lie desolate; no one will ever again pass through it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.11', 'BSB', 'The desert owl and screech owl will possess it, and the great owl and raven will dwell in it. The LORD will stretch out over Edom a measuring line of chaos and a plumb line of destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.12', 'BSB', 'No nobles will be left to proclaim a king, and all her princes will come to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.13', 'BSB', 'Her towers will be overgrown with thorns, her fortresses with thistles and briers. She will become a haunt for jackals, an abode for ostriches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.14', 'BSB', 'The desert creatures will meet with hyenas, and one wild goat will call to another. There the night creature will settle and find her place of repose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.15', 'BSB', 'There the owl will make her nest; she will lay and hatch her eggs and gather her brood under her shadow. Even there the birds of prey will gather, each with its mate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.16', 'BSB', 'Search and read the scroll of the LORD: Not one of these will go missing, not one will lack her mate, because He has ordered it by His mouth, and He will gather them by His Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.34.17', 'BSB', 'He has allotted their portion; His hand has distributed it by measure. They will possess it forever; they will dwell in it from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.1', 'BSB', 'The wilderness and the land will be glad; the desert will rejoice and blossom like a rose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.2', 'BSB', 'It will bloom profusely and rejoice with joy and singing. The glory of Lebanon will be given to it, the splendor of Carmel and Sharon. They will see the glory of the LORD, the splendor of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.3', 'BSB', 'Strengthen the limp hands and steady the feeble knees!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.4', 'BSB', 'Say to those with anxious hearts: “Be strong, do not fear! Behold, your God will come with vengeance. With divine retribution He will come to save you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.5', 'BSB', 'Then the eyes of the blind will be opened and the ears of the deaf unstopped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.6', 'BSB', 'Then the lame will leap like a deer and the mute tongue will shout for joy. For waters will gush forth in the wilderness, and streams in the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.7', 'BSB', 'The parched ground will become a pool, the thirsty land springs of water. In the haunt where jackals once lay, there will be grass and reeds and papyrus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.8', 'BSB', 'And there will be a highway called the Way of Holiness. The unclean will not travel it— only those who walk in the Way— and fools will not stray onto it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.9', 'BSB', 'No lion will be there, and no vicious beast will go up on it. Such will not be found there, but the redeemed will walk upon it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.35.10', 'BSB', 'So the redeemed of the LORD will return and enter Zion with singing, crowned with everlasting joy. Gladness and joy will overtake them, and sorrow and sighing will flee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.1', 'BSB', 'In the fourteenth year of Hezekiah’s reign, Sennacherib king of Assyria attacked and captured all the fortified cities of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.2', 'BSB', 'And the king of Assyria sent the Rabshakeh, with a great army, from Lachish to King Hezekiah at Jerusalem. And he stopped by the aqueduct of the upper pool, on the road to the Launderer’s Field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.3', 'BSB', 'Then Eliakim son of Hilkiah the palace administrator, Shebna the scribe, and Joah son of Asaph the recorder, went out to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.4', 'BSB', 'The Rabshakeh said to them, “Tell Hezekiah that this is what the great king, the king of Assyria, says: What is the basis of this confidence of yours?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.5', 'BSB', 'You claim to have a strategy and strength for war, but these are empty words. In whom are you now trusting, that you have rebelled against me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.6', 'BSB', 'Look now, you are trusting in Egypt, that splintered reed of a staff that will pierce the hand of anyone who leans on it. Such is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.7', 'BSB', 'But if you say to me, ‘We trust in the LORD our God,’ is He not the One whose high places and altars Hezekiah has removed, saying to Judah and Jerusalem, ‘You must worship before this altar’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.8', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, make a bargain with my master, the king of Assyria. I will give you two thousand horses—if you can put riders on them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.9', 'BSB', 'For how can you repel a single officer among the least of my master’s servants when you depend on Egypt for chariots and horsemen?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.10', 'BSB', 'So now, was it apart from the LORD that I have come up against this land to destroy it? The LORD Himself said to me, ‘Go up against this land and destroy it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.11', 'BSB', 'Then Eliakim, Shebna, and Joah said to the Rabshakeh, “Please speak to your servants in Aramaic, since we understand it. Do not speak to us in Hebrew in the hearing of the people on the wall.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.12', 'BSB', 'But the Rabshakeh replied, “Has my master sent me to speak these words only to you and your master, and not to the men sitting on the wall, who are destined with you to eat their own dung and drink their own urine?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.13', 'BSB', 'Then the Rabshakeh stood and called out loudly in Hebrew: “Hear the words of the great king, the king of Assyria!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.14', 'BSB', 'This is what the king says: Do not let Hezekiah deceive you, for he cannot deliver you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.15', 'BSB', 'Do not let Hezekiah persuade you to trust in the LORD when he says, ‘The LORD will surely deliver us; this city will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.16', 'BSB', 'Do not listen to Hezekiah, for this is what the king of Assyria says: Make peace with me and come out to me. Then every one of you will eat from his own vine and his own fig tree, and drink water from his own cistern,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.17', 'BSB', 'until I come and take you away to a land like your own—a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.18', 'BSB', 'Do not let Hezekiah mislead you when he says, ‘The LORD will deliver us.’ Has the god of any nation ever delivered his land from the hand of the king of Assyria?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.19', 'BSB', 'Where are the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim? Have they delivered Samaria from my hand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.20', 'BSB', 'Who among all the gods of these lands has delivered his land from my hand? How then can the LORD deliver Jerusalem from my hand?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.21', 'BSB', 'But the people remained silent and did not answer a word, for Hezekiah had commanded, “Do not answer him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.36.22', 'BSB', 'Then Hilkiah’s son Eliakim the palace administrator, Shebna the scribe, and Asaph’s son Joah the recorder came to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and they relayed to him the words of the Rabshakeh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.1', 'BSB', 'On hearing this report, King Hezekiah tore his clothes, put on sackcloth, and entered the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.2', 'BSB', 'And he sent Eliakim the palace administrator, Shebna the scribe, and the leading priests, all wearing sackcloth, to the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.3', 'BSB', 'to tell him, “This is what Hezekiah says: Today is a day of distress, rebuke, and disgrace; for children have come to the point of birth, but there is no strength to deliver them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.4', 'BSB', 'Perhaps the LORD your God will hear the words of the Rabshakeh, whom his master the king of Assyria has sent to defy the living God, and He will rebuke him for the words that the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up a prayer for the remnant that still survives.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.5', 'BSB', 'So the servants of King Hezekiah went to Isaiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.6', 'BSB', 'who replied, “Tell your master that this is what the LORD says: ‘Do not be afraid of the words you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will put a spirit in him so that he will hear a rumor and return to his own land, where I will cause him to fall by the sword.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.8', 'BSB', 'When the Rabshakeh heard that the king of Assyria had left Lachish, he withdrew and found the king fighting against Libnah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.9', 'BSB', 'Now Sennacherib had been warned about Tirhakah king of Cush: “He has set out to fight against you.” On hearing this, Sennacherib sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.10', 'BSB', '“Give this message to Hezekiah king of Judah: ‘Do not let your God, in whom you trust, deceive you by saying that Jerusalem will not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.11', 'BSB', 'Surely you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all the other countries, devoting them to destruction. Will you then be spared?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.12', 'BSB', 'Did the gods of the nations destroyed by my fathers rescue those nations—the gods of Gozan, Haran, and Rezeph, and of the people of Eden in Telassar?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.13', 'BSB', 'Where are the kings of Hamath, Arpad, Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivvah?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.14', 'BSB', 'So Hezekiah received the letter from the messengers, read it, and went up to the house of the LORD and spread it out before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.15', 'BSB', 'And Hezekiah prayed to the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.16', 'BSB', '“O LORD of Hosts, God of Israel, enthroned above the cherubim, You alone are God over all the kingdoms of the earth. You made the heavens and the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.17', 'BSB', 'Incline Your ear, O LORD, and hear; open Your eyes, O LORD, and see. Listen to all the words that Sennacherib has sent to defy the living God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.18', 'BSB', 'Truly, O LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste all these countries and their lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.19', 'BSB', 'They have cast their gods into the fire and destroyed them, for they were not gods, but only wood and stone—the work of human hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.20', 'BSB', 'And now, O LORD our God, save us from his hand, so that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that You alone, O LORD, are God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.21', 'BSB', 'Then Isaiah son of Amoz sent a message to Hezekiah: “This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: Because you have prayed to Me concerning Sennacherib king of Assyria,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.22', 'BSB', 'this is the word that the LORD has spoken against him: ‘The Virgin Daughter of Zion despises you and mocks you; the Daughter of Jerusalem shakes her head behind you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.23', 'BSB', 'Whom have you taunted and blasphemed? Against whom have you raised your voice and lifted your eyes in pride? Against the Holy One of Israel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.24', 'BSB', 'Through your servants you have taunted the Lord, and you have said: “With my many chariots I have ascended to the heights of the mountains, to the remote peaks of Lebanon. I have cut down its tallest cedars, the finest of its cypresses. I have reached its farthest heights, the densest of its forests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.25', 'BSB', 'I have dug wells and drunk foreign waters. With the soles of my feet I have dried up all the streams of Egypt.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.26', 'BSB', 'Have you not heard? Long ago I ordained it; in days of old I planned it. Now I have brought it to pass, that you should crush fortified cities into piles of rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore their inhabitants, devoid of power, are dismayed and ashamed. They are like plants in the field, tender green shoots, grass on the rooftops, scorched before it is grown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.28', 'BSB', 'But I know your sitting down, your going out and coming in, and your raging against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.29', 'BSB', 'Because your rage and arrogance against Me have reached My ears, I will put My hook in your nose and My bit in your mouth; I will send you back the way you came.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.30', 'BSB', 'And this will be a sign to you, O Hezekiah: This year you will eat what grows on its own, and in the second year what springs from the same. But in the third year you will sow and reap; you will plant vineyards and eat their fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.31', 'BSB', 'And the surviving remnant of the house of Judah will again take root below and bear fruit above.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.32', 'BSB', 'For a remnant will go forth from Jerusalem, and survivors from Mount Zion. The zeal of the LORD of Hosts will accomplish this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.33', 'BSB', 'So this is what the LORD says about the king of Assyria: ‘He will not enter this city or shoot an arrow into it. He will not come before it with a shield or build up a siege ramp against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.34', 'BSB', 'He will go back the way he came, and he will not enter this city,’ declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.35', 'BSB', '‘I will defend this city and save it for My own sake and for the sake of My servant David.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.36', 'BSB', 'Then the angel of the LORD went out and struck down 185,000 men in the camp of the Assyrians. When the people got up the next morning, there were all the dead bodies!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.37', 'BSB', 'So Sennacherib king of Assyria broke camp and withdrew. He returned to Nineveh and stayed there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.37.38', 'BSB', 'One day, while he was worshiping in the temple of his god Nisroch, his sons Adrammelech and Sharezer put him to the sword and escaped to the land of Ararat. And his son Esar-haddon reigned in his place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.1', 'BSB', 'In those days Hezekiah became mortally ill. The prophet Isaiah son of Amoz came to him and said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Put your house in order, for you are about to die; you will not recover.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.2', 'BSB', 'Then Hezekiah turned his face to the wall and prayed to the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.3', 'BSB', 'saying, “Please, O LORD, remember how I have walked before You faithfully and with wholehearted devotion; I have done what was good in Your sight.” And Hezekiah wept bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.4', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to Isaiah, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.5', 'BSB', '“Go and tell Hezekiah that this is what the LORD, the God of your father David, says: ‘I have heard your prayer; I have seen your tears. Behold, I will add fifteen years to your life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.6', 'BSB', 'And I will deliver you and this city from the hand of the king of Assyria. I will defend this city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.7', 'BSB', 'This will be a sign to you from the LORD that He will do what He has promised:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.8', 'BSB', 'I will make the sun’s shadow that falls on the stairway of Ahaz go back ten steps.’” So the sunlight went back the ten steps it had descended.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.9', 'BSB', 'This is a writing by Hezekiah king of Judah after his illness and recovery:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.10', 'BSB', 'I said, “In the prime of my life I must go through the gates of Sheol and be deprived of the remainder of my years.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.11', 'BSB', 'I said, “I will never again see the LORD, even the LORD, in the land of the living; I will no longer look on mankind with those who dwell in this world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.12', 'BSB', 'My dwelling has been picked up and removed from me like a shepherd’s tent. I have rolled up my life like a weaver; He cuts me off from the loom; from day until night You make an end of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.13', 'BSB', 'I composed myself until the morning. Like a lion He breaks all my bones; from day until night You make an end of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.14', 'BSB', 'I chirp like a swallow or crane; I moan like a dove. My eyes grow weak as I look upward. O Lord, I am oppressed; be my security.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.15', 'BSB', 'What can I say? He has spoken to me, and He Himself has done this. I will walk slowly all my years because of the anguish of my soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.16', 'BSB', 'O Lord, by such things men live, and in all of them my spirit finds life. You have restored me to health and have let me live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.17', 'BSB', 'Surely for my own welfare I had such great anguish; but Your love has delivered me from the pit of oblivion, for You have cast all my sins behind Your back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.18', 'BSB', 'For Sheol cannot thank You; Death cannot praise You. Those who descend to the Pit cannot hope for Your faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.19', 'BSB', 'The living, only the living, can thank You, as I do today; fathers will tell their children about Your faithfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.20', 'BSB', 'The LORD will save me; we will play songs on stringed instruments all the days of our lives in the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.21', 'BSB', 'Now Isaiah had said, “Prepare a lump of pressed figs and apply it to the boil, and he will recover.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.38.22', 'BSB', 'And Hezekiah had asked, “What will be the sign that I will go up to the house of the LORD?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.1', 'BSB', 'At that time Merodach-baladan son of Baladan king of Babylon sent letters and a gift to Hezekiah, for he had heard about Hezekiah’s illness and recovery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.2', 'BSB', 'And Hezekiah welcomed the envoys gladly and showed them what was in his treasure house—the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, as well as his entire armory—all that was found in his storehouses. There was nothing in his palace or in all his dominion that Hezekiah did not show them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.3', 'BSB', 'Then the prophet Isaiah went to King Hezekiah and asked, “Where did those men come from, and what did they say to you?” “They came to me from a distant land,” Hezekiah replied, “from Babylon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.4', 'BSB', '“What have they seen in your palace?” Isaiah asked. “They have seen everything in my palace,” answered Hezekiah. “There is nothing among my treasures that I did not show them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.5', 'BSB', 'Then Isaiah said to Hezekiah, “Hear the word of the LORD of Hosts:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.6', 'BSB', 'The time will surely come when everything in your palace and all that your fathers have stored up until this day will be carried off to Babylon. Nothing will be left, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.7', 'BSB', 'And some of your descendants, your own flesh and blood, will be taken away to be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.39.8', 'BSB', 'But Hezekiah said to Isaiah, “The word of the LORD that you have spoken is good.” For he thought, “At least there will be peace and security in my lifetime.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.1', 'BSB', '“Comfort, comfort My people,” says your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.2', 'BSB', '“Speak tenderly to Jerusalem, and proclaim to her that her forced labor has been completed; her iniquity has been pardoned. For she has received from the hand of the LORD double for all her sins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.3', 'BSB', 'A voice of one calling: “Prepare the way for the LORD in the wilderness; make a straight highway for our God in the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.4', 'BSB', 'Every valley shall be lifted up, and every mountain and hill made low; the uneven ground will become smooth, and the rugged land a plain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.5', 'BSB', 'And the glory of the LORD will be revealed, and all humanity together will see it. For the mouth of the LORD has spoken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.6', 'BSB', 'A voice says, “Cry out!” And I asked, “What should I cry out?” “All flesh is like grass, and all its glory like the flowers of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.7', 'BSB', 'The grass withers and the flowers fall when the breath of the LORD blows on them; indeed, the people are grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.8', 'BSB', 'The grass withers and the flowers fall, but the word of our God stands forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.9', 'BSB', 'Go up on a high mountain, O Zion, herald of good news. Raise your voice loudly, O Jerusalem, herald of good news. Lift it up, do not be afraid! Say to the cities of Judah, “Here is your God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.10', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Lord GOD comes with might, and His arm establishes His rule. His reward is with Him, and His recompense accompanies Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.11', 'BSB', 'He tends His flock like a shepherd; He gathers the lambs in His arms and carries them close to His heart. He gently leads the nursing ewes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.12', 'BSB', 'Who has measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, or marked off the heavens with the span of his hand? Who has held the dust of the earth in a basket, or weighed the mountains on a scale and the hills with a balance?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.13', 'BSB', 'Who has directed the Spirit of the LORD, or informed Him as His counselor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.14', 'BSB', 'Whom did He consult to enlighten Him, and who taught Him the paths of justice? Who imparted knowledge to Him and showed Him the way of understanding?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.15', 'BSB', 'Surely the nations are like a drop in a bucket; they are considered a speck of dust on the scales; He lifts up the islands like fine dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.16', 'BSB', 'Lebanon is not sufficient for fuel, nor its animals enough for a burnt offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.17', 'BSB', 'All the nations are as nothing before Him; He regards them as nothingness and emptiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.18', 'BSB', 'To whom will you liken God? To what image will you compare Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.19', 'BSB', 'To an idol that a craftsman casts and a metalworker overlays with gold and fits with silver chains?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.20', 'BSB', 'To one bereft of an offering who chooses wood that will not rot, who seeks a skilled craftsman to set up an idol that will not topple?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.21', 'BSB', 'Do you not know? Have you not heard? Has it not been declared to you from the beginning? Have you not understood since the foundation of the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.22', 'BSB', 'He sits enthroned above the circle of the earth; its dwellers are like grasshoppers. He stretches out the heavens like a curtain, and spreads them out like a tent to dwell in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.23', 'BSB', 'He brings the princes to nothing and makes the rulers of the earth meaningless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.24', 'BSB', 'No sooner are they planted, no sooner are they sown, no sooner have their stems taken root in the ground, than He blows on them and they wither, and a whirlwind sweeps them away like stubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.25', 'BSB', '“To whom will you liken Me, or who is My equal?” asks the Holy One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.26', 'BSB', 'Lift up your eyes on high: Who created all these? He leads forth the starry host by number; He calls each one by name. Because of His great power and mighty strength, not one of them is missing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.27', 'BSB', 'Why do you say, O Jacob, and why do you assert, O Israel, “My way is hidden from the LORD, and my claim is ignored by my God”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.28', 'BSB', 'Do you not know? Have you not heard? The LORD is the everlasting God, the Creator of the ends of the earth. He will not grow tired or weary; His understanding is beyond searching out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.29', 'BSB', 'He gives power to the faint and increases the strength of the weak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.30', 'BSB', 'Even youths grow tired and weary, and young men stumble and fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.40.31', 'BSB', 'But those who wait upon the LORD will renew their strength; they will mount up with wings like eagles; they will run and not grow weary, they will walk and not faint.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.1', 'BSB', '“Be silent before Me, O islands, and let the peoples renew their strength. Let them come forward and testify; let us together draw near for judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.2', 'BSB', 'Who has aroused one from the east and called him to his feet in righteousness? He hands nations over to him and subdues kings before him. He turns them to dust with his sword, to windblown chaff with his bow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.3', 'BSB', 'He pursues them, going on safely, hardly touching the path with his feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.4', 'BSB', 'Who has performed this and carried it out, calling forth the generations from the beginning? I, the LORD—the first and the last— I am He.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.5', 'BSB', 'The islands see and fear; the ends of the earth tremble. They approach and come forward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.6', 'BSB', 'Each one helps the other and says to his brother, “Be strong!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.7', 'BSB', 'The craftsman encourages the goldsmith, and he who wields the hammer cheers him who strikes the anvil, saying of the welding, “It is good.” He nails it down so it will not be toppled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.8', 'BSB', '“But you, O Israel, My servant, Jacob, whom I have chosen, descendant of Abraham My friend—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.9', 'BSB', 'I brought you from the ends of the earth and called you from its farthest corners. I said, ‘You are My servant.’ I have chosen and not rejected you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.10', 'BSB', 'Do not fear, for I am with you; do not be afraid, for I am your God. I will strengthen you; I will surely help you; I will uphold you with My right hand of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.11', 'BSB', 'Behold, all who rage against you will be ashamed and disgraced; those who contend with you will be reduced to nothing and will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.12', 'BSB', 'You will seek them but will not find them. Those who wage war against you will come to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.13', 'BSB', 'For I am the LORD your God, who takes hold of your right hand and tells you: Do not fear, I will help you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.14', 'BSB', 'Do not fear, O worm of Jacob, O few men of Israel. I will help you,” declares the LORD. “Your Redeemer is the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.15', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will make you into a threshing sledge, new and sharp, with many teeth. You will thresh the mountains and crush them, and reduce the hills to chaff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.16', 'BSB', 'You will winnow them, and a wind will carry them away; a gale will scatter them. But you will rejoice in the LORD; you will glory in the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.17', 'BSB', 'The poor and needy seek water, but there is none; their tongues are parched with thirst. I, the LORD, will answer them; I, the God of Israel, will not forsake them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.18', 'BSB', 'I will open rivers on the barren heights, and fountains in the middle of the valleys. I will turn the desert into a pool of water, and the dry land into flowing springs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.19', 'BSB', 'I will plant cedars in the wilderness, acacias, myrtles, and olive trees. I will set cypresses in the desert, elms and boxwood together,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.20', 'BSB', 'so that all may see and know, may consider and understand, that the hand of the LORD has done this and the Holy One of Israel has created it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.21', 'BSB', '“Present your case,” says the LORD. “Submit your arguments,” says the King of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.22', 'BSB', '“Let them come and tell us what will happen. Tell the former things, so that we may reflect on them and know the outcome. Or announce to us what is coming.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.23', 'BSB', 'Tell us the things that are to come, so that we may know that you are gods. Yes, do something good or evil, that we may look on together in dismay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.24', 'BSB', 'Behold, you are nothing and your work is of no value. Anyone who chooses you is detestable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.25', 'BSB', 'I have raised up one from the north, and he has come— one from the east who calls on My name. He will march over rulers as if they were mortar, like a potter who treads the clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.26', 'BSB', 'Who has declared this from the beginning, so that we may know, and from times past, so that we may say: ‘He was right’? No one announced it, no one foretold it, no one heard your words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.27', 'BSB', 'I was the first to tell Zion: ‘Look, here they are!’ And I gave to Jerusalem a herald of good news.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.28', 'BSB', 'When I look, there is no one; there is no counselor among them; when I ask them, they have nothing to say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.41.29', 'BSB', 'See, they are all a delusion; their works amount to nothing; their images are as empty as the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.1', 'BSB', '“Here is My Servant, whom I uphold, My Chosen One, in whom My soul delights. I will put My Spirit on Him, and He will bring justice to the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.2', 'BSB', 'He will not cry out or raise His voice, nor make His voice heard in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.3', 'BSB', 'A bruised reed He will not break and a smoldering wick He will not extinguish; He will faithfully bring forth justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.4', 'BSB', 'He will not grow weak or discouraged before He has established justice on the earth. In His law the islands will put their hope.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.5', 'BSB', 'This is what God the LORD says— He who created the heavens and stretched them out, who spread out the earth and its offspring, who gives breath to the people on it and life to those who walk in it:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.6', 'BSB', '“I, the LORD, have called you for a righteous purpose, and I will take hold of your hand. I will keep you and appoint you to be a covenant for the people and a light to the nations,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.7', 'BSB', 'to open the eyes of the blind, to bring prisoners out of the dungeon and those sitting in darkness out from the prison house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.8', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD; that is My name! I will not yield My glory to another or My praise to idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.9', 'BSB', 'Behold, the former things have happened, and now I declare new things. Before they spring forth I proclaim them to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.10', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD a new song— His praise from the ends of the earth— you who go down to the sea, and all that is in it, you islands, and all who dwell in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.11', 'BSB', 'Let the desert and its cities raise their voices; let the villages of Kedar cry aloud. Let the people of Sela sing for joy; let them cry out from the mountaintops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.12', 'BSB', 'Let them give glory to the LORD and declare His praise in the islands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.13', 'BSB', 'The LORD goes forth like a mighty one; He stirs up His zeal like a warrior. He shouts; yes, He roars in triumph over His enemies:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.14', 'BSB', '“I have kept silent from ages past; I have remained quiet and restrained. But now I will groan like a woman in labor; I will at once gasp and pant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.15', 'BSB', 'I will lay waste the mountains and hills and dry up all their vegetation. I will turn the rivers into dry land and drain the marshes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.16', 'BSB', 'I will lead the blind by a way they did not know; I will guide them on unfamiliar paths. I will turn darkness into light before them and rough places into level ground. These things I will do for them, and I will not forsake them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.17', 'BSB', 'But those who trust in idols and say to molten images, ‘You are our gods!’ will be turned back in utter shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.18', 'BSB', 'Listen, you deaf ones; look, you blind ones, that you may see!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.19', 'BSB', 'Who is blind but My servant, or deaf like the messenger I am sending? Who is blind like My covenant partner, or blind like the servant of the LORD?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.20', 'BSB', 'Though seeing many things, you do not keep watch. Though your ears are open, you do not hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.21', 'BSB', 'The LORD was pleased, for the sake of His righteousness, to magnify His law and make it glorious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.22', 'BSB', 'But this is a people plundered and looted, all trapped in caves or imprisoned in dungeons. They have become plunder with no one to rescue them, and loot with no one to say, “Send them back!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.23', 'BSB', 'Who among you will pay attention to this? Who will listen and obey hereafter?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.24', 'BSB', 'Who gave Jacob up for spoil, and Israel to the plunderers? Was it not the LORD, against whom we have sinned? They were unwilling to walk in His ways, and they would not obey His law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.42.25', 'BSB', 'So He poured out on them His furious anger and the fierceness of battle. It enveloped them in flames, but they did not understand; it consumed them, but they did not take it to heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.1', 'BSB', 'Now this is what the LORD says— He who created you, O Jacob, and He who formed you, O Israel: “Do not fear, for I have redeemed you; I have called you by your name; you are Mine!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.2', 'BSB', 'When you pass through the waters, I will be with you; and when you go through the rivers, they will not overwhelm you. When you walk through the fire, you will not be scorched; the flames will not set you ablaze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.3', 'BSB', 'For I am the LORD your God, the Holy One of Israel, your Savior; I give Egypt for your ransom, Cush and Seba in your place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.4', 'BSB', 'Because you are precious and honored in My sight, and because I love you, I will give men in exchange for you and nations in place of your life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.5', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid, for I am with you; I will bring your offspring from the east and gather you from the west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.6', 'BSB', 'I will say to the north, ‘Give them up!’ and to the south, ‘Do not hold them back!’ Bring My sons from afar, and My daughters from the ends of the earth—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.7', 'BSB', 'everyone called by My name and created for My glory, whom I have indeed formed and made.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.8', 'BSB', 'Bring out a people who have eyes but are blind, and who have ears but are deaf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.9', 'BSB', 'All the nations gather together and the peoples assemble. Who among them can declare this, and proclaim to us the former things? Let them present their witnesses to vindicate them, so that others may hear and say, “It is true.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.10', 'BSB', '“You are My witnesses,” declares the LORD, “and My servant whom I have chosen, so that you may consider and believe Me and understand that I am He. Before Me no god was formed, and after Me none will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.11', 'BSB', 'I, yes I, am the LORD, and there is no Savior but Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.12', 'BSB', 'I alone decreed and saved and proclaimed— I, and not some foreign god among you. So you are My witnesses,” declares the LORD, “that I am God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.13', 'BSB', 'Even from eternity I am He, and none can deliver out of My hand. When I act, who can reverse it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.14', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel: “For your sake, I will send to Babylon and bring them all as fugitives, even the Chaldeans, in the ships in which they rejoice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.15', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD, your Holy One, the Creator of Israel, and your King.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.16', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, who makes a way in the sea and a path through the surging waters,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.17', 'BSB', 'who brings out the chariots and horses, the armies and warriors together, to lie down, never to rise again; to be extinguished, snuffed out like a wick:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.18', 'BSB', '“Do not call to mind the former things; pay no attention to the things of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am about to do something new; even now it is coming. Do you not see it? Indeed, I will make a way in the wilderness and streams in the desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.20', 'BSB', 'The beasts of the field will honor Me, the jackals and the ostriches, because I provide water in the wilderness and rivers in the desert, to give drink to My chosen people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.21', 'BSB', 'The people I formed for Myself will declare My praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.22', 'BSB', 'But you have not called on Me, O Jacob, because you have grown weary of Me, O Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.23', 'BSB', 'You have not brought Me sheep for burnt offerings, nor honored Me with your sacrifices. I have not burdened you with offerings, nor wearied you with frankincense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.24', 'BSB', 'You have not bought Me sweet cane with your silver, nor satisfied Me with the fat of your sacrifices. But you have burdened Me with your sins; you have wearied Me with your iniquities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.25', 'BSB', 'I, yes I, am He who blots out your transgressions for My own sake and remembers your sins no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.26', 'BSB', 'Remind Me, let us argue the matter together. State your case, so that you may be vindicated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.27', 'BSB', 'Your first father sinned, and your spokesmen rebelled against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.43.28', 'BSB', 'So I will disgrace the princes of your sanctuary, and I will devote Jacob to destruction and Israel to reproach.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.1', 'BSB', 'But now listen, O Jacob My servant, Israel, whom I have chosen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.2', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD, your Maker, who formed you from the womb and who will help you: “Do not be afraid, O Jacob My servant, Jeshurun, whom I have chosen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.3', 'BSB', 'For I will pour water on the thirsty land, and currents on the dry ground. I will pour out My Spirit on your descendants, and My blessing on your offspring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.4', 'BSB', 'They will sprout among the grass like willows by flowing streams.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.5', 'BSB', 'One will say, ‘I belong to the LORD,’ another will call himself by the name of Jacob, and still another will write on his hand, ‘The LORD’s,’ and will take the name of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.6', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, the King and Redeemer of Israel, the LORD of Hosts: “I am the first and I am the last, and there is no God but Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.7', 'BSB', 'Who then is like Me? Let him say so! Let him declare his case before Me, since I established an ancient people. Let him foretell the things to come, and what is to take place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.8', 'BSB', 'Do not tremble or fear. Have I not told you and declared it long ago? You are My witnesses! Is there any God but Me? There is no other Rock; I know not one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.9', 'BSB', 'All makers of idols are nothing, and the things they treasure are worthless. Their witnesses fail to see or comprehend, so they are put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.10', 'BSB', 'Who fashions a god or casts an idol which profits him nothing?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.11', 'BSB', 'Behold, all his companions will be put to shame, for the craftsmen themselves are only human. Let them all assemble and take their stand; they will all be brought to terror and shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.12', 'BSB', 'The blacksmith takes a tool and labors over the coals; he fashions an idol with hammers and forges it with his strong arms. Yet he grows hungry and loses his strength; he fails to drink water and grows faint.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.13', 'BSB', 'The woodworker extends a measuring line; he marks it out with a stylus; he shapes it with chisels and outlines it with a compass. He fashions it in the likeness of man, like man in all his glory, that it may dwell in a shrine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.14', 'BSB', 'He cuts down cedars or retrieves a cypress or oak. He lets it grow strong among the trees of the forest. He plants a laurel, and the rain makes it grow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.15', 'BSB', 'It serves as fuel for man. He takes some of it to warm himself, and he kindles a fire and bakes his bread; he even fashions it into a god and worships it; he makes an idol and bows down to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.16', 'BSB', 'He burns half of it in the fire, and he roasts meat on that half. He eats the roast and is satisfied. Indeed, he warms himself and says, “Ah! I am warm; I see the fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.17', 'BSB', 'From the rest he makes a god, his graven image. He bows down to it and worships; he prays to it and says, “Save me, for you are my god.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.18', 'BSB', 'They do not comprehend or discern, for He has shut their eyes so they cannot see and closed their minds so they cannot understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.19', 'BSB', 'And no one considers in his heart, no one has the knowledge or insight to say, “I burned half of it in the fire, and I baked bread on its coals; I roasted meat and I ate. Shall I make something detestable with the rest of it? Shall I bow down to a block of wood?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.20', 'BSB', 'He feeds on ashes. His deluded heart has led him astray, and he cannot deliver himself or say, “Is not this thing in my right hand a lie?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.21', 'BSB', 'Remember these things, O Jacob, for you are My servant, O Israel. I have made you, and you are My servant; O Israel, I will never forget you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.22', 'BSB', 'I have blotted out your transgressions like a cloud, and your sins like a mist. Return to Me, for I have redeemed you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.23', 'BSB', 'Sing for joy, O heavens, for the LORD has done this; shout aloud, O depths of the earth. Break forth in song, O mountains, you forests and all your trees. For the LORD has redeemed Jacob, and revealed His glory in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.24', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, your Redeemer who formed you from the womb: “I am the LORD, who has made all things, who alone stretched out the heavens, who by Myself spread out the earth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.25', 'BSB', 'who foils the signs of false prophets and makes fools of diviners, who confounds the wise and turns their knowledge into nonsense,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.26', 'BSB', 'who confirms the message of His servant and fulfills the counsel of His messengers, who says of Jerusalem, ‘She will be inhabited,’ and of the cities of Judah, ‘They will be rebuilt, and I will restore their ruins,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.27', 'BSB', 'who says to the depths of the sea, ‘Be dry, and I will dry up your currents,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.44.28', 'BSB', 'who says of Cyrus, ‘My shepherd will fulfill all that I desire,’ who says of Jerusalem, ‘She will be rebuilt,’ and of the temple, ‘Let its foundation be laid.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says to Cyrus His anointed, whose right hand I have grasped to subdue nations before him, to disarm kings, to open the doors before him, so that the gates will not be shut:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.2', 'BSB', '“I will go before you and level the mountains; I will break down the gates of bronze and cut through the bars of iron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.3', 'BSB', 'I will give you the treasures of darkness and the riches hidden in secret places, so that you may know that I am the LORD, the God of Israel, who calls you by name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.4', 'BSB', 'For the sake of Jacob My servant and Israel My chosen one, I call you by name; I have given you a title of honor, though you have not known Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.5', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD, and there is no other; there is no God but Me. I will equip you for battle, though you have not known Me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.6', 'BSB', 'so that all may know, from where the sun rises to where it sets, that there is none but Me; I am the LORD, and there is no other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.7', 'BSB', 'I form the light and create the darkness; I bring prosperity and create calamity. I, the LORD, do all these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.8', 'BSB', 'Drip down, O heavens, from above, and let the skies pour down righteousness. Let the earth open up that salvation may sprout and righteousness spring up with it; I, the LORD, have created it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.9', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who quarrels with his Maker— one clay pot among many. Does the clay ask the potter, ‘What are you making?’ Does your work say, ‘He has no hands’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.10', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who says to his father, ‘What have you begotten?’ or to his mother, ‘What have you brought forth?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.11', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, and its Maker: “How dare you question Me about My sons, or instruct Me in the work of My hands?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.12', 'BSB', 'It is I who made the earth and created man upon it. It was My hands that stretched out the heavens, and I ordained all their host.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.13', 'BSB', 'I will raise up Cyrus in righteousness, and I will make all his ways straight. He will rebuild My city and set My exiles free, but not for payment or reward, says the LORD of Hosts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.14', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “The products of Egypt and the merchandise of Cush, along with the Sabeans, men of stature, will come over to you and will be yours; they will trudge behind you; they will come over in chains and bow down to you. They will confess to you: ‘God is indeed with you, and there is no other; there is no other God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.15', 'BSB', 'Truly You are a God who hides Himself, O God of Israel, the Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.16', 'BSB', 'They will all be put to shame and humiliated; the makers of idols will depart together in disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.17', 'BSB', 'But Israel will be saved by the LORD with an everlasting salvation; you will not be put to shame or humiliated, to ages everlasting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.18', 'BSB', 'For thus says the LORD, who created the heavens—He is God; He formed the earth and fashioned it; He established it; He did not create it to be empty, but formed it to be inhabited: “I am the LORD, and there is no other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.19', 'BSB', 'I have not spoken in secret, from a place in a land of darkness. I did not say to the descendants of Jacob, ‘Seek Me in a wasteland.’ I, the LORD, speak the truth; I say what is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.20', 'BSB', 'Come, gather together, and draw near, you fugitives from the nations. Ignorant are those who carry idols of wood and pray to a god that cannot save.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.21', 'BSB', 'Speak up and present your case— yes, let them take counsel together. Who foretold this long ago? Who announced it from ancient times? Was it not I, the LORD? There is no other God but Me, a righteous God and Savior; there is none but Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.22', 'BSB', 'Turn to Me and be saved, all the ends of the earth; for I am God, and there is no other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.23', 'BSB', 'By Myself I have sworn; truth has gone out from My mouth, a word that will not be revoked: Every knee will bow before Me, every tongue will swear allegiance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.24', 'BSB', 'Surely they will say of Me, ‘In the LORD alone are righteousness and strength.’” All who rage against Him will come to Him and be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.45.25', 'BSB', 'In the LORD all descendants of Israel will be justified and will exult.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.1', 'BSB', 'Bel crouches; Nebo cowers. Their idols weigh down beasts and cattle. The images you carry are burdensome, a load to the weary animal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.2', 'BSB', 'The gods cower; they crouch together, unable to relieve the burden; but they themselves go into captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.3', 'BSB', '“Listen to Me, O house of Jacob, all the remnant of the house of Israel, who have been sustained from the womb, carried along since birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.4', 'BSB', 'Even to your old age, I will be the same, and I will bear you up when you turn gray. I have made you, and I will carry you; I will sustain you and deliver you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.5', 'BSB', 'To whom will you liken Me or count Me equal? To whom will you compare Me, that we should be alike?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.6', 'BSB', 'They pour out their bags of gold and weigh out silver on scales; they hire a goldsmith to fashion it into a god, so they can bow down and worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.7', 'BSB', 'They lift it to their shoulder and carry it along; they set it in its place, and there it stands, not budging from that spot. They cry out to it, but it does not answer; it saves no one from his troubles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.8', 'BSB', 'Remember this and be brave; take it to heart, you transgressors!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.9', 'BSB', 'Remember what happened long ago, for I am God, and there is no other; I am God, and there is none like Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.10', 'BSB', 'I declare the end from the beginning, and ancient times from what is still to come. I say, ‘My purpose will stand, and all My good pleasure I will accomplish.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.11', 'BSB', 'I summon a bird of prey from the east, a man for My purpose from a far-off land. Truly I have spoken, and truly I will bring it to pass. I have planned it, and I will surely do it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.12', 'BSB', 'Listen to Me, you stubborn people, far removed from righteousness:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.46.13', 'BSB', 'I am bringing My righteousness near; it is not far away, and My salvation will not be delayed. I will grant salvation to Zion and adorn Israel with My splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.1', 'BSB', '“Go down and sit in the dust, O Virgin Daughter of Babylon. Sit on the ground without a throne, O Daughter of Chaldea! For you will no longer be called tender or delicate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.2', 'BSB', 'Take millstones and grind flour; remove your veil; strip off your skirt, bare your thigh, and wade through the streams.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.3', 'BSB', 'Your nakedness will be uncovered and your shame will be exposed. I will take vengeance; I will spare no one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.4', 'BSB', 'Our Redeemer—the LORD of Hosts is His name— is the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.5', 'BSB', '“Sit in silence and go into darkness, O Daughter of Chaldea. For you will no longer be called the queen of kingdoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.6', 'BSB', 'I was angry with My people; I profaned My heritage, and I placed them under your control. You showed them no mercy; even on the elderly you laid a most heavy yoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.7', 'BSB', 'You said, ‘I will be queen forever.’ You did not take these things to heart or consider their outcome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.8', 'BSB', 'So now hear this, O lover of luxury who sits securely, who says to herself, ‘I am, and there is none besides me. I will never be a widow or know the loss of children.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.9', 'BSB', 'These two things will overtake you in a moment, in a single day: loss of children, and widowhood. They will come upon you in full measure, in spite of your many sorceries and the potency of your spells.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.10', 'BSB', 'You were secure in your wickedness; you said, ‘No one sees me.’ Your wisdom and knowledge led you astray; you told yourself, ‘I am, and there is none besides me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.11', 'BSB', 'But disaster will come upon you; you will not know how to charm it away. A calamity will befall you that you will be unable to ward off. Devastation will happen to you suddenly and unexpectedly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.12', 'BSB', 'So take your stand with your spells and with your many sorceries, with which you have wearied yourself from your youth. Perhaps you will succeed; perhaps you will inspire terror!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.13', 'BSB', 'You are wearied by your many counselors; let them come forward now and save you— your astrologers who observe the stars, who monthly predict your fate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.14', 'BSB', 'Surely they are like stubble; the fire will burn them up. They cannot deliver themselves from the power of the flame. There will be no coals to warm them or fire to sit beside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.47.15', 'BSB', 'This is what they are to you— those with whom you have labored and traded from youth— each one strays in his own direction; not one of them can save you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.1', 'BSB', '“Listen to this, O house of Jacob, you who are called by the name of Israel, who have descended from the line of Judah, who swear by the name of the LORD, who invoke the God of Israel— but not in truth or righteousness—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.2', 'BSB', 'who indeed call yourselves after the holy city and lean on the God of Israel; the LORD of Hosts is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.3', 'BSB', 'I foretold the former things long ago; they came out of My mouth and I proclaimed them. Suddenly I acted, and they came to pass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.4', 'BSB', 'For I knew that you are stubborn; your neck is iron and your forehead is bronze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore I declared it to you long ago; I announced it before it came to pass, so that you could not claim, ‘My idol has done this; my carved image and molten god has ordained it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.6', 'BSB', 'You have heard these things; look at them all. Will you not acknowledge them? From now on I will tell you of new things, hidden things unknown to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.7', 'BSB', 'They are created now, and not long ago; you have not heard of them before today. So you cannot claim, ‘I already knew them!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.8', 'BSB', 'You have never heard; you have never understood; for a long time your ears have not been open. For I knew how deceitful you are; you have been called a rebel from birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.9', 'BSB', 'For the sake of My name I will delay My wrath; for the sake of My praise I will restrain it, so that you will not be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.10', 'BSB', 'See, I have refined you, but not as silver; I have tested you in the furnace of affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.11', 'BSB', 'For My own sake, My very own sake, I will act; for how can I let Myself be defamed? I will not yield My glory to another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.12', 'BSB', 'Listen to Me, O Jacob, and Israel, whom I have called: I am He; I am the first, and I am the last.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.13', 'BSB', 'Surely My own hand founded the earth, and My right hand spread out the heavens; when I summon them, they stand up together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.14', 'BSB', 'Come together, all of you, and listen: Which of the idols has foretold these things? The LORD’s chosen ally will carry out His desire against Babylon, and His arm will be against the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.15', 'BSB', 'I, even I, have spoken; yes, I have called him. I have brought him, and he will succeed in his mission.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.16', 'BSB', 'Come near to Me and listen to this: From the beginning I have not spoken in secret; from the time it happened, I was there.” And now the Lord GOD has sent me, accompanied by His Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.17', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel: “I am the LORD your God, who teaches you for your benefit, who directs you in the way you should go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.18', 'BSB', 'If only you had paid attention to My commandments, your peace would have been like a river, and your righteousness like waves of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.19', 'BSB', 'Your descendants would have been as countless as the sand, and your offspring as numerous as its grains; their name would never be cut off or eliminated from My presence.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.20', 'BSB', 'Leave Babylon! Flee from the Chaldeans! Declare it with a shout of joy, proclaim it, let it go out to the ends of the earth, saying, “The LORD has redeemed His servant Jacob!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.21', 'BSB', 'They did not thirst when He led them through the deserts; He made water flow for them from the rock; He split the rock, and water gushed out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.48.22', 'BSB', '“There is no peace,” says the LORD, “for the wicked.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.1', 'BSB', 'Listen to Me, O islands; pay attention, O distant peoples: The LORD called Me from the womb; from the body of My mother He named Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.2', 'BSB', 'He made My mouth like a sharp sword; He hid Me in the shadow of His hand. He made Me like a polished arrow; He hid Me in His quiver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.3', 'BSB', 'He said to Me, “You are My Servant, Israel, in whom I will display My glory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.4', 'BSB', 'But I said, “I have labored in vain, I have spent My strength in futility and vanity; yet My vindication is with the LORD, and My reward is with My God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.5', 'BSB', 'And now says the LORD, who formed Me from the womb to be His Servant, to bring Jacob back to Him, that Israel might be gathered to Him— for I am honored in the sight of the LORD, and My God is My strength—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.6', 'BSB', 'He says: “It is not enough for You to be My Servant, to raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to restore the protected ones of Israel. I will also make You a light for the nations, to bring My salvation to the ends of the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.7', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, the Redeemer and Holy One of Israel, to Him who was despised and abhorred by the nation, to the Servant of rulers: “Kings will see You and rise, and princes will bow down, because of the LORD, who is faithful, the Holy One of Israel, who has chosen You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.8', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “In the time of favor I will answer You, and in the day of salvation I will help You; I will keep You and appoint You to be a covenant for the people, to restore the land, to apportion its desolate inheritances,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.9', 'BSB', 'to say to the prisoners, ‘Come out,’ and to those in darkness, ‘Show yourselves.’ They will feed along the pathways, and find pasture on every barren hill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.10', 'BSB', 'They will not hunger or thirst, nor will scorching heat or sun beat down on them. For He who has compassion on them will guide them and lead them beside springs of water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.11', 'BSB', 'I will turn all My mountains into roads, and My highways will be raised up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.12', 'BSB', 'Behold, they will come from far away, from the north and from the west, and from the land of Aswan.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.13', 'BSB', 'Shout for joy, O heavens; rejoice, O earth; break forth in song, O mountains! For the LORD has comforted His people, and He will have compassion on His afflicted ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.14', 'BSB', 'But Zion said, “The LORD has forsaken me; the Lord has forgotten me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.15', 'BSB', '“Can a woman forget her nursing child, or lack compassion for the son of her womb? Even if she could forget, I will not forget you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.16', 'BSB', 'Behold, I have inscribed you on the palms of My hands; your walls are ever before Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.17', 'BSB', 'Your builders hasten back; your destroyers and wreckers depart from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.18', 'BSB', 'Lift up your eyes and look around. They all gather together; they come to you. As surely as I live,” declares the LORD, “you will wear them all as jewelry and put them on like a bride.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.19', 'BSB', 'For your ruined and desolate places and your ravaged land will now indeed be too small for your people, and those who devoured you will be far away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.20', 'BSB', 'Yet the children of your bereavement will say in your hearing, ‘This place is too small for us; make room for us to live here.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.21', 'BSB', 'Then you will say in your heart, ‘Who has begotten these for me? I was bereaved and barren; I was exiled and rejected. So who has reared them? Look, I was left all alone, so where did they come from?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.22', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: “Behold, I will lift up My hand to the nations, and raise My banner to the peoples. They will bring your sons in their arms and carry your daughters on their shoulders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.23', 'BSB', 'Kings will be your foster fathers, and their queens your nursing mothers. They will bow to you facedown and lick the dust at your feet. Then you will know that I am the LORD; those who hope in Me will never be put to shame.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.24', 'BSB', 'Can the plunder be snatched from the mighty, or the captives of a tyrant be delivered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.25', 'BSB', 'Indeed, this is what the LORD says: “Even the captives of the mighty will be taken away, and the plunder of the tyrant will be retrieved; I will contend with those who contend with you, and I will save your children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.49.26', 'BSB', 'I will make your oppressors eat their own flesh; they will be drunk on their own blood, as with wine. Then all mankind will know that I, the LORD, am your Savior and your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Where is your mother’s certificate of divorce with which I sent her away? Or to which of My creditors did I sell you? Look, you were sold for your iniquities, and for your transgressions your mother was sent away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.2', 'BSB', 'Why was no one there when I arrived? Why did no one answer when I called? Is My hand too short to redeem you? Or do I lack the strength to deliver you? Behold, My rebuke dries up the sea; I turn the rivers into a desert; the fish rot for lack of water and die of thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.3', 'BSB', 'I clothe the heavens in black and make sackcloth their covering.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.4', 'BSB', 'The Lord GOD has given Me the tongue of discipleship, to sustain the weary with a word. He awakens Me morning by morning; He awakens My ear to listen as a disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.5', 'BSB', 'The Lord GOD has opened My ears, and I have not been rebellious, nor have I turned back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.6', 'BSB', 'I offered My back to those who struck Me, and My cheeks to those who tore out My beard. I did not hide My face from scorn and spittle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.7', 'BSB', 'Because the Lord GOD helps Me, I have not been disgraced; therefore I have set My face like flint, and I know that I will not be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.8', 'BSB', 'The One who vindicates Me is near. Who will dare to contend with Me? Let us confront each other! Who has a case against Me? Let him approach Me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.9', 'BSB', 'Surely the Lord GOD helps Me. Who is there to condemn Me? See, they will all wear out like a garment; the moths will devour them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.10', 'BSB', 'Who among you fears the LORD and obeys the voice of His Servant? Who among you walks in darkness and has no light? Let him trust in the name of the LORD; let him lean on his God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.50.11', 'BSB', 'Behold, all you who kindle a fire, who array yourselves with firebrands, walk in the light of your fire and of the firebrands you have lit! This is what you will receive from My hand: You will lie down in a place of torment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.1', 'BSB', '“Listen to Me, you who pursue righteousness, you who seek the LORD: Look to the rock from which you were cut, and to the quarry from which you were hewn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.2', 'BSB', 'Look to Abraham your father, and to Sarah who gave you birth. When I called him, he was but one; then I blessed him and multiplied him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.3', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will comfort Zion and will look with compassion on all her ruins; He will make her wilderness like Eden and her desert like the garden of the LORD. Joy and gladness will be found in her, thanksgiving and melodious song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.4', 'BSB', 'Pay attention to Me, My people, and listen to Me, My nation; for a law will go out from Me, and My justice will become a light to the nations; I will bring it about quickly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.5', 'BSB', 'My righteousness draws near, My salvation is on the way, and My arms will bring justice to the nations. The islands will look for Me and wait in hope for My arm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.6', 'BSB', 'Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look at the earth below; for the heavens will vanish like smoke, the earth will wear out like a garment, and its people will die like gnats. But My salvation will last forever, and My righteousness will never fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.7', 'BSB', 'Listen to Me, you who know what is right, you people with My law in your hearts: Do not fear the scorn of men; do not be broken by their insults.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.8', 'BSB', 'For the moth will devour them like a garment, and the worm will eat them like wool. But My righteousness will last forever, My salvation through all generations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.9', 'BSB', 'Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm of the LORD. Wake up as in days past, as in generations of old. Was it not You who cut Rahab to pieces, who pierced through the dragon?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.10', 'BSB', 'Was it not You who dried up the sea, the waters of the great deep, who made a road in the depths of the sea for the redeemed to cross over?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.11', 'BSB', 'So the redeemed of the LORD will return and enter Zion with singing, crowned with everlasting joy. Gladness and joy will overtake them, and sorrow and sighing will flee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.12', 'BSB', '“I, even I, am He who comforts you. Why should you be afraid of mortal man, of a son of man who withers like grass?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.13', 'BSB', 'But you have forgotten the LORD, your Maker, who stretched out the heavens and laid the foundations of the earth. You live in terror all day long because of the fury of the oppressor who is bent on destruction. But where is the fury of the oppressor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.14', 'BSB', 'The captive will soon be freed; he will not die in the dungeon, and his bread will not be lacking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.15', 'BSB', 'For I am the LORD your God who stirs up the sea so that its waves roar— the LORD of Hosts is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.16', 'BSB', 'I have put My words in your mouth, and covered you with the shadow of My hand, to establish the heavens, to found the earth, and to say to Zion, ‘You are My people.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.17', 'BSB', 'Awake, awake! Rise up, O Jerusalem, you who have drunk from the hand of the LORD the cup of His fury; you who have drained the goblet to the dregs— the cup that makes men stagger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.18', 'BSB', 'Among all the sons she bore, there is no one to guide her; among all the sons she brought up, there is no one to take her hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.19', 'BSB', 'These pairs have befallen you: devastation and destruction, famine and sword. Who will grieve for you? Who can comfort you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.20', 'BSB', 'Your sons have fainted; they lie at the head of every street, like an antelope in a net. They are full of the wrath of the LORD, the rebuke of your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore now hear this, you afflicted one, drunken, but not with wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.22', 'BSB', 'Thus says your Lord, the LORD, even your God, who defends His people: “See, I have removed from your hand the cup of staggering. From that goblet, the cup of My fury, you will never drink again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.51.23', 'BSB', 'I will place it in the hands of your tormentors, who told you: ‘Lie down, so we can walk over you,’ so that you made your back like the ground, like a street to be traversed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.1', 'BSB', 'Awake, awake, clothe yourself with strength, O Zion! Put on your garments of splendor, O Jerusalem, holy city! For the uncircumcised and unclean will no longer enter you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.2', 'BSB', 'Shake off your dust! Rise up and sit on your throne, O Jerusalem. Remove the chains from your neck, O captive Daughter of Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.3', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “You were sold for nothing, and without money you will be redeemed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: “At first My people went down to Egypt to live, then Assyria oppressed them without cause.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.5', 'BSB', 'And now what have I here? declares the LORD. For My people have been taken without cause; those who rule them taunt, declares the LORD, and My name is blasphemed continually all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore My people will know My name; therefore they will know on that day that I am He who speaks. Here I am!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.7', 'BSB', 'How beautiful on the mountains are the feet of those who bring good news, who proclaim peace, who bring good tidings, who proclaim salvation, who say to Zion, “Your God reigns!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.8', 'BSB', 'Listen! Your watchmen lift up their voices, together they shout for joy. For every eye will see when the LORD returns to Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.9', 'BSB', 'Break forth in joy, sing together, O ruins of Jerusalem, for the LORD has comforted His people; He has redeemed Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.10', 'BSB', 'The LORD has bared His holy arm in the sight of all the nations; all the ends of the earth will see the salvation of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.11', 'BSB', 'Depart, depart, go out from there! Touch no unclean thing; come out from it, purify yourselves, you who carry the vessels of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.12', 'BSB', 'For you will not leave in a hurry nor flee in haste, for the LORD goes before you, and the God of Israel is your rear guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.13', 'BSB', 'Behold, My Servant will prosper; He will be raised and lifted up and highly exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.14', 'BSB', 'Just as many were appalled at Him — His appearance was disfigured beyond that of any man, and His form was marred beyond human likeness—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.52.15', 'BSB', 'so He will sprinkle many nations. Kings will shut their mouths because of Him. For they will see what they have not been told, and they will understand what they have not heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.1', 'BSB', 'Who has believed our message? And to whom has the arm of the LORD been revealed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.2', 'BSB', 'He grew up before Him like a tender shoot, and like a root out of dry ground. He had no stately form or majesty to attract us, no beauty that we should desire Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.3', 'BSB', 'He was despised and rejected by men, a man of sorrows, acquainted with grief. Like one from whom men hide their faces, He was despised, and we esteemed Him not.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.4', 'BSB', 'Surely He took on our infirmities and carried our sorrows; yet we considered Him stricken by God, struck down and afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.5', 'BSB', 'But He was pierced for our transgressions, He was crushed for our iniquities; the punishment that brought us peace was upon Him, and by His stripes we are healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.6', 'BSB', 'We all like sheep have gone astray, each one has turned to his own way; and the LORD has laid upon Him the iniquity of us all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.7', 'BSB', 'He was oppressed and afflicted, yet He did not open His mouth. He was led like a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is silent, so He did not open His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.8', 'BSB', 'By oppression and judgment He was taken away, and who can recount His descendants? For He was cut off from the land of the living; He was stricken for the transgression of My people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.9', 'BSB', 'He was assigned a grave with the wicked, and with a rich man in His death, although He had done no violence, nor was any deceit in His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.10', 'BSB', 'Yet it was the LORD’s will to crush Him and to cause Him to suffer; and when His soul is made a guilt offering, He will see His offspring, He will prolong His days, and the good pleasure of the LORD will prosper in His hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.11', 'BSB', 'After the anguish of His soul, He will see the light of life and be satisfied. By His knowledge My righteous Servant will justify many, and He will bear their iniquities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.53.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will allot Him a portion with the great, and He will divide the spoils with the strong, because He has poured out His life unto death, and He was numbered with the transgressors. Yet He bore the sin of many and made intercession for the transgressors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.1', 'BSB', '“Shout for joy, O barren woman, who bears no children; break forth in song and cry aloud, you who have never travailed; because more are the children of the desolate woman than of her who has a husband,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.2', 'BSB', '“Enlarge the site of your tent, stretch out the curtains of your dwellings, do not hold back. Lengthen your ropes and drive your stakes in deep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.3', 'BSB', 'For you will spread out to the right and left; your descendants will dispossess the nations and inhabit the desolate cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.4', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid, for you will not be put to shame; do not be intimidated, for you will not be humiliated. For you will forget the shame of your youth and will remember no more the reproach of your widowhood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.5', 'BSB', 'For your husband is your Maker— the LORD of Hosts is His name— the Holy One of Israel is your Redeemer; He is called the God of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.6', 'BSB', 'For the LORD has called you back, like a wife deserted and wounded in spirit, like the rejected wife of one’s youth,” says your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.7', 'BSB', '“For a brief moment I forsook you, but with great compassion I will bring you back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.8', 'BSB', 'In a surge of anger I hid My face from you for a moment, but with everlasting kindness I will have compassion on you,” says the LORD your Redeemer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.9', 'BSB', '“For to Me this is like the days of Noah, when I swore that the waters of Noah would never again cover the earth. So I have sworn that I will not be angry with you or rebuke you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.10', 'BSB', 'Though the mountains may be removed and the hills may be shaken, My loving devotion will not depart from you, and My covenant of peace will not be broken,” says the LORD, who has compassion on you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.11', 'BSB', '“O afflicted city, lashed by storms, without solace, surely I will set your stones in antimony and lay your foundations with sapphires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.12', 'BSB', 'I will make your pinnacles of rubies, your gates of sparkling jewels, and all your walls of precious stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.13', 'BSB', 'Then all your sons will be taught by the LORD, and great will be their prosperity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.14', 'BSB', 'In righteousness you will be established, far from oppression, for you will have no fear. Terror will be far removed, for it will not come near you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.15', 'BSB', 'If anyone attacks you, it is not from Me; whoever assails you will fall before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.16', 'BSB', 'Behold, I have created the craftsman who fans the coals into flame and forges a weapon fit for its task; and I have created the destroyer to wreak havoc.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.54.17', 'BSB', 'No weapon formed against you shall prosper, and you will refute every tongue that accuses you. This is the heritage of the servants of the LORD, and their vindication is from Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.1', 'BSB', '“Come, all you who are thirsty, come to the waters; and you without money, come, buy, and eat! Come, buy wine and milk without money and without cost!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.2', 'BSB', 'Why spend money on that which is not bread, and your labor on that which does not satisfy? Listen carefully to Me, and eat what is good, and your soul will delight in the richest of foods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.3', 'BSB', 'Incline your ear and come to Me; listen, so that your soul may live. I will make with you an everlasting covenant— My loving devotion promised to David.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.4', 'BSB', 'Behold, I have made him a witness to the nations, a leader and commander of the peoples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.5', 'BSB', 'Surely you will summon a nation you do not know, and nations who do not know you will run to you. For the LORD your God, the Holy One of Israel, has bestowed glory on you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.6', 'BSB', 'Seek the LORD while He may be found; call on Him while He is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.7', 'BSB', 'Let the wicked man forsake his own way and the unrighteous man his own thoughts; let him return to the LORD, that He may have compassion, and to our God, for He will freely pardon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.8', 'BSB', '“For My thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways My ways,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.9', 'BSB', '“For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so My ways are higher than your ways and My thoughts than your thoughts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.10', 'BSB', 'For just as rain and snow fall from heaven and do not return without watering the earth, making it bud and sprout, and providing seed to sow and food to eat,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.11', 'BSB', 'so My word that proceeds from My mouth will not return to Me empty, but it will accomplish what I please, and it will prosper where I send it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.12', 'BSB', 'You will indeed go out with joy and be led forth in peace; the mountains and hills will burst into song before you, and all the trees of the field will clap their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.55.13', 'BSB', 'Instead of the thornbush, a cypress will grow, and instead of the brier, a myrtle will spring up; they will make a name for the LORD, an everlasting sign, never to be destroyed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Maintain justice and do what is right, for My salvation is coming soon, and My righteousness will be revealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.2', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man who does this, and the son of man who holds it fast, who keeps the Sabbath without profaning it and keeps his hand from doing any evil.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.3', 'BSB', 'Let no foreigner who has joined himself to the LORD say, “The LORD will utterly exclude me from His people.” And let the eunuch not say, “I am but a dry tree.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “To the eunuchs who keep My Sabbaths, who choose what pleases Me and hold fast to My covenant—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.5', 'BSB', 'I will give them, in My house and within My walls, a memorial and a name better than that of sons and daughters. I will give them an everlasting name that will not be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.6', 'BSB', 'And the foreigners who join themselves to the LORD to minister to Him, to love the name of the LORD, and to be His servants— all who keep the Sabbath without profaning it and who hold fast to My covenant—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.7', 'BSB', 'I will bring them to My holy mountain and make them joyful in My house of prayer. Their burnt offerings and sacrifices will be accepted on My altar, for My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.8', 'BSB', 'Thus declares the Lord GOD, who gathers the dispersed of Israel: “I will gather to them still others besides those already gathered.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.9', 'BSB', 'Come, all you beasts of the field; eat greedily, all you beasts of the forest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.10', 'BSB', 'Israel’s watchmen are blind, they are all oblivious; they are all mute dogs, they cannot bark; they are dreamers lying around, loving to slumber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.11', 'BSB', 'Like ravenous dogs, they are never satisfied. They are shepherds with no discernment; they all turn to their own way, each one seeking his own gain:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.56.12', 'BSB', '“Come, let me get the wine, let us imbibe the strong drink, and tomorrow will be like today, only far better!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.1', 'BSB', 'The righteous perish, and no one takes it to heart; devout men are swept away, while no one considers that the righteous are guided from the presence of evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.2', 'BSB', 'Those who walk uprightly enter into peace; they find rest, lying down in death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.3', 'BSB', '“But come here, you sons of a sorceress, you offspring of adulterers and prostitutes!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.4', 'BSB', 'Whom are you mocking? At whom do you snarl and stick out your tongue? Are you not children of transgression, offspring of deceit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.5', 'BSB', 'who burn with lust among the oaks, under every luxuriant tree, who slaughter your children in the valleys, under the clefts of the rocks?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.6', 'BSB', 'Your portion is among the smooth stones of the valley; indeed, they are your lot. Even to them you have poured out a drink offering and offered a grain offering. Should I relent because of these?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.7', 'BSB', 'On a high and lofty hill you have made your bed, and there you went up to offer sacrifices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.8', 'BSB', 'Behind the door and doorpost you have set up your memorial. Forsaking Me, you uncovered your bed; you climbed up and opened it wide. And you have made a pact with those whose bed you have loved; you have gazed upon their nakedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.9', 'BSB', 'You went to Molech with oil and multiplied your perfumes. You have sent your envoys a great distance; you have descended even to Sheol itself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.10', 'BSB', 'You are wearied by your many journeys, but you did not say, “There is no hope!” You found renewal of your strength; therefore you did not grow weak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.11', 'BSB', 'Whom have you dreaded and feared, so that you lied and failed to remember Me or take this to heart? Is it not because I have long been silent that you do not fear Me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.12', 'BSB', 'I will expose your righteousness and your works, and they will not profit you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.13', 'BSB', 'When you cry out, let your companies of idols deliver you! Yet the wind will carry off all of them, a breath will take them away. But he who seeks refuge in Me will inherit the land and possess My holy mountain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.14', 'BSB', 'And it will be said, “Build it up, build it up, prepare the way, take every obstacle out of the way of My people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.15', 'BSB', 'For thus says the One who is high and lifted up, who inhabits eternity, whose name is Holy: “I dwell in a high and holy place, and with the oppressed and humble in spirit, to restore the spirit of the lowly and revive the heart of the contrite.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.16', 'BSB', 'For I will not accuse you forever, nor will I always be angry; for then the spirit of man would grow weak before Me, with the breath of those I have made.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.17', 'BSB', 'I was enraged by his sinful greed, so I struck him and hid My face in anger; yet he kept turning back to the desires of his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.18', 'BSB', 'I have seen his ways, but I will heal him; I will guide him and restore comfort to him and his mourners,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.19', 'BSB', 'bringing praise to their lips. Peace, peace to those far and near,” says the LORD, “and I will heal them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.20', 'BSB', 'But the wicked are like the storm-tossed sea, for it cannot be still, and its waves churn up mire and muck.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.57.21', 'BSB', '“There is no peace,” says my God, “for the wicked.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.1', 'BSB', '“Cry aloud, do not hold back! Raise your voice like a ram’s horn. Declare to My people their transgression and to the house of Jacob their sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.2', 'BSB', 'For day after day they seek Me and delight to know My ways, like a nation that does what is right and does not forsake the justice of their God. They ask Me for righteous judgments; they delight in the nearness of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.3', 'BSB', '“Why have we fasted, and You have not seen? Why have we humbled ourselves, and You have not noticed?” “Behold, on the day of your fast, you do as you please, and you oppress all your workers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.4', 'BSB', 'You fast with contention and strife to strike viciously with your fist. You cannot fast as you do today and have your voice be heard on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.5', 'BSB', 'Is this the fast I have chosen: a day for a man to deny himself, to bow his head like a reed, and to spread out sackcloth and ashes? Will you call this a fast and a day acceptable to the LORD?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.6', 'BSB', 'Isn’t this the fast that I have chosen: to break the chains of wickedness, to untie the cords of the yoke, to set the oppressed free and tear off every yoke?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.7', 'BSB', 'Isn’t it to share your bread with the hungry, to bring the poor and homeless into your home, to clothe the naked when you see him, and not to turn away from your own flesh and blood?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.8', 'BSB', 'Then your light will break forth like the dawn, and your healing will come quickly. Your righteousness will go before you, and the glory of the LORD will be your rear guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.9', 'BSB', 'Then you will call, and the LORD will answer; you will cry out, and He will say, ‘Here I am.’ If you remove the yoke from your midst, the pointing of the finger and malicious talk,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.10', 'BSB', 'and if you give yourself to the hungry and satisfy the afflicted soul, then your light will go forth in the darkness, and your night will be like noonday.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD will always guide you; He will satisfy you in a sun-scorched land and strengthen your frame. You will be like a well-watered garden, like a spring whose waters never fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.12', 'BSB', 'Your people will rebuild the ancient ruins; you will restore the age-old foundations; you will be called Repairer of the Breach, Restorer of the Streets of Dwelling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.13', 'BSB', 'If you turn your foot from breaking the Sabbath, from doing as you please on My holy day, if you call the Sabbath a delight, and the LORD’s holy day honorable, if you honor it by not going your own way or seeking your own pleasure or speaking idle words,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.58.14', 'BSB', 'then you will delight yourself in the LORD, and I will make you ride on the heights of the land and feed you with the heritage of your father Jacob.” For the mouth of the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.1', 'BSB', 'Surely the arm of the LORD is not too short to save, nor His ear too dull to hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.2', 'BSB', 'But your iniquities have built barriers between you and your God, and your sins have hidden His face from you, so that He does not hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.3', 'BSB', 'For your hands are stained with blood, and your fingers with iniquity; your lips have spoken lies, and your tongue mutters injustice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.4', 'BSB', 'No one calls for justice; no one pleads his case honestly. They rely on empty pleas; they tell lies; they conceive mischief and give birth to iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.5', 'BSB', 'They hatch the eggs of vipers and weave a spider’s web. Whoever eats their eggs will die; crack one open, and a viper is hatched.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.6', 'BSB', 'Their cobwebs cannot be made into clothing, and they cannot cover themselves with their works. Their deeds are sinful deeds, and acts of violence are in their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.7', 'BSB', 'Their feet run to evil; they are swift to shed innocent blood. Their thoughts are sinful thoughts; ruin and destruction lie in their wake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.8', 'BSB', 'The way of peace they have not known, and there is no justice in their tracks. They have turned them into crooked paths; no one who treads on them will know peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore justice is far from us, and righteousness does not reach us. We hope for light, but there is darkness; for brightness, but we walk in gloom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.10', 'BSB', 'Like the blind, we feel our way along the wall, groping like those without eyes. We stumble at midday as in the twilight; among the vigorous we are like the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.11', 'BSB', 'We all growl like bears and moan like doves. We hope for justice, but find none, for salvation, but it is far from us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.12', 'BSB', 'For our transgressions are multiplied before You, and our sins testify against us. Our transgressions are indeed with us, and we know our iniquities:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.13', 'BSB', 'rebelling and denying the LORD, turning away from our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering lies from the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.14', 'BSB', 'So justice is turned away, and righteousness stands at a distance. For truth has stumbled in the public square, and honesty cannot enter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.15', 'BSB', 'Truth is missing, and whoever turns from evil becomes prey. The LORD looked and was displeased that there was no justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.16', 'BSB', 'He saw that there was no man; He was amazed that there was no one to intercede. So His own arm brought salvation, and His own righteousness sustained Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.17', 'BSB', 'He put on righteousness like a breastplate, and the helmet of salvation on His head; He put on garments of vengeance and wrapped Himself in a cloak of zeal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.18', 'BSB', 'So He will repay according to their deeds: fury to His enemies, retribution to His foes, and recompense to the islands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.19', 'BSB', 'So shall they fear the name of the LORD where the sun sets, and His glory where it rises. For He will come like a raging flood, driven by the breath of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.20', 'BSB', '“The Redeemer will come to Zion, to those in Jacob who turn from transgression,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.59.21', 'BSB', '“As for Me, this is My covenant with them,” says the LORD. “My Spirit will not depart from you, and My words that I have put in your mouth will not depart from your mouth or from the mouths of your children and grandchildren, from now on and forevermore,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.1', 'BSB', 'Arise, shine, for your light has come, and the glory of the LORD rises upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.2', 'BSB', 'For behold, darkness covers the earth, and thick darkness is over the peoples; but the LORD will rise upon you, and His glory will appear over you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.3', 'BSB', 'Nations will come to your light, and kings to the brightness of your dawn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.4', 'BSB', 'Lift up your eyes and look around: They all gather and come to you; your sons will come from afar, and your daughters will be carried on the arm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.5', 'BSB', 'Then you will look and be radiant, and your heart will tremble and swell with joy, because the riches of the sea will be brought to you, and the wealth of the nations will come to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.6', 'BSB', 'Caravans of camels will cover your land, young camels of Midian and Ephah, and all from Sheba will come, bearing gold and frankincense and proclaiming the praises of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.7', 'BSB', 'All the flocks of Kedar will be gathered to you; the rams of Nebaioth will serve you and go up on My altar with acceptance; I will adorn My glorious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.8', 'BSB', 'Who are these who fly like clouds, like doves to their shelters?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.9', 'BSB', 'Surely the islands will wait for Me, with the ships of Tarshish in the lead, to bring your children from afar, with their silver and gold, to the honor of the LORD your God, the Holy One of Israel, for He has glorified you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.10', 'BSB', 'Foreigners will rebuild your walls, and their kings will serve you. Although I struck you in anger, yet in favor I will show you mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.11', 'BSB', 'Your gates will always stand open; they will never be shut, day or night, so that the wealth of the nations may be brought into you, with their kings being led in procession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.12', 'BSB', 'For the nation or kingdom that will not serve you will perish; it will be utterly destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.13', 'BSB', 'The glory of Lebanon will come to you— its cypress, elm, and boxwood together— to adorn the place of My sanctuary, and I will glorify the place of My feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.14', 'BSB', 'The sons of your oppressors will come and bow down to you; all who reviled you will fall facedown at your feet and call you the City of the LORD, Zion of the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.15', 'BSB', 'Whereas you have been forsaken and despised, with no one passing through, I will make you an everlasting pride, a joy from age to age.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.16', 'BSB', 'You will drink the milk of nations and nurse at the breasts of royalty; you will know that I, the LORD, am your Savior and your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.17', 'BSB', 'Instead of bronze I will bring you gold; I will bring silver in place of iron, bronze instead of wood, and iron instead of stones. I will appoint peace as your governor and righteousness as your ruler.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.18', 'BSB', 'No longer will violence be heard in your land, nor ruin or destruction within your borders. But you will name your walls Salvation and your gates Praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.19', 'BSB', 'No longer will the sun be your light by day, nor the brightness of the moon shine on your night; for the LORD will be your everlasting light, and your God will be your splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.20', 'BSB', 'Your sun will no longer set, and your moon will not wane; for the LORD will be your everlasting light, and the days of your sorrow will cease.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.21', 'BSB', 'Then all your people will be righteous; they will possess the land forever; they are the branch of My planting, the work of My hands, so that I may be glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.60.22', 'BSB', 'The least of you will become a thousand, and the smallest a mighty nation. I am the LORD; in its time I will accomplish it quickly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.1', 'BSB', 'The Spirit of the Lord GOD is on Me, because the LORD has anointed Me to preach good news to the poor. He has sent Me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives and freedom to the prisoners,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.2', 'BSB', 'to proclaim the year of the LORD’s favor and the day of our God’s vengeance, to comfort all who mourn,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.3', 'BSB', 'to console the mourners in Zion— to give them a crown of beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, and a garment of praise for a spirit of despair. So they will be called oaks of righteousness, the planting of the LORD, that He may be glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.4', 'BSB', 'They will rebuild the ancient ruins; they will restore the places long devastated; they will renew the ruined cities, the desolations of many generations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.5', 'BSB', 'Strangers will stand and feed your flocks, and foreigners will be your plowmen and vinedressers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.6', 'BSB', 'But you will be called the priests of the LORD; they will speak of you as ministers of our God; you will feed on the wealth of nations, and you will boast in their riches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.7', 'BSB', 'Instead of shame, My people will have a double portion, and instead of humiliation, they will rejoice in their share; and so they will inherit a double portion in their land, and everlasting joy will be theirs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.8', 'BSB', 'For I, the LORD, love justice; I hate robbery and iniquity; in My faithfulness I will give them their recompense and make an everlasting covenant with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.9', 'BSB', 'Their descendants will be known among the nations, and their offspring among the peoples. All who see them will acknowledge that they are a people the LORD has blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.10', 'BSB', 'I will rejoice greatly in the LORD, my soul will exult in my God; for He has clothed me with garments of salvation and wrapped me in a robe of righteousness, as a bridegroom wears a priestly headdress, as a bride adorns herself with her jewels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.61.11', 'BSB', 'For as the earth brings forth its growth, and as a garden enables seed to spring up, so the Lord GOD will cause righteousness and praise to spring up before all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.1', 'BSB', 'For Zion’s sake I will not keep silent, and for Jerusalem’s sake I will not keep still, until her righteousness shines like a bright light, her salvation like a blazing torch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.2', 'BSB', 'Nations will see your righteousness, and all kings your glory. You will be called by a new name that the mouth of the LORD will bestow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.3', 'BSB', 'You will be a crown of glory in the hand of the LORD, a royal diadem in the palm of your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.4', 'BSB', 'No longer will you be called Forsaken, nor your land named Desolate; but you will be called Hephzibah, and your land Beulah; for the LORD will take delight in you, and your land will be His bride.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.5', 'BSB', 'For as a young man marries a young woman, so your sons will marry you; and as a bridegroom rejoices over his bride, so your God will rejoice over you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.6', 'BSB', 'On your walls, O Jerusalem, I have posted watchmen; they will never be silent day or night. You who call on the LORD shall take no rest for yourselves,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.7', 'BSB', 'nor give Him any rest until He establishes Jerusalem and makes her the praise of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD has sworn by His right hand and by His mighty arm: “Never again will I give your grain to your enemies for food, nor will foreigners drink the new wine for which you have toiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.9', 'BSB', 'For those who harvest grain will eat it and praise the LORD, and those who gather grapes will drink the wine in My holy courts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.10', 'BSB', 'Go out, go out through the gates; prepare the way for the people! Build it up, build up the highway; clear away the stones; raise a banner for the nations!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.11', 'BSB', 'Behold, the LORD has proclaimed to the ends of the earth, “Say to Daughter Zion: See, your Savior comes! Look, His reward is with Him, and His recompense goes before Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.62.12', 'BSB', 'And they will be called the Holy People, the Redeemed of The LORD; and you will be called Sought Out, A City Not Forsaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.1', 'BSB', 'Who is this coming from Edom, from Bozrah with crimson-stained garments? Who is this robed in splendor, marching in the greatness of His strength? “It is I, proclaiming vindication, mighty to save.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.2', 'BSB', 'Why are Your clothes red, and Your garments like one who treads the winepress?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.3', 'BSB', '“I have trodden the winepress alone, and no one from the nations was with Me. I trampled them in My anger and trod them down in My fury; their blood spattered My garments, and all My clothes were stained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.4', 'BSB', 'For the day of vengeance was in My heart, and the year of My redemption had come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.5', 'BSB', 'I looked, but there was no one to help; I was appalled that no one assisted. So My arm brought Me salvation, and My own wrath upheld Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.6', 'BSB', 'I trampled the nations in My anger; in My wrath I made them drunk and poured out their blood on the ground.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.7', 'BSB', 'I will make known the LORD’s loving devotion and His praiseworthy acts, because of all that the LORD has done for us— the many good things for the house of Israel according to His great compassion and loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.8', 'BSB', 'For He said, “They are surely My people, sons who will not be disloyal.” So He became their Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.9', 'BSB', 'In all their distress, He too was afflicted, and the Angel of His Presence saved them. In His love and compassion He redeemed them; He lifted them up and carried them all the days of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.10', 'BSB', 'But they rebelled and grieved His Holy Spirit. So He turned and became their enemy, and He Himself fought against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.11', 'BSB', 'Then His people remembered the days of old, the days of Moses. Where is He who brought them through the sea with the shepherds of His flock? Where is the One who set His Holy Spirit among them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.12', 'BSB', 'who sent His glorious arm to lead them by the right hand of Moses, who divided the waters before them to gain for Himself everlasting renown,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.13', 'BSB', 'who led them through the depths like a horse in the wilderness, so that they did not stumble?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.14', 'BSB', 'Like cattle going down to the valley, the Spirit of the LORD gave them rest. You led Your people this way to make for Yourself a glorious name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.15', 'BSB', 'Look down from heaven and see, from Your holy and glorious habitation. Where are Your zeal and might? Your yearning and compassion for me are restrained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.16', 'BSB', 'Yet You are our Father, though Abraham does not know us and Israel does not acknowledge us. You, O LORD, are our Father; our Redeemer from Everlasting is Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.17', 'BSB', 'Why, O LORD, do You make us stray from Your ways and harden our hearts from fearing You? Return, for the sake of Your servants, the tribes of Your heritage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.18', 'BSB', 'For a short while Your people possessed Your holy place, but our enemies have trampled Your sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.63.19', 'BSB', 'We have become like those You never ruled, like those not called by Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.1', 'BSB', 'If only You would rend the heavens and come down, so that mountains would quake at Your presence,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.2', 'BSB', 'as fire kindles the brushwood and causes the water to boil, to make Your name known to Your enemies, so that the nations will tremble at Your presence!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.3', 'BSB', 'When You did awesome works that we did not expect, You came down, and the mountains trembled at Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.4', 'BSB', 'From ancient times no one has heard, no ear has perceived, no eye has seen any God besides You, who acts on behalf of those who wait for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.5', 'BSB', 'You welcome those who gladly do right, who remember Your ways. Surely You were angry, for we sinned. How can we be saved if we remain in our sins?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.6', 'BSB', 'Each of us has become like something unclean, and all our righteous acts are like filthy rags; we all wither like a leaf, and our iniquities carry us away like the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.7', 'BSB', 'No one calls on Your name or strives to take hold of You. For You have hidden Your face from us and delivered us into the hand of our iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.8', 'BSB', 'But now, O LORD, You are our Father; we are the clay, and You are the potter; we are all the work of Your hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.9', 'BSB', 'Do not be angry, O LORD, beyond measure; do not remember our iniquity forever. Oh, look upon us, we pray; we are all Your people!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.10', 'BSB', 'Your holy cities have become a wilderness. Zion has become a wasteland and Jerusalem a desolation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.11', 'BSB', 'Our holy and beautiful temple, where our fathers praised You, has been burned with fire, and all that was dear to us lies in ruins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.64.12', 'BSB', 'After all this, O LORD, will You restrain Yourself? Will You keep silent and afflict us beyond measure?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.1', 'BSB', '“I revealed Myself to those who did not ask for Me; I was found by those who did not seek Me. To a nation that did not call My name, I said, ‘Here I am! Here I am!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.2', 'BSB', 'All day long I have held out My hands to an obstinate people who walk in the wrong path, who follow their own imaginations,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.3', 'BSB', 'to a people who continually provoke Me to My face, sacrificing in the gardens and burning incense on altars of brick,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.4', 'BSB', 'sitting among the graves, spending nights in secret places, eating the meat of pigs and polluted broth from their bowls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.5', 'BSB', 'They say, ‘Keep to yourself; do not come near me, for I am holier than you!’ Such people are smoke in My nostrils, a fire that burns all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.6', 'BSB', 'Behold, it is written before Me: I will not keep silent, but I will repay; I will pay it back into their laps,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.7', 'BSB', 'both for your iniquities and for those of your fathers,” says the LORD. “Because they burned incense on the mountains and scorned Me on the hills, I will measure into their laps full payment for their former deeds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.8', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “As the new wine is found in a cluster of grapes, and men say, ‘Do not destroy it, for it contains a blessing,’ so I will act on behalf of My servants; I will not destroy them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.9', 'BSB', 'And I will bring forth descendants from Jacob, and heirs from Judah; My elect will possess My mountains, and My servants will dwell there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.10', 'BSB', 'Sharon will become a pasture for flocks, and the Valley of Achor a resting place for herds, for My people who seek Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.11', 'BSB', 'But you who forsake the LORD, who forget My holy mountain, who set a table for Fortune and fill bowls of mixed wine for Destiny,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.12', 'BSB', 'I will destine you for the sword, and you will all kneel down to be slaughtered, because I called and you did not answer, I spoke and you did not listen; you did evil in My sight and chose that in which I did not delight.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: “My servants will eat, but you will go hungry; My servants will drink, but you will go thirsty; My servants will rejoice, but you will be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.14', 'BSB', 'My servants will shout for joy with a glad heart, but you will cry out with a heavy heart and wail with a broken spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.15', 'BSB', 'You will leave behind your name as a curse for My chosen ones, and the Lord GOD will slay you; but to His servants He will give another name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.16', 'BSB', 'Whoever invokes a blessing in the land will do so by the God of truth, and whoever takes an oath in the land will swear by the God of truth. For the former troubles will be forgotten and hidden from My sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.17', 'BSB', 'For behold, I will create new heavens and a new earth. The former things will not be remembered, nor will they come to mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.18', 'BSB', 'But be glad and rejoice forever in what I create; for I will create Jerusalem to be a joy and its people to be a delight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.19', 'BSB', 'I will rejoice in Jerusalem and take delight in My people. The sounds of weeping and crying will no longer be heard in her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.20', 'BSB', 'No longer will a nursing infant live but a few days, or an old man fail to live out his years. For the youth will die at a hundred years, and he who fails to reach a hundred will be considered accursed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.21', 'BSB', 'They will build houses and dwell in them; they will plant vineyards and eat their fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.22', 'BSB', 'No longer will they build houses for others to inhabit, nor plant for others to eat. For as is the lifetime of a tree, so will be the days of My people, and My chosen ones will fully enjoy the work of their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.23', 'BSB', 'They will not labor in vain or bear children doomed to disaster; for they will be a people blessed by the LORD— they and their descendants with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.24', 'BSB', 'Even before they call, I will answer, and while they are still speaking, I will hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.65.25', 'BSB', 'The wolf and the lamb will feed together, and the lion will eat straw like the ox, but the food of the serpent will be dust. They will neither harm nor destroy on all My holy mountain,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Heaven is My throne, and earth is My footstool. What kind of house will you build for Me? Or where will My place of repose be?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.2', 'BSB', 'Has not My hand made all these things? And so they came into being,” declares the LORD. “This is the one I will esteem: he who is humble and contrite in spirit, who trembles at My word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.3', 'BSB', 'Whoever slaughters an ox is like one who slays a man; whoever sacrifices a lamb is like one who breaks a dog’s neck; whoever presents a grain offering is like one who offers pig’s blood; whoever offers frankincense is like one who blesses an idol. Indeed, they have chosen their own ways and delighted in their abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.4', 'BSB', 'So I will choose their punishment and I will bring terror upon them, because I called and no one answered, I spoke and no one listened. But they did evil in My sight and chose that in which I did not delight.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.5', 'BSB', 'You who tremble at His word, hear the word of the LORD: “Your brothers who hate you and exclude you because of My name have said, ‘Let the LORD be glorified that we may see your joy!’ But they will be put to shame.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.6', 'BSB', 'Hear the uproar from the city; listen to the voice from the temple! It is the voice of the LORD, repaying His enemies what they deserve!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.7', 'BSB', '“Before she was in labor, she gave birth; before she was in pain, she delivered a boy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.8', 'BSB', 'Who has heard of such as this? Who has seen such things? Can a country be born in a day or a nation be delivered in an instant? Yet as soon as Zion was in labor, she gave birth to her children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.9', 'BSB', 'Shall I bring a baby to the point of birth and not deliver it?” says the LORD. “Or will I who deliver close the womb?” says your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.10', 'BSB', 'Be glad for Jerusalem and rejoice over her, all who love her. Rejoice greatly with her, all who mourn over her,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.11', 'BSB', 'so that you may nurse and be satisfied at her comforting breasts; you may drink deeply and delight yourselves in her glorious abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.12', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “I will extend peace to her like a river, and the wealth of nations like a flowing stream; you will nurse and be carried on her arm, and bounced upon her knees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.13', 'BSB', 'As a mother comforts her son, so will I comfort you, and you will be consoled over Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.14', 'BSB', 'When you see, you will rejoice, and you will flourish like grass; then the hand of the LORD will be revealed to His servants, but His wrath will be shown to His enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.15', 'BSB', 'For behold, the LORD will come with fire— His chariots are like a whirlwind— to execute His anger with fury and His rebuke with flames of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.16', 'BSB', 'For by fire and by His sword, the LORD will execute judgment on all flesh, and many will be slain by the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.17', 'BSB', '“Those who consecrate and purify themselves to enter the groves—to follow one in the center of those who eat the flesh of swine and vermin and rats—will perish together,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.18', 'BSB', '“And I, knowing their deeds and thoughts, am coming to gather all nations and tongues, and they will come and see My glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.19', 'BSB', 'I will establish a sign among them, and I will send survivors from among them to the nations—to Tarshish, Put, and the archers of Lud; to Tubal, Javan, and the islands far away who have not heard of My fame or seen My glory. So they will proclaim My glory among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.20', 'BSB', 'And they will bring all your brothers from all the nations as a gift to the LORD on horses and chariots and wagons, on mules and camels, to My holy mountain Jerusalem,” says the LORD, “just as the Israelites bring an offering in a clean vessel to the house of the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.21', 'BSB', '“And I will select some of them as priests and Levites,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.22', 'BSB', '“For just as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, will endure before Me,” declares the LORD, “so your descendants and your name will endure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.23', 'BSB', 'From one New Moon to another and from one Sabbath to another, all mankind will come to worship before Me,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Isa.66.24', 'BSB', '“As they go forth, they will see the corpses of the men who have rebelled against Me; for their worm will never die, their fire will never be quenched, and they will be a horror to all mankind.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of Jeremiah son of Hilkiah, one of the priests in Anathoth in the territory of Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.2', 'BSB', 'The word of the LORD came to Jeremiah in the thirteenth year of the reign of Josiah son of Amon king of Judah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.3', 'BSB', 'and through the days of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, until the fifth month of the eleventh year of Zedekiah son of Josiah king of Judah, when the people of Jerusalem went into exile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.4', 'BSB', 'The word of the LORD came to me, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.5', 'BSB', '“Before I formed you in the womb I knew you, and before you were born I set you apart and appointed you as a prophet to the nations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.6', 'BSB', '“Ah, Lord GOD,” I said, “I surely do not know how to speak, for I am only a child!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.7', 'BSB', 'But the LORD told me: “Do not say, ‘I am only a child.’ For to everyone I send you, you must go, and all that I command you, you must speak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.8', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid of them, for I am with you to deliver you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.9', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD reached out His hand, touched my mouth, and said to me: “Behold, I have put My words in your mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.10', 'BSB', 'See, I have appointed you today over nations and kingdoms to uproot and tear down, to destroy and overthrow, to build and plant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.11', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, asking, “Jeremiah, what do you see?” “I see a branch of an almond tree,” I replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.12', 'BSB', '“You have observed correctly,” said the LORD, “for I am watching over My word to accomplish it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.13', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, asking, “What do you see?” “I see a boiling pot,” I replied, “and it is tilting toward us from the north.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.14', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Disaster from the north will be poured out on all who live in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.15', 'BSB', 'For I am about to summon all the clans and kingdoms of the north,” declares the LORD. “Their kings will come and set up their thrones at the entrance of the gates of Jerusalem. They will attack all her surrounding walls and all the other cities of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.16', 'BSB', 'I will pronounce My judgments against them for all their wickedness, because they have forsaken Me to burn incense to other gods and to worship the works of their own hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.17', 'BSB', 'Get yourself ready. Stand up and tell them everything that I command you. Do not be intimidated by them, or I will terrify you before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.18', 'BSB', 'Now behold, this day I have made you like a fortified city, an iron pillar, and bronze walls against the whole land—against the kings of Judah, its officials, its priests, and the people of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.1.19', 'BSB', 'They will fight against you but will never overcome you, since I am with you to deliver you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.1', 'BSB', 'Now the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.2', 'BSB', '“Go and proclaim in the hearing of Jerusalem that this is what the LORD says: ‘I remember the devotion of your youth, your love as a bride, how you followed Me in the wilderness, in a land not sown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.3', 'BSB', 'Israel was holy to the LORD, the firstfruits of His harvest. All who devoured her found themselves guilty; disaster came upon them,’” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.4', 'BSB', 'Hear the word of the LORD, O house of Jacob, and all you families of the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “What fault did your fathers find in Me that they strayed so far from Me, and followed worthless idols, and became worthless themselves?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.6', 'BSB', 'They did not ask, ‘Where is the LORD who brought us up from the land of Egypt, who led us through the wilderness, through a land of deserts and pits, a land of drought and darkness, a land where no one travels and no one lives?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.7', 'BSB', 'I brought you into a fertile land to eat its fruit and bounty, but you came and defiled My land, and made My inheritance detestable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.8', 'BSB', 'The priests did not ask, ‘Where is the LORD?’ The experts in the law no longer knew Me, and the leaders rebelled against Me. The prophets prophesied by Baal and followed useless idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore, I will contend with you again, declares the LORD, and I will bring a case against your children’s children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.10', 'BSB', 'Cross over to the coasts of Cyprus and take a look; send to Kedar and consider carefully; see if there has ever been anything like this:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.11', 'BSB', 'Has a nation ever changed its gods, though they are no gods at all? Yet My people have exchanged their Glory for useless idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.12', 'BSB', 'Be stunned by this, O heavens; be shocked and utterly appalled,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.13', 'BSB', '“For My people have committed two evils: They have forsaken Me, the fountain of living water, and they have dug their own cisterns— broken cisterns that cannot hold water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.14', 'BSB', 'Is Israel a slave? Was he born into slavery? Why then has he become prey?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.15', 'BSB', 'The young lions have roared at him; they have growled with a loud voice. They have laid waste his land; his cities lie in ruins, without inhabitant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.16', 'BSB', 'The men of Memphis and Tahpanhes have shaved the crown of your head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.17', 'BSB', 'Have you not brought this on yourself by forsaking the LORD your God when He led you in the way?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.18', 'BSB', 'Now what will you gain on your way to Egypt to drink the waters of the Nile? What will you gain on your way to Assyria to drink the waters of the Euphrates?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.19', 'BSB', 'Your own evil will discipline you; your own apostasies will reprimand you. Consider and realize how evil and bitter it is for you to forsake the LORD your God and to have no fear of Me,” declares the Lord GOD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.20', 'BSB', '“For long ago you broke your yoke and tore off your chains, saying, ‘I will not serve!’ Indeed, on every high hill and under every green tree you lay down as a prostitute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.21', 'BSB', 'I had planted you like a choice vine from the very best seed. How could you turn yourself before Me into a rotten, wild vine?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.22', 'BSB', 'Although you wash with lye and use an abundance of soap, the stain of your guilt is still before Me,” declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.23', 'BSB', '“How can you say, ‘I am not defiled; I have not run after the Baals’? Look at your behavior in the valley; acknowledge what you have done. You are a swift young she-camel galloping here and there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.24', 'BSB', 'a wild donkey at home in the wilderness, sniffing the wind in the heat of her desire. Who can restrain her passion? All who seek her need not weary themselves; in mating season they will find her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.25', 'BSB', 'You should have kept your feet from going bare and your throat from being thirsty. But you said, ‘It is hopeless! For I love foreign gods, and I must go after them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.26', 'BSB', 'As the thief is ashamed when he is caught, so the house of Israel is disgraced. They, their kings, their officials, their priests, and their prophets', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.27', 'BSB', 'say to a tree, ‘You are my father,’ and to a stone, ‘You gave me birth.’ For they have turned their backs to Me and not their faces, yet in the time of trouble they beg, ‘Rise up and save us!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.28', 'BSB', 'But where are the gods you made for yourselves? Let them rise up in your time of trouble and save you if they can; for your gods are as numerous as your cities, O Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.29', 'BSB', 'Why do you bring a case against Me? You have all rebelled against Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.30', 'BSB', '“I have struck your sons in vain; they accepted no discipline. Your own sword has devoured your prophets like a voracious lion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.31', 'BSB', 'You people of this generation, consider the word of the LORD: “Have I been a wilderness to Israel or a land of dense darkness? Why do My people say, ‘We are free to roam; we will come to You no more’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.32', 'BSB', 'Does a maiden forget her jewelry or a bride her wedding sash? Yet My people have forgotten Me for days without number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.33', 'BSB', 'How skillfully you pursue love! Even the most immoral of women could learn from your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.34', 'BSB', 'Moreover, your skirts are stained with the blood of the innocent poor, though you did not find them breaking in. But in spite of all these things', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.35', 'BSB', 'you say, ‘I am innocent. Surely His anger will turn from me.’ Behold, I will judge you, because you say, ‘I have not sinned.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.36', 'BSB', 'How unstable you are, constantly changing your ways! You will be disappointed by Egypt just as you were by Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.2.37', 'BSB', 'Moreover, you will leave that place with your hands on your head, for the LORD has rejected those you trust; you will not prosper by their help.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.1', 'BSB', '“If a man divorces his wife and she leaves him to marry another, can he ever return to her? Would not such a land be completely defiled? But you have played the harlot with many lovers— and you would return to Me?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.2', 'BSB', '“Lift up your eyes to the barren heights and see. Is there any place where you have not been violated? You sat beside the highways waiting for your lovers, like a nomad in the desert. You have defiled the land with your prostitution and wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore the showers have been withheld, and no spring rains have fallen. Yet you have the brazen look of a prostitute; you refuse to be ashamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.4', 'BSB', 'Have you not just called to Me, ‘My Father, You are my friend from youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.5', 'BSB', 'Will He be angry forever? Will He be indignant to the end?’ This you have spoken, but you keep doing all the evil you can.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.6', 'BSB', 'Now in the days of King Josiah, the LORD said to me, “Have you seen what faithless Israel has done? She has gone up on every high hill and under every green tree to prostitute herself there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.7', 'BSB', 'I thought that after she had done all these things, she would return to Me. But she did not return, and her unfaithful sister Judah saw it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.8', 'BSB', 'She saw that because faithless Israel had committed adultery, I gave her a certificate of divorce and sent her away. Yet that unfaithful sister Judah had no fear and prostituted herself as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.9', 'BSB', 'Indifferent to her own infidelity, Israel had defiled the land and committed adultery with stones and trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.10', 'BSB', 'Yet in spite of all this, her unfaithful sister Judah did not return to Me with all her heart, but only in pretense,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.11', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to me, “Faithless Israel has shown herself more righteous than unfaithful Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.12', 'BSB', 'Go, proclaim this message toward the north: ‘Return, O faithless Israel,’ declares the LORD. ‘I will no longer look on you with anger, for I am merciful,’ declares the LORD. ‘I will not be angry forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.13', 'BSB', 'Only acknowledge your guilt, that you have rebelled against the LORD your God. You have scattered your favors to foreign gods under every green tree and have not obeyed My voice,’” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.14', 'BSB', '“Return, O faithless children,” declares the LORD, “for I am your master, and I will take you—one from a city and two from a family—and bring you to Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.15', 'BSB', 'Then I will give you shepherds after My own heart, who will feed you with knowledge and understanding.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.16', 'BSB', '“In those days, when you multiply and increase in the land,” declares the LORD, “they will no longer discuss the ark of the covenant of the LORD. It will never come to mind, and no one will remember it or miss it, nor will another one be made.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.17', 'BSB', 'At that time Jerusalem will be called The Throne of the LORD, and all the nations will be gathered in Jerusalem to honor the name of the LORD. They will no longer follow the stubbornness of their evil hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.18', 'BSB', 'In those days the house of Judah will walk with the house of Israel, and they will come together from the land of the north to the land that I gave to your fathers as an inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.19', 'BSB', 'Then I said, ‘How I long to make you My sons and give you a desirable land, the most beautiful inheritance of all the nations!’ I thought you would call Me ‘Father’ and never turn away from following Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.20', 'BSB', 'But as a woman may betray her husband, so you have betrayed Me, O house of Israel,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.21', 'BSB', 'A voice is heard on the barren heights, the children of Israel weeping and begging for mercy, because they have perverted their ways and forgotten the LORD their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.22', 'BSB', '“Return, O faithless children, and I will heal your faithlessness.” “Here we are. We come to You, for You are the LORD our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.23', 'BSB', 'Surely deception comes from the hills, and commotion from the mountains. Surely the salvation of Israel is in the LORD our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.24', 'BSB', 'From our youth, that shameful god has consumed what our fathers have worked for— their flocks and herds, their sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.3.25', 'BSB', 'Let us lie down in our shame; let our disgrace cover us. We have sinned against the LORD our God, both we and our fathers; from our youth even to this day we have not obeyed the voice of the LORD our God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.1', 'BSB', '“If you will return, O Israel, return to Me,” declares the LORD. “If you will remove your detestable idols from My sight and no longer waver,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.2', 'BSB', 'and if you can swear, ‘As surely as the LORD lives,’ in truth, in justice, and in righteousness, then the nations will be blessed by Him, and in Him they will glory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.3', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says to the men of Judah and Jerusalem: “Break up your unplowed ground, and do not sow among the thorns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.4', 'BSB', 'Circumcise yourselves to the LORD, and remove the foreskins of your hearts, O men of Judah and people of Jerusalem. Otherwise, My wrath will break out like fire and burn with no one to extinguish it, because of your evil deeds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.5', 'BSB', 'Announce in Judah, proclaim in Jerusalem, and say: “Blow the ram’s horn throughout the land. Cry aloud and say, ‘Assemble yourselves and let us flee to the fortified cities.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.6', 'BSB', 'Raise a signal flag toward Zion. Seek refuge! Do not delay! For I am bringing disaster from the north, and terrible destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.7', 'BSB', 'A lion has gone up from his thicket, and a destroyer of nations has set out. He has left his lair to lay waste your land. Your cities will be reduced to ruins and lie uninhabited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.8', 'BSB', 'So put on sackcloth, mourn and wail, for the fierce anger of the LORD has not turned away from us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.9', 'BSB', '“In that day,” declares the LORD, “the king and officials will lose their courage. The priests will tremble in fear, and the prophets will be astounded.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.10', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “Ah, Lord GOD, how completely You have deceived this people and Jerusalem by saying, ‘You will have peace,’ while a sword is at our throats.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.11', 'BSB', 'At that time it will be said to this people and to Jerusalem, “A searing wind from the barren heights in the desert blows toward the daughter of My people, but not to winnow or to sift;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.12', 'BSB', 'a wind too strong for that comes from Me. Now I also pronounce judgments against them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.13', 'BSB', 'Behold, he advances like the clouds, his chariots like the whirlwind. His horses are swifter than eagles. Woe to us, for we are ruined!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.14', 'BSB', 'Wash the evil from your heart, O Jerusalem, so that you may be saved. How long will you harbor wicked thoughts within you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.15', 'BSB', 'For a voice resounds from Dan, proclaiming disaster from the hills of Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.16', 'BSB', 'Warn the nations now! Proclaim to Jerusalem: “A besieging army comes from a distant land; they raise their voices against the cities of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.17', 'BSB', 'They surround her like men guarding a field, because she has rebelled against Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.18', 'BSB', '“Your ways and deeds have brought this upon you. This is your punishment; how bitter it is, because it pierces to the heart!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.19', 'BSB', 'My anguish, my anguish! I writhe in pain! Oh, the pain in my chest! My heart pounds within me; I cannot be silent. For I have heard the sound of the horn, the alarm of battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.20', 'BSB', 'Disaster after disaster is proclaimed, for the whole land is laid waste. My tents are destroyed in an instant, my curtains in a moment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.21', 'BSB', 'How long must I see the signal flag and hear the sound of the horn?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.22', 'BSB', '“For My people are fools; they have not known Me. They are foolish children, without understanding. They are skilled in doing evil, but they know not how to do good.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.23', 'BSB', 'I looked at the earth, and it was formless and void; I looked to the heavens, and they had no light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.24', 'BSB', 'I looked at the mountains, and behold, they were quaking; all the hills were swaying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.25', 'BSB', 'I looked, and no man was left; all the birds of the air had fled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.26', 'BSB', 'I looked, and the fruitful land was a desert. All its cities were torn down before the LORD, before His fierce anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.27', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “The whole land will be desolate, but I will not finish its destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore the earth will mourn and the heavens above will grow dark. I have spoken, I have planned, and I will not relent or turn back.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.29', 'BSB', 'Every city flees at the sound of the horseman and archer. They enter the thickets and climb among the rocks. Every city is abandoned; no inhabitant is left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.30', 'BSB', 'And you, O devastated one, what will you do, though you dress yourself in scarlet, though you adorn yourself with gold jewelry, though you enlarge your eyes with paint? You adorn yourself in vain; your lovers despise you; they want to take your life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.4.31', 'BSB', 'For I hear a cry like a woman in labor, a cry of anguish like one bearing her first child— the cry of the Daughter of Zion gasping for breath, stretching out her hands to say, “Woe is me, for my soul faints before the murderers!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.1', 'BSB', '“Go up and down the streets of Jerusalem. Look now and take note; search her squares. If you can find a single person, anyone who acts justly, anyone who seeks the truth, then I will forgive the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.2', 'BSB', 'Although they say, ‘As surely as the LORD lives,’ they are swearing falsely.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.3', 'BSB', 'O LORD, do not Your eyes look for truth? You struck them, but they felt no pain. You finished them off, but they refused to accept discipline. They have made their faces harder than stone and refused to repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.4', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “They are only the poor; they have played the fool, for they do not know the way of the LORD, the justice of their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.5', 'BSB', 'I will go to the powerful and speak to them. Surely they know the way of the LORD, the justice of their God.” But they too, with one accord, had broken the yoke and torn off the chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore a lion from the forest will strike them down, a wolf from the desert will ravage them. A leopard will lie in wait near their cities, and everyone who ventures out will be torn to pieces. For their rebellious acts are many, and their unfaithful deeds are numerous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.7', 'BSB', '“Why should I forgive you? Your children have forsaken Me and sworn by gods that are not gods. I satisfied their needs, yet they committed adultery and assembled at the houses of prostitutes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.8', 'BSB', 'They are well-fed, lusty stallions, each neighing after his neighbor’s wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.9', 'BSB', 'Should I not punish them for these things?” declares the LORD. “Should I not avenge Myself on such a nation as this?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.10', 'BSB', 'Go up through her vineyards and ravage them, but do not finish them off. Strip off her branches, for they do not belong to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.11', 'BSB', 'For the house of Israel and the house of Judah have been utterly unfaithful to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.12', 'BSB', 'They have lied about the LORD and said: “He will not do anything; harm will not come to us; we will not see sword or famine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.13', 'BSB', 'The prophets are but wind, for the word is not in them. So let their own predictions befall them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD God of Hosts says: “Because you have spoken this word, I will make My words a fire in your mouth and this people the wood it consumes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.15', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am bringing a distant nation against you, O house of Israel,” declares the LORD. “It is an established nation, an ancient nation, a nation whose language you do not know and whose speech you do not understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.16', 'BSB', 'Their quivers are like open graves; they are all mighty men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.17', 'BSB', 'They will devour your harvest and food; they will consume your sons and daughters; they will eat up your flocks and herds; they will feed on your vines and fig trees. With the sword they will destroy the fortified cities in which you trust.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.18', 'BSB', '“Yet even in those days,” declares the LORD, “I will not make a full end of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.19', 'BSB', 'And when the people ask, ‘For what offense has the LORD our God done all these things to us?’ You are to tell them, ‘Just as you have forsaken Me and served foreign gods in your land, so will you serve foreigners in a land that is not your own.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.20', 'BSB', 'Declare this in the house of Jacob and proclaim it in Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.21', 'BSB', '“Hear this, O foolish and senseless people, who have eyes but do not see, who have ears but do not hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.22', 'BSB', 'Do you not fear Me?” declares the LORD. “Do you not tremble before Me, the One who set the sand as the boundary for the sea, an enduring barrier it cannot cross? The waves surge, but they cannot prevail. They roar but cannot cross it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.23', 'BSB', 'But these people have stubborn and rebellious hearts. They have turned aside and gone away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.24', 'BSB', 'They have not said in their hearts, ‘Let us fear the LORD our God, who gives the rains, both autumn and spring, in season, who keeps for us the appointed weeks of harvest.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.25', 'BSB', 'Your iniquities have diverted these from you; your sins have deprived you of My bounty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.26', 'BSB', 'For among My people are wicked men; they watch like fowlers lying in wait; they set a trap to catch men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.27', 'BSB', 'Like cages full of birds, so their houses are full of deceit. Therefore they have become powerful and rich.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.28', 'BSB', 'They have grown fat and sleek, and have excelled in the deeds of the wicked. They have not taken up the cause of the fatherless, that they might prosper; nor have they defended the rights of the needy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.29', 'BSB', 'Should I not punish them for these things?” declares the LORD. “Should I not avenge Myself on such a nation as this?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.30', 'BSB', 'A horrible and shocking thing has happened in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.5.31', 'BSB', 'The prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests rule by their own authority. My people love it so, but what will you do in the end?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.1', 'BSB', '“Run for cover, O sons of Benjamin; flee from Jerusalem! Sound the ram’s horn in Tekoa; send up a signal over Beth-haccherem, for disaster looms from the north, even great destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.2', 'BSB', 'Though she is beautiful and delicate, I will destroy the Daughter of Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.3', 'BSB', 'Shepherds and their flocks will come against her; they will pitch their tents all around her, each tending his own portion:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.4', 'BSB', '‘Prepare for battle against her; rise up, let us attack at noon. Woe to us, for the daylight is fading; the evening shadows grow long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.5', 'BSB', 'Rise up, let us attack by night and destroy her fortresses!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Cut down the trees and raise a siege ramp against Jerusalem. This city must be punished; there is nothing but oppression in her midst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.7', 'BSB', 'As a well gushes its water, so she pours out her evil. Violence and destruction resound in her; sickness and wounds are ever before Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.8', 'BSB', 'Be forewarned, O Jerusalem, or I will turn away from you; I will make you a desolation, a land without inhabitant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.9', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Glean the remnant of Israel as thoroughly as a vine. Pass your hand once more like a grape gatherer over the branches.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.10', 'BSB', 'To whom can I give this warning? Who will listen to me? Look, their ears are closed, so they cannot hear. See, the word of the LORD has become offensive to them; they find no pleasure in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.11', 'BSB', 'But I am full of the LORD’s wrath; I am tired of holding it back. “Pour it out on the children in the street, and on the young men gathered together. For both husband and wife will be captured, the old and the very old alike.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.12', 'BSB', 'Their houses will be turned over to others, their fields and wives as well, for I will stretch out My hand against the inhabitants of the land,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.13', 'BSB', '“For from the least of them to the greatest, all are greedy for gain; from prophet to priest, all practice deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.14', 'BSB', 'They dress the wound of My people with very little care, saying, ‘Peace, peace,’ when there is no peace at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.15', 'BSB', 'Are they ashamed of the abomination they have committed? No, they have no shame at all; they do not even know how to blush. So they will fall among the fallen; when I punish them, they will collapse,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.16', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Stand at the crossroads and look. Ask for the ancient paths: ‘Where is the good way?’ Then walk in it, and you will find rest for your souls. But they said, ‘We will not walk in it!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.17', 'BSB', 'I appointed watchmen over you and said, ‘Listen for the sound of the ram’s horn.’ But they answered, ‘We will not listen!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore hear, O nations, and learn, O congregations, what will happen to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.19', 'BSB', 'Hear, O earth! I am bringing disaster on this people, the fruit of their own schemes, because they have paid no attention to My word and have rejected My instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.20', 'BSB', 'What use to Me is frankincense from Sheba or sweet cane from a distant land? Your burnt offerings are not acceptable; your sacrifices do not please Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: “I will lay stumbling blocks before this people; fathers and sons alike will be staggered; friends and neighbors will perish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.22', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Behold, an army is coming from the land of the north; a great nation is stirred up from the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.23', 'BSB', 'They grasp the bow and spear; they are cruel and merciless. Their voice roars like the sea, and they ride upon horses, lined up like men in formation against you, O Daughter of Zion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.24', 'BSB', 'We have heard the report; our hands hang limp. Anguish has gripped us, pain like that of a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.25', 'BSB', 'Do not go out to the fields; do not walk the road. For the enemy has a sword; terror is on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.26', 'BSB', 'O daughter of my people, dress yourselves in sackcloth and roll in ashes. Mourn with bitter wailing, as you would for an only son, for suddenly the destroyer will come upon us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.27', 'BSB', '“I have appointed you to examine My people like ore, so you may know and try their ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.28', 'BSB', 'All are hardened rebels, walking around as slanderers. They are bronze and iron; all of them are corrupt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.29', 'BSB', 'The bellows blow fiercely, blasting away the lead with fire. The refining proceeds in vain, for the wicked are not purged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.6.30', 'BSB', 'They are called rejected silver, because the LORD has rejected them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.2', 'BSB', '“Stand in the gate of the house of the LORD and proclaim this message: Hear the word of the LORD, all you people of Judah who enter through these gates to worship the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.3', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel: Correct your ways and deeds, and I will let you live in this place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.4', 'BSB', 'Do not trust in deceptive words, chanting: ‘This is the temple of the LORD, the temple of the LORD, the temple of the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.5', 'BSB', 'For if you really correct your ways and deeds, if you act justly toward one another,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.6', 'BSB', 'if you no longer oppress the foreigner and the fatherless and the widow, and if you no longer shed innocent blood in this place or follow other gods to your own harm,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.7', 'BSB', 'then I will let you live in this place, in the land that I gave to your fathers forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.8', 'BSB', 'But look, you keep trusting in deceptive words to no avail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.9', 'BSB', 'Will you steal and murder, commit adultery and perjury, burn incense to Baal, and follow other gods that you have not known,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.10', 'BSB', 'and then come and stand before Me in this house, which bears My Name, and say, ‘We are delivered, so we can continue with all these abominations’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.11', 'BSB', 'Has this house, which bears My Name, become a den of robbers in your sight? Yes, I too have seen it, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.12', 'BSB', 'But go now to the place in Shiloh where I first made a dwelling for My Name, and see what I did to it because of the wickedness of My people Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.13', 'BSB', 'And now, because you have done all these things, declares the LORD, and because I have spoken to you again and again but you would not listen, and I have called to you but you would not answer,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.14', 'BSB', 'therefore what I did to Shiloh I will now do to the house that bears My Name, the house in which you trust, the place that I gave to you and your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.15', 'BSB', 'And I will cast you out of My presence, just as I have cast out all your brothers, all the descendants of Ephraim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.16', 'BSB', 'As for you, do not pray for these people, do not offer a plea or petition on their behalf, and do not beg Me, for I will not listen to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.17', 'BSB', 'Do you not see what they are doing in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.18', 'BSB', 'The sons gather wood, the fathers light the fire, and the women knead the dough to make cakes for the Queen of Heaven; they pour out drink offerings to other gods to provoke Me to anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.19', 'BSB', 'But am I the One they are provoking? declares the LORD. Is it not themselves they spite, to their own shame?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, My anger and My fury will be poured out on this place, on man and beast, on the trees of the field and the produce of the land, and it will burn and not be extinguished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.21', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Add your burnt offerings to your other sacrifices and eat the meat yourselves!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.22', 'BSB', 'For when I brought your fathers out of the land of Egypt, I did not merely command them about burnt offerings and sacrifices,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.23', 'BSB', 'but this is what I commanded them: Obey Me, and I will be your God, and you will be My people. You must walk in all the ways I have commanded you, so that it may go well with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.24', 'BSB', 'Yet they did not listen or incline their ear, but they followed the stubborn inclinations of their own evil hearts. They went backward and not forward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.25', 'BSB', 'From the day your fathers came out of the land of Egypt until this day, I have sent you all My servants the prophets again and again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.26', 'BSB', 'Yet they would not listen to Me or incline their ear, but they stiffened their necks and did more evil than their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.27', 'BSB', 'When you tell them all these things, they will not listen to you. When you call to them, they will not answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore you must say to them, ‘This is the nation that would not listen to the voice of the LORD their God and would not receive correction. Truth has perished; it has disappeared from their lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.29', 'BSB', 'Cut off your hair and throw it away. Raise up a lamentation on the barren heights, for the LORD has rejected and forsaken the generation of His wrath.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.30', 'BSB', 'For the people of Judah have done evil in My sight, declares the LORD. They have set up their abominations in the house that bears My Name, and so have defiled it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.31', 'BSB', 'They have built the high places of Topheth in the Valley of Hinnom so they could burn their sons and daughters in the fire—something I never commanded, nor did it even enter My mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.32', 'BSB', 'So behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when this place will no longer be called Topheth and the Valley of Hinnom, but the Valley of Slaughter. For they will bury the dead in Topheth until there is no more room.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.33', 'BSB', 'The corpses of this people will become food for the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth, and there will be no one to scare them away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.7.34', 'BSB', 'I will remove from the cities of Judah and the streets of Jerusalem the sounds of joy and gladness and the voices of the bride and bridegroom, for the land will become a wasteland.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.1', 'BSB', '“At that time,” declares the LORD, “the bones of the kings of Judah, the bones of the officials, the bones of the priests, the bones of the prophets, and the bones of the people of Jerusalem will be removed from their graves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.2', 'BSB', 'They will be exposed to the sun and moon, and to all the host of heaven which they have loved, served, followed, consulted, and worshiped. Their bones will not be gathered up or buried, but will become like dung lying on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.3', 'BSB', 'And wherever I have banished them, the remnant of this evil family will choose death over life,” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.4', 'BSB', 'So you are to tell them this is what the LORD says: “Do men fall and not get up again? Does one turn away and not return?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.5', 'BSB', 'Why then have these people turned away? Why does Jerusalem always turn away? They cling to deceit; they refuse to return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.6', 'BSB', 'I have listened and heard; they do not speak what is right. No one repents of his wickedness, asking, ‘What have I done?’ Everyone has pursued his own course like a horse charging into battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.7', 'BSB', 'Even the stork in the sky knows her appointed seasons. The turtledove, the swift, and the thrush keep their time of migration, but My people do not know the requirements of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.8', 'BSB', 'How can you say, ‘We are wise, and the Law of the LORD is with us,’ when in fact the lying pen of the scribes has produced a deception?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.9', 'BSB', 'The wise will be put to shame; they will be dismayed and trapped. Since they have rejected the word of the LORD, what wisdom do they really have?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will give their wives to other men and their fields to new owners. For from the least of them to the greatest, all are greedy for gain; from prophet to priest, all practice deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.11', 'BSB', 'They dress the wound of the daughter of My people with very little care, saying, ‘Peace, peace,’ when there is no peace at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.12', 'BSB', 'Are they ashamed of the abomination they have committed? No, they have no shame at all; they do not even know how to blush. So they will fall among the fallen; when I punish them, they will collapse, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.13', 'BSB', 'I will take away their harvest, declares the LORD. There will be no grapes on the vine, nor figs on the tree, and even the leaf will wither. Whatever I have given them will be lost to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.14', 'BSB', 'Why are we just sitting here? Gather together, let us flee to the fortified cities and perish there, for the LORD our God has doomed us. He has given us poisoned water to drink, because we have sinned against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.15', 'BSB', 'We hoped for peace, but no good has come, for a time of healing, but there was only terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.16', 'BSB', 'The snorting of enemy horses is heard from Dan. At the sound of the neighing of mighty steeds, the whole land quakes. They come to devour the land and everything in it, the city and all who dwell in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.17', 'BSB', '“For behold, I will send snakes among you, vipers that cannot be charmed, and they will bite you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.18', 'BSB', 'My sorrow is beyond healing; my heart is faint within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.19', 'BSB', 'Listen to the cry of the daughter of my people from a land far away: “Is the LORD no longer in Zion? Is her King no longer there?” “Why have they provoked Me to anger with their carved images, with their worthless foreign idols?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.20', 'BSB', '“The harvest has passed, the summer has ended, but we have not been saved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.21', 'BSB', 'For the brokenness of the daughter of my people I am crushed. I mourn; horror has gripped me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.8.22', 'BSB', 'Is there no balm in Gilead? Is no physician there? Why then has the health of the daughter of my people not been restored?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.1', 'BSB', 'Oh, that my head were a spring of water, and my eyes a fountain of tears! I would weep day and night over the slain daughter of my people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.2', 'BSB', 'If only I had a traveler’s lodge in the wilderness, I would abandon my people and depart from them, for they are all adulterers, a crowd of faithless people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.3', 'BSB', '“They bend their tongues like bows; lies prevail over truth in the land. For they proceed from evil to evil, and they do not take Me into account,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.4', 'BSB', '“Let everyone guard against his neighbor; do not trust any brother, for every brother deals craftily, and every friend spreads slander.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.5', 'BSB', 'Each one betrays his friend; no one tells the truth. They have taught their tongues to lie; they wear themselves out committing iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.6', 'BSB', 'You dwell in the midst of deception; in their deceit they refuse to know Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Behold, I will refine them and test them, for what else can I do because of the daughter of My people?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.8', 'BSB', 'Their tongues are deadly arrows; they speak deception. With his mouth a man speaks peace to his neighbor, but in his heart he sets a trap for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.9', 'BSB', 'Should I not punish them for these things? declares the LORD. Should I not avenge Myself on such a nation as this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.10', 'BSB', 'I will take up a weeping and wailing for the mountains, a dirge over the wilderness pasture, for they have been scorched so no one passes through, and the lowing of cattle is not heard. Both the birds of the air and the beasts have fled; they have gone away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.11', 'BSB', '“And I will make Jerusalem a heap of rubble, a haunt for jackals; and I will make the cities of Judah a desolation, without inhabitant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.12', 'BSB', 'Who is the man wise enough to understand this? To whom has the mouth of the LORD spoken, that he may explain it? Why is the land destroyed and scorched like a desert, so no one can pass through it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.13', 'BSB', 'And the LORD answered, “It is because they have forsaken My law, which I set before them; they have not walked in it or obeyed My voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.14', 'BSB', 'Instead, they have followed the stubbornness of their hearts and gone after the Baals, as their fathers taught them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “Behold, I will feed this people wormwood and give them poisoned water to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.16', 'BSB', 'I will scatter them among the nations that neither they nor their fathers have known, and I will send a sword after them until I have finished them off.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.17', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Take note, and summon the wailing women; send for the most skillful among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.18', 'BSB', 'Let them come quickly and take up a lament over us, that our eyes may overflow with tears, and our eyelids may gush with water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.19', 'BSB', 'For the sound of wailing is heard from Zion: ‘How devastated we are! How great is our shame! For we have abandoned the land because our dwellings have been torn down.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.20', 'BSB', 'Now, O women, hear the word of the LORD. Open your ears to the word of His mouth. Teach your daughters to wail, and one another to lament.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.21', 'BSB', 'For death has climbed in through our windows; it has entered our fortresses to cut off the children from the streets, the young men from the town squares.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.22', 'BSB', 'Declare that this is what the LORD says: “The corpses of men will fall like dung upon the open field, like newly cut grain behind the reaper, with no one to gather it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.23', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Let not the wise man boast in his wisdom, nor the strong man in his strength, nor the wealthy man in his riches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.24', 'BSB', 'But let him who boasts boast in this, that he understands and knows Me, that I am the LORD, who exercises loving devotion, justice and righteousness on the earth— for I delight in these things,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.25', 'BSB', '“Behold, the days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when I will punish all who are circumcised yet uncircumcised:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.9.26', 'BSB', 'Egypt, Judah, Edom, Ammon, Moab, and all the inhabitants of the desert who clip the hair of their temples. For all these nations are uncircumcised, and the whole house of Israel is uncircumcised in heart.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.1', 'BSB', 'Hear the word that the LORD speaks to you, O house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Do not learn the ways of the nations or be terrified by the signs in the heavens, though the nations themselves are terrified by them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.3', 'BSB', 'For the customs of the peoples are worthless; they cut down a tree from the forest; it is shaped with a chisel by the hands of a craftsman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.4', 'BSB', 'They adorn it with silver and gold and fasten it with hammer and nails, so that it will not totter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.5', 'BSB', 'Like scarecrows in a cucumber patch, their idols cannot speak. They must be carried because they cannot walk. Do not fear them, for they can do no harm, and neither can they do any good.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.6', 'BSB', 'There is none like You, O LORD. You are great, and Your name is mighty in power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.7', 'BSB', 'Who would not fear You, O King of nations? This is Your due. For among all the wise men of the nations, and in all their kingdoms, there is none like You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.8', 'BSB', 'But they are altogether senseless and foolish, instructed by worthless idols made of wood!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.9', 'BSB', 'Hammered silver is brought from Tarshish, and gold from Uphaz— the work of a craftsman from the hands of a goldsmith. Their clothes are blue and purple, all fashioned by skilled workers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.10', 'BSB', 'But the LORD is the true God; He is the living God and eternal King. The earth quakes at His wrath, and the nations cannot endure His indignation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.11', 'BSB', 'Thus you are to tell them: “These gods, who have made neither the heavens nor the earth, will perish from this earth and from under these heavens.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.12', 'BSB', 'The LORD made the earth by His power; He established the world by His wisdom and stretched out the heavens by His understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.13', 'BSB', 'When He thunders, the waters in the heavens roar; He causes the clouds to rise from the ends of the earth. He generates the lightning with the rain and brings forth the wind from His storehouses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.14', 'BSB', 'Every man is senseless and devoid of knowledge; every goldsmith is put to shame by his idols. For his molten images are a fraud, and there is no breath in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.15', 'BSB', 'They are worthless, a work to be mocked. In the time of their punishment they will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.16', 'BSB', 'The Portion of Jacob is not like these, for He is the Maker of all things, and Israel is the tribe of His inheritance— the LORD of Hosts is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.17', 'BSB', 'Gather up your belongings from this land, you who live under siege.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.18', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “Behold, at this time I will sling out the inhabitants of the land and bring distress upon them so that they may be captured.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.19', 'BSB', 'Woe to me because of my brokenness; my wound is grievous! But I said, “This is truly my sickness, and I must bear it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.20', 'BSB', 'My tent is destroyed, and all its ropes are snapped. My sons have departed from me and are no more. I have no one left to pitch my tent or set up my curtains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.21', 'BSB', 'For the shepherds have become senseless; they do not seek the LORD. Therefore they have not prospered, and all their flock is scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.22', 'BSB', 'Listen! The sound of a report is coming— a great commotion from the land to the north. The cities of Judah will be made a desolation, a haunt for jackals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.23', 'BSB', 'I know, O LORD, that a man’s way is not his own; no one who walks directs his own steps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.24', 'BSB', 'Correct me, O LORD, but only with justice— not in Your anger, or You will bring me to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.10.25', 'BSB', 'Pour out Your wrath on the nations that do not acknowledge You, and on the families that do not call on Your name. For they have devoured Jacob; they have consumed him and finished him off; they have devastated his homeland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.2', 'BSB', '“Listen to the words of this covenant and tell them to the men of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.3', 'BSB', 'You must tell them that this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: Cursed is the man who does not obey the words of this covenant,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.4', 'BSB', 'which I commanded your forefathers when I brought them out of the land of Egypt, out of the iron furnace, saying, ‘Obey Me, and do everything I command you, and you will be My people, and I will be your God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.5', 'BSB', 'This was in order to establish the oath I swore to your forefathers, to give them a land flowing with milk and honey, as it is to this day.” “Amen, LORD,” I answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.6', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Proclaim all these words in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem, saying: Hear the words of this covenant and carry them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.7', 'BSB', 'For from the time I brought your fathers out of the land of Egypt until today, I strongly warned them again and again, saying, ‘Obey My voice.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.8', 'BSB', 'Yet they would not obey or incline their ears, but each one followed the stubbornness of his evil heart. So I brought on them all the curses of this covenant I had commanded them to follow but they did not keep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.9', 'BSB', 'And the LORD told me, “There is a conspiracy among the men of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.10', 'BSB', 'They have returned to the sins of their forefathers who refused to obey My words. They have followed other gods to serve them. The house of Israel and the house of Judah have broken the covenant I made with their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: ‘I am about to bring upon them a disaster that they cannot escape. They will cry out to Me, but I will not listen to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.12', 'BSB', 'Then the cities of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem will go and cry out to the gods to which they have been burning incense, but these gods certainly will not save them in their time of disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.13', 'BSB', 'Your gods are indeed as numerous as your cities, O Judah; the altars of shame you have set up—the altars to burn incense to Baal—are as many as the streets of Jerusalem.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.14', 'BSB', 'As for you, do not pray for these people. Do not raise up a cry or a prayer on their behalf, for I will not be listening when they call out to Me in their time of disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.15', 'BSB', 'What right has My beloved in My house, having carried out so many evil schemes? Can consecrated meat avert your doom, so that you can rejoice?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.16', 'BSB', 'The LORD once called you a flourishing olive tree, beautiful with well-formed fruit. But with a mighty roar He will set it on fire, and its branches will be consumed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.17', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts, who planted you, has decreed disaster against you on account of the evil that the house of Israel and the house of Judah have brought upon themselves, provoking Me to anger by burning incense to Baal.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.18', 'BSB', 'And the LORD informed me, so I knew. Then You showed me their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.19', 'BSB', 'For I was like a gentle lamb led to slaughter; I did not know that they had plotted against me: “Let us destroy the tree with its fruit; let us cut him off from the land of the living, that his name may be remembered no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.20', 'BSB', 'O LORD of Hosts, who judges righteously, who examines the heart and mind, let me see Your vengeance upon them, for to You I have committed my cause.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says concerning the people of Anathoth who are seeking your life and saying, “You must not prophesy in the name of the LORD, or you will die by our hand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.22', 'BSB', 'So this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “I will punish them. Their young men will die by the sword, their sons and daughters by famine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.11.23', 'BSB', 'There will be no remnant, for I will bring disaster on the people of Anathoth in the year of their punishment.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.1', 'BSB', 'Righteous are You, O LORD, when I plead before You. Yet about Your judgments I wish to contend with You: Why does the way of the wicked prosper? Why do all the faithless live at ease?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.2', 'BSB', 'You planted them, and they have taken root. They have grown and produced fruit. You are ever on their lips, but far from their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.3', 'BSB', 'But You know me, O LORD; You see me and test my heart toward You. Drag away the wicked like sheep to the slaughter and set them apart for the day of carnage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.4', 'BSB', 'How long will the land mourn and the grass of every field be withered? Because of the evil of its residents, the animals and birds have been swept away, for the people have said, “He cannot see what our end will be.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.5', 'BSB', '“If you have raced with men on foot and they have worn you out, how can you compete with horses? If you stumble in a peaceful land, how will you do in the thickets of the Jordan?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.6', 'BSB', 'Even your brothers— your own father’s household— even they have betrayed you; even they have cried aloud against you. Do not trust them, though they speak well of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.7', 'BSB', 'I have forsaken My house; I have abandoned My inheritance. I have given the love of My life into the hands of her enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.8', 'BSB', 'My inheritance has become to Me like a lion in the forest. She has roared against Me; therefore I hate her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.9', 'BSB', 'Is not My inheritance to Me like a speckled bird of prey with other birds of prey circling against her? Go, gather all the beasts of the field; bring them to devour her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.10', 'BSB', 'Many shepherds have destroyed My vineyard; they have trampled My plot of ground. They have turned My pleasant field into a desolate wasteland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.11', 'BSB', 'They have made it a desolation; desolate before Me, it mourns. All the land is laid waste, but no man takes it to heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.12', 'BSB', 'Over all the barren heights in the wilderness the destroyers have come, for the sword of the LORD devours from one end of the earth to the other. No flesh has peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.13', 'BSB', 'They have sown wheat but harvested thorns. They have exhausted themselves to no avail. Bear the shame of your harvest because of the fierce anger of the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.14', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “As for all My evil neighbors who attack the inheritance that I bequeathed to My people Israel, I am about to uproot them from their land, and I will uproot the house of Judah from among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.15', 'BSB', 'But after I have uprooted them, I will once again have compassion on them and return each one to his inheritance and to his land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.16', 'BSB', 'And if they will diligently learn the ways of My people and swear by My name, saying, ‘As surely as the LORD lives’—just as they once taught My people to swear by Baal—then they will be established among My people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.12.17', 'BSB', 'But if they will not obey, then I will uproot that nation; I will uproot it and destroy it, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD said to me: “Go and buy yourself a linen loincloth and put it around your waist, but do not let it touch water.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.2', 'BSB', 'So I bought a loincloth as the LORD had instructed me, and I put it around my waist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.3', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me a second time:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.4', 'BSB', '“Take the loincloth that you bought and are wearing, and go at once to Perath and hide it there in a crevice of the rocks.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.5', 'BSB', 'So I went and hid it at Perath, as the LORD had commanded me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.6', 'BSB', 'Many days later the LORD said to me, “Arise, go to Perath, and get the loincloth that I commanded you to hide there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.7', 'BSB', 'So I went to Perath and dug up the loincloth, and I took it from the place where I had hidden it. But now it was ruined—of no use at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.8', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.9', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD says: In the same way I will ruin the pride of Judah and the great pride of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.10', 'BSB', 'These evil people, who refuse to listen to My words, who follow the stubbornness of their own hearts, and who go after other gods to serve and worship them, they will be like this loincloth—of no use at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.11', 'BSB', 'For just as a loincloth clings to a man’s waist, so I have made the whole house of Israel and the whole house of Judah cling to Me, declares the LORD, so that they might be My people for My renown and praise and glory. But they did not listen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore you are to tell them that this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Every wineskin shall be filled with wine.’ And when they reply, ‘Don’t we surely know that every wineskin should be filled with wine?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.13', 'BSB', 'then you are to tell them that this is what the LORD says: ‘I am going to fill with drunkenness all who live in this land—the kings who sit on David’s throne, the priests, the prophets, and all the people of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.14', 'BSB', 'I will smash them against one another, fathers and sons alike, declares the LORD. I will allow no mercy or pity or compassion to keep Me from destroying them.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.15', 'BSB', 'Listen and give heed. Do not be arrogant, for the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.16', 'BSB', 'Give glory to the LORD your God before He brings darkness, before your feet stumble on the dusky mountains. You wait for light, but He turns it into deep gloom and thick darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.17', 'BSB', 'But if you do not listen, I will weep in secret because of your pride. My eyes will overflow with tears, because the LORD’s flock has been taken captive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.18', 'BSB', 'Say to the king and to the queen mother: “Take a lowly seat, for your glorious crowns have fallen from your heads.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.19', 'BSB', 'The cities of the Negev have been shut tight, and no one can open them. All Judah has been carried into exile, wholly taken captive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.20', 'BSB', 'Lift up your eyes and see those coming from the north. Where is the flock entrusted to you, the sheep that were your pride?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.21', 'BSB', 'What will you say when He sets over you close allies whom you yourself trained? Will not pangs of anguish grip you, as they do a woman in labor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.22', 'BSB', 'And if you ask yourself, “Why has this happened to me?” It is because of the magnitude of your iniquity that your skirts have been stripped off and your body has been exposed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.23', 'BSB', 'Can the Ethiopian change his skin, or the leopard his spots? Neither are you able to do good— you who are accustomed to doing evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.24', 'BSB', '“I will scatter you like chaff driven by the desert wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.25', 'BSB', 'This is your lot, the portion I have measured to you,” declares the LORD, “because you have forgotten Me and trusted in falsehood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.26', 'BSB', 'So I will pull your skirts up over your face, that your shame may be seen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.13.27', 'BSB', 'Your adulteries and lustful neighings, your shameless prostitution on the hills and in the fields— I have seen your detestable acts. Woe to you, O Jerusalem! How long will you remain unclean?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah concerning the drought:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.2', 'BSB', '“Judah mourns and her gates languish. Her people wail for the land, and a cry goes up from Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.3', 'BSB', 'The nobles send their servants for water; they go to the cisterns, but find no water; their jars return empty. They are ashamed and humiliated; they cover their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.4', 'BSB', 'The ground is cracked because no rain has fallen on the land. The farmers are ashamed; they cover their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.5', 'BSB', 'Even the doe in the field deserts her newborn fawn because there is no grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.6', 'BSB', 'Wild donkeys stand on barren heights; they pant for air like jackals; their eyes fail for lack of pasture.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.7', 'BSB', 'Although our iniquities testify against us, O LORD, act for the sake of Your name. Indeed, our rebellions are many; we have sinned against You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.8', 'BSB', 'O Hope of Israel, its Savior in times of distress, why are You like a stranger in the land, like a traveler who stays but a night?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.9', 'BSB', 'Why are You like a man taken by surprise, like a warrior powerless to save? Yet You are among us, O LORD, and we are called by Your name. Do not forsake us!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.10', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says about this people: “Truly they love to wander; they have not restrained their feet. So the LORD does not accept them; He will now remember their guilt and call their sins to account.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.11', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Do not pray for the well-being of this people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.12', 'BSB', 'Although they may fast, I will not listen to their cry; although they may offer burnt offerings and grain offerings, I will not accept them. Instead, I will finish them off by sword and famine and plague.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.13', 'BSB', '“Ah, Lord GOD!” I replied, “Look, the prophets are telling them, ‘You will not see the sword or suffer famine, but I will give you lasting peace in this place.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.14', 'BSB', '“The prophets are prophesying lies in My name,” replied the LORD. “I did not send them or appoint them or speak to them. They are prophesying to you a false vision, a worthless divination, the futility and delusion of their own minds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says about the prophets who prophesy in My name: I did not send them, yet they say, ‘No sword or famine will touch this land.’ By sword and famine these very prophets will meet their end!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.16', 'BSB', 'And the people to whom they prophesy will be thrown into the streets of Jerusalem because of famine and sword. There will be no one to bury them or their wives, their sons or their daughters. I will pour out their own evil upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.17', 'BSB', 'You are to speak this word to them: ‘My eyes overflow with tears; day and night they do not cease, for the virgin daughter of my people has been shattered by a crushing blow, a severely grievous wound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.18', 'BSB', 'If I go out to the country, I see those slain by the sword; if I enter the city, I see those ravaged by famine! For both prophet and priest travel to a land they do not know.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.19', 'BSB', 'Have You rejected Judah completely? Do You despise Zion? Why have You stricken us so that we are beyond healing? We hoped for peace, but no good has come, and for the time of healing, but there was only terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.20', 'BSB', 'We acknowledge our wickedness, O LORD, the guilt of our fathers; indeed, we have sinned against You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.21', 'BSB', 'For the sake of Your name do not despise us; do not disgrace Your glorious throne. Remember Your covenant with us; do not break it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.14.22', 'BSB', 'Can the worthless idols of the nations bring rain? Do the skies alone send showers? Is this not by You, O LORD our God? So we put our hope in You, for You have done all these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me: “Even if Moses and Samuel should stand before Me, My heart would not go out to this people. Send them from My presence, and let them go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.2', 'BSB', 'If they ask you, ‘Where shall we go?’ you are to tell them that this is what the LORD says: ‘Those destined for death, to death; those destined for the sword, to the sword; those destined for famine, to famine; and those destined for captivity, to captivity.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.3', 'BSB', 'I will appoint over them four kinds of destroyers, declares the LORD: the sword to kill, the dogs to drag away, and the birds of the air and beasts of the earth to devour and destroy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.4', 'BSB', 'I will make them a horror to all the kingdoms of the earth because of what Manasseh son of Hezekiah king of Judah did in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.5', 'BSB', 'Who will have pity on you, O Jerusalem? Who will mourn for you? Who will turn aside to ask about your welfare?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.6', 'BSB', 'You have forsaken Me, declares the LORD. You have turned your back. So I will stretch out My hand against you and I will destroy you; I am weary of showing compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.7', 'BSB', 'I will scatter them with a winnowing fork at the gates of the land. I will bereave and destroy My people who have not turned from their ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.8', 'BSB', 'I will make their widows more numerous than the sand of the sea. I will bring a destroyer at noon against the mothers of young men. I will suddenly bring upon them anguish and dismay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.9', 'BSB', 'The mother of seven will grow faint; she will breathe her last breath. Her sun will set while it is still day; she will be disgraced and humiliated. And the rest I will put to the sword in the presence of their enemies,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.10', 'BSB', 'Woe to me, my mother, that you have borne me, a man of strife and conflict in all the land. I have neither lent nor borrowed, yet everyone curses me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD said: “Surely I will deliver you for a good purpose; surely I will intercede with your enemy in your time of trouble, in your time of distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.12', 'BSB', 'Can anyone smash iron— iron from the north—or bronze?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.13', 'BSB', 'Your wealth and your treasures I will give up as plunder, without charge for all your sins within all your borders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.14', 'BSB', 'Then I will enslave you to your enemies in a land you do not know, for My anger will kindle a fire that will burn against you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.15', 'BSB', 'You understand, O LORD; remember me and attend to me. Avenge me against my persecutors. In Your patience, do not take me away. Know that I endure reproach for Your honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.16', 'BSB', 'Your words were found, and I ate them. Your words became my joy and my heart’s delight. For I bear Your name, O LORD God of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.17', 'BSB', 'I never sat with the band of revelers, nor did I celebrate with them. Because Your hand was on me, I sat alone, for You have filled me with indignation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.18', 'BSB', 'Why is my pain unending, and my wound incurable, refusing to be healed? You have indeed become like a mirage to me— water that is not there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: “If you return, I will restore you; you will stand in My presence. And if you speak words that are noble instead of worthless, you will be My spokesman. It is they who must turn to you, but you must not turn to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.20', 'BSB', 'Then I will make you a wall to this people, a fortified wall of bronze; they will fight against you but will not overcome you, for I am with you to save and deliver you, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.15.21', 'BSB', 'I will deliver you from the hand of the wicked and redeem you from the grasp of the ruthless.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.2', 'BSB', '“You must not marry or have sons or daughters in this place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.3', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says concerning the sons and daughters born in this place, and the mothers who bore them, and the fathers who fathered them in this land:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.4', 'BSB', '“They will die from deadly diseases. They will not be mourned or buried, but will lie like dung on the ground. They will be finished off by sword and famine, and their corpses will become food for the birds of the air and beasts of the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.5', 'BSB', 'Indeed, this is what the LORD says: “Do not enter a house where there is a funeral meal. Do not go to mourn or show sympathy, for I have removed from this people My peace, My loving devotion, and My compassion,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.6', 'BSB', '“Both great and small will die in this land. They will not be buried or mourned, nor will anyone cut himself or shave his head for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.7', 'BSB', 'No food will be offered to comfort those who mourn the dead; not even a cup of consolation will be given for the loss of a father or mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.8', 'BSB', 'You must not enter a house where there is feasting and sit down with them to eat and drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.9', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: I am going to remove from this place, before your very eyes and in your days, the sounds of joy and gladness, the voices of the bride and bridegroom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.10', 'BSB', 'When you tell these people all these things, they will ask you, ‘Why has the LORD pronounced all this great disaster against us? What is our guilt? What is the sin that we have committed against the LORD our God?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.11', 'BSB', 'Then you are to answer them: ‘It is because your fathers have forsaken Me, declares the LORD, and followed other gods, and served and worshiped them. They abandoned Me and did not keep My instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.12', 'BSB', 'And you have done more evil than your fathers. See how each of you follows the stubbornness of his evil heart instead of obeying Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.13', 'BSB', 'So I will cast you out of this land into a land that neither you nor your fathers have known. There you will serve other gods day and night, for I will show you no favor.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.14', 'BSB', 'Yet behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when they will no longer say, ‘As surely as the LORD lives, who brought the Israelites up out of the land of Egypt.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.15', 'BSB', 'Instead they will say, ‘As surely as the LORD lives, who brought the Israelites up out of the land of the north and all the other lands to which He had banished them.’ For I will return them to their land that I gave to their forefathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.16', 'BSB', 'But for now I will send for many fishermen, declares the LORD, and they will catch them. After that I will send for many hunters, and they will hunt them down on every mountain and hill, even from the clefts of the rocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.17', 'BSB', 'For My eyes are on all their ways. They are not hidden from My face, and their guilt is not concealed from My eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.18', 'BSB', 'And I will first repay them double their iniquity and their sin, because they have defiled My land with the carcasses of their detestable idols, and they have filled My inheritance with their abominations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.19', 'BSB', 'O LORD, my strength and my fortress, my refuge in the day of distress, the nations will come to You from the ends of the earth, and they will say, “Our fathers inherited nothing but lies, worthless idols of no benefit at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.20', 'BSB', 'Can man make gods for himself? Such are not gods!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.16.21', 'BSB', '“Therefore behold, I will inform them, and this time I will make them know My power and My might; then they will know that My name is the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.1', 'BSB', '“The sin of Judah is written with an iron stylus, engraved with a diamond point on the tablets of their hearts and on the horns of their altars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.2', 'BSB', 'Even their children remember their altars and Asherah poles by the green trees and on the high hills.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.3', 'BSB', 'O My mountain in the countryside, I will give over your wealth and all your treasures as plunder, because of the sin of your high places, within all your borders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.4', 'BSB', 'And you yourself will relinquish the inheritance that I gave you. I will enslave you to your enemies in a land that you do not know, for you have kindled My anger; it will burn forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Cursed is the man who trusts in mankind, who makes the flesh his strength and turns his heart from the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.6', 'BSB', 'He will be like a shrub in the desert; he will not see when prosperity comes. He will dwell in the parched places of the desert, in a salt land where no one lives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.7', 'BSB', 'But blessed is the man who trusts in the LORD, whose confidence is in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.8', 'BSB', 'He is like a tree planted by the waters that sends out its roots toward the stream. It does not fear when the heat comes, and its leaves are always green. It does not worry in a year of drought, nor does it cease to produce fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.9', 'BSB', 'The heart is deceitful above all things and beyond cure. Who can understand it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.10', 'BSB', 'I, the LORD, search the heart; I examine the mind to reward a man according to his way, by what his deeds deserve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.11', 'BSB', 'Like a partridge hatching eggs it did not lay is the man who makes a fortune unjustly. In the middle of his days his riches will desert him, and in the end he will be the fool.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.12', 'BSB', 'A glorious throne, exalted from the beginning, is the place of our sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.13', 'BSB', 'O LORD, the hope of Israel, all who abandon You will be put to shame. All who turn away will be written in the dust, for they have abandoned the LORD, the fountain of living water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.14', 'BSB', 'Heal me, O LORD, and I will be healed; save me, and I will be saved, for You are my praise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.15', 'BSB', 'Behold, they keep saying to me, “Where is the word of the LORD? Let it come now!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.16', 'BSB', 'But I have not run away from being Your shepherd; I have not desired the day of despair. You know that the utterance of my lips was spoken in Your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.17', 'BSB', 'Do not become a terror to me; You are my refuge in the day of disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.18', 'BSB', 'Let my persecutors be put to shame, but do not let me be put to shame. Let them be terrified, but do not let me be terrified. Bring upon them the day of disaster and shatter them with double destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.19', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD said to me: “Go and stand at the gate of the people, through which the kings of Judah go in and out; and stand at all the other gates of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.20', 'BSB', 'Say to them, ‘Hear the word of the LORD, O kings of Judah, all people of Judah and Jerusalem who enter through these gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.21', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: Take heed for yourselves; do not carry a load or bring it through the gates of Jerusalem on the Sabbath day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.22', 'BSB', 'You must not carry a load out of your houses or do any work on the Sabbath day, but you must keep the Sabbath day holy, just as I commanded your forefathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.23', 'BSB', 'Yet they would not listen or incline their ear, but they stiffened their necks and would not listen or receive My discipline.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.24', 'BSB', 'If, however, you listen carefully to Me, says the LORD, and bring no load through the gates of this city on the Sabbath day, and keep the Sabbath day holy, and do no work on it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.25', 'BSB', 'then kings and princes will enter through the gates of this city. They will sit on the throne of David, riding in chariots and on horses with their officials, along with the men of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem, and this city will be inhabited forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.26', 'BSB', 'And people will come from the cities of Judah and the places around Jerusalem, from the land of Benjamin, and from the foothills, the hill country, and the Negev, bringing burnt offerings and sacrifices, grain offerings and frankincense, and thank offerings to the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.17.27', 'BSB', 'But if you do not listen to Me to keep the Sabbath day holy by not carrying a load while entering the gates of Jerusalem on the Sabbath day, then I will kindle an unquenchable fire in its gates to consume the citadels of Jerusalem.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.2', 'BSB', '“Go down at once to the potter’s house, and there I will reveal My message to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.3', 'BSB', 'So I went down to the potter’s house and saw him working at the wheel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.4', 'BSB', 'But the vessel that he was shaping from the clay became flawed in his hand; so he formed it into another vessel, as it seemed best for him to do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.5', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.6', 'BSB', '“O house of Israel, declares the LORD, can I not treat you as this potter treats his clay? Just like clay in the potter’s hand, so are you in My hand, O house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.7', 'BSB', 'At any time I might announce that a nation or kingdom will be uprooted, torn down, and destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.8', 'BSB', 'But if that nation I warned turns from its evil, then I will relent of the disaster I had planned to bring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.9', 'BSB', 'And if at another time I announce that I will build up and establish a nation or kingdom,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.10', 'BSB', 'and if it does evil in My sight and does not listen to My voice, then I will relent of the good I had intended for it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.11', 'BSB', 'Now therefore, tell the men of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem that this is what the LORD says: ‘Behold, I am planning a disaster for you and devising a plan against you. Turn now, each of you, from your evil ways, and correct your ways and deeds.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.12', 'BSB', 'But they will reply, ‘It is hopeless. We will follow our own plans, and each of us will act according to the stubbornness of his evil heart.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: “Inquire among the nations: Who has ever heard things like these? Virgin Israel has done a most terrible thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.14', 'BSB', 'Does the snow of Lebanon ever leave its rocky slopes? Or do its cool waters flowing from a distance ever run dry?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.15', 'BSB', 'Yet My people have forgotten Me. They burn incense to worthless idols that make them stumble in their ways, leaving the ancient roads to walk on rutted bypaths instead of on the highway.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.16', 'BSB', 'They have made their land a desolation, a perpetual object of scorn; all who pass by will be appalled and shake their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.17', 'BSB', 'I will scatter them before the enemy like the east wind. I will show them My back and not My face in the day of their calamity.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.18', 'BSB', 'Then some said, “Come, let us make plans against Jeremiah, for the law will never be lost to the priest, nor counsel to the wise, nor an oracle to the prophet. Come, let us denounce him and pay no heed to any of his words.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.19', 'BSB', 'Attend to me, O LORD. Hear what my accusers are saying!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.20', 'BSB', 'Should good be repaid with evil? Yet they have dug a pit for me. Remember how I stood before You to speak good on their behalf, to turn Your wrath from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore, hand their children over to famine; pour out the power of the sword upon them. Let their wives become childless and widowed; let their husbands be slain by disease, their young men struck down by the sword in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.22', 'BSB', 'Let a cry be heard from their houses when You suddenly bring raiders against them, for they have dug a pit to capture me and have hidden snares for my feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.18.23', 'BSB', 'But You, O LORD, know all their deadly plots against me. Do not wipe out their guilt or blot out their sin from Your sight. Let them be overthrown before You; deal with them in the time of Your anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Go and buy a clay jar from a potter. Take some of the elders of the people and leaders of the priests,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.2', 'BSB', 'and go out to the Valley of Ben-hinnom near the entrance of the Potsherd Gate. Proclaim there the words I speak to you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.3', 'BSB', 'saying, ‘Hear the word of the LORD, O kings of Judah and residents of Jerusalem. This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: I am going to bring such disaster on this place that the ears of all who hear of it will ring,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.4', 'BSB', 'because they have abandoned Me and made this a foreign place. They have burned incense in this place to other gods that neither they nor their fathers nor the kings of Judah have ever known. They have filled this place with the blood of the innocent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.5', 'BSB', 'They have built high places to Baal on which to burn their children in the fire as offerings to Baal—something I never commanded or mentioned, nor did it even enter My mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.6', 'BSB', 'So behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when this place will no longer be called Topheth or the Valley of Ben-hinnom, but the Valley of Slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.7', 'BSB', 'And in this place I will ruin the plans of Judah and Jerusalem. I will make them fall by the sword before their enemies, by the hands of those who seek their lives, and I will give their carcasses as food to the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.8', 'BSB', 'I will make this city a desolation and an object of scorn. All who pass by will be appalled and will scoff at all her wounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.9', 'BSB', 'I will make them eat the flesh of their sons and daughters, and they will eat one another’s flesh in the siege and distress inflicted on them by their enemies who seek their lives.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.10', 'BSB', 'Then you are to shatter the jar in the presence of the men who accompany you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.11', 'BSB', 'and you are to proclaim to them that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: I will shatter this nation and this city, like one shatters a potter’s jar that can never again be repaired. They will bury the dead in Topheth until there is no more room to bury them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.12', 'BSB', 'This is what I will do to this place and to its residents, declares the LORD. I will make this city like Topheth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.13', 'BSB', 'The houses of Jerusalem and the houses of the kings of Judah will be defiled like that place, Topheth—all the houses on whose rooftops they burned incense to all the host of heaven and poured out drink offerings to other gods.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.14', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah returned from Topheth, where the LORD had sent him to prophesy, and he stood in the courtyard of the house of the LORD and proclaimed to all the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.19.15', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘Behold, I am about to bring on this city and on all the villages around it every disaster I have pronounced against them, because they have stiffened their necks so as not to heed My words.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.1', 'BSB', 'When Pashhur the priest, the son of Immer and the chief official in the house of the LORD, heard Jeremiah prophesying these things,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.2', 'BSB', 'he had Jeremiah the prophet beaten and put in the stocks at the Upper Gate of Benjamin, which was by the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.3', 'BSB', 'The next day, when Pashhur released Jeremiah from the stocks, Jeremiah said to him, “The LORD does not call you Pashhur, but Magor-missabib.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: ‘I will make you a terror to yourself and to all your friends. They will fall by the sword of their enemies before your very eyes. And I will hand Judah over to the king of Babylon, and he will carry them away to Babylon and put them to the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.5', 'BSB', 'I will give away all the wealth of this city—all its products and valuables, and all the treasures of the kings of Judah—to their enemies. They will plunder them, seize them, and carry them off to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.6', 'BSB', 'And you, Pashhur, and all who live in your house, will go into captivity. You will go to Babylon, and there you will die and be buried—you and all your friends to whom you have prophesied these lies.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.7', 'BSB', 'You have deceived me, O LORD, and I was deceived. You have overcome me and prevailed. I am a laughingstock all day long; everyone mocks me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.8', 'BSB', 'For whenever I speak, I cry out; I proclaim violence and destruction. For the word of the LORD has become to me a reproach and derision all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.9', 'BSB', 'If I say, “I will not mention Him or speak any more in His name,” His message becomes a fire burning in my heart, shut up in my bones, and I become weary of holding it in, and I cannot prevail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.10', 'BSB', 'For I have heard the whispering of many: “Terror is on every side! Report him; let us report him!” All my trusted friends watch for my fall: “Perhaps he will be deceived so that we may prevail against him and take our vengeance upon him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.11', 'BSB', 'But the LORD is with me like a fearsome warrior. Therefore, my persecutors will stumble and will not prevail. Since they have not succeeded, they will be utterly put to shame, with an everlasting disgrace that will never be forgotten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.12', 'BSB', 'O LORD of Hosts, who examines the righteous, who sees the heart and mind, let me see Your vengeance upon them, for to You I have committed my cause.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.13', 'BSB', 'Sing to the LORD! Praise the LORD! For He rescues the life of the needy from the hands of evildoers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.14', 'BSB', 'Cursed be the day I was born! May the day my mother bore me never be blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.15', 'BSB', 'Cursed be the man who brought my father the news, saying, “A son is born to you,” bringing him great joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.16', 'BSB', 'May that man be like the cities that the LORD overthrew without compassion. May he hear an outcry in the morning and a battle cry at noon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.17', 'BSB', 'because he did not kill me in the womb so that my mother might have been my grave, and her womb forever enlarged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.20.18', 'BSB', 'Why did I come out of the womb to see only trouble and sorrow, and to end my days in shame?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD when King Zedekiah sent to him Pashhur son of Malchijah and the priest Zephaniah son of Maaseiah. They said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.2', 'BSB', '“Please inquire of the LORD on our behalf, since Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon is waging war against us. Perhaps the LORD will perform for us something like all His past wonders, so that Nebuchadnezzar will withdraw from us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.3', 'BSB', 'But Jeremiah answered, “You are to tell Zedekiah that', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.4', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘I will turn against you the weapons of war in your hands, with which you are fighting the king of Babylon and the Chaldeans who besiege you outside the wall, and I will assemble their forces in the center of this city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.5', 'BSB', 'And I Myself will fight against you with an outstretched hand and a mighty arm, with anger, fury, and great wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.6', 'BSB', 'I will strike down the residents of this city, both man and beast. They will die in a terrible plague.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.7', 'BSB', '‘After that,’ declares the LORD, ‘I will hand over Zedekiah king of Judah, his officers, and the people in this city who survive the plague and sword and famine, to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and to their enemies who seek their lives. He will put them to the sword; he will not spare them or show pity or compassion.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.8', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, you are to tell this people that this is what the LORD says: ‘Behold, I set before you the way of life and the way of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.9', 'BSB', 'Whoever stays in this city will die by sword and famine and plague, but whoever goes out and surrenders to the Chaldeans who besiege you will live; he will retain his life like a spoil of war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.10', 'BSB', 'For I have set My face against this city to bring disaster and not good, declares the LORD. It will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, who will destroy it with fire.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.11', 'BSB', 'Moreover, tell the house of the king of Judah to hear the word of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.12', 'BSB', 'O house of David, this is what the LORD says: ‘Administer justice every morning, and rescue the victim of robbery from the hand of his oppressor, or My wrath will go forth like fire and burn with no one to extinguish it because of their evil deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.13', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am against you who dwell above the valley, atop the rocky plateau— declares the LORD— you who say, “Who can come against us? Who can enter our dwellings?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.21.14', 'BSB', 'I will punish you as your deeds deserve, declares the LORD. I will kindle a fire in your forest that will consume everything around you.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Go down to the palace of the king of Judah and proclaim this message there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.2', 'BSB', 'saying, ‘Hear the word of the LORD, O king of Judah, who sits on the throne of David—you and your officials and your people who enter these gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: Administer justice and righteousness. Rescue the victim of robbery from the hand of his oppressor. Do no wrong or violence to the foreigner, the fatherless, or the widow. Do not shed innocent blood in this place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.4', 'BSB', 'For if you will indeed carry out these commands, then kings who sit on David’s throne will enter through the gates of this palace riding on chariots and horses—they and their officials and their people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.5', 'BSB', 'But if you do not obey these words, then I swear by Myself, declares the LORD, that this house will become a pile of rubble.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says concerning the house of the king of Judah: “You are like Gilead to Me, like the summit of Lebanon; but I will surely turn you into a desert, like cities that are uninhabited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.7', 'BSB', 'I will appoint destroyers against you, each man with his weapons, and they will cut down the choicest of your cedars and throw them into the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.8', 'BSB', 'And many nations will pass by this city and ask one another, ‘Why has the LORD done such a thing to this great city?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.9', 'BSB', 'Then people will reply, ‘Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD their God and have worshiped and served other gods.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.10', 'BSB', 'Do not weep for the dead king; do not mourn his loss. Weep bitterly for the one who is exiled, for he will never return to see his native land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.11', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says concerning Shallum son of Josiah, king of Judah, who succeeded his father Josiah but has gone forth from this place: “He will never return,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.12', 'BSB', 'but he will die in the place to which he was exiled; he will never see this land again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.13', 'BSB', '“Woe to him who builds his palace by unrighteousness, and his upper rooms without justice, who makes his countrymen serve without pay, and fails to pay their wages,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.14', 'BSB', 'who says, ‘I will build myself a great palace, with spacious upper rooms.’ So he cuts windows in it, panels it with cedar, and paints it with vermilion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.15', 'BSB', 'Does it make you a king to excel in cedar? Did not your father have food and drink? He administered justice and righteousness, and so it went well with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.16', 'BSB', 'He took up the cause of the poor and needy, and so it went well with him. Is this not what it means to know Me?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.17', 'BSB', '“But your eyes and heart are set on nothing except your own dishonest gain, on shedding innocent blood, on practicing extortion and oppression.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says concerning Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah: “They will not mourn for him: ‘Alas, my brother! Alas, my sister!’ They will not mourn for him: ‘Alas, my master! Alas, his splendor!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.19', 'BSB', 'He will be buried like a donkey, dragged away and thrown outside the gates of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.20', 'BSB', 'Go up to Lebanon and cry out; raise your voice in Bashan; cry out from Abarim, for all your lovers have been crushed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.21', 'BSB', 'I warned you when you were secure. You said, ‘I will not listen.’ This has been your way from youth, that you have not obeyed My voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.22', 'BSB', 'The wind will drive away all your shepherds, and your lovers will go into captivity. Then you will be ashamed and humiliated because of all your wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.23', 'BSB', 'O inhabitant of Lebanon, nestled in the cedars, how you will groan when pangs of anguish come upon you, agony like a woman in labor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.24', 'BSB', '“As surely as I live,” declares the LORD, “even if you, Coniah son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, were a signet ring on My right hand, I would pull you off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.25', 'BSB', 'In fact, I will hand you over to those you dread, who want to take your life—to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and to the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.26', 'BSB', 'I will hurl you and the mother who gave you birth into another land, where neither of you were born—and there you both will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.27', 'BSB', 'You will never return to the land for which you long.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.28', 'BSB', 'Is this man Coniah a despised and shattered pot, a jar that no one wants? Why are he and his descendants hurled out and cast into a land they do not know?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.29', 'BSB', 'O land, land, land, hear the word of the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.22.30', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Enroll this man as childless, a man who will not prosper in his lifetime. None of his descendants will prosper to sit on the throne of David or to rule again in Judah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.1', 'BSB', '“Woe to the shepherds who destroy and scatter the sheep of My pasture!” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.2', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says about the shepherds who tend My people: “You have scattered My flock and driven them away, and have not attended to them. Behold, I will attend to you for the evil of your deeds, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.3', 'BSB', 'Then I Myself will gather the remnant of My flock from all the lands to which I have banished them, and I will return them to their pasture, where they will be fruitful and multiply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.4', 'BSB', 'I will raise up shepherds over them who will tend them, and they will no longer be afraid or dismayed, nor will any go missing, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.5', 'BSB', 'Behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will raise up for David a righteous Branch, and He will reign wisely as King and will administer justice and righteousness in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.6', 'BSB', 'In His days Judah will be saved, and Israel will dwell securely. And this is His name by which He will be called: The LORD Our Righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.7', 'BSB', 'So behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when they will no longer say, ‘As surely as the LORD lives, who brought the Israelites up out of the land of Egypt.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.8', 'BSB', 'Instead they will say, ‘As surely as the LORD lives, who brought and led the descendants of the house of Israel up out of the land of the north and all the other lands to which He had banished them.’ Then they will dwell once more in their own land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.9', 'BSB', 'As for the prophets: My heart is broken within me, and all my bones tremble. I have become like a drunkard, like a man overcome by wine, because of the LORD, because of His holy words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.10', 'BSB', 'For the land is full of adulterers— because of the curse, the land mourns and the pastures of the wilderness have dried up— their course is evil and their power is misused.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.11', 'BSB', '“For both prophet and priest are ungodly; even in My house I have found their wickedness,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.12', 'BSB', '“Therefore their path will become slick; they will be driven away into the darkness and fall into it. For I will bring disaster upon them in the year of their punishment,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.13', 'BSB', '“Among the prophets of Samaria I saw an offensive thing: They prophesied by Baal and led My people Israel astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.14', 'BSB', 'And among the prophets of Jerusalem I have seen a horrible thing: They commit adultery and walk in lies. They strengthen the hands of evildoers, so that no one turns his back on wickedness. They are all like Sodom to Me; the people of Jerusalem are like Gomorrah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts says concerning the prophets: “I will feed them wormwood and give them poisoned water to drink, for from the prophets of Jerusalem ungodliness has spread throughout the land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.16', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Do not listen to the words of the prophets who prophesy to you. They are filling you with false hopes. They speak visions from their own minds, not from the mouth of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.17', 'BSB', 'They keep saying to those who despise Me, ‘The LORD says that you will have peace,’ and to everyone who walks in the stubbornness of his own heart, ‘No harm will come to you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.18', 'BSB', 'But which of them has stood in the council of the LORD to see and hear His word? Who has given heed to His word and obeyed it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, the storm of the LORD has gone out with fury, a whirlwind swirling down upon the heads of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.20', 'BSB', 'The anger of the LORD will not turn back until He has fully accomplished the purposes of His heart. In the days to come you will understand this clearly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.21', 'BSB', 'I did not send these prophets, yet they have run with their message; I did not speak to them, yet they have prophesied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.22', 'BSB', 'But if they had stood in My council, they would have proclaimed My words to My people and turned them back from their evil ways and deeds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.23', 'BSB', '“Am I only a God nearby,” declares the LORD, “and not a God far away?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.24', 'BSB', '“Can a man hide in secret places where I cannot see him?” declares the LORD. “Do I not fill the heavens and the earth?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.25', 'BSB', '“I have heard the sayings of the prophets who prophesy lies in My name: ‘I had a dream! I had a dream!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.26', 'BSB', 'How long will this continue in the hearts of these prophets who prophesy falsehood, these prophets of the delusion of their own minds?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.27', 'BSB', 'They suppose the dreams that they tell one another will make My people forget My name, just as their fathers forgot My name through the worship of Baal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.28', 'BSB', 'Let the prophet who has a dream retell it, but let him who has My word speak it truthfully. For what is straw compared to grain?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.29', 'BSB', '“Is not My word like fire,” declares the LORD, “and like a hammer that smashes a rock?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.30', 'BSB', '“Therefore behold,” declares the LORD, “I am against the prophets who steal from one another words they attribute to Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.31', 'BSB', '“Yes,” declares the LORD, “I am against the prophets who wag their own tongues and proclaim, ‘The LORD declares it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.32', 'BSB', '“Indeed,” declares the LORD, “I am against those who prophesy false dreams and retell them to lead My people astray with their reckless lies. It was not I who sent them or commanded them, and they are of no benefit at all to these people,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.33', 'BSB', '“Now when this people or a prophet or priest asks you, ‘What is the burden of the LORD?’ you are to say to them, ‘What burden? I will forsake you, declares the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.34', 'BSB', 'As for the prophet or priest or anyone who claims, ‘This is the burden of the LORD,’ I will punish that man and his household.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.35', 'BSB', 'This is what each man is to say to his friend and to his brother: ‘What has the LORD answered?’ or ‘What has the LORD spoken?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.36', 'BSB', 'But refer no more to the burden of the LORD, for each man’s word becomes the burden, so that you pervert the words of the living God, the LORD of Hosts, our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.37', 'BSB', 'Thus you are to say to the prophet: ‘What has the LORD answered you?’ and ‘What has the LORD spoken?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.38', 'BSB', 'But if you claim, ‘This is the burden of the LORD,’ then this is what the LORD says: Because you have said, ‘This is the burden of the LORD,’ and I specifically told you not to make this claim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.39', 'BSB', 'therefore I will surely forget you and will cast you out of My presence, both you and the city that I gave to you and your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.23.40', 'BSB', 'And I will bring upon you everlasting shame and perpetual humiliation that will never be forgotten.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.1', 'BSB', 'After Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had carried away Jeconiah son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, as well as the officials of Judah and the craftsmen and metalsmiths from Jerusalem, and had brought them to Babylon, the LORD showed me two baskets of figs placed in front of the temple of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.2', 'BSB', 'One basket had very good figs, like those that ripen early, but the other basket contained very poor figs, so bad they could not be eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.3', 'BSB', '“Jeremiah,” the LORD asked, “what do you see?” “Figs!” I replied. “The good figs are very good, but the bad figs are very bad, so bad they cannot be eaten.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.4', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.5', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Like these good figs, so I regard as good the exiles from Judah, whom I have sent away from this place to the land of the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.6', 'BSB', 'I will keep My eyes on them for good and will return them to this land. I will build them up and not tear them down; I will plant them and not uproot them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.7', 'BSB', 'I will give them a heart to know Me, that I am the LORD. They will be My people, and I will be their God, for they will return to Me with all their heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.8', 'BSB', 'But like the bad figs, so bad they cannot be eaten,’ says the LORD, ‘so will I deal with Zedekiah king of Judah, his officials, and the remnant of Jerusalem—those remaining in this land and those living in the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.9', 'BSB', 'I will make them a horror and an offense to all the kingdoms of the earth, a disgrace and an object of scorn, ridicule, and cursing wherever I have banished them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.24.10', 'BSB', 'And I will send against them sword and famine and plague, until they have perished from the land that I gave to them and their fathers.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, which was the first year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.2', 'BSB', 'So the prophet Jeremiah spoke to all the people of Judah and all the residents of Jerusalem as follows:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.3', 'BSB', '“From the thirteenth year of Josiah son of Amon king of Judah until this very day—twenty-three years—the word of the LORD has come to me, and I have spoken to you again and again, but you have not listened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.4', 'BSB', 'And the LORD has sent all His servants the prophets to you again and again, but you have not listened or inclined your ear to hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.5', 'BSB', 'The prophets told you, ‘Turn now, each of you, from your evil ways and deeds, and you can dwell in the land that the LORD has given to you and your fathers forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.6', 'BSB', 'Do not follow other gods to serve and worship them, and do not provoke Me to anger with the works of your hands. Then I will do you no harm.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.7', 'BSB', '‘But to your own harm, you have not listened to Me,’ declares the LORD, ‘so you have provoked Me to anger with the works of your hands.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Because you have not obeyed My words,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.9', 'BSB', 'behold, I will summon all the families of the north, declares the LORD, and I will send for My servant Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, whom I will bring against this land, against its residents, and against all the surrounding nations. So I will devote them to destruction and make them an object of horror and contempt, an everlasting desolation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.10', 'BSB', 'Moreover, I will banish from them the sounds of joy and gladness, the voices of the bride and bridegroom, the sound of the millstones, and the light of the lamp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.11', 'BSB', 'And this whole land will become a desolate wasteland, and these nations will serve the king of Babylon for seventy years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.12', 'BSB', 'But when seventy years are complete, I will punish the king of Babylon and that nation, the land of the Chaldeans, for their guilt, declares the LORD, and I will make it an everlasting desolation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.13', 'BSB', 'I will bring upon that land all the words I have pronounced against it, all that is written in this book, which Jeremiah has prophesied against all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.14', 'BSB', 'For many nations and great kings will enslave them, and I will repay them according to their deeds and according to the work of their hands.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, said to me: “Take from My hand this cup of the wine of wrath, and make all the nations to whom I send you drink from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.16', 'BSB', 'And they will drink and stagger and go out of their minds, because of the sword that I will send among them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.17', 'BSB', 'So I took the cup from the LORD’s hand and made all the nations drink from it, each one to whom the LORD had sent me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.18', 'BSB', 'to make them a ruin, an object of horror and contempt and cursing, as they are to this day—Jerusalem and the cities of Judah, its kings and officials;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.19', 'BSB', 'Pharaoh king of Egypt, his officials, his leaders, and all his people;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.20', 'BSB', 'all the mixed tribes; all the kings of Uz; all the kings of the Philistines: Ashkelon, Gaza, Ekron, and the remnant of Ashdod;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.21', 'BSB', 'Edom, Moab, and the Ammonites;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.22', 'BSB', 'all the kings of Tyre and Sidon; the kings of the coastlands across the sea;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.23', 'BSB', 'Dedan, Tema, Buz, and all who cut the corners of their hair;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.24', 'BSB', 'all the kings of Arabia, and all the kings of the mixed tribes who dwell in the desert;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.25', 'BSB', 'all the kings of Zimri, Elam, and Media;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.26', 'BSB', 'all the kings of the north, both near and far, one after another—all the kingdoms on the face of the earth. And after all of them, the king of Sheshach will drink it too.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.27', 'BSB', '“Then you are to tell them that this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘Drink, get drunk, and vomit. Fall down and never get up again, because of the sword I will send among you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.28', 'BSB', 'If they refuse to take the cup from your hand and drink it, you are to tell them that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘You most certainly must drink it!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.29', 'BSB', 'For behold, I am beginning to bring disaster on the city that bears My Name, so how could you possibly go unpunished? You will not go unpunished, for I am calling down a sword upon all the inhabitants of the earth, declares the LORD of Hosts.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.30', 'BSB', 'So you are to prophesy all these words against them and say to them: ‘The LORD will roar from on high; He will raise His voice from His holy habitation. He will roar loudly over His pasture; like those who tread the grapes, He will call out with a shout against all the inhabitants of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.31', 'BSB', 'The tumult will resound to the ends of the earth because the LORD brings a charge against the nations. He brings judgment on all mankind and puts the wicked to the sword,’” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.32', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Behold! Disaster is spreading from nation to nation; a mighty storm is rising from the ends of the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.33', 'BSB', 'Those slain by the LORD on that day will be spread from one end of the earth to the other. They will not be mourned, gathered, or buried. They will be like dung lying on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.34', 'BSB', 'Wail, you shepherds, and cry out; roll in the dust, you leaders of the flock. For the days of your slaughter have come; you will fall and be shattered like fine pottery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.35', 'BSB', 'Flight will evade the shepherds, and escape will elude the leaders of the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.36', 'BSB', 'Hear the cry of the shepherds, the wailing of the leaders of the flock, for the LORD is destroying their pasture.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.37', 'BSB', 'The peaceful meadows have been silenced because of the LORD’s burning anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.25.38', 'BSB', 'He has left His den like a lion, for their land has been made a desolation by the sword of the oppressor, and because of the fierce anger of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.1', 'BSB', 'At the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, this word came from the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD says: Stand in the courtyard of the house of the LORD and speak all the words I have commanded you to speak to all the cities of Judah who come to worship there. Do not omit a word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.3', 'BSB', 'Perhaps they will listen and turn—each from his evil way of life—so that I may relent of the disaster I am planning to bring upon them because of the evil of their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.4', 'BSB', 'And you are to tell them that this is what the LORD says: ‘If you do not listen to Me and walk in My law, which I have set before you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.5', 'BSB', 'and if you do not listen to the words of My servants the prophets, whom I have sent you again and again even though you did not listen,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.6', 'BSB', 'then I will make this house like Shiloh, and I will make this city an object of cursing among all the nations of the earth.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.7', 'BSB', 'Now the priests and prophets and all the people heard Jeremiah speaking these words in the house of the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.8', 'BSB', 'and as soon as he had finished telling all the people everything the LORD had commanded him to say, the priests and prophets and all the people seized him, shouting, “You must surely die!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.9', 'BSB', 'How dare you prophesy in the name of the LORD that this house will become like Shiloh and this city will be desolate and deserted!” And all the people assembled against Jeremiah in the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.10', 'BSB', 'When the officials of Judah heard these things, they went up from the king’s palace to the house of the LORD and sat there at the entrance of the New Gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.11', 'BSB', 'Then the priests and prophets said to the officials and all the people, “This man is worthy of death, for he has prophesied against this city, as you have heard with your own ears!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.12', 'BSB', 'But Jeremiah said to all the officials and all the people, “The LORD sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city all the words that you have heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.13', 'BSB', 'So now, correct your ways and deeds, and obey the voice of the LORD your God, so that He might relent of the disaster He has pronounced against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.14', 'BSB', 'As for me, here I am in your hands; do to me what you think is good and right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.15', 'BSB', 'But know for certain that if you put me to death, you will bring innocent blood upon yourselves, upon this city, and upon its residents; for truly the LORD has sent me to speak all these words in your hearing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.16', 'BSB', 'Then the officials and all the people told the priests and prophets, “This man is not worthy of death, for he has spoken to us in the name of the LORD our God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.17', 'BSB', 'Some of the elders of the land stood up and said to the whole assembly of the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.18', 'BSB', '“Micah the Moreshite prophesied in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah and told all the people of Judah that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Zion will be plowed like a field, Jerusalem will become a heap of rubble, and the temple mount a wooded ridge.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.19', 'BSB', 'Did Hezekiah king of Judah or anyone else in Judah put him to death? Did Hezekiah not fear the LORD and seek His favor, and did not the LORD relent of the disaster He had pronounced against them? But we are about to bring great harm on ourselves!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.20', 'BSB', 'Now there was another man prophesying in the name of the LORD, Uriah son of Shemaiah from Kiriath-jearim. He prophesied against this city and against this land the same things that Jeremiah did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.21', 'BSB', 'King Jehoiakim and all his mighty men and officials heard his words, and the king sought to put him to death. But when Uriah found out about it, he fled in fear and went to Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.22', 'BSB', 'Then King Jehoiakim sent men to Egypt: Elnathan son of Achbor along with some other men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.23', 'BSB', 'They brought Uriah out of Egypt and took him to King Jehoiakim, who had him put to the sword and his body thrown into the burial place of the common people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.26.24', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, Ahikam son of Shaphan supported Jeremiah, so he was not handed over to the people to be put to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.1', 'BSB', 'At the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah son of Josiah king of Judah, this word came to Jeremiah from the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD said to me: “Make for yourself a yoke out of leather straps and put it on your neck.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.3', 'BSB', 'Send word to the kings of Edom, Moab, Ammon, Tyre, and Sidon through the envoys who have come to Jerusalem to Zedekiah king of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.4', 'BSB', 'Give them a message from the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, to relay to their masters:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.5', 'BSB', 'By My great power and outstretched arm, I made the earth and the men and beasts on the face of it, and I give it to whom I please.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.6', 'BSB', 'So now I have placed all these lands under the authority of My servant Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon. I have even made the beasts of the field subject to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.7', 'BSB', 'All nations will serve him and his son and grandson, until the time of his own land comes; then many nations and great kings will enslave him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.8', 'BSB', 'As for the nation or kingdom that does not serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and does not place its neck under his yoke, I will punish that nation by sword and famine and plague, declares the LORD, until I have destroyed it by his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.9', 'BSB', 'But as for you, do not listen to your prophets, your diviners, your interpreters of dreams, your mediums, or your sorcerers who declare, ‘You will not serve the king of Babylon.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.10', 'BSB', 'For they prophesy to you a lie that will serve to remove you from your land; I will banish you and you will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.11', 'BSB', 'But the nation that will put its neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon and serve him, I will leave in its own land, to cultivate it and reside in it, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.12', 'BSB', 'And to Zedekiah king of Judah I spoke the same message: “Put your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon; serve him and his people, and live!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.13', 'BSB', 'Why should you and your people die by sword and famine and plague, as the LORD has decreed against any nation that does not serve the king of Babylon?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.14', 'BSB', 'Do not listen to the words of the prophets who say, ‘You must not serve the king of Babylon,’ for they are prophesying to you a lie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.15', 'BSB', 'For I have not sent them, declares the LORD, and yet they are prophesying falsely in My name; therefore I will banish you, and you will perish—you and the prophets who prophesy to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.16', 'BSB', 'Then I said to the priests and to all this people, “This is what the LORD says: Do not listen to the words of your prophets who prophesy to you, saying, ‘Look, very soon now the articles from the house of the LORD will be brought back from Babylon.’ They are prophesying to you a lie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.17', 'BSB', 'Do not listen to them. Serve the king of Babylon and live! Why should this city become a ruin?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.18', 'BSB', 'If they are indeed prophets and the word of the LORD is with them, let them now plead with the LORD of Hosts that the articles remaining in the house of the LORD, in the palace of the king of Judah, and in Jerusalem, not be taken to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.19', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts says about the pillars, the sea, the bases, and the rest of the articles that remain in this city,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.20', 'BSB', 'which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon did not take when he carried Jeconiah son of Jehoiakim king of Judah into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon, along with all the nobles of Judah and Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.21', 'BSB', 'Yes, this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says about the articles that remain in the house of the LORD, in the palace of the king of Judah, and in Jerusalem:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.27.22', 'BSB', '‘They will be carried to Babylon and will remain there until the day I attend to them again,’ declares the LORD. ‘Then I will bring them back and restore them to this place.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.1', 'BSB', 'In the fifth month of that same year, the fourth year, near the beginning of the reign of King Zedekiah of Judah, the prophet Hananiah son of Azzur, who was from Gibeon, said to me in the house of the LORD in the presence of the priests and all the people:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.3', 'BSB', 'Within two years I will restore to this place all the articles of the house of the LORD that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon removed from here and carried to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.4', 'BSB', 'And I will restore to this place Jeconiah son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, along with all the exiles from Judah who went to Babylon,’ declares the LORD, ‘for I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.5', 'BSB', 'Then the prophet Jeremiah replied to the prophet Hananiah in the presence of the priests and all the people who were standing in the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.6', 'BSB', '“Amen!” Jeremiah said. “May the LORD do so! May the LORD fulfill the words you have prophesied, and may He restore the articles of His house and all the exiles back to this place from Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.7', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, listen now to this message I am speaking in your hearing and in the hearing of all the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.8', 'BSB', 'The prophets of old who preceded you and me prophesied war, disaster, and plague against many lands and great kingdoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.9', 'BSB', 'As for the prophet who prophesies peace, only if the word of the prophet comes true will the prophet be recognized as one the LORD has truly sent.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.10', 'BSB', 'Then the prophet Hananiah took the yoke off the neck of Jeremiah the prophet and broke it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.11', 'BSB', 'And in the presence of all the people Hananiah proclaimed, “This is what the LORD says: ‘In this way, within two years I will break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon off the neck of all the nations.’” At this, Jeremiah the prophet went on his way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.12', 'BSB', 'But shortly after Hananiah the prophet had broken the yoke off his neck, the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.13', 'BSB', '“Go and tell Hananiah that this is what the LORD says: ‘You have broken a yoke of wood, but in its place you have fashioned a yoke of iron.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.14', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘I have put a yoke of iron on the neck of all these nations to make them serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and they will serve him. I have even given him control of the beasts of the field.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.15', 'BSB', 'Then the prophet Jeremiah said to the prophet Hananiah, “Listen, Hananiah! The LORD did not send you, but you have persuaded this people to trust in a lie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: ‘I am about to remove you from the face of the earth. You will die this year because you have preached rebellion against the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.28.17', 'BSB', 'And in the seventh month of that very year, the prophet Hananiah died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.1', 'BSB', 'This is the text of the letter that Jeremiah the prophet sent from Jerusalem to the surviving elders among the exiles and to the priests, the prophets, and all the others Nebuchadnezzar had carried into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.2', 'BSB', '(This was after King Jeconiah, the queen mother, the court officials, the officials of Judah and Jerusalem, the craftsmen, and the metalsmiths had been exiled from Jerusalem.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.3', 'BSB', 'The letter was entrusted to Elasah son of Shaphan and Gemariah son of Hilkiah, whom Zedekiah king of Judah sent to King Nebuchadnezzar in Babylon. It stated:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.4', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says to all the exiles who were carried away from Jerusalem to Babylon:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.5', 'BSB', '“Build houses and settle down. Plant gardens and eat their produce.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.6', 'BSB', 'Take wives and have sons and daughters. Take wives for your sons and give your daughters in marriage, so that they too may have sons and daughters. Multiply there; do not decrease.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.7', 'BSB', 'Seek the prosperity of the city to which I have sent you as exiles. Pray to the LORD on its behalf, for if it prospers, you too will prosper.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.8', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “Do not be deceived by the prophets and diviners among you, and do not listen to the dreams you elicit from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.9', 'BSB', 'For they are falsely prophesying to you in My name; I have not sent them, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.10', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “When Babylon’s seventy years are complete, I will attend to you and confirm My promise to restore you to this place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.11', 'BSB', 'For I know the plans I have for you, declares the LORD, plans to prosper you and not to harm you, to give you a future and a hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.12', 'BSB', 'Then you will call upon Me and come and pray to Me, and I will listen to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.13', 'BSB', 'You will seek Me and find Me when you search for Me with all your heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.14', 'BSB', 'I will be found by you, declares the LORD, and I will restore you from captivity and gather you from all the nations and places to which I have banished you, declares the LORD. I will restore you to the place from which I sent you into exile.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.15', 'BSB', 'Because you may say, “The LORD has raised up for us prophets in Babylon,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.16', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD says about the king who sits on David’s throne and all the people who remain in this city, your brothers who did not go with you into exile—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.17', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “I will send against them sword and famine and plague, and I will make them like rotten figs, so bad they cannot be eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.18', 'BSB', 'I will pursue them with sword and famine and plague. I will make them a horror to all the kingdoms of the earth—a curse, a desolation, and an object of scorn and reproach among all the nations to which I banish them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.19', 'BSB', 'I will do this because they have not listened to My words, declares the LORD, which I sent to them again and again through My servants the prophets. And neither have you exiles listened, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.20', 'BSB', 'So hear the word of the LORD, all you exiles I have sent away from Jerusalem to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.21', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says about Ahab son of Kolaiah and Zedekiah son of Maaseiah, who are prophesying to you lies in My name: “I will deliver them to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and he will kill them before your very eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.22', 'BSB', 'Because of them, all the exiles of Judah who are in Babylon will use this curse: ‘May the LORD make you like Zedekiah and Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.23', 'BSB', 'For they have committed an outrage in Israel by committing adultery with the wives of their neighbors and speaking lies in My name, which I did not command them to do. I am He who knows, and I am a witness, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.24', 'BSB', 'You are to tell Shemaiah the Nehelamite that', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.25', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “In your own name you have sent out letters to all the people of Jerusalem, to the priest Zephaniah son of Maaseiah, and to all the priests. You said to Zephaniah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.26', 'BSB', '‘The LORD has appointed you priest in place of Jehoiada, to be the chief officer in the house of the LORD, responsible for any madman who acts like a prophet—you must put him in stocks and neck irons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.27', 'BSB', 'So now, why have you not rebuked Jeremiah of Anathoth, who poses as a prophet among you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.28', 'BSB', 'For he has sent to us in Babylon, claiming: Since the exile will be lengthy, build houses and settle down; plant gardens and eat their produce.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.29', 'BSB', '(Zephaniah the priest, however, had read this letter to Jeremiah the prophet.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.30', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.31', 'BSB', '“Send a message telling all the exiles what the LORD says concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite. Because Shemaiah has prophesied to you—though I did not send him—and has made you trust in a lie,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.29.32', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD says: ‘I will surely punish Shemaiah the Nehelamite and his descendants. He will have no one left among this people, nor will he see the good that I will bring to My people, declares the LORD, for he has preached rebellion against the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Write in a book all the words that I have spoken to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.3', 'BSB', 'For behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will restore from captivity My people Israel and Judah, declares the LORD. I will restore them to the land that I gave to their fathers, and they will possess it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.4', 'BSB', 'These are the words that the LORD spoke concerning Israel and Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.5', 'BSB', 'Yes, this is what the LORD says: “A cry of panic is heard— a cry of terror, not of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.6', 'BSB', 'Ask now, and see: Can a male give birth? Why then do I see every man with his hands on his stomach like a woman in labor and every face turned pale?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.7', 'BSB', 'How awful that day will be! None will be like it! It is the time of Jacob’s distress, but he will be saved out of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.8', 'BSB', 'On that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, I will break the yoke off their necks and tear off their bonds, and no longer will strangers enslave them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.9', 'BSB', 'Instead, they will serve the LORD their God and David their king, whom I will raise up for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.10', 'BSB', 'As for you, O Jacob My servant, do not be afraid, declares the LORD, and do not be dismayed, O Israel. For I will surely save you out of a distant place, your descendants from the land of their captivity! Jacob will return to quiet and ease, with no one to make him afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.11', 'BSB', 'For I am with you to save you, declares the LORD. Though I will completely destroy all the nations to which I have scattered you, I will not completely destroy you. Yet I will discipline you justly, and will by no means leave you unpunished.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.12', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “Your injury is incurable; your wound is grievous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.13', 'BSB', 'There is no one to plead your cause, no remedy for your sores, no recovery for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.14', 'BSB', 'All your lovers have forgotten you; they no longer seek you, for I have struck you as an enemy would, with the discipline of someone cruel, because of your great iniquity and your numerous sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.15', 'BSB', 'Why do you cry out over your wound? Your pain has no cure! Because of your great iniquity and your numerous sins I have done these things to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.16', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, all who devour you will be devoured, and all your adversaries—every one of them— will go off into exile. Those who plundered you will be plundered, and all who raided you will be raided.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.17', 'BSB', 'But I will restore your health and heal your wounds, declares the LORD, because they call you an outcast, Zion, for whom no one cares.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.18', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “I will restore the fortunes of Jacob’s tents and have compassion on his dwellings. And the city will be rebuilt on her own ruins, and the palace will stand in its rightful place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.19', 'BSB', 'Thanksgiving will proceed from them, a sound of celebration. I will multiply them, and they will not be decreased; I will honor them, and they will not be belittled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.20', 'BSB', 'Their children will be as in days of old, and their congregation will be established before Me; and I will punish all their oppressors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.21', 'BSB', 'Their leader will be one of their own, and their ruler will arise from their midst. And I will bring him near, and he will approach Me, for who would dare on his own to approach Me?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.22', 'BSB', '“And you will be My people, and I will be your God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.23', 'BSB', 'Behold, the storm of the LORD has gone out with fury, a whirlwind swirling down upon the heads of the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.30.24', 'BSB', 'The fierce anger of the LORD will not turn back until He has fully accomplished the purposes of His heart. In the days to come you will understand this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.1', 'BSB', '“At that time,” declares the LORD, “I will be the God of all the families of Israel, and they will be My people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “The people who survived the sword found favor in the wilderness when Israel went to find rest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.3', 'BSB', 'The LORD appeared to us in the past, saying: “I have loved you with an everlasting love; therefore I have drawn you with loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.4', 'BSB', 'Again I will build you, and you will be rebuilt, O Virgin Israel. Again you will take up your tambourines and go out in joyful dancing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.5', 'BSB', 'Again you will plant vineyards on the hills of Samaria; the farmers will plant and enjoy the fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.6', 'BSB', 'For there will be a day when watchmen will call out on the hills of Ephraim, ‘Arise, let us go up to Zion, to the LORD our God!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.7', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “Sing with joy for Jacob; shout for the foremost of the nations! Make your praises heard, and say, ‘O LORD, save Your people, the remnant of Israel!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.8', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will bring them from the land of the north and gather them from the farthest parts of the earth, including the blind and the lame, expectant mothers and women in labor. They will return as a great assembly!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.9', 'BSB', 'They will come with weeping, and by their supplication I will lead them; I will make them walk beside streams of waters, on a level path where they will not stumble. For I am Israel’s Father, and Ephraim is My firstborn.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.10', 'BSB', 'Hear, O nations, the word of the LORD, and proclaim it in distant coastlands: “The One who scattered Israel will gather them and keep them as a shepherd keeps his flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.11', 'BSB', 'For the LORD has ransomed Jacob and redeemed him from the hand that had overpowered him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.12', 'BSB', 'They will come and shout for joy on the heights of Zion; they will be radiant over the bounty of the LORD— the grain, new wine, and oil, and the young of the flocks and herds. Their life will be like a well-watered garden, and never again will they languish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.13', 'BSB', 'Then the maidens will rejoice with dancing, young men and old as well. I will turn their mourning into joy, and give them comfort and joy for their sorrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.14', 'BSB', 'I will fill the souls of the priests abundantly, and will fill My people with My goodness,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “A voice is heard in Ramah, mourning and great weeping, Rachel weeping for her children, and refusing to be comforted, because they are no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.16', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Keep your voice from weeping and your eyes from tears, for the reward for your work will come, declares the LORD. Then your children will return from the land of the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.17', 'BSB', 'So there is hope for your future, declares the LORD, and your children will return to their own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.18', 'BSB', 'I have surely heard Ephraim’s moaning: ‘You disciplined me severely, like an untrained calf. Restore me, that I may return, for You are the LORD my God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.19', 'BSB', 'After I returned, I repented; and after I was instructed, I struck my thigh in grief. I was ashamed and humiliated because I bore the disgrace of my youth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.20', 'BSB', 'Is not Ephraim a precious son to Me, a delightful child? Though I often speak against him, I still remember him. Therefore My heart yearns for him; I have great compassion for him,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.21', 'BSB', '“Set up the roadmarks, establish the signposts. Keep the highway in mind, the road you have traveled. Return, O Virgin Israel, return to these cities of yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.22', 'BSB', 'How long will you wander, O faithless daughter? For the LORD has created a new thing in the land— a woman will shelter a man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.23', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “When I restore them from captivity, they will once again speak this word in the land of Judah and in its cities: ‘May the LORD bless you, O righteous dwelling place, O holy mountain.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.24', 'BSB', 'And Judah and all its cities will dwell together in the land, the farmers and those who move with the flocks,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.25', 'BSB', 'for I will refresh the weary soul and replenish all who are weak.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.26', 'BSB', 'At this I awoke and looked around. My sleep had been most pleasant to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.27', 'BSB', '“The days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when I will sow the house of Israel and the house of Judah with the seed of man and of beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.28', 'BSB', 'Just as I watched over them to uproot and tear down, to demolish, destroy, and bring disaster, so I will watch over them to build and to plant,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.29', 'BSB', '“In those days, it will no longer be said: ‘The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the teeth of the children are set on edge.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.30', 'BSB', 'Instead, each will die for his own iniquity. If anyone eats the sour grapes, his own teeth will be set on edge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.31', 'BSB', 'Behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.32', 'BSB', 'It will not be like the covenant I made with their fathers when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt— a covenant they broke, though I was a husband to them,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.33', 'BSB', '“But this is the covenant I will make with the house of Israel after those days, declares the LORD. I will put My law in their minds and inscribe it on their hearts. And I will be their God, and they will be My people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.34', 'BSB', 'No longer will each man teach his neighbor or his brother, saying, ‘Know the LORD,’ because they will all know Me, from the least of them to the greatest, declares the LORD. For I will forgive their iniquities and will remember their sins no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.35', 'BSB', 'Thus says the LORD, who gives the sun for light by day, who sets in order the moon and stars for light by night, who stirs up the sea so that its waves roar—the LORD of Hosts is His name:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.36', 'BSB', '“Only if this fixed order departed from My presence, declares the LORD, would Israel’s descendants ever cease to be a nation before Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.37', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Only if the heavens above could be measured and the foundations of the earth below searched out would I reject all of Israel’s descendants because of all they have done,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.38', 'BSB', '“The days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when this city will be rebuilt for Me, from the tower of Hananel to the Corner Gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.39', 'BSB', 'The measuring line will once again stretch out straight to the hill of Gareb and then turn toward Goah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.31.40', 'BSB', 'The whole valley of the dead bodies and ashes, and all the fields as far as the Kidron Valley, to the corner of the Horse Gate to the east, will be holy to the LORD. It will never again be uprooted or demolished.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, which was the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.2', 'BSB', 'At that time the army of the king of Babylon was besieging Jerusalem, and Jeremiah the prophet was imprisoned in the courtyard of the guard, which was in the palace of the king of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.3', 'BSB', 'For Zedekiah king of Judah had imprisoned him, saying: “Why are you prophesying like this? You claim that the LORD says, ‘Behold, I am about to deliver this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will capture it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.4', 'BSB', 'Zedekiah king of Judah will not escape from the hands of the Chaldeans, but he will surely be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, and will speak with him face to face and see him eye to eye.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.5', 'BSB', 'He will take Zedekiah to Babylon, where he will stay until I attend to him, declares the LORD. If you fight against the Chaldeans, you will not succeed.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.6', 'BSB', 'Jeremiah replied, “The word of the LORD came to me, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.7', 'BSB', 'Behold! Hanamel, the son of your uncle Shallum, is coming to you to say, ‘Buy for yourself my field in Anathoth, for you have the right of redemption to buy it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.8', 'BSB', 'Then, as the LORD had said, my cousin Hanamel came to me in the courtyard of the guard and urged me, ‘Please buy my field in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin, for you own the right of inheritance and redemption. Buy it for yourself.’” Then I knew that this was the word of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.9', 'BSB', 'So I bought the field in Anathoth from my cousin Hanamel, and I weighed out seventeen shekels of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.10', 'BSB', 'I signed and sealed the deed, called in witnesses, and weighed out the silver on the scales.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.11', 'BSB', 'Then I took the deed of purchase—the sealed copy with its terms and conditions, as well as the open copy—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.12', 'BSB', 'and I gave this deed to Baruch son of Neriah, the son of Mahseiah, in the sight of my cousin Hanamel and the witnesses who were signing the purchase agreement and all the Jews sitting in the courtyard of the guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.13', 'BSB', 'In their sight I instructed Baruch,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.14', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Take these deeds—both the sealed copy and the open copy of the deed of purchase—and put them in a clay jar to preserve them for a long time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.15', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Houses, fields, and vineyards will again be bought in this land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.16', 'BSB', 'After I had given the deed of purchase to Baruch son of Neriah, I prayed to the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.17', 'BSB', '“Oh, Lord GOD! You have made the heavens and the earth by Your great power and outstretched arm. Nothing is too difficult for You!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.18', 'BSB', 'You show loving devotion to thousands but lay the iniquity of the fathers into the laps of their children after them, O great and mighty God whose name is the LORD of Hosts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.19', 'BSB', 'the One great in counsel and mighty in deed, whose eyes are on all the ways of the sons of men, to reward each one according to his ways and according to the fruit of his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.20', 'BSB', 'You performed signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, and You do so to this very day, both in Israel and among all mankind. And You have made a name for Yourself, as is the case to this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.21', 'BSB', 'You brought Your people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs and wonders, with a strong hand and an outstretched arm, and with great terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.22', 'BSB', 'You gave them this land that You had sworn to give their fathers, a land flowing with milk and honey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.23', 'BSB', 'They came in and possessed it, but they did not obey Your voice or walk in Your law. They failed to perform all that You commanded them to do, and so You have brought upon them all this disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.24', 'BSB', 'See how the siege ramps are mounted against the city to capture it. And by sword and famine and plague, the city has been given into the hands of the Chaldeans who are fighting against it. What You have spoken has happened, as You now see!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.25', 'BSB', 'Yet You, O Lord GOD, have said to me, ‘Buy for yourself the field with silver and call in witnesses, even though the city has been delivered into the hands of the Chaldeans!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.26', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.27', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am the LORD, the God of all flesh. Is anything too difficult for Me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: Behold, I am about to deliver this city into the hands of the Chaldeans and of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, who will capture it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.29', 'BSB', 'And the Chaldeans who are fighting against this city will come in, set it on fire, and burn it, along with the houses of those who provoked Me to anger by burning incense to Baal on their rooftops and by pouring out drink offerings to other gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.30', 'BSB', 'For the children of Israel and of Judah have done nothing but evil in My sight from their youth; indeed, they have done nothing but provoke Me to anger by the work of their hands, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.31', 'BSB', 'For this city has aroused My wrath and fury from the day it was built until now. Therefore I will remove it from My presence', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.32', 'BSB', 'because of all the evil the children of Israel and of Judah have done to provoke Me to anger—they, their kings, their officials, their priests and prophets, the men of Judah, and the residents of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.33', 'BSB', 'They have turned their backs to Me and not their faces. Though I taught them again and again, they would not listen or respond to discipline.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.34', 'BSB', 'They have placed their abominations in the house that bears My Name, and so have defiled it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.35', 'BSB', 'They have built the high places of Baal in the Valley of Hinnom to make their sons and daughters pass through the fire to Molech—something I never commanded them, nor had it ever entered My mind, that they should commit such an abomination and cause Judah to sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.36', 'BSB', 'Now therefore, about this city of which you say, ‘It will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon by sword and famine and plague,’ this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.37', 'BSB', 'I will surely gather My people from all the lands to which I have banished them in My furious anger and great wrath, and I will return them to this place and make them dwell in safety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.38', 'BSB', 'They will be My people, and I will be their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.39', 'BSB', 'I will give them one heart and one way, so that they will always fear Me for their own good and for the good of their children after them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.40', 'BSB', 'I will make an everlasting covenant with them: I will never turn away from doing good to them, and I will put My fear in their hearts, so that they will never turn away from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.41', 'BSB', 'Yes, I will rejoice in doing them good, and I will faithfully plant them in this land with all My heart and with all My soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.42', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: Just as I have brought all this great disaster on this people, so I will bring on them all the good I have promised them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.43', 'BSB', 'And fields will be bought in this land about which you are saying, ‘It is a desolation, without man or beast; it has been delivered into the hands of the Chaldeans.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.32.44', 'BSB', 'Fields will be purchased with silver, and deeds will be signed, sealed, and witnessed in the land of Benjamin, in the areas surrounding Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah—the cities of the hill country, the foothills, and the Negev—because I will restore them from captivity, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.1', 'BSB', 'While Jeremiah was still confined in the courtyard of the guard, the word of the LORD came to him a second time:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.2', 'BSB', '“Thus says the LORD who made the earth, the LORD who formed it and established it, the LORD is His name:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.3', 'BSB', 'Call to Me, and I will answer and show you great and unsearchable things you do not know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says about the houses of this city and the palaces of the kings of Judah that have been torn down for defense against the siege ramps and the sword:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.5', 'BSB', 'The Chaldeans are coming to fight and to fill those places with the corpses of the men I will strike down in My anger and in My wrath. I have hidden My face from this city because of all its wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.6', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, I will bring to it health and healing, and I will heal its people and reveal to them the abundance of peace and truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.7', 'BSB', 'I will restore Judah and Israel from captivity and will rebuild them as in former times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.8', 'BSB', 'And I will cleanse them from all the iniquity they have committed against Me, and will forgive all their sins of rebellion against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.9', 'BSB', 'So this city will bring Me renown, joy, praise, and glory before all the nations of the earth, who will hear of all the good I do for it. They will tremble in awe because of all the goodness and prosperity that I will provide for it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.10', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: In this place you say is a wasteland without man or beast, in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem that are deserted—inhabited by neither man nor beast—there will be heard again', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.11', 'BSB', 'the sounds of joy and gladness, the voices of the bride and bridegroom, and the voices of those bringing thank offerings into the house of the LORD, saying: ‘Give thanks to the LORD of Hosts, for the LORD is good; His loving devotion endures forever.’ For I will restore the land from captivity as in former times, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.12', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: In this desolate place, without man or beast, and in all its cities, there will once more be pastures for shepherds to rest their flocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.13', 'BSB', 'In the cities of the hill country, the foothills, and the Negev, in the land of Benjamin and the cities surrounding Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, the flocks will again pass under the hands of the one who counts them, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.14', 'BSB', 'Behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will fulfill the gracious promise that I have spoken to the house of Israel and the house of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.15', 'BSB', 'In those days and at that time I will cause to sprout for David a righteous Branch, and He will administer justice and righteousness in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.16', 'BSB', 'In those days Judah will be saved, and Jerusalem will dwell securely, and this is the name by which it will be called: The LORD Our Righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.17', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: David will never lack a man to sit on the throne of the house of Israel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.18', 'BSB', 'nor will the priests who are Levites ever fail to have a man before Me to offer burnt offerings, to burn grain offerings, and to present sacrifices.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.19', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.20', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD says: If you can break My covenant with the day and My covenant with the night, so that day and night cease to occupy their appointed time,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.21', 'BSB', 'then My covenant may also be broken with David My servant and with My ministers the Levites who are priests, so that David will not have a son to reign on his throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.22', 'BSB', 'As the hosts of heaven cannot be counted and as the sand on the seashore cannot be measured, so too will I multiply the descendants of My servant David and the Levites who minister before Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.23', 'BSB', 'Moreover, the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.24', 'BSB', '“Have you not noticed what these people are saying: ‘The LORD has rejected the two families He had chosen’? So they despise My people and no longer regard them as a nation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.25', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: If I have not established My covenant with the day and the night and the fixed order of heaven and earth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.33.26', 'BSB', 'then I would also reject the descendants of Jacob and of My servant David, so as not to take from his descendants rulers over the descendants of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. For I will restore them from captivity and will have compassion on them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, all his army, all the earthly kingdoms under his control, and all the other nations were fighting against Jerusalem and all its surrounding cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD, the God of Israel, told Jeremiah to go and speak to Zedekiah king of Judah and tell him that this is what the LORD says: “Behold, I am about to deliver this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will burn it down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.3', 'BSB', 'And you yourself will not escape his grasp, but will surely be captured and delivered into his hand. You will see the king of Babylon eye to eye and speak with him face to face; and you will go to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.4', 'BSB', 'Yet hear the word of the LORD, O Zedekiah king of Judah. This is what the LORD says concerning you: You will not die by the sword;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.5', 'BSB', 'you will die in peace. As spices were burned for your fathers, the former kings who preceded you, so people will burn spices for you and lament, ‘Alas, O master!’ For I Myself have spoken this word, declares the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.6', 'BSB', 'In Jerusalem, then, Jeremiah the prophet relayed all these words to Zedekiah king of Judah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.7', 'BSB', 'as the army of the king of Babylon was fighting against Jerusalem and the remaining cities of Judah—against Lachish and Azekah. For these were the only fortified cities remaining in Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.8', 'BSB', 'After King Zedekiah had made a covenant with all the people in Jerusalem to proclaim liberty, the word came to Jeremiah from the LORD', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.9', 'BSB', 'that each man should free his Hebrew slaves, both male and female, and no one should hold his fellow Jew in bondage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.10', 'BSB', 'So all the officials and all the people who entered into this covenant agreed that they would free their menservants and maidservants and no longer hold them in bondage. They obeyed and released them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.11', 'BSB', 'but later they changed their minds and took back the menservants and maidservants they had freed, and they forced them to become slaves again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.12', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.13', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: I made a covenant with your forefathers when I brought them out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of slavery, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.14', 'BSB', 'Every seventh year, each of you must free his Hebrew brother who has sold himself to you. He may serve you six years, but then you must let him go free. But your fathers did not listen or incline their ear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.15', 'BSB', 'Recently you repented and did what pleased Me; each of you proclaimed freedom for his neighbor. You made a covenant before Me in the house that bears My Name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.16', 'BSB', 'But now you have changed your minds and profaned My name. Each of you has taken back the menservants and maidservants whom you had set at liberty to go wherever they wanted, and you have again forced them to be your slaves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: You have not obeyed Me; you have not proclaimed freedom, each man for his brother and for his neighbor. So now I proclaim freedom for you, declares the LORD—freedom to fall by sword, by plague, and by famine! I will make you a horror to all the kingdoms of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.18', 'BSB', 'And those who have transgressed My covenant and have not fulfilled the terms of the covenant they made before Me, I will treat like the calf they cut in two in order to pass between its pieces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.19', 'BSB', 'The officials of Judah and Jerusalem, the court officials, the priests, and all the people of the land who passed between the pieces of the calf,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.20', 'BSB', 'I will deliver into the hands of their enemies who seek their lives. Their corpses will become food for the birds of the air and the beasts of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.21', 'BSB', 'And I will deliver Zedekiah king of Judah and his officials into the hands of their enemies who seek their lives, to the army of the king of Babylon that had withdrawn from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.34.22', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am going to give the command, declares the LORD, and I will bring them back to this city. They will fight against it, capture it, and burn it down. And I will make the cities of Judah a desolation, without inhabitant.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the days of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.2', 'BSB', '“Go to the house of the Rechabites, speak to them, and bring them to one of the chambers of the house of the LORD to offer them a drink of wine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.3', 'BSB', 'So I took Jaazaniah son of Jeremiah, the son of Habazziniah, and his brothers and all his sons—the entire house of the Rechabites—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.4', 'BSB', 'and I brought them into the house of the LORD, to a chamber occupied by the sons of Hanan son of Igdaliah, a man of God. This room was near the chamber of the officials, which was above the chamber of Maaseiah son of Shallum the doorkeeper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.5', 'BSB', 'Then I set pitchers full of wine and some cups before the men of the house of the Rechabites, and I said to them, “Drink some wine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.6', 'BSB', '“We do not drink wine,” they replied, “for our forefather Jonadab son of Rechab commanded us, ‘Neither you nor your descendants are ever to drink wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.7', 'BSB', 'Nor are you ever to build a house or sow seed or plant a vineyard. Those things are not for you. Instead, you must live in tents all your lives, so that you may live a long time in the land where you wander.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.8', 'BSB', 'And we have obeyed the voice of our forefather Jonadab son of Rechab in all he commanded us. So we have not drunk wine all our lives—neither we nor our wives nor our sons and daughters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.9', 'BSB', 'Nor have we built houses in which to live, and we have not owned any vineyards or fields or crops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.10', 'BSB', 'But we have lived in tents and have obeyed and done exactly as our forefather Jonadab commanded us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.11', 'BSB', 'So when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon marched into the land, we said: ‘Come, let us go into Jerusalem to escape the armies of the Chaldeans and the Arameans.’ So we have remained in Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.12', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.13', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Go and tell the men of Judah and the residents of Jerusalem: ‘Will you not accept discipline and obey My words?’ declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.14', 'BSB', 'The words of Jonadab son of Rechab have been carried out. He commanded his sons not to drink wine, and they have not drunk it to this very day because they have obeyed the command of their forefather. But I have spoken to you again and again, and you have not obeyed Me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.15', 'BSB', 'Again and again I have sent you all My servants the prophets, proclaiming: ‘Turn now, each of you, from your wicked ways, and correct your actions. Do not go after other gods to serve them. Live in the land that I have given to you and your fathers.’ But you have not inclined your ear or listened to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.16', 'BSB', 'Yes, the sons of Jonadab son of Rechab carried out the command their forefather gave them, but these people have not listened to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD God of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘Behold, I will bring to Judah and to all the residents of Jerusalem all the disaster I have pronounced against them, because I have spoken to them but they have not obeyed, and I have called to them but they have not answered.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.18', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah said to the house of the Rechabites: “This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘Because you have obeyed the command of your forefather Jonadab and have kept all his commandments and have done all that he charged you to do,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.35.19', 'BSB', 'this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Jonadab son of Rechab will never fail to have a man to stand before Me.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.1', 'BSB', 'In the fourth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, this word came to Jeremiah from the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.2', 'BSB', '“Take a scroll and write on it all the words I have spoken to you concerning Israel, Judah, and all the nations, from the day I first spoke to you during the reign of Josiah until today.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.3', 'BSB', 'Perhaps when the people of Judah hear about all the calamity I plan to bring upon them, each of them will turn from his wicked way. Then I will forgive their iniquity and their sin.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.4', 'BSB', 'So Jeremiah called Baruch son of Neriah, and at the dictation of Jeremiah, Baruch wrote on a scroll all the words that the LORD had spoken to Jeremiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.5', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah commanded Baruch, “I am restricted; I cannot enter the house of the LORD;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.6', 'BSB', 'so you are to go to the house of the LORD on a day of fasting, and in the hearing of the people you are to read the words of the LORD from the scroll you have written at my dictation. Read them in the hearing of all the people of Judah who are coming from their cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.7', 'BSB', 'Perhaps they will bring their petition before the LORD, and each one will turn from his wicked way; for great are the anger and fury that the LORD has pronounced against this people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.8', 'BSB', 'So Baruch son of Neriah did everything that Jeremiah the prophet had commanded him. In the house of the LORD he read the words of the LORD from the scroll.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.9', 'BSB', 'Now in the ninth month of the fifth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah king of Judah, a fast before the LORD was proclaimed to all the people of Jerusalem and all who had come there from the cities of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.10', 'BSB', 'From the chamber of Gemariah son of Shaphan the scribe, which was in the upper courtyard at the opening of the New Gate of the house of the LORD, Baruch read from the scroll the words of Jeremiah in the hearing of all the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.11', 'BSB', 'When Micaiah son of Gemariah, the son of Shaphan, heard all the words of the LORD from the scroll,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.12', 'BSB', 'he went down to the scribe’s chamber in the king’s palace, where all the officials were sitting: Elishama the scribe, Delaiah son of Shemaiah, Elnathan son of Achbor, Gemariah son of Shaphan, Zedekiah son of Hananiah, and all the other officials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.13', 'BSB', 'And Micaiah reported to them all the words he had heard Baruch read from the scroll in the hearing of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.14', 'BSB', 'Then all the officials sent word to Baruch through Jehudi son of Nethaniah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, saying, “Bring the scroll that you read in the hearing of the people, and come here.” So Baruch son of Neriah took the scroll and went to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.15', 'BSB', '“Please sit down,” they said, “and read it in our hearing.” So Baruch read it in their hearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.16', 'BSB', 'When they had heard all these words, they turned to one another in fear and said to Baruch, “Surely we must report all these words to the king.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.17', 'BSB', '“Tell us now,” they asked Baruch, “how did you write all these words? Was it at Jeremiah’s dictation?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.18', 'BSB', '“It was at his dictation,” Baruch replied. “He recited all these words to me and I wrote them in ink on the scroll.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.19', 'BSB', 'Then the officials said to Baruch, “You and Jeremiah must hide yourselves and tell no one where you are.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.20', 'BSB', 'So the officials went to the king in the courtyard. And having stored the scroll in the chamber of Elishama the scribe, they reported everything to the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.21', 'BSB', 'Then the king sent Jehudi to get the scroll, and he took it from the chamber of Elishama the scribe. And Jehudi read it in the hearing of the king and all the officials who were standing beside him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.22', 'BSB', 'Since it was the ninth month, the king was sitting in his winter quarters with a fire burning before him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.23', 'BSB', 'And as soon as Jehudi had read three or four columns, Jehoiakim would cut them off with a scribe’s knife and throw them into the firepot, until the entire scroll had been consumed by the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.24', 'BSB', 'Yet in hearing all these words, the king and his servants did not become frightened or tear their garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.25', 'BSB', 'Even though Elnathan, Delaiah, and Gemariah urged the king not to burn the scroll, he would not listen to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.26', 'BSB', 'Instead, the king commanded Jerahmeel, a son of the king, as well as Seraiah son of Azriel and Shelemiah son of Abdeel, to seize Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet. But the LORD had hidden them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.27', 'BSB', 'After the king had burned the scroll containing the words that Baruch had written at Jeremiah’s dictation, the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.28', 'BSB', '“Take another scroll and rewrite on it the very words that were on the original scroll, which Jehoiakim king of Judah has burned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.29', 'BSB', 'You are to proclaim concerning Jehoiakim king of Judah that this is what the LORD says: You have burned the scroll and said, ‘Why have you written on it that the king of Babylon would surely come and destroy this land and deprive it of man and beast?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.30', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says about Jehoiakim king of Judah: He will have no one to sit on David’s throne, and his body will be thrown out and exposed to heat by day and frost by night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.31', 'BSB', 'I will punish him and his descendants and servants for their iniquity. I will bring on them, on the residents of Jerusalem, and on the men of Judah, all the calamity about which I warned them but they did not listen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.36.32', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah took another scroll and gave it to the scribe Baruch son of Neriah, and at Jeremiah’s dictation he wrote on it all the words of the scroll that Jehoiakim king of Judah had burned in the fire. And many similar words were added to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.1', 'BSB', 'Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon made Zedekiah son of Josiah the king of Judah, and he reigned in place of Coniah son of Jehoiakim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.2', 'BSB', 'But he and his officers and the people of the land refused to obey the words that the LORD had spoken through Jeremiah the prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.3', 'BSB', 'Yet King Zedekiah sent Jehucal son of Shelemiah and Zephaniah the priest, the son of Maaseiah, to Jeremiah the prophet with the message, “Please pray to the LORD our God for us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.4', 'BSB', 'Now Jeremiah was free to come and go among the people, for they had not yet put him in prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.5', 'BSB', 'Pharaoh’s army had left Egypt, and when the Chaldeans who were besieging Jerusalem heard the report, they withdrew from Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.6', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah the prophet:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.7', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says that you are to tell the king of Judah, who sent you to Me: Behold, Pharaoh’s army, which has marched out to help you, will go back to its own land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.8', 'BSB', 'Then the Chaldeans will return and fight against this city. They will capture it and burn it down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.9', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: Do not deceive yourselves by saying, ‘The Chaldeans will go away for good,’ for they will not!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.10', 'BSB', 'Indeed, if you were to strike down the entire army of the Chaldeans that is fighting against you, and only wounded men remained in their tents, they would still get up and burn this city down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.11', 'BSB', 'When the Chaldean army withdrew from Jerusalem for fear of Pharaoh’s army,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.12', 'BSB', 'Jeremiah started to leave Jerusalem to go to the land of Benjamin to claim his portion there among the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.13', 'BSB', 'But when he reached the Gate of Benjamin, the captain of the guard, whose name was Irijah son of Shelemiah, the son of Hananiah, seized him and said, “You are deserting to the Chaldeans!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.14', 'BSB', '“That is a lie,” Jeremiah replied. “I am not deserting to the Chaldeans!” But Irijah would not listen to him; instead, he arrested Jeremiah and took him to the officials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.15', 'BSB', 'The officials were angry with Jeremiah, and they beat him and placed him in jail in the house of Jonathan the scribe, for it had been made into a prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.16', 'BSB', 'So Jeremiah went into a cell in the dungeon and remained there a long time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.17', 'BSB', 'Later, King Zedekiah sent for Jeremiah and received him in his palace, where he asked him privately, “Is there a word from the LORD?” “There is,” Jeremiah replied. “You will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.18', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah asked King Zedekiah, “How have I sinned against you or your servants or these people, that you have put me in prison?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.19', 'BSB', 'Where are your prophets who prophesied to you, claiming, ‘The king of Babylon will not come against you or this land’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.20', 'BSB', 'But now please listen, O my lord the king. May my petition come before you. Do not send me back to the house of Jonathan the scribe, or I will die there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.37.21', 'BSB', 'So King Zedekiah gave orders for Jeremiah to be placed in the courtyard of the guard and given a loaf of bread daily from the street of the bakers, until all the bread in the city was gone. So Jeremiah remained in the courtyard of the guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.1', 'BSB', 'Now Shephatiah son of Mattan, Gedaliah son of Pashhur, Jucal son of Shelemiah, and Pashhur son of Malchijah heard that Jeremiah had been telling all the people:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD says: Whoever stays in this city will die by sword and famine and plague, but whoever surrenders to the Chaldeans will live; he will retain his life like a spoil of war, and he will live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: This city will surely be delivered into the hands of the army of the king of Babylon, and he will capture it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.4', 'BSB', 'Then the officials said to the king, “This man ought to die, for he is discouraging the warriors who remain in this city, as well as all the people, by speaking such words to them; this man is not seeking the well-being of these people, but their ruin.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.5', 'BSB', '“Here he is,” replied King Zedekiah. “He is in your hands, since the king can do nothing to stop you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.6', 'BSB', 'So they took Jeremiah and dropped him into the cistern of Malchiah, the king’s son, which was in the courtyard of the guard. They lowered Jeremiah with ropes into the cistern, which had no water but only mud, and Jeremiah sank down into the mud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.7', 'BSB', 'Now Ebed-melech the Cushite, a court official in the royal palace, heard that Jeremiah had been put into the cistern. While the king was sitting at the Gate of Benjamin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.8', 'BSB', 'Ebed-melech went out from the king’s palace and said to the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.9', 'BSB', '“My lord the king, these men have acted wickedly in all that they have done to Jeremiah the prophet. They have dropped him into the cistern, where he will starve to death, for there is no more bread in the city.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.10', 'BSB', 'So the king commanded Ebed-melech the Cushite, “Take thirty men from here with you and pull Jeremiah the prophet out of the cistern before he dies.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.11', 'BSB', 'Then Ebed-melech took the men with him and went to the king’s palace, to a place below the storehouse. From there he took old rags and worn-out clothes and lowered them with ropes to Jeremiah in the cistern.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.12', 'BSB', 'Ebed-melech the Cushite cried out to Jeremiah, “Put these worn-out rags and clothes under your arms to pad the ropes.” Jeremiah did so,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.13', 'BSB', 'and they pulled him up with the ropes and lifted him out of the cistern. And Jeremiah remained in the courtyard of the guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.14', 'BSB', 'Then King Zedekiah sent for Jeremiah the prophet and received him at the third entrance to the house of the LORD. “I am going to ask you something,” said the king to Jeremiah. “Do not hide anything from me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.15', 'BSB', '“If I tell you,” Jeremiah replied, “you will surely put me to death. And even if I give you advice, you will not listen to me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.16', 'BSB', 'But King Zedekiah swore secretly to Jeremiah, “As surely as the LORD lives, who has given us this life, I will not kill you, nor will I deliver you into the hands of these men who are seeking your life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.17', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah said to Zedekiah, “This is what the LORD God of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘If you indeed surrender to the officers of the king of Babylon, then you will live, this city will not be burned down, and you and your household will survive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.18', 'BSB', 'But if you do not surrender to the officers of the king of Babylon, then this city will be delivered into the hands of the Chaldeans. They will burn it down, and you yourself will not escape their grasp.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.19', 'BSB', 'But King Zedekiah said to Jeremiah, “I am afraid of the Jews who have deserted to the Chaldeans, for the Chaldeans may deliver me into their hands to abuse me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.20', 'BSB', '“They will not hand you over,” Jeremiah replied. “Obey the voice of the LORD in what I am telling you, that it may go well with you and you may live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.21', 'BSB', 'But if you refuse to surrender, this is the word that the LORD has shown me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.22', 'BSB', 'All the women who remain in the palace of the king of Judah will be brought out to the officials of the king of Babylon, and those women will say: ‘They misled you and overcame you— those trusted friends of yours. Your feet sank into the mire, and they deserted you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.23', 'BSB', 'All your wives and children will be brought out to the Chaldeans. And you yourself will not escape their grasp, for you will be seized by the king of Babylon, and this city will be burned down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.24', 'BSB', 'Then Zedekiah warned Jeremiah, “Do not let anyone know about this conversation, or you will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.25', 'BSB', 'If the officials hear that I have spoken with you, and they come and demand of you, ‘Tell us what you said to the king and what he said to you; do not hide it from us, or we will kill you,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.26', 'BSB', 'then tell them, ‘I was presenting to the king my petition that he not return me to the house of Jonathan to die there.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.27', 'BSB', 'When all the officials came to Jeremiah and questioned him, he relayed to them the exact words the king had commanded him to say. So they said no more to him, for no one had overheard the conversation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.38.28', 'BSB', 'And Jeremiah remained in the courtyard of the guard until the day Jerusalem was captured.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.1', 'BSB', 'In the ninth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the tenth month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon marched against Jerusalem with his entire army and laid siege to the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.2', 'BSB', 'And on the ninth day of the fourth month of Zedekiah’s eleventh year, the city was breached.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.3', 'BSB', 'Then all the officials of the king of Babylon entered and sat in the Middle Gate: Nergal-sharezer of Samgar, Nebo-sarsekim the Rabsaris, Nergal-sharezer the Rabmag, and all the rest of the officials of the king of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.4', 'BSB', 'When Zedekiah king of Judah and all the soldiers saw them, they fled. They left the city at night by way of the king’s garden, through the gate between the two walls, and they went out along the route to the Arabah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.5', 'BSB', 'But the army of the Chaldeans pursued them and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho. They seized him and brought him up to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon at Riblah in the land of Hamath, where he pronounced judgment on him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.6', 'BSB', 'There at Riblah the king of Babylon slaughtered the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and he also killed all the nobles of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.7', 'BSB', 'Then he put out Zedekiah’s eyes and bound him with bronze chains to take him to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.8', 'BSB', 'The Chaldeans set fire to the palace of the king and to the houses of the people, and they broke down the walls of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.9', 'BSB', 'Then Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried away to Babylon the remnant of the people who had remained in the city, along with the deserters who had defected to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.10', 'BSB', 'But Nebuzaradan left behind in the land of Judah some of the poor people who had no property, and at that time he gave them vineyards and fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.11', 'BSB', 'Now Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had given orders about Jeremiah through Nebuzaradan captain of the guard, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.12', 'BSB', '“Take him, look after him, and do not let any harm come to him; do for him whatever he says.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.13', 'BSB', 'So Nebuzaradan captain of the guard, Nebushazban the Rabsaris, Nergal-sharezer the Rabmag, and all the captains of the king of Babylon', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.14', 'BSB', 'had Jeremiah brought from the courtyard of the guard, and they turned him over to Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, to take him home. So Jeremiah remained among his own people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.15', 'BSB', 'And while Jeremiah had been confined in the courtyard of the guard, the word of the LORD had come to him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.16', 'BSB', '“Go and tell Ebed-melech the Cushite that this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘I am about to fulfill My words against this city for harm and not for good, and on that day they will be fulfilled before your eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.17', 'BSB', 'But I will deliver you on that day, declares the LORD, and you will not be delivered into the hands of the men whom you fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.39.18', 'BSB', 'For I will surely rescue you so that you do not fall by the sword. Because you have trusted in Me, you will escape with your life like a spoil of war, declares the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD after Nebuzaradan captain of the guard had released him at Ramah, having found him bound in chains among all the captives of Jerusalem and Judah who were being exiled to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.2', 'BSB', 'The captain of the guard found Jeremiah and said to him, “The LORD your God decreed this disaster on this place,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.3', 'BSB', 'and now the LORD has fulfilled it; He has done just as He said. Because you people have sinned against the LORD and have not obeyed His voice, this thing has happened to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.4', 'BSB', 'But now, behold, I am freeing you today from the chains that were on your wrists. If it pleases you to come with me to Babylon, then come, and I will take care of you. But if it seems wrong to you to come with me to Babylon, go no farther. Look, the whole land is before you. Wherever it seems good and right to you, go there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.5', 'BSB', 'But before Jeremiah turned to go, Nebuzaradan added, “Return to Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, whom the king of Babylon has appointed over the cities of Judah, and stay with him among the people, or go anywhere else that seems right.” Then the captain of the guard gave him a ration and a gift and released him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.6', 'BSB', 'So Jeremiah went to Gedaliah son of Ahikam at Mizpah and stayed with him among the people who were left in the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.7', 'BSB', 'When all the commanders and men of the armies in the field heard that the king of Babylon had appointed Gedaliah son of Ahikam over the land and that he had put him in charge of the men, women, and children who were the poorest of the land and had not been exiled to Babylon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.8', 'BSB', 'they came to Gedaliah at Mizpah—Ishmael son of Nethaniah, Johanan and Jonathan the sons of Kareah, Seraiah son of Tanhumeth, the sons of Ephai the Netophathite, and Jezaniah son of the Maacathite—they and their men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.9', 'BSB', 'Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, swore an oath to them and their men, assuring them, “Do not be afraid to serve the Chaldeans. Live in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and it will go well with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.10', 'BSB', 'As for me, I will stay in Mizpah to represent you before the Chaldeans who come to us. As for you, gather wine grapes, summer fruit, and oil, place them in your storage jars, and live in the cities you have taken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.11', 'BSB', 'When all the Jews in Moab, Ammon, Edom, and all the other lands heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant in Judah and had appointed Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, over them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.12', 'BSB', 'they all returned from all the places to which they had been banished and came to the land of Judah, to Gedaliah at Mizpah. And they gathered an abundance of wine grapes and summer fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.13', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the armies in the field came to Gedaliah at Mizpah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.14', 'BSB', 'and said to him, “Are you aware that Baalis king of the Ammonites has sent Ishmael son of Nethaniah to take your life?” But Gedaliah son of Ahikam did not believe them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.15', 'BSB', 'Then Johanan son of Kareah spoke privately to Gedaliah at Mizpah. “Let me go and kill Ishmael son of Nethaniah,” he said. “No one will know it. Why should he take your life and scatter all the people of Judah who have gathered to you, so that the remnant of Judah would perish?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.40.16', 'BSB', 'But Gedaliah son of Ahikam said to Johanan son of Kareah, “Do not do such a thing! What you are saying about Ishmael is a lie.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.1', 'BSB', 'In the seventh month, Ishmael son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, who was a member of the royal family and one of the king’s chief officers, came with ten men to Gedaliah son of Ahikam at Mizpah, and they ate a meal together there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.2', 'BSB', 'Then Ishmael son of Nethaniah and the ten men who were with him got up and struck down Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, with the sword, killing the one whom the king of Babylon had appointed to govern the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.3', 'BSB', 'Ishmael also killed all the Jews who were with Gedaliah at Mizpah, as well as the Chaldean soldiers who were there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.4', 'BSB', 'On the second day after the murder of Gedaliah, when no one yet knew about it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.5', 'BSB', 'eighty men who had shaved off their beards, torn their garments, and cut themselves came from Shechem, Shiloh, and Samaria, carrying grain offerings and frankincense for the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.6', 'BSB', 'And Ishmael son of Nethaniah went out from Mizpah to meet them, weeping as he went. When Ishmael encountered the men, he said, “Come to Gedaliah son of Ahikam.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.7', 'BSB', 'And when they came into the city, Ishmael son of Nethaniah and the men with him slaughtered them and threw them into a cistern.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.8', 'BSB', 'But ten of the men among them said to Ishmael, “Do not kill us, for we have hidden treasure in the field—wheat, barley, oil, and honey!” So he refrained from killing them with the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.9', 'BSB', 'Now the cistern into which Ishmael had thrown all the bodies of the men he had struck down along with Gedaliah was a large one that King Asa had made for fear of Baasha king of Israel. Ishmael son of Nethaniah filled it with the slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.10', 'BSB', 'Then Ishmael took captive all the remnant of the people of Mizpah—the daughters of the king along with all the others who remained in Mizpah—over whom Nebuzaradan captain of the guard had appointed Gedaliah son of Ahikam. Ishmael son of Nethaniah took them captive and set off to cross over to the Ammonites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.11', 'BSB', 'When Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the armies with him heard of all the crimes that Ishmael son of Nethaniah had committed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.12', 'BSB', 'they took all their men and went to fight Ishmael son of Nethaniah. And they found him near the great pool in Gibeon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.13', 'BSB', 'When all the people with Ishmael saw Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the army with him, they rejoiced,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.14', 'BSB', 'and all the people whom Ishmael had taken captive at Mizpah turned and went over to Johanan son of Kareah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.15', 'BSB', 'But Ishmael son of Nethaniah and eight of his men escaped from Johanan and went to the Ammonites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.16', 'BSB', 'Then Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the armies with him took the whole remnant of the people from Mizpah whom he had recovered from Ishmael son of Nethaniah after Ishmael had killed Gedaliah son of Ahikam: the soldiers, women, children, and court officials he had brought back from Gibeon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.17', 'BSB', 'And they went and stayed in Geruth Chimham, near Bethlehem, in order to proceed into Egypt', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.41.18', 'BSB', 'to escape the Chaldeans. For they were afraid of the Chaldeans because Ishmael son of Nethaniah had struck down Gedaliah son of Ahikam, whom the king of Babylon had appointed over the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.1', 'BSB', 'Then all the commanders of the forces, along with Johanan son of Kareah, Jezaniah son of Hoshaiah, and all the people from the least to the greatest, approached', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.2', 'BSB', 'Jeremiah the prophet and said, “May our petition come before you; pray to the LORD your God on behalf of this entire remnant. For few of us remain of the many, as you can see with your own eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.3', 'BSB', 'Pray that the LORD your God will tell us the way we should walk and the thing we should do.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.4', 'BSB', '“I have heard you,” replied Jeremiah the prophet. “I will surely pray to the LORD your God as you request, and I will tell you everything that the LORD answers; I will not withhold a word from you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.5', 'BSB', 'Then they said to Jeremiah, “May the LORD be a true and faithful witness against us if we do not act upon every word that the LORD your God sends you to tell us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.6', 'BSB', 'Whether it is pleasant or unpleasant, we will obey the voice of the LORD our God to whom we are sending you, so that it may go well with us, for we will obey the voice of the LORD our God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.7', 'BSB', 'After ten days the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.8', 'BSB', 'and he summoned Johanan son of Kareah, all the commanders of the forces who were with him, and all the people from the least to the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.9', 'BSB', 'Jeremiah told them, “Thus says the LORD, the God of Israel, to whom you sent me to present your petition:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.10', 'BSB', '‘If you will indeed stay in this land, then I will build you up and not tear you down; I will plant you and not uproot you, for I will relent of the disaster I have brought upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.11', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid of the king of Babylon, whom you now fear; do not be afraid of him, declares the LORD, for I am with you to save you and deliver you from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.12', 'BSB', 'And I will show you compassion, and he will have compassion on you and restore you to your own land.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.13', 'BSB', 'But if you say, ‘We will not stay in this land,’ and you thus disobey the voice of the LORD your God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.14', 'BSB', 'and if you say, ‘No, but we will go to the land of Egypt and live there, where we will not see war or hear the sound of the ram’s horn or hunger for bread,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.15', 'BSB', 'then hear the word of the LORD, O remnant of Judah! This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘If you are determined to go to Egypt and reside there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.16', 'BSB', 'then the sword you fear will overtake you there, and the famine you dread will follow on your heels into Egypt, and you will die there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.17', 'BSB', 'So all who resolve to go to Egypt to reside there will die by sword and famine and plague. Not one of them will survive or escape the disaster I will bring upon them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.18', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘Just as My anger and wrath were poured out on the residents of Jerusalem, so will My wrath be poured out on you if you go to Egypt. You will become an object of cursing and horror, of vilification and disgrace, and you will never see this place again.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.19', 'BSB', 'The LORD has told you, O remnant of Judah, ‘Do not go to Egypt.’ Know for sure that I have warned you today!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.20', 'BSB', 'For you have deceived yourselves by sending me to the LORD your God, saying, ‘Pray to the LORD our God on our behalf, and as for all that the LORD our God says, tell it to us and we will do it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.21', 'BSB', 'For I have told you today, but you have not obeyed the voice of the LORD your God in all He has sent me to tell you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.42.22', 'BSB', 'Now therefore, know for sure that by sword and famine and plague you will die in the place where you desire to go to reside.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.1', 'BSB', 'When Jeremiah had finished telling all the people all the words of the LORD their God—everything that the LORD had sent him to say—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.2', 'BSB', 'Azariah son of Hoshaiah, Johanan son of Kareah, and all the arrogant men said to Jeremiah, “You are lying! The LORD our God has not sent you to say, ‘You must not go to Egypt to reside there.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.3', 'BSB', 'Rather, Baruch son of Neriah is inciting you against us to deliver us into the hands of the Chaldeans, so that they may put us to death or exile us to Babylon!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.4', 'BSB', 'So Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the forces disobeyed the command of the LORD to stay in the land of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.5', 'BSB', 'Instead, Johanan son of Kareah and all the commanders of the forces took the whole remnant of Judah, those who had returned to the land of Judah from all the nations to which they had been scattered,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.6', 'BSB', 'the men, the women, the children, the king’s daughters, and everyone whom Nebuzaradan captain of the guard had allowed to remain with Gedaliah son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, as well as Jeremiah the prophet and Baruch son of Neriah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.7', 'BSB', 'So they entered the land of Egypt because they did not obey the voice of the LORD, and they went as far as Tahpanhes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.8', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah at Tahpanhes:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.9', 'BSB', '“In the sight of the Jews, pick up some large stones and bury them in the clay of the brick pavement at the entrance to Pharaoh’s palace at Tahpanhes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.10', 'BSB', 'Then tell them that this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: ‘I will send for My servant Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and I will set his throne over these stones that I have embedded, and he will spread his royal pavilion over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.11', 'BSB', 'He will come and strike down the land of Egypt, bringing death to those destined for death, captivity to those destined for captivity, and the sword to those destined for the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.12', 'BSB', 'I will kindle a fire in the temples of the gods of Egypt, and Nebuchadnezzar will burn those temples and take their gods as captives. So he will wrap himself with the land of Egypt as a shepherd wraps himself in his garment, and he will depart from there unscathed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.43.13', 'BSB', 'He will demolish the sacred pillars of the temple of the sun in the land of Egypt, and he will burn down the temples of the gods of Egypt.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews living in the land of Egypt —in Migdol, Tahpanhes, and Memphis —and in the land of Pathros:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: You have seen all the disaster that I brought against Jerusalem and all the cities of Judah; and behold, they lie today in ruins and desolation', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.3', 'BSB', 'because of the evil they have done. They provoked Me to anger by continuing to burn incense and to serve other gods that neither they nor you nor your fathers ever knew.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.4', 'BSB', 'Yet I sent you all My servants the prophets again and again, saying: ‘Do not do this detestable thing that I hate.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.5', 'BSB', 'But they did not listen or incline their ears; they did not turn from their wickedness or stop burning incense to other gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore My wrath and anger poured out and burned in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem, so that they have become the desolate ruin they are today.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.7', 'BSB', 'So now, this is what the LORD God of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: Why are you doing such great harm to yourselves by cutting off from Judah man and woman, child and infant, leaving yourselves without a remnant?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.8', 'BSB', 'Why are you provoking Me to anger by the work of your hands by burning incense to other gods in the land of Egypt, where you have gone to reside? As a result, you will be cut off and will become an object of cursing and reproach among all the nations of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.9', 'BSB', 'Have you forgotten the wickedness of your fathers and of the kings of Judah and their wives, as well as the wickedness that you and your wives committed in the land of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.10', 'BSB', 'To this day they have not humbled themselves or shown reverence, nor have they followed My instruction or the statutes that I set before you and your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: I will set My face to bring disaster and to cut off all Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.12', 'BSB', 'And I will take away the remnant of Judah who have resolved to go to the land of Egypt to reside there; they will meet their end. They will all fall by the sword or be consumed by famine. From the least to the greatest, they will die by sword or famine; and they will become an object of cursing and horror, of vilification and reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.13', 'BSB', 'I will punish those who live in the land of Egypt, just as I punished Jerusalem, by sword and famine and plague,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.14', 'BSB', 'so that none of the remnant of Judah who have gone to reside in Egypt will escape or survive to return to the land of Judah, where they long to return and live; for none will return except a few fugitives.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.15', 'BSB', 'Then all the men who knew that their wives were burning incense to other gods, and all the women standing by—a great assembly—along with all the people living in the land of Egypt and in Pathros, said to Jeremiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.16', 'BSB', '“As for the word you have spoken to us in the name of the LORD, we will not listen to you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.17', 'BSB', 'Instead, we will do everything we vowed to do: We will burn incense to the Queen of Heaven and offer drink offerings to her, just as we, our fathers, our kings, and our officials did in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem. At that time we had plenty of food and good things, and we saw no disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.18', 'BSB', 'But from the time we stopped burning incense to the Queen of Heaven and pouring out drink offerings to her, we have lacked everything and have been perishing by sword and famine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.19', 'BSB', '“Moreover,” said the women, “when we burned incense to the Queen of Heaven and poured out drink offerings to her, was it without our husbands’ knowledge that we made sacrificial cakes in her image and poured out drink offerings to her?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.20', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah said to all the people, both men and women, who were answering him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.21', 'BSB', '“As for the incense you burned in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem—you, your fathers, your kings, your officials, and the people of the land—did the LORD not remember and bring this to mind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.22', 'BSB', 'So the LORD could no longer endure the evil deeds and detestable acts you committed, and your land became a desolation, a horror, and an object of cursing, without inhabitant, as it is this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.23', 'BSB', 'Because you burned incense and sinned against the LORD, and did not obey the voice of the LORD or walk in His instruction, His statutes, and His testimonies, this disaster has befallen you, as you see today.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.24', 'BSB', 'Then Jeremiah said to all the people, including all the women, “Hear the word of the LORD, all those of Judah who are in the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.25', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: As for you and your wives, you have spoken with your mouths and fulfilled with your hands your words: ‘We will surely perform our vows that we have made to burn incense to the Queen of Heaven and to pour out drink offerings to her.’ Go ahead, then, do what you have promised! Keep your vows!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.26', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, hear the word of the LORD, all you people of Judah living in Egypt: Behold, I have sworn by My great name, says the LORD, that never again will any man of Judah living in the land of Egypt invoke My name or say, ‘As surely as the Lord GOD lives.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.27', 'BSB', 'I am watching over them for harm and not for good, and every man of Judah who is in the land of Egypt will meet his end by sword or famine, until they are finished off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.28', 'BSB', 'Those who escape the sword will return from Egypt to Judah, few in number, and the whole remnant of Judah who went to dwell in the land of Egypt will know whose word will stand, Mine or theirs!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.29', 'BSB', 'This will be a sign to you that I will punish you in this place, declares the LORD, so that you may know that My threats of harm against you will surely stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.44.30', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: Behold, I will deliver Pharaoh Hophra king of Egypt into the hands of his enemies who seek his life, just as I delivered Zedekiah king of Judah into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the enemy who was seeking his life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.45.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that Jeremiah the prophet spoke to Baruch son of Neriah when he wrote these words on a scroll at the dictation of Jeremiah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim son of Josiah, king of Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.45.2', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says to you, Baruch:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.45.3', 'BSB', 'You have said, ‘Woe is me because the LORD has added sorrow to my pain! I am worn out with groaning and have found no rest.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.45.4', 'BSB', 'Thus Jeremiah was to say to Baruch: “This is what the LORD says: Throughout the land I will demolish what I have built and uproot what I have planted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.45.5', 'BSB', 'But as for you, do you seek great things for yourself? Stop seeking! For I will bring disaster on every living creature, declares the LORD, but wherever you go, I will grant your life as a spoil of war.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD about the nations—the word that came to Jeremiah the prophet', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.2', 'BSB', 'concerning Egypt and the army of Pharaoh Neco king of Egypt, which was defeated at Carchemish on the Euphrates River by Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.3', 'BSB', '“Deploy your shields, small and large; advance for battle!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.4', 'BSB', 'Harness the horses; mount the steeds; take your positions with helmets on! Polish your spears; put on armor!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.5', 'BSB', 'Why am I seeing this? They are terrified, they are retreating; their warriors are defeated, they flee in haste without looking back; terror is on every side!” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.6', 'BSB', '“The swift cannot flee, and the warrior cannot escape! In the north by the River Euphrates they stumble and fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.7', 'BSB', 'Who is this, rising like the Nile, like rivers whose waters churn?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.8', 'BSB', 'Egypt rises like the Nile, and its waters churn like rivers, boasting, ‘I will rise and cover the earth; I will destroy the cities and their people.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.9', 'BSB', 'Advance, O horses! Race furiously, O chariots! Let the warriors come forth— Cush and Put carrying their shields, men of Lydia drawing the bow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.10', 'BSB', 'For that day belongs to the Lord GOD of Hosts, a day of vengeance against His foes. The sword will devour until it is satisfied, until it is quenched with their blood. For the Lord GOD of Hosts will hold a sacrifice in the land of the north by the River Euphrates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.11', 'BSB', 'Go up to Gilead for balm, O Virgin Daughter of Egypt! In vain you try many remedies, but for you there is no healing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.12', 'BSB', 'The nations have heard of your shame, and your outcry fills the earth, because warrior stumbles over warrior and both of them have fallen together.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.13', 'BSB', 'This is the word that the LORD spoke to Jeremiah the prophet about the coming of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon to strike the land of Egypt:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.14', 'BSB', '“Announce it in Egypt, and proclaim it in Migdol; proclaim it in Memphis and Tahpanhes: ‘Take your positions and prepare yourself, for the sword devours those around you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.15', 'BSB', 'Why have your warriors been laid low? They cannot stand, for the LORD has thrust them down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.16', 'BSB', 'They continue to stumble; indeed, they have fallen over one another. They say, ‘Get up! Let us return to our people and to the land of our birth, away from the sword of the oppressor.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.17', 'BSB', 'There they will cry out: ‘Pharaoh king of Egypt was all noise; he has let the appointed time pass him by.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.18', 'BSB', 'As surely as I live, declares the King, whose name is the LORD of Hosts, there will come one who is like Tabor among the mountains and like Carmel by the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.19', 'BSB', 'Pack your bags for exile, O daughter dwelling in Egypt! For Memphis will be laid waste, destroyed and uninhabited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.20', 'BSB', 'Egypt is a beautiful heifer, but a gadfly from the north is coming against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.21', 'BSB', 'Even the mercenaries among her are like fattened calves. They too will turn back; together they will flee, they will not stand their ground, for the day of calamity is coming upon them— the time of their punishment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.22', 'BSB', 'Egypt will hiss like a fleeing serpent, for the enemy will advance in force; with axes they will come against her like woodsmen cutting down trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.23', 'BSB', 'They will chop down her forest, declares the LORD, dense though it may be, for they are more numerous than locusts; they cannot be counted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.24', 'BSB', 'The Daughter of Egypt will be put to shame; she will be delivered into the hands of the people of the north.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.25', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “Behold, I am about to punish Amon god of Thebes, along with Pharaoh, Egypt with her gods and kings, and those who trust in Pharaoh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.26', 'BSB', 'I will deliver them into the hands of those who seek their lives—of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and his officers. But after this, Egypt will be inhabited as in days of old, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.27', 'BSB', 'But you, O Jacob My servant, do not be afraid, and do not be dismayed, O Israel. For I will surely save you out of a distant place, your descendants from the land of their captivity! Jacob will return to quiet and ease, with no one to make him afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.46.28', 'BSB', 'And you, My servant Jacob, do not be afraid, declares the LORD, for I am with you. Though I will completely destroy all the nations to which I have banished you, I will not completely destroy you. Yet I will discipline you justly, and will by no means leave you unpunished.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah the prophet about the Philistines before Pharaoh struck down Gaza.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “See how the waters are rising from the north and becoming an overflowing torrent. They will overflow the land and its fullness, the cities and their inhabitants. The people will cry out, and all who dwell in the land will wail', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.3', 'BSB', 'at the sound of the galloping hooves of stallions, the rumbling of chariots, and the clatter of their wheels. The fathers will not turn back for their sons; their hands will hang limp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.4', 'BSB', 'For the day has come to destroy all the Philistines, to cut off from Tyre and Sidon every remaining ally. Indeed, the LORD is about to destroy the Philistines, the remnant from the coasts of Caphtor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.5', 'BSB', 'The people of Gaza will shave their heads in mourning; Ashkelon will be silenced. O remnant of their valley, how long will you gash yourself?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.6', 'BSB', '‘Alas, O sword of the LORD, how long until you rest? Return to your sheath; cease and be still!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.47.7', 'BSB', 'How can it rest when the LORD has commanded it? He has appointed it against Ashkelon and the shore of its coastland.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.1', 'BSB', 'Concerning Moab, this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “Woe to Nebo, for it will be devastated. Kiriathaim will be captured and disgraced; the fortress will be shattered and dismantled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.2', 'BSB', 'There is no longer praise for Moab; in Heshbon they devise evil against her: ‘Come, let us cut her off from nationhood.’ You too, O people of Madmen, will be silenced; the sword will pursue you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.3', 'BSB', 'A voice cries out from Horonaim: ‘Devastation and great destruction!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.4', 'BSB', 'Moab will be shattered; her little ones will cry out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.5', 'BSB', 'For on the ascent to Luhith they weep bitterly as they go, and on the descent to Horonaim cries of distress resound over the destruction:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.6', 'BSB', '‘Flee! Run for your lives! Become like a juniper in the desert.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.7', 'BSB', 'Because you trust in your works and treasures, you too will be captured, and Chemosh will go into exile with his priests and officials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.8', 'BSB', 'The destroyer will move against every city, and not one town will escape. The valley will also be ruined, and the high plain will be destroyed, as the LORD has said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.9', 'BSB', 'Put salt on Moab, for she will be laid waste; her cities will become desolate, with no one to dwell in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.10', 'BSB', 'Cursed is the one who is remiss in doing the work of the LORD, and cursed is he who withholds his sword from bloodshed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.11', 'BSB', 'Moab has been at ease from youth, settled like wine on its dregs; he has not been poured from vessel to vessel or gone into exile. So his flavor has remained the same, and his aroma is unchanged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will send to him wanderers, who will pour him out. They will empty his vessels and shatter his jars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.13', 'BSB', 'Then Moab will be ashamed of Chemosh, just as the house of Israel was ashamed when they trusted in Bethel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.14', 'BSB', 'How can you say, ‘We are warriors, mighty men ready for battle’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.15', 'BSB', 'Moab has been destroyed and its towns have been invaded; the best of its young men have gone down in the slaughter, declares the King, whose name is the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.16', 'BSB', 'Moab’s calamity is at hand, and his affliction is rushing swiftly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.17', 'BSB', 'Mourn for him, all you who surround him, everyone who knows his name; tell how the mighty scepter is shattered— the glorious staff!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.18', 'BSB', 'Come down from your glory; sit on parched ground, O daughter dwelling in Dibon, for the destroyer of Moab has come against you; he has destroyed your fortresses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.19', 'BSB', 'Stand by the road and watch, O dweller of Aroer! Ask the man fleeing or the woman escaping, ‘What has happened?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.20', 'BSB', 'Moab is put to shame, for it has been shattered. Wail and cry out! Declare by the Arnon that Moab is destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.21', 'BSB', 'Judgment has come upon the high plain— upon Holon, Jahzah, and Mephaath,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.22', 'BSB', 'upon Dibon, Nebo, and Beth-diblathaim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.23', 'BSB', 'upon Kiriathaim, Beth-gamul, and Beth-meon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.24', 'BSB', 'upon Kerioth, Bozrah, and all the towns of Moab, those far and near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.25', 'BSB', 'The horn of Moab has been cut off, and his arm is broken,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.26', 'BSB', '“Make him drunk, because he has magnified himself against the LORD; so Moab will wallow in his own vomit, and he will also become a laughingstock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.27', 'BSB', 'Was not Israel your object of ridicule? Was he ever found among thieves? For whenever you speak of him you shake your head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.28', 'BSB', 'Abandon the towns and settle among the rocks, O dwellers of Moab! Be like a dove that nests at the mouth of a cave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.29', 'BSB', 'We have heard of Moab’s pomposity, his exceeding pride and conceit, his proud arrogance and haughtiness of heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.30', 'BSB', 'I know his insolence,” declares the LORD, “but it is futile. His boasting is as empty as his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will wail for Moab; I will cry out for all of Moab; I will moan for the men of Kir-heres.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.32', 'BSB', 'I will weep for you, O vine of Sibmah, more than I weep for Jazer. Your tendrils have extended to the sea; they reach even to Jazer. The destroyer has descended on your summer fruit and grape harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.33', 'BSB', 'Joy and gladness are removed from the orchard and from the fields of Moab. I have stopped the flow of wine from the presses; no one treads them with shouts of joy; their shouts are not for joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.34', 'BSB', 'There is a cry from Heshbon to Elealeh; they raise their voices to Jahaz, from Zoar to Horonaim and Eglath-shelishiyah; for even the waters of Nimrim have dried up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.35', 'BSB', 'In Moab, declares the LORD, I will bring an end to those who make offerings on the high places and burn incense to their gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.36', 'BSB', 'Therefore My heart laments like a flute for Moab; it laments like a flute for the men of Kir-heres, because the wealth they acquired has perished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.37', 'BSB', 'For every head is shaved and every beard is clipped; on every hand is a gash, and around every waist is sackcloth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.38', 'BSB', 'On all the rooftops of Moab and in the public squares, everyone is mourning; for I have shattered Moab like an unwanted jar,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.39', 'BSB', '“How shattered it is! How they wail! How Moab has turned his back in shame! Moab has become an object of ridicule and horror to all those around him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.40', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “Behold, an eagle swoops down and spreads his wings against Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.41', 'BSB', 'Kirioth has been taken, and the strongholds seized. In that day the heart of Moab’s warriors will be like the heart of a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.42', 'BSB', 'Moab will be destroyed as a nation because he vaunted himself against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.43', 'BSB', 'Terror and pit and snare await you, O dweller of Moab,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.44', 'BSB', '“Whoever flees the panic will fall into the pit, and whoever climbs from the pit will be caught in the snare. For I will bring upon Moab the year of their punishment,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.45', 'BSB', '“Those who flee will stand helpless in Heshbon’s shadow, because fire has gone forth from Heshbon and a flame from within Sihon. It devours the foreheads of Moab and the skulls of the sons of tumult.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.46', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, O Moab! The people of Chemosh have perished; for your sons have been taken into exile and your daughters have gone into captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.48.47', 'BSB', 'Yet in the latter days I will restore Moab from captivity,” declares the LORD. Here ends the judgment on Moab.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.1', 'BSB', 'Concerning the Ammonites, this is what the LORD says: “Has Israel no sons? Is he without heir? Why then has Milcom taken possession of Gad? Why have his people settled in their cities?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.2', 'BSB', 'Therefore, behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will sound the battle cry against Rabbah of the Ammonites. It will become a heap of ruins, and its villages will be burned. Then Israel will drive out their dispossessors, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.3', 'BSB', 'Wail, O Heshbon, for Ai has been destroyed; cry out, O daughters of Rabbah! Put on sackcloth and mourn; run back and forth within your walls, for Milcom will go into exile together with his priests and officials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.4', 'BSB', 'Why do you boast of your valleys— your valleys so fruitful, O faithless daughter? You trust in your riches and say, ‘Who can come against me?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.5', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am about to bring terror upon you, declares the Lord GOD of Hosts, from all those around you. You will each be driven headlong, with no one to regather the fugitives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.6', 'BSB', 'Yet afterward I will restore the Ammonites from captivity,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.7', 'BSB', 'Concerning Edom, this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Is there no longer wisdom in Teman? Has counsel perished from the prudent? Has their wisdom decayed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.8', 'BSB', 'Turn and run! Lie low, O dwellers of Dedan, for I will bring disaster on Esau at the time I punish him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.9', 'BSB', 'If grape gatherers came to you, would they not leave some gleanings? Were thieves to come in the night, would they not steal only what they wanted?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.10', 'BSB', 'But I will strip Esau bare; I will uncover his hiding places, and he will be unable to conceal himself. His descendants will be destroyed along with his relatives and neighbors, and he will be no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.11', 'BSB', 'Abandon your orphans; I will preserve their lives. Let your widows trust in Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.12', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: “If those who do not deserve to drink the cup must drink it, can you possibly remain unpunished? You will not go unpunished, for you must drink it too.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.13', 'BSB', 'For by Myself I have sworn, declares the LORD, that Bozrah will become a desolation, a disgrace, a ruin, and a curse, and all her cities will be in ruins forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.14', 'BSB', 'I have heard a message from the LORD; an envoy has been sent to the nations: “Assemble yourselves to march against her! Rise up for battle!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.15', 'BSB', '“For behold, I will make you small among nations, despised among men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.16', 'BSB', 'The terror you cause and the pride of your heart have deceived you, O dwellers in the clefts of the rocks, O occupiers of the mountain summit. Though you elevate your nest like the eagle, even from there I will bring you down,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.17', 'BSB', '“Edom will become an object of horror. All who pass by will be appalled and will scoff at all her wounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.18', 'BSB', 'As Sodom and Gomorrah were overthrown along with their neighbors,” says the LORD, “no one will dwell there; no man will abide there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, one will come up like a lion from the thickets of the Jordan to the watered pasture. For in an instant I will chase Edom from her land. Who is the chosen one I will appoint for this? For who is like Me, and who can challenge Me? What shepherd can stand against Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore hear the plans that the LORD has drawn up against Edom and the strategies He has devised against the people of Teman: Surely the little ones of the flock will be dragged away; certainly their pasture will be made desolate because of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.21', 'BSB', 'At the sound of their fall the earth will quake; their cry will resound to the Red Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.22', 'BSB', 'Look! An eagle will soar and swoop down, spreading its wings over Bozrah. In that day the hearts of Edom’s mighty men will be like the heart of a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.23', 'BSB', 'Concerning Damascus: “Hamath and Arpad are put to shame, for they have heard a bad report; they are agitated like the sea; their anxiety cannot be calmed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.24', 'BSB', 'Damascus has become feeble; she has turned to flee. Panic has gripped her; anguish and pain have seized her like a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.25', 'BSB', 'How is the city of praise not forsaken, the town that brings Me joy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.26', 'BSB', 'For her young men will fall in the streets, and all her warriors will be silenced in that day,” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.27', 'BSB', '“I will set fire to the walls of Damascus; it will consume the fortresses of Ben-hadad.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.28', 'BSB', 'Concerning Kedar and the kingdoms of Hazor, which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon defeated, this is what the LORD says: “Rise up, advance against Kedar, and destroy the people of the east!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.29', 'BSB', 'They will take their tents and flocks, their tent curtains and all their goods. They will take their camels for themselves. They will shout to them: ‘Terror is on every side!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.30', 'BSB', 'Run! Escape quickly! Lie low, O residents of Hazor,” declares the LORD, “for Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon has drawn up a plan against you; he has devised a strategy against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.31', 'BSB', 'Rise up, advance against a nation at ease, one that dwells securely,” declares the LORD. “They have no gates or bars; they live alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.32', 'BSB', 'Their camels will become plunder, and their large herds will be spoil. I will scatter to the wind in every direction those who shave their temples; I will bring calamity on them from all sides,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.33', 'BSB', '“Hazor will become a haunt for jackals, a desolation forever. No one will dwell there; no man will abide there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.34', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah the prophet concerning Elam at the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.35', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Behold, I will shatter Elam’s bow, the mainstay of their might.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.36', 'BSB', 'I will bring the four winds against Elam from the four corners of the heavens, and I will scatter them to all these winds. There will not be a nation to which Elam’s exiles will not go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.37', 'BSB', 'So I will shatter Elam before their foes, before those who seek their lives. I will bring disaster upon them, even My fierce anger,” declares the LORD. “I will send out the sword after them until I finish them off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.38', 'BSB', 'I will set My throne in Elam, and destroy its king and officials,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.49.39', 'BSB', '“Yet in the last days, I will restore Elam from captivity,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word that the LORD spoke through Jeremiah the prophet concerning Babylon and the land of the Chaldeans:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.2', 'BSB', '“Announce and declare to the nations; lift up a banner and proclaim it; hold nothing back when you say, ‘Babylon is captured; Bel is put to shame; Marduk is shattered, her images are disgraced, her idols are broken in pieces.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.3', 'BSB', 'For a nation from the north will come against her; it will make her land a desolation. No one will live in it; both man and beast will flee.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.4', 'BSB', '“In those days and at that time, declares the LORD, the children of Israel and the children of Judah will come together, weeping as they come, and will seek the LORD their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.5', 'BSB', 'They will ask the way to Zion and turn their faces toward it. They will come and join themselves to the LORD in an everlasting covenant that will never be forgotten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.6', 'BSB', 'My people are lost sheep; their shepherds have led them astray, causing them to roam the mountains. They have wandered from mountain to hill; they have forgotten their resting place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.7', 'BSB', 'All who found them devoured them, and their enemies said, ‘We are not guilty, for they have sinned against the LORD, their true pasture, the LORD, the hope of their fathers.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.8', 'BSB', 'Flee from the midst of Babylon; depart from the land of the Chaldeans; be like the he-goats that lead the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.9', 'BSB', 'For behold, I stir up and bring against Babylon an assembly of great nations from the land of the north. They will line up against her; from the north she will be captured. Their arrows will be like skilled warriors who do not return empty-handed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.10', 'BSB', 'Chaldea will be plundered; all who plunder her will have their fill,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.11', 'BSB', '“Because you rejoice, because you sing in triumph— you who plunder My inheritance— because you frolic like a heifer treading grain and neigh like stallions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.12', 'BSB', 'your mother will be greatly ashamed; she who bore you will be disgraced. Behold, she will be the least of the nations, a wilderness, a dry land, and a desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.13', 'BSB', 'Because of the wrath of the LORD, she will not be inhabited; she will become completely desolate. All who pass through Babylon will be horrified and will hiss at all her wounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.14', 'BSB', 'Line up in formation around Babylon, all you who draw the bow! Shoot at her! Spare no arrows! For she has sinned against the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.15', 'BSB', 'Raise a war cry against her on every side! She has thrown up her hands in surrender; her towers have fallen; her walls are torn down. Since this is the vengeance of the LORD, take out your vengeance upon her; as she has done, do the same to her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.16', 'BSB', 'Cut off the sower from Babylon, and the one who wields the sickle at harvest time. In the face of the oppressor’s sword, each will turn to his own people, each will flee to his own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.17', 'BSB', 'Israel is a scattered flock, chased away by lions. The first to devour him was the king of Assyria; the last to crush his bones was Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “I will punish the king of Babylon and his land as I punished the king of Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.19', 'BSB', 'I will return Israel to his pasture, and he will graze on Carmel and Bashan; his soul will be satisfied on the hills of Ephraim and Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.20', 'BSB', 'In those days and at that time, declares the LORD, a search will be made for Israel’s guilt, but there will be none, and for Judah’s sins, but they will not be found; for I will forgive the remnant I preserve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.21', 'BSB', 'Go up against the land of Merathaim, and against the residents of Pekod. Kill them and devote them to destruction. Do all that I have commanded you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.22', 'BSB', '“The noise of battle is in the land— the noise of great destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.23', 'BSB', 'How the hammer of the whole earth lies broken and shattered! What a horror Babylon has become among the nations!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.24', 'BSB', 'I laid a snare for you, O Babylon, and you were caught before you knew it. You were found and captured because you challenged the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.25', 'BSB', 'The LORD has opened His armory and brought out His weapons of wrath, for this is the work of the Lord GOD of Hosts in the land of the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.26', 'BSB', 'Come against her from the farthest border. Break open her granaries; pile her up like mounds of grain. Devote her to destruction; leave her no survivors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.27', 'BSB', 'Kill all her young bulls; let them go down to the slaughter. Woe to them, for their day has come— the time of their punishment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.28', 'BSB', 'Listen to the fugitives and refugees from the land of Babylon, declaring in Zion the vengeance of the LORD our God, the vengeance for His temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.29', 'BSB', 'Summon the archers against Babylon, all who string the bow. Encamp all around her; let no one escape. Repay her according to her deeds; do to her as she has done. For she has defied the LORD, the Holy One of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.30', 'BSB', 'Therefore, her young men will fall in the streets, and all her warriors will be silenced in that day,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.31', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am against you, O arrogant one,” declares the Lord GOD of Hosts, “for your day has come, the time when I will punish you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.32', 'BSB', 'The arrogant one will stumble and fall with no one to pick him up. And I will kindle a fire in his cities to consume all those around him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.33', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “The sons of Israel are oppressed, and the sons of Judah as well. All their captors hold them fast, refusing to release them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.34', 'BSB', 'Their Redeemer is strong; the LORD of Hosts is His name. He will fervently plead their case so that He may bring rest to the earth, but turmoil to those who live in Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.35', 'BSB', 'A sword is against the Chaldeans, declares the LORD, against those who live in Babylon, and against her officials and wise men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.36', 'BSB', 'A sword is against her false prophets, and they will become fools. A sword is against her warriors, and they will be filled with terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.37', 'BSB', 'A sword is against her horses and chariots and against all the foreigners in her midst, and they will become like women. A sword is against her treasuries, and they will be plundered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.38', 'BSB', 'A drought is upon her waters, and they will be dried up. For it is a land of graven images, and the people go mad over idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.39', 'BSB', 'So the desert creatures and hyenas will live there and ostriches will dwell there. It will never again be inhabited or lived in from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.40', 'BSB', 'As God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah along with their neighbors,” declares the LORD, “no one will dwell there; no man will abide there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.41', 'BSB', 'Behold, an army is coming from the north; a great nation and many kings are stirred up from the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.42', 'BSB', 'They grasp the bow and spear; they are cruel and merciless. Their voice roars like the sea, and they ride upon horses, lined up like men in formation against you, O Daughter of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.43', 'BSB', 'The king of Babylon has heard the report, and his hands hang limp. Anguish has gripped him, pain like that of a woman in labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.44', 'BSB', 'Behold, one will come up like a lion from the thickets of the Jordan to the watered pasture. For in an instant I will chase Babylon from her land. Who is the chosen one I will appoint for this? For who is like Me, and who can challenge Me? What shepherd can stand against Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.45', 'BSB', 'Therefore hear the plans that the LORD has drawn up against Babylon and the strategies He has devised against the land of the Chaldeans: Surely the little ones of the flock will be dragged away; certainly their pasture will be made desolate because of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.50.46', 'BSB', 'At the sound of Babylon’s capture the earth will quake; a cry will be heard among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Behold, I will stir up against Babylon and against the people of Leb-kamai the spirit of a destroyer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.2', 'BSB', 'I will send strangers to Babylon to winnow her and empty her land; for they will come against her from every side in her day of disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.3', 'BSB', 'Do not let the archer bend his bow or put on his armor. Do not spare her young men; devote all her army to destruction!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.4', 'BSB', 'And they will fall slain in the land of the Chaldeans, and pierced through in her streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.5', 'BSB', 'For Israel and Judah have not been abandoned by their God, the LORD of Hosts, though their land is full of guilt before the Holy One of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.6', 'BSB', 'Flee from Babylon! Escape with your lives! Do not be destroyed in her punishment. For this is the time of the LORD’s vengeance; He will pay her what she deserves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.7', 'BSB', 'Babylon was a gold cup in the hand of the LORD, making the whole earth drunk. The nations drank her wine; therefore the nations have gone mad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.8', 'BSB', 'Suddenly Babylon has fallen and been shattered. Wail for her; get her balm for her pain; perhaps she can be healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.9', 'BSB', '“We tried to heal Babylon, but she could not be healed. Abandon her! Let each of us go to his own land, for her judgment extends to the sky and reaches to the clouds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.10', 'BSB', '“The LORD has brought forth our vindication; come, let us tell in Zion what the LORD our God has accomplished.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.11', 'BSB', 'Sharpen the arrows! Fill the quivers! The LORD has aroused the spirit of the kings of the Medes, because His plan is aimed at Babylon to destroy her, for it is the vengeance of the LORD— vengeance for His temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.12', 'BSB', 'Raise a banner against the walls of Babylon; post the guard; station the watchmen; prepare the ambush. For the LORD has both devised and accomplished what He spoke against the people of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.13', 'BSB', 'You who dwell by many waters, rich in treasures, your end has come; the thread of your life is cut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts has sworn by Himself: “Surely I will fill you up with men as with locusts, and they will shout in triumph over you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.15', 'BSB', 'The LORD made the earth by His power; He established the world by His wisdom and stretched out the heavens by His understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.16', 'BSB', 'When He thunders, the waters in the heavens roar; He causes the clouds to rise from the ends of the earth. He generates the lightning with the rain and brings forth the wind from His storehouses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.17', 'BSB', 'Every man is senseless and devoid of knowledge; every goldsmith is put to shame by his idols. For his molten images are a fraud, and there is no breath in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.18', 'BSB', 'They are worthless, a work to be mocked. In the time of their punishment they will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.19', 'BSB', 'The Portion of Jacob is not like these, for He is the Maker of all things, and of the tribe of His inheritance— the LORD of Hosts is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.20', 'BSB', '“You are My war club, My weapon for battle. With you I shatter nations; with you I bring kingdoms to ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.21', 'BSB', 'With you I shatter the horse and rider; with you I shatter the chariot and driver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.22', 'BSB', 'With you I shatter man and woman; with you I shatter the old man and the youth; with you I shatter the young man and the maiden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.23', 'BSB', 'With you I shatter the shepherd and his flock; with you I shatter the farmer and his oxen; with you I shatter the governors and officials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.24', 'BSB', 'Before your very eyes I will repay Babylon and all the dwellers of Chaldea for all the evil they have done in Zion,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.25', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am against you, O destroying mountain, you who devastate the whole earth, declares the LORD. I will stretch out My hand against you; I will roll you over the cliffs and turn you into a charred mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.26', 'BSB', 'No one shall retrieve from you a cornerstone or a foundation stone, because you will become desolate forever,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.27', 'BSB', '“Raise a banner in the land! Blow the ram’s horn among the nations! Prepare the nations against her. Summon the kingdoms against her— Ararat, Minni, and Ashkenaz. Appoint a captain against her; bring up horses like swarming locusts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.28', 'BSB', 'Prepare the nations for battle against her— the kings of the Medes, their governors and all their officials, and all the lands they rule.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.29', 'BSB', 'The earth quakes and writhes because the LORD’s intentions against Babylon stand: to make the land of Babylon a desolation, without inhabitant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.30', 'BSB', 'The warriors of Babylon have stopped fighting; they sit in their strongholds. Their strength is exhausted; they have become like women. Babylon’s homes have been set ablaze, the bars of her gates are broken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.31', 'BSB', 'One courier races to meet another, and messenger follows messenger, to announce to the king of Babylon that his city has been captured from end to end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.32', 'BSB', 'The fords have been seized, the marshes set on fire, and the soldiers are terrified.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.33', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “The Daughter of Babylon is like a threshing floor at the time it is trampled. In just a little while her harvest time will come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.34', 'BSB', '“Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon has devoured me; he has crushed me. He has set me aside like an empty vessel; he has swallowed me like a monster; he filled his belly with my delicacies and vomited me out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.35', 'BSB', 'May the violence done to me and to my flesh be upon Babylon,” says the dweller of Zion. “May my blood be on the dwellers of Chaldea,” says Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.36', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: “Behold, I will plead your case and take vengeance on your behalf; I will dry up her sea and make her springs run dry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.37', 'BSB', 'Babylon will become a heap of rubble, a haunt for jackals, an object of horror and scorn, without inhabitant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.38', 'BSB', 'They will roar together like young lions; they will growl like lion cubs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.39', 'BSB', 'While they are flushed with heat, I will serve them a feast, and I will make them drunk so that they may revel; then they will fall asleep forever and never wake up, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.40', 'BSB', 'I will bring them down like lambs to the slaughter, like rams with male goats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.41', 'BSB', 'How Sheshach has been captured! The praise of all the earth has been seized. What a horror Babylon has become among the nations!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.42', 'BSB', 'The sea has come up over Babylon; she is covered in turbulent waves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.43', 'BSB', 'Her cities have become a desolation, a dry and arid land, a land where no one lives, where no son of man passes through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.44', 'BSB', 'I will punish Bel in Babylon. I will make him spew out what he swallowed. The nations will no longer stream to him; even the wall of Babylon will fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.45', 'BSB', 'Come out of her, My people! Save your lives, each of you, from the fierce anger of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.46', 'BSB', 'Do not let your heart grow faint, and do not be afraid when the rumor is heard in the land; for a rumor will come one year— and then another the next year— of violence in the land and of ruler against ruler.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.47', 'BSB', 'Therefore, behold, the days are coming when I will punish the idols of Babylon. Her entire land will suffer shame, and all her slain will lie fallen within her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.48', 'BSB', 'Then heaven and earth and all that is in them will shout for joy over Babylon because the destroyers from the north will come against her,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.49', 'BSB', '“Babylon must fall on account of the slain of Israel, just as the slain of all the earth have fallen because of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.50', 'BSB', 'You who have escaped the sword, depart and do not linger! Remember the LORD from far away, and let Jerusalem come to mind.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.51', 'BSB', '“We are ashamed because we have heard reproach; disgrace has covered our faces, because foreigners have entered the holy places of the LORD’s house.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.52', 'BSB', '“Therefore, behold, the days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when I will punish her idols, and throughout her land the wounded will groan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.53', 'BSB', 'Even if Babylon ascends to the heavens and fortifies her lofty stronghold, the destroyers I send will come against her,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.54', 'BSB', '“The sound of a cry comes from Babylon, the sound of great destruction from the land of the Chaldeans!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.55', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will destroy Babylon; He will silence her mighty voice. The waves will roar like great waters; the tumult of their voices will resound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.56', 'BSB', 'For a destroyer is coming against her— against Babylon. Her warriors will be captured, and their bows will be broken, for the LORD is a God of retribution; He will repay in full.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.57', 'BSB', 'I will make her princes and wise men drunk, along with her governors, officials, and warriors. Then they will fall asleep forever and not wake up,” declares the King, whose name is the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.58', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Babylon’s thick walls will be leveled, and her high gates consumed by fire. So the labor of the people will be for nothing; the nations will exhaust themselves to fuel the flames.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.59', 'BSB', 'This is the message that Jeremiah the prophet gave to the quartermaster Seraiah son of Neriah, the son of Mahseiah, when he went to Babylon with King Zedekiah of Judah in the fourth year of Zedekiah’s reign.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.60', 'BSB', 'Jeremiah had written on a single scroll about all the disaster that would come upon Babylon—all these words that had been written concerning Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.61', 'BSB', 'And Jeremiah said to Seraiah, “When you get to Babylon, see that you read all these words aloud,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.62', 'BSB', 'and say, ‘O LORD, You have promised to cut off this place so that no one will remain—neither man nor beast. Indeed, it will be desolate forever.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.63', 'BSB', 'When you finish reading this scroll, tie a stone to it and cast it into the Euphrates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.51.64', 'BSB', 'Then you are to say, ‘In the same way Babylon will sink and never rise again, because of the disaster I will bring upon her. And her people will grow weary.’” Here end the words of Jeremiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.1', 'BSB', 'Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. His mother’s name was Hamutal daughter of Jeremiah; she was from Libnah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.2', 'BSB', 'And Zedekiah did evil in the sight of the LORD, just as Jehoiakim had done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.3', 'BSB', 'For because of the anger of the LORD, all this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until He finally banished them from His presence. And Zedekiah also rebelled against the king of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.4', 'BSB', 'So in the ninth year of Zedekiah’s reign, on the tenth day of the tenth month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon marched against Jerusalem with his entire army. They encamped outside the city and built a siege wall all around it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.5', 'BSB', 'And the city was kept under siege until King Zedekiah’s eleventh year.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.6', 'BSB', 'By the ninth day of the fourth month, the famine in the city was so severe that the people of the land had no food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.7', 'BSB', 'Then the city was breached; and though the Chaldeans had surrounded the city, all the men of war fled the city by night by way of the gate between the two walls near the king’s garden. They headed toward the Arabah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.8', 'BSB', 'but the army of the Chaldeans pursued the king and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho, and all his army was separated from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.9', 'BSB', 'The Chaldeans seized the king and brought him up to the king of Babylon at Riblah in the land of Hamath, where he pronounced judgment on Zedekiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.10', 'BSB', 'There at Riblah the king of Babylon slaughtered the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and he also killed all the officials of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.11', 'BSB', 'Then he put out Zedekiah’s eyes, bound him with bronze shackles, and took him to Babylon, where he kept him in custody until his dying day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.12', 'BSB', 'On the tenth day of the fifth month, in the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar’s reign over Babylon, Nebuzaradan captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, entered Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.13', 'BSB', 'He burned down the house of the LORD, the royal palace, and all the houses of Jerusalem—every significant building.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.14', 'BSB', 'And the whole army of the Chaldeans under the captain of the guard broke down all the walls around Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.15', 'BSB', 'Then Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried into exile some of the poorest people and those who remained in the city, along with the deserters who had defected to the king of Babylon and the rest of the craftsmen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.16', 'BSB', 'But Nebuzaradan captain of the guard left behind some of the poorest of the land to tend the vineyards and fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.17', 'BSB', 'Moreover, the Chaldeans broke up the bronze pillars and stands and the bronze Sea in the house of the LORD, and they carried all the bronze to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.18', 'BSB', 'They also took away the pots, shovels, wick trimmers, sprinkling bowls, dishes, and all the articles of bronze used in the temple service.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.19', 'BSB', 'The captain of the guard also took away the basins, censers, sprinkling bowls, pots, lampstands, pans, and drink offering bowls—anything made of pure gold or fine silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.20', 'BSB', 'As for the two pillars, the Sea, the twelve bronze bulls under it, and the movable stands that King Solomon had made for the house of the LORD, the weight of the bronze from all these articles was beyond measure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.21', 'BSB', 'Each pillar was eighteen cubits tall and twelve cubits in circumference; each was hollow, four fingers thick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.22', 'BSB', 'The bronze capital atop one pillar was five cubits high, with a network of bronze pomegranates all around. The second pillar, with its pomegranates, was similar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.23', 'BSB', 'Each capital had ninety-six pomegranates on the sides, and a total of a hundred pomegranates were above the surrounding network.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.24', 'BSB', 'The captain of the guard also took away Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the priest of second rank, and the three doorkeepers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.25', 'BSB', 'Of those still in the city, he took a court official who had been appointed over the men of war, as well as seven trusted royal advisers. He also took the scribe of the captain of the army, who had enlisted the people of the land, and sixty men who were found in the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.26', 'BSB', 'Nebuzaradan captain of the guard took them and brought them to the king of Babylon at Riblah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.27', 'BSB', 'There at Riblah in the land of Hamath, the king of Babylon struck them down and put them to death. So Judah was taken into exile, away from its own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.28', 'BSB', 'These are the people Nebuchadnezzar carried away: in the seventh year, 3,023 Jews;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.29', 'BSB', 'in Nebuchadnezzar’s eighteenth year, 832 people from Jerusalem;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.30', 'BSB', 'in Nebuchadnezzar’s twenty-third year, Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried away 745 Jews. So in all, 4,600 people were taken away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.31', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-fifth day of the twelfth month of the thirty-seventh year of the exile of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the first year of the reign of Evil-merodach king of Babylon, he pardoned Jehoiachin king of Judah and released him from prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.32', 'BSB', 'And he spoke kindly to Jehoiachin and set his throne above the thrones of the other kings who were with him in Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.33', 'BSB', 'So Jehoiachin changed out of his prison clothes, and he dined regularly at the king’s table for the rest of his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jer.52.34', 'BSB', 'And the king of Babylon provided Jehoiachin a daily portion for the rest of his life, until the day of his death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.1', 'BSB', 'How lonely lies the city, once so full of people! She who was great among the nations has become a widow. The princess of the provinces has become a slave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.2', 'BSB', 'She weeps aloud in the night, with tears upon her cheeks. Among all her lovers there is no one to comfort her. All her friends have betrayed her; they have become her enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.3', 'BSB', 'Judah has gone into exile under affliction and harsh slavery; she dwells among the nations but finds no place to rest. All her pursuers have overtaken her in the midst of her distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.4', 'BSB', 'The roads to Zion mourn, because no one comes to her appointed feasts. All her gates are deserted; her priests groan, her maidens grieve, and she herself is bitter with anguish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.5', 'BSB', 'Her foes have become her masters; her enemies are at ease. For the LORD has brought her grief because of her many transgressions. Her children have gone away as captives before the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.6', 'BSB', 'All the splendor has departed from the Daughter of Zion. Her princes are like deer that find no pasture; they lack the strength to flee in the face of the hunter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.7', 'BSB', 'In the days of her affliction and wandering Jerusalem remembers all the treasures that were hers in days of old. When her people fell into enemy hands she received no help. Her enemies looked upon her, laughing at her downfall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.8', 'BSB', 'Jerusalem has sinned greatly; therefore she has become an object of scorn. All who honored her now despise her, for they have seen her nakedness; she herself groans and turns away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.9', 'BSB', 'Her uncleanness stains her skirts; she did not consider her end. Her downfall was astounding; there was no one to comfort her. Look, O LORD, on my affliction, for the enemy has triumphed!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.10', 'BSB', 'The adversary has seized all her treasures. For she has seen the nations enter her sanctuary— those You had forbidden to enter Your assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.11', 'BSB', 'All her people groan as they search for bread. They have traded their treasures for food to keep themselves alive. Look, O LORD, and consider, for I have become despised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.12', 'BSB', 'Is this nothing to you, all you who pass by? Look around and see! Is there any sorrow like mine, which was inflicted on me, which the LORD made me suffer on the day of His fierce anger?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.13', 'BSB', 'He sent fire from on high, and it overpowered my bones. He spread a net for my feet and turned me back. He made me desolate, faint all the day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.14', 'BSB', 'My transgressions are bound into a yoke, knit together by His hand; they are draped over my neck, and the Lord has broken my strength. He has delivered me into the hands of those I cannot withstand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.15', 'BSB', 'The Lord has rejected all the mighty men in my midst; He has summoned an army against me to crush my young warriors. Like grapes in a winepress, the Lord has trampled the Virgin Daughter of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.16', 'BSB', 'For these things I weep; my eyes flow with tears. For there is no one nearby to comfort me, no one to revive my soul. My children are destitute because the enemy has prevailed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.17', 'BSB', 'Zion stretches out her hands, but there is no one to comfort her. The LORD has decreed against Jacob that his neighbors become his foes. Jerusalem has become an unclean thing among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.18', 'BSB', 'The LORD is righteous, for I have rebelled against His command. Listen, all you people; look upon my suffering. My young men and maidens have gone into captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.19', 'BSB', 'I called out to my lovers, but they have betrayed me. My priests and elders perished in the city while they searched for food to keep themselves alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.20', 'BSB', 'See, O LORD, how distressed I am! I am churning within; my heart is pounding within me, for I have been most rebellious. Outside, the sword bereaves; inside, there is death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.21', 'BSB', 'People have heard my groaning, but there is no one to comfort me. All my enemies have heard of my trouble; they are glad that You have caused it. May You bring the day You have announced, so that they may become like me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.1.22', 'BSB', 'Let all their wickedness come before You, and deal with them as You have dealt with me because of all my transgressions. For my groans are many, and my heart is faint.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.1', 'BSB', 'How the Lord has covered the Daughter of Zion with the cloud of His anger! He has cast the glory of Israel from heaven to earth. He has abandoned His footstool in the day of His anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.2', 'BSB', 'Without pity the Lord has swallowed up all the dwellings of Jacob. In His wrath He has demolished the fortified cities of the Daughter of Judah. He brought to the ground and defiled her kingdom and its princes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.3', 'BSB', 'In fierce anger He has cut off every horn of Israel and withdrawn His right hand at the approach of the enemy. He has burned in Jacob like a flaming fire that consumes everything around it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.4', 'BSB', 'He has bent His bow like an enemy; His right hand is positioned. Like a foe He has killed all who were pleasing to the eye; He has poured out His wrath like fire on the tent of the Daughter of Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.5', 'BSB', 'The Lord is like an enemy; He has swallowed up Israel. He has swallowed up all her palaces and destroyed her strongholds. He has multiplied mourning and lamentation for the Daughter of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.6', 'BSB', 'He has laid waste His tabernacle like a garden booth; He has destroyed His place of meeting. The LORD has made Zion forget her appointed feasts and Sabbaths. In His fierce anger He has despised both king and priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.7', 'BSB', 'The Lord has rejected His altar; He has abandoned His sanctuary; He has delivered the walls of her palaces into the hand of the enemy. They have raised a shout in the house of the LORD as on the day of an appointed feast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.8', 'BSB', 'The LORD determined to destroy the wall of the Daughter of Zion. He stretched out a measuring line and did not withdraw His hand from destroying. He made the ramparts and walls lament; together they waste away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.9', 'BSB', 'Her gates have sunk into the ground; He has destroyed and shattered their bars. Her king and her princes are exiled among the nations, the law is no more, and even her prophets find no vision from the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.10', 'BSB', 'The elders of the Daughter of Zion sit on the ground in silence. They have thrown dust on their heads and put on sackcloth. The young women of Jerusalem have bowed their heads to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.11', 'BSB', 'My eyes fail from weeping; I am churning within. My heart is poured out in grief over the destruction of the daughter of my people, because children and infants faint in the streets of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.12', 'BSB', 'They cry out to their mothers: “Where is the grain and wine?” as they faint like the wounded in the streets of the city, as their lives fade away in the arms of their mothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.13', 'BSB', 'What can I say for you? To what can I compare you, O Daughter of Jerusalem? To what can I liken you, that I may console you, O Virgin Daughter of Zion? For your wound is as deep as the sea. Who can ever heal you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.14', 'BSB', 'The visions of your prophets were empty and deceptive; they did not expose your guilt to ward off your captivity. The burdens they envisioned for you were empty and misleading.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.15', 'BSB', 'All who pass by clap their hands at you in scorn. They hiss and shake their heads at the Daughter of Jerusalem: “Is this the city that was called the perfection of beauty, the joy of all the earth?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.16', 'BSB', 'All your enemies open their mouths against you. They hiss and gnash their teeth, saying, “We have swallowed her up. This is the day for which we have waited. We have lived to see it!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.17', 'BSB', 'The LORD has done what He planned; He has accomplished His decree, which He ordained in days of old; He has overthrown you without pity. He has let the enemy gloat over you and exalted the horn of your foes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.18', 'BSB', 'The hearts of the people cry out to the Lord. O wall of the Daughter of Zion, let your tears run down like a river day and night. Give yourself no relief, and your eyes no rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.19', 'BSB', 'Arise, cry out in the night from the first watch of the night. Pour out your heart like water in the presence of the Lord. Lift up your hands to Him for the lives of your children who are fainting from hunger on the corner of every street.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.20', 'BSB', 'Look, O LORD, and consider: Whom have You ever treated like this? Should women eat their offspring, the infants they have nurtured? Should priests and prophets be killed in the sanctuary of the Lord?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.21', 'BSB', 'Both young and old lie together in the dust of the streets. My young men and maidens have fallen by the sword. You have slain them in the day of Your anger; You have slaughtered them without compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.2.22', 'BSB', 'You summoned my attackers on every side, as for the day of an appointed feast. In the day of the LORD’s anger no one escaped or survived; my enemy has destroyed those I nurtured and reared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.1', 'BSB', 'I am the man who has seen affliction under the rod of God’s wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.2', 'BSB', 'He has driven me away and made me walk in darkness instead of light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.3', 'BSB', 'Indeed, He keeps turning His hand against me all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.4', 'BSB', 'He has worn away my flesh and skin; He has shattered my bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.5', 'BSB', 'He has besieged me and surrounded me with bitterness and hardship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.6', 'BSB', 'He has made me dwell in darkness like those dead for ages.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.7', 'BSB', 'He has walled me in so I cannot escape; He has weighed me down with chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.8', 'BSB', 'Even when I cry out and plead for help, He shuts out my prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.9', 'BSB', 'He has barred my ways with cut stones; He has made my paths crooked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.10', 'BSB', 'He is a bear lying in wait, a lion hiding in ambush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.11', 'BSB', 'He forced me off my path and tore me to pieces; He left me without help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.12', 'BSB', 'He bent His bow and set me as the target for His arrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.13', 'BSB', 'He pierced my kidneys with His arrows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.14', 'BSB', 'I am a laughingstock to all my people; they mock me in song all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.15', 'BSB', 'He has filled me with bitterness; He has intoxicated me with wormwood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.16', 'BSB', 'He has ground my teeth with gravel and trampled me in the dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.17', 'BSB', 'My soul has been deprived of peace; I have forgotten what prosperity is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.18', 'BSB', 'So I say, “My strength has perished, along with my hope from the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.19', 'BSB', 'Remember my affliction and wandering, the wormwood and the gall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.20', 'BSB', 'Surely my soul remembers and is humbled within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.21', 'BSB', 'Yet I call this to mind, and therefore I have hope:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.22', 'BSB', 'Because of the loving devotion of the LORD we are not consumed, for His mercies never fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.23', 'BSB', 'They are new every morning; great is Your faithfulness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.24', 'BSB', '“The LORD is my portion,” says my soul, “therefore I will hope in Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.25', 'BSB', 'The LORD is good to those who wait for Him, to the soul who seeks Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.26', 'BSB', 'It is good to wait quietly for the salvation of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.27', 'BSB', 'It is good for a man to bear the yoke while he is still young.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.28', 'BSB', 'Let him sit alone in silence, for God has disciplined him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.29', 'BSB', 'Let him bury his face in the dust— perhaps there is still hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.30', 'BSB', 'Let him offer his cheek to the one who would strike him; let him be filled with reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.31', 'BSB', 'For the Lord will not cast us off forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.32', 'BSB', 'Even if He causes grief, He will show compassion according to His abundant loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.33', 'BSB', 'For He does not willingly afflict or grieve the sons of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.34', 'BSB', 'To crush underfoot all the prisoners of the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.35', 'BSB', 'to deny a man justice before the Most High,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.36', 'BSB', 'to subvert a man in his lawsuit— of these the Lord does not approve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.37', 'BSB', 'Who has spoken and it came to pass, unless the Lord has ordained it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.38', 'BSB', 'Do not both adversity and good come from the mouth of the Most High?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.39', 'BSB', 'Why should any mortal man complain, in view of his sins?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.40', 'BSB', 'Let us examine and test our ways, and turn back to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.41', 'BSB', 'Let us lift up our hearts and hands to God in heaven:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.42', 'BSB', '“We have sinned and rebelled; You have not forgiven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.43', 'BSB', 'You have covered Yourself in anger and pursued us; You have killed without pity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.44', 'BSB', 'You have covered Yourself with a cloud that no prayer can pass through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.45', 'BSB', 'You have made us scum and refuse among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.46', 'BSB', 'All our enemies open their mouths against us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.47', 'BSB', 'Panic and pitfall have come upon us— devastation and destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.48', 'BSB', 'Streams of tears flow from my eyes over the destruction of the daughter of my people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.49', 'BSB', 'My eyes overflow unceasingly, without relief,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.50', 'BSB', 'until the LORD looks down from heaven and sees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.51', 'BSB', 'My eyes bring grief to my soul because of all the daughters of my city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.52', 'BSB', 'Without cause my enemies hunted me like a bird.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.53', 'BSB', 'They dropped me alive into a pit and cast stones upon me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.54', 'BSB', 'The waters flowed over my head, and I thought I was going to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.55', 'BSB', 'I called on Your name, O LORD, out of the depths of the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.56', 'BSB', 'You heard my plea: “Do not ignore my cry for relief.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.57', 'BSB', 'You drew near when I called on You; You said, “Do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.58', 'BSB', 'You defend my cause, O Lord; You redeem my life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.59', 'BSB', 'You have seen, O LORD, the wrong done to me; vindicate my cause!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.60', 'BSB', 'You have seen all their malice, all their plots against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.61', 'BSB', 'O LORD, You have heard their insults, all their plots against me—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.62', 'BSB', 'the slander and murmuring of my assailants against me all day long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.63', 'BSB', 'When they sit and when they rise, see how they mock me in song.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.64', 'BSB', 'You will pay them back what they deserve, O LORD, according to the work of their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.65', 'BSB', 'Put a veil of anguish over their hearts; may Your curse be upon them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.3.66', 'BSB', 'You will pursue them in anger and exterminate them from under Your heavens, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.1', 'BSB', 'How the gold has become tarnished, the pure gold has become dull! The gems of the temple lie scattered on every street corner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.2', 'BSB', 'How the precious sons of Zion, once worth their weight in pure gold, are now esteemed as jars of clay, the work of a potter’s hands!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.3', 'BSB', 'Even jackals offer their breasts to nurse their young, but the daughter of my people has become cruel, like an ostrich in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.4', 'BSB', 'The nursing infant’s tongue clings in thirst to the roof of his mouth. Little children beg for bread, but no one gives them any.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.5', 'BSB', 'Those who once ate delicacies are destitute in the streets; those brought up in crimson huddle in ash heaps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.6', 'BSB', 'The punishment of the daughter of my people is greater than that of Sodom, which was overthrown in an instant without a hand turned to help her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.7', 'BSB', 'Her dignitaries were brighter than snow, whiter than milk; their bodies were more ruddy than rubies, their appearance like sapphires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.8', 'BSB', 'But now their appearance is blacker than soot; they are not recognized in the streets. Their skin has shriveled on their bones; it has become as dry as a stick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.9', 'BSB', 'Those slain by the sword are better off than those who die of hunger, who waste away, pierced with pain because the fields lack produce.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.10', 'BSB', 'The hands of compassionate women have cooked their own children, who became their food in the destruction of the daughter of my people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD has exhausted His wrath; He has poured out His fierce anger; He has kindled a fire in Zion, and it has consumed her foundations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.12', 'BSB', 'The kings of the earth did not believe, nor any people of the world, that an enemy or a foe could enter the gates of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.13', 'BSB', 'But this was for the sins of her prophets and the guilt of her priests, who shed the blood of the righteous in her midst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.14', 'BSB', 'They wandered blind in the streets, defiled by this blood, so that no one dared to touch their garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.15', 'BSB', '“Go away! Unclean!” men shouted at them. “Away, away! Do not touch us!” So they fled and wandered. Among the nations it was said, “They can stay here no longer.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.16', 'BSB', 'The presence of the LORD has scattered them; He regards them no more. The priests are shown no honor; the elders find no favor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.17', 'BSB', 'All the while our eyes were failing as we looked in vain for help. We watched from our towers for a nation that could not save us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.18', 'BSB', 'They stalked our every step, so that we could not walk in our streets. Our end drew near, our time ran out, for our end had come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.19', 'BSB', 'Those who chased us were swifter than the eagles in the sky; they pursued us over the mountains and ambushed us in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.20', 'BSB', 'The LORD’s anointed, the breath of our life, was captured in their pits. We had said of him, “Under his shadow we will live among the nations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.21', 'BSB', 'So rejoice and be glad, O Daughter of Edom, you who dwell in the land of Uz. Yet the cup will pass to you as well; you will get drunk and expose yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.4.22', 'BSB', 'O Daughter of Zion, your punishment is complete; He will not prolong your exile. But He will punish your iniquity, O Daughter of Edom; He will expose your sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.1', 'BSB', 'Remember, O LORD, what has happened to us. Look and see our disgrace!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.2', 'BSB', 'Our inheritance has been turned over to strangers, our houses to foreigners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.3', 'BSB', 'We have become fatherless orphans; our mothers are widows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.4', 'BSB', 'We must buy the water we drink; our wood comes at a price.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.5', 'BSB', 'We are closely pursued; we are weary and find no rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.6', 'BSB', 'We submitted to Egypt and Assyria to get enough bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.7', 'BSB', 'Our fathers sinned and are no more, but we bear their punishment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.8', 'BSB', 'Slaves rule over us; there is no one to deliver us from their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.9', 'BSB', 'We get our bread at the risk of our lives because of the sword in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.10', 'BSB', 'Our skin is as hot as an oven with fever from our hunger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.11', 'BSB', 'Women have been ravished in Zion, virgins in the cities of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.12', 'BSB', 'Princes have been hung up by their hands; elders receive no respect.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.13', 'BSB', 'Young men toil at millstones; boys stagger under loads of wood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.14', 'BSB', 'The elders have left the city gate; the young men have stopped their music.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.15', 'BSB', 'Joy has left our hearts; our dancing has turned to mourning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.16', 'BSB', 'The crown has fallen from our head. Woe to us, for we have sinned!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.17', 'BSB', 'Because of this, our hearts are faint; because of these, our eyes grow dim—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.18', 'BSB', 'because of Mount Zion, which lies desolate, patrolled by foxes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.19', 'BSB', 'You, O LORD, reign forever; Your throne endures from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.20', 'BSB', 'Why have You forgotten us forever? Why have You forsaken us for so long?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.21', 'BSB', 'Restore us to Yourself, O LORD, so we may return; renew our days as of old,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Lam.5.22', 'BSB', 'unless You have utterly rejected us and remain angry with us beyond measure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.1', 'BSB', 'In the thirtieth year, on the fifth day of the fourth month, while I was among the exiles by the River Kebar, the heavens opened and I saw visions of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.2', 'BSB', 'On the fifth day of the month—it was the fifth year of the exile of King Jehoiachin—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.3', 'BSB', 'the word of the LORD came directly to Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans by the River Kebar. And there the LORD’s hand was upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.4', 'BSB', 'I looked and saw a whirlwind coming from the north, a great cloud with fire flashing back and forth and brilliant light all around it. In the center of the fire was a gleam like amber,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.5', 'BSB', 'and within it was the form of four living creatures. And this was their appearance: They had a human form,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.6', 'BSB', 'but each had four faces and four wings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.7', 'BSB', 'Their legs were straight, and the soles of their feet were like the hooves of a calf, gleaming like polished bronze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.8', 'BSB', 'Under their wings on their four sides they had human hands. All four living creatures had faces and wings,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.9', 'BSB', 'and their wings were touching one another. They did not turn as they moved; each one went straight ahead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.10', 'BSB', 'The form of their faces was that of a man, and each of the four had the face of a lion on the right side, the face of an ox on the left side, and also the face of an eagle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.11', 'BSB', 'Such were their faces. Their wings were spread upward; each had two wings touching the wings of the creature on either side, and two wings covering its body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.12', 'BSB', 'Each creature went straight ahead. Wherever the spirit would go, they would go, without turning as they moved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.13', 'BSB', 'In the midst of the living creatures was the appearance of glowing coals of fire, or of torches. Fire moved back and forth between the living creatures; it was bright, and lightning flashed out of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.14', 'BSB', 'The creatures were darting back and forth as quickly as flashes of lightning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.15', 'BSB', 'When I looked at the living creatures, I saw a wheel on the ground beside each creature with its four faces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.16', 'BSB', 'The workmanship of the wheels looked like the gleam of beryl, and all four had the same likeness. Their workmanship looked like a wheel within a wheel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.17', 'BSB', 'As they moved, they went in any of the four directions, without pivoting as they moved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.18', 'BSB', 'Their rims were high and awesome, and all four rims were full of eyes all around.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.19', 'BSB', 'So as the living creatures moved, the wheels moved beside them, and when the creatures rose from the ground, the wheels also rose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.20', 'BSB', 'Wherever the spirit would go, they would go, and the wheels would rise alongside them, because the spirit of the living creatures was in the wheels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.21', 'BSB', 'When the creatures moved, the wheels moved; when the creatures stood still, the wheels stood still; and when the creatures rose from the ground, the wheels rose alongside them, because the spirit of the living creatures was in the wheels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.22', 'BSB', 'Spread out above the heads of the living creatures was the likeness of an awesome expanse, gleaming like crystal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.23', 'BSB', 'And under the expanse, their wings stretched out toward one another. Each one also had two wings covering its body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.24', 'BSB', 'When the creatures moved, I heard the sound of their wings like the roar of many waters, like the voice of the Almighty, like the tumult of an army. When they stood still, they lowered their wings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.25', 'BSB', 'And there came a voice from above the expanse over their heads as they stood still with their wings lowered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.26', 'BSB', 'Above the expanse over their heads was the likeness of a throne with the appearance of sapphire, and on the throne high above was a figure like that of a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.27', 'BSB', 'From what seemed to be His waist up, I saw a gleam like amber, with what looked like fire within it all around. And from what seemed to be His waist down, I saw what looked like fire; and brilliant light surrounded Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.1.28', 'BSB', 'The appearance of the brilliant light all around Him was like that of a rainbow in a cloud on a rainy day. This was the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the LORD. And when I saw it, I fell facedown and heard a voice speaking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.1', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “stand up on your feet and I will speak to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.2', 'BSB', 'And as He spoke to me, the Spirit entered me and set me on my feet, and I heard Him speaking to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.3', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “I am sending you to the Israelites, to a rebellious nation that has rebelled against Me. To this very day they and their fathers have rebelled against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.4', 'BSB', 'They are obstinate and stubborn children. I am sending you to them, and you are to say to them, ‘This is what the Lord GOD says.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.5', 'BSB', 'And whether they listen or refuse to listen—for they are a rebellious house—they will know that a prophet has been among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.6', 'BSB', 'But you, son of man, do not be afraid of them or their words. Do not be afraid, though briers and thorns surround you, and you dwell among scorpions. Do not be afraid of their words or dismayed by their presence, though they are a rebellious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.7', 'BSB', 'But speak My words to them, whether they listen or refuse to listen, for they are rebellious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.8', 'BSB', 'And you, son of man, listen to what I tell you. Do not be rebellious like that rebellious house. Open your mouth and eat what I give you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.9', 'BSB', 'Then I looked and saw a hand reaching out to me, and in it was a scroll,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.2.10', 'BSB', 'which He unrolled before me. And written on the front and back of it were words of lamentation, mourning, and woe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.1', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “eat what you find here. Eat this scroll, then go and speak to the house of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.2', 'BSB', 'So I opened my mouth, and He fed me the scroll.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.3', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “eat and fill your stomach with this scroll I am giving you.” So I ate, and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.4', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me, “Son of man, go now to the house of Israel and speak My words to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.5', 'BSB', 'For you are not being sent to a people of unfamiliar speech or difficult language, but to the house of Israel—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.6', 'BSB', 'not to the many peoples of unfamiliar speech and difficult language whose words you cannot understand. Surely if I had sent you to them, they would have listened to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.7', 'BSB', 'But the house of Israel will be unwilling to listen to you, since they are unwilling to listen to Me. For the whole house of Israel is hard-headed and hard-hearted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.8', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will make your face as hard as their faces, and your forehead as hard as their foreheads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.9', 'BSB', 'I will make your forehead like a diamond, harder than flint. Do not be afraid of them or dismayed at their presence, even though they are a rebellious house.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.10', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He added, “listen carefully to all the words I speak to you, and take them to heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.11', 'BSB', 'Go to your people, the exiles; speak to them and tell them, ‘This is what the Lord GOD says,’ whether they listen or refuse to listen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.12', 'BSB', 'Then the Spirit lifted me up, and I heard a great rumbling sound behind me: ‘Blessed be the glory of the LORD in His dwelling place!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.13', 'BSB', 'It was the sound of the wings of the living creatures brushing against one another and the sound of the wheels beside them, a great rumbling sound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.14', 'BSB', 'So the Spirit lifted me up and took me away, and I went in bitterness and in the anger of my spirit, with the strong hand of the LORD upon me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.15', 'BSB', 'I came to the exiles at Tel-abib who dwelt by the River Kebar. And for seven days I sat where they sat and remained there among them, overwhelmed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.16', 'BSB', 'At the end of seven days the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.17', 'BSB', '“Son of man, I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel. Whenever you hear a word from My mouth, give them a warning from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.18', 'BSB', 'If I say to the wicked man, ‘You will surely die,’ but you do not warn him or speak out to warn him from his wicked way to save his life, that wicked man will die in his iniquity, and I will hold you responsible for his blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.19', 'BSB', 'But if you warn a wicked man and he does not turn from his wickedness and his wicked way, he will die in his iniquity, but you will have saved yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.20', 'BSB', 'Now if a righteous man turns from his righteousness and commits iniquity, and I put a stumbling block before him, he will die. If you did not warn him, he will die in his sin, and the righteous acts he did will not be remembered. And I will hold you responsible for his blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.21', 'BSB', 'But if you warn the righteous man not to sin, and he does not sin, he will indeed live because he heeded your warning, and you will have saved yourself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.22', 'BSB', 'And there the hand of the LORD was upon me, and He said to me, “Get up, go out to the plain, and there I will speak with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.23', 'BSB', 'So I got up and went out to the plain, and behold, the glory of the LORD was present there, like the glory I had seen by the River Kebar, and I fell facedown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.24', 'BSB', 'Then the Spirit entered me and set me on my feet. He spoke with me and said, “Go, shut yourself inside your house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.25', 'BSB', 'And you, son of man, they will tie with ropes, and you will be bound so that you cannot go out among the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.26', 'BSB', 'I will make your tongue stick to the roof of your mouth, and you will be silent and unable to rebuke them, though they are a rebellious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.3.27', 'BSB', 'But when I speak with you, I will open your mouth, and you are to tell them, ‘This is what the Lord GOD says.’ Whoever listens, let him listen; and whoever refuses, let him refuse, for they are a rebellious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.1', 'BSB', '“Now you, son of man, take a brick, place it before you, and draw on it the city of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.2', 'BSB', 'Then lay siege against it: Construct a siege wall, build a ramp to it, set up camps against it, and place battering rams around it on all sides.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.3', 'BSB', 'Then take an iron plate and set it up as an iron wall between yourself and the city. Turn your face toward it so that it is under siege, and besiege it. This will be a sign to the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.4', 'BSB', 'Then lie down on your left side and place the iniquity of the house of Israel upon yourself. You are to bear their iniquity for the number of days you lie on your side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.5', 'BSB', 'For I have assigned to you 390 days, according to the number of years of their iniquity. So you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.6', 'BSB', 'When you have completed these days, lie down again, but on your right side, and bear the iniquity of the house of Judah. I have assigned to you 40 days, a day for each year.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.7', 'BSB', 'You must turn your face toward the siege of Jerusalem with your arm bared, and prophesy against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.8', 'BSB', 'Now behold, I will tie you up with ropes so you cannot turn from side to side until you have finished the days of your siege.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.9', 'BSB', 'But take wheat, barley, beans, lentils, millet, and spelt; put them in a single container and make them into bread for yourself. This is what you are to eat during the 390 days you lie on your side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.10', 'BSB', 'You are to weigh out twenty shekels of food to eat each day, and you are to eat it at set times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.11', 'BSB', 'You are also to measure out a sixth of a hin of water to drink, and you are to drink it at set times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.12', 'BSB', 'And you shall eat the food as you would a barley cake, after you bake it over dried human excrement in the sight of the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.13', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said, “This is how the Israelites will eat their defiled bread among the nations to which I will banish them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.14', 'BSB', '“Ah, Lord GOD,” I said, “I have never defiled myself. From my youth until now I have not eaten anything found dead or mauled by wild beasts. No unclean meat has ever entered my mouth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.15', 'BSB', '“Look,” He replied, “I will let you use cow dung instead of human excrement, and you may bake your bread over that.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.16', 'BSB', 'Then He told me, “Son of man, I am going to cut off the supply of food in Jerusalem. They will anxiously eat bread rationed by weight, and in despair they will drink water by measure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.4.17', 'BSB', 'So they will lack food and water; they will be appalled at the sight of one another wasting away in their iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.1', 'BSB', '“As for you, son of man, take a sharp sword, use it as a barber’s razor, and shave your head and beard. Then take a set of scales and divide the hair.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.2', 'BSB', 'When the days of the siege have ended, you are to burn up a third of the hair inside the city; you are also to take a third and slash it with the sword all around the city; and you are to scatter a third to the wind. For I will unleash a sword behind them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.3', 'BSB', 'But you are to take a few strands of hair and secure them in the folds of your garment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.4', 'BSB', 'Again, take a few of these, throw them into the fire, and burn them. From there a fire will spread to the whole house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘This is Jerusalem, which I have set in the center of the nations, with countries all around her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.6', 'BSB', 'But she has rebelled against My ordinances more wickedly than the nations, and against My statutes worse than the countries around her. For her people have rejected My ordinances and have not walked in My statutes.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘You have been more insubordinate than the nations around you; you have not walked in My statutes or kept My ordinances, nor have you even conformed to the ordinances of the nations around you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, I Myself am against you, Jerusalem, and I will execute judgments among you in the sight of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.9', 'BSB', 'Because of all your abominations, I will do to you what I have never done before and will never do again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.10', 'BSB', 'As a result, fathers among you will eat their sons, and sons will eat their fathers. I will execute judgments against you and scatter all your remnant to every wind.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, because you have defiled My sanctuary with all your detestable idols and abominations, I Myself will withdraw My favor; I will not look upon you with pity, nor will I spare you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.12', 'BSB', 'A third of your people will die by plague or be consumed by famine within you, a third will fall by the sword outside your walls, and a third I will scatter to every wind and unleash a sword behind them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.13', 'BSB', 'And when My anger is spent and I have vented My wrath against them, I will be appeased. And when I have spent My wrath on them, they will know that I, the LORD, in My zeal have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.14', 'BSB', 'I will make you a ruin and a disgrace among the nations around you, in the sight of all who pass by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.15', 'BSB', 'So you will be a reproach and a taunt, a warning and a horror to the nations around you, when I execute judgments against you in anger, wrath, and raging fury. I, the LORD, have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.16', 'BSB', 'When I shower you with the deadly arrows of famine and destruction that I will send to destroy you, I will intensify the famine against you and cut off your supply of food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.5.17', 'BSB', 'I will send famine and wild beasts against you, and they will leave you childless. Plague and bloodshed will sweep through you, and I will bring a sword against you. I, the LORD, have spoken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.1', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against the mountains of Israel and prophesy against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.3', 'BSB', 'You are to say: ‘O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD! This is what the Lord GOD says to the mountains and hills, to the ravines and valleys: I am about to bring a sword against you, and I will destroy your high places.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.4', 'BSB', 'Your altars will be demolished and your incense altars will be smashed; and I will cast down your slain before your idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.5', 'BSB', 'I will lay the corpses of the Israelites before their idols and scatter your bones around your altars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.6', 'BSB', 'Wherever you live, the cities will be laid waste and the high places will be demolished, so that your altars will be laid waste and desecrated, your idols smashed and obliterated, your incense altars cut down, and your works blotted out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.7', 'BSB', 'The slain will fall among you, and you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.8', 'BSB', 'Yet I will leave a remnant, for some of you will escape the sword when you are scattered among the nations and throughout the lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.9', 'BSB', 'Then in the nations to which they have been carried captive, your survivors will remember Me—how I have been grieved by their adulterous hearts that turned away from Me, and by their eyes that lusted after idols. So they will loathe themselves for the evil they have done and for all their abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.10', 'BSB', 'And they will know that I am the LORD; I did not declare in vain that I would bring this calamity upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.11', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Clap your hands, stomp your feet, and cry out “Alas!” because of all the wicked abominations of the house of Israel, who will fall by sword and famine and plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.12', 'BSB', 'He who is far off will die by the plague, he who is near will fall by the sword, and he who remains will die by famine. So I will vent My fury upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.13', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I am the LORD, when their slain lie among their idols around their altars, on every high hill, on all the mountaintops, and under every green tree and leafy oak—the places where they offered fragrant incense to all their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.6.14', 'BSB', 'I will stretch out My hand against them, and wherever they live I will make the land a desolate waste, from the wilderness to Diblah. Then they will know that I am the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.1', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.2', 'BSB', '“O son of man, this is what the Lord GOD says to the land of Israel: ‘The end! The end has come upon the four corners of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.3', 'BSB', 'The end is now upon you, and I will unleash My anger against you. I will judge you according to your ways and repay you for all your abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.4', 'BSB', 'I will not look on you with pity, nor will I spare you, but I will punish you for your ways and for the abominations among you. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Disaster! An unprecedented disaster — behold, it is coming!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.6', 'BSB', 'The end has come! The end has come! It has roused itself against you. Behold, it has come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.7', 'BSB', 'Doom has come to you, O inhabitants of the land. The time has come; the day is near; there is panic on the mountains instead of shouts of joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.8', 'BSB', 'Very soon I will pour out My wrath upon you and vent My anger against you; I will judge you according to your ways and repay you for all your abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.9', 'BSB', 'I will not look on you with pity, nor will I spare you, but I will punish you for your ways and for the abominations among you. Then you will know that it is I, the LORD, who strikes the blow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.10', 'BSB', 'Behold, the day is here! It has come! Doom has gone out, the rod has budded, arrogance has bloomed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.11', 'BSB', 'Their violence has grown into a rod to punish their wickedness. None of them will remain: none of their multitude, none of their wealth, and nothing of value.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.12', 'BSB', 'The time has come; the day has arrived. Let the buyer not rejoice and the seller not mourn, for wrath is upon the whole multitude.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.13', 'BSB', 'The seller will surely not recover what he sold while both remain alive. For the vision concerning the whole multitude will not be revoked, and because of their iniquity, not one of them will preserve his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.14', 'BSB', 'They have blown the trumpet and made everything ready, but no one goes to war, for My wrath is upon the whole multitude.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.15', 'BSB', 'The sword is outside; plague and famine are within. Those in the country will die by the sword, and those in the city will be devoured by famine and plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.16', 'BSB', 'The survivors will escape and live in the mountains, moaning like doves of the valley, each for his own iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.17', 'BSB', 'Every hand will go limp, and every knee will turn to water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.18', 'BSB', 'They will put on sackcloth, and terror will overwhelm them. Shame will cover all their faces, and all their heads will be shaved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.19', 'BSB', 'They will throw their silver into the streets, and their gold will seem unclean. Their silver and gold cannot save them in the day of the wrath of the LORD. They cannot satisfy their appetites or fill their stomachs with wealth, for it became the stumbling block that brought their iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.20', 'BSB', 'His beautiful ornaments they transformed into pride and used them to fashion their vile images and detestable idols. Therefore I will make these into something unclean for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.21', 'BSB', 'And I will hand these things over as plunder to foreigners and loot to the wicked of the earth, who will defile them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.22', 'BSB', 'I will turn My face away from them, and they will defile My treasured place. Violent men will enter it, and they will defile it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.23', 'BSB', 'Forge the chain, for the land is full of crimes of bloodshed, and the city is full of violence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.24', 'BSB', 'So I will bring the most wicked of nations to take possession of their houses. I will end the pride of the mighty, and their holy places will be profaned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.25', 'BSB', 'Anguish is coming! They will seek peace, but find none.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.26', 'BSB', 'Disaster upon disaster will come, and rumor after rumor. Then they will seek a vision from a prophet, but instruction from the priests will perish, as will counsel from the elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.7.27', 'BSB', 'The king will mourn, the prince will be clothed with despair, and the hands of the people of the land will tremble. I will deal with them according to their conduct, and I will judge them by their own standards. Then they will know that I am the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.1', 'BSB', 'In the sixth year, on the fifth day of the sixth month, I was sitting in my house, and the elders of Judah were sitting before me; and there the hand of the Lord GOD fell upon me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.2', 'BSB', 'Then I looked and saw a figure like that of a man. From His waist down His appearance was like fire, and from His waist up He was as bright as the gleam of amber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.3', 'BSB', 'He stretched out what looked like a hand and took me by the hair of my head. Then the Spirit lifted me up between earth and heaven and carried me in visions of God to Jerusalem, to the entrance of the north gate of the inner court, where the idol that provokes jealousy was seated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.4', 'BSB', 'And there I saw the glory of the God of Israel, like the vision I had seen in the plain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.5', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “now lift up your eyes to the north.” So I lifted up my eyes to the north, and in the entrance north of the Altar Gate I saw this idol of jealousy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.6', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “do you see what they are doing—the great abominations that the house of Israel is committing—to drive Me far from My sanctuary? Yet you will see even greater abominations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.7', 'BSB', 'Then He brought me to the entrance to the court, and I looked and saw a hole in the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.8', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He told me, “dig through the wall.” So I dug through the wall and discovered a doorway.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.9', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me, “Go in and see the wicked abominations they are committing here.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.10', 'BSB', 'So I went in and looked, and engraved all around the wall was every kind of crawling creature and detestable beast, along with all the idols of the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.11', 'BSB', 'Before them stood seventy elders of the house of Israel, with Jaazaniah son of Shaphan standing among them. Each had a censer in his hand, and a fragrant cloud of incense was rising.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.12', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “do you see what the elders of the house of Israel are doing in the darkness, each at the shrine of his own idol? For they are saying, ‘The LORD does not see us; the LORD has forsaken the land.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.13', 'BSB', 'Again, He told me, “You will see them committing even greater abominations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.14', 'BSB', 'Then He brought me to the entrance of the north gate of the house of the LORD, and I saw women sitting there, weeping for Tammuz.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.15', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “do you see this? Yet you will see even greater abominations than these.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.16', 'BSB', 'So He brought me to the inner court of the house of the LORD, and there at the entrance to the temple of the LORD, between the portico and the altar, were about twenty-five men with their backs to the temple of the LORD and their faces toward the east; and they were bowing to the east in worship of the sun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.17', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” He said to me, “do you see this? Is it not enough for the house of Judah to commit the abominations they are practicing here, that they must also fill the land with violence and continually provoke Me to anger? Look, they are even putting the branch to their nose!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.8.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will respond with wrath. I will not look on them with pity, nor will I spare them. Although they shout loudly in My ears, I will not listen to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.1', 'BSB', 'Then I heard Him call out in a loud voice, saying, “Draw near, O executioners of the city, each with a weapon of destruction in hand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.2', 'BSB', 'And I saw six men coming from the direction of the Upper Gate, which faces north, each with a weapon of slaughter in his hand. With them was another man clothed in linen who had a writing kit at his side. And they came in and stood beside the bronze altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.3', 'BSB', 'Then the glory of the God of Israel rose from above the cherubim, where it had been, and moved to the threshold of the temple. And He called to the man clothed in linen who had the writing kit at his side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.4', 'BSB', '“Go throughout the city of Jerusalem,” said the LORD, “and put a mark on the foreheads of the men sighing and groaning over all the abominations committed there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.5', 'BSB', 'And as I listened, He said to the others, “Follow him through the city and start killing; do not show pity or spare anyone!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.6', 'BSB', 'Slaughter the old men, the young men and maidens, the women and children; but do not go near anyone who has the mark. Now begin at My sanctuary.” So they began with the elders who were before the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.7', 'BSB', 'Then He told them, “Defile the temple and fill the courts with the slain. Go forth!” So they went out and began killing throughout the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.8', 'BSB', 'While they were killing, I was left alone. And I fell facedown and cried out, “Oh, Lord GOD, when You pour out Your wrath on Jerusalem, will You destroy the entire remnant of Israel?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.9', 'BSB', 'He replied, “The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is exceedingly great. The land is full of bloodshed, and the city is full of perversity. For they say, ‘The LORD has forsaken the land; the LORD does not see.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.10', 'BSB', 'But as for Me, I will not look on them with pity, nor will I spare them. I will bring their deeds down upon their own heads.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.9.11', 'BSB', 'Then the man clothed in linen with the writing kit at his side reported back, “I have done as You commanded.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.1', 'BSB', 'And I looked and saw above the expanse, above the heads of the cherubim, the likeness of a throne of sapphire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.2', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to the man clothed in linen, “Go inside the wheelwork beneath the cherubim. Fill your hands with burning coals from among the cherubim and scatter them over the city.” And as I watched, he went in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.3', 'BSB', 'Now when the man went in, the cherubim were standing on the south side of the temple, and a cloud filled the inner court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.4', 'BSB', 'Then the glory of the LORD rose from above the cherubim and stood over the threshold of the temple. The temple was filled with the cloud, and the court was filled with the brightness of the glory of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.5', 'BSB', 'The sound of the wings of the cherubim could be heard as far as the outer court, like the voice of God Almighty when He speaks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.6', 'BSB', 'When the LORD commanded the man clothed in linen, saying, “Take fire from within the wheelwork, from among the cherubim,” the man went in and stood beside a wheel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.7', 'BSB', 'Then one of the cherubim reached out his hand and took some of the fire that was among them. And he put it into the hands of the man clothed in linen, who received it and went out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.8', 'BSB', '(The cherubim appeared to have the form of human hands under their wings.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.9', 'BSB', 'Then I looked and saw four wheels beside the cherubim, one wheel beside each cherub. And the wheels gleamed like a beryl stone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.10', 'BSB', 'As for their appearance, all four had the same form, like a wheel within a wheel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.11', 'BSB', 'When they moved, they would go in any of the four directions, without turning as they moved. For wherever the head faced, the cherubim would go in that direction, without turning as they moved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.12', 'BSB', 'Their entire bodies, including their backs, hands, and wings, were full of eyes all around, as were their four wheels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.13', 'BSB', 'I heard the wheels being called “the whirling wheels.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.14', 'BSB', 'Each of the cherubim had four faces: the first face was that of a cherub, the second that of a man, the third that of a lion, and the fourth that of an eagle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.15', 'BSB', 'Then the cherubim rose upward. These were the living creatures I had seen by the River Kebar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.16', 'BSB', 'When the cherubim moved, the wheels moved beside them, and even when they spread their wings to rise from the ground, the wheels did not veer away from their side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.17', 'BSB', 'When the cherubim stood still, the wheels also stood still, and when they ascended, the wheels ascended with them, for the spirit of the living creatures was in the wheels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.18', 'BSB', 'Then the glory of the LORD moved away from the threshold of the temple and stood above the cherubim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.19', 'BSB', 'As I watched, the cherubim lifted their wings and rose up from the ground, with the wheels beside them as they went. And they stopped at the entrance of the east gate of the house of the LORD, with the glory of the God of Israel above them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.20', 'BSB', 'These were the living creatures I had seen beneath the God of Israel by the River Kebar, and I knew that they were cherubim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.21', 'BSB', 'Each had four faces and four wings, with what looked like human hands under their wings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.10.22', 'BSB', 'Their faces looked like the faces I had seen by the River Kebar. Each creature went straight ahead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.1', 'BSB', 'Then the Spirit lifted me up and brought me to the gate of the house of the LORD that faces east. And there at the entrance of the gate were twenty-five men. Among them I saw Jaazaniah son of Azzur and Pelatiah son of Benaiah, who were leaders of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.2', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to me, “Son of man, these are the men who plot evil and give wicked counsel in this city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.3', 'BSB', 'They are saying, ‘Is not the time near to build houses? The city is the cooking pot, and we are the meat.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore prophesy against them; prophesy, O son of man!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.5', 'BSB', 'And the Spirit of the LORD fell upon me and told me to declare that this is what the LORD says: “That is what you are thinking, O house of Israel; and I know the thoughts that arise in your minds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.6', 'BSB', 'You have multiplied those you killed in this city and filled its streets with the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: The slain you have laid within this city are the meat, and the city is the pot; but I will remove you from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.8', 'BSB', 'You fear the sword, so I will bring the sword against you, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.9', 'BSB', 'I will bring you out of the city and deliver you into the hands of foreigners, and I will execute judgments against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.10', 'BSB', 'You will fall by the sword, and I will judge you even to the borders of Israel. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.11', 'BSB', 'The city will not be a pot for you, nor will you be the meat within it. I will judge you even to the borders of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.12', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I am the LORD. For you have neither followed My statutes nor practiced My ordinances, but you have conformed to the ordinances of the nations around you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.13', 'BSB', 'Now as I was prophesying, Pelatiah son of Benaiah died. Then I fell facedown and cried out in a loud voice, “Oh, Lord GOD, will You bring the remnant of Israel to a complete end?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.14', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.15', 'BSB', '“Son of man, your brothers—your relatives, your fellow exiles, and the whole house of Israel—are those of whom the people of Jerusalem have said, ‘They are far away from the LORD; this land has been given to us as a possession.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Although I sent them far away among the nations and scattered them among the countries, yet for a little while I have been a sanctuary for them in the countries to which they have gone.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will gather you from the peoples and assemble you from the countries to which you have been scattered, and I will give back to you the land of Israel.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.18', 'BSB', 'When they return to it, they will remove all its detestable things and all its abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.19', 'BSB', 'And I will give them singleness of heart and put a new spirit within them; I will remove their heart of stone and give them a heart of flesh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.20', 'BSB', 'so that they may follow My statutes, keep My ordinances, and practice them. Then they will be My people, and I will be their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.21', 'BSB', 'But as for those whose hearts pursue detestable things and abominations, I will bring their conduct down upon their own heads, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.22', 'BSB', 'Then the cherubim, with the wheels beside them, spread their wings, and the glory of the God of Israel was above them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.23', 'BSB', 'And the glory of the LORD rose up from within the city and stood over the mountain east of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.24', 'BSB', 'And the Spirit lifted me up and carried me back to Chaldea, to the exiles in the vision given by the Spirit of God. After the vision had gone up from me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.11.25', 'BSB', 'I told the exiles everything the LORD had shown me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, you are living in a rebellious house. They have eyes to see but do not see, and ears to hear but do not hear, for they are a rebellious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore, son of man, pack your bags for exile. In broad daylight, set out from your place and go to another as they watch. Perhaps they will understand, though they are a rebellious house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.4', 'BSB', 'Bring out your baggage for exile by day, as they watch. Then in the evening, as they watch, go out like those who go into exile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.5', 'BSB', 'As they watch, dig through the wall and carry your belongings out through it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.6', 'BSB', 'And as they watch, lift your bags to your shoulder and take them out at dusk; cover your face so that you cannot see the land. For I have made you a sign to the house of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.7', 'BSB', 'So I did as I was commanded. I brought out my bags for exile by day, and in the evening I dug through the wall by hand. I took my belongings out at dusk, carrying them on my shoulder as they watched.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.8', 'BSB', 'And in the morning the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.9', 'BSB', '“Son of man, hasn’t the rebellious house of Israel asked you, ‘What are you doing?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.10', 'BSB', 'Tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘This burden concerns the prince in Jerusalem and all the house of Israel who are there.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.11', 'BSB', 'You are to say, ‘I am a sign to you.’ Just as it happened here, so will it be done to them; they will go into exile as captives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.12', 'BSB', 'And at dusk the prince among them will lift his bags to his shoulder and go out. They will dig through the wall to bring him out. He will cover his face so he cannot see the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.13', 'BSB', 'But I will spread My net over him, and he will be caught in My snare. I will bring him to Babylon, the land of the Chaldeans; yet he will not see it, and there he will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.14', 'BSB', 'And I will scatter to every wind all the attendants around him and all his troops, and I will draw a sword to chase after them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.15', 'BSB', 'And they will know that I am the LORD, when I disperse them among the nations and scatter them throughout the countries.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.16', 'BSB', 'But I will spare a few of them from sword and famine and plague, so that in the nations to which they go, they can recount all their abominations. Then they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.17', 'BSB', 'Moreover, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.18', 'BSB', '“Son of man, eat your bread with trembling, and drink your water with quivering and anxiety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.19', 'BSB', 'Then tell the people of the land that this is what the Lord GOD says about those living in Jerusalem and in the land of Israel: ‘They will eat their bread with anxiety and drink their water in dread, for their land will be stripped of everything in it because of the violence of all who dwell in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.20', 'BSB', 'The inhabited cities will be laid waste, and the land will become desolate. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.21', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.22', 'BSB', '“Son of man, what is this proverb that you have in the land of Israel: ‘The days go by, and every vision fails’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.23', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will put an end to this proverb, and in Israel they will no longer recite it.’ But say to them: ‘The days are at hand when every vision will be fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.24', 'BSB', 'For there will be no more false visions or flattering divinations within the house of Israel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.25', 'BSB', 'because I, the LORD, will speak whatever word I speak, and it will be fulfilled without delay. For in your days, O rebellious house, I will speak a message and bring it to pass, declares the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.26', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.27', 'BSB', '“Son of man, take note that the house of Israel is saying, ‘The vision that he sees is for many years from now; he prophesies about the distant future.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.12.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘None of My words will be delayed any longer. The message I speak will be fulfilled, declares the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel who are now prophesying. Tell those who prophesy out of their own imagination: Hear the word of the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Woe to the foolish prophets who follow their own spirit, yet have seen nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.4', 'BSB', 'Your prophets, O Israel, are like foxes among the ruins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.5', 'BSB', 'You did not go up to the gaps or restore the wall around the house of Israel so that it would stand in the battle on the Day of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.6', 'BSB', 'They see false visions and speak lying divinations. They claim, ‘Thus declares the LORD,’ when the LORD did not send them; yet they wait for the fulfillment of their message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.7', 'BSB', 'Haven’t you seen a false vision and spoken a lying divination when you proclaim, ‘Thus declares the LORD,’ even though I have not spoken?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Because you have uttered vain words and seen false visions, I am against you, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.9', 'BSB', 'My hand will be against the prophets who see false visions and speak lying divinations. They will not belong to the council of My people or be recorded in the register of the house of Israel, nor will they enter the land of Israel. Then you will know that I am the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.10', 'BSB', 'Because they have led My people astray, saying, ‘Peace,’ when there is no peace, and whitewashing any flimsy wall that is built,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.11', 'BSB', 'tell those whitewashing the wall that it will fall. Rain will come in torrents, I will send hailstones plunging down, and a windstorm will burst forth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.12', 'BSB', 'Surely when the wall has fallen, you will not be asked, ‘Where is the whitewash with which you covered it?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: In My wrath I will release a windstorm, and in My anger torrents of rain and hail will fall with destructive fury.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.14', 'BSB', 'I will tear down the wall you whitewashed and level it to the ground, so that its foundation is exposed. The city will fall, and you will be destroyed within it. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.15', 'BSB', 'And after I have vented My wrath against the wall and against those who whitewashed it, I will say to you: ‘The wall is gone, and so are those who whitewashed it—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.16', 'BSB', 'those prophets of Israel who prophesied to Jerusalem and saw a vision of peace for her when there was no peace, declares the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.17', 'BSB', 'Now, O son of man, set your face against the daughters of your people who prophesy out of their own imagination. Prophesy against them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.18', 'BSB', 'and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: Woe to the women who sew magic charms on their wrists and make veils for the heads of people of every height, in order to ensnare their souls. Will you ensnare the souls of My people but preserve your own?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.19', 'BSB', 'You have profaned Me among My people for handfuls of barley and scraps of bread. By lying to My people who would listen, you have killed those who should not have died and spared those who should not have lived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: See, I am against the magic charms with which you ensnare souls like birds, and I will tear them from your arms. So I will free the souls you have ensnared like birds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.21', 'BSB', 'I will also tear off your veils and deliver My people from your hands, so that they will no longer be prey in your hands. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.22', 'BSB', 'Because you have disheartened the righteous with your lies, even though I have caused them no grief, and because you have encouraged the wicked not to turn from their evil ways to save their lives,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.13.23', 'BSB', 'therefore you will no longer see false visions or practice divination. I will deliver My people from your hands. Then you will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.1', 'BSB', 'Then some of the elders of Israel came and sat down before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.2', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.3', 'BSB', '“Son of man, these men have set up idols in their hearts and put wicked stumbling blocks before their faces. Should I consult with them in any way?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore speak to them and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘When any Israelite sets up idols in his heart and puts a wicked stumbling block before his face, and then comes to the prophet, I the LORD will answer him according to his great idolatry,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.5', 'BSB', 'so that I may take hold of the hearts of the people of Israel. For because of their idols, they are all estranged from Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell the house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Repent and turn away from your idols; turn your faces away from all your abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.7', 'BSB', 'For when any Israelite or any foreigner dwelling in Israel separates himself from Me, sets up idols in his heart, and puts a wicked stumbling block before his face, and then comes to the prophet to inquire of Me, I the LORD will answer him Myself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.8', 'BSB', 'I will set My face against that man and make him a sign and a proverb; I will cut him off from among My people. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.9', 'BSB', 'But if the prophet is enticed to speak a message, then it was I the LORD who enticed him, and I will stretch out My hand against him and destroy him from among My people Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.10', 'BSB', 'They will bear their punishment—the punishment of the inquirer will be the same as that of the prophet—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.11', 'BSB', 'in order that the house of Israel may no longer stray from Me and no longer defile themselves with all their transgressions. Then they will be My people and I will be their God, declares the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.12', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.13', 'BSB', '“Son of man, if a land sins against Me by acting unfaithfully, and I stretch out My hand against it to cut off its supply of food, to send famine upon it, and to cut off from it both man and beast,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.14', 'BSB', 'then even if these three men—Noah, Daniel, and Job—were in it, their righteousness could deliver only themselves, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.15', 'BSB', 'Or if I send wild beasts through the land to leave it childless and desolate, with no man passing through it for fear of the beasts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.16', 'BSB', 'then as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, even if these three men were in it, they could not deliver their own sons or daughters. They alone would be delivered, but the land would be desolate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.17', 'BSB', 'Or if I bring a sword against that land and say, ‘Let a sword pass through it,’ so that I cut off from it both man and beast,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.18', 'BSB', 'then as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, even if these three men were in it, they could not deliver their own sons or daughters. They alone would be delivered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.19', 'BSB', 'Or if I send a plague into that land and pour out My wrath upon it through bloodshed, cutting off from it both man and beast,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.20', 'BSB', 'then as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, even if Noah, Daniel, and Job were in it, they could not deliver their own sons or daughters. Their righteousness could deliver only themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.21', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘How much worse will it be when I send against Jerusalem My four dire judgments—sword, famine, wild beasts, and plague—in order to cut off from it both man and beast?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.22', 'BSB', 'Yet, behold, some survivors will be left in it—sons and daughters who will be brought out. They will come out to you, and when you see their conduct and actions, you will be comforted regarding the disaster I have brought upon Jerusalem—all that I have brought upon it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.14.23', 'BSB', 'They will bring you consolation when you see their conduct and actions, and you will know that it was not without cause that I have done all these things within it,’ declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, how does the wood of the vine surpass any other branch among the trees in the forest?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.3', 'BSB', 'Can wood be taken from it to make something useful? Or can one make from it a peg on which to hang utensils?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.4', 'BSB', 'No, it is cast into the fire for fuel. The fire devours both ends, and the middle is charred. Can it be useful for anything?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.5', 'BSB', 'Even when it was whole, it could not be made useful. How much less can it ever be useful when the fire has consumed it and charred it!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Like the wood of the vine among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so I will give up the people of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.7', 'BSB', 'And I will set My face against them. Though they may have escaped the fire, yet another fire will consume them. And when I set My face against them, you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.15.8', 'BSB', 'Thus I will make the land desolate, because they have acted unfaithfully,’ declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.1', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, confront Jerusalem with her abominations', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.3', 'BSB', 'and tell her that this is what the Lord GOD says to Jerusalem: Your origin and your birth were in the land of the Canaanites. Your father was an Amorite and your mother a Hittite.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.4', 'BSB', 'On the day of your birth your cord was not cut, nor were you washed with water for cleansing. You were not rubbed with salt or wrapped in cloths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.5', 'BSB', 'No one cared enough for you to do even one of these things out of compassion for you. Instead, you were thrown out into the open field, because you were despised on the day of your birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.6', 'BSB', 'Then I passed by and saw you wallowing in your blood, and as you lay there in your blood I said to you, ‘Live!’ There I said to you, ‘Live!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.7', 'BSB', 'I made you thrive like a plant of the field. You grew up and matured and became very beautiful. Your breasts were formed and your hair grew, but you were naked and bare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.8', 'BSB', 'Then I passed by and saw you, and you were indeed old enough for love. So I spread My cloak over you and covered your nakedness. I pledged Myself to you, entered into a covenant with you, and you became Mine, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.9', 'BSB', 'Then I bathed you with water, rinsed off your blood, and anointed you with oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.10', 'BSB', 'I clothed you in embroidered cloth and gave you sandals of fine leather. I wrapped you in fine linen and covered you with silk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.11', 'BSB', 'I adorned you with jewelry, and I put bracelets on your wrists and a chain around your neck.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.12', 'BSB', 'I put a ring in your nose, earrings on your ears, and a beautiful crown upon your head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.13', 'BSB', 'So you were adorned with gold and silver, and your clothing was made of fine linen, silk, and embroidered cloth. You ate fine flour, honey, and oil. You became very beautiful and rose to be queen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.14', 'BSB', 'Your fame spread among the nations on account of your beauty, for it was perfect in the splendor I bestowed on you, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.15', 'BSB', 'But because of your fame, you trusted in your beauty and played the harlot. You lavished your favors on everyone who passed by, and your beauty was theirs for the asking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.16', 'BSB', 'You took some of your garments and made colorful high places for yourself, and on them you prostituted yourself. Such things should not have happened; never should they have occurred!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.17', 'BSB', 'You also took the fine jewelry of gold and silver I had given you, and you made male idols with which to prostitute yourself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.18', 'BSB', 'You took your embroidered garments to cover them, and you set My oil and incense before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.19', 'BSB', 'And you set before them as a pleasing aroma the food I had given you—the fine flour, oil, and honey that I had fed you. That is what happened, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.20', 'BSB', 'You even took the sons and daughters you bore to Me and sacrificed them as food to idols. Was your prostitution not enough?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.21', 'BSB', 'You slaughtered My children and delivered them up through the fire to idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.22', 'BSB', 'And in all your abominations and acts of prostitution, you did not remember the days of your youth when you were naked and bare, wallowing in your own blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.23', 'BSB', 'Woe! Woe to you, declares the Lord GOD. And in addition to all your other wickedness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.24', 'BSB', 'you built yourself a mound and made yourself a lofty shrine in every public square.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.25', 'BSB', 'At the head of every street you built your lofty shrines and degraded your beauty. With increasing promiscuity, you spread your legs to all who passed by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.26', 'BSB', 'You prostituted yourself with your lustful neighbors, the Egyptians, and increased your promiscuity to provoke Me to anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore I stretched out My hand against you and reduced your portion. I gave you over to the desire of those who hate you, the daughters of the Philistines, who were ashamed of your lewd conduct.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.28', 'BSB', 'Then you prostituted yourself with the Assyrians, because you were not yet satisfied. Even after that, you were still not satisfied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.29', 'BSB', 'So you extended your promiscuity to Chaldea, the land of merchants—but even with this you were not satisfied!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.30', 'BSB', 'How weak-willed is your heart, declares the Lord GOD, while you do all these things, the acts of a shameless prostitute!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.31', 'BSB', 'But when you built your mounds at the head of every street and made your lofty shrines in every public square, you were not even like a prostitute, because you scorned payment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.32', 'BSB', 'You adulterous wife! You receive strangers instead of your own husband!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.33', 'BSB', 'Men give gifts to all their prostitutes, but you gave gifts to all your lovers. You bribed them to come to you from everywhere for your illicit favors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.34', 'BSB', 'So your prostitution is the opposite of that of other women: No one solicited your favors, and you paid a fee instead of receiving one; so you are the very opposite!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.35', 'BSB', 'Therefore, O prostitute, hear the word of the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.36', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Because you poured out your wealth and exposed your nakedness in your promiscuity with your lovers and with all your detestable idols, and because of the blood of your children which you gave to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.37', 'BSB', 'therefore I will surely gather all the lovers with whom you found pleasure, all those you loved and all those you hated. I will gather them against you from all around and expose you before them, and they will see you completely naked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.38', 'BSB', 'And I will sentence you to the punishment of women who commit adultery and those who shed blood; so I will bring upon you the wrath of your bloodshed and jealousy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.39', 'BSB', 'Then I will deliver you into the hands of your lovers, and they will level your mounds and tear down your lofty shrines. They will strip off your clothes, take your fine jewelry, and leave you naked and bare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.40', 'BSB', 'They will bring a mob against you, who will stone you and cut you to pieces with their swords.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.41', 'BSB', 'Then they will burn down your houses and execute judgment against you in the sight of many women. I will put an end to your prostitution, and you will never again pay your lovers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.42', 'BSB', 'So I will lay to rest My wrath against you, and My jealousy will turn away from you. Then I will be calm and no longer angry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.43', 'BSB', 'Because you did not remember the days of your youth, but enraged Me with all these things, I will surely bring your deeds down upon your own head, declares the Lord GOD. Have you not committed this lewdness on top of all your other abominations?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.44', 'BSB', 'Behold, all who speak in proverbs will quote this proverb about you: ‘Like mother, like daughter.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.45', 'BSB', 'You are the daughter of your mother, who despised her husband and children. You are the sister of your sisters, who despised their husbands and children. Your mother was a Hittite and your father an Amorite.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.46', 'BSB', 'Your older sister was Samaria, who lived with her daughters to your north; and your younger sister was Sodom, who lived with her daughters to your south.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.47', 'BSB', 'And you not only walked in their ways and practiced their abominations, but soon you were more depraved than they were.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.48', 'BSB', 'As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, your sister Sodom and her daughters never did as you and your daughters have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.49', 'BSB', 'Now this was the iniquity of your sister Sodom: She and her daughters were arrogant, overfed, and complacent; they did not help the poor and needy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.50', 'BSB', 'Thus they were haughty and committed abominations before Me. Therefore I removed them, as you have seen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.51', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, Samaria did not commit half the sins you did. You have multiplied your abominations beyond theirs, and all the abominations you have committed have made your sisters appear righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.52', 'BSB', 'So now you must bear your disgrace, since you have brought justification for your sisters. For they appear more righteous than you, because your sins were more vile than theirs. So you too must bear your shame and disgrace, since you have made your sisters appear righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.53', 'BSB', 'But I will restore Sodom and her daughters from captivity, as well as Samaria and her daughters. And I will restore you along with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.54', 'BSB', 'So you will bear your disgrace and be ashamed of all you did to comfort them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.55', 'BSB', 'And your sisters, Sodom with her daughters and Samaria with her daughters, will return to their former state. You and your daughters will also return to your former state.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.56', 'BSB', 'Did you not treat your sister Sodom as an object of scorn in the day of your pride,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.57', 'BSB', 'before your wickedness was uncovered? Even so, you are now scorned by the daughters of Edom and all those around her, and by the daughters of the Philistines—all those around you who despise you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.58', 'BSB', 'You will bear the consequences of your lewdness and your abominations, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.59', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: I will deal with you according to your deeds, since you have despised the oath by breaking the covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.60', 'BSB', 'But I will remember the covenant I made with you in the days of your youth, and I will establish an everlasting covenant with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.61', 'BSB', 'Then you will remember your ways and be ashamed when you receive your older and younger sisters. I will give them to you as daughters, but not because of My covenant with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.62', 'BSB', 'So I will establish My covenant with you, and you will know that I am the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.16.63', 'BSB', 'so that when I make atonement for all you have done, you will remember and be ashamed and never again open your mouth because of your disgrace, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.1', 'BSB', 'Now the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, pose a riddle; speak a parable to the house of Israel', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.3', 'BSB', 'and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘A great eagle with great wings and long pinions, full of feathers of many colors, came to Lebanon and took away the top of the cedar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.4', 'BSB', 'He plucked off its topmost shoot, carried it to the land of merchants, and planted it in a city of traders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.5', 'BSB', 'He took some of the seed of the land and planted it in fertile soil; he placed it by abundant waters and set it out like a willow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.6', 'BSB', 'It sprouted and became a spreading vine, low in height, with branches turned toward him; yet its roots remained where it stood. So it became a vine and yielded branches and sent out shoots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.7', 'BSB', 'But there was another great eagle with great wings and many feathers. And behold, this vine bent its roots toward him. It stretched out its branches to him from its planting bed, so that he might water it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.8', 'BSB', 'It had been planted in good soil by abundant waters in order to yield branches and bear fruit and become a splendid vine.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.9', 'BSB', 'So you are to tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Will it flourish? Will it not be uprooted and stripped of its fruit so that it shrivels? All its foliage will wither! It will not take a strong arm or many people to pull it up by its roots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.10', 'BSB', 'Even if it is transplanted, will it flourish? Will it not completely wither when the east wind strikes? It will wither on the bed where it sprouted.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.11', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.12', 'BSB', '“Now say to this rebellious house: ‘Do you not know what these things mean?’ Tell them, ‘Behold, the king of Babylon came to Jerusalem, carried off its king and officials, and brought them back with him to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.13', 'BSB', 'He took a member of the royal family and made a covenant with him, putting him under oath. Then he carried away the leading men of the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.14', 'BSB', 'so that the kingdom would be brought low, unable to lift itself up, surviving only by keeping his covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.15', 'BSB', 'But this king rebelled against Babylon by sending his envoys to Egypt to ask for horses and a large army. Will he flourish? Will the one who does such things escape? Can he break a covenant and yet escape?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.16', 'BSB', '‘As surely as I live,’ declares the Lord GOD, ‘he will die in Babylon, in the land of the king who enthroned him, whose oath he despised and whose covenant he broke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.17', 'BSB', 'Pharaoh with his mighty army and vast horde will not help him in battle, when ramps are built and siege walls constructed to destroy many lives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.18', 'BSB', 'He despised the oath by breaking the covenant. Seeing that he gave his hand in pledge yet did all these things, he will not escape!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘As surely as I live, I will bring down upon his head My oath that he despised and My covenant that he broke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.20', 'BSB', 'I will spread My net over him and catch him in My snare. I will bring him to Babylon and execute judgment upon him there for the treason he committed against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.21', 'BSB', 'All his choice troops will fall by the sword, and those who survive will be scattered to every wind. Then you will know that I, the LORD, have spoken.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.22', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will take a shoot from the lofty top of the cedar, and I will set it out. I will pluck a tender sprig from its topmost shoots, and I will plant it on a high and lofty mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.23', 'BSB', 'I will plant it on the mountain heights of Israel so that it will bear branches; it will yield fruit and become a majestic cedar. Birds of every kind will nest under it, taking shelter in the shade of its branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.17.24', 'BSB', 'Then all the trees of the field will know that I am the LORD. I bring the tall tree down and make the low tree tall. I dry up the green tree and make the withered tree flourish. I, the LORD, have spoken, and I have done it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.2', 'BSB', '“What do you people mean by quoting this proverb about the land of Israel: ‘The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the teeth of the children are set on edge’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.3', 'BSB', 'As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, you will no longer quote this proverb in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.4', 'BSB', 'Behold, every soul belongs to Me; both father and son are Mine. The soul who sins is the one who will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.5', 'BSB', 'Now suppose a man is righteous and does what is just and right:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.6', 'BSB', 'He does not eat at the mountain or look to the idols of the house of Israel. He does not defile his neighbor’s wife or approach a woman during her period.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.7', 'BSB', 'He does not oppress another, but restores the pledge to the debtor. He does not commit robbery, but gives his bread to the hungry and covers the naked with clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.8', 'BSB', 'He does not engage in usury or take excess interest, but he withholds his hand from iniquity and executes true justice between men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.9', 'BSB', 'He follows My statutes and faithfully keeps My ordinances. That man is righteous; surely he will live, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.10', 'BSB', 'Now suppose that man has a violent son, who sheds blood or does any of these things,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.11', 'BSB', 'though the father has done none of them: Indeed, the son eats at the mountain and defiles his neighbor’s wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.12', 'BSB', 'He oppresses the poor and needy; he commits robbery and does not restore a pledge. He lifts his eyes to idols; he commits abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.13', 'BSB', 'He engages in usury and takes excess interest. Will this son live? He will not! Since he has committed all these abominations, he will surely die; his blood will be on his own head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.14', 'BSB', 'Now suppose this son has a son who sees all the sins his father has committed, considers them, and does not do likewise:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.15', 'BSB', 'He does not eat at the mountain or look to the idols of the house of Israel. He does not defile his neighbor’s wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.16', 'BSB', 'He does not oppress another, or retain a pledge, or commit robbery. He gives his bread to the hungry and covers the naked with clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.17', 'BSB', 'He withholds his hand from harming the poor and takes no interest or usury. He keeps My ordinances and follows My statutes. Such a man will not die for his father’s iniquity. He will surely live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.18', 'BSB', 'As for his father, he will die for his own iniquity, because he practiced extortion, robbed his brother, and did what was wrong among his people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.19', 'BSB', 'Yet you may ask, ‘Why shouldn’t the son bear the iniquity of his father?’ Since the son has done what is just and right, carefully observing all My statutes, he will surely live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.20', 'BSB', 'The soul who sins is the one who will die. A son will not bear the iniquity of his father, and a father will not bear the iniquity of his son. The righteousness of the righteous man will fall upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked man will fall upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.21', 'BSB', 'But if the wicked man turns from all the sins he has committed, keeps all My statutes, and does what is just and right, he will surely live; he will not die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.22', 'BSB', 'None of the transgressions he has committed will be held against him. Because of the righteousness he has practiced, he will live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.23', 'BSB', 'Do I take any pleasure in the death of the wicked? declares the Lord GOD. Wouldn’t I prefer that he turn from his ways and live?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.24', 'BSB', 'But if a righteous man turns from his righteousness and practices iniquity, committing the same abominations as the wicked, will he live? None of the righteous acts he did will be remembered. Because of the unfaithfulness and sin he has committed, he will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.25', 'BSB', 'Yet you say, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ Hear now, O house of Israel: Is it My way that is unjust? Is it not your ways that are unjust?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.26', 'BSB', 'If a righteous man turns from his righteousness and practices iniquity, he will die for this. He will die because of the iniquity he has committed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.27', 'BSB', 'But if a wicked man turns from the wickedness he has committed and does what is just and right, he will save his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.28', 'BSB', 'Because he considered and turned from all the transgressions he had committed, he will surely live; he will not die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.29', 'BSB', 'Yet the house of Israel says, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ Are My ways unjust, O house of Israel? Is it not your ways that are unjust?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.30', 'BSB', 'Therefore, O house of Israel, I will judge you, each according to his ways, declares the Lord GOD. Repent and turn from all your transgressions, so that your iniquity will not become your downfall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.31', 'BSB', 'Cast away from yourselves all the transgressions you have committed, and fashion for yourselves a new heart and a new spirit. Why should you die, O house of Israel?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.18.32', 'BSB', 'For I take no pleasure in anyone’s death, declares the Lord GOD. So repent and live!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.1', 'BSB', '“As for you, take up a lament for the princes of Israel', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.2', 'BSB', 'and say: ‘What was your mother? A lioness among the lions! She lay down among the young lions; she reared her cubs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.3', 'BSB', 'She brought up one of her cubs, and he became a young lion. After learning to tear his prey, he devoured men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.4', 'BSB', 'When the nations heard of him, he was trapped in their pit. With hooks they led him away to the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.5', 'BSB', 'When she saw that she had waited in vain, that her hope was lost, she took another of her cubs and made him a young lion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.6', 'BSB', 'He prowled among the lions, and became a young lion. After learning to tear his prey, he devoured men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.7', 'BSB', 'He broke down their strongholds and devastated their cities. The land and everything in it shuddered at the sound of his roaring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.8', 'BSB', 'Then the nations set out against him from the provinces on every side. They spread their net over him; he was trapped in their pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.9', 'BSB', 'With hooks they caged him and brought him to the king of Babylon. They brought him into captivity so that his roar was heard no longer on the mountains of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.10', 'BSB', 'Your mother was like a vine in your vineyard, planted by the water; it was fruitful and full of branches because of the abundant waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.11', 'BSB', 'It had strong branches, fit for a ruler’s scepter. It towered high above the thick branches, conspicuous for its height and for its dense foliage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.12', 'BSB', 'But it was uprooted in fury, cast down to the ground, and the east wind dried up its fruit. Its strong branches were stripped off and they withered; the fire consumed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.13', 'BSB', 'Now it is planted in the wilderness, in a dry and thirsty land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.19.14', 'BSB', 'Fire has gone out from its main branch and devoured its fruit; on it no strong branch remains fit for a ruler’s scepter.’ This is a lament and shall be used as a lament.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.1', 'BSB', 'In the seventh year, on the tenth day of the fifth month, some of the elders of Israel came to inquire of the LORD, and they sat down before me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.2', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.3', 'BSB', '“Son of man, speak to the elders of Israel and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: Have you come to inquire of Me? As surely as I live, I will not be consulted by you, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.4', 'BSB', 'Will you judge them, will you judge them, son of man? Confront them with the abominations of their fathers', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.5', 'BSB', 'and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: On the day I chose Israel, I swore an oath to the descendants of the house of Jacob and made Myself known to them in the land of Egypt. With an uplifted hand I said to them, ‘I am the LORD your God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.6', 'BSB', 'On that day I swore to bring them out of the land of Egypt into a land that I had searched out for them, a land flowing with milk and honey, the glory of all lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.7', 'BSB', 'And I said to them: ‘Each of you must throw away the abominations before his eyes, and you must not defile yourselves with the idols of Egypt. I am the LORD your God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.8', 'BSB', 'But they rebelled against Me and refused to listen. None of them cast away the abominations before their eyes, and they did not forsake the idols of Egypt. So I resolved to pour out My wrath upon them and vent My anger against them in the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.9', 'BSB', 'But I acted for the sake of My name, that it should not be profaned in the eyes of the nations among whom they were living, in whose sight I had revealed Myself to Israel by bringing them out of the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.10', 'BSB', 'So I brought them out of the land of Egypt and led them into the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.11', 'BSB', 'And I gave them My statutes and made known to them My ordinances—for the man who does these things will live by them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.12', 'BSB', 'I also gave them My Sabbaths as a sign between us, so that they would know that I am the LORD who sanctifies them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.13', 'BSB', 'Yet the house of Israel rebelled against Me in the wilderness. They did not follow My statutes and they rejected My ordinances—though the man who does these things will live by them—and they utterly profaned My Sabbaths. Then I resolved to pour out My wrath upon them and put an end to them in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.14', 'BSB', 'But I acted for the sake of My name, so that it would not be profaned in the eyes of the nations in whose sight I had brought them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.15', 'BSB', 'Moreover, with an uplifted hand I swore to them in the wilderness that I would not bring them into the land that I had given them—a land flowing with milk and honey, the glory of all lands—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.16', 'BSB', 'because they kept rejecting My ordinances, refusing to walk in My statutes, and profaning My Sabbaths; for their hearts continually went after their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.17', 'BSB', 'Yet I looked on them with pity and did not destroy them or bring them to an end in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.18', 'BSB', 'In the wilderness I said to their children: ‘Do not walk in the statutes of your fathers or keep their ordinances or defile yourselves with their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.19', 'BSB', 'I am the LORD your God; walk in My statutes, keep My ordinances, and practice them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.20', 'BSB', 'Keep My Sabbaths holy, that they may be a sign between us, so that you may know that I am the LORD your God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.21', 'BSB', 'But the children rebelled against Me. They did not walk in My statutes or carefully observe My ordinances—though the man who does these things will live by them—and they profaned My Sabbaths. So I resolved to pour out My wrath upon them and vent My anger against them in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.22', 'BSB', 'But I withheld My hand and acted for the sake of My name, so that it would not be profaned in the eyes of the nations in whose sight I had brought them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.23', 'BSB', 'However, with an uplifted hand I swore to them in the wilderness that I would scatter them among the nations and disperse them throughout the lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.24', 'BSB', 'For they did not practice My ordinances, but they rejected My statutes and profaned My Sabbaths, fixing their eyes on the idols of their fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.25', 'BSB', 'I also gave them over to statutes that were not good and ordinances by which they could not live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.26', 'BSB', 'And I pronounced them unclean through their gifts—the sacrifice of every firstborn in the fire—so that I might devastate them, in order that they would know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore, son of man, speak to the house of Israel, and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: In this way also your fathers blasphemed Me by their unfaithfulness against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.28', 'BSB', 'When I brought them into the land that I swore to give them and they saw any high hill or leafy tree, there they offered their sacrifices, presented offerings that provoked Me, sent up their fragrant incense, and poured out their drink offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.29', 'BSB', 'So I asked them: ‘What is this high place to which you go?’ (And to this day it is called Bamah. )', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.30', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell the house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: Will you defile yourselves the way your fathers did, prostituting yourselves with their abominations?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.31', 'BSB', 'When you offer your gifts, sacrificing your sons in the fire, you continue to defile yourselves with all your idols to this day. So should I be consulted by you, O house of Israel? As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, I will not be consulted by you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.32', 'BSB', 'When you say, ‘Let us be like the nations, like the peoples of the lands, serving wood and stone,’ what you have in mind will never come to pass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.33', 'BSB', 'As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, with a strong hand, an outstretched arm, and outpoured wrath I will rule over you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.34', 'BSB', 'With a strong hand, an outstretched arm, and outpoured wrath I will bring you out from the peoples and gather you from the lands to which you have been scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.35', 'BSB', 'And I will bring you into the wilderness of the nations, where I will enter into judgment with you face to face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.36', 'BSB', 'Just as I entered into judgment with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so I will enter into judgment with you, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.37', 'BSB', 'I will make you pass under the rod and will bring you into the bond of the covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.38', 'BSB', 'And I will purge you of those who rebel and transgress against Me. I will bring them out of the land in which they dwell, but they will not enter the land of Israel. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.39', 'BSB', 'And as for you, O house of Israel, this is what the Lord GOD says: Go and serve your idols, every one of you. But afterward, you will surely listen to Me, and you will no longer defile My holy name with your gifts and idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.40', 'BSB', 'For on My holy mountain, the high mountain of Israel, declares the Lord GOD, there the whole house of Israel, all of them, will serve Me in the land. There I will accept them and will require your offerings and choice gifts, along with all your holy sacrifices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.41', 'BSB', 'When I bring you from the peoples and gather you from the lands to which you have been scattered, I will accept you as a pleasing aroma. And I will show My holiness through you in the sight of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.42', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I am the LORD, when I bring you into the land of Israel, the land that I swore to give your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.43', 'BSB', 'There you will remember your ways and all the deeds with which you have defiled yourselves, and you will loathe yourselves for all the evils you have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.44', 'BSB', 'Then you will know, O house of Israel, that I am the LORD, when I have dealt with you for the sake of My name and not according to your wicked ways and corrupt acts, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.45', 'BSB', 'Now the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.46', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face toward the south, preach against it, and prophesy against the forest of the Negev.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.47', 'BSB', 'Say to the forest of the Negev: Hear the word of the LORD! This is what the Lord GOD says: I am about to ignite in you a fire, and it will devour all your trees, both green and dry. The blazing flame will not be quenched, and by it every face from south to north will be scorched.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.48', 'BSB', 'Then all people will see that I, the LORD, have kindled it; it will not be quenched.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.20.49', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “Ah, Lord GOD, they are saying of me, ‘Is he not just telling parables?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.1', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against Jerusalem and preach against the sanctuaries. Prophesy against the land of Israel', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.3', 'BSB', 'and tell her that this is what the LORD says: ‘I am against you, and I will draw My sword from its sheath and cut off from you both the righteous and the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.4', 'BSB', 'Because I will cut off both the righteous and the wicked, My sword will be unsheathed against everyone from south to north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.5', 'BSB', 'Then all flesh will know that I, the LORD, have taken My sword from its sheath, not to return it again.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.6', 'BSB', 'But you, son of man, groan! Groan before their eyes with a broken heart and bitter grief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.7', 'BSB', 'And when they ask, ‘Why are you groaning?’ you are to say, ‘Because of the news that is coming. Every heart will melt, and every hand will go limp. Every spirit will faint, and every knee will turn to water.’ Yes, it is coming and it will surely happen, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.8', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.9', 'BSB', '“Son of man, prophesy and tell them that this is what the Lord says: ‘A sword, a sword, sharpened and polished—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.10', 'BSB', 'it is sharpened for the slaughter, polished to flash like lightning! Should we rejoice in the scepter of My son? The sword despises every such stick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.11', 'BSB', 'The sword is appointed to be polished, to be grasped in the hand. It is sharpened and polished, to be placed in the hand of the slayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.12', 'BSB', 'Cry out and wail, O son of man, for the sword is wielded against My people; it is against all the princes of Israel! They are tossed to the sword with My people; therefore strike your thigh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.13', 'BSB', 'Surely testing will come! And what if even the scepter, which the sword despises, does not continue?’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.14', 'BSB', '‘So then, son of man, prophesy and strike your hands together. Let the sword strike two times, even three. It is a sword that slays, a sword of great slaughter closing in on every side!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.15', 'BSB', 'So that their hearts may melt and many may stumble, I have appointed at all their gates a sword for slaughter. Yes, it is ready to flash like lightning; it is drawn for slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.16', 'BSB', 'Slash to the right; set your blade to the left— wherever your blade is directed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.17', 'BSB', 'I too will strike My hands together, and I will satisfy My wrath.’ I, the LORD, have spoken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.18', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.19', 'BSB', '“Now you, son of man, mark out two roads for the sword of the king of Babylon to take, both starting from the same land. And make a signpost where the road branches off to each city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.20', 'BSB', 'Mark out one road for the sword to come against Rabbah of the Ammonites, and another against Judah into fortified Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.21', 'BSB', 'For the king of Babylon stands at the fork in the road, at the junction of the two roads, to seek an omen: He shakes the arrows, he consults the idols, he examines the liver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.22', 'BSB', 'In his right hand appears the portent for Jerusalem, where he is to set up battering rams, to call for the slaughter, to lift a battle cry, to direct the battering rams against the gates, to build a ramp, and to erect a siege wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.23', 'BSB', 'It will seem like a false omen to the eyes of those who have sworn allegiance to him, but it will draw attention to their guilt and take them captive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because you have drawn attention to your guilt, exposing your transgressions, so that your sins are revealed in all your deeds—because you have come to remembrance—you shall be taken in hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.25', 'BSB', 'And you, O profane and wicked prince of Israel, the day has come for your final punishment.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.26', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Remove the turban, and take off the crown. Things will not remain as they are: Exalt the lowly and bring low the exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.27', 'BSB', 'A ruin, a ruin, I will make it a ruin! And it will not be restored until the arrival of Him to whom it belongs, to whom I have assigned the right of judgment.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.28', 'BSB', 'Now prophesy, son of man, and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says concerning the Ammonites and their contempt: ‘A sword! A sword is drawn for slaughter, polished to consume, to flash like lightning—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.29', 'BSB', 'while they offer false visions for you and lying divinations about you— to be placed on the necks of the wicked who are slain, whose day has come, the time of their final punishment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.30', 'BSB', 'Return the sword to its sheath! In the place where you were created, in the land of your origin, I will judge you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.31', 'BSB', 'I will pour out My anger upon you; I will breathe the fire of My fury against you; I will hand you over to brutal men, skilled in destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.21.32', 'BSB', 'You will be fuel for the fire. Your blood will stain your own land. You will not be remembered, for I, the LORD, have spoken.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.2', 'BSB', '“As for you, son of man, will you judge her? Will you pass judgment on the city of bloodshed? Then confront her with all her abominations', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.3', 'BSB', 'and tell her that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘O city who brings her own doom by shedding blood within her walls and making idols to defile herself,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.4', 'BSB', 'you are guilty of the blood you have shed, and you are defiled by the idols you have made. You have brought your days to a close and have come to the end of your years. Therefore I have made you a reproach to the nations and a mockery to all the lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.5', 'BSB', 'Those near and far will mock you, O infamous city, full of turmoil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.6', 'BSB', 'See how every prince of Israel within you has used his power to shed blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.7', 'BSB', 'Father and mother are treated with contempt. Within your walls the foreign resident is exploited, the fatherless and the widow are oppressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.8', 'BSB', 'You have despised My holy things and profaned My Sabbaths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.9', 'BSB', 'Among you are slanderous men bent on bloodshed; within you are those who eat on the mountain shrines and commit acts of indecency.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.10', 'BSB', 'In you they have uncovered the nakedness of their fathers; in you they violate women during their menstrual impurity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.11', 'BSB', 'One man commits an abomination with his neighbor’s wife; another wickedly defiles his daughter-in-law; and yet another violates his sister, his own father’s daughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.12', 'BSB', 'In you they take bribes to shed blood. You engage in usury, take excess interest, and extort your neighbors. But Me you have forgotten, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.13', 'BSB', 'Now look, I strike My hands together against your unjust gain and against the blood you have shed in your midst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.14', 'BSB', 'Will your courage endure or your hands be strong in the day I deal with you? I, the LORD, have spoken, and I will act.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.15', 'BSB', 'I will disperse you among the nations and scatter you throughout the lands; I will purge your uncleanness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.16', 'BSB', 'And when you have defiled yourself in the eyes of the nations, then you will know that I am the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.17', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.18', 'BSB', '“Son of man, the house of Israel has become dross to Me. All of them are copper, tin, iron, and lead inside the furnace; they are but the dross of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because all of you have become dross, behold, I will gather you into Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.20', 'BSB', 'Just as one gathers silver, copper, iron, lead, and tin into the furnace to melt with a fiery blast, so I will gather you in My anger and wrath, leave you there, and melt you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.21', 'BSB', 'Yes, I will gather you together and blow on you with the fire of My wrath, and you will be melted within the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.22', 'BSB', 'As silver is melted in a furnace, so you will be melted within the city. Then you will know that I, the LORD, have poured out My wrath upon you.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.23', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.24', 'BSB', '“Son of man, say to her, ‘In the day of indignation, you are a land that has not been cleansed, upon which no rain has fallen.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.25', 'BSB', 'The conspiracy of the princes in her midst is like a roaring lion tearing its prey. They devour the people, seize the treasures and precious things, and multiply the widows within her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.26', 'BSB', 'Her priests do violence to My law and profane My holy things. They make no distinction between the holy and the common, and they fail to distinguish between the clean and the unclean. They disregard My Sabbaths, so that I am profaned among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.27', 'BSB', 'Her officials within her are like wolves tearing their prey, shedding blood, and destroying lives for dishonest gain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.28', 'BSB', 'Her prophets whitewash these deeds by false visions and lying divinations, saying, ‘This is what the Lord GOD says,’ when the LORD has not spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.29', 'BSB', 'The people of the land have practiced extortion and committed robbery. They have oppressed the poor and needy and have exploited the foreign resident without justice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.30', 'BSB', 'I searched for a man among them to repair the wall and stand in the gap before Me on behalf of the land, so that I should not destroy it. But I found no one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.22.31', 'BSB', 'So I have poured out My indignation upon them and consumed them with the fire of My fury. I have brought their ways down upon their own heads, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.1', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, there were two women, daughters of the same mother,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.3', 'BSB', 'and they played in Egypt, prostituting themselves from their youth. Their breasts were fondled there, and their virgin bosoms caressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.4', 'BSB', 'The older was named Oholah, and her sister was named Oholibah. They became Mine and gave birth to sons and daughters. As for their identities, Oholah is Samaria, and Oholibah is Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.5', 'BSB', 'Oholah prostituted herself while she was still Mine. She lusted after her lovers, the Assyrians—warriors', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.6', 'BSB', 'clothed in blue, governors and commanders, all desirable young men, horsemen mounted on steeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.7', 'BSB', 'She offered sexual favors to all the elite of Assyria. She defiled herself with all the idols of those for whom she lusted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.8', 'BSB', 'She did not give up the prostitution she began in Egypt, when men slept with her in her youth, caressed her virgin bosom, and poured out their lust upon her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore I delivered her into the hands of her lovers, the Assyrians for whom she lusted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.10', 'BSB', 'They exposed her nakedness, seized her sons and daughters, and put her to the sword. Thus she became a byword among women, and they executed judgment against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.11', 'BSB', 'Her sister Oholibah saw this, yet in her lust and prostitution she was more depraved than her sister.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.12', 'BSB', 'She too lusted after the Assyrians—governors and commanders, warriors dressed in splendor, horsemen riding on steeds, all desirable young men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.13', 'BSB', 'And I saw that she too had defiled herself; both of them had taken the same path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.14', 'BSB', 'But Oholibah carried her prostitution even further. She saw the men portrayed on the wall, images of the Chaldeans, engraved in vermilion,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.15', 'BSB', 'wearing belts on their waists and flowing turbans on their heads; all of them looked like officers of the Babylonians in Chaldea, the land of their birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.16', 'BSB', 'At the sight of them, she lusted for them and sent messengers to them in Chaldea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.17', 'BSB', 'Then the Babylonians came to her, to the bed of love, and in their lust they defiled her. But after she had been defiled by them, she turned away in disgust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.18', 'BSB', 'When Oholibah openly prostituted herself and exposed her nakedness, I turned away from her in disgust, just as I had turned away from her sister.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.19', 'BSB', 'Yet she multiplied her promiscuity, remembering the days of her youth, when she had prostituted herself in the land of Egypt', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.20', 'BSB', 'and lusted after their lovers, whose genitals were like those of donkeys and whose emission was like that of stallions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.21', 'BSB', 'So you revisited the indecency of your youth, when the Egyptians caressed your bosom and pressed your young breasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.22', 'BSB', 'Therefore, Oholibah, this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will incite your lovers against you, those from whom you turned away in disgust. And I will bring them against you from every side—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.23', 'BSB', 'the Babylonians and all the Chaldeans, the men of Pekod, Shoa, and Koa, and all the Assyrians with them—all desirable young men, governors and commanders, officers and men of renown, mounted on horses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.24', 'BSB', 'They will come against you with a host of peoples, with weapons, chariots, and wagons. They will array themselves against you on every side with buckler and shield and helmet. I will delegate judgment to them, and they will punish you according to their own standards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.25', 'BSB', 'And I will set My jealous rage against you, and they will deal with you in fury. They will cut off your noses and ears, and your survivors will fall by the sword. They will seize your sons and daughters, and your remnant will be consumed by fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.26', 'BSB', 'They will strip off your clothes and take your fine jewelry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.27', 'BSB', 'So I will put an end to your indecency and prostitution, which began in the land of Egypt, and you will not lift your eyes to them or remember Egypt anymore.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.28', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Surely I will deliver you into the hands of those you hate, from whom you turned away in disgust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.29', 'BSB', 'They will treat you with hatred, take all for which you have worked, and leave you naked and bare, so that the shame of your prostitution will be exposed. Your indecency and promiscuity', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.30', 'BSB', 'have brought these things upon you, because you have prostituted yourself with the nations and defiled yourself with their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.31', 'BSB', 'Because you have followed the path of your sister, I will put her cup into your hand.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.32', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘You will drink your sister’s cup, a cup deep and wide. It will bring scorn and derision, for it holds so much.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.33', 'BSB', 'You will be filled with drunkenness and grief, with a cup of devastation and desolation, the cup of your sister Samaria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.34', 'BSB', 'You will drink it and drain it; you will dash it to pieces, and tear your breasts. For I have spoken,’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.35', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because you have forgotten Me and have cast Me behind your back, you must bear the consequences of your indecency and prostitution.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.36', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me: “Son of man, will you pass judgment against Oholah and Oholibah? Then declare to them their abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.37', 'BSB', 'For they have committed adultery, and blood is on their hands. They have committed adultery with their idols. They have even sacrificed their children, whom they bore to Me, in the fire as food for their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.38', 'BSB', 'They have also done this to Me: On that very same day, they defiled My sanctuary and profaned My Sabbaths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.39', 'BSB', 'On the very day they slaughtered their children for their idols, they entered My sanctuary to profane it. Yes, they did this inside My house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.40', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, you sisters sent messengers for men who came from afar; and behold, when they arrived, you bathed for them, painted your eyes, and adorned yourself with jewelry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.41', 'BSB', 'You sat on a couch of luxury with a table spread before it, on which you had set My incense and My oil,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.42', 'BSB', 'accompanied by the sound of a carefree crowd. Drunkards were brought in from the desert along with men from the rabble, who put bracelets on your wrists and beautiful crowns on your head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.43', 'BSB', 'Then I said of her who had grown old in adulteries: ‘Now let them use her as a prostitute, for that is all she is!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.44', 'BSB', 'And they slept with her as with a prostitute; they slept with Oholah and Oholibah, those lewd women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.45', 'BSB', 'But righteous men will sentence them to the punishment of those who commit adultery and bloodshed, because they are adulteresses with blood on their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.46', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Bring a mob against them and consign them to terror and plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.47', 'BSB', 'The mob will stone them and cut them down with their swords. They will kill their sons and daughters and burn down their houses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.48', 'BSB', 'So I will put an end to indecency in the land, and all the women will be admonished not to imitate your behavior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.23.49', 'BSB', 'They will repay you for your indecency, and you will bear the consequences of your sins of idolatry. Then you will know that I am the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.1', 'BSB', 'In the ninth year, on the tenth day of the tenth month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, write down today’s date, for on this very day the king of Babylon has laid siege to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.3', 'BSB', 'Now speak a parable to this rebellious house and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Put the pot on the fire; put it on and pour in the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.4', 'BSB', 'Put in the pieces of meat, every good piece— thigh and shoulder— fill it with choice bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.5', 'BSB', 'Take the choicest of the flock and pile the fuel beneath it. Bring it to a boil and cook the bones in it.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Woe to the city of bloodshed, to the pot now rusted, whose rust will not come off! Empty it piece by piece; cast no lots for its contents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.7', 'BSB', 'For the blood she shed is still within her; she poured it out on the bare rock; she did not pour it on the ground to cover it with dust.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.8', 'BSB', 'In order to stir up wrath and take vengeance, I have placed her blood on the bare rock, so that it would not be covered.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.9', 'BSB', 'Yes, this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Woe to the city of bloodshed! I, too, will pile the kindling high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.10', 'BSB', 'Pile on the logs and kindle the fire; cook the meat well and mix in the spices; let the bones be burned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.11', 'BSB', 'Set the empty pot on its coals until it becomes hot and its copper glows. Then its impurity will melt within; its rust will be consumed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.12', 'BSB', 'It has frustrated every effort; its thick rust has not been removed, even by the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.13', 'BSB', 'Because of the indecency of your uncleanness I tried to cleanse you, but you would not be purified from your filthiness. You will not be pure again until My wrath against you has subsided.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.14', 'BSB', 'I, the LORD, have spoken; the time is coming, and I will act. I will not refrain or show pity, nor will I relent. I will judge you according to your ways and deeds,’ declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.15', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.16', 'BSB', '“Son of man, behold, I am about to take away the desire of your eyes with a fatal blow. But you must not mourn or weep or let your tears flow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.17', 'BSB', 'Groan quietly; do not mourn for the dead. Put on your turban and strap your sandals on your feet; do not cover your lips or eat the bread of mourners.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.18', 'BSB', 'So I spoke to the people in the morning, and in the evening my wife died. And the next morning I did as I had been commanded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.19', 'BSB', 'Then the people asked me, “Won’t you tell us what these things you are doing mean to us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.20', 'BSB', 'So I answered them, “The word of the LORD came to me, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.21', 'BSB', 'Tell the house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I am about to desecrate My sanctuary, the pride of your power, the desire of your eyes, and the delight of your soul. And the sons and daughters you left behind will fall by the sword.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.22', 'BSB', 'Then you will do as I have done: You will not cover your lips or eat the bread of mourners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.23', 'BSB', 'Your turbans will remain on your heads and your sandals on your feet. You will not mourn or weep, but you will waste away because of your sins, and you will groan among yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.24', 'BSB', '‘Thus Ezekiel will be a sign for you; you will do everything that he has done. When this happens, you will know that I am the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.25', 'BSB', 'And you, son of man, know that on the day I take away their stronghold, their pride and joy—the desire of their eyes which uplifted their souls—and their sons and daughters as well,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.26', 'BSB', 'on that day a fugitive will come and tell you the news.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.24.27', 'BSB', 'On that day your mouth will be opened to him who has escaped; you will speak and no longer be mute. So you will be a sign to them, and they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against the Ammonites and prophesy against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.3', 'BSB', 'Tell the Ammonites to hear the word of the Lord GOD, for this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because you exclaimed, “Aha!” when My sanctuary was profaned, when the land of Israel was laid waste, and when the house of Judah went into exile,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.4', 'BSB', 'therefore I will indeed give you as a possession to the people of the East. They will set up their camps and pitch their tents among you. They will eat your fruit and drink your milk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.5', 'BSB', 'I will make Rabbah a pasture for camels, and Ammon a resting place for sheep. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because you clapped your hands and stomped your feet and rejoiced over the land of Israel with a heart full of contempt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.7', 'BSB', 'therefore I will indeed stretch out My hand against you and give you as plunder to the nations. I will cut you off from the peoples and exterminate you from the countries. I will destroy you, and you will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.8', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because Moab and Seir said, “Look, the house of Judah is like all the other nations,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.9', 'BSB', 'therefore I will indeed expose the flank of Moab beginning with its frontier cities—Beth-jeshimoth, Baal-meon, and Kiriathaim—the glory of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.10', 'BSB', 'I will give it along with the Ammonites as a possession to the people of the East, so that the Ammonites will no longer be remembered among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.11', 'BSB', 'So I will execute judgments on Moab, and they will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.12', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because Edom acted vengefully against the house of Judah, and in so doing incurred grievous guilt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.13', 'BSB', 'therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: I will stretch out My hand against Edom and cut off from it both man and beast. I will make it a wasteland, and from Teman to Dedan they will fall by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.14', 'BSB', 'I will take My vengeance on Edom by the hand of My people Israel, and they will deal with Edom according to My anger and wrath. Then they will know My vengeance, declares the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Because the Philistines acted in vengeance, taking vengeance with malice of soul to destroy Judah with ancient hostility,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.16', 'BSB', 'therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I will stretch out My hand against the Philistines, and I will cut off the Cherethites and destroy the remnant along the coast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.25.17', 'BSB', 'I will execute great vengeance against them with furious reproof. Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I lay My vengeance upon them.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.1', 'BSB', 'In the eleventh month of the twelfth year, on the first day of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, because Tyre has said of Jerusalem, ‘Aha! The gate to the nations is broken; it has swung open to me; now that she lies in ruins I will be filled,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.3', 'BSB', 'therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, O Tyre, I am against you, and I will raise up many nations against you, as the sea brings up its waves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.4', 'BSB', 'They will destroy the walls of Tyre and demolish her towers. I will scrape the soil from her and make her a bare rock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.5', 'BSB', 'She will become a place to spread nets in the sea, for I have spoken, declares the Lord GOD. She will become plunder for the nations,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.6', 'BSB', 'and the villages on her mainland will be slain by the sword. Then they will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.7', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, I will bring against Tyre from the north Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, king of kings, with horses and chariots, with cavalry and a great company of troops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.8', 'BSB', 'He will slaughter the villages of your mainland with the sword; he will set up siege works against you, build a ramp to your walls, and raise his shields against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.9', 'BSB', 'He will direct the blows of his battering rams against your walls and tear down your towers with his axes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.10', 'BSB', 'His multitude of horses will cover you in their dust. When he enters your gates as an army entering a breached city, your walls will shake from the noise of cavalry, wagons, and chariots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.11', 'BSB', 'The hooves of his horses will trample all your streets. He will slaughter your people with the sword, and your mighty pillars will fall to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.12', 'BSB', 'They will plunder your wealth and pillage your merchandise. They will demolish your walls, tear down your beautiful homes, and throw your stones and timber and soil into the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.13', 'BSB', 'So I will silence the sound of your songs, and the music of your lyres will no longer be heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.14', 'BSB', 'I will make you a bare rock, and you will become a place to spread the fishing nets. You will never be rebuilt, for I, the LORD, have spoken, declares the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says to Tyre: ‘Will not the coastlands quake at the sound of your downfall, when the wounded groan at the slaughter in your midst?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.16', 'BSB', 'All the princes of the sea will descend from their thrones, remove their robes, and strip off their embroidered garments. Clothed with terror, they will sit on the ground, trembling every moment, appalled over you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.17', 'BSB', 'Then they will lament for you, saying, “How you have perished, O city of renown inhabited by seafaring men— she who was powerful on the sea, along with her people, who imposed terror on all peoples!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.18', 'BSB', 'Now the coastlands tremble on the day of your downfall; the islands in the sea are dismayed by your demise.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.19', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘When I make you a desolate city like other deserted cities, and when I raise up the deep against you so that the mighty waters cover you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.20', 'BSB', 'then I will bring you down with those who descend to the Pit, to the people of antiquity. I will make you dwell in the earth below like the ancient ruins, with those who descend to the Pit, so that you will no longer be inhabited or set in splendor in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.26.21', 'BSB', 'I will make you an object of horror, and you will be no more. You will be sought, but will never be found,’ declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.2', 'BSB', '“Now you, son of man, take up a lament for Tyre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.3', 'BSB', 'Tell Tyre, who dwells at the gateway to the sea, merchant of the peoples on many coasts, that this is what the Lord GOD says: You have said, O Tyre, ‘I am perfect in beauty.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.4', 'BSB', 'Your borders are in the heart of the seas; your builders perfected your beauty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.5', 'BSB', 'They constructed all your planking with cypress from Senir. They took a cedar from Lebanon to make a mast for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.6', 'BSB', 'Of oaks from Bashan they made your oars; of wood from the coasts of Cyprus they made your deck, inlaid with ivory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.7', 'BSB', 'Of embroidered fine linen from Egypt they made your sail, which served as your banner. Of blue and purple from the coasts of Elishah they made your awning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.8', 'BSB', 'The men of Sidon and Arvad were your oarsmen. Your men of skill, O Tyre, were there as your captains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.9', 'BSB', 'The elders of Gebal were aboard as shipwrights, repairing your leaks. All the ships of the sea and their sailors came alongside to barter for your merchandise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.10', 'BSB', 'Men of Persia, Lydia, and Put served as warriors in your army. They hung their shields and helmets on your walls; they gave you splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.11', 'BSB', 'Men of Arvad and Helech manned your walls all around, and the men of Gammad were in your towers. They hung their shields around your walls; they perfected your beauty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.12', 'BSB', 'Tarshish was your merchant because of your great wealth of goods; they exchanged silver, iron, tin, and lead for your wares.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.13', 'BSB', 'Javan, Tubal, and Meshech were your merchants. They exchanged slaves and bronze utensils for your merchandise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.14', 'BSB', 'The men of Beth-togarmah exchanged horses, war horses, and mules for your wares.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.15', 'BSB', 'The men of Dedan were your clients; many coastlands were your market; they paid you with ivory tusks and ebony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.16', 'BSB', 'Aram was your customer because of your many products; they exchanged turquoise, purple, embroidered work, fine linen, coral, and rubies for your wares.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.17', 'BSB', 'Judah and the land of Israel traded with you; they exchanged wheat from Minnith, cakes and honey, oil and balm for your merchandise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.18', 'BSB', 'Because of your many products and your great wealth of goods, Damascus traded with you wine from Helbon, wool from Zahar,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.19', 'BSB', 'and casks of wine from Izal for your wares. Wrought iron, cassia, and sweet cane were exchanged for your merchandise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.20', 'BSB', 'Dedan was your merchant in saddlecloths for riding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.21', 'BSB', 'Arabia and all the princes of Kedar were your customers, trading in lambs, rams, and goats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.22', 'BSB', 'The merchants of Sheba and Raamah traded with you; for your wares they exchanged gold, the finest of all spices, and precious stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.23', 'BSB', 'Haran, Canneh, and Eden traded with you, and so did the merchants of Sheba, Asshur, and Chilmad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.24', 'BSB', 'In your marketplace they traded with you fine garments of blue, embroidered work, and multicolored rugs with cords tightly twisted and knotted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.25', 'BSB', 'The ships of Tarshish carried your merchandise. And you were filled with heavy cargo in the heart of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.26', 'BSB', 'Your oarsmen have brought you onto the high seas, but the east wind will shatter you in the heart of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.27', 'BSB', 'Your wealth, wares, and merchandise, your sailors, captains, and shipwrights, your merchants and all the warriors within you, with all the other people on board, will sink into the heart of the sea on the day of your downfall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.28', 'BSB', 'The countryside will shake when your sailors cry out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.29', 'BSB', 'All who handle the oars will abandon their ships. The sailors and all the captains of the sea will stand on the shore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.30', 'BSB', 'They will raise their voices for you and cry out bitterly. They will throw dust on their heads and roll in ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.31', 'BSB', 'They will shave their heads for you and wrap themselves in sackcloth. They will weep over you with anguish of soul and bitter mourning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.32', 'BSB', 'As they wail and mourn over you, they will take up a lament for you: ‘Who was ever like Tyre, silenced in the middle of the sea?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.33', 'BSB', 'When your wares went out to sea, you satisfied many nations. You enriched the kings of the earth with your abundant wealth and merchandise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.34', 'BSB', 'Now you are shattered by the seas in the depths of the waters; your merchandise and the people among you have gone down with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.35', 'BSB', 'All the people of the coastlands are appalled over you. Their kings shudder with fear; their faces are contorted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.27.36', 'BSB', 'Those who trade among the nations hiss at you; you have come to a horrible end and will be no more.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.1', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, tell the ruler of Tyre that this is what the Lord GOD says: Your heart is proud, and you have said, ‘I am a god; I sit in the seat of gods in the heart of the sea.’ Yet you are a man and not a god, though you have regarded your heart as that of a god.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.3', 'BSB', 'Behold, you are wiser than Daniel; no secret is hidden from you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.4', 'BSB', 'By your wisdom and understanding you have gained your wealth and amassed gold and silver for your treasuries.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.5', 'BSB', 'By your great skill in trading you have increased your wealth, but your heart has grown proud because of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Because you regard your heart as the heart of a god,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.7', 'BSB', 'behold, I will bring foreigners against you, the most ruthless of nations. They will draw their swords against the beauty of your wisdom and will defile your splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.8', 'BSB', 'They will bring you down to the Pit, and you will die a violent death in the heart of the seas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.9', 'BSB', 'Will you still say, ‘I am a god,’ in the presence of those who slay you? You will be only a man, not a god, in the hands of those who wound you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.10', 'BSB', 'You will die the death of the uncircumcised at the hands of foreigners. For I have spoken, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.11', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.12', 'BSB', '“Son of man, take up a lament for the king of Tyre and tell him that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘You were the seal of perfection, full of wisdom and perfect in beauty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.13', 'BSB', 'You were in Eden, the garden of God. Every kind of precious stone adorned you: ruby, topaz, and diamond, beryl, onyx, and jasper, sapphire, turquoise, and emerald. Your mountings and settings were crafted in gold, prepared on the day of your creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.14', 'BSB', 'You were anointed as a guardian cherub, for I had ordained you. You were on the holy mountain of God; you walked among the fiery stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.15', 'BSB', 'From the day you were created you were blameless in your ways— until wickedness was found in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.16', 'BSB', 'By the vastness of your trade, you were filled with violence, and you sinned. So I drove you in disgrace from the mountain of God, and I banished you, O guardian cherub, from among the fiery stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.17', 'BSB', 'Your heart grew proud of your beauty; you corrupted your wisdom because of your splendor; so I cast you to the earth; I made you a spectacle before kings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.18', 'BSB', 'By the multitude of your iniquities and the dishonesty of your trading you have profaned your sanctuaries. So I made fire come from within you, and it consumed you. I reduced you to ashes on the ground in the eyes of all who saw you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.19', 'BSB', 'All the nations who know you are appalled over you. You have come to a horrible end and will be no more.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.20', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.21', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against Sidon and prophesy against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.22', 'BSB', 'And you are to declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, I am against you, O Sidon, and I will be glorified within you. They will know that I am the LORD when I execute judgments against her and demonstrate My holiness through her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.23', 'BSB', 'I will send a plague against her and shed blood in her streets; the slain will fall within her, while the sword is against her on every side. Then they will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.24', 'BSB', 'For the people of Israel will no longer face a pricking brier or a painful thorn from all around them who treat them with contempt. Then they will know that I am the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.25', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘When I gather the house of Israel from the peoples among whom they have been scattered, I will show Myself holy among them in the sight of the nations. Then they will dwell in their own land, which I have given to My servant Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.28.26', 'BSB', 'And there they will dwell securely, build houses, and plant vineyards. They will dwell securely when I execute judgments against all those around them who treat them with contempt. Then they will know that I am the LORD their God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.1', 'BSB', 'In the tenth year, on the twelfth day of the tenth month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against Pharaoh king of Egypt and prophesy against him and against all Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.3', 'BSB', 'Speak to him and tell him that this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I am against you, O Pharaoh king of Egypt, O great monster who lies among his rivers, who says, ‘The Nile is mine; I made it myself.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.4', 'BSB', 'But I will put hooks in your jaws and cause the fish of your streams to cling to your scales. I will haul you up out of your rivers, and all the fish of your streams will cling to your scales.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.5', 'BSB', 'I will leave you in the desert, you and all the fish of your streams. You will fall on the open field and will not be taken away or gathered for burial. I have given you as food to the beasts of the earth and the birds of the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.6', 'BSB', 'Then all the people of Egypt will know that I am the LORD. For you were only a staff of reeds to the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.7', 'BSB', 'When Israel took hold of you with their hands, you splintered, tearing all their shoulders; when they leaned on you, you broke, and their backs were wrenched.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: I will bring a sword against you and cut off from you man and beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.9', 'BSB', 'The land of Egypt will become a desolate wasteland. Then they will know that I am the LORD. Because you said, ‘The Nile is mine; I made it,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.10', 'BSB', 'therefore I am against you and against your rivers. I will turn the land of Egypt into a ruin, a desolate wasteland from Migdol to Syene, and as far as the border of Cush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.11', 'BSB', 'No foot of man or beast will pass through, and it will be uninhabited for forty years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.12', 'BSB', 'I will make the land of Egypt a desolation among desolate lands, and her cities will lie desolate for forty years among the ruined cities. And I will disperse the Egyptians among the nations and scatter them throughout the countries.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.13', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: At the end of forty years I will gather the Egyptians from the nations to which they were scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.14', 'BSB', 'I will restore Egypt from captivity and bring them back to the land of Pathros, the land of their origin. There they will be a lowly kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.15', 'BSB', 'Egypt will be the lowliest of kingdoms and will never again exalt itself above the nations. For I will diminish Egypt so that it will never again rule over the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.16', 'BSB', 'Egypt will never again be an object of trust for the house of Israel, but will remind them of their iniquity in turning to the Egyptians. Then they will know that I am the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.17', 'BSB', 'In the twenty-seventh year, on the first day of the first month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.18', 'BSB', '“Son of man, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon caused his army to labor strenuously against Tyre. Every head was made bald and every shoulder made raw. But he and his army received no wages from Tyre for the labor they expended on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: I will give the land of Egypt to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, who will carry off its wealth, seize its spoil, and remove its plunder. This will be the wages for his army.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.20', 'BSB', 'I have given him the land of Egypt as the reward for his labor, because it was done for Me, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.29.21', 'BSB', 'In that day I will cause a horn to sprout for the house of Israel, and I will open your mouth to speak among them. Then they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.1', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, prophesy and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: Wail, ‘Alas for that day!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.3', 'BSB', 'For the day is near, the Day of the LORD is near. It will be a day of clouds, a time of doom for the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.4', 'BSB', 'A sword will come against Egypt, and there will be anguish in Cush when the slain fall in Egypt, its wealth is taken away, and its foundations are torn down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.5', 'BSB', 'Cush, Put, and Lud, and all the various peoples, as well as Libya and the men of the covenant land, will fall with Egypt by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says: The allies of Egypt will fall, and her proud strength will collapse. From Migdol to Syene they will fall by the sword within her, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.7', 'BSB', 'They will be desolate among desolate lands, and their cities will lie among ruined cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.8', 'BSB', 'Then they will know that I am the LORD when I set fire to Egypt and all her helpers are shattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.9', 'BSB', 'On that day messengers will go out from Me in ships to frighten Cush out of complacency. Anguish will come upon them on the day of Egypt’s doom. For it is indeed coming.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.10', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: I will put an end to the hordes of Egypt by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.11', 'BSB', 'He and his people with him, the most ruthless of the nations, will be brought in to destroy the land. They will draw their swords against Egypt and fill the land with the slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.12', 'BSB', 'I will make the streams dry up and sell the land to the wicked. By the hands of foreigners I will bring desolation upon the land and everything in it. I, the LORD, have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.13', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: I will destroy the idols and put an end to the images in Memphis. There will no longer be a prince in Egypt, and I will instill fear in that land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.14', 'BSB', 'I will lay waste Pathros, set fire to Zoan, and execute judgment on Thebes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.15', 'BSB', 'I will pour out My wrath on Pelusium, the stronghold of Egypt, and cut off the crowds of Thebes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.16', 'BSB', 'I will set fire to Egypt, Pelusium will writhe in anguish, Thebes will be split open, and Memphis will face daily distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.17', 'BSB', 'The young men of On and Pi-beseth will fall by the sword, and those cities will go into captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.18', 'BSB', 'The day will be darkened in Tahpanhes when I break the yoke of Egypt and her proud strength comes to an end. A cloud will cover her, and her daughters will go into captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.19', 'BSB', 'So I will execute judgment on Egypt, and they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.20', 'BSB', 'In the eleventh year, on the seventh day of the first month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.21', 'BSB', '“Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt. See, it has not been bound up for healing, or splinted for strength to hold the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.22', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of Egypt. I will break his arms, both the strong one and the one already broken, and will make the sword fall from his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.23', 'BSB', 'I will disperse the Egyptians among the nations and scatter them throughout the lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.24', 'BSB', 'I will strengthen the arms of Babylon’s king and place My sword in his hand, but I will break the arms of Pharaoh, who will groan before him like a mortally wounded man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.25', 'BSB', 'I will strengthen the arms of Babylon’s king, but Pharaoh’s arms will fall limp. Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I place My sword in the hand of Babylon’s king, and he wields it against the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.30.26', 'BSB', 'I will disperse the Egyptians among the nations and scatter them throughout the lands. Then they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.1', 'BSB', 'In the eleventh year, on the first day of the third month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, say to Pharaoh king of Egypt and to his multitude: ‘Who can be compared to your greatness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.3', 'BSB', 'Look at Assyria, a cedar in Lebanon, with beautiful branches that shaded the forest. It towered on high; its top was among the clouds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.4', 'BSB', 'The waters made it grow; the deep springs made it tall, directing their streams all around its base and sending their channels to all the trees of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore it towered higher than all the trees of the field. Its branches multiplied, and its boughs grew long as it spread them out because of the abundant waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.6', 'BSB', 'All the birds of the air nested in its branches, and all the beasts of the field gave birth beneath its boughs; all the great nations lived in its shade.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.7', 'BSB', 'It was beautiful in its greatness, in the length of its limbs, for its roots extended to abundant waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.8', 'BSB', 'The cedars in the garden of God could not rival it; the cypresses could not compare with its branches, nor the plane trees match its boughs. No tree in the garden of God could compare with its beauty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.9', 'BSB', 'I made it beautiful with its many branches, the envy of all the trees of Eden, which were in the garden of God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Since it became great in height and set its top among the clouds, and it grew proud on account of its height,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.11', 'BSB', 'I delivered it into the hand of the ruler of the nations, for him to deal with it according to its wickedness. I have banished it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.12', 'BSB', 'Foreigners, the most ruthless of the nations, cut it down and left it. Its branches have fallen on the mountains and in every valley; its boughs lay broken in all the earth’s ravines. And all the peoples of the earth left its shade and abandoned it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.13', 'BSB', 'All the birds of the air nested on its fallen trunk, and all the beasts of the field lived among its boughs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.14', 'BSB', 'This happened so that no other trees by the waters would become great in height and set their tops among the clouds, and no other well-watered trees would reach them in height. For they have all been consigned to death, to the depths of the earth, among the mortals who descend to the Pit.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.15', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘On the day it was brought down to Sheol, I caused mourning. I covered the deep because of it; I held back its rivers; its abundant waters were restrained. I made Lebanon mourn for it, and all the trees of the field fainted because of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.16', 'BSB', 'I made the nations quake at the sound of its downfall, when I cast it down to Sheol with those who descend to the Pit. Then all the trees of Eden, the choicest and best of Lebanon, all the well-watered trees, were consoled in the earth below.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.17', 'BSB', 'They too descended with it to Sheol, to those slain by the sword. As its allies they had lived in its shade among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.31.18', 'BSB', 'Who then is like you in glory and greatness among the trees of Eden? You also will be brought down to the depths of the earth to be with the trees of Eden. You will lie among the uncircumcised, with those slain by the sword. This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, declares the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.1', 'BSB', 'In the twelfth year, on the first day of the twelfth month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, take up a lament for Pharaoh king of Egypt and say to him: ‘You are like a lion among the nations; you are like a monster in the seas. You thrash about in your rivers, churning up the waters with your feet and muddying the streams.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will spread My net over you with a company of many peoples, and they will draw you up in My net.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.4', 'BSB', 'I will abandon you on the land and hurl you into the open field. I will cause all the birds of the air to settle upon you, and all the beasts of the earth to eat their fill of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.5', 'BSB', 'I will put your flesh on the mountains and fill the valleys with your remains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.6', 'BSB', 'I will drench the land with the flow of your blood, all the way to the mountains— the ravines will be filled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.7', 'BSB', 'When I extinguish you, I will cover the heavens and darken their stars. I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon will not give its light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.8', 'BSB', 'All the shining lights in the heavens I will darken over you, and I will bring darkness upon your land,’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.9', 'BSB', '‘I will trouble the hearts of many peoples, when I bring about your destruction among the nations, in countries you do not know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.10', 'BSB', 'I will cause many peoples to be appalled over you, and their kings will shudder in horror because of you when I brandish My sword before them. On the day of your downfall each of them will tremble every moment for his life.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.11', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘The sword of the king of Babylon will come against you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.12', 'BSB', 'I will make your hordes fall by the swords of the mighty, the most ruthless of all nations. They will ravage the pride of Egypt and all her multitudes will be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.13', 'BSB', 'I will slaughter all her cattle beside the abundant waters. No human foot will muddy them again, and no cattle hooves will disturb them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.14', 'BSB', 'Then I will let her waters settle and will make her rivers flow like oil,’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.15', 'BSB', '‘When I make the land of Egypt a desolation and empty it of all that filled it, when I strike down all who live there, then they will know that I am the LORD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.16', 'BSB', 'This is the lament they will chant for her; the daughters of the nations will chant it. Over Egypt and all her multitudes they will chant it, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.17', 'BSB', 'In the twelfth year, on the fifteenth day of the month, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.18', 'BSB', '“Son of man, wail for the multitudes of Egypt, and consign her and the daughters of the mighty nations to the depths of the earth with those who descend to the Pit:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.19', 'BSB', 'Whom do you surpass in beauty? Go down and be placed with the uncircumcised!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.20', 'BSB', 'They will fall among those slain by the sword. The sword is appointed! Let them drag her away along with all her multitudes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.21', 'BSB', 'Mighty chiefs will speak from the midst of Sheol about Egypt and her allies: ‘They have come down and lie with the uncircumcised, with those slain by the sword.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.22', 'BSB', 'Assyria is there with her whole company; her graves are all around her. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.23', 'BSB', 'Her graves are set in the depths of the Pit, and her company is all around her grave. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword— those who once spread terror in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.24', 'BSB', 'Elam is there with all her multitudes around her grave. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword— those who went down uncircumcised to the earth below, who once spread their terror in the land of the living. They bear their disgrace with those who descend to the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.25', 'BSB', 'Among the slain they prepare a resting place for Elam with all her hordes, with her graves all around her. All of them are uncircumcised, slain by the sword, although their terror was once spread in the land of the living. They bear their disgrace with those who descend to the Pit. They are placed among the slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.26', 'BSB', 'Meshech and Tubal are there with all their multitudes, with their graves all around them. All of them are uncircumcised, slain by the sword, because they spread their terror in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.27', 'BSB', 'They do not lie down with the fallen warriors of old, who went down to Sheol with their weapons of war, whose swords were placed under their heads, whose shields rested on their bones, although the terror of the mighty was once in the land of the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.28', 'BSB', 'But you too will be shattered and lie down among the uncircumcised, with those slain by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.29', 'BSB', 'Edom is there, and all her kings and princes, who despite their might are laid among those slain by the sword. They lie down with the uncircumcised, with those who descend to the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.30', 'BSB', 'All the leaders of the north and all the Sidonians are there; they went down in disgrace with the slain, despite the terror of their might. They lie uncircumcised with those slain by the sword and bear their shame with those who descend to the Pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.31', 'BSB', 'Pharaoh will see them and be comforted over all his multitude— Pharaoh and all his army, slain by the sword, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.32.32', 'BSB', 'For I will spread My terror in the land of the living, so that Pharaoh and all his multitude will be laid to rest among the uncircumcised, with those slain by the sword, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.1', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, speak to your people and tell them: ‘Suppose I bring the sword against a land, and the people of that land choose a man from among them, appointing him as their watchman,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.3', 'BSB', 'and he sees the sword coming against that land and blows the ram’s horn to warn the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.4', 'BSB', 'Then if anyone hears the sound of the horn but fails to heed the warning, and the sword comes and takes him away, his blood will be on his own head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.5', 'BSB', 'Since he heard the sound of the horn but failed to heed the warning, his blood will be on his own head. If he had heeded the warning, he would have saved his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.6', 'BSB', 'But if the watchman sees the sword coming and fails to blow the horn to warn the people, and the sword comes and takes away a life, then that one will be taken away in his iniquity, but I will hold the watchman accountable for his blood.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.7', 'BSB', 'As for you, O son of man, I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel; so hear the word from My mouth and give them the warning from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.8', 'BSB', 'If I say to the wicked, ‘O wicked man, you will surely die,’ but you do not speak out to dissuade him from his way, then that wicked man will die in his iniquity, yet I will hold you accountable for his blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.9', 'BSB', 'But if you warn the wicked man to turn from his way, and he does not turn from it, he will die in his iniquity, but you will have saved your life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.10', 'BSB', 'Now as for you, son of man, tell the house of Israel that this is what they have said: ‘Our transgressions and our sins are heavy upon us, and we are wasting away because of them! How can we live?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.11', 'BSB', 'Say to them: ‘As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, I take no pleasure in the death of the wicked, but rather that the wicked should turn from their ways and live. Turn! Turn from your evil ways! For why should you die, O house of Israel?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, son of man, say to your people: ‘The righteousness of the righteous man will not deliver him in the day of his transgression; neither will the wickedness of the wicked man cause him to stumble on the day he turns from his wickedness. Nor will the righteous man be able to survive by his righteousness on the day he sins.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.13', 'BSB', 'If I tell the righteous man that he will surely live, but he then trusts in his righteousness and commits iniquity, then none of his righteous works will be remembered; he will die because of the iniquity he has committed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.14', 'BSB', 'But if I tell the wicked man, ‘You will surely die,’ and he turns from his sin and does what is just and right—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.15', 'BSB', 'if he restores a pledge, makes restitution for what he has stolen, and walks in the statutes of life without practicing iniquity—then he will surely live; he will not die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.16', 'BSB', 'None of the sins he has committed will be held against him. He has done what is just and right; he will surely live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.17', 'BSB', 'Yet your people say, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ But it is their way that is not just.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.18', 'BSB', 'If a righteous man turns from his righteousness and commits iniquity, he will die for it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.19', 'BSB', 'But if a wicked man turns from his wickedness and does what is just and right, he will live because of this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.20', 'BSB', 'Yet you say, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ But I will judge each of you according to his ways, O house of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.21', 'BSB', 'In the twelfth year of our exile, on the fifth day of the tenth month, a fugitive from Jerusalem came to me and reported, “The city has been taken!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.22', 'BSB', 'Now the evening before the fugitive arrived, the hand of the LORD was upon me, and He opened my mouth before the man came to me in the morning. So my mouth was opened and I was no longer mute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.23', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.24', 'BSB', '“Son of man, those living in the ruins in the land of Israel are saying, ‘Abraham was only one man, yet he possessed the land. But we are many; surely the land has been given to us as a possession.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘You eat meat with the blood in it, lift up your eyes to your idols, and shed blood. Should you then possess the land?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.26', 'BSB', 'You have relied on your swords, you have committed detestable acts, and each of you has defiled his neighbor’s wife. Should you then possess the land?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.27', 'BSB', 'Tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘As surely as I live, those in the ruins will fall by the sword, those in the open field I will give to be devoured by wild animals, and those in the strongholds and caves will die by plague.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.28', 'BSB', 'I will make the land a desolate waste, and the pride of her strength will come to an end. The mountains of Israel will become desolate, so that no one will pass through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.29', 'BSB', 'Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I have made the land a desolate waste because of all the abominations they have committed.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.30', 'BSB', 'As for you, son of man, your people are talking about you near the city walls and in the doorways of their houses. One speaks to another, each saying to his brother, ‘Come and hear the message that has come from the LORD!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.31', 'BSB', 'So My people come to you as usual, sit before you, and hear your words; but they do not put them into practice. Although they express love with their mouths, their hearts pursue dishonest gain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.32', 'BSB', 'Indeed, you are to them like a singer of love songs with a beautiful voice, who skillfully plays an instrument. They hear your words but do not put them into practice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.33.33', 'BSB', 'So when it comes to pass—and surely it will come—then they will know that a prophet has been among them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel. Prophesy and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Woe to the shepherds of Israel, who only feed themselves! Should not the shepherds feed their flock?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.3', 'BSB', 'You eat the fat, wear the wool, and butcher the fattened sheep, but you do not feed the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.4', 'BSB', 'You have not strengthened the weak, healed the sick, bound up the injured, brought back the strays, or searched for the lost. Instead, you have ruled them with violence and cruelty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.5', 'BSB', 'They were scattered for lack of a shepherd, and when they were scattered they became food for all the wild beasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.6', 'BSB', 'My flock went astray on all the mountains and every high hill. They were scattered over the face of all the earth, with no one to search for them or seek them out.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore, you shepherds, hear the word of the LORD:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.8', 'BSB', '‘As surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, because My flock lacks a shepherd and has become prey and food for every wild beast, and because My shepherds did not search for My flock but fed themselves instead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.9', 'BSB', 'therefore, you shepherds, hear the word of the LORD!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.10', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, I am against the shepherds, and I will demand from them My flock and remove them from tending the flock, so that they can no longer feed themselves. For I will deliver My flock from their mouths, and it will no longer be food for them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.11', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Behold, I Myself will search for My flock and seek them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.12', 'BSB', 'As a shepherd looks for his scattered sheep when he is among the flock, so I will look for My flock. I will rescue them from all the places to which they were scattered on a day of clouds and darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.13', 'BSB', 'I will bring them out from the peoples, gather them from the countries, and bring them into their own land. I will feed them on the mountains of Israel, in the ravines, and in all the settlements of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.14', 'BSB', 'I will feed them in good pasture, and the lofty mountains of Israel will be their grazing land. There they will lie down in a good grazing land; they will feed in rich pasture on the mountains of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.15', 'BSB', 'I will tend My flock and make them lie down, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.16', 'BSB', 'I will seek the lost, bring back the strays, bind up the broken, and strengthen the weak; but the sleek and strong I will destroy. I will shepherd them with justice.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.17', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says to you, My flock: ‘I will judge between one sheep and another, between the rams and the goats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.18', 'BSB', 'Is it not enough for you to feed on the good pasture? Must you also trample the rest of the pasture with your feet? Is it not enough for you to drink the clear waters? Must you also muddy the rest with your feet?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.19', 'BSB', 'Why must My flock feed on what your feet have trampled, and drink what your feet have muddied?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says to them: ‘Behold, I Myself will judge between the fat sheep and the lean sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.21', 'BSB', 'Since you shove with flank and shoulder, butting all the weak ones with your horns until you have scattered them abroad,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.22', 'BSB', 'I will save My flock, and they will no longer be prey. I will judge between one sheep and another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.23', 'BSB', 'I will appoint over them one shepherd, My servant David, and he will feed them. He will feed them and be their shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.24', 'BSB', 'I, the LORD, will be their God, and My servant David will be a prince among them. I, the LORD, have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.25', 'BSB', 'I will make with them a covenant of peace and rid the land of wild animals, so that they may dwell securely in the wilderness and sleep in the forest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.26', 'BSB', 'I will make them and the places around My hill a blessing. I will send down showers in season—showers of blessing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.27', 'BSB', 'The trees of the field will give their fruit, and the land will yield its produce; My flock will be secure in their land. Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I have broken the bars of their yoke and delivered them from the hands that enslaved them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.28', 'BSB', 'They will no longer be prey for the nations, and the beasts of the earth will not consume them. They will dwell securely, and no one will frighten them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.29', 'BSB', 'And I will raise up for them a garden of renown, and they will no longer be victims of famine in the land or bear the scorn of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.30', 'BSB', 'Then they will know that I, the LORD their God, am with them, and that they, the house of Israel, are My people,’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.34.31', 'BSB', '‘You are My flock, the sheep of My pasture, My people, and I am your God,’ declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.1', 'BSB', 'Moreover, the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against Mount Seir and prophesy against it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.3', 'BSB', 'and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I am against you, O Mount Seir. I will stretch out My hand against you and make you a desolate waste.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.4', 'BSB', 'I will turn your cities into ruins, and you will become a desolation. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.5', 'BSB', 'Because you harbored an ancient hatred and delivered the Israelites over to the sword in the time of their disaster at the final stage of their punishment,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.6', 'BSB', 'therefore as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, I will give you over to bloodshed and it will pursue you. Since you did not hate bloodshed, it will pursue you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.7', 'BSB', 'I will make Mount Seir a desolate waste and will cut off from it those who come and go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.8', 'BSB', 'I will fill its mountains with the slain; those killed by the sword will fall on your hills, in your valleys, and in all your ravines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.9', 'BSB', 'I will make you a perpetual desolation, and your cities will not be inhabited. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.10', 'BSB', 'Because you have said, ‘These two nations and countries will be ours, and we will possess them,’ even though the LORD was there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.11', 'BSB', 'therefore as surely as I live, declares the Lord GOD, I will treat you according to the anger and jealousy you showed in your hatred against them, and I will make Myself known among them when I judge you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.12', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I, the LORD, have heard every contemptuous word you uttered against the mountains of Israel when you said, ‘They are desolate; they are given to us to devour!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.13', 'BSB', 'You boasted against Me with your mouth and multiplied your words against Me. I heard it Myself!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.14', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: While the whole earth rejoices, I will make you desolate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.35.15', 'BSB', 'As you rejoiced when the inheritance of the house of Israel became desolate, so will I do to you. You will become a desolation, O Mount Seir, and so will all of Edom. Then they will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.1', 'BSB', '“And you, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel and say: O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Because the enemy has said of you, ‘Aha! The ancient heights have become our possession,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.3', 'BSB', 'therefore prophesy and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: Because they have made you desolate and have trampled you on every side, so that you became a possession of the rest of the nations and were taken up in slander by the lips of their talkers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.4', 'BSB', 'therefore, O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD. This is what the Lord GOD says to the mountains and hills, to the ravines and valleys, to the desolate ruins and abandoned cities, which have become a spoil and a mockery to the rest of the nations around you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Surely in My burning zeal I have spoken against the rest of the nations, and against all Edom, who took My land as their own possession with wholehearted joy and utter contempt, so that its pastureland became plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore, prophesy concerning the land of Israel and tell the mountains and hills, the ravines and valleys, that this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I have spoken in My burning zeal because you have endured the reproach of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: I have sworn with an uplifted hand that surely the nations around you will endure reproach of their own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.8', 'BSB', 'But you, O mountains of Israel, will produce branches and bear fruit for My people Israel, for they will soon come home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.9', 'BSB', 'For behold, I am on your side; I will turn toward you, and you will be tilled and sown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.10', 'BSB', 'I will multiply the people upon you—the house of Israel in its entirety. The cities will be inhabited and the ruins rebuilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.11', 'BSB', 'I will fill you with people and animals, and they will multiply and be fruitful. I will make you as inhabited as you once were, and I will make you prosper more than before. Then you will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.12', 'BSB', 'Yes, I will cause My people Israel to walk upon you; they will possess you, and you will be their inheritance, and you will no longer deprive them of their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.13', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: Because people say to you, ‘You devour men and deprive your nation of its children,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.14', 'BSB', 'therefore you will no longer devour men or deprive your nation of its children, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.15', 'BSB', 'I will no longer allow the taunts of the nations to be heard against you, and you will no longer endure the reproach of the peoples or cause your nation to stumble, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.16', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.17', 'BSB', '“Son of man, when the people of Israel lived in their land, they defiled it by their own ways and deeds. Their behavior before Me was like the uncleanness of a woman’s impurity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.18', 'BSB', 'So I poured out My wrath upon them because of the blood they had shed on the land, and because they had defiled it with their idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.19', 'BSB', 'I dispersed them among the nations, and they were scattered throughout the lands. I judged them according to their ways and deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.20', 'BSB', 'And wherever they went among the nations, they profaned My holy name, because it was said of them, ‘These are the people of the LORD, yet they had to leave His land.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.21', 'BSB', 'But I had concern for My holy name, which the house of Israel had profaned among the nations to which they had gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.22', 'BSB', 'Therefore tell the house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: It is not for your sake that I will act, O house of Israel, but for My holy name, which you profaned among the nations to which you went.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.23', 'BSB', 'I will show the holiness of My great name, which has been profaned among the nations—the name you have profaned among them. Then the nations will know that I am the LORD, declares the Lord GOD, when I show My holiness in you before their eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.24', 'BSB', 'For I will take you from among the nations and gather you out of all the countries, and I will bring you back into your own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.25', 'BSB', 'I will also sprinkle clean water on you, and you will be clean. I will cleanse you from all your impurities and all your idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.26', 'BSB', 'I will give you a new heart and put a new spirit within you; I will remove your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.27', 'BSB', 'And I will put My Spirit within you and cause you to walk in My statutes and to carefully observe My ordinances.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.28', 'BSB', 'Then you will live in the land that I gave your forefathers; you will be My people, and I will be your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.29', 'BSB', 'I will save you from all your uncleanness. I will summon the grain and make it plentiful, and I will not bring famine upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.30', 'BSB', 'I will also make the fruit of the trees and the crops of the field plentiful, so that you will no longer bear reproach among the nations on account of famine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.31', 'BSB', 'Then you will remember your evil ways and wicked deeds, and you will loathe yourselves for your iniquities and abominations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.32', 'BSB', 'It is not for your sake that I will act, declares the Lord GOD—let it be known to you. Be ashamed and disgraced for your ways, O house of Israel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.33', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: On the day I cleanse you from all your iniquities, I will cause the cities to be resettled and the ruins to be rebuilt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.34', 'BSB', 'The desolate land will be cultivated instead of lying desolate in the sight of all who pass through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.35', 'BSB', 'Then they will say, ‘This land that was desolate has become like the garden of Eden. The cities that were once ruined, desolate, and destroyed are now fortified and inhabited.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.36', 'BSB', 'Then the nations around you that remain will know that I, the LORD, have rebuilt what was destroyed, and I have replanted what was desolate. I, the LORD, have spoken, and I will do it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.37', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Once again I will hear the plea of the house of Israel and do for them this: I will multiply their people like a flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.36.38', 'BSB', 'Like the numerous flocks for sacrifices at Jerusalem during her appointed feasts, so the ruined cities will be filled with flocks of people. Then they will know that I am the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.1', 'BSB', 'The hand of the LORD was upon me, and He brought me out by His Spirit and set me down in the middle of the valley, and it was full of bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.2', 'BSB', 'He led me all around among them, and I saw a great many bones on the floor of the valley, and indeed, they were very dry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.3', 'BSB', 'Then He asked me, “Son of man, can these bones come to life?” “O Lord GOD,” I replied, “only You know.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.4', 'BSB', 'And He said to me, “Prophesy concerning these bones and tell them, ‘Dry bones, hear the word of the LORD!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says to these bones: I will cause breath to enter you, and you will come to life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.6', 'BSB', 'I will attach tendons to you and make flesh grow upon you and cover you with skin. I will put breath within you so that you will come to life. Then you will know that I am the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.7', 'BSB', 'So I prophesied as I had been commanded. And as I prophesied, there was suddenly a noise, a rattling, and the bones came together, bone to bone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.8', 'BSB', 'As I looked on, tendons appeared on them, flesh grew, and skin covered them; but there was no breath in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.9', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me, “Prophesy to the breath; prophesy, son of man, and tell the breath that this is what the Lord GOD says: Come from the four winds, O breath, and breathe into these slain, so that they may live!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.10', 'BSB', 'So I prophesied as He had commanded me, and the breath entered them, and they came to life and stood on their feet—a vast army.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.11', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me, “Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel. Look, they are saying, ‘Our bones are dried up, and our hope has perished; we are cut off.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore prophesy and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘O My people, I will open your graves and bring you up from them, and I will bring you back to the land of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.13', 'BSB', 'Then you, My people, will know that I am the LORD, when I open your graves and bring you up from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.14', 'BSB', 'I will put My Spirit in you and you will live, and I will settle you in your own land. Then you will know that I, the LORD, have spoken, and I will do it, declares the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.15', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.16', 'BSB', '“And you, son of man, take a single stick and write on it: ‘Belonging to Judah and to the Israelites associated with him.’ Then take another stick and write on it: ‘Belonging to Joseph—the stick of Ephraim—and to all the house of Israel associated with him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.17', 'BSB', 'Then join them together into one stick, so that they become one in your hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.18', 'BSB', 'When your people ask you, ‘Won’t you explain to us what you mean by these?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.19', 'BSB', 'you are to tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel associated with him, and I will put them together with the stick of Judah. I will make them into a single stick, and they will become one in My hand.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.20', 'BSB', 'When the sticks on which you write are in your hand and in full view of the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.21', 'BSB', 'you are to tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I will take the Israelites out of the nations to which they have gone, and I will gather them from all around and bring them into their own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.22', 'BSB', 'I will make them one nation in the land, on the mountains of Israel, and one king will rule over all of them. Then they will no longer be two nations and will never again be divided into two kingdoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.23', 'BSB', 'They will no longer defile themselves with their idols or detestable images, or with any of their transgressions. I will save them from all their apostasies by which they sinned, and I will cleanse them. Then they will be My people, and I will be their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.24', 'BSB', 'My servant David will be king over them, and there will be one shepherd for all of them. They will follow My ordinances and keep and observe My statutes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.25', 'BSB', 'They will live in the land that I gave to My servant Jacob, where your fathers lived. They will live there forever with their children and grandchildren, and My servant David will be their prince forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.26', 'BSB', 'And I will make a covenant of peace with them; it will be an everlasting covenant. I will establish them and multiply them, and I will set My sanctuary among them forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.27', 'BSB', 'My dwelling place will be with them; I will be their God, and they will be My people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.37.28', 'BSB', 'Then the nations will know that I the LORD sanctify Israel, when My sanctuary is among them forever.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.1', 'BSB', 'And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.2', 'BSB', '“Son of man, set your face against Gog of the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal. Prophesy against him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.3', 'BSB', 'and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I am against you, O Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.4', 'BSB', 'I will turn you around, put hooks in your jaws, and bring you out with all your army—your horses, your horsemen in full armor, and a great company armed with shields and bucklers, all brandishing their swords.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.5', 'BSB', 'Persia, Cush, and Put will accompany them, all with shields and helmets,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.6', 'BSB', 'as well as Gomer with all its troops, and Beth-togarmah from the far north with all its troops—the many nations with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.7', 'BSB', 'Get ready; prepare yourself, you and all your company gathered around you; you will be their guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.8', 'BSB', 'After a long time you will be summoned. In the latter years you will enter a land that has recovered from war, whose people were gathered from many nations to the mountains of Israel, which had long been desolate. They had been brought out from the nations, and all now dwell securely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.9', 'BSB', 'You and all your troops, and many peoples with you will go up, advancing like a thunderstorm; you will be like a cloud covering the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.10', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: On that day, thoughts will arise in your mind, and you will devise an evil plan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.11', 'BSB', 'You will say, ‘I will go up against a land of unwalled villages; I will come against a tranquil people who dwell securely, all of them living without walls or bars or gates—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.12', 'BSB', 'in order to seize the spoil and carry off the plunder, to turn a hand against the desolate places now inhabited and against a people gathered from the nations, who have acquired livestock and possessions and who live at the center of the land.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.13', 'BSB', 'Sheba and Dedan and the merchants of Tarshish with all its villages will ask, ‘Have you come to capture the plunder? Have you assembled your hordes to carry away loot, to make off with silver and gold, to take cattle and goods, to seize great spoil?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore prophesy, son of man, and tell Gog that this is what the Lord GOD says: On that day when My people Israel are dwelling securely, will you not take notice of this?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.15', 'BSB', 'And you will come from your place out of the far north—you and many peoples with you, all riding horses—a mighty horde, a huge army.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.16', 'BSB', 'You will advance against My people Israel like a cloud covering the land. It will happen in the latter days, O Gog, that I will bring you against My land, so that the nations may know Me when I show Myself holy in you before their eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.17', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: Are you the one of whom I have spoken in former days through My servants, the prophets of Israel, who in those times prophesied for years that I would bring you against them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.18', 'BSB', 'Now on that day when Gog comes against the land of Israel, declares the Lord GOD, My wrath will flare up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.19', 'BSB', 'In My zeal and fiery rage I proclaim that on that day there will be a great earthquake in the land of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.20', 'BSB', 'The fish of the sea, the birds of the air, the beasts of the field, every creature that crawls upon the ground, and all mankind on the face of the earth will tremble at My presence. The mountains will be thrown down, the cliffs will collapse, and every wall will fall to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.21', 'BSB', 'And I will summon a sword against Gog on all My mountains, declares the Lord GOD, and every man’s sword will be against his brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.22', 'BSB', 'I will execute judgment upon him with plague and bloodshed. I will pour out torrents of rain, hailstones, fire, and sulfur on him and on his troops and on the many nations with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.38.23', 'BSB', 'I will magnify and sanctify Myself, and will reveal Myself in the sight of many nations. Then they will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.1', 'BSB', '“As for you, O son of man, prophesy against Gog and declare that this is what the Lord GOD says: Behold, I am against you, O Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.2', 'BSB', 'I will turn you around, drive you along, bring you up from the far north, and send you against the mountains of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.3', 'BSB', 'Then I will strike the bow from your left hand and dash down the arrows from your right hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.4', 'BSB', 'On the mountains of Israel you will fall—you and all your troops and the nations with you. I will give you as food to every kind of ravenous bird and wild beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.5', 'BSB', 'You will fall in the open field, for I have spoken, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.6', 'BSB', 'I will send fire on Magog and on those who dwell securely in the coastlands, and they will know that I am the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.7', 'BSB', 'So I will make My holy name known among My people Israel and will no longer allow it to be profaned. Then the nations will know that I am the LORD, the Holy One in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.8', 'BSB', 'Yes, it is coming, and it will surely happen, declares the Lord GOD. This is the day of which I have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.9', 'BSB', 'Then those who dwell in the cities of Israel will go out, kindle fires, and burn up the weapons—the bucklers and shields, the bows and arrows, the clubs and spears. For seven years they will use them for fuel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.10', 'BSB', 'They will not gather wood from the countryside or cut it from the forests, for they will use the weapons for fuel. They will loot those who looted them and plunder those who plundered them, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.11', 'BSB', 'And on that day I will give Gog a burial place in Israel, the Valley of the Travelers, east of the Sea. It will block those who travel through, because Gog and all his hordes will be buried there. So it will be called the Valley of Hamon-gog.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.12', 'BSB', 'For seven months the house of Israel will be burying them in order to cleanse the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.13', 'BSB', 'All the people of the land will bury them, and it will bring them renown on the day I display My glory, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.14', 'BSB', 'And men will be employed to continually pass through the land to cleanse it by burying the invaders who remain on the ground. At the end of the seven months they will begin their search.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.15', 'BSB', 'As they pass through the land, anyone who sees a human bone will set up a pillar next to it, until the gravediggers have buried it in the Valley of Hamon-gog.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.16', 'BSB', '(Even the city will be named Hamonah. ) And so they will cleanse the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.17', 'BSB', 'And as for you, son of man, this is what the Lord GOD says: Call out to every kind of bird and to every beast of the field: ‘Assemble and come together from all around to the sacrificial feast that I am preparing for you, a great feast on the mountains of Israel. There you will eat flesh and drink blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.18', 'BSB', 'You will eat the flesh of the mighty and drink the blood of the princes of the earth as though they were rams, lambs, goats, and bulls—all the fattened animals of Bashan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.19', 'BSB', 'At the sacrifice I am preparing, you will eat fat until you are gorged and drink blood until you are drunk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.20', 'BSB', 'And at My table you will eat your fill of horses and riders, of mighty men and warriors of every kind,’ declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.21', 'BSB', 'I will display My glory among the nations, and all the nations will see the judgment that I execute and the hand that I lay upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.22', 'BSB', 'From that day forward the house of Israel will know that I am the LORD their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.23', 'BSB', 'And the nations will know that the house of Israel went into exile for their iniquity, because they were unfaithful to Me. So I hid My face from them and delivered them into the hands of their enemies, so that they all fell by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.24', 'BSB', 'I dealt with them according to their uncleanness and transgressions, and I hid My face from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: Now I will restore Jacob from captivity and will have compassion on the whole house of Israel, and I will be jealous for My holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.26', 'BSB', 'They will forget their disgrace and all the treachery they committed against Me, when they dwell securely in their land, with no one to frighten them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.27', 'BSB', 'When I bring them back from the peoples and gather them out of the lands of their enemies, I will show My holiness in them in the sight of many nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.28', 'BSB', 'Then they will know that I am the LORD their God, when I regather them to their own land, not leaving any of them behind after their exile among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.39.29', 'BSB', 'And I will no longer hide My face from them, for I will pour out My Spirit on the house of Israel, declares the Lord GOD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.1', 'BSB', 'In the twenty-fifth year of our exile, at the beginning of the year, on the tenth day of the month—in the fourteenth year after Jerusalem had been struck down—on that very day the hand of the LORD was upon me, and He took me there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.2', 'BSB', 'In visions of God He took me to the land of Israel and set me on a very high mountain, on whose southern slope was a structure that resembled a city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.3', 'BSB', 'So He took me there, and I saw a man whose appearance was like bronze. He was standing in the gateway with a linen cord and a measuring rod in his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.4', 'BSB', '“Son of man,” he said to me, “look with your eyes, hear with your ears, and pay attention to everything I am going to show you, for that is why you have been brought here. Report to the house of Israel everything you see.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.5', 'BSB', 'And I saw a wall surrounding the temple area. Now the length of the measuring rod in the man’s hand was six long cubits (each measuring a cubit and a handbreadth), and he measured the wall to be one rod thick and one rod high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.6', 'BSB', 'Then he came to the gate facing east and climbed its steps. He measured the threshold of the gate to be one rod deep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.7', 'BSB', 'Each gate chamber was one rod long and one rod wide, and there were five cubits between the gate chambers. The inner threshold of the gate by the portico facing inward was one rod deep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.8', 'BSB', 'Then he measured the portico of the gateway inside;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.9', 'BSB', 'it was eight cubits deep, and its jambs were two cubits thick. And the portico of the gateway faced the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.10', 'BSB', 'There were three gate chambers on each side of the east gate, each with the same measurements, and the gateposts on either side also had the same measurements.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.11', 'BSB', 'And he measured the width of the gateway entrance to be ten cubits, and its length was thirteen cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.12', 'BSB', 'In front of each gate chamber was a wall one cubit high, and the gate chambers were six cubits square.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.13', 'BSB', 'Then he measured the gateway from the roof of one gate chamber to the roof of the opposite one; the distance was twenty-five cubits from doorway to doorway.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.14', 'BSB', 'Next he measured the gateposts to be sixty cubits high. The gateway extended around to the gatepost of the courtyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.15', 'BSB', 'And the distance from the entrance of the gateway to the far end of its inner portico was fifty cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.16', 'BSB', 'The gate chambers and their side pillars had beveled windows all around the inside of the gateway. The porticos also had windows all around on the inside. Each side pillar was decorated with palm trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.17', 'BSB', 'Then he brought me into the outer court, and there were chambers and a pavement laid out all around the court. Thirty chambers faced the pavement,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.18', 'BSB', 'which flanked the gateways and corresponded to the length of the gates; this was the lower pavement.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.19', 'BSB', 'Then he measured the distance from the front of the lower gateway to the outside of the inner court; it was a hundred cubits on the east side as well as on the north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.20', 'BSB', 'He also measured the length and width of the gateway of the outer court facing north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.21', 'BSB', 'Its three gate chambers on each side, its side pillars, and its portico all had the same measurements as the first gate: fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.22', 'BSB', 'Its windows, portico, and palm trees had the same measurements as those of the gate facing east. Seven steps led up to it, with its portico opposite them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.23', 'BSB', 'There was a gate to the inner court facing the north gate, just as there was on the east. He measured the distance from gateway to gateway to be a hundred cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.24', 'BSB', 'Then he led me to the south side, and I saw a gateway facing south. He measured its side pillars and portico, and they had the same measurements as the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.25', 'BSB', 'Both the gateway and its portico had windows all around, like the other windows. It was fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.26', 'BSB', 'Seven steps led up to it, and its portico was opposite them; it had palm trees on its side pillars, one on each side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.27', 'BSB', 'The inner court also had a gate facing south, and he measured the distance from gateway to gateway toward the south to be a hundred cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.28', 'BSB', 'Next he brought me into the inner court through the south gate, and he measured the south gate; it had the same measurements as the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.29', 'BSB', 'Its gate chambers, side pillars, and portico had the same measurements as the others. Both the gateway and its portico had windows all around; it was fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.30', 'BSB', '(The porticoes around the inner court were twenty-five cubits long and five cubits deep. )', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.31', 'BSB', 'Its portico faced the outer court, and its side pillars were decorated with palm trees. Eight steps led up to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.32', 'BSB', 'And he brought me to the inner court on the east side, and he measured the gateway; it had the same measurements as the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.33', 'BSB', 'Its gate chambers, side pillars, and portico had the same measurements as the others. Both the gateway and its portico had windows all around. It was fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.34', 'BSB', 'Its portico faced the outer court, and its side pillars were decorated with palm trees on each side. Eight steps led up to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.35', 'BSB', 'Then he brought me to the north gate and measured it. It had the same measurements as the others,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.36', 'BSB', 'as did its gate chambers, side pillars, and portico. It also had windows all around. It was fifty cubits long and twenty-five cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.37', 'BSB', 'Its portico faced the outer court, and its side pillars were decorated with palm trees on each side. Eight steps led up to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.38', 'BSB', 'There was a chamber with a doorway by the portico in each of the inner gateways. There the burnt offering was to be washed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.39', 'BSB', 'Inside the portico of the gateway were two tables on each side, on which the burnt offerings, sin offerings, and guilt offerings were to be slaughtered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.40', 'BSB', 'Outside, as one goes up to the entrance of the north gateway, there were two tables on one side and two more tables on the other side of the gate’s portico.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.41', 'BSB', 'So there were four tables inside the gateway and four outside—eight tables in all—on which the sacrifices were to be slaughtered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.42', 'BSB', 'There were also four tables of dressed stone for the burnt offering, each a cubit and a half long, a cubit and a half wide, and a cubit high. On these were placed the utensils used to slaughter the burnt offerings and the other sacrifices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.43', 'BSB', 'The double-pronged hooks, each a handbreadth long, were fastened all around the inside of the room, and the flesh of the offering was to be placed on the tables.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.44', 'BSB', 'Outside the inner gate, within the inner court, were two chambers, one beside the north gate and facing south, and another beside the south gate and facing north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.45', 'BSB', 'Then the man said to me: “The chamber that faces south is for the priests who keep charge of the temple,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.46', 'BSB', 'and the chamber that faces north is for the priests who keep charge of the altar. These are the sons of Zadok, the only Levites who may approach the LORD to minister before Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.47', 'BSB', 'Next he measured the court. It was square, a hundred cubits long and a hundred cubits wide. And the altar was in front of the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.48', 'BSB', 'Then he brought me to the portico of the temple and measured the side pillars of the portico to be five cubits on each side. The width of the gateway was fourteen cubits and its sidewalls were three cubits on either side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.40.49', 'BSB', 'The portico was twenty cubits wide and twelve cubits deep, and ten steps led up to it. There were columns by the side pillars, one on each side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.1', 'BSB', 'Then the man brought me into the outer sanctuary and measured the side pillars to be six cubits wide on each side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.2', 'BSB', 'The width of the entrance was ten cubits, and the sides of the entrance were five cubits on each side. He also measured the length of the outer sanctuary to be forty cubits, and the width to be twenty cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.3', 'BSB', 'And he went into the inner sanctuary and measured the side pillars at the entrance to be two cubits wide. The entrance was six cubits wide, and the walls on each side were seven cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.4', 'BSB', 'Then he measured the room adjacent to the inner sanctuary to be twenty cubits long and twenty cubits wide. And he said to me, “This is the Most Holy Place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.5', 'BSB', 'Next he measured the wall of the temple to be six cubits thick, and the width of each side room around the temple was four cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.6', 'BSB', 'The side rooms were arranged one above another in three levels of thirty rooms each. There were ledges all around the wall of the temple to serve as supports for the side rooms, so that the supports would not be fastened into the wall of the temple itself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.7', 'BSB', 'The side rooms surrounding the temple widened at each successive level, because the structure surrounding the temple ascended by stages corresponding to the narrowing of the temple wall as it rose upward. And so a stairway went up from the lowest story to the highest, through the middle one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.8', 'BSB', 'I saw that the temple had a raised base all around it, forming the foundation of the side rooms. It was the full length of a rod, six long cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.9', 'BSB', 'The outer wall of the side rooms was five cubits thick, and the open area between the side rooms of the temple', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.10', 'BSB', 'and the outer chambers was twenty cubits wide all around the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.11', 'BSB', 'The side rooms opened into this area, with one entrance on the north and another on the south. The open area was five cubits wide all around.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.12', 'BSB', 'Now the building that faced the temple courtyard on the west was seventy cubits wide, and the wall of the building was five cubits thick all around, with a length of ninety cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.13', 'BSB', 'Then he measured the temple to be a hundred cubits long, and the temple courtyard and the building with its walls were also a hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.14', 'BSB', 'The width of the temple courtyard on the east, including the front of the temple, was a hundred cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.15', 'BSB', 'Next he measured the length of the building facing the temple courtyard at the rear of the temple, including its galleries on each side; it was a hundred cubits. The outer sanctuary, the inner sanctuary, and the porticoes facing the court,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.16', 'BSB', 'as well as the thresholds and the beveled windows and the galleries all around with their three levels opposite the threshold, were overlaid with wood on all sides. They were paneled from the ground to the windows, and the windows were covered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.17', 'BSB', 'In the space above the outside of the entrance to the inner sanctuary on all the walls, spaced evenly around the inner and outer sanctuary,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.18', 'BSB', 'were alternating carved cherubim and palm trees. Each cherub had two faces:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.19', 'BSB', 'the face of a man was toward the palm tree on one side, and the face of a young lion was toward the palm tree on the other side. They were carved all the way around the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.20', 'BSB', 'Cherubim and palm trees were carved on the wall of the outer sanctuary from the floor to the space above the entrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.21', 'BSB', 'The outer sanctuary had a rectangular doorframe, and the doorframe of the sanctuary was similar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.22', 'BSB', 'There was an altar of wood three cubits high and two cubits square. Its corners, base, and sides were of wood. And the man told me, “This is the table that is before the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.23', 'BSB', 'Both the outer sanctuary and the inner sanctuary had double doors,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.24', 'BSB', 'and each door had two swinging panels. There were two panels for one door and two for the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.25', 'BSB', 'Cherubim and palm trees like those on the walls were carved on the doors of the outer sanctuary, and there was a wooden canopy outside, on the front of the portico.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.41.26', 'BSB', 'There were beveled windows and palm trees on the sidewalls of the portico. The side rooms of the temple also had canopies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.1', 'BSB', 'Then the man led me out northward into the outer court, and he brought me to the group of chambers opposite the temple courtyard and the outer wall on the north side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.2', 'BSB', 'The building with the door facing north was a hundred cubits long and fifty cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.3', 'BSB', 'Gallery faced gallery in three levels opposite the twenty cubits that belonged to the inner court and opposite the pavement that belonged to the outer court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.4', 'BSB', 'In front of the chambers was an inner walkway ten cubits wide and a hundred cubits long. Their doors were on the north.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.5', 'BSB', 'Now the upper chambers were smaller because the galleries took more space from the chambers on the lower and middle floors of the building.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.6', 'BSB', 'For they were arranged in three stories, and unlike the courts, they had no pillars. So the upper chambers were set back further than the lower and middle floors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.7', 'BSB', 'An outer wall in front of the chambers was fifty cubits long and ran parallel to the chambers and the outer court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.8', 'BSB', 'For the chambers on the outer court were fifty cubits long, while those facing the temple were a hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.9', 'BSB', 'And below these chambers was the entrance on the east side as one enters them from the outer court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.10', 'BSB', 'On the south side along the length of the wall of the outer court were chambers adjoining the courtyard and opposite the building,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.11', 'BSB', 'with a passageway in front of them, just like the chambers that were on the north. They had the same length and width, with similar exits and dimensions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.12', 'BSB', 'And corresponding to the doors of the chambers that were facing south, there was a door in front of the walkway that was parallel to the wall extending eastward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.13', 'BSB', 'Then the man said to me, “The north and south chambers facing the temple courtyard are the holy chambers where the priests who approach the LORD will eat the most holy offerings. There they will place the most holy offerings—the grain offerings, the sin offerings, and the guilt offerings—for the place is holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.14', 'BSB', 'Once the priests have entered the holy area, they must not go out into the outer court until they have left behind the garments in which they minister, for these are holy. They are to put on other clothes before they approach the places that are for the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.15', 'BSB', 'Now when the man had finished measuring the interior of the temple area, he led me out by the gate that faced east, and he measured the area all around:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.16', 'BSB', 'With a measuring rod he measured the east side to be five hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.17', 'BSB', 'He measured the north side to be five hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.18', 'BSB', 'He measured the south side to be five hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.19', 'BSB', 'And he came around and measured the west side to be five hundred cubits long.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.42.20', 'BSB', 'So he measured the area on all four sides. It had a wall all around, five hundred cubits long and five hundred cubits wide, to separate the holy from the common.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.1', 'BSB', 'Then the man brought me back to the gate that faces east,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.2', 'BSB', 'and I saw the glory of the God of Israel coming from the east. His voice was like the roar of many waters, and the earth shone with His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.3', 'BSB', 'The vision I saw was like the vision I had seen when He came to destroy the city and like the visions I had seen by the River Kebar. I fell facedown,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.4', 'BSB', 'and the glory of the LORD entered the temple through the gate facing east.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.5', 'BSB', 'Then the Spirit lifted me up and brought me into the inner court, and the glory of the LORD filled the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.6', 'BSB', 'While the man was standing beside me, I heard someone speaking to me from inside the temple,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.7', 'BSB', 'and He said to me, “Son of man, this is the place of My throne and the place for the soles of My feet, where I will dwell among the Israelites forever. The house of Israel will never again defile My holy name—neither they nor their kings—by their prostitution and by the funeral offerings for their kings at their deaths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.8', 'BSB', 'When they placed their threshold next to My threshold and their doorposts beside My doorposts, with only a wall between Me and them, they defiled My holy name by the abominations they committed. Therefore I have consumed them in My anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.9', 'BSB', 'Now let them remove far from Me their prostitution and the funeral offerings for their kings, and I will dwell among them forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.10', 'BSB', 'As for you, son of man, describe the temple to the people of Israel, so that they may be ashamed of their iniquities. Let them measure the plan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.11', 'BSB', 'and if they are ashamed of all they have done, then make known to them the design of the temple—its arrangement and its exits and entrances—its whole design along with all its statutes, forms, and laws. Write it down in their sight, so that they may keep its complete design and all its statutes and may carry them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.12', 'BSB', 'This is the law of the temple: All its surrounding territory on top of the mountain will be most holy. Yes, this is the law of the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.13', 'BSB', 'These are the measurements of the altar in long cubits (a cubit and a handbreadth): Its gutter shall be a cubit deep and a cubit wide, with a rim of one span around its edge. And this is the height of the altar:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.14', 'BSB', 'The space from the gutter on the ground to the lower ledge shall be two cubits, and the ledge one cubit wide. The space from the smaller ledge to the larger ledge shall be four cubits, and the ledge one cubit wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.15', 'BSB', 'The altar hearth shall be four cubits high, and four horns shall project upward from the hearth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.16', 'BSB', 'The altar hearth shall be square at its four corners, twelve cubits long and twelve cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.17', 'BSB', 'The ledge shall also be square, fourteen cubits long and fourteen cubits wide, with a rim of half a cubit and a gutter of a cubit all around it. The steps of the altar shall face east.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.18', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me: “Son of man, this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘These are the statutes for the altar on the day it is constructed, so that burnt offerings may be sacrificed on it and blood may be sprinkled on it:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.19', 'BSB', 'You are to give a young bull from the herd as a sin offering to the Levitical priests who are of the family of Zadok, who approach Me to minister before Me, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.20', 'BSB', 'You are to take some of its blood and put it on the four horns of the altar, on the four corners of the ledge, and all around the rim; thus you will cleanse the altar and make atonement for it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.21', 'BSB', 'Then you are to take away the bull for the sin offering and burn it in the appointed part of the temple area outside the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.22', 'BSB', 'On the second day you are to present an unblemished male goat as a sin offering, and the altar is to be cleansed as it was with the bull.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.23', 'BSB', 'When you have finished the purification, you are to present a young, unblemished bull and an unblemished ram from the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.24', 'BSB', 'You must present them before the LORD; the priests are to sprinkle salt on them and sacrifice them as a burnt offering to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.25', 'BSB', 'For seven days you are to provide a male goat daily for a sin offering; you are also to provide a young bull and a ram from the flock, both unblemished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.26', 'BSB', 'For seven days the priests are to make atonement for the altar and cleanse it; so they shall consecrate it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.43.27', 'BSB', 'At the end of these days, from the eighth day on, the priests are to present your burnt offerings and peace offerings on the altar. Then I will accept you, declares the Lord GOD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.1', 'BSB', 'The man then brought me back to the outer gate of the sanctuary that faced east, but it was shut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.2', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to me, “This gate is to remain shut. It shall not be opened, and no man shall enter through it, because the LORD, the God of Israel, has entered through it. Therefore it will remain shut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.3', 'BSB', 'Only the prince himself may sit inside the gateway to eat in the presence of the LORD. He must enter by way of the portico of the gateway and go out the same way.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.4', 'BSB', 'Then the man brought me to the front of the temple by way of the north gate. I looked and saw the glory of the LORD filling His temple, and I fell facedown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD said to me: “Son of man, pay attention; look carefully with your eyes and listen closely with your ears to everything I tell you concerning all the statutes and laws of the house of the LORD. Take careful note of the entrance to the temple, along with all the exits of the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.6', 'BSB', 'Tell the rebellious house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘I have had enough of all your abominations, O house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.7', 'BSB', 'In addition to all your other abominations, you brought in foreigners uncircumcised in both heart and flesh to occupy My sanctuary; you defiled My temple when you offered My food—the fat and the blood; you broke My covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.8', 'BSB', 'And you have not kept charge of My holy things, but have appointed others to keep charge of My sanctuary for you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.9', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: No foreigner uncircumcised in heart and flesh may enter My sanctuary—not even a foreigner who lives among the Israelites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.10', 'BSB', 'Surely the Levites who wandered away from Me when Israel went astray, and who wandered away from Me after their idols, will bear the consequences of their iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.11', 'BSB', 'Yet they shall be ministers in My sanctuary, having charge of the gates of the temple and ministering there. They shall slaughter the burnt offerings and other sacrifices for the people and stand before them to minister to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.12', 'BSB', 'Because they ministered before their idols and became a stumbling block of iniquity to the house of Israel, therefore I swore with an uplifted hand concerning them that they would bear the consequences of their iniquity, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.13', 'BSB', 'They must not approach Me to serve Me as priests or come near any of My holy things or the most holy things. They will bear the shame of the abominations they have committed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.14', 'BSB', 'Yet I will appoint them to keep charge of all the work for the temple and everything to be done in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.15', 'BSB', 'But the Levitical priests, who are descended from Zadok and who kept charge of My sanctuary when the Israelites went astray from Me, are to approach Me to minister before Me. They will stand before Me to offer Me fat and blood, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.16', 'BSB', 'They alone shall enter My sanctuary and draw near to My table to minister before Me. They will keep My charge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.17', 'BSB', 'When they enter the gates of the inner court, they are to wear linen garments; they must not wear anything made of wool when they minister at the gates of the inner court or inside the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.18', 'BSB', 'They are to wear linen turbans on their heads and linen undergarments around their waists. They must not wear anything that makes them perspire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.19', 'BSB', 'When they go out to the outer court, to the people, they are to take off the garments in which they have ministered, leave them in the holy chambers, and dress in other clothes so that they do not transmit holiness to the people with their garments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.20', 'BSB', 'They must not shave their heads or let their hair grow long, but must carefully trim their hair.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.21', 'BSB', 'No priest may drink wine before he enters the inner court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.22', 'BSB', 'And they shall not marry a widow or a divorced woman, but must marry a virgin of the descendants of the house of Israel, or a widow of a priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.23', 'BSB', 'They are to teach My people the difference between the holy and the common, and show them how to discern between the clean and the unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.24', 'BSB', 'In any dispute, they shall officiate as judges and judge according to My ordinances. They must keep My laws and statutes regarding all My appointed feasts, and they must keep My Sabbaths holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.25', 'BSB', 'A priest must not defile himself by going near a dead person. However, for a father, a mother, a son, a daughter, a brother, or an unmarried sister, he may do so,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.26', 'BSB', 'and after he is cleansed, he must count off seven days for himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.27', 'BSB', 'And on the day he goes into the sanctuary, into the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he must present his sin offering, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.28', 'BSB', 'In regard to their inheritance, I am their inheritance. You are to give them no possession in Israel, for I am their possession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.29', 'BSB', 'They shall eat the grain offerings, the sin offerings, and the guilt offerings. Everything in Israel devoted to the LORD will belong to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.30', 'BSB', 'The best of all the firstfruits and of every contribution from all your offerings will belong to the priests. You are to give your first batch of dough to the priest, so that a blessing may rest upon your homes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.44.31', 'BSB', 'The priests may not eat any bird or animal found dead or torn by wild beasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.1', 'BSB', '“When you divide the land by lot as an inheritance, you are to set aside a portion for the LORD, a holy portion of the land 25,000 cubits long and 20,000 cubits wide. This entire tract of land will be holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.2', 'BSB', 'Within this area there is to be a section for the sanctuary 500 cubits square, with 50 cubits around it for open land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.3', 'BSB', 'From this holy portion, you are to measure off a length of 25,000 cubits and a width of 10,000 cubits, and in it will be the sanctuary, the Most Holy Place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.4', 'BSB', 'It will be a holy portion of the land to be used by the priests who minister in the sanctuary, who draw near to minister before the LORD. It will be a place for their houses, as well as a holy area for the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.5', 'BSB', 'An adjacent area 25,000 cubits long and 10,000 cubits wide shall belong to the Levites who minister in the temple; it will be their possession for towns in which to live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.6', 'BSB', 'As the property of the city, you are to set aside an area 5,000 cubits wide and 25,000 cubits long, adjacent to the holy district. It will belong to the whole house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.7', 'BSB', 'Now the prince will have the area bordering each side of the area formed by the holy district and the property of the city, extending westward from the western side and eastward from the eastern side, running lengthwise from the western boundary to the eastern boundary and parallel to one of the tribal portions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.8', 'BSB', 'This land will be his possession in Israel. And My princes will no longer oppress My people, but will give the rest of the land to the house of Israel according to their tribes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.9', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord GOD says: ‘Enough, O princes of Israel! Cease your violence and oppression, and do what is just and right. Stop dispossessing My people, declares the Lord GOD.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.10', 'BSB', 'You must use honest scales, a just ephah, and a just bath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.11', 'BSB', 'The ephah and the bath shall be the same quantity so that the bath will contain a tenth of a homer, and the ephah a tenth of a homer; the homer will be the standard measure for both.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.12', 'BSB', 'The shekel will consist of twenty gerahs. Twenty shekels plus twenty-five shekels plus fifteen shekels will equal one mina.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.13', 'BSB', 'This is the contribution you are to offer: a sixth of an ephah from each homer of wheat, and a sixth of an ephah from each homer of barley.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.14', 'BSB', 'The prescribed portion of oil, measured by the bath, is a tenth of a bath from each cor (a cor consists of ten baths or one homer, since ten baths are equivalent to a homer).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.15', 'BSB', 'And one sheep shall be given from each flock of two hundred from the well-watered pastures of Israel. These are for the grain offerings, burnt offerings, and peace offerings, to make atonement for the people, declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.16', 'BSB', 'All the people of the land must participate in this contribution for the prince in Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.17', 'BSB', 'And it shall be the prince’s part to provide the burnt offerings, grain offerings, and drink offerings for the feasts, New Moons, and Sabbaths—for all the appointed feasts of the house of Israel. He will provide the sin offerings, grain offerings, burnt offerings, and peace offerings to make atonement for the house of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.18', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘On the first day of the first month you are to take a young bull without blemish and purify the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.19', 'BSB', 'And the priest is to take some of the blood from the sin offering and put it on the doorposts of the temple, on the four corners of the ledge of the altar, and on the gateposts of the inner court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.20', 'BSB', 'You must do the same thing on the seventh day of the month for anyone who strays unintentionally or in ignorance. In this way you will make atonement for the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.21', 'BSB', 'On the fourteenth day of the first month you are to observe the Passover, a feast of seven days, during which unleavened bread shall be eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.22', 'BSB', 'On that day the prince shall provide a bull as a sin offering for himself and for all the people of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.23', 'BSB', 'Each day during the seven days of the feast, he shall provide seven bulls and seven rams without blemish as a burnt offering to the LORD, along with a male goat for a sin offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.24', 'BSB', 'He shall also provide as a grain offering an ephah for each bull and an ephah for each ram, along with a hin of olive oil for each ephah of grain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.45.25', 'BSB', 'During the seven days of the feast that begins on the fifteenth day of the seventh month, he is to make the same provision for sin offerings, burnt offerings, grain offerings, and oil.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.1', 'BSB', '“This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘The gate of the inner court that faces east must be kept shut during the six days of work, but on the Sabbath day and on the day of the New Moon it shall be opened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.2', 'BSB', 'The prince is to enter from the outside through the portico of the gateway and stand by the gatepost, while the priests sacrifice his burnt offerings and peace offerings. He is to bow in worship at the threshold of the gate and then depart, but the gate must not be shut until evening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.3', 'BSB', 'On the Sabbaths and New Moons the people of the land are also to bow in worship before the LORD at the entrance to that gateway.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.4', 'BSB', 'The burnt offering that the prince presents to the LORD on the Sabbath day shall be six unblemished male lambs and an unblemished ram.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.5', 'BSB', 'The grain offering with the ram shall be one ephah, and the grain offering with the lambs shall be as much as he is able, along with a hin of oil per ephah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.6', 'BSB', 'On the day of the New Moon he shall offer a young, unblemished bull, six lambs, and a ram without blemish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.7', 'BSB', 'He is to provide a grain offering of an ephah with the bull, an ephah with the ram, and as much as he is able with the lambs, along with a hin of oil per ephah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.8', 'BSB', 'When the prince enters, he shall go in through the portico of the gateway, and he shall go out the same way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.9', 'BSB', 'When the people of the land come before the LORD at the appointed feasts, whoever enters by the north gate to worship must go out by the south gate, and whoever enters by the south gate must go out by the north gate. No one is to return through the gate by which he entered, but each must go out by the opposite gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.10', 'BSB', 'When the people enter, the prince shall go in with them, and when they leave, he shall leave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.11', 'BSB', 'At the festivals and appointed feasts, the grain offering shall be an ephah with a bull, an ephah with a ram, and as much as one is able to give with the lambs, along with a hin of oil per ephah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.12', 'BSB', 'When the prince makes a freewill offering to the LORD, whether a burnt offering or a peace offering, the gate facing east must be opened for him. He is to offer his burnt offering or peace offering just as he does on the Sabbath day. Then he shall go out, and the gate must be closed after he goes out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.13', 'BSB', 'And you shall provide an unblemished year-old lamb as a daily burnt offering to the LORD; you are to offer it every morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.14', 'BSB', 'You are also to provide with it every morning a grain offering of a sixth of an ephah with a third of a hin of oil to moisten the fine flour—a grain offering to the LORD. This is a permanent statute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.15', 'BSB', 'Thus they shall provide the lamb, the grain offering, and the oil every morning as a regular burnt offering.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.16', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: ‘If the prince gives a gift to any of his sons as an inheritance, it will belong to his descendants. It will become their property by inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.17', 'BSB', 'But if he gives a gift from his inheritance to one of his servants, it will belong to that servant until the year of freedom; then it will revert to the prince. His inheritance belongs only to his sons; it shall be theirs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.18', 'BSB', 'The prince must not take any of the inheritance of the people by evicting them from their property. He is to provide an inheritance for his sons from his own property, so that none of My people will be displaced from his property.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.19', 'BSB', 'Then the man brought me through the entrance at the side of the gate into the holy chambers facing north, which belonged to the priests, and he showed me a place there at the far western end', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.20', 'BSB', 'and said to me, “This is the place where the priests shall boil the guilt offering and the sin offering, and where they shall bake the grain offering, so that they do not bring them into the outer court and transmit holiness to the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.21', 'BSB', 'Then he brought me into the outer court and led me around to its four corners, and I saw a separate court in each of its corners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.22', 'BSB', 'In the four corners of the outer court there were enclosed courts, each forty cubits long and thirty cubits wide. Each of the four corner areas had the same dimensions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.23', 'BSB', 'Around the inside of each of the four courts was a row of masonry with ovens built at the base of the walls on all sides.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.46.24', 'BSB', 'And he said to me, “These are the kitchens where those who minister at the temple will cook the sacrifices offered by the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.1', 'BSB', 'Then the man brought me back to the entrance of the temple, and I saw water flowing from under the threshold of the temple toward the east (for the temple faced east). The water was coming down from under the south side of the temple, south of the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.2', 'BSB', 'Next he brought me out through the north gate and led me around the outside to the outer gate facing east, and there I saw the water trickling out from the south side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.3', 'BSB', 'As the man went eastward with a measuring line in his hand, he measured off a thousand cubits and led me through ankle-deep water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.4', 'BSB', 'Then he measured off a thousand cubits and led me through knee-deep water. Again he measured a thousand cubits and led me through waist-deep water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.5', 'BSB', 'Once again he measured off a thousand cubits, but now it was a river that I could not cross, because the water had risen and was deep enough for swimming—a river that could not be crossed on foot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.6', 'BSB', '“Son of man, do you see this?” he asked. Then he led me back to the bank of the river.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.7', 'BSB', 'When I arrived, I saw a great number of trees along both banks of the river.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.8', 'BSB', 'And he said to me, “This water flows out to the eastern region and goes down into the Arabah. When it empties into the Sea, the water there becomes fresh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.9', 'BSB', 'Wherever the river flows, there will be swarms of living creatures and a great number of fish, because it flows there and makes the waters fresh; so wherever the river flows, everything will flourish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.10', 'BSB', 'Fishermen will stand by the shore; from En-gedi to En-eglaim they will spread their nets to catch fish of many kinds, like the fish of the Great Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.11', 'BSB', 'But the swamps and marshes will not become fresh; they will be left for salt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.12', 'BSB', 'Along both banks of the river, fruit trees of all kinds will grow. Their leaves will not wither, and their fruit will not fail. Each month they will bear fruit, because the water from the sanctuary flows to them. Their fruit will be used for food and their leaves for healing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.13', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: “These are the boundaries by which you are to divide the land as an inheritance among the twelve tribes of Israel; Joseph shall receive two portions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.14', 'BSB', 'You are to divide it equally among them. Because I swore with an uplifted hand to give it to your forefathers, this land will fall to you as an inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.15', 'BSB', 'This shall be the boundary of the land: On the north side it will extend from the Great Sea by way of Hethlon through Lebo-hamath to Zedad,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.16', 'BSB', 'Berothah, and Sibraim (which is on the border between Damascus and Hamath), as far as Hazer-hatticon, which is on the border of Hauran.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.17', 'BSB', 'So the border will run from the Sea to Hazar-enan, along the northern border of Damascus, with the territory of Hamath to the north. This will be the northern boundary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.18', 'BSB', 'On the east side the border will run between Hauran and Damascus, along the Jordan between Gilead and the land of Israel, to the Eastern Sea and as far as Tamar. This will be the eastern boundary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.19', 'BSB', 'On the south side it will run from Tamar to the waters of Meribath-kadesh, and along the Brook of Egypt to the Great Sea. This will be the southern boundary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.20', 'BSB', 'And on the west side, the Great Sea will be the boundary up to a point opposite Lebo-hamath. This will be the western boundary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.21', 'BSB', 'You are to divide this land among yourselves according to the tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.22', 'BSB', 'You shall allot it as an inheritance for yourselves and for the foreigners who dwell among you and who have children. You are to treat them as native-born Israelites; along with you, they shall be allotted an inheritance among the tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.47.23', 'BSB', 'In whatever tribe a foreigner dwells, you are to assign his inheritance there,” declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.1', 'BSB', '“Now these are the names of the tribes: At the northern frontier, Dan will have one portion bordering the road of Hethlon to Lebo-hamath and running on to Hazar-enan on the border of Damascus with Hamath to the north, and extending from the east side to the west side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.2', 'BSB', 'Asher will have one portion bordering the territory of Dan from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.3', 'BSB', 'Naphtali will have one portion bordering the territory of Asher from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.4', 'BSB', 'Manasseh will have one portion bordering the territory of Naphtali from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.5', 'BSB', 'Ephraim will have one portion bordering the territory of Manasseh from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.6', 'BSB', 'Reuben will have one portion bordering the territory of Ephraim from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.7', 'BSB', 'Judah will have one portion bordering the territory of Reuben from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.8', 'BSB', 'Bordering the territory of Judah, from east to west, will be the portion you are to set apart. It will be 25,000 cubits wide, and the length of a tribal portion from east to west. In the center will be the sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.9', 'BSB', 'The special portion you set apart to the LORD shall be 25,000 cubits long and 10,000 cubits wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.10', 'BSB', 'This will be the holy portion for the priests. It will be 25,000 cubits long on the north side, 10,000 cubits wide on the west side, 10,000 cubits wide on the east side, and 25,000 cubits long on the south side. In the center will be the sanctuary of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.11', 'BSB', 'It will be for the consecrated priests, the descendants of Zadok, who kept My charge and did not go astray as the Levites did when the Israelites went astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.12', 'BSB', 'It will be a special portion for them set apart from the land, a most holy portion adjacent to the territory of the Levites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.13', 'BSB', 'Bordering the territory of the priests, the Levites shall have an area 25,000 cubits long and 10,000 cubits wide. The whole length will be 25,000 cubits, and the width 10,000 cubits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.14', 'BSB', 'They must not sell or exchange any of it, and they must not transfer this best part of the land, for it is holy to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.15', 'BSB', 'The remaining area, 5,000 cubits wide and 25,000 cubits long, will be for common use by the city, for houses, and for pastureland. The city will be in the center of it', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.16', 'BSB', 'and will have these measurements: 4,500 cubits on the north side, 4,500 cubits on the south side, 4,500 cubits on the east side, and 4,500 cubits on the west side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.17', 'BSB', 'The pastureland of the city will extend 250 cubits to the north, 250 cubits to the south, 250 cubits to the east, and 250 cubits to the west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.18', 'BSB', 'The remainder of the length bordering the holy portion and running adjacent to it will be 10,000 cubits on the east side and 10,000 cubits on the west side. Its produce will supply food for the workers of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.19', 'BSB', 'The workers of the city who cultivate it will come from all the tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.20', 'BSB', 'The entire portion will be a square, 25,000 cubits by 25,000 cubits. You are to set apart the holy portion, along with the city property.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.21', 'BSB', 'The remaining area on both sides of the holy portion and of the property of the city will belong to the prince. He will own the land adjacent to the tribal portions, extending eastward from the 25,000 cubits of the holy district toward the eastern border, and westward from the 25,000 cubits to the western border. And in the center of them will be the holy portion and the sanctuary of the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.22', 'BSB', 'So the Levitical property and the city property will lie in the center of the area belonging to the prince—the area between the borders of Judah and Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.23', 'BSB', 'As for the rest of the tribes: Benjamin will have one portion extending from the east side to the west side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.24', 'BSB', 'Simeon will have one portion bordering the territory of Benjamin from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.25', 'BSB', 'Issachar will have one portion bordering the territory of Simeon from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.26', 'BSB', 'Zebulun will have one portion bordering the territory of Issachar from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.27', 'BSB', 'And Gad will have one portion bordering the territory of Zebulun from east to west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.28', 'BSB', 'The southern border of Gad will run from Tamar to the waters of Meribath-kadesh, then along the Brook of Egypt and out to the Great Sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.29', 'BSB', 'This is the land you are to allot as an inheritance to the tribes of Israel, and these will be their portions,” declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.30', 'BSB', '“These will be the exits of the city: Beginning on the north side, which will be 4,500 cubits long,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.31', 'BSB', 'the gates of the city will be named after the tribes of Israel. On the north side there will be three gates: the gate of Reuben, the gate of Judah, and the gate of Levi.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.32', 'BSB', 'On the east side, which will be 4,500 cubits long, there will be three gates: the gate of Joseph, the gate of Benjamin, and the gate of Dan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.33', 'BSB', 'On the south side, which will be 4,500 cubits long, there will be three gates: the gate of Simeon, the gate of Issachar, and the gate of Zebulun.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.34', 'BSB', 'And on the west side, which will be 4,500 cubits long, there will be three gates: the gate of Gad, the gate of Asher, and the gate of Naphtali.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Ezek.48.35', 'BSB', 'The perimeter of the city will be 18,000 cubits, and from that day on the name of the city will be: THE LORD IS THERE.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.1', 'BSB', 'In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to Jerusalem and besieged it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.2', 'BSB', 'And the Lord delivered into his hand Jehoiakim king of Judah, along with some of the articles from the house of God. He carried these off to the land of Shinar, to the house of his god, where he put them in the treasury of his god.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.3', 'BSB', 'Then the king ordered Ashpenaz, the chief of his court officials, to bring in some Israelites from the royal family and the nobility—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.4', 'BSB', 'young men without blemish, handsome, gifted in all wisdom, knowledgeable, quick to understand, and qualified to serve in the king’s palace—and to teach them the language and literature of the Chaldeans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.5', 'BSB', 'The king assigned them daily provisions of the royal food and wine. They were to be trained for three years, after which they were to enter the king’s service.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.6', 'BSB', 'Among these young men were some from Judah: Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.7', 'BSB', 'The chief official gave them new names: To Daniel he gave the name Belteshazzar; to Hananiah, Shadrach; to Mishael, Meshach; and to Azariah, Abednego.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.8', 'BSB', 'But Daniel made up his mind that he would not defile himself with the king’s food or wine. So he asked the chief official for permission not to defile himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.9', 'BSB', 'Now God had granted Daniel favor and compassion from the chief official,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.10', 'BSB', 'but he said to Daniel, “I fear my lord the king, who has assigned your food and drink. For why should he see your faces looking thinner than those of the other young men your age? You would endanger my head before the king!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.11', 'BSB', 'Then Daniel said to the steward whom the chief official had appointed over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.12', 'BSB', '“Please test your servants for ten days. Let us be given only vegetables to eat and water to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.13', 'BSB', 'Then compare our appearances with those of the young men who are eating the royal food, and deal with your servants according to what you see.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.14', 'BSB', 'So he consented to this and tested them for ten days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.15', 'BSB', 'And at the end of ten days, they looked healthier and better nourished than all the young men who were eating the king’s food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.16', 'BSB', 'So the steward continued to withhold their choice food and the wine they were to drink, and he gave them vegetables instead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.17', 'BSB', 'To these four young men God gave knowledge and understanding in every kind of literature and wisdom. And Daniel had insight into all kinds of visions and dreams.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.18', 'BSB', 'Now at the end of the time specified by the king, the chief official presented them to Nebuchadnezzar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.19', 'BSB', 'And the king spoke with them, and among all the young men he found no one equal to Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah. So they entered the king’s service.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.20', 'BSB', 'In every matter of wisdom and understanding about which the king consulted them, he found them ten times better than all the magicians and enchanters in his entire kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.1.21', 'BSB', 'And Daniel remained there until the first year of King Cyrus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.1', 'BSB', 'In the second year of his reign, Nebuchadnezzar had dreams that troubled his spirit, and sleep escaped him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.2', 'BSB', 'So the king gave orders to summon the magicians, enchanters, sorcerers, and astrologers to explain his dreams. When they came and stood before the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.3', 'BSB', 'he said to them, “I have had a dream, and my spirit is anxious to understand it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.4', 'BSB', 'Then the astrologers answered the king in Aramaic, “O king, may you live forever! Tell your servants the dream, and we will give the interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.5', 'BSB', 'The king replied to the astrologers, “My word is final: If you do not tell me the dream and its interpretation, you will be cut into pieces and your houses will be reduced to rubble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.6', 'BSB', 'But if you tell me the dream and its interpretation, you will receive from me gifts and rewards and great honor. So tell me the dream and its interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.7', 'BSB', 'They answered a second time, “Let the king tell the dream to his servants, and we will give the interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.8', 'BSB', 'The king replied, “I know for sure that you are stalling for time, because you see that my word is final.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.9', 'BSB', 'If you do not tell me the dream, there is only one decree for you. You have conspired to speak before me false and fraudulent words, hoping the situation will change. Therefore tell me the dream, and I will know that you can give me its interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.10', 'BSB', 'The astrologers answered the king, “No one on earth can do what the king requests! No king, however great and powerful, has ever asked anything like this of any magician, enchanter, or astrologer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.11', 'BSB', 'What the king requests is so difficult that no one can tell it to him except the gods, whose dwelling is not with mortals.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.12', 'BSB', 'This response made the king so furious with anger that he gave orders to destroy all the wise men of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.13', 'BSB', 'So the decree went out that the wise men were to be executed, and men went to look for Daniel and his friends to execute them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.14', 'BSB', 'When Arioch, the commander of the king’s guard, had gone out to execute the wise men of Babylon, Daniel replied with discretion and tact.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.15', 'BSB', '“Why is the decree from the king so harsh?” he asked. At this time Arioch explained the situation to Daniel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.16', 'BSB', 'So Daniel went in and asked the king to give him some time, so that he could give him the interpretation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.17', 'BSB', 'Then Daniel returned to his house and explained the matter to his friends Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.18', 'BSB', 'urging them to plead for mercy from the God of heaven concerning this mystery, so that Daniel and his friends would not be killed with the rest of the wise men of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.19', 'BSB', 'During the night, the mystery was revealed to Daniel in a vision, and he blessed the God of heaven', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.20', 'BSB', 'and declared: “Blessed be the name of God forever and ever, for wisdom and power belong to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.21', 'BSB', 'He changes the times and seasons; He removes kings and establishes them. He gives wisdom to the wise and knowledge to the discerning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.22', 'BSB', 'He reveals the deep and hidden things; He knows what lies in darkness, and light dwells with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.23', 'BSB', 'To You, O God of my fathers, I give thanks and praise, because You have given me wisdom and power. And now You have made known to me what we have requested, for You have made known to us the dream of the king.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore Daniel went to Arioch, whom the king had appointed to destroy the wise men of Babylon, and said to him, “Do not execute the wise men of Babylon! Bring me before the king, and I will give him the interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.25', 'BSB', 'Arioch hastily brought Daniel before the king and said to him, “I have found a man among the exiles from Judah who will tell the king the interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.26', 'BSB', 'The king responded to Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, “Are you able to tell me what I saw in the dream, as well as its interpretation?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.27', 'BSB', 'Daniel answered the king, “No wise man, enchanter, medium, or magician can explain to the king the mystery of which he inquires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.28', 'BSB', 'But there is a God in heaven who reveals mysteries, and He has made known to King Nebuchadnezzar what will happen in the latter days. Your dream and the visions that came into your mind as you lay on your bed were these:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.29', 'BSB', 'As you lay on your bed, O king, your thoughts turned to the future, and the Revealer of Mysteries made known to you what will happen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.30', 'BSB', 'And to me this mystery has been revealed, not because I have more wisdom than any man alive, but in order that the interpretation might be made known to the king, and that you may understand the thoughts of your mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.31', 'BSB', 'As you, O king, were watching, a great statue appeared. A great and dazzling statue stood before you, and its form was awesome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.32', 'BSB', 'The head of the statue was pure gold, its chest and arms were silver, its belly and thighs were bronze,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.33', 'BSB', 'its legs were iron, and its feet were part iron and part clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.34', 'BSB', 'As you watched, a stone was cut out, but not by human hands. It struck the statue on its feet of iron and clay, and crushed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.35', 'BSB', 'Then the iron, clay, bronze, silver, and gold were shattered and became like chaff on the threshing floor in summer. The wind carried them away, and not a trace of them could be found. But the stone that had struck the statue became a great mountain and filled the whole earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.36', 'BSB', 'This was the dream; now we will tell the king its interpretation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.37', 'BSB', 'You, O king, are the king of kings, to whom the God of heaven has given sovereignty, power, strength, and glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.38', 'BSB', 'Wherever the sons of men or beasts of the field or birds of the air dwell, He has given them into your hand and has made you ruler over them all. You are that head of gold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.39', 'BSB', 'But after you, there will arise another kingdom, inferior to yours. Next, a third kingdom, one of bronze, will rule the whole earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.40', 'BSB', 'Finally, there will be a fourth kingdom as strong as iron; for iron shatters and crushes all things, and like iron that crushes all things, it will shatter and crush all the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.41', 'BSB', 'And just as you saw that the feet and toes were made partly of fired clay and partly of iron, so this will be a divided kingdom, yet some of the strength of iron will be in it—just as you saw the iron mixed with clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.42', 'BSB', 'And as the toes of the feet were partly iron and partly clay, so this kingdom will be partly strong and partly brittle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.43', 'BSB', 'As you saw the iron mixed with clay, so the peoples will mix with one another, but will not hold together any more than iron mixes with clay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.44', 'BSB', 'In the days of those kings, the God of heaven will set up a kingdom that will never be destroyed, nor will it be left to another people. It will shatter all these kingdoms and bring them to an end, but will itself stand forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.45', 'BSB', 'And just as you saw a stone being cut out of the mountain without human hands, and it shattered the iron, bronze, clay, silver, and gold, so the great God has told the king what will happen in the future. The dream is true, and its interpretation is trustworthy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.46', 'BSB', 'At this, King Nebuchadnezzar fell on his face, paid homage to Daniel, and ordered that an offering of incense be presented to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.47', 'BSB', 'The king said to Daniel, “Your God is truly the God of gods and Lord of kings, the Revealer of Mysteries, since you were able to reveal this mystery.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.48', 'BSB', 'Then the king promoted Daniel and gave him many generous gifts. He made him ruler over the entire province of Babylon and chief administrator over all the wise men of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.2.49', 'BSB', 'And at Daniel’s request, the king appointed Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego to manage the province of Babylon, while Daniel remained in the king’s court.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.1', 'BSB', 'King Nebuchadnezzar made a golden statue sixty cubits high and six cubits wide, and he set it up on the plain of Dura in the province of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.2', 'BSB', 'Then King Nebuchadnezzar sent word to assemble the satraps, prefects, governors, advisers, treasurers, judges, magistrates, and all the other officials of the provinces to attend the dedication of the statue he had set up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.3', 'BSB', 'So the satraps, prefects, governors, advisers, treasurers, judges, magistrates, and all the rulers of the provinces assembled for the dedication of the statue that King Nebuchadnezzar had set up, and they stood before it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.4', 'BSB', 'Then the herald loudly proclaimed, “O people of every nation and language, this is what you are commanded:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.5', 'BSB', 'As soon as you hear the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipes, and all kinds of music, you must fall down and worship the golden statue that King Nebuchadnezzar has set up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.6', 'BSB', 'And whoever does not fall down and worship will immediately be thrown into the blazing fiery furnace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as soon as all the people heard the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, and all kinds of music, the people of every nation and language would fall down and worship the golden statue that King Nebuchadnezzar had set up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.8', 'BSB', 'At this time some astrologers came forward and maliciously accused the Jews,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.9', 'BSB', 'saying to King Nebuchadnezzar, “O king, may you live forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.10', 'BSB', 'You, O king, have issued a decree that everyone who hears the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipes, and all kinds of music must fall down and worship the golden statue,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.11', 'BSB', 'and that whoever does not fall down and worship will be thrown into the blazing fiery furnace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.12', 'BSB', 'But there are some Jews you have appointed to manage the province of Babylon—Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego—who have ignored you, O king, and have refused to serve your gods or worship the golden statue you have set up.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.13', 'BSB', 'Then Nebuchadnezzar, furious with rage, summoned Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. So these men were brought before the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.14', 'BSB', 'and Nebuchadnezzar said to them, “Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, is it true that you do not serve my gods or worship the golden statue I have set up?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.15', 'BSB', 'Now, if you are ready, as soon as you hear the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipes, and all kinds of music, you must fall down and worship the statue I have made. But if you refuse to worship, you will be thrown at once into the blazing fiery furnace. Then what god will be able to deliver you from my hands?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.16', 'BSB', 'Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego replied to the king, “O Nebuchadnezzar, we have no need to answer you in this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.17', 'BSB', 'If the God whom we serve exists, then He is able to deliver us from the blazing fiery furnace and from your hand, O king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.18', 'BSB', 'But even if He does not, let it be known to you, O king, that we will not serve your gods or worship the golden statue you have set up.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.19', 'BSB', 'At this, Nebuchadnezzar was filled with rage, and the expression on his face changed toward Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. He gave orders to heat the furnace seven times hotter than usual,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.20', 'BSB', 'and he commanded some mighty men of valor in his army to tie up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego and throw them into the blazing fiery furnace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.21', 'BSB', 'So they were tied up, wearing robes, trousers, turbans, and other clothes, and they were thrown into the blazing fiery furnace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.22', 'BSB', 'The king’s command was so urgent and the furnace so hot that the fiery flames killed the men who carried up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.23', 'BSB', 'And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, firmly bound, fell into the blazing fiery furnace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.24', 'BSB', 'Suddenly King Nebuchadnezzar jumped up in amazement and asked his advisers, “Did we not throw three men, firmly bound, into the fire?” “Certainly, O king,” they replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.25', 'BSB', '“Look!” he exclaimed. “I see four men, unbound and unharmed, walking around in the fire—and the fourth looks like a son of the gods!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.26', 'BSB', 'Then Nebuchadnezzar approached the door of the blazing fiery furnace and called out, “Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, servants of the Most High God, come out!” So Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego came out of the fire,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.27', 'BSB', 'and when the satraps, prefects, governors, and royal advisers had gathered around, they saw that the fire had no effect on the bodies of these men. Not a hair of their heads was singed, their robes were unaffected, and there was no smell of fire on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.28', 'BSB', 'Nebuchadnezzar declared, “Blessed be the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, who has sent His angel and delivered His servants who trusted in Him. They violated the king’s command and risked their lives rather than serve or worship any god except their own God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.29', 'BSB', 'Therefore I decree that the people of any nation or language who say anything offensive against the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego will be cut into pieces and their houses reduced to rubble. For there is no other god who can deliver in this way.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.3.30', 'BSB', 'Then the king promoted Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego in the province of Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.1', 'BSB', 'King Nebuchadnezzar, To the people of every nation and language who dwell in all the earth: May your prosperity be multiplied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.2', 'BSB', 'I am pleased to declare the signs and wonders that the Most High God has performed for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.3', 'BSB', 'How great are His signs, how mighty His wonders! His kingdom is an eternal kingdom; His dominion endures from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.4', 'BSB', 'I, Nebuchadnezzar, was at ease in my house and flourishing in my palace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.5', 'BSB', 'I had a dream, and it frightened me; while in my bed, the images and visions in my mind alarmed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.6', 'BSB', 'So I issued a decree that all the wise men of Babylon be brought before me to interpret the dream for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.7', 'BSB', 'When the magicians, enchanters, astrologers, and diviners came in, I told them the dream, and they could not interpret it for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.8', 'BSB', 'But at last, into my presence came Daniel (whose name is Belteshazzar after the name of my god, and in whom is the spirit of the holy gods). And I told him the dream:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.9', 'BSB', '“O Belteshazzar, chief of the magicians, I know that the spirit of the holy gods is in you and that no mystery baffles you. So explain to me the visions I saw in my dream, and their interpretation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.10', 'BSB', 'In these visions of my mind as I was lying in bed, I saw this come to pass: There was a tree in the midst of the land, and its height was great.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.11', 'BSB', 'The tree grew large and strong; its top reached the sky, and it was visible to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.12', 'BSB', 'Its leaves were beautiful, its fruit was abundant, and upon it was food for all. Under it the beasts of the field found shelter, in its branches the birds of the air nested, and from it every creature was fed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.13', 'BSB', 'As I lay on my bed, I also saw in the visions of my mind a watcher, a holy one, coming down from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.14', 'BSB', 'He called out in a loud voice: ‘Cut down the tree and chop off its branches; strip off its leaves and scatter its fruit. Let the beasts flee from under it, and the birds from its branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.15', 'BSB', 'But leave the stump with its roots in the ground, and a band of iron and bronze around it, in the tender grass of the field. Let him be drenched with the dew of heaven and graze with the beasts on the grass of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.16', 'BSB', 'Let his mind be changed from that of a man, and let him be given the mind of a beast till seven times pass him by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.17', 'BSB', 'This decision is the decree of the watchers, the verdict declared by the holy ones, so that the living will know that the Most High rules over the kingdom of mankind and gives it to whom He wishes, setting over it the lowliest of men.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.18', 'BSB', 'This is the dream that I, King Nebuchadnezzar, saw. Now, Belteshazzar, tell me the interpretation, because none of the wise men of my kingdom can interpret it for me. But you are able, because the spirit of the holy gods is in you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.19', 'BSB', 'For a time, Daniel, who was also known as Belteshazzar, was perplexed, and his thoughts alarmed him. So the king said, “Belteshazzar, do not let the dream or its interpretation alarm you.” “My lord,” replied Belteshazzar, “may the dream apply to those who hate you, and its interpretation to your enemies!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.20', 'BSB', 'The tree you saw that grew large and strong, whose top reached the sky and was visible to all the earth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.21', 'BSB', 'whose foliage was beautiful and whose fruit was abundant, providing food for all, under which the beasts of the field lived, and in whose branches the birds of the air nested—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.22', 'BSB', 'you, O king, are that tree! For you have become great and strong; your greatness has grown to reach the sky, and your dominion extends to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.23', 'BSB', 'And you, O king, saw a watcher, a holy one, coming down from heaven and saying: ‘Cut down the tree and destroy it, but leave the stump with its roots in the ground, and a band of iron and bronze around it, in the tender grass of the field. Let him be drenched with the dew of heaven, and graze with the beasts of the field till seven times pass him by.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.24', 'BSB', 'This is the interpretation, O king, and this is the decree that the Most High has issued against my lord the king:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.25', 'BSB', 'You will be driven away from mankind, and your dwelling will be with the beasts of the field. You will feed on grass like an ox and be drenched with the dew of heaven, and seven times shall pass you by, until you acknowledge that the Most High rules over the kingdom of mankind and gives it to whom He wishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.26', 'BSB', 'As for the command to leave the stump of the tree with its roots, your kingdom will be restored to you as soon as you acknowledge that Heaven rules.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore, may my advice be pleasing to you, O king. Break away from your sins by doing what is right, and from your iniquities by showing mercy to the oppressed. Perhaps there will be an extension of your prosperity.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.28', 'BSB', 'All this happened to King Nebuchadnezzar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.29', 'BSB', 'Twelve months later, as he was walking on the roof of the royal palace of Babylon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.30', 'BSB', 'the king exclaimed, “Is this not Babylon the Great, which I myself have built by the might of my power as a royal residence and for the glory of my majesty?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.31', 'BSB', 'While the words were still in the king’s mouth, a voice came from heaven: “It is decreed to you, King Nebuchadnezzar, that the kingdom has departed from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.32', 'BSB', 'You will be driven away from mankind to live with the beasts of the field, and you will feed on grass like an ox. And seven times will pass you by, until you acknowledge that the Most High rules over the kingdom of mankind and gives it to whom He wishes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.33', 'BSB', 'At that moment the sentence against Nebuchadnezzar was fulfilled. He was driven away from mankind. He ate grass like an ox, and his body was drenched with the dew of heaven, until his hair grew like the feathers of an eagle and his nails like the claws of a bird.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.34', 'BSB', 'But at the end of those days I, Nebuchadnezzar, looked up to heaven, and my sanity was restored to me. Then I praised the Most High, and I honored and glorified Him who lives forever: “For His dominion is an everlasting dominion, and His kingdom endures from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.35', 'BSB', 'All the peoples of the earth are counted as nothing, and He does as He pleases with the army of heaven and the peoples of the earth. There is no one who can restrain His hand or say to Him, ‘What have You done?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.36', 'BSB', 'At the same time my sanity was restored, my honor and splendor returned to me for the glory of my kingdom. My advisers and nobles sought me out, and I was restored to my throne, and surpassing greatness was added to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.4.37', 'BSB', 'Now I, Nebuchadnezzar, praise and exalt and glorify the King of heaven, for all His works are true and all His ways are just. And He is able to humble those who walk in pride.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.1', 'BSB', 'Later, King Belshazzar held a great feast for a thousand of his nobles, and he drank wine with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.2', 'BSB', 'Under the influence of the wine, Belshazzar gave orders to bring in the gold and silver vessels that Nebuchadnezzar his father had taken from the temple in Jerusalem, so that the king could drink from them, along with his nobles, his wives, and his concubines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.3', 'BSB', 'Thus they brought in the gold vessels that had been taken from the temple, the house of God in Jerusalem, and the king drank from them, along with his nobles, his wives, and his concubines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.4', 'BSB', 'As they drank the wine, they praised their gods of gold and silver, bronze and iron, wood and stone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.5', 'BSB', 'At that moment the fingers of a human hand appeared and wrote on the plaster of the wall, near the lampstand in the royal palace. As the king watched the hand that was writing,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.6', 'BSB', 'his face grew pale and his thoughts so alarmed him that his hips gave way and his knees knocked together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.7', 'BSB', 'The king called out for the enchanters, astrologers, and diviners to be brought in, and he said to these wise men of Babylon, “Whoever reads this inscription and tells me its interpretation will be clothed in purple and have a gold chain placed around his neck, and he will be made the third highest ruler in the kingdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.8', 'BSB', 'So all the king’s wise men came in, but they could not read the inscription or interpret it for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.9', 'BSB', 'Then King Belshazzar became even more terrified, his face grew even more pale, and his nobles were bewildered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.10', 'BSB', 'Hearing the outcry of the king and his nobles, the queen entered the banquet hall. “O king, may you live forever!” she said. “Do not let your thoughts terrify you, or your face grow pale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.11', 'BSB', 'There is a man in your kingdom who has the spirit of the holy gods in him. In the days of your father he was found to have insight, intelligence, and wisdom like that of the gods. Your father, King Nebuchadnezzar, appointed him chief of the magicians, enchanters, astrologers, and diviners. Your own father, the king,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.12', 'BSB', 'did this because Daniel, the one he named Belteshazzar, was found to have an extraordinary spirit, as well as knowledge, understanding, and the ability to interpret dreams, explain riddles, and solve difficult problems. Summon Daniel, therefore, and he will give you the interpretation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.13', 'BSB', 'So Daniel was brought before the king, who asked him, “Are you Daniel, one of the exiles my father the king brought from Judah?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.14', 'BSB', 'I have heard that the spirit of the gods is in you, and that you have insight, intelligence, and extraordinary wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.15', 'BSB', 'Now the wise men and enchanters were brought before me to read this inscription and interpret it for me, but they could not give its interpretation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.16', 'BSB', 'But I have heard about you, that you are able to give interpretations and solve difficult problems. Therefore, if you can read this inscription and give me its interpretation, you will be clothed in purple and have a gold chain placed around your neck, and you will be made the third highest ruler in the kingdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.17', 'BSB', 'In response, Daniel said to the king, “You may keep your gifts for yourself and give your rewards to someone else. Nevertheless, I will read the inscription for the king and interpret it for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.18', 'BSB', 'As for you, O king, the Most High God gave your father Nebuchadnezzar sovereignty and greatness, glory and honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.19', 'BSB', 'Because of the greatness that He bestowed on him, the people of every nation and language trembled in fear before him. He killed whom he wished and kept alive whom he wished; he exalted whom he wished and humbled whom he wished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.20', 'BSB', 'But when his heart became arrogant and his spirit was hardened with pride, he was deposed from his royal throne, and his glory was taken from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.21', 'BSB', 'He was driven away from mankind, and his mind was like that of a beast. He lived with the wild donkeys and ate grass like an ox, and his body was drenched with the dew of heaven until he acknowledged that the Most High God rules over the kingdom of mankind, setting over it whom He wishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.22', 'BSB', 'But you his son, O Belshazzar, have not humbled your heart, even though you knew all this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.23', 'BSB', 'Instead, you have exalted yourself against the Lord of heaven. The vessels from His house were brought to you, and as you drank wine from them with your nobles, wives, and concubines, you praised your gods of silver and gold, bronze and iron, wood and stone, which cannot see or hear or understand. But you have failed to glorify the God who holds in His hand your very breath and all your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore He sent the hand that wrote the inscription.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.25', 'BSB', 'Now this is the inscription that was written: MENE, MENE, TEKEL, PARSIN.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.26', 'BSB', 'And this is the interpretation of the message: MENE means that God has numbered the days of your reign and brought it to an end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.27', 'BSB', 'TEKEL means that you have been weighed on the scales and found deficient.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.28', 'BSB', 'PERES means that your kingdom has been divided and given over to the Medes and Persians.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.29', 'BSB', 'Then Belshazzar gave the command, and they clothed Daniel in purple, placed a gold chain around his neck, and proclaimed him the third highest ruler in the kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.30', 'BSB', 'That very night Belshazzar king of the Chaldeans was slain,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.5.31', 'BSB', 'and Darius the Mede received the kingdom at the age of sixty-two.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.1', 'BSB', 'Now it pleased Darius to appoint 120 satraps to rule throughout the kingdom,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.2', 'BSB', 'and over them three administrators, including Daniel, to whom these satraps were accountable so that the king would not suffer loss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.3', 'BSB', 'Soon, by his extraordinary spirit, Daniel distinguished himself among the administrators and satraps. So the king planned to set him over the whole kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.4', 'BSB', 'Thus the administrators and satraps sought a charge against Daniel concerning the kingdom, but they could find no charge or corruption, because he was trustworthy, and no negligence or corruption was found in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.5', 'BSB', 'Finally these men said, “We will never find any charge against this Daniel, unless we find something against him concerning the law of his God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.6', 'BSB', 'So the administrators and satraps went together to the king and said, “O King Darius, may you live forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.7', 'BSB', 'All the royal administrators, prefects, satraps, advisers, and governors have agreed that the king should establish an ordinance and enforce a decree that for thirty days anyone who petitions any god or man except you, O king, will be thrown into the den of lions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore, O king, establish the decree and sign the document so that it cannot be changed—in accordance with the law of the Medes and Persians, which cannot be repealed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore King Darius signed the written decree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.10', 'BSB', 'Now when Daniel learned that the document had been signed, he went into his house, where the windows of his upper room opened toward Jerusalem, and three times a day he got down on his knees, prayed, and gave thanks to his God, just as he had done before.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.11', 'BSB', 'Then these men went as a group and found Daniel petitioning and imploring his God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.12', 'BSB', 'So they approached the king and asked about his royal decree: “Did you not sign a decree that for thirty days any man who petitions any god or man except you, O king, will be thrown into the den of lions?” The king replied, “According to the law of the Medes and Persians the order stands, and it cannot be repealed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.13', 'BSB', 'Then they told the king, “Daniel, one of the exiles from Judah, shows no regard for you, O king, or for the decree that you have signed. He still makes his petition three times a day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.14', 'BSB', 'As soon as the king heard this, he was deeply distressed and set his mind on delivering Daniel, and he labored until sundown to rescue him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.15', 'BSB', 'Then the men approached the king together and said to him, “Remember, O king, that by the law of the Medes and Persians no decree or ordinance established by the king can be changed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.16', 'BSB', 'So the king gave the order, and they brought Daniel and threw him into the den of lions. The king said to Daniel, “May your God, whom you serve continually, deliver you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.17', 'BSB', 'A stone was brought and placed over the mouth of the den, and the king sealed it with his own signet ring and with the rings of his nobles, so that nothing concerning Daniel could be changed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.18', 'BSB', 'Then the king went to his palace and spent the night fasting. No entertainment was brought before him, and sleep fled from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.19', 'BSB', 'At the first light of dawn, the king got up and hurried to the den of lions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.20', 'BSB', 'When he reached the den, he cried out in a voice of anguish, “O Daniel, servant of the living God, has your God, whom you serve continually, been able to deliver you from the lions?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.21', 'BSB', 'Then Daniel replied, “O king, may you live forever!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.22', 'BSB', 'My God sent His angel and shut the mouths of the lions. They have not hurt me, for I was found innocent in His sight, and I have done no wrong against you, O king.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.23', 'BSB', 'The king was overjoyed and gave orders to lift Daniel out of the den, and when Daniel was lifted out of the den, no wounds whatsoever were found on him, because he had trusted in his God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.24', 'BSB', 'At the command of the king, the men who had falsely accused Daniel were brought and thrown into the den of lions—they and their children and wives. And before they had reached the bottom of the den, the lions overpowered them and crushed all their bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.25', 'BSB', 'Then King Darius wrote to the people of every nation and language throughout the land: “May your prosperity abound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.26', 'BSB', 'I hereby decree that in every part of my kingdom, men are to tremble in fear before the God of Daniel: For He is the living God, and He endures forever; His kingdom will never be destroyed, and His dominion will never end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.27', 'BSB', 'He delivers and rescues; He performs signs and wonders in the heavens and on the earth, for He has rescued Daniel from the power of the lions.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.6.28', 'BSB', 'So Daniel prospered during the reign of Darius and the reign of Cyrus the Persian.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.1', 'BSB', 'In the first year of the reign of Belshazzar over Babylon, Daniel had a dream, and visions passed through his mind as he lay on his bed. He wrote down the dream, and this is the summary of his account.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.2', 'BSB', 'Daniel declared: “In my vision in the night I looked, and suddenly the four winds of heaven were churning up the great sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.3', 'BSB', 'Then four great beasts came up out of the sea, each one different from the others:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.4', 'BSB', 'The first beast was like a lion, and it had the wings of an eagle. I watched until its wings were torn off and it was lifted up from the ground and made to stand on two feet like a man, and given the mind of a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.5', 'BSB', 'Suddenly another beast appeared, which looked like a bear. It was raised up on one of its sides, and it had three ribs in its mouth between its teeth. So it was told, ‘Get up and gorge yourself on flesh!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.6', 'BSB', 'Next, as I watched, another beast appeared. It was like a leopard, and on its back it had four wings like those of a bird. The beast also had four heads, and it was given authority to rule.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.7', 'BSB', 'After this, as I watched in my vision in the night, suddenly a fourth beast appeared, and it was terrifying—dreadful and extremely strong—with large iron teeth. It devoured and crushed; then it trampled underfoot whatever was left. It was different from all the beasts before it, and it had ten horns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.8', 'BSB', 'While I was contemplating the horns, suddenly another horn, a little one, came up among them, and three of the first horns were uprooted before it. This horn had eyes like those of a man and a mouth that spoke words of arrogance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.9', 'BSB', 'As I continued to watch, thrones were set in place, and the Ancient of Days took His seat. His clothing was white as snow, and the hair of His head was like pure wool. His throne was flaming with fire, and its wheels were all ablaze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.10', 'BSB', 'A river of fire was flowing, coming out from His presence. Thousands upon thousands attended Him, and myriads upon myriads stood before Him. The court was convened, and the books were opened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.11', 'BSB', 'Then I kept watching because of the arrogant words the horn was speaking. As I continued to watch, the beast was slain, and its body was destroyed and thrown into the blazing fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.12', 'BSB', 'As for the rest of the beasts, their dominion was removed, but they were granted an extension of life for a season and a time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.13', 'BSB', 'In my vision in the night I continued to watch, and I saw One like the Son of Man coming with the clouds of heaven. He approached the Ancient of Days and was led into His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.14', 'BSB', 'And He was given dominion, glory, and kingship, that the people of every nation and language should serve Him. His dominion is an everlasting dominion that will not pass away, and His kingdom is one that will never be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.15', 'BSB', 'I, Daniel, was grieved in my spirit, and the visions in my mind alarmed me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.16', 'BSB', 'I approached one of those who were standing there, and I asked him the true meaning of all this. So he told me the interpretation of these things:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.17', 'BSB', '‘These four great beasts are four kings who will arise from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.18', 'BSB', 'But the saints of the Most High will receive the kingdom and possess it forever—yes, forever and ever.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.19', 'BSB', 'Then I wanted to know the true meaning of the fourth beast, which was different from all the others—extremely terrifying—devouring and crushing with iron teeth and bronze claws, then trampling underfoot whatever was left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.20', 'BSB', 'I also wanted to know about the ten horns on its head and the other horn that came up, before which three of them fell—the horn whose appearance was more imposing than the others, with eyes and with a mouth that spoke words of arrogance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.21', 'BSB', 'As I watched, this horn was waging war against the saints and prevailing against them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.22', 'BSB', 'until the Ancient of Days arrived and pronounced judgment in favor of the saints of the Most High, and the time came for them to possess the kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.23', 'BSB', 'This is what he said: ‘The fourth beast is a fourth kingdom that will appear on the earth, different from all the other kingdoms, and it will devour the whole earth, trample it down, and crush it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.24', 'BSB', 'And the ten horns are ten kings who will rise from this kingdom. After them another king, different from the earlier ones, will rise and subdue three kings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.25', 'BSB', 'He will speak out against the Most High and oppress the saints of the Most High, intending to change the appointed times and laws; and the saints will be given into his hand for a time, and times, and half a time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.26', 'BSB', 'But the court will convene, and his dominion will be taken away and completely destroyed forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.27', 'BSB', 'Then the sovereignty, dominion, and greatness of the kingdoms under all of heaven will be given to the people, the saints of the Most High. His kingdom will be an everlasting kingdom, and all rulers will serve and obey Him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.7.28', 'BSB', 'Thus ends the matter. As for me, Daniel, my thoughts troubled me greatly, and my face turned pale. But I kept the matter to myself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.1', 'BSB', 'In the third year of the reign of King Belshazzar, a vision appeared to me, Daniel, subsequent to the one that had appeared to me earlier.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.2', 'BSB', 'And in the vision I saw myself in the citadel of Susa, in the province of Elam. I saw in the vision that I was beside the Ulai Canal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.3', 'BSB', 'Then I lifted up my eyes and saw a ram with two horns standing beside the canal. The horns were long, but one was longer than the other, and the longer one grew up later.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.4', 'BSB', 'I saw the ram charging toward the west and the north and the south. No animal could stand against him, and there was no deliverance from his power. He did as he pleased and became great.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.5', 'BSB', 'As I was contemplating all this, suddenly a goat with a prominent horn between his eyes came out of the west, crossing the surface of the entire earth without touching the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.6', 'BSB', 'He came toward the two-horned ram I had seen standing beside the canal and rushed at him with furious power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.7', 'BSB', 'I saw him approach the ram in a rage against him, and he struck the ram and shattered his two horns. The ram was powerless to stand against him, and the goat threw him to the ground and trampled him, and no one could deliver the ram from his power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.8', 'BSB', 'Thus the goat became very great, but at the height of his power, his large horn was broken off, and four prominent horns came up in its place, pointing toward the four winds of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.9', 'BSB', 'From one of these horns a little horn emerged and grew extensively toward the south and the east and toward the Beautiful Land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.10', 'BSB', 'It grew as high as the host of heaven, and it cast down some of the host and some of the stars to the earth, and trampled them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.11', 'BSB', 'It magnified itself, even to the Prince of the host; it removed His daily sacrifice and overthrew the place of His sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.12', 'BSB', 'And in the rebellion, the host and the daily sacrifice were given over to the horn, and it flung truth to the ground and prospered in whatever it did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.13', 'BSB', 'Then I heard a holy one speaking, and another holy one said to him, “How long until the fulfillment of the vision of the daily sacrifice, the rebellion that causes desolation, and the surrender of the sanctuary and of the host to be trampled?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.14', 'BSB', 'He said to me, “It will take 2,300 evenings and mornings; then the sanctuary will be properly restored.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.15', 'BSB', 'While I, Daniel, was watching the vision and trying to understand it, there stood before me one having the appearance of a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.16', 'BSB', 'And I heard the voice of a man calling from between the banks of the Ulai: “Gabriel, explain the vision to this man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.17', 'BSB', 'As he came near to where I stood, I was terrified and fell facedown. “Son of man,” he said to me, “understand that the vision concerns the time of the end.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.18', 'BSB', 'While he was speaking with me, I fell into a deep sleep, with my face to the ground. Then he touched me, helped me to my feet,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.19', 'BSB', 'and said, “Behold, I will make known to you what will happen in the latter time of wrath, because it concerns the appointed time of the end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.20', 'BSB', 'The two-horned ram that you saw represents the kings of Media and Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.21', 'BSB', 'The shaggy goat represents the king of Greece, and the large horn between his eyes is the first king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.22', 'BSB', 'The four horns that replaced the broken one represent four kingdoms that will rise from that nation, but will not have the same power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.23', 'BSB', 'In the latter part of their reign, when the rebellion has reached its full measure, an insolent king, skilled in intrigue, will come to the throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.24', 'BSB', 'His power will be great, but it will not be his own. He will cause terrible destruction and succeed in whatever he does. He will destroy the mighty men along with the holy people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.25', 'BSB', 'Through his craft and by his hand, he will cause deceit to prosper, and in his own mind he will make himself great. In a time of peace he will destroy many, and he will even stand against the Prince of princes. Yet he will be broken off, but not by human hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.26', 'BSB', 'The vision of the evenings and the mornings that has been spoken is true. Now you must seal up the vision, for it concerns the distant future.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.8.27', 'BSB', 'I, Daniel, was exhausted and lay ill for days. Then I got up and went about the king’s business. I was confounded by the vision; it was beyond understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.1', 'BSB', 'In the first year of Darius son of Xerxes, a Mede by descent, who was made ruler over the kingdom of the Chaldeans —', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.2', 'BSB', 'in the first year of his reign, I, Daniel, understood from the sacred books, according to the word of the LORD to Jeremiah the prophet, that the desolation of Jerusalem would last seventy years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.3', 'BSB', 'So I turned my attention to the Lord God to seek Him by prayer and petition, with fasting, sackcloth, and ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.4', 'BSB', 'And I prayed to the LORD my God and confessed, “O, Lord, the great and awesome God, who keeps His covenant of loving devotion to those who love Him and keep His commandments,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.5', 'BSB', 'we have sinned and done wrong. We have acted wickedly and rebelled. We have turned away from Your commandments and ordinances.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.6', 'BSB', 'We have not listened to Your servants the prophets, who spoke in Your name to our kings, leaders, and fathers, and to all the people of the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.7', 'BSB', 'To You, O Lord, belongs righteousness, but this day we are covered with shame—the men of Judah, the people of Jerusalem, and all Israel near and far, in all the countries to which You have driven us because of our unfaithfulness to You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.8', 'BSB', 'O LORD, we are covered with shame—our kings, our leaders, and our fathers—because we have sinned against You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.9', 'BSB', 'To the Lord our God belong compassion and forgiveness, even though we have rebelled against Him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.10', 'BSB', 'and have not obeyed the voice of the LORD our God to walk in His laws, which He set before us through His servants the prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.11', 'BSB', 'All Israel has transgressed Your law and turned away, refusing to obey Your voice; so the oath and the curse written in the Law of Moses the servant of God has been poured out on us, because we have sinned against You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.12', 'BSB', 'You have carried out the words spoken against us and against our rulers by bringing upon us a great disaster. For under all of heaven, nothing has ever been done like what has been done to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.13', 'BSB', 'Just as it is written in the Law of Moses, all this disaster has come upon us, yet we have not sought the favor of the LORD our God by turning from our iniquities and giving attention to Your truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore the LORD has kept the calamity in store and brought it upon us. For the LORD our God is righteous in all He does; yet we have not obeyed His voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.15', 'BSB', 'Now, O Lord our God, who brought Your people out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and who made for Yourself a name renowned to this day, we have sinned; we have acted wickedly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.16', 'BSB', 'O Lord, in keeping with all Your righteous acts, I pray that Your anger and wrath may turn away from Your city Jerusalem, Your holy mountain; for because of our sins and the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and Your people are a reproach to all around us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.17', 'BSB', 'So now, our God, hear the prayers and petitions of Your servant. For Your sake, O Lord, cause Your face to shine upon Your desolate sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.18', 'BSB', 'Incline Your ear, O my God, and hear; open Your eyes and see the desolation of the city that bears Your name. For we are not presenting our petitions before You because of our righteous acts, but because of Your great compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.19', 'BSB', 'O Lord, listen! O Lord, forgive! O Lord, hear and act! For Your sake, O my God, do not delay, because Your city and Your people bear Your name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.20', 'BSB', 'While I was speaking, praying, confessing my sin and that of my people Israel, and presenting my petition before the LORD my God concerning His holy mountain—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.21', 'BSB', 'while I was still praying, Gabriel, the man I had seen in the earlier vision, came to me in swift flight about the time of the evening sacrifice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.22', 'BSB', 'He instructed me and spoke with me, saying: “O Daniel, I have come now to give you insight and understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.23', 'BSB', 'At the beginning of your petitions, an answer went out, and I have come to tell you, for you are highly precious. So consider the message and understand the vision:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.24', 'BSB', 'Seventy weeks are decreed for your people and your holy city to stop their transgression, to put an end to sin, to make atonement for iniquity, to bring in everlasting righteousness, to seal up vision and prophecy, and to anoint the Most Holy Place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.25', 'BSB', 'Know and understand this: From the issuance of the decree to restore and rebuild Jerusalem, until the Messiah, the Prince, there will be seven weeks and sixty-two weeks. It will be rebuilt with streets and a trench, but in times of distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.26', 'BSB', 'Then after the sixty-two weeks the Messiah will be cut off and will have nothing. Then the people of the prince who is to come will destroy the city and the sanctuary. The end will come like a flood, and until the end there will be war; desolations have been decreed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.9.27', 'BSB', 'And he will confirm a covenant with many for one week, but in the middle of the week he will put an end to sacrifice and offering. And on the wing of the temple will come the abomination that causes desolation, until the decreed destruction is poured out upon him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.1', 'BSB', 'In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia, a message was revealed to Daniel, who was called Belteshazzar. The message was true, and it concerned a great conflict. And the understanding of the message was given to him in a vision.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.2', 'BSB', 'In those days I, Daniel, was mourning for three full weeks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.3', 'BSB', 'I ate no rich food, no meat or wine entered my mouth, and I did not anoint myself with oil until the three weeks were completed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.4', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-fourth day of the first month, as I was standing on the bank of the great river, the Tigris,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.5', 'BSB', 'I lifted up my eyes, and behold, there was a certain man dressed in linen, with a belt of fine gold from Uphaz around his waist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.6', 'BSB', 'His body was like beryl, his face like the brilliance of lightning, his eyes like flaming torches, his arms and legs like the gleam of polished bronze, and his voice like the sound of a multitude.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.7', 'BSB', 'Only I, Daniel, saw the vision; the men with me did not see it, but a great terror fell upon them, and they ran and hid themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.8', 'BSB', 'So I was left alone, gazing at this great vision. No strength remained in me; my face grew deathly pale, and I was powerless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.9', 'BSB', 'I heard the sound of his words, and as I listened, I fell into a deep sleep, with my face to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.10', 'BSB', 'Suddenly, a hand touched me and set me trembling on my hands and knees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.11', 'BSB', 'He said to me, “Daniel, you are a man who is highly precious. Consider carefully the words that I am about to say to you. Stand up, for I have now been sent to you.” And when he had said this to me, I stood up trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.12', 'BSB', '“Do not be afraid, Daniel,” he said, “for from the first day that you purposed to understand and to humble yourself before your God, your words were heard, and I have come in response to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.13', 'BSB', 'However, the prince of the kingdom of Persia opposed me for twenty-one days. Then Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me, for I had been left there with the kings of Persia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.14', 'BSB', 'Now I have come to explain to you what will happen to your people in the latter days, for the vision concerns those days.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.15', 'BSB', 'While he was speaking these words to me, I set my face toward the ground and became speechless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.16', 'BSB', 'And suddenly one with the likeness of a man touched my lips, and I opened my mouth and said to the one standing before me, “My lord, because of the vision, I am overcome with anguish, and I have no strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.17', 'BSB', 'How can I, your servant, speak with you, my lord? Now I have no strength, nor is any breath left in me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.18', 'BSB', 'Again the one with the likeness of a man touched me and strengthened me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.19', 'BSB', '“Do not be afraid, you who are highly precious,” he said. “Peace be with you! Be strong now; be very strong!” As he spoke with me, I was strengthened and said, “Speak, my lord, for you have strengthened me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.20', 'BSB', '“Do you know why I have come to you?” he said. “I must return at once to fight against the prince of Persia, and when I have gone forth, behold, the prince of Greece will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.10.21', 'BSB', 'But first I will tell you what is inscribed in the Book of Truth. Yet no one has the courage to support me against these, except Michael your prince.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.1', 'BSB', '“And I, in the first year of Darius the Mede, stood up to strengthen and protect him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.2', 'BSB', 'Now then, I will tell you the truth: Three more kings will arise in Persia, and then a fourth, who will be far richer than all the others. By the power of his wealth, he will stir up everyone against the kingdom of Greece.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.3', 'BSB', 'Then a mighty king will arise, who will rule with great authority and do as he pleases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.4', 'BSB', 'But as soon as he is established, his kingdom will be broken up and parceled out toward the four winds of heaven. It will not go to his descendants, nor will it have the authority with which he ruled, because his kingdom will be uprooted and given to others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.5', 'BSB', 'The king of the South will grow strong, but one of his commanders will grow even stronger and will rule his own kingdom with great authority.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.6', 'BSB', 'After some years they will form an alliance, and the daughter of the king of the South will go to the king of the North to seal the agreement. But his daughter will not retain her position of power, nor will his strength endure. At that time she will be given up, along with her royal escort and her father and the one who supported her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.7', 'BSB', 'But one from her family line will rise up in his place, come against the army of the king of the North, and enter his fortress, fighting and prevailing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.8', 'BSB', 'He will take even their gods captive to Egypt, with their metal images and their precious vessels of silver and gold. For some years he will stay away from the king of the North,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.9', 'BSB', 'who will invade the realm of the king of the South and then return to his own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.10', 'BSB', 'But his sons will stir up strife and assemble a great army, which will advance forcefully, sweeping through like a flood, and will again carry the battle as far as his fortress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.11', 'BSB', 'In a rage, the king of the South will march out to fight the king of the North, who will raise a large army, but it will be delivered into the hand of his enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.12', 'BSB', 'When the army is carried off, the king of the South will be proud in heart and will cast down tens of thousands, but he will not triumph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.13', 'BSB', 'For the king of the North will raise another army, larger than the first, and after some years he will advance with a great army and many supplies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.14', 'BSB', 'In those times many will rise up against the king of the South. Violent ones among your own people will exalt themselves in fulfillment of the vision, but they will fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.15', 'BSB', 'Then the king of the North will come, build up a siege ramp, and capture a fortified city. The forces of the South will not stand; even their best troops will not be able to resist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.16', 'BSB', 'The invader will do as he pleases, and no one will stand against him. He will establish himself in the Beautiful Land, with destruction in his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.17', 'BSB', 'He will resolve to come with the strength of his whole kingdom, and will reach an agreement with the king of the South. He will give him a daughter in marriage in order to overthrow the kingdom, but his plan will not succeed or help him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.18', 'BSB', 'Then he will turn his face to the coastlands and capture many of them. But a commander will put an end to his reproach and will turn it back upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.19', 'BSB', 'After this, he will turn back toward the fortresses of his own land, but he will stumble and fall and be no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.20', 'BSB', 'In his place one will arise who will send out a tax collector for the glory of the kingdom; but within a few days he will be destroyed, though not in anger or in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.21', 'BSB', 'In his place a despicable person will arise; royal honors will not be given to him, but he will come in a time of peace and seize the kingdom by intrigue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.22', 'BSB', 'Then a flood of forces will be swept away before him and destroyed, along with a prince of the covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.23', 'BSB', 'After an alliance is made with him, he will act deceitfully; for he will rise to power with only a few people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.24', 'BSB', 'In a time of peace, he will invade the richest provinces and do what his fathers and forefathers never did. He will lavish plunder, loot, and wealth on his followers, and he will plot against the strongholds—but only for a time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.25', 'BSB', 'And with a large army he will stir up his power and his courage against the king of the South, who will mobilize a very large and powerful army but will not withstand the plots devised against him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.26', 'BSB', 'Those who eat from his provisions will seek to destroy him; his army will be swept away, and many will fall slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.27', 'BSB', 'And the two kings, with their hearts bent on evil, will speak lies at the same table, but to no avail, for still the end will come at the appointed time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.28', 'BSB', 'The king of the North will return to his land with great wealth, but his heart will be set against the holy covenant; so he will do damage and return to his own land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.29', 'BSB', 'At the appointed time he will invade the South again, but this time will not be like the first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.30', 'BSB', 'Ships of Kittim will come against him, and he will lose heart. Then he will turn back and rage against the holy covenant and do damage. So he will return and show favor to those who forsake the holy covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.31', 'BSB', 'His forces will rise up and desecrate the temple fortress. They will abolish the daily sacrifice and set up the abomination of desolation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.32', 'BSB', 'With flattery he will corrupt those who violate the covenant, but the people who know their God will firmly resist him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.33', 'BSB', 'Those with insight will instruct many, though for a time they will fall by sword or flame, or be captured or plundered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.34', 'BSB', 'Now when they fall, they will be granted a little help, but many will join them insincerely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.35', 'BSB', 'Some of the wise will fall, so that they may be refined, purified, and made spotless until the time of the end, for it will still come at the appointed time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.36', 'BSB', 'Then the king will do as he pleases and will exalt and magnify himself above every god, and he will speak monstrous things against the God of gods. He will be successful until the time of wrath is completed, for what has been decreed must be accomplished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.37', 'BSB', 'He will show no regard for the gods of his fathers, nor for the one desired by women, nor for any other god, because he will magnify himself above them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.38', 'BSB', 'And in their place, he will honor a god of fortresses—a god his fathers did not know—with gold, silver, precious stones, and riches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.39', 'BSB', 'He will attack the strongest fortresses with the help of a foreign god and will greatly honor those who acknowledge him, making them rulers over many and distributing the land for a price.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.40', 'BSB', 'At the time of the end, the king of the South will engage him in battle, but the king of the North will storm out against him with chariots, horsemen, and many ships, invading many countries and sweeping through them like a flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.41', 'BSB', 'He will also invade the Beautiful Land, and many countries will fall. But these will be delivered from his hand: Edom, Moab, and the leaders of the Ammonites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.42', 'BSB', 'He will extend his power over many countries, and not even the land of Egypt will escape.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.43', 'BSB', 'He will gain control of the treasures of gold and silver and over all the riches of Egypt, and the Libyans and Cushites will also submit to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.44', 'BSB', 'But news from the east and the north will alarm him, and he will go out with great fury to destroy many and devote them to destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.11.45', 'BSB', 'He will pitch his royal tents between the sea and the beautiful holy mountain, but he will meet his end with no one to help him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.1', 'BSB', '“At that time Michael, the great prince who stands watch over your people, will rise up. There will be a time of distress, the likes of which will not have occurred from the beginning of nations until that time. But at that time your people—everyone whose name is found written in the book—will be delivered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.2', 'BSB', 'And many who sleep in the dust of the earth will awake, some to everlasting life, but others to shame and everlasting contempt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.3', 'BSB', 'Then the wise will shine like the brightness of the heavens, and those who lead many to righteousness will shine like the stars forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.4', 'BSB', 'But you, Daniel, shut up these words and seal the book until the time of the end. Many will roam to and fro, and knowledge will increase.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.5', 'BSB', 'Then I, Daniel, looked and saw two others standing there, one on this bank of the river and one on the opposite bank.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.6', 'BSB', 'One of them said to the man dressed in linen, who was above the waters of the river, “How long until the fulfillment of these wonders?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.7', 'BSB', 'And the man dressed in linen, who was above the waters of the river, raised his right hand and his left hand toward heaven, and I heard him swear by Him who lives forever, saying, “It will be for a time, and times, and half a time. When the power of the holy people has finally been shattered, all these things will be completed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.8', 'BSB', 'I heard, but I did not understand. So I asked, “My lord, what will be the outcome of these things?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.9', 'BSB', '“Go on your way, Daniel,” he replied, “for the words are closed up and sealed until the time of the end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.10', 'BSB', 'Many will be purified, made spotless, and refined, but the wicked will continue to act wickedly. None of the wicked will understand, but the wise will understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.11', 'BSB', 'And from the time the daily sacrifice is abolished and the abomination of desolation set up, there will be 1,290 days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.12', 'BSB', 'Blessed is he who waits and reaches the end of the 1,335 days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Dan.12.13', 'BSB', 'But as for you, go on your way until the end. You will rest, and will arise to your inheritance at the end of the days.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Hosea son of Beeri in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and of Jeroboam son of Jehoash, king of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.2', 'BSB', 'When the LORD first spoke through Hosea, He told him, “Go, take a prostitute as your wife and have children of adultery, because this land is flagrantly prostituting itself by departing from the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.3', 'BSB', 'So Hosea went and married Gomer daughter of Diblaim, and she conceived and bore him a son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.4', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to Hosea, “Name him Jezreel, for soon I will bring the bloodshed of Jezreel upon the house of Jehu, and I will put an end to the kingdom of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.5', 'BSB', 'And on that day I will break the bow of Israel in the Valley of Jezreel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.6', 'BSB', 'Gomer again conceived and gave birth to a daughter, and the LORD said to Hosea, “Name her Lo-ruhamah, for I will no longer have compassion on the house of Israel, that I should ever forgive them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.7', 'BSB', 'Yet I will have compassion on the house of Judah, and I will save them—not by bow or sword or war, not by horses and cavalry, but by the LORD their God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.8', 'BSB', 'After she had weaned Lo-ruhamah, Gomer conceived and gave birth to a son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.9', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said, “Name him Lo-ammi, for you are not My people, and I am not your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.10', 'BSB', 'Yet the number of the Israelites will be like the sand of the sea, which cannot be measured or counted. And it will happen that in the very place where it was said to them, ‘You are not My people,’ they will be called ‘sons of the living God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.1.11', 'BSB', 'Then the people of Judah and of Israel will be gathered together, and they will appoint for themselves one leader, and will go up out of the land. For great will be the day of Jezreel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.1', 'BSB', '“Say of your brothers, ‘My people,’ and of your sisters, ‘My loved one.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.2', 'BSB', 'Rebuke your mother, rebuke her, for she is not My wife, and I am not her husband. Let her remove the adultery from her face and the unfaithfulness from between her breasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.3', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, I will strip her naked and expose her like the day of her birth. I will make her like a desert and turn her into a parched land, and I will let her die of thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.4', 'BSB', 'I will have no compassion on her children, because they are the children of adultery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.5', 'BSB', 'For their mother has played the harlot and has conceived them in disgrace. For she thought, ‘I will go after my lovers, who give me bread and water, wool and linen, oil and drink.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore, behold, I will hedge up her path with thorns; I will enclose her with a wall, so she cannot find her way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.7', 'BSB', 'She will pursue her lovers but not catch them; she will seek them but not find them. Then she will say, ‘I will return to my first husband, for then I was better off than now.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.8', 'BSB', 'For she does not acknowledge that it was I who gave her grain, new wine, and oil, who lavished on her silver and gold— which they crafted for Baal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will take back My grain in its time and My new wine in its season; I will take away My wool and linen, which were given to cover her nakedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.10', 'BSB', 'And then I will expose her lewdness in the sight of her lovers, and no one will deliver her out of My hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.11', 'BSB', 'I will put an end to all her exultation: her feasts, New Moons, and Sabbaths— all her appointed feasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.12', 'BSB', 'I will destroy her vines and fig trees, which she thinks are the wages paid by her lovers. So I will make them into a thicket, and the beasts of the field will devour them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.13', 'BSB', 'I will punish her for the days of the Baals when she burned incense to them, when she decked herself with rings and jewelry, and went after her lovers. But Me she forgot,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.14', 'BSB', '“Therefore, behold, I will allure her and lead her to the wilderness, and speak to her tenderly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.15', 'BSB', 'There I will give back her vineyards and make the Valley of Achor into a gateway of hope. There she will respond as she did in the days of her youth, as in the day she came up out of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.16', 'BSB', 'In that day,” declares the LORD, “you will call Me ‘my Husband,’ and no longer call Me ‘my Master.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.17', 'BSB', 'For I will remove from her lips the names of the Baals; no longer will their names be invoked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.18', 'BSB', 'On that day I will make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field and the birds of the air and the creatures that crawl on the ground. And I will abolish bow and sword and weapons of war in the land, and will make them lie down in safety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.19', 'BSB', 'So I will betroth you to Me forever; I will betroth you in righteousness and justice, in loving devotion and compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.20', 'BSB', 'And I will betroth you in faithfulness, and you will know the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.21', 'BSB', '“On that day I will respond—” declares the LORD— “I will respond to the heavens, and they will respond to the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.22', 'BSB', 'And the earth will respond to the grain, to the new wine and oil, and they will respond to Jezreel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.2.23', 'BSB', 'And I will sow her as My own in the land, and I will have compassion on ‘No Compassion.’ I will say to those called ‘Not My People,’ ‘You are My people,’ and they will say, ‘You are my God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.3.1', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD said to me, “Go show love to your wife again, though she is loved by another and is an adulteress. Love her as the LORD loves the Israelites, though they turn to other gods and offer raisin cakes to idols.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.3.2', 'BSB', 'So I bought her for fifteen shekels of silver and a homer and a lethech of barley.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.3.3', 'BSB', 'Then I said to her, “You must live with me for many days; you must not be promiscuous or belong to another, and I will do the same for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.3.4', 'BSB', 'For the Israelites must live many days without king or prince, without sacrifice or sacred pillar, and without ephod or idol.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.3.5', 'BSB', 'Afterward, the people of Israel will return and seek the LORD their God and David their king. They will come trembling to the LORD and to His goodness in the last days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.1', 'BSB', 'Hear the word of the LORD, O children of Israel, for the LORD has a case against the people of the land: “There is no truth, no loving devotion, and no knowledge of God in the land!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.2', 'BSB', 'Cursing and lying, murder and stealing, and adultery are rampant; one act of bloodshed follows another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore the land mourns, and all who dwell in it will waste away with the beasts of the field and the birds of the air; even the fish of the sea disappear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.4', 'BSB', 'But let no man contend; let no man offer reproof; for your people are like those who contend with a priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.5', 'BSB', 'You will stumble by day, and the prophet will stumble with you by night; so I will destroy your mother—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.6', 'BSB', 'My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge. Because you have rejected knowledge, I will also reject you as My priests. Since you have forgotten the law of your God, I will also forget your children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.7', 'BSB', 'The more they multiplied, the more they sinned against Me; they exchanged their Glory for a thing of disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.8', 'BSB', 'They feed on the sins of My people and set their hearts on iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.9', 'BSB', 'And it shall be like people, like priest. I will punish both of them for their ways and repay them for their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.10', 'BSB', 'They will eat but not be satisfied; they will be promiscuous but not multiply. For they have stopped obeying the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.11', 'BSB', 'Promiscuity, wine, and new wine take away understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.12', 'BSB', 'My people consult their wooden idols, and their divining rods inform them. For a spirit of prostitution leads them astray and they have played the harlot against their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.13', 'BSB', 'They sacrifice on the mountaintops and burn offerings on the hills, under oak, poplar, and terebinth, because their shade is pleasant. And so your daughters turn to prostitution and your daughters-in-law to adultery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.14', 'BSB', 'I will not punish your daughters when they prostitute themselves, nor your daughters-in-law when they commit adultery. For the men themselves go off with prostitutes and offer sacrifices with shrine prostitutes. So a people without understanding will come to ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.15', 'BSB', 'Though you prostitute yourself, O Israel, may Judah avoid such guilt! Do not journey to Gilgal, do not go up to Beth-aven, and do not swear on oath, ‘As surely as the LORD lives!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.16', 'BSB', 'For Israel is as obstinate as a stubborn heifer. Can the LORD now shepherd them like lambs in an open meadow?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.17', 'BSB', 'Ephraim is joined to idols; leave him alone!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.18', 'BSB', 'When their liquor is gone, they turn to prostitution; their rulers dearly love disgrace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.4.19', 'BSB', 'The whirlwind has wrapped them in its wings, and their sacrifices will bring them shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.1', 'BSB', '“Hear this, O priests! Take heed, O house of Israel! Give ear, O royal house! For this judgment is against you because you have been a snare at Mizpah, a net spread out on Tabor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.2', 'BSB', 'The rebels are deep in slaughter; but I will chastise them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.3', 'BSB', 'I know all about Ephraim, and Israel is not hidden from Me. For now, O Ephraim, you have turned to prostitution; Israel is defiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.4', 'BSB', 'Their deeds do not permit them to return to their God, for a spirit of prostitution is within them, and they do not know the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.5', 'BSB', 'Israel’s arrogance testifies against them; Israel and Ephraim stumble in their iniquity; even Judah stumbles with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.6', 'BSB', 'They go with their flocks and herds to seek the LORD, but they do not find Him; He has withdrawn Himself from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.7', 'BSB', 'They have been unfaithful to the LORD; for they have borne illegitimate children. Now the New Moon will devour them along with their land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.8', 'BSB', 'Blow the ram’s horn in Gibeah, the trumpet in Ramah; raise the battle cry in Beth-aven: Lead on, O Benjamin!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.9', 'BSB', 'Ephraim will be laid waste on the day of rebuke. Among the tribes of Israel I proclaim what is certain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.10', 'BSB', 'The princes of Judah are like those who move boundary stones; I will pour out My fury upon them like water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.11', 'BSB', 'Ephraim is oppressed, crushed in judgment, for he is determined to follow worthless idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.12', 'BSB', 'So I am like a moth to Ephraim, and like decay to the house of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.13', 'BSB', 'When Ephraim saw his sickness and Judah his wound, then Ephraim turned to Assyria and sent to the great king. But he cannot cure you or heal your wound.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.14', 'BSB', 'For I am like a lion to Ephraim and like a young lion to the house of Judah. I, even I, will tear them to pieces and then go away. I will carry them off where no one can rescue them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.5.15', 'BSB', 'Then I will return to My place until they admit their guilt and seek My face; in their affliction they will earnestly seek Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.1', 'BSB', 'Come, let us return to the LORD. For He has torn us to pieces, but He will heal us; He has wounded us, but He will bind up our wounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.2', 'BSB', 'After two days He will revive us; on the third day He will raise us up, that we may live in His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.3', 'BSB', 'So let us know— let us press on to know the LORD. As surely as the sun rises, He will appear; He will come to us like the rain, like the spring showers that water the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.4', 'BSB', 'What shall I do with you, O Ephraim? What shall I do with you, O Judah? For your loyalty is like a morning mist, like the early dew that vanishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore I have hewn them by the prophets; I have slain them by the words of My mouth, and My judgments go forth like lightning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.6', 'BSB', 'For I desire mercy, not sacrifice, and the knowledge of God rather than burnt offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.7', 'BSB', 'But they, like Adam, have transgressed the covenant; there they were unfaithful to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.8', 'BSB', 'Gilead is a city of evildoers, tracked with footprints of blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.9', 'BSB', 'Like raiders who lie in ambush, so does a band of priests; they murder on the way to Shechem; surely they have committed atrocities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.10', 'BSB', 'In the house of Israel I have seen a horrible thing: Ephraim practices prostitution there, and Israel is defiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.6.11', 'BSB', 'Also for you, O Judah, a harvest is appointed, when I restore My people from captivity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.1', 'BSB', 'When I heal Israel, the iniquity of Ephraim will be exposed, as well as the crimes of Samaria. For they practice deceit and thieves break in; bandits raid in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.2', 'BSB', 'But they fail to consider in their hearts that I remember all their evil. Now their deeds are all around them; they are before My face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.3', 'BSB', 'They delight the king with their evil, and the princes with their lies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.4', 'BSB', 'They are all adulterers, like an oven heated by a baker who needs not stoke the fire from the kneading to the rising of the dough.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.5', 'BSB', 'The princes are inflamed with wine on the day of our king; so he joins hands with those who mock him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.6', 'BSB', 'For they prepare their heart like an oven while they lie in wait; all night their anger smolders; in the morning it blazes like a flaming fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.7', 'BSB', 'All of them are hot as an oven, and they devour their rulers. All their kings fall; not one of them calls upon Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.8', 'BSB', 'Ephraim mixes with the nations; Ephraim is an unturned cake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.9', 'BSB', 'Foreigners consume his strength, but he does not notice. Even his hair is streaked with gray, but he does not know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.10', 'BSB', 'Israel’s arrogance testifies against them, yet they do not return to the LORD their God; despite all this, they do not seek Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.11', 'BSB', 'So Ephraim has become like a silly, senseless dove— calling out to Egypt, then turning to Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.12', 'BSB', 'As they go, I will spread My net over them; I will bring them down like birds of the air. I will chastise them when I hear them flocking together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.13', 'BSB', 'Woe to them, for they have strayed from Me! Destruction to them, for they have rebelled against Me! Though I would redeem them, they speak lies against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.14', 'BSB', 'They do not cry out to Me from their hearts when they wail upon their beds. They slash themselves for grain and new wine, but turn away from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.15', 'BSB', 'Although I trained and strengthened their arms, they plot evil against Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.7.16', 'BSB', 'They turn, but not to the Most High; they are like a faulty bow. Their leaders will fall by the sword for the cursing of their tongue; for this they will be ridiculed in the land of Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.1', 'BSB', 'Put the ram’s horn to your lips! An eagle looms over the house of the LORD, because the people have transgressed My covenant and rebelled against My law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.2', 'BSB', 'Israel cries out to Me, “O our God, we know You!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.3', 'BSB', 'But Israel has rejected good; an enemy will pursue him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.4', 'BSB', 'They set up kings, but not by Me. They make princes, but without My approval. With their silver and gold they make themselves idols, to their own destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.5', 'BSB', 'He has rejected your calf, O Samaria. My anger burns against them. How long will they be incapable of innocence?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.6', 'BSB', 'For this thing is from Israel— a craftsman made it, and it is not God. It will be broken to pieces, that calf of Samaria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.7', 'BSB', 'For they sow the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind. There is no standing grain; what sprouts fails to yield flour. Even if it should produce, the foreigners would swallow it up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.8', 'BSB', 'Israel is swallowed up! Now they are among the nations like a worthless vessel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.9', 'BSB', 'For they have gone up to Assyria like a wild donkey on its own. Ephraim has hired lovers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.10', 'BSB', 'Though they hire allies among the nations, I will now round them up, and they will begin to diminish under the oppression of the king of princes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.11', 'BSB', 'Though Ephraim multiplied the altars for sin, they became his altars for sinning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.12', 'BSB', 'Though I wrote for them the great things of My law, they regarded them as something strange.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.13', 'BSB', 'Though they offer sacrifices as gifts to Me, and though they eat the meat, the LORD does not accept them. Now He will remember their iniquity and punish their sins: They will return to Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.8.14', 'BSB', 'Israel has forgotten his Maker and built palaces; Judah has multiplied its fortified cities. But I will send fire upon their cities, and it will consume their citadels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.1', 'BSB', 'Do not rejoice, O Israel, with exultation like the nations, for you have played the harlot against your God; you have made love for hire on every threshing floor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.2', 'BSB', 'The threshing floor and winepress will not feed them, and the new wine will fail them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.3', 'BSB', 'They will not remain in the land of the LORD; Ephraim will return to Egypt and eat unclean food in Assyria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.4', 'BSB', 'They will not pour out wine offerings to the LORD, and their sacrifices will not please Him, but will be to them like the bread of mourners; all who eat will be defiled. For their bread will be for themselves; it will not enter the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.5', 'BSB', 'What will you do on the appointed day, on the day of the LORD’s feast?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.6', 'BSB', 'For even if they flee destruction, Egypt will gather them and Memphis will bury them. Their precious silver will be taken over by thistles, and thorns will overrun their tents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.7', 'BSB', 'The days of punishment have come; the days of retribution have arrived— let Israel know it. The prophet is called a fool, and the inspired man insane, because of the greatness of your iniquity and hostility.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.8', 'BSB', 'The prophet is Ephraim’s watchman, along with my God, yet the snare of the fowler lies on all his paths. Hostility is in the house of his God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.9', 'BSB', 'They have deeply corrupted themselves as in the days of Gibeah; He will remember their guilt; He will punish their sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.10', 'BSB', 'I found Israel like grapes in the wilderness. I saw your fathers as the firstfruits of the fig tree in its first season. But they went to Baal-peor, and consecrated themselves to Shame; so they became as detestable as the thing they loved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.11', 'BSB', 'Ephraim’s glory will fly away like a bird, with no birth, no pregnancy, and no conception.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.12', 'BSB', 'Even if they raise their children, I will bereave them of each one. Yes, woe be to them when I turn away from them!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.13', 'BSB', 'I have seen Ephraim, like Tyre, planted in a meadow. But Ephraim will bring out his children for slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.14', 'BSB', 'Give them, O LORD— what will You give? Give them wombs that miscarry and breasts that dry up!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.15', 'BSB', 'All their evil appears at Gilgal, for there I hated them. I will drive them from My house for the wickedness of their deeds. I will no longer love them; all their leaders are rebellious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.16', 'BSB', 'Ephraim is struck down; their root is withered; they cannot bear fruit. Even if they bear children, I will slay the darlings of their wombs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.9.17', 'BSB', 'My God will reject them because they have not obeyed Him; and they shall be wanderers among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.1', 'BSB', 'Israel was a luxuriant vine, yielding fruit for himself. The more his fruit increased, the more he increased the altars. The better his land produced, the better he made the sacred pillars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.2', 'BSB', 'Their hearts are devious; now they must bear their guilt. The LORD will break down their altars and demolish their sacred pillars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.3', 'BSB', 'Surely now they will say, “We have no king, for we do not revere the LORD. What can a king do for us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.4', 'BSB', 'They speak mere words; with false oaths they make covenants. So judgment springs up like poisonous weeds in the furrows of a field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.5', 'BSB', 'The people of Samaria will fear for the calf of Beth-aven. Indeed, its people will mourn with its idolatrous priests— those who rejoiced in its glory— for it has been taken from them into exile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.6', 'BSB', 'Yes, it will be carried to Assyria as tribute to the great king. Ephraim will be seized with shame; Israel will be ashamed of its wooden idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.7', 'BSB', 'Samaria will be carried off with her king like a twig on the surface of the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.8', 'BSB', 'The high places of Aven will be destroyed— it is the sin of Israel; thorns and thistles will overgrow their altars. Then they will say to the mountains, “Cover us!” and to the hills, “Fall on us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.9', 'BSB', 'Since the days of Gibeah you have sinned, O Israel, and there you have remained. Did not the battle in Gibeah overtake the sons of iniquity?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.10', 'BSB', 'I will chasten them when I please; nations will be gathered against them to put them in bondage for their double transgression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.11', 'BSB', 'Ephraim is a well-trained heifer that loves to thresh; but I will place a yoke on her fair neck. I will harness Ephraim, Judah will plow, and Jacob will break the hard ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.12', 'BSB', 'Sow for yourselves righteousness and reap the fruit of loving devotion; break up your unplowed ground. For it is time to seek the LORD until He comes and sends righteousness upon you like rain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.13', 'BSB', 'You have plowed wickedness and reaped injustice; you have eaten the fruit of lies. Because you have trusted in your own way and in the multitude of your mighty men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.14', 'BSB', 'the roar of battle will rise against your people, so that all your fortresses will be demolished as Shalman devastated Beth-arbel in the day of battle, when mothers were dashed to pieces along with their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.10.15', 'BSB', 'Thus it will be done to you, O Bethel, because of your great wickedness. When the day dawns, the king of Israel will be utterly cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.1', 'BSB', 'When Israel was a child, I loved him, and out of Egypt I called My son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.2', 'BSB', 'But the more I called Israel, the farther they departed from Me. They sacrificed to the Baals and burned incense to carved images.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.3', 'BSB', 'It was I who taught Ephraim to walk, taking them in My arms, but they never realized that it was I who healed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.4', 'BSB', 'I led them with cords of kindness, with ropes of love; I lifted the yoke from their necks and bent down to feed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.5', 'BSB', 'Will they not return to the land of Egypt and be ruled by Assyria because they refused to repent?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.6', 'BSB', 'A sword will flash through their cities; it will destroy the bars of their gates and consume them in their own plans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.7', 'BSB', 'My people are bent on turning from Me. Though they call to the Most High, He will by no means exalt them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.8', 'BSB', 'How could I give you up, O Ephraim? How could I surrender you, O Israel? How could I make you like Admah? How could I treat you like Zeboiim? My heart is turned within Me; My compassion is stirred!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.9', 'BSB', 'I will not execute the full fury of My anger; I will not turn back to destroy Ephraim. For I am God and not man— the Holy One among you— and I will not come in wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.10', 'BSB', 'They will walk after the LORD; He will roar like a lion. When He roars, His children will come trembling from the west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.11', 'BSB', 'They will come trembling like birds from Egypt and like doves from the land of Assyria. Then I will settle them in their homes, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.11.12', 'BSB', 'Ephraim surrounds Me with lies, the house of Israel with deceit; but Judah still walks with God and is faithful to the Holy One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.1', 'BSB', 'Ephraim chases the wind and pursues the east wind all day long; he multiplies lies and violence; he makes a covenant with Assyria and sends olive oil to Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD also brings a charge against Judah. He will punish Jacob according to his ways and repay him according to his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.3', 'BSB', 'In the womb he grasped his brother’s heel, and in his vigor he wrestled with God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.4', 'BSB', 'Yes, he struggled with the angel and prevailed; he wept and sought His favor; he found Him at Bethel and spoke with Him there —', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.5', 'BSB', 'the LORD is the God of Hosts— the LORD is His name of renown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.6', 'BSB', 'But you must return to your God, maintaining love and justice, and always waiting on your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.7', 'BSB', 'A merchant loves to defraud with dishonest scales in his hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.8', 'BSB', 'And Ephraim boasts: “How rich I have become! I have found wealth for myself. In all my labors, they can find in me no iniquity that is sinful.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.9', 'BSB', 'But I am the LORD your God ever since the land of Egypt. I will again make you dwell in tents, as in the days of the appointed feast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.10', 'BSB', 'I spoke through the prophets and multiplied their visions; I gave parables through the prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.11', 'BSB', 'Is there iniquity in Gilead? They will surely come to nothing. Do they sacrifice bulls in Gilgal? Indeed, their altars will be heaps of stones in the furrows of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.12', 'BSB', 'Jacob fled to the land of Aram and Israel worked for a wife— for a wife he tended sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.13', 'BSB', 'But by a prophet the LORD brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet he was preserved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.12.14', 'BSB', 'Ephraim has provoked bitter anger, so his Lord will leave his bloodguilt upon him and repay him for his contempt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.1', 'BSB', 'When Ephraim spoke, there was trembling; he was exalted in Israel. But he incurred guilt through Baal, and he died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.2', 'BSB', 'Now they sin more and more and make for themselves cast images, idols skillfully made from their silver, all of them the work of craftsmen. People say of them, “They offer human sacrifice and kiss the calves!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore they will be like the morning mist, like the early dew that vanishes, like chaff blown from a threshing floor, like smoke through an open window.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.4', 'BSB', 'Yet I am the LORD your God ever since the land of Egypt; you know no God but Me, for there is no Savior besides Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.5', 'BSB', 'I knew you in the wilderness, in the land of drought.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.6', 'BSB', 'When they had pasture, they became satisfied; when they were satisfied, their hearts became proud, and as a result they forgot Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.7', 'BSB', 'So like a lion I will pounce on them; like a leopard I will lurk by the path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.8', 'BSB', 'Like a bear robbed of her cubs I will attack them, and I will tear open their chests. There I will devour them like a lion, like a wild beast would tear them apart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.9', 'BSB', 'You are destroyed, O Israel, because you are against Me— against your helper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.10', 'BSB', 'Where is your king now to save you in all your cities, and the rulers to whom you said, “Give me a king and princes”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.11', 'BSB', 'So in My anger I gave you a king, and in My wrath I took him away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.12', 'BSB', 'The iniquity of Ephraim is bound up; his sin is stored up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.13', 'BSB', 'Labor pains come upon him, but he is an unwise son. When the time arrives, he fails to present himself at the opening of the womb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.14', 'BSB', 'I will ransom them from the power of Sheol; I will redeem them from Death. Where, O Death, are your plagues? Where, O Sheol, is your sting? Compassion is hidden from My eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.15', 'BSB', 'Although he flourishes among his brothers, an east wind will come— a wind from the LORD rising up from the desert. His fountain will fail, and his spring will run dry. The wind will plunder his treasury of every precious article.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.13.16', 'BSB', 'Samaria will bear her guilt because she has rebelled against her God. They will fall by the sword; their little ones will be dashed to pieces, and their pregnant women ripped open.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.1', 'BSB', 'Return, O Israel, to the LORD your God, for you have stumbled by your iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.2', 'BSB', 'Bring your confessions and return to the LORD. Say to Him: “Take away all our iniquity and receive us graciously, that we may present the fruit of our lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.3', 'BSB', 'Assyria will not save us, nor will we ride on horses. We will never again say, ‘Our gods!’ to the work of our own hands. For in You the fatherless find compassion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.4', 'BSB', 'I will heal their apostasy; I will freely love them, for My anger has turned away from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.5', 'BSB', 'I will be like the dew to Israel; he will blossom like the lily and take root like the cedars of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.6', 'BSB', 'His shoots will sprout, and his splendor will be like the olive tree, his fragrance like the cedars of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.7', 'BSB', 'They will return and dwell in his shade; they will grow grain and blossom like the vine. His renown will be like the wine of Lebanon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.8', 'BSB', 'O Ephraim, what have I to do anymore with idols? It is I who answer and watch over him. I am like a flourishing cypress; your fruit comes from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hos.14.9', 'BSB', 'Whoever is wise, let him understand these things; whoever is discerning, let him know them. For the ways of the LORD are right, and the righteous walk in them but the rebellious stumble in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Joel son of Pethuel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.2', 'BSB', 'Hear this, O elders; and give ear, all who dwell in the land. Has anything like this ever happened in your days or in the days of your fathers?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.3', 'BSB', 'Tell it to your children; let your children tell it to their children, and their children to the next generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.4', 'BSB', 'What the devouring locust has left, the swarming locust has eaten; what the swarming locust has left, the young locust has eaten; and what the young locust has left, the destroying locust has eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.5', 'BSB', 'Wake up, you drunkards, and weep; wail, all you drinkers of wine, because of the sweet wine, for it has been cut off from your mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.6', 'BSB', 'For a nation has invaded My land, powerful and without number; its teeth are the teeth of a lion, and its fangs are the fangs of a lioness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.7', 'BSB', 'It has laid waste My grapevine and splintered My fig tree. It has stripped off the bark and thrown it away; the branches have turned white.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.8', 'BSB', 'Wail like a virgin dressed in sackcloth, grieving for the husband of her youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.9', 'BSB', 'Grain and drink offerings have been cut off from the house of the LORD; the priests are in mourning, those who minister before the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.10', 'BSB', 'The field is ruined; the land mourns. For the grain is destroyed, the new wine is dried up, and the oil fails.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.11', 'BSB', 'Be dismayed, O farmers, wail, O vinedressers, over the wheat and barley, because the harvest of the field has perished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.12', 'BSB', 'The grapevine is dried up, and the fig tree is withered; the pomegranate, palm, and apple— all the trees of the orchard—are withered. Surely the joy of mankind has dried up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.13', 'BSB', 'Put on sackcloth and lament, O priests; wail, O ministers of the altar. Come, spend the night in sackcloth, O ministers of my God, because the grain and drink offerings are withheld from the house of your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.14', 'BSB', 'Consecrate a fast; proclaim a solemn assembly! Gather the elders and all the residents of the land to the house of the LORD your God, and cry out to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.15', 'BSB', 'Alas for the day! For the Day of the LORD is near, and it will come as destruction from the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.16', 'BSB', 'Has not the food been cut off before our very eyes— joy and gladness from the house of our God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.17', 'BSB', 'The seeds lie shriveled beneath the clods; the storehouses are in ruins; the granaries are broken down, for the grain has withered away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.18', 'BSB', 'How the cattle groan! The herds wander in confusion because they have no pasture. Even the flocks of sheep are suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.19', 'BSB', 'To You, O LORD, I call, for fire has consumed the open pastures and flames have scorched all the trees of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.1.20', 'BSB', 'Even the beasts of the field pant for You, for the streams of water have dried up, and fire has consumed the open pastures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.1', 'BSB', 'Blow the ram’s horn in Zion; sound the alarm on My holy mountain! Let all who dwell in the land tremble, for the Day of the LORD is coming; indeed, it is near—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.2', 'BSB', 'a day of darkness and gloom, a day of clouds and blackness. Like the dawn overspreading the mountains a great and strong army appears, such as never was of old, nor will ever be in ages to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.3', 'BSB', 'Before them a fire devours, and behind them a flame scorches. The land before them is like the Garden of Eden, but behind them, it is like a desert wasteland— surely nothing will escape them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.4', 'BSB', 'Their appearance is like that of horses, and they gallop like swift steeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.5', 'BSB', 'With a sound like that of chariots they bound over the mountaintops, like the crackling of fire consuming stubble, like a mighty army deployed for battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.6', 'BSB', 'Nations writhe in horror before them; every face turns pale.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.7', 'BSB', 'They charge like mighty men; they scale the walls like men of war. Each one marches in formation, not swerving from the course.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.8', 'BSB', 'They do not jostle one another; each proceeds in his path. They burst through the defenses, never breaking ranks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.9', 'BSB', 'They storm the city; they run along the wall; they climb into houses, entering through windows like thieves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.10', 'BSB', 'Before them the earth quakes; the heavens tremble. The sun and moon grow dark, and the stars lose their brightness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD raises His voice in the presence of His army. Indeed, His camp is very large, for mighty are those who obey His command. For the Day of the LORD is great and very dreadful. Who can endure it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.12', 'BSB', '“Yet even now,” declares the LORD, “return to Me with all your heart, with fasting, weeping, and mourning.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.13', 'BSB', 'So rend your hearts and not your garments, and return to the LORD your God. For He is gracious and compassionate, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion. And He relents from sending disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.14', 'BSB', 'Who knows? He may turn and relent and leave a blessing behind Him— grain and drink offerings for the LORD your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.15', 'BSB', 'Blow the ram’s horn in Zion, consecrate a fast, proclaim a sacred assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.16', 'BSB', 'Gather the people, sanctify the congregation, assemble the aged, gather the children, even those nursing at the breast. Let the bridegroom leave his room, and the bride her chamber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.17', 'BSB', 'Let the priests who minister before the LORD weep between the portico and the altar, saying, “Spare Your people, O LORD, and do not make Your heritage a reproach, an object of scorn among the nations. Why should they say among the peoples, ‘Where is their God?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.18', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD became jealous for His land, and He spared His people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.19', 'BSB', 'And the LORD answered His people: “Behold, I will send you grain, new wine, and oil, and by them you will be satisfied. I will never again make you a reproach among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.20', 'BSB', 'The northern army I will drive away from you, banishing it to a barren and desolate land, its front ranks into the Eastern Sea, and its rear guard into the Western Sea. And its stench will rise; its foul odor will ascend. For He has done great things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.21', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid, O land; rejoice and be glad, for the LORD has done great things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.22', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid, O beasts of the field, for the open pastures have turned green, the trees bear their fruit, and the fig tree and vine yield their best.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.23', 'BSB', 'Be glad, O children of Zion, and rejoice in the LORD your God, for He has given you the autumn rains for your vindication. He sends you showers, both autumn and spring rains, as before.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.24', 'BSB', 'The threshing floors will be full of grain, and the vats will overflow with new wine and oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.25', 'BSB', 'I will repay you for the years eaten by locusts— the swarming locust, the young locust, the destroying locust, and the devouring locust — My great army that I sent against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.26', 'BSB', 'You will have plenty to eat, until you are satisfied. You will praise the name of the LORD your God, who has worked wonders for you. My people will never again be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.27', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I am present in Israel and that I am the LORD your God, and there is no other. My people will never again be put to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.28', 'BSB', 'And afterward, I will pour out My Spirit on all people. Your sons and daughters will prophesy, your old men will dream dreams, your young men will see visions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.29', 'BSB', 'Even on My menservants and maidservants, I will pour out My Spirit in those days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.30', 'BSB', 'I will show wonders in the heavens and on the earth, blood and fire and columns of smoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.31', 'BSB', 'The sun will be turned to darkness and the moon to blood before the coming of the great and awesome Day of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.2.32', 'BSB', 'And everyone who calls on the name of the LORD will be saved; for on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there will be deliverance, as the LORD has promised, among the remnant called by the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.1', 'BSB', '“Yes, in those days and at that time, when I restore Judah and Jerusalem from captivity,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.2', 'BSB', 'I will gather all the nations and bring them down to the Valley of Jehoshaphat. There I will enter into judgment against them concerning My people, My inheritance, Israel, whom they have scattered among the nations as they divided up My land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.3', 'BSB', 'They cast lots for My people; they bartered a boy for a prostitute and sold a girl for wine to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.4', 'BSB', 'Now what do you have against Me, O Tyre, Sidon, and all the regions of Philistia? Are you rendering against Me a recompense? If you retaliate against Me, I will swiftly and speedily return your recompense upon your heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.5', 'BSB', 'For you took My silver and gold and carried off My finest treasures to your temples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.6', 'BSB', 'You sold the people of Judah and Jerusalem to the Greeks, to send them far from their homeland.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will rouse them from the places to which you sold them; I will return your recompense upon your heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.8', 'BSB', 'I will sell your sons and daughters into the hands of the people of Judah, and they will sell them to the Sabeans—to a distant nation.” Indeed, the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.9', 'BSB', 'Proclaim this among the nations: “Prepare for war; rouse the mighty men; let all the men of war advance and attack!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.10', 'BSB', 'Beat your plowshares into swords and your pruning hooks into spears. Let the weak say, ‘I am strong!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.11', 'BSB', 'Come quickly, all you surrounding nations, and gather yourselves. Bring down Your mighty ones, O LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.12', 'BSB', 'Let the nations be roused and advance to the Valley of Jehoshaphat, for there I will sit down to judge all the nations on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.13', 'BSB', 'Swing the sickle, for the harvest is ripe. Come, trample the grapes, for the winepress is full; the wine vats overflow because their wickedness is great.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.14', 'BSB', 'Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision! For the Day of the LORD is near in the valley of decision.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.15', 'BSB', 'The sun and moon will grow dark, and the stars will no longer shine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.16', 'BSB', 'The LORD will roar from Zion and raise His voice from Jerusalem; heaven and earth will tremble. But the LORD will be a refuge for His people, a stronghold for the people of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.17', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I am the LORD your God, who dwells in Zion, My holy mountain. Jerusalem will be holy, never again to be overrun by foreigners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.18', 'BSB', 'And in that day the mountains will drip with sweet wine, and the hills will flow with milk. All the streams of Judah will run with water, and a spring will flow from the house of the LORD to water the Valley of Acacias.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.19', 'BSB', 'Egypt will become desolate, and Edom a desert wasteland, because of the violence done to the people of Judah, in whose land they shed innocent blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.20', 'BSB', 'But Judah will be inhabited forever, and Jerusalem from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Joel.3.21', 'BSB', 'For I will avenge their blood, which I have not yet avenged.” For the LORD dwells in Zion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.1', 'BSB', 'These are the words of Amos, who was among the sheepherders of Tekoa—what he saw concerning Israel two years before the earthquake, in the days when Uzziah was king of Judah and Jeroboam son of Jehoash was king of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.2', 'BSB', 'He said: “The LORD roars from Zion and raises His voice from Jerusalem; the pastures of the shepherds mourn, and the summit of Carmel withers.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Damascus, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they threshed Gilead with sledges of iron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.4', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire upon the house of Hazael to consume the citadels of Ben-hadad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.5', 'BSB', 'I will break down the gates of Damascus; I will cut off the ruler of the Valley of Aven and the one who wields the scepter in Beth-eden. The people of Aram will be exiled to Kir,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.6', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Gaza, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they exiled a whole population, delivering them up to Edom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.7', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire upon the walls of Gaza, to consume its citadels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.8', 'BSB', 'I will cut off the ruler of Ashdod and the one who wields the scepter in Ashkelon. I will turn My hand against Ekron, and the remnant of the Philistines will perish,” says the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.9', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Tyre, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they delivered up a whole congregation of exiles to Edom and broke a covenant of brotherhood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.10', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire upon the walls of Tyre to consume its citadels.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.11', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Edom, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because he pursued his brother with the sword and stifled all compassion; his anger raged continually, and his fury flamed incessantly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.12', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire upon Teman to consume the citadels of Bozrah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.13', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of the Ammonites, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they ripped open the pregnant women of Gilead in order to enlarge their territory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.14', 'BSB', 'So I will kindle a fire in the walls of Rabbah to consume its citadels amid war cries on the day of battle and a violent wind on the day of tempest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.1.15', 'BSB', 'Their king will go into exile — he and his princes together,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Moab, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because he burned to lime the bones of Edom’s king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.2', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire against Moab to consume the citadels of Kerioth. Moab will die in tumult, amid war cries and the sound of the ram’s horn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.3', 'BSB', 'I will cut off the ruler of Moab and kill all the officials with him,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.4', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Judah, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they reject the Law of the LORD and fail to keep His statutes; they are led astray by the lies in which their fathers walked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.5', 'BSB', 'So I will send fire upon Judah to consume the citadels of Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.6', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Israel, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because they sell the righteous for silver and the needy for a pair of sandals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.7', 'BSB', 'They trample on the heads of the poor as on the dust of the earth; they push the needy out of their way. A man and his father have relations with the same girl and so profane My holy name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.8', 'BSB', 'They lie down beside every altar on garments taken in pledge. And in the house of their God, they drink wine obtained through fines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.9', 'BSB', 'Yet it was I who destroyed the Amorite before them, though his height was like that of the cedars, and he was as strong as the oaks. Yet I destroyed his fruit above and his roots below.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.10', 'BSB', 'And I brought you up from the land of Egypt and led you forty years in the wilderness, that you might take possession of the land of the Amorite.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.11', 'BSB', 'I raised up prophets from your sons and Nazirites from your young men. Is this not true, O children of Israel?” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.12', 'BSB', '“But you made the Nazirites drink wine and commanded the prophets not to prophesy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.13', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am about to crush you in your place as with a cart full of grain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.14', 'BSB', 'Escape will fail the swift, the strong will not prevail by his strength, and the mighty will not save his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.15', 'BSB', 'The archer will not stand his ground, the fleet of foot will not escape, and the horseman will not save his life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.2.16', 'BSB', 'Even the bravest of mighty men will flee naked on that day,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.1', 'BSB', 'Hear this word that the LORD has spoken against you, O children of Israel, against the whole family that I brought up out of the land of Egypt:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.2', 'BSB', '“Only you have I known from all the families of the earth; therefore I will punish you for all your iniquities.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.3', 'BSB', 'Can two walk together without agreeing where to go?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.4', 'BSB', 'Does a lion roar in the forest when he has no prey? Does a young lion growl in his den if he has caught nothing?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.5', 'BSB', 'Does a bird land in a snare where no bait has been set? Does a trap spring from the ground when it has nothing to catch?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.6', 'BSB', 'If a ram’s horn sounds in a city, do the people not tremble? If calamity comes to a city, has not the LORD caused it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.7', 'BSB', 'Surely the Lord GOD does nothing without revealing His plan to His servants the prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.8', 'BSB', 'The lion has roared— who will not fear? The Lord GOD has spoken— who will not prophesy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.9', 'BSB', 'Proclaim to the citadels of Ashdod and to the citadels of Egypt: “Assemble on the mountains of Samaria; see the great unrest in the city and the acts of oppression in her midst.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.10', 'BSB', '“For they know not how to do right,” declares the LORD. “They store up violence and destruction in their citadels.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the Lord GOD says: “An enemy will surround the land; he will pull down your strongholds and plunder your citadels.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.12', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “As the shepherd snatches from the mouth of the lion two legs or a piece of an ear, so the Israelites dwelling in Samaria will be rescued having just the corner of a bed or the cushion of a couch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.13', 'BSB', 'Hear and testify against the house of Jacob, declares the Lord GOD, the God of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.14', 'BSB', 'On the day I punish Israel for their transgressions, I will visit destruction on the altars of Bethel; the horns of the altar will be cut off, and they will fall to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.3.15', 'BSB', 'I will tear down the winter house along with the summer house; the houses of ivory will also perish, and the great houses will come to an end,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.1', 'BSB', 'Hear this word, you cows of Bashan on Mount Samaria, you women who oppress the poor and crush the needy, who say to your husbands, “Bring us more to drink.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.2', 'BSB', 'The Lord GOD has sworn by His holiness: “Behold, the days are coming when you will be taken away with hooks, and your posterity with fishhooks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.3', 'BSB', 'You will go out through broken walls, each one straight ahead of her, and you will be cast out toward Harmon,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.4', 'BSB', '“Go to Bethel and transgress; rebel even more at Gilgal! Bring your sacrifices every morning, your tithes every three days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.5', 'BSB', 'Offer leavened bread as a thank offering, and loudly proclaim your freewill offerings. For that is what you children of Israel love to do,” declares the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.6', 'BSB', '“I beset all your cities with cleanness of teeth and all your towns with lack of bread, yet you did not return to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.7', 'BSB', '“I also withheld the rain from you when the harvest was three months away. I sent rain on one city but withheld it from another. One field received rain; another without rain withered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.8', 'BSB', 'People staggered from city to city for water to drink, but they were not satisfied; yet you did not return to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.9', 'BSB', '“I struck you with blight and mildew in your growing gardens and vineyards; the locust devoured your fig and olive trees, yet you did not return to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.10', 'BSB', '“I sent plagues among you like those of Egypt; I killed your young men with the sword, along with your captured horses. I filled your nostrils with the stench of your camp, yet you did not return to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.11', 'BSB', '“Some of you I overthrew as I overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah, and you were like a firebrand snatched from a blaze, yet you did not return to Me,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.12', 'BSB', '“Therefore, that is what I will do to you, O Israel, and since I will do this to you, prepare to meet your God, O Israel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.4.13', 'BSB', 'For behold, He who forms the mountains, who creates the wind and reveals His thoughts to man, who turns the dawn to darkness and strides on the heights of the earth— the LORD, the God of Hosts, is His name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.1', 'BSB', 'Hear this word, O house of Israel, this lamentation I take up against you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.2', 'BSB', '“Fallen is Virgin Israel, never to rise again. She lies abandoned on her land, with no one to raise her up.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD says: “The city that marches out a thousand strong will only see a hundred return, and the one that marches out a hundred strong will have but ten left in the house of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.4', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD says to the house of Israel: “Seek Me and live!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.5', 'BSB', 'Do not seek Bethel or go to Gilgal; do not journey to Beersheba, for Gilgal will surely go into exile, and Bethel will come to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.6', 'BSB', 'Seek the LORD and live, or He will sweep like fire through the house of Joseph; it will devour everything, with no one at Bethel to extinguish it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.7', 'BSB', 'There are those who turn justice into wormwood and cast righteousness to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.8', 'BSB', 'He who made the Pleiades and Orion, who turns darkness into dawn and darkens day into night, who summons the waters of the sea and pours them over the face of the earth— the LORD is His name—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.9', 'BSB', 'He flashes destruction on the strong, so that fury comes upon the stronghold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.10', 'BSB', 'There are those who hate the one who reproves in the gate and despise him who speaks with integrity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore, because you trample on the poor and exact from him a tax of grain, you will never live in the stone houses you have built; you will never drink the wine from the lush vineyards you have planted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.12', 'BSB', 'For I know that your transgressions are many and your sins are numerous. You oppress the righteous by taking bribes; you deprive the poor of justice in the gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore, the prudent keep silent in such times, for the days are evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.14', 'BSB', 'Seek good, not evil, so that you may live. And the LORD, the God of Hosts, will be with you, as you have claimed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.15', 'BSB', 'Hate evil and love good; establish justice in the gate. Perhaps the LORD, the God of Hosts, will be gracious to the remnant of Joseph.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD, the God of Hosts, the Lord, says: “There will be wailing in all the public squares and cries of ‘Alas! Alas!’ in all the streets. The farmer will be summoned to mourn, and the mourners to wail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.17', 'BSB', 'There will be wailing in all the vineyards, for I will pass through your midst,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.18', 'BSB', 'Woe to you who long for the Day of the LORD! What will the Day of the LORD be for you? It will be darkness and not light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.19', 'BSB', 'It will be like a man who flees from a lion, only to encounter a bear, or who enters his house and rests his hand against the wall, only to be bitten by a snake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.20', 'BSB', 'Will not the Day of the LORD be darkness and not light, even gloom with no brightness in it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.21', 'BSB', '“I hate, I despise your feasts! I cannot stand the stench of your solemn assemblies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.22', 'BSB', 'Even though you offer Me burnt offerings and grain offerings, I will not accept them; for your peace offerings of fattened cattle I will have no regard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.23', 'BSB', 'Take away from Me the noise of your songs! I will not listen to the music of your harps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.24', 'BSB', 'But let justice roll on like a river, and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.25', 'BSB', 'Did you bring Me sacrifices and offerings forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.26', 'BSB', 'You have taken along Sakkuth your king and Kaiwan your star god, the idols you made for yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.5.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will send you into exile beyond Damascus,” says the LORD, whose name is the God of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to those at ease in Zion and those secure on Mount Samaria, the distinguished ones of the foremost nation, to whom the house of Israel comes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.2', 'BSB', 'Cross over to Calneh and see; go from there to the great Hamath; then go down to Gath of the Philistines. Are you better than these kingdoms? Is their territory larger than yours?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.3', 'BSB', 'You dismiss the day of calamity and bring near a reign of violence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.4', 'BSB', 'You lie on beds inlaid with ivory, and lounge upon your couches. You dine on lambs from the flock and calves from the stall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.5', 'BSB', 'You improvise songs on the harp like David and invent your own musical instruments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.6', 'BSB', 'You drink wine by the bowlful and anoint yourselves with the finest oils, but you fail to grieve over the ruin of Joseph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore, you will now go into exile as the first of the captives, and your feasting and lounging will come to an end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.8', 'BSB', 'The Lord GOD has sworn by Himself—the LORD, the God of Hosts, has declared: “I abhor Jacob’s pride and detest his citadels, so I will deliver up the city and everything in it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.9', 'BSB', 'And if there are ten men left in one house, they too will die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.10', 'BSB', 'And when the relative who is to burn the bodies picks them up to remove them from the house, he will call to one inside, “Is anyone else with you?” “None,” that person will answer. “Silence,” the relative will retort, “for the name of the LORD must not be invoked.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.11', 'BSB', 'For the LORD gives a command: “The great house will be smashed to pieces, and the small house to rubble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.12', 'BSB', '“Do horses gallop on the cliffs? Does one plow the sea with oxen? But you have turned justice into poison and the fruit of righteousness into wormwood—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.13', 'BSB', 'you who rejoice in Lo-debar and say, ‘Did we not take Karnaim by our own strength?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.6.14', 'BSB', 'For behold, I will raise up a nation against you, O house of Israel,” declares the LORD, the God of Hosts, “and they will oppress you from Lebo-hamath to the Brook of the Arabah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD showed me: He was preparing swarms of locusts just after the king’s harvest, as the late spring crop was coming up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.2', 'BSB', 'And when the locusts had eaten every green plant in the land, I said, “Lord GOD, please forgive! How will Jacob survive, since he is so small?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.3', 'BSB', 'So the LORD relented from this plan. “It will not happen,” He said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.4', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD showed me: The Lord GOD was calling for judgment by fire. It consumed the great deep and devoured the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.5', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “Lord GOD, please stop! How will Jacob survive, since he is so small?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.6', 'BSB', 'So the LORD relented from this plan. “It will not happen either,” said the Lord GOD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.7', 'BSB', 'This is what He showed me: Behold, the Lord was standing by a wall true to plumb, with a plumb line in His hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.8', 'BSB', '“Amos, what do you see?” asked the LORD. “A plumb line,” I replied. “Behold,” said the Lord, “I am setting a plumb line among My people Israel; I will no longer spare them:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.9', 'BSB', 'The high places of Isaac will be deserted, and the sanctuaries of Israel will be laid waste; and I will rise up against the house of Jeroboam with My sword.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.10', 'BSB', 'Then Amaziah the priest of Bethel sent word to Jeroboam king of Israel, saying, “Amos has conspired against you in the midst of the house of Israel. The land cannot bear all his words,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.11', 'BSB', 'for this is what Amos has said: ‘Jeroboam will die by the sword, and Israel will surely go into exile, away from their homeland.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.12', 'BSB', 'And Amaziah said to Amos, “Go away, you seer! Flee to the land of Judah; earn your bread there and do your prophesying there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.13', 'BSB', 'But never prophesy at Bethel again, because it is the sanctuary of the king and the temple of the kingdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.14', 'BSB', '“I was not a prophet,” Amos replied, “nor was I the son of a prophet; rather, I was a herdsman and a tender of sycamore-fig trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.15', 'BSB', 'But the LORD took me from following the flock and said to me, ‘Go, prophesy to My people Israel.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.16', 'BSB', 'Now, therefore, hear the word of the LORD. You say: ‘Do not prophesy against Israel; do not preach against the house of Isaac.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.7.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: ‘Your wife will become a prostitute in the city, and your sons and daughters will fall by the sword. Your land will be divided by a measuring line, and you yourself will die on pagan soil. And Israel will surely go into exile, away from their homeland.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.1', 'BSB', 'This is what the Lord GOD showed me: I saw a basket of summer fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.2', 'BSB', '“Amos, what do you see?” He asked. “A basket of summer fruit,” I replied. So the LORD said to me, “The end has come for My people Israel; I will no longer spare them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.3', 'BSB', '“In that day,” declares the Lord GOD, “the songs of the temple will turn to wailing. Many will be the corpses, strewn in silence everywhere!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.4', 'BSB', 'Hear this, you who trample the needy, who do away with the poor of the land,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.5', 'BSB', 'asking, “When will the New Moon be over, that we may sell grain? When will the Sabbath end, that we may market wheat? Let us reduce the ephah and increase the shekel; let us cheat with dishonest scales.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.6', 'BSB', 'Let us buy the poor with silver and the needy for a pair of sandals, selling even the chaff with the wheat!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.7', 'BSB', 'The LORD has sworn by the Pride of Jacob: “I will never forget any of their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.8', 'BSB', 'Will not the land quake for this, and all its dwellers mourn? All of it will swell like the Nile; it will surge and then subside like the Nile in Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.9', 'BSB', 'And in that day, declares the Lord GOD, I will make the sun go down at noon, and I will darken the earth in the daytime.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.10', 'BSB', 'I will turn your feasts into mourning and all your songs into lamentation. I will cause everyone to wear sackcloth and every head to be shaved. I will make it like a time of mourning for an only son, and its outcome like a bitter day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.11', 'BSB', 'Behold, the days are coming, declares the Lord GOD, when I will send a famine on the land— not a famine of bread or a thirst for water, but a famine of hearing the words of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.12', 'BSB', 'People will stagger from sea to sea and roam from north to east, seeking the word of the LORD, but they will not find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.13', 'BSB', 'In that day the lovely young women— the young men as well— will faint from thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.8.14', 'BSB', 'Those who swear by the guilt of Samaria and say, ‘As surely as your god lives, O Dan,’ or, ‘As surely as the way of Beersheba lives’— they will fall, never to rise again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.1', 'BSB', 'I saw the Lord standing beside the altar, and He said: “Strike the tops of the pillars so that the thresholds shake. Topple them on the heads of all the people, and I will kill the rest with the sword. None of those who flee will get away; none of the fugitives will escape.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.2', 'BSB', 'Though they dig down to Sheol, from there My hand will take them; and though they climb up to heaven, from there I will pull them down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.3', 'BSB', 'Though they hide themselves atop Carmel, there I will track them and seize them; and though they hide from Me at the bottom of the sea, there I will command the serpent to bite them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.4', 'BSB', 'Though they are driven by their enemies into captivity, there I will command the sword to slay them. I will fix My eyes upon them for harm and not for good.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.5', 'BSB', 'The Lord GOD of Hosts, He who touches the earth and it melts, and all its dwellers mourn— all the land rises like the Nile, then sinks like the river of Egypt—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.6', 'BSB', 'He builds His upper rooms in the heavens and founds His vault upon the earth. He summons the waters of the sea and pours them over the face of the earth. The LORD is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.7', 'BSB', '“Are you not like the Cushites to Me, O children of Israel?” declares the LORD. “Did I not bring Israel up from the land of Egypt, the Philistines from Caphtor, and the Arameans from Kir?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.8', 'BSB', 'Surely the eyes of the Lord GOD are on the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from the face of the earth. Yet I will not utterly destroy the house of Jacob,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.9', 'BSB', '“For surely I will give the command, and I will shake the house of Israel among all the nations as grain is sifted in a sieve; but not a pebble will reach the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.10', 'BSB', 'All the sinners among My people will die by the sword— all those who say, ‘Disaster will never draw near or confront us.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.11', 'BSB', '“In that day I will restore the fallen tent of David. I will repair its gaps, restore its ruins, and rebuild it as in the days of old,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.12', 'BSB', 'that they may possess the remnant of Edom and all the nations that bear My name,” declares the LORD, who will do this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.13', 'BSB', '“Behold, the days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when the plowman will overtake the reaper and the treader of grapes, the sower of seed. The mountains will drip with sweet wine, with which all the hills will flow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.14', 'BSB', 'I will restore My people Israel from captivity; they will rebuild and inhabit the ruined cities. They will plant vineyards and drink their wine; they will make gardens and eat their fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Amos.9.15', 'BSB', 'I will firmly plant them in their own land, never again to be uprooted from the land that I have given them,” says the LORD your God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the vision of Obadiah: This is what the Lord GOD says about Edom— We have heard a message from the LORD; an envoy has been sent among the nations to say, “Rise up, and let us go to battle against her!”—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.2', 'BSB', '“Behold, I will make you small among the nations; you will be deeply despised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.3', 'BSB', 'The pride of your heart has deceived you, O dwellers in the clefts of the rocks whose habitation is the heights, who say in your heart, ‘Who can bring me down to the ground?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.4', 'BSB', 'Though you soar like the eagle and make your nest among the stars, even from there I will bring you down,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.5', 'BSB', '“If thieves came to you, if robbers by night— oh, how you will be ruined— would they not steal only what they wanted? If grape gatherers came to you, would they not leave some gleanings?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.6', 'BSB', 'But how Esau will be pillaged, his hidden treasures sought out!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.7', 'BSB', 'All the men allied with you will drive you to the border; the men at peace with you will deceive and overpower you. Those who eat your bread will set a trap for you without your awareness of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.8', 'BSB', 'In that day, declares the LORD, will I not destroy the wise men of Edom and the men of understanding in the mountains of Esau?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.9', 'BSB', 'Then your mighty men, O Teman, will be terrified, so that everyone in the mountains of Esau will be cut down in the slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.10', 'BSB', 'Because of the violence against your brother Jacob, you will be covered with shame and cut off forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.11', 'BSB', 'On the day you stood aloof while strangers carried off his wealth and foreigners entered his gate and cast lots for Jerusalem, you were just like one of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.12', 'BSB', 'But you should not gloat in that day, your brother’s day of misfortune, nor rejoice over the people of Judah in the day of their destruction, nor boast proudly in the day of their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.13', 'BSB', 'You should not enter the gate of My people in the day of their disaster, nor gloat over their affliction in the day of their disaster, nor loot their wealth in the day of their disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.14', 'BSB', 'Nor should you stand at the crossroads to cut off their fugitives, nor deliver up their survivors in the day of their distress.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.15', 'BSB', 'For the Day of the LORD is near for all the nations. As you have done, it will be done to you; your recompense will return upon your own head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.16', 'BSB', 'For as you drank on My holy mountain, so all the nations will drink continually. They will drink and gulp it down; they will be as if they had never existed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.17', 'BSB', 'But on Mount Zion there will be deliverance, and it will be holy, and the house of Jacob will reclaim their possession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.18', 'BSB', 'Then the house of Jacob will be a blazing fire, and the house of Joseph a burning flame; but the house of Esau will be stubble— Jacob will set it ablaze and consume it. Therefore no survivor will remain from the house of Esau.” For the LORD has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.19', 'BSB', 'Those from the Negev will possess the mountains of Esau; those from the foothills will possess the land of the Philistines. They will occupy the fields of Ephraim and Samaria, and Benjamin will possess Gilead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.20', 'BSB', 'And the exiles of this host of the Israelites will possess the land of the Canaanites as far as Zarephath; and the exiles from Jerusalem who are in Sepharad will possess the cities of the Negev.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Obad.1.21', 'BSB', 'The deliverers will ascend Mount Zion to rule over the mountains of Esau. And the kingdom will belong to the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.1', 'BSB', 'Now the word of the LORD came to Jonah son of Amittai, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.2', 'BSB', '“Get up! Go to the great city of Nineveh and preach against it, because its wickedness has come up before Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.3', 'BSB', 'Jonah, however, got up to flee to Tarshish, away from the presence of the LORD. He went down to Joppa and found a ship bound for Tarshish. So he paid the fare and went aboard to sail for Tarshish, away from the presence of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.4', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD hurled a great wind upon the sea, and such a violent storm arose that the ship was in danger of breaking apart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.5', 'BSB', 'The sailors were afraid, and each cried out to his own god. And they threw the ship’s cargo into the sea to lighten the load. But Jonah had gone down to the lowest part of the vessel, where he lay down and fell into a deep sleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.6', 'BSB', 'The captain approached him and said, “How can you sleep? Get up and call upon your God. Perhaps this God will consider us, so that we may not perish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.7', 'BSB', '“Come!” said the sailors to one another. “Let us cast lots to find out who is responsible for this calamity that is upon us.” So they cast lots, and the lot fell on Jonah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.8', 'BSB', '“Tell us now,” they demanded, “who is to blame for this calamity that is upon us? What is your occupation, and where have you come from? What is your country, and who are your people?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.9', 'BSB', '“I am a Hebrew,” replied Jonah. “I worship the LORD, the God of the heavens, who made the sea and the dry land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.10', 'BSB', 'Then the men were even more afraid and said to him, “What have you done?” The men knew that he was fleeing from the presence of the LORD, because he had told them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.11', 'BSB', 'Now the sea was growing worse and worse, so they said to Jonah, “What must we do to you to calm this sea for us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.12', 'BSB', '“Pick me up,” he answered, “and cast me into the sea, so it may quiet down for you. For I know that I am to blame for this violent storm that has come upon you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.13', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, the men rowed hard to get back to dry land, but they could not, for the sea was raging against them more and more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.14', 'BSB', 'So they cried out to the LORD: “Please, O LORD, do not let us perish on account of this man’s life! Do not charge us with innocent blood! For You, O LORD, have done as You pleased.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.15', 'BSB', 'At this, they picked up Jonah and cast him into the sea, and the raging sea grew calm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.16', 'BSB', 'Then the men feared the LORD greatly, and they offered a sacrifice to the LORD and made vows to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.1.17', 'BSB', 'Now the LORD had appointed a great fish to swallow Jonah, and Jonah spent three days and three nights in the belly of the fish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.1', 'BSB', 'From inside the fish, Jonah prayed to the LORD his God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.2', 'BSB', 'saying: “In my distress I called to the LORD, and He answered me. From the belly of Sheol I called for help, and You heard my voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.3', 'BSB', 'For You cast me into the deep, into the heart of the seas, and the current swirled about me; all Your breakers and waves swept over me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.4', 'BSB', 'At this, I said, ‘I have been banished from Your sight; yet I will look once more toward Your holy temple.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.5', 'BSB', 'The waters engulfed me to take my life; the watery depths closed around me; the seaweed wrapped around my head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.6', 'BSB', 'To the roots of the mountains I descended; the earth beneath me barred me in forever! But You raised my life from the pit, O LORD my God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.7', 'BSB', 'As my life was fading away, I remembered the LORD. My prayer went up to You, to Your holy temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.8', 'BSB', 'Those who cling to worthless idols forsake His loving devotion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.9', 'BSB', 'But I, with the voice of thanksgiving, will sacrifice to You. I will fulfill what I have vowed. Salvation is from the LORD!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.2.10', 'BSB', 'And the LORD commanded the fish, and it vomited Jonah onto dry land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.1', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Jonah a second time:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.2', 'BSB', '“Get up! Go to the great city of Nineveh and proclaim to it the message that I give you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.3', 'BSB', 'This time Jonah got up and went to Nineveh, in accordance with the word of the LORD. Now Nineveh was an exceedingly great city, requiring a three-day journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.4', 'BSB', 'On the first day of his journey, Jonah set out into the city and proclaimed, “Forty more days and Nineveh will be overturned!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.5', 'BSB', 'And the Ninevites believed God. They proclaimed a fast and dressed in sackcloth, from the greatest of them to the least.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.6', 'BSB', 'When word reached the king of Nineveh, he got up from his throne, took off his royal robe, covered himself with sackcloth, and sat in ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.7', 'BSB', 'Then he issued a proclamation in Nineveh: “By the decree of the king and his nobles: Let no man or beast, herd or flock, taste anything at all. They must not eat or drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.8', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, let both man and beast be covered with sackcloth, and have everyone call out earnestly to God. Let each one turn from his evil ways and from the violence in his hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.9', 'BSB', 'Who knows? God may turn and relent; He may turn from His fierce anger, so that we will not perish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.3.10', 'BSB', 'When God saw their actions—that they had turned from their evil ways—He relented from the disaster He had threatened to bring upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.1', 'BSB', 'Jonah, however, was greatly displeased, and he became angry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.2', 'BSB', 'So he prayed to the LORD, saying, “O LORD, is this not what I said while I was still in my own country? This is why I was so quick to flee toward Tarshish. I knew that You are a gracious and compassionate God, slow to anger, abounding in loving devotion—One who relents from sending disaster.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.3', 'BSB', 'And now, O LORD, please take my life from me, for it is better for me to die than to live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.4', 'BSB', 'But the LORD replied, “Have you any right to be angry?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.5', 'BSB', 'Then Jonah left the city and sat down east of it, where he made himself a shelter and sat in its shade to see what would happen to the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.6', 'BSB', 'So the LORD God appointed a vine, and it grew up to provide shade over Jonah’s head to ease his discomfort, and Jonah was greatly pleased with the plant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.7', 'BSB', 'When dawn came the next day, God appointed a worm that attacked the plant so that it withered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.8', 'BSB', 'As the sun was rising, God appointed a scorching east wind, and the sun beat down on Jonah’s head so that he grew faint and wished to die, saying, “It is better for me to die than to live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.9', 'BSB', 'Then God asked Jonah, “Have you any right to be angry about the plant?” “I do,” he replied. “I am angry enough to die!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.10', 'BSB', 'But the LORD said, “You cared about the plant, which you neither tended nor made grow. It sprang up in a night and perished in a night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jonah.4.11', 'BSB', 'So should I not care about the great city of Nineveh, which has more than 120,000 people who cannot tell their right hand from their left, and many cattle as well?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Micah the Moreshite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah—what he saw regarding Samaria and Jerusalem:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.2', 'BSB', 'Hear, O peoples, all of you; listen, O earth, and everyone in it! May the Lord GOD bear witness against you, the Lord from His holy temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.3', 'BSB', 'For behold, the LORD comes forth from His dwelling place; He will come down and tread on the high places of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.4', 'BSB', 'The mountains will melt beneath Him, and the valleys will split apart, like wax before the fire, like water rushing down a slope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.5', 'BSB', 'All this is for the transgression of Jacob and the sins of the house of Israel. What is the transgression of Jacob? Is it not Samaria? And what is the high place of Judah? Is it not Jerusalem?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will make Samaria a heap of rubble in the open field, a planting area for a vineyard. I will pour her stones into the valley and expose her foundations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.7', 'BSB', 'All her carved images will be smashed to pieces; all her wages will be burned in the fire, and I will destroy all her idols. Since she collected the wages of a prostitute, they will be used again on a prostitute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.8', 'BSB', 'Because of this I will lament and wail; I will walk barefoot and naked. I will howl like a jackal and mourn like an ostrich.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.9', 'BSB', 'For her wound is incurable; it has reached even Judah; it has approached the gate of my people, as far as Jerusalem itself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.10', 'BSB', 'Do not tell it in Gath; do not weep at all. Roll in the dust in Beth-leaphrah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.11', 'BSB', 'Depart in shameful nakedness, O dwellers of Shaphir. The dwellers of Zaanan will not come out. Beth-ezel is in mourning; its support is taken from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.12', 'BSB', 'For the dwellers of Maroth pined for good, but calamity came down from the LORD, even to the gate of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.13', 'BSB', 'Harness your chariot horses, O dweller of Lachish. You were the beginning of sin to the Daughter of Zion, for the transgressions of Israel were found in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore, send farewell gifts to Moresheth-gath; the houses of Achzib will prove deceptive to the kings of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.15', 'BSB', 'I will again bring a conqueror against you, O dweller of Mareshah. The glory of Israel will come to Adullam.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.1.16', 'BSB', 'Shave yourselves bald and cut off your hair in mourning for your precious children; make yourselves as bald as an eagle, for they will go from you into exile.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to those who devise iniquity and plot evil on their beds! At morning’s light they accomplish it because the power is in their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.2', 'BSB', 'They covet fields and seize them; they take away houses. They deprive a man of his home, a fellow man of his inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: “I am planning against this nation a disaster from which you cannot free your necks. Then you will not walk so proudly, for it will be a time of calamity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.4', 'BSB', 'In that day they will take up a proverb against you and taunt you with this bitter lamentation: ‘We are utterly ruined! He has changed the portion of my people. How He has removed it from me! He has allotted our fields to traitors.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore, you will have no one in the assembly of the LORD to divide the land by lot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.6', 'BSB', '“Do not preach,” they preach. “Do not preach these things; disgrace will not overtake us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.7', 'BSB', 'Should it be said, O house of Jacob, “Is the Spirit of the LORD impatient? Are these the things He does?” Do not My words bring good to him who walks uprightly?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.8', 'BSB', 'But of late My people have risen up like an enemy: You strip off the splendid robe from unsuspecting passersby like men returning from battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.9', 'BSB', 'You drive the women of My people from their pleasant homes. You take away My blessing from their children forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.10', 'BSB', 'Arise and depart, for this is not your place of rest, because its defilement brings destruction— a grievous destruction!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.11', 'BSB', 'If a man of wind were to come and say falsely, “I will preach to you of wine and strong drink,” he would be just the preacher for this people!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.12', 'BSB', 'I will surely gather all of you, O Jacob; I will collect the remnant of Israel. I will bring them together like sheep in a pen, like a flock in the midst of its pasture— a noisy throng.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.2.13', 'BSB', 'One who breaks open the way will go up before them; they will break through the gate, and go out by it. Their King will pass through before them, the LORD as their leader.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.1', 'BSB', 'Then I said: “Hear now, O leaders of Jacob, you rulers of the house of Israel. Should you not know justice?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.2', 'BSB', 'You hate good and love evil. You tear the skin from my people and strip the flesh from their bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.3', 'BSB', 'You eat the flesh of my people after stripping off their skin and breaking their bones. You chop them up like flesh for the cooking pot, like meat in a cauldron.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.4', 'BSB', 'Then they will cry out to the LORD, but He will not answer them. At that time He will hide His face from them because of the evil they have done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.5', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “As for the prophets who lead My people astray, who proclaim peace while they chew with their teeth, but declare war against one who puts nothing in their mouths:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore night will come over you without visions, and darkness without divination. The sun will set on these prophets, and the daylight will turn black over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.7', 'BSB', 'Then the seers will be ashamed and the diviners will be disgraced. They will all cover their mouths because there is no answer from God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.8', 'BSB', 'As for me, however, I am filled with power by the Spirit of the LORD, with justice and courage, to declare to Jacob his transgression and to Israel his sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.9', 'BSB', 'Now hear this, O leaders of the house of Jacob and rulers of the house of Israel, who despise justice and pervert all that is right,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.10', 'BSB', 'who build Zion with bloodshed and Jerusalem with iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.11', 'BSB', 'Her leaders judge for a bribe, her priests teach for a price, and her prophets practice divination for money. Yet they lean upon the LORD, saying, “Is not the LORD among us? No disaster can come upon us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.3.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, because of you, Zion will be plowed like a field, Jerusalem will become a heap of rubble, and the temple mount a wooded ridge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.1', 'BSB', 'In the last days the mountain of the house of the LORD will be established as the chief of the mountains; it will be raised above the hills, and the peoples will stream to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.2', 'BSB', 'And many nations will come and say: “Come, let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob. He will teach us His ways, so that we may walk in His paths.” For the law will go forth from Zion and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.3', 'BSB', 'Then He will judge between many peoples and arbitrate for strong nations far and wide. Then they will beat their swords into plowshares and their spears into pruning hooks. Nation will no longer take up the sword against nation, nor will they train anymore for war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.4', 'BSB', 'And each man will sit under his own vine and under his own fig tree, with no one to frighten him. For the mouth of the LORD of Hosts has spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.5', 'BSB', 'Though each of the peoples may walk in the name of his god, yet we will walk in the name of the LORD our God forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.6', 'BSB', '“On that day,” declares the LORD, “I will gather the lame; I will assemble the outcast, even those whom I have afflicted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.7', 'BSB', 'And I will make the lame into a remnant, and the outcast into a strong nation. Then the LORD will rule over them in Mount Zion from that day and forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.8', 'BSB', 'And you, O watchtower of the flock, O stronghold of the Daughter of Zion— the former dominion will be restored to you; sovereignty will come to the Daughter of Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.9', 'BSB', 'Why do you now cry aloud? Is there no king among you? Has your counselor perished so that anguish grips you like a woman in labor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.10', 'BSB', 'Writhe in agony, O Daughter of Zion, like a woman in labor. For now you will leave the city and camp in the open fields. You will go to Babylon; there you will be rescued; there the LORD will redeem you from the hand of your enemies!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.11', 'BSB', 'But now many nations have assembled against you, saying, “Let her be defiled, and let us feast our eyes on Zion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.12', 'BSB', 'But they do not know the thoughts of the LORD or understand His plan, for He has gathered them like sheaves to the threshing floor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.4.13', 'BSB', 'Rise and thresh, O Daughter of Zion, for I will give you horns of iron and hooves of bronze to break to pieces many peoples. Then you will devote their gain to the LORD, their wealth to the Lord of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.1', 'BSB', 'Now, O daughter of troops, mobilize your troops; for a siege is laid against us! With a rod they will strike the cheek of the judge of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.2', 'BSB', 'But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come forth for Me One to be ruler over Israel — One whose origins are of old, from the days of eternity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore Israel will be abandoned until she who is in labor has given birth; then the rest of His brothers will return to the children of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.4', 'BSB', 'He will stand and shepherd His flock in the strength of the LORD, in the majestic name of the LORD His God. And they will dwell securely, for then His greatness will extend to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.5', 'BSB', 'And He will be our peace when Assyria invades our land and tramples our citadels. We will raise against it seven shepherds, even eight leaders of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.6', 'BSB', 'And they will rule the land of Assyria with the sword, and the land of Nimrod with the blade drawn. So He will deliver us when Assyria invades our land and marches into our borders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.7', 'BSB', 'Then the remnant of Jacob will be in the midst of many peoples like dew from the LORD, like showers on the grass, which do not wait for man or linger for mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.8', 'BSB', 'Then the remnant of Jacob will be among the nations, in the midst of many peoples, like a lion among the beasts of the forest, like a young lion among flocks of sheep, which tramples and tears as it passes through, with no one to rescue them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.9', 'BSB', 'Your hand will be lifted over your foes, and all your enemies will be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.10', 'BSB', '“In that day,” declares the LORD, “I will remove your horses from among you and wreck your chariots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.11', 'BSB', 'I will remove the cities of your land and tear down all your strongholds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.12', 'BSB', 'I will cut the sorceries from your hand, and you will have no fortune-tellers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.13', 'BSB', 'I will also cut off the carved images and sacred pillars from among you, so that you will no longer bow down to the work of your own hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.14', 'BSB', 'I will root out the Asherah poles from your midst and demolish your cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.5.15', 'BSB', 'I will take vengeance in anger and wrath upon the nations that have not obeyed Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.1', 'BSB', 'Hear now what the LORD says: “Arise, plead your case before the mountains, and let the hills hear your voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.2', 'BSB', 'Hear, O mountains, the LORD’s indictment, you enduring foundations of the earth. For the LORD has a case against His people, and He will argue it against Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.3', 'BSB', '‘My people, what have I done to you? Testify against Me how I have wearied you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.4', 'BSB', 'For I brought you up from the land of Egypt and redeemed you from the house of slavery. I sent Moses before you, as well as Aaron and Miriam.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.5', 'BSB', 'My people, remember what Balak king of Moab counseled and what Balaam son of Beor answered. Remember your journey from Shittim to Gilgal, so that you may acknowledge the righteousness of the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.6', 'BSB', 'With what shall I come before the LORD when I bow before the God on high? Should I come to Him with burnt offerings, with year-old calves?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.7', 'BSB', 'Would the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams, with ten thousand rivers of oil? Shall I present my firstborn for my transgression, the fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.8', 'BSB', 'He has shown you, O man, what is good. And what does the LORD require of you but to act justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.9', 'BSB', 'The voice of the LORD calls out to the city (and it is sound wisdom to fear Your name): “Heed the rod and the One who ordained it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.10', 'BSB', 'Can I forget any longer, O house of the wicked, the treasures of wickedness and the short ephah, which is accursed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.11', 'BSB', 'Can I excuse dishonest scales or bags of false weights?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.12', 'BSB', 'For the wealthy of the city are full of violence, and its residents speak lies; their tongues are deceitful in their mouths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore I am striking you severely, to ruin you because of your sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.14', 'BSB', 'You will eat but not be satisfied, and your hunger will remain with you. What you acquire, you will not preserve; and what you save, I will give to the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.15', 'BSB', 'You will sow but not reap; you will press olives but not anoint yourselves with oil; you will tread grapes but not drink the wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.6.16', 'BSB', 'You have kept the statutes of Omri and all the practices of Ahab’s house; you have followed their counsel. Therefore I will make you a desolation, and your inhabitants an object of contempt; you will bear the scorn of the nations.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.1', 'BSB', 'Woe is me! For I am like one gathering summer fruit at the gleaning of the vineyard; there is no cluster to eat, no early fig that I crave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.2', 'BSB', 'The godly man has perished from the earth; there is no one upright among men. They all lie in wait for blood; they hunt one another with a net.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.3', 'BSB', 'Both hands are skilled at evil; the prince and the judge demand a bribe. When the powerful utters his evil desire, they all conspire together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.4', 'BSB', 'The best of them is like a brier; the most upright is sharper than a hedge of thorns. The day for your watchmen has come, the day of your visitation. Now is the time of their confusion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.5', 'BSB', 'Do not rely on a friend; do not trust in a companion. Seal the doors of your mouth from her who lies in your arms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.6', 'BSB', 'For a son dishonors his father, a daughter rises against her mother, and a daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law. A man’s enemies are the members of his own household.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.7', 'BSB', 'But as for me, I will look to the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation. My God will hear me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.8', 'BSB', 'Do not gloat over me, my enemy! Though I have fallen, I will arise; though I sit in darkness, the LORD will be my light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.9', 'BSB', 'Because I have sinned against Him, I must endure the rage of the LORD, until He argues my case and executes justice for me. He will bring me into the light; I will see His righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.10', 'BSB', 'Then my enemy will see and will be covered with shame— she who said to me, “Where is the LORD your God?” My eyes will see her; at that time she will be trampled like mud in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.11', 'BSB', 'The day for rebuilding your walls will come— the day for extending your boundary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.12', 'BSB', 'On that day they will come to you from Assyria and the cities of Egypt, even from Egypt to the Euphrates, from sea to sea and mountain to mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.13', 'BSB', 'Then the earth will become desolate because of its inhabitants, as the fruit of their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.14', 'BSB', 'Shepherd with Your staff Your people, the flock of Your inheritance. They live alone in a woodland, surrounded by pastures. Let them graze in Bashan and Gilead, as in the days of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.15', 'BSB', 'As in the days when you came out of Egypt, I will show My wonders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.16', 'BSB', 'Nations will see and be ashamed, deprived of all their might. They will put their hands over their mouths, and their ears will become deaf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.17', 'BSB', 'They will lick the dust like a snake, like reptiles slithering on the ground. They will crawl from their holes in the presence of the LORD our God; they will tremble in fear of You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.18', 'BSB', 'Who is a God like You, who pardons iniquity and passes over the transgression of the remnant of His inheritance— who does not retain His anger forever, because He delights in loving devotion?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.19', 'BSB', 'He will again have compassion on us; He will vanquish our iniquities. You will cast out all our sins into the depths of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mic.7.20', 'BSB', 'You will show faithfulness to Jacob and loving devotion to Abraham, as You swore to our fathers from the days of old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden against Nineveh, the book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.2', 'BSB', 'The LORD is a jealous and avenging God; the LORD is avenging and full of wrath. The LORD takes vengeance on His foes and reserves wrath for His enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.3', 'BSB', 'The LORD is slow to anger and great in power; the LORD will by no means leave the guilty unpunished. His path is in the whirlwind and storm, and clouds are the dust beneath His feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.4', 'BSB', 'He rebukes the sea and dries it up; He makes all the rivers run dry. Bashan and Carmel wither, and the flower of Lebanon wilts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.5', 'BSB', 'The mountains quake before Him, and the hills melt away; the earth trembles at His presence— the world and all its dwellers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.6', 'BSB', 'Who can withstand His indignation? Who can endure His burning anger? His wrath is poured out like fire; even rocks are shattered before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.7', 'BSB', 'The LORD is good, a stronghold in the day of distress; He cares for those who trust in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.8', 'BSB', 'But with an overwhelming flood He will make an end of Nineveh and pursue His enemies into darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.9', 'BSB', 'Whatever you plot against the LORD, He will bring to an end. Affliction will not rise up a second time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.10', 'BSB', 'For they will be entangled as with thorns and consumed like the drink of a drunkard— like stubble that is fully dry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.11', 'BSB', 'From you, O Nineveh, comes forth a plotter of evil against the LORD, a counselor of wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.12', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “Though they are allied and numerous, yet they will be cut down and pass away. Though I have afflicted you, O Judah, I will afflict you no longer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.13', 'BSB', 'For I will now break their yoke from your neck and tear away your shackles.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.14', 'BSB', 'The LORD has issued a command concerning you, O Nineveh: “There will be no descendants to carry on your name. I will cut off the carved image and cast idol from the house of your gods; I will prepare your grave, for you are contemptible.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.1.15', 'BSB', 'Look to the mountains— the feet of one who brings good news, who proclaims peace! Celebrate your feasts, O Judah; fulfill your vows. For the wicked will never again march through you; they will be utterly cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.1', 'BSB', 'One who scatters advances against you, O Nineveh. Guard the fortress! Watch the road! Brace yourselves! Summon all your strength!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.2', 'BSB', 'For the LORD will restore the splendor of Jacob like the splendor of Israel, though destroyers have laid them waste and ruined the branches of their vine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.3', 'BSB', 'The shields of his mighty men are red; the valiant warriors are dressed in scarlet. The fittings of the chariots flash like fire on the day they are prepared, and the spears of cypress have been brandished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.4', 'BSB', 'The chariots dash through the streets; they rush around the plazas, appearing like torches, darting about like lightning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.5', 'BSB', 'He summons his nobles; they stumble as they advance. They race to its wall; the protective shield is set in place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.6', 'BSB', 'The river gates are thrown open and the palace collapses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.7', 'BSB', 'It is decreed that the city be exiled and carried away; her maidservants moan like doves, and beat upon their breasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.8', 'BSB', 'Nineveh has been like a pool of water throughout her days, but now it is draining away. “Stop! Stop!” they cry, but no one turns back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.9', 'BSB', '“Plunder the silver! Plunder the gold!” There is no end to the treasure, an abundance of every precious thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.10', 'BSB', 'She is emptied! Yes, she is desolate and laid waste! Hearts melt, knees knock, bodies tremble, and every face grows pale!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.11', 'BSB', 'Where is the lions’ lair or the feeding ground of the young lions, where the lion and lioness prowled with their cubs, with nothing to frighten them away?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.12', 'BSB', 'The lion mauled enough for its cubs and strangled prey for the lioness. It filled its dens with the kill, and its lairs with mauled prey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.2.13', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am against you,” declares the LORD of Hosts. “I will send your chariots up in smoke, and the sword will devour your young lions. I will cut off your prey from the earth, and the voices of your messengers will no longer be heard.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to the city of blood, full of lies, full of plunder, never without prey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.2', 'BSB', 'The crack of the whip, the rumble of the wheel, galloping horse and bounding chariot!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.3', 'BSB', 'Charging horseman, flashing sword, shining spear; heaps of slain, mounds of corpses, dead bodies without end— they stumble over their dead—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.4', 'BSB', 'because of the many harlotries of the harlot, the seductive mistress of sorcery, who betrays nations by her prostitution and clans by her witchcraft.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.5', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am against you,” declares the LORD of Hosts. “I will lift your skirts over your face. I will show your nakedness to the nations and your shame to the kingdoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.6', 'BSB', 'I will pelt you with filth and treat you with contempt; I will make a spectacle of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.7', 'BSB', 'Then all who see you will recoil from you and say, ‘Nineveh is devastated; who will grieve for her?’ Where can I find comforters for you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.8', 'BSB', 'Are you better than Thebes, stationed by the Nile with water around her, whose rampart was the sea, whose wall was the water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.9', 'BSB', 'Cush and Egypt were her boundless strength; Put and Libya were her allies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.10', 'BSB', 'Yet she became an exile; she went into captivity. Her infants were dashed to pieces at the head of every street. They cast lots for her dignitaries, and all her nobles were bound in chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.11', 'BSB', 'You too will become drunk; you will go into hiding and seek refuge from the enemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.12', 'BSB', 'All your fortresses are fig trees with the first ripe figs; when shaken, they fall into the mouth of the eater!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.13', 'BSB', 'Look at your troops— they are like your women! The gates of your land are wide open to your enemies; fire consumes their bars.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.14', 'BSB', 'Draw your water for the siege; strengthen your fortresses. Work the clay and tread the mortar; repair the brick kiln!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.15', 'BSB', 'There the fire will devour you; the sword will cut you down and consume you like a young locust. Make yourself many like the young locust; make yourself many like the swarming locust!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.16', 'BSB', 'You have multiplied your merchants more than the stars of the sky. The young locust strips the land and flies away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.17', 'BSB', 'Your guards are like the swarming locust, and your scribes like clouds of locusts that settle on the walls on a cold day. When the sun rises, they fly away, and no one knows where.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.18', 'BSB', 'O king of Assyria, your shepherds slumber; your officers sleep. Your people are scattered on the mountains with no one to gather them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Nah.3.19', 'BSB', 'There is no healing for your injury; your wound is severe. All who hear the news of you applaud your downfall, for who has not experienced your constant cruelty?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden that Habakkuk the prophet received in a vision:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.2', 'BSB', 'How long, O LORD, must I call for help but You do not hear, or cry out to You, “Violence!” but You do not save?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.3', 'BSB', 'Why do You make me see iniquity? Why do You tolerate wrongdoing? Destruction and violence are before me. Strife is ongoing, and conflict abounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore the law is paralyzed, and justice never goes forth. For the wicked hem in the righteous, so that justice is perverted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.5', 'BSB', '“Look at the nations and observe— be utterly astounded! For I am doing a work in your days that you would never believe even if someone told you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.6', 'BSB', 'For behold, I am raising up the Chaldeans — that ruthless and impetuous nation which marches through the breadth of the earth to seize dwellings not their own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.7', 'BSB', 'They are dreaded and feared; from themselves they derive justice and sovereignty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.8', 'BSB', 'Their horses are swifter than leopards, fiercer than wolves of the night. Their horsemen charge ahead, and their cavalry comes from afar. They fly like a vulture, swooping down to devour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.9', 'BSB', 'All of them come bent on violence; their hordes advance like the east wind; they gather prisoners like sand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.10', 'BSB', 'They scoff at kings and make rulers an object of scorn. They laugh at every fortress and build up siege ramps to seize it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.11', 'BSB', 'Then they sweep by like the wind and pass on through. They are guilty; their own strength is their god.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.12', 'BSB', 'Are You not from everlasting, O LORD, my God, my Holy One? We will not die. O LORD, You have appointed them to execute judgment; O Rock, You have established them for correction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.13', 'BSB', 'Your eyes are too pure to look upon evil, and You cannot tolerate wrongdoing. So why do You tolerate the faithless? Why are You silent while the wicked swallow up those more righteous than themselves?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.14', 'BSB', 'You have made men like the fish of the sea, like creeping things that have no ruler.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.15', 'BSB', 'The foe pulls all of them up with a hook; he catches them in his dragnet, and gathers them in his fishing net; so he rejoices gladly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore he sacrifices to his dragnet and burns incense to his fishing net, for by these things his portion is sumptuous and his food is rich.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.1.17', 'BSB', 'Will he, therefore, empty his net and continue to slay nations without mercy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.1', 'BSB', 'I will stand at my guard post and station myself on the ramparts. I will watch to see what He will say to me, and how I should answer when corrected.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.2', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD answered me: “Write down this vision and clearly inscribe it on tablets, so that a herald may run with it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.3', 'BSB', 'For the vision awaits an appointed time; it testifies of the end and does not lie. Though it lingers, wait for it, since it will surely come and will not delay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.4', 'BSB', 'Look at the proud one; his soul is not upright — but the righteous will live by faith —', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.5', 'BSB', 'and wealth indeed betrays him. He is an arrogant man never at rest. He enlarges his appetite like Sheol, and like Death, he is never satisfied. He gathers all the nations to himself and collects all the peoples as his own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.6', 'BSB', 'Will not all of these take up a taunt against him, speaking with mockery and derision: ‘Woe to him who amasses what is not his and makes himself rich with many loans! How long will this go on?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.7', 'BSB', 'Will not your creditors suddenly arise and those who disturb you awaken? Then you will become their prey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.8', 'BSB', 'Because you have plundered many nations, the remnant of the people will plunder you— because of your bloodshed against man and your violence against the land, the city, and all their dwellers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.9', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who builds his house by unjust gain, to place his nest on high and escape the hand of disaster!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.10', 'BSB', 'You have plotted shame for your house by cutting off many peoples and forfeiting your life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.11', 'BSB', 'For the stones will cry out from the wall, and the rafters will echo it from the woodwork.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.12', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who builds a city with bloodshed and establishes a town by iniquity!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.13', 'BSB', 'Is it not indeed from the LORD of Hosts that the labor of the people only feeds the fire, and the nations weary themselves in vain?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.14', 'BSB', 'For the earth will be filled with the knowledge of the glory of the LORD as the waters cover the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.15', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who gives drink to his neighbors, pouring it from the wineskin until they are drunk, in order to gaze at their nakedness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.16', 'BSB', 'You will be filled with shame instead of glory. You too must drink and expose your uncircumcision! The cup in the LORD’s right hand will come around to you, and utter disgrace will cover your glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.17', 'BSB', 'For your violence against Lebanon will overwhelm you, and the destruction of animals will terrify you, because of your bloodshed against men and your violence against the land, the city, and all their dwellers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.18', 'BSB', 'What use is an idol, that a craftsman should carve it— or an image, a teacher of lies? For its maker trusts in his own creation; he makes idols that cannot speak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.19', 'BSB', 'Woe to him who says to wood, ‘Awake!’ or to silent stone, ‘Arise!’ Can it give guidance? Behold, it is overlaid with gold and silver, yet there is no breath in it at all.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.2.20', 'BSB', 'But the LORD is in His holy temple; let all the earth be silent before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.1', 'BSB', 'This is a prayer of Habakkuk the prophet, according to Shigionoth:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.2', 'BSB', 'O LORD, I have heard the report of You; I stand in awe, O LORD, of Your deeds. Revive them in these years; make them known in these years. In Your wrath, remember mercy!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.3', 'BSB', 'God came from Teman, and the Holy One from Mount Paran. Selah His glory covered the heavens, and His praise filled the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.4', 'BSB', 'His radiance was like the sunlight; rays flashed from His hand, where His power is hidden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.5', 'BSB', 'Plague went before Him, and fever followed in His steps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.6', 'BSB', 'He stood and measured the earth; He looked and startled the nations; the ancient mountains crumbled; the perpetual hills collapsed. His ways are everlasting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.7', 'BSB', 'I saw the tents of Cushan in distress; the curtains of Midian were trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.8', 'BSB', 'Were You angry at the rivers, O LORD? Was Your wrath against the streams? Did You rage against the sea when You rode on Your horses, on Your chariots of salvation?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.9', 'BSB', 'You brandished Your bow; You called for many arrows. Selah You split the earth with rivers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.10', 'BSB', 'The mountains saw You and quaked; torrents of water swept by. The deep roared with its voice and lifted its hands on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.11', 'BSB', 'Sun and moon stood still in their places at the flash of Your flying arrows, at the brightness of Your shining spear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.12', 'BSB', 'You marched across the earth with fury; You threshed the nations in wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.13', 'BSB', 'You went forth for the salvation of Your people, to save Your anointed. You crushed the head of the house of the wicked and stripped him from head to toe. Selah', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.14', 'BSB', 'With his own spear You pierced his head, when his warriors stormed out to scatter us, gloating as though ready to secretly devour the weak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.15', 'BSB', 'You trampled the sea with Your horses, churning the great waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.16', 'BSB', 'I heard and trembled within; my lips quivered at the sound. Decay entered my bones; I trembled where I stood. Yet I must wait patiently for the day of distress to come upon the people who invade us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.17', 'BSB', 'Though the fig tree does not bud and no fruit is on the vines, though the olive crop fails and the fields produce no food, though the sheep are cut off from the fold and no cattle are in the stalls,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.18', 'BSB', 'yet I will exult in the LORD; I will rejoice in the God of my salvation!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hab.3.19', 'BSB', 'GOD the Lord is my strength; He makes my feet like those of a deer; He makes me walk upon the heights! For the choirmaster. With stringed instruments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the word of the LORD that came to Zephaniah son of Cushi, the son of Gedaliah, the son of Amariah, the son of Hezekiah, in the days of Josiah son of Amon king of Judah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.2', 'BSB', '“I will completely sweep away everything from the face of the earth,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.3', 'BSB', '“I will sweep away man and beast; I will sweep away the birds of the air, and the fish of the sea, and the idols with their wicked worshipers. I will cut off mankind from the face of the earth,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.4', 'BSB', '“I will stretch out My hand against Judah and against all who dwell in Jerusalem. I will cut off from this place every remnant of Baal, the names of the idolatrous and pagan priests—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.5', 'BSB', 'those who bow on the rooftops to worship the host of heaven, those who bow down and swear by the LORD but also swear by Milcom,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.6', 'BSB', 'and those who turn back from following the LORD, neither seeking the LORD nor inquiring of Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.7', 'BSB', 'Be silent in the presence of the Lord GOD, for the Day of the LORD is near. Indeed, the LORD has prepared a sacrifice; He has consecrated His guests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.8', 'BSB', '“On the Day of the LORD’s sacrifice I will punish the princes, the sons of the king, and all who are dressed in foreign apparel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.9', 'BSB', 'On that day I will punish all who leap over the threshold, who fill the house of their master with violence and deceit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.10', 'BSB', 'On that day,” declares the LORD, “a cry will go up from the Fish Gate, a wail from the Second District, and a loud crashing from the hills.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.11', 'BSB', 'Wail, O dwellers of the Hollow, for all your merchants will be silenced; all who weigh out silver will be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.12', 'BSB', 'And at that time I will search Jerusalem with lamps and punish the men settled in complacency, who say to themselves, ‘The LORD will do nothing, either good or bad.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.13', 'BSB', 'Their wealth will be plundered and their houses laid waste. They will build houses but not inhabit them, and plant vineyards but never drink their wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.14', 'BSB', 'The great Day of the LORD is near— near and coming quickly. Listen, the Day of the LORD! Then the cry of the mighty will be bitter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.15', 'BSB', 'That day will be a day of wrath, a day of trouble and distress, a day of destruction and desolation, a day of darkness and gloom, a day of clouds and blackness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.16', 'BSB', 'a day of horn blast and battle cry against the fortified cities, and against the high corner towers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.17', 'BSB', 'I will bring such distress on mankind that they will walk like the blind, because they have sinned against the LORD. Their blood will be poured out like dust and their flesh like dung.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.1.18', 'BSB', 'Neither their silver nor their gold will be able to deliver them on the Day of the LORD’s wrath. The whole earth will be consumed by the fire of His jealousy.” For indeed, He will make a sudden end of all who dwell on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.1', 'BSB', 'Gather yourselves, gather together, O shameful nation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.2', 'BSB', 'before the decree takes effect and the day passes like chaff, before the burning anger of the LORD comes upon you, before the Day of the LORD’s anger comes upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.3', 'BSB', 'Seek the LORD, all you humble of the earth who carry out His justice. Seek righteousness; seek humility. Perhaps you will be sheltered on the day of the LORD’s anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.4', 'BSB', 'For Gaza will be abandoned, and Ashkelon left in ruins. Ashdod will be driven out at noon, and Ekron will be uprooted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.5', 'BSB', 'Woe to the dwellers of the seacoast, O nation of the Cherethites! The word of the LORD is against you, O Canaan, land of the Philistines: “I will destroy you, and no one will be left.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.6', 'BSB', 'So the seacoast will become a land of pastures, with wells for shepherds and folds for sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.7', 'BSB', 'The coast will belong to the remnant of the house of Judah; there they will find pasture. They will lie down in the evening among the houses of Ashkelon, for the LORD their God will attend to them and restore their captives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.8', 'BSB', '“I have heard the reproach of Moab and the insults of the Ammonites, who have taunted My people and threatened their borders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as surely as I live,” declares the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, “surely Moab will be like Sodom and the Ammonites like Gomorrah— a place of weeds and salt pits, a perpetual wasteland. The remnant of My people will plunder them; the remainder of My nation will dispossess them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.10', 'BSB', 'This they shall have in return for their pride, for taunting and mocking the people of the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.11', 'BSB', 'The LORD will be terrifying to them when He starves all the gods of the earth. Then the nations of every shore will bow in worship to Him, each in its own place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.12', 'BSB', '“You too, O Cushites, will be slain by My sword.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.13', 'BSB', 'And He will stretch out His hand against the north and destroy Assyria; He will make Nineveh a desolation, as dry as a desert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.14', 'BSB', 'Herds will lie down in her midst, creatures of every kind. Both the desert owl and screech owl will roost atop her pillars. Their calls will sound from the window, but desolation will lie on the threshold, for He will expose the beams of cedar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.2.15', 'BSB', 'This carefree city that dwells securely, that thinks to herself: “I am it, and there is none besides me,” what a ruin she has become, a resting place for beasts. Everyone who passes by her hisses and shakes his fist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.1', 'BSB', 'Woe to the city of oppressors, rebellious and defiled!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.2', 'BSB', 'She heeded no voice; she accepted no correction. She does not trust in the LORD; she has not drawn near to her God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.3', 'BSB', 'Her princes are roaring lions; her judges are evening wolves, leaving nothing for the morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.4', 'BSB', 'Her prophets are reckless, faithless men. Her priests profane the sanctuary; they do violence to the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.5', 'BSB', 'The LORD within her is righteous; He does no wrong. He applies His justice morning by morning; He does not fail at dawn, yet the unjust know no shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.6', 'BSB', '“I have cut off the nations; their corner towers are destroyed. I have made their streets deserted with no one to pass through. Their cities are laid waste, with no man, no inhabitant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.7', 'BSB', 'I said, ‘Surely you will fear Me and accept correction.’ Then her dwelling place would not be cut off despite all for which I punished her. But they rose early to corrupt all their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore wait for Me,” declares the LORD, “until the day I rise to testify. For My decision is to gather nations, to assemble kingdoms, to pour out upon them My indignation— all My burning anger. For all the earth will be consumed by the fire of My jealousy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.9', 'BSB', 'For then I will restore pure lips to the peoples, that all may call upon the name of the LORD and serve Him shoulder to shoulder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.10', 'BSB', 'From beyond the rivers of Cush My worshipers, My scattered people, will bring Me an offering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.11', 'BSB', 'On that day you will not be put to shame for any of the deeds by which you have transgressed against Me. For then I will remove from among you those who rejoice in their pride, and you will never again be haughty on My holy mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.12', 'BSB', 'But I will leave within you a meek and humble people, and they will trust in the name of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.13', 'BSB', 'The remnant of Israel will no longer do wrong or speak lies, nor will a deceitful tongue be found in their mouths. But they will feed and lie down, with no one to make them tremble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.14', 'BSB', 'Sing for joy, O Daughter of Zion; shout aloud, O Israel! Be glad and rejoice with all your heart, O Daughter of Jerusalem!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.15', 'BSB', 'The LORD has taken away your punishment; He has turned back your enemy. Israel’s King, the LORD, is among you; no longer will you fear any harm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.16', 'BSB', 'On that day they will say to Jerusalem: “Do not fear, O Zion; do not let your hands fall limp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.17', 'BSB', 'The LORD your God is among you; He is mighty to save. He will rejoice over you with gladness; He will quiet you with His love; He will rejoice over you with singing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.18', 'BSB', '“I will gather those among you who grieve over the appointed feasts, so that you will no longer suffer reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, at that time, I will deal with all who afflict you. I will save the lame and gather the scattered; and I will appoint praise and fame for the disgraced throughout the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zeph.3.20', 'BSB', 'At that time I will bring you in; yes, at that time I will gather you. For I will give you fame and praise among all the peoples of the earth when I restore your captives before your very eyes,” says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.1', 'BSB', 'In the second year of the reign of Darius, on the first day of the sixth month, the word of the LORD came through Haggai the prophet to Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest, stating', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.2', 'BSB', 'that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “These people say, ‘The time has not yet come to rebuild the house of the LORD.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.3', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came through Haggai the prophet, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.4', 'BSB', '“Is it a time for you yourselves to live in your paneled houses, while this house lies in ruins?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.5', 'BSB', 'Now this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Consider carefully your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.6', 'BSB', 'You have planted much but harvested little. You eat but never have enough. You drink but never have your fill. You put on clothes but never get warm. You earn wages to put into a bag pierced through.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.7', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Consider carefully your ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.8', 'BSB', 'Go up into the hills, bring down lumber, and build the house, so that I may take pleasure in it and be glorified, says the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.9', 'BSB', 'You expected much, but behold, it amounted to little. And what you brought home, I blew away. Why? declares the LORD of Hosts. Because My house still lies in ruins, while each of you is busy with his own house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore, on account of you the heavens have withheld their dew and the earth has withheld its crops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.11', 'BSB', 'I have summoned a drought on the fields and on the mountains, on the grain, new wine, and oil, and on whatever the ground yields, on man and beast, and on all the labor of your hands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.12', 'BSB', 'Then Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel and Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest, as well as all the remnant of the people, obeyed the voice of the LORD their God and the words of the prophet Haggai, because the LORD their God had sent him. So the people feared the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.13', 'BSB', 'Haggai, the messenger of the LORD, delivered the message of the LORD to the people: “I am with you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.14', 'BSB', 'So the LORD stirred the spirit of Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and the spirit of Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest, as well as the spirit of all the remnant of the people. And they came and began the work on the house of the LORD of Hosts, their God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.1.15', 'BSB', 'on the twenty-fourth day of the sixth month, in the second year of King Darius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.1', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-first day of the seventh month, the word of the LORD came through Haggai the prophet, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.2', 'BSB', '“Speak to Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and also to the remnant of the people. Ask them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.3', 'BSB', '‘Who is left among you who saw this house in its former glory? How does it look to you now? Does it not appear to you like nothing in comparison?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.4', 'BSB', 'But now be strong, O Zerubbabel, declares the LORD. Be strong, O Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest. And be strong, all you people of the land, declares the LORD. Work! For I am with you, declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.5', 'BSB', 'This is the promise I made to you when you came out of Egypt. And My Spirit remains among you; do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.6', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Once more, in a little while, I will shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.7', 'BSB', 'I will shake all the nations, and they will come with all their treasures, and I will fill this house with glory, says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.8', 'BSB', 'The silver is Mine, and the gold is Mine, declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.9', 'BSB', 'The latter glory of this house will be greater than the former, says the LORD of Hosts. And in this place I will provide peace, declares the LORD of Hosts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.10', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, in the second year of Darius, the word of the LORD came to Haggai the prophet, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.11', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Ask the priests for a ruling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.12', 'BSB', 'If a man carries consecrated meat in the fold of his garment, and it touches bread, stew, wine, oil, or any other food, does that item become holy?’” “No,” replied the priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.13', 'BSB', 'So Haggai asked, “If one who is defiled by contact with a corpse touches any of these, does it become defiled?” “Yes, it becomes defiled,” the priests answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.14', 'BSB', 'Then Haggai replied, “So it is with this people and this nation before Me, declares the LORD, and so it is with every work of their hands; whatever they offer there is defiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.15', 'BSB', 'Now consider carefully from this day forward: Before one stone was placed on another in the temple of the LORD,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.16', 'BSB', 'from that time, when one came expecting a heap of twenty ephahs of grain, there were but ten. When one came to the winepress to draw out fifty baths, there were but twenty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.17', 'BSB', 'I struck you—all the work of your hands—with blight, mildew, and hail, but you did not turn to Me, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.18', 'BSB', 'Consider carefully from this day forward—from the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, the day the foundation of the LORD’s temple was laid—consider carefully:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.19', 'BSB', 'Is there still seed in the barn? The vine, the fig, the pomegranate, and the olive tree have not yet yielded fruit. But from this day on, I will bless you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.20', 'BSB', 'For the second time that day, the twenty-fourth day of the month, the word of the LORD came to Haggai, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.21', 'BSB', '“Tell Zerubbabel governor of Judah that I am about to shake the heavens and the earth:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.22', 'BSB', 'I will overturn royal thrones and destroy the power of the kingdoms of the nations. I will overturn chariots and their riders; horses and their riders will fall, each by the sword of his brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Hag.2.23', 'BSB', 'On that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, I will take you, My servant, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, declares the LORD, and I will make you like My signet ring, for I have chosen you, declares the LORD of Hosts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.1', 'BSB', 'In the eighth month of the second year of Darius, the word of the LORD came to the prophet Zechariah son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.2', 'BSB', '“The LORD was very angry with your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.3', 'BSB', 'So tell the people that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Return to Me, declares the LORD of Hosts, and I will return to you, says the LORD of Hosts.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.4', 'BSB', 'Do not be like your fathers, to whom the former prophets proclaimed that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Turn now from your evil ways and deeds.’ But they did not listen or pay attention to Me, declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.5', 'BSB', 'Where are your fathers now? And the prophets, do they live forever?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.6', 'BSB', 'But did not My words and My statutes, which I commanded My servants the prophets, overtake your fathers? They repented and said, ‘Just as the LORD of Hosts purposed to do to us according to our ways and deeds, so He has done to us.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.7', 'BSB', 'On the twenty-fourth day of the eleventh month, the month of Shebat, in the second year of Darius, the word of the LORD came to the prophet Zechariah son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.8', 'BSB', 'I looked out into the night and saw a man riding on a red horse. He was standing among the myrtle trees in the hollow, and behind him were red, sorrel, and white horses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.9', 'BSB', '“What are these, my lord?” I asked. And the angel who was speaking with me replied, “I will show you what they are.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.10', 'BSB', 'Then the man standing among the myrtle trees explained, “They are the ones the LORD has sent to patrol the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.11', 'BSB', 'And the riders answered the angel of the LORD who was standing among the myrtle trees, “We have patrolled the earth, and behold, all the earth is at rest and tranquil.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.12', 'BSB', 'Then the angel of the LORD said, “How long, O LORD of Hosts, will You withhold mercy from Jerusalem and the cities of Judah, with which You have been angry these seventy years?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.13', 'BSB', 'So the LORD spoke kind and comforting words to the angel who was speaking with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.14', 'BSB', 'Then the angel who was speaking with me said, “Proclaim this word: This is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘I am very jealous for Jerusalem and Zion,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.15', 'BSB', 'but I am fiercely angry with the nations that are at ease. For I was a little angry, but they have added to the calamity.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore this is what the LORD says: ‘I will return to Jerusalem with mercy, and there My house will be rebuilt, declares the LORD of Hosts, and a measuring line will be stretched out over Jerusalem.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.17', 'BSB', 'Proclaim further that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘My cities will again overflow with prosperity; the LORD will again comfort Zion and choose Jerusalem.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.18', 'BSB', 'Then I looked up and saw four horns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.19', 'BSB', 'So I asked the angel who was speaking with me, “What are these?” And he told me, “These are the horns that have scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.20', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD showed me four craftsmen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.1.21', 'BSB', '“What are these coming to do?” I asked. And He replied, “These are the horns that scattered Judah so that no one could raise his head; but the craftsmen have come to terrify them and throw down these horns of the nations that have lifted up their horns against the land of Judah to scatter it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.1', 'BSB', 'Then I lifted up my eyes and saw a man with a measuring line in his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.2', 'BSB', '“Where are you going?” I asked. “To measure Jerusalem,” he replied, “and to determine its width and length.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.3', 'BSB', 'Then the angel who was speaking with me went out, and another angel came out to meet him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.4', 'BSB', 'and said to him, “Run and tell that young man: ‘Jerusalem will be a city without walls because of the multitude of men and livestock within it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.5', 'BSB', 'For I will be a wall of fire around it, declares the LORD, and I will be the glory within it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.6', 'BSB', '“Get up! Get up! Flee from the land of the north,” declares the LORD, “for I have scattered you like the four winds of heaven,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.7', 'BSB', '“Get up, O Zion! Escape, you who dwell with the Daughter of Babylon!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.8', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “After His Glory has sent Me against the nations that have plundered you—for whoever touches you touches the apple of His eye—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.9', 'BSB', 'I will surely wave My hand over them, so that they will become plunder for their own servants. Then you will know that the LORD of Hosts has sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.10', 'BSB', '“Shout for joy and be glad, O Daughter of Zion, for I am coming to dwell among you,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.11', 'BSB', '“On that day many nations will join themselves to the LORD, and they will become My people. I will dwell among you, and you will know that the LORD of Hosts has sent Me to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.12', 'BSB', 'And the LORD will take possession of Judah as His portion in the Holy Land, and He will once again choose Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.2.13', 'BSB', 'Be silent before the LORD, all people, for He has roused Himself from His holy dwelling.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.1', 'BSB', 'Then the angel showed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, with Satan standing at his right hand to accuse him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.2', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to Satan: “The LORD rebukes you, Satan! Indeed, the LORD, who has chosen Jerusalem, rebukes you! Is not this man a firebrand snatched from the fire?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.3', 'BSB', 'Now Joshua was dressed in filthy garments as he stood before the angel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.4', 'BSB', 'So the angel said to those standing before him, “Take off his filthy clothes!” Then he said to Joshua, “See, I have removed your iniquity, and I will clothe you with splendid robes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.5', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “Let them put a clean turban on his head.” So a clean turban was placed on his head, and they clothed him, as the angel of the LORD stood by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.6', 'BSB', 'Then the angel of the LORD gave this charge to Joshua:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.7', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘If you walk in My ways and keep My instructions, then you will govern My house and will also have charge of My courts; and I will give you a place among these who are standing here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.8', 'BSB', 'Hear now, O high priest Joshua, you and your companions seated before you, who are indeed a sign. For behold, I am going to bring My servant, the Branch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.9', 'BSB', 'See the stone I have set before Joshua; on that one stone are seven eyes. Behold, I will engrave on it an inscription, declares the LORD of Hosts, and I will remove the iniquity of this land in a single day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.3.10', 'BSB', 'On that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, you will each invite your neighbor to sit under your own vine and fig tree.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.1', 'BSB', 'Then the angel who was speaking with me returned and woke me, as a man is awakened from his sleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.2', 'BSB', '“What do you see?” he asked. “I see a solid gold lampstand,” I replied, “with a bowl at the top and seven lamps on it, with seven spouts to the lamps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.3', 'BSB', 'There are also two olive trees beside it, one on the right side of the bowl and the other on its left.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.4', 'BSB', '“What are these, my lord?” I asked the angel who was speaking with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.5', 'BSB', '“Do you not know what they are?” replied the angel. “No, my lord,” I answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.6', 'BSB', 'So he said to me, “This is the word of the LORD to Zerubbabel: Not by might nor by power, but by My Spirit, says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.7', 'BSB', 'What are you, O great mountain? Before Zerubbabel you will become a plain. Then he will bring forth the capstone accompanied by shouts of ‘Grace, grace to it!’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.8', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.9', 'BSB', '“The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house, and his hands will complete it. Then you will know that the LORD of Hosts has sent me to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.10', 'BSB', 'For who has despised the day of small things? But these seven eyes of the LORD, which scan the whole earth, will rejoice when they see the plumb line in the hand of Zerubbabel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.11', 'BSB', 'Then I asked the angel, “What are the two olive trees on the right and left of the lampstand?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.12', 'BSB', 'And I questioned him further, “What are the two olive branches beside the two gold pipes from which the golden oil pours?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.13', 'BSB', '“Do you not know what these are?” he inquired. “No, my lord,” I replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.4.14', 'BSB', 'So he said, “These are the two anointed ones who are standing beside the Lord of all the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.1', 'BSB', 'Again I lifted up my eyes and saw before me a flying scroll.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.2', 'BSB', '“What do you see?” asked the angel. “I see a flying scroll,” I replied, “twenty cubits long and ten cubits wide.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.3', 'BSB', 'Then he told me, “This is the curse that is going out over the face of all the land, for according to one side of the scroll, every thief will be removed; and according to the other side, every perjurer will be removed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.4', 'BSB', 'I will send it out, declares the LORD of Hosts, and it will enter the house of the thief and the house of him who swears falsely by My name. It will remain inside his house and destroy it, down to its timbers and stones.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.5', 'BSB', 'Then the angel who was speaking with me came forward and told me, “Now lift up your eyes and see what is approaching.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.6', 'BSB', '“What is it?” I asked. And he replied, “A measuring basket is going forth.” Then he continued, “This is their iniquity in all the land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.7', 'BSB', 'And behold, the cover of lead was raised, and there was a woman sitting inside the basket.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.8', 'BSB', '“This is Wickedness,” he said. And he shoved her down into the basket, pushing down the lead cover over its opening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.9', 'BSB', 'Then I lifted up my eyes and saw two women approaching, with the wind in their wings. Their wings were like those of a stork, and they lifted up the basket between heaven and earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.10', 'BSB', '“Where are they taking the basket?” I asked the angel who was speaking with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.5.11', 'BSB', '“To build a house for it in the land of Shinar,” he told me. “And when it is ready, the basket will be set there on its pedestal.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.1', 'BSB', 'And again I lifted up my eyes and saw four chariots coming out from between two mountains—mountains of bronze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.2', 'BSB', 'The first chariot had red horses, the second black horses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.3', 'BSB', 'the third white horses, and the fourth dappled horses—all of them strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.4', 'BSB', 'So I inquired of the angel who was speaking with me, “What are these, my lord?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.5', 'BSB', 'And the angel told me, “These are the four spirits of heaven, going forth from their station before the Lord of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.6', 'BSB', 'The one with the black horses is going toward the land of the north, the one with the white horses toward the west, and the one with the dappled horses toward the south.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.7', 'BSB', 'As the strong horses went out, they were eager to go and patrol the earth; and the LORD said, “Go and patrol the earth.” So they patrolled the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.8', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD summoned me and said, “Behold, those going to the land of the north have given rest to My Spirit in the land of the north.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.9', 'BSB', 'The word of the LORD also came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.10', 'BSB', '“Take an offering from the exiles—from Heldai, Tobijah, and Jedaiah, who have arrived from Babylon—and go that same day to the house of Josiah son of Zephaniah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.11', 'BSB', 'Take silver and gold, make an ornate crown, and set it on the head of the high priest, Joshua son of Jehozadak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.12', 'BSB', 'And you are to tell him that this is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Here is a man whose name is the Branch, and He will branch out from His place and build the temple of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.13', 'BSB', 'Yes, He will build the temple of the LORD; He will be clothed in splendor and will sit on His throne and rule. And He will be a priest on His throne, and there will be peaceful counsel between the two.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.14', 'BSB', 'The crown will reside in the temple of the LORD as a memorial to Helem, Tobijah, Jedaiah, and the gracious son of Zephaniah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.6.15', 'BSB', 'Even those far away will come and build the temple of the LORD, and you will know that the LORD of Hosts has sent Me to you. This will happen if you diligently obey the voice of the LORD your God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.1', 'BSB', 'In the fourth year of King Darius, the word of the LORD came to Zechariah on the fourth day of the ninth month, the month of Chislev.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.2', 'BSB', 'Now the people of Bethel had sent Sharezer and Regem-melech, along with their men, to plead before the LORD', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.3', 'BSB', 'by asking the priests of the house of the LORD of Hosts, as well as the prophets, “Should I weep and fast in the fifth month, as I have done these many years?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.4', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD of Hosts came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.5', 'BSB', '“Ask all the people of the land and the priests, ‘When you fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh months for these seventy years, was it really for Me that you fasted?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.6', 'BSB', 'And when you were eating and drinking, were you not doing so simply for yourselves?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.7', 'BSB', 'Are these not the words that the LORD proclaimed through the earlier prophets, when Jerusalem and its surrounding towns were populous and prosperous, and the Negev and the foothills were inhabited?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.8', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD came to Zechariah, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.9', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts says: ‘Administer true justice. Show loving devotion and compassion to one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.10', 'BSB', 'Do not oppress the widow or the fatherless, the foreigner or the poor. And do not plot evil in your hearts against one another.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.11', 'BSB', 'But they refused to pay attention and turned a stubborn shoulder; they stopped up their ears from hearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.12', 'BSB', 'They made their hearts like flint and would not listen to the law or to the words that the LORD of Hosts had sent by His Spirit through the earlier prophets. Therefore great anger came from the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.13', 'BSB', 'And just as I had called and they would not listen, so when they called I would not listen, says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.7.14', 'BSB', 'But I scattered them with a whirlwind among all the nations that they had not known, and the land was left desolate behind them so that no one could come or go. Thus they turned the pleasant land into a desolation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.1', 'BSB', 'Again the word of the LORD of Hosts came to me, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.2', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “I am jealous for Zion with great zeal; I am jealous for her with great fervor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.3', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD says: “I will return to Zion and dwell in Jerusalem. Then Jerusalem will be called the City of Truth, and the mountain of the LORD of Hosts will be called the Holy Mountain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.4', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Old men and old women will again sit along the streets of Jerusalem, each with a staff in hand because of great age.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.5', 'BSB', 'And the streets of the city will be filled with boys and girls playing there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.6', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “If this is impossible in the eyes of the remnant of this people in these days, should it also be impossible in My eyes?” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.7', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “I will save My people from the land of the east and from the land of the west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.8', 'BSB', 'I will bring them back to dwell in Jerusalem, where they will be My people, and I will be their faithful and righteous God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.9', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Let your hands be strong, you who now hear these words spoken by the prophets who were present when the foundations were laid to rebuild the temple, the house of the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.10', 'BSB', 'For before those days neither man nor beast received wages, nor was there safety from the enemy for anyone who came or went, for I had turned every man against his neighbor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.11', 'BSB', 'But now I will not treat the remnant of this people as I did in the past,” declares the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.12', 'BSB', '“For the seed will be prosperous, the vine will yield its fruit, the ground will yield its produce, and the skies will give their dew. To the remnant of this people I will give all these things as an inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.13', 'BSB', 'As you have been a curse among the nations, O house of Judah and house of Israel, so I will save you, and you will be a blessing. Do not be afraid; let your hands be strong.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.14', 'BSB', 'For this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Just as I resolved to bring disaster upon you when your fathers provoked Me to anger, and I did not relent,” says the LORD of Hosts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.15', 'BSB', '“so now I have resolved to do good again to Jerusalem and Judah. Do not be afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.16', 'BSB', 'These are the things you must do: Speak truth to one another, render true and sound judgments in your gates,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.17', 'BSB', 'do not plot evil in your hearts against your neighbor, and do not love to swear falsely, for I hate all these things,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.18', 'BSB', 'Then the word of the LORD of Hosts came to me, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.19', 'BSB', '“This is what the LORD of Hosts says: The fasts of the fourth, the fifth, the seventh, and the tenth months will become times of joy and gladness, cheerful feasts for the house of Judah. Therefore you are to love both truth and peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.20', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Peoples will yet come—the residents of many cities—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.21', 'BSB', 'and the residents of one city will go to another, saying: ‘Let us go at once to plead before the LORD and to seek the LORD of Hosts. I myself am going.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.22', 'BSB', 'And many peoples and strong nations will come to seek the LORD of Hosts in Jerusalem and to plead before the LORD.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.8.23', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD of Hosts says: “In those days ten men from the nations of every tongue will tightly grasp the robe of a Jew, saying, ‘Let us go with you, for we have heard that God is with you.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden of the word of the LORD against the land of Hadrach and Damascus its resting place— for the eyes of men and of all the tribes of Israel are upon the LORD —', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.2', 'BSB', 'and also against Hamath, which borders it, as well as Tyre and Sidon, though they are very shrewd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.3', 'BSB', 'Tyre has built herself a fortress; she has heaped up silver like dust, and gold like the dirt of the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.4', 'BSB', 'Behold, the Lord will impoverish her and cast her wealth into the sea, and she will be consumed by fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.5', 'BSB', 'Ashkelon will see and fear; Gaza will writhe in agony, as will Ekron, for her hope will wither. There will cease to be a king in Gaza, and Ashkelon will be uninhabited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.6', 'BSB', 'A mixed race will occupy Ashdod, and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.7', 'BSB', 'I will remove the blood from their mouths and the abominations from between their teeth. Then they too will become a remnant for our God; they will become like a clan in Judah, and Ekron will be like the Jebusites.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.8', 'BSB', 'But I will camp around My house because of an army, because of those who march to and fro, and never again will an oppressor overrun My people, for now I keep watch with My own eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.9', 'BSB', 'Rejoice greatly, O Daughter of Zion! Shout in triumph, O Daughter of Jerusalem! See, your King comes to you, righteous and victorious, humble and riding on a donkey, on a colt, the foal of a donkey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.10', 'BSB', 'And I will cut off the chariot from Ephraim and the horse from Jerusalem, and the bow of war will be broken. Then He will proclaim peace to the nations. His dominion will extend from sea to sea, and from the Euphrates to the ends of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.11', 'BSB', 'As for you, because of the blood of My covenant, I will release your prisoners from the waterless pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.12', 'BSB', 'Return to your stronghold, O prisoners of hope; even today I declare that I will restore to you double.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.13', 'BSB', 'For I will bend Judah as My bow and fit it with Ephraim. I will rouse your sons, O Zion, against the sons of Greece. I will make you like the sword of a mighty man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.14', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD will appear over them, and His arrow will go forth like lightning. The Lord GOD will sound the ram’s horn and advance in the whirlwinds of the south.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.15', 'BSB', 'The LORD of Hosts will shield them. They will destroy and conquer with slingstones; they will drink and roar as with wine. And they will be filled like sprinkling bowls, drenched like the corners of the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.16', 'BSB', 'On that day the LORD their God will save them as the flock of His people; for like jewels in a crown they will sparkle over His land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.9.17', 'BSB', 'How lovely they will be, and how beautiful! Grain will make the young men flourish, and new wine, the young women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.1', 'BSB', 'Ask the LORD for rain in springtime; the LORD makes the storm clouds, and He will give everyone showers of rain and crops in the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.2', 'BSB', 'For idols speak deceit and diviners see illusions; they tell false dreams and offer empty comfort. Therefore the people wander like sheep, oppressed for lack of a shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.3', 'BSB', '“My anger burns against the shepherds, and I will punish the leaders. For the LORD of Hosts attends to His flock, the house of Judah; He will make them like His royal steed in battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.4', 'BSB', 'The cornerstone will come from Judah, the tent peg from him, as well as the battle bow and every ruler together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.5', 'BSB', 'They will be like mighty men in battle, trampling the enemy in the mire of the streets. They will fight because the LORD is with them, and they will put the horsemen to shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.6', 'BSB', 'I will strengthen the house of Judah and save the house of Joseph. I will restore them because I have compassion on them, and they will be as though I had not rejected them. For I am the LORD their God, and I will answer them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.7', 'BSB', 'Ephraim will be like a mighty man, and their hearts will be glad as with wine. Their children will see it and be joyful; their hearts will rejoice in the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.8', 'BSB', 'I will whistle for them to gather, for I have redeemed them; and they will be as numerous as they once were.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.9', 'BSB', 'Though I sow them among the nations, they will remember Me in distant lands; they and their children will live and return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.10', 'BSB', 'I will bring them back from Egypt and gather them from Assyria. I will bring them to Gilead and Lebanon until no more room is found for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.11', 'BSB', 'They will pass through the sea of distress and strike the waves of the sea; all the depths of the Nile will dry up. The pride of Assyria will be brought down, and the scepter of Egypt will depart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.10.12', 'BSB', 'I will strengthen them in the LORD, and in His name they will walk,” declares the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.1', 'BSB', 'Open your doors, O Lebanon, that the fire may consume your cedars!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.2', 'BSB', 'Wail, O cypress, for the cedar has fallen; the majestic trees are ruined! Wail, O oaks of Bashan, for the dense forest has been cut down!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.3', 'BSB', 'Listen to the wailing of the shepherds, for their glory is in ruins. Listen to the roaring of the young lions, for the thickets of the Jordan are destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.4', 'BSB', 'This is what the LORD my God says: “Pasture the flock marked for slaughter,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.5', 'BSB', 'whose buyers slaughter them without remorse. Those who sell them say, ‘Blessed be the LORD, for I am rich!’ Even their own shepherds have no compassion on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.6', 'BSB', 'For I will no longer have compassion on the people of the land, declares the LORD, but behold, I will cause each man to fall into the hands of his neighbor and his king, who will devastate the land, and I will not deliver it from their hands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.7', 'BSB', 'So I pastured the flock marked for slaughter, especially the afflicted of the flock. Then I took for myself two staffs, calling one Favor and the other Union, and I pastured the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.8', 'BSB', 'And in one month I dismissed three shepherds. My soul grew impatient with the flock, and their souls also detested me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.9', 'BSB', 'Then I said, “I will no longer shepherd you. Let the dying die, and the perishing perish; and let those who remain devour one another’s flesh.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.10', 'BSB', 'Next I took my staff called Favor and cut it in two, revoking the covenant I had made with all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.11', 'BSB', 'It was revoked on that day, and so the afflicted of the flock who were watching me knew that it was the word of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.12', 'BSB', 'Then I told them, “If it seems right to you, give me my wages; but if not, keep them.” So they weighed out my wages, thirty pieces of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.13', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to me, “Throw it to the potter”—this magnificent price at which they valued me. So I took the thirty pieces of silver and threw them to the potter in the house of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.14', 'BSB', 'Then I cut in two my second staff called Union, breaking the brotherhood between Judah and Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.15', 'BSB', 'And the LORD said to me: “Take up once more the equipment of a foolish shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.16', 'BSB', 'For behold, I will raise up a shepherd in the land who will neither care for the lost, nor seek the young, nor heal the broken, nor sustain the healthy, but he will devour the flesh of the choice sheep and tear off their hooves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.11.17', 'BSB', 'Woe to the worthless shepherd, who deserts the flock! May a sword strike his arm and his right eye! May his arm be completely withered and his right eye utterly blinded!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden of the word of the LORD concerning Israel. Thus declares the LORD, who stretches out the heavens and lays the foundation of the earth, who forms the spirit of man within him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.2', 'BSB', '“Behold, I will make Jerusalem a cup of drunkenness to all the surrounding peoples. Judah will be besieged, as well as Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.3', 'BSB', 'On that day, when all the nations of the earth gather against her, I will make Jerusalem a heavy stone for all the peoples; all who would heave it away will be severely injured.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.4', 'BSB', 'On that day, declares the LORD, I will strike every horse with panic, and every rider with madness. I will keep a watchful eye on the house of Judah, but I will strike with blindness all the horses of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.5', 'BSB', 'Then the leaders of Judah will say in their hearts: ‘The people of Jerusalem are my strength, for the LORD of Hosts is their God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.6', 'BSB', 'On that day I will make the clans of Judah like a firepot in a woodpile, like a flaming torch among the sheaves; they will consume all the peoples around them on the right and on the left, while the people of Jerusalem remain secure there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.7', 'BSB', 'The LORD will save the tents of Judah first, so that the glory of the house of David and of the people of Jerusalem may not be greater than that of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.8', 'BSB', 'On that day the LORD will defend the people of Jerusalem, so that the weakest among them will be like David, and the house of David will be like God, like the angel of the LORD going before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.9', 'BSB', 'So on that day I will set out to destroy all the nations that come against Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.10', 'BSB', 'Then I will pour out on the house of David and on the people of Jerusalem a spirit of grace and prayer, and they will look on Me, the One they have pierced. They will mourn for Him as one mourns for an only child, and grieve bitterly for Him as one grieves for a firstborn son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.11', 'BSB', 'On that day the wailing in Jerusalem will be as great as the wailing of Hadad-rimmon in the plain of Megiddo.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.12', 'BSB', 'The land will mourn, each clan on its own: the clan of the house of David and their wives, the clan of the house of Nathan and their wives,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.13', 'BSB', 'the clan of the house of Levi and their wives, the clan of Shimei and their wives,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.12.14', 'BSB', 'and all the remaining clans and their wives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.1', 'BSB', '“On that day a fountain will be opened to the house of David and the people of Jerusalem, to cleanse them from sin and impurity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.2', 'BSB', 'And on that day, declares the LORD of Hosts, I will erase the names of the idols from the land, and they will no longer be remembered. I will also remove the prophets and the spirit of impurity from the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.3', 'BSB', 'And if anyone still prophesies, his father and mother who bore him will say to him, ‘You shall not remain alive, because you have spoken falsely in the name of the LORD.’ When he prophesies, his father and mother who bore him will pierce him through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.4', 'BSB', 'And on that day every prophet who prophesies will be ashamed of his vision, and he will not put on a hairy cloak in order to deceive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.5', 'BSB', 'He will say, ‘I am not a prophet; I work the land, for I was purchased as a servant in my youth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.6', 'BSB', 'If someone asks him, ‘What are these wounds on your chest?’ he will answer, ‘These are the wounds I received in the house of my friends.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.7', 'BSB', 'Awake, O sword, against My Shepherd, against the man who is My Companion, declares the LORD of Hosts. Strike the Shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered, and I will turn My hand against the little ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.8', 'BSB', 'And in all the land, declares the LORD, two-thirds will be cut off and perish, but a third will be left in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.13.9', 'BSB', 'This third I will bring through the fire; I will refine them like silver and test them like gold. They will call on My name, and I will answer them. I will say, ‘They are My people,’ and they will say, ‘The LORD is our God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.1', 'BSB', 'Behold, a day of the LORD is coming when your plunder will be divided in your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.2', 'BSB', 'For I will gather all the nations for battle against Jerusalem, and the city will be captured, the houses looted, and the women ravished. Half of the city will go into exile, but the rest of the people will not be removed from the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.3', 'BSB', 'Then the LORD will go out to fight against those nations, as He fights in the day of battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.4', 'BSB', 'On that day His feet will stand on the Mount of Olives, east of Jerusalem, and the Mount of Olives will be split in two from east to west, forming a great valley, with half the mountain moving to the north and half to the south.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.5', 'BSB', 'You will flee by My mountain valley, for it will extend to Azal. You will flee as you fled from the earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah. Then the LORD my God will come, and all the holy ones with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.6', 'BSB', 'On that day there will be no light, no cold or frost.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.7', 'BSB', 'It will be a day known only to the LORD, without day or night; but when evening comes, there will be light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.8', 'BSB', 'And on that day living water will flow out from Jerusalem, half of it toward the Eastern Sea and the other half toward the Western Sea, in summer and winter alike.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.9', 'BSB', 'On that day the LORD will become King over all the earth—the LORD alone, and His name alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.10', 'BSB', 'All the land from Geba to Rimmon south of Jerusalem will be turned into a plain, but Jerusalem will be raised up and will remain in her place, from the Benjamin Gate to the site of the First Gate to the Corner Gate, and from the Tower of Hananel to the royal winepresses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.11', 'BSB', 'People will live there, and never again will there be an utter destruction. So Jerusalem will dwell securely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.12', 'BSB', 'And this will be the plague with which the LORD strikes all the peoples who have warred against Jerusalem: Their flesh will rot while they stand on their feet, their eyes will rot in their sockets, and their tongues will rot in their mouths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.13', 'BSB', 'On that day a great panic from the LORD will come upon them, so that each will seize the hand of another, and the hand of one will rise against the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.14', 'BSB', 'Judah will also fight at Jerusalem, and the wealth of all the surrounding nations will be collected—gold, silver, and apparel in great abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.15', 'BSB', 'And a similar plague will strike the horses and mules, camels and donkeys, and all the animals in those camps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.16', 'BSB', 'Then all the survivors from the nations that came against Jerusalem will go up year after year to worship the King, the LORD of Hosts, and to celebrate the Feast of Tabernacles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.17', 'BSB', 'And should any of the families of the earth not go up to Jerusalem to worship the King, the LORD of Hosts, then the rain will not fall on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.18', 'BSB', 'And if the people of Egypt will not go up and enter in, then the rain will not fall on them; this will be the plague with which the LORD strikes the nations who do not go up to celebrate the Feast of Tabernacles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.19', 'BSB', 'This will be the punishment of Egypt and of all the nations that do not go up to celebrate the Feast of Tabernacles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.20', 'BSB', 'On that day, HOLY TO THE LORD will be inscribed on the bells of the horses, and the cooking pots in the house of the LORD will be like the sprinkling bowls before the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Zech.14.21', 'BSB', 'Indeed, every pot in Jerusalem and Judah will be holy to the LORD of Hosts, and all who sacrifice will come and take some pots and cook in them. And on that day there will no longer be a Canaanite in the house of the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the burden of the word of the LORD to Israel through Malachi:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.2', 'BSB', '“I have loved you,” says the LORD. But you ask, “How have You loved us?” “Was not Esau Jacob’s brother?” declares the LORD. “Yet Jacob I have loved,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.3', 'BSB', 'but Esau I have hated, and I have made his mountains a wasteland and left his inheritance to the desert jackals.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.4', 'BSB', 'Though Edom may say, “We have been devastated, but we will rebuild the ruins,” this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “They may build, but I will demolish. They will be called the Land of Wickedness, and a people with whom the LORD is indignant forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.5', 'BSB', 'You will see this with your own eyes, and you yourselves will say, ‘The LORD is great—even beyond the borders of Israel.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.6', 'BSB', '“A son honors his father, and a servant his master. But if I am a father, where is My honor? And if I am a master, where is your fear of Me?” says the LORD of Hosts to you priests who despise My name. “But you ask, ‘How have we despised Your name?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.7', 'BSB', 'By presenting defiled food on My altar. But you ask, ‘How have we defiled You?’ By saying that the table of the LORD is contemptible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.8', 'BSB', 'When you offer blind animals for sacrifice, is it not wrong? And when you present the lame and sick ones, is it not wrong? Try offering them to your governor! Would he be pleased with you or show you favor?” asks the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.9', 'BSB', '“But ask now for God’s favor. Will He be gracious? Since this has come from your hands, will He show you favor?” asks the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.10', 'BSB', '“Oh, that one of you would shut the temple doors, so that you would no longer kindle useless fires on My altar! I take no pleasure in you,” says the LORD of Hosts, “and I will accept no offering from your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.11', 'BSB', 'For My name will be great among the nations, from where the sun rises to where it sets. In every place, incense and pure offerings will be presented in My name, because My name will be great among the nations,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.12', 'BSB', '“But you profane it when you say, ‘The table of the Lord is defiled, and as for its fruit, its food is contemptible.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.13', 'BSB', 'You also say: ‘Oh, what a nuisance!’ And you turn up your nose at it,” says the LORD of Hosts. “You bring offerings that are stolen, lame, or sick! Should I accept these from your hands?” asks the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.1.14', 'BSB', '“But cursed is the deceiver who has an acceptable male in his flock and vows to give it, but sacrifices a defective animal to the Lord. For I am a great King,” says the LORD of Hosts, “and My name is to be feared among the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.1', 'BSB', '“And now this decree is for you, O priests:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.2', 'BSB', 'If you do not listen, and if you do not take it to heart to honor My name,” says the LORD of Hosts, “I will send a curse among you, and I will curse your blessings. Yes, I have already begun to curse them, because you are not taking it to heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.3', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will rebuke your descendants, and I will spread dung on your faces, the waste from your feasts, and you will be carried off with it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.4', 'BSB', 'Then you will know that I have sent you this commandment so that My covenant with Levi may continue,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.5', 'BSB', '“My covenant with him was one of life and peace, which I gave to him; it called for reverence, and he revered Me and stood in awe of My name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.6', 'BSB', 'True instruction was in his mouth, and nothing false was found on his lips. He walked with Me in peace and uprightness, and he turned many from iniquity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.7', 'BSB', 'For the lips of a priest should preserve knowledge, and people should seek instruction from his mouth, because he is the messenger of the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.8', 'BSB', 'But you have departed from the way, and your instruction has caused many to stumble. You have violated the covenant of Levi,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.9', 'BSB', '“So I in turn have made you despised and humiliated before all the people, because you have not kept My ways, but have shown partiality in matters of the law.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.10', 'BSB', 'Do we not all have one Father? Did not one God create us? Why then do we break faith with one another so as to profane the covenant of our fathers?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.11', 'BSB', 'Judah has broken faith; an abomination has been committed in Israel and in Jerusalem. For Judah has profaned the LORD’s beloved sanctuary by marrying the daughter of a foreign god.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.12', 'BSB', 'As for the man who does this, may the LORD cut off from the tents of Jacob everyone who is awake and aware—even if he brings an offering to the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.13', 'BSB', 'And this is another thing you do: You cover the altar of the LORD with tears, with weeping and groaning, because He no longer regards your offerings or receives them gladly from your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.14', 'BSB', 'Yet you ask, “Why?” It is because the LORD has been a witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have broken faith, though she is your companion and your wife by covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.15', 'BSB', 'Has not the LORD made them one, having a portion of the Spirit? And why one? Because He seeks godly offspring. So guard yourselves in your spirit and do not break faith with the wife of your youth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.16', 'BSB', '“For I hate divorce,” says the LORD, the God of Israel. “He who divorces his wife covers his garment with violence,” says the LORD of Hosts. So guard yourselves in your spirit and do not break faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.2.17', 'BSB', 'You have wearied the LORD with your words; yet you ask, “How have we wearied Him?” By saying, “All who do evil are good in the sight of the LORD, and in them He delights,” or, “Where is the God of justice?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.1', 'BSB', '“Behold, I will send My messenger, who will prepare the way before Me. Then the Lord whom you seek will suddenly come to His temple—the Messenger of the covenant, in whom you delight—see, He is coming,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.2', 'BSB', 'But who can endure the day of His coming? And who can stand when He appears? For He will be like a refiner’s fire, like a launderer’s soap.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.3', 'BSB', 'And He will sit as a refiner and purifier of silver; He will purify the sons of Levi and refine them like gold and silver. Then they will present offerings to the LORD in righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.4', 'BSB', 'Then the offerings of Judah and Jerusalem will please the LORD, as in days of old and years gone by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.5', 'BSB', '“Then I will draw near to you for judgment. And I will be a swift witness against sorcerers and adulterers and perjurers, against oppressors of the widowed and fatherless, and against those who defraud laborers of their wages and deny justice to the foreigner but do not fear Me,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.6', 'BSB', '“Because I, the LORD, do not change, you descendants of Jacob have not been destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.7', 'BSB', 'Yet from the days of your fathers, you have turned away from My statutes and have not kept them. Return to Me, and I will return to you,” says the LORD of Hosts. “But you ask, ‘How can we return?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.8', 'BSB', 'Will a man rob God? Yet you are robbing Me! But you ask, ‘How do we rob You?’ In tithes and offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.9', 'BSB', 'You are cursed with a curse, yet you—the whole nation—are still robbing Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.10', 'BSB', 'Bring the full tithe into the storehouse, so that there may be food in My house. Test Me in this,” says the LORD of Hosts. “See if I will not open the windows of heaven and pour out for you blessing without measure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.11', 'BSB', 'I will rebuke the devourer for you, so that it will not destroy the fruits of your land, and the vine in your field will not fail to produce fruit,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.12', 'BSB', '“Then all the nations will call you blessed, for you will be a land of delight,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.13', 'BSB', '“Your words against Me have been harsh,” says the LORD. “Yet you ask, ‘What have we spoken against You?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.14', 'BSB', 'You have said, ‘It is futile to serve God. What have we gained by keeping His requirements and walking mournfully before the LORD of Hosts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.15', 'BSB', 'So now we call the arrogant blessed. Not only do evildoers prosper, they even test God and escape.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.16', 'BSB', 'At that time those who feared the LORD spoke with one another, and the LORD listened and heard them. So a scroll of remembrance was written before Him regarding those who feared the LORD and honored His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.17', 'BSB', '“They will be Mine,” says the LORD of Hosts, “on the day when I prepare My treasured possession. And I will spare them as a man spares his own son who serves him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.3.18', 'BSB', 'So you will again distinguish between the righteous and the wicked, between those who serve God and those who do not.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.1', 'BSB', '“For behold, the day is coming, burning like a furnace, when all the arrogant and every evildoer will be stubble; the day is coming when I will set them ablaze,” says the LORD of Hosts. “Not a root or branch will be left to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.2', 'BSB', '“But for you who fear My name, the sun of righteousness will rise with healing in its wings, and you will go out and leap like calves from the stall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.3', 'BSB', 'Then you will trample the wicked, for they will be ashes under the soles of your feet on the day I am preparing,” says the LORD of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.4', 'BSB', '“Remember the law of My servant Moses, the statutes and ordinances I commanded him for all Israel at Horeb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.5', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and awesome Day of the LORD.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mal.4.6', 'BSB', 'And he will turn the hearts of the fathers to their children, and the hearts of the children to their fathers. Otherwise, I will come and strike the land with a curse.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the record of the genealogy of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.2', 'BSB', 'Abraham was the father of Isaac, Isaac the father of Jacob, and Jacob the father of Judah and his brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.3', 'BSB', 'Judah was the father of Perez and Zerah by Tamar, Perez the father of Hezron, and Hezron the father of Ram.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.4', 'BSB', 'Ram was the father of Amminadab, Amminadab the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon the father of Salmon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.5', 'BSB', 'Salmon was the father of Boaz by Rahab, Boaz the father of Obed by Ruth, Obed the father of Jesse,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.6', 'BSB', 'and Jesse the father of David the king. Next: David was the father of Solomon by Uriah’s wife,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.7', 'BSB', 'Solomon the father of Rehoboam, Rehoboam the father of Abijah, and Abijah the father of Asa.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.8', 'BSB', 'Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat, Jehoshaphat the father of Joram, and Joram the father of Uzziah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.9', 'BSB', 'Uzziah was the father of Jotham, Jotham the father of Ahaz, and Ahaz the father of Hezekiah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.10', 'BSB', 'Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh, Manasseh the father of Amon, Amon the father of Josiah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.11', 'BSB', 'and Josiah the father of Jeconiah and his brothers at the time of the exile to Babylon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.12', 'BSB', 'After the exile to Babylon: Jeconiah was the father of Shealtiel, Shealtiel the father of Zerubbabel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.13', 'BSB', 'Zerubbabel the father of Abiud, Abiud the father of Eliakim, and Eliakim the father of Azor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.14', 'BSB', 'Azor was the father of Zadok, Zadok the father of Achim, and Achim the father of Eliud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.15', 'BSB', 'Eliud was the father of Eleazar, Eleazar the father of Matthan, Matthan the father of Jacob,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.16', 'BSB', 'and Jacob the father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.17', 'BSB', 'In all, then, there were fourteen generations from Abraham to David, fourteen from David to the exile to Babylon, and fourteen from the exile to the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.18', 'BSB', 'This is how the birth of Jesus Christ came about: His mother Mary was pledged in marriage to Joseph, but before they came together, she was found to be with child through the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.19', 'BSB', 'Because Joseph her husband was a righteous man and was unwilling to disgrace her publicly, he resolved to divorce her quietly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.20', 'BSB', 'But after he had pondered these things, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said, “Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to embrace Mary as your wife, for the One conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.21', 'BSB', 'She will give birth to a Son, and you are to give Him the name Jesus, because He will save His people from their sins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.22', 'BSB', 'All this took place to fulfill what the Lord had said through the prophet:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.23', 'BSB', '“Behold, the virgin will be with child and will give birth to a son, and they will call Him Immanuel” (which means, “God with us” ).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.24', 'BSB', 'When Joseph woke up, he did as the angel of the Lord had commanded him, and embraced Mary as his wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.1.25', 'BSB', 'But he had no union with her until she gave birth to a Son. And he gave Him the name Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.1', 'BSB', 'After Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea, during the time of King Herod, Magi from the east arrived in Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.2', 'BSB', 'asking, “Where is the One who has been born King of the Jews? We saw His star in the east and have come to worship Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.3', 'BSB', 'When King Herod heard this, he was disturbed, and all Jerusalem with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.4', 'BSB', 'And when he had assembled all the chief priests and scribes of the people, he asked them where the Christ was to be born.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.5', 'BSB', '“In Bethlehem in Judea,” they replied, “for this is what the prophet has written:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.6', 'BSB', '‘But you, Bethlehem, in the land of Judah, are by no means least among the rulers of Judah, for out of you will come a ruler who will be the shepherd of My people Israel.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.7', 'BSB', 'Then Herod called the Magi secretly and learned from them the exact time the star had appeared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.8', 'BSB', 'And sending them to Bethlehem, he said: “Go and search carefully for the Child, and when you find Him, report to me, so that I too may go and worship Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.9', 'BSB', 'After they had heard the king, they went on their way, and the star they had seen in the east went ahead of them until it stood over the place where the Child was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.10', 'BSB', 'When they saw the star, they rejoiced with great delight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.11', 'BSB', 'On coming to the house, they saw the Child with His mother Mary, and they fell down and worshiped Him. Then they opened their treasures and presented Him with gifts of gold and frankincense and myrrh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.12', 'BSB', 'And having been warned in a dream not to return to Herod, they withdrew to their country by another route.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.13', 'BSB', 'When the Magi had gone, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream. “Get up!” he said. “Take the Child and His mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you, for Herod is going to search for the Child to kill Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.14', 'BSB', 'So he got up, took the Child and His mother by night, and withdrew to Egypt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.15', 'BSB', 'where he stayed until the death of Herod. This fulfilled what the Lord had spoken through the prophet: “Out of Egypt I called My Son.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.16', 'BSB', 'When Herod saw that he had been outwitted by the Magi, he was filled with rage. Sending orders, he put to death all the boys in Bethlehem and its vicinity who were two years old and under, according to the time he had learned from the Magi.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.17', 'BSB', 'Then what was spoken through the prophet Jeremiah was fulfilled:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.18', 'BSB', '“A voice is heard in Ramah, weeping and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children, and refusing to be comforted, because they are no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.19', 'BSB', 'After Herod died, an angel of the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.20', 'BSB', '“Get up!” he said. “Take the Child and His mother and go to the land of Israel, for those seeking the Child’s life are now dead.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.21', 'BSB', 'So Joseph got up, took the Child and His mother, and went to the land of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.22', 'BSB', 'But when he learned that Archelaus was reigning in Judea in place of his father Herod, he was afraid to go there. And having been warned in a dream, he withdrew to the district of Galilee,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.2.23', 'BSB', 'and he went and lived in a town called Nazareth. So was fulfilled what was spoken through the prophets: “He will be called a Nazarene.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.1', 'BSB', 'In those days John the Baptist came, preaching in the wilderness of Judea', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.2', 'BSB', 'and saying, “Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is near.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.3', 'BSB', 'This is he who was spoken of through the prophet Isaiah: “A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.4', 'BSB', 'John wore a garment of camel’s hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.5', 'BSB', 'People went out to him from Jerusalem and all Judea and the whole region around the Jordan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.6', 'BSB', 'Confessing their sins, they were baptized by him in the Jordan River.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.7', 'BSB', 'But when John saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming to his place of baptism, he said to them, “You brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the coming wrath?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.8', 'BSB', 'Produce fruit, then, in keeping with repentance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.9', 'BSB', 'And do not presume to say to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham as our father.’ For I tell you that out of these stones God can raise up children for Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.10', 'BSB', 'The axe lies ready at the root of the trees, and every tree that does not produce good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.11', 'BSB', 'I baptize you with water for repentance, but after me will come One more powerful than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.12', 'BSB', 'His winnowing fork is in His hand to clear His threshing floor and to gather His wheat into the barn; but He will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.13', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to be baptized by John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.14', 'BSB', 'But John tried to prevent Him, saying, “I need to be baptized by You, and do You come to me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.15', 'BSB', '“Let it be so now,” Jesus replied. “It is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness in this way.” Then John permitted Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.16', 'BSB', 'As soon as Jesus was baptized, He went up out of the water. Suddenly the heavens were opened, and He saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and resting on Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.3.17', 'BSB', 'And a voice from heaven said, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.2', 'BSB', 'After fasting forty days and forty nights, He was hungry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.3', 'BSB', 'The tempter came to Him and said, “If You are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.4', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone, but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.5', 'BSB', 'Then the devil took Him to the holy city and set Him on the pinnacle of the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.6', 'BSB', '“If You are the Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down. For it is written: ‘He will command His angels concerning You, and they will lift You up in their hands, so that You will not strike Your foot against a stone.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.7', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “It is also written: ‘Do not put the Lord your God to the test.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.8', 'BSB', 'Again, the devil took Him to a very high mountain and showed Him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.9', 'BSB', '“All this I will give You,” he said, “if You will fall down and worship me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.10', 'BSB', '“Away from Me, Satan!” Jesus declared. “For it is written: ‘Worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.11', 'BSB', 'Then the devil left Him, and angels came and ministered to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.12', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard that John had been imprisoned, He withdrew to Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.13', 'BSB', 'Leaving Nazareth, He went and lived in Capernaum, which is by the sea in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.14', 'BSB', 'to fulfill what was spoken through the prophet Isaiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.15', 'BSB', '“Land of Zebulun and land of Naphtali, the Way of the Sea, beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.16', 'BSB', 'the people living in darkness have seen a great light; on those living in the land of the shadow of death, a light has dawned.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.17', 'BSB', 'From that time on Jesus began to preach, “Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is near.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.18', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw two brothers, Simon called Peter and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.19', 'BSB', '“Come, follow Me,” Jesus said, “and I will make you fishers of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.20', 'BSB', 'And at once they left their nets and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.21', 'BSB', 'Going on from there, He saw two other brothers, James son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat with their father Zebedee, mending their nets. Jesus called them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.22', 'BSB', 'and immediately they left the boat and their father and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus went throughout Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every disease and sickness among the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.24', 'BSB', 'News about Him spread all over Syria, and people brought to Him all who were ill with various diseases, those suffering acute pain, the demon-possessed, those having seizures, and the paralyzed—and He healed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.4.25', 'BSB', 'The large crowds that followed Him came from Galilee, the Decapolis, Jerusalem, Judea, and beyond the Jordan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw the crowds, He went up on the mountain and sat down. His disciples came to Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.2', 'BSB', 'and He began to teach them, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.3', 'BSB', '“Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.4', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who mourn, for they will be comforted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.5', 'BSB', 'Blessed are the meek, for they will inherit the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.6', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they will be filled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.7', 'BSB', 'Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.8', 'BSB', 'Blessed are the pure in heart, for they will see God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.9', 'BSB', 'Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called sons of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.10', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who are persecuted because of righteousness, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.11', 'BSB', 'Blessed are you when people insult you, persecute you, and falsely say all kinds of evil against you because of Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.12', 'BSB', 'Rejoice and be glad, because great is your reward in heaven; for in the same way they persecuted the prophets before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.13', 'BSB', 'You are the salt of the earth. But if the salt loses its savor, how can it be made salty again? It is no longer good for anything, except to be thrown out and trampled by men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.14', 'BSB', 'You are the light of the world. A city on a hill cannot be hidden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.15', 'BSB', 'Neither do people light a lamp and put it under a basket. Instead, they set it on a stand, and it gives light to everyone in the house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.16', 'BSB', 'In the same way, let your light shine before men, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.17', 'BSB', 'Do not think that I have come to abolish the Law or the Prophets. I have not come to abolish them, but to fulfill them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.18', 'BSB', 'For I tell you truly, until heaven and earth pass away, not a single jot, not a stroke of a pen, will disappear from the Law until everything is accomplished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.19', 'BSB', 'So then, whoever breaks one of the least of these commandments and teaches others to do likewise will be called least in the kingdom of heaven; but whoever practices and teaches them will be called great in the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.20', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that unless your righteousness exceeds that of the scribes and Pharisees, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.21', 'BSB', 'You have heard that it was said to the ancients, ‘Do not murder’ and ‘Anyone who murders will be subject to judgment.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.22', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that anyone who is angry with his brother will be subject to judgment. Again, anyone who says to his brother, ‘Raca,’ will be subject to the Sanhedrin. But anyone who says, ‘You fool!’ will be subject to the fire of hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.23', 'BSB', 'So if you are offering your gift at the altar and there remember that your brother has something against you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.24', 'BSB', 'leave your gift there before the altar. First go and be reconciled to your brother; then come and offer your gift.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.25', 'BSB', 'Reconcile quickly with your adversary, while you are still on the way to court. Otherwise, he may hand you over to the judge, and the judge may hand you over to the officer, and you may be thrown into prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.26', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, you will not get out until you have paid the last penny.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.27', 'BSB', 'You have heard that it was said, ‘Do not commit adultery.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.28', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that anyone who looks at a woman to lust after her has already committed adultery with her in his heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.29', 'BSB', 'If your right eye causes you to sin, gouge it out and throw it away. It is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to be thrown into hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.30', 'BSB', 'And if your right hand causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. It is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to depart into hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.31', 'BSB', 'It has also been said, ‘Whoever divorces his wife must give her a certificate of divorce.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.32', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that anyone who divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, brings adultery upon her. And he who marries a divorced woman commits adultery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.33', 'BSB', 'Again, you have heard that it was said to the ancients, ‘Do not break your oath, but fulfill your vows to the Lord.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.34', 'BSB', 'But I tell you not to swear at all: either by heaven, for it is God’s throne;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.35', 'BSB', 'or by the earth, for it is His footstool; or by Jerusalem, for it is the city of the great King.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.36', 'BSB', 'Nor should you swear by your head, for you cannot make a single hair white or black.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.37', 'BSB', 'Simply let your ‘Yes’ be ‘Yes,’ and your ‘No,’ ‘No.’ Anything more comes from the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.38', 'BSB', 'You have heard that it was said, ‘Eye for eye and tooth for tooth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.39', 'BSB', 'But I tell you not to resist an evil person. If someone slaps you on your right cheek, turn to him the other also;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.40', 'BSB', 'if someone wants to sue you and take your tunic, let him have your cloak as well;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.41', 'BSB', 'and if someone forces you to go one mile, go with him two miles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.42', 'BSB', 'Give to the one who asks you, and do not turn away from the one who wants to borrow from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.43', 'BSB', 'You have heard that it was said, ‘Love your neighbor’ and ‘Hate your enemy.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.44', 'BSB', 'But I tell you, love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.45', 'BSB', 'that you may be sons of your Father in heaven. He causes His sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the righteous and the unrighteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.46', 'BSB', 'If you love those who love you, what reward will you get? Do not even tax collectors do the same?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.47', 'BSB', 'And if you greet only your brothers, what are you doing more than others? Do not even Gentiles do the same?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.5.48', 'BSB', 'Be perfect, therefore, as your heavenly Father is perfect.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.1', 'BSB', '“Be careful not to perform your righteous acts before men to be seen by them. If you do, you will have no reward from your Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.2', 'BSB', 'So when you give to the needy, do not sound a trumpet before you, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and on the streets, to be honored by men. Truly I tell you, they already have their full reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.3', 'BSB', 'But when you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.4', 'BSB', 'so that your giving may be in secret. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.5', 'BSB', 'And when you pray, do not be like the hypocrites. For they love to pray standing in the synagogues and on the street corners to be seen by men. Truly I tell you, they already have their full reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.6', 'BSB', 'But when you pray, go into your inner room, shut your door, and pray to your Father, who is unseen. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.7', 'BSB', 'And when you pray, do not babble on like pagans, for they think that by their many words they will be heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.8', 'BSB', 'Do not be like them, for your Father knows what you need before you ask Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.9', 'BSB', 'So then, this is how you should pray: ‘Our Father in heaven, hallowed be Your name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.10', 'BSB', 'Your kingdom come, Your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.11', 'BSB', 'Give us this day our daily bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.12', 'BSB', 'And forgive us our debts, as we also have forgiven our debtors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.13', 'BSB', 'And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.14', 'BSB', 'For if you forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.15', 'BSB', 'But if you do not forgive men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.16', 'BSB', 'When you fast, do not be somber like the hypocrites, for they disfigure their faces to show men they are fasting. Truly I tell you, they already have their full reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.17', 'BSB', 'But when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.18', 'BSB', 'so that your fasting will not be obvious to men, but only to your Father, who is unseen. And your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.19', 'BSB', 'Do not store up for yourselves treasures on earth, where moth and rust destroy, and where thieves break in and steal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.20', 'BSB', 'But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where moth and rust do not destroy, and where thieves do not break in and steal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.21', 'BSB', 'For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.22', 'BSB', 'The eye is the lamp of the body. If your eyes are good, your whole body will be full of light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.23', 'BSB', 'But if your eyes are bad, your whole body will be full of darkness. If then the light within you is darkness, how great is that darkness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.24', 'BSB', 'No one can serve two masters: Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat or drink; or about your body, what you will wear. Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothes?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.26', 'BSB', 'Look at the birds of the air: They do not sow or reap or gather into barns—and yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.27', 'BSB', 'Who of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.28', 'BSB', 'And why do you worry about clothes? Consider how the lilies of the field grow: They do not labor or spin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.29', 'BSB', 'Yet I tell you that not even Solomon in all his glory was adorned like one of these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.30', 'BSB', 'If that is how God clothes the grass of the field, which is here today and tomorrow is thrown into the furnace, will He not much more clothe you, O you of little faith?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore do not worry, saying, ‘What shall we eat?’ or ‘What shall we drink?’ or ‘What shall we wear?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.32', 'BSB', 'For the Gentiles strive after all these things, and your heavenly Father knows that you need them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.33', 'BSB', 'But seek first the kingdom of God and His righteousness, and all these things will be added unto you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.6.34', 'BSB', 'Therefore do not worry about tomorrow, for tomorrow will worry about itself. Today has enough trouble of its own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.1', 'BSB', '“Do not judge, or you will be judged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.2', 'BSB', 'For with the same judgment you pronounce, you will be judged; and with the measure you use, it will be measured to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.3', 'BSB', 'Why do you look at the speck in your brother’s eye, but fail to notice the beam in your own eye?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.4', 'BSB', 'How can you say to your brother, ‘Let me take the speck out of your eye,’ while there is still a beam in your own eye?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.5', 'BSB', 'You hypocrite! First take the beam out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother’s eye.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.6', 'BSB', 'Do not give dogs what is holy; do not throw your pearls before swine. If you do, they may trample them under their feet, and then turn and tear you to pieces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.7', 'BSB', 'Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock, and the door will be opened to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.8', 'BSB', 'For everyone who asks receives; he who seeks finds; and to him who knocks, the door will be opened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.9', 'BSB', 'Which of you, if his son asks for bread, will give him a stone?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.10', 'BSB', 'Or if he asks for a fish, will give him a snake?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.11', 'BSB', 'So if you who are evil know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father in heaven give good things to those who ask Him!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.12', 'BSB', 'In everything, then, do to others as you would have them do to you. For this is the essence of the Law and the Prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.13', 'BSB', 'Enter through the narrow gate. For wide is the gate and broad is the way that leads to destruction, and many enter through it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.14', 'BSB', 'But small is the gate and narrow the way that leads to life, and only a few find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.15', 'BSB', 'Beware of false prophets. They come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly they are ravenous wolves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.16', 'BSB', 'By their fruit you will recognize them. Are grapes gathered from thornbushes, or figs from thistles?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.17', 'BSB', 'Likewise, every good tree bears good fruit, but a bad tree bears bad fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.18', 'BSB', 'A good tree cannot bear bad fruit, and a bad tree cannot bear good fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.19', 'BSB', 'Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.20', 'BSB', 'So then, by their fruit you will recognize them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.21', 'BSB', 'Not everyone who says to Me, ‘Lord, Lord,’ will enter the kingdom of heaven, but only he who does the will of My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.22', 'BSB', 'Many will say to Me on that day, ‘Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in Your name, and in Your name drive out demons and perform many miracles?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.23', 'BSB', 'Then I will tell them plainly, ‘I never knew you; depart from Me, you workers of lawlessness!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore everyone who hears these words of Mine and acts on them is like a wise man who built his house on the rock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.25', 'BSB', 'The rain fell, the torrents raged, and the winds blew and beat against that house; yet it did not fall, because its foundation was on the rock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.26', 'BSB', 'But everyone who hears these words of Mine and does not act on them is like a foolish man who built his house on sand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.27', 'BSB', 'The rain fell, the torrents raged, and the winds blew and beat against that house, and it fell—and great was its collapse!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.28', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had finished saying these things, the crowds were astonished at His teaching,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.7.29', 'BSB', 'because He taught as one who had authority, and not as their scribes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus came down from the mountain, large crowds followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.2', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a leper came and knelt before Him, saying, “Lord, if You are willing, You can make me clean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!” And immediately his leprosy was cleansed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.4', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus instructed him, “See that you don’t tell anyone. But go, show yourself to the priest and offer the gift prescribed by Moses, as a testimony to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.5', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had entered Capernaum, a centurion came and pleaded with Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.6', 'BSB', '“Lord, my servant lies at home, paralyzed and in terrible agony.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.7', 'BSB', '“I will go and heal him,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.8', 'BSB', 'The centurion answered, “Lord, I am not worthy to have You come under my roof. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.9', 'BSB', 'For I myself am a man under authority, with soldiers under me. I tell one to go, and he goes; and another to come, and he comes. I tell my servant to do something, and he does it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.10', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard this, He marveled and said to those following Him, “Truly I tell you, I have not found anyone in Israel with such great faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.11', 'BSB', 'I say to you that many will come from the east and the west to share the banquet with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob in the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.12', 'BSB', 'But the sons of the kingdom will be thrown into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.13', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the centurion, “Go! As you have believed, so will it be done for you.” And his servant was healed at that very hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.14', 'BSB', 'When Jesus arrived at Peter’s house, He saw Peter’s mother-in-law sick in bed with a fever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.15', 'BSB', 'So He touched her hand, and the fever left her, and she got up and began to serve them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.16', 'BSB', 'When evening came, many who were demon-possessed were brought to Jesus, and He drove out the spirits with a word and healed all the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.17', 'BSB', 'This was to fulfill what was spoken through the prophet Isaiah: “He took on our infirmities and carried our diseases.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.18', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw a large crowd around Him, He gave orders to cross to the other side of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.19', 'BSB', 'And one of the scribes came to Him and said, “Teacher, I will follow You wherever You go.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.20', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Foxes have dens and birds of the air have nests, but the Son of Man has no place to lay His head.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.21', 'BSB', 'Another of His disciples requested, “Lord, first let me go and bury my father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.22', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told him, “Follow Me, and let the dead bury their own dead.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.23', 'BSB', 'When He got into the boat, His disciples followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.24', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a violent storm came up on the sea, so that the boat was engulfed by the waves; but Jesus was sleeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.25', 'BSB', 'The disciples went and woke Him, saying, “Lord, save us! We are perishing!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.26', 'BSB', '“You of little faith,” Jesus replied, “why are you so afraid?” Then He got up and rebuked the winds and the sea, and it was perfectly calm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.27', 'BSB', 'The men were amazed and asked, “What kind of man is this? Even the winds and the sea obey Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.28', 'BSB', 'When Jesus arrived on the other side in the region of the Gadarenes, He was met by two demon-possessed men coming from the tombs. They were so violent that no one could pass that way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.29', 'BSB', '“What do You want with us, Son of God?” they shouted. “Have You come here to torture us before the appointed time?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.30', 'BSB', 'In the distance a large herd of pigs was feeding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.31', 'BSB', 'So the demons begged Jesus, “If You drive us out, send us into the herd of pigs.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.32', 'BSB', '“Go!” He told them. So they came out and went into the pigs, and the whole herd rushed down the steep bank into the sea and died in the waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.33', 'BSB', 'Those tending the pigs ran off into the town and reported all this, including the account of the demon-possessed men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.8.34', 'BSB', 'Then the whole town went out to meet Jesus. And when they saw Him, they begged Him to leave their region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.1', 'BSB', 'Jesus got into a boat, crossed over, and came to His own town.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.2', 'BSB', 'Just then some men brought to Him a paralytic lying on a mat. When Jesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Take courage, son; your sins are forgiven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.3', 'BSB', 'On seeing this, some of the scribes said to themselves, “This man is blaspheming!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.4', 'BSB', 'But Jesus knew what they were thinking and said, “Why do you harbor evil in your hearts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.5', 'BSB', 'Which is easier: to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up and walk?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.6', 'BSB', 'But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...” Then He said to the paralytic, “Get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.7', 'BSB', 'And the man got up and went home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.8', 'BSB', 'When the crowds saw this, they were filled with awe and glorified God, who had given such authority to men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.9', 'BSB', 'As Jesus went on from there, He saw a man named Matthew sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him, and Matthew got up and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.10', 'BSB', 'Later, as Jesus was dining at Matthew’s house, many tax collectors and sinners came and ate with Him and His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.11', 'BSB', 'When the Pharisees saw this, they asked His disciples, “Why does your Teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.12', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, Jesus said, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.13', 'BSB', 'But go and learn what this means: ‘I desire mercy, not sacrifice.’ For I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.14', 'BSB', 'At that time John’s disciples came to Jesus and asked, “Why is it that we and the Pharisees fast so often, but Your disciples do not fast?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.15', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “How can the guests of the bridegroom mourn while He is with them? But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.16', 'BSB', 'No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. For the patch will pull away from the garment, and a worse tear will result.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.17', 'BSB', 'Neither do men pour new wine into old wineskins. If they do, the skins will burst, the wine will spill, and the wineskins will be ruined. Instead, they pour new wine into new wineskins, and both are preserved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.18', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was saying these things, a synagogue leader came and knelt before Him. “My daughter has just died,” he said. “But come and place Your hand on her, and she will live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.19', 'BSB', 'So Jesus got up and went with him, along with His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.20', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a woman who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years came up behind Him and touched the fringe of His cloak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.21', 'BSB', 'She said to herself, “If only I touch His cloak, I will be healed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.22', 'BSB', 'Jesus turned and saw her. “Take courage, daughter,” He said, “your faith has healed you.” And the woman was cured from that very hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.23', 'BSB', 'When Jesus entered the house of the synagogue leader, He saw the flute players and the noisy crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.24', 'BSB', '“Go away,” He told them. “The girl is not dead, but asleep.” And they laughed at Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.25', 'BSB', 'After the crowd had been put outside, Jesus went in and took the girl by the hand, and she got up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.26', 'BSB', 'And the news about this spread throughout that region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.27', 'BSB', 'As Jesus went on from there, two blind men followed Him, crying out, “Have mercy on us, Son of David!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.28', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had entered the house, the blind men came to Him. “Do you believe that I am able to do this?” He asked. “Yes, Lord,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.29', 'BSB', 'Then He touched their eyes and said, “According to your faith will it be done to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.30', 'BSB', 'And their eyes were opened. Jesus warned them sternly, “See that no one finds out about this!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.31', 'BSB', 'But they went out and spread the news about Him throughout the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.32', 'BSB', 'As they were leaving, a demon-possessed man who was mute was brought to Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.33', 'BSB', 'And when the demon had been driven out, the man began to speak. The crowds were amazed and said, “Nothing like this has ever been seen in Israel!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.34', 'BSB', 'But the Pharisees said, “It is by the prince of demons that He drives out demons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.35', 'BSB', 'Jesus went through all the towns and villages, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every disease and sickness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.36', 'BSB', 'When He saw the crowds, He was moved with compassion for them, because they were harassed and helpless, like sheep without a shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.37', 'BSB', 'Then He said to His disciples, “The harvest is plentiful, but the workers are few.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.9.38', 'BSB', 'Ask the Lord of the harvest, therefore, to send out workers into His harvest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.1', 'BSB', 'And calling His twelve disciples to Him, Jesus gave them authority over unclean spirits, so that they could drive them out and heal every disease and sickness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.2', 'BSB', 'These are the names of the twelve apostles: first Simon, called Peter, and his brother Andrew; James son of Zebedee, and his brother John;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.3', 'BSB', 'Philip and Bartholomew; Thomas and Matthew the tax collector; James son of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.4', 'BSB', 'Simon the Zealot, and Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.5', 'BSB', 'These twelve Jesus sent out with the following instructions: “Do not go onto the road of the Gentiles or enter any town of the Samaritans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.6', 'BSB', 'Go rather to the lost sheep of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.7', 'BSB', 'As you go, preach this message: ‘The kingdom of heaven is near.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.8', 'BSB', 'Heal the sick, raise the dead, cleanse the lepers, drive out demons. Freely you have received; freely give.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.9', 'BSB', 'Do not carry any gold or silver or copper in your belts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.10', 'BSB', 'Take no bag for the road, or second tunic, or sandals, or staff; for the worker is worthy of his provisions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.11', 'BSB', 'Whatever town or village you enter, find out who is worthy there and stay at his house until you move on.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.12', 'BSB', 'As you enter the home, greet its occupants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.13', 'BSB', 'If the home is worthy, let your peace rest on it; but if it is not, let your peace return to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.14', 'BSB', 'And if anyone will not welcome you or heed your words, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that home or town.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.15', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, it will be more bearable for Sodom and Gomorrah on the day of judgment than for that town.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.16', 'BSB', 'Behold, I am sending you out like sheep among wolves; therefore be as shrewd as snakes and as innocent as doves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.17', 'BSB', 'But beware of men; for they will hand you over to their councils and flog you in their synagogues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.18', 'BSB', 'On My account, you will be brought before governors and kings as witnesses to them and to the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.19', 'BSB', 'But when they hand you over, do not worry about how to respond or what to say. In that hour you will be given what to say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.20', 'BSB', 'For it will not be you speaking, but the Spirit of your Father speaking through you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.21', 'BSB', 'Brother will betray brother to death, and a father his child; children will rise against their parents and have them put to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.22', 'BSB', 'You will be hated by everyone because of My name, but the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.23', 'BSB', 'When they persecute you in one town, flee to the next. Truly I tell you, you will not reach all the towns of Israel before the Son of Man comes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.24', 'BSB', 'A disciple is not above his teacher, nor a servant above his master.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.25', 'BSB', 'It is enough for a disciple to be like his teacher, and a servant like his master. If the head of the house has been called Beelzebul, how much more the members of his household!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.26', 'BSB', 'So do not be afraid of them. For there is nothing concealed that will not be disclosed, and nothing hidden that will not be made known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.27', 'BSB', 'What I tell you in the dark, speak in the daylight; what is whispered in your ear, proclaim from the housetops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.28', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid of those who kill the body but cannot kill the soul. Instead, fear the One who can destroy both soul and body in hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.29', 'BSB', 'Are not two sparrows sold for a penny? Yet not one of them will fall to the ground apart from the will of your Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.30', 'BSB', 'And even the very hairs of your head are all numbered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.31', 'BSB', 'So do not be afraid; you are worth more than many sparrows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.32', 'BSB', 'Therefore everyone who confesses Me before men, I will also confess him before My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.33', 'BSB', 'But whoever denies Me before men, I will also deny him before My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.34', 'BSB', 'Do not assume that I have come to bring peace to the earth; I have not come to bring peace, but a sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.35', 'BSB', 'For I have come to turn ‘a man against his father, a daughter against her mother, a daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.36', 'BSB', 'A man’s enemies will be the members of his own household.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.37', 'BSB', 'Anyone who loves his father or mother more than Me is not worthy of Me; anyone who loves his son or daughter more than Me is not worthy of Me;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.38', 'BSB', 'and anyone who does not take up his cross and follow Me is not worthy of Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.39', 'BSB', 'Whoever finds his life will lose it, and whoever loses his life for My sake will find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.40', 'BSB', 'He who receives you receives Me, and he who receives Me receives the One who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.41', 'BSB', 'Whoever receives a prophet because he is a prophet will receive a prophet’s reward, and whoever receives a righteous man because he is a righteous man will receive a righteous man’s reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.10.42', 'BSB', 'And if anyone gives even a cup of cold water to one of these little ones because he is My disciple, truly I tell you, he will never lose his reward.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.1', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had finished instructing His twelve disciples, He went on from there to teach and preach in their cities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.2', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile John heard in prison about the works of Christ, and he sent his disciples', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.3', 'BSB', 'to ask Him, “Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.4', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Go back and report to John what you hear and see:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.5', 'BSB', 'The blind receive sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, and the good news is preached to the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.6', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.7', 'BSB', 'As John’s disciples were leaving, Jesus began to speak to the crowds about John: “What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed swaying in the wind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.8', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, what did you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? Look, those who wear fine clothing are found in kings’ palaces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.9', 'BSB', 'What then did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.10', 'BSB', 'This is the one about whom it is written: ‘Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way before You.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.11', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, among those born of women there has risen no one greater than John the Baptist. Yet even the least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.12', 'BSB', 'From the days of John the Baptist until now, the kingdom of heaven has been subject to violence, and the violent lay claim to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.13', 'BSB', 'For all the Prophets and the Law prophesied until John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.14', 'BSB', 'And if you are willing to accept it, he is the Elijah who was to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.15', 'BSB', 'He who has ears, let him hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.16', 'BSB', 'To what can I compare this generation? They are like children sitting in the marketplaces and calling out to others:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.17', 'BSB', '‘We played the flute for you, and you did not dance; we sang a dirge, and you did not mourn.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.18', 'BSB', 'For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, ‘He has a demon!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.19', 'BSB', 'The Son of Man came eating and drinking, and they say, ‘Look at this glutton and drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!’ But wisdom is vindicated by her actions.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.20', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus began to denounce the cities in which most of His miracles had been performed, because they did not repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.21', 'BSB', '“Woe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.22', 'BSB', 'But I tell you, it will be more bearable for Tyre and Sidon on the day of judgment than for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.23', 'BSB', 'And you, Capernaum, will you be lifted up to heaven? No, you will be brought down to Hades! For if the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Sodom, it would have remained to this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.24', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that it will be more bearable for Sodom on the day of judgment than for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.25', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus declared, “I praise You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because You have hidden these things from the wise and learned, and revealed them to little children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.26', 'BSB', 'Yes, Father, for this was well-pleasing in Your sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.27', 'BSB', 'All things have been entrusted to Me by My Father. No one knows the Son except the Father, and no one knows the Father except the Son and those to whom the Son chooses to reveal Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.28', 'BSB', 'Come to Me, all you who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.29', 'BSB', 'Take My yoke upon you and learn from Me; for I am gentle and humble in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.11.30', 'BSB', 'For My yoke is easy and My burden is light.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.1', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus went through the grainfields on the Sabbath. His disciples were hungry and began to pick the heads of grain and eat them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.2', 'BSB', 'When the Pharisees saw this, they said to Him, “Look, Your disciples are doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Have you not read what David did when he and his companions were hungry?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.4', 'BSB', 'He entered the house of God, and he and his companions ate the consecrated bread, which was not lawful for them to eat, but only for the priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.5', 'BSB', 'Or haven’t you read in the Law that on the Sabbath the priests in the temple break the Sabbath and yet are innocent?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.6', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that something greater than the temple is here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.7', 'BSB', 'If only you had known the meaning of ‘I desire mercy, not sacrifice,’ you would not have condemned the innocent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.8', 'BSB', 'For the Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.9', 'BSB', 'Moving on from there, Jesus entered their synagogue,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.10', 'BSB', 'and a man with a withered hand was there. In order to accuse Jesus, they asked Him, “Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.11', 'BSB', 'He replied, “If one of you has a sheep and it falls into a pit on the Sabbath, will he not take hold of it and lift it out?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.12', 'BSB', 'How much more valuable is a man than a sheep! Therefore it is lawful to do good on the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.13', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” So he stretched it out, and it was restored to full use, just like the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.14', 'BSB', 'But the Pharisees went out and plotted how they might kill Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.15', 'BSB', 'Aware of this, Jesus withdrew from that place. Large crowds followed Him, and He healed them all,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.16', 'BSB', 'warning them not to make Him known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.17', 'BSB', 'This was to fulfill what was spoken through the prophet Isaiah:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.18', 'BSB', '“Here is My Servant, whom I have chosen, My beloved, in whom My soul delights. I will put My Spirit on Him, and He will proclaim justice to the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.19', 'BSB', 'He will not quarrel or cry out; no one will hear His voice in the streets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.20', 'BSB', 'A bruised reed He will not break, and a smoldering wick He will not extinguish, till He leads justice to victory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.21', 'BSB', 'In His name the nations will put their hope.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.22', 'BSB', 'Then a demon-possessed man who was blind and mute was brought to Jesus, and He healed the man so that he could speak and see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.23', 'BSB', 'The crowds were astounded and asked, “Could this be the Son of David?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.24', 'BSB', 'But when the Pharisees heard this, they said, “Only by Beelzebul, the prince of demons, does this man drive out demons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.25', 'BSB', 'Knowing their thoughts, Jesus said to them, “Every kingdom divided against itself will be laid waste, and every city or household divided against itself will not stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.26', 'BSB', 'If Satan drives out Satan, he is divided against himself. How then can his kingdom stand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.27', 'BSB', 'And if I drive out demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your sons drive them out? So then, they will be your judges.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.28', 'BSB', 'But if I drive out demons by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God has come upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.29', 'BSB', 'Or again, how can anyone enter a strong man’s house and steal his possessions, unless he first ties up the strong man? Then he can plunder his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.30', 'BSB', 'He who is not with Me is against Me, and he who does not gather with Me scatters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore I tell you, every sin and blasphemy will be forgiven men, but the blasphemy against the Spirit will not be forgiven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.32', 'BSB', 'Whoever speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven, but whoever speaks against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven, either in this age or in the one to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.33', 'BSB', 'Make a tree good and its fruit will be good, or make a tree bad and its fruit will be bad; for a tree is known by its fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.34', 'BSB', 'You brood of vipers, how can you who are evil say anything good? For out of the overflow of the heart, the mouth speaks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.35', 'BSB', 'The good man brings good things out of his good store of treasure, and the evil man brings evil things out of his evil store of treasure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.36', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that men will give an account on the day of judgment for every careless word they have spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.37', 'BSB', 'For by your words you will be acquitted, and by your words you will be condemned.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.38', 'BSB', 'Then some of the scribes and Pharisees said to Him, “Teacher, we want to see a sign from You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.39', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “A wicked and adulterous generation demands a sign, but none will be given it except the sign of the prophet Jonah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.40', 'BSB', 'For as Jonah was three days and three nights in the belly of the great fish, so the Son of Man will be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.41', 'BSB', 'The men of Nineveh will stand at the judgment with this generation and condemn it; for they repented at the preaching of Jonah, and now One greater than Jonah is here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.42', 'BSB', 'The Queen of the South will rise at the judgment with this generation and condemn it; for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and now One greater than Solomon is here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.43', 'BSB', 'When an unclean spirit comes out of a man, it passes through arid places seeking rest and does not find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.44', 'BSB', 'Then it says, ‘I will return to the house I left.’ On its return, it finds the house vacant, swept clean, and put in order.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.45', 'BSB', 'Then it goes and brings with it seven other spirits more wicked than itself, and they go in and dwell there; and the final plight of that man is worse than the first. So will it be with this wicked generation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.46', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was still speaking to the crowds, His mother and brothers stood outside, wanting to speak to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.47', 'BSB', 'Someone told Him, “Look, Your mother and brothers are standing outside, wanting to speak to You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.48', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “Who is My mother, and who are My brothers?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.49', 'BSB', 'Pointing to His disciples, He said, “Here are My mother and My brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.12.50', 'BSB', 'For whoever does the will of My Father in heaven is My brother and sister and mother.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.1', 'BSB', 'That same day Jesus went out of the house and sat by the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.2', 'BSB', 'Such large crowds gathered around Him that He got into a boat and sat down, while all the people stood on the shore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.3', 'BSB', 'And He told them many things in parables, saying, “A farmer went out to sow his seed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.4', 'BSB', 'And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, and the birds came and devoured it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.5', 'BSB', 'Some fell on rocky ground, where it did not have much soil. It sprang up quickly because the soil was shallow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.6', 'BSB', 'But when the sun rose, the seedlings were scorched, and they withered because they had no root.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.7', 'BSB', 'Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up and choked the seedlings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.8', 'BSB', 'Still other seed fell on good soil and produced a crop—a hundredfold, sixtyfold, or thirtyfold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.9', 'BSB', 'He who has ears, let him hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.10', 'BSB', 'Then the disciples came to Jesus and asked, “Why do You speak to the people in parables?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.11', 'BSB', 'He replied, “The knowledge of the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven has been given to you, but not to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.12', 'BSB', 'Whoever has will be given more, and he will have an abundance. Whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.13', 'BSB', 'This is why I speak to them in parables: ‘Though seeing, they do not see; though hearing, they do not hear or understand.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.14', 'BSB', 'In them the prophecy of Isaiah is fulfilled: ‘You will be ever hearing but never understanding; you will be ever seeing but never perceiving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.15', 'BSB', 'For this people’s heart has grown callous; they hardly hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.16', 'BSB', 'But blessed are your eyes because they see, and your ears because they hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.17', 'BSB', 'For truly I tell you, many prophets and righteous men longed to see what you see but did not see it, and to hear what you hear but did not hear it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.18', 'BSB', 'Consider, then, the parable of the sower:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.19', 'BSB', 'When anyone hears the message of the kingdom but does not understand it, the evil one comes and snatches away what was sown in his heart. This is the seed sown along the path.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.20', 'BSB', 'The seed sown on rocky ground is the one who hears the word and at once receives it with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.21', 'BSB', 'But since he has no root, he remains for only a season. When trouble or persecution comes because of the word, he quickly falls away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.22', 'BSB', 'The seed sown among the thorns is the one who hears the word, but the worries of this life and the deceitfulness of wealth choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.23', 'BSB', 'But the seed sown on good soil is the one who hears the word and understands it. He indeed bears fruit and produces a crop—a hundredfold, sixtyfold, or thirtyfold.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.24', 'BSB', 'Jesus put before them another parable: “The kingdom of heaven is like a man who sowed good seed in his field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.25', 'BSB', 'But while everyone was asleep, his enemy came and sowed weeds among the wheat, and slipped away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.26', 'BSB', 'When the wheat sprouted and bore grain, then the weeds also appeared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.27', 'BSB', 'The owner’s servants came to him and said, ‘Sir, didn’t you sow good seed in your field? Where then did the weeds come from?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.28', 'BSB', '‘An enemy did this,’ he replied. So the servants asked him, ‘Do you want us to go and pull them up?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.29', 'BSB', '‘No,’ he said, ‘if you pull the weeds now, you might uproot the wheat with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.30', 'BSB', 'Let both grow together until the harvest. At that time I will tell the harvesters: First collect the weeds and tie them in bundles to be burned; then gather the wheat into my barn.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.31', 'BSB', 'He put before them another parable: “The kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed that a man planted in his field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.32', 'BSB', 'Although it is the smallest of all seeds, yet it grows into the largest of garden plants and becomes a tree, so that the birds of the air come and nest in its branches.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.33', 'BSB', 'He told them still another parable: “The kingdom of heaven is like leaven that a woman took and mixed into three measures of flour, until all of it was leavened.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus spoke all these things to the crowds in parables. He did not tell them anything without using a parable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.35', 'BSB', 'So was fulfilled what was spoken through the prophet: “I will open My mouth in parables; I will utter things hidden since the foundation of the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.36', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus dismissed the crowds and went into the house. His disciples came to Him and said, “Explain to us the parable of the weeds in the field.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.37', 'BSB', 'He replied, “The One who sows the good seed is the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.38', 'BSB', 'The field is the world, and the good seed represents the sons of the kingdom. The weeds are the sons of the evil one,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.39', 'BSB', 'and the enemy who sows them is the devil. The harvest is the end of the age, and the harvesters are angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.40', 'BSB', 'As the weeds are collected and burned in the fire, so will it be at the end of the age.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.41', 'BSB', 'The Son of Man will send out His angels, and they will weed out of His kingdom every cause of sin and all who practice lawlessness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.42', 'BSB', 'And they will throw them into the fiery furnace, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.43', 'BSB', 'Then the righteous will shine like the sun in the kingdom of their Father. He who has ears, let him hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.44', 'BSB', 'The kingdom of heaven is like treasure hidden in a field. When a man found it, he hid it again, and in his joy he went and sold all he had and bought that field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.45', 'BSB', 'Again, the kingdom of heaven is like a merchant in search of fine pearls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.46', 'BSB', 'When he found one very precious pearl, he went away and sold all he had and bought it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.47', 'BSB', 'Once again, the kingdom of heaven is like a net that was cast into the sea and caught all kinds of fish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.48', 'BSB', 'When it was full, the men pulled it ashore. Then they sat down and sorted the good fish into containers, but threw the bad away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.49', 'BSB', 'So will it be at the end of the age: The angels will come and separate the wicked from the righteous,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.50', 'BSB', 'and throw them into the fiery furnace, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.51', 'BSB', 'Have you understood all these things?” “Yes,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.52', 'BSB', 'Then He told them, “For this reason, every scribe who has been discipled in the kingdom of heaven is like a homeowner who brings out of his storeroom new treasures as well as old.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.53', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had finished these parables, He withdrew from that place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.54', 'BSB', 'Coming to His hometown, He taught the people in their synagogue, and they were astonished. “Where did this man get such wisdom and miraculous powers?” they asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.55', 'BSB', '“Isn’t this the carpenter’s son? Isn’t His mother’s name Mary, and aren’t His brothers James, Joseph, Simon, and Judas?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.56', 'BSB', 'Aren’t all His sisters with us as well? Where then did this man get all these things?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.57', 'BSB', 'And they took offense at Him. But Jesus said to them, “Only in his hometown and in his own household is a prophet without honor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.13.58', 'BSB', 'And He did not do many miracles there, because of their unbelief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.1', 'BSB', 'At that time Herod the tetrarch heard the reports about Jesus', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.2', 'BSB', 'and said to his servants, “This is John the Baptist; he has risen from the dead! That is why miraculous powers are at work in him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.3', 'BSB', 'Now Herod had arrested John and bound him and put him in prison on account of Herodias, his brother Philip’s wife,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.4', 'BSB', 'because John had been telling him, “It is not lawful for you to have her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.5', 'BSB', 'Although Herod wanted to kill John, he was afraid of the people, because they regarded John as a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.6', 'BSB', 'On Herod’s birthday, however, the daughter of Herodias danced before them and pleased Herod', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.7', 'BSB', 'so much that he promised with an oath to give to her whatever she asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.8', 'BSB', 'Prompted by her mother, she said, “Give me here on a platter the head of John the Baptist.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.9', 'BSB', 'The king was grieved, but because of his oaths and his guests, he ordered that her wish be granted', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.10', 'BSB', 'and sent to have John beheaded in the prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.11', 'BSB', 'John’s head was brought in on a platter and presented to the girl, who carried it to her mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.12', 'BSB', 'Then John’s disciples came and took his body and buried it. And they went and informed Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.13', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard about John, He withdrew by boat privately to a solitary place. But the crowds found out about it and followed Him on foot from the towns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.14', 'BSB', 'When He stepped ashore and saw a large crowd, He had compassion on them and healed their sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.15', 'BSB', 'When evening came, the disciples came to Him and said, “This is a desolate place, and the hour is already late. Dismiss the crowds so they can go to the villages and buy themselves some food.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.16', 'BSB', '“They do not need to go away,” Jesus replied. “You give them something to eat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.17', 'BSB', '“We have here only five loaves of bread and two fish,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.18', 'BSB', '“Bring them here to Me,” Jesus said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.19', 'BSB', 'And He directed the crowds to sit down on the grass. Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, He spoke a blessing. Then He broke the loaves and gave them to the disciples, and the disciples gave them to the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.20', 'BSB', 'They all ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.21', 'BSB', 'About five thousand men were fed, in addition to women and children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.22', 'BSB', 'Immediately Jesus made the disciples get into the boat and go on ahead of Him to the other side, while He dismissed the crowds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.23', 'BSB', 'After He had sent them away, He went up on the mountain by Himself to pray. When evening came, He was there alone,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.24', 'BSB', 'but the boat was already far from land, buffeted by the waves because the wind was against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.25', 'BSB', 'During the fourth watch of the night, Jesus went out to them, walking on the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.26', 'BSB', 'When the disciples saw Him walking on the sea, they were terrified. “It’s a ghost!” they said, and cried out in fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.27', 'BSB', 'But Jesus spoke up at once: “Take courage! It is I. Do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.28', 'BSB', '“Lord, if it is You,” Peter replied, “command me to come to You on the water.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.29', 'BSB', '“Come,” said Jesus. Then Peter got down out of the boat, walked on the water, and came toward Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.30', 'BSB', 'But when he saw the strength of the wind, he was afraid, and beginning to sink, cried out, “Lord, save me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.31', 'BSB', 'Immediately Jesus reached out His hand and took hold of Peter. “You of little faith,” He said, “why did you doubt?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.32', 'BSB', 'And when they had climbed back into the boat, the wind died down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.33', 'BSB', 'Then those who were in the boat worshiped Him, saying, “Truly You are the Son of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.34', 'BSB', 'When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.35', 'BSB', 'And when the men of that place recognized Jesus, they sent word to all the surrounding region. People brought all the sick to Him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.14.36', 'BSB', 'and begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak. And all who touched Him were healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then some Pharisees and scribes came to Jesus from Jerusalem and asked,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.2', 'BSB', '“Why do Your disciples break the tradition of the elders? They do not wash their hands before they eat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “And why do you break the command of God for the sake of your tradition?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.4', 'BSB', 'For God said, ‘Honor your father and mother’ and ‘Anyone who curses his father or mother must be put to death.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.5', 'BSB', 'But you say that if anyone says to his father or mother, ‘Whatever you would have received from me is a gift devoted to God,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.6', 'BSB', 'he need not honor his father or mother with it. Thus you nullify the word of God for the sake of your tradition.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.7', 'BSB', 'You hypocrites! Isaiah prophesied correctly about you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.8', 'BSB', '‘These people honor Me with their lips, but their hearts are far from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.9', 'BSB', 'They worship Me in vain; they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.10', 'BSB', 'Jesus called the crowd to Him and said, “Listen and understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.11', 'BSB', 'A man is not defiled by what enters his mouth, but by what comes out of it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.12', 'BSB', 'Then the disciples came to Him and said, “Are You aware that the Pharisees were offended when they heard this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.13', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “Every plant that My heavenly Father has not planted will be pulled up by its roots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.14', 'BSB', 'Disregard them! They are blind guides. If a blind man leads a blind man, both will fall into a pit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.15', 'BSB', 'Peter said to Him, “Explain this parable to us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.16', 'BSB', '“Do you still not understand?” Jesus asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.17', 'BSB', '“Do you not yet realize that whatever enters the mouth goes into the stomach and then is eliminated?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.18', 'BSB', 'But the things that come out of the mouth come from the heart, and these things defile a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.19', 'BSB', 'For out of the heart come evil thoughts, murder, adultery, sexual immorality, theft, false testimony, and slander.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.20', 'BSB', 'These are what defile a man, but eating with unwashed hands does not defile him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.21', 'BSB', 'Leaving that place, Jesus withdrew to the district of Tyre and Sidon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.22', 'BSB', 'And a Canaanite woman from that region came to Him, crying out, “Lord, Son of David, have mercy on me! My daughter is miserably possessed by a demon.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.23', 'BSB', 'But Jesus did not answer a word. So His disciples came and urged Him, “Send her away, for she keeps crying out after us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.24', 'BSB', 'He answered, “I was sent only to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.25', 'BSB', 'The woman came and knelt before Him. “Lord, help me!” she said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.26', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “It is not right to take the children’s bread and toss it to the dogs.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.27', 'BSB', '“Yes, Lord,” she said, “even the dogs eat the crumbs that fall from their master’s table.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.28', 'BSB', '“O woman,” Jesus answered, “your faith is great! Let it be done for you as you desire.” And her daughter was healed from that very hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.29', 'BSB', 'Moving on from there, Jesus went along the Sea of Galilee. Then He went up on a mountain and sat down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.30', 'BSB', 'Large crowds came to Him, bringing the lame, the blind, the crippled, the mute, and many others, and laid them at His feet, and He healed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.31', 'BSB', 'The crowd was amazed when they saw the mute speaking, the crippled restored, the lame walking, and the blind seeing. And they glorified the God of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.32', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus called His disciples to Him and said, “I have compassion for this crowd, because they have already been with Me three days and have nothing to eat. I do not want to send them away hungry, or they may faint along the way.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.33', 'BSB', 'The disciples replied, “Where in this desolate place could we find enough bread to feed such a large crowd?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.34', 'BSB', '“How many loaves do you have?” Jesus asked. “Seven,” they replied, “and a few small fish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.35', 'BSB', 'And He instructed the crowd to sit down on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.36', 'BSB', 'Taking the seven loaves and the fish, He gave thanks and broke them. Then He gave them to the disciples, and the disciples gave them to the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.37', 'BSB', 'They all ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up seven basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.38', 'BSB', 'A total of four thousand men were fed, in addition to women and children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.15.39', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had dismissed the crowds, He got into the boat and went to the region of Magadan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.1', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees and Sadducees came and tested Jesus by asking Him to show them a sign from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.2', 'BSB', 'But He replied, “When evening comes, you say, ‘The weather will be fair, for the sky is red,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.3', 'BSB', 'and in the morning, ‘Today it will be stormy, for the sky is red and overcast.’ You know how to interpret the appearance of the sky, but not the signs of the times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.4', 'BSB', 'A wicked and adulterous generation demands a sign, but none will be given it except the sign of Jonah.” Then He left them and went away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.5', 'BSB', 'When they crossed to the other side, the disciples forgot to take bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.6', 'BSB', '“Watch out!” Jesus told them. “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.7', 'BSB', 'They discussed this among themselves and concluded, “It is because we did not bring any bread.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.8', 'BSB', 'Aware of their conversation, Jesus said, “You of little faith, why are you debating among yourselves about having no bread?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.9', 'BSB', 'Do you still not understand? Do you not remember the five loaves for the five thousand, and how many basketfuls you gathered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.10', 'BSB', 'Or the seven loaves for the four thousand, and how many basketfuls you gathered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.11', 'BSB', 'How do you not understand that I was not telling you about bread? But beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.12', 'BSB', 'Then they understood that He was not telling them to beware of the leaven used in bread, but of the teaching of the Pharisees and Sadducees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.13', 'BSB', 'When Jesus came to the region of Caesarea Philippi, He questioned His disciples: “Who do people say the Son of Man is?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.14', 'BSB', 'They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, Jeremiah or one of the prophets.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.15', 'BSB', '“But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.16', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter answered, “You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.17', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Blessed are you, Simon son of Jonah! For this was not revealed to you by flesh and blood, but by My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.18', 'BSB', 'And I tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My church, and the gates of Hades will not prevail against it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.19', 'BSB', 'I will give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven. Whatever you bind on earth will be bound in heaven, and whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.20', 'BSB', 'Then He admonished the disciples not to tell anyone that He was the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.21', 'BSB', 'From that time on Jesus began to show His disciples that He must go to Jerusalem and suffer many things at the hands of the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and that He must be killed and on the third day be raised to life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.22', 'BSB', 'Peter took Him aside and began to rebuke Him. “Far be it from You, Lord!” he said. “This shall never happen to You!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.23', 'BSB', 'But Jesus turned and said to Peter, “Get behind Me, Satan! You are a stumbling block to Me. For you do not have in mind the things of God, but the things of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.24', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told His disciples, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross and follow Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.25', 'BSB', 'For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake will find it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.26', 'BSB', 'What will it profit a man if he gains the whole world, yet forfeits his soul? Or what can a man give in exchange for his soul?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.27', 'BSB', 'For the Son of Man will come in His Father’s glory with His angels, and then He will repay each one according to what he has done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.16.28', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, some who are standing here will not taste death before they see the Son of Man coming in His kingdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.1', 'BSB', 'After six days Jesus took with Him Peter, James, and John the brother of James, and led them up a high mountain by themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.2', 'BSB', 'There He was transfigured before them. His face shone like the sun, and His clothes became as white as the light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.3', 'BSB', 'Suddenly Moses and Elijah appeared before them, talking with Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.4', 'BSB', 'Peter said to Jesus, “Lord, it is good for us to be here. If You wish, I will put up three shelters —one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.5', 'BSB', 'While Peter was still speaking, a bright cloud enveloped them, and a voice from the cloud said, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. Listen to Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.6', 'BSB', 'When the disciples heard this, they fell facedown in terror.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.7', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus came over and touched them. “Get up,” He said. “Do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.8', 'BSB', 'And when they looked up, they saw no one except Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.9', 'BSB', 'As they were coming down the mountain, Jesus commanded them, “Do not tell anyone about this vision until the Son of Man has been raised from the dead.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.10', 'BSB', 'The disciples asked Him, “Why then do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.11', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Elijah does indeed come, and he will restore all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.12', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that Elijah has already come, and they did not recognize him, but have done to him whatever they wished. In the same way, the Son of Man will suffer at their hands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.13', 'BSB', 'Then the disciples understood that He was speaking to them about John the Baptist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.14', 'BSB', 'When they came to the crowd, a man came up to Jesus and knelt before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.15', 'BSB', '“Lord, have mercy on my son,” he said. “He has seizures and is suffering terribly. He often falls into the fire or into the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.16', 'BSB', 'I brought him to Your disciples, but they could not heal him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.17', 'BSB', '“O unbelieving and perverse generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you? How long must I put up with you? Bring the boy here to Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.18', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus rebuked the demon, and it came out of the boy, and he was healed from that moment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.19', 'BSB', 'Afterward the disciples came to Jesus privately and asked, “Why couldn’t we drive it out?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.20', 'BSB', '“Because you have so little faith,” He answered. “For truly I tell you, if you have faith the size of a mustard seed, you can say to this mountain, ‘Move from here to there,’ and it will move. Nothing will be impossible for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.22', 'BSB', 'When they gathered together in Galilee, Jesus told them, “The Son of Man is about to be delivered into the hands of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.23', 'BSB', 'They will kill Him, and on the third day He will be raised to life.” And the disciples were deeply grieved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.24', 'BSB', 'After they had arrived in Capernaum, the collectors of the two-drachma tax came to Peter and asked, “Does your Teacher pay the two drachmas?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.25', 'BSB', '“Yes,” he answered. When Peter entered the house, Jesus preempted him. “What do you think, Simon?” He asked. “From whom do the kings of the earth collect customs and taxes: from their own sons, or from others?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.26', 'BSB', '“From others,” Peter answered. “Then the sons are exempt,” Jesus declared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.17.27', 'BSB', '“But so that we may not offend them, go to the sea, cast a hook, and take the first fish you catch. When you open its mouth, you will find a four-drachma coin. Take it and give it to them for My tax and yours.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.1', 'BSB', 'At that time the disciples came to Jesus and asked, “Who then is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.2', 'BSB', 'Jesus invited a little child to stand among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.3', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” He said, “unless you change and become like little children, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore, whoever humbles himself like this little child is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.5', 'BSB', 'And whoever welcomes a little child like this in My name welcomes Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.6', 'BSB', 'But if anyone causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be drowned in the depths of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.7', 'BSB', 'Woe to the world for the causes of sin. These stumbling blocks must come, but woe to the man through whom they come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.8', 'BSB', 'If your hand or your foot causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. It is better for you to enter life crippled or lame than to have two hands and two feet and be thrown into the eternal fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.9', 'BSB', 'And if your eye causes you to sin, gouge it out and throw it away. It is better for you to enter life with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into the fire of hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.10', 'BSB', 'See that you do not look down on any of these little ones. For I tell you that their angels in heaven always see the face of My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.12', 'BSB', 'What do you think? If a man has a hundred sheep and one of them goes astray, will he not leave the ninety-nine on the hills and go out to search for the one that is lost?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.13', 'BSB', 'And if he finds it, truly I tell you, he rejoices more over that one sheep than over the ninety-nine that did not go astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.14', 'BSB', 'In the same way, your Father in heaven is not willing that any of these little ones should perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.15', 'BSB', 'If your brother sins against you, go and confront him privately. If he listens to you, you have won your brother over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.16', 'BSB', 'But if he will not listen, take one or two others along, so that ‘every matter may be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.17', 'BSB', 'If he refuses to listen to them, tell it to the church. And if he refuses to listen even to the church, regard him as you would a pagan or a tax collector.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.18', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, whatever you bind on earth will be bound in heaven, and whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.19', 'BSB', 'Again, I tell you truly that if two of you on the earth agree about anything you ask for, it will be done for you by My Father in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.20', 'BSB', 'For where two or three gather together in My name, there am I with them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.21', 'BSB', 'Then Peter came to Jesus and asked, “Lord, how many times shall I forgive my brother who sins against me? Up to seven times?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.22', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “I tell you, not just seven times, but seventy-seven times!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.23', 'BSB', 'Because of this, the kingdom of heaven is like a king who wanted to settle accounts with his servants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.24', 'BSB', 'As he began the settlements, a debtor was brought to him owing ten thousand talents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.25', 'BSB', 'Since the man was unable to pay, the master ordered that he be sold to pay his debt, along with his wife and children and everything he owned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.26', 'BSB', 'Then the servant fell on his knees before him. ‘Have patience with me,’ he begged, ‘and I will pay back everything.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.27', 'BSB', 'His master had compassion on him, forgave his debt, and released him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.28', 'BSB', 'But when that servant went out, he found one of his fellow servants who owed him a hundred denarii. He grabbed him and began to choke him, saying, ‘Pay back what you owe me!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.29', 'BSB', 'So his fellow servant fell down and begged him, ‘Have patience with me, and I will pay you back.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.30', 'BSB', 'But he refused. Instead, he went and had the man thrown into prison until he could pay his debt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.31', 'BSB', 'When his fellow servants saw what had happened, they were greatly distressed, and they went and recounted all of this to their master.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.32', 'BSB', 'Then the master summoned him and declared, ‘You wicked servant! I forgave all your debt because you begged me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.33', 'BSB', 'Shouldn’t you have had mercy on your fellow servant, just as I had on you?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.34', 'BSB', 'In anger his master turned him over to the jailers to be tortured, until he should repay all that he owed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.18.35', 'BSB', 'That is how My heavenly Father will treat each of you unless you forgive your brother from your heart.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had finished saying these things, He left Galilee and went into the region of Judea beyond the Jordan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.2', 'BSB', 'Large crowds followed Him, and He healed them there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.3', 'BSB', 'Then some Pharisees came and tested Him by asking, “Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any reason?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.4', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “Have you not read that from the beginning the Creator ‘made them male and female,’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.5', 'BSB', 'and said, ‘For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.6', 'BSB', 'So they are no longer two, but one flesh. Therefore what God has joined together, let man not separate.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.7', 'BSB', '“Why then,” they asked, “did Moses order a man to give his wife a certificate of divorce and send her away?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.8', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Moses permitted you to divorce your wives because of your hardness of heart; but it was not this way from the beginning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.9', 'BSB', 'Now I tell you that whoever divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, and marries another woman, commits adultery.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.10', 'BSB', 'His disciples said to Him, “If this is the case between a man and his wife, it is better not to marry.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.11', 'BSB', '“Not everyone can accept this word,” He replied, “but only those to whom it has been given.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.12', 'BSB', 'For there are eunuchs who were born that way; others were made that way by men; and still others live like eunuchs for the sake of the kingdom of heaven. The one who can accept this should accept it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.13', 'BSB', 'Then the little children were brought to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them and pray for them. And the disciples rebuked those who brought them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.14', 'BSB', 'But Jesus said, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of heaven belongs to such as these.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.15', 'BSB', 'And after He had placed His hands on them, He went on from there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.16', 'BSB', 'Just then a man came up to Jesus and inquired, “Teacher, what good thing must I do to obtain eternal life?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.17', 'BSB', '“Why do you ask Me about what is good?” Jesus replied. “There is only One who is good. If you want to enter life, keep the commandments.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.18', 'BSB', '“Which ones?” the man asked. Jesus answered, “‘Do not murder, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not bear false witness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.19', 'BSB', 'honor your father and mother, and love your neighbor as yourself.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.20', 'BSB', '“All these I have kept,” said the young man. “What do I still lack?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus told him, “If you want to be perfect, go, sell your possessions and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.22', 'BSB', 'When the young man heard this, he went away in sorrow, because he had great wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.23', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to His disciples, “Truly I tell you, it is hard for a rich man to enter the kingdom of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.24', 'BSB', 'Again I tell you, it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.25', 'BSB', 'When the disciples heard this, they were greatly astonished and asked, “Who then can be saved?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus looked at them and said, “With man this is impossible, but with God all things are possible.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.27', 'BSB', '“Look,” Peter replied, “we have left everything to follow You. What then will there be for us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.28', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “Truly I tell you, in the renewal of all things, when the Son of Man sits on His glorious throne, you who have followed Me will also sit on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.29', 'BSB', 'And everyone who has left houses or brothers or sisters or father or mother or wife or children or fields for the sake of My name will receive a hundredfold and will inherit eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.19.30', 'BSB', 'But many who are first will be last, and the last will be first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.1', 'BSB', '“For the kingdom of heaven is like a landowner who went out early in the morning to hire workers for his vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.2', 'BSB', 'He agreed to pay them a denarius for the day and sent them into his vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.3', 'BSB', 'About the third hour he went out and saw others standing in the marketplace doing nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.4', 'BSB', '‘You also go into my vineyard,’ he said, ‘and I will pay you whatever is right.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.5', 'BSB', 'So they went. He went out again about the sixth hour and the ninth hour and did the same thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.6', 'BSB', 'About the eleventh hour he went out and found still others standing around. ‘Why have you been standing here all day long doing nothing?’ he asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.7', 'BSB', '‘Because no one has hired us,’ they answered. So he told them, ‘You also go into my vineyard.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.8', 'BSB', 'When evening came, the owner of the vineyard said to his foreman, ‘Call the workers and pay them their wages, starting with the last ones hired and moving on to the first.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.9', 'BSB', 'The workers who were hired about the eleventh hour came and each received a denarius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.10', 'BSB', 'So when the original workers came, they assumed they would receive more. But each of them also received a denarius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.11', 'BSB', 'On receiving their pay, they began to grumble against the landowner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.12', 'BSB', '‘These men who were hired last worked only one hour,’ they said, ‘and you have made them equal to us who have borne the burden and the scorching heat of the day.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.13', 'BSB', 'But he answered one of them, ‘Friend, I am not being unfair to you. Did you not agree with me on one denarius?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.14', 'BSB', 'Take your pay and go. I want to give this last man the same as I gave you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.15', 'BSB', 'Do I not have the right to do as I please with what is mine? Or are you envious because I am generous?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.16', 'BSB', 'So the last will be first, and the first will be last.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.17', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, He took the twelve disciples aside and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.18', 'BSB', '“Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be delivered over to the chief priests and scribes. They will condemn Him to death', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.19', 'BSB', 'and will deliver Him over to the Gentiles to be mocked and flogged and crucified. And on the third day He will be raised to life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.20', 'BSB', 'Then the mother of Zebedee’s sons came to Jesus with her sons and knelt down to make a request of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.21', 'BSB', '“What do you want?” He inquired. She answered, “Declare that in Your kingdom one of these two sons of mine may sit at Your right hand, and the other at Your left.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.22', 'BSB', '“You do not know what you are asking,” Jesus replied. “Can you drink the cup I am going to drink?” “We can,” the brothers answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.23', 'BSB', '“You will indeed drink My cup,” Jesus said. “But to sit at My right or left is not Mine to grant. These seats belong to those for whom My Father has prepared them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.24', 'BSB', 'When the ten heard about this, they were indignant with the two brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.25', 'BSB', 'But Jesus called them aside and said, “You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their superiors exercise authority over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.26', 'BSB', 'It shall not be this way among you. Instead, whoever wants to become great among you must be your servant,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.27', 'BSB', 'and whoever wants to be first among you must be your slave—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.28', 'BSB', 'just as the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.29', 'BSB', 'As they were leaving Jericho, a large crowd followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.30', 'BSB', 'And there were two blind men sitting beside the road. When they heard that Jesus was passing by, they cried out, “Lord, Son of David, have mercy on us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.31', 'BSB', 'The crowd admonished them to be silent, but they cried out all the louder, “Lord, Son of David, have mercy on us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.32', 'BSB', 'Jesus stopped and called them. “What do you want Me to do for you?” He asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.33', 'BSB', '“Lord,” they answered, “let our eyes be opened.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.20.34', 'BSB', 'Moved with compassion, Jesus touched their eyes, and at once they received their sight and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.1', 'BSB', 'As they approached Jerusalem and came to Bethphage on the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent out two disciples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.2', 'BSB', 'saying to them, “Go into the village ahead of you, and at once you will find a donkey tied there, with her colt beside her. Untie them and bring them to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.3', 'BSB', 'If anyone questions you, tell him that the Lord needs them, and he will send them right away.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.4', 'BSB', 'This took place to fulfill what was spoken through the prophet:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.5', 'BSB', '“Say to the Daughter of Zion, ‘See, your King comes to you, gentle and riding on a donkey, on a colt, the foal of a donkey.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.6', 'BSB', 'So the disciples went and did as Jesus had directed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.7', 'BSB', 'They brought the donkey and the colt and laid their cloaks on them, and Jesus sat on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.8', 'BSB', 'A massive crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others cut branches from the trees and spread them on the road.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.9', 'BSB', 'The crowds that went ahead of Him and those that followed were shouting: “Hosanna to the Son of David!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Hosanna in the highest!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.10', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had entered Jerusalem, the whole city was stirred and asked, “Who is this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.11', 'BSB', 'The crowds replied, “This is Jesus, the prophet from Nazareth in Galilee.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.12', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus entered the temple courts and drove out all who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling doves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.13', 'BSB', 'And He declared to them, “It is written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer.’ But you are making it ‘a den of robbers.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.14', 'BSB', 'The blind and the lame came to Him at the temple, and He healed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.15', 'BSB', 'But the chief priests and scribes were indignant when they saw the wonders He performed and the children shouting in the temple courts, “Hosanna to the Son of David!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.16', 'BSB', '“Do you hear what these children are saying?” they asked. “Yes,” Jesus answered. “Have you never read: ‘From the mouths of children and infants You have ordained praise’?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.17', 'BSB', 'Then He left them and went out of the city to Bethany, where He spent the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.18', 'BSB', 'In the morning, as Jesus was returning to the city, He was hungry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.19', 'BSB', 'Seeing a fig tree by the road, He went up to it but found nothing on it except leaves. “May you never bear fruit again!” He said. And immediately the tree withered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.20', 'BSB', 'When the disciples saw this, they marveled and asked, “How did the fig tree wither so quickly?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.21', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “if you have faith and do not doubt, not only will you do what was done to the fig tree, but even if you say to this mountain, ‘Be lifted up and thrown into the sea,’ it will happen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.22', 'BSB', 'If you believe, you will receive whatever you ask for in prayer.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.23', 'BSB', 'When Jesus returned to the temple courts and began to teach, the chief priests and elders of the people came up to Him. “By what authority are You doing these things?” they asked. “And who gave You this authority?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.24', 'BSB', '“I will also ask you one question,” Jesus replied, “and if you answer Me, I will tell you by what authority I am doing these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.25', 'BSB', 'What was the source of John’s baptism? Was it from heaven or from men?” They deliberated among themselves and said, “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why then did you not believe him?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.26', 'BSB', 'But if we say, ‘From men,’ we are afraid of the people, for they all regard John as a prophet.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.27', 'BSB', 'So they answered, “We do not know.” And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.28', 'BSB', 'But what do you think? There was a man who had two sons. He went to the first one and said, ‘Son, go and work today in the vineyard.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.29', 'BSB', '‘I will not,’ he replied. But later he changed his mind and went.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.30', 'BSB', 'Then the man went to the second son and told him the same thing. ‘I will, sir,’ he said. But he did not go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.31', 'BSB', 'Which of the two did the will of his father?” “The first,” they answered. Jesus said to them, “Truly I tell you, the tax collectors and prostitutes are entering the kingdom of God before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.32', 'BSB', 'For John came to you in a righteous way and you did not believe him, but the tax collectors and prostitutes did. And even after you saw this, you did not repent and believe him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.33', 'BSB', 'Listen to another parable: There was a landowner who planted a vineyard. He put a wall around it, dug a winepress in it, and built a tower. Then he rented it out to some tenants and went away on a journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.34', 'BSB', 'When the harvest time drew near, he sent his servants to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.35', 'BSB', 'But the tenants seized his servants. They beat one, killed another, and stoned a third.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.36', 'BSB', 'Again, he sent other servants, more than the first group. But the tenants did the same to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.37', 'BSB', 'Finally, he sent his son to them. ‘They will respect my son,’ he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.38', 'BSB', 'But when the tenants saw the son, they said to one another, ‘This is the heir. Come, let us kill him and take his inheritance.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.39', 'BSB', 'So they seized him and threw him out of the vineyard and killed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.40', 'BSB', 'Therefore, when the owner of the vineyard returns, what will he do to those tenants?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.41', 'BSB', '“He will bring those wretches to a wretched end,” they replied, “and will rent out the vineyard to other tenants who will give him his share of the fruit at harvest time.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.42', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “Have you never read in the Scriptures: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone. This is from the Lord, and it is marvelous in our eyes’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.43', 'BSB', 'Therefore I tell you that the kingdom of God will be taken away from you and given to a people who will produce its fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.44', 'BSB', 'He who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces, but he on whom it falls will be crushed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.45', 'BSB', 'When the chief priests and Pharisees heard His parables, they knew that Jesus was speaking about them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.21.46', 'BSB', 'Although they wanted to arrest Him, they were afraid of the crowds, because the people regarded Him as a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.1', 'BSB', 'Once again, Jesus spoke to them in parables:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.2', 'BSB', '“The kingdom of heaven is like a king who prepared a wedding banquet for his son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.3', 'BSB', 'He sent his servants to call those he had invited to the banquet, but they refused to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.4', 'BSB', 'Again, he sent other servants and said, ‘Tell those who have been invited that I have prepared my dinner. My oxen and fattened cattle have been killed, and everything is ready. Come to the wedding banquet.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.5', 'BSB', 'But they paid no attention and went away, one to his field, another to his business.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.6', 'BSB', 'The rest seized his servants, mistreated them, and killed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.7', 'BSB', 'The king was enraged, and he sent his troops to destroy those murderers and burn their city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.8', 'BSB', 'Then he said to his servants, ‘The wedding banquet is ready, but those I invited were not worthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.9', 'BSB', 'Go therefore to the crossroads and invite to the banquet as many as you can find.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.10', 'BSB', 'So the servants went out into the streets and gathered everyone they could find, both evil and good, and the wedding hall was filled with guests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.11', 'BSB', 'But when the king came in to see the guests, he spotted a man who was not dressed in wedding clothes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.12', 'BSB', '‘Friend,’ he asked, ‘how did you get in here without wedding clothes?’ But the man was speechless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.13', 'BSB', 'Then the king told the servants, ‘Tie him hand and foot, and throw him into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.14', 'BSB', 'For many are called, but few are chosen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.15', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees went out and conspired to trap Jesus in His words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.16', 'BSB', 'They sent their disciples to Him along with the Herodians. “Teacher,” they said, “we know that You are honest and that You teach the way of God in accordance with the truth. You seek favor from no one, because You pay no attention to external appearance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.17', 'BSB', 'So tell us what You think: Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar or not?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.18', 'BSB', 'But Jesus knew their evil intent and said, “You hypocrites, why are you testing Me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.19', 'BSB', 'Show Me the coin used for the tax.” And they brought Him a denarius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.20', 'BSB', '“Whose image is this,” He asked, “and whose inscription?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.21', 'BSB', '“Caesar’s,” they answered. So Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.22', 'BSB', 'And when they heard this, they were amazed. So they left Him and went away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.23', 'BSB', 'That same day the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to Jesus and questioned Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.24', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” they said, “Moses declared that if a man dies without having children, his brother is to marry the widow and raise up offspring for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.25', 'BSB', 'Now there were seven brothers among us. The first one married and died without having children. So he left his wife to his brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.26', 'BSB', 'The same thing happened to the second and third brothers, down to the seventh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.27', 'BSB', 'And last of all, the woman died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.28', 'BSB', 'In the resurrection, then, whose wife will she be of the seven? For all of them were married to her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.29', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “You are mistaken because you do not know the Scriptures or the power of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.30', 'BSB', 'In the resurrection, people will neither marry nor be given in marriage. Instead, they will be like the angels in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.31', 'BSB', 'But concerning the resurrection of the dead, have you not read what God said to you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.32', 'BSB', '‘I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob’? He is not the God of the dead, but of the living.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.33', 'BSB', 'When the crowds heard this, they were astonished at His teaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.34', 'BSB', 'And when the Pharisees heard that Jesus had silenced the Sadducees, they themselves gathered together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.35', 'BSB', 'One of them, an expert in the law, tested Him with a question:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.36', 'BSB', '“Teacher, which commandment is the greatest in the Law?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.37', 'BSB', 'Jesus declared, “‘Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.38', 'BSB', 'This is the first and greatest commandment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.39', 'BSB', 'And the second is like it: ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.40', 'BSB', 'All the Law and the Prophets hang on these two commandments.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.41', 'BSB', 'While the Pharisees were assembled, Jesus questioned them:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.42', 'BSB', '“What do you think about the Christ? Whose son is He?” “David’s,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.43', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “How then does David in the Spirit call Him ‘Lord’? For he says:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.44', 'BSB', '‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand until I put Your enemies under Your feet.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.45', 'BSB', 'So if David calls Him ‘Lord,’ how can He be David’s son?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.22.46', 'BSB', 'No one was able to answer a word, and from that day on no one dared to question Him any further.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus spoke to the crowds and to His disciples:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.2', 'BSB', '“The scribes and Pharisees sit in Moses’ seat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.3', 'BSB', 'So practice and observe everything they tell you. But do not do what they do, for they do not practice what they preach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.4', 'BSB', 'They tie up heavy, burdensome loads and lay them on men’s shoulders, but they themselves are not willing to lift a finger to move them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.5', 'BSB', 'All their deeds are done for men to see. They broaden their phylacteries and lengthen their tassels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.6', 'BSB', 'They love the places of honor at banquets, the chief seats in the synagogues,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.7', 'BSB', 'the greetings in the marketplaces, and the title of ‘Rabbi’ by which they are addressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.8', 'BSB', 'But you are not to be called ‘Rabbi,’ for you have one Teacher, and you are all brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.9', 'BSB', 'And do not call anyone on earth your father, for you have one Father, who is in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.10', 'BSB', 'Nor are you to be called instructors, for you have one Instructor, the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.11', 'BSB', 'The greatest among you shall be your servant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.12', 'BSB', 'For whoever exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.13', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You shut the kingdom of heaven in men’s faces. You yourselves do not enter, nor will you let in those who wish to enter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.15', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You traverse land and sea to win a single convert, and when he becomes one, you make him twice as much a son of hell as you are.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.16', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, blind guides! You say, ‘If anyone swears by the temple, it means nothing; but if anyone swears by the gold of the temple, he is bound by his oath.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.17', 'BSB', 'You blind fools! Which is greater: the gold, or the temple that makes it sacred?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.18', 'BSB', 'And you say, ‘If anyone swears by the altar, it means nothing; but if anyone swears by the gift on it, he is bound by his oath.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.19', 'BSB', 'You blind men! Which is greater: the gift, or the altar that makes it sacred?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.20', 'BSB', 'So then, he who swears by the altar swears by it and by everything on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.21', 'BSB', 'And he who swears by the temple swears by it and by the One who dwells in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.22', 'BSB', 'And he who swears by heaven swears by God’s throne and by the One who sits on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.23', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You pay tithes of mint, dill, and cumin. But you have disregarded the weightier matters of the law: justice, mercy, and faithfulness. You should have practiced the latter, without neglecting the former.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.24', 'BSB', 'You blind guides! You strain out a gnat but swallow a camel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.25', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.26', 'BSB', 'Blind Pharisee! First clean the inside of the cup and dish, so that the outside may become clean as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.27', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You are like whitewashed tombs, which look beautiful on the outside, but on the inside are full of dead men’s bones and every kind of impurity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.28', 'BSB', 'In the same way, on the outside you appear to be righteous, but on the inside you are full of hypocrisy and wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.29', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You build tombs for the prophets and decorate the monuments of the righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.30', 'BSB', 'And you say, ‘If we had lived in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partners with them in shedding the blood of the prophets.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.31', 'BSB', 'So you testify against yourselves that you are the sons of those who murdered the prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.32', 'BSB', 'Fill up, then, the measure of the sin of your fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.33', 'BSB', 'You snakes! You brood of vipers! How will you escape the sentence of hell?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.34', 'BSB', 'Because of this, I am sending you prophets and wise men and teachers. Some of them you will kill and crucify, and others you will flog in your synagogues and persecute in town after town.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.35', 'BSB', 'And so upon you will come all the righteous blood shed on earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah son of Berechiah, whom you murdered between the temple and the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.36', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, all these things will come upon this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.37', 'BSB', 'O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those sent to her, how often I have longed to gather your children together, as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, but you were unwilling!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.38', 'BSB', 'Look, your house is left to you desolate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.23.39', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that you will not see Me again until you say, ‘Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.1', 'BSB', 'As Jesus left the temple and was walking away, His disciples came up to Him to point out its buildings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.2', 'BSB', '“Do you see all these things?” He replied. “Truly I tell you, not one stone here will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.3', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives, the disciples came to Him privately. “Tell us,” they said, “when will these things happen, and what will be the sign of Your coming and of the end of the age?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.4', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “See to it that no one deceives you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.5', 'BSB', 'For many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am the Christ,’ and will deceive many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.6', 'BSB', 'You will hear of wars and rumors of wars, but see to it that you are not alarmed. These things must happen, but the end is still to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.7', 'BSB', 'Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be famines and earthquakes in various places.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.8', 'BSB', 'All these are the beginning of birth pains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.9', 'BSB', 'Then they will deliver you over to be persecuted and killed, and you will be hated by all nations because of My name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.10', 'BSB', 'At that time many will fall away and will betray and hate one another,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.11', 'BSB', 'and many false prophets will arise and mislead many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.12', 'BSB', 'Because of the multiplication of wickedness, the love of most will grow cold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.13', 'BSB', 'But the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.14', 'BSB', 'And this gospel of the kingdom will be preached in all the world as a testimony to all nations, and then the end will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.15', 'BSB', 'So when you see standing in the holy place ‘the abomination of desolation,’ described by the prophet Daniel (let the reader understand),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.16', 'BSB', 'then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.17', 'BSB', 'Let no one on the housetop come down to retrieve anything from his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.18', 'BSB', 'And let no one in the field return for his cloak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.19', 'BSB', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.20', 'BSB', 'Pray that your flight will not occur in the winter or on the Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.21', 'BSB', 'For at that time there will be great tribulation, unmatched from the beginning of the world until now, and never to be seen again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.22', 'BSB', 'If those days had not been cut short, nobody would be saved. But for the sake of the elect, those days will be cut short.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.23', 'BSB', 'At that time, if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is the Christ!’ or ‘There He is!’ do not believe it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.24', 'BSB', 'For false Christs and false prophets will appear and perform great signs and wonders that would deceive even the elect, if that were possible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.25', 'BSB', 'See, I have told you in advance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.26', 'BSB', 'So if they tell you, ‘There He is in the wilderness,’ do not go out; or, ‘Here He is in the inner rooms,’ do not believe it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.27', 'BSB', 'For just as the lightning comes from the east and flashes as far as the west, so will be the coming of the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.28', 'BSB', 'Wherever there is a carcass, there the vultures will gather.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.29', 'BSB', 'Immediately after the tribulation of those days: ‘The sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light; the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.30', 'BSB', 'At that time the sign of the Son of Man will appear in heaven, and all the tribes of the earth will mourn. They will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of heaven, with power and great glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.31', 'BSB', 'And He will send out His angels with a loud trumpet call, and they will gather His elect from the four winds, from one end of the heavens to the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.32', 'BSB', 'Now learn this lesson from the fig tree: As soon as its branches become tender and sprout leaves, you know that summer is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.33', 'BSB', 'So also, when you see all these things, you will know that He is near, right at the door.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.34', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.35', 'BSB', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.36', 'BSB', 'No one knows about that day or hour, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.37', 'BSB', 'As it was in the days of Noah, so will it be at the coming of the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.38', 'BSB', 'For in the days before the flood, people were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, up to the day Noah entered the ark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.39', 'BSB', 'And they were oblivious, until the flood came and swept them all away. So will it be at the coming of the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.40', 'BSB', 'Two men will be in the field: one will be taken and the other left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.41', 'BSB', 'Two women will be grinding at the mill: one will be taken and the other left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.42', 'BSB', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know the day on which your Lord will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.43', 'BSB', 'But understand this: If the homeowner had known in which watch of the night the thief was coming, he would have kept watch and would not have let his house be broken into.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.44', 'BSB', 'For this reason, you also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour you do not expect.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.45', 'BSB', 'Who then is the faithful and wise servant, whom the master has put in charge of his household, to give the others their food at the proper time?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.46', 'BSB', 'Blessed is that servant whose master finds him doing so when he returns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.47', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, he will put him in charge of all his possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.48', 'BSB', 'But suppose that servant is wicked and says in his heart, ‘My master will be away a long time.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.49', 'BSB', 'And he begins to beat his fellow servants and to eat and drink with drunkards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.50', 'BSB', 'The master of that servant will come on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not anticipate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.24.51', 'BSB', 'Then he will cut him to pieces and assign him a place with the hypocrites, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.1', 'BSB', '“At that time the kingdom of heaven will be like ten virgins who took their lamps and went out to meet the bridegroom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.2', 'BSB', 'Five of them were foolish, and five were wise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.3', 'BSB', 'The foolish ones took their lamps but did not take along any extra oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.4', 'BSB', 'But the wise ones took oil in flasks along with their lamps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.5', 'BSB', 'When the bridegroom was delayed, they all became drowsy and fell asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.6', 'BSB', 'At midnight the cry rang out: ‘Here is the bridegroom! Come out to meet him!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.7', 'BSB', 'Then all the virgins woke up and trimmed their lamps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.8', 'BSB', 'The foolish ones said to the wise, ‘Give us some of your oil; our lamps are going out.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.9', 'BSB', '‘No,’ said the wise ones, ‘or there may not be enough for both us and you. Instead, go to those who sell oil and buy some for yourselves.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.10', 'BSB', 'But while they were on their way to buy it, the bridegroom arrived. Those who were ready went in with him to the wedding banquet, and the door was shut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.11', 'BSB', 'Later the other virgins arrived and said, ‘Lord, lord, open the door for us!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.12', 'BSB', 'But he replied, ‘Truly I tell you, I do not know you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know the day or the hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.14', 'BSB', 'For it is just like a man going on a journey, who called his servants and entrusted them with his possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.15', 'BSB', 'To one he gave five talents, to another two talents, and to another one talent—each according to his own ability. And he went on his journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.16', 'BSB', 'The servant who had received the five talents went at once and put them to work and gained five more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.17', 'BSB', 'Likewise, the one with the two talents gained two more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.18', 'BSB', 'But the servant who had received the one talent went off, dug a hole in the ground, and hid his master’s money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.19', 'BSB', 'After a long time the master of those servants returned to settle accounts with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.20', 'BSB', 'The servant who had received the five talents came and presented five more. ‘Master,’ he said, ‘you entrusted me with five talents. See, I have gained five more.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.21', 'BSB', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Enter into the joy of your master!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.22', 'BSB', 'The servant who had received the two talents also came and said, ‘Master, you entrusted me with two talents. See, I have gained two more.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.23', 'BSB', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Enter into the joy of your master!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.24', 'BSB', 'Finally, the servant who had received the one talent came and said, ‘Master, I knew that you are a hard man, reaping where you have not sown and gathering where you have not scattered seed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.25', 'BSB', 'So I was afraid and went out and hid your talent in the ground. See, you have what belongs to you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.26', 'BSB', '‘You wicked, lazy servant!’ replied his master. ‘You knew that I reap where I have not sown and gather where I have not scattered seed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.27', 'BSB', 'Then you should have deposited my money with the bankers, and on my return I would have received it back with interest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore take the talent from him and give it to the one who has ten talents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.29', 'BSB', 'For everyone who has will be given more, and he will have an abundance. But the one who does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.30', 'BSB', 'And throw that worthless servant into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.31', 'BSB', 'When the Son of Man comes in His glory, and all the angels with Him, He will sit on His glorious throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.32', 'BSB', 'All the nations will be gathered before Him, and He will separate the people one from another, as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.33', 'BSB', 'He will place the sheep on His right and the goats on His left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.34', 'BSB', 'Then the King will say to those on His right, ‘Come, you who are blessed by My Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.35', 'BSB', 'For I was hungry and you gave Me something to eat, I was thirsty and you gave Me something to drink, I was a stranger and you took Me in,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.36', 'BSB', 'I was naked and you clothed Me, I was sick and you looked after Me, I was in prison and you visited Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.37', 'BSB', 'Then the righteous will answer Him, ‘Lord, when did we see You hungry and feed You, or thirsty and give You something to drink?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.38', 'BSB', 'When did we see You a stranger and take You in, or naked and clothe You?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.39', 'BSB', 'When did we see You sick or in prison and visit You?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.40', 'BSB', 'And the King will reply, ‘Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers of Mine, you did for Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.41', 'BSB', 'Then He will say to those on His left, ‘Depart from Me, you who are cursed, into the eternal fire prepared for the devil and his angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.42', 'BSB', 'For I was hungry and you gave Me nothing to eat, I was thirsty and you gave Me nothing to drink,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.43', 'BSB', 'I was a stranger and you did not take Me in, I was naked and you did not clothe Me, I was sick and in prison and you did not visit Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.44', 'BSB', 'And they too will reply, ‘Lord, when did we see You hungry or thirsty or a stranger or naked or sick or in prison, and did not minister to You?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.45', 'BSB', 'Then the King will answer, ‘Truly I tell you, whatever you did not do for one of the least of these, you did not do for Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.25.46', 'BSB', 'And they will go away into eternal punishment, but the righteous into eternal life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had finished saying all these things, He told His disciples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.2', 'BSB', '“You know that the Passover is two days away, and the Son of Man will be handed over to be crucified.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.3', 'BSB', 'At that time the chief priests and elders of the people assembled in the courtyard of the high priest, whose name was Caiaphas,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.4', 'BSB', 'and they conspired to arrest Jesus covertly and kill Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.5', 'BSB', '“But not during the feast,” they said, “or there may be a riot among the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.6', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was in Bethany in the home of Simon the Leper,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.7', 'BSB', 'a woman came to Him with an alabaster jar of expensive perfume, which she poured on His head as He reclined at the table.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.8', 'BSB', 'When the disciples saw this, they were indignant and asked, “Why this waste?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.9', 'BSB', 'This perfume could have been sold at a high price, and the money given to the poor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.10', 'BSB', 'Aware of this, Jesus asked, “Why are you bothering this woman? She has done a beautiful deed to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.11', 'BSB', 'The poor you will always have with you, but you will not always have Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.12', 'BSB', 'By pouring this perfume on Me, she has prepared My body for burial.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.13', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, wherever this gospel is preached in all the world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.14', 'BSB', 'Then one of the Twelve, the one called Judas Iscariot, went to the chief priests', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.15', 'BSB', 'and asked, “What are you willing to give me if I hand Him over to you?” And they set out for him thirty pieces of silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.16', 'BSB', 'So from then on Judas looked for an opportunity to betray Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.17', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, the disciples came to Jesus and asked, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.18', 'BSB', 'He answered, “Go into the city to a certain man and tell him that the Teacher says, ‘My time is near. I will keep the Passover with My disciples at your house.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.19', 'BSB', 'So the disciples did as Jesus had directed them and prepared the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.20', 'BSB', 'When evening came, Jesus was reclining with the twelve disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.21', 'BSB', 'And while they were eating, He said to them, “Truly I tell you, one of you will betray Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.22', 'BSB', 'They were deeply grieved and began to ask Him one after another, “Surely not I, Lord?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “The one who has dipped his hand into the bowl with Me will betray Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.24', 'BSB', 'The Son of Man will go just as it is written about Him, but woe to that man by whom He is betrayed. It would be better for him if he had not been born.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.25', 'BSB', 'Then Judas, who would betray Him, said, “Surely not I, Rabbi?” Jesus answered, “You have said it yourself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.26', 'BSB', 'While they were eating, Jesus took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to the disciples, saying, “Take and eat; this is My body.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.27', 'BSB', 'Then He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying, “Drink from it, all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.28', 'BSB', 'This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many for the forgiveness of sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.29', 'BSB', 'I tell you, I will not drink of this fruit of the vine from now on until that day when I drink it anew with you in My Father’s kingdom.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.30', 'BSB', 'And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.31', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “This very night you will all fall away on account of Me. For it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep of the flock will be scattered.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.32', 'BSB', 'But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.33', 'BSB', 'Peter said to Him, “Even if all fall away on account of You, I never will.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.34', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus declared, “this very night, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.35', 'BSB', 'Peter replied, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You.” And all the other disciples said the same thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.36', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus went with His disciples to a place called Gethsemane, and He told them, “Sit here while I go over there and pray.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.37', 'BSB', 'He took with Him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee and began to be sorrowful and deeply distressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.38', 'BSB', 'Then He said to them, “My soul is consumed with sorrow to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch with Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.39', 'BSB', 'Going a little farther, He fell facedown and prayed, “My Father, if it is possible, let this cup pass from Me. Yet not as I will, but as You will.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.40', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus returned to the disciples and found them sleeping. “Were you not able to keep watch with Me for one hour?” He asked Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.41', 'BSB', '“Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the body is weak.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.42', 'BSB', 'A second time He went away and prayed, “My Father, if this cup cannot pass unless I drink it, may Your will be done.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.43', 'BSB', 'And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping—for their eyes were heavy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.44', 'BSB', 'So He left them and went away once more and prayed a third time, saying the same thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.45', 'BSB', 'Then He returned to the disciples and said, “Are you still sleeping and resting? Look, the hour is near, and the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.46', 'BSB', 'Rise, let us go! See, My betrayer is approaching!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.47', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was still speaking, Judas, one of the Twelve, arrived, accompanied by a large crowd armed with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests and elders of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.48', 'BSB', 'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them: “The One I kiss is the man; arrest Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.49', 'BSB', 'Going directly to Jesus, he said, “Greetings, Rabbi!” and kissed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.50', 'BSB', '“Friend,” Jesus replied, “do what you came for.” Then the men stepped forward, seized Jesus, and arrested Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.51', 'BSB', 'At this, one of Jesus’ companions drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.52', 'BSB', '“Put your sword back in its place,” Jesus said to him. “For all who draw the sword will die by the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.53', 'BSB', 'Are you not aware that I can call on My Father, and He will at once put at My disposal more than twelve legions of angels?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.54', 'BSB', 'But how then would the Scriptures be fulfilled that say it must happen this way?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.55', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus said to the crowd, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as you would an outlaw? Every day I sat teaching in the temple courts, and you did not arrest Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.56', 'BSB', 'But this has all happened so that the writings of the prophets would be fulfilled.” Then all the disciples deserted Him and fled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.57', 'BSB', 'Those who had arrested Jesus led Him away to the house of Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and elders had gathered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.58', 'BSB', 'But Peter followed Him at a distance, right up to the courtyard of the high priest. And he went in and sat down with the guards to see the outcome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.59', 'BSB', 'Now the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin were seeking false testimony against Jesus in order to put Him to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.60', 'BSB', 'But they did not find any, though many false witnesses came forward. Finally two came forward', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.61', 'BSB', 'and declared, “This man said, ‘I am able to destroy the temple of God and rebuild it in three days.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.62', 'BSB', 'So the high priest stood up and asked Him, “Have You no answer? What are these men testifying against You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.63', 'BSB', 'But Jesus remained silent. Then the high priest said to Him, “I charge You under oath by the living God: Tell us if You are the Christ, the Son of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.64', 'BSB', '“You have said it yourself,” Jesus answered. “But I say to all of you, from now on you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming on the clouds of heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.65', 'BSB', 'At this, the high priest tore his clothes and declared, “He has blasphemed! Why do we need any more witnesses? Look, now you have heard the blasphemy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.66', 'BSB', 'What do you think?” “He deserves to die,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.67', 'BSB', 'Then they spit in His face and struck Him. Others slapped Him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.68', 'BSB', 'and said, “Prophesy to us, Christ! Who hit You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.69', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, Peter was sitting out in the courtyard, and a servant girl came up to him. “You also were with Jesus the Galilean,” she said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.70', 'BSB', 'But he denied it before them all: “I do not know what you are talking about.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.71', 'BSB', 'When Peter had gone out to the gateway, another servant girl saw him and said to the people there, “This man was with Jesus of Nazareth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.72', 'BSB', 'And again he denied it with an oath: “I do not know the man!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.73', 'BSB', 'After a little while, those standing nearby came up to Peter. “Surely you are one of them,” they said, “for your accent gives you away.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.74', 'BSB', 'At that he began to curse and swear to them, “I do not know the man!” And immediately a rooster crowed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.26.75', 'BSB', 'Then Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken: “Before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.” And he went outside and wept bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.1', 'BSB', 'When morning came, all the chief priests and elders of the people conspired against Jesus to put Him to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.2', 'BSB', 'They bound Him, led Him away, and handed Him over to Pilate the governor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.3', 'BSB', 'When Judas, who had betrayed Him, saw that Jesus was condemned, he was filled with remorse and returned the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.4', 'BSB', '“I have sinned by betraying innocent blood,” he said. “What is that to us?” they replied. “You bear the responsibility.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.5', 'BSB', 'So Judas threw the silver into the temple and left. Then he went away and hanged himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.6', 'BSB', 'The chief priests picked up the pieces of silver and said, “It is unlawful to put this into the treasury, since it is blood money.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.7', 'BSB', 'After conferring together, they used the money to buy the potter’s field as a burial place for foreigners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.8', 'BSB', 'That is why it has been called the Field of Blood to this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.9', 'BSB', 'Then what was spoken through Jeremiah the prophet was fulfilled: “They took the thirty pieces of silver, the price set on Him by the people of Israel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.10', 'BSB', 'and they gave them for the potter’s field, as the Lord had commanded me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.11', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile Jesus stood before the governor, who questioned Him: “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.12', 'BSB', 'And when He was accused by the chief priests and elders, He gave no answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.13', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate asked Him, “Do You not hear how many charges they are bringing against You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.14', 'BSB', 'But Jesus gave no answer, not even to a single charge, much to the governor’s amazement.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.15', 'BSB', 'Now it was the governor’s custom at the feast to release to the crowd a prisoner of their choosing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.16', 'BSB', 'At that time they were holding a notorious prisoner named Barabbas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.17', 'BSB', 'So when the crowd had assembled, Pilate asked them, “Which one do you want me to release to you: Barabbas, or Jesus who is called Christ?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.18', 'BSB', 'For he knew it was out of envy that they had handed Jesus over to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.19', 'BSB', 'While Pilate was sitting on the judgment seat, his wife sent him this message: “Have nothing to do with that innocent man, for I have suffered terribly in a dream today because of Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.20', 'BSB', 'But the chief priests and elders persuaded the crowds to ask for Barabbas and to have Jesus put to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.21', 'BSB', '“Which of the two do you want me to release to you?” asked the governor. “Barabbas,” they replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.22', 'BSB', '“What then should I do with Jesus who is called Christ?” Pilate asked. They all answered, “Crucify Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.23', 'BSB', '“Why?” asked Pilate. “What evil has He done?” But they shouted all the louder, “Crucify Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.24', 'BSB', 'When Pilate saw that he was accomplishing nothing, but that instead a riot was breaking out, he took water and washed his hands before the crowd. “I am innocent of this man’s blood,” he said. “You bear the responsibility.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.25', 'BSB', 'All the people answered, “His blood be on us and on our children!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.26', 'BSB', 'So Pilate released Barabbas to them. But he had Jesus flogged, and handed Him over to be crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.27', 'BSB', 'Then the governor’s soldiers took Jesus into the Praetorium and gathered the whole company around Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.28', 'BSB', 'They stripped Him and put a scarlet robe on Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.29', 'BSB', 'And they twisted together a crown of thorns and set it on His head. They put a staff in His right hand and knelt down before Him to mock Him, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.30', 'BSB', 'Then they spit on Him and took the staff and struck Him on the head repeatedly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.31', 'BSB', 'After they had mocked Him, they removed the robe and put His own clothes back on Him. Then they led Him away to crucify Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.32', 'BSB', 'Along the way they found a man from Cyrene, named Simon, and they forced him to carry the cross of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.33', 'BSB', 'And when they came to a place called Golgotha, which means The Place of the Skull,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.34', 'BSB', 'they offered Him wine to drink, mixed with gall; but after tasting it, He refused to drink it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.35', 'BSB', 'When they had crucified Him, they divided up His garments by casting lots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.36', 'BSB', 'And sitting down, they kept watch over Him there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.37', 'BSB', 'Above His head they posted the written charge against Him: THIS IS JESUS, THE KING OF THE JEWS.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.38', 'BSB', 'Two robbers were crucified with Him, one on His right hand and the other on His left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.39', 'BSB', 'And those who passed by heaped abuse on Him, shaking their heads', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.40', 'BSB', 'and saying, “You who are going to destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days, save Yourself! If You are the Son of God, come down from the cross!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.41', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the chief priests, scribes, and elders mocked Him, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.42', 'BSB', '“He saved others, but He cannot save Himself. He is the King of Israel! Let Him come down now from the cross, and we will believe in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.43', 'BSB', 'He trusts in God. Let God deliver Him now if He wants Him. For He said, ‘I am the Son of God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.44', 'BSB', 'In the same way, even the robbers who were crucified with Him berated Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.45', 'BSB', 'From the sixth hour until the ninth hour darkness came over all the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.46', 'BSB', 'About the ninth hour Jesus cried out in a loud voice, “Eli, Eli, lema sabachthani?” which means, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.47', 'BSB', 'When some of those standing there heard this, they said, “He is calling Elijah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.48', 'BSB', 'One of them quickly ran and brought a sponge. He filled it with sour wine, put it on a reed, and held it up for Jesus to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.49', 'BSB', 'But the others said, “Leave Him alone. Let us see if Elijah comes to save Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.50', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had cried out again in a loud voice, He yielded up His spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.51', 'BSB', 'At that moment the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom. The earth quaked and the rocks were split.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.52', 'BSB', 'The tombs broke open, and the bodies of many saints who had fallen asleep were raised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.53', 'BSB', 'After Jesus’ resurrection, when they had come out of the tombs, they entered the holy city and appeared to many people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.54', 'BSB', 'When the centurion and those with him who were guarding Jesus saw the earthquake and all that had happened, they were terrified and said, “Truly this was the Son of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.55', 'BSB', 'And many women were there, watching from a distance. They had followed Jesus from Galilee to minister to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.56', 'BSB', 'Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joseph, and the mother of Zebedee’s sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.57', 'BSB', 'When it was evening, there came a rich man from Arimathea named Joseph, who himself was a disciple of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.58', 'BSB', 'He went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus, and Pilate ordered that it be given to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.59', 'BSB', 'So Joseph took the body, wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.60', 'BSB', 'and placed it in his own new tomb that he had cut into the rock. Then he rolled a great stone across the entrance to the tomb and went away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.61', 'BSB', 'Mary Magdalene and the other Mary were sitting there opposite the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.62', 'BSB', 'The next day, the one after Preparation Day, the chief priests and Pharisees assembled before Pilate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.63', 'BSB', '“Sir,” they said, “we remember that while He was alive that deceiver said, ‘After three days I will rise again.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.64', 'BSB', 'So give the order that the tomb be secured until the third day. Otherwise, His disciples may come and steal Him away and tell the people He has risen from the dead. And this last deception would be worse than the first.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.65', 'BSB', '“You have a guard,” Pilate said. “Go, make the tomb as secure as you know how.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.27.66', 'BSB', 'So they went and secured the tomb by sealing the stone and posting the guard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.1', 'BSB', 'After the Sabbath, at dawn on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene and the other Mary went to see the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.2', 'BSB', 'Suddenly there was a great earthquake, for an angel of the Lord descended from heaven, rolled away the stone, and sat on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.3', 'BSB', 'His appearance was like lightning, and his clothes were white as snow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.4', 'BSB', 'The guards trembled in fear of him and became like dead men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.5', 'BSB', 'But the angel said to the women, “Do not be afraid, for I know that you are looking for Jesus, who was crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.6', 'BSB', 'He is not here; He has risen, just as He said! Come, see the place where He lay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.7', 'BSB', 'Then go quickly and tell His disciples, ‘He has risen from the dead and is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him.’ See, I have told you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.8', 'BSB', 'So they hurried away from the tomb in fear and great joy, and ran to tell His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.9', 'BSB', 'Suddenly Jesus met them and said, “Greetings!” They came to Him, grasped His feet, and worshiped Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.10', 'BSB', '“Do not be afraid,” said Jesus. “Go and tell My brothers to go to Galilee. There they will see Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.11', 'BSB', 'While the women were on their way, some of the guards went into the city and reported to the chief priests all that had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.12', 'BSB', 'And after the chief priests had met with the elders and formed a plan, they gave the soldiers a large sum of money', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.13', 'BSB', 'and instructed them: “You are to say, ‘His disciples came by night and stole Him away while we were asleep.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.14', 'BSB', 'If this report reaches the governor, we will satisfy him and keep you out of trouble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.15', 'BSB', 'So the guards took the money and did as they were instructed. And this account has been circulated among the Jews to this very day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.16', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain Jesus had designated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.17', 'BSB', 'When they saw Him, they worshiped Him, but some doubted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.18', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus came to them and said, “All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Matt.28.20', 'BSB', 'and teaching them to obey all that I have commanded you. And surely I am with you always, even to the end of the age.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.2', 'BSB', 'As it is written in Isaiah the prophet: “Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.3', 'BSB', '“A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.4', 'BSB', 'John the Baptist appeared in the wilderness, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.5', 'BSB', 'People went out to him from all of Jerusalem and the countryside of Judea. Confessing their sins, they were baptized by him in the Jordan River.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.6', 'BSB', 'John was clothed in camel’s hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.7', 'BSB', 'And he began to proclaim: “After me will come One more powerful than I, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to stoop down and untie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.8', 'BSB', 'I baptize you with water, but He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.9', 'BSB', 'In those days Jesus came from Nazareth in Galilee and was baptized by John in the Jordan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.10', 'BSB', 'As soon as Jesus came up out of the water, He saw the heavens breaking open and the Spirit descending on Him like a dove.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.11', 'BSB', 'And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.12', 'BSB', 'At once the Spirit drove Jesus into the wilderness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.13', 'BSB', 'and He was there for forty days, being tempted by Satan. He was with the wild animals, and the angels ministered to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.14', 'BSB', 'After the arrest of John, Jesus went into Galilee and proclaimed the gospel of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.15', 'BSB', '“The time is fulfilled,” He said, “and the kingdom of God is near. Repent and believe in the gospel!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.16', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was walking beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw Simon and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.17', 'BSB', '“Come, follow Me,” Jesus said, “and I will make you fishers of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.18', 'BSB', 'And at once they left their nets and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.19', 'BSB', 'Going on a little farther, He saw James son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat, mending their nets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.20', 'BSB', 'Immediately Jesus called them, and they left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.21', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus and His companions went to Capernaum, and right away Jesus entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and began to teach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.22', 'BSB', 'The people were astonished at His teaching, because He taught as one who had authority, and not as the scribes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.23', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a man with an unclean spirit cried out in the synagogue:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.24', 'BSB', '“What do You want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.25', 'BSB', 'But Jesus rebuked the spirit. “Be silent!” He said. “Come out of him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.26', 'BSB', 'At this, the unclean spirit threw the man into convulsions and came out with a loud shriek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.27', 'BSB', 'All the people were amazed and began to ask one another, “What is this? A new teaching with authority! He commands even the unclean spirits, and they obey Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.28', 'BSB', 'And the news about Jesus spread quickly through the whole region of Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.29', 'BSB', 'As soon as Jesus and His companions had left the synagogue, they went with James and John to the home of Simon and Andrew.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.30', 'BSB', 'Simon’s mother-in-law was sick in bed with a fever, and they promptly told Jesus about her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.31', 'BSB', 'So He went to her, took her by the hand, and helped her up. The fever left her, and she began to serve them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.32', 'BSB', 'That evening, after sunset, people brought to Jesus all who were sick and demon-possessed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.33', 'BSB', 'and the whole town gathered at the door.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.34', 'BSB', 'And He healed many who were ill with various diseases and drove out many demons. But He would not allow the demons to speak, because they knew who He was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.35', 'BSB', 'Early in the morning, while it was still dark, Jesus got up and slipped out to a solitary place to pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.36', 'BSB', 'Simon and his companions went to look for Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.37', 'BSB', 'and when they found Him, they said, “Everyone is looking for You!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.38', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “Let us go on to the neighboring towns so I can preach there as well, for that is why I have come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.39', 'BSB', 'So He went throughout Galilee, preaching in their synagogues and driving out demons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.40', 'BSB', 'Then a leper came to Jesus, begging on his knees: “If You are willing, You can make me clean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.41', 'BSB', 'Moved with compassion, Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.42', 'BSB', 'And immediately the leprosy left him, and the man was cleansed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.43', 'BSB', 'Jesus promptly sent him away with a stern warning:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.44', 'BSB', '“See that you don’t tell anyone. But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.1.45', 'BSB', 'But the man went out and openly began to proclaim and spread the news. Consequently, Jesus could no longer enter a town in plain view, but He stayed out in solitary places. Yet people came to Him from every quarter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.1', 'BSB', 'A few days later Jesus went back to Capernaum. And when the people heard that He was home,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.2', 'BSB', 'they gathered in such large numbers that there was no more room, not even outside the door, as Jesus spoke the word to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.3', 'BSB', 'Then a paralytic was brought to Him, carried by four men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.4', 'BSB', 'Since they were unable to get to Jesus through the crowd, they uncovered the roof above Him, made an opening, and lowered the paralytic on his mat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.5', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins are forgiven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.6', 'BSB', 'But some of the scribes were sitting there and thinking in their hearts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.7', 'BSB', '“Why does this man speak like this? He is blaspheming! Who can forgive sins but God alone?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.8', 'BSB', 'At once Jesus knew in His spirit that they were thinking this way within themselves. “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?” He asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.9', 'BSB', '“Which is easier: to say to a paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up, pick up your mat, and walk’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.10', 'BSB', 'But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins...” He said to the paralytic,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.11', 'BSB', '“I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.12', 'BSB', 'And immediately the man got up, picked up his mat, and walked out in front of them all. As a result, they were all astounded and glorified God, saying, “We have never seen anything like this!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.13', 'BSB', 'Once again Jesus went out beside the sea. All the people came to Him, and He taught them there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.14', 'BSB', 'As He was walking along, He saw Levi son of Alphaeus sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him, and Levi got up and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.15', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was dining at Levi’s house, many tax collectors and sinners were eating with Him and His disciples—for there were many who followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.16', 'BSB', 'When the scribes who were Pharisees saw Jesus eating with these people, they asked His disciples, “Why does He eat with tax collectors and sinners?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.17', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, Jesus told them, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick. I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.18', 'BSB', 'Now John’s disciples and the Pharisees were often fasting. So people came to Jesus and asked, “Why don’t Your disciples fast like John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.19', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them? As long as He is with them, they cannot fast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.20', 'BSB', 'But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.21', 'BSB', 'No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. If he does, the new piece will pull away from the old, and a worse tear will result.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.22', 'BSB', 'And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.23', 'BSB', 'One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain as they walked along.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.24', 'BSB', 'So the Pharisees said to Him, “Look, why are they doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.25', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Have you never read what David did when he and his companions were hungry and in need?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.26', 'BSB', 'During the high priesthood of Abiathar, he entered the house of God and ate the consecrated bread, which was lawful only for the priests. And he gave some to his companions as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.27', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus declared, “The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.2.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore, the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.1', 'BSB', 'Once again Jesus entered the synagogue, and a man with a withered hand was there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.2', 'BSB', 'In order to accuse Jesus, they were watching to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.3', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the man with the withered hand, “Stand up among us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.4', 'BSB', 'And He asked them, “Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?” But they were silent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.5', 'BSB', 'Jesus looked around at them with anger and sorrow at their hardness of heart. Then He said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” So he stretched it out, and it was restored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.6', 'BSB', 'At this, the Pharisees went out and began plotting with the Herodians how they might kill Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.7', 'BSB', 'So Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, accompanied by a large crowd from Galilee, Judea,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.8', 'BSB', 'Jerusalem, Idumea, the region beyond the Jordan, and the vicinity of Tyre and Sidon. The large crowd came to Him when they heard what great things He was doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.9', 'BSB', 'Jesus asked His disciples to have a boat ready for Him so that the crowd would not crush Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.10', 'BSB', 'For He had healed so many that all who had diseases were pressing forward to touch Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.11', 'BSB', 'And when the unclean spirits saw Him, they fell down before Him and cried out, “You are the Son of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.12', 'BSB', 'But He warned them sternly not to make Him known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.13', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus went up on the mountain and called for those He wanted, and they came to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.14', 'BSB', 'He appointed twelve of them, whom He designated as apostles, to accompany Him, to be sent out to preach,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.15', 'BSB', 'and to have authority to drive out demons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.16', 'BSB', 'These are the twelve He appointed: Simon (whom He named Peter),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.17', 'BSB', 'James son of Zebedee and his brother John (whom He named Boanerges, meaning “Sons of Thunder”),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.18', 'BSB', 'Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, James son of Alphaeus, Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.19', 'BSB', 'and Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.20', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus went home, and once again a crowd gathered, so that He and His disciples could not even eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.21', 'BSB', 'When His family heard about this, they went out to take custody of Him, saying, “He is out of His mind.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.22', 'BSB', 'And the scribes who had come down from Jerusalem were saying, “He is possessed by Beelzebul,” and, “By the prince of the demons He drives out demons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.23', 'BSB', 'So Jesus called them together and began to speak to them in parables: “How can Satan drive out Satan?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.24', 'BSB', 'If a kingdom is divided against itself, it cannot stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.25', 'BSB', 'If a house is divided against itself, it cannot stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.26', 'BSB', 'And if Satan is divided and rises against himself, he cannot stand; his end has come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.27', 'BSB', 'Indeed, no one can enter a strong man’s house to steal his possessions unless he first ties up the strong man. Then he can plunder his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.28', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, the sons of men will be forgiven all sins and blasphemies, as many as they utter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.29', 'BSB', 'But whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will never be forgiven; he is guilty of eternal sin.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.30', 'BSB', 'Jesus made this statement because they were saying, “He has an unclean spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.31', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came and stood outside. They sent someone in to summon Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.32', 'BSB', 'and a crowd was sitting around Him. “Look,” He was told, “Your mother and brothers are outside, asking for You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.33', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “Who are My mother and My brothers?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.34', 'BSB', 'Looking at those seated in a circle around Him, He said, “Here are My mother and My brothers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.3.35', 'BSB', 'For whoever does the will of God is My brother and sister and mother.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.1', 'BSB', 'Once again Jesus began to teach beside the sea, and such a large crowd gathered around Him that He got into a boat and sat in it, while all the people crowded along the shore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.2', 'BSB', 'And He taught them many things in parables, and in His teaching He said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.3', 'BSB', '“Listen! A farmer went out to sow his seed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.4', 'BSB', 'And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, and the birds came and devoured it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.5', 'BSB', 'Some fell on rocky ground, where it did not have much soil. It sprang up quickly because the soil was shallow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.6', 'BSB', 'But when the sun rose, the seedlings were scorched, and they withered because they had no root.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.7', 'BSB', 'Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up and choked the seedlings, and they yielded no crop.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.8', 'BSB', 'Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprouted, grew up, and produced a crop—one bearing thirtyfold, another sixtyfold, and another a hundredfold.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.9', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said, “He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.10', 'BSB', 'As soon as Jesus was alone with the Twelve and those around Him, they asked Him about the parable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.11', 'BSB', 'He replied, “The mystery of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to those on the outside everything is expressed in parables,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.12', 'BSB', 'so that, ‘they may be ever seeing but never perceiving, and ever hearing but never understanding; otherwise they might turn and be forgiven.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.13', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Do you not understand this parable? Then how will you understand any of the parables?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.14', 'BSB', 'The farmer sows the word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.15', 'BSB', 'Some are like the seeds along the path, where the word is sown. As soon as they hear it, Satan comes and takes away the word that was sown in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.16', 'BSB', 'Some are like the seeds sown on rocky ground. They hear the word and at once receive it with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.17', 'BSB', 'But they themselves have no root, and they remain for only a season. When trouble or persecution comes because of the word, they quickly fall away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.18', 'BSB', 'Others are like the seeds sown among the thorns. They hear the word,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.19', 'BSB', 'but the worries of this life, the deceitfulness of wealth, and the desire for other things come in and choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.20', 'BSB', 'Still others are like the seeds sown on good soil. They hear the word, receive it, and produce a crop—thirtyfold, sixtyfold, or a hundredfold.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus also said to them, “Does anyone bring in a lamp to put it under a basket or under a bed? Doesn’t he set it on a stand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.22', 'BSB', 'For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, and nothing concealed that will not be brought to light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.23', 'BSB', 'If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.24', 'BSB', 'He went on to say, “Pay attention to what you hear. With the measure you use, it will be measured to you, and even more will be added to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.25', 'BSB', 'For whoever has will be given more. But whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus also said, “The kingdom of God is like a man who scatters seed on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.27', 'BSB', 'Night and day he sleeps and wakes, and the seed sprouts and grows, though he knows not how.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.28', 'BSB', 'All by itself the earth produces a crop—first the stalk, then the head, then grain that ripens within.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.29', 'BSB', 'And as soon as the grain is ripe, he swings the sickle, because the harvest has come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.30', 'BSB', 'Then He asked, “To what can we compare the kingdom of God? With what parable shall we present it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.31', 'BSB', 'It is like a mustard seed, which is the smallest of all seeds sown upon the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.32', 'BSB', 'But after it is planted, it grows to be the largest of all garden plants and puts forth great branches, so that the birds of the air nest in its shade.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.33', 'BSB', 'With many such parables Jesus spoke the word to them, to the extent that they could understand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.34', 'BSB', 'He did not tell them anything without using a parable. But privately He explained everything to His own disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.35', 'BSB', 'When that evening came, He said to His disciples, “Let us cross to the other side.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.36', 'BSB', 'After they had dismissed the crowd, they took Jesus with them, since He was already in the boat. And there were other boats with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.37', 'BSB', 'Soon a violent windstorm came up, and the waves were breaking over the boat, so that it was being swamped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.38', 'BSB', 'But Jesus was in the stern, sleeping on the cushion. So they woke Him and said, “Teacher, don’t You care that we are perishing?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.39', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus got up and rebuked the wind and the sea. “Silence!” He commanded. “Be still!” And the wind died down, and it was perfectly calm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.40', 'BSB', '“Why are you so afraid?” He asked. “Do you still have no faith?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.4.41', 'BSB', 'Overwhelmed with fear, they asked one another, “Who is this, that even the wind and the sea obey Him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.1', 'BSB', 'On the other side of the sea, they arrived in the region of the Gerasenes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.2', 'BSB', 'As soon as Jesus got out of the boat, He was met by a man with an unclean spirit, who was coming from the tombs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.3', 'BSB', 'This man had been living in the tombs and could no longer be restrained, even with chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.4', 'BSB', 'Though he was often bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains and shattered the shackles. Now there was no one with the strength to subdue him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.5', 'BSB', 'Night and day in the tombs and in the mountains he kept crying out and cutting himself with stones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.6', 'BSB', 'When the man saw Jesus from a distance, he ran and fell on his knees before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.7', 'BSB', 'And he shouted in a loud voice, “What do You want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You before God not to torture me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.8', 'BSB', 'For Jesus had already declared, “Come out of this man, you unclean spirit!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.9', 'BSB', '“What is your name?” Jesus asked. “My name is Legion,” he replied, “for we are many.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.10', 'BSB', 'And he begged Jesus repeatedly not to send them out of that region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.11', 'BSB', 'There on the nearby hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.12', 'BSB', 'So the demons begged Jesus, “Send us to the pigs, so that we may enter them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.13', 'BSB', 'He gave them permission, and the unclean spirits came out and went into the pigs, and the herd of about two thousand rushed down the steep bank into the sea and drowned in the water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.14', 'BSB', 'Those tending the pigs ran off and reported this in the town and countryside, and the people went out to see what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.15', 'BSB', 'When they came to Jesus, they saw the man who had been possessed by the legion of demons sitting there, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.16', 'BSB', 'Those who had seen it described what had happened to the demon-possessed man and also to the pigs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.17', 'BSB', 'And the people began to beg Jesus to leave their region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.18', 'BSB', 'As He was getting into the boat, the man who had been possessed by the demons begged to go with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.19', 'BSB', 'But Jesus would not allow him. “Go home to your own people,” He said, “and tell them how much the Lord has done for you, and what mercy He has shown you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.20', 'BSB', 'So the man went away and began to proclaim throughout the Decapolis how much Jesus had done for him. And everyone was amazed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.21', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had again crossed by boat to the other side, a large crowd gathered around Him beside the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.22', 'BSB', 'A synagogue leader named Jairus arrived, and seeing Jesus, he fell at His feet', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.23', 'BSB', 'and pleaded with Him urgently, “My little daughter is near death. Please come and place Your hands on her, so that she will be healed and live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.24', 'BSB', 'So Jesus went with him, and a large crowd followed and pressed around Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.25', 'BSB', 'And a woman was there who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.26', 'BSB', 'She had borne much agony under the care of many physicians and had spent all she had, but to no avail. Instead, her condition had only grown worse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.27', 'BSB', 'When the woman heard about Jesus, she came up through the crowd behind Him and touched His cloak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.28', 'BSB', 'For she kept saying, “If only I touch His garments, I will be healed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.29', 'BSB', 'Immediately her bleeding stopped, and she sensed in her body that she was healed of her affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.30', 'BSB', 'At once Jesus was aware that power had gone out from Him. Turning to the crowd, He asked, “Who touched My garments?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.31', 'BSB', 'His disciples answered, “You can see the crowd pressing in on You, and yet You ask, ‘Who touched Me?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.32', 'BSB', 'But He kept looking around to see who had done this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.33', 'BSB', 'Then the woman, knowing what had happened to her, came and fell down before Him trembling in fear, and she told Him the whole truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.34', 'BSB', '“Daughter,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you. Go in peace and be free of your affliction.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.35', 'BSB', 'While He was still speaking, messengers from the house of Jairus arrived and said, “Your daughter is dead; why bother the Teacher anymore?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.36', 'BSB', 'But Jesus overheard their conversation and said to Jairus, “Do not be afraid; just believe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.37', 'BSB', 'And He did not allow anyone to accompany Him except Peter, James, and John the brother of James.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.38', 'BSB', 'When they arrived at the house of the synagogue leader, Jesus saw the commotion and the people weeping and wailing loudly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.39', 'BSB', 'He went inside and asked, “Why all this commotion and weeping? The child is not dead, but asleep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.40', 'BSB', 'And they laughed at Him. After He had put them all outside, He took the child’s father and mother and His own companions, and went in to see the child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.41', 'BSB', 'Taking her by the hand, Jesus said, “Talitha koum!” which means, “Little girl, I say to you, get up!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.42', 'BSB', 'Immediately the girl got up and began to walk around. She was twelve years old, and at once they were utterly astounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.5.43', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus gave strict orders that no one should know about this, and He told them to give her something to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.1', 'BSB', 'Jesus went on from there and came to His hometown, accompanied by His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.2', 'BSB', 'When the Sabbath came, He began to teach in the synagogue, and many who heard Him were astonished. “Where did this man get these ideas?” they asked. “What is this wisdom He has been given? And how can He perform such miracles?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.3', 'BSB', 'Isn’t this the carpenter, the son of Mary and the brother of James, Joses, Judas, and Simon? Aren’t His sisters here with us as well?” And they took offense at Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.4', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Only in his hometown, among his relatives, and in his own household is a prophet without honor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.5', 'BSB', 'So He could not perform any miracles there, except to lay His hands on a few of the sick and heal them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.6', 'BSB', 'And He was amazed at their unbelief. And He went around from village to village, teaching the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.7', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus called the Twelve to Him and began to send them out two by two, giving them authority over unclean spirits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.8', 'BSB', 'He instructed them to take nothing but a staff for the journey—no bread, no bag, no money in their belts—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.9', 'BSB', 'and to wear sandals, but not a second tunic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.10', 'BSB', 'And He told them, “When you enter a house, stay there until you leave that area.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.11', 'BSB', 'If anyone will not welcome you or listen to you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that place, as a testimony against them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.12', 'BSB', 'So they set out and preached that the people should repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.13', 'BSB', 'They also drove out many demons and healed many of the sick, anointing them with oil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.14', 'BSB', 'Now King Herod heard about this, for Jesus’ name had become well known, and people were saying, “John the Baptist has risen from the dead! That is why miraculous powers are at work in him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.15', 'BSB', 'Others were saying, “He is Elijah,” and still others, “He is a prophet, like one of the prophets of old.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.16', 'BSB', 'But when Herod heard this, he said, “John, whom I beheaded, has risen from the dead!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.17', 'BSB', 'For Herod himself had ordered that John be arrested and bound and imprisoned, on account of his brother Philip’s wife Herodias, whom Herod had married.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.18', 'BSB', 'For John had been telling Herod, “It is not lawful for you to have your brother’s wife!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.19', 'BSB', 'So Herodias held a grudge against John and wanted to kill him. But she had been unable,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.20', 'BSB', 'because Herod feared John and protected him, knowing that he was a righteous and holy man. When he heard John’s words, he was greatly perplexed; yet he listened to him gladly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.21', 'BSB', 'On Herod’s birthday, her opportunity arose. Herod held a banquet for his nobles and military commanders and the leading men of Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.22', 'BSB', 'When the daughter of Herodias came and danced, she pleased Herod and his guests, and the king said to the girl, “Ask me for whatever you wish, and I will give it to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.23', 'BSB', 'And he swore to her, “Whatever you ask of me, I will give you, up to half my kingdom!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.24', 'BSB', 'Then she went out and asked her mother, “What should I request?” And her mother answered, “The head of John the Baptist.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.25', 'BSB', 'At once the girl hurried back to the king with her request: “I want you to give me the head of John the Baptist on a platter immediately.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.26', 'BSB', 'The king was consumed with sorrow, but because of his oaths and his guests, he did not want to refuse her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.27', 'BSB', 'So without delay, the king commanded that John’s head be brought in. He sent an executioner, who went and beheaded him in the prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.28', 'BSB', 'The man brought John’s head on a platter and presented it to the girl, who gave it to her mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.29', 'BSB', 'When John’s disciples heard about this, they came and took his body and placed it in a tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.30', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the apostles gathered around Jesus and brought Him news of all they had done and taught.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.31', 'BSB', 'And He said to them, “Come with Me privately to a solitary place, and let us rest for a while.” For many people were coming and going, and they did not even have time to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.32', 'BSB', 'So they went away in a boat by themselves to a solitary place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.33', 'BSB', 'But many people saw them leaving and recognized them. They ran together on foot from all the towns and arrived before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.34', 'BSB', 'When Jesus stepped ashore and saw a large crowd, He had compassion on them, because they were like sheep without a shepherd. And He began to teach them many things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.35', 'BSB', 'By now the hour was already late. So the disciples came to Jesus and said, “This is a desolate place, and the hour is already late.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.36', 'BSB', 'Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding countryside and villages and buy themselves something to eat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.37', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told them, “You give them something to eat.” They asked Him, “Should we go out and spend two hundred denarii to give all of them bread to eat?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.38', 'BSB', '“Go and see how many loaves you have,” He told them. And after checking, they said, “Five—and two fish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.39', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus directed them to have the people sit in groups on the green grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.40', 'BSB', 'So they sat down in groups of hundreds and fifties.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.41', 'BSB', 'Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing and broke the loaves. Then He gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And He divided the two fish among them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.42', 'BSB', 'They all ate and were satisfied,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.43', 'BSB', 'and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces of bread and fish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.44', 'BSB', 'And there were five thousand men who had eaten the loaves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.45', 'BSB', 'Immediately Jesus made His disciples get into the boat and go on ahead of Him to Bethsaida, while He dismissed the crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.46', 'BSB', 'After bidding them farewell, He went up on the mountain to pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.47', 'BSB', 'When evening came, the boat was in the middle of the sea, and Jesus was alone on land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.48', 'BSB', 'He could see that the disciples were straining to row, because the wind was against them. About the fourth watch of the night, Jesus went out to them, walking on the sea. He intended to pass by them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.49', 'BSB', 'but when they saw Him walking on the sea, they cried out, thinking He was a ghost—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.50', 'BSB', 'for they all saw Him and were terrified. But Jesus spoke up at once: “Take courage! It is I. Do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.51', 'BSB', 'Then He climbed into the boat with them, and the wind died down. And the disciples were utterly astounded,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.52', 'BSB', 'for they had not understood about the loaves, but their hearts had been hardened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.53', 'BSB', 'When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret and moored the boat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.54', 'BSB', 'As soon as they got out of the boat, the people recognized Jesus', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.55', 'BSB', 'and ran through that whole region, carrying the sick on mats to wherever they heard He was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.6.56', 'BSB', 'And wherever He went—villages and towns and countrysides—they laid the sick in the marketplaces and begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak. And all who touched Him were healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.1', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees and some of the scribes who had come from Jerusalem gathered around Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.2', 'BSB', 'and they saw some of His disciples eating with hands that were defiled—that is, unwashed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.3', 'BSB', 'Now in holding to the tradition of the elders, the Pharisees and all the Jews do not eat until they wash their hands ceremonially.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.4', 'BSB', 'And on returning from the market, they do not eat unless they wash. And there are many other traditions for them to observe, including the washing of cups, pitchers, kettles, and couches for dining.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.5', 'BSB', 'So the Pharisees and scribes questioned Jesus: “Why do Your disciples not walk according to the tradition of the elders? Instead, they eat with defiled hands.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.6', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered them, “Isaiah prophesied correctly about you hypocrites, as it is written: ‘These people honor Me with their lips, but their hearts are far from Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.7', 'BSB', 'They worship Me in vain; they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.8', 'BSB', 'You have disregarded the commandment of God to keep the tradition of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.9', 'BSB', 'He went on to say, “You neatly set aside the command of God to maintain your own tradition.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.10', 'BSB', 'For Moses said, ‘Honor your father and your mother’ and ‘Anyone who curses his father or mother must be put to death.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.11', 'BSB', 'But you say that if a man says to his father or mother, ‘Whatever you would have received from me is Corban’ (that is, a gift devoted to God),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.12', 'BSB', 'he is no longer permitted to do anything for his father or mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.13', 'BSB', 'Thus you nullify the word of God by the tradition you have handed down. And you do so in many such matters.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.14', 'BSB', 'Once again Jesus called the crowd to Him and said, “All of you, listen to Me and understand:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.15', 'BSB', 'Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him; but the things that come out of a man, these are what defile him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.17', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had left the crowd and gone into the house, His disciples inquired about the parable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.18', 'BSB', '“Are you still so dull?” He asked. “Do you not understand? Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.19', 'BSB', 'because it does not enter his heart, but it goes into the stomach and then is eliminated.” (Thus all foods are clean.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.20', 'BSB', 'He continued: “What comes out of a man, that is what defiles him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.21', 'BSB', 'For from within the hearts of men come evil thoughts, sexual immorality, theft, murder, adultery,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.22', 'BSB', 'greed, wickedness, deceit, debauchery, envy, slander, arrogance, and foolishness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.23', 'BSB', 'All these evils come from within, and these are what defile a man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.24', 'BSB', 'Jesus left that place and went to the region of Tyre. Not wanting anyone to know He was there, He entered a house, but was unable to escape their notice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.25', 'BSB', 'Instead, a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit soon heard about Jesus, and she came and fell at His feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.26', 'BSB', 'Now she was a Greek woman of Syrophoenician origin, and she kept asking Jesus to drive the demon out of her daughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.27', 'BSB', '“First let the children have their fill,” He said. “For it is not right to take the children’s bread and toss it to the dogs.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.28', 'BSB', '“Yes, Lord,” she replied, “even the dogs under the table eat the children’s crumbs.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.29', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told her, “Because of this answer, you may go. The demon has left your daughter.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.30', 'BSB', 'And she went home and found her child lying on the bed, and the demon was gone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.31', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus left the region of Tyre and went through Sidon to the Sea of Galilee and into the region of the Decapolis.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.32', 'BSB', 'Some people brought to Him a man who was deaf and hardly able to speak, and they begged Jesus to place His hand on him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.33', 'BSB', 'So Jesus took him aside privately, away from the crowd, and put His fingers into the man’s ears. Then He spit and touched the man’s tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.34', 'BSB', 'And looking up to heaven, He sighed deeply and said to him, “Ephphatha!” (which means, “Be opened!”).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.35', 'BSB', 'Immediately the man’s ears were opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak plainly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.36', 'BSB', 'Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone. But the more He ordered them, the more widely they proclaimed it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.7.37', 'BSB', 'The people were utterly astonished and said, “He has done all things well! He makes even the deaf hear and the mute speak!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.1', 'BSB', 'In those days the crowd once again became very large, and they had nothing to eat. Jesus called the disciples to Him and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.2', 'BSB', '“I have compassion for this crowd, because they have already been with Me three days and have nothing to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.3', 'BSB', 'If I send them home hungry, they will faint along the way. For some of them have come a great distance.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.4', 'BSB', 'His disciples replied, “Where in this desolate place could anyone find enough bread to feed all these people?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.5', 'BSB', '“How many loaves do you have?” Jesus asked. “Seven,” they replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.6', 'BSB', 'And He instructed the crowd to sit down on the ground. Then He took the seven loaves, gave thanks and broke them, and gave them to His disciples to set before the people. And they distributed them to the crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.7', 'BSB', 'They also had a few small fish, and Jesus blessed them and ordered that these be set before them as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.8', 'BSB', 'The people ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up seven basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.9', 'BSB', 'And about four thousand men were present. As soon as Jesus had dismissed the crowd,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.10', 'BSB', 'He got into the boat with His disciples and went to the district of Dalmanutha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.11', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees came and began to argue with Jesus, testing Him by demanding from Him a sign from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.12', 'BSB', 'Jesus sighed deeply in His spirit and said, “Why does this generation demand a sign? Truly I tell you, no sign will be given to this generation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.13', 'BSB', 'And He left them, got back into the boat, and crossed to the other side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.14', 'BSB', 'Now the disciples had forgotten to take bread, except for one loaf they had with them in the boat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.15', 'BSB', '“Watch out!” He cautioned them. “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of Herod.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.16', 'BSB', 'So they began to discuss with one another the fact that they had no bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.17', 'BSB', 'Aware of their conversation, Jesus asked them, “Why are you debating about having no bread? Do you still not see or understand? Do you have such hard hearts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.18', 'BSB', '‘Having eyes, do you not see? And having ears, do you not hear?’ And do you not remember?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.19', 'BSB', 'When I broke the five loaves for the five thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Twelve,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.20', 'BSB', '“And when I broke the seven loaves for the four thousand, how many basketfuls of broken pieces did you collect?” “Seven,” they said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.21', 'BSB', 'Then He asked them, “Do you still not understand?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.22', 'BSB', 'When they arrived at Bethsaida, some people brought a blind man and begged Jesus to touch him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.23', 'BSB', 'So He took the blind man by the hand and led him out of the village. Then He spit on the man’s eyes and placed His hands on him. “Can you see anything?” He asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.24', 'BSB', 'The man looked up and said, “I can see the people, but they look like trees walking around.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.25', 'BSB', 'Once again Jesus placed His hands on the man’s eyes, and when he opened them his sight was restored, and he could see everything clearly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus sent him home and said, “Do not go back into the village.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.27', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus and His disciples went on to the villages around Caesarea Philippi. On the way, He questioned His disciples: “Who do people say I am?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.28', 'BSB', 'They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, one of the prophets.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.29', 'BSB', '“But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?” Peter answered, “You are the Christ.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.30', 'BSB', 'And Jesus warned them not to tell anyone about Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.31', 'BSB', 'Then He began to teach them that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and that He must be killed and after three days rise again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.32', 'BSB', 'He spoke this message quite frankly, and Peter took Him aside and began to rebuke Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.33', 'BSB', 'But Jesus, turning and looking at His disciples, rebuked Peter and said, “Get behind Me, Satan! For you do not have in mind the things of God, but the things of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.34', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus called the crowd to Him along with His disciples, and He told them, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross and follow Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.35', 'BSB', 'For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake and for the gospel will save it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.36', 'BSB', 'What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet forfeit his soul?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.37', 'BSB', 'Or what can a man give in exchange for his soul?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.8.38', 'BSB', 'If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words in this adulterous and sinful generation, the Son of Man will also be ashamed of him when He comes in His Father’s glory with the holy angels.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Truly I tell you, there are some standing here who will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God arrive with power.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.2', 'BSB', 'After six days Jesus took with Him Peter, James, and John, and led them up a high mountain by themselves. There He was transfigured before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.3', 'BSB', 'His clothes became radiantly white, brighter than any launderer on earth could bleach them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.4', 'BSB', 'And Elijah and Moses appeared before them, talking with Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.5', 'BSB', 'Peter said to Jesus, “Rabbi, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters —one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.6', 'BSB', 'For they were all so terrified that Peter did not know what else to say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.7', 'BSB', 'Then a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and a voice came from the cloud: “This is My beloved Son. Listen to Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.8', 'BSB', 'Suddenly, when they looked around, they saw no one with them except Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.9', 'BSB', 'As they were coming down the mountain, Jesus admonished them not to tell anyone what they had seen until the Son of Man had risen from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.10', 'BSB', 'So they kept this matter to themselves, discussing what it meant to rise from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.11', 'BSB', 'And they asked Jesus, “Why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.12', 'BSB', 'He replied, “Elijah does indeed come first, and he restores all things. Why then is it written that the Son of Man must suffer many things and be rejected?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.13', 'BSB', 'But I tell you that Elijah has indeed come, and they have done to him whatever they wished, just as it is written about him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.14', 'BSB', 'When they returned to the other disciples, they saw a large crowd around them, and scribes arguing with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.15', 'BSB', 'As soon as all the people saw Jesus, they were filled with awe and ran to greet Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.16', 'BSB', '“What are you disputing with them?” He asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.17', 'BSB', 'Someone in the crowd replied, “Teacher, I brought You my son, who has a spirit that makes him mute.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.18', 'BSB', 'Whenever it seizes him, it throws him to the ground. He foams at the mouth, gnashes his teeth, and becomes rigid. I asked Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.19', 'BSB', '“O unbelieving generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you? How long must I put up with you? Bring the boy to Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.20', 'BSB', 'So they brought him, and seeing Jesus, the spirit immediately threw the boy into a convulsion. He fell to the ground and rolled around, foaming at the mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus asked the boy’s father, “How long has this been with him?” “From childhood,” he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.22', 'BSB', '“It often throws him into the fire or into the water, trying to kill him. But if You can do anything, have compassion on us and help us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.23', 'BSB', '“If You can?” echoed Jesus. “All things are possible to him who believes!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.24', 'BSB', 'Immediately the boy’s father cried out, “I do believe; help my unbelief!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.25', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw that a crowd had come running, He rebuked the unclean spirit. “You deaf and mute spirit,” He said, “I command you to come out and never enter him again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.26', 'BSB', 'After shrieking and convulsing him violently, the spirit came out. The boy became like a corpse, so that many said, “He is dead.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.27', 'BSB', 'But Jesus took him by the hand and helped him to his feet, and he stood up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.28', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had gone into the house, His disciples asked Him privately, “Why couldn’t we drive it out?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.29', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “This kind cannot come out, except by prayer.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.30', 'BSB', 'Going on from there, they passed through Galilee. But Jesus did not want anyone to know,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.31', 'BSB', 'because He was teaching His disciples. He told them, “The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men. They will kill Him, and after three days He will rise.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.32', 'BSB', 'But they did not understand this statement, and they were afraid to ask Him about it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.33', 'BSB', 'Then they came to Capernaum. While Jesus was in the house, He asked them, “What were you discussing on the way?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.34', 'BSB', 'But they were silent, for on the way they had been arguing about which of them was the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.35', 'BSB', 'Sitting down, Jesus called the Twelve and said, “If anyone wants to be first, he must be the last of all and the servant of all.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.36', 'BSB', 'Then He had a little child stand among them. Taking the child in His arms, He said to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.37', 'BSB', '“Whoever welcomes one of these little children in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes not only Me, but the One who sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.38', 'BSB', 'John said to Him, “Teacher, we saw someone else driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.39', 'BSB', '“Do not stop him,” Jesus replied. “For no one who performs a miracle in My name can turn around and speak evil of Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.40', 'BSB', 'For whoever is not against us is for us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.41', 'BSB', 'Indeed, if anyone gives you even a cup of water because you bear the name of Christ, truly I tell you, he will never lose his reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.42', 'BSB', 'But if anyone causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it would be better for him to have a large millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.43', 'BSB', 'If your hand causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life crippled than to have two hands and go into hell, into the unquenchable fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.45', 'BSB', 'If your foot causes you to sin, cut it off. It is better for you to enter life lame than to have two feet and be thrown into hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.47', 'BSB', 'And if your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of God with one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into hell,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.48', 'BSB', 'where ‘their worm never dies, and the fire is never quenched.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.49', 'BSB', 'For everyone will be salted with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.9.50', 'BSB', 'Salt is good, but if the salt loses its saltiness, with what will you season it? Have salt among yourselves, and be at peace with one another.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus left that place and went into the region of Judea, beyond the Jordan. Again the crowds came to Him and He taught them, as was His custom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.2', 'BSB', 'Some Pharisees came to test Him. “Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife?” they inquired.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.3', 'BSB', '“What did Moses command you?” He replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.4', 'BSB', 'They answered, “Moses permitted a man to write his wife a certificate of divorce and send her away.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.5', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told them, “Moses wrote this commandment for you because of your hardness of heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.6', 'BSB', 'However, from the beginning of creation, ‘God made them male and female.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.7', 'BSB', '‘For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.8', 'BSB', 'and the two will become one flesh.’ So they are no longer two, but one flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore what God has joined together, let man not separate.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.10', 'BSB', 'When they were back inside the house, the disciples asked Jesus about this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.11', 'BSB', 'So He told them, “Whoever divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.12', 'BSB', 'And if a woman divorces her husband and marries another man, she commits adultery.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.13', 'BSB', 'Now people were bringing the little children to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them, and the disciples rebuked those who brought them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.14', 'BSB', 'But when Jesus saw this, He was indignant and told them, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.15', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.16', 'BSB', 'And He took the children in His arms, placed His hands on them, and blessed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.17', 'BSB', 'As Jesus started on His way, a man ran up and knelt before Him. “Good Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.18', 'BSB', '“Why do you call Me good?” Jesus replied. “No one is good except God alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.19', 'BSB', 'You know the commandments: ‘Do not murder, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not bear false witness, do not cheat others, honor your father and mother.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.20', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” he replied, “all these I have kept from my youth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus looked at him, loved him, and said to him, “There is one thing you lack: Go, sell everything you own and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.22', 'BSB', 'But the man was saddened by these words and went away in sorrow, because he had great wealth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.23', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus looked around and said to His disciples, “How hard it is for the rich to enter the kingdom of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.24', 'BSB', 'And the disciples were amazed at His words. But Jesus said to them again, “Children, how hard it is to enter the kingdom of God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.25', 'BSB', 'It is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.26', 'BSB', 'They were even more astonished and said to one another, “Who then can be saved?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.27', 'BSB', 'Jesus looked at them and said, “With man this is impossible, but not with God. For all things are possible with God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.28', 'BSB', 'Peter began to say to Him, “Look, we have left everything and followed You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.29', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “no one who has left home or brothers or sisters or mother or father or children or fields for My sake and for the gospel', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.30', 'BSB', 'will fail to receive a hundredfold in the present age—houses and brothers and sisters and mothers and children and fields, along with persecutions—and in the age to come, eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.31', 'BSB', 'But many who are first will be last, and the last will be first.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.32', 'BSB', 'As they were going up the road to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking ahead of them. The disciples were amazed, but those who followed were afraid. Again Jesus took the Twelve aside and began to tell them what was going to happen to Him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.33', 'BSB', '“Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be delivered over to the chief priests and scribes. They will condemn Him to death and will deliver Him over to the Gentiles,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.34', 'BSB', 'who will mock Him and spit on Him and flog Him and kill Him. And after three days He will rise again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.35', 'BSB', 'Then James and John, the sons of Zebedee, came to Jesus and declared, “Teacher, we want You to do for us whatever we ask.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.36', 'BSB', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” He inquired.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.37', 'BSB', 'They answered, “Grant that one of us may sit at Your right hand and the other at Your left in Your glory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.38', 'BSB', '“You do not know what you are asking,” Jesus replied. “Can you drink the cup I will drink, or be baptized with the baptism I will undergo?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.39', 'BSB', '“We can,” the brothers answered. “You will drink the cup that I drink,” Jesus said, “and you will be baptized with the baptism that I undergo.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.40', 'BSB', 'But to sit at My right or left is not Mine to grant. These seats belong to those for whom they have been prepared.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.41', 'BSB', 'When the ten heard about this, they became indignant with James and John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.42', 'BSB', 'So Jesus called them together and said, “You know that those regarded as rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their superiors exercise authority over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.43', 'BSB', 'But it shall not be this way among you. Instead, whoever wants to become great among you must be your servant,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.44', 'BSB', 'and whoever wants to be first must be the slave of all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.45', 'BSB', 'For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.46', 'BSB', 'Next, they came to Jericho. And as Jesus and His disciples were leaving Jericho with a large crowd, a blind beggar named Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, was sitting beside the road.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.47', 'BSB', 'When he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.48', 'BSB', 'Many people admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.49', 'BSB', 'Jesus stopped and said, “Call him.” So they called the blind man. “Take courage!” they said. “Get up! He is calling for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.50', 'BSB', 'Throwing off his cloak, Bartimaeus jumped up and came to Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.51', 'BSB', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” Jesus asked. “Rabboni,” said the blind man, “let me see again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.10.52', 'BSB', '“Go,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you.” And immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus along the road.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.1', 'BSB', 'As they approached Jerusalem and came to Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, Jesus sent out two of His disciples', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.2', 'BSB', 'and said to them, “Go into the village ahead of you, and as soon as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there, on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.3', 'BSB', 'If anyone asks, ‘Why are you doing this?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it and will return it shortly.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.4', 'BSB', 'So they went and found the colt outside in the street, tied at a doorway. They untied it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.5', 'BSB', 'and some who were standing there asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.6', 'BSB', 'The disciples answered as Jesus had instructed them, and the people gave them permission.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.7', 'BSB', 'Then they led the colt to Jesus and threw their cloaks over it, and He sat on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.8', 'BSB', 'Many in the crowd spread their cloaks on the road, while others spread branches they had cut from the fields.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.9', 'BSB', 'The ones who went ahead and those who followed were shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.10', 'BSB', '“Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!” “Hosanna in the highest!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.11', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus entered Jerusalem and went into the temple courts. He looked around at everything, but since it was already late, He went out to Bethany with the Twelve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.12', 'BSB', 'The next day, when they had left Bethany, Jesus was hungry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.13', 'BSB', 'Seeing in the distance a fig tree in leaf, He went to see if there was any fruit on it. But when He reached it, He found nothing on it except leaves, since it was not the season for figs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.14', 'BSB', 'Then He said to the tree, “May no one ever eat of your fruit again.” And His disciples heard this statement.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.15', 'BSB', 'When they arrived in Jerusalem, Jesus entered the temple courts and began to drive out those who were buying and selling there. He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling doves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.16', 'BSB', 'And He would not allow anyone to carry merchandise through the temple courts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.17', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus began to teach them, and He declared, “Is it not written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’? But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.18', 'BSB', 'When the chief priests and scribes heard this, they looked for a way to kill Him. For they were afraid of Him, because the whole crowd was astonished at His teaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.19', 'BSB', 'And when evening came, Jesus and His disciples went out of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.20', 'BSB', 'As they were walking back in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered from its roots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.21', 'BSB', 'Peter remembered it and said, “Look, Rabbi! The fig tree You cursed has withered.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.22', 'BSB', '“Have faith in God,” Jesus said to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.23', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you that if anyone says to this mountain, ‘Be lifted up and thrown into the sea,’ and has no doubt in his heart but believes that it will happen, it will be done for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore I tell you, whatever you ask for in prayer, believe that you have received it, and it will be yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.25', 'BSB', 'And when you stand to pray, if you hold anything against another, forgive it, so that your Father in heaven will forgive your trespasses as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.27', 'BSB', 'After their return to Jerusalem, Jesus was walking in the temple courts, and the chief priests, scribes, and elders came up to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.28', 'BSB', '“By what authority are You doing these things?” they asked. “And who gave You the authority to do them?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.29', 'BSB', '“I will ask you one question,” Jesus replied, “and if you answer Me, I will tell you by what authority I am doing these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.30', 'BSB', 'John’s baptism—was it from heaven or from men? Answer Me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.31', 'BSB', 'They deliberated among themselves what they should answer: “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why then did you not believe him?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.32', 'BSB', 'But if we say, ‘From men’...” they were afraid of the people, for they all held that John truly was a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.11.33', 'BSB', 'So they answered, “We do not know.” And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus began to speak to them in parables: “A man planted a vineyard. He put a wall around it, dug a wine vat, and built a watchtower. Then he rented it out to some tenants and went away on a journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.2', 'BSB', 'At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.3', 'BSB', 'But they seized the servant, beat him, and sent him away empty-handed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.4', 'BSB', 'Then he sent them another servant, and they struck him over the head and treated him shamefully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.5', 'BSB', 'He sent still another, and this one they killed. He sent many others; some they beat and others they killed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.6', 'BSB', 'Finally, having one beloved son, he sent him to them. ‘They will respect my son,’ he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.7', 'BSB', 'But the tenants said to one another, ‘This is the heir. Come, let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.8', 'BSB', 'So they seized the son, killed him, and threw him out of the vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.9', 'BSB', 'What then will the owner of the vineyard do? He will come and kill those tenants, and will give the vineyard to others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.10', 'BSB', 'Have you never read this Scripture: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.11', 'BSB', 'This is from the Lord, and it is marvelous in our eyes’?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.12', 'BSB', 'At this, the leaders sought to arrest Jesus, for they knew that He had spoken this parable against them. But fearing the crowd, they left Him and went away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.13', 'BSB', 'Later, they sent some of the Pharisees and Herodians to catch Jesus in His words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.14', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” they said, “we know that You are honest and seek favor from no one. Indeed, You are impartial and teach the way of God in accordance with the truth. Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar or not? Should we pay them or not?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.15', 'BSB', 'But Jesus saw through their hypocrisy and said, “Why are you testing Me? Bring Me a denarius to inspect.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.16', 'BSB', 'So they brought it, and He asked them, “Whose image is this? And whose inscription?” “Caesar’s,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.17', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.” And they marveled at Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.18', 'BSB', 'Then the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to Jesus and questioned Him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.19', 'BSB', '“Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies and leaves a wife but no children, the man is to marry his brother’s widow and raise up offspring for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.20', 'BSB', 'Now there were seven brothers. The first one married and died, leaving no children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.21', 'BSB', 'Then the second one married the widow, but he also died and left no children. And the third did likewise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.22', 'BSB', 'In this way, none of the seven left any children. And last of all, the woman died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.23', 'BSB', 'In the resurrection, then, whose wife will she be? For all seven were married to her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.24', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “Aren’t you mistaken, because you do not know the Scriptures or the power of God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.25', 'BSB', 'When the dead rise, they will neither marry nor be given in marriage. Instead, they will be like the angels in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.26', 'BSB', 'But concerning the dead rising, have you not read about the burning bush in the Book of Moses, how God told him, ‘I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.27', 'BSB', 'He is not the God of the dead, but of the living. You are badly mistaken!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.28', 'BSB', 'Now one of the scribes had come up and heard their debate. Noticing how well Jesus had answered them, he asked Him, “Which commandment is the most important of all?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.29', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “This is the most important: ‘Hear O Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.30', 'BSB', 'Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind and with all your strength.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.31', 'BSB', 'The second is this: ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’ No other commandment is greater than these.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.32', 'BSB', '“Right, Teacher,” the scribe replied. “You have stated correctly that God is One and there is no other but Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.33', 'BSB', 'and to love Him with all your heart and with all your understanding and with all your strength, and to love your neighbor as yourself, which is more important than all burnt offerings and sacrifices.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.34', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw that the man had answered wisely, He said, “You are not far from the kingdom of God.” And no one dared to question Him any further.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.35', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was teaching in the temple courts, He asked, “How can the scribes say that the Christ is the Son of David?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.36', 'BSB', 'Speaking by the Holy Spirit, David himself declared: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand until I put Your enemies under Your feet.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.37', 'BSB', 'David himself calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be David’s son?” And the large crowd listened to Him with delight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.38', 'BSB', 'In His teaching Jesus also said, “Watch out for the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, to receive greetings in the marketplaces,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.39', 'BSB', 'and to have the chief seats in the synagogues and the places of honor at banquets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.40', 'BSB', 'They defraud widows of their houses, and for a show make lengthy prayers. These men will receive greater condemnation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.41', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was sitting opposite the treasury, He watched the crowd putting money into it. And many rich people put in large amounts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.42', 'BSB', 'Then one poor widow came and put in two small copper coins, which amounted to a small fraction of a denarius.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.43', 'BSB', 'Jesus called His disciples to Him and said, “Truly I tell you, this poor widow has put more than all the others into the treasury.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.12.44', 'BSB', 'For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.1', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was leaving the temple, one of His disciples said to Him, “Teacher, look at the magnificent stones and buildings!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.2', 'BSB', '“Do you see all these great buildings?” Jesus replied. “Not one stone here will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.3', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives opposite the temple, Peter, James, John, and Andrew asked Him privately,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.4', 'BSB', '“Tell us, when will these things happen? And what will be the sign that they are about to be fulfilled?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.5', 'BSB', 'Jesus began by telling them, “See to it that no one deceives you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.6', 'BSB', 'Many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am He,’ and will deceive many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.7', 'BSB', 'When you hear of wars and rumors of wars, do not be alarmed. These things must happen, but the end is still to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.8', 'BSB', 'Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be earthquakes in various places, as well as famines. These are the beginning of birth pains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.9', 'BSB', 'So be on your guard. You will be delivered over to the councils and beaten in the synagogues. On My account you will stand before governors and kings as witnesses to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.10', 'BSB', 'And the gospel must first be proclaimed to all the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.11', 'BSB', 'But when they arrest you and hand you over, do not worry beforehand what to say. Instead, speak whatever you are given at that time, for it will not be you speaking, but the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.12', 'BSB', 'Brother will betray brother to death, and a father his child. Children will rise against their parents and have them put to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.13', 'BSB', 'You will be hated by everyone because of My name, but the one who perseveres to the end will be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.14', 'BSB', 'So when you see the abomination of desolation standing where it should not be (let the reader understand), then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.15', 'BSB', 'Let no one on the housetop go back inside to retrieve anything from his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.16', 'BSB', 'And let no one in the field return for his cloak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.17', 'BSB', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.18', 'BSB', 'Pray that this will not occur in the winter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.19', 'BSB', 'For those will be days of tribulation unmatched from the beginning of God’s creation until now, and never to be seen again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.20', 'BSB', 'If the Lord had not cut short those days, nobody would be saved. But for the sake of the elect, whom He has chosen, He has cut them short.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.21', 'BSB', 'At that time if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is the Christ!’ or ‘There He is!’ do not believe it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.22', 'BSB', 'For false Christs and false prophets will appear and perform signs and wonders that would deceive even the elect, if that were possible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.23', 'BSB', 'So be on your guard; I have told you everything in advance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.24', 'BSB', 'But in those days, after that tribulation: ‘The sun will be darkened, and the moon will not give its light;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.25', 'BSB', 'the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.26', 'BSB', 'At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in the clouds with great power and glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.27', 'BSB', 'And He will send out the angels to gather His elect from the four winds, from the ends of the earth to the ends of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.28', 'BSB', 'Now learn this lesson from the fig tree: As soon as its branches become tender and sprout leaves, you know that summer is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.29', 'BSB', 'So also, when you see these things happening, know that He is near, right at the door.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.30', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.31', 'BSB', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.32', 'BSB', 'No one knows about that day or hour, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.33', 'BSB', 'Be on your guard and stay alert! For you do not know when the appointed time will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.34', 'BSB', 'It is like a man going on a journey who left his house, put each servant in charge of his own task, and instructed the doorkeeper to keep watch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.35', 'BSB', 'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know when the master of the house will return—whether in the evening, at midnight, when the rooster crows, or in the morning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.36', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, he may arrive without notice and find you sleeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.13.37', 'BSB', 'And what I say to you, I say to everyone: Keep watch!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.1', 'BSB', 'Now the Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread were two days away, and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a covert way to arrest Jesus and kill Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.2', 'BSB', '“But not during the feast,” they said, “or there may be a riot among the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.3', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was in Bethany reclining at the table in the home of Simon the Leper, a woman came with an alabaster jar of expensive perfume, made of pure nard. She broke open the jar and poured it on Jesus’ head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.4', 'BSB', 'Some of those present, however, expressed their indignation to one another: “Why this waste of perfume?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.5', 'BSB', 'It could have been sold for over three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor.” And they scolded her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.6', 'BSB', 'But Jesus said, “Leave her alone; why are you bothering her? She has done a beautiful deed to Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.7', 'BSB', 'The poor you will always have with you, and you can help them whenever you want. But you will not always have Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.8', 'BSB', 'She has done what she could to anoint My body in advance of My burial.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.9', 'BSB', 'And truly I tell you, wherever the gospel is preached in all the world, what she has done will also be told in memory of her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.10', 'BSB', 'Then Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve, went to the chief priests to betray Jesus to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.11', 'BSB', 'They were delighted to hear this, and they promised to give him money. So Judas began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.12', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread, when the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed, Jesus’ disciples asked Him, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.13', 'BSB', 'So He sent two of His disciples and told them, “Go into the city, and a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.14', 'BSB', 'and whichever house he enters, say to the owner, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is My guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.15', 'BSB', 'And he will show you a large upper room, furnished and ready. Make preparations for us there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.16', 'BSB', 'So the disciples left and went into the city, where they found everything as Jesus had described. And they prepared the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.17', 'BSB', 'When evening came, Jesus arrived with the Twelve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.18', 'BSB', 'And while they were reclining and eating, Jesus said, “Truly I tell you, one of you who is eating with Me will betray Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.19', 'BSB', 'They began to be grieved and to ask Him one after another, “Surely not I?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.20', 'BSB', 'He answered, “It is one of the Twelve—the one who is dipping his hand into the bowl with Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.21', 'BSB', 'The Son of Man will go just as it is written about Him, but woe to that man by whom He is betrayed! It would be better for him if he had not been born.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.22', 'BSB', 'While they were eating, Jesus took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to the disciples, saying, “Take it; this is My body.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.23', 'BSB', 'Then He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave it to them, and they all drank from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.24', 'BSB', 'He said to them, “This is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.25', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, I will no longer drink of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it anew in the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.26', 'BSB', 'And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.27', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “You will all fall away, for it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.28', 'BSB', 'But after I have risen, I will go ahead of you into Galilee.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.29', 'BSB', 'Peter declared, “Even if all fall away, I never will.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.30', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “this very night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.31', 'BSB', 'But Peter kept insisting, “Even if I have to die with You, I will never deny You.” And all the others said the same thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.32', 'BSB', 'Then they came to a place called Gethsemane, and Jesus told His disciples, “Sit here while I pray.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.33', 'BSB', 'He took with Him Peter, James, and John, and began to be deeply troubled and distressed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.34', 'BSB', 'Then He said to them, “My soul is consumed with sorrow to the point of death. Stay here and keep watch.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.35', 'BSB', 'Going a little farther, He fell to the ground and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour would pass from Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.36', 'BSB', '“Abba, Father,” He said, “all things are possible for You. Take this cup from Me. Yet not what I will, but what You will.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.37', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus returned and found them sleeping. “Simon, are you asleep?” He asked. “Were you not able to keep watch for one hour?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.38', 'BSB', 'Watch and pray so that you will not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the body is weak.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.39', 'BSB', 'Again He went away and prayed, saying the same thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.40', 'BSB', 'And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping—for their eyes were heavy. And they did not know what to answer Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.41', 'BSB', 'When Jesus returned the third time, He said, “Are you still sleeping and resting? That is enough! The hour has come. Look, the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.42', 'BSB', 'Rise, let us go. See, My betrayer is approaching!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.43', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was still speaking, Judas, one of the Twelve, arrived, accompanied by a crowd armed with swords and clubs, sent from the chief priests, scribes, and elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.44', 'BSB', 'Now the betrayer had arranged a signal with them: “The One I kiss is the man; arrest Him and lead Him away securely.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.45', 'BSB', 'Going directly to Jesus, he said, “Rabbi!” and kissed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.46', 'BSB', 'Then the men seized Jesus and arrested Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.47', 'BSB', 'And one of the bystanders drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his ear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.48', 'BSB', 'Jesus asked the crowd, “Have you come out with swords and clubs to arrest Me as you would an outlaw?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.49', 'BSB', 'Every day I was with you, teaching in the temple courts, and you did not arrest Me. But this has happened that the Scriptures would be fulfilled.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.50', 'BSB', 'Then everyone deserted Him and fled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.51', 'BSB', 'One young man who had been following Jesus was wearing a linen cloth around his body. They caught hold of him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.52', 'BSB', 'but he pulled free of the linen cloth and ran away naked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.53', 'BSB', 'They led Jesus away to the high priest, and all the chief priests, elders, and scribes assembled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.54', 'BSB', 'Peter followed Him at a distance, right into the courtyard of the high priest. And he sat with the officers and warmed himself by the fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.55', 'BSB', 'Now the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin were seeking testimony against Jesus to put Him to death, but they did not find any.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.56', 'BSB', 'For many bore false witness against Jesus, but their testimony was inconsistent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.57', 'BSB', 'Then some men stood up and testified falsely against Him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.58', 'BSB', '“We heard Him say, ‘I will destroy this man-made temple, and in three days I will build another that is made without hands.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.59', 'BSB', 'But even their testimony was inconsistent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.60', 'BSB', 'So the high priest stood up before them and questioned Jesus, “Have You no answer? What are these men testifying against You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.61', 'BSB', 'But Jesus remained silent and made no reply. Again the high priest questioned Him, “Are You the Christ, the Son of the Blessed One?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.62', 'BSB', '“I am,” said Jesus, “and you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming with the clouds of heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.63', 'BSB', 'At this, the high priest tore his clothes and declared, “Why do we need any more witnesses?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.64', 'BSB', 'You have heard the blasphemy. What is your verdict?” And they all condemned Him as deserving of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.65', 'BSB', 'Then some of them began to spit on Him. They blindfolded Him, struck Him with their fists, and said to Him, “Prophesy!” And the officers received Him with slaps in His face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.66', 'BSB', 'While Peter was in the courtyard below, one of the servant girls of the high priest came down', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.67', 'BSB', 'and saw him warming himself there. She looked at Peter and said, “You also were with Jesus the Nazarene.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.68', 'BSB', 'But he denied it. “I do not know or even understand what you are talking about,” he said. Then he went out to the gateway, and the rooster crowed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.69', 'BSB', 'There the servant girl saw him and again said to those standing nearby, “This man is one of them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.70', 'BSB', 'But he denied it again. After a little while, those standing nearby said once more to Peter, “Surely you are one of them, for you too are a Galilean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.71', 'BSB', 'But he began to curse and swear, “I do not know this man of whom you speak!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.14.72', 'BSB', 'And immediately the rooster crowed a second time. Then Peter remembered the word that Jesus had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.” And he broke down and wept.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.1', 'BSB', 'Early in the morning, the chief priests, elders, scribes, and the whole Sanhedrin devised a plan. They bound Jesus, led Him away, and handed Him over to Pilate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.2', 'BSB', 'So Pilate questioned Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.3', 'BSB', 'And the chief priests began to accuse Him of many things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.4', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate questioned Him again, “Have You no answer? Look how many charges they are bringing against You!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.5', 'BSB', 'But to Pilate’s amazement, Jesus made no further reply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.6', 'BSB', 'Now it was Pilate’s custom at the feast to release to the people a prisoner of their choosing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.7', 'BSB', 'And a man named Barabbas was imprisoned with the rebels who had committed murder during the insurrection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.8', 'BSB', 'So the crowd went up and began asking Pilate to keep his custom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.9', 'BSB', '“Do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?” Pilate asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.10', 'BSB', 'For he knew it was out of envy that the chief priests had handed Jesus over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.11', 'BSB', 'But the chief priests stirred up the crowd to have him release Barabbas to them instead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.12', 'BSB', 'So Pilate asked them again, “What then do you want me to do with the One you call the King of the Jews?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.13', 'BSB', 'And they shouted back, “Crucify Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.14', 'BSB', '“Why?” asked Pilate. “What evil has He done?” But they shouted all the louder, “Crucify Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.15', 'BSB', 'And wishing to satisfy the crowd, Pilate released Barabbas to them. But he had Jesus flogged, and handed Him over to be crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.16', 'BSB', 'Then the soldiers led Jesus away into the palace (that is, the Praetorium) and called the whole company together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.17', 'BSB', 'They dressed Him in a purple robe, twisted together a crown of thorns, and set it on His head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.18', 'BSB', 'And they began to salute Him: “Hail, King of the Jews!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.19', 'BSB', 'They kept striking His head with a staff and spitting on Him. And they knelt down and bowed before Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.20', 'BSB', 'After they had mocked Him, they removed the purple robe and put His own clothes back on Him. Then they led Him out to crucify Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.21', 'BSB', 'Now Simon of Cyrene, the father of Alexander and Rufus, was passing by on his way in from the country, and the soldiers forced him to carry the cross of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.22', 'BSB', 'They brought Jesus to a place called Golgotha, which means The Place of the Skull.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.23', 'BSB', 'There they offered Him wine mixed with myrrh, but He did not take it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.24', 'BSB', 'And they crucified Him. They also divided His garments by casting lots to decide what each of them would take.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.25', 'BSB', 'It was the third hour when they crucified Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.26', 'BSB', 'And the charge inscribed against Him read: THE KING OF THE JEWS.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.27', 'BSB', 'Along with Jesus, they crucified two robbers, one on His right and one on His left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.29', 'BSB', 'And those who passed by heaped abuse on Him, shaking their heads and saying, “Aha! You who are going to destroy the temple and rebuild it in three days,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.30', 'BSB', 'come down from the cross and save Yourself!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.31', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the chief priests and scribes mocked Him among themselves, saying, “He saved others, but He cannot save Himself!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.32', 'BSB', 'Let the Christ, the King of Israel, come down now from the cross, so that we may see and believe!” And even those who were crucified with Him berated Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.33', 'BSB', 'From the sixth hour until the ninth hour darkness came over all the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.34', 'BSB', 'At the ninth hour, Jesus cried out in a loud voice, “Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani?” which means, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.35', 'BSB', 'When some of those standing nearby heard this, they said, “Behold, He is calling Elijah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.36', 'BSB', 'And someone ran and filled a sponge with sour wine. He put it on a reed and held it up for Jesus to drink, saying, “Leave Him alone. Let us see if Elijah comes to take Him down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.37', 'BSB', 'But Jesus let out a loud cry and breathed His last.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.38', 'BSB', 'And the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.39', 'BSB', 'When the centurion standing there in front of Jesus saw how He had breathed His last, he said, “Truly this man was the Son of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.40', 'BSB', 'And there were also women watching from a distance. Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James the younger and of Joses, and Salome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.41', 'BSB', 'These women had followed Jesus and ministered to Him while He was in Galilee, and there were many other women who had come up to Jerusalem with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.42', 'BSB', 'Now it was already evening. Since it was Preparation Day (that is, the day before the Sabbath),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.43', 'BSB', 'Joseph of Arimathea, a prominent Council member who himself was waiting for the kingdom of God, boldly went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.44', 'BSB', 'Pilate was surprised to hear that Jesus was already dead, so he summoned the centurion to ask if this was so.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.45', 'BSB', 'When Pilate had confirmed it with the centurion, he granted the body to Joseph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.46', 'BSB', 'So Joseph bought a linen cloth, took down the body of Jesus, wrapped it in the cloth, and placed it in a tomb that had been cut out of the rock. Then he rolled a stone against the entrance to the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.15.47', 'BSB', 'Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joseph saw where His body was placed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.1', 'BSB', 'When the Sabbath was over, Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought spices so they could go and anoint the body of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.2', 'BSB', 'Very early on the first day of the week, just after sunrise, they went to the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.3', 'BSB', 'They were asking one another, “Who will roll away the stone from the entrance of the tomb?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.4', 'BSB', 'But when they looked up, they saw that the stone had been rolled away, even though it was extremely large.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.5', 'BSB', 'When they entered the tomb, they saw a young man dressed in a white robe sitting on the right side, and they were alarmed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.6', 'BSB', 'But he said to them, “Do not be alarmed. You are looking for Jesus the Nazarene, who was crucified. He has risen! He is not here! See the place where they put Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.7', 'BSB', 'But go, tell His disciples and Peter, ‘He is going ahead of you into Galilee. There you will see Him, just as He told you.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.8', 'BSB', 'So the women left the tomb and ran away, trembling and bewildered. And in their fear they did not say a word to anyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.9', 'BSB', 'Early on the first day of the week, after Jesus had risen, He appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom He had driven out seven demons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.10', 'BSB', 'She went and told those who had been with Him, who were mourning and weeping.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.11', 'BSB', 'And when they heard that Jesus was alive and she had seen Him, they did not believe it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.12', 'BSB', 'After this, Jesus appeared in a different form to two of them as they walked along in the country.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.13', 'BSB', 'And they went back and reported it to the rest, but they did not believe them either.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.14', 'BSB', 'Later, as they were eating, Jesus appeared to the Eleven and rebuked them for their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they did not believe those who had seen Him after He had risen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.15', 'BSB', 'And He said to them, “Go into all the world and preach the gospel to every creature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.16', 'BSB', 'Whoever believes and is baptized will be saved, but whoever does not believe will be condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.17', 'BSB', 'And these signs will accompany those who believe: In My name they will drive out demons; they will speak in new tongues;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.18', 'BSB', 'they will pick up snakes with their hands, and if they drink any deadly poison, it will not harm them; they will lay their hands on the sick, and they will be made well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.19', 'BSB', 'After the Lord Jesus had spoken to them, He was taken up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Mark.16.20', 'BSB', 'And they went out and preached everywhere, and the Lord worked through them, confirming His word by the signs that accompanied it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.1', 'BSB', 'Many have undertaken to compose an account of the things that have been fulfilled among us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.2', 'BSB', 'just as they were handed down to us by the initial eyewitnesses and servants of the word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore, having carefully investigated everything from the beginning, it seemed good also to me to write an orderly account for you, most excellent Theophilus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.4', 'BSB', 'so that you may know the certainty of the things you have been taught.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.5', 'BSB', 'In the time of Herod king of Judea there was a priest named Zechariah, who belonged to the priestly division of Abijah, and whose wife Elizabeth was a daughter of Aaron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.6', 'BSB', 'Both of them were righteous in the sight of God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and decrees of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.7', 'BSB', 'But they had no children, because Elizabeth was barren, and they were both well along in years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.8', 'BSB', 'One day while Zechariah’s division was on duty and he was serving as priest before God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.9', 'BSB', 'he was chosen by lot, according to the custom of the priesthood, to enter the temple of the Lord and burn incense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.10', 'BSB', 'And at the hour of the incense offering, the whole congregation was praying outside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.11', 'BSB', 'Just then an angel of the Lord appeared to Zechariah, standing at the right side of the altar of incense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.12', 'BSB', 'When Zechariah saw him, he was startled and gripped with fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.13', 'BSB', 'But the angel said to him, “Do not be afraid, Zechariah, because your prayer has been heard. Your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you are to give him the name John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.14', 'BSB', 'He will be a joy and delight to you, and many will rejoice at his birth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.15', 'BSB', 'for he will be great in the sight of the Lord. He shall never take wine or strong drink, and he will be filled with the Holy Spirit even from his mother’s womb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.16', 'BSB', 'Many of the sons of Israel he will turn back to the Lord their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.17', 'BSB', 'And he will go on before the Lord in the spirit and power of Elijah, to turn the hearts of the fathers to their children and the disobedient to the wisdom of the righteous—to make ready a people prepared for the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.18', 'BSB', '“How can I be sure of this?” Zechariah asked the angel. “I am an old man, and my wife is well along in years.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.19', 'BSB', '“I am Gabriel,” replied the angel. “I stand in the presence of God, and I have been sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.20', 'BSB', 'And now you will be silent and unable to speak until the day this comes to pass, because you did not believe my words, which will be fulfilled at their proper time.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.21', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the people were waiting for Zechariah and wondering why he took so long in the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.22', 'BSB', 'When he came out and was unable to speak to them, they realized he had seen a vision in the temple. He kept making signs to them but remained speechless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.23', 'BSB', 'And when the days of his service were complete, he returned home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.24', 'BSB', 'After these days, his wife Elizabeth became pregnant and for five months remained in seclusion. She declared,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.25', 'BSB', '“The Lord has done this for me. In these days He has shown me favor and taken away my disgrace among the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.26', 'BSB', 'In the sixth month, God sent the angel Gabriel to a town in Galilee called Nazareth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.27', 'BSB', 'to a virgin pledged in marriage to a man named Joseph, who was of the house of David. And the virgin’s name was Mary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.28', 'BSB', 'The angel appeared to her and said, “Greetings, you who are highly favored! The Lord is with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.29', 'BSB', 'Mary was greatly troubled at his words and wondered what kind of greeting this might be.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.30', 'BSB', 'So the angel told her, “Do not be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.31', 'BSB', 'Behold, you will conceive and give birth to a son, and you are to give Him the name Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.32', 'BSB', 'He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High. The Lord God will give Him the throne of His father David,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.33', 'BSB', 'and He will reign over the house of Jacob forever. His kingdom will never end!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.34', 'BSB', '“How can this be,” Mary asked the angel, “since I am a virgin?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.35', 'BSB', 'The angel replied, “The Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you. So the Holy One to be born will be called the Son of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.36', 'BSB', 'Look, even Elizabeth your relative has conceived a son in her old age, and she who was called barren is in her sixth month.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.37', 'BSB', 'For no word from God will ever fail.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.38', 'BSB', '“I am the Lord’s servant,” Mary answered. “May it happen to me according to your word.” Then the angel left her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.39', 'BSB', 'In those days Mary got ready and hurried to a town in the hill country of Judah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.40', 'BSB', 'where she entered the home of Zechariah and greeted Elizabeth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.41', 'BSB', 'When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the baby leaped in her womb, and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.42', 'BSB', 'In a loud voice she exclaimed, “Blessed are you among women, and blessed is the fruit of your womb!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.43', 'BSB', 'And why am I so honored, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.44', 'BSB', 'For as soon as the sound of your greeting reached my ears, the baby in my womb leaped for joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.45', 'BSB', 'Blessed is she who has believed that the Lord’s word to her will be fulfilled.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.46', 'BSB', 'Then Mary said: “My soul magnifies the Lord,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.47', 'BSB', 'and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.48', 'BSB', 'For He has looked with favor on the humble state of His servant. From now on all generations will call me blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.49', 'BSB', 'For the Mighty One has done great things for me. Holy is His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.50', 'BSB', 'His mercy extends to those who fear Him, from generation to generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.51', 'BSB', 'He has performed mighty deeds with His arm; He has scattered those who are proud in the thoughts of their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.52', 'BSB', 'He has brought down rulers from their thrones, but has exalted the humble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.53', 'BSB', 'He has filled the hungry with good things, but has sent the rich away empty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.54', 'BSB', 'He has helped His servant Israel, remembering to be merciful,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.55', 'BSB', 'as He promised to our fathers, to Abraham and his descendants forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.56', 'BSB', 'Mary stayed with Elizabeth for about three months and then returned home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.57', 'BSB', 'When the time came for Elizabeth to have her child, she gave birth to a son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.58', 'BSB', 'Her neighbors and relatives heard that the Lord had shown her great mercy, and they rejoiced with her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.59', 'BSB', 'On the eighth day, when they came to circumcise the child, they were going to name him after his father Zechariah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.60', 'BSB', 'But his mother replied, “No! He shall be called John.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.61', 'BSB', 'They said to her, “There is no one among your relatives who bears this name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.62', 'BSB', 'So they made signs to his father to find out what he wanted to name the child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.63', 'BSB', 'Zechariah asked for a tablet and wrote, “His name is John.” And they were all amazed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.64', 'BSB', 'Immediately Zechariah’s mouth was opened and his tongue was released, and he began to speak, praising God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.65', 'BSB', 'All their neighbors were filled with awe, and people throughout the hill country of Judea were talking about these events.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.66', 'BSB', 'And all who heard this wondered in their hearts and asked, “What then will this child become?” For the Lord’s hand was with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.67', 'BSB', 'Then his father Zechariah was filled with the Holy Spirit and prophesied:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.68', 'BSB', '“Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, because He has visited and redeemed His people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.69', 'BSB', 'He has raised up a horn of salvation for us in the house of His servant David,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.70', 'BSB', 'as He spoke through His holy prophets, those of ages past,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.71', 'BSB', 'salvation from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.72', 'BSB', 'to show mercy to our fathers and to remember His holy covenant,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.73', 'BSB', 'the oath He swore to our father Abraham, to grant us', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.74', 'BSB', 'deliverance from hostile hands, that we may serve Him without fear,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.75', 'BSB', 'in holiness and righteousness before Him all the days of our lives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.76', 'BSB', 'And you, child, will be called a prophet of the Most High; for you will go on before the Lord to prepare the way for Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.77', 'BSB', 'to give to His people the knowledge of salvation through the forgiveness of their sins,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.78', 'BSB', 'because of the tender mercy of our God, by which the Dawn will visit us from on high,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.79', 'BSB', 'to shine on those who live in darkness and in the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the path of peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.1.80', 'BSB', 'And the child grew and became strong in spirit; and he lived in the wilderness until the time of his public appearance to Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.1', 'BSB', 'Now in those days a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that a census should be taken of the whole empire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.2', 'BSB', 'This was the first census to take place while Quirinius was governor of Syria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.3', 'BSB', 'And everyone went to his own town to register.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.4', 'BSB', 'So Joseph also went up from Nazareth in Galilee to Judea, to the city of David called Bethlehem, since he was from the house and line of David.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.5', 'BSB', 'He went there to register with Mary, who was pledged to him in marriage and was expecting a child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.6', 'BSB', 'While they were there, the time came for her Child to be born.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.7', 'BSB', 'And she gave birth to her firstborn, a Son. She wrapped Him in swaddling cloths and laid Him in a manger, because there was no room for them in the inn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.8', 'BSB', 'And there were shepherds residing in the fields nearby, keeping watch over their flocks by night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.9', 'BSB', 'Just then an angel of the Lord stood before them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them, and they were terrified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.10', 'BSB', 'But the angel said to them, “Do not be afraid! For behold, I bring you good news of great joy that will be for all the people:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.11', 'BSB', 'Today in the city of David a Savior has been born to you. He is Christ the Lord!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.12', 'BSB', 'And this will be a sign to you: You will find a baby wrapped in swaddling cloths and lying in a manger.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.13', 'BSB', 'And suddenly there appeared with the angel a great multitude of the heavenly host, praising God and saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.14', 'BSB', '“Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace to men on whom His favor rests!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.15', 'BSB', 'When the angels had left them and gone into heaven, the shepherds said to one another, “Let us go to Bethlehem and see this thing that has happened, which the Lord has made known to us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.16', 'BSB', 'So they hurried off and found Mary and Joseph and the Baby, who was lying in the manger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.17', 'BSB', 'After they had seen the Child, they spread the message they had received about Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.18', 'BSB', 'And all who heard it were amazed at what the shepherds said to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.19', 'BSB', 'But Mary treasured up all these things and pondered them in her heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.20', 'BSB', 'The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all they had heard and seen, which was just as the angel had told them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.21', 'BSB', 'When the eight days until His circumcision had passed, He was named Jesus, the name the angel had given Him before He had been conceived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.22', 'BSB', 'And when the time of purification according to the Law of Moses was complete, His parents brought Him to Jerusalem to present Him to the Lord', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.23', 'BSB', '(as it is written in the Law of the Lord: “Every firstborn male shall be consecrated to the Lord” ),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.24', 'BSB', 'and to offer the sacrifice specified in the Law of the Lord: “A pair of turtledoves or two young pigeons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.25', 'BSB', 'Now there was a man in Jerusalem named Simeon, who was righteous and devout. He was waiting for the consolation of Israel, and the Holy Spirit was upon him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.26', 'BSB', 'The Holy Spirit had revealed to him that he would not see death before he had seen the Lord’s Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.27', 'BSB', 'Led by the Spirit, he went into the temple courts. And when the parents brought in the child Jesus to do for Him what was customary under the Law,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.28', 'BSB', 'Simeon took Him in his arms and blessed God, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.29', 'BSB', '“Sovereign Lord, as You have promised, You now dismiss Your servant in peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.30', 'BSB', 'For my eyes have seen Your salvation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.31', 'BSB', 'which You have prepared in the sight of all people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.32', 'BSB', 'a light for revelation to the Gentiles, and for glory to Your people Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.33', 'BSB', 'The Child’s father and mother were amazed at what was spoken about Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.34', 'BSB', 'Then Simeon blessed them and said to His mother Mary: “Behold, this Child is appointed to cause the rise and fall of many in Israel, and to be a sign that will be spoken against,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.35', 'BSB', 'so that the thoughts of many hearts will be revealed— and a sword will pierce your soul as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.36', 'BSB', 'There was also a prophetess named Anna, the daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Asher, who was well along in years. She had been married for seven years,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.37', 'BSB', 'and then was a widow to the age of eighty-four. She never left the temple, but worshiped night and day, fasting and praying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.38', 'BSB', 'Coming forward at that moment, she gave thanks to God and spoke about the Child to all who were waiting for the redemption of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.39', 'BSB', 'When Jesus’ parents had done everything required by the Law of the Lord, they returned to Galilee, to their own town of Nazareth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.40', 'BSB', 'And the Child grew and became strong. He was filled with wisdom, and the grace of God was upon Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.41', 'BSB', 'Every year His parents went to Jerusalem for the Feast of the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.42', 'BSB', 'And when He was twelve years old, they went up according to the custom of the Feast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.43', 'BSB', 'When those days were over and they were returning home, the boy Jesus remained behind in Jerusalem, but His parents were unaware He had stayed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.44', 'BSB', 'Assuming He was in their company, they traveled on for a day before they began to look for Him among their relatives and friends.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.45', 'BSB', 'When they could not find Him, they returned to Jerusalem to search for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.46', 'BSB', 'Finally, after three days they found Him in the temple courts, sitting among the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.47', 'BSB', 'And all who heard Him were astounded at His understanding and His answers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.48', 'BSB', 'When His parents saw Him, they were astonished. “Child, why have You done this to us?” His mother asked. “Your father and I have been anxiously searching for You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.49', 'BSB', '“Why were you looking for Me?” He asked. “Did you not know that I had to be in My Father’s house?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.50', 'BSB', 'But they did not understand the statement He was making to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.51', 'BSB', 'Then He went down to Nazareth with them and was obedient to them. But His mother treasured up all these things in her heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.2.52', 'BSB', 'And Jesus grew in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.1', 'BSB', 'In the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, while Pontius Pilate was governor of Judea, Herod tetrarch of Galilee, his brother Philip tetrarch of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias tetrarch of Abilene,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.2', 'BSB', 'during the high priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, the word of God came to John son of Zechariah in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.3', 'BSB', 'He went into all the region around the Jordan, preaching a baptism of repentance for the forgiveness of sins,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.4', 'BSB', 'as it is written in the book of the words of Isaiah the prophet: “A voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way for the Lord, make straight paths for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.5', 'BSB', 'Every valley shall be filled in, and every mountain and hill made low. The crooked ways shall be made straight, and the rough ways smooth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.6', 'BSB', 'And all humanity will see God’s salvation.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.7', 'BSB', 'Then John said to the crowds coming out to be baptized by him, “You brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the coming wrath?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.8', 'BSB', 'Produce fruit, then, in keeping with repentance. And do not begin to say to yourselves, ‘We have Abraham as our father.’ For I tell you that out of these stones God can raise up children for Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.9', 'BSB', 'The axe lies ready at the root of the trees, and every tree that does not produce good fruit will be cut down and thrown into the fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.10', 'BSB', 'The crowds asked him, “What then should we do?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.11', 'BSB', 'John replied, “Whoever has two tunics should share with him who has none, and whoever has food should do the same.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.12', 'BSB', 'Even tax collectors came to be baptized. “Teacher,” they asked, “what should we do?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.13', 'BSB', '“Collect no more than you are authorized,” he answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.14', 'BSB', 'Then some soldiers asked him, “And what should we do?” “Do not take money by force or false accusation,” he said. “Be content with your wages.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.15', 'BSB', 'The people were waiting expectantly and were all wondering in their hearts if John could be the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.16', 'BSB', 'John answered all of them: “I baptize you with water, but One more powerful than I will come, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.17', 'BSB', 'His winnowing fork is in His hand to clear His threshing floor and to gather the wheat into His barn; but He will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.18', 'BSB', 'With these and many other exhortations, John proclaimed the good news to the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.19', 'BSB', 'But when he rebuked Herod the tetrarch regarding his brother’s wife Herodias and all the evils he had done,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.20', 'BSB', 'Herod added this to them all: He locked John up in prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.21', 'BSB', 'When all the people were being baptized, Jesus was baptized too. And as He was praying, heaven was opened,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.22', 'BSB', 'and the Holy Spirit descended on Him in a bodily form like a dove. And a voice came from heaven: “You are My beloved Son; in You I am well pleased.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus Himself was about thirty years old when He began His ministry. He was regarded as the son of Joseph, the son of Heli,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.24', 'BSB', 'the son of Matthat, the son of Levi, the son of Melchi, the son of Jannai, the son of Joseph,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.25', 'BSB', 'the son of Mattathias, the son of Amos, the son of Nahum, the son of Esli, the son of Naggai,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.26', 'BSB', 'the son of Maath, the son of Mattathias, the son of Semein, the son of Josech, the son of Joda,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.27', 'BSB', 'the son of Joanan, the son of Rhesa, the son of Zerubbabel, the son of Shealtiel, the son of Neri,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.28', 'BSB', 'the son of Melchi, the son of Addi, the son of Cosam, the son of Elmadam, the son of Er,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.29', 'BSB', 'the son of Joshua, the son of Eliezer, the son of Jorim, the son of Matthat, the son of Levi,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.30', 'BSB', 'the son of Simeon, the son of Judah, the son of Joseph, the son of Jonam, the son of Eliakim,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.31', 'BSB', 'the son of Melea, the son of Menna, the son of Mattatha, the son of Nathan, the son of David,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.32', 'BSB', 'the son of Jesse, the son of Obed, the son of Boaz, the son of Sala, the son of Nahshon,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.33', 'BSB', 'the son of Amminadab, the son of Admin, the son of Arni, the son of Hezron, the son of Perez, the son of Judah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.34', 'BSB', 'the son of Jacob, the son of Isaac, the son of Abraham, the son of Terah, the son of Nahor,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.35', 'BSB', 'the son of Serug, the son of Reu, the son of Peleg, the son of Eber, the son of Shelah,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.36', 'BSB', 'the son of Cainan, the son of Arphaxad, the son of Shem, the son of Noah, the son of Lamech,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.37', 'BSB', 'the son of Methuselah, the son of Enoch, the son of Jared, the son of Mahalalel, the son of Cainan,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.3.38', 'BSB', 'the son of Enosh, the son of Seth, the son of Adam, the son of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.2', 'BSB', 'where for forty days He was tempted by the devil. He ate nothing during those days, and when they had ended, He was hungry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.3', 'BSB', 'The devil said to Him, “If You are the Son of God, tell this stone to become bread.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.4', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Man shall not live on bread alone.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.5', 'BSB', 'Then the devil led Him up to a high place and showed Him in an instant all the kingdoms of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.6', 'BSB', '“I will give You authority over all these kingdoms and all their glory,” he said. “For it has been relinquished to me, and I can give it to anyone I wish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.7', 'BSB', 'So if You worship me, it will all be Yours.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.8', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “It is written: ‘Worship the Lord your God and serve Him only.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.9', 'BSB', 'Then the devil led Him to Jerusalem and set Him on the pinnacle of the temple. “If You are the Son of God,” he said, “throw Yourself down from here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.10', 'BSB', 'For it is written: ‘He will command His angels concerning You to guard You carefully;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.11', 'BSB', 'and they will lift You up in their hands, so that You will not strike Your foot against a stone.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.12', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “It also says, ‘Do not put the Lord your God to the test.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.13', 'BSB', 'When the devil had finished every temptation, he left Him until an opportune time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.14', 'BSB', 'Jesus returned to Galilee in the power of the Spirit, and the news about Him spread throughout the surrounding region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.15', 'BSB', 'He taught in their synagogues and was glorified by everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.16', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus came to Nazareth, where He had been brought up. As was His custom, He entered the synagogue on the Sabbath. And when He stood up to read,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.17', 'BSB', 'the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to Him. Unrolling it, He found the place where it was written:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.18', 'BSB', '“The Spirit of the Lord is on Me, because He has anointed Me to preach good news to the poor. He has sent Me to proclaim liberty to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to release the oppressed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.19', 'BSB', 'to proclaim the year of the Lord’s favor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.20', 'BSB', 'Then He rolled up the scroll, returned it to the attendant, and sat down. The eyes of everyone in the synagogue were fixed on Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.21', 'BSB', 'and He began by saying, “Today this Scripture is fulfilled in your hearing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.22', 'BSB', 'All spoke well of Him and marveled at the gracious words that came from His lips. “Isn’t this the son of Joseph?” they asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “Surely you will quote this proverb to Me: ‘Physician, heal yourself! Do here in Your hometown what we have heard that You did in Capernaum.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.24', 'BSB', 'Then He added, “Truly I tell you, no prophet is accepted in his hometown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.25', 'BSB', 'But I tell you truthfully that there were many widows in Israel in the time of Elijah, when the sky was shut for three and a half years and great famine swept over all the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.26', 'BSB', 'Yet Elijah was not sent to any of them, but to the widow of Zarephath in Sidon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.27', 'BSB', 'And there were many lepers in Israel in the time of Elisha the prophet. Yet not one of them was cleansed—only Naaman the Syrian.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.28', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, all the people in the synagogue were enraged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.29', 'BSB', 'They got up, drove Him out of the town, and led Him to the brow of the hill on which the town was built, in order to throw Him over the cliff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.30', 'BSB', 'But Jesus passed through the crowd and went on His way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.31', 'BSB', 'Then He went down to Capernaum, a town in Galilee, and on the Sabbath He began to teach the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.32', 'BSB', 'They were astonished at His teaching, because His message had authority.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.33', 'BSB', 'In the synagogue there was a man possessed by the spirit of an unclean demon. He cried out in a loud voice,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.34', 'BSB', '“Ha! What do You want with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.35', 'BSB', 'But Jesus rebuked the demon. “Be silent!” He said. “Come out of him!” At this, the demon threw the man down before them all and came out without harming him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.36', 'BSB', 'All the people were overcome with amazement and asked one another, “What is this message? With authority and power He commands the unclean spirits, and they come out!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.37', 'BSB', 'And the news about Jesus spread throughout the surrounding region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.38', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had left the synagogue, He went to the home of Simon, whose mother-in-law was suffering from a high fever. So they appealed to Jesus on her behalf,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.39', 'BSB', 'and He stood over her and rebuked the fever, and it left her. And she got up at once and began to serve them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.40', 'BSB', 'At sunset, all who were ill with various diseases were brought to Jesus, and laying His hands on each one, He healed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.41', 'BSB', 'Demons also came out of many people, shouting, “You are the Son of God!” But He rebuked the demons and would not allow them to speak, because they knew He was the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.42', 'BSB', 'At daybreak, Jesus went out to a solitary place, and the crowds were looking for Him. They came to Him and tried to keep Him from leaving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.43', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told them, “I must preach the good news of the kingdom of God to the other towns as well, because that is why I was sent.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.4.44', 'BSB', 'And He continued to preach in the synagogues of Judea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.1', 'BSB', 'On one occasion, while Jesus was standing by the Lake of Gennesaret with the crowd pressing in on Him to hear the word of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.2', 'BSB', 'He saw two boats at the edge of the lake. The fishermen had left them and were washing their nets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus got into the boat belonging to Simon and asked him to put out a little from shore. And sitting down, He taught the people from the boat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.4', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had finished speaking, He said to Simon, “Put out into deep water and let down your nets for a catch.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.5', 'BSB', '“Master,” Simon replied, “we have worked hard all night without catching anything. But because You say so, I will let down the nets.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.6', 'BSB', 'When they had done so, they caught such a large number of fish that their nets began to tear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.7', 'BSB', 'So they signaled to their partners in the other boat to come and help them, and they came and filled both boats so full that they began to sink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.8', 'BSB', 'When Simon Peter saw this, he fell at Jesus’ knees. “Go away from me, Lord,” he said, “for I am a sinful man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.9', 'BSB', 'For he and his companions were astonished at the catch of fish they had taken,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.10', 'BSB', 'and so were his partners James and John, the sons of Zebedee. “Do not be afraid,” Jesus said to Simon. “From now on you will catch men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.11', 'BSB', 'And when they had brought their boats ashore, they left everything and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.12', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was in one of the towns, a man came along who was covered with leprosy. When he saw Jesus, he fell facedown and begged Him, “Lord, if You are willing, You can make me clean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.13', 'BSB', 'Jesus reached out His hand and touched the man. “I am willing,” He said. “Be clean!” And immediately the leprosy left him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.14', 'BSB', '“Do not tell anyone,” Jesus instructed him. “But go, show yourself to the priest and present the offering Moses prescribed for your cleansing, as a testimony to them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.15', 'BSB', 'But the news about Jesus spread all the more, and great crowds came to hear Him and to be healed of their sicknesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.16', 'BSB', 'Yet He frequently withdrew to the wilderness to pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.17', 'BSB', 'One day Jesus was teaching, and the Pharisees and teachers of the law were sitting there. People had come from Jerusalem and from every village of Galilee and Judea, and the power of the Lord was present for Him to heal the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.18', 'BSB', 'Just then some men came carrying a paralyzed man on a mat. They tried to bring him inside to set him before Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.19', 'BSB', 'but they could not find a way through the crowd. So they went up on the roof and lowered him on his mat through the tiles into the middle of the crowd, right in front of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.20', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw their faith, He said, “Friend, your sins are forgiven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.21', 'BSB', 'But the scribes and Pharisees began thinking to themselves, “Who is this man who speaks blasphemy? Who can forgive sins but God alone?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.22', 'BSB', 'Knowing what they were thinking, Jesus replied, “Why are you thinking these things in your hearts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.23', 'BSB', 'Which is easier: to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Get up and walk?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.24', 'BSB', 'But so that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on the earth to forgive sins...” He said to the paralytic, “I tell you, get up, pick up your mat, and go home.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.25', 'BSB', 'And immediately the man stood up before them, took what he had been lying on, and went home glorifying God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.26', 'BSB', 'Everyone was taken with amazement and glorified God. They were filled with awe and said, “We have seen remarkable things today.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.27', 'BSB', 'After this, Jesus went out and saw a tax collector named Levi sitting at the tax booth. “Follow Me,” He told him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.28', 'BSB', 'and Levi got up, left everything, and followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.29', 'BSB', 'Then Levi hosted a great banquet for Jesus at his house. A large crowd of tax collectors was there, along with others who were eating with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.30', 'BSB', 'But the Pharisees and their scribes complained to Jesus’ disciples, “Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and sinners?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.31', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.32', 'BSB', 'I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners, to repentance.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.33', 'BSB', 'Then they said to Him, “John’s disciples and those of the Pharisees frequently fast and pray, but Yours keep on eating and drinking.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Can you make the guests of the bridegroom fast while He is with them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.35', 'BSB', 'But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them; then they will fast.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.36', 'BSB', 'He also told them a parable: “No one tears a piece of cloth from a new garment and sews it on an old one. If he does, he will tear the new garment as well, and the patch from the new will not match the old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.37', 'BSB', 'And no one pours new wine into old wineskins. If he does, the new wine will burst the skins, the wine will spill, and the wineskins will be ruined.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.38', 'BSB', 'Instead, new wine is poured into new wineskins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.5.39', 'BSB', 'And no one after drinking old wine wants new, for he says, ‘The old is better.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.1', 'BSB', 'One Sabbath Jesus was passing through the grainfields, and His disciples began to pick the heads of grain, rub them in their hands, and eat them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.2', 'BSB', 'But some of the Pharisees asked, “Why are you doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Have you not read what David did when he and his companions were hungry?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.4', 'BSB', 'He entered the house of God, took the consecrated bread and gave it to his companions, and ate what is lawful only for the priests to eat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.5', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus declared, “The Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.6', 'BSB', 'On another Sabbath Jesus entered the synagogue and was teaching, and a man was there whose right hand was withered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.7', 'BSB', 'Looking for a reason to accuse Jesus, the scribes and Pharisees were watching Him closely to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.8', 'BSB', 'But Jesus knew their thoughts and said to the man with the withered hand, “Get up and stand among us.” So he got up and stood there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.9', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “I ask you, which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.10', 'BSB', 'And after looking around at all of them, He said to the man, “Stretch out your hand.” He did so, and it was restored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.11', 'BSB', 'But the scribes and Pharisees were filled with rage and began to discuss with one another what they might do to Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.12', 'BSB', 'In those days Jesus went out to the mountain to pray, and He spent the night in prayer to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.13', 'BSB', 'When daylight came, He called His disciples to Him and chose twelve of them, whom He also designated as apostles:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.14', 'BSB', 'Simon, whom He named Peter, and his brother Andrew; James and John; Philip and Bartholomew;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.15', 'BSB', 'Matthew and Thomas; James son of Alphaeus and Simon called the Zealot;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.16', 'BSB', 'Judas son of James, and Judas Iscariot, who became a traitor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.17', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus came down with them and stood on a level place. A large crowd of His disciples was there, along with a great number of people from all over Judea, Jerusalem, and the sea coast of Tyre and Sidon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.18', 'BSB', 'They had come to hear Him and to be healed of their diseases, and those troubled by unclean spirits were healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.19', 'BSB', 'The entire crowd was trying to touch Him, because power was coming from Him and healing them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.20', 'BSB', 'Looking up at His disciples, Jesus said: “Blessed are you who are poor, for yours is the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.21', 'BSB', 'Blessed are you who hunger now, for you will be filled. Blessed are you who weep now, for you will laugh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.22', 'BSB', 'Blessed are you when people hate you, and when they exclude you and insult you and reject your name as evil because of the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.23', 'BSB', 'Rejoice in that day and leap for joy, because great is your reward in heaven. For their fathers treated the prophets in the same way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.24', 'BSB', 'But woe to you who are rich, for you have already received your comfort.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.25', 'BSB', 'Woe to you who are well fed now, for you will hunger. Woe to you who laugh now, for you will mourn and weep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.26', 'BSB', 'Woe to you when all men speak well of you, for their fathers treated the false prophets in the same way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.27', 'BSB', 'But to those of you who will listen, I say: Love your enemies, do good to those who hate you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.28', 'BSB', 'bless those who curse you, pray for those who mistreat you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.29', 'BSB', 'If someone strikes you on one cheek, turn to him the other also. And if someone takes your cloak, do not withhold your tunic as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.30', 'BSB', 'Give to everyone who asks you, and if anyone takes what is yours, do not demand it back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.31', 'BSB', 'Do to others as you would have them do to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.32', 'BSB', 'If you love those who love you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners love those who love them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.33', 'BSB', 'If you do good to those who do good to you, what credit is that to you? Even sinners do the same.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.34', 'BSB', 'And if you lend to those from whom you expect repayment, what credit is that to you? Even sinners lend to sinners, expecting to be repaid in full.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.35', 'BSB', 'But love your enemies, do good to them, and lend to them, expecting nothing in return. Then your reward will be great, and you will be sons of the Most High; for He is kind to the ungrateful and wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.36', 'BSB', 'Be merciful, just as your Father is merciful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.37', 'BSB', 'Do not judge, and you will not be judged. Do not condemn, and you will not be condemned. Forgive, and you will be forgiven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.38', 'BSB', 'Give, and it will be given to you. A good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over will be poured into your lap. For with the measure you use, it will be measured back to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.39', 'BSB', 'Jesus also told them a parable: “Can a blind man lead a blind man? Will they not both fall into a pit?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.40', 'BSB', 'A disciple is not above his teacher, but everyone who is fully trained will be like his teacher.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.41', 'BSB', 'Why do you look at the speck in your brother’s eye, but fail to notice the beam in your own eye?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.42', 'BSB', 'How can you say, ‘Brother, let me take the speck out of your eye,’ while you yourself fail to see the beam in your own eye? You hypocrite! First take the beam out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother’s eye.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.43', 'BSB', 'No good tree bears bad fruit, nor does a bad tree bear good fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.44', 'BSB', 'For each tree is known by its own fruit. Indeed, figs are not gathered from thornbushes, nor grapes from brambles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.45', 'BSB', 'The good man brings good things out of the good treasure of his heart, and the evil man brings evil things out of the evil treasure of his heart. For out of the overflow of the heart, the mouth speaks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.46', 'BSB', 'Why do you call Me ‘Lord, Lord,’ but not do what I say?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.47', 'BSB', 'I will show you what he is like who comes to Me and hears My words and acts on them:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.48', 'BSB', 'He is like a man building a house, who dug down deep and laid his foundation on the rock. When the flood came, the torrent crashed against that house but could not shake it, because it was well built.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.6.49', 'BSB', 'But the one who hears My words and does not act on them is like a man who built his house on ground without a foundation. The torrent crashed against that house, and immediately it fell—and great was its destruction!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had concluded His discourse in the hearing of the people, He went to Capernaum.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.2', 'BSB', 'There a highly valued servant of a centurion was sick and about to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.3', 'BSB', 'When the centurion heard about Jesus, he sent some Jewish elders to ask Him to come and heal his servant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.4', 'BSB', 'They came to Jesus and pleaded with Him earnestly, “This man is worthy to have You grant this,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.5', 'BSB', 'for he loves our nation and has built our synagogue.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.6', 'BSB', 'So Jesus went with them. But when He was not far from the house, the centurion sent friends with the message: “Lord, do not trouble Yourself, for I am not worthy to have You come under my roof.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.7', 'BSB', 'That is why I did not consider myself worthy to come to You. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.8', 'BSB', 'For I myself am a man under authority, with soldiers under me. I tell one to go, and he goes; and another to come, and he comes. I tell my servant to do something, and he does it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.9', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard this, He marveled at the centurion. Turning to the crowd following Him, He said, “I tell you, not even in Israel have I found such great faith.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.10', 'BSB', 'And when the messengers returned to the house, they found the servant in good health.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.11', 'BSB', 'Soon afterward, Jesus went to a town called Nain. His disciples went with Him, accompanied by a large crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.12', 'BSB', 'As He approached the town gate, He saw a dead man being carried out, the only son of his mother, and she was a widow. And a large crowd from the town was with her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.13', 'BSB', 'When the Lord saw her, He had compassion on her and said, “Do not weep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.14', 'BSB', 'Then He went up and touched the coffin, and those carrying it stood still. “Young man,” He said, “I tell you, get up!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.15', 'BSB', 'And the dead man sat up and began to speak! Then Jesus gave him back to his mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.16', 'BSB', 'A sense of awe swept over all of them, and they glorified God. “A great prophet has appeared among us!” they said. “God has visited His people!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.17', 'BSB', 'And the news about Jesus spread throughout Judea and all the surrounding region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.18', 'BSB', 'Then John’s disciples informed him about all these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.19', 'BSB', 'So John called two of his disciples and sent them to ask the Lord, “Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.20', 'BSB', 'When the men came to Jesus, they said, “John the Baptist sent us to ask, ‘Are You the One who was to come, or should we look for someone else?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.21', 'BSB', 'At that very hour Jesus healed many people of their diseases, afflictions, and evil spirits, and He gave sight to many who were blind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.22', 'BSB', 'So He replied, “Go back and report to John what you have seen and heard: The blind receive sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, and the good news is preached to the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.23', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the one who does not fall away on account of Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.24', 'BSB', 'After John’s messengers had left, Jesus began to speak to the crowds about John: “What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed swaying in the wind?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.25', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, what did you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? Look, those who wear elegant clothing and live in luxury are found in palaces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.26', 'BSB', 'What then did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.27', 'BSB', 'This is the one about whom it is written: ‘Behold, I will send My messenger ahead of You, who will prepare Your way before You.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.28', 'BSB', 'I tell you, among those born of women there is no one greater than John, yet even the least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.29', 'BSB', 'All the people who heard this, even the tax collectors, acknowledged God’s justice. For they had received the baptism of John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.30', 'BSB', 'But the Pharisees and experts in the law rejected God’s purpose for themselves, because they had not been baptized by John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.31', 'BSB', '“To what, then, can I compare the men of this generation? What are they like?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.32', 'BSB', 'They are like children sitting in the marketplace and calling out to one another: ‘We played the flute for you, and you did not dance; we sang a dirge, and you did not weep.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.33', 'BSB', 'For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine, and you say, ‘He has a demon!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.34', 'BSB', 'The Son of Man came eating and drinking, and you say, ‘Look at this glutton and drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.35', 'BSB', 'But wisdom is vindicated by all her children.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.36', 'BSB', 'Then one of the Pharisees invited Jesus to eat with him, and He entered the Pharisee’s house and reclined at the table.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.37', 'BSB', 'When a sinful woman from that town learned that Jesus was dining there, she brought an alabaster jar of perfume.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.38', 'BSB', 'As she stood behind Him at His feet weeping, she began to wet His feet with her tears and wipe them with her hair. Then she kissed His feet and anointed them with the perfume.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.39', 'BSB', 'When the Pharisee who had invited Jesus saw this, he said to himself, “If this man were a prophet, He would know who this is and what kind of woman is touching Him—for she is a sinner!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.40', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered him, “Simon, I have something to tell you.” “Tell me, Teacher,” he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.41', 'BSB', '“Two men were debtors to a certain moneylender. One owed him five hundred denarii, and the other fifty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.42', 'BSB', 'When they were unable to repay him, he forgave both of them. Which one, then, will love him more?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.43', 'BSB', '“I suppose the one who was forgiven more,” Simon replied. “You have judged correctly,” Jesus said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.44', 'BSB', 'And turning toward the woman, He said to Simon, “Do you see this woman? When I entered your house, you did not give Me water for My feet, but she wet My feet with her tears and wiped them with her hair.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.45', 'BSB', 'You did not greet Me with a kiss, but she has not stopped kissing My feet since I arrived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.46', 'BSB', 'You did not anoint My head with oil, but she has anointed My feet with perfume.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.47', 'BSB', 'Therefore I tell you, because her many sins have been forgiven, she has loved much. But he who has been forgiven little loves little.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.48', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to her, “Your sins are forgiven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.49', 'BSB', 'But those at the table began to say to themselves, “Who is this who even forgives sins?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.7.50', 'BSB', 'And Jesus told the woman, “Your faith has saved you; go in peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.1', 'BSB', 'Soon afterward, Jesus traveled from one town and village to another, preaching and proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God. The Twelve were with Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.2', 'BSB', 'as well as some women who had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities: Mary called Magdalene, from whom seven demons had gone out,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.3', 'BSB', 'Joanna the wife of Herod’s household manager Chuza, Susanna, and many others. These women were ministering to them out of their own means.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.4', 'BSB', 'While a large crowd was gathering and people were coming to Jesus from town after town, He told them this parable:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.5', 'BSB', '“A farmer went out to sow his seed. And as he was sowing, some seed fell along the path, where it was trampled, and the birds of the air devoured it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.6', 'BSB', 'Some fell on rocky ground, and when it came up, the seedlings withered because they had no moisture.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.7', 'BSB', 'Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up with it and choked the seedlings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.8', 'BSB', 'Still other seed fell on good soil, where it sprang up and produced a crop—a hundredfold.” As Jesus said this, He called out, “He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.9', 'BSB', 'Then His disciples asked Him what this parable meant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.10', 'BSB', 'He replied, “The knowledge of the mysteries of the kingdom of God has been given to you, but to others I speak in parables, so that, ‘though seeing, they may not see; though hearing, they may not understand.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.11', 'BSB', 'Now this is the meaning of the parable: The seed is the word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.12', 'BSB', 'The seeds along the path are those who hear, but the devil comes and takes away the word from their hearts, so that they may not believe and be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.13', 'BSB', 'The seeds on rocky ground are those who hear the word and receive it with joy, but they have no root. They believe for a season, but in the time of testing, they fall away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.14', 'BSB', 'The seeds that fell among the thorns are those who hear, but as they go on their way, they are choked by the worries, riches, and pleasures of this life, and their fruit does not mature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.15', 'BSB', 'But the seeds on good soil are those with a noble and good heart, who hear the word, cling to it, and by persevering produce a crop.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.16', 'BSB', 'No one lights a lamp and covers it with a jar or puts it under a bed. Instead, he sets it on a stand, so those who enter can see the light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.17', 'BSB', 'For there is nothing hidden that will not be disclosed, and nothing concealed that will not be made known and brought to light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.18', 'BSB', 'Pay attention, therefore, to how you listen. Whoever has will be given more, but whoever does not have, even what he thinks he has will be taken away from him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.19', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came to see Him, but they were unable to reach Him because of the crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.20', 'BSB', 'He was told, “Your mother and brothers are standing outside, wanting to see You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.21', 'BSB', 'But He replied, “My mother and brothers are those who hear the word of God and carry it out.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.22', 'BSB', 'One day Jesus said to His disciples, “Let us cross to the other side of the lake.” So He got into a boat with them and set out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.23', 'BSB', 'As they sailed, He fell asleep, and a windstorm came down on the lake, so that the boat was being swamped, and they were in great danger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.24', 'BSB', 'The disciples went and woke Him, saying, “Master, Master, we are perishing!” Then Jesus got up and rebuked the wind and the raging waters, and they subsided, and all was calm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.25', 'BSB', '“Where is your faith?” He asked. Frightened and amazed, they asked one another, “Who is this? He commands even the winds and the water, and they obey Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.26', 'BSB', 'Then they sailed to the region of the Gerasenes, across the lake from Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.27', 'BSB', 'When Jesus stepped ashore, He was met by a demon-possessed man from the town. For a long time this man had not worn clothing or lived in a house, but he stayed in the tombs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.28', 'BSB', 'When the man saw Jesus, he cried out and fell down before Him, shouting in a loud voice, “What do You want with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I beg You not to torture me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.29', 'BSB', 'For Jesus had commanded the unclean spirit to come out of the man. Many times it had seized him, and though he was bound with chains and shackles, he had broken the chains and been driven by the demon into solitary places.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.30', 'BSB', '“What is your name?” Jesus asked. “Legion,” he replied, because many demons had gone into him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.31', 'BSB', 'And the demons kept begging Jesus not to order them to go into the Abyss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.32', 'BSB', 'There on the hillside a large herd of pigs was feeding. So the demons begged Jesus to let them enter the pigs, and He gave them permission.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.33', 'BSB', 'Then the demons came out of the man and went into the pigs, and the herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and was drowned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.34', 'BSB', 'When those tending the pigs saw what had happened, they ran off and reported this in the town and countryside.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.35', 'BSB', 'So the people went out to see what had happened. They came to Jesus and found the man whom the demons had left, sitting at Jesus’ feet, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.36', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, those who had seen it reported how the demon-possessed man had been healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.37', 'BSB', 'Then all the people of the region of the Gerasenes asked Jesus to depart from them, because great fear had taken hold of them. So He got into the boat and started back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.38', 'BSB', 'The man whom the demons had left begged to go with Jesus. But He sent him away, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.39', 'BSB', '“Return home and describe how much God has done for you.” So the man went away and proclaimed all over the town how much Jesus had done for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.40', 'BSB', 'When Jesus returned, the crowd welcomed Him, for they had all been waiting for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.41', 'BSB', 'Just then a synagogue leader named Jairus came and fell at Jesus’ feet. He begged Him to come to his house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.42', 'BSB', 'because his only daughter, who was about twelve, was dying. As Jesus went with him, the crowds pressed around Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.43', 'BSB', 'including a woman who had suffered from bleeding for twelve years. She had spent all her money on physicians, but no one was able to heal her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.44', 'BSB', 'She came up behind Jesus and touched the fringe of His cloak, and immediately her bleeding stopped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.45', 'BSB', '“Who touched Me?” Jesus asked. But they all denied it. “Master,” said Peter, “the people are crowding and pressing against You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.46', 'BSB', 'But Jesus declared, “Someone touched Me, for I know that power has gone out from Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.47', 'BSB', 'Then the woman, seeing that she could not escape notice, came trembling and fell down before Him. In the presence of all the people, she explained why she had touched Him and how she had immediately been healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.48', 'BSB', '“Daughter,” said Jesus, “your faith has healed you. Go in peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.49', 'BSB', 'While He was still speaking, someone arrived from the house of the synagogue leader. “Your daughter is dead,” he told Jairus. “Do not bother the Teacher anymore.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.50', 'BSB', 'But Jesus overheard them and said to Jairus, “Do not be afraid; just believe, and she will be healed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.51', 'BSB', 'When He entered the house, He did not allow anyone to go in with Him except Peter, John, James, and the child’s father and mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.52', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, everyone was weeping and mourning for her. But Jesus said, “Stop weeping; she is not dead but asleep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.53', 'BSB', 'And they laughed at Him, knowing that she was dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.54', 'BSB', 'But Jesus took her by the hand and called out, “Child, get up!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.55', 'BSB', 'Her spirit returned, and at once she got up. And He directed that she be given something to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.8.56', 'BSB', 'Her parents were astounded, but Jesus ordered them not to tell anyone what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus called the Twelve together and gave them power and authority over all demons, and power to cure diseases.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.2', 'BSB', 'And He sent them out to proclaim the kingdom of God and to heal the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.3', 'BSB', '“Take nothing for the journey,” He told them, “no staff, no bag, no bread, no money, no second tunic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.4', 'BSB', 'Whatever house you enter, stay there until you leave that area.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.5', 'BSB', 'If anyone does not welcome you, shake the dust off your feet when you leave that town, as a testimony against them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.6', 'BSB', 'So they set out and went from village to village, preaching the gospel and healing people everywhere.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.7', 'BSB', 'When Herod the tetrarch heard about all that was happening, he was perplexed. For some were saying that John had risen from the dead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.8', 'BSB', 'others that Elijah had appeared, and still others that a prophet of old had arisen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.9', 'BSB', '“I beheaded John,” Herod said, “but who is this man I hear such things about?” And he kept trying to see Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.10', 'BSB', 'Then the apostles returned and reported to Jesus all that they had done. Taking them away privately, He withdrew to a town called Bethsaida.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.11', 'BSB', 'But the crowds found out and followed Him. He welcomed them and spoke to them about the kingdom of God, and He healed those who needed healing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.12', 'BSB', 'As the day neared its end, the Twelve came to Jesus and said, “Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding villages and countryside for lodging and provisions. For we are in a desolate place here.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.13', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told them, “You give them something to eat.” “We have only five loaves of bread and two fish,” they answered, “unless we go and buy food for all these people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.14', 'BSB', '(There were about five thousand men.) He told His disciples, “Have them sit down in groups of about fifty each.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.15', 'BSB', 'They did so, and everyone was seated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.16', 'BSB', 'Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing and broke them. Then He gave them to the disciples to set before the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.17', 'BSB', 'They all ate and were satisfied, and the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces that were left over.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.18', 'BSB', 'One day as Jesus was praying in private and the disciples were with Him, He questioned them: “Who do the crowds say I am?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.19', 'BSB', 'They replied, “Some say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and still others, that a prophet of old has arisen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.20', 'BSB', '“But what about you?” Jesus asked. “Who do you say I am?” Peter answered, “The Christ of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus strictly warned them not to tell this to anyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.22', 'BSB', '“The Son of Man must suffer many things,” He said. “He must be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and He must be killed and on the third day be raised to life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.23', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to all of them, “If anyone wants to come after Me, he must deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.24', 'BSB', 'For whoever wants to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life for My sake will save it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.25', 'BSB', 'What does it profit a man to gain the whole world, yet lose or forfeit his very self?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.26', 'BSB', 'If anyone is ashamed of Me and My words, the Son of Man will be ashamed of him when He comes in His glory and in the glory of the Father and of the holy angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.27', 'BSB', 'But I tell you truthfully, some who are standing here will not taste death before they see the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.28', 'BSB', 'About eight days after Jesus had said these things, He took with Him Peter, John, and James, and went up on a mountain to pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.29', 'BSB', 'And as He was praying, the appearance of His face changed, and His clothes became radiantly white.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.30', 'BSB', 'Suddenly two men, Moses and Elijah, began talking with Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.31', 'BSB', 'They appeared in glory and spoke about His departure, which He was about to accomplish at Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.32', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile Peter and his companions were overcome by sleep, but when they awoke, they saw Jesus’ glory and the two men standing with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.33', 'BSB', 'As Moses and Elijah were leaving, Peter said to Jesus, “Master, it is good for us to be here. Let us put up three shelters —one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.” (He did not know what he was saying.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.34', 'BSB', 'While Peter was speaking, a cloud appeared and enveloped them, and they were afraid as they entered the cloud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.35', 'BSB', 'And a voice came from the cloud, saying, “This is My Son, whom I have chosen. Listen to Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.36', 'BSB', 'After the voice had spoken, only Jesus was present with them. The disciples kept this to themselves, and in those days they did not tell anyone what they had seen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.37', 'BSB', 'The next day, when they came down from the mountain, Jesus was met by a large crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.38', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a man in the crowd cried out, “Teacher, I beg You to look at my son, for he is my only child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.39', 'BSB', 'A spirit keeps seizing him, and he screams abruptly. It throws him into convulsions so that he foams at the mouth. It keeps mauling him and rarely departs from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.40', 'BSB', 'I begged Your disciples to drive it out, but they were unable.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.41', 'BSB', '“O unbelieving and perverse generation!” Jesus replied. “How long must I remain with you and put up with you? Bring your son here.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.42', 'BSB', 'Even while the boy was approaching, the demon slammed him to the ground in a convulsion. But Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, healed the boy, and gave him back to his father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.43', 'BSB', 'And they were all astonished at the greatness of God. While everyone was marveling at all that Jesus was doing, He said to His disciples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.44', 'BSB', '“Let these words sink into your ears: The Son of Man is about to be delivered into the hands of men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.45', 'BSB', 'But they did not understand this statement. It was veiled from them so that they could not comprehend it, and they were afraid to ask Him about it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.46', 'BSB', 'Then an argument started among the disciples as to which of them would be the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.47', 'BSB', 'But Jesus, knowing the thoughts of their hearts, had a little child stand beside Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.48', 'BSB', 'And He said to them, “Whoever welcomes this little child in My name welcomes Me, and whoever welcomes Me welcomes the One who sent Me. For whoever is the least among all of you, he is the greatest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.49', 'BSB', '“Master,” said John, “we saw someone driving out demons in Your name, and we tried to stop him, because he does not accompany us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.50', 'BSB', '“Do not stop him,” Jesus replied, “for whoever is not against you is for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.51', 'BSB', 'As the day of His ascension approached, Jesus resolutely set out for Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.52', 'BSB', 'He sent messengers on ahead, who went into a village of the Samaritans to make arrangements for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.53', 'BSB', 'But the people there refused to welcome Him, because He was heading for Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.54', 'BSB', 'When the disciples James and John saw this, they asked, “Lord, do You want us to call down fire from heaven to consume them?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.55', 'BSB', 'But Jesus turned and rebuked them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.56', 'BSB', 'And He and His disciples went on to another village.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.57', 'BSB', 'As they were walking along the road, someone said to Jesus, “I will follow You wherever You go.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.58', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Foxes have dens and birds of the air have nests, but the Son of Man has no place to lay His head.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.59', 'BSB', 'Then He said to another man, “Follow Me.” The man replied, “Lord, first let me go and bury my father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.60', 'BSB', 'But Jesus told him, “Let the dead bury their own dead. You, however, go and proclaim the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.61', 'BSB', 'Still another said, “I will follow You, Lord; but first let me bid farewell to my family.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.9.62', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus declared, “No one who puts his hand to the plow and then looks back is fit for the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.1', 'BSB', 'After this, the Lord appointed seventy-two others and sent them two by two ahead of Him to every town and place He was about to visit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.2', 'BSB', 'And He told them, “The harvest is plentiful, but the workers are few. Ask the Lord of the harvest, therefore, to send out workers into His harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.3', 'BSB', 'Go! I am sending you out like lambs among wolves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.4', 'BSB', 'Carry no purse or bag or sandals. Do not greet anyone along the road.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.5', 'BSB', 'Whatever house you enter, begin by saying, ‘Peace to this house.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.6', 'BSB', 'If a man of peace is there, your peace will rest on him; if not, it will return to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.7', 'BSB', 'Stay at the same house, eating and drinking whatever you are offered. For the worker is worthy of his wages. Do not move around from house to house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.8', 'BSB', 'If you enter a town and they welcome you, eat whatever is set before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.9', 'BSB', 'Heal the sick who are there and tell them, ‘The kingdom of God is near you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.10', 'BSB', 'But if you enter a town and they do not welcome you, go into the streets and declare,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.11', 'BSB', '‘Even the dust of your town that clings to our feet, we wipe off as a testimony against you. Yet be sure of this: The kingdom of God is near.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.12', 'BSB', 'I tell you, it will be more bearable on that day for Sodom than for that town.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.13', 'BSB', 'Woe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the miracles that were performed in you had been performed in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.14', 'BSB', 'But it will be more bearable for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment than for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.15', 'BSB', 'And you, Capernaum, will you be lifted up to heaven? No, you will be brought down to Hades!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.16', 'BSB', 'Whoever listens to you listens to Me; whoever rejects you rejects Me; and whoever rejects Me rejects the One who sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.17', 'BSB', 'The seventy-two returned with joy and said, “Lord, even the demons submit to us in Your name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.18', 'BSB', 'So He told them, “I saw Satan fall like lightning from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.19', 'BSB', 'Behold, I have given you authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will harm you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.20', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, do not rejoice that the spirits submit to you, but rejoice that your names are written in heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.21', 'BSB', 'At that time Jesus rejoiced in the Holy Spirit and declared, “I praise You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because You have hidden these things from the wise and learned, and revealed them to little children. Yes, Father, for this was well-pleasing in Your sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.22', 'BSB', 'All things have been entrusted to Me by My Father. No one knows who the Son is except the Father, and no one knows who the Father is except the Son and those to whom the Son chooses to reveal Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.23', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus turned to the disciples and said privately, “Blessed are the eyes that see what you see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.24', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that many prophets and kings desired to see what you see but did not see it, and to hear what you hear but did not hear it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.25', 'BSB', 'One day an expert in the law stood up to test Him. “Teacher,” he asked, “what must I do to inherit eternal life?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.26', 'BSB', '“What is written in the Law?” Jesus replied. “How do you read it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.27', 'BSB', 'He answered, “‘Love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your strength and with all your mind’ and ‘Love your neighbor as yourself.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.28', 'BSB', '“You have answered correctly,” Jesus said. “Do this and you will live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.29', 'BSB', 'But wanting to justify himself, he asked Jesus, “And who is my neighbor?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.30', 'BSB', 'Jesus took up this question and said, “A man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho when he fell into the hands of robbers. They stripped him, beat him, and went away, leaving him half dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.31', 'BSB', 'Now by chance a priest was going down the same road, but when he saw him, he passed by on the other side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.32', 'BSB', 'So too, when a Levite came to that spot and saw him, he passed by on the other side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.33', 'BSB', 'But when a Samaritan on a journey came upon him, he looked at him and had compassion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.34', 'BSB', 'He went to him and bandaged his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. Then he put him on his own animal, brought him to an inn, and took care of him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.35', 'BSB', 'The next day he took out two denarii and gave them to the innkeeper. ‘Take care of him,’ he said, ‘and on my return I will repay you for any additional expense.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.36', 'BSB', 'Which of these three do you think was a neighbor to the man who fell into the hands of robbers?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.37', 'BSB', '“The one who showed him mercy,” replied the expert in the law. Then Jesus told him, “Go and do likewise.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.38', 'BSB', 'As they traveled along, Jesus entered a village where a woman named Martha welcomed Him into her home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.39', 'BSB', 'She had a sister named Mary, who sat at the Lord’s feet listening to His message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.40', 'BSB', 'But Martha was distracted by all the preparations to be made. She came to Jesus and said, “Lord, do You not care that my sister has left me to serve alone? Tell her to help me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.41', 'BSB', '“Martha, Martha,” the Lord replied, “you are worried and upset about many things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.10.42', 'BSB', 'But only one thing is necessary. Mary has chosen the good portion, and it will not be taken away from her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.1', 'BSB', 'One day in a place where Jesus had just finished praying, one of His disciples requested, “Lord, teach us to pray, just as John taught his disciples.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.2', 'BSB', 'So Jesus told them, “When you pray, say: ‘Father, hallowed be Your name. Your kingdom come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.3', 'BSB', 'Give us each day our daily bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.4', 'BSB', 'And forgive us our sins, for we also forgive everyone who sins against us. And lead us not into temptation.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.5', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “Suppose one of you goes to his friend at midnight and says, ‘Friend, lend me three loaves of bread,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.6', 'BSB', 'because a friend of mine has come to me on a journey, and I have nothing to set before him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.7', 'BSB', 'And suppose the one inside answers, ‘Do not bother me. My door is already shut, and my children and I are in bed. I cannot get up to give you anything.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.8', 'BSB', 'I tell you, even though he will not get up to provide for him because of his friendship, yet because of the man’s persistence, he will get up and give him as much as he needs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.9', 'BSB', 'So I tell you: Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock, and the door will be opened to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.10', 'BSB', 'For everyone who asks receives; he who seeks finds; and to him who knocks, the door will be opened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.11', 'BSB', 'What father among you, if his son asks for a fish, will give him a snake instead?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.12', 'BSB', 'Or if he asks for an egg, will give him a scorpion?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.13', 'BSB', 'So if you who are evil know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father in heaven give the Holy Spirit to those who ask Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.14', 'BSB', 'One day Jesus was driving out a demon that was mute. And when the demon was gone, the man who had been mute spoke. The crowds were amazed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.15', 'BSB', 'but some of them said, “It is by Beelzebul, the prince of the demons, that He drives out demons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.16', 'BSB', 'And others tested Him by demanding a sign from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.17', 'BSB', 'Knowing their thoughts, Jesus said to them, “Every kingdom divided against itself will be laid waste, and a house divided against a house will fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.18', 'BSB', 'If Satan is divided against himself, how can his kingdom stand? After all, you say that I drive out demons by Beelzebul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.19', 'BSB', 'And if I drive out demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your sons drive them out? So then, they will be your judges.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.20', 'BSB', 'But if I drive out demons by the finger of God, then the kingdom of God has come upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.21', 'BSB', 'When a strong man, fully armed, guards his house, his possessions are secure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.22', 'BSB', 'But when someone stronger attacks and overpowers him, he takes away the armor in which the man trusted, and then he divides up his plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.23', 'BSB', 'He who is not with Me is against Me, and he who does not gather with Me scatters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.24', 'BSB', 'When an unclean spirit comes out of a man, it passes through arid places seeking rest and does not find it. Then it says, ‘I will return to the house I left.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.25', 'BSB', 'On its return, it finds the house swept clean and put in order.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.26', 'BSB', 'Then it goes and brings seven other spirits more wicked than itself, and they go in and dwell there. And the final plight of that man is worse than the first.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.27', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was saying these things, a woman in the crowd raised her voice and said, “Blessed is the womb that bore You, and blessed are the breasts that nursed You!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.28', 'BSB', 'But He replied, “Blessed rather are those who hear the word of God and obey it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.29', 'BSB', 'As the crowds were increasing, Jesus said, “This is a wicked generation. It demands a sign, but none will be given it except the sign of Jonah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.30', 'BSB', 'For as Jonah was a sign to the Ninevites, so the Son of Man will be a sign to this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.31', 'BSB', 'The Queen of the South will rise at the judgment with the men of this generation and condemn them; for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon, and now One greater than Solomon is here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.32', 'BSB', 'The men of Nineveh will stand at the judgment with this generation and condemn it; for they repented at the preaching of Jonah, and now One greater than Jonah is here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.33', 'BSB', 'No one lights a lamp and puts it in a cellar or under a basket. Instead, he sets it on a stand, so those who enter can see the light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.34', 'BSB', 'Your eye is the lamp of your body. When your eyes are good, your whole body also is full of light. But when they are bad, your body is full of darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.35', 'BSB', 'Be careful, then, that the light within you is not darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.36', 'BSB', 'So if your whole body is full of light, with no part of it in darkness, you will be radiant, as though a lamp were shining on you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.37', 'BSB', 'As Jesus was speaking, a Pharisee invited Him to dine with him; so He went in and reclined at the table.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.38', 'BSB', 'But the Pharisee was surprised to see that Jesus did not first wash before the meal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.39', 'BSB', '“Now then,” said the Lord, “you Pharisees clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside you are full of greed and wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.40', 'BSB', 'You fools! Did not the One who made the outside make the inside as well?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.41', 'BSB', 'But give as alms the things that are within you, and you will see that everything is clean for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.42', 'BSB', 'Woe to you Pharisees! You pay tithes of mint, rue, and every herb, but you disregard justice and the love of God. You should have practiced the latter without neglecting the former.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.43', 'BSB', 'Woe to you Pharisees! You love the chief seats in the synagogues and the greetings in the marketplaces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.44', 'BSB', 'Woe to you! For you are like unmarked graves, which men walk over without even noticing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.45', 'BSB', 'One of the experts in the law told Him, “Teacher, when You say these things, You insult us as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.46', 'BSB', '“Woe to you as well, experts in the law!” He replied. “You weigh men down with heavy burdens, but you yourselves will not lift a finger to lighten their load.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.47', 'BSB', 'Woe to you! You build tombs for the prophets, but it was your fathers who killed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.48', 'BSB', 'So you are witnesses consenting to the deeds of your fathers: They killed the prophets, and you build their tombs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.49', 'BSB', 'Because of this, the wisdom of God said, ‘I will send them prophets and apostles; some of them they will kill and others they will persecute.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.50', 'BSB', 'As a result, this generation will be charged with the blood of all the prophets that has been shed since the foundation of the world,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.51', 'BSB', 'from the blood of Abel to the blood of Zechariah, who was killed between the altar and the sanctuary. Yes, I tell you, all of it will be charged to this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.52', 'BSB', 'Woe to you experts in the law! For you have taken away the key to knowledge. You yourselves have not entered, and you have hindered those who were entering.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.53', 'BSB', 'As Jesus went on from there, the scribes and Pharisees began to oppose Him bitterly and to ply Him with questions about many things,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.11.54', 'BSB', 'waiting to catch Him in something He might say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.1', 'BSB', 'In the meantime, a crowd of many thousands had gathered, so that they were trampling one another. Jesus began to speak first to His disciples: “Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.2', 'BSB', 'There is nothing concealed that will not be disclosed, and nothing hidden that will not be made known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.3', 'BSB', 'What you have spoken in the dark will be heard in the daylight, and what you have whispered in the inner rooms will be proclaimed from the housetops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.4', 'BSB', 'I tell you, My friends, do not be afraid of those who kill the body and after that can do no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.5', 'BSB', 'But I will show you whom you should fear: Fear the One who, after you have been killed, has authority to throw you into hell. Yes, I tell you, fear Him!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.6', 'BSB', 'Are not five sparrows sold for two pennies? Yet not one of them is forgotten by God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.7', 'BSB', 'And even the very hairs of your head are all numbered. So do not be afraid; you are worth more than many sparrows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.8', 'BSB', 'I tell you, everyone who confesses Me before men, the Son of Man will also confess him before the angels of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.9', 'BSB', 'But whoever denies Me before men will be denied before the angels of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.10', 'BSB', 'And everyone who speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven, but whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.11', 'BSB', 'When you are brought before synagogues, rulers, and authorities, do not worry about how to defend yourselves or what to say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.12', 'BSB', 'For at that time the Holy Spirit will teach you what you should say.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.13', 'BSB', 'Someone in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.14', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “Man, who appointed Me judge or executor between you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.15', 'BSB', 'And He said to them, “Watch out! Guard yourselves against every form of greed, for one’s life does not consist in the abundance of his possessions.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.16', 'BSB', 'Then He told them a parable: “The ground of a certain rich man produced an abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.17', 'BSB', 'So he thought to himself, ‘What shall I do, since I have nowhere to store my crops?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.18', 'BSB', 'Then he said, ‘This is what I will do: I will tear down my barns and will build bigger ones, and there I will store up all my grain and my goods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.19', 'BSB', 'Then I will say to myself, “You have plenty of good things laid up for many years. Take it easy. Eat, drink, and be merry!”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.20', 'BSB', 'But God said to him, ‘You fool! This very night your life will be required of you. Then who will own what you have accumulated?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.21', 'BSB', 'This is how it will be for anyone who stores up treasure for himself but is not rich toward God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.22', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to His disciples, “Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat, or about your body, what you will wear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.23', 'BSB', 'For life is more than food, and the body more than clothes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.24', 'BSB', 'Consider the ravens: They do not sow or reap, they have no storehouse or barn; yet God feeds them. How much more valuable you are than the birds!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.25', 'BSB', 'Who of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.26', 'BSB', 'So if you cannot do such a small thing, why do you worry about the rest?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.27', 'BSB', 'Consider how the lilies grow: They do not labor or spin. Yet I tell you, not even Solomon in all his glory was adorned like one of these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.28', 'BSB', 'If that is how God clothes the grass of the field, which is here today and tomorrow is thrown into the furnace, how much more will He clothe you, O you of little faith!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.29', 'BSB', 'And do not be concerned about what you will eat or drink. Do not worry about it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.30', 'BSB', 'For the Gentiles of the world strive after all these things, and your Father knows that you need them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.31', 'BSB', 'But seek His kingdom, and these things will be added unto you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.32', 'BSB', 'Do not be afraid, little flock, for your Father is pleased to give you the kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.33', 'BSB', 'Sell your possessions and give to the poor. Provide yourselves with purses that will not wear out, an inexhaustible treasure in heaven, where no thief approaches and no moth destroys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.34', 'BSB', 'For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.35', 'BSB', 'Be dressed for service and keep your lamps burning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.36', 'BSB', 'Then you will be like servants waiting for their master to return from the wedding banquet, so that when he comes and knocks, they can open the door for him at once.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.37', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those servants whom the master finds on watch when he returns. Truly I tell you, he will dress himself to serve and will have them recline at the table, and he himself will come and wait on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.38', 'BSB', 'Even if he comes in the second or third watch of the night and finds them alert, those servants will be blessed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.39', 'BSB', 'But understand this: If the homeowner had known at what hour the thief was coming, he would not have let his house be broken into.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.40', 'BSB', 'You also must be ready, because the Son of Man will come at an hour you do not expect.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.41', 'BSB', '“Lord,” said Peter, “are You addressing this parable to us, or to everyone else as well?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.42', 'BSB', 'And the Lord answered, “Who then is the faithful and wise manager, whom the master puts in charge of his servants to give them their portion at the proper time?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.43', 'BSB', 'Blessed is that servant whose master finds him doing so when he returns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.44', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, he will put him in charge of all his possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.45', 'BSB', 'But suppose that servant says in his heart, ‘My master will be a long time in coming,’ and he begins to beat the menservants and maidservants, and to eat and drink and get drunk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.46', 'BSB', 'The master of that servant will come on a day he does not expect and at an hour he does not anticipate. Then he will cut him to pieces and assign him a place with the unbelievers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.47', 'BSB', 'That servant who knows his master’s will but does not get ready or follow his instructions will be beaten with many blows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.48', 'BSB', 'But the one who unknowingly does things worthy of punishment will be beaten with few blows. From everyone who has been given much, much will be required; and from him who has been entrusted with much, even more will be demanded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.49', 'BSB', 'I have come to ignite a fire on the earth, and how I wish it were already kindled!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.50', 'BSB', 'But I have a baptism to undergo, and how distressed I am until it is accomplished!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.51', 'BSB', 'Do you think that I have come to bring peace to the earth? No, I tell you, but division.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.52', 'BSB', 'From now on, five in one household will be divided, three against two and two against three.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.53', 'BSB', 'They will be divided, father against son and son against father, mother against daughter and daughter against mother, mother-in-law against daughter-in-law and daughter-in-law against mother-in-law.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.54', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the crowds, “As soon as you see a cloud rising in the west, you say, ‘A shower is coming,’ and that is what happens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.55', 'BSB', 'And when the south wind blows, you say, ‘It will be hot,’ and it is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.56', 'BSB', 'You hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the earth and sky. Why don’t you know how to interpret the present time?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.57', 'BSB', 'And why don’t you judge for yourselves what is right?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.58', 'BSB', 'Make every effort to reconcile with your adversary while you are on your way to the magistrate. Otherwise, he may drag you off to the judge, and the judge may hand you over to the officer, and the officer may throw you into prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.12.59', 'BSB', 'I tell you, you will not get out until you have paid the very last penny.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.1', 'BSB', 'At that time some of those present told Jesus about the Galileans whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.2', 'BSB', 'To this He replied, “Do you think that these Galileans were worse sinners than all the other Galileans, because they suffered this fate?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.3', 'BSB', 'No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.4', 'BSB', 'Or those eighteen who were killed when the tower of Siloam collapsed on them: Do you think that they were more sinful than all the others living in Jerusalem?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.5', 'BSB', 'No, I tell you. But unless you repent, you too will all perish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.6', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told this parable: “A man had a fig tree that was planted in his vineyard. He went to look for fruit on it, but did not find any.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.7', 'BSB', 'So he said to the keeper of the vineyard, ‘Look, for the past three years I have come to search for fruit on this fig tree and haven’t found any. Therefore cut it down! Why should it use up the soil?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.8', 'BSB', '‘Sir,’ the man replied, ‘leave it alone again this year, until I dig around it and fertilize it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.9', 'BSB', 'If it bears fruit next year, fine. But if not, you can cut it down.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.10', 'BSB', 'One Sabbath Jesus was teaching in one of the synagogues,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.11', 'BSB', 'and a woman there had been disabled by a spirit for eighteen years. She was hunched over and could not stand up straight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.12', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw her, He called her over and said, “Woman, you are set free from your disability.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.13', 'BSB', 'Then He placed His hands on her, and immediately she straightened up and began to glorify God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.14', 'BSB', 'But the synagogue leader was indignant that Jesus had healed on the Sabbath. “There are six days for work,” he told the crowd. “So come and be healed on those days and not on the Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.15', 'BSB', '“You hypocrites!” the Lord replied. “Does not each of you on the Sabbath untie his ox or donkey from the stall and lead it to water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.16', 'BSB', 'Then should not this daughter of Abraham, whom Satan has kept bound for eighteen long years, be released from her bondage on the Sabbath day?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.17', 'BSB', 'When Jesus said this, all His adversaries were humiliated. And the whole crowd rejoiced at all the glorious things He was doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.18', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus asked, “What is the kingdom of God like? To what can I compare it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.19', 'BSB', 'It is like a mustard seed that a man tossed into his garden. It grew and became a tree, and the birds of the air nested in its branches.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.20', 'BSB', 'Again He asked, “To what can I compare the kingdom of God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.21', 'BSB', 'It is like leaven that a woman took and mixed into three measures of flour, until all of it was leavened.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.22', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus traveled throughout the towns and villages, teaching as He made His way toward Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.23', 'BSB', '“Lord,” someone asked Him, “will only a few people be saved?” Jesus answered,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.24', 'BSB', '“Make every effort to enter through the narrow door. For many, I tell you, will try to enter and will not be able.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.25', 'BSB', 'After the master of the house gets up and shuts the door, you will stand outside knocking and saying, ‘Lord, open the door for us.’ But he will reply, ‘I do not know where you are from.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.26', 'BSB', 'Then you will say, ‘We ate and drank with you, and you taught in our streets.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.27', 'BSB', 'And he will answer, ‘I tell you, I do not know where you are from. Depart from me, all you evildoers.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.28', 'BSB', 'There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth when you see Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and all the prophets in the kingdom of God, but you yourselves are thrown out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.29', 'BSB', 'People will come from east and west and north and south, and will recline at the table in the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.30', 'BSB', 'And indeed, some who are last will be first, and some who are first will be last.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.31', 'BSB', 'At that very hour, some Pharisees came to Jesus and told Him, “Leave this place and get away, because Herod wants to kill You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.32', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “Go tell that fox, ‘Look, I will keep driving out demons and healing people today and tomorrow, and on the third day I will reach My goal.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.33', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, I must keep going today and tomorrow and the next day, for it is not admissible for a prophet to perish outside of Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.34', 'BSB', 'O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those sent to her, how often I have longed to gather your children together as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, but you were unwilling!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.13.35', 'BSB', 'Look, your house is left to you desolate. And I tell you that you will not see Me again until you say, ‘Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.1', 'BSB', 'One Sabbath, Jesus went to eat in the home of a leading Pharisee, and those in attendance were watching Him closely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.2', 'BSB', 'Right there before Him was a man with dropsy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.3', 'BSB', 'So Jesus asked the experts in the law and the Pharisees, “Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath or not?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.4', 'BSB', 'But they remained silent. Then Jesus took hold of the man, healed him, and sent him on his way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.5', 'BSB', 'And He asked them, “Which of you whose son or ox falls into a pit on the Sabbath day will not immediately pull him out?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.6', 'BSB', 'And they were unable to answer these questions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.7', 'BSB', 'When Jesus noticed how the guests chose the places of honor, He told them a parable:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.8', 'BSB', '“When you are invited to a wedding banquet, do not sit in the place of honor, in case someone more distinguished than you has been invited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.9', 'BSB', 'Then the host who invited both of you will come and tell you, ‘Give this man your seat.’ And in humiliation, you will have to take the last place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.10', 'BSB', 'But when you are invited, go and sit in the last place, so that your host will come and tell you, ‘Friend, move up to a better place.’ Then you will be honored in front of everyone at the table with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.11', 'BSB', 'For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, and the one who humbles himself will be exalted.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.12', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the man who had invited Him, “When you host a dinner or a banquet, do not invite your friends or brothers or relatives or rich neighbors. Otherwise, they may invite you in return, and you will be repaid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.13', 'BSB', 'But when you host a banquet, invite the poor, the crippled, the lame, and the blind,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.14', 'BSB', 'and you will be blessed. Since they cannot repay you, you will be repaid at the resurrection of the righteous.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.15', 'BSB', 'When one of those reclining with Him heard this, he said to Jesus, “Blessed is everyone who will eat at the feast in the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.16', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “A certain man prepared a great banquet and invited many guests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.17', 'BSB', 'When it was time for the banquet, he sent his servant to tell those who had been invited, ‘Come, for everything is now ready.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.18', 'BSB', 'But one after another they all began to make excuses. The first one said, ‘I have bought a field, and I need to go see it. Please excuse me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.19', 'BSB', 'Another said, ‘I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I am going to try them out. Please excuse me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.20', 'BSB', 'Still another said, ‘I have married a wife, so I cannot come.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.21', 'BSB', 'The servant returned and reported all this to his master. Then the owner of the house became angry and said to his servant, ‘Go out quickly into the streets and alleys of the city, and bring in the poor, the crippled, the blind, and the lame.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.22', 'BSB', '‘Sir,’ the servant replied, ‘what you ordered has been done, and there is still room.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.23', 'BSB', 'So the master told his servant, ‘Go out to the highways and hedges and compel them to come in, so that my house will be full.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.24', 'BSB', 'For I tell you, not one of those men who were invited will taste my banquet.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.25', 'BSB', 'Large crowds were now traveling with Jesus, and He turned and said to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.26', 'BSB', '“If anyone comes to Me and does not hate his father and mother and wife and children and brothers and sisters—yes, even his own life—he cannot be My disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.27', 'BSB', 'And whoever does not carry his cross and follow Me cannot be My disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.28', 'BSB', 'Which of you, wishing to build a tower, does not first sit down and count the cost to see if he has the resources to complete it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.29', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, if he lays the foundation and is unable to finish the work, everyone who sees it will ridicule him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.30', 'BSB', 'saying, ‘This man could not finish what he started to build.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.31', 'BSB', 'Or what king on his way to war with another king will not first sit down and consider whether he can engage with ten thousand men the one coming against him with twenty thousand?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.32', 'BSB', 'And if he is unable, he will send a delegation while the other king is still far off, to ask for terms of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.33', 'BSB', 'In the same way, any one of you who does not give up everything he has cannot be My disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.34', 'BSB', 'Salt is good, but if the salt loses its savor, with what will it be seasoned?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.14.35', 'BSB', 'It is fit neither for the soil nor for the manure pile, and it is thrown out. He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.1', 'BSB', 'Now all the tax collectors and sinners were gathering around to listen to Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.2', 'BSB', 'So the Pharisees and scribes began to grumble: “This man welcomes sinners and eats with them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.3', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told them this parable:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.4', 'BSB', '“What man among you, if he has a hundred sheep and loses one of them, does not leave the ninety-nine in the pasture and go after the one that is lost, until he finds it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.5', 'BSB', 'And when he finds it, he joyfully puts it on his shoulders,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.6', 'BSB', 'comes home, and calls together his friends and neighbors to tell them, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my lost sheep!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.7', 'BSB', 'In the same way, I tell you that there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous ones who do not need to repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.8', 'BSB', 'Or what woman who has ten silver coins and loses one of them does not light a lamp, sweep her house, and search carefully until she finds it?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.9', 'BSB', 'And when she finds it, she calls together her friends and neighbors to say, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my lost coin.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.10', 'BSB', 'In the same way, I tell you, there is joy in the presence of God’s angels over one sinner who repents.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.11', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said, “There was a man who had two sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.12', 'BSB', 'The younger son said to him, ‘Father, give me my share of the estate.’ So he divided his property between them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.13', 'BSB', 'After a few days, the younger son got everything together and journeyed to a distant country, where he squandered his wealth in wild living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.14', 'BSB', 'After he had spent all he had, a severe famine swept through that country, and he began to be in need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.15', 'BSB', 'So he went and hired himself out to a citizen of that country, who sent him into his fields to feed the pigs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.16', 'BSB', 'He longed to fill his belly with the pods the pigs were eating, but no one would give him a thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.17', 'BSB', 'Finally he came to his senses and said, ‘How many of my father’s hired servants have plenty of food? But here I am, starving to death!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.18', 'BSB', 'I will get up and go back to my father and say to him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.19', 'BSB', 'I am no longer worthy to be called your son. Make me like one of your hired servants.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.20', 'BSB', 'So he got up and went to his father. But while he was still in the distance, his father saw him and was filled with compassion. He ran to his son, embraced him, and kissed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.21', 'BSB', 'The son declared, ‘Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you. I am no longer worthy to be called your son.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.22', 'BSB', 'But the father said to his servants, ‘Quick! Bring the best robe and put it on him. Put a ring on his finger and sandals on his feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.23', 'BSB', 'Bring the fattened calf and kill it. Let us feast and celebrate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.24', 'BSB', 'For this son of mine was dead and is alive again! He was lost and is found!’ So they began to celebrate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.25', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile the older son was in the field, and as he approached the house, he heard music and dancing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.26', 'BSB', 'So he called one of the servants and asked what was going on.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.27', 'BSB', '‘Your brother has returned,’ he said, ‘and your father has killed the fattened calf, because he has him back safe and sound.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.28', 'BSB', 'The older son became angry and refused to go in. So his father came out and pleaded with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.29', 'BSB', 'But he answered his father, ‘Look, all these years I have served you and never disobeyed a commandment of yours. Yet you never gave me even a young goat so I could celebrate with my friends.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.30', 'BSB', 'But when this son of yours returns from squandering your wealth with prostitutes, you kill the fattened calf for him!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.31', 'BSB', '‘Son, you are always with me,’ the father said, ‘and all that is mine is yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.15.32', 'BSB', 'But it was fitting to celebrate and be glad, because this brother of yours was dead and is alive again; he was lost and is found.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.1', 'BSB', 'Jesus also said to His disciples, “There was a rich man whose manager was accused of wasting his possessions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.2', 'BSB', 'So he called him in to ask, ‘What is this I hear about you? Turn in an account of your management, for you cannot be manager any longer.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.3', 'BSB', 'The manager said to himself, ‘What shall I do, now that my master is taking away my position? I am too weak to dig and too ashamed to beg.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.4', 'BSB', 'I know what I will do, so that after my removal from management, people will welcome me into their homes.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.5', 'BSB', 'And he called in each one of his master’s debtors. ‘How much do you owe my master?’ he asked the first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.6', 'BSB', '‘A hundred measures of olive oil,’ he answered. ‘Take your bill,’ said the manager. ‘Sit down quickly, and write fifty.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.7', 'BSB', 'Then he asked another, ‘And how much do you owe?’ ‘A hundred measures of wheat,’ he replied. ‘Take your bill and write eighty,’ he told him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.8', 'BSB', 'The master commended the dishonest manager because he had acted shrewdly. For the sons of this age are more shrewd in dealing with their own kind than are the sons of light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.9', 'BSB', 'I tell you, use worldly wealth to make friends for yourselves, so that when it is gone, they will welcome you into eternal dwellings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.10', 'BSB', 'Whoever is faithful with very little will also be faithful with much, and whoever is dishonest with very little will also be dishonest with much.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.11', 'BSB', 'So if you have not been faithful with worldly wealth, who will entrust you with true riches?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.12', 'BSB', 'And if you have not been faithful with the belongings of another, who will give you belongings of your own?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.13', 'BSB', 'No servant can serve two masters. Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.14', 'BSB', 'The Pharisees, who were lovers of money, heard all of this and were scoffing at Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.15', 'BSB', 'So He said to them, “You are the ones who justify yourselves before men, but God knows your hearts. For what is prized among men is detestable before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.16', 'BSB', 'The Law and the Prophets were proclaimed until John. Since that time, the gospel of the kingdom of God is being preached, and everyone is forcing his way into it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.17', 'BSB', 'But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for a single stroke of a pen to drop out of the Law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.18', 'BSB', 'Anyone who divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery, and he who marries a divorced woman commits adultery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.19', 'BSB', 'Now there was a rich man dressed in purple and fine linen, who lived each day in joyous splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.20', 'BSB', 'And a beggar named Lazarus lay at his gate, covered with sores', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.21', 'BSB', 'and longing to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man’s table. Even the dogs came and licked his sores.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.22', 'BSB', 'One day the beggar died and was carried by the angels to Abraham’s side. And the rich man also died and was buried.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.23', 'BSB', 'In Hades, where he was in torment, he looked up and saw Abraham from afar, with Lazarus by his side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.24', 'BSB', 'So he cried out, ‘Father Abraham, have mercy on me and send Lazarus to dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue. For I am in agony in this fire.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.25', 'BSB', 'But Abraham answered, ‘Child, remember that during your lifetime you received your good things, while Lazarus received bad things. But now he is comforted here, while you are in agony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.26', 'BSB', 'And besides all this, a great chasm has been fixed between us and you, so that even those who wish cannot cross from here to you, nor can anyone cross from there to us.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.27', 'BSB', '‘Then I beg you, father,’ he said, ‘send Lazarus to my father’s house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.28', 'BSB', 'for I have five brothers. Let him warn them, so that they will not also end up in this place of torment.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.29', 'BSB', 'But Abraham replied, ‘They have Moses and the prophets; let your brothers listen to them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.30', 'BSB', '‘No, father Abraham,’ he said, ‘but if someone is sent to them from the dead, they will repent.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.16.31', 'BSB', 'Then Abraham said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from the dead.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.1', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to His disciples, “It is inevitable that stumbling blocks will come, but woe to the one through whom they come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.2', 'BSB', 'It would be better for him to have a millstone hung around his neck and to be thrown into the sea than to cause one of these little ones to stumble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.3', 'BSB', 'Watch yourselves. If your brother sins, rebuke him; and if he repents, forgive him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.4', 'BSB', 'Even if he sins against you seven times in a day, and seven times returns to say, ‘I repent,’ you must forgive him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.5', 'BSB', 'The apostles said to the Lord, “Increase our faith!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.6', 'BSB', 'And the Lord answered, “If you have faith the size of a mustard seed, you can say to this mulberry tree, ‘Be uprooted and planted in the sea,’ and it will obey you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.7', 'BSB', 'Which of you whose servant comes in from plowing or shepherding in the field will say to him, ‘Come at once and sit down to eat’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.8', 'BSB', 'Instead, won’t he tell him, ‘Prepare my meal and dress yourself to serve me while I eat and drink; and afterward you may eat and drink’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.9', 'BSB', 'Does he thank the servant because he did what he was told?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.10', 'BSB', 'So you also, when you have done everything commanded of you, should say, ‘We are unworthy servants; we have only done our duty.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.11', 'BSB', 'While Jesus was on His way to Jerusalem, He was passing between Samaria and Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.12', 'BSB', 'As He entered one of the villages, He was met by ten lepers. They stood at a distance', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.13', 'BSB', 'and raised their voices, shouting, “Jesus, Master, have mercy on us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.14', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw them, He said, “Go, show yourselves to the priests.” And as they were on their way, they were cleansed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.15', 'BSB', 'When one of them saw that he was healed, he came back, praising God in a loud voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.16', 'BSB', 'He fell facedown at Jesus’ feet in thanksgiving to Him—and he was a Samaritan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.17', 'BSB', '“Were not all ten cleansed?” Jesus asked. “Where then are the other nine?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.18', 'BSB', 'Was no one found except this foreigner to return and give glory to God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.19', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to him, “Rise and go; your faith has made you well!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.20', 'BSB', 'When asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom of God would come, Jesus replied, “The kingdom of God will not come with observable signs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.21', 'BSB', 'Nor will people say, ‘Look, here it is,’ or ‘There it is.’ For you see, the kingdom of God is in your midst.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.22', 'BSB', 'Then He said to the disciples, “The time is coming when you will long to see one of the days of the Son of Man, but you will not see it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.23', 'BSB', 'People will tell you, ‘Look, there He is!’ or ‘Look, here He is!’ Do not go out or chase after them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.24', 'BSB', 'For just as the lightning flashes and lights up the sky from one end to the other, so will be the Son of Man in His day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.25', 'BSB', 'But first He must suffer many things and be rejected by this generation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.26', 'BSB', 'Just as it was in the days of Noah, so also will it be in the days of the Son of Man:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.27', 'BSB', 'People were eating and drinking, marrying and being given in marriage, up to the day Noah entered the ark. Then the flood came and destroyed them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.28', 'BSB', 'It was the same in the days of Lot: People were eating and drinking, buying and selling, planting and building.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.29', 'BSB', 'But on the day Lot left Sodom, fire and sulfur rained down from heaven and destroyed them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.30', 'BSB', 'It will be just like that on the day the Son of Man is revealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.31', 'BSB', 'On that day, let no one on the housetop come down to retrieve his possessions. Likewise, let no one in the field return for anything he has left behind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.32', 'BSB', 'Remember Lot’s wife!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.33', 'BSB', 'Whoever tries to save his life will lose it, but whoever loses his life will preserve it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.34', 'BSB', 'I tell you, on that night two people will be in one bed: One will be taken and the other left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.35', 'BSB', 'Two women will be grinding grain together: One will be taken and the other left.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.17.37', 'BSB', '“Where, Lord?” they asked. Jesus answered, “Wherever there is a carcass, there the vultures will gather.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told them a parable about their need to pray at all times and not lose heart:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.2', 'BSB', '“In a certain town there was a judge who neither feared God nor respected men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.3', 'BSB', 'And there was a widow in that town who kept appealing to him, ‘Give me justice against my adversary.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.4', 'BSB', 'For a while he refused, but later he said to himself, ‘Though I neither fear God nor respect men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.5', 'BSB', 'yet because this widow keeps pestering me, I will give her justice. Then she will stop wearing me out with her perpetual requests.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.6', 'BSB', 'And the Lord said, “Listen to the words of the unjust judge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.7', 'BSB', 'Will not God bring about justice for His elect who cry out to Him day and night? Will He continue to defer their help?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.8', 'BSB', 'I tell you, He will promptly carry out justice on their behalf. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, will He find faith on earth?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.9', 'BSB', 'To some who trusted in their own righteousness and viewed others with contempt, He also told this parable:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.10', 'BSB', '“Two men went up to the temple to pray. One was a Pharisee and the other a tax collector.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.11', 'BSB', 'The Pharisee stood by himself and prayed, ‘God, I thank You that I am not like the other men—swindlers, evildoers, adulterers—or even like this tax collector.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.12', 'BSB', 'I fast twice a week and pay tithes of all that I acquire.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.13', 'BSB', 'But the tax collector stood at a distance, unwilling even to lift up his eyes to heaven. Instead, he beat his breast and said, ‘God, have mercy on me, a sinner!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.14', 'BSB', 'I tell you, this man, rather than the Pharisee, went home justified. For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but the one who humbles himself will be exalted.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.15', 'BSB', 'Now people were even bringing their babies to Jesus for Him to place His hands on them. And when the disciples saw this, they rebuked those who brought them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.16', 'BSB', 'But Jesus called the children to Him and said, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not hinder them! For the kingdom of God belongs to such as these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.17', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, anyone who does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will never enter it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.18', 'BSB', 'Then a certain ruler asked Him, “Good Teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.19', 'BSB', '“Why do you call Me good?” Jesus replied. “No one is good except God alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.20', 'BSB', 'You know the commandments: ‘Do not commit adultery, do not murder, do not steal, do not bear false witness, honor your father and mother.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.21', 'BSB', '“All these I have kept from my youth,” he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.22', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, Jesus told him, “You still lack one thing: Sell everything you own and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven. Then come, follow Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.23', 'BSB', 'But when the ruler heard this, he became very sad, because he was extremely wealthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.24', 'BSB', 'Seeing the man’s sadness, Jesus said, “How hard it is for the rich to enter the kingdom of God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.25', 'BSB', 'Indeed, it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.26', 'BSB', 'Those who heard this asked, “Who then can be saved?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.27', 'BSB', 'But Jesus said, “What is impossible with man is possible with God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.28', 'BSB', '“Look,” said Peter, “we have left all we had to follow You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.29', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” Jesus replied, “no one who has left home or wife or brothers or parents or children for the sake of the kingdom of God', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.30', 'BSB', 'will fail to receive many times more in this age—and in the age to come, eternal life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.31', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus took the Twelve aside and said to them, “Look, we are going up to Jerusalem, and everything the prophets have written about the Son of Man will be fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.32', 'BSB', 'He will be delivered over to the Gentiles and will be mocked and insulted and spit upon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.33', 'BSB', 'They will flog Him and kill Him, and on the third day He will rise again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.34', 'BSB', 'But the disciples did not understand any of these things. The meaning was hidden from them, and they did not comprehend what He was saying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.35', 'BSB', 'As Jesus drew near to Jericho, a blind man was sitting beside the road, begging.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.36', 'BSB', 'When he heard the crowd going by, he asked what was happening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.37', 'BSB', '“Jesus of Nazareth is passing by,” they told him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.38', 'BSB', 'So he called out, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.39', 'BSB', 'Those who led the way admonished him to be silent, but he cried out all the louder, “Son of David, have mercy on me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.40', 'BSB', 'Jesus stopped and directed that the man be brought to Him. When he had been brought near, Jesus asked him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.41', 'BSB', '“What do you want Me to do for you?” “Lord,” he said, “let me see again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.42', 'BSB', '“Receive your sight!” Jesus replied. “Your faith has healed you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.18.43', 'BSB', 'Immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus, glorifying God. And all the people who saw this gave praise to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus entered Jericho and was passing through.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.2', 'BSB', 'And there was a man named Zacchaeus, a chief tax collector, who was very wealthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.3', 'BSB', 'He was trying to see who Jesus was, but could not see over the crowd because he was small in stature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.4', 'BSB', 'So he ran on ahead and climbed a sycamore tree to see Him, since Jesus was about to pass that way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.5', 'BSB', 'When Jesus came to that place, He looked up and said, “Zacchaeus, hurry down, for I must stay at your house today.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.6', 'BSB', 'So Zacchaeus hurried down and welcomed Him joyfully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.7', 'BSB', 'And all who saw this began to grumble, saying, “He has gone to be the guest of a sinful man!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.8', 'BSB', 'But Zacchaeus stood up and said to the Lord, “Look, Lord, half of my possessions I give to the poor, and if I have cheated anyone, I will repay it fourfold.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.9', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to him, “Today salvation has come to this house, because this man too is a son of Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.10', 'BSB', 'For the Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.11', 'BSB', 'While the people were listening to this, Jesus proceeded to tell them a parable, because He was near Jerusalem and they thought the kingdom of God would appear imminently.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.12', 'BSB', 'So He said, “A man of noble birth went to a distant country to lay claim to his kingship and then return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.13', 'BSB', 'Beforehand, he called ten of his servants and gave them ten minas. ‘Conduct business with this until I return,’ he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.14', 'BSB', 'But his subjects hated him and sent a delegation after him to say, ‘We do not want this man to rule over us.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.15', 'BSB', 'When he returned from procuring his kingship, he summoned the servants to whom he had given the money, to find out what each one had earned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.16', 'BSB', 'The first servant came forward and said, ‘Master, your mina has produced ten more minas.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.17', 'BSB', 'His master replied, ‘Well done, good servant! Because you have been faithful in a very small matter, you shall have authority over ten cities.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.18', 'BSB', 'The second servant came and said, ‘Master, your mina has made five minas.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.19', 'BSB', 'And to this one he said, ‘You shall have authority over five cities.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.20', 'BSB', 'Then another servant came and said, ‘Master, here is your mina, which I have laid away in a piece of cloth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.21', 'BSB', 'For I was afraid of you, because you are a harsh man. You withdraw what you did not deposit and reap what you did not sow.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.22', 'BSB', 'His master replied, ‘You wicked servant, I will judge you by your own words. So you knew that I am a harsh man, withdrawing what I did not deposit and reaping what I did not sow?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.23', 'BSB', 'Why then did you not deposit my money in the bank, and upon my return I could have collected it with interest?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.24', 'BSB', 'Then he told those standing by, ‘Take the mina from him and give it to the one who has ten minas.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.25', 'BSB', '‘Master,’ they said, ‘he already has ten!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.26', 'BSB', 'He replied, ‘I tell you that everyone who has will be given more; but the one who does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.27', 'BSB', 'And these enemies of mine who were unwilling for me to rule over them, bring them here and slay them in front of me.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.28', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had said this, He went on ahead, going up to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.29', 'BSB', 'As He approached Bethphage and Bethany at the Mount of Olives, He sent out two of His disciples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.30', 'BSB', 'saying, “Go into the village ahead of you, and as you enter it, you will find a colt tied there, on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.31', 'BSB', 'If anyone asks, ‘Why are you untying it?’ tell him, ‘The Lord needs it.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.32', 'BSB', 'So those who were sent went out and found it just as Jesus had told them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.33', 'BSB', 'As they were untying the colt, its owners asked, “Why are you untying the colt?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.34', 'BSB', '“The Lord needs it,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.35', 'BSB', 'Then they led the colt to Jesus, threw their cloaks over it, and put Jesus on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.36', 'BSB', 'As He rode along, the people spread their cloaks on the road.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.37', 'BSB', 'And as He approached the descent from the Mount of Olives, the whole multitude of disciples began to praise God joyfully in a loud voice for all the miracles they had seen:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.38', 'BSB', '“Blessed is the King who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Peace in heaven and glory in the highest!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.39', 'BSB', 'But some of the Pharisees in the crowd said to Him, “Teacher, rebuke Your disciples!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.40', 'BSB', '“I tell you,” He answered, “if they remain silent, the very stones will cry out.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.41', 'BSB', 'As Jesus approached Jerusalem and saw the city, He wept over it', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.42', 'BSB', 'and said, “If only you had known on this day what would bring you peace! But now it is hidden from your eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.43', 'BSB', 'For the days will come upon you when your enemies will barricade you and surround you and hem you in on every side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.44', 'BSB', 'They will level you to the ground—you and the children within your walls. They will not leave one stone on another, because you did not recognize the time of your visitation from God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.45', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus entered the temple courts and began to drive out those who were selling there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.46', 'BSB', 'He declared to them, “It is written: ‘My house will be a house of prayer.’ But you have made it ‘a den of robbers.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.47', 'BSB', 'Jesus was teaching at the temple every day, but the chief priests, scribes, and leaders of the people were intent on killing Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.19.48', 'BSB', 'Yet they could not find a way to do so, because all the people hung on His words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.1', 'BSB', 'One day as Jesus was teaching the people in the temple courts and proclaiming the gospel, the chief priests and scribes, together with the elders, came up to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.2', 'BSB', '“Tell us,” they said, “by what authority are You doing these things, and who gave You this authority?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.3', 'BSB', '“I will also ask you a question,” Jesus replied. “Tell Me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.4', 'BSB', 'John’s baptism—was it from heaven, or from men?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.5', 'BSB', 'They deliberated among themselves and said, “If we say, ‘From heaven,’ He will ask, ‘Why did you not believe him?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.6', 'BSB', 'But if we say, ‘From men,’ all the people will stone us, for they are convinced that John was a prophet.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.7', 'BSB', 'So they answered that they did not know where it was from.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.8', 'BSB', 'And Jesus replied, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I am doing these things.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.9', 'BSB', 'Then He proceeded to tell the people this parable: “A man planted a vineyard, rented it out to some tenants, and went away for a long time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.10', 'BSB', 'At harvest time, he sent a servant to the tenants to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard. But the tenants beat the servant and sent him away empty-handed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.11', 'BSB', 'So he sent another servant, but they beat him and treated him shamefully, sending him away empty-handed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.12', 'BSB', 'Then he sent a third, but they wounded him and threw him out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.13', 'BSB', '‘What shall I do?’ asked the owner of the vineyard. ‘I will send my beloved son. Perhaps they will respect him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.14', 'BSB', 'But when the tenants saw the son, they discussed it among themselves and said, ‘This is the heir. Let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.15', 'BSB', 'So they threw him out of the vineyard and killed him. What then will the owner of the vineyard do to them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.16', 'BSB', 'He will come and kill those tenants, and will give the vineyard to others.” And when the people heard this, they said, “May such a thing never happen!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.17', 'BSB', 'But Jesus looked directly at them and said, “Then what is the meaning of that which is written: ‘The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.18', 'BSB', 'Everyone who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces, but he on whom it falls will be crushed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.19', 'BSB', 'When the scribes and chief priests realized that Jesus had spoken this parable against them, they sought to arrest Him that very hour. But they were afraid of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.20', 'BSB', 'So they watched Him closely and sent spies who pretended to be sincere. They were hoping to catch Him in His words in order to hand Him over to the rule and authority of the governor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.21', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” they inquired, “we know that You speak and teach correctly. You show no partiality, but teach the way of God in accordance with the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.22', 'BSB', 'Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to Caesar or not?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.23', 'BSB', 'But Jesus saw through their duplicity and said to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.24', 'BSB', '“Show Me a denarius. Whose image and inscription are on it?” “Caesar’s,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.25', 'BSB', 'So Jesus told them, “Give to Caesar what is Caesar’s, and to God what is God’s.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.26', 'BSB', 'And they were unable to trap Him in His words before the people; and amazed at His answer, they fell silent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.27', 'BSB', 'Then some of the Sadducees, who say there is no resurrection, came to question Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.28', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” they said, “Moses wrote for us that if a man’s brother dies and leaves a wife but no children, the man is to marry his brother’s widow and raise up offspring for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.29', 'BSB', 'Now there were seven brothers. The first one married a wife, but died childless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.30', 'BSB', 'Then the second', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.31', 'BSB', 'and the third married the widow, and in the same way all seven died, leaving no children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.32', 'BSB', 'And last of all, the woman died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.33', 'BSB', 'So then, in the resurrection, whose wife will she be? For all seven were married to her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “The sons of this age marry and are given in marriage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.35', 'BSB', 'But those who are considered worthy to share in the age to come and in the resurrection from the dead will neither marry nor be given in marriage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.36', 'BSB', 'In fact, they can no longer die, because they are like the angels. And since they are sons of the resurrection, they are sons of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.37', 'BSB', 'Even Moses demonstrates that the dead are raised, in the passage about the burning bush. For he calls the Lord ‘the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.38', 'BSB', 'He is not the God of the dead, but of the living, for to Him all are alive.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.39', 'BSB', 'Some of the scribes answered, “Teacher, You have spoken well!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.40', 'BSB', 'And they did not dare to question Him any further.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.41', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus declared, “How can it be said that the Christ is the Son of David?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.42', 'BSB', 'For David himself says in the book of Psalms: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.43', 'BSB', 'until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.44', 'BSB', 'Thus David calls Him ‘Lord.’ So how can He be David’s son?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.45', 'BSB', 'In the hearing of all the people, Jesus said to His disciples,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.46', 'BSB', '“Beware of the scribes. They like to walk around in long robes, and they love the greetings in the marketplaces, the chief seats in the synagogues, and the places of honor at banquets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.20.47', 'BSB', 'They defraud widows of their houses, and for a show make lengthy prayers. These men will receive greater condemnation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.1', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus looked up and saw the rich putting their gifts into the treasury,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.2', 'BSB', 'and He saw a poor widow put in two small copper coins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.3', 'BSB', '“Truly I tell you,” He said, “this poor widow has put in more than all the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.4', 'BSB', 'For they all contributed out of their surplus, but she out of her poverty has put in all she had to live on.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.5', 'BSB', 'As some of the disciples were remarking how the temple was adorned with beautiful stones and consecrated gifts, Jesus said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.6', 'BSB', '“As for what you see here, the time will come when not one stone will be left on another; every one will be thrown down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.7', 'BSB', '“Teacher,” they asked, “when will these things happen? And what will be the sign that they are about to take place?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.8', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “See to it that you are not deceived. For many will come in My name, claiming, ‘I am He,’ and, ‘The time is near.’ Do not follow them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.9', 'BSB', 'When you hear of wars and rebellions, do not be alarmed. These things must happen first, but the end is not imminent.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.10', 'BSB', 'Then He told them, “Nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.11', 'BSB', 'There will be great earthquakes, famines, and pestilences in various places, along with fearful sights and great signs from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.12', 'BSB', 'But before all this, they will seize you and persecute you. On account of My name they will deliver you to the synagogues and prisons, and they will bring you before kings and governors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.13', 'BSB', 'This will be your opportunity to serve as witnesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.14', 'BSB', 'So make up your mind not to worry beforehand how to defend yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.15', 'BSB', 'For I will give you speech and wisdom that none of your adversaries will be able to resist or contradict.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.16', 'BSB', 'You will be betrayed even by parents and brothers and relatives and friends, and some of you will be put to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.17', 'BSB', 'And you will be hated by everyone because of My name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.18', 'BSB', 'Yet not even a hair of your head will perish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.19', 'BSB', 'By your patient endurance you will gain your souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.20', 'BSB', 'But when you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, you will know that her desolation is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.21', 'BSB', 'Then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains, let those in the city get out, and let those in the country stay out of the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.22', 'BSB', 'For these are the days of vengeance, to fulfill all that is written.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.23', 'BSB', 'How miserable those days will be for pregnant and nursing mothers! For there will be great distress upon the land and wrath against this people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.24', 'BSB', 'They will fall by the edge of the sword and be led captive into all the nations. And Jerusalem will be trodden down by the Gentiles, until the times of the Gentiles are fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.25', 'BSB', 'There will be signs in the sun and moon and stars, and on the earth dismay among the nations, bewildered by the roaring of the sea and the surging of the waves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.26', 'BSB', 'Men will faint from fear and anxiety over what is coming upon the earth, for the powers of the heavens will be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.27', 'BSB', 'At that time they will see the Son of Man coming in a cloud with power and great glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.28', 'BSB', 'When these things begin to happen, stand up and lift up your heads, because your redemption is drawing near.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.29', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told them a parable: “Look at the fig tree and all the trees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.30', 'BSB', 'When they sprout leaves, you can see for yourselves and know that summer is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.31', 'BSB', 'So also, when you see these things happening, know that the kingdom of God is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.32', 'BSB', 'Truly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things have happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.33', 'BSB', 'Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.34', 'BSB', 'But watch yourselves, or your hearts will be weighed down by dissipation, drunkenness, and the worries of life—and that day will spring upon you suddenly like a snare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.35', 'BSB', 'For it will come upon all who dwell on the face of all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.36', 'BSB', 'So keep watch at all times, and pray that you may have the strength to escape all that is about to happen and to stand before the Son of Man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.37', 'BSB', 'Every day Jesus taught at the temple, but every evening He went out to spend the night on the Mount of Olives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.21.38', 'BSB', 'And early in the morning all the people would come to hear Him at the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.1', 'BSB', 'Now the Feast of Unleavened Bread, called the Passover, was approaching,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.2', 'BSB', 'and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a way to put Jesus to death; for they feared the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.3', 'BSB', 'Then Satan entered Judas Iscariot, who was one of the Twelve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.4', 'BSB', 'And Judas went to discuss with the chief priests and temple officers how he might betray Jesus to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.5', 'BSB', 'They were delighted and agreed to give him money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.6', 'BSB', 'Judas consented, and began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus to them in the absence of a crowd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.7', 'BSB', 'Then came the day of Unleavened Bread on which the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.8', 'BSB', 'Jesus sent Peter and John, saying, “Go and prepare for us to eat the Passover.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.9', 'BSB', '“Where do You want us to prepare it?” they asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.10', 'BSB', 'He answered, “When you enter the city, a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him to the house he enters,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.11', 'BSB', 'and say to the owner of that house, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.12', 'BSB', 'And he will show you a large upper room, already furnished. Make preparations there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.13', 'BSB', 'So they went and found it just as Jesus had told them. And they prepared the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.14', 'BSB', 'When the hour had come, Jesus reclined at the table with His apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.15', 'BSB', 'And He said to them, “I have eagerly desired to eat this Passover with you before My suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.16', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that I will not eat it again until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.17', 'BSB', 'After taking the cup, He gave thanks and said, “Take this and divide it among yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.18', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine from now on until the kingdom of God comes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.19', 'BSB', 'And He took the bread, gave thanks and broke it, and gave it to them, saying, “This is My body, given for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.20', 'BSB', 'In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood, which is poured out for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.21', 'BSB', 'Look! The hand of My betrayer is with Mine on the table.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.22', 'BSB', 'Indeed, the Son of Man will go as it has been determined, but woe to that man who betrays Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.23', 'BSB', 'Then they began to question among themselves which of them was going to do this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.24', 'BSB', 'A dispute also arose among the disciples as to which of them would be considered the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.25', 'BSB', 'So Jesus declared, “The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those in authority over them call themselves benefactors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.26', 'BSB', 'But you shall not be like them. Instead, the greatest among you should be like the youngest, and the one who leads like the one who serves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.27', 'BSB', 'For who is greater, the one who reclines at the table or the one who serves? Is it not the one who reclines? But I am among you as one who serves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.28', 'BSB', 'You are the ones who have stood by Me in My trials.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.29', 'BSB', 'And I bestow on you a kingdom, just as My Father has bestowed one on Me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.30', 'BSB', 'so that you may eat and drink at My table in My kingdom, and sit on thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.31', 'BSB', 'Simon, Simon, Satan has asked to sift each of you like wheat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.32', 'BSB', 'But I have prayed for you, Simon, that your faith will not fail. And when you have turned back, strengthen your brothers.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.33', 'BSB', '“Lord,” said Peter, “I am ready to go with You even to prison and to death.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.34', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “I tell you, Peter, the rooster will not crow today until you have denied three times that you know Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.35', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus asked them, “When I sent you out without purse or bag or sandals, did you lack anything?” “Nothing,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.36', 'BSB', '“Now, however,” He told them, “the one with a purse should take it, and likewise a bag; and the one without a sword should sell his cloak and buy one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.37', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that this Scripture must be fulfilled in Me: ‘And He was numbered with the transgressors.’ For what is written about Me is reaching its fulfillment.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.38', 'BSB', 'So they said, “Look, Lord, here are two swords.” “That is enough,” He answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.39', 'BSB', 'Jesus went out as usual to the Mount of Olives, and the disciples followed Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.40', 'BSB', 'When He came to the place, He told them, “Pray that you will not enter into temptation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.41', 'BSB', 'And He withdrew about a stone’s throw beyond them, where He knelt down and prayed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.42', 'BSB', '“Father, if You are willing, take this cup from Me. Yet not My will, but Yours be done.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.43', 'BSB', 'Then an angel from heaven appeared to Him and strengthened Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.44', 'BSB', 'And in His anguish, He prayed more earnestly, and His sweat became like drops of blood falling to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.45', 'BSB', 'When Jesus rose from prayer and returned to the disciples, He found them asleep, exhausted from sorrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.46', 'BSB', '“Why are you sleeping?” He asked. “Get up and pray so that you will not enter into temptation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.47', 'BSB', 'While He was still speaking, a crowd arrived, led by the man called Judas, one of the Twelve. He approached Jesus to kiss Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.48', 'BSB', 'But Jesus asked him, “Judas, are you betraying the Son of Man with a kiss?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.49', 'BSB', 'Those around Jesus saw what was about to happen and said, “Lord, should we strike with our swords?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.50', 'BSB', 'And one of them struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.51', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered, “No more of this!” And He touched the man’s ear and healed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.52', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to the chief priests, temple officers, and elders who had come for Him, “Have you come out with swords and clubs as you would against an outlaw?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.53', 'BSB', 'Every day I was with you in the temple courts, and you did not lay a hand on Me. But this hour belongs to you and to the power of darkness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.54', 'BSB', 'Then they seized Jesus, led Him away, and took Him into the house of the high priest. And Peter followed at a distance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.55', 'BSB', 'When those present had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and sat down together, Peter sat down among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.56', 'BSB', 'A servant girl saw him seated in the firelight and looked intently at him. “This man also was with Him,” she said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.57', 'BSB', 'But Peter denied it. “Woman, I do not know Him,” he said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.58', 'BSB', 'A short time later, someone else saw him and said, “You also are one of them.” But Peter said, “Man, I am not.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.59', 'BSB', 'About an hour later, another man insisted, “Certainly this man was with Him, for he too is a Galilean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.60', 'BSB', '“Man, I do not know what you are talking about,” Peter replied. While he was still speaking, the rooster crowed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.61', 'BSB', 'And the Lord turned and looked at Peter. Then Peter remembered the word that the Lord had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows today, you will deny Me three times.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.62', 'BSB', 'And he went outside and wept bitterly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.63', 'BSB', 'The men who were holding Jesus began to mock Him and beat Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.64', 'BSB', 'They blindfolded Him and kept demanding, “Prophesy! Who hit You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.65', 'BSB', 'And they said many other blasphemous things against Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.66', 'BSB', 'At daybreak the council of the elders of the people, both the chief priests and scribes, met together. They led Jesus into their Sanhedrin and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.67', 'BSB', '“If You are the Christ, tell us.” Jesus answered, “If I tell you, you will not believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.68', 'BSB', 'And if I ask you a question, you will not answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.69', 'BSB', 'But from now on the Son of Man will be seated at the right hand of the power of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.70', 'BSB', 'So they all asked, “Are You then the Son of God?” He replied, “You say that I am.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.22.71', 'BSB', '“Why do we need any more testimony?” they declared. “We have heard it for ourselves from His own lips.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.1', 'BSB', 'Then the whole council rose and led Jesus away to Pilate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.2', 'BSB', 'And they began to accuse Him, saying, “We found this man subverting our nation, forbidding payment of taxes to Caesar, and proclaiming Himself to be Christ, a King.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.3', 'BSB', 'So Pilate asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” “You have said so,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.4', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate said to the chief priests and the crowds, “I find no basis for a charge against this man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.5', 'BSB', 'But they kept insisting, “He stirs up the people all over Judea with His teaching. He began in Galilee and has come all the way here.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.6', 'BSB', 'When Pilate heard this, he asked if the man was a Galilean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.7', 'BSB', 'And learning that Jesus was under Herod’s jurisdiction, he sent Him to Herod, who himself was in Jerusalem at that time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.8', 'BSB', 'When Herod saw Jesus, he was greatly pleased. He had wanted to see Him for a long time, because he had heard about Him and was hoping to see Him perform a miracle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.9', 'BSB', 'Herod questioned Jesus at great length, but He gave no answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.10', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the chief priests and scribes stood there, vehemently accusing Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.11', 'BSB', 'And even Herod and his soldiers ridiculed and mocked Him. Dressing Him in a fine robe, they sent Him back to Pilate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.12', 'BSB', 'That day Herod and Pilate became friends; before this time they had been enemies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.13', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate called together the chief priests, the rulers, and the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.14', 'BSB', 'and said to them, “You brought me this man as one who was inciting the people to rebellion. I have examined Him here in your presence and found Him not guilty of your charges against Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.15', 'BSB', 'Neither has Herod, for he sent Him back to us. As you can see, He has done nothing deserving of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will punish Him and release Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.18', 'BSB', 'But they all cried out in unison: “Away with this man! Release Barabbas to us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.19', 'BSB', '(Barabbas had been imprisoned for an insurrection in the city, and for murder.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.20', 'BSB', 'Wanting to release Jesus, Pilate addressed them again,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.21', 'BSB', 'but they kept shouting, “Crucify Him! Crucify Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.22', 'BSB', 'A third time he said to them, “What evil has this man done? I have found in Him no offense worthy of death. So after I punish Him, I will release Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.23', 'BSB', 'But they were insistent, demanding with loud voices for Jesus to be crucified. And their clamor prevailed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.24', 'BSB', 'So Pilate sentenced that their demand be met.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.25', 'BSB', 'As they had requested, he released the one imprisoned for insurrection and murder, and handed Jesus over to their will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.26', 'BSB', 'As the soldiers led Him away, they seized Simon of Cyrene on his way in from the country, and put the cross on him to carry behind Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.27', 'BSB', 'A great number of people followed Him, including women who kept mourning and wailing for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.28', 'BSB', 'But Jesus turned to them and said, “Daughters of Jerusalem, do not weep for Me, but weep for yourselves and for your children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.29', 'BSB', 'Look, the days are coming when people will say, ‘Blessed are the barren women, the wombs that never bore, and breasts that never nursed!’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.30', 'BSB', 'At that time ‘they will say to the mountains, “Fall on us!” and to the hills, “Cover us!”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.31', 'BSB', 'For if men do these things while the tree is green, what will happen when it is dry?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.32', 'BSB', 'Two others, who were criminals, were also led away to be executed with Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.33', 'BSB', 'When they came to the place called The Skull, they crucified Him there, along with the criminals, one on His right and the other on His left.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.34', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said, “Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing.” And they divided up His garments by casting lots.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.35', 'BSB', 'The people stood watching, and the rulers sneered at Him, saying, “He saved others; let Him save Himself if He is the Christ of God, the Chosen One.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.36', 'BSB', 'The soldiers also mocked Him and came up to offer Him sour wine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.37', 'BSB', '“If You are the King of the Jews,” they said, “save Yourself!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.38', 'BSB', 'Above Him was posted an inscription: THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.39', 'BSB', 'One of the criminals who hung there heaped abuse on Him. “Are You not the Christ?” he said. “Save Yourself and us!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.40', 'BSB', 'But the other one rebuked him, saying, “Do you not even fear God, since you are under the same judgment?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.41', 'BSB', 'We are punished justly, for we are receiving what our actions deserve. But this man has done nothing wrong.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.42', 'BSB', 'Then he said, “Jesus, remember me when You come into Your kingdom!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.43', 'BSB', 'And Jesus said to him, “Truly I tell you, today you will be with Me in Paradise.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.44', 'BSB', 'It was now about the sixth hour, and darkness came over all the land until the ninth hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.45', 'BSB', 'The sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was torn down the middle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.46', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus called out in a loud voice, “Father, into Your hands I commit My Spirit.” And when He had said this, He breathed His last.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.47', 'BSB', 'When the centurion saw what had happened, he gave glory to God, saying, “Surely this was a righteous man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.48', 'BSB', 'And when all the people who had gathered for this spectacle saw what had happened, they returned home beating their breasts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.49', 'BSB', 'But all those who knew Jesus, including the women who had followed Him from Galilee, stood at a distance watching these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.50', 'BSB', 'Now there was a Council member named Joseph, a good and righteous man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.51', 'BSB', 'who had not consented to their decision or action. He was from the Judean town of Arimathea, and was waiting for the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.52', 'BSB', 'He went to Pilate to ask for the body of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.53', 'BSB', 'Then he took it down, wrapped it in a linen cloth, and placed it in a tomb cut into the rock, where no one had yet been laid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.54', 'BSB', 'It was Preparation Day, and the Sabbath was beginning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.55', 'BSB', 'The women who had come with Jesus from Galilee followed, and they saw the tomb and how His body was placed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.23.56', 'BSB', 'Then they returned to prepare spices and perfumes. And they rested on the Sabbath, according to the commandment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.1', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the week, very early in the morning, the women came to the tomb, bringing the spices they had prepared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.2', 'BSB', 'They found the stone rolled away from the tomb,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.3', 'BSB', 'but when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.4', 'BSB', 'While they were puzzling over this, suddenly two men in radiant apparel stood beside them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.5', 'BSB', 'As the women bowed their faces to the ground in terror, the two men asked them, “Why do you look for the living among the dead?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.6', 'BSB', 'He is not here; He has risen! Remember how He told you while He was still in Galilee:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.7', 'BSB', '‘The Son of Man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and on the third day rise again.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.8', 'BSB', 'Then they remembered His words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.9', 'BSB', 'And when they returned from the tomb, they reported all these things to the Eleven and to all the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.10', 'BSB', 'It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the mother of James, and the other women with them who told this to the apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.11', 'BSB', 'But their words seemed like nonsense to them, and they did not believe the women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.12', 'BSB', 'Peter, however, got up and ran to the tomb. And after bending down and seeing only the linen cloths, he went away, wondering to himself what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.13', 'BSB', 'That same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles from Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.14', 'BSB', 'They were talking with each other about everything that had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.15', 'BSB', 'And as they talked and deliberated, Jesus Himself came up and walked along with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.16', 'BSB', 'But their eyes were kept from recognizing Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.17', 'BSB', 'He asked them, “What are you discussing so intently as you walk along?” They stood still, with sadness on their faces.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.18', 'BSB', 'One of them, named Cleopas, asked Him, “Are You the only visitor to Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in recent days?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.19', 'BSB', '“What things?” He asked. “The events involving Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. “This man was a prophet, powerful in speech and action before God and all the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.20', 'BSB', 'Our chief priests and rulers delivered Him up to the sentence of death, and they crucified Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.21', 'BSB', 'But we were hoping He was the One who would redeem Israel. And besides all this, it is the third day since these things took place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.22', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, some of our women astounded us. They were at the tomb early this morning,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.23', 'BSB', 'but they did not find His body. They came and told us they had seen a vision of angels, who said that Jesus was alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.24', 'BSB', 'Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had described. But Him they did not see.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.25', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to them, “O foolish ones, how slow are your hearts to believe all that the prophets have spoken!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.26', 'BSB', 'Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things and then to enter His glory?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.27', 'BSB', 'And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what was written in all the Scriptures about Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.28', 'BSB', 'As they approached the village where they were headed, He seemed to be going farther.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.29', 'BSB', 'But they pleaded with Him, “Stay with us, for it is nearly evening and the day is almost over.” So He went in to stay with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.30', 'BSB', 'While He was reclining at the table with them, He took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.31', 'BSB', 'Then their eyes were opened and they recognized Jesus—and He disappeared from their sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.32', 'BSB', 'They asked each other, “Were not our hearts burning within us as He spoke with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.33', 'BSB', 'And they got up that very hour and returned to Jerusalem. There they found the Eleven and those with them, gathered together', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.34', 'BSB', 'and saying, “The Lord has indeed risen and has appeared to Simon!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.35', 'BSB', 'Then the two told what had happened on the road, and how they had recognized Jesus in the breaking of the bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.36', 'BSB', 'While they were describing these events, Jesus Himself stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.37', 'BSB', 'But they were startled and frightened, thinking they had seen a spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.38', 'BSB', '“Why are you troubled,” Jesus asked, “and why do doubts arise in your hearts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.39', 'BSB', 'Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself. Touch Me and see—for a spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.40', 'BSB', 'And when He had said this, He showed them His hands and feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.41', 'BSB', 'While they were still in disbelief because of their joy and amazement, He asked them, “Do you have anything here to eat?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.42', 'BSB', 'So they gave Him a piece of broiled fish,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.43', 'BSB', 'and He took it and ate it in front of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.44', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “These are the words I spoke to you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that is written about Me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and the Psalms.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.45', 'BSB', 'Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.46', 'BSB', 'And He told them, “This is what is written: The Christ will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.47', 'BSB', 'and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.48', 'BSB', 'You are witnesses of these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.49', 'BSB', 'And behold, I am sending the promise of My Father upon you. But remain in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.50', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had led them out as far as Bethany, He lifted up His hands and blessed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.51', 'BSB', 'While He was blessing them, He left them and was carried up into heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.52', 'BSB', 'And they worshiped Him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Luke.24.53', 'BSB', 'praising God continually in the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.1', 'BSB', 'In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.2', 'BSB', 'He was with God in the beginning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.3', 'BSB', 'Through Him all things were made, and without Him nothing was made that has been made.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.4', 'BSB', 'In Him was life, and that life was the light of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.5', 'BSB', 'The Light shines in the darkness, and the darkness has not overcome it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.6', 'BSB', 'There came a man who was sent from God. His name was John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.7', 'BSB', 'He came as a witness to testify about the Light, so that through him everyone might believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.8', 'BSB', 'He himself was not the Light, but he came to testify about the Light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.9', 'BSB', 'The true Light who gives light to every man was coming into the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.10', 'BSB', 'He was in the world, and though the world was made through Him, the world did not recognize Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.11', 'BSB', 'He came to His own, and His own did not receive Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.12', 'BSB', 'But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.13', 'BSB', 'children born not of blood, nor of the desire or will of man, but born of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.14', 'BSB', 'The Word became flesh and made His dwelling among us. We have seen His glory, the glory of the one and only Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.15', 'BSB', 'John testified concerning Him. He cried out, saying, “This is He of whom I said, ‘He who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.16', 'BSB', 'From His fullness we have all received grace upon grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.17', 'BSB', 'For the law was given through Moses; grace and truth came through Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.18', 'BSB', 'No one has ever seen God, but the one and only Son, who is Himself God and is at the Father’s side, has made Him known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.19', 'BSB', 'And this was John’s testimony when the Jews of Jerusalem sent priests and Levites to ask him, “Who are you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.20', 'BSB', 'He did not refuse to confess, but openly declared, “I am not the Christ.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.21', 'BSB', '“Then who are you?” they inquired. “Are you Elijah?” He said, “I am not.” “Are you the Prophet?” He answered, “No.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.22', 'BSB', 'So they said to him, “Who are you? We need an answer for those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.23', 'BSB', 'John replied in the words of Isaiah the prophet: “I am a voice of one calling in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way for the Lord.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.24', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees who had been sent', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.25', 'BSB', 'asked him, “Why then do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.26', 'BSB', '“I baptize with water,” John replied, “but among you stands One you do not know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.27', 'BSB', 'He is the One who comes after me, the straps of whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.28', 'BSB', 'All this happened at Bethany beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.29', 'BSB', 'The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him and said, “Look, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.30', 'BSB', 'This is He of whom I said, ‘A man who comes after me has surpassed me because He was before me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.31', 'BSB', 'I myself did not know Him, but the reason I came baptizing with water was that He might be revealed to Israel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.32', 'BSB', 'Then John testified, “I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove and resting on Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.33', 'BSB', 'I myself did not know Him, but the One who sent me to baptize with water told me, ‘The man on whom you see the Spirit descend and rest is He who will baptize with the Holy Spirit.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.34', 'BSB', 'I have seen and testified that this is the Son of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.35', 'BSB', 'The next day John was there again with two of his disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.36', 'BSB', 'When he saw Jesus walking by, he said, “Look, the Lamb of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.37', 'BSB', 'And when the two disciples heard him say this, they followed Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.38', 'BSB', 'Jesus turned and saw them following. “What do you want?” He asked. They said to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.39', 'BSB', '“Come and see,” He replied. So they went and saw where He was staying, and spent that day with Him. It was about the tenth hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.40', 'BSB', 'Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, was one of the two who heard John’s testimony and followed Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.41', 'BSB', 'He first found his brother Simon and told him, “We have found the Messiah” (which is translated as Christ).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.42', 'BSB', 'Andrew brought him to Jesus, who looked at him and said, “You are Simon son of John. You will be called Cephas” (which is translated as Peter).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.43', 'BSB', 'The next day Jesus decided to set out for Galilee. Finding Philip, He told him, “Follow Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.44', 'BSB', 'Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the same town as Andrew and Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.45', 'BSB', 'Philip found Nathanael and told him, “We have found the One Moses wrote about in the Law, the One the prophets foretold—Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.46', 'BSB', '“Can anything good come from Nazareth?” Nathanael asked. “Come and see,” said Philip.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.47', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw Nathanael approaching, He said of him, “Here is a true Israelite, in whom there is no deceit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.48', 'BSB', '“How do You know me?” Nathanael asked. Jesus replied, “Before Philip called you, I saw you under the fig tree.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.49', 'BSB', '“Rabbi,” Nathanael answered, “You are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.50', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to him, “Do you believe just because I told you I saw you under the fig tree? You will see greater things than these.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.1.51', 'BSB', 'Then He declared, “Truly, truly, I tell you, you will all see heaven open and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.1', 'BSB', 'On the third day a wedding took place at Cana in Galilee. Jesus’ mother was there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.2', 'BSB', 'and Jesus and His disciples had also been invited to the wedding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.3', 'BSB', 'When the wine ran out, Jesus’ mother said to Him, “They have no more wine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.4', 'BSB', '“Woman, why does this concern us?” Jesus replied. “My hour has not yet come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.5', 'BSB', 'His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever He tells you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.6', 'BSB', 'Now six stone water jars had been set there for the Jewish rites of purification. Each could hold from twenty to thirty gallons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.7', 'BSB', 'Jesus told the servants, “Fill the jars with water.” So they filled them to the brim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.8', 'BSB', '“Now draw some out,” He said, “and take it to the master of the banquet.” They did so,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.9', 'BSB', 'and the master of the banquet tasted the water that had been turned into wine. He did not know where it was from, but the servants who had drawn the water knew. Then he called the bridegroom aside', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.10', 'BSB', 'and said, “Everyone serves the fine wine first, and then the cheap wine after the guests are drunk. But you have saved the fine wine until now!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.11', 'BSB', 'Jesus performed this, the first of His signs, at Cana in Galilee. He thus revealed His glory, and His disciples believed in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.12', 'BSB', 'After this, He went down to Capernaum with His mother and brothers and His disciples, and they stayed there a few days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.13', 'BSB', 'When the Jewish Passover was near, Jesus went up to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.14', 'BSB', 'In the temple courts He found men selling cattle, sheep, and doves, and money changers seated at their tables.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.15', 'BSB', 'So He made a whip out of cords and drove all from the temple courts, both sheep and cattle. He poured out the coins of the money changers and overturned their tables.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.16', 'BSB', 'To those selling doves He said, “Get these out of here! How dare you turn My Father’s house into a marketplace!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.17', 'BSB', 'His disciples remembered that it is written: “Zeal for Your house will consume Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.18', 'BSB', 'On account of this, the Jews demanded, “What sign can You show us to prove Your authority to do these things?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.19', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.20', 'BSB', '“This temple took forty-six years to build,” the Jews replied, “and You are going to raise it up in three days?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.21', 'BSB', 'But Jesus was speaking about the temple of His body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.22', 'BSB', 'After He was raised from the dead, His disciples remembered that He had said this. Then they believed the Scripture and the word that Jesus had spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.23', 'BSB', 'While He was in Jerusalem at the Passover Feast, many people saw the signs He was doing and believed in His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.24', 'BSB', 'But Jesus did not entrust Himself to them, for He knew them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.2.25', 'BSB', 'He did not need any testimony about man, for He knew what was in a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.1', 'BSB', 'Now there was a man of the Pharisees named Nicodemus, a leader of the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.2', 'BSB', 'He came to Jesus at night and said, “Rabbi, we know that You are a teacher who has come from God. For no one could perform the signs You are doing if God were not with him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can see the kingdom of God unless he is born again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.4', 'BSB', '“How can a man be born when he is old?” Nicodemus asked. “Can he enter his mother’s womb a second time to be born?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.5', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “Truly, truly, I tell you, no one can enter the kingdom of God unless he is born of water and the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.6', 'BSB', 'Flesh is born of flesh, but spirit is born of the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.7', 'BSB', 'Do not be amazed that I said, ‘You must be born again.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.8', 'BSB', 'The wind blows where it wishes. You hear its sound, but you do not know where it comes from or where it is going. So it is with everyone born of the Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.9', 'BSB', '“How can this be?” Nicodemus asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.10', 'BSB', '“You are Israel’s teacher,” said Jesus, “and you do not understand these things?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.11', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, we speak of what we know, and we testify to what we have seen, and yet you people do not accept our testimony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.12', 'BSB', 'If I have told you about earthly things and you do not believe, how will you believe if I tell you about heavenly things?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.13', 'BSB', 'No one has ascended into heaven except the One who descended from heaven—the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.14', 'BSB', 'Just as Moses lifted up the snake in the wilderness, so the Son of Man must be lifted up,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.15', 'BSB', 'that everyone who believes in Him may have eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.16', 'BSB', 'For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.17', 'BSB', 'For God did not send His Son into the world to condemn the world, but to save the world through Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.18', 'BSB', 'Whoever believes in Him is not condemned, but whoever does not believe has already been condemned, because he has not believed in the name of God’s one and only Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.19', 'BSB', 'And this is the verdict: The Light has come into the world, but men loved the darkness rather than the Light because their deeds were evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.20', 'BSB', 'Everyone who does evil hates the Light, and does not come into the Light for fear that his deeds will be exposed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.21', 'BSB', 'But whoever practices the truth comes into the Light, so that it may be seen clearly that what he has done has been accomplished in God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.22', 'BSB', 'After this, Jesus and His disciples went into the Judean countryside, where He spent some time with them and baptized.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.23', 'BSB', 'Now John was also baptizing at Aenon near Salim, because the water was plentiful there, and people kept coming to be baptized.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.24', 'BSB', '(For John had not yet been thrown into prison.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.25', 'BSB', 'Then a dispute arose between John’s disciples and a certain Jew over the issue of ceremonial washing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.26', 'BSB', 'So John’s disciples came to him and said, “Look, Rabbi, the One who was with you beyond the Jordan, the One you testified about—He is baptizing, and everyone is going to Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.27', 'BSB', 'John replied, “A man can receive only what is given him from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.28', 'BSB', 'You yourselves can testify that I said, ‘I am not the Christ, but am sent ahead of Him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.29', 'BSB', 'The bride belongs to the bridegroom. The friend of the bridegroom stands and listens for him, and is overjoyed to hear the bridegroom’s voice. That joy is mine, and it is now complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.30', 'BSB', 'He must increase; I must decrease.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.31', 'BSB', 'The One who comes from above is above all. The one who is from the earth belongs to the earth and speaks as one from the earth. The One who comes from heaven is above all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.32', 'BSB', 'He testifies to what He has seen and heard, yet no one accepts His testimony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.33', 'BSB', 'Whoever accepts His testimony has certified that God is truthful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.34', 'BSB', 'For the One whom God has sent speaks the words of God, for God gives the Spirit without limit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.35', 'BSB', 'The Father loves the Son and has placed all things in His hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.3.36', 'BSB', 'Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. Whoever rejects the Son will not see life. Instead, the wrath of God remains on him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus realized that the Pharisees were aware He was gaining and baptizing more disciples than John', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.2', 'BSB', '(although it was not Jesus who baptized, but His disciples),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.3', 'BSB', 'He left Judea and returned to Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.4', 'BSB', 'Now He had to pass through Samaria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.5', 'BSB', 'So He came to a town of Samaria called Sychar, near the plot of ground that Jacob had given to his son Joseph.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.6', 'BSB', 'Since Jacob’s well was there, Jesus, weary from His journey, sat down by the well. It was about the sixth hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.7', 'BSB', 'When a Samaritan woman came to draw water, Jesus said to her, “Give Me a drink.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.8', 'BSB', '(His disciples had gone into the town to buy food.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.9', 'BSB', '“You are a Jew,” said the woman. “How can You ask for a drink from me, a Samaritan woman?” (For Jews do not associate with Samaritans.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.10', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “If you knew the gift of God and who is asking you for a drink, you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.11', 'BSB', '“Sir,” the woman replied, “You have nothing to draw with and the well is deep. Where then will You get this living water?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.12', 'BSB', 'Are You greater than our father Jacob, who gave us this well and drank from it himself, as did his sons and his livestock?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.13', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to her, “Everyone who drinks this water will be thirsty again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.14', 'BSB', 'But whoever drinks the water I give him will never thirst. Indeed, the water I give him will become in him a fount of water springing up to eternal life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.15', 'BSB', 'The woman said to Him, “Sir, give me this water so that I will not get thirsty and have to keep coming here to draw water.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.16', 'BSB', 'Jesus told her, “Go, call your husband and come back.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.17', 'BSB', '“I have no husband,” the woman replied. Jesus said to her, “You are correct to say that you have no husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.18', 'BSB', 'In fact, you have had five husbands, and the man you now have is not your husband. You have spoken truthfully.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.19', 'BSB', '“Sir,” the woman said, “I see that You are a prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.20', 'BSB', 'Our fathers worshiped on this mountain, but you Jews say that the place where one must worship is in Jerusalem.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.21', 'BSB', '“Believe Me, woman,” Jesus replied, “a time is coming when you will worship the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.22', 'BSB', 'You worship what you do not know; we worship what we do know, for salvation is from the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.23', 'BSB', 'But a time is coming and has now come when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and in truth, for the Father is seeking such as these to worship Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.24', 'BSB', 'God is Spirit, and His worshipers must worship Him in spirit and in truth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.25', 'BSB', 'The woman said, “I know that Messiah” (called Christ) “is coming. When He comes, He will explain everything to us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “I who speak to you am He.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.27', 'BSB', 'Just then His disciples returned and were surprised that He was speaking with a woman. But no one asked Him, “What do You want from her?” or “Why are You talking with her?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.28', 'BSB', 'Then the woman left her water jar, went back into the town, and said to the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.29', 'BSB', '“Come, see a man who told me everything I ever did. Could this be the Christ?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.30', 'BSB', 'So they left the town and made their way toward Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.31', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile the disciples urged Him, “Rabbi, eat something.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.32', 'BSB', 'But He told them, “I have food to eat that you know nothing about.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.33', 'BSB', 'So the disciples asked one another, “Could someone have brought Him food?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus explained, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me and to finish His work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.35', 'BSB', 'Do you not say, ‘There are still four months until the harvest’? I tell you, lift up your eyes and look at the fields, for they are ripe for harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.36', 'BSB', 'Already the reaper draws his wages and gathers a crop for eternal life, so that the sower and the reaper may rejoice together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.37', 'BSB', 'For in this case the saying ‘One sows and another reaps’ is true.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.38', 'BSB', 'I sent you to reap what you have not worked for; others have done the hard work, and now you have taken up their labor.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.39', 'BSB', 'Many of the Samaritans from that town believed in Jesus because of the woman’s testimony, “He told me everything I ever did.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.40', 'BSB', 'So when the Samaritans came to Him, they asked Him to stay with them, and He stayed two days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.41', 'BSB', 'And many more believed because of His message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.42', 'BSB', 'They said to the woman, “We now believe not only because of your words; we have heard for ourselves, and we know that this man truly is the Savior of the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.43', 'BSB', 'After two days, Jesus left for Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.44', 'BSB', 'Now He Himself had testified that a prophet has no honor in his own hometown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.45', 'BSB', 'Yet when He arrived, the Galileans welcomed Him. They had seen all the great things He had done in Jerusalem at the feast, for they had gone there as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.46', 'BSB', 'So once again He came to Cana in Galilee, where He had turned the water into wine. And there was a royal official whose son lay sick at Capernaum.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.47', 'BSB', 'When he heard that Jesus had come from Judea to Galilee, he went and begged Him to come down and heal his son, who was about to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.48', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to him, “Unless you people see signs and wonders, you will never believe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.49', 'BSB', '“Sir,” the official said, “come down before my child dies.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.50', 'BSB', '“Go,” said Jesus. “Your son will live.” The man took Jesus at His word and departed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.51', 'BSB', 'And while he was still on the way, his servants met him with the news that his boy was alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.52', 'BSB', 'So he inquired as to the hour when his son had recovered, and they told him, “The fever left him yesterday at the seventh hour.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.53', 'BSB', 'Then the father realized that this was the very hour in which Jesus had told him, “Your son will live.” And he and all his household believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.4.54', 'BSB', 'This was now the second sign that Jesus performed after coming from Judea into Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.1', 'BSB', 'Some time later there was a feast of the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.2', 'BSB', 'Now there is in Jerusalem near the Sheep Gate a pool with five covered colonnades, which in Hebrew is called Bethesda.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.3', 'BSB', 'On these walkways lay a great number of the sick, the blind, the lame, and the paralyzed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.5', 'BSB', 'One man there had been an invalid for thirty-eight years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.6', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw him lying there and realized that he had spent a long time in this condition, He asked him, “Do you want to get well?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.7', 'BSB', '“Sir,” the invalid replied, “I have no one to help me into the pool when the water is stirred. While I am on my way, someone else goes in before me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.8', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told him, “Get up, pick up your mat, and walk.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.9', 'BSB', 'Immediately the man was made well, and he picked up his mat and began to walk. Now this happened on the Sabbath day,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.10', 'BSB', 'so the Jews said to the man who had been healed, “This is the Sabbath! It is unlawful for you to carry your mat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.11', 'BSB', 'But he answered, “The man who made me well told me, ‘Pick up your mat and walk.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.12', 'BSB', '“Who is this man who told you to pick it up and walk?” they asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.13', 'BSB', 'But the man who was healed did not know who it was, for Jesus had slipped away while the crowd was there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.14', 'BSB', 'Afterward, Jesus found the man at the temple and said to him, “See, you have been made well. Stop sinning, or something worse may happen to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.15', 'BSB', 'And the man went away and told the Jews that it was Jesus who had made him well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.16', 'BSB', 'Now because Jesus was doing these things on the Sabbath, the Jews began to persecute Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.17', 'BSB', 'But Jesus answered them, “To this very day My Father is at His work, and I too am working.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.18', 'BSB', 'Because of this, the Jews tried all the harder to kill Him. Not only was He breaking the Sabbath, but He was even calling God His own Father, making Himself equal with God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.19', 'BSB', 'So Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, the Son can do nothing by Himself, unless He sees the Father doing it. For whatever the Father does, the Son also does.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.20', 'BSB', 'The Father loves the Son and shows Him all He does. And to your amazement, He will show Him even greater works than these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.21', 'BSB', 'For just as the Father raises the dead and gives them life, so also the Son gives life to whom He wishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.22', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, the Father judges no one, but has assigned all judgment to the Son,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.23', 'BSB', 'so that all may honor the Son just as they honor the Father. Whoever does not honor the Son does not honor the Father who sent Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.24', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever hears My word and believes Him who sent Me has eternal life and will not come under judgment. Indeed, he has crossed over from death to life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.25', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, the hour is coming and has now come when the dead will hear the voice of the Son of God, and those who hear will live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.26', 'BSB', 'For as the Father has life in Himself, so also He has granted the Son to have life in Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.27', 'BSB', 'And He has given Him authority to execute judgment, because He is the Son of Man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.28', 'BSB', 'Do not be amazed at this, for the hour is coming when all who are in their graves will hear His voice', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.29', 'BSB', 'and come out—those who have done good to the resurrection of life, and those who have done evil to the resurrection of judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.30', 'BSB', 'I can do nothing by Myself; I judge only as I hear. And My judgment is just, because I do not seek My own will, but the will of Him who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.31', 'BSB', 'If I testify about Myself, My testimony is not valid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.32', 'BSB', 'There is another who testifies about Me, and I know that His testimony about Me is valid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.33', 'BSB', 'You have sent to John, and he has testified to the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.34', 'BSB', 'Even though I do not accept human testimony, I say these things so that you may be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.35', 'BSB', 'John was a lamp that burned and gave light, and you were willing for a season to bask in his light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.36', 'BSB', 'But I have testimony more substantial than that of John. For the works that the Father has given Me to accomplish—the very works I am doing—testify about Me that the Father has sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.37', 'BSB', 'And the Father who sent Me has Himself testified about Me. You have never heard His voice nor seen His form,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.38', 'BSB', 'nor does His word abide in you, because you do not believe the One He sent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.39', 'BSB', 'You pore over the Scriptures because you presume that by them you possess eternal life. These are the very words that testify about Me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.40', 'BSB', 'yet you refuse to come to Me to have life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.41', 'BSB', 'I do not accept glory from men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.42', 'BSB', 'but I know you, that you do not have the love of God within you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.43', 'BSB', 'I have come in My Father’s name, and you have not received Me; but if someone else comes in his own name, you will receive him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.44', 'BSB', 'How can you believe if you accept glory from one another, yet do not seek the glory that comes from the only God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.45', 'BSB', 'Do not think that I will accuse you before the Father. Your accuser is Moses, in whom you have put your hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.46', 'BSB', 'If you had believed Moses, you would believe Me, because he wrote about Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.5.47', 'BSB', 'But since you do not believe what he wrote, how will you believe what I say?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.1', 'BSB', 'After this, Jesus crossed to the other side of the Sea of Galilee (that is, the Sea of Tiberias).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.2', 'BSB', 'A large crowd followed Him because they saw the signs He was performing on the sick.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.3', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus went up on the mountain and sat down with His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.4', 'BSB', 'Now the Jewish Feast of the Passover was near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.5', 'BSB', 'When Jesus looked up and saw a large crowd coming toward Him, He said to Philip, “Where can we buy bread for these people to eat?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.6', 'BSB', 'But He was asking this to test him, for He knew what He was about to do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.7', 'BSB', 'Philip answered, “Two hundred denarii would not buy enough bread for each of them to have a small piece.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.8', 'BSB', 'One of His disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother, said to Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.9', 'BSB', '“Here is a boy with five barley loaves and two small fish. But what difference will these make among so many?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.10', 'BSB', '“Have the people sit down,” Jesus said. Now there was plenty of grass in that place, so the men sat down, about five thousand of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.11', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus took the loaves and the fish, gave thanks, and distributed to those who were seated as much as they wanted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.12', 'BSB', 'And when everyone was full, He said to His disciples, “Gather the pieces that are left over, so that nothing will be wasted.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.13', 'BSB', 'So they collected them and filled twelve baskets with the pieces of the five barley loaves left over by those who had eaten.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.14', 'BSB', 'When the people saw the sign that Jesus had performed, they began to say, “Truly this is the Prophet who is to come into the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.15', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus, realizing that they were about to come and make Him king by force, withdrew again to a mountain by Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.16', 'BSB', 'When evening came, His disciples went down to the sea,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.17', 'BSB', 'got into a boat, and started across the sea to Capernaum. It was already dark, and Jesus had not yet gone out to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.18', 'BSB', 'A strong wind was blowing, and the sea grew agitated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.19', 'BSB', 'When they had rowed about three or four miles, they saw Jesus approaching the boat, walking on the sea—and they were terrified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.20', 'BSB', 'But Jesus spoke up: “It is I; do not be afraid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.21', 'BSB', 'Then they were willing to take Him into the boat, and at once the boat reached the shore where they were heading.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.22', 'BSB', 'The next day, the crowd that had remained on the other side of the sea realized that only one boat had been there, and that Jesus had not boarded it with His disciples, but they had gone away alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.23', 'BSB', 'However, some boats from Tiberias landed near the place where the people had eaten the bread after the Lord had given thanks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.24', 'BSB', 'So when the crowd saw that neither Jesus nor His disciples were there, they got into the boats and went to Capernaum to look for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.25', 'BSB', 'When they found Him on the other side of the sea, they asked Him, “Rabbi, when did You get here?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it is not because you saw these signs that you are looking for Me, but because you ate the loaves and had your fill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.27', 'BSB', 'Do not work for food that perishes, but for food that endures to eternal life, which the Son of Man will give you. For on Him God the Father has placed His seal of approval.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.28', 'BSB', 'Then they inquired, “What must we do to perform the works of God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.29', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “The work of God is this: to believe in the One He has sent.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.30', 'BSB', 'So they asked Him, “What sign then will You perform, so that we may see it and believe You? What will You do?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.31', 'BSB', 'Our fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, as it is written: ‘He gave them bread from heaven to eat.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.32', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, it was not Moses who gave you the bread from heaven, but it is My Father who gives you the true bread from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.33', 'BSB', 'For the bread of God is He who comes down from heaven and gives life to the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.34', 'BSB', '“Sir,” they said, “give us this bread at all times.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.35', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to Me will never hunger, and whoever believes in Me will never thirst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.36', 'BSB', 'But as I stated, you have seen Me and still you do not believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.37', 'BSB', 'Everyone the Father gives Me will come to Me, and the one who comes to Me I will never drive away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.38', 'BSB', 'For I have come down from heaven, not to do My own will, but to do the will of Him who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.39', 'BSB', 'And this is the will of Him who sent Me, that I shall lose none of those He has given Me, but raise them up at the last day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.40', 'BSB', 'For it is My Father’s will that everyone who looks to the Son and believes in Him shall have eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.41', 'BSB', 'At this, the Jews began to grumble about Jesus because He had said, “I am the bread that came down from heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.42', 'BSB', 'They were asking, “Is this not Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then can He say, ‘I have come down from heaven?’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.43', 'BSB', '“Stop grumbling among yourselves,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.44', 'BSB', '“No one can come to Me unless the Father who sent Me draws him, and I will raise him up at the last day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.45', 'BSB', 'It is written in the Prophets: ‘And they will all be taught by God.’ Everyone who has heard the Father and learned from Him comes to Me—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.46', 'BSB', 'not that anyone has seen the Father except the One who is from God; only He has seen the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.47', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, he who believes has eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.48', 'BSB', 'I am the bread of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.49', 'BSB', 'Your fathers ate the manna in the wilderness, yet they died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.50', 'BSB', 'This is the bread that comes down from heaven, so that anyone may eat of it and not die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.51', 'BSB', 'I am the living bread that came down from heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever. And this bread, which I will give for the life of the world, is My flesh.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.52', 'BSB', 'At this, the Jews began to argue among themselves, “How can this man give us His flesh to eat?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.53', 'BSB', 'So Jesus said to them, “Truly, truly, I tell you, unless you eat the flesh and drink the blood of the Son of Man, you have no life in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.54', 'BSB', 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood has eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.55', 'BSB', 'For My flesh is real food, and My blood is real drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.56', 'BSB', 'Whoever eats My flesh and drinks My blood remains in Me, and I in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.57', 'BSB', 'Just as the living Father sent Me and I live because of the Father, so also the one who feeds on Me will live because of Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.58', 'BSB', 'This is the bread that came down from heaven. Unlike your fathers, who ate the manna and died, the one who eats this bread will live forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.59', 'BSB', 'Jesus said this while teaching in the synagogue in Capernaum.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.60', 'BSB', 'On hearing it, many of His disciples said, “This is a difficult teaching. Who can accept it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.61', 'BSB', 'Aware that His disciples were grumbling about this teaching, Jesus asked them, “Does this offend you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.62', 'BSB', 'Then what will happen if you see the Son of Man ascend to where He was before?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.63', 'BSB', 'The Spirit gives life; the flesh profits nothing. The words I have spoken to you are spirit and they are life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.64', 'BSB', 'However, there are some of you who do not believe.” (For Jesus had known from the beginning which of them did not believe and who would betray Him.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.65', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said, “This is why I told you that no one can come to Me unless the Father has granted it to him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.66', 'BSB', 'From that time on many of His disciples turned back and no longer walked with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.67', 'BSB', 'So Jesus asked the Twelve, “Do you want to leave too?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.68', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter replied, “Lord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.69', 'BSB', 'We believe and know that You are the Holy One of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.70', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered them, “Have I not chosen you, the Twelve? Yet one of you is a devil!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.6.71', 'BSB', 'He was speaking about Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot. For although Judas was one of the Twelve, he was later to betray Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.1', 'BSB', 'After this, Jesus traveled throughout Galilee. He did not want to travel in Judea, because the Jews there were trying to kill Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.2', 'BSB', 'However, the Jewish Feast of Tabernacles was near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.3', 'BSB', 'So Jesus’ brothers said to Him, “Leave here and go to Judea, so that Your disciples there may see the works You are doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.4', 'BSB', 'For no one who wants to be known publicly acts in secret. Since You are doing these things, show Yourself to the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.5', 'BSB', 'For even His own brothers did not believe in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore Jesus told them, “Although your time is always at hand, My time has not yet come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.7', 'BSB', 'The world cannot hate you, but it hates Me, because I testify that its works are evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.8', 'BSB', 'Go up to the feast on your own. I am not going up to this feast, because My time has not yet come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.9', 'BSB', 'Having said this, Jesus remained in Galilee.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.10', 'BSB', 'But after His brothers had gone up to the feast, He also went—not publicly, but in secret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.11', 'BSB', 'So the Jews were looking for Him at the feast and asking, “Where is He?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.12', 'BSB', 'Many in the crowds were whispering about Him. Some said, “He is a good man.” But others replied, “No, He deceives the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.13', 'BSB', 'Yet no one would speak publicly about Him for fear of the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.14', 'BSB', 'About halfway through the feast, Jesus went up to the temple courts and began to teach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.15', 'BSB', 'The Jews were amazed and asked, “How did this man attain such learning without having studied?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.16', 'BSB', '“My teaching is not My own,” Jesus replied. “It comes from Him who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.17', 'BSB', 'If anyone desires to do His will, he will know whether My teaching is from God or whether I speak on My own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.18', 'BSB', 'He who speaks on his own authority seeks his own glory, but He who seeks the glory of the One who sent Him is a man of truth; in Him there is no falsehood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.19', 'BSB', 'Has not Moses given you the law? Yet not one of you keeps it. Why are you trying to kill Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.20', 'BSB', '“You have a demon,” the crowd replied. “Who is trying to kill You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.21', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered them, “I did one miracle, and you are all amazed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.22', 'BSB', 'But because Moses gave you circumcision, you circumcise a boy on the Sabbath (not that it is from Moses, but from the patriarchs.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.23', 'BSB', 'If a boy can be circumcised on the Sabbath so that the law of Moses will not be broken, why are you angry with Me for making the whole man well on the Sabbath?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.24', 'BSB', 'Stop judging by outward appearances, and start judging justly.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.25', 'BSB', 'Then some of the people of Jerusalem began to say, “Isn’t this the man they are trying to kill?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.26', 'BSB', 'Yet here He is, speaking publicly, and they are not saying anything to Him. Have the rulers truly recognized that this is the Christ?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.27', 'BSB', 'But we know where this man is from. When the Christ comes, no one will know where He is from.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.28', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus, still teaching in the temple courts, cried out, “You know Me, and you know where I am from. I have not come of My own accord, but He who sent Me is true. You do not know Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.29', 'BSB', 'but I know Him, because I am from Him and He sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.30', 'BSB', 'So they tried to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him, because His hour had not yet come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.31', 'BSB', 'Many in the crowd, however, believed in Him and said, “When the Christ comes, will He perform more signs than this man?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.32', 'BSB', 'When the Pharisees heard the crowd whispering these things about Jesus, they and the chief priests sent officers to arrest Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.33', 'BSB', 'So Jesus said, “I am with you only a little while longer, and then I am going to the One who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.34', 'BSB', 'You will look for Me, but you will not find Me; and where I am, you cannot come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.35', 'BSB', 'At this, the Jews said to one another, “Where does He intend to go that we will not find Him? Will He go where the Jews are dispersed among the Greeks, and teach the Greeks?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.36', 'BSB', 'What does He mean by saying, ‘You will look for Me, but you will not find Me,’ and, ‘Where I am, you cannot come’?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.37', 'BSB', 'On the last and greatest day of the feast, Jesus stood up and called out in a loud voice, “If anyone is thirsty, let him come to Me and drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.38', 'BSB', 'Whoever believes in Me, as the Scripture has said: ‘Streams of living water will flow from within him.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.39', 'BSB', 'He was speaking about the Spirit, whom those who believed in Him were later to receive. For the Spirit had not yet been given, because Jesus had not yet been glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.40', 'BSB', 'On hearing these words, some of the people said, “This is truly the Prophet.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.41', 'BSB', 'Others declared, “This is the Christ.” But still others asked, “How can the Christ come from Galilee?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.42', 'BSB', 'Doesn’t the Scripture say that the Christ will come from the line of David and from Bethlehem, the village where David lived?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.43', 'BSB', 'So there was division in the crowd because of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.44', 'BSB', 'Some of them wanted to seize Him, but no one laid a hand on Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.45', 'BSB', 'Then the officers returned to the chief priests and Pharisees, who asked them, “Why didn’t you bring Him in?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.46', 'BSB', '“Never has anyone spoken like this man!” the officers answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.47', 'BSB', '“Have you also been deceived?” replied the Pharisees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.48', 'BSB', '“Have any of the rulers or Pharisees believed in Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.49', 'BSB', 'But this crowd that does not know the law, they are under a curse.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.50', 'BSB', 'Nicodemus, who had gone to Jesus earlier and who himself was one of them, asked,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.51', 'BSB', '“Does our law convict a man without first hearing from him to determine what he has done?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.52', 'BSB', '“Aren’t you also from Galilee?” they replied. “Look into it, and you will see that no prophet comes out of Galilee.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.7.53', 'BSB', 'Then each went to his own home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.1', 'BSB', 'But Jesus went to the Mount of Olives.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.2', 'BSB', 'Early in the morning He went back into the temple courts. All the people came to Him, and He sat down to teach them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.3', 'BSB', 'The scribes and Pharisees, however, brought to Him a woman caught in adultery. They made her stand before them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.4', 'BSB', 'and said, “Teacher, this woman was caught in the act of adultery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.5', 'BSB', 'In the Law Moses commanded us to stone such a woman. So what do You say?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.6', 'BSB', 'They said this to test Him, in order to have a basis for accusing Him. But Jesus bent down and began to write on the ground with His finger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.7', 'BSB', 'When they continued to question Him, He straightened up and said to them, “Let him who is without sin among you be the first to cast a stone at her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.8', 'BSB', 'And again He bent down and wrote on the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.9', 'BSB', 'When they heard this, they began to go away one by one, beginning with the older ones, until only Jesus was left, with the woman standing there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.10', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus straightened up and asked her, “Woman, where are your accusers? Has no one condemned you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.11', 'BSB', '“No one, Lord,” she answered. “Then neither do I condemn you,” Jesus declared. “Now go and sin no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.12', 'BSB', 'Once again, Jesus spoke to the people and said, “I am the light of the world. Whoever follows Me will never walk in the darkness, but will have the light of life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.13', 'BSB', 'So the Pharisees said to Him, “You are testifying about Yourself; Your testimony is not valid.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.14', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Even if I testify about Myself, My testimony is valid, because I know where I came from and where I am going. But you do not know where I came from or where I am going.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.15', 'BSB', 'You judge according to the flesh; I judge no one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.16', 'BSB', 'But even if I do judge, My judgment is true, because I am not alone; I am with the Father who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.17', 'BSB', 'Even in your own Law it is written that the testimony of two men is valid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.18', 'BSB', 'I am One who testifies about Myself, and the Father, who sent Me, also testifies about Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.19', 'BSB', '“Where is Your Father?” they asked Him. “You do not know Me or My Father,” Jesus answered. “If you knew Me, you would know My Father as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.20', 'BSB', 'He spoke these words while teaching in the temple courts, near the treasury. Yet no one seized Him, because His hour had not yet come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.21', 'BSB', 'Again He said to them, “I am going away, and you will look for Me, but you will die in your sin. Where I am going, you cannot come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.22', 'BSB', 'So the Jews began to ask, “Will He kill Himself, since He says, ‘Where I am going, you cannot come’?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.23', 'BSB', 'Then He told them, “You are from below; I am from above. You are of this world; I am not of this world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.24', 'BSB', 'That is why I told you that you would die in your sins. For unless you believe that I am He, you will die in your sins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.25', 'BSB', '“Who are You?” they asked. “Just what I have been telling you from the beginning,” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.26', 'BSB', '“I have much to say about you and much to judge. But the One who sent Me is truthful, and what I have heard from Him, I tell the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.27', 'BSB', 'They did not understand that He was telling them about the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.28', 'BSB', 'So Jesus said, “When you have lifted up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am He, and that I do nothing on My own, but speak exactly what the Father has taught Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.29', 'BSB', 'He who sent Me is with Me. He has not left Me alone, because I always do what pleases Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.30', 'BSB', 'As Jesus spoke these things, many believed in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.31', 'BSB', 'So He said to the Jews who had believed Him, “If you continue in My word, you are truly My disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.32', 'BSB', 'Then you will know the truth, and the truth will set you free.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.33', 'BSB', '“We are Abraham’s descendants,” they answered. “We have never been slaves to anyone. How can You say we will be set free?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Truly, truly, I tell you, everyone who sins is a slave to sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.35', 'BSB', 'A slave is not a permanent member of the family, but a son belongs to it forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.36', 'BSB', 'So if the Son sets you free, you will be free indeed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.37', 'BSB', 'I know you are Abraham’s descendants, but you are trying to kill Me because My word has no place within you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.38', 'BSB', 'I speak of what I have seen in the presence of the Father, and you do what you have heard from your father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.39', 'BSB', '“Abraham is our father,” they replied. “If you were children of Abraham,” said Jesus, “you would do the works of Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.40', 'BSB', 'But now you are trying to kill Me, a man who has told you the truth that I heard from God. Abraham never did such a thing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.41', 'BSB', 'You are doing the works of your father.” “We are not illegitimate children,” they declared. “Our only Father is God Himself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.42', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to them, “If God were your Father, you would love Me, for I have come here from God. I have not come on My own, but He sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.43', 'BSB', 'Why do you not understand what I am saying? It is because you are unable to accept My message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.44', 'BSB', 'You belong to your father, the devil, and you want to carry out his desires. He was a murderer from the beginning, refusing to uphold the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he lies, he speaks his native language, because he is a liar and the father of lies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.45', 'BSB', 'But because I speak the truth, you do not believe Me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.46', 'BSB', 'Which of you can prove Me guilty of sin? If I speak the truth, why do you not believe Me?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.47', 'BSB', 'Whoever belongs to God hears the words of God. The reason you do not hear is that you do not belong to God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.48', 'BSB', 'The Jews answered Him, “Are we not right to say that You are a Samaritan and You have a demon?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.49', 'BSB', '“I do not have a demon,” Jesus replied, “but I honor My Father, and you dishonor Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.50', 'BSB', 'I do not seek My own glory. There is One who seeks it, and He is the Judge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.51', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, if anyone keeps My word, he will never see death.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.52', 'BSB', '“Now we know that You have a demon!” declared the Jews. “Abraham died, and so did the prophets, yet You say that anyone who keeps Your word will never taste death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.53', 'BSB', 'Are You greater than our father Abraham? He died, as did the prophets. Who do You claim to be?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.54', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “If I glorify Myself, My glory means nothing. The One who glorifies Me is My Father, of whom you say ‘He is our God.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.55', 'BSB', 'You do not know Him, but I know Him. If I said I did not know Him, I would be a liar like you. But I do know Him, and I keep His word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.56', 'BSB', 'Your father Abraham rejoiced that he would see My day. He saw it and was glad.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.57', 'BSB', 'Then the Jews said to Him, “You are not yet fifty years old, and You have seen Abraham?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.58', 'BSB', '“Truly, truly, I tell you,” Jesus declared, “before Abraham was born, I am!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.8.59', 'BSB', 'At this, they picked up stones to throw at Him. But Jesus was hidden and went out of the temple area.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.1', 'BSB', 'Now as Jesus was passing by, He saw a man blind from birth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.2', 'BSB', 'and His disciples asked Him, “Rabbi, who sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “Neither this man nor his parents sinned, but this happened so that the works of God would be displayed in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.4', 'BSB', 'While it is daytime, we must do the works of Him who sent Me. Night is coming, when no one can work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.5', 'BSB', 'While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.6', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had said this, He spit on the ground, made some mud, and applied it to the man’s eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.7', 'BSB', 'Then He told him, “Go, wash in the Pool of Siloam” (which means “Sent”). So the man went and washed, and came back seeing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.8', 'BSB', 'At this, his neighbors and those who had formerly seen him begging began to ask, “Isn’t this the man who used to sit and beg?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.9', 'BSB', 'Some claimed that he was, but others said, “No, he just looks like him.” But the man kept saying, “I am the one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.10', 'BSB', '“How then were your eyes opened?” they asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.11', 'BSB', 'He answered, “The man they call Jesus made some mud and anointed my eyes, and He told me to go to Siloam and wash. So I went and washed and received my sight.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.12', 'BSB', '“Where is He?” they asked. “I do not know,” he answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.13', 'BSB', 'They brought to the Pharisees the man who had been blind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.14', 'BSB', 'Now the day on which Jesus had made the mud and opened his eyes was a Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.15', 'BSB', 'So the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight. The man answered, “He put mud on my eyes, and I washed, and now I can see.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.16', 'BSB', 'Because of this, some of the Pharisees said, “This man is not from God, for He does not keep the Sabbath.” But others said, “How can a sinful man perform such signs?” And there was division among them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.17', 'BSB', 'So once again they asked the man who had been blind, “What do you say about Him, since it was your eyes He opened?” “He is a prophet,” the man replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.18', 'BSB', 'The Jews still did not believe that the man had been blind and had received his sight until they summoned his parents', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.19', 'BSB', 'and asked, “Is this your son, the one you say was born blind? So how is it that he can now see?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.20', 'BSB', 'His parents answered, “We know he is our son, and we know he was born blind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.21', 'BSB', 'But how he can now see or who opened his eyes, we do not know. Ask him. He is old enough to speak for himself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.22', 'BSB', 'His parents said this because they were afraid of the Jews. For the Jews had already determined that anyone who confessed Jesus as the Christ would be put out of the synagogue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.23', 'BSB', 'That was why his parents said, “He is old enough. Ask him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.24', 'BSB', 'So a second time they called for the man who had been blind and said, “Give glory to God! We know that this man is a sinner.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.25', 'BSB', 'He answered, “Whether He is a sinner I do not know. There is one thing I do know: I was blind, but now I see!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.26', 'BSB', '“What did He do to you?” they asked. “How did He open your eyes?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.27', 'BSB', 'He replied, “I already told you, and you did not listen. Why do you want to hear it again? Do you also want to become His disciples?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.28', 'BSB', 'Then they heaped insults on him and said, “You are His disciple; we are disciples of Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.29', 'BSB', 'We know that God spoke to Moses, but we do not know where this man is from.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.30', 'BSB', '“That is remarkable indeed!” the man said. “You do not know where He is from, and yet He opened my eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.31', 'BSB', 'We know that God does not listen to sinners, but He does listen to the one who worships Him and does His will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.32', 'BSB', 'Never before has anyone heard of opening the eyes of a man born blind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.33', 'BSB', 'If this man were not from God, He could do no such thing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.34', 'BSB', 'They replied, “You were born in utter sin, and you are instructing us?” And they threw him out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.35', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard that they had thrown him out, He found the man and said, “Do you believe in the Son of Man?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.36', 'BSB', '“Who is He, Sir?” he replied. “Tell me so that I may believe in Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.37', 'BSB', '“You have already seen Him,” Jesus answered. “He is the One speaking with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.38', 'BSB', '“Lord, I believe,” he said. And he worshiped Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.39', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus declared, “For judgment I have come into this world, so that the blind may see and those who see may become blind.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.40', 'BSB', 'Some of the Pharisees who were with Him heard this, and they asked Him, “Are we blind too?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.9.41', 'BSB', '“If you were blind,” Jesus replied, “you would not be guilty of sin. But since you claim you can see, your guilt remains.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.1', 'BSB', '“Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever does not enter the sheepfold by the gate, but climbs in some other way, is a thief and a robber.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.2', 'BSB', 'But the one who enters by the gate is the shepherd of the sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.3', 'BSB', 'The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep listen for his voice. He calls his own sheep by name and leads them out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.4', 'BSB', 'When he has brought out all his own, he goes on ahead of them, and his sheep follow him because they know his voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.5', 'BSB', 'But they will never follow a stranger; in fact, they will flee from him because they do not recognize his voice.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.6', 'BSB', 'Jesus spoke to them using this illustration, but they did not understand what He was telling them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.7', 'BSB', 'So He said to them again, “Truly, truly, I tell you, I am the gate for the sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.8', 'BSB', 'All who came before Me were thieves and robbers, but the sheep did not listen to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.9', 'BSB', 'I am the gate. If anyone enters through Me, he will be saved. He will come in and go out and find pasture.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.10', 'BSB', 'The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy. I have come that they may have life, and have it in all its fullness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.11', 'BSB', 'I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down His life for the sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.12', 'BSB', 'The hired hand is not the shepherd, and the sheep are not his own. When he sees the wolf coming, he abandons the sheep and runs away. Then the wolf pounces on them and scatters the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.13', 'BSB', 'The man runs away because he is a hired servant and is unconcerned for the sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.14', 'BSB', 'I am the good shepherd. I know My sheep and My sheep know Me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.15', 'BSB', 'just as the Father knows Me and I know the Father. And I lay down My life for the sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.16', 'BSB', 'I have other sheep that are not of this fold. I must bring them in as well, and they will listen to My voice. Then there will be one flock and one shepherd.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.17', 'BSB', 'The reason the Father loves Me is that I lay down My life in order to take it up again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.18', 'BSB', 'No one takes it from Me, but I lay it down of My own accord. I have authority to lay it down and authority to take it up again. This charge I have received from My Father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.19', 'BSB', 'Again there was division among the Jews because of Jesus’ message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.20', 'BSB', 'Many of them said, “He is demon-possessed and insane. Why would you listen to Him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.21', 'BSB', 'But others replied, “These are not the words of a man possessed by a demon. Can a demon open the eyes of the blind?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.22', 'BSB', 'At that time the Feast of Dedication took place in Jerusalem. It was winter,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.23', 'BSB', 'and Jesus was walking in the temple courts in Solomon’s Colonnade.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.24', 'BSB', 'So the Jews gathered around Him and demanded, “How long will You keep us in suspense? If You are the Christ, tell us plainly.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.25', 'BSB', '“I already told you,” Jesus replied, “but you did not believe. The works I do in My Father’s name testify on My behalf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.26', 'BSB', 'But because you are not My sheep, you refuse to believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.27', 'BSB', 'My sheep listen to My voice; I know them, and they follow Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.28', 'BSB', 'I give them eternal life, and they will never perish. No one can snatch them out of My hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.29', 'BSB', 'My Father who has given them to Me is greater than all. No one can snatch them out of My Father’s hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.30', 'BSB', 'I and the Father are one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.31', 'BSB', 'At this, the Jews again picked up stones to stone Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.32', 'BSB', 'But Jesus responded, “I have shown you many good works from the Father. For which of these do you stone Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.33', 'BSB', '“We are not stoning You for any good work,” said the Jews, “but for blasphemy, because You, who are a man, declare Yourself to be God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.34', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Is it not written in your Law: ‘I have said you are gods’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.35', 'BSB', 'If he called them gods to whom the word of God came—and the Scripture cannot be broken—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.36', 'BSB', 'then what about the One whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world? How then can you accuse Me of blasphemy for stating that I am the Son of God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.37', 'BSB', 'If I am not doing the works of My Father, then do not believe Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.38', 'BSB', 'But if I am doing them, even though you do not believe Me, believe the works themselves, so that you may know and understand that the Father is in Me, and I am in the Father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.39', 'BSB', 'At this, they tried again to seize Him, but He escaped their grasp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.40', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus went back across the Jordan to the place where John had first been baptizing, and He stayed there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.41', 'BSB', 'Many came to Him and said, “Although John never performed a sign, everything he said about this man was true.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.10.42', 'BSB', 'And many in that place believed in Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.1', 'BSB', 'At this time a man named Lazarus was sick. He lived in Bethany, the village of Mary and her sister Martha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.2', 'BSB', '(Mary, whose brother Lazarus was sick, was to anoint the Lord with perfume and wipe His feet with her hair.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.3', 'BSB', 'So the sisters sent word to Jesus, “Lord, the one You love is sick.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.4', 'BSB', 'When Jesus heard this, He said, “This sickness will not end in death. No, it is for the glory of God, so that the Son of God may be glorified through it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.5', 'BSB', 'Now Jesus loved Martha and her sister and Lazarus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.6', 'BSB', 'So on hearing that Lazarus was sick, He stayed where He was for two days,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.7', 'BSB', 'and then He said to the disciples, “Let us go back to Judea.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.8', 'BSB', '“Rabbi,” they replied, “the Jews just tried to stone You, and You are going back there?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.9', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “Are there not twelve hours of daylight? If anyone walks in the daytime, he will not stumble, because he sees by the light of this world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.10', 'BSB', 'But if anyone walks at night, he will stumble, because he has no light.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.11', 'BSB', 'After He had said this, He told them, “Our friend Lazarus has fallen asleep, but I am going there to wake him up.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.12', 'BSB', 'His disciples replied, “Lord, if he is sleeping, he will get better.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.13', 'BSB', 'They thought that Jesus was talking about actual sleep, but He was speaking about the death of Lazarus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.14', 'BSB', 'So Jesus told them plainly, “Lazarus is dead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.15', 'BSB', 'and for your sake I am glad I was not there, so that you may believe. But let us go to him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.16', 'BSB', 'Then Thomas called Didymus said to his fellow disciples, “Let us also go, so that we may die with Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.17', 'BSB', 'When Jesus arrived, He found that Lazarus had already spent four days in the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.18', 'BSB', 'Now Bethany was near Jerusalem, a little less than two miles away,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.19', 'BSB', 'and many of the Jews had come to Martha and Mary to console them in the loss of their brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.20', 'BSB', 'So when Martha heard that Jesus was coming, she went out to meet Him; but Mary stayed at home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.21', 'BSB', 'Martha said to Jesus, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.22', 'BSB', 'But even now I know that God will give You whatever You ask of Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.23', 'BSB', '“Your brother will rise again,” Jesus told her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.24', 'BSB', 'Martha replied, “I know that he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.25', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. Whoever believes in Me will live, even though he dies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.26', 'BSB', 'And everyone who lives and believes in Me will never die. Do you believe this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.27', 'BSB', '“Yes, Lord,” she answered, “I believe that You are the Christ, the Son of God, who was to come into the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.28', 'BSB', 'After Martha had said this, she went back and called her sister Mary aside to tell her, “The Teacher is here and is asking for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.29', 'BSB', 'And when Mary heard this, she got up quickly and went to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.30', 'BSB', 'Now Jesus had not yet entered the village, but was still at the place where Martha had met Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.31', 'BSB', 'When the Jews who were in the house consoling Mary saw how quickly she got up and went out, they followed her, supposing she was going to the tomb to mourn there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.32', 'BSB', 'When Mary came to Jesus and saw Him, she fell at His feet and said, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.33', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw her weeping, and the Jews who had come with her also weeping, He was deeply moved in spirit and troubled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.34', 'BSB', '“Where have you put him?” He asked. “Come and see, Lord,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.35', 'BSB', 'Jesus wept.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.36', 'BSB', 'Then the Jews said, “See how He loved him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.37', 'BSB', 'But some of them asked, “Could not this man who opened the eyes of the blind also have kept Lazarus from dying?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.38', 'BSB', 'Jesus, once again deeply moved, came to the tomb. It was a cave with a stone laid across the entrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.39', 'BSB', '“Take away the stone,” Jesus said. “Lord, by now he stinks,” said Martha, the sister of the dead man. “It has already been four days.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.40', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Did I not tell you that if you believed, you would see the glory of God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.41', 'BSB', 'So they took away the stone. Then Jesus lifted His eyes upward and said, “Father, I thank You that You have heard Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.42', 'BSB', 'I knew that You always hear Me, but I say this for the benefit of the people standing here, so they may believe that You sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.43', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had said this, He called out in a loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.44', 'BSB', 'The man who had been dead came out with his hands and feet bound in strips of linen, and his face wrapped in a cloth. “Unwrap him and let him go,” Jesus told them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.45', 'BSB', 'Therefore many of the Jews who had come to Mary, and had seen what Jesus did, believed in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.46', 'BSB', 'But some of them went to the Pharisees and told them what Jesus had done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.47', 'BSB', 'Then the chief priests and Pharisees convened the Sanhedrin and said, “What are we to do? This man is performing many signs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.48', 'BSB', 'If we let Him go on like this, everyone will believe in Him, and then the Romans will come and take away both our place and our nation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.49', 'BSB', 'But one of them, named Caiaphas, who was high priest that year, said to them, “You know nothing at all!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.50', 'BSB', 'You do not realize that it is better for you that one man die for the people than that the whole nation perish.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.51', 'BSB', 'Caiaphas did not say this on his own. Instead, as high priest that year, he was prophesying that Jesus would die for the nation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.52', 'BSB', 'and not only for the nation, but also for the scattered children of God, to gather them together into one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.53', 'BSB', 'So from that day on they plotted to kill Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.54', 'BSB', 'As a result, Jesus no longer went about publicly among the Jews, but He withdrew to a town called Ephraim in an area near the wilderness. And He stayed there with the disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.55', 'BSB', 'Now the Jewish Passover was near, and many people went up from the country to Jerusalem to purify themselves before the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.56', 'BSB', 'They kept looking for Jesus and asking one another as they stood in the temple courts, “What do you think? Will He come to the feast at all?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.11.57', 'BSB', 'But the chief priests and Pharisees had given orders that anyone who knew where He was must report it, so that they could arrest Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.1', 'BSB', 'Six days before the Passover, Jesus came to Bethany, the hometown of Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.2', 'BSB', 'So they hosted a dinner for Jesus there. Martha served, and Lazarus was among those reclining at the table with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.3', 'BSB', 'Then Mary took about a pint of expensive perfume, made of pure nard, and she anointed Jesus’ feet and wiped them with her hair. And the house was filled with the fragrance of the perfume.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.4', 'BSB', 'But one of His disciples, Judas Iscariot, who was going to betray Him, asked,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.5', 'BSB', '“Why wasn’t this perfume sold for three hundred denarii and the money given to the poor?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.6', 'BSB', 'Judas did not say this because he cared about the poor, but because he was a thief. As keeper of the money bag, he used to take from what was put into it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.7', 'BSB', '“Leave her alone,” Jesus replied. “She has kept this perfume in preparation for the day of My burial.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.8', 'BSB', 'The poor you will always have with you, but you will not always have Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.9', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile a large crowd of Jews learned that Jesus was there. And they came not only because of Him, but also to see Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.10', 'BSB', 'So the chief priests made plans to kill Lazarus as well,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.11', 'BSB', 'for on account of him many of the Jews were deserting them and believing in Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.12', 'BSB', 'The next day the great crowd that had come to the feast heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.13', 'BSB', 'They took palm branches and went out to meet Him, shouting: “Hosanna!” “Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord!” “Blessed is the King of Israel!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.14', 'BSB', 'Finding a young donkey, Jesus sat on it, as it is written:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.15', 'BSB', '“Do not be afraid, O Daughter of Zion. See, your King is coming, seated on the colt of a donkey.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.16', 'BSB', 'At first His disciples did not understand these things, but after Jesus was glorified they remembered what had been done to Him, and they realized that these very things had also been written about Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.17', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, many people continued to testify that they had been with Jesus when He called Lazarus from the tomb and raised him from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.18', 'BSB', 'That is also why the crowd went out to meet Him, because they heard that He had performed this sign.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.19', 'BSB', 'Then the Pharisees said to one another, “You can see that this is doing you no good. Look how the whole world has gone after Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.20', 'BSB', 'Now there were some Greeks among those who went up to worship at the feast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.21', 'BSB', 'They came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida in Galilee, and requested of him, “Sir, we want to see Jesus.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.22', 'BSB', 'Philip relayed this appeal to Andrew, and both of them went and told Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.23', 'BSB', 'But Jesus replied, “The hour has come for the Son of Man to be glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.24', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, unless a kernel of wheat falls to the ground and dies, it remains only a seed; but if it dies, it bears much fruit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.25', 'BSB', 'Whoever loves his life will lose it, but whoever hates his life in this world will keep it for eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.26', 'BSB', 'If anyone serves Me, he must follow Me; and where I am, My servant will be as well. If anyone serves Me, the Father will honor him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.27', 'BSB', 'Now My soul is troubled, and what shall I say? ‘Father, save Me from this hour’? No, it is for this purpose that I have come to this hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.28', 'BSB', 'Father, glorify Your name!” Then a voice came from heaven: “I have glorified it, and I will glorify it again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.29', 'BSB', 'The crowd standing there heard it and said that it had thundered. Others said that an angel had spoken to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.30', 'BSB', 'In response, Jesus said, “This voice was not for My benefit, but yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.31', 'BSB', 'Now judgment is upon this world; now the prince of this world will be cast out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.32', 'BSB', 'And I, when I am lifted up from the earth, will draw everyone to Myself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.33', 'BSB', 'He said this to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.34', 'BSB', 'The crowd replied, “We have heard from the Law that the Christ will remain forever. So how can you say that the Son of Man must be lifted up? Who is this Son of Man?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.35', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus told them, “For a little while longer, the Light will be among you. Walk while you have the Light, so that darkness will not overtake you. The one who walks in the darkness does not know where he is going.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.36', 'BSB', 'While you have the Light, believe in the Light, so that you may become sons of light.” After Jesus had spoken these things, He went away and was hidden from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.37', 'BSB', 'Although Jesus had performed so many signs in their presence, they still did not believe in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.38', 'BSB', 'This was to fulfill the word of Isaiah the prophet: “Lord, who has believed our message? And to whom has the arm of the Lord been revealed?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.39', 'BSB', 'For this reason they were unable to believe. For again, Isaiah says:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.40', 'BSB', '“He has blinded their eyes and hardened their hearts, so that they cannot see with their eyes, and understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.41', 'BSB', 'Isaiah said these things because he saw Jesus’ glory and spoke about Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.42', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, many of the leaders believed in Him; but because of the Pharisees they did not confess Him, for fear that they would be put out of the synagogue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.43', 'BSB', 'For they loved praise from men more than praise from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.44', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus cried out, “Whoever believes in Me does not believe in Me alone, but in the One who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.45', 'BSB', 'And whoever sees Me sees the One who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.46', 'BSB', 'I have come into the world as a light, so that no one who believes in Me should remain in darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.47', 'BSB', 'As for anyone who hears My words and does not keep them, I do not judge him. For I have not come to judge the world, but to save the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.48', 'BSB', 'There is a judge for the one who rejects Me and does not receive My words: The word that I have spoken will judge him on the last day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.49', 'BSB', 'I have not spoken on My own, but the Father who sent Me has commanded Me what to say and how to say it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.12.50', 'BSB', 'And I know that His command leads to eternal life. So I speak exactly what the Father has told Me to say.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.1', 'BSB', 'It was now just before the Passover Feast, and Jesus knew that His hour had come to leave this world and return to the Father. Having loved His own who were in the world, He loved them to the very end.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.2', 'BSB', 'The evening meal was underway, and the devil had already put into the heart of Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, to betray Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.3', 'BSB', 'Jesus knew that the Father had delivered all things into His hands, and that He had come from God and was returning to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.4', 'BSB', 'So He got up from the supper, laid aside His outer garments, and wrapped a towel around His waist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.5', 'BSB', 'After that, He poured water into a basin and began to wash the disciples’ feet and dry them with the towel that was around Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.6', 'BSB', 'He came to Simon Peter, who asked Him, “Lord, are You going to wash my feet?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.7', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “You do not realize now what I am doing, but later you will understand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.8', 'BSB', '“Never shall You wash my feet!” Peter told Him. Jesus answered, “Unless I wash you, you have no part with Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.9', 'BSB', '“Then, Lord,” Simon Peter replied, “not only my feet, but my hands and my head as well!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.10', 'BSB', 'Jesus told him, “Whoever has already bathed needs only to wash his feet, and he will be completely clean. And you are clean, though not all of you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.11', 'BSB', 'For He knew who would betray Him. That is why He said, “Not all of you are clean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.12', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had washed their feet and put on His outer garments, He reclined with them again and asked, “Do you know what I have done for you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.13', 'BSB', 'You call Me Teacher and Lord, and rightly so, because I am.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.14', 'BSB', 'So if I, your Lord and Teacher, have washed your feet, you also should wash one another’s feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.15', 'BSB', 'I have set you an example so that you should do as I have done for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.16', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, no servant is greater than his master, nor is a messenger greater than the one who sent him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.17', 'BSB', 'If you know these things, you will be blessed if you do them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.18', 'BSB', 'I am not speaking about all of you; I know whom I have chosen. But this is to fulfill the Scripture: ‘The one who shares My bread has lifted up his heel against Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.19', 'BSB', 'I am telling you now before it happens, so that when it comes to pass, you will believe that I am He.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.20', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever receives the one I send receives Me, and whoever receives Me receives the One who sent Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.21', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had said this, He became troubled in spirit and testified, “Truly, truly, I tell you, one of you will betray Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.22', 'BSB', 'The disciples looked at one another, perplexed as to which of them He meant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.23', 'BSB', 'One of His disciples, the one whom Jesus loved, was reclining at His side.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.24', 'BSB', 'So Simon Peter motioned to him to ask Jesus which one He was talking about.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.25', 'BSB', 'Leaning back against Jesus, he asked, “Lord, who is it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.26', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “It is the one to whom I give this morsel after I have dipped it.” Then He dipped the morsel and gave it to Judas son of Simon Iscariot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.27', 'BSB', 'And when Judas had taken the morsel, Satan entered into him. Then Jesus said to Judas, “What you are about to do, do quickly.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.28', 'BSB', 'But no one at the table knew why Jesus had said this to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.29', 'BSB', 'Since Judas kept the money bag, some thought that Jesus was telling him to buy what was needed for the feast, or to give something to the poor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.30', 'BSB', 'As soon as he had received the morsel, Judas went out into the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.31', 'BSB', 'When Judas had gone out, Jesus said, “Now the Son of Man is glorified, and God is glorified in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.32', 'BSB', 'If God is glorified in Him, God will also glorify the Son in Himself—and will glorify Him at once.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.33', 'BSB', 'Little children, I am with you only a little while longer. You will look for Me, and as I said to the Jews, so now I say to you: ‘Where I am going, you cannot come.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.34', 'BSB', 'A new commandment I give you: Love one another. As I have loved you, so you also must love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.35', 'BSB', 'By this everyone will know that you are My disciples, if you love one another.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.36', 'BSB', '“Lord, where are You going?” Simon Peter asked. Jesus answered, “Where I am going, you cannot follow Me now, but you will follow later.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.37', 'BSB', '“Lord,” said Peter, “why can’t I follow You now? I will lay down my life for You.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.13.38', 'BSB', '“Will you lay down your life for Me?” Jesus replied. “Truly, truly, I tell you, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.1', 'BSB', '“Do not let your hearts be troubled. You believe in God; believe in Me as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.2', 'BSB', 'In My Father’s house are many rooms. If it were not so, would I have told you that I am going there to prepare a place for you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.3', 'BSB', 'And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come back and welcome you into My presence, so that you also may be where I am.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.4', 'BSB', 'You know the way to the place where I am going.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.5', 'BSB', '“Lord,” said Thomas, “we do not know where You are going, so how can we know the way?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.6', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.7', 'BSB', 'If you had known Me, you would know My Father as well. From now on you do know Him and have seen Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.8', 'BSB', 'Philip said to Him, “Lord, show us the Father, and that will be enough for us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.9', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “Philip, I have been with you all this time, and still you do not know Me? Anyone who has seen Me has seen the Father. How can you say, ‘Show us the Father’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.10', 'BSB', 'Do you not believe that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me? The words I say to you, I do not speak on My own. Instead, it is the Father dwelling in Me, performing His works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.11', 'BSB', 'Believe Me that I am in the Father and the Father is in Me—or at least believe on account of the works themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.12', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, whoever believes in Me will also do the works that I am doing. He will do even greater things than these, because I am going to the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.13', 'BSB', 'And I will do whatever you ask in My name, so that the Father may be glorified in the Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.14', 'BSB', 'If you ask Me for anything in My name, I will do it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.15', 'BSB', 'If you love Me, you will keep My commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.16', 'BSB', 'And I will ask the Father, and He will give you another Advocate to be with you forever—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.17', 'BSB', 'the Spirit of truth. The world cannot receive Him, because it neither sees Him nor knows Him. But you do know Him, for He abides with you and will be in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.18', 'BSB', 'I will not leave you as orphans; I will come to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.19', 'BSB', 'In a little while the world will see Me no more, but you will see Me. Because I live, you also will live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.20', 'BSB', 'On that day you will know that I am in My Father, and you are in Me, and I am in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.21', 'BSB', 'Whoever has My commandments and keeps them is the one who loves Me. The one who loves Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and reveal Myself to him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.22', 'BSB', 'Judas (not Iscariot) asked Him, “Lord, why are You going to reveal Yourself to us and not to the world?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “If anyone loves Me, he will keep My word. My Father will love him, and We will come to him and make Our home with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.24', 'BSB', 'Whoever does not love Me does not keep My words. The word that you hear is not My own, but it is from the Father who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.25', 'BSB', 'All this I have spoken to you while I am still with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.26', 'BSB', 'But the Advocate, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My name, will teach you all things and will remind you of everything I have told you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.27', 'BSB', 'Peace I leave with you; My peace I give to you. I do not give to you as the world gives. Do not let your hearts be troubled; do not be afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.28', 'BSB', 'You heard Me say, ‘I am going away, and I am coming back to you.’ If you loved Me, you would rejoice that I am going to the Father, because the Father is greater than I.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.29', 'BSB', 'And now I have told you before it happens, so that when it does happen, you will believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.30', 'BSB', 'I will not speak with you much longer, for the prince of this world is coming, and he has no claim on Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.14.31', 'BSB', 'But I do exactly what the Father has commanded Me, so that the world may know that I love the Father. Get up! Let us go on from here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.1', 'BSB', '“I am the true vine, and My Father is the keeper of the vineyard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.2', 'BSB', 'He cuts off every branch in Me that bears no fruit, and every branch that does bear fruit, He prunes to make it even more fruitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.3', 'BSB', 'You are already clean because of the word I have spoken to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.4', 'BSB', 'Remain in Me, and I will remain in you. Just as no branch can bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, neither can you bear fruit unless you remain in Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.5', 'BSB', 'I am the vine and you are the branches. The one who remains in Me, and I in him, will bear much fruit. For apart from Me you can do nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.6', 'BSB', 'If anyone does not remain in Me, he is like a branch that is thrown away and withers. Such branches are gathered up, thrown into the fire, and burned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.7', 'BSB', 'If you remain in Me and My words remain in you, ask whatever you wish, and it will be done for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.8', 'BSB', 'This is to My Father’s glory, that you bear much fruit, proving yourselves to be My disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.9', 'BSB', 'As the Father has loved Me, so have I loved you. Remain in My love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.10', 'BSB', 'If you keep My commandments, you will remain in My love, just as I have kept My Father’s commandments and remain in His love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.11', 'BSB', 'I have told you these things so that My joy may be in you and your joy may be complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.12', 'BSB', 'This is My commandment, that you love one another as I have loved you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.13', 'BSB', 'Greater love has no one than this, that he lay down his life for his friends.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.14', 'BSB', 'You are My friends if you do what I command you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.15', 'BSB', 'No longer do I call you servants, for a servant does not understand what his master is doing. But I have called you friends, because everything I have learned from My Father I have made known to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.16', 'BSB', 'You did not choose Me, but I chose you. And I appointed you to go and bear fruit—fruit that will remain—so that whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.17', 'BSB', 'This is My command to you: Love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.18', 'BSB', 'If the world hates you, understand that it hated Me first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.19', 'BSB', 'If you were of the world, it would love you as its own. Instead, the world hates you, because you are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.20', 'BSB', 'Remember the word that I spoke to you: ‘No servant is greater than his master.’ If they persecuted Me, they will persecute you as well; if they kept My word, they will keep yours as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.21', 'BSB', 'But they will treat you like this because of My name, since they do not know the One who sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.22', 'BSB', 'If I had not come and spoken to them, they would not be guilty of sin. Now, however, they have no excuse for their sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.23', 'BSB', 'Whoever hates Me hates My Father as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.24', 'BSB', 'If I had not done among them the works that no one else did, they would not be guilty of sin; but now they have seen and hated both Me and My Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.25', 'BSB', 'But this is to fulfill what is written in their Law: ‘They hated Me without reason.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.26', 'BSB', 'When the Advocate comes, whom I will send to you from the Father—the Spirit of truth who proceeds from the Father—He will testify about Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.15.27', 'BSB', 'And you also must testify, because you have been with Me from the beginning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.1', 'BSB', '“I have told you these things so that you will not fall away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.2', 'BSB', 'They will put you out of the synagogues. In fact, a time is coming when anyone who kills you will think he is offering a service to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.3', 'BSB', 'They will do these things because they have not known the Father or Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.4', 'BSB', 'But I have told you these things so that when their hour comes, you will remember that I told you about them. I did not tell you these things from the beginning, because I was with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.5', 'BSB', 'Now, however, I am going to Him who sent Me; yet none of you asks Me, ‘Where are You going?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.6', 'BSB', 'Instead, your hearts are filled with sorrow because I have told you these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.7', 'BSB', 'But I tell you the truth, it is for your benefit that I am going away. Unless I go away, the Advocate will not come to you; but if I go, I will send Him to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.8', 'BSB', 'And when He comes, He will convict the world in regard to sin and righteousness and judgment:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.9', 'BSB', 'in regard to sin, because they do not believe in Me;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.10', 'BSB', 'in regard to righteousness, because I am going to the Father and you will no longer see Me;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.11', 'BSB', 'and in regard to judgment, because the prince of this world has been condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.12', 'BSB', 'I still have much to tell you, but you cannot yet bear to hear it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.13', 'BSB', 'However, when the Spirit of truth comes, He will guide you into all truth. For He will not speak on His own, but He will speak what He hears, and He will declare to you what is to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.14', 'BSB', 'He will glorify Me by taking from what is Mine and disclosing it to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.15', 'BSB', 'Everything that belongs to the Father is Mine. That is why I said that the Spirit will take from what is Mine and disclose it to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.16', 'BSB', 'In a little while you will see Me no more, and then after a little while you will see Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.17', 'BSB', 'Then some of His disciples asked one another, “Why is He telling us, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’ and ‘Because I am going to the Father’?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.18', 'BSB', 'They kept asking, “Why is He saying, ‘a little while’? We do not understand what He is saying.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.19', 'BSB', 'Aware that they wanted to question Him, Jesus said to them, “Are you asking one another why I said, ‘In a little while you will not see Me, and then after a little while you will see Me’?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.20', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, you will weep and wail while the world rejoices. You will grieve, but your grief will turn to joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.21', 'BSB', 'A woman has pain in childbirth because her time has come; but when she brings forth her child, she forgets her anguish because of her joy that a child has been born into the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.22', 'BSB', 'So also you have sorrow now, but I will see you again and your hearts will rejoice, and no one will take away your joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.23', 'BSB', 'In that day you will no longer ask Me anything. Truly, truly, I tell you, whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.24', 'BSB', 'Until now you have not asked for anything in My name. Ask and you will receive, so that your joy may be complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.25', 'BSB', 'I have spoken these things to you in figures of speech. An hour is coming when I will no longer speak to you this way, but will tell you plainly about the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.26', 'BSB', 'In that day you will ask in My name. I am not saying that I will ask the Father on your behalf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.27', 'BSB', 'For the Father Himself loves you, because you have loved Me and have believed that I came from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.28', 'BSB', 'I came from the Father and entered the world. In turn, I will leave the world and go to the Father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.29', 'BSB', 'His disciples said, “See, now You are speaking plainly and without figures of speech.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.30', 'BSB', 'Now we understand that You know all things and that You have no need for anyone to question You. Because of this, we believe that You came from God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.31', 'BSB', '“Do you finally believe?” Jesus replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.32', 'BSB', '“Look, an hour is coming and has already come when you will be scattered, each to his own home, and you will leave Me all alone. Yet I am not alone, because the Father is with Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.16.33', 'BSB', 'I have told you these things so that in Me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take courage; I have overcome the world!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.1', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had spoken these things, He lifted up His eyes to heaven and said, “Father, the hour has come. Glorify Your Son, that Your Son may glorify You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.2', 'BSB', 'For You granted Him authority over all people, so that He may give eternal life to all those You have given Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.3', 'BSB', 'Now this is eternal life, that they may know You, the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom You have sent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.4', 'BSB', 'I have glorified You on earth by accomplishing the work You gave Me to do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.5', 'BSB', 'And now, Father, glorify Me in Your presence with the glory I had with You before the world existed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.6', 'BSB', 'I have revealed Your name to those You have given Me out of the world. They were Yours; You gave them to Me, and they have kept Your word.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.7', 'BSB', 'Now they know that everything You have given Me comes from You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.8', 'BSB', 'For I have given them the words You gave Me, and they have received them. They knew with certainty that I came from You, and they believed that You sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.9', 'BSB', 'I ask on their behalf. I do not ask on behalf of the world, but on behalf of those You have given Me; for they are Yours.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.10', 'BSB', 'All I have is Yours, and all You have is Mine; and in them I have been glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.11', 'BSB', 'I will no longer be in the world, but they are in the world, and I am coming to You. Holy Father, protect them by Your name, the name You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.12', 'BSB', 'While I was with them, I protected and preserved them by Your name, the name You gave Me. Not one of them has been lost, except the son of destruction, so that the Scripture would be fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.13', 'BSB', 'But now I am coming to You; and I am saying these things while I am in the world, so that they may have My joy fulfilled within them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.14', 'BSB', 'I have given them Your word and the world has hated them; for they are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.15', 'BSB', 'I am not asking that You take them out of the world, but that You keep them from the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.16', 'BSB', 'They are not of the world, just as I am not of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.17', 'BSB', 'Sanctify them by the truth; Your word is truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.18', 'BSB', 'As You sent Me into the world, I have also sent them into the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.19', 'BSB', 'For them I sanctify Myself, so that they too may be sanctified by the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.20', 'BSB', 'I am not asking on behalf of them alone, but also on behalf of those who will believe in Me through their message,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.21', 'BSB', 'that all of them may be one, as You, Father, are in Me, and I am in You. May they also be in Us, so that the world may believe that You sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.22', 'BSB', 'I have given them the glory You gave Me, so that they may be one as We are one—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.23', 'BSB', 'I in them and You in Me—that they may be perfectly united, so that the world may know that You sent Me and have loved them just as You have loved Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.24', 'BSB', 'Father, I want those You have given Me to be with Me where I am, that they may see the glory You gave Me because You loved Me before the foundation of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.25', 'BSB', 'Righteous Father, although the world has not known You, I know You, and they know that You sent Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.17.26', 'BSB', 'And I have made Your name known to them and will continue to make it known, so that the love You have for Me may be in them, and I in them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.1', 'BSB', 'After Jesus had spoken these words, He went out with His disciples across the Kidron Valley, where they entered a garden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.2', 'BSB', 'Now Judas His betrayer also knew the place, because Jesus had often met there with His disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.3', 'BSB', 'So Judas brought a band of soldiers and officers from the chief priests and Pharisees. They arrived at the garden carrying lanterns, torches, and weapons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.4', 'BSB', 'Jesus, knowing all that was coming upon Him, stepped forward and asked them, “Whom are you seeking?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.5', 'BSB', '“Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. Jesus said, “I am He.” And Judas His betrayer was standing there with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.6', 'BSB', 'When Jesus said, “I am He,” they drew back and fell to the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.7', 'BSB', 'So He asked them again, “Whom are you seeking?” “Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.8', 'BSB', '“I told you that I am He,” Jesus replied. “So if you are looking for Me, let these men go.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.9', 'BSB', 'This was to fulfill the word He had spoken: “I have not lost one of those You have given Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.10', 'BSB', 'Then Simon Peter drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear. The servant’s name was Malchus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.11', 'BSB', '“Put your sword back in its sheath!” Jesus said to Peter. “Shall I not drink the cup the Father has given Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.12', 'BSB', 'Then the band of soldiers, with its commander and the officers of the Jews, arrested Jesus and bound Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.13', 'BSB', 'They brought Him first to Annas, who was the father-in-law of Caiaphas, the high priest that year.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.14', 'BSB', 'Caiaphas was the one who had advised the Jews that it would be better if one man died for the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.15', 'BSB', 'Now Simon Peter and another disciple were following Jesus. Since that disciple was known to the high priest, he also went with Jesus into the courtyard of the high priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.16', 'BSB', 'But Peter stood outside at the door. Then the disciple who was known to the high priest went out and spoke to the doorkeeper, and brought Peter in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.17', 'BSB', 'At this, the servant girl watching the door said to Peter, “Aren’t you also one of this man’s disciples?” “I am not,” he answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.18', 'BSB', 'Because it was cold, the servants and officers were standing around a charcoal fire they had made to keep warm. And Peter was also standing with them, warming himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.19', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the high priest questioned Jesus about His disciples and His teaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.20', 'BSB', '“I have spoken openly to the world,” Jesus answered. “I always taught in the synagogues and at the temple, where all the Jews come together. I said nothing in secret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.21', 'BSB', 'Why are you asking Me? Ask those who heard My message. Surely they know what I said.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.22', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had said this, one of the officers standing nearby slapped Him in the face and said, “Is this how You answer the high priest?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.23', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “If I said something wrong, testify as to what was wrong. But if I spoke correctly, why did you strike Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.24', 'BSB', 'Then Annas sent Him, still bound, to Caiaphas the high priest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.25', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter was still standing and warming himself. So they asked him, “Aren’t you also one of His disciples?” He denied it and said, “I am not.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.26', 'BSB', 'One of the high priest’s servants, a relative of the man whose ear Peter had cut off, asked, “Didn’t I see you with Him in the garden?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.27', 'BSB', 'Peter denied it once more, and immediately a rooster crowed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.28', 'BSB', 'Then they led Jesus away from Caiaphas into the Praetorium. By now it was early morning, and the Jews did not enter the Praetorium, to avoid being defiled and unable to eat the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.29', 'BSB', 'So Pilate went out to them and asked, “What accusation are you bringing against this man?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.30', 'BSB', '“If He were not a criminal,” they replied, “we would not have handed Him over to you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.31', 'BSB', '“You take Him and judge Him by your own law,” Pilate told them. “We are not permitted to execute anyone,” the Jews replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.32', 'BSB', 'This was to fulfill the word that Jesus had spoken to indicate the kind of death He was going to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.33', 'BSB', 'Pilate went back into the Praetorium, summoned Jesus, and asked Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.34', 'BSB', '“Are you saying this on your own,” Jesus asked, “or did others tell you about Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.35', 'BSB', '“Am I a Jew?” Pilate replied. “Your own people and chief priests handed You over to me. What have You done?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.36', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “My kingdom is not of this world; if it were, My servants would fight to prevent My arrest by the Jews. But now My kingdom is not of this realm.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.37', 'BSB', '“Then You are a king!” Pilate said. “You say that I am a king,” Jesus answered. “For this reason I was born and have come into the world, to testify to the truth. Everyone who belongs to the truth listens to My voice.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.38', 'BSB', '“What is truth?” Pilate asked. And having said this, he went out again to the Jews and told them, “I find no basis for a charge against Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.39', 'BSB', 'But it is your custom that I release to you one prisoner at the Passover. So then, do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.18.40', 'BSB', '“Not this man,” they shouted, “but Barabbas!” (Now Barabbas was an insurrectionist.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.1', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate took Jesus and had Him flogged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.2', 'BSB', 'The soldiers twisted together a crown of thorns, set it on His head, and dressed Him in a purple robe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.3', 'BSB', 'And they went up to Him again and again, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!” and slapping Him in the face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.4', 'BSB', 'Once again Pilate came out and said to the Jews, “Look, I am bringing Him out to you to let you know that I find no basis for a charge against Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.5', 'BSB', 'When Jesus came out wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe, Pilate said to them, “Here is the man!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.6', 'BSB', 'As soon as the chief priests and officers saw Him, they shouted, “Crucify Him! Crucify Him!” “You take Him and crucify Him,” Pilate replied, “for I find no basis for a charge against Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.7', 'BSB', '“We have a law,” answered the Jews, “and according to that law He must die, because He declared Himself to be the Son of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.8', 'BSB', 'When Pilate heard this statement, he was even more afraid,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.9', 'BSB', 'and he went back into the Praetorium. “Where are You from?” he asked. But Jesus gave no answer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.10', 'BSB', 'So Pilate said to Him, “Do You refuse to speak to me? Do You not know that I have authority to release You and authority to crucify You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.11', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “You would have no authority over Me if it were not given to you from above. Therefore the one who handed Me over to you is guilty of greater sin.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.12', 'BSB', 'From then on, Pilate tried to release Him, but the Jews kept shouting, “If you release this man, you are no friend of Caesar. Anyone who declares himself a king is defying Caesar.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.13', 'BSB', 'When Pilate heard these words, he brought Jesus out and sat on the judgment seat at a place called the Stone Pavement, which in Hebrew is Gabbatha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.14', 'BSB', 'It was the day of Preparation for the Passover, about the sixth hour. And Pilate said to the Jews, “Here is your King!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.15', 'BSB', 'At this, they shouted, “Away with Him! Away with Him! Crucify Him!” “Shall I crucify your King?” Pilate asked. “We have no king but Caesar,” replied the chief priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.16', 'BSB', 'Then Pilate handed Jesus over to be crucified, and the soldiers took Him away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.17', 'BSB', 'Carrying His own cross, He went out to The Place of the Skull, which in Hebrew is called Golgotha.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.18', 'BSB', 'There they crucified Him, and with Him two others, one on each side, with Jesus in the middle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.19', 'BSB', 'Pilate also had a notice posted on the cross. It read: JESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.20', 'BSB', 'Many of the Jews read this sign, because the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city, and it was written in Hebrew, Latin, and Greek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.21', 'BSB', 'So the chief priests of the Jews said to Pilate, “Do not write, ‘The King of the Jews,’ but only that He said, ‘I am the King of the Jews.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.22', 'BSB', 'Pilate answered, “What I have written, I have written.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.23', 'BSB', 'When the soldiers had crucified Jesus, they divided His garments into four parts, one for each soldier, with the tunic remaining. It was seamless, woven in one piece from top to bottom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.24', 'BSB', 'So they said to one another, “Let us not tear it. Instead, let us cast lots to see who will get it.” This was to fulfill the Scripture: “They divided My garments among them, and cast lots for My clothing.” So that is what the soldiers did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.25', 'BSB', 'Near the cross of Jesus stood His mother and her sister, as well as Mary the wife of Clopas and Mary Magdalene.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.26', 'BSB', 'When Jesus saw His mother and the disciple whom He loved standing nearby, He said to His mother, “Woman, here is your son.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.27', 'BSB', 'Then He said to the disciple, “Here is your mother.” So from that hour, this disciple took her into his home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.28', 'BSB', 'After this, knowing that everything had now been accomplished, and to fulfill the Scripture, Jesus said, “I am thirsty.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.29', 'BSB', 'A jar of sour wine was sitting there. So they soaked a sponge in the wine, put it on a stalk of hyssop, and lifted it to His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.30', 'BSB', 'When Jesus had received the sour wine, He said, “It is finished.” And bowing His head, He yielded up His spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.31', 'BSB', 'It was the day of Preparation, and the next day was a High Sabbath. In order that the bodies would not remain on the cross during the Sabbath, the Jews asked Pilate to have the legs broken and the bodies removed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.32', 'BSB', 'So the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first man who had been crucified with Jesus, and those of the other.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.33', 'BSB', 'But when they came to Jesus and saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.34', 'BSB', 'Instead, one of the soldiers pierced His side with a spear, and immediately blood and water flowed out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.35', 'BSB', 'The one who saw it has testified to this, and his testimony is true. He knows that he is telling the truth, so that you also may believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.36', 'BSB', 'Now these things happened so that the Scripture would be fulfilled: “Not one of His bones will be broken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.37', 'BSB', 'And, as another Scripture says: “They will look on the One they have pierced.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.38', 'BSB', 'Afterward, Joseph of Arimathea, who was a disciple of Jesus (but secretly for fear of the Jews), asked Pilate to let him remove the body of Jesus. Pilate gave him permission, so he came and removed His body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.39', 'BSB', 'Nicodemus, who had previously come to Jesus at night, also brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about seventy-five pounds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.40', 'BSB', 'So they took the body of Jesus and wrapped it in linen cloths with the spices, according to the Jewish burial custom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.41', 'BSB', 'Now there was a garden in the place where Jesus was crucified, and in the garden a new tomb in which no one had yet been laid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.19.42', 'BSB', 'And because it was the Jewish day of Preparation and the tomb was nearby, they placed Jesus there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.1', 'BSB', 'Early on the first day of the week, while it was still dark, Mary Magdalene went to the tomb and saw that the stone had been removed from the entrance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.2', 'BSB', 'So she came running to Simon Peter and the other disciple, the one whom Jesus loved. “They have taken the Lord out of the tomb,” she said, “and we do not know where they have put Him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.3', 'BSB', 'Then Peter and the other disciple set out for the tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.4', 'BSB', 'The two were running together, but the other disciple outran Peter and reached the tomb first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.5', 'BSB', 'He bent down and looked in at the linen cloths lying there, but he did not go in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.6', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter arrived just after him. He entered the tomb and saw the linen cloths lying there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.7', 'BSB', 'The cloth that had been around Jesus’ head was rolled up, lying separate from the linen cloths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.8', 'BSB', 'Then the other disciple, who had reached the tomb first, also went in. And he saw and believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.9', 'BSB', 'For they still did not understand from the Scripture that Jesus had to rise from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.10', 'BSB', 'Then the disciples returned to their homes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.11', 'BSB', 'But Mary stood outside the tomb weeping. And as she wept, she bent down to look into the tomb,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.12', 'BSB', 'and she saw two angels in white sitting where the body of Jesus had lain, one at the head and the other at the feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.13', 'BSB', '“Woman, why are you weeping?” they asked. “Because they have taken my Lord away,” she said, “and I do not know where they have put Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.14', 'BSB', 'When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing there; but she did not recognize that it was Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.15', 'BSB', '“Woman, why are you weeping?” Jesus asked. “Whom are you seeking?” Thinking He was the gardener, she said, “Sir, if you have carried Him off, tell me where you have put Him, and I will get Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.16', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to her, “Mary.” She turned and said to Him in Hebrew, “Rabboni!” (which means “Teacher”).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.17', 'BSB', '“Do not cling to Me,” Jesus said, “for I have not yet ascended to the Father. But go and tell My brothers, ‘I am ascending to My Father and your Father, to My God and your God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.18', 'BSB', 'Mary Magdalene went and announced to the disciples, “I have seen the Lord!” And she told them what He had said to her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.19', 'BSB', 'It was the first day of the week, and that very evening, while the disciples were together with the doors locked for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood among them. “Peace be with you!” He said to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.20', 'BSB', 'After He had said this, He showed them His hands and His side. The disciples rejoiced when they saw the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.21', 'BSB', 'Again Jesus said to them, “Peace be with you. As the Father has sent Me, so also I am sending you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.22', 'BSB', 'When He had said this, He breathed on them and said, “Receive the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.23', 'BSB', 'If you forgive anyone his sins, they are forgiven; if you withhold forgiveness from anyone, it is withheld.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.24', 'BSB', 'Now Thomas called Didymus, one of the Twelve, was not with the disciples when Jesus came.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.25', 'BSB', 'So the other disciples told him, “We have seen the Lord!” But he replied, “Unless I see the nail marks in His hands, and put my finger where the nails have been, and put my hand into His side, I will never believe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.26', 'BSB', 'Eight days later, His disciples were once again inside with the doors locked, and Thomas was with them. Jesus came and stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.27', 'BSB', 'Then Jesus said to Thomas, “Put your finger here and look at My hands. Reach out your hand and put it into My side. Stop doubting and believe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.28', 'BSB', 'Thomas replied, “My Lord and my God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.29', 'BSB', 'Jesus said to him, “Because you have seen Me, you have believed; blessed are those who have not seen and yet have believed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.30', 'BSB', 'Jesus performed many other signs in the presence of His disciples, which are not written in this book.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.20.31', 'BSB', 'But these are written so that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that by believing you may have life in His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.1', 'BSB', 'Later, by the Sea of Tiberias, Jesus again revealed Himself to the disciples. He made Himself known in this way:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.2', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael from Cana in Galilee, the sons of Zebedee, and two other disciples were together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.3', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter told them, “I am going fishing.” “We will go with you,” they said. So they went out and got into the boat, but caught nothing that night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.4', 'BSB', 'Early in the morning, Jesus stood on the shore, but the disciples did not recognize that it was Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.5', 'BSB', 'So He called out to them, “Children, do you have any fish?” “No,” they answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.6', 'BSB', 'He told them, “Cast the net on the right side of the boat, and you will find some.” So they cast it there, and they were unable to haul it in because of the great number of fish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.7', 'BSB', 'Then the disciple whom Jesus loved said to Peter, “It is the Lord!” As soon as Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he put on his outer garment (for he had removed it) and jumped into the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.8', 'BSB', 'The other disciples came ashore in the boat. They dragged in the net full of fish, for they were not far from land, only about a hundred yards.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.9', 'BSB', 'When they landed, they saw a charcoal fire there with fish on it, and some bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.10', 'BSB', 'Jesus told them, “Bring some of the fish you have just caught.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.11', 'BSB', 'So Simon Peter went aboard and dragged the net ashore. It was full of large fish, 153, but even with so many, the net was not torn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.12', 'BSB', '“Come, have breakfast,” Jesus said to them. None of the disciples dared to ask Him, “Who are You?” They knew it was the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.13', 'BSB', 'Jesus came and took the bread and gave it to them, and He did the same with the fish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.14', 'BSB', 'This was now the third time that Jesus appeared to the disciples after He was raised from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.15', 'BSB', 'When they had finished eating, Jesus asked Simon Peter, “Simon son of John, do you love Me more than these?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus replied, “Feed My lambs.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.16', 'BSB', 'Jesus asked a second time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” “Yes, Lord,” he answered, “You know I love You.” Jesus told him, “Shepherd My sheep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.17', 'BSB', 'Jesus asked a third time, “Simon son of John, do you love Me?” Peter was deeply hurt that Jesus had asked him a third time, “Do you love Me?” “Lord, You know all things,” he replied. “You know I love You.” Jesus said to him, “Feed My sheep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.18', 'BSB', 'Truly, truly, I tell you, when you were young, you dressed yourself and walked where you wanted; but when you are old, you will stretch out your hands, and someone else will dress you and lead you where you do not want to go.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.19', 'BSB', 'Jesus said this to indicate the kind of death by which Peter would glorify God. And after He had said this, He told him, “Follow Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.20', 'BSB', 'Peter turned and saw the disciple whom Jesus loved following them. He was the one who had leaned back against Jesus at the supper to ask, “Lord, who is going to betray You?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.21', 'BSB', 'When Peter saw him, he asked, “Lord, what about him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.22', 'BSB', 'Jesus answered, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you? You follow Me!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.23', 'BSB', 'Because of this, the rumor spread among the brothers that this disciple would not die. However, Jesus did not say that he would not die, but only, “If I want him to remain until I return, what is that to you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.24', 'BSB', 'This is the disciple who testifies to these things and who has written them down. And we know that his testimony is true.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('John.21.25', 'BSB', 'There are many more things that Jesus did. If all of them were written down, I suppose that not even the world itself would have space for the books that would be written.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.1', 'BSB', 'In my first book, O Theophilus, I wrote about all that Jesus began to do and to teach,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.2', 'BSB', 'until the day He was taken up to heaven, after giving instructions through the Holy Spirit to the apostles He had chosen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.3', 'BSB', 'After His suffering, He presented Himself to them with many convincing proofs that He was alive. He appeared to them over a span of forty days and spoke about the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.4', 'BSB', 'And while they were gathered together, He commanded them: “Do not leave Jerusalem, but wait for the gift the Father promised, which you have heard Me discuss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.5', 'BSB', 'For John baptized with water, but in a few days you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.6', 'BSB', 'So when they came together, they asked Him, “Lord, will You at this time restore the kingdom to Israel?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.7', 'BSB', 'Jesus replied, “It is not for you to know times or seasons that the Father has fixed by His own authority.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.8', 'BSB', 'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes upon you, and you will be My witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.9', 'BSB', 'After He had said this, they watched as He was taken up, and a cloud hid Him from their sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.10', 'BSB', 'They were looking intently into the sky as He was going, when suddenly two men dressed in white stood beside them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.11', 'BSB', '“Men of Galilee,” they said, “why do you stand here looking into the sky? This same Jesus, who has been taken from you into heaven, will come back in the same way you have seen Him go into heaven.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.12', 'BSB', 'Then they returned to Jerusalem from the Mount of Olives, which is near the city, a Sabbath day’s journey away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.13', 'BSB', 'When they arrived, they went to the upper room where they were staying: Peter and John, James and Andrew, Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas son of James.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.14', 'BSB', 'With one accord they all continued in prayer, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.15', 'BSB', 'In those days Peter stood up among the brothers (a gathering of about a hundred and twenty) and said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.16', 'BSB', '“Brothers, the Scripture had to be fulfilled which the Holy Spirit foretold through the mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide for those who arrested Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.17', 'BSB', 'He was one of our number and shared in this ministry.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.18', 'BSB', '(Now with the reward for his wickedness Judas bought a field; there he fell headlong and burst open in the middle, and all his intestines spilled out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.19', 'BSB', 'This became known to all who lived in Jerusalem, so they called that field in their own language Akeldama, that is, Field of Blood.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.20', 'BSB', '“For it is written in the book of Psalms: ‘May his place be deserted; let there be no one to dwell in it,’ and, ‘May another take his position.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore it is necessary to choose one of the men who have accompanied us the whole time the Lord Jesus went in and out among us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.22', 'BSB', 'beginning from John’s baptism until the day Jesus was taken up from us. For one of these must become a witness with us of His resurrection.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.23', 'BSB', 'So they proposed two men: Joseph called Barsabbas (also known as Justus) and Matthias.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.24', 'BSB', 'And they prayed, “Lord, You know everyone’s heart. Show us which of these two You have chosen', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.25', 'BSB', 'to take up this ministry and apostleship, which Judas abandoned to go to his rightful place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.1.26', 'BSB', 'Then they cast lots, and the lot fell to Matthias; so he was added to the eleven apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.1', 'BSB', 'When the day of Pentecost came, they were all together in one place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.2', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a sound like a mighty rushing wind came from heaven and filled the whole house where they were sitting.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.3', 'BSB', 'They saw tongues like flames of fire that separated and came to rest on each of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.4', 'BSB', 'And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit enabled them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.5', 'BSB', 'Now there were dwelling in Jerusalem God-fearing Jews from every nation under heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.6', 'BSB', 'And when this sound rang out, a crowd came together in bewilderment, because each one heard them speaking his own language.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.7', 'BSB', 'Astounded and amazed, they asked, “Are not all these men who are speaking Galileans?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.8', 'BSB', 'How is it then that each of us hears them in his own native language?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.9', 'BSB', 'Parthians, Medes, and Elamites; residents of Mesopotamia, Judea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.10', 'BSB', 'Phrygia and Pamphylia, Egypt and the parts of Libya near Cyrene; visitors from Rome,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.11', 'BSB', 'both Jews and converts to Judaism; Cretans and Arabs—we hear them declaring the wonders of God in our own tongues!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.12', 'BSB', 'Astounded and perplexed, they asked one another, “What does this mean?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.13', 'BSB', 'But others mocked them and said, “They are drunk on new wine!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.14', 'BSB', 'Then Peter stood up with the Eleven, lifted up his voice, and addressed the crowd: “Men of Judea and all who dwell in Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen carefully to my words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.15', 'BSB', 'These men are not drunk, as you suppose. It is only the third hour of the day!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.16', 'BSB', 'No, this is what was spoken by the prophet Joel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.17', 'BSB', '‘In the last days, God says, I will pour out My Spirit on all people. Your sons and daughters will prophesy, your young men will see visions, your old men will dream dreams.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.18', 'BSB', 'Even on My menservants and maidservants I will pour out My Spirit in those days, and they will prophesy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.19', 'BSB', 'I will show wonders in the heavens above and signs on the earth below, blood and fire and billows of smoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.20', 'BSB', 'The sun will be turned to darkness, and the moon to blood, before the coming of the great and glorious Day of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.21', 'BSB', 'And everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.22', 'BSB', 'Men of Israel, listen to this message: Jesus of Nazareth was a man certified by God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs, which God did among you through Him, as you yourselves know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.23', 'BSB', 'He was delivered up by God’s set plan and foreknowledge, and you, by the hands of the lawless, put Him to death by nailing Him to the cross.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.24', 'BSB', 'But God raised Him from the dead, releasing Him from the agony of death, because it was impossible for Him to be held in its clutches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.25', 'BSB', 'David says about Him: ‘I saw the Lord always before me; because He is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.26', 'BSB', 'Therefore my heart is glad and my tongue rejoices; my body also will dwell in hope,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.27', 'BSB', 'because You will not abandon my soul to Hades, nor will You let Your Holy One see decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.28', 'BSB', 'You have made known to me the paths of life; You will fill me with joy in Your presence.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.29', 'BSB', 'Brothers, I can tell you with confidence that the patriarch David died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.30', 'BSB', 'But he was a prophet and knew that God had promised him on oath that He would place one of his descendants on his throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.31', 'BSB', 'Foreseeing this, David spoke about the resurrection of the Christ, that He was not abandoned to Hades, nor did His body see decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.32', 'BSB', 'God has raised this Jesus to life, to which we are all witnesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.33', 'BSB', 'Exalted, then, to the right hand of God, He has received from the Father the promised Holy Spirit and has poured out what you now see and hear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.34', 'BSB', 'For David did not ascend into heaven, but he himself says: ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at My right hand', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.35', 'BSB', 'until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet.”’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.36', 'BSB', 'Therefore let all Israel know with certainty that God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Christ!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.37', 'BSB', 'When the people heard this, they were cut to the heart and asked Peter and the other apostles, “Brothers, what shall we do?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.38', 'BSB', 'Peter replied, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.39', 'BSB', 'This promise belongs to you and your children and to all who are far off—to all whom the Lord our God will call to Himself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.40', 'BSB', 'With many other words he testified, and he urged them, “Be saved from this corrupt generation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.41', 'BSB', 'Those who embraced his message were baptized, and about three thousand were added to the believers that day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.42', 'BSB', 'They devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching and to the fellowship, to the breaking of bread and to prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.43', 'BSB', 'A sense of awe came over everyone, and the apostles performed many wonders and signs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.44', 'BSB', 'All the believers were together and had everything in common.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.45', 'BSB', 'Selling their possessions and goods, they shared with anyone who was in need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.46', 'BSB', 'With one accord they continued to meet daily in the temple courts and to break bread from house to house, sharing their meals with gladness and sincerity of heart,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.2.47', 'BSB', 'praising God and enjoying the favor of all the people. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.1', 'BSB', 'One afternoon Peter and John were going up to the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.2', 'BSB', 'And a man who was lame from birth was being carried to the temple gate called Beautiful, where he was put every day to beg from those entering the temple courts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.3', 'BSB', 'When he saw Peter and John about to enter, he asked them for money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.4', 'BSB', 'Peter looked directly at him, as did John. “Look at us!” said Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.5', 'BSB', 'So the man gave them his attention, expecting to receive something from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.6', 'BSB', 'But Peter said, “Silver or gold I do not have, but what I have I give you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.7', 'BSB', 'Taking him by the right hand, Peter helped him up, and at once the man’s feet and ankles were made strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.8', 'BSB', 'He sprang to his feet and began to walk. Then he went with them into the temple courts, walking and leaping and praising God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.9', 'BSB', 'When all the people saw him walking and praising God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.10', 'BSB', 'they recognized him as the man who used to sit begging at the Beautiful Gate of the temple, and they were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.11', 'BSB', 'While the man clung to Peter and John, all the people were astonished and ran to them in the walkway called Solomon’s Colonnade.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.12', 'BSB', 'And when Peter saw this, he addressed the people: “Men of Israel, why are you surprised by this? Why do you stare at us as if by our own power or godliness we had made this man walk?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.13', 'BSB', 'The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified His servant Jesus. You handed Him over and rejected Him before Pilate, even though he had decided to release Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.14', 'BSB', 'You rejected the Holy and Righteous One and asked that a murderer be released to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.15', 'BSB', 'You killed the Author of life, but God raised Him from the dead, and we are witnesses of the fact.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.16', 'BSB', 'By faith in the name of Jesus, this man whom you see and know has been made strong. It is Jesus’ name and the faith that comes through Him that has given him this complete healing in your presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.17', 'BSB', 'And now, brothers, I know that you acted in ignorance, as did your leaders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.18', 'BSB', 'But in this way God has fulfilled what He foretold through all the prophets, saying that His Christ would suffer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.19', 'BSB', 'Repent, then, and turn back, so that your sins may be wiped away,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.20', 'BSB', 'that times of refreshing may come from the presence of the Lord, and that He may send Jesus, the Christ, who has been appointed for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.21', 'BSB', 'Heaven must take Him in until the time comes for the restoration of all things, which God announced long ago through His holy prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.22', 'BSB', 'For Moses said, ‘The Lord your God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers. You must listen to Him in everything He tells you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.23', 'BSB', 'Everyone who does not listen to Him will be completely cut off from among his people.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.24', 'BSB', 'Indeed, all the prophets from Samuel on, as many as have spoken, have proclaimed these days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.25', 'BSB', 'And you are sons of the prophets and of the covenant God made with your fathers when He said to Abraham, ‘Through your offspring all the families of the earth will be blessed.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.3.26', 'BSB', 'When God raised up His Servant, He sent Him first to you to bless you by turning each of you from your wicked ways.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.1', 'BSB', 'While Peter and John were speaking to the people, the priests and the captain of the temple guard and the Sadducees came up to them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.2', 'BSB', 'greatly disturbed that they were teaching the people and proclaiming in Jesus the resurrection of the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.3', 'BSB', 'They seized Peter and John, and because it was evening, they put them in custody until the next day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.4', 'BSB', 'But many who heard the message believed, and the number of men grew to about five thousand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.5', 'BSB', 'The next day the rulers, elders, and scribes assembled in Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.6', 'BSB', 'along with Annas the high priest, Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and many others from the high priest’s family.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.7', 'BSB', 'They had Peter and John brought in and began to question them: “By what power or what name did you do this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.8', 'BSB', 'Then Peter, filled with the Holy Spirit, said to them, “Rulers and elders of the people!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.9', 'BSB', 'If we are being examined today about a kind service to a man who was lame, to determine how he was healed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.10', 'BSB', 'then let this be known to all of you and to all the people of Israel: It is by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified but whom God raised from the dead, that this man stands before you healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.11', 'BSB', 'This Jesus is ‘the stone you builders rejected, which has become the cornerstone.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.12', 'BSB', 'Salvation exists in no one else, for there is no other name under heaven given to men by which we must be saved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.13', 'BSB', 'When they saw the boldness of Peter and John and realized that they were unschooled, ordinary men, they marveled and took note that these men had been with Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.14', 'BSB', 'And seeing the man who had been healed standing there with them, they had nothing to say in response.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.15', 'BSB', 'So they ordered them to leave the Sanhedrin and then conferred together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.16', 'BSB', '“What shall we do with these men?” they asked. “It is clear to everyone living in Jerusalem that a remarkable miracle has occurred through them, and we cannot deny it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.17', 'BSB', 'But to keep this message from spreading any further among the people, we must warn them not to speak to anyone in this name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.18', 'BSB', 'Then they called them in again and commanded them not to speak or teach at all in the name of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.19', 'BSB', 'But Peter and John replied, “Judge for yourselves whether it is right in God’s sight to listen to you rather than God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.20', 'BSB', 'For we cannot stop speaking about what we have seen and heard.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.21', 'BSB', 'After further threats they let them go. They could not find a way to punish them, because all the people were glorifying God for what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.22', 'BSB', 'For the man who was miraculously healed was over forty years old.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.23', 'BSB', 'On their release, Peter and John returned to their own people and reported everything that the chief priests and elders had said to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.24', 'BSB', 'When the believers heard this, they lifted up their voices to God with one accord. “Sovereign Lord,” they said, “You made the heaven and the earth and the sea and everything in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.25', 'BSB', 'You spoke by the Holy Spirit through the mouth of Your servant, our father David: ‘Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.26', 'BSB', 'The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together against the Lord and against His Anointed One.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.27', 'BSB', 'In fact, this is the very city where Herod and Pontius Pilate conspired with the Gentiles and the people of Israel against Your holy servant Jesus, whom You anointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.28', 'BSB', 'They carried out what Your hand and will had decided beforehand would happen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.29', 'BSB', 'And now, Lord, consider their threats, and enable Your servants to speak Your word with complete boldness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.30', 'BSB', 'as You stretch out Your hand to heal and perform signs and wonders through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.31', 'BSB', 'After they had prayed, their meeting place was shaken, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and spoke the word of God boldly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.32', 'BSB', 'The multitude of believers was one in heart and soul. No one claimed that any of his possessions was his own, but they shared everything they owned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.33', 'BSB', 'With great power the apostles continued to give their testimony about the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. And abundant grace was upon them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.34', 'BSB', 'There were no needy ones among them, because those who owned lands or houses would sell their property, bring the proceeds from the sales,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.35', 'BSB', 'and lay them at the apostles’ feet for distribution to anyone as he had need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.36', 'BSB', 'Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas (meaning Son of Encouragement),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.4.37', 'BSB', 'sold a field he owned, brought the money, and laid it at the apostles’ feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.1', 'BSB', 'Now a man named Ananias, together with his wife Sapphira, also sold a piece of property.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.2', 'BSB', 'With his wife’s full knowledge, he kept back some of the proceeds for himself, but brought a portion and laid it at the apostles’ feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.3', 'BSB', 'Then Peter said, “Ananias, how is it that Satan has filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and withhold some of the proceeds from the land?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.4', 'BSB', 'Did it not belong to you before it was sold? And after it was sold, was it not at your disposal? How could you conceive such a deed in your heart? You have not lied to men, but to God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.5', 'BSB', 'On hearing these words, Ananias fell down and died. And great fear came over all who heard what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.6', 'BSB', 'Then the young men stepped forward, wrapped up his body, and carried him out and buried him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.7', 'BSB', 'About three hours later his wife also came in, unaware of what had happened.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.8', 'BSB', '“Tell me,” said Peter, “is this the price you and your husband got for the land?” “Yes,” she answered, “that is the price.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.9', 'BSB', '“How could you agree to test the Spirit of the Lord?” Peter replied. “Look, the feet of the men who buried your husband are at the door, and they will carry you out also.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.10', 'BSB', 'At that instant she fell down at his feet and died. Then the young men came in and, finding her dead, carried her out and buried her beside her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.11', 'BSB', 'And great fear came over the whole church and all who heard about these events.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.12', 'BSB', 'The apostles performed many signs and wonders among the people, and with one accord the believers gathered together in Solomon’s Colonnade.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.13', 'BSB', 'Although the people regarded them highly, no one else dared to join them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.14', 'BSB', 'Yet more and more believers were brought to the Lord—large numbers of both men and women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.15', 'BSB', 'As a result, people brought the sick into the streets and laid them on cots and mats, so that at least Peter’s shadow might fall on some of them as he passed by.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.16', 'BSB', 'Crowds also gathered from the towns around Jerusalem, bringing the sick and those tormented by unclean spirits, and all of them were healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.17', 'BSB', 'Then the high priest and all his associates, who belonged to the party of the Sadducees, were filled with jealousy. They went out', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.18', 'BSB', 'and arrested the apostles and put them in the public jail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.19', 'BSB', 'But during the night an angel of the Lord opened the doors of the jail and brought them out, saying,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.20', 'BSB', '“Go, stand in the temple courts and tell the people the full message of this new life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.21', 'BSB', 'At daybreak the apostles entered the temple courts as they had been told and began to teach the people. When the high priest and his associates arrived, they convened the Sanhedrin —the full assembly of the elders of Israel—and sent to the jail for the apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.22', 'BSB', 'But on arriving at the jail, the officers did not find them there. So they returned with the report:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.23', 'BSB', '“We found the jail securely locked, with the guards posted at the doors; but when we opened them, we found no one inside.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.24', 'BSB', 'When the captain of the temple guard and the chief priests heard this account, they were perplexed as to what was happening.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.25', 'BSB', 'Then someone came in and announced, “Look, the men you put in jail are standing in the temple courts teaching the people!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.26', 'BSB', 'At that point, the captain went with the officers and brought the apostles—but not by force, for fear the people would stone them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.27', 'BSB', 'They brought them in and made them stand before the Sanhedrin, where the high priest interrogated them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.28', 'BSB', '“We gave you strict orders not to teach in this name,” he said. “Yet you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching and are determined to make us responsible for this man’s blood.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.29', 'BSB', 'But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.30', 'BSB', 'The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you had killed by hanging Him on a tree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.31', 'BSB', 'God exalted Him to His right hand as Prince and Savior, in order to grant repentance and forgiveness of sins to Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.32', 'BSB', 'We are witnesses of these things, and so is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.33', 'BSB', 'When the Council members heard this, they were enraged, and they resolved to put the apostles to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.34', 'BSB', 'But a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law who was honored by all the people, stood up in the Sanhedrin and ordered that the men be put outside for a short time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.35', 'BSB', '“Men of Israel,” he said, “consider carefully what you are about to do to these men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.36', 'BSB', 'Some time ago Theudas rose up, claiming to be somebody, and about four hundred men joined him. He was killed, all his followers were dispersed, and it all came to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.37', 'BSB', 'After him, Judas the Galilean appeared in the days of the census and drew away people after him. He too perished, and all his followers were scattered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.38', 'BSB', 'So in the present case I advise you: Leave these men alone. Let them go! For if their purpose or endeavor is of human origin, it will fail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.39', 'BSB', 'But if it is from God, you will not be able to stop them. You may even find yourselves fighting against God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.40', 'BSB', 'At this, they yielded to Gamaliel. They called the apostles in and had them flogged. Then they ordered them not to speak in the name of Jesus, and released them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.41', 'BSB', 'The apostles left the Sanhedrin, rejoicing that they had been counted worthy of suffering disgrace for the Name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.5.42', 'BSB', 'Every day, in the temple courts and from house to house, they did not stop teaching and proclaiming the good news that Jesus is the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.1', 'BSB', 'In those days when the disciples were increasing in number, the Grecian Jews among them began to grumble against the Hebraic Jews because their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution of food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.2', 'BSB', 'So the Twelve summoned all the disciples and said, “It is unacceptable for us to neglect the word of God in order to wait on tables.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, select from among you seven men confirmed to be full of the Spirit and wisdom. We will appoint this responsibility to them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.4', 'BSB', 'and will devote ourselves to prayer and to the ministry of the word.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.5', 'BSB', 'This proposal pleased the whole group. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit, as well as Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolas from Antioch, a convert to Judaism.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.6', 'BSB', 'They presented these seven to the apostles, who prayed and laid their hands on them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.7', 'BSB', 'So the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.8', 'BSB', 'Now Stephen, who was full of grace and power, was performing great wonders and signs among the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.9', 'BSB', 'But resistance arose from what was called the Synagogue of the Freedmen, including Cyrenians, Alexandrians, and men from the provinces of Cilicia and Asia. They began to argue with Stephen,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.10', 'BSB', 'but they could not stand up to his wisdom or the Spirit by whom he spoke.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.11', 'BSB', 'Then they prompted some men to say, “We heard Stephen speak words of blasphemy against Moses and against God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.12', 'BSB', 'So they stirred up the people, elders, and scribes and confronted Stephen. They seized him and brought him before the Sanhedrin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.13', 'BSB', 'where they presented false witnesses who said, “This man never stops speaking against this holy place and against the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.14', 'BSB', 'For we have heard him say that Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place and change the customs that Moses handed down to us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.6.15', 'BSB', 'All who were sitting in the Sanhedrin looked intently at Stephen, and they saw that his face was like the face of an angel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.1', 'BSB', 'Then the high priest asked Stephen, “Are these charges true?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.2', 'BSB', 'And Stephen declared: “Brothers and fathers, listen to me! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham while he was still in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.3', 'BSB', 'and told him, ‘Leave your country and your kindred and go to the land I will show you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.4', 'BSB', 'So Abraham left the land of the Chaldeans and settled in Haran. After his father died, God brought him out of that place and into this land where you are now living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.5', 'BSB', 'He gave him no inheritance here, not even a foot of ground. But God promised to give possession of the land to Abraham and his descendants, even though he did not yet have a child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.6', 'BSB', 'God told him that his descendants would be foreigners in a strange land, and that they would be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.7', 'BSB', '‘But I will punish the nation that enslaves them,’ God said, ‘and afterward they will come forth and worship Me in this place.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.8', 'BSB', 'Then God gave Abraham the covenant of circumcision, and Abraham became the father of Isaac and circumcised him on the eighth day. And Isaac became the father of Jacob, and Jacob of the twelve patriarchs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.9', 'BSB', 'Because the patriarchs were jealous of Joseph, they sold him as a slave into Egypt. But God was with him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.10', 'BSB', 'and rescued him from all his troubles. He granted Joseph favor and wisdom in the sight of Pharaoh king of Egypt, who appointed him ruler over Egypt and all his household.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.11', 'BSB', 'Then famine and great suffering swept across Egypt and Canaan, and our fathers could not find food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.12', 'BSB', 'When Jacob heard that there was grain in Egypt, he sent our fathers on their first visit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.13', 'BSB', 'On their second visit, Joseph revealed his identity to his brothers, and his family became known to Pharaoh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.14', 'BSB', 'Then Joseph sent for his father Jacob and all his relatives, seventy-five in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.15', 'BSB', 'So Jacob went down to Egypt, where he and our fathers died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.16', 'BSB', 'Their bones were carried back to Shechem and placed in the tomb that Abraham had bought from the sons of Hamor at Shechem for a price he paid in silver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.17', 'BSB', 'As the time drew near for God to fulfill His promise to Abraham, our people in Egypt increased greatly in number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.18', 'BSB', 'Then another king, who knew nothing of Joseph, arose over Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.19', 'BSB', 'He exploited our people and oppressed our fathers, forcing them to abandon their infants so they would die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.20', 'BSB', 'At that time Moses was born, and he was beautiful in the sight of God. For three months he was nurtured in his father’s house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.21', 'BSB', 'When he was set outside, Pharaoh’s daughter took him and brought him up as her own son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.22', 'BSB', 'So Moses was educated in all the wisdom of the Egyptians and was powerful in speech and action.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.23', 'BSB', 'When Moses was forty years old, he decided to visit his brothers, the children of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.24', 'BSB', 'And when he saw one of them being mistreated, Moses went to his defense and avenged him by striking down the Egyptian who was oppressing him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.25', 'BSB', 'He assumed his brothers would understand that God was using him to deliver them, but they did not.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.26', 'BSB', 'The next day he came upon two Israelites who were fighting, and he tried to reconcile them, saying, ‘Men, you are brothers. Why are you mistreating each other?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.27', 'BSB', 'But the man who was abusing his neighbor pushed Moses aside and said, ‘Who made you ruler and judge over us?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.28', 'BSB', 'Do you want to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.29', 'BSB', 'At this remark, Moses fled to the land of Midian, where he lived as a foreigner and had two sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.30', 'BSB', 'After forty years had passed, an angel appeared to Moses in the flames of a burning bush in the desert near Mount Sinai.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.31', 'BSB', 'When Moses saw it, he marveled at the sight. As he approached to look more closely, the voice of the Lord came to him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.32', 'BSB', '‘I am the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.’ Moses trembled with fear and did not dare to look.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.33', 'BSB', 'Then the Lord said to him, ‘Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.34', 'BSB', 'I have indeed seen the oppression of My people in Egypt. I have heard their groaning and have come down to deliver them. Now come, I will send you back to Egypt.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.35', 'BSB', 'This Moses, whom they had rejected with the words, ‘Who made you ruler and judge?’ is the one whom God sent to be their ruler and redeemer through the angel who appeared to him in the bush.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.36', 'BSB', 'He led them out and performed wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, at the Red Sea, and for forty years in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.37', 'BSB', 'This is the same Moses who told the Israelites, ‘God will raise up for you a prophet like me from among your brothers.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.38', 'BSB', 'He was in the assembly in the wilderness with the angel who spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and with our fathers. And he received living words to pass on to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.39', 'BSB', 'But our fathers refused to obey him. Instead, they rejected him and in their hearts turned back to Egypt.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.40', 'BSB', 'They said to Aaron, ‘Make us gods who will go before us! As for this Moses who led us out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what has happened to him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.41', 'BSB', 'At that time they made a calf and offered a sacrifice to the idol, rejoicing in the works of their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.42', 'BSB', 'But God turned away from them and gave them over to the worship of the host of heaven, as it is written in the book of the prophets: ‘Did you bring Me sacrifices and offerings forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.43', 'BSB', 'You have taken along the tabernacle of Molech and the star of your god Rephan, the idols you made to worship. Therefore I will send you into exile beyond Babylon.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.44', 'BSB', 'Our fathers had the tabernacle of the Testimony with them in the wilderness. It was constructed exactly as God had directed Moses, according to the pattern he had seen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.45', 'BSB', 'And our fathers who received it brought it in with Joshua when they dispossessed the nations God drove out before them. It remained until the time of David,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.46', 'BSB', 'who found favor in the sight of God and asked to provide a dwelling place for the God of Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.47', 'BSB', 'But it was Solomon who built the house for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.48', 'BSB', 'However, the Most High does not dwell in houses made by human hands. As the prophet says:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.49', 'BSB', '‘Heaven is My throne and the earth is My footstool. What kind of house will you build for Me, says the Lord, or where will My place of repose be?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.50', 'BSB', 'Has not My hand made all these things?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.51', 'BSB', 'You stiff-necked people with uncircumcised hearts and ears! You always resist the Holy Spirit, just as your fathers did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.52', 'BSB', 'Which of the prophets did your fathers fail to persecute? They even killed those who foretold the coming of the Righteous One. And now you are His betrayers and murderers—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.53', 'BSB', 'you who received the law ordained by angels, yet have not kept it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.54', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, the members of the Sanhedrin were enraged, and they gnashed their teeth at him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.55', 'BSB', 'But Stephen, full of the Holy Spirit, looked intently into heaven and saw the glory of God and Jesus standing at the right hand of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.56', 'BSB', '“Look,” he said, “I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.57', 'BSB', 'At this they covered their ears, cried out in a loud voice, and rushed together at him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.58', 'BSB', 'They dragged him out of the city and began to stone him. Meanwhile the witnesses laid their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.59', 'BSB', 'While they were stoning him, Stephen appealed, “Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.7.60', 'BSB', 'Falling on his knees, he cried out in a loud voice, “Lord, do not hold this sin against them.” And when he had said this, he fell asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.1', 'BSB', 'And Saul was there, giving approval to Stephen’s death. On that day a great persecution broke out against the church in Jerusalem, and all except the apostles were scattered throughout Judea and Samaria.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.2', 'BSB', 'God-fearing men buried Stephen and mourned deeply over him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.3', 'BSB', 'But Saul began to destroy the church. Going from house to house, he dragged off men and women and put them in prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.4', 'BSB', 'Those who had been scattered preached the word wherever they went.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.5', 'BSB', 'Philip went down to a city in Samaria and proclaimed the Christ to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.6', 'BSB', 'The crowds gave their undivided attention to Philip’s message and to the signs they saw him perform.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.7', 'BSB', 'With loud shrieks, unclean spirits came out of many who were possessed, and many of the paralyzed and lame were healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.8', 'BSB', 'So there was great joy in that city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.9', 'BSB', 'Prior to that time, a man named Simon had practiced sorcery in the city and astounded the people of Samaria. He claimed to be someone great,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.10', 'BSB', 'and all the people, from the least to the greatest, heeded his words and said, “This man is the divine power called the Great Power.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.11', 'BSB', 'They paid close attention to him because he had astounded them for a long time with his sorcery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.12', 'BSB', 'But when they believed Philip as he preached the gospel of the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.13', 'BSB', 'Even Simon himself believed and was baptized. He followed Philip closely and was astounded by the great signs and miracles he observed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.14', 'BSB', 'When the apostles in Jerusalem heard that Samaria had received the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.15', 'BSB', 'On their arrival, they prayed for them to receive the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.16', 'BSB', 'For the Holy Spirit had not yet fallen upon any of them; they had simply been baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.17', 'BSB', 'Then Peter and John laid their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.18', 'BSB', 'When Simon saw that the Spirit was given through the laying on of the apostles’ hands, he offered them money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.19', 'BSB', '“Give me this power as well,” he said, “so that everyone on whom I lay my hands may receive the Holy Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.20', 'BSB', 'But Peter replied, “May your silver perish with you, because you thought you could buy the gift of God with money!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.21', 'BSB', 'You have no part or share in our ministry, because your heart is not right before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.22', 'BSB', 'Repent, therefore, of your wickedness, and pray to the Lord. Perhaps He will forgive you for the intent of your heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.23', 'BSB', 'For I see that you are poisoned by bitterness and captive to iniquity.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.24', 'BSB', 'Then Simon answered, “Pray to the Lord for me, so that nothing you have said may happen to me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.25', 'BSB', 'And after Peter and John had testified and spoken the word of the Lord, they returned to Jerusalem, preaching the gospel in many of the Samaritan villages.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.26', 'BSB', 'Now an angel of the Lord said to Philip, “Get up and go south to the desert road that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.27', 'BSB', 'So he started out, and on his way he met an Ethiopian eunuch, a court official in charge of the entire treasury of Candace, queen of the Ethiopians. He had gone to Jerusalem to worship,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.28', 'BSB', 'and on his return was sitting in his chariot reading Isaiah the prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.29', 'BSB', 'The Spirit said to Philip, “Go over to that chariot and stay by it.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.30', 'BSB', 'So Philip ran up and heard the man reading Isaiah the prophet. “Do you understand what you are reading?” Philip asked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.31', 'BSB', '“How can I,” he said, “unless someone guides me?” And he invited Philip to come up and sit with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.32', 'BSB', 'The eunuch was reading this passage of Scripture: “He was led like a sheep to the slaughter, and as a lamb before the shearer is silent, so He did not open His mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.33', 'BSB', 'In His humiliation He was deprived of justice. Who can recount His descendants? For His life was removed from the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.34', 'BSB', '“Tell me,” said the eunuch, “who is the prophet talking about, himself or someone else?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.35', 'BSB', 'Then Philip began with this very Scripture and told him the good news about Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.36', 'BSB', 'As they traveled along the road and came to some water, the eunuch said, “Look, here is water! What is there to prevent me from being baptized?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.38', 'BSB', 'And he gave orders to stop the chariot. Then both Philip and the eunuch went down into the water, and Philip baptized him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.39', 'BSB', 'When they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord carried Philip away, and the eunuch saw him no more, but went on his way rejoicing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.8.40', 'BSB', 'But Philip appeared at Azotus and traveled through that region, preaching the gospel in all the towns until he came to Caesarea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.1', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, Saul was still breathing out murderous threats against the disciples of the Lord. He approached the high priest', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.2', 'BSB', 'and requested letters to the synagogues in Damascus, so that if he found any men or women belonging to the Way, he could bring them as prisoners to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.3', 'BSB', 'As Saul drew near to Damascus on his journey, suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.4', 'BSB', 'He fell to the ground and heard a voice say to him, “Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.5', 'BSB', '“Who are You, Lord?” Saul asked. “I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,” He replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.6', 'BSB', '“Now get up and go into the city, and you will be told what you must do.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.7', 'BSB', 'The men traveling with Saul stood there speechless. They heard the voice but did not see anyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.8', 'BSB', 'Saul got up from the ground, but when he opened his eyes he could not see a thing. So they led him by the hand into Damascus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.9', 'BSB', 'For three days he was without sight, and he did not eat or drink anything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.10', 'BSB', 'In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord spoke to him in a vision, “Ananias!” “Here I am, Lord,” he answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.11', 'BSB', '“Get up!” the Lord told him. “Go to the house of Judas on Straight Street and ask for a man from Tarsus named Saul, for he is praying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.12', 'BSB', 'In a vision he has seen a man named Ananias come and place his hands on him to restore his sight.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.13', 'BSB', 'But Ananias answered, “Lord, many people have told me about this man and all the harm he has done to Your saints in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.14', 'BSB', 'And now he is here with authority from the chief priests to arrest all who call on Your name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.15', 'BSB', '“Go!” said the Lord. “This man is My chosen instrument to carry My name before the Gentiles and their kings, and before the people of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.16', 'BSB', 'I will show him how much he must suffer for My name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.17', 'BSB', 'So Ananias went to the house, and when he arrived, he placed his hands on Saul. “Brother Saul,” he said, “the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road as you were coming here, has sent me so that you may see again and be filled with the Holy Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.18', 'BSB', 'At that instant, something like scales fell from Saul’s eyes, and his sight was restored. He got up and was baptized,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.19', 'BSB', 'and after taking some food, he regained his strength. And he spent several days with the disciples in Damascus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.20', 'BSB', 'Saul promptly began to proclaim Jesus in the synagogues, declaring, “He is the Son of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.21', 'BSB', 'All who heard him were astounded and asked, “Isn’t this the man who wreaked havoc in Jerusalem on those who call on this name? And hasn’t he come here to take them as prisoners to the chief priests?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.22', 'BSB', 'But Saul was empowered all the more, and he confounded the Jews living in Damascus by proving that Jesus is the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.23', 'BSB', 'After many days had passed, the Jews conspired to kill him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.24', 'BSB', 'but Saul learned of their plot. Day and night they watched the city gates in order to kill him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.25', 'BSB', 'One night, however, his disciples took him and lowered him in a basket through a window in the wall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.26', 'BSB', 'When Saul arrived in Jerusalem, he tried to join the disciples, but they were all afraid of him, not believing that he was a disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.27', 'BSB', 'Then Barnabas brought him to the apostles and described how Saul had seen the Lord, who spoke to him on the road to Damascus, and how Saul had spoken boldly in that city in the name of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.28', 'BSB', 'So Saul stayed with them, moving about freely in Jerusalem and speaking boldly in the name of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.29', 'BSB', 'He talked and debated with the Grecian Jews, but they tried to kill him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.30', 'BSB', 'When the brothers learned of this, they took him down to Caesarea and sent him off to Tarsus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.31', 'BSB', 'Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria experienced a time of peace. It grew in strength and numbers, living in the fear of the Lord and the encouragement of the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.32', 'BSB', 'As Peter traveled throughout the area, he went to visit the saints in Lydda.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.33', 'BSB', 'There he found a man named Aeneas, who had been paralyzed and bedridden for eight years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.34', 'BSB', '“Aeneas,” Peter said to him, “Jesus Christ heals you! Get up and put away your mat.” Immediately Aeneas got up,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.35', 'BSB', 'and all who lived in Lydda and Sharon saw him and turned to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.36', 'BSB', 'In Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (which is translated as Dorcas), who was always occupied with works of kindness and charity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.37', 'BSB', 'At that time, however, she became sick and died, and her body was washed and placed in an upper room.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.38', 'BSB', 'Since Lydda was near Joppa, the disciples heard that Peter was there and sent two men to urge him, “Come to us without delay.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.39', 'BSB', 'So Peter got up and went with them. On his arrival, they took him to the upper room. All the widows stood around him, weeping and showing him the tunics and other clothing that Dorcas had made while she was still with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.40', 'BSB', 'Then Peter sent them all out of the room. He knelt down and prayed, and turning toward her body, he said, “Tabitha, get up!” She opened her eyes, and seeing Peter, she sat up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.41', 'BSB', 'Peter took her by the hand and helped her up. Then he called the saints and widows and presented her to them alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.42', 'BSB', 'This became known all over Joppa, and many people believed in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.9.43', 'BSB', 'And Peter stayed for several days in Joppa with a tanner named Simon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.1', 'BSB', 'At Caesarea there was a man named Cornelius, a centurion in what was called the Italian Regiment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.2', 'BSB', 'He and all his household were devout and God-fearing. He gave generously to the people and prayed to God regularly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.3', 'BSB', 'One day at about the ninth hour, he had a clear vision of an angel of God who came to him and said, “Cornelius!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.4', 'BSB', 'Cornelius stared at him in fear and asked, “What is it, Lord?” The angel answered, “Your prayers and gifts to the poor have ascended as a memorial offering before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.5', 'BSB', 'Now send men to Joppa to call for a man named Simon who is called Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.6', 'BSB', 'He is staying with Simon the tanner, whose house is by the sea.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.7', 'BSB', 'When the angel who spoke to him had gone, Cornelius called two of his servants and a devout soldier from among his attendants.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.8', 'BSB', 'He explained what had happened and sent them to Joppa.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.9', 'BSB', 'The next day at about the sixth hour, as the men were approaching the city on their journey, Peter went up on the roof to pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.10', 'BSB', 'He became hungry and wanted something to eat, but while the meal was being prepared, he fell into a trance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.11', 'BSB', 'He saw heaven open and something like a large sheet being let down to earth by its four corners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.12', 'BSB', 'It contained all kinds of four-footed animals and reptiles of the earth, as well as birds of the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.13', 'BSB', 'Then a voice said to him: “Get up, Peter, kill and eat!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.14', 'BSB', '“No, Lord!” Peter answered. “I have never eaten anything impure or unclean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.15', 'BSB', 'The voice spoke to him a second time: “Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.16', 'BSB', 'This happened three times, and all at once the sheet was taken back up into heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.17', 'BSB', 'While Peter was puzzling over the meaning of the vision, the men sent by Cornelius found Simon’s house and approached the gate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.18', 'BSB', 'They called out to ask if Simon called Peter was staying there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.19', 'BSB', 'As Peter continued to reflect on the vision, the Spirit said to him, “Behold, three men are looking for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.20', 'BSB', 'So get up! Go downstairs and accompany them without hesitation, because I have sent them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.21', 'BSB', 'So Peter went down to the men and said, “Here am I, the one you are looking for. Why have you come?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.22', 'BSB', '“Cornelius the centurion has sent us,” they said. “He is a righteous and God-fearing man with a good reputation among the whole Jewish nation. A holy angel instructed him to request your presence in his home so he could hear a message from you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.23', 'BSB', 'So Peter invited them in as his guests. And the next day he got ready and went with them, accompanied by some of the brothers from Joppa.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.24', 'BSB', 'The following day he arrived in Caesarea, where Cornelius was expecting them and had called together his relatives and close friends.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.25', 'BSB', 'As Peter was about to enter, Cornelius met him and fell at his feet to worship him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.26', 'BSB', 'But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.27', 'BSB', 'As Peter talked with him, he went inside and found many people gathered together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.28', 'BSB', 'He said to them, “You know how unlawful it is for a Jew to associate with a foreigner or visit him. But God has shown me that I should not call any man impure or unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.29', 'BSB', 'So when I was invited, I came without objection. I ask, then, why have you sent for me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.30', 'BSB', 'Cornelius answered: “Four days ago I was in my house praying at this, the ninth hour. Suddenly a man in radiant clothing stood before me', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.31', 'BSB', 'and said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer has been heard, and your gifts to the poor have been remembered before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.32', 'BSB', 'Therefore send to Joppa for Simon, who is called Peter. He is a guest in the home of Simon the tanner, by the sea.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.33', 'BSB', 'So I sent for you immediately, and you were kind enough to come. Now then, we are all here in the presence of God to listen to everything the Lord has instructed you to tell us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.34', 'BSB', 'Then Peter began to speak: “I now truly understand that God does not show favoritism,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.35', 'BSB', 'but welcomes those from every nation who fear Him and do what is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.36', 'BSB', 'He has sent this message to the people of Israel, proclaiming the gospel of peace through Jesus Christ, who is Lord of all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.37', 'BSB', 'You yourselves know what has happened throughout Judea, beginning in Galilee with the baptism that John proclaimed:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.38', 'BSB', 'how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, and how Jesus went around doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, because God was with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.39', 'BSB', 'We are witnesses of all that He did, both in the land of the Jews and in Jerusalem. And although they put Him to death by hanging Him on a tree,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.40', 'BSB', 'God raised Him up on the third day and caused Him to be seen—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.41', 'BSB', 'not by all the people, but by the witnesses God had chosen beforehand, by us who ate and drank with Him after He rose from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.42', 'BSB', 'And He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that He is the One appointed by God to judge the living and the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.43', 'BSB', 'All the prophets testify about Him that everyone who believes in Him receives forgiveness of sins through His name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.44', 'BSB', 'While Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon all who heard his message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.45', 'BSB', 'All the circumcised believers who had accompanied Peter were astounded that the gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.46', 'BSB', 'For they heard them speaking in tongues and exalting God. Then Peter said,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.47', 'BSB', '“Can anyone withhold the water to baptize these people? They have received the Holy Spirit just as we have!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.10.48', 'BSB', 'So he ordered that they be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ. Then they asked him to stay for a few days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.1', 'BSB', 'The apostles and brothers throughout Judea soon heard that the Gentiles also had received the word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.2', 'BSB', 'So when Peter went up to Jerusalem, the circumcised believers took issue with him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.3', 'BSB', 'and said, “You visited uncircumcised men and ate with them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.4', 'BSB', 'But Peter began and explained to them the whole sequence of events:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.5', 'BSB', '“I was in the city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision of something like a large sheet being let down from heaven by its four corners, and it came right down to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.6', 'BSB', 'I looked at it closely and saw four-footed animals of the earth, wild beasts, reptiles, and birds of the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.7', 'BSB', 'Then I heard a voice saying to me, ‘Get up, Peter, kill and eat.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.8', 'BSB', '‘No, Lord,’ I said, ‘for nothing impure or unclean has ever entered my mouth.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.9', 'BSB', 'But the voice spoke from heaven a second time, ‘Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.10', 'BSB', 'This happened three times, and everything was drawn back up into heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.11', 'BSB', 'Just then three men sent to me from Caesarea stopped at the house where I was staying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.12', 'BSB', 'The Spirit told me to accompany them without hesitation. These six brothers also went with me, and we entered the man’s home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.13', 'BSB', 'He told us how he had seen an angel standing in his house and saying, ‘Send to Joppa for Simon who is called Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.14', 'BSB', 'He will convey to you a message by which you and all your household will be saved.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.15', 'BSB', 'As I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, just as He had fallen upon us at the beginning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.16', 'BSB', 'Then I remembered the word of the Lord, as He used to say, ‘John baptized with water, but you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.17', 'BSB', 'So if God gave them the same gift He gave us who believed in the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I to hinder the work of God?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.18', 'BSB', 'When they heard this, their objections were put to rest, and they glorified God, saying, “So then, God has granted even the Gentiles repentance unto life.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.19', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile those scattered by the persecution that began with Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, speaking the message only to Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.20', 'BSB', 'But some of them, men from Cyprus and Cyrene, went to Antioch and began speaking to the Greeks as well, proclaiming the good news about the Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.21', 'BSB', 'The hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number of people believed and turned to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.22', 'BSB', 'When news of this reached the ears of the church in Jerusalem, they sent Barnabas to Antioch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.23', 'BSB', 'When he arrived and saw the grace of God, he rejoiced and encouraged them all to abide in the Lord with all their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.24', 'BSB', 'Barnabas was a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and faith, and a great number of people were brought to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.25', 'BSB', 'Then Barnabas went to Tarsus to look for Saul,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.26', 'BSB', 'and when he found him, he brought him back to Antioch. So for a full year they met together with the church and taught large numbers of people. The disciples were first called Christians at Antioch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.27', 'BSB', 'In those days some prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.28', 'BSB', 'One of them named Agabus stood up and predicted through the Spirit that a great famine would sweep across the whole world. (This happened under Claudius.)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.29', 'BSB', 'So the disciples, each according to his ability, decided to send relief to the brothers living in Judea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.11.30', 'BSB', 'This they did, sending their gifts to the elders with Barnabas and Saul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.1', 'BSB', 'About that time, King Herod reached out to harm some who belonged to the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.2', 'BSB', 'He had James, the brother of John, put to death with the sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.3', 'BSB', 'And seeing that this pleased the Jews, Herod proceeded to seize Peter during the Feast of Unleavened Bread.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.4', 'BSB', 'He arrested him and put him in prison, handing him over to be guarded by four squads of four soldiers each. Herod intended to bring him out to the people after the Passover.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.5', 'BSB', 'So Peter was kept in prison, but the church was fervently praying to God for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.6', 'BSB', 'On the night before Herod was to bring him to trial, Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains, with sentries standing guard at the entrance to the prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.7', 'BSB', 'Suddenly an angel of the Lord appeared and a light shone in the cell. He tapped Peter on the side and woke him up, saying, “Get up quickly.” And the chains fell off his wrists.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.8', 'BSB', '“Get dressed and put on your sandals,” said the angel. Peter did so, and the angel told him, “Wrap your cloak around you and follow me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.9', 'BSB', 'So Peter followed him out, but he was unaware that what the angel was doing was real. He thought he was only seeing a vision.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.10', 'BSB', 'They passed the first and second guards and came to the iron gate leading to the city, which opened for them by itself. When they had gone outside and walked the length of one block, the angel suddenly left him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.11', 'BSB', 'Then Peter came to himself and said, “Now I know for sure that the Lord has sent His angel and rescued me from Herod’s grasp and from everything the Jewish people were anticipating.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.12', 'BSB', 'And when he had realized this, he went to the house of Mary the mother of John, also called Mark, where many people had gathered together and were praying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.13', 'BSB', 'He knocked at the outer gate, and a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.14', 'BSB', 'When she recognized Peter’s voice, she was so overjoyed that she forgot to open the gate, but ran inside and announced, “Peter is standing at the gate!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.15', 'BSB', '“You are out of your mind,” they told her. But when she kept insisting it was so, they said, “It must be his angel.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.16', 'BSB', 'But Peter kept on knocking, and when they opened the door and saw him, they were astounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.17', 'BSB', 'Peter motioned with his hand for silence, and he described how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. “Send word to James and to the brothers,” he said, and he left for another place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.18', 'BSB', 'At daybreak there was no small commotion among the soldiers as to what had become of Peter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.19', 'BSB', 'After Herod had searched for him unsuccessfully, he examined the guards and ordered that they be executed. Then he went down from Judea to Caesarea and spent some time there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.20', 'BSB', 'Now Herod was in a furious dispute with the people of Tyre and Sidon, and they convened before him. Having secured the support of Blastus, the king’s chamberlain, they asked for peace, because their region depended on the king’s country for food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.21', 'BSB', 'On the appointed day, Herod donned his royal robes, sat on his throne, and addressed the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.22', 'BSB', 'And they began to shout, “This is the voice of a god, not a man!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.23', 'BSB', 'Immediately, because Herod did not give glory to God, an angel of the Lord struck him down, and he was eaten by worms and died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.24', 'BSB', 'But the word of God continued to spread and multiply.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.12.25', 'BSB', 'When Barnabas and Saul had fulfilled their mission to Jerusalem, they returned, bringing with them John, also called Mark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.1', 'BSB', 'Now in the church at Antioch there were prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen (who had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch), and Saul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.2', 'BSB', 'While they were worshiping the Lord and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, “Set apart for Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.3', 'BSB', 'And after they had fasted and prayed, they laid their hands on them and sent them off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.4', 'BSB', 'So Barnabas and Saul, sent forth by the Holy Spirit, went down to Seleucia and sailed from there to Cyprus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.5', 'BSB', 'When they arrived at Salamis, they proclaimed the word of God in the Jewish synagogues. And John was with them as their helper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.6', 'BSB', 'They traveled through the whole island as far as Paphos, where they found a Jewish sorcerer and false prophet named Bar-Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.7', 'BSB', 'an attendant of the proconsul, Sergius Paulus. The proconsul, a man of intelligence, summoned Barnabas and Saul because he wanted to hear the word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.8', 'BSB', 'But Elymas the sorcerer (for that is what his name means) opposed them and tried to turn the proconsul from the faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.9', 'BSB', 'Then Saul, who was also called Paul, filled with the Holy Spirit, looked directly at Elymas', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.10', 'BSB', 'and said, “O child of the devil and enemy of all righteousness, you are full of all kinds of deceit and trickery! Will you never stop perverting the straight ways of the Lord?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.11', 'BSB', 'Now look, the hand of the Lord is against you, and for a time you will be blind and unable to see the light of the sun.” Immediately mist and darkness came over him, and he groped about, seeking someone to lead him by the hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.12', 'BSB', 'When the proconsul saw what had happened, he believed, for he was astonished at the teaching about the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.13', 'BSB', 'After setting sail from Paphos, Paul and his companions came to Perga in Pamphylia, where John left them to return to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.14', 'BSB', 'And from Perga, they traveled inland to Pisidian Antioch, where they entered the synagogue on the Sabbath and sat down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.15', 'BSB', 'After the reading from the Law and the Prophets, the synagogue leaders sent word to them: “Brothers, if you have a word of encouragement for the people, please speak.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.16', 'BSB', 'Paul stood up, motioned with his hand, and began to speak: “Men of Israel and you Gentiles who fear God, listen to me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.17', 'BSB', 'The God of the people of Israel chose our fathers. He made them into a great people during their stay in Egypt, and with an uplifted arm He led them out of that land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.18', 'BSB', 'He endured their conduct for about forty years in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.19', 'BSB', 'And having vanquished seven nations in Canaan, He gave their land to His people as an inheritance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.20', 'BSB', 'All this took about 450 years. After this, God gave them judges until the time of Samuel the prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.21', 'BSB', 'Then the people asked for a king, and God gave them forty years under Saul son of Kish, from the tribe of Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.22', 'BSB', 'After removing Saul, He raised up David as their king and testified about him: ‘I have found David son of Jesse a man after My own heart; he will carry out My will in its entirety.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.23', 'BSB', 'From the descendants of this man, God has brought to Israel the Savior Jesus, as He promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.24', 'BSB', 'Before the arrival of Jesus, John preached a baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.25', 'BSB', 'As John was completing his course, he said, ‘Who do you suppose I am? I am not that One. But He is coming after me whose sandals I am not worthy to untie.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.26', 'BSB', 'Brothers, children of Abraham, and you Gentiles who fear God, it is to us that this message of salvation has been sent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.27', 'BSB', 'The people of Jerusalem and their rulers did not recognize Jesus, yet in condemning Him they fulfilled the words of the prophets that are read every Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.28', 'BSB', 'And though they found no ground for a death sentence, they asked Pilate to have Him executed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.29', 'BSB', 'When they had carried out all that was written about Him, they took Him down from the tree and laid Him in a tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.30', 'BSB', 'But God raised Him from the dead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.31', 'BSB', 'and for many days He was seen by those who had accompanied Him from Galilee to Jerusalem. They are now His witnesses to our people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.32', 'BSB', 'And now we proclaim to you the good news: What God promised our fathers', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.33', 'BSB', 'He has fulfilled for us, their children, by raising up Jesus. As it is written in the second Psalm: ‘You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.34', 'BSB', 'In fact, God raised Him from the dead, never to see decay. As He has said: ‘I will give you the holy and sure blessings promised to David.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.35', 'BSB', 'So also, He says in another Psalm: ‘You will not let Your Holy One see decay.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.36', 'BSB', 'For when David had served God’s purpose in his own generation, he fell asleep. His body was buried with his fathers and saw decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.37', 'BSB', 'But the One whom God raised from the dead did not see decay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.38', 'BSB', 'Therefore let it be known to you, brothers, that through Jesus the forgiveness of sins is proclaimed to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.39', 'BSB', 'Through Him everyone who believes is justified from everything you could not be justified from by the law of Moses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.40', 'BSB', 'Watch out, then, that what was spoken by the prophets does not happen to you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.41', 'BSB', '‘Look, you scoffers, wonder and perish! For I am doing a work in your days that you would never believe, even if someone told you.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.42', 'BSB', 'As Paul and Barnabas were leaving the synagogue, the people urged them to continue this message on the next Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.43', 'BSB', 'After the synagogue was dismissed, many of the Jews and devout converts to Judaism followed Paul and Barnabas, who spoke to them and urged them to continue in the grace of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.44', 'BSB', 'On the following Sabbath, nearly the whole city gathered to hear the word of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.45', 'BSB', 'But when the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and they blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.46', 'BSB', 'Then Paul and Barnabas answered them boldly: “It was necessary to speak the word of God to you first. But since you reject it and do not consider yourselves worthy of eternal life, we now turn to the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.47', 'BSB', 'For this is what the Lord has commanded us: ‘I have made you a light for the Gentiles, to bring salvation to the ends of the earth.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.48', 'BSB', 'When the Gentiles heard this, they rejoiced and glorified the word of the Lord, and all who were appointed for eternal life believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.49', 'BSB', 'And the word of the Lord spread throughout that region.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.50', 'BSB', 'The Jews, however, incited the religious women of prominence and the leading men of the city. They stirred up persecution against Paul and Barnabas and drove them out of their district.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.51', 'BSB', 'So they shook the dust off their feet in protest against them and went to Iconium.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.13.52', 'BSB', 'And the disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.1', 'BSB', 'At Iconium, Paul and Barnabas went as usual into the Jewish synagogue, where they spoke so well that a great number of Jews and Greeks believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.2', 'BSB', 'But the unbelieving Jews stirred up the Gentiles and poisoned their minds against the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.3', 'BSB', 'So Paul and Barnabas spent considerable time there, speaking boldly for the Lord, who affirmed the message of His grace by enabling them to perform signs and wonders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.4', 'BSB', 'The people of the city were divided. Some sided with the Jews, and others with the apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.5', 'BSB', 'But when the Gentiles and Jews, together with their rulers, set out to mistreat and stone them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.6', 'BSB', 'they found out about it and fled to the Lycaonian cities of Lystra and Derbe and to the surrounding region,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.7', 'BSB', 'where they continued to preach the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.8', 'BSB', 'In Lystra there sat a man crippled in his feet, who was lame from birth and had never walked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.9', 'BSB', 'This man was listening to the words of Paul, who looked intently at him and saw that he had faith to be healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.10', 'BSB', 'In a loud voice Paul called out, “Stand up on your feet!” And the man jumped up and began to walk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.11', 'BSB', 'When the crowds saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voices in the Lycaonian language: “The gods have come down to us in human form!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.12', 'BSB', 'Barnabas they called Zeus, and Paul they called Hermes, because he was the chief speaker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.13', 'BSB', 'The priest of Zeus, whose temple was just outside the city, brought bulls and wreaths to the city gates, hoping to offer a sacrifice along with the crowds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.14', 'BSB', 'But when the apostles Barnabas and Paul found out about this, they tore their clothes and rushed into the crowd, shouting,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.15', 'BSB', '“Men, why are you doing this? We too are only men, human like you. We are bringing you good news that you should turn from these worthless things to the living God, who made heaven and earth and sea and everything in them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.16', 'BSB', 'In past generations, He let all nations go their own way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.17', 'BSB', 'Yet He has not left Himself without testimony to His goodness: He gives you rain from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your hearts with food and gladness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.18', 'BSB', 'Even with these words, Paul and Barnabas could hardly stop the crowds from sacrificing to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.19', 'BSB', 'Then some Jews arrived from Antioch and Iconium and won over the crowds. They stoned Paul and dragged him outside the city, presuming he was dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.20', 'BSB', 'But after the disciples had gathered around him, he got up and went back into the city. And the next day he left with Barnabas for Derbe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.21', 'BSB', 'They preached the gospel to that city and made many disciples. Then they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.22', 'BSB', 'strengthening the souls of the disciples and encouraging them to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” they said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.23', 'BSB', 'Paul and Barnabas appointed elders for them in each church, praying and fasting as they entrusted them to the Lord, in whom they had believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.24', 'BSB', 'After passing through Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.25', 'BSB', 'And when they had spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.26', 'BSB', 'From Attalia they sailed to Antioch, where they had been commended to the grace of God for the work they had just completed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.27', 'BSB', 'When they arrived, they gathered the church together and reported all that God had done through them, and how He had opened the door of faith to the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.14.28', 'BSB', 'And they spent a long time there with the disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then some men came down from Judea and were teaching the brothers, “Unless you are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you cannot be saved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.2', 'BSB', 'And after engaging these men in sharp debate, Paul and Barnabas were appointed, along with some other believers, to go up to Jerusalem to see the apostles and elders about this question.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.3', 'BSB', 'Sent on their way by the church, they passed through Phoenicia and Samaria, recounting the conversion of the Gentiles and bringing great joy to all the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.4', 'BSB', 'On their arrival in Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church and apostles and elders, to whom they reported all that God had done through them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.5', 'BSB', 'But some believers from the party of the Pharisees stood up and declared, “The Gentiles must be circumcised and required to obey the law of Moses.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.6', 'BSB', 'So the apostles and elders met to look into this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.7', 'BSB', 'After much discussion, Peter got up and said to them, “Brothers, you know that in the early days God made a choice among you that the Gentiles would hear from my lips the message of the gospel and believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.8', 'BSB', 'And God, who knows the heart, showed His approval by giving the Holy Spirit to them, just as He did to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.9', 'BSB', 'He made no distinction between us and them, for He cleansed their hearts by faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.10', 'BSB', 'Now then, why do you test God by placing on the necks of the disciples a yoke that neither we nor our fathers have been able to bear?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.11', 'BSB', 'On the contrary, we believe it is through the grace of the Lord Jesus that we are saved, just as they are.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.12', 'BSB', 'The whole assembly fell silent as they listened to Barnabas and Paul describing the signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles through them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.13', 'BSB', 'When they had finished speaking, James declared, “Brothers, listen to me!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.14', 'BSB', 'Simon has told us how God first visited the Gentiles to take from them a people to be His own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.15', 'BSB', 'The words of the prophets agree with this, as it is written:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.16', 'BSB', '‘After this I will return and rebuild the fallen tent of David. Its ruins I will rebuild, and I will restore it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.17', 'BSB', 'so that the remnant of men may seek the Lord, and all the Gentiles who are called by My name, says the Lord who does these things', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.18', 'BSB', 'that have been known for ages.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.19', 'BSB', 'It is my judgment, therefore, that we should not cause trouble for the Gentiles who are turning to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.20', 'BSB', 'Instead, we should write and tell them to abstain from food polluted by idols, from sexual immorality, from the meat of strangled animals, and from blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.21', 'BSB', 'For Moses has been proclaimed in every city from ancient times and is read in the synagogues on every Sabbath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.22', 'BSB', 'Then the apostles and elders, with the whole church, decided to select men from among them to send to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas. They chose Judas called Barsabbas and Silas, two leaders among the brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.23', 'BSB', 'and sent them with this letter: The apostles and the elders, your brothers, To the brothers among the Gentiles in Antioch, Syria, and Cilicia: Greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.24', 'BSB', 'It has come to our attention that some went out from us without our authorization and unsettled you, troubling your minds by what they said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.25', 'BSB', 'So we all agreed to choose men to send to you along with our beloved Barnabas and Paul,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.26', 'BSB', 'men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore we are sending Judas and Silas to tell you in person the same things we are writing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.28', 'BSB', 'It seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to us not to burden you with anything beyond these essential requirements:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.29', 'BSB', 'You must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality. You will do well to avoid these things. Farewell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.30', 'BSB', 'So the men were sent off and went down to Antioch, where they assembled the congregation and delivered the letter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.31', 'BSB', 'When the people read it, they rejoiced at its encouraging message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.32', 'BSB', 'Judas and Silas, who themselves were prophets, said much to encourage and strengthen the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.33', 'BSB', 'After spending some time there, they were sent off by the brothers in peace to return to those who had sent them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.35', 'BSB', 'But Paul and Barnabas remained at Antioch, along with many others, teaching and preaching the word of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.36', 'BSB', 'Some time later Paul said to Barnabas, “Let us go back and visit the brothers in every town where we proclaimed the word of the Lord, to see how they are doing.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.37', 'BSB', 'Barnabas wanted to take John, also called Mark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.38', 'BSB', 'But Paul thought it best not to take him, because he had deserted them in Pamphylia and had not accompanied them in the work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.39', 'BSB', 'Their disagreement was so sharp that they parted company. Barnabas took Mark and sailed for Cyprus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.40', 'BSB', 'but Paul chose Silas and left, commended by the brothers to the grace of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.15.41', 'BSB', 'And he traveled through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.1', 'BSB', 'Paul came to Derbe and then to Lystra, where he found a disciple named Timothy, the son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.2', 'BSB', 'The brothers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.3', 'BSB', 'Paul wanted Timothy to accompany him, so he took him and circumcised him on account of the Jews in that area, for they all knew that his father was a Greek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.4', 'BSB', 'As they went from town to town, they delivered the decisions handed down by the apostles and elders in Jerusalem for the people to obey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.5', 'BSB', 'So the churches were strengthened in the faith and grew daily in numbers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.6', 'BSB', 'After the Holy Spirit had prevented them from speaking the word in the province of Asia, they traveled through the region of Phrygia and Galatia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.7', 'BSB', 'And when they came to the border of Mysia, they tried to enter Bithynia, but the Spirit of Jesus would not permit them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.8', 'BSB', 'So they passed by Mysia and went down to Troas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.9', 'BSB', 'During the night, Paul had a vision of a man of Macedonia standing and pleading with him, “Come over to Macedonia and help us.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.10', 'BSB', 'As soon as Paul had seen the vision, we got ready to leave for Macedonia, concluding that God had called us to preach the gospel to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.11', 'BSB', 'We sailed from Troas straight to Samothrace, and the following day on to Neapolis.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.12', 'BSB', 'From there we went to the Roman colony of Philippi, the leading city of that district of Macedonia. And we stayed there several days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.13', 'BSB', 'On the Sabbath we went outside the city gate along the river, where it was customary to find a place of prayer. After sitting down, we spoke to the women who had gathered there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.14', 'BSB', 'Among those listening was a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, who was a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul’s message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.15', 'BSB', 'And when she and her household had been baptized, she urged us, “If you consider me a believer in the Lord, come and stay at my house.” And she persuaded us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.16', 'BSB', 'One day as we were going to the place of prayer, we were met by a slave girl with a spirit of divination, who earned a large income for her masters by fortune-telling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.17', 'BSB', 'This girl followed Paul and the rest of us, shouting, “These men are servants of the Most High God, who are proclaiming to you the way of salvation!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.18', 'BSB', 'She continued this for many days. Eventually Paul grew so aggravated that he turned and said to the spirit, “In the name of Jesus Christ I command you to come out of her!” And the spirit left her at that very moment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.19', 'BSB', 'When the girl’s owners saw that their hope of making money was gone, they seized Paul and Silas and dragged them before the authorities in the marketplace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.20', 'BSB', 'They brought them to the magistrates and said, “These men are Jews and are throwing our city into turmoil', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.21', 'BSB', 'by promoting customs that are unlawful for us Romans to adopt or practice.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.22', 'BSB', 'The crowd joined in the attack against Paul and Silas, and the magistrates ordered that they be stripped and beaten with rods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.23', 'BSB', 'And after striking them with many blows, they threw them into prison and ordered the jailer to guard them securely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.24', 'BSB', 'On receiving this order, he placed them in the inner cell and fastened their feet in the stocks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.25', 'BSB', 'About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.26', 'BSB', 'Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyone’s chains came loose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.27', 'BSB', 'When the jailer woke up and saw the prison doors open, he drew his sword and was about to kill himself, presuming that the prisoners had escaped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.28', 'BSB', 'But Paul called out in a loud voice, “Do not harm yourself! We are all here!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.29', 'BSB', 'Calling for lights, the jailer rushed in and fell trembling before Paul and Silas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.30', 'BSB', 'Then he brought them out and asked, “Sirs, what must I do to be saved?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.31', 'BSB', 'They replied, “Believe in the Lord Jesus and you will be saved, you and your household.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.32', 'BSB', 'Then Paul and Silas spoke the word of the Lord to him and to everyone in his house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.33', 'BSB', 'At that hour of the night, the jailer took them and washed their wounds. And without delay, he and all his household were baptized.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.34', 'BSB', 'Then he brought them into his home and set a meal before them. So he and all his household rejoiced that they had come to believe in God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.35', 'BSB', 'When daylight came, the magistrates sent their officers with the order: “Release those men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.36', 'BSB', 'The jailer informed Paul: “The magistrates have sent orders to release you. Now you may go on your way in peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.37', 'BSB', 'But Paul said to the officers, “They beat us publicly without a trial and threw us into prison, even though we are Roman citizens. And now do they want to send us away secretly? Absolutely not! Let them come themselves and escort us out!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.38', 'BSB', 'So the officers relayed this message to the magistrates, who were alarmed to hear that Paul and Silas were Roman citizens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.39', 'BSB', 'They came to appease them and led them out, requesting that they leave the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.16.40', 'BSB', 'After Paul and Silas came out of the prison, they went to Lydia’s house to see the brothers and encourage them. Then they left the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.1', 'BSB', 'When they had passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a Jewish synagogue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.2', 'BSB', 'As was his custom, Paul went into the synagogue, and on three Sabbaths he reasoned with them from the Scriptures,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.3', 'BSB', 'explaining and proving that the Christ had to suffer and rise from the dead. “This Jesus I am proclaiming to you is the Christ,” he declared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.4', 'BSB', 'Some of the Jews were persuaded and joined Paul and Silas, along with a large number of God-fearing Greeks and quite a few leading women.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.5', 'BSB', 'The Jews, however, became jealous. So they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, and sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jason’s house in search of Paul and Silas, hoping to bring them out to the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.6', 'BSB', 'But when they could not find them, they dragged Jason and some other brothers before the city officials, shouting, “These men who have turned the world upside down have now come here,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.7', 'BSB', 'and Jason has welcomed them into his home. They are all defying Caesar’s decrees, saying that there is another king, named Jesus!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.8', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, the crowd and city officials were greatly disturbed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.9', 'BSB', 'And they collected bond from Jason and the others, and then released them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.10', 'BSB', 'As soon as night had fallen, the brothers sent Paul and Silas away to Berea. On arriving there, they went into the Jewish synagogue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.11', 'BSB', 'Now the Bereans were more noble-minded than the Thessalonians, for they received the message with great eagerness and examined the Scriptures every day to see if these teachings were true.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.12', 'BSB', 'As a result, many of them believed, along with quite a few prominent Greek women and men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.13', 'BSB', 'But when the Jews from Thessalonica learned that Paul was also proclaiming the word of God in Berea, they went there themselves to incite and agitate the crowds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.14', 'BSB', 'The brothers immediately sent Paul to the coast, but Silas and Timothy remained in Berea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.15', 'BSB', 'Those who escorted Paul brought him to Athens and then returned with instructions for Silas and Timothy to join him as soon as possible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.16', 'BSB', 'While Paul was waiting for them in Athens, he was deeply disturbed in his spirit to see that the city was full of idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.17', 'BSB', 'So he reasoned in the synagogue with the Jews and God-fearing Gentiles, and in the marketplace with those he met each day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.18', 'BSB', 'Some Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also began to debate with him. Some of them asked, “What is this babbler trying to say?” Others said, “He seems to be advocating foreign gods.” They said this because Paul was proclaiming the good news of Jesus and the resurrection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.19', 'BSB', 'So they took Paul and brought him to the Areopagus, where they asked him, “May we know what this new teaching is that you are presenting?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.20', 'BSB', 'For you are bringing some strange notions to our ears, and we want to know what they mean.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.21', 'BSB', 'Now all the Athenians and foreigners who lived there spent their time doing nothing more than hearing and articulating new ideas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.22', 'BSB', 'Then Paul stood up in the meeting of the Areopagus and said, “Men of Athens, I see that in every way you are very religious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.23', 'BSB', 'For as I walked around and examined your objects of worship, I even found an altar with this inscription: TO AN UNKNOWN GOD. Therefore what you worship as something unknown, I now proclaim to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.24', 'BSB', 'The God who made the world and everything in it is the Lord of heaven and earth and does not live in temples made by human hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.25', 'BSB', 'Nor is He served by human hands, as if He needed anything, because He Himself gives everyone life and breath and everything else.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.26', 'BSB', 'From one man He made every nation of men, that they should inhabit the whole earth; and He determined their appointed times and the boundaries of their lands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.27', 'BSB', 'God intended that they would seek Him and perhaps reach out for Him and find Him, though He is not far from each one of us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.28', 'BSB', '‘For in Him we live and move and have our being.’ As some of your own poets have said, ‘We are His offspring.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.29', 'BSB', 'Therefore, being offspring of God, we should not think that the Divine Being is like gold or silver or stone, an image formed by man’s skill and imagination.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.30', 'BSB', 'Although God overlooked the ignorance of earlier times, He now commands all people everywhere to repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.31', 'BSB', 'For He has set a day when He will judge the world with justice by the Man He has appointed. He has given proof of this to everyone by raising Him from the dead.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.32', 'BSB', 'When they heard about the resurrection of the dead, some began to mock him, but others said, “We want to hear you again on this topic.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.33', 'BSB', 'At that, Paul left the Areopagus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.17.34', 'BSB', 'But some joined him and believed, including Dionysius the Areopagite, a woman named Damaris, and others who were with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.1', 'BSB', 'After this, Paul left Athens and went to Corinth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.2', 'BSB', 'There he found a Jew named Aquila, a native of Pontus, who had recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla because Claudius had ordered all the Jews to leave Rome. Paul went to visit them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.3', 'BSB', 'and he stayed and worked with them because they were tentmakers by trade, just as he was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.4', 'BSB', 'Every Sabbath he reasoned in the synagogue, trying to persuade Jews and Greeks alike.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.5', 'BSB', 'And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.6', 'BSB', 'But when they opposed and insulted him, he shook out his garments and told them, “Your blood be on your own heads! I am innocent of it. From now on I will go to the Gentiles.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.7', 'BSB', 'So Paul left the synagogue and went next door to the house of Titus Justus, a worshiper of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.8', 'BSB', 'Crispus, the synagogue leader, and his whole household believed in the Lord. And many of the Corinthians who heard the message believed and were baptized.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.9', 'BSB', 'One night the Lord spoke to Paul in a vision: “Do not be afraid; keep on speaking; do not be silent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.10', 'BSB', 'For I am with you and no one will lay a hand on you, because I have many people in this city.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.11', 'BSB', 'So Paul stayed for a year and a half, teaching the word of God among the Corinthians.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.12', 'BSB', 'While Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews coordinated an attack on Paul and brought him before the judgment seat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.13', 'BSB', '“This man is persuading the people to worship God in ways contrary to the law,” they said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.14', 'BSB', 'But just as Paul was about to speak, Gallio told the Jews, “If this matter involved a wrongdoing or vicious crime, O Jews, it would be reasonable for me to hear your complaint.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.15', 'BSB', 'But since it is a dispute about words and names and your own law, settle it yourselves. I refuse to be a judge of such things.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.16', 'BSB', 'And he drove them away from the judgment seat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.17', 'BSB', 'At this, the crowd seized Sosthenes the synagogue leader and beat him in front of the judgment seat. But none of this was of concern to Gallio.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.18', 'BSB', 'Paul remained in Corinth for quite some time before saying goodbye to the brothers. He had his head shaved in Cenchrea to keep a vow he had made, and then he sailed for Syria, accompanied by Priscilla and Aquila.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.19', 'BSB', 'When they reached Ephesus, Paul parted ways with Priscilla and Aquila. He himself went into the synagogue there and reasoned with the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.20', 'BSB', 'When they asked him to stay for a while longer, he declined.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.21', 'BSB', 'But as he left, he said, “I will come back to you if God is willing.” And he set sail from Ephesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.22', 'BSB', 'When Paul had landed at Caesarea, he went up and greeted the church at Jerusalem. Then he went down to Antioch.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.23', 'BSB', 'After Paul had spent some time in Antioch, he traveled from place to place throughout the region of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.24', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile a Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria, came to Ephesus. He was an eloquent man, well versed in the Scriptures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.25', 'BSB', 'He had been instructed in the way of the Lord and was fervent in spirit. He spoke and taught accurately about Jesus, though he knew only the baptism of John.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.26', 'BSB', 'And he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. When Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him in and explained to him the way of God more accurately.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.27', 'BSB', 'When Apollos resolved to cross over to Achaia, the brothers encouraged him and wrote to the disciples there to welcome him. On his arrival, he was a great help to those who by grace had believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.18.28', 'BSB', 'For he powerfully refuted the Jews in public debate, proving from the Scriptures that Jesus is the Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.1', 'BSB', 'While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul passed through the interior and came to Ephesus. There he found some disciples', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.2', 'BSB', 'and asked them, “Did you receive the Holy Spirit when you became believers?” “No,” they answered, “we have not even heard that there is a Holy Spirit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.3', 'BSB', '“Into what, then, were you baptized?” Paul asked. “The baptism of John,” they replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.4', 'BSB', 'Paul explained: “John’s baptism was a baptism of repentance. He told the people to believe in the One coming after him, that is, in Jesus.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.5', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, they were baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.6', 'BSB', 'And when Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they spoke in tongues and prophesied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.7', 'BSB', 'There were about twelve men in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.8', 'BSB', 'Then Paul went into the synagogue and spoke boldly there for three months, arguing persuasively about the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.9', 'BSB', 'But when some of them stubbornly refused to believe and publicly maligned the Way, Paul took his disciples and left the synagogue to conduct daily discussions in the lecture hall of Tyrannus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.10', 'BSB', 'This continued for two years, so that everyone who lived in the province of Asia, Jews and Greeks alike, heard the word of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.11', 'BSB', 'God did extraordinary miracles through the hands of Paul,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.12', 'BSB', 'so that even handkerchiefs and aprons that had touched him were taken to the sick, and the diseases and evil spirits left them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.13', 'BSB', 'Now there were some itinerant Jewish exorcists who tried to invoke the name of the Lord Jesus over those with evil spirits. They would say, “I bind you by Jesus, whom Paul proclaims.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.14', 'BSB', 'Seven sons of Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, were doing this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.15', 'BSB', 'Eventually, one of the evil spirits answered them, “Jesus I know, and I know about Paul, but who are you?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.16', 'BSB', 'Then the man with the evil spirit jumped on them and overpowered them all. The attack was so violent that they ran out of the house naked and wounded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.17', 'BSB', 'This became known to all the Jews and Greeks living in Ephesus, and fear came over all of them. So the name of the Lord Jesus was held in high honor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.18', 'BSB', 'Many who had believed now came forward, confessing and disclosing their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.19', 'BSB', 'And a number of those who had practiced magic arts brought their books and burned them in front of everyone. When the value of the books was calculated, the total came to fifty thousand drachmas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.20', 'BSB', 'So the word of the Lord powerfully continued to spread and prevail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.21', 'BSB', 'After these things had happened, Paul resolved in the Spirit to go to Jerusalem after he had passed through Macedonia and Achaia. “After I have been there,” he said, “I must see Rome as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.22', 'BSB', 'He sent two of his helpers, Timothy and Erastus, to Macedonia, while he stayed for a time in the province of Asia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.23', 'BSB', 'About that time there arose a great disturbance about the Way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.24', 'BSB', 'It began with a silversmith named Demetrius who made silver shrines of Artemis, bringing much business to the craftsmen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.25', 'BSB', 'Demetrius assembled the craftsmen, along with the workmen in related trades. “Men,” he said, “you know that this business is our source of prosperity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.26', 'BSB', 'And you can see and hear that not only in Ephesus, but in nearly the whole province of Asia, Paul has persuaded a great number of people to turn away. He says that man-made gods are no gods at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.27', 'BSB', 'There is danger not only that our business will fall into disrepute, but also that the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be discredited and her majesty deposed—she who is worshiped by all the province of Asia and the whole world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.28', 'BSB', 'When the men heard this, they were enraged and began shouting, “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.29', 'BSB', 'Soon the whole city was in disarray. They rushed together into the theatre, dragging with them Gaius and Aristarchus, Paul’s traveling companions from Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.30', 'BSB', 'Paul wanted to go before the assembly, but the disciples would not allow him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.31', 'BSB', 'Even some of Paul’s friends who were officials of the province of Asia sent word to him, begging him not to venture into the theatre.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.32', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile the assembly was in turmoil. Some were shouting one thing and some another, and most of them did not even know why they were there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.33', 'BSB', 'The Jews in the crowd pushed Alexander forward to explain himself, and he motioned for silence so he could make his defense to the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.34', 'BSB', 'But when they realized that he was a Jew, they all shouted in unison for about two hours: “Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.35', 'BSB', 'Finally the city clerk quieted the crowd and declared, “Men of Ephesus, doesn’t everyone know that the city of Ephesus is guardian of the temple of the great Artemis and of her image, which fell from heaven?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.36', 'BSB', 'Since these things are undeniable, you ought to be calm and not do anything rash.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.37', 'BSB', 'For you have brought these men here, though they have neither robbed our temple nor blasphemed our goddess.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.38', 'BSB', 'So if Demetrius and his fellow craftsmen have a complaint against anyone, the courts are open and proconsuls are available. Let them bring charges against one another there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.39', 'BSB', 'But if you are seeking anything beyond this, it must be settled in a legal assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.40', 'BSB', 'For we are in jeopardy of being charged with rioting for today’s events, and we have no justification to account for this commotion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.19.41', 'BSB', 'After he had said this, he dismissed the assembly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.1', 'BSB', 'When the uproar had ended, Paul sent for the disciples. And after encouraging them, he said goodbye to them and left for Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.2', 'BSB', 'After traveling through that area and speaking many words of encouragement, he arrived in Greece,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.3', 'BSB', 'where he stayed three months. And when the Jews formed a plot against him as he was about to sail for Syria, he decided to go back through Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.4', 'BSB', 'Paul was accompanied by Sopater son of Pyrrhus from Berea, Aristarchus and Secundus from Thessalonica, Gaius from Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus from the province of Asia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.5', 'BSB', 'These men went on ahead and waited for us in Troas.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.6', 'BSB', 'And after the Feast of Unleavened Bread, we sailed from Philippi, and five days later we rejoined them in Troas, where we stayed seven days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.7', 'BSB', 'On the first day of the week we came together to break bread. Since Paul was ready to leave the next day, he talked to them and kept on speaking until midnight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.8', 'BSB', 'Now there were many lamps in the upper room where we were gathered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.9', 'BSB', 'And a certain young man named Eutychus, seated in the window, was sinking into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and on. When he was sound asleep, he fell from the third story and was picked up dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.10', 'BSB', 'But Paul went down, threw himself on the young man, and embraced him. “Do not be alarmed!” he said. “He is still alive!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.11', 'BSB', 'Then Paul went back upstairs, broke bread, and ate. And after speaking until daybreak, he departed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.12', 'BSB', 'And the people were greatly relieved to take the boy home alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.13', 'BSB', 'We went on ahead to the ship and sailed to Assos, where we were to take Paul aboard. He had arranged this because he was going there on foot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.14', 'BSB', 'And when he met us at Assos, we took him aboard and went on to Mitylene.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.15', 'BSB', 'Sailing on from there, we arrived the next day opposite Chios. The day after that we arrived at Samos, and on the following day we came to Miletus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.16', 'BSB', 'Paul had decided to sail past Ephesus to avoid spending time in the province of Asia, because he was in a hurry to reach Jerusalem, if possible, by the day of Pentecost.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.17', 'BSB', 'From Miletus, Paul sent to Ephesus for the elders of the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.18', 'BSB', 'When they came to him, he said, “You know how I lived the whole time I was with you, from the first day I arrived in the province of Asia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.19', 'BSB', 'I served the Lord with great humility and with tears, especially in the trials that came upon me through the plots of the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.20', 'BSB', 'I did not shrink back from declaring anything that was helpful to you as I taught you publicly and from house to house,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.21', 'BSB', 'testifying to Jews and Greeks alike about repentance to God and faith in our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.22', 'BSB', 'And now, compelled by the Spirit, I am going to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.23', 'BSB', 'I only know that in town after town the Holy Spirit warns me that chains and afflictions await me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.24', 'BSB', 'But I consider my life of no value to me, if only I may finish my course and complete the ministry I have received from the Lord Jesus—the ministry of testifying to the good news of God’s grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.25', 'BSB', 'Now I know that none of you among whom I have preached the kingdom will see my face again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.26', 'BSB', 'Therefore I testify to you this day that I am innocent of the blood of all men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.27', 'BSB', 'For I did not shrink back from declaring to you the whole will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.28', 'BSB', 'Keep watch over yourselves and the entire flock of which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers. Be shepherds of the church of God, which He purchased with His own blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.29', 'BSB', 'I know that after my departure, savage wolves will come in among you and will not spare the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.30', 'BSB', 'Even from your own number, men will rise up and distort the truth to draw away disciples after them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore be alert and remember that for three years I never stopped warning each of you night and day with tears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.32', 'BSB', 'And now I commit you to God and to the word of His grace, which can build you up and give you an inheritance among all who are sanctified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.33', 'BSB', 'I have not coveted anyone’s silver or gold or clothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.34', 'BSB', 'You yourselves know that these hands of mine have ministered to my own needs and those of my companions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.35', 'BSB', 'In everything, I showed you that by this kind of hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words of the Lord Jesus Himself: ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.36', 'BSB', 'When Paul had said this, he knelt down with all of them and prayed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.37', 'BSB', 'They all wept openly as they embraced Paul and kissed him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.20.38', 'BSB', 'They were especially grieved by his statement that they would never see his face again. Then they accompanied him to the ship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.1', 'BSB', 'After we had torn ourselves away from them, we sailed directly to Cos, and the next day on to Rhodes, and from there to Patara.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.2', 'BSB', 'Finding a ship crossing over to Phoenicia, we boarded it and set sail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.3', 'BSB', 'After sighting Cyprus and passing south of it, we sailed on to Syria and landed at Tyre, where the ship was to unload its cargo.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.4', 'BSB', 'We sought out the disciples in Tyre and stayed with them seven days. Through the Spirit they kept telling Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.5', 'BSB', 'But when our time there had ended, we set out on our journey. All the disciples, with their wives and children, accompanied us out of the city and knelt down on the beach to pray with us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.6', 'BSB', 'And after we had said our farewells, we went aboard the ship, and they returned home.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.7', 'BSB', 'When we had finished our voyage from Tyre, we landed at Ptolemais, where we greeted the brothers and stayed with them for a day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.8', 'BSB', 'Leaving the next day, we went on to Caesarea and stayed at the home of Philip the evangelist, who was one of the Seven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.9', 'BSB', 'He had four unmarried daughters who prophesied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.10', 'BSB', 'After we had been there several days, a prophet named Agabus came down from Judea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.11', 'BSB', 'Coming over to us, he took Paul’s belt, bound his own feet and hands, and said, “The Holy Spirit says: ‘In this way the Jews of Jerusalem will bind the owner of this belt and hand him over to the Gentiles.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.12', 'BSB', 'When we heard this, we and the people there pleaded with Paul not to go up to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.13', 'BSB', 'Then Paul answered, “Why are you weeping and breaking my heart? I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die in Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.14', 'BSB', 'When he would not be dissuaded, we fell silent and said, “The Lord’s will be done.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.15', 'BSB', 'After these days, we packed up and went on to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.16', 'BSB', 'Some of the disciples from Caesarea accompanied us, and they took us to stay at the home of Mnason the Cypriot, an early disciple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.17', 'BSB', 'When we arrived in Jerusalem, the brothers welcomed us joyfully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.18', 'BSB', 'The next day Paul went in with us to see James, and all the elders were present.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.19', 'BSB', 'Paul greeted them and recounted one by one the things that God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.20', 'BSB', 'When they heard this, they glorified God. Then they said to Paul, “You see, brother, how many thousands of Jews have believed, and all of them are zealous for the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.21', 'BSB', 'But they are under the impression that you teach all the Jews who live among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, telling them not to circumcise their children or observe our customs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.22', 'BSB', 'What then should we do? They will certainly hear that you have come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.23', 'BSB', 'Therefore do what we advise you. There are four men with us who have taken a vow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.24', 'BSB', 'Take these men, purify yourself along with them, and pay their expenses so they can have their heads shaved. Then everyone will know that there is no truth to these rumors about you, but that you also live in obedience to the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.25', 'BSB', 'As for the Gentile believers, we have written to them our decision that they must abstain from food sacrificed to idols, from blood, from the meat of strangled animals, and from sexual immorality.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.26', 'BSB', 'So the next day Paul took the men and purified himself along with them. Then he entered the temple to give notice of the date when their purification would be complete and the offering would be made for each of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.27', 'BSB', 'When the seven days were almost over, some Jews from the province of Asia saw Paul at the temple. They stirred up the whole crowd and seized him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.28', 'BSB', 'crying out, “Men of Israel, help us! This is the man who teaches everywhere against our people and against our law and against this place. Furthermore, he has brought Greeks into the temple and defiled this holy place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.29', 'BSB', 'For they had previously seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, and they assumed that Paul had brought him into the temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.30', 'BSB', 'The whole city was stirred up, and the people rushed together. They seized Paul and dragged him out of the temple, and at once the gates were shut.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.31', 'BSB', 'While they were trying to kill him, the commander of the Roman regiment received a report that all Jerusalem was in turmoil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.32', 'BSB', 'Immediately he took some soldiers and centurions and ran down to the crowd. When the people saw the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.33', 'BSB', 'The commander came up and arrested Paul, ordering that he be bound with two chains. Then he asked who he was and what he had done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.34', 'BSB', 'Some in the crowd were shouting one thing, and some another. And since the commander could not get at the truth because of the uproar, he ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.35', 'BSB', 'When Paul reached the steps, he had to be carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the mob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.36', 'BSB', 'For the crowd that followed him kept shouting, “Away with him!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.37', 'BSB', 'As they were about to take Paul into the barracks, he asked the commander, “May I say something to you?” “Do you speak Greek?” he replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.38', 'BSB', '“Aren’t you the Egyptian who incited a rebellion some time ago and led four thousand members of the ‘Assassins’ into the wilderness?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.39', 'BSB', 'But Paul answered, “I am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no ordinary city. Now I beg you to allow me to speak to the people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.21.40', 'BSB', 'Having received permission, Paul stood on the steps and motioned to the crowd. A great hush came over the crowd, and he addressed them in Hebrew:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.1', 'BSB', '“Brothers and fathers, listen now to my defense before you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.2', 'BSB', 'When they heard him speak to them in Hebrew, they became even more silent. Then Paul declared,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.3', 'BSB', '“I am a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but raised in this city. I was educated at the feet of Gamaliel in strict conformity to the law of our fathers. I am just as zealous for God as any of you here today.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.4', 'BSB', 'I persecuted this Way even to the death, detaining both men and women and throwing them into prison,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.5', 'BSB', 'as the high priest and the whole Council can testify about me. I even obtained letters from them to their brothers in Damascus, and I was on my way to apprehend these people and bring them to Jerusalem to be punished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.6', 'BSB', 'About noon as I was approaching Damascus, suddenly a bright light from heaven flashed around me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.7', 'BSB', 'I fell to the ground and heard a voice say to me, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.8', 'BSB', '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting,’ He replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.9', 'BSB', 'My companions saw the light, but they could not understand the voice of the One speaking to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.10', 'BSB', 'Then I asked, ‘What should I do, Lord?’ ‘Get up and go into Damascus,’ He told me. ‘There you will be told all that you have been appointed to do.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.11', 'BSB', 'Because the brilliance of the light had blinded me, my companions led me by the hand into Damascus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.12', 'BSB', 'There a man named Ananias, a devout observer of the law who was highly regarded by all the Jews living there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.13', 'BSB', 'came and stood beside me. ‘Brother Saul,’ he said, ‘receive your sight.’ And at that moment I could see him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.14', 'BSB', 'Then he said, ‘The God of our fathers has appointed you to know His will, and to see the Righteous One, and to hear His voice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.15', 'BSB', 'You will be His witness to everyone of what you have seen and heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.16', 'BSB', 'And now what are you waiting for? Get up, be baptized, and wash your sins away, calling on His name.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.17', 'BSB', 'Later, when I had returned to Jerusalem and was praying at the temple, I fell into a trance', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.18', 'BSB', 'and saw the Lord saying to me, ‘Hurry! Leave Jerusalem quickly, because the people here will not accept your testimony about Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.19', 'BSB', '‘Lord,’ I answered, ‘they know very well that in one synagogue after another I imprisoned and beat those who believed in You.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.20', 'BSB', 'And when the blood of Your witness Stephen was shed, I stood there giving my approval and watching over the garments of those who killed him.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.21', 'BSB', 'Then He said to me, ‘Go! I will send you far away to the Gentiles.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.22', 'BSB', 'The crowd listened to Paul until he made this statement. Then they lifted up their voices and shouted, “Rid the earth of him! He is not fit to live!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.23', 'BSB', 'As they were shouting and throwing off their cloaks and tossing dust into the air,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.24', 'BSB', 'the commander ordered that Paul be brought into the barracks. He directed that Paul be flogged and interrogated to determine the reason for this outcry against him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.25', 'BSB', 'But as they stretched him out to strap him down, Paul said to the centurion standing there, “Is it lawful for you to flog a Roman citizen without a trial?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.26', 'BSB', 'On hearing this, the centurion went and reported it to the commander. “What are you going to do?” he said. “This man is a Roman citizen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.27', 'BSB', 'The commander went to Paul and asked, “Tell me, are you a Roman citizen?” “Yes,” he answered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.28', 'BSB', '“I paid a high price for my citizenship,” said the commander. “But I was born a citizen,” Paul replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.29', 'BSB', 'Then those who were about to interrogate Paul stepped back, and the commander himself was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen in chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.22.30', 'BSB', 'The next day the commander, wanting to learn the real reason Paul was accused by the Jews, released him and ordered the chief priests and the whole Sanhedrin to assemble. Then he brought Paul down and had him stand before them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.1', 'BSB', 'Paul looked directly at the Sanhedrin and said, “Brothers, I have conducted myself before God in all good conscience to this day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.2', 'BSB', 'At this, the high priest Ananias ordered those standing near Paul to strike him on the mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.3', 'BSB', 'Then Paul said to him, “God will strike you, you whitewashed wall! You sit here to judge me according to the law, yet you yourself violate the law by commanding that I be struck.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.4', 'BSB', 'But those standing nearby said, “How dare you insult the high priest of God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.5', 'BSB', '“Brothers,” Paul replied, “I was not aware that he was the high priest, for it is written: ‘Do not speak evil about the ruler of your people.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.6', 'BSB', 'Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and others Pharisees, called out in the Sanhedrin, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee. It is because of my hope in the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.7', 'BSB', 'As soon as he had said this, a dispute broke out between the Pharisees and Sadducees, and the assembly was divided.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.8', 'BSB', 'For the Sadducees say that there is neither a resurrection, nor angels, nor spirits, but the Pharisees acknowledge them all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.9', 'BSB', 'A great clamor arose, and some scribes from the party of the Pharisees got up and contended sharply, “We find nothing wrong with this man. What if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.10', 'BSB', 'The dispute grew so violent that the commander was afraid they would tear Paul to pieces. He ordered the soldiers to go down and remove him by force and bring him into the barracks.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.11', 'BSB', 'The following night the Lord stood near Paul and said, “Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so also you must testify in Rome.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.12', 'BSB', 'When daylight came, the Jews formed a conspiracy and bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they had killed Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.13', 'BSB', 'More than forty of them were involved in this plot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.14', 'BSB', 'They went to the chief priests and elders and said, “We have bound ourselves with a solemn oath not to eat anything until we have killed Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.15', 'BSB', 'Now then, you and the Sanhedrin petition the commander to bring him down to you on the pretext of examining his case more carefully. We are ready to kill him on the way.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.16', 'BSB', 'But when the son of Paul’s sister heard about the plot, he went into the barracks and told Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.17', 'BSB', 'Then Paul called one of the centurions and said, “Take this young man to the commander; he has something to tell him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.18', 'BSB', 'So the centurion took him to the commander and said, “Paul the prisoner sent and asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.19', 'BSB', 'The commander took the young man by the hand, drew him aside, and asked, “What do you need to tell me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.20', 'BSB', 'He answered, “The Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul to the Sanhedrin tomorrow on the pretext of acquiring more information about him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.21', 'BSB', 'Do not let them persuade you, because more than forty men are waiting to ambush him. They have bound themselves with an oath not to eat or drink until they have killed him; they are ready now, awaiting your consent.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.22', 'BSB', 'So the commander dismissed the young man and instructed him, “Do not tell anyone that you have reported this to me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.23', 'BSB', 'Then he called two of his centurions and said, “Prepare two hundred soldiers, seventy horsemen, and two hundred spearmen to go to Caesarea in the third hour of the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.24', 'BSB', 'Provide mounts for Paul to take him safely to Governor Felix.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.25', 'BSB', 'And he wrote the following letter:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.26', 'BSB', 'Claudius Lysias, To His Excellency, Governor Felix: Greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.27', 'BSB', 'This man was seized by the Jews, and they were about to kill him when I came with my troops to rescue him. For I had learned that he is a Roman citizen,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.28', 'BSB', 'and since I wanted to understand their charges against him, I brought him down to their Sanhedrin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.29', 'BSB', 'I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.30', 'BSB', 'When I was informed that there was a plot against the man, I sent him to you at once. I also instructed his accusers to present their case against him before you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.31', 'BSB', 'So the soldiers followed their orders and brought Paul by night to Antipatris.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.32', 'BSB', 'The next day they returned to the barracks and let the horsemen go on with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.33', 'BSB', 'When the horsemen arrived in Caesarea, they delivered the letter to the governor and presented Paul to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.34', 'BSB', 'The governor read the letter and asked what province Paul was from. Learning that he was from Cilicia,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.23.35', 'BSB', 'he said, “I will hear your case when your accusers arrive.” Then he ordered that Paul be kept under guard in Herod’s Praetorium.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.1', 'BSB', 'Five days later the high priest Ananias came down with some elders and a lawyer named Tertullus, who presented to the governor their case against Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.2', 'BSB', 'When Paul had been called in, Tertullus opened the prosecution: “Because of you, we have enjoyed a lasting peace, and your foresight has brought improvements to this nation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.3', 'BSB', 'In every way and everywhere, most excellent Felix, we acknowledge this with all gratitude.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.4', 'BSB', 'But in order not to burden you any further, I beg your indulgence to hear us briefly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.5', 'BSB', 'We have found this man to be a pestilence, stirring up dissension among the Jews all over the world. He is a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.6', 'BSB', 'and he even tried to desecrate the temple; so we seized him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.8', 'BSB', 'By examining him yourself, you will be able to learn the truth about all our charges against him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.9', 'BSB', 'The Jews concurred, asserting that these charges were true.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.10', 'BSB', 'When the governor motioned for Paul to speak, he began his response: “Knowing that you have been a judge over this nation for many years, I gladly make my defense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.11', 'BSB', 'You can verify for yourself that no more than twelve days ago I went up to Jerusalem to worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.12', 'BSB', 'Yet my accusers did not find me debating with anyone in the temple or riling up a crowd in the synagogues or in the city.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.13', 'BSB', 'Nor can they prove to you any of their charges against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.14', 'BSB', 'I do confess to you, however, that I worship the God of our fathers according to the Way, which they call a sect. I believe everything that is laid down by the Law and written in the Prophets,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.15', 'BSB', 'and I have the same hope in God that they themselves cherish, that there will be a resurrection of both the righteous and the wicked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.16', 'BSB', 'In this hope, I strive always to maintain a clear conscience before God and man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.17', 'BSB', 'After several years, then, I returned to Jerusalem to bring alms to my people and to present offerings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.18', 'BSB', 'At the time they found me in the temple, I was ceremonially clean and was not inciting a crowd or an uproar. But there are some Jews from the province of Asia', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.19', 'BSB', 'who ought to appear before you and bring charges, if they have anything against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.20', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, let these men state for themselves any crime they found in me when I stood before the Sanhedrin,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.21', 'BSB', 'unless it was this one thing I called out as I stood in their presence: ‘It is concerning the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial before you today.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.22', 'BSB', 'Then Felix, who was well informed about the Way, adjourned the hearing and said, “When Lysias the commander comes, I will decide your case.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.23', 'BSB', 'He ordered the centurion to keep Paul under guard, but to allow him some freedom and permit his friends to minister to his needs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.24', 'BSB', 'After several days, Felix returned with his wife Drusilla, who was a Jewess. He sent for Paul and listened to him speak about faith in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.25', 'BSB', 'As Paul expounded on righteousness, self-control, and the coming judgment, Felix became frightened and said, “You may go for now. When I find the time, I will call for you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.26', 'BSB', 'At the same time, he was hoping that Paul would offer him a bribe. So he sent for Paul frequently and talked with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.24.27', 'BSB', 'After two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.1', 'BSB', 'Three days after his arrival in the province, Festus went up from Caesarea to Jerusalem,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.2', 'BSB', 'where the chief priests and Jewish leaders presented their case against Paul. They urged Festus', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.3', 'BSB', 'to grant them a concession against Paul by summoning him to Jerusalem, because they were preparing an ambush to kill him along the way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.4', 'BSB', 'But Festus replied, “Paul is being held in Caesarea, and I myself am going there soon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.5', 'BSB', 'So if this man has done anything wrong, let some of your leaders come down with me and accuse him there.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.6', 'BSB', 'After spending no more than eight or ten days with them, Festus went down to Caesarea. The next day he sat on the judgment seat and ordered that Paul be brought in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.7', 'BSB', 'When Paul arrived, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many serious charges that they could not prove.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.8', 'BSB', 'Then Paul made his defense: “I have committed no offense against the law of the Jews or against the temple or against Caesar.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.9', 'BSB', 'But Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor, said to Paul, “Are you willing to go up to Jerusalem to stand trial before me on these charges?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.10', 'BSB', 'Paul replied, “I am standing before the judgment seat of Caesar, where I ought to be tried. I have done nothing wrong to the Jews, as you yourself know very well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.11', 'BSB', 'If, however, I am guilty of anything worthy of death, I do not refuse to die. But if there is no truth to their accusations against me, no one has the right to hand me over to them. I appeal to Caesar!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.12', 'BSB', 'Then Festus conferred with his council and replied, “You have appealed to Caesar. To Caesar you will go!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.13', 'BSB', 'After several days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice came down to Caesarea to pay their respects to Festus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.14', 'BSB', 'Since they were staying several days, Festus laid out Paul’s case before the king: “There is a certain man whom Felix left in prison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.15', 'BSB', 'While I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and elders of the Jews presented their case and requested a judgment against him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.16', 'BSB', 'I told them that it is not the Roman custom to hand a man over before he has had an opportunity to face his accusers and defend himself against their charges.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.17', 'BSB', 'So when they came here with me, I did not delay. The next day I sat on the judgment seat and ordered that the man be brought in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.18', 'BSB', 'But when his accusers rose to speak, they did not charge him with any of the crimes I had expected.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.19', 'BSB', 'They only had some contentions with him regarding their own religion and a certain Jesus who had died, but whom Paul affirmed to be alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.20', 'BSB', 'Since I was at a loss as to how to investigate these matters, I asked if he was willing to go to Jerusalem and be tried there on these charges.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.21', 'BSB', 'But when Paul appealed to be held over for the decision of the Emperor, I ordered that he be held until I could send him to Caesar.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.22', 'BSB', 'Then Agrippa said to Festus, “I would like to hear this man myself.” “Tomorrow you will hear him,” Festus declared.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.23', 'BSB', 'The next day Agrippa and Bernice came with great pomp and entered the auditorium, along with the commanders and leading men of the city. And Festus ordered that Paul be brought in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.24', 'BSB', 'Then Festus said, “King Agrippa and all who are present with us, you see this man. The whole Jewish community has petitioned me about him, both here and in Jerusalem, crying out that he ought not to live any longer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.25', 'BSB', 'But I found he had done nothing worthy of death, and since he has now appealed to the Emperor, I decided to send him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.26', 'BSB', 'I have nothing definite to write to our sovereign one about him. Therefore I have brought him before all of you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, so that after this inquiry I may have something to write.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.25.27', 'BSB', 'For it seems unreasonable to me to send on a prisoner without specifying the charges against him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.1', 'BSB', 'Agrippa said to Paul, “You have permission to speak for yourself.” Then Paul stretched out his hand and began his defense:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.2', 'BSB', '“King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate to stand before you today to defend myself against all the accusations of the Jews,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.3', 'BSB', 'especially since you are acquainted with all the Jewish customs and controversies. I beg you, therefore, to listen to me patiently.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.4', 'BSB', 'Surely all the Jews know how I have lived from the earliest days of my youth, among my own people and in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.5', 'BSB', 'They have known me for a long time and can testify, if they are willing, that I lived as a Pharisee, adhering to the strictest sect of our religion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.6', 'BSB', 'And now I stand on trial because of my hope in the promise that God made to our fathers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.7', 'BSB', 'the promise our twelve tribes are hoping to realize as they earnestly serve God day and night. It is because of this hope, O king, that I am accused by the Jews.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.8', 'BSB', 'Why would any of you consider it incredible that God raises the dead?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.9', 'BSB', 'So then, I too was convinced that I ought to do all I could to oppose the name of Jesus of Nazareth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.10', 'BSB', 'And that is what I did in Jerusalem. With authority from the chief priests I put many of the saints in prison, and when they were condemned to death, I cast my vote against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.11', 'BSB', 'I frequently had them punished in the synagogues, and I tried to make them blaspheme. In my raging fury against them, I even went to foreign cities to persecute them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.12', 'BSB', 'In this pursuit I was on my way to Damascus with the authority and commission of the chief priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.13', 'BSB', 'About noon, O king, as I was on the road, I saw a light from heaven, brighter than the sun, shining around me and my companions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.14', 'BSB', 'We all fell to the ground, and I heard a voice say to me in Hebrew, ‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.15', 'BSB', '‘Who are You, Lord?’ I asked. ‘I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting,’ the Lord replied.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.16', 'BSB', '‘But get up and stand on your feet. For I have appeared to you to appoint you as a servant and as a witness of what you have seen from Me and what I will show you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.17', 'BSB', 'I will rescue you from your own people and from the Gentiles. I am sending you to them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.18', 'BSB', 'to open their eyes, so that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, that they may receive forgiveness of sins and an inheritance among those sanctified by faith in Me.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.19', 'BSB', 'So then, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.20', 'BSB', 'First to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, then to everyone in the region of Judea, and then to the Gentiles, I declared that they should repent and turn to God, performing deeds worthy of their repentance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.21', 'BSB', 'For this reason the Jews seized me in the temple courts and tried to kill me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.22', 'BSB', 'But I have had God’s help to this day, and I stand here to testify to small and great alike. I am saying nothing beyond what the prophets and Moses said would happen:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.23', 'BSB', 'that the Christ would suffer, and as the first to rise from the dead, would proclaim light to our people and to the Gentiles.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.24', 'BSB', 'At this stage of Paul’s defense, Festus exclaimed in a loud voice, “You are insane, Paul! Your great learning is driving you to madness!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.25', 'BSB', 'But Paul answered, “I am not insane, most excellent Festus; I am speaking words of truth and sobriety.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.26', 'BSB', 'For the king knows about these matters, and I can speak freely to him. I am confident that none of this has escaped his notice, because it was not done in a corner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.27', 'BSB', 'King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you do.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.28', 'BSB', 'Then Agrippa said to Paul, “Can you persuade me in such a short time to become a Christian?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.29', 'BSB', '“Short time or long,” Paul replied, “I wish to God that not only you but all who hear me this day may become what I am, except for these chains.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.30', 'BSB', 'Then the king and the governor rose, along with Bernice and those seated with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.31', 'BSB', 'On their way out, they said to one another, “This man has done nothing worthy of death or imprisonment.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.26.32', 'BSB', 'And Agrippa said to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.1', 'BSB', 'When it was decided that we would sail for Italy, Paul and some other prisoners were handed over to a centurion named Julius, who belonged to the Imperial Regiment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.2', 'BSB', 'We boarded an Adramyttian ship about to sail for ports along the coast of Asia, and we put out to sea. Aristarchus, a Macedonian from Thessalonica, was with us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.3', 'BSB', 'The next day we landed at Sidon, and Julius treated Paul with consideration, allowing him to visit his friends and receive their care.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.4', 'BSB', 'After putting out from there, we sailed to the lee of Cyprus because the winds were against us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.5', 'BSB', 'And when we had sailed across the open sea off the coast of Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra in Lycia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.6', 'BSB', 'There the centurion found an Alexandrian ship sailing for Italy and put us on board.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.7', 'BSB', 'After sailing slowly for many days, we arrived off Cnidus. When the wind impeded us, we sailed to the lee of Crete, opposite Salmone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.8', 'BSB', 'After we had moved along the coast with difficulty, we came to a place called Fair Havens, near the town of Lasea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.9', 'BSB', 'By now much time had passed, and the voyage had already become dangerous because it was after the Fast. So Paul advised them,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.10', 'BSB', '“Men, I can see that our voyage will be filled with disaster and great loss, not only to ship and cargo, but to our own lives as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.11', 'BSB', 'But contrary to Paul’s advice, the centurion was persuaded by the pilot and by the owner of the ship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.12', 'BSB', 'Since the harbor was unsuitable to winter in, the majority decided to sail on, if somehow they could reach Phoenix to winter there. Phoenix was a harbor in Crete facing both southwest and northwest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.13', 'BSB', 'When a gentle south wind began to blow, they thought they had their opportunity. So they weighed anchor and sailed along, hugging the coast of Crete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.14', 'BSB', 'But it was not long before a cyclone called the Northeaster swept down across the island.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.15', 'BSB', 'Unable to head into the wind, the ship was caught up. So we gave way and let ourselves be driven along.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.16', 'BSB', 'Passing to the lee of a small island called Cauda, we barely managed to secure the lifeboat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.17', 'BSB', 'After hoisting it up, the crew used ropes to undergird the ship. And fearing that they would run aground on the sandbars of Syrtis, they lowered the sea anchor and were driven along.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.18', 'BSB', 'We were tossed so violently that the next day the men began to jettison the cargo.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.19', 'BSB', 'On the third day, they threw the ship’s tackle overboard with their own hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.20', 'BSB', 'When neither sun nor stars appeared for many days and the great storm continued to batter us, we abandoned all hope of being saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.21', 'BSB', 'After the men had gone a long time without food, Paul stood up among them and said, “Men, you should have followed my advice not to sail from Crete. Then you would have averted this disaster and loss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.22', 'BSB', 'But now I urge you to keep up your courage, because you will not experience any loss of life, but only of the ship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.23', 'BSB', 'For just last night an angel of God, whose I am and whom I serve, stood beside me', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.24', 'BSB', 'and said, ‘Do not be afraid, Paul; you must stand before Caesar. And look, God has granted you the lives of all who sail with you.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.25', 'BSB', 'So take courage, men, for I believe God that it will happen just as He told me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.26', 'BSB', 'However, we must run aground on some island.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.27', 'BSB', 'On the fourteenth night we were still being driven across the Adriatic Sea. About midnight the sailors sensed they were approaching land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.28', 'BSB', 'They took soundings and found that the water was twenty fathoms deep. Going a little farther, they took another set of soundings that read fifteen fathoms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.29', 'BSB', 'Fearing that we would run aground on the rocks, they dropped four anchors from the stern and prayed for daybreak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.30', 'BSB', 'Meanwhile, the sailors attempted to escape from the ship. Pretending to lower anchors from the bow, they let the lifeboat down into the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.31', 'BSB', 'But Paul said to the centurion and the soldiers, “Unless these men remain with the ship, you cannot be saved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.32', 'BSB', 'So the soldiers cut the ropes to the lifeboat and set it adrift.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.33', 'BSB', 'Right up to daybreak, Paul kept urging them all to eat: “Today is your fourteenth day in constant suspense, without taking any food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.34', 'BSB', 'So for your own preservation, I urge you to eat something, because not a single hair of your head will be lost.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.35', 'BSB', 'After he had said this, Paul took bread and gave thanks to God in front of them all. Then he broke it and began to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.36', 'BSB', 'They were all encouraged and took some food themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.37', 'BSB', 'In all, there were 276 of us on board.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.38', 'BSB', 'After the men had eaten their fill, they lightened the ship by throwing the grain into the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.39', 'BSB', 'When daylight came, they did not recognize the land, but they sighted a bay with a sandy beach, where they decided to run the ship aground if they could.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.40', 'BSB', 'Cutting away the anchors, they left them in the sea as they loosened the ropes that held the rudders. Then they hoisted the foresail to the wind and made for the beach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.41', 'BSB', 'But the vessel struck a sandbar and ran aground. The bow stuck fast and would not move, and the stern was being broken up by the pounding of the waves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.42', 'BSB', 'The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners so none of them could swim to freedom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.43', 'BSB', 'But the centurion, wanting to spare Paul’s life, thwarted their plan. He commanded those who could swim to jump overboard first and get to land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.27.44', 'BSB', 'The rest were to follow on planks and various parts of the ship. In this way everyone was brought safely to land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.1', 'BSB', 'Once we were safely ashore, we learned that the island was called Malta.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.2', 'BSB', 'The islanders showed us extraordinary kindness. They kindled a fire and welcomed all of us because it was raining and cold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.3', 'BSB', 'Paul gathered a bundle of sticks, and as he laid them on the fire, a viper, driven out by the heat, fastened itself to his hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.4', 'BSB', 'When the islanders saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, “Surely this man is a murderer. Although he was saved from the sea, Justice has not allowed him to live.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.5', 'BSB', 'But Paul shook the creature off into the fire and suffered no ill effects.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.6', 'BSB', 'The islanders were expecting him to swell up or suddenly drop dead. But after waiting a long time and seeing nothing unusual happen to him, they changed their minds and said he was a god.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.7', 'BSB', 'Nearby stood an estate belonging to Publius, the chief official of the island. He welcomed us and entertained us hospitably for three days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.8', 'BSB', 'The father of Publius was sick in bed, suffering from fever and dysentery. Paul went in to see him, and after praying and placing his hands on him, he healed the man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.9', 'BSB', 'After this had happened, the rest of the sick on the island came and were cured as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.10', 'BSB', 'The islanders honored us in many ways and supplied our needs when we were ready to sail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.11', 'BSB', 'After three months we set sail in an Alexandrian ship that had wintered in the island. It had the Twin Brothers as a figurehead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.12', 'BSB', 'Putting in at Syracuse, we stayed there three days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.13', 'BSB', 'From there we weighed anchor and came to Rhegium. After one day, a south wind came up, and on the second day we arrived at Puteoli.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.14', 'BSB', 'There we found some brothers who invited us to spend the week with them. And so we came to Rome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.15', 'BSB', 'The brothers there had heard about us and traveled as far as the Forum of Appius and the Three Taverns to meet us. When Paul saw them, he was encouraged and gave thanks to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.16', 'BSB', 'When we arrived in Rome, Paul was permitted to stay by himself, with a soldier to guard him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.17', 'BSB', 'After three days, he called together the leaders of the Jews. When they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, although I have done nothing against our people or the customs of our fathers, I was taken prisoner in Jerusalem and handed over to the Romans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.18', 'BSB', 'They examined me and wanted to release me, because there was no basis for a death sentence against me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.19', 'BSB', 'But when the Jews objected, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, even though I have no charge to bring against my nation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.20', 'BSB', 'So for this reason I have called to see you and speak with you. It is because of the hope of Israel that I am bound with this chain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.21', 'BSB', 'The leaders replied, “We have not received any letters about you from Judea, nor have any of the brothers from there reported or even mentioned anything bad about you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.22', 'BSB', 'But we consider your views worth hearing, because we know that people everywhere are speaking against this sect.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.23', 'BSB', 'So they set a day to meet with Paul, and many people came to the place he was staying. He expounded to them from morning to evening, testifying about the kingdom of God and persuading them about Jesus from the Law of Moses and the Prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.24', 'BSB', 'Some of them were convinced by what he said, but others refused to believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.25', 'BSB', 'They disagreed among themselves and began to leave after Paul had made this final statement: “The Holy Spirit was right when He spoke to your fathers through Isaiah the prophet:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.26', 'BSB', '‘Go to this people and say, “You will be ever hearing but never understanding; you will be ever seeing but never perceiving.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.27', 'BSB', 'For this people’s heart has grown callous; they hardly hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.28', 'BSB', 'Be advised, therefore, that God’s salvation has been sent to the Gentiles, and they will listen!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.30', 'BSB', 'Paul stayed there two full years in his own rented house, welcoming all who came to visit him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Acts.28.31', 'BSB', 'Boldly and freely he proclaimed the kingdom of God and taught about the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus, called to be an apostle, and set apart for the gospel of God—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.2', 'BSB', 'the gospel He promised beforehand through His prophets in the Holy Scriptures,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.3', 'BSB', 'regarding His Son, who was a descendant of David according to the flesh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.4', 'BSB', 'and who through the Spirit of holiness was declared with power to be the Son of God by His resurrection from the dead: Jesus Christ our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.5', 'BSB', 'Through Him and on behalf of His name, we received grace and apostleship to call all those among the Gentiles to the obedience that comes from faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.6', 'BSB', 'And you also are among those who are called to belong to Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.7', 'BSB', 'To all in Rome who are loved by God and called to be saints: Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.8', 'BSB', 'First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for all of you, because your faith is being proclaimed all over the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.9', 'BSB', 'God, whom I serve with my spirit in preaching the gospel of His Son, is my witness how constantly I remember you', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.10', 'BSB', 'in my prayers at all times, asking that now at last by God’s will I may succeed in coming to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.11', 'BSB', 'For I long to see you so that I may impart to you some spiritual gift to strengthen you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.12', 'BSB', 'that is, that you and I may be mutually encouraged by each other’s faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.13', 'BSB', 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, how often I planned to come to you (but have been prevented from visiting until now), in order that I might have a harvest among you, just as I have had among the other Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.14', 'BSB', 'I am obligated both to Greeks and non-Greeks, both to the wise and the foolish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.15', 'BSB', 'That is why I am so eager to preach the gospel also to you who are in Rome.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.16', 'BSB', 'I am not ashamed of the gospel, because it is the power of God for salvation to everyone who believes, first to the Jew, then to the Greek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.17', 'BSB', 'For the gospel reveals the righteousness of God that comes by faith from start to finish, just as it is written: “The righteous will live by faith.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.18', 'BSB', 'The wrath of God is being revealed from heaven against all the godlessness and wickedness of men who suppress the truth by their wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.19', 'BSB', 'For what may be known about God is plain to them, because God has made it plain to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.20', 'BSB', 'For since the creation of the world God’s invisible qualities, His eternal power and divine nature, have been clearly seen, being understood from His workmanship, so that men are without excuse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.21', 'BSB', 'For although they knew God, they neither glorified Him as God nor gave thanks to Him, but they became futile in their thinking and darkened in their foolish hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.22', 'BSB', 'Although they claimed to be wise, they became fools,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.23', 'BSB', 'and exchanged the glory of the immortal God for images of mortal man and birds and animals and reptiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.24', 'BSB', 'Therefore God gave them over in the desires of their hearts to impurity for the dishonoring of their bodies with one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.25', 'BSB', 'They exchanged the truth of God for a lie, and worshiped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is forever worthy of praise! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.26', 'BSB', 'For this reason God gave them over to dishonorable passions. Even their women exchanged natural relations for unnatural ones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.27', 'BSB', 'Likewise, the men abandoned natural relations with women and burned with lust for one another. Men committed indecent acts with other men, and received in themselves the due penalty for their error.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.28', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, since they did not see fit to acknowledge God, He gave them up to a depraved mind, to do what ought not to be done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.29', 'BSB', 'They have become filled with every kind of wickedness, evil, greed, and depravity. They are full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, and malice. They are gossips,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.30', 'BSB', 'slanderers, God-haters, insolent, arrogant, and boastful. They invent new forms of evil; they disobey their parents.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.31', 'BSB', 'They are senseless, faithless, heartless, merciless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.1.32', 'BSB', 'Although they know God’s righteous decree that those who do such things are worthy of death, they not only continue to do these things, but also approve of those who practice them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.1', 'BSB', 'You, therefore, have no excuse, you who pass judgment on another. For on whatever grounds you judge the other, you are condemning yourself, because you who pass judgment do the same things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.2', 'BSB', 'And we know that God’s judgment against those who do such things is based on truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.3', 'BSB', 'So when you, O man, pass judgment on others, yet do the same things, do you think you will escape God’s judgment?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.4', 'BSB', 'Or do you disregard the riches of His kindness, tolerance, and patience, not realizing that God’s kindness leads you to repentance?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.5', 'BSB', 'But because of your hard and unrepentant heart, you are storing up wrath against yourself for the day of wrath, when God’s righteous judgment will be revealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.6', 'BSB', 'God “will repay each one according to his deeds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.7', 'BSB', 'To those who by perseverance in doing good seek glory, honor, and immortality, He will give eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.8', 'BSB', 'But for those who are self-seeking and who reject the truth and follow wickedness, there will be wrath and anger.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.9', 'BSB', 'There will be trouble and distress for every human being who does evil, first for the Jew, then for the Greek;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.10', 'BSB', 'but glory, honor, and peace for everyone who does good, first for the Jew, then for the Greek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.11', 'BSB', 'For God does not show favoritism.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.12', 'BSB', 'All who sin apart from the law will also perish apart from the law, and all who sin under the law will be judged by the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.13', 'BSB', 'For it is not the hearers of the law who are righteous before God, but it is the doers of the law who will be declared righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.14', 'BSB', 'Indeed, when Gentiles, who do not have the law, do by nature what the law requires, they are a law to themselves, even though they do not have the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.15', 'BSB', 'So they show that the work of the law is written on their hearts, their consciences also bearing witness, and their thoughts either accusing or defending them', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.16', 'BSB', 'on the day when God will judge men’s secrets through Christ Jesus, as proclaimed by my gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.17', 'BSB', 'Now you, if you call yourself a Jew; if you rely on the law and boast in God;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.18', 'BSB', 'if you know His will and approve of what is superior because you are instructed by the law;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.19', 'BSB', 'if you are convinced that you are a guide for the blind, a light for those in darkness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.20', 'BSB', 'an instructor of the foolish, a teacher of infants, because you have in the law the embodiment of knowledge and truth—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.21', 'BSB', 'you, then, who teach others, do you not teach yourself? You who preach against stealing, do you steal?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.22', 'BSB', 'You who forbid adultery, do you commit adultery? You who abhor idols, do you rob temples?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.23', 'BSB', 'You who boast in the law, do you dishonor God by breaking the law?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.24', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “God’s name is blasphemed among the Gentiles because of you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.25', 'BSB', 'Circumcision has value if you observe the law, but if you break the law, your circumcision has become uncircumcision.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.26', 'BSB', 'If a man who is not circumcised keeps the requirements of the law, will not his uncircumcision be regarded as circumcision?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.27', 'BSB', 'The one who is physically uncircumcised yet keeps the law will condemn you who, even though you have the written code and circumcision, are a lawbreaker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.28', 'BSB', 'A man is not a Jew because he is one outwardly, nor is circumcision only outward and physical.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.2.29', 'BSB', 'No, a man is a Jew because he is one inwardly, and circumcision is a matter of the heart, by the Spirit, not by the written code. Such a man’s praise does not come from men, but from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.1', 'BSB', 'What, then, is the advantage of being a Jew? Or what is the value of circumcision?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.2', 'BSB', 'Much in every way. First of all, they have been entrusted with the very words of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.3', 'BSB', 'What if some did not have faith? Will their lack of faith nullify God’s faithfulness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.4', 'BSB', 'Certainly not! Let God be true and every man a liar. As it is written: “So that You may be proved right when You speak and victorious when You judge.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.5', 'BSB', 'But if our unrighteousness highlights the righteousness of God, what shall we say? That God is unjust to inflict His wrath on us? I am speaking in human terms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.6', 'BSB', 'Certainly not! In that case, how could God judge the world?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.7', 'BSB', 'However, if my falsehood accentuates God’s truthfulness, to the increase of His glory, why am I still condemned as a sinner?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.8', 'BSB', 'Why not say, as some slanderously claim that we say, “Let us do evil that good may result”? Their condemnation is deserved!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.9', 'BSB', 'What then? Are we any better? Not at all. For we have already made the charge that Jews and Greeks alike are all under sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.10', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “There is no one righteous, not even one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.11', 'BSB', 'There is no one who understands, no one who seeks God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.12', 'BSB', 'All have turned away, they have together become worthless; there is no one who does good, not even one.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.13', 'BSB', '“Their throats are open graves; their tongues practice deceit.” “The venom of vipers is on their lips.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.14', 'BSB', '“Their mouths are full of cursing and bitterness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.15', 'BSB', '“Their feet are swift to shed blood;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.16', 'BSB', 'ruin and misery lie in their wake,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.17', 'BSB', 'and the way of peace they have not known.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.18', 'BSB', '“There is no fear of God before their eyes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.19', 'BSB', 'Now we know that whatever the law says, it says to those who are under the law, so that every mouth may be silenced and the whole world held accountable to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore no one will be justified in His sight by works of the law. For the law merely brings awareness of sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.21', 'BSB', 'But now, apart from the law, the righteousness of God has been revealed, as attested by the Law and the Prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.22', 'BSB', 'And this righteousness from God comes through faith in Jesus Christ to all who believe. There is no distinction,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.23', 'BSB', 'for all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.24', 'BSB', 'and are justified freely by His grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.25', 'BSB', 'God presented Him as the atoning sacrifice through faith in His blood, in order to demonstrate His righteousness, because in His forbearance He had passed over the sins committed beforehand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.26', 'BSB', 'He did this to demonstrate His righteousness at the present time, so as to be just and to justify the one who has faith in Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.27', 'BSB', 'Where, then, is boasting? It is excluded. On what principle? On that of works? No, but on that of faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.28', 'BSB', 'For we maintain that a man is justified by faith apart from works of the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.29', 'BSB', 'Is God the God of Jews only? Is He not the God of Gentiles too? Yes, of Gentiles too,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.30', 'BSB', 'since there is only one God, who will justify the circumcised by faith and the uncircumcised through that same faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.3.31', 'BSB', 'Do we, then, nullify the law by this faith? Certainly not! Instead, we uphold the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.1', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say that Abraham, our forefather, has discovered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.2', 'BSB', 'If Abraham was indeed justified by works, he had something to boast about, but not before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.3', 'BSB', 'For what does the Scripture say? “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.4', 'BSB', 'Now the wages of the worker are not credited as a gift, but as an obligation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.5', 'BSB', 'However, to the one who does not work, but believes in Him who justifies the wicked, his faith is credited as righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.6', 'BSB', 'And David speaks likewise of the blessedness of the man to whom God credits righteousness apart from works:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.7', 'BSB', '“Blessed are they whose lawless acts are forgiven, whose sins are covered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.8', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man whose sin the Lord will never count against him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.9', 'BSB', 'Is this blessing only on the circumcised, or also on the uncircumcised? We have been saying that Abraham’s faith was credited to him as righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.10', 'BSB', 'In what context was it credited? Was it after his circumcision, or before? It was not after, but before.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.11', 'BSB', 'And he received the sign of circumcision as a seal of the righteousness that he had by faith while he was still uncircumcised. So then, he is the father of all who believe but are not circumcised, in order that righteousness might be credited to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.12', 'BSB', 'And he is also the father of the circumcised who not only are circumcised, but who also walk in the footsteps of the faith that our father Abraham had before he was circumcised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.13', 'BSB', 'For the promise to Abraham and his offspring that he would be heir of the world was not given through the law, but through the righteousness that comes by faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.14', 'BSB', 'For if those who live by the law are heirs, faith is useless and the promise is worthless,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.15', 'BSB', 'because the law brings wrath. And where there is no law, there is no transgression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore, the promise comes by faith, so that it may rest on grace and may be guaranteed to all Abraham’s offspring—not only to those who are of the law, but also to those who are of the faith of Abraham. He is the father of us all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.17', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “I have made you a father of many nations.” He is our father in the presence of God, in whom he believed, the God who gives life to the dead and calls into being what does not yet exist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.18', 'BSB', 'Against all hope, Abraham in hope believed and so became the father of many nations, just as he had been told, “So shall your offspring be.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.19', 'BSB', 'Without weakening in his faith, he acknowledged the decrepitness of his body (since he was about a hundred years old) and the lifelessness of Sarah’s womb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.20', 'BSB', 'Yet he did not waver through disbelief in the promise of God, but was strengthened in his faith and gave glory to God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.21', 'BSB', 'being fully persuaded that God was able to do what He had promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.22', 'BSB', 'This is why “it was credited to him as righteousness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.23', 'BSB', 'Now the words “it was credited to him” were written not only for Abraham,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.24', 'BSB', 'but also for us, to whom righteousness will be credited—for us who believe in Him who raised Jesus our Lord from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.4.25', 'BSB', 'He was delivered over to death for our trespasses and was raised to life for our justification.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we have been justified through faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.2', 'BSB', 'through whom we have gained access by faith into this grace in which we stand. And we rejoice in the hope of the glory of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.3', 'BSB', 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in our sufferings, because we know that suffering produces perseverance;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.4', 'BSB', 'perseverance, character; and character, hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.5', 'BSB', 'And hope does not disappoint us, because God has poured out His love into our hearts through the Holy Spirit, whom He has given us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.6', 'BSB', 'For at just the right time, while we were still powerless, Christ died for the ungodly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.7', 'BSB', 'Very rarely will anyone die for a righteous man, though for a good man someone might possibly dare to die.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.8', 'BSB', 'But God proves His love for us in this: While we were still sinners, Christ died for us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we have now been justified by His blood, how much more shall we be saved from wrath through Him!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.10', 'BSB', 'For if, when we were enemies of God, we were reconciled to Him through the death of His Son, how much more, having been reconciled, shall we be saved through His life!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.11', 'BSB', 'Not only that, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received reconciliation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, just as sin entered the world through one man, and death through sin, so also death was passed on to all men, because all sinned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.13', 'BSB', 'For sin was in the world before the law was given; but sin is not taken into account when there is no law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.14', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, death reigned from Adam until Moses, even over those who did not sin in the way that Adam transgressed. He is a pattern of the One to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.15', 'BSB', 'But the gift is not like the trespass. For if the many died by the trespass of the one man, how much more did God’s grace and the gift that came by the grace of the one man, Jesus Christ, abound to the many!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.16', 'BSB', 'Again, the gift is not like the result of the one man’s sin: The judgment that followed one sin brought condemnation, but the gift that followed many trespasses brought justification.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.17', 'BSB', 'For if, by the trespass of the one man, death reigned through that one man, how much more will those who receive an abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness reign in life through the one man, Jesus Christ!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.18', 'BSB', 'So then, just as one trespass brought condemnation for all men, so also one act of righteousness brought justification and life for all men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.19', 'BSB', 'For just as through the disobedience of the one man the many were made sinners, so also through the obedience of the one man the many will be made righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.20', 'BSB', 'The law came in so that the trespass would increase; but where sin increased, grace increased all the more,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.5.21', 'BSB', 'so that, just as sin reigned in death, so also grace might reign through righteousness to bring eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.1', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say? Shall we continue in sin so that grace may increase?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.2', 'BSB', 'Certainly not! How can we who died to sin live in it any longer?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.3', 'BSB', 'Or aren’t you aware that all of us who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into His death?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.4', 'BSB', 'We were therefore buried with Him through baptism into death, in order that, just as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, we too may walk in newness of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.5', 'BSB', 'For if we have been united with Him like this in His death, we will certainly also be united with Him in His resurrection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.6', 'BSB', 'We know that our old self was crucified with Him so that the body of sin might be rendered powerless, that we should no longer be slaves to sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.7', 'BSB', 'For anyone who has died has been freed from sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.8', 'BSB', 'Now if we died with Christ, we believe that we will also live with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.9', 'BSB', 'For we know that since Christ was raised from the dead, He cannot die again; death no longer has dominion over Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.10', 'BSB', 'The death He died, He died to sin once for all; but the life He lives, He lives to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.11', 'BSB', 'So you too must count yourselves dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore do not let sin reign in your mortal body so that you obey its desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.13', 'BSB', 'Do not present the parts of your body to sin as instruments of wickedness, but present yourselves to God as those who have been brought from death to life; and present the parts of your body to Him as instruments of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.14', 'BSB', 'For sin shall not be your master, because you are not under law, but under grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.15', 'BSB', 'What then? Shall we sin because we are not under law, but under grace? Certainly not!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.16', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that when you offer yourselves as obedient slaves, you are slaves to the one you obey, whether you are slaves to sin leading to death, or to obedience leading to righteousness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.17', 'BSB', 'But thanks be to God that, though you once were slaves to sin, you wholeheartedly obeyed the form of teaching to which you were committed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.18', 'BSB', 'You have been set free from sin and have become slaves to righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.19', 'BSB', 'I am speaking in human terms because of the weakness of your flesh. Just as you used to offer the parts of your body in slavery to impurity and to escalating wickedness, so now offer them in slavery to righteousness leading to holiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.20', 'BSB', 'For when you were slaves to sin, you were free of obligation to righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.21', 'BSB', 'What fruit did you reap at that time from the things of which you are now ashamed? The outcome of those things is death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.22', 'BSB', 'But now that you have been set free from sin and have become slaves to God, the fruit you reap leads to holiness, and the outcome is eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.6.23', 'BSB', 'For the wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.1', 'BSB', 'Do you not know, brothers (for I am speaking to those who know the law), that the law has authority over a man only as long as he lives?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.2', 'BSB', 'For instance, a married woman is bound by law to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is released from the law of marriage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.3', 'BSB', 'So then, if she is joined to another man while her husband is still alive, she is called an adulteress; but if her husband dies, she is free from that law and is not an adulteress, even if she marries another man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.4', 'BSB', 'Therefore, my brothers, you also died to the law through the body of Christ, that you might belong to another, to Him who was raised from the dead, in order that we might bear fruit to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.5', 'BSB', 'For when we lived according to the flesh, the sinful passions aroused by the law were at work in our bodies, bearing fruit for death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.6', 'BSB', 'But now, having died to what bound us, we have been released from the law, so that we serve in the new way of the Spirit, and not in the old way of the written code.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.7', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say? Is the law sin? Certainly not! Indeed, I would not have been mindful of sin if not for the law. For I would not have been aware of coveting if the law had not said, “Do not covet.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.8', 'BSB', 'But sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, produced in me every kind of covetous desire. For apart from the law, sin is dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.9', 'BSB', 'Once I was alive apart from the law; but when the commandment came, sin sprang to life and I died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.10', 'BSB', 'So I discovered that the very commandment that was meant to bring life actually brought death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.11', 'BSB', 'For sin, seizing its opportunity through the commandment, deceived me and through the commandment put me to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.12', 'BSB', 'So then, the law is holy, and the commandment is holy, righteous, and good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.13', 'BSB', 'Did that which is good, then, become death to me? Certainly not! But in order that sin might be exposed as sin, it produced death in me through what was good, so that through the commandment sin might become utterly sinful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.14', 'BSB', 'We know that the law is spiritual; but I am unspiritual, sold as a slave to sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.15', 'BSB', 'I do not understand what I do. For what I want to do, I do not do. But what I hate, I do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.16', 'BSB', 'And if I do what I do not want to do, I admit that the law is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.17', 'BSB', 'In that case, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.18', 'BSB', 'I know that nothing good lives in me, that is, in my flesh; for I have the desire to do what is good, but I cannot carry it out.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.19', 'BSB', 'For I do not do the good I want to do. Instead, I keep on doing the evil I do not want to do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.20', 'BSB', 'And if I do what I do not want, it is no longer I who do it, but it is sin living in me that does it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.21', 'BSB', 'So this is the principle I have discovered: When I want to do good, evil is right there with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.22', 'BSB', 'For in my inner being I delight in God’s law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.23', 'BSB', 'But I see another law at work in my body, warring against the law of my mind and holding me captive to the law of sin that dwells within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.24', 'BSB', 'What a wretched man I am! Who will rescue me from this body of death?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.7.25', 'BSB', 'Thanks be to God, through Jesus Christ our Lord! So then, with my mind I serve the law of God, but with my flesh I serve the law of sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, there is now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.2', 'BSB', 'For in Christ Jesus the law of the Spirit of life set you free from the law of sin and death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.3', 'BSB', 'For what the law was powerless to do in that it was weakened by the flesh, God did by sending His own Son in the likeness of sinful man, as an offering for sin. He thus condemned sin in the flesh,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.4', 'BSB', 'so that the righteous standard of the law might be fulfilled in us, who do not walk according to the flesh but according to the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.5', 'BSB', 'Those who live according to the flesh set their minds on the things of the flesh; but those who live according to the Spirit set their minds on the things of the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.6', 'BSB', 'The mind of the flesh is death, but the mind of the Spirit is life and peace,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.7', 'BSB', 'because the mind of the flesh is hostile to God: It does not submit to God’s law, nor can it do so.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.8', 'BSB', 'Those controlled by the flesh cannot please God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.9', 'BSB', 'You, however, are controlled not by the flesh, but by the Spirit, if the Spirit of God lives in you. And if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ, he does not belong to Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.10', 'BSB', 'But if Christ is in you, your body is dead because of sin, yet your spirit is alive because of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.11', 'BSB', 'And if the Spirit of Him who raised Jesus from the dead is living in you, He who raised Christ Jesus from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through His Spirit, who lives in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, we have an obligation, but it is not to the flesh, to live according to it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.13', 'BSB', 'For if you live according to the flesh, you will die; but if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body, you will live.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.14', 'BSB', 'For all who are led by the Spirit of God are sons of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.15', 'BSB', 'For you did not receive a spirit of slavery that returns you to fear, but you received the Spirit of sonship, by whom we cry, “Abba! Father!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.16', 'BSB', 'The Spirit Himself testifies with our spirit that we are God’s children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.17', 'BSB', 'And if we are children, then we are heirs: heirs of God and co-heirs with Christ—if indeed we suffer with Him, so that we may also be glorified with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.18', 'BSB', 'I consider that our present sufferings are not comparable to the glory that will be revealed in us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.19', 'BSB', 'The creation waits in eager expectation for the revelation of the sons of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.20', 'BSB', 'For the creation was subjected to futility, not by its own will, but because of the One who subjected it, in hope', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.21', 'BSB', 'that the creation itself will be set free from its bondage to decay and brought into the glorious freedom of the children of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.22', 'BSB', 'We know that the whole creation has been groaning together in the pains of childbirth until the present time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.23', 'BSB', 'Not only that, but we ourselves, who have the firstfruits of the Spirit, groan inwardly as we wait eagerly for our adoption as sons, the redemption of our bodies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.24', 'BSB', 'For in this hope we were saved; but hope that is seen is no hope at all. Who hopes for what he can already see?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.25', 'BSB', 'But if we hope for what we do not yet see, we wait for it patiently.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.26', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the Spirit helps us in our weakness. For we do not know how we ought to pray, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us with groans too deep for words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.27', 'BSB', 'And He who searches our hearts knows the mind of the Spirit, because the Spirit intercedes for the saints according to the will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.28', 'BSB', 'And we know that God works all things together for the good of those who love Him, who are called according to His purpose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.29', 'BSB', 'For those God foreknew, He also predestined to be conformed to the image of His Son, so that He would be the firstborn among many brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.30', 'BSB', 'And those He predestined, He also called; those He called, He also justified; those He justified, He also glorified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.31', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.32', 'BSB', 'He who did not spare His own Son but gave Him up for us all, how will He not also, along with Him, freely give us all things?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.33', 'BSB', 'Who will bring any charge against God’s elect? It is God who justifies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.34', 'BSB', 'Who is there to condemn us? For Christ Jesus, who died, and more than that was raised to life, is at the right hand of God—and He is interceding for us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.35', 'BSB', 'Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? Shall trouble or distress or persecution or famine or nakedness or danger or sword?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.36', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “For Your sake we face death all day long; we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.37', 'BSB', 'No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through Him who loved us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.38', 'BSB', 'For I am convinced that neither death nor life, neither angels nor principalities, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.8.39', 'BSB', 'neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.1', 'BSB', 'I speak the truth in Christ; I am not lying, as confirmed by my conscience in the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.2', 'BSB', 'I have deep sorrow and unceasing anguish in my heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.3', 'BSB', 'For I could wish that I myself were cursed and cut off from Christ for the sake of my brothers, my own flesh and blood,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.4', 'BSB', 'the people of Israel. Theirs is the adoption as sons; theirs the divine glory and the covenants; theirs the giving of the law, the temple worship, and the promises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.5', 'BSB', 'Theirs are the patriarchs, and from them proceeds the human descent of Christ, who is God over all, forever worthy of praise! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.6', 'BSB', 'It is not as though God’s word has failed. For not all who are descended from Israel are Israel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.7', 'BSB', 'Nor because they are Abraham’s descendants are they all his children. On the contrary, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.8', 'BSB', 'So it is not the children of the flesh who are God’s children, but it is the children of the promise who are regarded as offspring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.9', 'BSB', 'For this is what the promise stated: “At the appointed time I will return, and Sarah will have a son.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.10', 'BSB', 'Not only that, but Rebecca’s children were conceived by one man, our father Isaac.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.11', 'BSB', 'Yet before the twins were born or had done anything good or bad, in order that God’s plan of election might stand,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.12', 'BSB', 'not by works but by Him who calls, she was told, “The older will serve the younger.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.13', 'BSB', 'So it is written: “Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.14', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say? Is God unjust? Certainly not!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.15', 'BSB', 'For He says to Moses: “I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.16', 'BSB', 'So then, it does not depend on man’s desire or effort, but on God’s mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.17', 'BSB', 'For the Scripture says to Pharaoh: “I raised you up for this very purpose, that I might display My power in you, and that My name might be proclaimed in all the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore God has mercy on whom He wants to have mercy, and He hardens whom He wants to harden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.19', 'BSB', 'One of you will say to me, “Then why does God still find fault? For who can resist His will?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.20', 'BSB', 'But who are you, O man, to talk back to God? Shall what is formed say to Him who formed it, “Why did You make me like this?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.21', 'BSB', 'Does not the potter have the right to make from the same lump of clay one vessel for special occasions and another for common use?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.22', 'BSB', 'What if God, intending to show His wrath and make His power known, bore with great patience the vessels of His wrath, prepared for destruction?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.23', 'BSB', 'What if He did this to make the riches of His glory known to the vessels of His mercy, whom He prepared in advance for glory—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.24', 'BSB', 'including us, whom He has called not only from the Jews, but also from the Gentiles?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.25', 'BSB', 'As He says in Hosea: “I will call them ‘My People’ who are not My people, and I will call her ‘My Beloved’ who is not My beloved,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.26', 'BSB', 'and, “It will happen that in the very place where it was said to them, ‘You are not My people,’ they will be called ‘sons of the living God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.27', 'BSB', 'Isaiah cries out concerning Israel: “Though the number of the Israelites is like the sand of the sea, only the remnant will be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.28', 'BSB', 'For the Lord will carry out His sentence on the earth thoroughly and decisively.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.29', 'BSB', 'It is just as Isaiah foretold: “Unless the Lord of Hosts had left us descendants, we would have become like Sodom, we would have resembled Gomorrah.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.30', 'BSB', 'What then will we say? That the Gentiles, who did not pursue righteousness, have obtained it, a righteousness that is by faith;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.31', 'BSB', 'but Israel, who pursued a law of righteousness, has not attained it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.32', 'BSB', 'Why not? Because their pursuit was not by faith, but as if it were by works. They stumbled over the stumbling stone,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.9.33', 'BSB', 'as it is written: “See, I lay in Zion a stone of stumbling and a rock of offense; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.1', 'BSB', 'Brothers, my heart’s desire and prayer to God for the Israelites is for their salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.2', 'BSB', 'For I testify about them that they are zealous for God, but not on the basis of knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.3', 'BSB', 'Because they were ignorant of God’s righteousness and sought to establish their own, they did not submit to God’s righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.4', 'BSB', 'For Christ is the end of the law, to bring righteousness to everyone who believes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.5', 'BSB', 'For concerning the righteousness that is by the law, Moses writes: “The man who does these things will live by them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.6', 'BSB', 'But the righteousness that is by faith says: “Do not say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ (that is, to bring Christ down)', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.7', 'BSB', 'or, ‘Who will descend into the Abyss?’ (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead).”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.8', 'BSB', 'But what does it say? “The word is near you; it is in your mouth and in your heart,” that is, the word of faith we are proclaiming:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.9', 'BSB', 'that if you confess with your mouth, “Jesus is Lord,” and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead, you will be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.10', 'BSB', 'For with your heart you believe and are justified, and with your mouth you confess and are saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.11', 'BSB', 'It is just as the Scripture says: “Anyone who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.12', 'BSB', 'For there is no difference between Jew and Greek: The same Lord is Lord of all, and gives richly to all who call on Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.13', 'BSB', 'for, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.14', 'BSB', 'How then can they call on the One in whom they have not believed? And how can they believe in the One of whom they have not heard? And how can they hear without someone to preach?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.15', 'BSB', 'And how can they preach unless they are sent? As it is written: “How beautiful are the feet of those who bring good news!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.16', 'BSB', 'But not all of them welcomed the good news. For Isaiah says, “Lord, who has believed our message?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.17', 'BSB', 'Consequently, faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.18', 'BSB', 'But I ask, did they not hear? Indeed they did: “Their voice has gone out into all the earth, their words to the ends of the world.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.19', 'BSB', 'I ask instead, did Israel not understand? First, Moses says: “I will make you jealous by those who are not a nation; I will make you angry by a nation without understanding.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.20', 'BSB', 'And Isaiah boldly says: “I was found by those who did not seek Me; I revealed Myself to those who did not ask for Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.10.21', 'BSB', 'But as for Israel he says: “All day long I have held out My hands to a disobedient and obstinate people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.1', 'BSB', 'I ask then, did God reject His people? Certainly not! I am an Israelite myself, a descendant of Abraham, from the tribe of Benjamin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.2', 'BSB', 'God did not reject His people, whom He foreknew. Do you not know what the Scripture says about Elijah, how he appealed to God against Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.3', 'BSB', '“Lord, they have killed Your prophets and torn down Your altars. I am the only one left, and they are seeking my life as well”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.4', 'BSB', 'And what was the divine reply to him? “I have reserved for Myself seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.5', 'BSB', 'In the same way, at the present time there is a remnant chosen by grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.6', 'BSB', 'And if it is by grace, then it is no longer by works. Otherwise, grace would no longer be grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.7', 'BSB', 'What then? What Israel was seeking, it failed to obtain, but the elect did. The others were hardened,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.8', 'BSB', 'as it is written: “God gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that could not see, and ears that could not hear, to this very day.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.9', 'BSB', 'And David says: “May their table become a snare and a trap, a stumbling block and a retribution to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.10', 'BSB', 'May their eyes be darkened so they cannot see, and their backs be bent forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.11', 'BSB', 'I ask then, did they stumble so as to fall beyond recovery? Certainly not! However, because of their trespass, salvation has come to the Gentiles to make Israel jealous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.12', 'BSB', 'But if their trespass means riches for the world, and their failure means riches for the Gentiles, how much greater riches will their fullness bring!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.13', 'BSB', 'I am speaking to you Gentiles. Inasmuch as I am the apostle to the Gentiles, I magnify my ministry', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.14', 'BSB', 'in the hope that I may provoke my own people to jealousy and save some of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.15', 'BSB', 'For if their rejection is the reconciliation of the world, what will their acceptance be but life from the dead?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.16', 'BSB', 'If the first part of the dough is holy, so is the whole batch; if the root is holy, so are the branches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.17', 'BSB', 'Now if some branches have been broken off, and you, a wild olive shoot, have been grafted in among the others to share in the nourishment of the olive root,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.18', 'BSB', 'do not boast over those branches. If you do, remember this: You do not support the root, but the root supports you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.19', 'BSB', 'You will say then, “Branches were broken off so that I could be grafted in.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.20', 'BSB', 'That is correct: They were broken off because of unbelief, but you stand by faith. Do not be arrogant, but be afraid.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.21', 'BSB', 'For if God did not spare the natural branches, He will certainly not spare you either.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.22', 'BSB', 'Take notice, therefore, of the kindness and severity of God: severity to those who fell, but kindness to you, if you continue in His kindness. Otherwise you also will be cut off.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.23', 'BSB', 'And if they do not persist in unbelief, they will be grafted in, for God is able to graft them in again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.24', 'BSB', 'For if you were cut from a wild olive tree, and contrary to nature were grafted into one that is cultivated, how much more readily will these, the natural branches, be grafted into their own olive tree!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.25', 'BSB', 'I do not want you to be ignorant of this mystery, brothers, so that you will not be conceited: A hardening in part has come to Israel, until the full number of the Gentiles has come in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.26', 'BSB', 'And so all Israel will be saved, as it is written: “The Deliverer will come from Zion; He will remove godlessness from Jacob.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.27', 'BSB', 'And this is My covenant with them when I take away their sins.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.28', 'BSB', 'Regarding the gospel, they are enemies on your account; but regarding election, they are loved on account of the patriarchs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.29', 'BSB', 'For God’s gifts and His call are irrevocable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.30', 'BSB', 'Just as you who formerly disobeyed God have now received mercy through their disobedience,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.31', 'BSB', 'so they too have now disobeyed, in order that they too may now receive mercy through the mercy shown to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.32', 'BSB', 'For God has consigned everyone to disobedience so that He may have mercy on everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.33', 'BSB', 'O, the depth of the riches of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How unsearchable are His judgments, and untraceable His ways!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.34', 'BSB', '“Who has known the mind of the Lord? Or who has been His counselor?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.35', 'BSB', '“Who has first given to God, that God should repay him?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.11.36', 'BSB', 'For from Him and through Him and to Him are all things. To Him be the glory forever! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore I urge you, brothers, on account of God’s mercy, to offer your bodies as living sacrifices, holy and pleasing to God, which is your spiritual service of worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.2', 'BSB', 'Do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind. Then you will be able to test and approve what is the good, pleasing, and perfect will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.3', 'BSB', 'For by the grace given me I say to every one of you: Do not think of yourself more highly than you ought, but think of yourself with sober judgment, according to the measure of faith God has given you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.4', 'BSB', 'Just as each of us has one body with many members, and not all members have the same function,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.5', 'BSB', 'so in Christ we who are many are one body, and each member belongs to one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.6', 'BSB', 'We have different gifts according to the grace given us. If one’s gift is prophecy, let him use it in proportion to his faith;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.7', 'BSB', 'if it is serving, let him serve; if it is teaching, let him teach;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.8', 'BSB', 'if it is encouraging, let him encourage; if it is giving, let him give generously; if it is leading, let him lead with diligence; if it is showing mercy, let him do it cheerfully.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.9', 'BSB', 'Love must be sincere. Detest what is evil; cling to what is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.10', 'BSB', 'Be devoted to one another in brotherly love. Outdo yourselves in honoring one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.11', 'BSB', 'Do not let your zeal subside; keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.12', 'BSB', 'Be joyful in hope, patient in affliction, persistent in prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.13', 'BSB', 'Share with the saints who are in need. Practice hospitality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.14', 'BSB', 'Bless those who persecute you. Bless and do not curse.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.15', 'BSB', 'Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.16', 'BSB', 'Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but enjoy the company of the lowly. Do not be conceited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.17', 'BSB', 'Do not repay anyone evil for evil. Carefully consider what is right in the eyes of everybody.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.18', 'BSB', 'If it is possible on your part, live at peace with everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.19', 'BSB', 'Do not avenge yourselves, beloved, but leave room for God’s wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay, says the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.20', 'BSB', 'On the contrary, “If your enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in so doing, you will heap burning coals on his head.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.12.21', 'BSB', 'Do not be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.1', 'BSB', 'Everyone must submit himself to the governing authorities, for there is no authority except that which is from God. The authorities that exist have been appointed by God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.2', 'BSB', 'Consequently, whoever resists authority is opposing what God has set in place, and those who do so will bring judgment on themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.3', 'BSB', 'For rulers are not a terror to good conduct, but to bad. Do you want to be unafraid of the one in authority? Then do what is right, and you will have his approval.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.4', 'BSB', 'For he is God’s servant for your good. But if you do wrong, be afraid, for he does not carry the sword in vain. He is God’s servant, an agent of retribution to the wrongdoer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore it is necessary to submit to authority, not only to avoid punishment, but also as a matter of conscience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.6', 'BSB', 'This is also why you pay taxes. For the authorities are God’s servants, who devote themselves to their work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.7', 'BSB', 'Pay everyone what you owe him: taxes to whom taxes are due, revenue to whom revenue is due, respect to whom respect is due, honor to whom honor is due.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.8', 'BSB', 'Be indebted to no one, except to one another in love. For he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.9', 'BSB', 'The commandments “Do not commit adultery,” “Do not murder,” “Do not steal,” “Do not covet,” and any other commandments, are summed up in this one decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.10', 'BSB', 'Love does no wrong to its neighbor. Therefore love is the fulfillment of the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.11', 'BSB', 'And do this, understanding the occasion. The hour has come for you to wake up from your slumber, for our salvation is nearer now than when we first believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.12', 'BSB', 'The night is nearly over; the day has drawn near. So let us lay aside the deeds of darkness and put on the armor of light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.13', 'BSB', 'Let us behave decently, as in the daytime, not in carousing and drunkenness, not in sexual immorality and debauchery, not in dissension and jealousy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.13.14', 'BSB', 'Instead, clothe yourselves with the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the desires of the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.1', 'BSB', 'Accept him whose faith is weak, without passing judgment on his opinions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.2', 'BSB', 'For one person has faith to eat all things, while another, who is weak, eats only vegetables.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.3', 'BSB', 'The one who eats everything must not belittle the one who does not, and the one who does not eat everything must not judge the one who does, for God has accepted him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.4', 'BSB', 'Who are you to judge someone else’s servant? To his own master he stands or falls. And he will stand, for the Lord is able to make him stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.5', 'BSB', 'One person regards a certain day above the others, while someone else considers every day alike. Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.6', 'BSB', 'He who observes a special day does so to the Lord; he who eats does so to the Lord, for he gives thanks to God; and he who abstains does so to the Lord and gives thanks to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.7', 'BSB', 'For none of us lives to himself alone, and none of us dies to himself alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.8', 'BSB', 'If we live, we live to the Lord, and if we die, we die to the Lord. So whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.9', 'BSB', 'For this reason Christ died and returned to life, that He might be the Lord of both the dead and the living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.10', 'BSB', 'Why, then, do you judge your brother? Or why do you belittle your brother? For we will all stand before God’s judgment seat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.11', 'BSB', 'It is written: “As surely as I live, says the Lord, every knee will bow before Me; every tongue will confess to God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.12', 'BSB', 'So then, each of us will give an account of himself to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore let us stop judging one another. Instead, make up your mind not to put any stumbling block or obstacle in your brother’s way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.14', 'BSB', 'I am convinced and fully persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean in itself. But if anyone regards something as unclean, then for him it is unclean.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.15', 'BSB', 'If your brother is distressed by what you eat, you are no longer acting in love. Do not by your eating destroy your brother, for whom Christ died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.16', 'BSB', 'Do not allow what you consider good, then, to be spoken of as evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.17', 'BSB', 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of eating and drinking, but of righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.18', 'BSB', 'For whoever serves Christ in this way is pleasing to God and approved by men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.19', 'BSB', 'So then, let us pursue what leads to peace and to mutual edification.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.20', 'BSB', 'Do not destroy the work of God for the sake of food. All food is clean, but it is wrong for a man to let his eating be a stumbling block.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.21', 'BSB', 'It is better not to eat meat or drink wine or to do anything to cause your brother to stumble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.22', 'BSB', 'Keep your belief about such matters between yourself and God. Blessed is the one who does not condemn himself by what he approves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.14.23', 'BSB', 'But the one who has doubts is condemned if he eats, because his eating is not from faith; and everything that is not from faith is sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.1', 'BSB', 'We who are strong ought to bear with the shortcomings of the weak and not to please ourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.2', 'BSB', 'Each of us should please his neighbor for his good, to build him up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.3', 'BSB', 'For even Christ did not please Himself, but as it is written: “The insults of those who insult You have fallen on Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.4', 'BSB', 'For everything that was written in the past was written for our instruction, so that through endurance and the encouragement of the Scriptures, we might have hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.5', 'BSB', 'Now may the God who gives endurance and encouragement grant you harmony with one another in Christ Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.6', 'BSB', 'so that with one mind and one voice you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.7', 'BSB', 'Accept one another, then, just as Christ accepted you, in order to bring glory to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.8', 'BSB', 'For I tell you that Christ has become a servant of the circumcised on behalf of God’s truth, to confirm the promises made to the patriarchs,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.9', 'BSB', 'so that the Gentiles may glorify God for His mercy. As it is written: “Therefore I will praise You among the Gentiles; I will sing hymns to Your name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.10', 'BSB', 'Again, it says: “Rejoice, O Gentiles, with His people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.11', 'BSB', 'And again: “Praise the Lord, all you Gentiles, and extol Him, all you peoples.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.12', 'BSB', 'And once more, Isaiah says: “The Root of Jesse will appear, One who will arise to rule over the Gentiles; in Him the Gentiles will put their hope.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.13', 'BSB', 'Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you believe in Him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.14', 'BSB', 'I myself am convinced, my brothers, that you yourselves are full of goodness, brimming with knowledge, and able to instruct one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.15', 'BSB', 'However, I have written you a bold reminder on some points, because of the grace God has given me', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.16', 'BSB', 'to be a minister of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles in the priestly service of the gospel of God, so that the Gentiles might become an offering acceptable to God, sanctified by the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore I exult in Christ Jesus in my service to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.18', 'BSB', 'I will not presume to speak of anything except what Christ has accomplished through me in leading the Gentiles to obedience by word and deed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.19', 'BSB', 'by the power of signs and wonders, and by the power of the Spirit of God. So from Jerusalem all the way around to Illyricum, I have fully proclaimed the gospel of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.20', 'BSB', 'In this way I have aspired to preach the gospel where Christ was not known, so that I would not be building on someone else’s foundation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.21', 'BSB', 'Rather, as it is written: “Those who were not told about Him will see, and those who have not heard will understand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.22', 'BSB', 'That is why I have often been hindered from coming to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.23', 'BSB', 'But now that there are no further opportunities for me in these regions, and since I have longed for many years to visit you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.24', 'BSB', 'I hope to see you on my way to Spain. And after I have enjoyed your company for a while, you can equip me for my journey.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.25', 'BSB', 'Now, however, I am on my way to Jerusalem to serve the saints there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.26', 'BSB', 'For Macedonia and Achaia were pleased to make a contribution for the poor among the saints in Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.27', 'BSB', 'They were pleased to do it, and indeed they owe it to them. For if the Gentiles have shared in their spiritual blessings, they are obligated to minister to them with material blessings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.28', 'BSB', 'So after I have completed this service and have safely delivered this bounty to them, I will set off to Spain by way of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.29', 'BSB', 'I know that when I come to you, I will come in the fullness of the blessing of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.30', 'BSB', 'Now I urge you, brothers, by our Lord Jesus Christ and by the love of the Spirit, to join me in my struggle by praying to God for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.31', 'BSB', 'Pray that I may be delivered from the unbelievers in Judea, and that my service in Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints there,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.32', 'BSB', 'so that by God’s will I may come to you with joy and together with you be refreshed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.15.33', 'BSB', 'The God of peace be with all of you. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.1', 'BSB', 'I commend to you our sister Phoebe, a servant of the church in Cenchrea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.2', 'BSB', 'Welcome her in the Lord in a manner worthy of the saints, and assist her with anything she may need from you. For she has been a great help to many people, including me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.3', 'BSB', 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.4', 'BSB', 'who have risked their lives for me. Not only I but all the churches of the Gentiles are grateful to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.5', 'BSB', 'Greet also the church that meets at their house. Greet my beloved Epenetus, who was the first convert to Christ in the province of Asia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.6', 'BSB', 'Greet Mary, who has worked very hard for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.7', 'BSB', 'Greet Andronicus and Junia, my fellow countrymen and fellow prisoners. They are outstanding among the apostles, and they were in Christ before I was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.8', 'BSB', 'Greet Ampliatus, my beloved in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.9', 'BSB', 'Greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ, and my beloved Stachys.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.10', 'BSB', 'Greet Apelles, who is approved in Christ. Greet those who belong to the household of Aristobulus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.11', 'BSB', 'Greet Herodion, my fellow countryman. Greet those from the household of Narcissus who are in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.12', 'BSB', 'Greet Tryphena and Tryphosa, women who have worked hard in the Lord. Greet my beloved Persis, who has worked very hard in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.13', 'BSB', 'Greet Rufus, chosen in the Lord, and his mother, who has been a mother to me as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.14', 'BSB', 'Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the brothers with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.15', 'BSB', 'Greet Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas and all the saints with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.16', 'BSB', 'Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.17', 'BSB', 'Now I urge you, brothers, to watch out for those who create divisions and obstacles that are contrary to the teaching you have learned. Turn away from them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.18', 'BSB', 'For such people are not serving our Lord Christ, but their own appetites. By smooth talk and flattery they deceive the hearts of the naive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.19', 'BSB', 'Everyone has heard about your obedience, so I rejoice over you. But I want you to be wise about what is good and innocent about what is evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.20', 'BSB', 'The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.21', 'BSB', 'Timothy, my fellow worker, sends you greetings, as do Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my fellow countrymen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.22', 'BSB', 'I, Tertius, who wrote down this letter, greet you in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.23', 'BSB', 'Gaius, who has hosted me and all the church, sends you greetings. Erastus, the city treasurer, sends you greetings, as does our brother Quartus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.25', 'BSB', 'Now to Him who is able to strengthen you by my gospel and by the proclamation of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery concealed for ages past', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.26', 'BSB', 'but now revealed and made known through the writings of the prophets by the command of the eternal God, in order to lead all nations to the obedience that comes from faith —', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rom.16.27', 'BSB', 'to the only wise God be glory forever through Jesus Christ! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, called to be an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.2', 'BSB', 'To the church of God in Corinth, to those sanctified in Christ Jesus and called to be holy, together with all those everywhere who call on the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, their Lord and ours:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.3', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.4', 'BSB', 'I always thank my God for you because of the grace He has given you in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.5', 'BSB', 'For in Him you have been enriched in every way, in all speech and all knowledge,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.6', 'BSB', 'because our testimony about Christ was confirmed in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore you do not lack any spiritual gift as you eagerly await the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.8', 'BSB', 'He will sustain you to the end, so that you will be blameless on the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.9', 'BSB', 'God, who has called you into fellowship with His Son Jesus Christ our Lord, is faithful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.10', 'BSB', 'I appeal to you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions among you and that you may be united in mind and conviction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.11', 'BSB', 'My brothers, some from Chloe’s household have informed me that there are quarrels among you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.12', 'BSB', 'What I mean is this: Individuals among you are saying, “I follow Paul,” “I follow Apollos,” “I follow Cephas,” or “I follow Christ.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.13', 'BSB', 'Is Christ divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Were you baptized into the name of Paul?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.14', 'BSB', 'I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.15', 'BSB', 'so no one can say that you were baptized into my name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.16', 'BSB', 'Yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanas; beyond that I do not remember if I baptized anyone else.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.17', 'BSB', 'For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel, not with words of wisdom, lest the cross of Christ be emptied of its power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.18', 'BSB', 'For the message of the cross is foolishness to those who are perishing, but to us who are being saved it is the power of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.19', 'BSB', 'For it is written: “I will destroy the wisdom of the wise; the intelligence of the intelligent I will frustrate.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.20', 'BSB', 'Where is the wise man? Where is the scribe? Where is the philosopher of this age? Has not God made foolish the wisdom of the world?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.21', 'BSB', 'For since in the wisdom of God the world through its wisdom did not know Him, God was pleased through the foolishness of what was preached to save those who believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.22', 'BSB', 'Jews demand signs and Greeks search for wisdom,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.23', 'BSB', 'but we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling block to Jews and foolishness to Gentiles,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.24', 'BSB', 'but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power of God and the wisdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.25', 'BSB', 'For the foolishness of God is wiser than man’s wisdom, and the weakness of God is stronger than man’s strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.26', 'BSB', 'Brothers, consider the time of your calling: Not many of you were wise by human standards; not many were powerful; not many were of noble birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.27', 'BSB', 'But God chose the foolish things of the world to shame the wise; God chose the weak things of the world to shame the strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.28', 'BSB', 'He chose the lowly and despised things of the world, and the things that are not, to nullify the things that are,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.29', 'BSB', 'so that no one may boast in His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.30', 'BSB', 'It is because of Him that you are in Christ Jesus, who has become for us wisdom from God: our righteousness, holiness, and redemption.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.1.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as it is written: “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.1', 'BSB', 'When I came to you, brothers, I did not come with eloquence or wisdom as I proclaimed to you the testimony about God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.2', 'BSB', 'For I resolved to know nothing while I was with you except Jesus Christ and Him crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.3', 'BSB', 'I came to you in weakness and fear, and with much trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.4', 'BSB', 'My message and my preaching were not with persuasive words of wisdom, but with a demonstration of the Spirit’s power,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.5', 'BSB', 'so that your faith would not rest on men’s wisdom, but on God’s power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.6', 'BSB', 'Among the mature, however, we speak a message of wisdom—but not the wisdom of this age or of the rulers of this age, who are coming to nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.7', 'BSB', 'No, we speak of the mysterious and hidden wisdom of God, which He destined for our glory before time began.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.8', 'BSB', 'None of the rulers of this age understood it. For if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.9', 'BSB', 'Rather, as it is written: “No eye has seen, no ear has heard, no heart has imagined, what God has prepared for those who love Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.10', 'BSB', 'But God has revealed it to us by the Spirit. The Spirit searches all things, even the deep things of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.11', 'BSB', 'For who among men knows the thoughts of man except his own spirit within him? So too, no one knows the thoughts of God except the Spirit of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.12', 'BSB', 'We have not received the spirit of the world, but the Spirit who is from God, that we may understand what God has freely given us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.13', 'BSB', 'And this is what we speak, not in words taught us by human wisdom, but in words taught by the Spirit, expressing spiritual truths in spiritual words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.14', 'BSB', 'The natural man does not accept the things that come from the Spirit of God. For they are foolishness to him, and he cannot understand them, because they are spiritually discerned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.15', 'BSB', 'The spiritual man judges all things, but he himself is not subject to anyone’s judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.2.16', 'BSB', '“For who has known the mind of the Lord, so as to instruct Him?” But we have the mind of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.1', 'BSB', 'Brothers, I could not address you as spiritual, but as worldly—as infants in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.2', 'BSB', 'I gave you milk, not solid food, for you were not yet ready for solid food. In fact, you are still not ready,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.3', 'BSB', 'for you are still worldly. For since there is jealousy and dissension among you, are you not worldly? Are you not walking in the way of man?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.4', 'BSB', 'For when one of you says, “I follow Paul,” and another, “I follow Apollos,” are you not mere men?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.5', 'BSB', 'What then is Apollos? And what is Paul? They are servants through whom you believed, as the Lord has assigned to each his role.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.6', 'BSB', 'I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.7', 'BSB', 'So neither he who plants nor he who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.8', 'BSB', 'He who plants and he who waters are one in purpose, and each will be rewarded according to his own labor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.9', 'BSB', 'For we are God’s fellow workers; you are God’s field, God’s building.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.10', 'BSB', 'By the grace God has given me, I laid a foundation as an expert builder, and someone else is building on it. But each one must be careful how he builds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.11', 'BSB', 'For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid, which is Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.12', 'BSB', 'If anyone builds on this foundation using gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or straw,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.13', 'BSB', 'his workmanship will be evident, because the Day will bring it to light. It will be revealed with fire, and the fire will prove the quality of each man’s work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.14', 'BSB', 'If what he has built survives, he will receive a reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.15', 'BSB', 'If it is burned up, he will suffer loss. He himself will be saved, but only as if through the flames.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.16', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that you yourselves are God’s temple, and that God’s Spirit dwells in you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.17', 'BSB', 'If anyone destroys God’s temple, God will destroy him; for God’s temple is holy, and you are that temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.18', 'BSB', 'Let no one deceive himself. If any of you thinks he is wise in this age, he should become a fool, so that he may become wise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.19', 'BSB', 'For the wisdom of this world is foolishness in God’s sight. As it is written: “He catches the wise in their craftiness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.20', 'BSB', 'And again, “The Lord knows that the thoughts of the wise are futile.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore, stop boasting in men. All things are yours,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.22', 'BSB', 'whether Paul or Apollos or Cephas or the world or life or death or the present or the future. All of them belong to you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.3.23', 'BSB', 'and you belong to Christ, and Christ belongs to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.1', 'BSB', 'So then, men ought to regard us as servants of Christ and stewards of the mysteries of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.2', 'BSB', 'Now it is required of stewards that they be found faithful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.3', 'BSB', 'I care very little, however, if I am judged by you or by any human court. In fact, I do not even judge myself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.4', 'BSB', 'My conscience is clear, but that does not vindicate me. It is the Lord who judges me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore judge nothing before the appointed time; wait until the Lord comes. He will bring to light what is hidden in darkness and will expose the motives of men’s hearts. At that time each will receive his praise from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.6', 'BSB', 'Brothers, I have applied these things to myself and Apollos for your benefit, so that you may learn from us not to go beyond what is written. Then you will not take pride in one man over another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.7', 'BSB', 'For who makes you so superior? What do you have that you did not receive? And if you did receive it, why do you boast as though you did not?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.8', 'BSB', 'Already you have all you want. Already you have become rich. Without us, you have become kings. How I wish you really were kings, so that we might be kings with you!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.9', 'BSB', 'For it seems to me that God has displayed us apostles at the end of the procession, like prisoners appointed for death. We have become a spectacle to the whole world, to angels as well as to men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.10', 'BSB', 'We are fools for Christ, but you are wise in Christ. We are weak, but you are strong. You are honored, but we are dishonored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.11', 'BSB', 'To this very hour we are hungry and thirsty, we are poorly clothed, we are brutally treated, we are homeless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.12', 'BSB', 'We work hard with our own hands. When we are vilified, we bless; when we are persecuted, we endure it;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.13', 'BSB', 'when we are slandered, we answer gently. Up to this moment we have become the scum of the earth, the refuse of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.14', 'BSB', 'I am not writing this to shame you, but to warn you as my beloved children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.15', 'BSB', 'Even if you have ten thousand guardians in Christ, you do not have many fathers; for in Christ Jesus I became your father through the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore I urge you to imitate me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.17', 'BSB', 'That is why I have sent you Timothy, my beloved and faithful child in the Lord. He will remind you of my way of life in Christ Jesus, which is exactly what I teach everywhere in every church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.18', 'BSB', 'Some of you have become arrogant, as if I were not coming to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.19', 'BSB', 'But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing, and then I will find out not only what these arrogant people are saying, but what power they have.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.20', 'BSB', 'For the kingdom of God is not a matter of talk but of power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.4.21', 'BSB', 'Which do you prefer? Shall I come to you with a rod, or in love and with a gentle spirit?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.1', 'BSB', 'It is actually reported that there is sexual immorality among you, and of a kind that is intolerable even among pagans: A man has his father’s wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.2', 'BSB', 'And you are proud! Shouldn’t you rather have been stricken with grief and have removed from your fellowship the man who did this?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.3', 'BSB', 'Although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I have already pronounced judgment on the one who did this, just as if I were present.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.4', 'BSB', 'When you are assembled in the name of our Lord Jesus and I am with you in spirit, along with the power of the Lord Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.5', 'BSB', 'hand this man over to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, so that his spirit may be saved on the Day of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.6', 'BSB', 'Your boasting is not good. Do you not know that a little leaven works through the whole batch of dough?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.7', 'BSB', 'Get rid of the old leaven, that you may be a new unleavened batch, as you really are. For Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore let us keep the feast, not with the old bread, leavened with malice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and of truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.9', 'BSB', 'I wrote you in my letter not to associate with sexually immoral people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.10', 'BSB', 'I was not including the sexually immoral of this world, or the greedy and swindlers, or idolaters. In that case you would have to leave this world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.11', 'BSB', 'But now I am writing you not to associate with anyone who claims to be a brother but is sexually immoral or greedy, an idolater or a verbal abuser, a drunkard or a swindler. With such a man do not even eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.12', 'BSB', 'What business of mine is it to judge those outside the church? Are you not to judge those inside?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.5.13', 'BSB', 'God will judge those outside. “Expel the wicked man from among you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.1', 'BSB', 'If any of you has a grievance against another, how dare he go to law before the unrighteous instead of before the saints!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.2', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that the saints will judge the world? And if you are to judge the world, are you not competent to judge trivial cases?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.3', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that we will judge angels? How much more the things of this life!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.4', 'BSB', 'So if you need to settle everyday matters, do you appoint as judges those of no standing in the church?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.5', 'BSB', 'I say this to your shame. Is there really no one among you wise enough to arbitrate between his brothers?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.6', 'BSB', 'Instead, one brother goes to law against another, and this in front of unbelievers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.7', 'BSB', 'The very fact that you have lawsuits among you means that you are thoroughly defeated already. Why not rather be wronged? Why not rather be cheated?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.8', 'BSB', 'Instead, you yourselves cheat and do wrong, even against your own brothers!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.9', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that the wicked will not inherit the kingdom of God? Do not be deceived: Neither the sexually immoral, nor idolaters, nor adulterers, nor men who submit to or perform homosexual acts,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.10', 'BSB', 'nor thieves, nor the greedy, nor drunkards, nor verbal abusers, nor swindlers, will inherit the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.11', 'BSB', 'And that is what some of you were. But you were washed, you were sanctified, you were justified, in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ and by the Spirit of our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.12', 'BSB', '“Everything is permissible for me,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible for me,” but I will not be mastered by anything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.13', 'BSB', '“Food for the stomach and the stomach for food,” but God will destroy them both. The body is not intended for sexual immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.14', 'BSB', 'By His power God raised the Lord from the dead, and He will raise us also.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.15', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that your bodies are members of Christ? Shall I then take the members of Christ and unite them with a prostitute? Never!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.16', 'BSB', 'Or don’t you know that he who unites himself with a prostitute is one with her in body? For it is said, “The two will become one flesh.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.17', 'BSB', 'But he who unites himself with the Lord is one with Him in spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.18', 'BSB', 'Flee from sexual immorality. Every other sin a man can commit is outside his body, but he who sins sexually sins against his own body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.19', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received from God? You are not your own;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.6.20', 'BSB', 'you were bought at a price. Therefore glorify God with your body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.1', 'BSB', 'Now for the matters you wrote about: It is good to abstain from sexual relations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.2', 'BSB', 'But because there is so much sexual immorality, each man should have his own wife, and each woman her own husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.3', 'BSB', 'The husband should fulfill his marital duty to his wife, and likewise the wife to her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.4', 'BSB', 'The wife does not have authority over her own body, but the husband. Likewise the husband does not have authority over his own body, but the wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.5', 'BSB', 'Do not deprive each other, except by mutual consent and for a time, so you may devote yourselves to prayer. Then come together again, so that Satan will not tempt you through your lack of self-control.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.6', 'BSB', 'I say this as a concession, not as a command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.7', 'BSB', 'I wish that all men were as I am. But each man has his own gift from God; one has this gift, another has that.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.8', 'BSB', 'Now to the unmarried and widows I say this: It is good for them to remain unmarried, as I am.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.9', 'BSB', 'But if they cannot control themselves, let them marry. For it is better to marry than to burn with passion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.10', 'BSB', 'To the married I give this command (not I, but the Lord): A wife must not separate from her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.11', 'BSB', 'But if she does, she must remain unmarried or else be reconciled to her husband. And a husband must not divorce his wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.12', 'BSB', 'To the rest I say this (I, not the Lord): If a brother has an unbelieving wife and she is willing to live with him, he must not divorce her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.13', 'BSB', 'And if a woman has an unbelieving husband and he is willing to live with her, she must not divorce him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.14', 'BSB', 'For the unbelieving husband is sanctified through his believing wife, and the unbelieving wife is sanctified through her believing husband. Otherwise your children would be unclean, but now they are holy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.15', 'BSB', 'But if the unbeliever leaves, let him go. The believing brother or sister is not bound in such cases. God has called you to live in peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.16', 'BSB', 'How do you know, wife, whether you will save your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.17', 'BSB', 'Regardless, each one should lead the life that the Lord has assigned to him and to which God has called him. This is what I prescribe in all the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.18', 'BSB', 'Was a man already circumcised when he was called? He should not become uncircumcised. Was a man still uncircumcised when called? He should not be circumcised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.19', 'BSB', 'Circumcision is nothing and uncircumcision is nothing. Keeping God’s commandments is what counts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.20', 'BSB', 'Each one should remain in the situation he was in when he was called.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.21', 'BSB', 'Were you a slave when you were called? Do not let it concern you—but if you can gain your freedom, take the opportunity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.22', 'BSB', 'For he who was a slave when he was called by the Lord is the Lord’s freedman. Conversely, he who was a free man when he was called is Christ’s slave.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.23', 'BSB', 'You were bought at a price; do not become slaves of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.24', 'BSB', 'Brothers, each one should remain in the situation he was in when God called him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.25', 'BSB', 'Now about virgins, I have no command from the Lord, but I give a judgment as one who by the Lord’s mercy is trustworthy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.26', 'BSB', 'Because of the present crisis, I think it is good for a man to remain as he is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.27', 'BSB', 'Are you committed to a wife? Do not seek to be released. Are you free of commitment? Do not look for a wife.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.28', 'BSB', 'But if you do marry, you have not sinned. And if a virgin marries, she has not sinned. But those who marry will face troubles in this life, and I want to spare you this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.29', 'BSB', 'What I am saying, brothers, is that the time is short. From now on those who have wives should live as if they had none;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.30', 'BSB', 'those who weep, as if they did not; those who are joyful, as if they were not; those who make a purchase, as if they had nothing;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.31', 'BSB', 'and those who use the things of this world, as if not dependent on them. For this world in its present form is passing away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.32', 'BSB', 'I want you to be free from concern. The unmarried man is concerned about the work of the Lord, how he can please the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.33', 'BSB', 'But the married man is concerned about the affairs of this world, how he can please his wife,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.34', 'BSB', 'and his interests are divided. The unmarried woman or virgin is concerned about the work of the Lord, how she can be holy in both body and spirit. But the married woman is concerned about the affairs of this world, how she can please her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.35', 'BSB', 'I am saying this for your own good, not to restrict you, but in order to promote proper decorum and undivided devotion to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.36', 'BSB', 'However, if someone thinks he is acting inappropriately toward his betrothed, and if she is beyond her youth and they ought to marry, let him do as he wishes; he is not sinning; they should get married.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.37', 'BSB', 'But the man who is firmly established in his heart and under no constraint, with control over his will and resolve in his heart not to marry the virgin, he will do well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.38', 'BSB', 'So then, he who marries the virgin does well, but he who does not marry her does even better.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.39', 'BSB', 'A wife is bound to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies, she is free to marry anyone she wishes, as long as he belongs to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.7.40', 'BSB', 'In my judgment, however, she is happier if she remains as she is. And I think that I too have the Spirit of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.1', 'BSB', 'Now about food sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.2', 'BSB', 'The one who thinks he knows something does not yet know as he ought to know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.3', 'BSB', 'But the one who loves God is known by God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.4', 'BSB', 'So about eating food sacrificed to idols: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.5', 'BSB', 'For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth (as there are many so-called gods and lords),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.6', 'BSB', 'yet for us there is but one God, the Father, from whom all things came and for whom we exist. And there is but one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things came and through whom we exist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.7', 'BSB', 'But not everyone has this knowledge. Some people are still so accustomed to idols that they eat such food as if it were sacrificed to an idol. And since their conscience is weak, it is defiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.8', 'BSB', 'But food does not bring us closer to God: We are no worse if we do not eat, and no better if we do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.9', 'BSB', 'Be careful, however, that your freedom does not become a stumbling block to the weak.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.10', 'BSB', 'For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged to eat food sacrificed to idols?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.11', 'BSB', 'So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed by your knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.12', 'BSB', 'By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding their weak conscience, you sin against Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.8.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble, I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.1', 'BSB', 'Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Have I not seen Jesus our Lord? Are you yourselves not my workmanship in the Lord?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.2', 'BSB', 'Even if I am not an apostle to others, surely I am to you. For you are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.3', 'BSB', 'This is my defense to those who scrutinize me:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.4', 'BSB', 'Have we no right to food and to drink?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.5', 'BSB', 'Have we no right to take along a believing wife, as do the other apostles and the Lord’s brothers and Cephas?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.6', 'BSB', 'Or are Barnabas and I the only apostles who must work for a living?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.7', 'BSB', 'Who serves as a soldier at his own expense? Who plants a vineyard and does not eat of its fruit? Who tends a flock and does not drink of its milk?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.8', 'BSB', 'Do I say this from a human perspective? Doesn’t the Law say the same thing?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.9', 'BSB', 'For it is written in the Law of Moses: “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.” Is it about oxen that God is concerned?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.10', 'BSB', 'Isn’t He actually speaking on our behalf? Indeed, this was written for us, because when the plowman plows and the thresher threshes, they should also expect to share in the harvest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.11', 'BSB', 'If we have sown spiritual seed among you, is it too much for us to reap a material harvest from you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.12', 'BSB', 'If others have this right to your support, shouldn’t we have it all the more? But we did not exercise this right. Instead, we put up with anything rather than hinder the gospel of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.13', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that those who work in the temple eat of its food, and those who serve at the altar partake of its offerings?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.14', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the Lord has prescribed that those who preach the gospel should receive their living from the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.15', 'BSB', 'But I have not used any of these rights. And I am not writing this to suggest that something be done for me. Indeed, I would rather die than let anyone nullify my boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.16', 'BSB', 'Yet when I preach the gospel, I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated to preach. Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.17', 'BSB', 'If my preaching is voluntary, I have a reward. But if it is not voluntary, I am still entrusted with a responsibility.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.18', 'BSB', 'What then is my reward? That in preaching the gospel I may offer it free of charge, and so not use up my rights in preaching it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.19', 'BSB', 'Though I am free of obligation to anyone, I make myself a slave to everyone, to win as many as possible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.20', 'BSB', 'To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win the Jews. To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.21', 'BSB', 'To those without the law I became like one without the law (though I am not outside the law of God but am under the law of Christ), to win those without the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.22', 'BSB', 'To the weak I became weak, to win the weak. I have become all things to all people so that by all possible means I might save some.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.23', 'BSB', 'I do all this for the sake of the gospel, so that I may share in its blessings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.24', 'BSB', 'Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize? Run in such a way as to take the prize.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.25', 'BSB', 'Everyone who competes in the games trains with strict discipline. They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.26', 'BSB', 'Therefore I do not run aimlessly; I do not fight like I am beating the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.9.27', 'BSB', 'No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.1', 'BSB', 'I do not want you to be unaware, brothers, that our forefathers were all under the cloud, and that they all passed through the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.2', 'BSB', 'They were all baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.3', 'BSB', 'They all ate the same spiritual food', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.4', 'BSB', 'and drank the same spiritual drink; for they drank from the spiritual rock that accompanied them, and that rock was Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.5', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, God was not pleased with most of them, for they were struck down in the wilderness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.6', 'BSB', 'These things took place as examples to keep us from craving evil things as they did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.7', 'BSB', 'Do not be idolaters, as some of them were. As it is written: “The people sat down to eat and to drink, and got up to indulge in revelry.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.8', 'BSB', 'We should not commit sexual immorality, as some of them did, and in one day twenty-three thousand of them died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.9', 'BSB', 'We should not test Christ, as some of them did, and were killed by snakes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.10', 'BSB', 'And do not complain, as some of them did, and were killed by the destroying angel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.11', 'BSB', 'Now these things happened to them as examples and were written down as warnings for us, on whom the fulfillment of the ages has come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.12', 'BSB', 'So the one who thinks he is standing firm should be careful not to fall.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.13', 'BSB', 'No temptation has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape, so that you can stand up under it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore, my beloved, flee from idolatry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.15', 'BSB', 'I speak to reasonable people; judge for yourselves what I say.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.16', 'BSB', 'Is not the cup of blessing that we bless a participation in the blood of Christ? And is not the bread that we break a participation in the body of Christ?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.17', 'BSB', 'Because there is one loaf, we who are many are one body; for we all partake of the one loaf.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.18', 'BSB', 'Consider the people of Israel: Are not those who eat the sacrifices fellow partakers in the altar?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.19', 'BSB', 'Am I suggesting, then, that food sacrificed to an idol is anything, or that an idol is anything?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.20', 'BSB', 'No, but the sacrifices of pagans are offered to demons, not to God. And I do not want you to be participants with demons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.21', 'BSB', 'You cannot drink the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons too; you cannot partake in the table of the Lord and the table of demons too.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.22', 'BSB', 'Are we trying to provoke the Lord to jealousy? Are we stronger than He?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.23', 'BSB', '“Everything is permissible,” but not everything is beneficial. “Everything is permissible,” but not everything is edifying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.24', 'BSB', 'No one should seek his own good, but the good of others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.25', 'BSB', 'Eat anything sold in the meat market without raising questions of conscience,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.26', 'BSB', 'for, “The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness thereof.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.27', 'BSB', 'If an unbeliever invites you to a meal and you want to go, eat anything set before you without raising questions of conscience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.28', 'BSB', 'But if someone tells you, “This food was offered to idols,” then do not eat it, for the sake of the one who told you and for the sake of conscience—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.29', 'BSB', 'the other one’s conscience, I mean, not your own. For why should my freedom be determined by someone else’s conscience?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.30', 'BSB', 'If I partake in the meal with thankfulness, why am I denounced because of that for which I give thanks?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.31', 'BSB', 'So whether you eat or drink or whatever you do, do it all to the glory of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.32', 'BSB', 'Do not become a stumbling block, whether to Jews or Greeks or the church of God—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.10.33', 'BSB', 'as I also try to please everyone in all I do. For I am not seeking my own good, but the good of many, that they may be saved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.1', 'BSB', 'You are to imitate me, just as I imitate Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.2', 'BSB', 'Now I commend you for remembering me in everything and for maintaining the traditions, just as I passed them on to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.3', 'BSB', 'But I want you to understand that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.4', 'BSB', 'Every man who prays or prophesies with his head covered dishonors his head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.5', 'BSB', 'And every woman who prays or prophesies with her head uncovered dishonors her head, for it is just as if her head were shaved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.6', 'BSB', 'If a woman does not cover her head, she should have her hair cut off. And if it is shameful for a woman to have her hair cut or shaved off, she should cover her head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.7', 'BSB', 'A man ought not to cover his head, since he is the image and glory of God; but the woman is the glory of man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.8', 'BSB', 'For man did not come from woman, but woman from man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.9', 'BSB', 'Neither was man created for woman, but woman for man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.10', 'BSB', 'For this reason a woman ought to have a sign of authority on her head, because of the angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.11', 'BSB', 'In the Lord, however, woman is not independent of man, nor is man independent of woman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.12', 'BSB', 'For just as woman came from man, so also man is born of woman. But everything comes from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.13', 'BSB', 'Judge for yourselves: Is it proper for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.14', 'BSB', 'Doesn’t nature itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a disgrace to him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.15', 'BSB', 'but that if a woman has long hair, it is her glory? For long hair is given to her as a covering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.16', 'BSB', 'If anyone is inclined to dispute this, we have no other practice, nor do the churches of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.17', 'BSB', 'In the following instructions I have no praise to offer, because your gatherings do more harm than good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.18', 'BSB', 'First of all, I hear that when you come together as a church, there are divisions among you, and in part I believe it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.19', 'BSB', 'And indeed, there must be differences among you to show which of you are approved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.20', 'BSB', 'Now then, when you come together, it is not the Lord’s Supper you eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.21', 'BSB', 'For as you eat, each of you goes ahead without sharing his meal. While one remains hungry, another gets drunk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.22', 'BSB', 'Don’t you have your own homes in which to eat and drink? Or do you despise the church of God and humiliate those who have nothing? What can I say to you? Shall I praise you for this? No, I will not!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.23', 'BSB', 'For I received from the Lord what I also passed on to you: The Lord Jesus, on the night He was betrayed, took bread,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.24', 'BSB', 'and when He had given thanks, He broke it and said, “This is My body, which is for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.25', 'BSB', 'In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood; do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.26', 'BSB', 'For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim the Lord’s death until He comes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.27', 'BSB', 'Therefore, whoever eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner will be guilty of sinning against the body and blood of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.28', 'BSB', 'Each one must examine himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.29', 'BSB', 'For anyone who eats and drinks without recognizing the body eats and drinks judgment on himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.30', 'BSB', 'That is why many among you are weak and sick, and a number of you have fallen asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.31', 'BSB', 'Now if we judged ourselves properly, we would not come under judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.32', 'BSB', 'But when we are judged by the Lord, we are being disciplined so that we will not be condemned with the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.33', 'BSB', 'So, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.11.34', 'BSB', 'If anyone is hungry, he should eat at home, so that when you come together it will not result in judgment. And when I come, I will give instructions about the remaining matters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.1', 'BSB', 'Now about spiritual gifts, brothers, I do not want you to be uninformed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.2', 'BSB', 'You know that when you were pagans, you were influenced and led astray to mute idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.3', 'BSB', 'Therefore I inform you that no one who is speaking by the Spirit of God says, “Jesus be cursed,” and no one can say, “Jesus is Lord,” except by the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.4', 'BSB', 'There are different gifts, but the same Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.5', 'BSB', 'There are different ministries, but the same Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.6', 'BSB', 'There are different ways of working, but the same God works all things in all people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.7', 'BSB', 'Now to each one the manifestation of the Spirit is given for the common good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.8', 'BSB', 'To one there is given through the Spirit the message of wisdom, to another the message of knowledge by the same Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.9', 'BSB', 'to another faith by the same Spirit, to another gifts of healing by that one Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.10', 'BSB', 'to another the working of miracles, to another prophecy, to another distinguishing between spirits, to another speaking in various tongues, and to still another the interpretation of tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.11', 'BSB', 'All these are the work of one and the same Spirit, who apportions them to each one as He determines.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.12', 'BSB', 'The body is a unit, though it is composed of many parts. And although its parts are many, they all form one body. So it is with Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.13', 'BSB', 'For in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, slave or free, and we were all given one Spirit to drink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.14', 'BSB', 'For the body does not consist of one part, but of many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.15', 'BSB', 'If the foot should say, “Because I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.16', 'BSB', 'And if the ear should say, “Because I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.17', 'BSB', 'If the whole body were an eye, where would the sense of hearing be? If the whole body were an ear, where would the sense of smell be?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.18', 'BSB', 'But in fact, God has arranged the members of the body, every one of them, according to His design.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.19', 'BSB', 'If they were all one part, where would the body be?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.20', 'BSB', 'As it is, there are many parts, but one body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.21', 'BSB', 'The eye cannot say to the hand, “I do not need you.” Nor can the head say to the feet, “I do not need you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.22', 'BSB', 'On the contrary, the parts of the body that seem to be weaker are indispensable,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.23', 'BSB', 'and the parts we consider less honorable, we treat with greater honor. And our unpresentable parts are treated with special modesty,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.24', 'BSB', 'whereas our presentable parts have no such need. But God has composed the body and has given greater honor to the parts that lacked it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.25', 'BSB', 'so that there should be no division in the body, but that its members should have mutual concern for one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.26', 'BSB', 'If one part suffers, every part suffers with it; if one part is honored, every part rejoices with it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.27', 'BSB', 'Now you are the body of Christ, and each of you is a member of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.28', 'BSB', 'And in the church God has appointed first of all apostles, second prophets, third teachers, then workers of miracles, and those with gifts of healing, helping, administration, and various tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.29', 'BSB', 'Are all apostles? Are all prophets? Are all teachers? Do all work miracles?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.30', 'BSB', 'Do all have gifts of healing? Do all speak in tongues? Do all interpret?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.12.31', 'BSB', 'But eagerly desire the greater gifts. And now I will show you the most excellent way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.1', 'BSB', 'If I speak in the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love, I am only a ringing gong or a clanging cymbal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.2', 'BSB', 'If I have the gift of prophecy and can fathom all mysteries and all knowledge, and if I have absolute faith so as to move mountains, but have not love, I am nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.3', 'BSB', 'If I give all I possess to the poor and exult in the surrender of my body, but have not love, I gain nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.4', 'BSB', 'Love is patient, love is kind. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.5', 'BSB', 'It is not rude, it is not self-seeking, it is not easily angered, it keeps no account of wrongs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.6', 'BSB', 'Love takes no pleasure in evil, but rejoices in the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.7', 'BSB', 'It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, endures all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.8', 'BSB', 'Love never fails. But where there are prophecies, they will cease; where there are tongues, they will be restrained; where there is knowledge, it will be dismissed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.9', 'BSB', 'For we know in part and we prophesy in part,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.10', 'BSB', 'but when the perfect comes, the partial passes away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.11', 'BSB', 'When I was a child, I talked like a child, I thought like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I became a man, I set aside childish ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.12', 'BSB', 'Now we see but a dim reflection as in a mirror; then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part; then I shall know fully, even as I am fully known.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.13.13', 'BSB', 'And now these three remain: faith, hope, and love; but the greatest of these is love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.1', 'BSB', 'Earnestly pursue love and eagerly desire spiritual gifts, especially the gift of prophecy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.2', 'BSB', 'For he who speaks in a tongue does not speak to men, but to God. Indeed, no one understands him; he utters mysteries in the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.3', 'BSB', 'But he who prophesies speaks to men for their edification, encouragement, and comfort.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.4', 'BSB', 'The one who speaks in a tongue edifies himself, but the one who prophesies edifies the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.5', 'BSB', 'I wish that all of you could speak in tongues, but I would rather have you prophesy. He who prophesies is greater than one who speaks in tongues, unless he interprets so that the church may be edified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.6', 'BSB', 'Now, brothers, if I come to you speaking in tongues, how will I benefit you, unless I bring you some revelation or knowledge or prophecy or teaching?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.7', 'BSB', 'Even in the case of lifeless instruments, such as the flute or harp, how will anyone recognize the tune they are playing unless the notes are distinct?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.8', 'BSB', 'Again, if the trumpet sounds a muffled call, who will prepare for battle?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.9', 'BSB', 'So it is with you. Unless you speak intelligible words with your tongue, how will anyone know what you are saying? You will just be speaking into the air.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.10', 'BSB', 'Assuredly, there are many different languages in the world, yet none of them is without meaning.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.11', 'BSB', 'If, then, I do not know the meaning of someone’s language, I am a foreigner to the speaker, and he is a foreigner to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.12', 'BSB', 'It is the same with you. Since you are eager to have spiritual gifts, strive to excel in gifts that build up the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore, the one who speaks in a tongue should pray that he may interpret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.14', 'BSB', 'For if I pray in a tongue, my spirit prays, but my mind is unfruitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.15', 'BSB', 'What then shall I do? I will pray with my spirit, but I will also pray with my mind. I will sing with my spirit, but I will also sing with my mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.16', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, if you speak a blessing in spirit, how can someone who is uninstructed say “Amen” to your thanksgiving, since he does not know what you are saying?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.17', 'BSB', 'You may be giving thanks well enough, but the other one is not edified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.18', 'BSB', 'I thank God that I speak in tongues more than all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.19', 'BSB', 'But in the church, I would rather speak five coherent words to instruct others than ten thousand words in a tongue.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.20', 'BSB', 'Brothers, stop thinking like children. In regard to evil be infants, but in your thinking be mature.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.21', 'BSB', 'It is written in the Law: “By strange tongues and foreign lips I will speak to this people, but even then they will not listen to Me, says the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.22', 'BSB', 'Tongues, then, are a sign, not for believers, but for unbelievers. Prophecy, however, is for believers, not for unbelievers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.23', 'BSB', 'So if the whole church comes together and everyone speaks in tongues, and some who are uninstructed or some unbelievers come in, will they not say that you are out of your minds?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.24', 'BSB', 'But if an unbeliever or uninstructed person comes in while everyone is prophesying, he will be convicted and called to account by all,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.25', 'BSB', 'and the secrets of his heart will be made known. So he will fall facedown and worship God, proclaiming, “God is truly among you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.26', 'BSB', 'What then shall we say, brothers? When you come together, everyone has a psalm or a teaching, a revelation, a tongue, or an interpretation. All of these must be done to build up the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.27', 'BSB', 'If anyone speaks in a tongue, two, or at most three, should speak in turn, and someone must interpret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.28', 'BSB', 'But if there is no interpreter, he should remain silent in the church and speak only to himself and God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.29', 'BSB', 'Two or three prophets should speak, and the others should weigh carefully what is said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.30', 'BSB', 'And if a revelation comes to someone who is seated, the first speaker should stop.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.31', 'BSB', 'For you can all prophesy in turn so that everyone may be instructed and encouraged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.32', 'BSB', 'The spirits of prophets are subject to prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.33', 'BSB', 'For God is not a God of disorder, but of peace—as in all the churches of the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.34', 'BSB', 'Women are to be silent in the churches. They are not permitted to speak, but must be in submission, as the law says.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.35', 'BSB', 'If they wish to inquire about something, they are to ask their own husbands at home; for it is dishonorable for a woman to speak in the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.36', 'BSB', 'Did the word of God originate with you? Or are you the only ones it has reached?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.37', 'BSB', 'If anyone considers himself a prophet or spiritual person, let him acknowledge that what I am writing you is the Lord’s command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.38', 'BSB', 'But if anyone ignores this, he himself will be ignored.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.39', 'BSB', 'So, my brothers, be eager to prophesy, and do not forbid speaking in tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.14.40', 'BSB', 'But everything must be done in a proper and orderly manner.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.1', 'BSB', 'Now, brothers, I want to remind you of the gospel I preached to you, which you received, and in which you stand firm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.2', 'BSB', 'By this gospel you are saved, if you hold firmly to the word I preached to you. Otherwise, you have believed in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.3', 'BSB', 'For what I received I passed on to you as of first importance: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.4', 'BSB', 'that He was buried, that He was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.5', 'BSB', 'and that He appeared to Cephas and then to the Twelve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.6', 'BSB', 'After that, He appeared to more than five hundred brothers at once, most of whom are still living, though some have fallen asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.7', 'BSB', 'Then He appeared to James, then to all the apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.8', 'BSB', 'And last of all He appeared to me also, as to one of untimely birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.9', 'BSB', 'For I am the least of the apostles and am unworthy to be called an apostle, because I persecuted the church of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.10', 'BSB', 'But by the grace of God I am what I am, and His grace to me was not in vain. No, I worked harder than all of them—yet not I, but the grace of God that was with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.11', 'BSB', 'Whether, then, it was I or they, this is what we preach, and this is what you believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.12', 'BSB', 'But if it is preached that Christ has been raised from the dead, how can some of you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.13', 'BSB', 'If there is no resurrection of the dead, then not even Christ has been raised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.14', 'BSB', 'And if Christ has not been raised, our preaching is worthless, and so is your faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.15', 'BSB', 'In that case, we are also exposed as false witnesses about God. For we have testified about God that He raised Christ from the dead, but He did not raise Him if in fact the dead are not raised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.16', 'BSB', 'For if the dead are not raised, then not even Christ has been raised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.17', 'BSB', 'And if Christ has not been raised, your faith is futile; you are still in your sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.18', 'BSB', 'Then those also who have fallen asleep in Christ have perished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.19', 'BSB', 'If our hope in Christ is for this life alone, we are to be pitied more than all men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.20', 'BSB', 'But Christ has indeed been raised from the dead, the firstfruits of those who have fallen asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.21', 'BSB', 'For since death came through a man, the resurrection of the dead comes also through a man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.22', 'BSB', 'For as in Adam all die, so in Christ all will be made alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.23', 'BSB', 'But each in his own turn: Christ the firstfruits; then at His coming, those who belong to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.24', 'BSB', 'Then the end will come, when He hands over the kingdom to God the Father after He has destroyed all dominion, authority, and power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.25', 'BSB', 'For He must reign until He has put all His enemies under His feet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.26', 'BSB', 'The last enemy to be destroyed is death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.27', 'BSB', 'For “God has put everything under His feet.” Now when it says that everything has been put under Him, this clearly does not include the One who put everything under Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.28', 'BSB', 'And when all things have been subjected to Him, then the Son Himself will be made subject to Him who put all things under Him, so that God may be all in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.29', 'BSB', 'If these things are not so, what will those do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead are not raised at all, why are people baptized for them?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.30', 'BSB', 'And why do we endanger ourselves every hour?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.31', 'BSB', 'I face death every day, brothers, as surely as I boast about you in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.32', 'BSB', 'If I fought wild beasts in Ephesus for human motives, what did I gain? If the dead are not raised, “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.33', 'BSB', 'Do not be deceived: “Bad company corrupts good character.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.34', 'BSB', 'Sober up as you ought, and stop sinning; for some of you are ignorant of God. I say this to your shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.35', 'BSB', 'But someone will ask, “How are the dead raised? With what kind of body will they come?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.36', 'BSB', 'You fool! What you sow does not come to life unless it dies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.37', 'BSB', 'And what you sow is not the body that will be, but just a seed, perhaps of wheat or something else.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.38', 'BSB', 'But God gives it a body as He has designed, and to each kind of seed He gives its own body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.39', 'BSB', 'Not all flesh is the same: Men have one kind of flesh, animals have another, birds another, and fish another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.40', 'BSB', 'There are also heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. But the splendor of the heavenly bodies is of one degree, and the splendor of the earthly bodies is of another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.41', 'BSB', 'The sun has one degree of splendor, the moon another, and the stars another; and star differs from star in splendor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.42', 'BSB', 'So will it be with the resurrection of the dead: What is sown is perishable; it is raised imperishable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.43', 'BSB', 'It is sown in dishonor; it is raised in glory. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.44', 'BSB', 'It is sown a natural body; it is raised a spiritual body. If there is a natural body, there is also a spiritual body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.45', 'BSB', 'So it is written: “The first man Adam became a living being;” the last Adam a life-giving spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.46', 'BSB', 'The spiritual, however, was not first, but the natural, and then the spiritual.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.47', 'BSB', 'The first man was of the dust of the earth, the second man from heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.48', 'BSB', 'As was the earthly man, so also are those who are of the earth; and as is the heavenly man, so also are those who are of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.49', 'BSB', 'And just as we have borne the likeness of the earthly man, so also shall we bear the likeness of the heavenly man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.50', 'BSB', 'Now I declare to you, brothers, that flesh and blood cannot inherit the kingdom of God, nor does the perishable inherit the imperishable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.51', 'BSB', 'Listen, I tell you a mystery: We will not all sleep, but we will all be changed—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.52', 'BSB', 'in an instant, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound, the dead will be raised imperishable, and we will be changed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.53', 'BSB', 'For the perishable must be clothed with the imperishable, and the mortal with immortality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.54', 'BSB', 'When the perishable has been clothed with the imperishable and the mortal with immortality, then the saying that is written will come to pass: “Death has been swallowed up in victory.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.55', 'BSB', '“Where, O Death, is your victory? Where, O Death, is your sting?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.56', 'BSB', 'The sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.57', 'BSB', 'But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.15.58', 'BSB', 'Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast and immovable. Always excel in the work of the Lord, because you know that your labor in the Lord is not in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.1', 'BSB', 'Now about the collection for the saints, you are to do as I directed the churches of Galatia:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.2', 'BSB', 'On the first day of every week, each of you should set aside a portion of his income, saving it up, so that when I come no collections will be needed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.3', 'BSB', 'Then, on my arrival, I will send letters with those you recommend to carry your gift to Jerusalem.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.4', 'BSB', 'And if it is advisable for me to go also, they can travel with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.5', 'BSB', 'After I go through Macedonia, however, I will come to you; for I will be going through Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.6', 'BSB', 'Perhaps I will stay with you awhile, or even spend the winter, so that you can help me on my journey, wherever I go.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.7', 'BSB', 'For I do not want to see you now only in passing; I hope to spend some time with you, if the Lord permits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.8', 'BSB', 'But I will stay in Ephesus until Pentecost,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.9', 'BSB', 'because a great door for effective work has opened to me, even though many oppose me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.10', 'BSB', 'If Timothy comes, see to it that he has nothing to fear while he is with you, for he is doing the work of the Lord, just as I am.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.11', 'BSB', 'No one, then, should treat him with contempt. Send him on his way in peace so that he can return to me, for I am expecting him along with the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.12', 'BSB', 'Now about our brother Apollos: I strongly urged him to go to you with the brothers. He was not at all inclined to go now, but he will go when he has the opportunity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.13', 'BSB', 'Be on the alert. Stand firm in the faith. Be men of courage. Be strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.14', 'BSB', 'Do everything in love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.15', 'BSB', 'You know that Stephanas and his household were the first converts in Achaia, and they have devoted themselves to the service of the saints. Now I urge you, brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.16', 'BSB', 'to submit to such as these, and to every fellow worker and laborer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.17', 'BSB', 'I am glad that Stephanas, Fortunatus, and Achaicus have arrived, because they have supplied what was lacking from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.18', 'BSB', 'For they refreshed my spirit and yours as well. Show your appreciation, therefore, to such men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.19', 'BSB', 'The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.20', 'BSB', 'All the brothers here send you greetings. Greet one another with a holy kiss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.21', 'BSB', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.22', 'BSB', 'If anyone does not love the Lord, let him be under a curse. Come, O Lord!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.23', 'BSB', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Cor.16.24', 'BSB', 'My love be with all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God in Corinth, together with all the saints throughout Achaia:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.2', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.3', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of compassion and the God of all comfort,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.4', 'BSB', 'who comforts us in all our troubles, so that we can comfort those in any trouble with the comfort we ourselves have received from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.5', 'BSB', 'For just as the sufferings of Christ overflow to us, so also through Christ our comfort overflows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.6', 'BSB', 'If we are afflicted, it is for your comfort and salvation; if we are comforted, it is for your comfort, which accomplishes in you patient endurance of the same sufferings we experience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.7', 'BSB', 'And our hope for you is sure, because we know that just as you share in our sufferings, so also you will share in our comfort.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.8', 'BSB', 'We do not want you to be unaware, brothers, of the hardships we encountered in the province of Asia. We were under a burden far beyond our ability to endure, so that we despaired even of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.9', 'BSB', 'Indeed, we felt we were under the sentence of death, in order that we would not trust in ourselves, but in God, who raises the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.10', 'BSB', 'He has delivered us from such a deadly peril, and He will deliver us. In Him we have placed our hope that He will yet again deliver us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.11', 'BSB', 'as you help us by your prayers. Then many will give thanks on our behalf for the favor shown us in answer to their prayers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.12', 'BSB', 'And this is our boast: Our conscience testifies that we have conducted ourselves in the world, and especially in relation to you, in the holiness and sincerity that are from God—not in worldly wisdom, but in the grace of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.13', 'BSB', 'For we do not write you anything that is beyond your ability to read and understand. And I hope that you will understand us completely,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.14', 'BSB', 'as you have already understood us in part, so that you may boast of us just as we will boast of you in the day of our Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.15', 'BSB', 'Confident of this, I planned to visit you first, so that you might receive a double blessing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.16', 'BSB', 'I wanted to visit you on my way to Macedonia, and to return to you from Macedonia, and then to have you help me on my way to Judea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.17', 'BSB', 'When I planned this, did I do it carelessly? Or do I make my plans by human standards, so as to say “Yes, yes” when I really mean “No, no”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.18', 'BSB', 'But as surely as God is faithful, our message to you is not “Yes” and “No.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.19', 'BSB', 'For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was proclaimed among you by me and Silvanus and Timothy, was not “Yes” and “No,” but in Him it has always been “Yes.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.20', 'BSB', 'For all the promises of God are “Yes” in Christ. And so through Him, our “Amen” is spoken to the glory of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.21', 'BSB', 'Now it is God who establishes both us and you in Christ. He anointed us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.22', 'BSB', 'placed His seal on us, and put His Spirit in our hearts as a pledge of what is to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.23', 'BSB', 'I call God as my witness that it was in order to spare you that I did not return to Corinth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.1.24', 'BSB', 'Not that we lord it over your faith, but we are fellow workers with you for your joy, because it is by faith that you stand firm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.1', 'BSB', 'So I made up my mind not to make another painful visit to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.2', 'BSB', 'For if I grieve you, who is left to cheer me but those whom I have grieved?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.3', 'BSB', 'I wrote as I did so that on my arrival I would not be saddened by those who ought to make me rejoice. I had confidence in all of you, that you would share my joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.4', 'BSB', 'For through many tears I wrote you out of great distress and anguish of heart, not to grieve you but to let you know how much I love you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.5', 'BSB', 'Now if anyone has caused grief, he has not grieved me but all of you—to some degree, not to overstate it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.6', 'BSB', 'The punishment imposed on him by the majority is sufficient for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.7', 'BSB', 'So instead, you ought to forgive and comfort him, so that he will not be overwhelmed by excessive sorrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore I urge you to reaffirm your love for him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.9', 'BSB', 'My purpose in writing you was to see if you would stand the test and be obedient in everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.10', 'BSB', 'If you forgive anyone, I also forgive him. And if I have forgiven anything, I have forgiven it in the presence of Christ for your sake,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.11', 'BSB', 'in order that Satan should not outwit us. For we are not unaware of his schemes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.12', 'BSB', 'Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.13', 'BSB', 'I had no peace in my spirit, because I did not find my brother Titus there. So I said goodbye to them and went on to Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.14', 'BSB', 'But thanks be to God, who always leads us triumphantly as captives in Christ and through us spreads everywhere the fragrance of the knowledge of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.15', 'BSB', 'For we are to God the sweet aroma of Christ among those who are being saved and those who are perishing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.16', 'BSB', 'To the one, we are an odor of death and demise; to the other, a fragrance that brings life. And who is qualified for such a task?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.2.17', 'BSB', 'For we are not like so many others, who peddle the word of God for profit. On the contrary, in Christ we speak before God with sincerity, as men sent from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.1', 'BSB', 'Are we beginning to commend ourselves again? Or do we need, like some people, letters of recommendation to you or from you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.2', 'BSB', 'You yourselves are our letter, inscribed on our hearts, known and read by everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.3', 'BSB', 'It is clear that you are a letter from Christ, the result of our ministry, written not with ink but with the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone but on tablets of human hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.4', 'BSB', 'Such confidence before God is ours through Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.5', 'BSB', 'Not that we are competent in ourselves to claim that anything comes from us, but our competence comes from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.6', 'BSB', 'And He has qualified us as ministers of a new covenant, not of the letter but of the Spirit; for the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.7', 'BSB', 'Now if the ministry of death, which was engraved in letters on stone, came with such glory that the Israelites could not gaze at the face of Moses because of its fleeting glory,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.8', 'BSB', 'will not the ministry of the Spirit be even more glorious?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.9', 'BSB', 'For if the ministry of condemnation was glorious, how much more glorious is the ministry of righteousness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.10', 'BSB', 'Indeed, what was once glorious has no glory now in comparison to the glory that surpasses it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.11', 'BSB', 'For if what was fading away came with glory, how much greater is the glory of that which endures!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we have such a hope, we are very bold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.13', 'BSB', 'We are not like Moses, who would put a veil over his face to keep the Israelites from gazing at the end of what was fading away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.14', 'BSB', 'But their minds were closed. For to this day the same veil remains at the reading of the old covenant. It has not been lifted, because only in Christ can it be removed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.15', 'BSB', 'And even to this day when Moses is read, a veil covers their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.16', 'BSB', 'But whenever anyone turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.17', 'BSB', 'Now the Lord is the Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is freedom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.3.18', 'BSB', 'And we, who with unveiled faces all reflect the glory of the Lord, are being transformed into His image with intensifying glory, which comes from the Lord, who is the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since God in His mercy has given us this ministry, we do not lose heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.2', 'BSB', 'Instead, we have renounced secret and shameful ways. We do not practice deceit, nor do we distort the word of God. On the contrary, by open proclamation of the truth, we commend ourselves to every man’s conscience in the sight of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.3', 'BSB', 'And even if our gospel is veiled, it is veiled to those who are perishing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.4', 'BSB', 'The god of this age has blinded the minds of unbelievers so they cannot see the light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.5', 'BSB', 'For we do not proclaim ourselves, but Jesus Christ as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus’ sake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.6', 'BSB', 'For God, who said, “Let light shine out of darkness,” made His light shine in our hearts to give us the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.7', 'BSB', 'Now we have this treasure in jars of clay to show that this surpassingly great power is from God and not from us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.8', 'BSB', 'We are hard pressed on all sides, but not crushed; perplexed, but not in despair;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.9', 'BSB', 'persecuted, but not forsaken; struck down, but not destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.10', 'BSB', 'We always carry around in our body the death of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.11', 'BSB', 'For we who are alive are always consigned to death for Jesus’ sake, so that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our mortal body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.12', 'BSB', 'So then, death is at work in us, but life is at work in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.13', 'BSB', 'And in keeping with what is written: “I believed, therefore I have spoken,” we who have the same spirit of faith also believe and therefore speak,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.14', 'BSB', 'knowing that the One who raised the Lord Jesus will also raise us with Jesus and present us with you in His presence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.15', 'BSB', 'All this is for your benefit, so that the grace that is extending to more and more people may overflow in thanksgiving, to the glory of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore we do not lose heart. Though our outer self is wasting away, yet our inner self is being renewed day by day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.17', 'BSB', 'For our light and momentary affliction is producing for us an eternal glory that is far beyond comparison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.4.18', 'BSB', 'So we fix our eyes not on what is seen, but on what is unseen. For what is seen is temporary, but what is unseen is eternal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.1', 'BSB', 'Now we know that if the earthly tent we live in is dismantled, we have a building from God, an eternal house in heaven, not built by human hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.2', 'BSB', 'For in this tent we groan, longing to be clothed with our heavenly dwelling,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.3', 'BSB', 'because when we are clothed, we will not be found naked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.4', 'BSB', 'So while we are in this tent, we groan under our burdens, because we do not wish to be unclothed but clothed, so that our mortality may be swallowed up by life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.5', 'BSB', 'And God has prepared us for this very purpose and has given us the Spirit as a pledge of what is to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore we are always confident, although we know that while we are at home in the body, we are away from the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.7', 'BSB', 'For we walk by faith, not by sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.8', 'BSB', 'We are confident, then, and would prefer to be away from the body and at home with the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.9', 'BSB', 'So we aspire to please Him, whether we are here in this body or away from it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.10', 'BSB', 'For we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ, that each one may receive his due for the things done in the body, whether good or bad.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we know what it means to fear the Lord, we try to persuade men. What we are is clear to God, and I hope it is clear to your conscience as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.12', 'BSB', 'We are not commending ourselves to you again. Instead, we are giving you an occasion to be proud of us, so that you can answer those who take pride in appearances rather than in the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.13', 'BSB', 'If we are out of our mind, it is for God; if we are of sound mind, it is for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.14', 'BSB', 'For Christ’s love compels us, because we are convinced that One died for all, therefore all died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.15', 'BSB', 'And He died for all, that those who live should no longer live for themselves, but for Him who died for them and was raised again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.16', 'BSB', 'So from now on we regard no one according to the flesh. Although we once regarded Christ in this way, we do so no longer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old has passed away. Behold, the new has come!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.18', 'BSB', 'All this is from God, who reconciled us to Himself through Christ and gave us the ministry of reconciliation:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.19', 'BSB', 'that God was reconciling the world to Himself in Christ, not counting men’s trespasses against them. And He has committed to us the message of reconciliation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.20', 'BSB', 'Therefore we are ambassadors for Christ, as though God were making His appeal through us. We implore you on behalf of Christ: Be reconciled to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.5.21', 'BSB', 'God made Him who knew no sin to be sin on our behalf, so that in Him we might become the righteousness of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.1', 'BSB', 'As God’s fellow workers, then, we urge you not to receive God’s grace in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.2', 'BSB', 'For He says: “In the time of favor I heard you, and in the day of salvation I helped you.” Behold, now is the time of favor; now is the day of salvation!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.3', 'BSB', 'We put no obstacle in anyone’s way, so that no one can discredit our ministry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.4', 'BSB', 'Rather, as servants of God we commend ourselves in every way: in great endurance; in troubles, hardships, and calamities;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.5', 'BSB', 'in beatings, imprisonments, and riots; in labor, sleepless nights, and hunger;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.6', 'BSB', 'in purity, knowledge, patience, and kindness; in the Holy Spirit and in sincere love;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.7', 'BSB', 'in truthful speech and in the power of God; with the weapons of righteousness in the right hand and in the left;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.8', 'BSB', 'through glory and dishonor, slander and praise; viewed as imposters, yet genuine;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.9', 'BSB', 'as unknown, yet well-known; dying, and yet we live on; punished, yet not killed;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.10', 'BSB', 'sorrowful, yet always rejoicing; poor, yet making many rich; having nothing, and yet possessing everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.11', 'BSB', 'We have spoken freely to you, Corinthians. Our hearts are open wide.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.12', 'BSB', 'It is not our affection, but yours, that is restrained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.13', 'BSB', 'As a fair exchange, I ask you as my children: Open wide your hearts also.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.14', 'BSB', 'Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers. For what partnership can righteousness have with wickedness? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.15', 'BSB', 'What harmony is there between Christ and Belial? Or what does a believer have in common with an unbeliever?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.16', 'BSB', 'What agreement can exist between the temple of God and idols? For we are the temple of the living God. As God has said: “I will dwell with them and walk among them, and I will be their God, and they will be My people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.17', 'BSB', '“Therefore come out from among them and be separate, says the Lord. Touch no unclean thing, and I will receive you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.6.18', 'BSB', 'And: “I will be a Father to you, and you will be My sons and daughters, says the Lord Almighty.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, beloved, since we have these promises, let us cleanse ourselves from everything that defiles body and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.2', 'BSB', 'Make room for us in your hearts. We have wronged no one, we have corrupted no one, we have exploited no one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.3', 'BSB', 'I do not say this to condemn you. I have said before that you so occupy our hearts that we live and die together with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.4', 'BSB', 'Great is my confidence in you; great is my pride in you; I am filled with encouragement; in all our troubles my joy overflows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.5', 'BSB', 'For when we arrived in Macedonia, our bodies had no rest, but we were pressed from every direction—conflicts on the outside, fears within.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.6', 'BSB', 'But God, who comforts the downcast, comforted us by the arrival of Titus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.7', 'BSB', 'and not only by his arrival, but also by the comfort he had received from you. He told us about your longing, your mourning, and your zeal for me, so that I rejoiced all the more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.8', 'BSB', 'Even if I caused you sorrow by my letter, I do not regret it. Although I did regret it, I now see that my letter caused you sorrow, but only for a short time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.9', 'BSB', 'And now I rejoice, not because you were made sorrowful, but because your sorrow led you to repentance. For you felt the sorrow that God had intended, and so were not harmed in any way by us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.10', 'BSB', 'Godly sorrow brings repentance that leads to salvation without regret, but worldly sorrow brings death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.11', 'BSB', 'Consider what this godly sorrow has produced in you: what earnestness, what eagerness to clear yourselves, what indignation, what alarm, what longing, what zeal, what vindication! In every way you have proved yourselves to be innocent in this matter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.12', 'BSB', 'So even though I wrote to you, it was not on account of the one who did wrong or the one who was harmed, but rather that your earnestness on our behalf would be made clear to you in the sight of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.13', 'BSB', 'On account of this, we are encouraged. In addition to our own encouragement, we were even more delighted by the joy of Titus. For his spirit has been refreshed by all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.14', 'BSB', 'Indeed, I was not embarrassed by anything I had boasted to him about you. But just as everything we said to you was true, so our boasting to Titus has proved to be true as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.15', 'BSB', 'And his affection for you is even greater when he remembers that you were all obedient as you welcomed him with fear and trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.7.16', 'BSB', 'I rejoice that I can have complete confidence in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.1', 'BSB', 'Now, brothers, we want you to know about the grace that God has given the churches of Macedonia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.2', 'BSB', 'In the terrible ordeal they suffered, their abundant joy and deep poverty overflowed into rich generosity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.3', 'BSB', 'For I testify that they gave according to their ability and even beyond it. Of their own accord,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.4', 'BSB', 'they earnestly pleaded with us for the privilege of sharing in this service to the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.5', 'BSB', 'And not only did they do as we expected, but they gave themselves first to the Lord and then to us, because it was the will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.6', 'BSB', 'So we urged Titus to help complete your act of grace, just as he had started it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.7', 'BSB', 'But just as you excel in everything—in faith, in speech, in knowledge, in complete earnestness, and in the love we inspired in you —see that you also excel in this grace of giving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.8', 'BSB', 'I am not making a demand, but I am testing the sincerity of your love in comparison to the earnestness of others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.9', 'BSB', 'For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, so that you through His poverty might become rich.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.10', 'BSB', 'And this is my opinion about what is helpful for you in this matter: Last year you were the first not only to give, but even to have such a desire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.11', 'BSB', 'Now finish the work, so that you may complete it just as eagerly as you began, according to your means.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.12', 'BSB', 'For if the eagerness is there, the gift is acceptable according to what one has, not according to what he does not have.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.13', 'BSB', 'It is not our intention that others may be relieved while you are burdened, but that there may be equality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.14', 'BSB', 'At the present time, your surplus will meet their need, so that in turn their surplus will meet your need. Then there will be equality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.15', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “He who gathered much had no excess, and he who gathered little had no shortfall.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.16', 'BSB', 'But thanks be to God, who put into the heart of Titus the same devotion I have for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.17', 'BSB', 'For not only did he welcome our appeal, but he is eagerly coming to you of his own volition.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.18', 'BSB', 'Along with Titus we are sending the brother who is praised by all the churches for his work in the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.19', 'BSB', 'More than that, this brother was chosen by the churches to accompany us with the offering —the gracious gift we administer to honor the Lord Himself and to show our eagerness to help.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.20', 'BSB', 'We hope to avoid any criticism of the way we administer this generous gift.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.21', 'BSB', 'For we are taking great care to do what is right, not only in the eyes of the Lord, but also in the eyes of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.22', 'BSB', 'And we are sending along with them our brother whose earnestness has been proven many times and in many ways, and now even more so by his great confidence in you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.23', 'BSB', 'As for Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker among you. As for our brothers, they are messengers of the churches, to the glory of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.8.24', 'BSB', 'In full view of the churches, then, show these men the proof of your love and the reason for our boasting about you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.1', 'BSB', 'Now about the service to the saints, there is no need for me to write to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.2', 'BSB', 'For I know your eagerness to help, and I have been boasting to the Macedonians that since last year you in Achaia were prepared to give. And your zeal has stirred most of them to do likewise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.3', 'BSB', 'But I am sending the brothers in order that our boasting about you in this matter should not prove empty, but that you will be prepared, just as I said.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.4', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, if any Macedonians come with me and find you unprepared, we—to say nothing of you—would be ashamed of having been so confident.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.5', 'BSB', 'So I thought it necessary to urge the brothers to visit you beforehand and make arrangements for the bountiful gift you had promised. This way, your gift will be prepared generously and not begrudgingly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.6', 'BSB', 'Remember this: Whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and whoever sows generously will also reap generously.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.7', 'BSB', 'Each one should give what he has decided in his heart to give, not out of regret or compulsion. For God loves a cheerful giver.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.8', 'BSB', 'And God is able to make all grace abound to you, so that in all things, at all times, having all that you need, you will abound in every good work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.9', 'BSB', 'As it is written: “He has scattered abroad His gifts to the poor; His righteousness endures forever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.10', 'BSB', 'Now He who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food will supply and multiply your store of seed and will increase the harvest of your righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.11', 'BSB', 'You will be enriched in every way to be generous on every occasion, so that through us your giving will produce thanksgiving to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.12', 'BSB', 'For this ministry of service is not only supplying the needs of the saints, but is also overflowing in many expressions of thanksgiving to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.13', 'BSB', 'Because of the proof this ministry provides, the saints will glorify God for your obedient confession of the gospel of Christ, and for the generosity of your contribution to them and to all the others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.14', 'BSB', 'And their prayers for you will express their affection for you, because of the surpassing grace God has given you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.9.15', 'BSB', 'Thanks be to God for His indescribable gift!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.1', 'BSB', 'Now by the mildness and gentleness of Christ, I appeal to you—I, Paul, who am humble when face to face with you, but bold when away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.2', 'BSB', 'I beg you that when I come I may not need to be as bold as I expect toward those who presume that we live according to the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.3', 'BSB', 'For though we live in the flesh, we do not wage war according to the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.4', 'BSB', 'The weapons of our warfare are not the weapons of the world. Instead, they have divine power to demolish strongholds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.5', 'BSB', 'We tear down arguments and every presumption set up against the knowledge of God; and we take captive every thought to make it obedient to Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.6', 'BSB', 'And we will be ready to punish every act of disobedience, as soon as your obedience is complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.7', 'BSB', 'You are looking at outward appearances. If anyone is confident that he belongs to Christ, he should remind himself that we belong to Christ just as much as he does.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.8', 'BSB', 'For even if I boast somewhat excessively about the authority the Lord gave us for building you up rather than tearing you down, I will not be ashamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.9', 'BSB', 'I do not want to seem to be trying to frighten you by my letters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.10', 'BSB', 'For some say, “His letters are weighty and forceful, but his physical presence is unimpressive, and his speaking is of no account.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.11', 'BSB', 'Such people should consider that what we are in our letters when absent, we will be in our actions when present.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.12', 'BSB', 'We do not dare to classify or compare ourselves with some who commend themselves. When they measure themselves by themselves and compare themselves with themselves, they show their ignorance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.13', 'BSB', 'We, however, will not boast beyond our limits, but only within the field of influence that God has assigned to us—a field that reaches even to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.14', 'BSB', 'We are not overstepping our bounds, as if we had not come to you. Indeed, we were the first to reach you with the gospel of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.15', 'BSB', 'Neither do we boast beyond our limits in the labors of others. But we hope that as your faith increases, our area of influence among you will greatly increase as well,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.16', 'BSB', 'so that we can preach the gospel in the regions beyond you. Then we will not be boasting in the work already done in another man’s territory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.17', 'BSB', 'Rather, “Let him who boasts boast in the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.10.18', 'BSB', 'For it is not the one who commends himself who is approved, but the one whom the Lord commends.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.1', 'BSB', 'I hope you will bear with a little of my foolishness, but you are already doing that.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.2', 'BSB', 'I am jealous for you with a godly jealousy. For I promised you to one husband, to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.3', 'BSB', 'I am afraid, however, that just as Eve was deceived by the serpent’s cunning, your minds may be led astray from your simple and pure devotion to Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.4', 'BSB', 'For if someone comes and proclaims a Jesus other than the One we proclaimed, or if you receive a different spirit than the One you received, or a different gospel than the one you accepted, you put up with it way too easily.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.5', 'BSB', 'I consider myself in no way inferior to those “super-apostles.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.6', 'BSB', 'Although I am not a polished speaker, I am certainly not lacking in knowledge. We have made this clear to you in every way possible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.7', 'BSB', 'Was it a sin for me to humble myself in order to exalt you, because I preached the gospel of God to you free of charge?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.8', 'BSB', 'I robbed other churches by accepting their support in order to serve you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.9', 'BSB', 'And when I was with you and in need, I was not a burden to anyone; for the brothers who came from Macedonia supplied my needs. I have refrained from being a burden to you in any way, and I will continue to do so.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.10', 'BSB', 'As surely as the truth of Christ is in me, this boasting of mine will not be silenced in the regions of Achaia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.11', 'BSB', 'Why? Because I do not love you? God knows I do!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.12', 'BSB', 'But I will keep on doing what I am doing, in order to undercut those who want an opportunity to be regarded as our equals in the things of which they boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.13', 'BSB', 'For such men are false apostles, deceitful workers, masquerading as apostles of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.14', 'BSB', 'And no wonder, for Satan himself masquerades as an angel of light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.15', 'BSB', 'It is not surprising, then, if his servants masquerade as servants of righteousness. Their end will correspond to their actions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.16', 'BSB', 'I repeat: Let no one take me for a fool. But if you do, then receive me as a fool, so that I too may boast a little.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.17', 'BSB', 'In this confident boasting of mine, I am not speaking as the Lord would, but as a fool.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.18', 'BSB', 'Since many are boasting according to the flesh, I too will boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.19', 'BSB', 'For you gladly tolerate fools, since you are so wise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.20', 'BSB', 'In fact, you even put up with anyone who enslaves you or exploits you or takes advantage of you or exalts himself or strikes you in the face.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.21', 'BSB', 'To my shame I concede that we were too weak for that! Speaking as a fool, however, I can match what anyone else dares to boast about.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.22', 'BSB', 'Are they Hebrews? So am I. Are they Israelites? So am I. Are they descendants of Abraham? So am I.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.23', 'BSB', 'Are they servants of Christ? I am speaking like I am out of my mind, but I am so much more: in harder labor, in more imprisonments, in worse beatings, in frequent danger of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.24', 'BSB', 'Five times I received from the Jews the forty lashes minus one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.25', 'BSB', 'Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. I spent a night and a day in the open sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.26', 'BSB', 'In my frequent journeys, I have been in danger from rivers and from bandits, in danger from my countrymen and from the Gentiles, in danger in the city and in the country, in danger on the sea and among false brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.27', 'BSB', 'in labor and toil and often without sleep, in hunger and thirst and often without food, in cold and exposure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.28', 'BSB', 'Apart from these external trials, I face daily the pressure of my concern for all the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.29', 'BSB', 'Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who is led into sin, and I do not burn with grief?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.30', 'BSB', 'If I must boast, I will boast of the things that show my weakness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.31', 'BSB', 'The God and Father of the Lord Jesus, who is forever worthy of praise, knows that I am not lying.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.32', 'BSB', 'In Damascus, the governor under King Aretas secured the city of the Damascenes in order to arrest me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.11.33', 'BSB', 'But I was lowered in a basket through a window in the wall and escaped his grasp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.1', 'BSB', 'I must go on boasting. Although there is nothing to gain, I will go on to visions and revelations from the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.2', 'BSB', 'I know a man in Christ who fourteen years ago was caught up to the third heaven. Whether it was in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.3', 'BSB', 'And I know that this man—whether in the body or out of it I do not know, but God knows—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.4', 'BSB', 'was caught up to Paradise. The things he heard were too sacred for words, things that man is not permitted to tell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.5', 'BSB', 'I will boast about such a man, but I will not boast about myself, except in my weaknesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.6', 'BSB', 'Even if I wanted to boast, I would not be a fool, because I would be speaking the truth. But I refrain, so no one will credit me with more than he sees in me or hears from me,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.7', 'BSB', 'or because of these surpassingly great revelations. So to keep me from becoming conceited, I was given a thorn in my flesh, a messenger of Satan, to torment me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.8', 'BSB', 'Three times I pleaded with the Lord to take it away from me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.9', 'BSB', 'But He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My power is perfected in weakness.” Therefore I will boast all the more gladly in my weaknesses, so that the power of Christ may rest on me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.10', 'BSB', 'That is why, for the sake of Christ, I delight in weaknesses, in insults, in hardships, in persecutions, in difficulties. For when I am weak, then I am strong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.11', 'BSB', 'I have become a fool, but you drove me to it. In fact, you should have commended me, since I am in no way inferior to those “super-apostles,” even though I am nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.12', 'BSB', 'The true marks of an apostle—signs, wonders, and miracles—were performed among you with great perseverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.13', 'BSB', 'In what way were you inferior to the other churches, except that I was not a burden to you? Forgive me this wrong!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.14', 'BSB', 'See, I am ready to come to you a third time, and I will not be a burden, because I am not seeking your possessions, but you. For children should not have to save up for their parents, but parents for their children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.15', 'BSB', 'And for the sake of your souls, I will most gladly spend my money and myself. If I love you more, will you love me less?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.16', 'BSB', 'Be that as it may, I was not a burden to you; but crafty as I am, I caught you by trickery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.17', 'BSB', 'Did I exploit you by anyone I sent you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.18', 'BSB', 'I urged Titus to visit you, and I sent our brother with him. Did Titus exploit you in any way? Did we not walk in the same Spirit and follow in the same footsteps?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.19', 'BSB', 'Have you been thinking all along that we were making a defense to you? We speak before God in Christ, and all of this, beloved, is to build you up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.20', 'BSB', 'For I am afraid that when I come, I may not find you as I wish, and you may not find me as you wish. I fear that there may be quarreling, jealousy, rage, rivalry, slander, gossip, arrogance, and disorder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.12.21', 'BSB', 'I am afraid that when I come again, my God will humble me before you, and I will be grieved over many who have sinned earlier and have not repented of their acts of impurity, sexual immorality, and debauchery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.1', 'BSB', 'This is the third time I am coming to you. “Every matter must be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.2', 'BSB', 'I already warned you the second time I was with you. So now in my absence I warn those who sinned earlier and everyone else: If I return, I will not spare anyone,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.3', 'BSB', 'since you are demanding proof that Christ is speaking through me. He is not weak in dealing with you, but is powerful among you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.4', 'BSB', 'For He was indeed crucified in weakness, yet He lives by God’s power. And though we are weak in Him, yet by God’s power we will live with Him to serve you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.5', 'BSB', 'Examine yourselves to see whether you are in the faith; test yourselves. Can’t you see for yourselves that Jesus Christ is in you—unless you actually fail the test?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.6', 'BSB', 'And I hope you will realize that we have not failed the test.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.7', 'BSB', 'Now we pray to God that you will not do anything wrong—not that we will appear to have stood the test, but that you will do what is right, even if we appear to have failed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.8', 'BSB', 'For we cannot do anything against the truth, but only for the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.9', 'BSB', 'In fact, we rejoice when we are weak but you are strong, and our prayer is for your perfection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.10', 'BSB', 'This is why I write these things while absent, so that when I am present I will not need to be severe in my use of the authority that the Lord gave me for building you up, not for tearing you down.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.11', 'BSB', 'Finally, brothers, rejoice! Aim for perfect harmony, encourage one another, be of one mind, live in peace. And the God of love and peace will be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.12', 'BSB', 'Greet one another with a holy kiss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.13', 'BSB', 'All the saints send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Cor.13.14', 'BSB', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, and the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle—sent not from men nor by man, but by Jesus Christ and God the Father, who raised Him from the dead—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.2', 'BSB', 'and all the brothers with me, To the churches of Galatia:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.3', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.4', 'BSB', 'who gave Himself for our sins to rescue us from the present evil age, according to the will of our God and Father,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.5', 'BSB', 'to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.6', 'BSB', 'I am amazed how quickly you are deserting the One who called you by the grace of Christ and are turning to a different gospel—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.7', 'BSB', 'which is not even a gospel. Evidently some people are troubling you and trying to distort the gospel of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.8', 'BSB', 'But even if we or an angel from heaven should preach a gospel contrary to the one we preached to you, let him be under a curse!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.9', 'BSB', 'As we have said before, so now I say again: If anyone is preaching to you a gospel contrary to the one you received, let him be under a curse!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.10', 'BSB', 'Am I now seeking the approval of men, or of God? Or am I striving to please men? If I were still trying to please men, I would not be a servant of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.11', 'BSB', 'For I certify to you, brothers, that the gospel I preached was not devised by man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.12', 'BSB', 'I did not receive it from any man, nor was I taught it; rather, I received it by revelation from Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.13', 'BSB', 'For you have heard of my former way of life in Judaism, how severely I persecuted the church of God and tried to destroy it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.14', 'BSB', 'I was advancing in Judaism beyond many of my contemporaries and was extremely zealous for the traditions of my fathers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.15', 'BSB', 'But when God, who set me apart from my mother’s womb and called me by His grace, was pleased', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.16', 'BSB', 'to reveal His Son in me so that I might preach Him among the Gentiles, I did not rush to consult with flesh and blood,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.17', 'BSB', 'nor did I go up to Jerusalem to the apostles who came before me, but I went into Arabia and later returned to Damascus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.18', 'BSB', 'Only after three years did I go up to Jerusalem to confer with Cephas, and I stayed with him fifteen days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.19', 'BSB', 'But I saw none of the other apostles except James, the Lord’s brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.20', 'BSB', 'I assure you before God that what I am writing to you is no lie.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.21', 'BSB', 'Later I went to the regions of Syria and Cilicia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.22', 'BSB', 'I was personally unknown, however, to the churches of Judea that are in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.23', 'BSB', 'They only heard the account: “The man who formerly persecuted us is now preaching the faith he once tried to destroy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.1.24', 'BSB', 'And they glorified God because of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.1', 'BSB', 'Fourteen years later I went up again to Jerusalem, accompanied by Barnabas. I took Titus along also.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.2', 'BSB', 'I went in response to a revelation and set before them the gospel that I preach among the Gentiles. But I spoke privately to those recognized as leaders, for fear that I was running or had already run in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.3', 'BSB', 'Yet not even Titus, who was with me, was compelled to be circumcised, even though he was a Greek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.4', 'BSB', 'This issue arose because some false brothers had come in under false pretenses to spy on our freedom in Christ Jesus, in order to enslave us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.5', 'BSB', 'We did not give in to them for a moment, so that the truth of the gospel would remain with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.6', 'BSB', 'But as for the highly esteemed—whatever they were makes no difference to me; God does not show favoritism —those leaders added nothing to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.7', 'BSB', 'On the contrary, they saw that I had been entrusted to preach the gospel to the uncircumcised, just as Peter had been to the circumcised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.8', 'BSB', 'For the One who was at work in Peter’s apostleship to the circumcised was also at work in my apostleship to the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.9', 'BSB', 'And recognizing the grace that I had been given, James, Cephas, and John—those reputed to be pillars—gave me and Barnabas the right hand of fellowship, so that we should go to the Gentiles, and they to the circumcised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.10', 'BSB', 'They only asked us to remember the poor, the very thing I was eager to do.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.11', 'BSB', 'When Cephas came to Antioch, however, I opposed him to his face, because he stood to be condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.12', 'BSB', 'For before certain men came from James, he used to eat with the Gentiles. But when they arrived, he began to draw back and separate himself, for fear of those in the circumcision group.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.13', 'BSB', 'The other Jews joined him in his hypocrisy, so that by their hypocrisy even Barnabas was led astray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.14', 'BSB', 'When I saw that they were not walking in line with the truth of the gospel, I said to Cephas in front of them all, “If you, who are a Jew, live like a Gentile and not like a Jew, how can you compel the Gentiles to live like Jews?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.15', 'BSB', 'We who are Jews by birth and not Gentile “sinners”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.16', 'BSB', 'know that a man is not justified by works of the law, but by faith in Jesus Christ. So we, too, have believed in Christ Jesus, that we may be justified by faith in Christ and not by works of the law, because by works of the law no one will be justified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.17', 'BSB', 'But if, while we seek to be justified in Christ, we ourselves are found to be sinners, does that make Christ a minister of sin? Certainly not!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.18', 'BSB', 'If I rebuild what I have already torn down, I prove myself to be a lawbreaker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.19', 'BSB', 'For through the law I died to the law so that I might live to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.20', 'BSB', 'I have been crucified with Christ, and I no longer live, but Christ lives in me. The life I live in the body, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself up for me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.2.21', 'BSB', 'I do not set aside the grace of God. For if righteousness comes through the law, Christ died for nothing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.1', 'BSB', 'O foolish Galatians! Who has bewitched you? Before your very eyes Jesus Christ was clearly portrayed as crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.2', 'BSB', 'I would like to learn just one thing from you: Did you receive the Spirit by works of the law, or by hearing with faith?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.3', 'BSB', 'Are you so foolish? After starting in the Spirit, are you now finishing in the flesh?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.4', 'BSB', 'Have you suffered so much for nothing, if it really was for nothing?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.5', 'BSB', 'Does God lavish His Spirit on you and work miracles among you because you practice the law, or because you hear and believe?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.6', 'BSB', 'So also, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.7', 'BSB', 'Understand, then, that those who have faith are sons of Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.8', 'BSB', 'The Scripture foresaw that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, and foretold the gospel to Abraham: “All nations will be blessed through you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.9', 'BSB', 'So those who have faith are blessed along with Abraham, the man of faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.10', 'BSB', 'All who rely on works of the law are under a curse. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who does not continue to do everything written in the Book of the Law.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.11', 'BSB', 'Now it is clear that no one is justified before God by the law, because, “The righteous will live by faith.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.12', 'BSB', 'The law, however, is not based on faith; on the contrary, “The man who does these things will live by them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.13', 'BSB', 'Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us. For it is written: “Cursed is everyone who is hung on a tree.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.14', 'BSB', 'He redeemed us in order that the blessing promised to Abraham would come to the Gentiles in Christ Jesus, so that by faith we might receive the promise of the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.15', 'BSB', 'Brothers, let me put this in human terms. Even a human covenant, once it is ratified, cannot be canceled or amended.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.16', 'BSB', 'The promises were spoken to Abraham and to his seed. The Scripture does not say, “and to seeds,” meaning many, but “and to your seed,” meaning One, who is Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.17', 'BSB', 'What I mean is this: The law that came 430 years later does not revoke the covenant previously established by God, so as to nullify the promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.18', 'BSB', 'For if the inheritance depends on the law, then it no longer depends on a promise; but God freely granted it to Abraham through a promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.19', 'BSB', 'Why then was the law given? It was added because of transgressions, until the arrival of the seed to whom the promise referred. It was administered through angels by a mediator.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.20', 'BSB', 'A mediator is unnecessary, however, for only one party; but God is one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.21', 'BSB', 'Is the law, then, opposed to the promises of God? Certainly not! For if a law had been given that could impart life, then righteousness would certainly have come from the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.22', 'BSB', 'But the Scripture pronounces all things confined by sin, so that by faith in Jesus Christ the promise might be given to those who believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.23', 'BSB', 'Before this faith came, we were held in custody under the law, locked up until faith should be revealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.24', 'BSB', 'So the law became our guardian to lead us to Christ, that we might be justified by faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.25', 'BSB', 'Now that faith has come, we are no longer under a guardian.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.26', 'BSB', 'You are all sons of God through faith in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.27', 'BSB', 'For all of you who were baptized into Christ have clothed yourselves with Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.28', 'BSB', 'There is neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free, male nor female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.3.29', 'BSB', 'And if you belong to Christ, then you are Abraham’s seed and heirs according to the promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.1', 'BSB', 'What I am saying is that as long as the heir is a child, he is no different from a slave, although he is the owner of everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.2', 'BSB', 'He is subject to guardians and trustees until the date set by his father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.3', 'BSB', 'So also, when we were children, we were enslaved under the basic principles of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.4', 'BSB', 'But when the time had fully come, God sent His Son, born of a woman, born under the law,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.5', 'BSB', 'to redeem those under the law, that we might receive our adoption as sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.6', 'BSB', 'And because you are sons, God sent the Spirit of His Son into our hearts, crying out, “Abba, Father!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.7', 'BSB', 'So you are no longer a slave, but a son; and since you are a son, you are also an heir through God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.8', 'BSB', 'Formerly, when you did not know God, you were slaves to those who by nature are not gods.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.9', 'BSB', 'But now that you know God, or rather are known by God, how is it that you are turning back to those weak and worthless principles? Do you wish to be enslaved by them all over again?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.10', 'BSB', 'You are observing special days and months and seasons and years!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.11', 'BSB', 'I fear for you, that my efforts for you may have been in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.12', 'BSB', 'I beg you, brothers, become like me, for I became like you. You have done me no wrong.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.13', 'BSB', 'You know that it was because of an illness that I first preached the gospel to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.14', 'BSB', 'And although my illness was a trial to you, you did not despise or reject me. Instead, you welcomed me as if I were an angel of God, as if I were Christ Jesus Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.15', 'BSB', 'What then has become of your blessing? For I can testify that, if it were possible, you would have torn out your eyes and given them to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.16', 'BSB', 'Have I now become your enemy by telling you the truth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.17', 'BSB', 'Those people are zealous for you, but not in a good way. Instead, they want to isolate you from us, so that you may be zealous for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.18', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, it is good to be zealous if it serves a noble purpose—at any time, and not only when I am with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.19', 'BSB', 'My children, for whom I am again in the pains of childbirth until Christ is formed in you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.20', 'BSB', 'how I wish I could be with you now and change my tone, because I am perplexed about you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.21', 'BSB', 'Tell me, you who want to be under the law, do you not understand what the law says?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.22', 'BSB', 'For it is written that Abraham had two sons, one by the slave woman and the other by the free woman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.23', 'BSB', 'His son by the slave woman was born according to the flesh, but his son by the free woman was born through the promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.24', 'BSB', 'These things serve as illustrations, for the women represent two covenants. One covenant is from Mount Sinai and bears children into slavery: This is Hagar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.25', 'BSB', 'Now Hagar stands for Mount Sinai in Arabia and corresponds to the present-day Jerusalem, because she is in slavery with her children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.26', 'BSB', 'But the Jerusalem above is free, and she is our mother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.27', 'BSB', 'For it is written: “Rejoice, O barren woman, who bears no children; break forth and cry aloud, you who have never travailed; because more are the children of the desolate woman than of her who has a husband.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.28', 'BSB', 'Now you, brothers, like Isaac, are children of promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.29', 'BSB', 'At that time, however, the son born by the flesh persecuted the son born by the Spirit. It is the same now.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.30', 'BSB', 'But what does the Scripture say? “Expel the slave woman and her son, for the slave woman’s son will never share in the inheritance with the free woman’s son.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.4.31', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, we are not children of the slave woman, but of the free woman.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.1', 'BSB', 'It is for freedom that Christ has set us free. Stand firm, then, and do not be encumbered once more by a yoke of slavery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.2', 'BSB', 'Take notice: I, Paul, tell you that if you let yourselves be circumcised, Christ will be of no value to you at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.3', 'BSB', 'Again I testify to every man who gets himself circumcised that he is obligated to obey the whole law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.4', 'BSB', 'You who are trying to be justified by the law have been severed from Christ; you have fallen away from grace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.5', 'BSB', 'But by faith we eagerly await through the Spirit the hope of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.6', 'BSB', 'For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision has any value. All that matters is faith, expressed through love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.7', 'BSB', 'You were running so well. Who has obstructed you from obeying the truth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.8', 'BSB', 'Such persuasion does not come from the One who calls you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.9', 'BSB', 'A little leaven works through the whole batch of dough.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.10', 'BSB', 'I am confident in the Lord that you will take no other view. The one who is troubling you will bear the judgment, whoever he may be.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.11', 'BSB', 'Now, brothers, if I am still preaching circumcision, why am I still being persecuted? In that case the offense of the cross has been abolished.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.12', 'BSB', 'As for those who are agitating you, I wish they would proceed to emasculate themselves!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.13', 'BSB', 'For you, brothers, were called to freedom; but do not use your freedom as an opportunity for the flesh. Rather, serve one another in love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.14', 'BSB', 'The entire law is fulfilled in a single decree: “Love your neighbor as yourself.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.15', 'BSB', 'But if you keep on biting and devouring one another, watch out, or you will be consumed by one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.16', 'BSB', 'So I say, walk by the Spirit, and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.17', 'BSB', 'For the flesh craves what is contrary to the Spirit, and the Spirit what is contrary to the flesh. They are opposed to each other, so that you do not do what you want.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.18', 'BSB', 'But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.19', 'BSB', 'The acts of the flesh are obvious: sexual immorality, impurity, and debauchery;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.20', 'BSB', 'idolatry and sorcery; hatred, discord, jealousy, and rage; rivalries, divisions, factions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.21', 'BSB', 'and envy; drunkenness, orgies, and the like. I warn you, as I did before, that those who practice such things will not inherit the kingdom of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.22', 'BSB', 'But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.23', 'BSB', 'gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.24', 'BSB', 'Those who belong to Christ Jesus have crucified the flesh with its passions and desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.25', 'BSB', 'Since we live by the Spirit, let us walk in step with the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.5.26', 'BSB', 'Let us not become conceited, provoking and envying one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.1', 'BSB', 'Brothers, if someone is caught in a trespass, you who are spiritual should restore him with a spirit of gentleness. But watch yourself, or you also may be tempted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.2', 'BSB', 'Carry one another’s burdens, and in this way you will fulfill the law of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.3', 'BSB', 'If anyone thinks he is something when he is nothing, he deceives himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.4', 'BSB', 'Each one should test his own work. Then he will have reason to boast in himself alone, and not in someone else.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.5', 'BSB', 'For each one should carry his own load.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.6', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, the one who receives instruction in the word must share in all good things with his instructor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.7', 'BSB', 'Do not be deceived: God is not to be mocked. Whatever a man sows, he will reap in return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.8', 'BSB', 'The one who sows to please his flesh, from the flesh will reap destruction; but the one who sows to please the Spirit, from the Spirit will reap eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.9', 'BSB', 'Let us not grow weary in well-doing, for in due time we will reap a harvest if we do not give up.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as we have opportunity, let us do good to everyone, and especially to the family of faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.11', 'BSB', 'See what large letters I am using to write to you with my own hand!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.12', 'BSB', 'Those who want to make a good impression outwardly are trying to compel you to be circumcised. They only do this to avoid persecution for the cross of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.13', 'BSB', 'For the circumcised do not even keep the law themselves, yet they want you to be circumcised that they may boast in your flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.14', 'BSB', 'But as for me, may I never boast, except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.15', 'BSB', 'For neither circumcision nor uncircumcision means anything. What counts is a new creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.16', 'BSB', 'Peace and mercy to all who walk by this rule, even to the Israel of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.17', 'BSB', 'From now on let no one cause me trouble, for I bear on my body the marks of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Gal.6.18', 'BSB', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, To the saints in Ephesus, the faithful in Christ Jesus:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.2', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.3', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly realms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.4', 'BSB', 'For He chose us in Him before the foundation of the world to be holy and blameless in His presence. In love', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.5', 'BSB', 'He predestined us for adoption as His sons through Jesus Christ, according to the good pleasure of His will,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.6', 'BSB', 'to the praise of His glorious grace, which He has freely given us in the Beloved One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.7', 'BSB', 'In Him we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of His grace', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.8', 'BSB', 'that He lavished on us with all wisdom and understanding.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.9', 'BSB', 'And He has made known to us the mystery of His will according to His good pleasure, which He purposed in Christ', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.10', 'BSB', 'as a plan for the fullness of time, to bring all things in heaven and on earth together in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.11', 'BSB', 'In Him we were also chosen as God’s own, having been predestined according to the plan of Him who works out everything by the counsel of His will,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.12', 'BSB', 'in order that we, who were the first to hope in Christ, would be for the praise of His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.13', 'BSB', 'And in Him, having heard and believed the word of truth—the gospel of your salvation—you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.14', 'BSB', 'who is the pledge of our inheritance until the redemption of those who are God’s possession, to the praise of His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.15', 'BSB', 'For this reason, ever since I heard about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.16', 'BSB', 'I have not stopped giving thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.17', 'BSB', 'that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in your knowledge of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.18', 'BSB', 'I ask that the eyes of your heart may be enlightened, so that you may know the hope of His calling, the riches of His glorious inheritance in the saints,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.19', 'BSB', 'and the surpassing greatness of His power to us who believe. These are in accordance with the working of His mighty strength,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.20', 'BSB', 'which He exerted in Christ when He raised Him from the dead and seated Him at His right hand in the heavenly realms,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.21', 'BSB', 'far above all rule and authority, power and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in the present age but also in the one to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.22', 'BSB', 'And God put everything under His feet and made Him head over everything for the church,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.1.23', 'BSB', 'which is His body, the fullness of Him who fills all in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.1', 'BSB', 'And you were dead in your trespasses and sins,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.2', 'BSB', 'in which you used to walk when you conformed to the ways of this world and of the ruler of the power of the air, the spirit who is now at work in the sons of disobedience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.3', 'BSB', 'All of us also lived among them at one time, fulfilling the cravings of our flesh and indulging its desires and thoughts. Like the rest, we were by nature children of wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.4', 'BSB', 'But because of His great love for us, God, who is rich in mercy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.5', 'BSB', 'made us alive with Christ even when we were dead in our trespasses. It is by grace you have been saved!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.6', 'BSB', 'And God raised us up with Christ and seated us with Him in the heavenly realms in Christ Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.7', 'BSB', 'in order that in the coming ages He might display the surpassing riches of His grace, demonstrated by His kindness to us in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.8', 'BSB', 'For it is by grace you have been saved through faith, and this not from yourselves; it is the gift of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.9', 'BSB', 'not by works, so that no one can boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.10', 'BSB', 'For we are God’s workmanship, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance as our way of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore remember that formerly you who are Gentiles in the flesh and called uncircumcised by the so-called circumcision (that done in the body by human hands)—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.12', 'BSB', 'remember that at that time you were separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers to the covenants of the promise, without hope and without God in the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.13', 'BSB', 'But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far away have been brought near through the blood of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.14', 'BSB', 'For He Himself is our peace, who has made the two one and has torn down the dividing wall of hostility', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.15', 'BSB', 'by abolishing in His flesh the law of commandments and decrees. He did this to create in Himself one new man out of the two, thus making peace', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.16', 'BSB', 'and reconciling both of them to God in one body through the cross, by which He extinguished their hostility.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.17', 'BSB', 'He came and preached peace to you who were far away and peace to those who were near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.18', 'BSB', 'For through Him we both have access to the Father by one Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but fellow citizens with the saints and members of God’s household,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.20', 'BSB', 'built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, with Christ Jesus Himself as the cornerstone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.21', 'BSB', 'In Him the whole building is fitted together and grows into a holy temple in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.2.22', 'BSB', 'And in Him you too are being built together into a dwelling place for God in His Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.1', 'BSB', 'For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus for the sake of you Gentiles...', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.2', 'BSB', 'Surely you have heard about the stewardship of God’s grace that was given to me for you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.3', 'BSB', 'that is, the mystery made known to me by revelation, as I have already written briefly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.4', 'BSB', 'In reading this, then, you will be able to understand my insight into the mystery of Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.5', 'BSB', 'which was not made known to men in other generations as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to God’s holy apostles and prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.6', 'BSB', 'This mystery is that through the gospel the Gentiles are fellow heirs, fellow members of the body, and fellow partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.7', 'BSB', 'I became a servant of this gospel by the gift of God’s grace, given me through the working of His power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.8', 'BSB', 'Though I am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given me: to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.9', 'BSB', 'and to illuminate for everyone the stewardship of this mystery, which for ages past was kept hidden in God, who created all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.10', 'BSB', 'His purpose was that now, through the church, the manifold wisdom of God should be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.11', 'BSB', 'according to the eternal purpose that He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.12', 'BSB', 'In Him and through faith in Him we may enter God’s presence with boldness and confidence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.13', 'BSB', 'So I ask you not to be discouraged because of my sufferings for you, which are your glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.14', 'BSB', '... for this reason I bow my knees before the Father,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.15', 'BSB', 'from whom every family in heaven and on earth derives its name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.16', 'BSB', 'I ask that out of the riches of His glory He may strengthen you with power through His Spirit in your inner being,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.17', 'BSB', 'so that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith. Then you, being rooted and grounded in love,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.18', 'BSB', 'will have power, together with all the saints, to comprehend the length and width and height and depth', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.19', 'BSB', 'of the love of Christ, and to know this love that surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.20', 'BSB', 'Now to Him who is able to do so much more than all we ask or imagine, according to His power that is at work within us,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.3.21', 'BSB', 'to Him be the glory in the church and in Christ Jesus throughout all generations, forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.1', 'BSB', 'As a prisoner in the Lord, then, I urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling you have received:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.2', 'BSB', 'with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.3', 'BSB', 'and with diligence to preserve the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.4', 'BSB', 'There is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope when you were called;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.5', 'BSB', 'one Lord, one faith, one baptism;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.6', 'BSB', 'one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.7', 'BSB', 'Now to each one of us grace has been given according to the measure of the gift of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.8', 'BSB', 'This is why it says: “When He ascended on high, He led captives away, and gave gifts to men.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.9', 'BSB', 'What does “He ascended” mean, except that He also descended to the lower parts of the earth?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.10', 'BSB', 'He who descended is the very One who ascended above all the heavens, in order to fill all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.11', 'BSB', 'And it was He who gave some to be apostles, some to be prophets, some to be evangelists, and some to be pastors and teachers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.12', 'BSB', 'to equip the saints for works of ministry and to build up the body of Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.13', 'BSB', 'until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, as we mature to the full measure of the stature of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.14', 'BSB', 'Then we will no longer be infants, tossed about by the waves and carried around by every wind of teaching and by the clever cunning of men in their deceitful scheming.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.15', 'BSB', 'Instead, speaking the truth in love, we will in all things grow up into Christ Himself, who is the head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.16', 'BSB', 'From Him the whole body, fitted and held together by every supporting ligament, grows and builds itself up in love through the work of each individual part.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.17', 'BSB', 'So I tell you this, and insist on it in the Lord, that you must no longer walk as the Gentiles do, in the futility of their thinking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.18', 'BSB', 'They are darkened in their understanding and alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them due to the hardness of their hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.19', 'BSB', 'Having lost all sense of shame, they have given themselves over to sensuality for the practice of every kind of impurity, with a craving for more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.20', 'BSB', 'But this is not the way you came to know Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.21', 'BSB', 'Surely you heard of Him and were taught in Him—in keeping with the truth that is in Jesus—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.22', 'BSB', 'to put off your former way of life, your old self, which is being corrupted by its deceitful desires;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.23', 'BSB', 'to be renewed in the spirit of your minds;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.24', 'BSB', 'and to put on the new self, created to be like God in true righteousness and holiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore each of you must put off falsehood and speak truthfully to his neighbor, for we are all members of one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.26', 'BSB', '“Be angry, yet do not sin.” Do not let the sun set upon your anger,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.27', 'BSB', 'and do not give the devil a foothold.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.28', 'BSB', 'He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with his own hands, that he may have something to share with the one in need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.29', 'BSB', 'Let no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the one in need and bringing grace to those who listen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.30', 'BSB', 'And do not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you were sealed for the day of redemption.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.31', 'BSB', 'Get rid of all bitterness, rage and anger, outcry and slander, along with every form of malice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.4.32', 'BSB', 'Be kind and tenderhearted to one another, forgiving each other just as in Christ God forgave you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.1', 'BSB', 'Be imitators of God, therefore, as beloved children,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.2', 'BSB', 'and walk in love, just as Christ loved us and gave Himself up for us as a fragrant sacrificial offering to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.3', 'BSB', 'But among you, as is proper among the saints, there must not be even a hint of sexual immorality, or of any kind of impurity, or of greed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.4', 'BSB', 'Nor should there be obscenity, foolish talk, or crude joking, which are out of character, but rather thanksgiving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.5', 'BSB', 'For of this you can be sure: No immoral, impure, or greedy person (that is, an idolater), has any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.6', 'BSB', 'Let no one deceive you with empty words, for because of such things the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore do not be partakers with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.8', 'BSB', 'For you were once darkness, but now you are light in the Lord. Walk as children of light,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.9', 'BSB', 'for the fruit of the light consists in all goodness, righteousness, and truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.10', 'BSB', 'Test and prove what pleases the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.11', 'BSB', 'Have no fellowship with the fruitless deeds of darkness, but rather expose them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.12', 'BSB', 'For it is shameful even to mention what the disobedient do in secret.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.13', 'BSB', 'But everything exposed by the light becomes visible, for everything that is illuminated becomes a light itself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.14', 'BSB', 'So it is said: “Wake up, O sleeper, rise up from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.15', 'BSB', 'Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.16', 'BSB', 'redeeming the time, because the days are evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lord’s will is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.18', 'BSB', 'Do not get drunk on wine, which leads to reckless indiscretion. Instead, be filled with the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.19', 'BSB', 'Speak to one another with psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs. Sing and make music in your hearts to the Lord,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.20', 'BSB', 'always giving thanks to God the Father for everything in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.21', 'BSB', 'Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.22', 'BSB', 'Wives, submit to your husbands as to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.23', 'BSB', 'For the husband is the head of the wife as Christ is the head of the church, His body, of which He is the Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.24', 'BSB', 'Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives should submit to their husbands in everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.25', 'BSB', 'Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.26', 'BSB', 'to sanctify her, cleansing her by the washing with water through the word,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.27', 'BSB', 'and to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such blemish, but holy and blameless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.28', 'BSB', 'In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.29', 'BSB', 'Indeed, no one ever hated his own body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ does the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.30', 'BSB', 'For we are members of His body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.31', 'BSB', '“For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.32', 'BSB', 'This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.5.33', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as he loves himself, and the wife must respect her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.1', 'BSB', 'Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.2', 'BSB', '“Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise),', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.3', 'BSB', '“that it may go well with you and that you may have a long life on the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.4', 'BSB', 'Fathers, do not provoke your children to wrath; instead, bring them up in the discipline and instruction of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.5', 'BSB', 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters with respect and fear and sincerity of heart, just as you would obey Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.6', 'BSB', 'And do this not only to please them while they are watching, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from your heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.7', 'BSB', 'Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.8', 'BSB', 'because you know that the Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether he is slave or free.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.9', 'BSB', 'And masters, do the same for your slaves. Give up your use of threats, because you know that He who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.10', 'BSB', 'Finally, be strong in the Lord and in His mighty power.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.11', 'BSB', 'Put on the full armor of God, so that you can make your stand against the devil’s schemes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.12', 'BSB', 'For our struggle is not against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the powers of this world’s darkness, and against the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenly realms.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore take up the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil comes, you will be able to stand your ground, and having done everything, to stand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.14', 'BSB', 'Stand firm then, with the belt of truth buckled around your waist, with the breastplate of righteousness arrayed,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.15', 'BSB', 'and with your feet fitted with the readiness of the gospel of peace.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.16', 'BSB', 'In addition to all this, take up the shield of faith, with which you can extinguish all the flaming arrows of the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.17', 'BSB', 'And take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.18', 'BSB', 'Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.19', 'BSB', 'Pray also for me, that whenever I open my mouth, words may be given me so that I will boldly make known the mystery of the gospel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.20', 'BSB', 'for which I am an ambassador in chains. Pray that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.21', 'BSB', 'Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will tell you everything, so that you also may know about me and what I am doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.22', 'BSB', 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.23', 'BSB', 'Peace to the brothers and love with faith from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Eph.6.24', 'BSB', 'Grace to all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus, To all the saints in Christ Jesus at Philippi, together with the overseers and deacons:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.2', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.3', 'BSB', 'I thank my God every time I remember you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.4', 'BSB', 'In every prayer for all of you, I always pray with joy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.5', 'BSB', 'because of your partnership in the gospel from the first day until now,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.6', 'BSB', 'being confident of this, that He who began a good work in you will carry it on to completion until the day of Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.7', 'BSB', 'It is right for me to feel this way about all of you, since I have you in my heart. For in my chains and in my defense and confirmation of the gospel, you are all partners in grace with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.8', 'BSB', 'God is my witness how I long for all of you with the affection of Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.9', 'BSB', 'And this is my prayer: that your love may abound more and more in knowledge and depth of insight,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.10', 'BSB', 'so that you may be able to test and prove what is best and may be pure and blameless for the day of Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.11', 'BSB', 'filled with the fruit of righteousness that comes through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.12', 'BSB', 'Now I want you to know, brothers, that my circumstances have actually served to advance the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.13', 'BSB', 'As a result, it has become clear throughout the whole palace guard and to everyone else that I am in chains for Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.14', 'BSB', 'And most of the brothers, confident in the Lord by my chains, now dare more greatly to speak the word without fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.15', 'BSB', 'It is true that some preach Christ out of envy and rivalry, but others out of goodwill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.16', 'BSB', 'The latter do so in love, knowing that I am appointed for the defense of the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.17', 'BSB', 'The former, however, preach Christ out of selfish ambition, not sincerely, supposing that they can add to the distress of my chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.18', 'BSB', 'What then is the issue? Just this: that in every way, whether by false motives or true, Christ is preached. And in this I rejoice. Yes, and I will continue to rejoice,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.19', 'BSB', 'because I know that through your prayers and the provision of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, my distress will turn out for my deliverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.20', 'BSB', 'I eagerly expect and hope that I will in no way be ashamed, but will have complete boldness so that now as always Christ will be exalted in my body, whether by life or by death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.21', 'BSB', 'For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.22', 'BSB', 'But if I go on living in the body, this will mean fruitful labor for me. So what shall I choose? I do not know.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.23', 'BSB', 'I am torn between the two. I desire to depart and be with Christ, which is far better indeed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.24', 'BSB', 'But it is more necessary for you that I remain in the body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.25', 'BSB', 'Convinced of this, I know that I will remain and will continue with all of you for your progress and joy in the faith,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.26', 'BSB', 'so that through my coming to you again your exultation in Christ Jesus will resound on account of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.27', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, conduct yourselves in a manner worthy of the gospel of Christ. Then, whether I come and see you or only hear about you in my absence, I will know that you stand firm in one spirit, contending side by side for the faith of the gospel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.28', 'BSB', 'without being frightened in any way by those who oppose you. This is a clear sign of their destruction but of your salvation, and it is from God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.29', 'BSB', 'For it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer for Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.1.30', 'BSB', 'since you are encountering the same struggle you saw I had, and now hear that I still have.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore if you have any encouragement in Christ, if any comfort from His love, if any fellowship with the Spirit, if any affection and compassion,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.2', 'BSB', 'then make my joy complete by being like-minded, having the same love, being united in spirit and purpose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.3', 'BSB', 'Do nothing out of selfish ambition or empty pride, but in humility consider others more important than yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.4', 'BSB', 'Each of you should look not only to your own interests, but also to the interests of others.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.5', 'BSB', 'Let this mind be in you which was also in Christ Jesus:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.6', 'BSB', 'Who, existing in the form of God, did not consider equality with God something to be grasped,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.7', 'BSB', 'but emptied Himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in human likeness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.8', 'BSB', 'And being found in appearance as a man, He humbled Himself and became obedient to death— even death on a cross.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.9', 'BSB', 'Therefore God exalted Him to the highest place and gave Him the name above all names,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.10', 'BSB', 'that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, in heaven and on earth and under the earth,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.11', 'BSB', 'and every tongue confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, my beloved, just as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but now even more in my absence, continue to work out your salvation with fear and trembling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.13', 'BSB', 'For it is God who works in you to will and to act on behalf of His good purpose.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.14', 'BSB', 'Do everything without complaining or arguing,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.15', 'BSB', 'so that you may be blameless and pure, children of God without fault in a crooked and perverse generation, in which you shine as lights in the world', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.16', 'BSB', 'as you hold forth the word of life, in order that I may boast on the day of Christ that I did not run or labor in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.17', 'BSB', 'But even if I am being poured out like a drink offering on the sacrifice and service of your faith, I am glad and rejoice with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.18', 'BSB', 'So you too should be glad and rejoice with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.19', 'BSB', 'Now I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, that I also may be cheered when I learn how you are doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.20', 'BSB', 'I have nobody else like him who will genuinely care for your needs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.21', 'BSB', 'For all the others look after their own interests, not those of Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.22', 'BSB', 'But you know Timothy’s proven worth, that as a child with his father he has served with me to advance the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.23', 'BSB', 'So I hope to send him as soon as I see what happens with me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.24', 'BSB', 'And I trust in the Lord that I myself will come soon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.25', 'BSB', 'But I thought it necessary to send back to you Epaphroditus, my brother, fellow worker, and fellow soldier, who is also your messenger and minister to my needs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.26', 'BSB', 'For he has been longing for all of you and is distressed because you heard he was ill.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.27', 'BSB', 'He was sick indeed, nearly unto death. But God had mercy on him, and not only on him but also on me, to spare me sorrow upon sorrow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore I am all the more eager to send him, so that when you see him again you may rejoice, and I may be less anxious.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.29', 'BSB', 'Welcome him in the Lord with great joy, and honor men like him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.2.30', 'BSB', 'because he nearly died for the work of Christ, risking his life to make up for your deficit of service to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.1', 'BSB', 'Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord. It is no trouble for me to write the same things to you again, and it is a safeguard for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.2', 'BSB', 'Watch out for those dogs, those workers of evil, those mutilators of the flesh!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.3', 'BSB', 'For it is we who are the circumcision, we who worship by the Spirit of God, who glory in Christ Jesus, and who put no confidence in the flesh—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.4', 'BSB', 'though I myself could have such confidence. If anyone else thinks he has grounds for confidence in the flesh, I have more:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.5', 'BSB', 'circumcised on the eighth day, of the people of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin; a Hebrew of Hebrews; as to the law, a Pharisee;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.6', 'BSB', 'as to zeal, persecuting the church; as to righteousness in the law, faultless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.7', 'BSB', 'But whatever was gain to me I count as loss for the sake of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.8', 'BSB', 'More than that, I count all things as loss compared to the surpassing excellence of knowing Christ Jesus my Lord, for whom I have lost all things. I consider them rubbish, that I may gain Christ', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.9', 'BSB', 'and be found in Him, not having my own righteousness from the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness from God on the basis of faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.10', 'BSB', 'I want to know Christ and the power of His resurrection and the fellowship of His sufferings, being conformed to Him in His death,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.11', 'BSB', 'and so, somehow, to attain to the resurrection from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.12', 'BSB', 'Not that I have already obtained all this, or have already been made perfect, but I press on to take hold of that for which Christ Jesus took hold of me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.13', 'BSB', 'Brothers, I do not consider myself yet to have taken hold of it. But one thing I do: Forgetting what is behind and straining toward what is ahead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.14', 'BSB', 'I press on toward the goal to win the prize of God’s heavenly calling in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.15', 'BSB', 'All of us who are mature should embrace this point of view. And if you think differently about some issue, God will reveal this to you as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.16', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, we must live up to what we have already attained.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.17', 'BSB', 'Join one another in following my example, brothers, and carefully observe those who walk according to the pattern we set for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.18', 'BSB', 'For as I have often told you before, and now say again even with tears: Many live as enemies of the cross of Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.19', 'BSB', 'Their end is destruction, their god is their belly, and their glory is in their shame. Their minds are set on earthly things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.20', 'BSB', 'But our citizenship is in heaven, and we eagerly await a Savior from there, the Lord Jesus Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.3.21', 'BSB', 'who, by the power that enables Him to subject all things to Himself, will transform our lowly bodies to be like His glorious body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, my brothers, whom I love and long for, my joy and crown, that is how you must stand firm in the Lord, my beloved.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.2', 'BSB', 'I urge Euodia and Syntyche to agree with each other in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.3', 'BSB', 'Yes, and I ask you, my true yokefellow, to help these women who have labored with me for the gospel, along with Clement and the rest of my fellow workers, whose names are in the Book of Life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.4', 'BSB', 'Rejoice in the Lord always. I will say it again: Rejoice!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.5', 'BSB', 'Let your gentleness be apparent to all. The Lord is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.6', 'BSB', 'Be anxious for nothing, but in everything, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.7', 'BSB', 'And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.8', 'BSB', 'Finally, brothers, whatever is true, whatever is honorable, whatever is right, whatever is pure, whatever is lovely, whatever is admirable—if anything is excellent or praiseworthy—think on these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.9', 'BSB', 'Whatever you have learned or received or heard from me, or seen in me, put it into practice. And the God of peace will be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.10', 'BSB', 'Now I rejoice greatly in the Lord that at last you have revived your concern for me. You were indeed concerned, but you had no opportunity to show it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.11', 'BSB', 'I am not saying this out of need, for I have learned to be content regardless of my circumstances.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.12', 'BSB', 'I know how to live humbly, and I know how to abound. I am accustomed to any and every situation—to being filled and being hungry, to having plenty and having need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.13', 'BSB', 'I can do all things through Christ who gives me strength.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.14', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, you have done well to share in my affliction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.15', 'BSB', 'And as you Philippians know, in the early days of the gospel, when I left Macedonia, no church but you partnered with me in the matter of giving and receiving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.16', 'BSB', 'For even while I was in Thessalonica, you provided for my needs again and again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.17', 'BSB', 'Not that I am seeking a gift, but I am looking for the fruit that may be credited to your account.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.18', 'BSB', 'I have all I need and more, now that I have received your gifts from Epaphroditus. They are a fragrant offering, an acceptable sacrifice, well-pleasing to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.19', 'BSB', 'And my God will supply all your needs according to His glorious riches in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.20', 'BSB', 'To our God and Father be glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.21', 'BSB', 'Greet all the saints in Christ Jesus. The brothers who are with me send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.22', 'BSB', 'All the saints send you greetings, especially those from the household of Caesar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phil.4.23', 'BSB', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and Timothy our brother,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.2', 'BSB', 'To the saints and faithful brothers in Christ at Colossae: Grace and peace to you from God our Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.3', 'BSB', 'We always thank God, the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, when we pray for you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.4', 'BSB', 'because we have heard about your faith in Christ Jesus and your love for all the saints—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.5', 'BSB', 'the faith and love proceeding from the hope stored up for you in heaven, of which you have already heard in the word of truth, the gospel', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.6', 'BSB', 'that has come to you. All over the world this gospel is bearing fruit and growing, just as it has been doing among you since the day you heard it and truly understood the grace of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.7', 'BSB', 'You learned it from Epaphras, our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our behalf,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.8', 'BSB', 'and who also informed us of your love in the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.9', 'BSB', 'For this reason, since the day we heard about you, we have not stopped praying for you and asking God to fill you with the knowledge of His will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.10', 'BSB', 'so that you may walk in a manner worthy of the Lord and may please Him in every way: bearing fruit in every good work, growing in the knowledge of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.11', 'BSB', 'being strengthened with all power according to His glorious might so that you may have full endurance and patience, and joyfully', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.12', 'BSB', 'giving thanks to the Father, who has qualified you to share in the inheritance of the saints in the light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.13', 'BSB', 'He has rescued us from the dominion of darkness and brought us into the kingdom of His beloved Son,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.14', 'BSB', 'in whom we have redemption, the forgiveness of sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.15', 'BSB', 'The Son is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.16', 'BSB', 'For in Him all things were created, things in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or authorities. All things were created through Him and for Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.17', 'BSB', 'He is before all things, and in Him all things hold together.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.18', 'BSB', 'And He is the head of the body, the church; He is the beginning and firstborn from among the dead, so that in all things He may have preeminence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.19', 'BSB', 'For God was pleased to have all His fullness dwell in Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.20', 'BSB', 'and through Him to reconcile to Himself all things, whether things on earth or things in heaven, by making peace through the blood of His cross.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.21', 'BSB', 'Once you were alienated from God and were hostile in your minds, engaging in evil deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.22', 'BSB', 'But now He has reconciled you by Christ’s physical body through death to present you holy, unblemished, and blameless in His presence—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.23', 'BSB', 'if indeed you continue in your faith, established and firm, not moved from the hope of the gospel you heard, which has been proclaimed to every creature under heaven, and of which I, Paul, have become a servant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.24', 'BSB', 'Now I rejoice in my sufferings for you, and I fill up in my flesh what is lacking in regard to Christ’s afflictions for the sake of His body, which is the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.25', 'BSB', 'I became its servant by the commission God gave me to fully proclaim to you the word of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.26', 'BSB', 'the mystery that was hidden for ages and generations but is now revealed to His saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.27', 'BSB', 'To them God has chosen to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.28', 'BSB', 'We proclaim Him, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone perfect in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.1.29', 'BSB', 'To this end I also labor, striving with all His energy working powerfully within me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.1', 'BSB', 'For I want you to know how much I am struggling for you and for those at Laodicea, and for all who have not met me face to face,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.2', 'BSB', 'that they may be encouraged in heart, knit together in love, and filled with the full riches of complete understanding, so that they may know the mystery of God, namely Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.3', 'BSB', 'in whom are hidden all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.4', 'BSB', 'I say this so that no one will deceive you by smooth rhetoric.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.5', 'BSB', 'For although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I delight to see your orderly condition and firm faith in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.6', 'BSB', 'Therefore, just as you have received Christ Jesus as Lord, continue to walk in Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.7', 'BSB', 'rooted and built up in Him, established in the faith as you were taught, and overflowing with thankfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.8', 'BSB', 'See to it that no one takes you captive through philosophy and empty deception, which are based on human tradition and the spiritual forces of the world rather than on Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.9', 'BSB', 'For in Christ all the fullness of the Deity dwells in bodily form.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.10', 'BSB', 'And you have been made complete in Christ, who is the head over every ruler and authority.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.11', 'BSB', 'In Him you were also circumcised, in the putting off of your sinful nature, with the circumcision performed by Christ and not by human hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.12', 'BSB', 'And having been buried with Him in baptism, you were raised with Him through your faith in the power of God, who raised Him from the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.13', 'BSB', 'When you were dead in your trespasses and in the uncircumcision of your sinful nature, God made you alive with Christ. He forgave us all our trespasses,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.14', 'BSB', 'having canceled the debt ascribed to us in the decrees that stood against us. He took it away, nailing it to the cross!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.15', 'BSB', 'And having disarmed the powers and authorities, He made a public spectacle of them, triumphing over them by the cross.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore let no one judge you by what you eat or drink, or with regard to a feast, a New Moon, or a Sabbath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.17', 'BSB', 'These are a shadow of the things to come, but the body that casts it belongs to Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.18', 'BSB', 'Do not let anyone who delights in false humility and the worship of angels disqualify you with speculation about what he has seen. Such a person is puffed up without basis by his unspiritual mind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.19', 'BSB', 'He has lost connection to the head, from whom the whole body, supported and knit together by its joints and ligaments, grows as God causes it to grow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.20', 'BSB', 'If you have died with Christ to the spiritual forces of the world, why, as though you still belonged to the world, do you submit to its regulations:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.21', 'BSB', '“Do not handle, do not taste, do not touch!”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.22', 'BSB', 'These will all perish with use, because they are based on human commands and teachings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.2.23', 'BSB', 'Such restrictions indeed have an appearance of wisdom, with their self-prescribed worship, their false humility, and their harsh treatment of the body; but they are of no value against the indulgence of the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since you have been raised with Christ, strive for the things above, where Christ is seated at the right hand of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.2', 'BSB', 'Set your minds on things above, not on earthly things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.3', 'BSB', 'For you died, and your life is now hidden with Christ in God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.4', 'BSB', 'When Christ, who is your life, appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.5', 'BSB', 'Put to death, therefore, the components of your earthly nature: sexual immorality, impurity, lust, evil desires, and greed, which is idolatry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.6', 'BSB', 'Because of these, the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.7', 'BSB', 'When you lived among them, you also used to walk in these ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.8', 'BSB', 'But now you must put aside all such things as these: anger, rage, malice, slander, and filthy language from your lips.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.9', 'BSB', 'Do not lie to one another, since you have taken off the old self with its practices,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.10', 'BSB', 'and have put on the new self, which is being renewed in knowledge in the image of its Creator.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.11', 'BSB', 'Here there is no Greek or Jew, circumcised or uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, or free, but Christ is all and is in all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.13', 'BSB', 'Bear with one another and forgive any complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.14', 'BSB', 'And over all these virtues put on love, which is the bond of perfect unity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.15', 'BSB', 'Let the peace of Christ rule in your hearts, for to this you were called as members of one body. And be thankful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.16', 'BSB', 'Let the word of Christ richly dwell within you as you teach and admonish one another with all wisdom, and as you sing psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs with gratitude in your hearts to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.17', 'BSB', 'And whatever you do, in word or deed, do it all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.18', 'BSB', 'Wives, submit to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.19', 'BSB', 'Husbands, love your wives and do not be harsh with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.20', 'BSB', 'Children, obey your parents in everything, for this is pleasing to the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.21', 'BSB', 'Fathers, do not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.22', 'BSB', 'Slaves, obey your earthly masters in everything, not only to please them while they are watching, but with sincerity of heart and fear of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.23', 'BSB', 'Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, for the Lord and not for men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.24', 'BSB', 'because you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as your reward. It is the Lord Christ you are serving.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.3.25', 'BSB', 'Whoever does wrong will be repaid for his wrong, and there is no favoritism.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.1', 'BSB', 'Masters, supply your slaves with what is right and fair, since you know that you also have a Master in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.2', 'BSB', 'Devote yourselves to prayer, being watchful and thankful,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.3', 'BSB', 'as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.4', 'BSB', 'Pray that I may declare it clearly, as I should.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.5', 'BSB', 'Act wisely toward outsiders, redeeming the time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.6', 'BSB', 'Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.7', 'BSB', 'Tychicus will tell you all the news about me. He is a beloved brother, a faithful minister, and a fellow servant in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.8', 'BSB', 'I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.9', 'BSB', 'With him I am sending Onesimus, our faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They will tell you about everything here.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.10', 'BSB', 'My fellow prisoner Aristarchus sends you greetings, as does Mark the cousin of Barnabas. You have already received instructions about him: If he comes to you, welcome him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.11', 'BSB', 'Jesus, who is called Justus, also sends greetings. These are the only Jews among my fellow workers for the kingdom of God, and they have been a comfort to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.12', 'BSB', 'Epaphras, who is one of you and a servant of Christ Jesus, sends you greetings. He is always wrestling in prayer for you, so that you may stand mature and fully assured in the full will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.13', 'BSB', 'For I testify about him that he goes to great pains for you and for those at Laodicea and Hierapolis.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.14', 'BSB', 'Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.15', 'BSB', 'Greet the brothers in Laodicea, as well as Nympha and the church that meets at her house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.16', 'BSB', 'After this letter has been read among you, make sure that it is also read in the church of the Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the letter from Laodicea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.17', 'BSB', 'Tell Archippus: “See to it that you complete the ministry you have received in the Lord.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Col.4.18', 'BSB', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. Remember my chains. Grace be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace and peace to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.2', 'BSB', 'We always thank God for all of you, remembering you in our prayers', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.3', 'BSB', 'and continually recalling before our God and Father your work of faith, your labor of love, and your enduring hope in our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.4', 'BSB', 'Brothers who are beloved by God, we know that He has chosen you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.5', 'BSB', 'because our gospel came to you not only in word, but also in power, in the Holy Spirit, and with great conviction—just as you know we lived among you for your sake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.6', 'BSB', 'And you became imitators of us and of the Lord when you welcomed the message with the joy of the Holy Spirit, in spite of your great suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.7', 'BSB', 'As a result, you have become an example to all the believers in Macedonia and Achaia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.8', 'BSB', 'For not only did the message of the Lord ring out from you to Macedonia and Achaia, but your faith in God has gone out to every place, so that we have no need to say anything more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.9', 'BSB', 'For they themselves report what kind of welcome you gave us, and how you turned to God from idols to serve the living and true God', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.1.10', 'BSB', 'and to await His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead—Jesus our deliverer from the coming wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.1', 'BSB', 'You yourselves know, brothers, that our visit to you was not in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.2', 'BSB', 'As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.3', 'BSB', 'For our appeal does not arise from deceit or ulterior motives or trickery.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.4', 'BSB', 'Instead, we speak as those approved by God to be entrusted with the gospel, not in order to please men but God, who examines our hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.5', 'BSB', 'As you know, we never used words of flattery or any pretext for greed. God is our witness!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.6', 'BSB', 'Nor did we seek praise from you or from anyone else, although as apostles of Christ we had authority to demand it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.7', 'BSB', 'On the contrary, we were gentle among you, like a nursing mother caring for her children.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.8', 'BSB', 'We cared so deeply that we were delighted to share with you not only the gospel of God, but our own lives as well. That is how beloved you have become to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.9', 'BSB', 'Surely you recall, brothers, our labor and toil. We worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to anyone while we proclaimed to you the gospel of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.10', 'BSB', 'You are witnesses, and so is God, of how holy, righteous, and blameless our conduct was among you who believed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.11', 'BSB', 'For you know that we treated each of you as a father treats his own children—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.12', 'BSB', 'encouraging you, comforting you, and urging you to walk in a manner worthy of God, who calls you into His own kingdom and glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.13', 'BSB', 'And we continually thank God because, when you received the word of God that you heard from us, you accepted it not as the word of men, but as the true word of God—the word which is now at work in you who believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.14', 'BSB', 'For you, brothers, became imitators of the churches of God in Judea that are in Christ Jesus. You suffered from your own countrymen the very things they suffered from the Jews,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.15', 'BSB', 'who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets, and drove us out as well. They are displeasing to God and hostile to all men,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.16', 'BSB', 'hindering us from telling the Gentiles how they may be saved. As a result, they continue to heap up their sins to full capacity; the utmost wrath has come upon them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.17', 'BSB', 'Brothers, although we were torn away from you for a short time (in person, not in heart), our desire to see you face to face was even more intense.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.18', 'BSB', 'For we wanted to come to you—indeed I, Paul, tried again and again—but Satan obstructed us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.19', 'BSB', 'After all, who is our hope, our joy, our crown of boasting, if it is not you yourselves in the presence of our Lord Jesus at His coming?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.2.20', 'BSB', 'You are indeed our glory and our joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.1', 'BSB', 'So when we could bear it no longer, we were willing to be left on our own in Athens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.2', 'BSB', 'We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.3', 'BSB', 'so that none of you would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.4', 'BSB', 'Indeed, when we were with you, we kept warning you that we would suffer persecution; and as you know, it has come to pass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.5', 'BSB', 'For this reason, when I could bear it no longer, I sent to find out about your faith, for fear that the tempter had somehow tempted you and caused our labor to be in vain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.6', 'BSB', 'But just now, Timothy has returned from his visit with the good news about your faith, your love, and the fond memories you have preserved, longing to see us just as we long to see you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.7', 'BSB', 'For this reason, brothers, in all our distress and persecution, we have been reassured about you, because of your faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.8', 'BSB', 'For now we can go on living, as long as you are standing firm in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.9', 'BSB', 'How can we adequately thank God for you in return for our great joy over you in His presence?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.10', 'BSB', 'Night and day we pray most earnestly that we may see you face to face and supply what is lacking from your faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.11', 'BSB', 'Now may our God and Father Himself, and our Lord Jesus, direct our way to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.12', 'BSB', 'And may the Lord cause you to increase and overflow with love for one another and for everyone else, just as our love for you overflows,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.3.13', 'BSB', 'so that He may establish your hearts in blamelessness and holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all His saints. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.1', 'BSB', 'Finally, brothers, we ask and encourage you in the Lord Jesus to live in a way that is pleasing to God, just as you have received from us. This is how you already live, so you should do so all the more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.2', 'BSB', 'For you know the instructions we gave you by the authority of the Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.3', 'BSB', 'For it is God’s will that you should be holy: You must abstain from sexual immorality;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.4', 'BSB', 'each of you must know how to control his own body in holiness and honor,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.5', 'BSB', 'not in lustful passion like the Gentiles who do not know God;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.6', 'BSB', 'and no one should ever violate or exploit his brother in this regard, because the Lord will avenge all such acts, as we have already told you and solemnly warned you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.7', 'BSB', 'For God has not called us to impurity, but to holiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.8', 'BSB', 'Anyone, then, who rejects this command does not reject man but God, the very One who gives you His Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.9', 'BSB', 'Now about brotherly love, you do not need anyone to write to you, because you yourselves have been taught by God to love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.10', 'BSB', 'And you are indeed showing this love to all the brothers throughout Macedonia. But we urge you, brothers, to excel more and more', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.11', 'BSB', 'and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own matters, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.12', 'BSB', 'Then you will behave properly toward outsiders, without being dependent on anyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.13', 'BSB', 'Brothers, we do not want you to be uninformed about those who sleep in death, so that you will not grieve like the rest, who are without hope.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.14', 'BSB', 'For since we believe that Jesus died and rose again, we also believe that God will bring with Jesus those who have fallen asleep in Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.15', 'BSB', 'By the word of the Lord, we declare to you that we who are alive and remain until the coming of the Lord will by no means precede those who have fallen asleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.16', 'BSB', 'For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a loud command, with the voice of an archangel, and with the trumpet of God, and the dead in Christ will be the first to rise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.17', 'BSB', 'After that, we who are alive and remain will be caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord in the air. And so we will always be with the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.4.18', 'BSB', 'Therefore encourage one another with these words.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.1', 'BSB', 'Now about the times and seasons, brothers, we do not need to write to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.2', 'BSB', 'For you are fully aware that the Day of the Lord will come like a thief in the night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.3', 'BSB', 'While people are saying, “Peace and security,” destruction will come upon them suddenly, like labor pains on a pregnant woman, and they will not escape.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.4', 'BSB', 'But you, brothers, are not in the darkness so that this day should overtake you like a thief.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.5', 'BSB', 'For you are all sons of the light and sons of the day; we do not belong to the night or to the darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.6', 'BSB', 'So then, let us not sleep as the others do, but let us remain awake and sober.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.7', 'BSB', 'For those who sleep, sleep at night; and those who get drunk, get drunk at night.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.8', 'BSB', 'But since we belong to the day, let us be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love, and the helmet of our hope of salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.9', 'BSB', 'For God has not appointed us to suffer wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.10', 'BSB', 'He died for us so that, whether we are awake or asleep, we may live together with Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.11', 'BSB', 'Therefore encourage and build one another up, just as you are already doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.12', 'BSB', 'But we ask you, brothers, to acknowledge those who work diligently among you, who preside over you in the Lord and give you instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.13', 'BSB', 'In love, hold them in highest regard because of their work. Live in peace with one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.14', 'BSB', 'And we urge you, brothers, to admonish the unruly, encourage the fainthearted, help the weak, and be patient with everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.15', 'BSB', 'Make sure that no one repays evil for evil. Always pursue what is good for one another and for all people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.16', 'BSB', 'Rejoice at all times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.17', 'BSB', 'Pray without ceasing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.18', 'BSB', 'Give thanks in every circumstance, for this is God’s will for you in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.19', 'BSB', 'Do not extinguish the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.20', 'BSB', 'Do not treat prophecies with contempt,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.21', 'BSB', 'but test all things. Hold fast to what is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.22', 'BSB', 'Abstain from every form of evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.23', 'BSB', 'Now may the God of peace Himself sanctify you completely, and may your entire spirit, soul, and body be kept blameless at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.24', 'BSB', 'The One who calls you is faithful, and He will do it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.25', 'BSB', 'Brothers, pray for us as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.26', 'BSB', 'Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.27', 'BSB', 'I charge you before the Lord to have this letter read to all the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Thess.5.28', 'BSB', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.2', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.3', 'BSB', 'We are obligated to thank God for you all the time, brothers, as is fitting, because your faith is growing more and more, and your love for one another is increasing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.4', 'BSB', 'That is why we boast among God’s churches about your perseverance and faith in the face of all the persecution and affliction you are enduring.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.5', 'BSB', 'All this is clear evidence of God’s righteous judgment. And so you will be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.6', 'BSB', 'After all, it is only right for God to repay with affliction those who afflict you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.7', 'BSB', 'and to grant relief to you who are oppressed and to us as well. This will take place when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with His mighty angels', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.8', 'BSB', 'in blazing fire, inflicting vengeance on those who do not know God and do not obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.9', 'BSB', 'They will suffer the penalty of eternal destruction, separated from the presence of the Lord and the glory of His might,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.10', 'BSB', 'on the day He comes to be glorified in His saints and regarded with wonder by all who have believed, including you who have believed our testimony.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.11', 'BSB', 'To this end, we always pray for you, that our God will count you worthy of His calling, and that He will powerfully fulfill your every good desire and work of faith,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.1.12', 'BSB', 'so that the name of our Lord Jesus will be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.1', 'BSB', 'Now concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our being gathered together to Him, we ask you, brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.2', 'BSB', 'not to be easily disconcerted or alarmed by any spirit or message or letter seeming to be from us, alleging that the Day of the Lord has already come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.3', 'BSB', 'Let no one deceive you in any way, for it will not come until the rebellion occurs and the man of lawlessness—the son of destruction—is revealed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.4', 'BSB', 'He will oppose and exalt himself above every so-called god or object of worship. So he will seat himself in the temple of God, proclaiming himself to be God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.5', 'BSB', 'Do you not remember that I told you these things while I was still with you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.6', 'BSB', 'And you know what is now restraining him, so that he may be revealed at the proper time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.7', 'BSB', 'For the mystery of lawlessness is already at work, but the one who now restrains it will continue until he is taken out of the way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.8', 'BSB', 'And then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus will slay with the breath of His mouth and annihilate by the majesty of His arrival.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.9', 'BSB', 'The coming of the lawless one will be accompanied by the working of Satan, with every kind of power, sign, and false wonder,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.10', 'BSB', 'and with every wicked deception directed against those who are perishing, because they refused the love of the truth that would have saved them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.11', 'BSB', 'For this reason God will send them a powerful delusion so that they believe the lie,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.12', 'BSB', 'in order that judgment may come upon all who have disbelieved the truth and delighted in wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.13', 'BSB', 'But we should always thank God for you, brothers who are loved by the Lord, because God has chosen you from the beginning to be saved by the sanctification of the Spirit and by faith in the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.14', 'BSB', 'To this He called you through our gospel, so that you may share in the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, stand firm and cling to the traditions we taught you, whether by speech or by letter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.16', 'BSB', 'Now may our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father, who by grace has loved us and given us eternal comfort and good hope,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.2.17', 'BSB', 'encourage your hearts and strengthen you in every good word and deed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.1', 'BSB', 'Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may spread quickly and be held in honor, just as it was with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.2', 'BSB', 'And pray that we may be delivered from wicked and evil men; for not everyone holds to the faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.3', 'BSB', 'But the Lord is faithful, and He will strengthen you and guard you from the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.4', 'BSB', 'And we have confidence in the Lord that you are doing and will continue to do what we command.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.5', 'BSB', 'May the Lord direct your hearts into God’s love and Christ’s perseverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.6', 'BSB', 'Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to keep away from any brother who leads an undisciplined life that is not in keeping with the tradition you received from us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.7', 'BSB', 'For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, because we were not undisciplined among you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.8', 'BSB', 'nor did we eat anyone’s food without paying for it. Instead, in labor and toil, we worked night and day so that we would not be a burden to any of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.9', 'BSB', 'Not that we lack this right, but we wanted to offer ourselves as an example for you to imitate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.10', 'BSB', 'For even while we were with you, we gave you this command: “If anyone is unwilling to work, he shall not eat.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.11', 'BSB', 'Yet we hear that some of you are leading undisciplined lives and accomplishing nothing but being busybodies.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.12', 'BSB', 'We command and urge such people by our Lord Jesus Christ to begin working quietly to earn their own living.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.13', 'BSB', 'But as for you, brothers, do not grow weary in well-doing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.14', 'BSB', 'Take note of anyone who does not obey the instructions we have given in this letter. Do not associate with him, so that he may be ashamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.15', 'BSB', 'Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but warn him as a brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.16', 'BSB', 'Now may the Lord of peace Himself give you peace at all times and in every way. The Lord be with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.17', 'BSB', 'This greeting is in my own hand—Paul. This is my mark in every letter; it is the way I write.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Thess.3.18', 'BSB', 'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the command of God our Savior and of Christ Jesus our hope,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.2', 'BSB', 'To Timothy, my true child in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.3', 'BSB', 'As I urged you on my departure to Macedonia, you should stay on at Ephesus to instruct certain men not to teach false doctrines', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.4', 'BSB', 'or devote themselves to myths and endless genealogies, which promote speculation rather than the stewardship of God’s work, which is by faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.5', 'BSB', 'The goal of our instruction is the love that comes from a pure heart, a clear conscience, and a sincere faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.6', 'BSB', 'Some have strayed from these ways and turned aside to empty talk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.7', 'BSB', 'They want to be teachers of the law, but they do not understand what they are saying or that which they so confidently assert.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.8', 'BSB', 'Now we know that the law is good, if one uses it legitimately.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.9', 'BSB', 'We realize that law is not enacted for the righteous, but for the lawless and rebellious, for the ungodly and sinful, for the unholy and profane, for killers of father or mother, for murderers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.10', 'BSB', 'for the sexually immoral, for homosexuals, for slave traders and liars and perjurers, and for anyone else who is averse to sound teaching', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.11', 'BSB', 'that agrees with the glorious gospel of the blessed God, with which I have been entrusted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.12', 'BSB', 'I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has strengthened me, that He considered me faithful and appointed me to service.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.13', 'BSB', 'I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and a violent man; yet because I had acted in ignorance and unbelief, I was shown mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.14', 'BSB', 'And the grace of our Lord overflowed to me, along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.15', 'BSB', 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am the worst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.16', 'BSB', 'But for this very reason I was shown mercy, so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His perfect patience as an example to those who would believe in Him for eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.17', 'BSB', 'Now to the King eternal, immortal, and invisible, the only God, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.18', 'BSB', 'Timothy, my child, I entrust you with this command in keeping with the previous prophecies about you, so that by them you may fight the good fight,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.19', 'BSB', 'holding on to faith and a good conscience, which some have rejected and thereby shipwrecked their faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.1.20', 'BSB', 'Among them are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I have handed over to Satan to be taught not to blaspheme.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.1', 'BSB', 'First of all, then, I urge that petitions, prayers, intercessions, and thanksgiving be offered for everyone—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.2', 'BSB', 'for kings and all those in authority—so that we may lead tranquil and quiet lives in all godliness and dignity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.3', 'BSB', 'This is good and pleasing in the sight of God our Savior,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.4', 'BSB', 'who wants everyone to be saved and to come to the knowledge of the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.5', 'BSB', 'For there is one God, and there is one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.6', 'BSB', 'who gave Himself as a ransom for all—the testimony that was given at just the right time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.7', 'BSB', 'For this reason I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a faithful and true teacher of the Gentiles. I am telling the truth; I am not lying about anything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore I want the men everywhere to pray, lifting up holy hands, without anger or dissension.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.9', 'BSB', 'Likewise, I want the women to adorn themselves with respectable apparel, with modesty, and with self-control, not with braided hair or gold or pearls or expensive clothes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.10', 'BSB', 'but with good deeds, as is proper for women who profess to worship God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.11', 'BSB', 'A woman must learn in quietness and full submissiveness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.12', 'BSB', 'I do not permit a woman to teach or to exercise authority over a man; she is to remain quiet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.13', 'BSB', 'For Adam was formed first, and then Eve.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.14', 'BSB', 'And it was not Adam who was deceived, but the woman who was deceived and fell into transgression.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.2.15', 'BSB', 'Women, however, will be saved through childbearing, if they continue in faith, love, and holiness, with self-control.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.1', 'BSB', 'This is a trustworthy saying: If anyone aspires to be an overseer, he desires a noble task.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.2', 'BSB', 'An overseer, then, must be above reproach, the husband of but one wife, temperate, self-controlled, respectable, hospitable, able to teach,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.3', 'BSB', 'not dependent on wine, not violent but gentle, peaceable, and free of the love of money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.4', 'BSB', 'An overseer must manage his own household well and keep his children under control, with complete dignity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.5', 'BSB', 'For if someone does not know how to manage his own household, how can he care for the church of God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.6', 'BSB', 'He must not be a recent convert, or he may become conceited and fall under the same condemnation as the devil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.7', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, he must have a good reputation with outsiders, so that he will not fall into disgrace and into the snare of the devil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.8', 'BSB', 'Deacons likewise must be dignified, not double-tongued or given to much wine or greedy for money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.9', 'BSB', 'They must hold to the mystery of the faith with a clear conscience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.10', 'BSB', 'Additionally, they must first be tested. Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.11', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.12', 'BSB', 'A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.13', 'BSB', 'For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.14', 'BSB', 'Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.15', 'BSB', 'in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.3.16', 'BSB', 'By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great: He appeared in the flesh, was vindicated by the Spirit, was seen by angels, was proclaimed among the nations, was believed in throughout the world, was taken up in glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.1', 'BSB', 'Now the Spirit expressly states that in later times some will abandon the faith to follow deceitful spirits and the teachings of demons,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.2', 'BSB', 'influenced by the hypocrisy of liars, whose consciences are seared with a hot iron.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.3', 'BSB', 'They will prohibit marriage and require abstinence from certain foods that God has created to be received with thanksgiving by those who believe and know the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.4', 'BSB', 'For every creation of God is good, and nothing that is received with thanksgiving should be rejected,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.5', 'BSB', 'because it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.6', 'BSB', 'By pointing out these things to the brothers, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, nourished by the words of faith and sound instruction that you have followed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.7', 'BSB', 'But reject irreverent, silly myths. Instead, train yourself for godliness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.8', 'BSB', 'For physical exercise is of limited value, but godliness is valuable in every way, holding promise for the present life and for the one to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.9', 'BSB', 'This is a trustworthy saying, worthy of full acceptance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.10', 'BSB', 'To this end we labor and strive, because we have set our hope on the living God, who is the Savior of everyone, and especially of those who believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.11', 'BSB', 'Command and teach these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.12', 'BSB', 'Let no one despise your youth, but set an example for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith, in purity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.13', 'BSB', 'Until I come, devote yourself to the public reading of Scripture, to exhortation, and to teaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.14', 'BSB', 'Do not neglect the gift that is in you, which was given you through the prophecy spoken over you at the laying on of the hands of the elders.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.15', 'BSB', 'Be diligent in these matters and absorbed in them, so that your progress will be evident to all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.4.16', 'BSB', 'Pay close attention to your life and to your teaching. Persevere in these things, for by so doing you will save both yourself and those who hear you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.1', 'BSB', 'Do not rebuke an older man, but appeal to him as to a father. Treat younger men as brothers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.2', 'BSB', 'older women as mothers, and younger women as sisters, with absolute purity.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.3', 'BSB', 'Honor the widows who are truly widows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.4', 'BSB', 'But if a widow has children or grandchildren, they must first learn to show godliness to their own family and repay their parents, for this is pleasing in the sight of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.5', 'BSB', 'The widow who is truly in need and left all alone puts her hope in God and continues night and day in her petitions and prayers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.6', 'BSB', 'But she who lives for pleasure is dead even while she is still alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.7', 'BSB', 'Give these instructions to the believers, so that they will be above reproach.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.8', 'BSB', 'If anyone does not provide for his own, and especially his own household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.9', 'BSB', 'A widow should be enrolled if she is at least sixty years old, the wife of one man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.10', 'BSB', 'and well known for good deeds such as bringing up children, entertaining strangers, washing the feet of the saints, imparting relief to the afflicted, and devoting herself to every good work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.11', 'BSB', 'But refuse to enroll younger widows. For when their passions draw them away from Christ, they will want to marry,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.12', 'BSB', 'and thus will incur judgment because they are setting aside their first faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.13', 'BSB', 'At the same time they will also learn to be idle, going from house to house and being not only idle, but also gossips and busybodies, discussing things they should not mention.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.14', 'BSB', 'So I advise the younger widows to marry, have children, and manage their households, denying the adversary occasion for slander.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.15', 'BSB', 'For some have already turned aside to follow Satan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.16', 'BSB', 'If any believing woman has dependent widows, she must assist them and not allow the church to be burdened, so that it can help the widows who are truly in need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.17', 'BSB', 'Elders who lead effectively are worthy of double honor, especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.18', 'BSB', 'For the Scripture says, “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain,” and, “The worker is worthy of his wages.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.19', 'BSB', 'Do not entertain an accusation against an elder, except on the testimony of two or three witnesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.20', 'BSB', 'But those who persist in sin should be rebuked in front of everyone, so that the others will stand in fear of sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.21', 'BSB', 'I solemnly charge you before God and Christ Jesus and the elect angels to maintain these principles without bias, and to do nothing out of partiality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.22', 'BSB', 'Do not be too quick in the laying on of hands and thereby share in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.23', 'BSB', 'Stop drinking only water and use a little wine instead, because of your stomach and your frequent ailments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.24', 'BSB', 'The sins of some men are obvious, going ahead of them to judgment; but the sins of others do not surface until later.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.5.25', 'BSB', 'In the same way, good deeds are obvious, and even the ones that are inconspicuous cannot remain hidden.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.1', 'BSB', 'All who are under the yoke of slavery should regard their masters as fully worthy of honor, so that God’s name and our teaching will not be discredited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.2', 'BSB', 'Those who have believing masters should not show disrespect because they are brothers, but should serve them all the more, since those receiving their good service are beloved believers. Teach and encourage these principles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.3', 'BSB', 'If anyone teaches another doctrine and disagrees with the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ and with godly teaching,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.4', 'BSB', 'he is conceited and understands nothing. Instead, he has an unhealthy interest in controversies and semantics, out of which come envy, strife, abusive talk, evil suspicions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.5', 'BSB', 'and constant friction between men of depraved mind who are devoid of the truth. These men regard godliness as a means of gain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.6', 'BSB', 'Of course, godliness with contentment is great gain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.7', 'BSB', 'For we brought nothing into the world, so we cannot carry anything out of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.8', 'BSB', 'But if we have food and clothing, we will be content with these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.9', 'BSB', 'Those who want to be rich, however, fall into temptation and become ensnared by many foolish and harmful desires that plunge them into ruin and destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.10', 'BSB', 'For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil. By craving it, some have wandered away from the faith and pierced themselves with many sorrows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.11', 'BSB', 'But you, O man of God, flee from these things and pursue righteousness, godliness, faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.12', 'BSB', 'Fight the good fight of the faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you were called when you made the good confession before many witnesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.13', 'BSB', 'I charge you in the presence of God, who gives life to all things, and of Christ Jesus, who made the good confession in His testimony before Pontius Pilate:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.14', 'BSB', 'Keep this commandment without stain or reproach until the appearance of our Lord Jesus Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.15', 'BSB', 'which the blessed and only Sovereign One—the King of kings and Lord of lords—will bring about in His own time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.16', 'BSB', 'He alone is immortal and dwells in unapproachable light. No one has ever seen Him, nor can anyone see Him. To Him be honor and eternal dominion! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.17', 'BSB', 'Instruct those who are rich in the present age not to be conceited and not to put their hope in the uncertainty of wealth, but in God, who richly provides all things for us to enjoy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.18', 'BSB', 'Instruct them to do good, to be rich in good works, and to be generous and ready to share,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.19', 'BSB', 'treasuring up for themselves a firm foundation for the future, so that they may take hold of that which is truly life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.20', 'BSB', 'O Timothy, guard what has been entrusted to you. Avoid irreverent, empty chatter and the opposing arguments of so-called “knowledge,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Tim.6.21', 'BSB', 'which some have professed and thus swerved away from the faith. Grace be with you all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by the will of God, according to the promise of life in Christ Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.2', 'BSB', 'To Timothy, my beloved child: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.3', 'BSB', 'I thank God, whom I serve with a clear conscience as did my forefathers, as I constantly remember you night and day in my prayers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.4', 'BSB', 'Recalling your tears, I long to see you so that I may be filled with joy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.5', 'BSB', 'I am reminded of your sincere faith, which first dwelt in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced is in you as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.6', 'BSB', 'For this reason I remind you to fan into flame the gift of God, which is in you through the laying on of my hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.7', 'BSB', 'For God has not given us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.8', 'BSB', 'So do not be ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, or of me, His prisoner. Instead, join me in suffering for the gospel by the power of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.9', 'BSB', 'He has saved us and called us to a holy calling, not because of our works, but by His own purpose and by the grace He granted us in Christ Jesus before time began.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.10', 'BSB', 'And now He has revealed this grace through the appearing of our Savior, Christ Jesus, who has abolished death and illuminated the way to life and immortality through the gospel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.11', 'BSB', 'to which I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.12', 'BSB', 'For this reason, even though I suffer as I do, I am not ashamed; for I know whom I have believed, and I am convinced that He is able to guard what I have entrusted to Him for that day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.13', 'BSB', 'Hold on to the pattern of sound teaching you have heard from me, with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.14', 'BSB', 'Guard the treasure entrusted to you, with the help of the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.15', 'BSB', 'You know that everyone in the Province of Asia has deserted me, including Phygelus and Hermogenes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.16', 'BSB', 'May the Lord grant mercy to the household of Onesiphorus, because he has often refreshed me and was unashamed of my chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.17', 'BSB', 'Indeed, when he arrived in Rome, he searched diligently until he found me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.1.18', 'BSB', 'May the Lord grant Onesiphorus His mercy on that day. You know very well how much he ministered to me in Ephesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.1', 'BSB', 'You therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.2', 'BSB', 'And the things that you have heard me say among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.3', 'BSB', 'Join me in suffering, like a good soldier of Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.4', 'BSB', 'A soldier refrains from entangling himself in civilian affairs, in order to please the one who enlisted him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.5', 'BSB', 'Likewise, a competitor does not receive the crown unless he competes according to the rules.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.6', 'BSB', 'The hardworking farmer should be the first to partake of the crops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.7', 'BSB', 'Consider what I am saying, for the Lord will give you insight into all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.8', 'BSB', 'Remember Jesus Christ, raised from the dead, descended from David, as proclaimed by my gospel,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.9', 'BSB', 'for which I suffer to the extent of being chained like a criminal. But the word of God cannot be chained!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.10', 'BSB', 'For this reason I endure all things for the sake of the elect, so that they too may obtain the salvation that is in Christ Jesus, with eternal glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.11', 'BSB', 'This is a trustworthy saying: If we died with Him, we will also live with Him;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.12', 'BSB', 'if we endure, we will also reign with Him; if we deny Him, He will also deny us;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.13', 'BSB', 'if we are faithless, He remains faithful, for He cannot deny Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.14', 'BSB', 'Remind the believers of these things, charging them before God to avoid quarreling over words, which succeeds only in leading the listeners to ruin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.15', 'BSB', 'Make every effort to present yourself approved to God, an unashamed workman who accurately handles the word of truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.16', 'BSB', 'But avoid irreverent, empty chatter, which will only lead to more ungodliness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.17', 'BSB', 'and the talk of such men will spread like gangrene. Among them are Hymenaeus and Philetus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.18', 'BSB', 'who have deviated from the truth. They say that the resurrection has already occurred, and they undermine the faith of some.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.19', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, God’s firm foundation stands, bearing this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord must turn away from iniquity.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.20', 'BSB', 'A large house contains not only vessels of gold and silver, but also of wood and clay. Some indeed are for honorable use, but others are for common use.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.21', 'BSB', 'So if anyone cleanses himself of what is unfit, he will be a vessel for honor: sanctified, useful to the Master, and prepared for every good work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.22', 'BSB', 'Flee from youthful passions and pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace, together with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.23', 'BSB', 'But reject foolish and ignorant speculation, for you know that it breeds quarreling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.24', 'BSB', 'And a servant of the Lord must not be quarrelsome, but must be kind to everyone, able to teach, and forbearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.25', 'BSB', 'He must gently reprove those who oppose him, in the hope that God may grant them repentance leading to a knowledge of the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.2.26', 'BSB', 'Then they will come to their senses and escape the snare of the devil, who has taken them captive to his will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.1', 'BSB', 'But understand this: In the last days terrible times will come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.2', 'BSB', 'For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, abusive, disobedient to their parents, ungrateful, unholy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.3', 'BSB', 'unloving, unforgiving, slanderous, without self-control, brutal, without love of good,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.4', 'BSB', 'traitorous, reckless, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.5', 'BSB', 'having a form of godliness but denying its power. Turn away from such as these!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.6', 'BSB', 'They are the kind who worm their way into households and captivate vulnerable women who are weighed down with sins and led astray by various passions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.7', 'BSB', 'who are always learning but never able to come to a knowledge of the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.8', 'BSB', 'Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so also these men oppose the truth. They are depraved in mind and disqualified from the faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.9', 'BSB', 'But they will not advance much further. For just like Jannes and Jambres, their folly will be plain to everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.10', 'BSB', 'You, however, have observed my teaching, my conduct, my purpose, my faith, my patience, my love, my perseverance,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.11', 'BSB', 'my persecutions, and the sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all of them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.12', 'BSB', 'Indeed, all who desire to live godly lives in Christ Jesus will be persecuted,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.13', 'BSB', 'while evil men and imposters go from bad to worse, deceiving and being deceived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.14', 'BSB', 'But as for you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.15', 'BSB', 'From infancy you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Christ Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.16', 'BSB', 'All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, and for training in righteousness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.3.17', 'BSB', 'so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.1', 'BSB', 'I charge you in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus, who will judge the living and the dead, and in view of His appearing and His kingdom:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.2', 'BSB', 'Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and encourage with every form of patient instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.3', 'BSB', 'For the time will come when men will not tolerate sound doctrine, but with itching ears they will gather around themselves teachers to suit their own desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.4', 'BSB', 'So they will turn their ears away from the truth and turn aside to myths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.5', 'BSB', 'But you, be sober in all things, endure hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfill your ministry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.6', 'BSB', 'For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.7', 'BSB', 'I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.8', 'BSB', 'From now on there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will award to me on that day—and not only to me, but to all who crave His appearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.9', 'BSB', 'Make every effort to come to me quickly,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.10', 'BSB', 'because Demas, in his love of this world, has deserted me and gone to Thessalonica. Crescens has gone to Galatia, and Titus to Dalmatia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.11', 'BSB', 'Only Luke is with me. Get Mark and bring him with you, because he is useful to me in the ministry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.12', 'BSB', 'Tychicus, however, I have sent to Ephesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.13', 'BSB', 'When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, and my scrolls, especially the parchments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.14', 'BSB', 'Alexander the coppersmith did great harm to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.15', 'BSB', 'You too should beware of him, for he has vigorously opposed our message.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.16', 'BSB', 'At my first defense, no one stood with me, but everyone deserted me. May it not be charged against them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.17', 'BSB', 'But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, so that through me the message would be fully proclaimed, and all the Gentiles would hear it. So I was delivered from the mouth of the lion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.18', 'BSB', 'And the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.19', 'BSB', 'Greet Prisca and Aquila, as well as the household of Onesiphorus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.20', 'BSB', 'Erastus has remained at Corinth, and Trophimus I left sick in Miletus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.21', 'BSB', 'Make every effort to come to me before winter. Eubulus sends you greetings, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Tim.4.22', 'BSB', 'The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, a servant of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ for the faith of God’s elect and their knowledge of the truth that leads to godliness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.2', 'BSB', 'in the hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before time began.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.3', 'BSB', 'In His own time He has made His word evident in the proclamation entrusted to me by the command of God our Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.4', 'BSB', 'To Titus, my true child in our common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.5', 'BSB', 'The reason I left you in Crete was that you would set in order what was unfinished and appoint elders in every town, as I directed you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.6', 'BSB', 'An elder must be blameless, the husband of but one wife, having children who are believers and who are not open to accusation of indiscretion or insubordination.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.7', 'BSB', 'As God’s steward, an overseer must be above reproach—not self-absorbed, not quick-tempered, not given to drunkenness, not violent, not greedy for money.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.8', 'BSB', 'Instead, he must be hospitable, a lover of good, self-controlled, upright, holy, and disciplined.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.9', 'BSB', 'He must hold firmly to the faithful word as it was taught, so that he can encourage others by sound teaching and refute those who contradict it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.10', 'BSB', 'For many are rebellious and full of empty talk and deception, especially those of the circumcision,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.11', 'BSB', 'who must be silenced. For the sake of dishonorable gain, they undermine entire households and teach things they should not.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.12', 'BSB', 'As one of their own prophets has said, “Cretans are always liars, evil beasts, lazy gluttons.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.13', 'BSB', 'This testimony is true. Therefore rebuke them sternly, so that they will be sound in the faith', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.14', 'BSB', 'and will pay no attention to Jewish myths or to the commands of men who have rejected the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.15', 'BSB', 'To the pure, all things are pure; but to the defiled and unbelieving, nothing is pure. Indeed, both their minds and their consciences are defiled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.1.16', 'BSB', 'They profess to know God, but by their actions they deny Him. They are detestable, disobedient, and unfit for any good deed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.1', 'BSB', 'But as for you, speak the things that are consistent with sound doctrine.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.2', 'BSB', 'Older men are to be temperate, dignified, self-controlled, and sound in faith, love, and perseverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.3', 'BSB', 'Older women, likewise, are to be reverent in their behavior, not slanderers or addicted to much wine, but teachers of good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.4', 'BSB', 'In this way they can train the young women to love their husbands and children,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.5', 'BSB', 'to be self-controlled, pure, managers of their households, kind, and submissive to their own husbands, so that the word of God will not be discredited.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.6', 'BSB', 'In the same way, urge the younger men to be self-controlled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.7', 'BSB', 'In everything, show yourself to be an example by doing good works. In your teaching show integrity, dignity,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.8', 'BSB', 'and wholesome speech that is above reproach, so that anyone who opposes us will be ashamed to have nothing bad to say about us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.9', 'BSB', 'Slaves are to submit to their own masters in everything, to be well-pleasing, not argumentative,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.10', 'BSB', 'not stealing from them, but showing all good faith, so that in every respect they will adorn the teaching about God our Savior.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.11', 'BSB', 'For the grace of God has appeared, bringing salvation to everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.12', 'BSB', 'It instructs us to renounce ungodliness and worldly passions, and to live sensible, upright, and godly lives in the present age,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.13', 'BSB', 'as we await the blessed hope and glorious appearance of our great God and Savior Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.14', 'BSB', 'He gave Himself for us to redeem us from all lawlessness and to purify for Himself a people for His own possession, zealous for good deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.2.15', 'BSB', 'Speak these things as you encourage and rebuke with all authority. Let no one despise you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.1', 'BSB', 'Remind the believers to submit to rulers and authorities, to be obedient and ready for every good work,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.2', 'BSB', 'to malign no one, and to be peaceable and gentle, showing full consideration to everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.3', 'BSB', 'For at one time we too were foolish, disobedient, misled, and enslaved to all sorts of desires and pleasures—living in malice and envy, being hated and hating one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.4', 'BSB', 'But when the kindness of God our Savior and His love for mankind appeared,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.5', 'BSB', 'He saved us, not by the righteous deeds we had done, but according to His mercy, through the washing of new birth and renewal by the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.6', 'BSB', 'This is the Spirit He poured out on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Savior,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.7', 'BSB', 'so that, having been justified by His grace, we would become heirs with the hope of eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.8', 'BSB', 'This saying is trustworthy. And I want you to emphasize these things, so that those who have believed God will take care to devote themselves to good deeds. These things are excellent and profitable for the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.9', 'BSB', 'But avoid foolish controversies, genealogies, arguments, and quarrels about the law, because these things are pointless and worthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.10', 'BSB', 'Reject a divisive man after a first and second admonition,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.11', 'BSB', 'knowing that such a man is corrupt and sinful; he is self-condemned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.12', 'BSB', 'As soon as I send Artemas or Tychicus to you, make every effort to come to me at Nicopolis, because I have decided to winter there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.13', 'BSB', 'Do your best to equip Zenas the lawyer and Apollos, so that they will have everything they need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.14', 'BSB', 'And our people must also learn to devote themselves to good works in order to meet the pressing needs of others, so that they will not be unfruitful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Titus.3.15', 'BSB', 'All who are with me send you greetings. Greet those who love us in the faith. Grace be with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.1', 'BSB', 'Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved fellow worker,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.2', 'BSB', 'to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.3', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.4', 'BSB', 'I always thank my God, remembering you in my prayers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.5', 'BSB', 'because I hear about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.6', 'BSB', 'I pray that your partnership in the faith may become effective as you fully acknowledge every good thing that is ours in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.7', 'BSB', 'I take great joy and encouragement in your love, because you, brother, have refreshed the hearts of the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.8', 'BSB', 'So although in Christ I am bold enough to order you to do what is proper,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.9', 'BSB', 'I prefer to appeal on the basis of love. For I, Paul, am now aged, and a prisoner of Christ Jesus as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.10', 'BSB', 'I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.11', 'BSB', 'Formerly he was useless to you, but now he has become useful both to you and to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.12', 'BSB', 'I am sending back to you him who is my very heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.13', 'BSB', 'I would have liked to keep him with me, so that on your behalf he could minister to me in my chains for the gospel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.14', 'BSB', 'But I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness will not be out of compulsion, but by your own free will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.15', 'BSB', 'For perhaps this is why he was separated from you for a while, so that you might have him back for good—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.16', 'BSB', 'no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.17', 'BSB', 'So if you consider me a partner, receive him as you would receive me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.18', 'BSB', 'But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to my account.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.19', 'BSB', 'I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it—not to mention that you owe me your very self.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.20', 'BSB', 'Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.21', 'BSB', 'Confident of your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even more than I ask.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.22', 'BSB', 'In the meantime, prepare a guest room for me, because I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.23', 'BSB', 'Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.24', 'BSB', 'as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Phlm.1.25', 'BSB', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.1', 'BSB', 'On many past occasions and in many different ways, God spoke to our fathers through the prophets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.2', 'BSB', 'But in these last days He has spoken to us by His Son, whom He appointed heir of all things, and through whom He made the universe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.3', 'BSB', 'The Son is the radiance of God’s glory and the exact representation of His nature, upholding all things by His powerful word. After He had provided purification for sins, He sat down at the right hand of the Majesty on high.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.4', 'BSB', 'So He became as far superior to the angels as the name He has inherited is excellent beyond theirs.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.5', 'BSB', 'For to which of the angels did God ever say: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father”? Or again: “I will be His Father, and He will be My Son”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.6', 'BSB', 'And again, when God brings His firstborn into the world, He says: “Let all God’s angels worship Him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.7', 'BSB', 'Now about the angels He says: “He makes His angels winds, His servants flames of fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.8', 'BSB', 'But about the Son He says: “Your throne, O God, endures forever and ever, and justice is the scepter of Your kingdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.9', 'BSB', 'You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; therefore God, Your God, has anointed You above Your companions with the oil of joy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.10', 'BSB', 'And: “In the beginning, O Lord, You laid the foundations of the earth, and the heavens are the work of Your hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.11', 'BSB', 'They will perish, but You remain; they will all wear out like a garment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.12', 'BSB', 'You will roll them up like a robe; like a garment they will be changed; but You remain the same, and Your years will never end.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.13', 'BSB', 'Yet to which of the angels did God ever say: “Sit at My right hand until I make Your enemies a footstool for Your feet”?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.1.14', 'BSB', 'Are not the angels ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.1', 'BSB', 'We must pay closer attention, therefore, to what we have heard, so that we do not drift away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.2', 'BSB', 'For if the message spoken by angels was binding, and every transgression and disobedience received its just punishment,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.3', 'BSB', 'how shall we escape if we neglect such a great salvation? This salvation was first announced by the Lord, was confirmed to us by those who heard Him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.4', 'BSB', 'and was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and gifts of the Holy Spirit distributed according to His will.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.5', 'BSB', 'For it is not to angels that He has subjected the world to come, about which we are speaking.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.6', 'BSB', 'But somewhere it is testified in these words: “What is man that You are mindful of him, or the son of man that You care for him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.7', 'BSB', 'You made him a little lower than the angels; You crowned him with glory and honor', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.8', 'BSB', 'and placed everything under his feet.” When God subjected all things to him, He left nothing outside of his control. Yet at present we do not see everything subject to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.9', 'BSB', 'But we see Jesus, who was made a little lower than the angels, now crowned with glory and honor because He suffered death, so that by the grace of God He might taste death for everyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.10', 'BSB', 'In bringing many sons to glory, it was fitting for God, for whom and through whom all things exist, to make the author of their salvation perfect through suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.11', 'BSB', 'For both the One who sanctifies and those who are sanctified are of the same family. So Jesus is not ashamed to call them brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.12', 'BSB', 'He says: “I will proclaim Your name to My brothers; I will sing Your praises in the assembly.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.13', 'BSB', 'And again: “I will put My trust in Him.” And once again: “Here am I, and the children God has given Me.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.14', 'BSB', 'Now since the children have flesh and blood, He too shared in their humanity, so that by His death He might destroy him who holds the power of death, that is, the devil,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.15', 'BSB', 'and free those who all their lives were held in slavery by their fear of death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.16', 'BSB', 'For surely it is not the angels He helps, but the descendants of Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.17', 'BSB', 'For this reason He had to be made like His brothers in every way, so that He might become a merciful and faithful high priest in service to God, in order to make atonement for the sins of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.2.18', 'BSB', 'Because He Himself suffered when He was tempted, He is able to help those who are being tempted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, holy brothers, who share in the heavenly calling, set your focus on Jesus, the apostle and high priest whom we confess.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.2', 'BSB', 'He was faithful to the One who appointed Him, just as Moses was faithful in all God’s house.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.3', 'BSB', 'For Jesus has been counted worthy of greater glory than Moses, just as the builder of a house has greater honor than the house itself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.4', 'BSB', 'And every house is built by someone, but God is the builder of everything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.5', 'BSB', 'Now Moses was faithful as a servant in all God’s house, testifying to what would be spoken later.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.6', 'BSB', 'But Christ is faithful as the Son over God’s house. And we are His house, if we hold firmly to our confidence and the hope of which we boast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.7', 'BSB', 'Therefore, as the Holy Spirit says: “Today, if you hear His voice,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.8', 'BSB', 'do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion, in the day of testing in the wilderness,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.9', 'BSB', 'where your fathers tested and tried Me, and for forty years saw My works.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore I was angry with that generation, and I said, ‘Their hearts are always going astray, and they have not known My ways.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.11', 'BSB', 'So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.12', 'BSB', 'See to it, brothers, that none of you has a wicked heart of unbelief that turns away from the living God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.13', 'BSB', 'But exhort one another daily, as long as it is called today, so that none of you may be hardened by sin’s deceitfulness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.14', 'BSB', 'We have come to share in Christ if we hold firmly to the end the assurance we had at first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.15', 'BSB', 'As it has been said: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts, as you did in the rebellion.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.16', 'BSB', 'For who were the ones who heard and rebelled? Were they not all those Moses led out of Egypt?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.17', 'BSB', 'And with whom was God angry for forty years? Was it not with those who sinned, whose bodies fell in the wilderness?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.18', 'BSB', 'And to whom did He swear that they would never enter His rest? Was it not to those who disobeyed?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.3.19', 'BSB', 'So we see that it was because of their unbelief that they were unable to enter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, while the promise of entering His rest still stands, let us be careful that none of you be deemed to have fallen short of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.2', 'BSB', 'For we also received the good news just as they did; but the message they heard was of no value to them, since they did not share the faith of those who comprehended it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.3', 'BSB', 'Now we who have believed enter that rest. As for the others, it is just as God has said: “So I swore on oath in My anger, ‘They shall never enter My rest.’” And yet His works have been finished since the foundation of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.4', 'BSB', 'For somewhere He has spoken about the seventh day in this manner: “And on the seventh day God rested from all His works.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.5', 'BSB', 'And again, as He says in the passage above: “They shall never enter My rest.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.6', 'BSB', 'Since, then, it remains for some to enter His rest, and since those who formerly heard the good news did not enter because of their disobedience,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.7', 'BSB', 'God again designated a certain day as “Today,” when a long time later He spoke through David as was just stated: “Today, if you hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.8', 'BSB', 'For if Joshua had given them rest, God would not have spoken later about another day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.9', 'BSB', 'There remains, then, a Sabbath rest for the people of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.10', 'BSB', 'For whoever enters God’s rest also rests from his own work, just as God did from His.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.11', 'BSB', 'Let us, therefore, make every effort to enter that rest, so that no one will fall by following the same pattern of disobedience.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.12', 'BSB', 'For the word of God is living and active. Sharper than any double-edged sword, it pierces even to dividing soul and spirit, joints and marrow. It judges the thoughts and intentions of the heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.13', 'BSB', 'Nothing in all creation is hidden from God’s sight; everything is uncovered and exposed before the eyes of Him to whom we must give account.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we have a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold firmly to what we profess.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.15', 'BSB', 'For we do not have a high priest who is unable to sympathize with our weaknesses, but we have one who was tempted in every way that we are, yet was without sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.4.16', 'BSB', 'Let us then approach the throne of grace with confidence, so that we may receive mercy and find grace to help us in our time of need.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.1', 'BSB', 'Every high priest is appointed from among men to represent them in matters relating to God, to offer gifts and sacrifices for sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.2', 'BSB', 'He is able to deal gently with those who are ignorant and misguided, since he himself is beset by weakness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.3', 'BSB', 'That is why he is obligated to offer sacrifices for his own sins, as well as for the sins of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.4', 'BSB', 'No one takes this honor upon himself; he must be called by God, just as Aaron was.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.5', 'BSB', 'So also Christ did not take upon Himself the glory of becoming a high priest, but He was called by the One who said to Him: “You are My Son; today I have become Your Father.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.6', 'BSB', 'And in another passage God says: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.7', 'BSB', 'During the days of Jesus’ earthly life, He offered up prayers and petitions with loud cries and tears to the One who could save Him from death, and He was heard because of His reverence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.8', 'BSB', 'Although He was a Son, He learned obedience from what He suffered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.9', 'BSB', 'And having been made perfect, He became the source of eternal salvation to all who obey Him', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.10', 'BSB', 'and was designated by God as high priest in the order of Melchizedek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.11', 'BSB', 'We have much to say about this, but it is hard to explain, because you are dull of hearing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.12', 'BSB', 'Although by this time you ought to be teachers, you need someone to reteach you the basic principles of God’s word. You need milk, not solid food!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.13', 'BSB', 'For everyone who lives on milk is still an infant, inexperienced in the message of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.5.14', 'BSB', 'But solid food is for the mature, who by constant use have trained their senses to distinguish good from evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore let us leave the elementary teachings about Christ and go on to maturity, not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith in God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.2', 'BSB', 'instruction about baptisms, the laying on of hands, the resurrection of the dead, and eternal judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.3', 'BSB', 'And this we will do, if God permits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.4', 'BSB', 'It is impossible for those who have once been enlightened, who have tasted the heavenly gift, who have shared in the Holy Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.5', 'BSB', 'who have tasted the goodness of the word of God and the powers of the coming age—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.6', 'BSB', 'and then have fallen away—to be restored to repentance, because they themselves are crucifying the Son of God all over again and subjecting Him to open shame.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.7', 'BSB', 'For land that drinks in the rain often falling on it and that produces a crop useful to those for whom it is tended receives the blessing of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.8', 'BSB', 'But land that produces thorns and thistles is worthless, and its curse is imminent. In the end it will be burned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.9', 'BSB', 'Even though we speak like this, beloved, we are convinced of better things in your case—things that accompany salvation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.10', 'BSB', 'For God is not unjust. He will not forget your work and the love you have shown for His name as you have ministered to the saints and continue to do so.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.11', 'BSB', 'We want each of you to show this same diligence to the very end, in order to make your hope sure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.12', 'BSB', 'Then you will not be sluggish, but will imitate those who through faith and patience inherit what has been promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.13', 'BSB', 'When God made His promise to Abraham, since He had no one greater to swear by, He swore by Himself,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.14', 'BSB', 'saying, “I will surely bless you and multiply your descendants.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.15', 'BSB', 'And so Abraham, after waiting patiently, obtained the promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.16', 'BSB', 'Men swear by someone greater than themselves, and their oath serves as a confirmation to end all argument.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.17', 'BSB', 'So when God wanted to make the unchanging nature of His purpose very clear to the heirs of the promise, He guaranteed it with an oath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.18', 'BSB', 'Thus by two unchangeable things in which it is impossible for God to lie, we who have fled to take hold of the hope set before us may be strongly encouraged.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.19', 'BSB', 'We have this hope as an anchor for the soul, firm and secure. It enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.6.20', 'BSB', 'where Jesus our forerunner has entered on our behalf. He has become a high priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.1', 'BSB', 'This Melchizedek was king of Salem and priest of God Most High. He met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.2', 'BSB', 'and Abraham apportioned to him a tenth of everything. First, his name means “king of righteousness.” Then also, “king of Salem” means “king of peace.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.3', 'BSB', 'Without father or mother or genealogy, without beginning of days or end of life, like the Son of God, he remains a priest for all time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.4', 'BSB', 'Consider how great Melchizedek was: Even the patriarch Abraham gave him a tenth of the plunder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.5', 'BSB', 'Now the law commands the sons of Levi who become priests to collect a tenth from the people—that is, from their brothers—though they too are descended from Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.6', 'BSB', 'But Melchizedek, who did not trace his descent from Levi, collected a tenth from Abraham and blessed him who had the promises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.7', 'BSB', 'And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.8', 'BSB', 'In the case of the Levites, mortal men collect the tenth; but in the case of Melchizedek, it is affirmed that he lives on.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.9', 'BSB', 'And so to speak, Levi, who collects the tenth, paid the tenth through Abraham.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.10', 'BSB', 'For when Melchizedek met Abraham, Levi was still in the loin of his ancestor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.11', 'BSB', 'Now if perfection could have been attained through the Levitical priesthood (for on this basis the people received the law), why was there still need for another priest to appear—one in the order of Melchizedek and not in the order of Aaron?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.12', 'BSB', 'For when the priesthood is changed, the law must be changed as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.13', 'BSB', 'He of whom these things are said belonged to a different tribe, from which no one has ever served at the altar.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.14', 'BSB', 'For it is clear that our Lord descended from Judah, a tribe as to which Moses said nothing about priests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.15', 'BSB', 'And this point is even more clear if another priest like Melchizedek appears,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.16', 'BSB', 'one who has become a priest not by a law of succession, but by the power of an indestructible life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.17', 'BSB', 'For it is testified: “You are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.18', 'BSB', 'So the former commandment is set aside because it was weak and useless', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.19', 'BSB', '(for the law made nothing perfect), and a better hope is introduced, by which we draw near to God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.20', 'BSB', 'And none of this happened without an oath. For others became priests without an oath,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.21', 'BSB', 'but Jesus became a priest with an oath by the One who said to Him: “The Lord has sworn and will not change His mind: ‘You are a priest forever.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.22', 'BSB', 'Because of this oath, Jesus has become the guarantee of a better covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.23', 'BSB', 'Now there have been many other priests, since death prevented them from continuing in office.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.24', 'BSB', 'But because Jesus lives forever, He has a permanent priesthood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.25', 'BSB', 'Therefore He is able to save completely those who draw near to God through Him, since He always lives to intercede for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.26', 'BSB', 'Such a high priest truly befits us—One who is holy, innocent, undefiled, set apart from sinners, and exalted above the heavens.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.27', 'BSB', 'Unlike the other high priests, He does not need to offer daily sacrifices, first for His own sins and then for the sins of the people; He sacrificed for sin once for all when He offered up Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.7.28', 'BSB', 'For the law appoints as high priests men who are weak; but the oath, which came after the law, appointed the Son, who has been made perfect forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.1', 'BSB', 'The point of what we are saying is this: We do have such a high priest, who sat down at the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.2', 'BSB', 'and who ministers in the sanctuary and true tabernacle set up by the Lord, not by man.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.3', 'BSB', 'And since every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices, it was necessary for this One also to have something to offer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.4', 'BSB', 'Now if He were on earth, He would not be a priest, since there are already priests who offer gifts according to the law.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.5', 'BSB', 'The place where they serve is a copy and shadow of what is in heaven. This is why Moses was warned when he was about to build the tabernacle: “See to it that you make everything according to the pattern shown you on the mountain.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.6', 'BSB', 'Now, however, Jesus has received a much more excellent ministry, just as the covenant He mediates is better and is founded on better promises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.7', 'BSB', 'For if that first covenant had been without fault, no place would have been sought for a second.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.8', 'BSB', 'But God found fault with the people and said: “Behold, the days are coming, declares the Lord, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.9', 'BSB', 'It will not be like the covenant I made with their fathers when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt, because they did not abide by My covenant, and I disregarded them, declares the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.10', 'BSB', 'For this is the covenant I will make with the house of Israel after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their minds and inscribe them on their hearts. And I will be their God, and they will be My people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.11', 'BSB', 'No longer will each one teach his neighbor or his brother, saying, ‘Know the Lord,’ because they will all know Me, from the least of them to the greatest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.12', 'BSB', 'For I will forgive their iniquities and will remember their sins no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.8.13', 'BSB', 'By speaking of a new covenant, He has made the first one obsolete; and what is obsolete and aging will soon disappear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.1', 'BSB', 'Now the first covenant had regulations for worship and also an earthly sanctuary.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.2', 'BSB', 'A tabernacle was prepared. In its first room were the lampstand, the table, and the consecrated bread. This was called the Holy Place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.3', 'BSB', 'Behind the second curtain was a room called the Most Holy Place,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.4', 'BSB', 'containing the golden altar of incense and the gold-covered ark of the covenant. Inside the ark were the gold jar of manna, Aaron’s staff that had budded, and the stone tablets of the covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.5', 'BSB', 'Above the ark were the cherubim of glory, overshadowing the mercy seat. But we cannot discuss these things in detail now.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.6', 'BSB', 'When everything had been prepared in this way, the priests entered regularly into the first room to perform their sacred duties.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.7', 'BSB', 'But only the high priest entered the second room, and then only once a year, and never without blood, which he offered for himself and for the sins the people had committed in ignorance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.8', 'BSB', 'By this arrangement the Holy Spirit was showing that the way into the Most Holy Place had not yet been disclosed as long as the first tabernacle was still standing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.9', 'BSB', 'It is an illustration for the present time, because the gifts and sacrifices being offered were unable to cleanse the conscience of the worshiper.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.10', 'BSB', 'They consist only in food and drink and special washings—external regulations imposed until the time of reform.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.11', 'BSB', 'But when Christ came as high priest of the good things that have come, He went through the greater and more perfect tabernacle that is not made by hands and is not a part of this creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.12', 'BSB', 'He did not enter by the blood of goats and calves, but He entered the Most Holy Place once for all by His own blood, thus securing eternal redemption.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.13', 'BSB', 'For if the blood of goats and bulls and the ashes of a heifer sprinkled on those who are ceremonially unclean sanctify them so that their bodies are clean,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.14', 'BSB', 'how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered Himself unblemished to God, purify our consciences from works of death, so that we may serve the living God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.15', 'BSB', 'Therefore Christ is the mediator of a new covenant, so that those who are called may receive the promised eternal inheritance, now that He has died to redeem them from the transgressions committed under the first covenant.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.16', 'BSB', 'In the case of a will, it is necessary to establish the death of the one who made it,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.17', 'BSB', 'because a will does not take effect until the one who made it has died; it cannot be executed while he is still alive.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.18', 'BSB', 'That is why even the first covenant was not put into effect without blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.19', 'BSB', 'For when Moses had proclaimed every commandment of the law to all the people, he took the blood of calves and goats, along with water, scarlet wool, and hyssop, and sprinkled the scroll and all the people,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.20', 'BSB', 'saying, “This is the blood of the covenant, which God has commanded you to keep.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.21', 'BSB', 'In the same way, he sprinkled with blood the tabernacle and all the vessels used in worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.22', 'BSB', 'According to the law, in fact, nearly everything must be purified with blood, and without the shedding of blood there is no forgiveness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.23', 'BSB', 'So it was necessary for the copies of the heavenly things to be purified with these sacrifices, but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.24', 'BSB', 'For Christ did not enter a man-made copy of the true sanctuary, but He entered heaven itself, now to appear on our behalf in the presence of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.25', 'BSB', 'Nor did He enter heaven to offer Himself again and again, as the high priest enters the Most Holy Place every year with blood that is not his own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.26', 'BSB', 'Otherwise, Christ would have had to suffer repeatedly since the foundation of the world. But now He has appeared once for all at the end of the ages to do away with sin by the sacrifice of Himself.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.27', 'BSB', 'Just as man is appointed to die once, and after that to face judgment,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.9.28', 'BSB', 'so also Christ was offered once to bear the sins of many; and He will appear a second time, not to bear sin, but to bring salvation to those who eagerly await Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.1', 'BSB', 'For the law is only a shadow of the good things to come, not the realities themselves. It can never, by the same sacrifices offered year after year, make perfect those who draw near to worship.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.2', 'BSB', 'If it could, would not the offerings have ceased? For the worshipers would have been cleansed once for all, and would no longer have felt the guilt of their sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.3', 'BSB', 'Instead, those sacrifices are an annual reminder of sins,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.4', 'BSB', 'because it is impossible for the blood of bulls and goats to take away sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore, when Christ came into the world, He said: “Sacrifice and offering You did not desire, but a body You prepared for Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.6', 'BSB', 'In burnt offerings and sin offerings You took no delight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.7', 'BSB', 'Then I said, ‘Here I am, it is written about Me in the scroll: I have come to do Your will, O God.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.8', 'BSB', 'In the passage above He says, “Sacrifices and offerings, burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not desire, nor did You delight in them” (although they are offered according to the law).', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.9', 'BSB', 'Then He adds, “Here I am, I have come to do Your will.” He takes away the first to establish the second.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.10', 'BSB', 'And by that will, we have been sanctified through the sacrifice of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.11', 'BSB', 'Day after day every priest stands to minister and to offer again and again the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.12', 'BSB', 'But when this Priest had offered for all time one sacrifice for sins, He sat down at the right hand of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.13', 'BSB', 'Since that time, He waits for His enemies to be made a footstool for His feet,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.14', 'BSB', 'because by a single offering He has made perfect for all time those who are being sanctified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.15', 'BSB', 'The Holy Spirit also testifies to us about this. First He says:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.16', 'BSB', '“This is the covenant I will make with them after those days, declares the Lord. I will put My laws in their hearts and inscribe them on their minds.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.17', 'BSB', 'Then He adds: “Their sins and lawless acts I will remember no more.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.18', 'BSB', 'And where these have been forgiven, an offering for sin is no longer needed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, since we have confidence to enter the Most Holy Place by the blood of Jesus,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.20', 'BSB', 'by the new and living way opened for us through the curtain of His body,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.21', 'BSB', 'and since we have a great priest over the house of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.22', 'BSB', 'let us draw near with a sincere heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled to cleanse us from a guilty conscience and our bodies washed with pure water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.23', 'BSB', 'Let us hold resolutely to the hope we profess, for He who promised is faithful.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.24', 'BSB', 'And let us consider how to spur one another on to love and good deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.25', 'BSB', 'Let us not neglect meeting together, as some have made a habit, but let us encourage one another, and all the more as you see the Day approaching.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.26', 'BSB', 'If we deliberately go on sinning after we have received the knowledge of the truth, no further sacrifice for sins remains,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.27', 'BSB', 'but only a fearful expectation of judgment and of raging fire that will consume all adversaries.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.28', 'BSB', 'Anyone who rejected the law of Moses died without mercy on the testimony of two or three witnesses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.29', 'BSB', 'How much more severely do you think one deserves to be punished who has trampled on the Son of God, profaned the blood of the covenant that sanctified him, and insulted the Spirit of grace?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.30', 'BSB', 'For we know Him who said, “Vengeance is Mine; I will repay,” and again, “The Lord will judge His people.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.31', 'BSB', 'It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.32', 'BSB', 'Remember the early days that you were in the light. In those days, you endured a great conflict in the face of suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.33', 'BSB', 'Sometimes you were publicly exposed to ridicule and persecution; at other times you were partners with those who were so treated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.34', 'BSB', 'You sympathized with those in prison and joyfully accepted the confiscation of your property, knowing that you yourselves had a better and permanent possession.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.35', 'BSB', 'So do not throw away your confidence; it holds a great reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.36', 'BSB', 'You need to persevere, so that after you have done the will of God, you will receive what He has promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.37', 'BSB', 'For, “In just a little while, He who is coming will come and will not delay.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.38', 'BSB', 'But My righteous one will live by faith; and if he shrinks back, I will take no pleasure in him.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.10.39', 'BSB', 'But we are not of those who shrink back and are destroyed, but of those who have faith and preserve their souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.1', 'BSB', 'Now faith is the assurance of what we hope for and the certainty of what we do not see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.2', 'BSB', 'This is why the ancients were commended.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.3', 'BSB', 'By faith we understand that the universe was formed at God’s command, so that what is seen was not made out of what was visible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.4', 'BSB', 'By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.5', 'BSB', 'By faith Enoch was taken up so that he did not see death: “He could not be found, because God had taken him away.” For before he was taken, he was commended as one who pleased God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.6', 'BSB', 'And without faith it is impossible to please God, because anyone who approaches Him must believe that He exists and that He rewards those who earnestly seek Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.7', 'BSB', 'By faith Noah, when warned about things not yet seen, in godly fear built an ark to save his family. By faith he condemned the world and became heir of the righteousness that comes by faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.8', 'BSB', 'By faith Abraham, when called to go to a place he would later receive as his inheritance, obeyed and went, without knowing where he was going.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.9', 'BSB', 'By faith he dwelt in the promised land as a stranger in a foreign country. He lived in tents, as did Isaac and Jacob, who were heirs with him of the same promise.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.10', 'BSB', 'For he was looking forward to the city with foundations, whose architect and builder is God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.11', 'BSB', 'By faith Sarah, even though she was barren and beyond the proper age, was enabled to conceive a child, because she considered Him faithful who had promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.12', 'BSB', 'And so from one man, and he as good as dead, came descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky and as countless as the sand on the seashore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.13', 'BSB', 'All these people died in faith, without having received the things they were promised. However, they saw them and welcomed them from afar. And they acknowledged that they were strangers and exiles on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.14', 'BSB', 'Now those who say such things show that they are seeking a country of their own.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.15', 'BSB', 'If they had been thinking of the country they had left, they would have had opportunity to return.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.16', 'BSB', 'Instead, they were longing for a better country, a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed to be called their God, for He has prepared a city for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.17', 'BSB', 'By faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac on the altar. He who had received the promises was ready to offer his one and only son,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.18', 'BSB', 'even though God had said to him, “Through Isaac your offspring will be reckoned.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.19', 'BSB', 'Abraham reasoned that God could raise the dead, and in a sense, he did receive Isaac back from death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.20', 'BSB', 'By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning the future.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.21', 'BSB', 'By faith Jacob, when he was dying, blessed each of Joseph’s sons and worshiped as he leaned on the top of his staff.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.22', 'BSB', 'By faith Joseph, when his end was near, spoke about the exodus of the Israelites and gave instructions about his bones.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.23', 'BSB', 'By faith Moses’ parents hid him for three months after his birth, because they saw that he was a beautiful child, and they were unafraid of the king’s edict.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.24', 'BSB', 'By faith Moses, when he was grown, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh’s daughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.25', 'BSB', 'He chose to suffer oppression with God’s people rather than to experience the fleeting enjoyment of sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.26', 'BSB', 'He valued disgrace for Christ above the treasures of Egypt, for he was looking ahead to his reward.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.27', 'BSB', 'By faith Moses left Egypt, not fearing the king’s anger; he persevered because he saw Him who is invisible.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.28', 'BSB', 'By faith he kept the Passover and the sprinkling of blood, so that the destroyer of the firstborn would not touch Israel’s own firstborn.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.29', 'BSB', 'By faith the people passed through the Red Sea as on dry land; but when the Egyptians tried to follow, they were drowned.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.30', 'BSB', 'By faith the walls of Jericho fell, after the people had marched around them for seven days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.31', 'BSB', 'By faith the prostitute Rahab, because she welcomed the spies in peace, did not perish with those who were disobedient.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.32', 'BSB', 'And what more shall I say? Time will not allow me to tell of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.33', 'BSB', 'who through faith conquered kingdoms, administered justice, and gained what was promised; who shut the mouths of lions,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.34', 'BSB', 'quenched the raging fire, and escaped the edge of the sword; who gained strength from weakness, became mighty in battle, and put foreign armies to flight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.35', 'BSB', 'Women received back their dead, raised to life again. Others were tortured and refused their release, so that they might gain a better resurrection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.36', 'BSB', 'Still others endured mocking and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.37', 'BSB', 'They were stoned, they were sawed in two, they were put to death by the sword. They went around in sheepskins and goatskins, destitute, oppressed, and mistreated.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.38', 'BSB', 'The world was not worthy of them. They wandered in deserts and mountains, and hid in caves and holes in the ground.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.39', 'BSB', 'These were all commended for their faith, yet they did not receive what was promised.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.11.40', 'BSB', 'God had planned something better for us, so that together with us they would be made perfect.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we are surrounded by such a great cloud of witnesses, let us throw off every encumbrance and the sin that so easily entangles, and let us run with endurance the race set out for us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.2', 'BSB', 'Let us fix our eyes on Jesus, the author and perfecter of our faith, who for the joy set before Him endured the cross, scorning its shame, and sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.3', 'BSB', 'Consider Him who endured such hostility from sinners, so that you will not grow weary and lose heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.4', 'BSB', 'In your struggle against sin, you have not yet resisted to the point of shedding your blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.5', 'BSB', 'And you have forgotten the exhortation that addresses you as sons: “My son, do not take lightly the discipline of the Lord, and do not lose heart when He rebukes you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.6', 'BSB', 'For the Lord disciplines the one He loves, and He chastises every son He receives.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.7', 'BSB', 'Endure suffering as discipline; God is treating you as sons. For what son is not disciplined by his father?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.8', 'BSB', 'If you do not experience discipline like everyone else, then you are illegitimate children and not true sons.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.9', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, we have all had earthly fathers who disciplined us, and we respected them. Should we not much more submit to the Father of our spirits and live?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.10', 'BSB', 'Our fathers disciplined us for a short time as they thought best, but God disciplines us for our good, so that we may share in His holiness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.11', 'BSB', 'No discipline seems enjoyable at the time, but painful. Later on, however, it yields a harvest of righteousness and peace to those who have been trained by it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore strengthen your limp hands and weak knees.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.13', 'BSB', 'Make straight paths for your feet, so that the lame may not be disabled, but rather healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.14', 'BSB', 'Pursue peace with everyone, as well as holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.15', 'BSB', 'See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God, and that no root of bitterness springs up to cause trouble and defile many.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.16', 'BSB', 'See to it that no one is sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.17', 'BSB', 'For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought the blessing with tears.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.18', 'BSB', 'For you have not come to a mountain that can be touched and that is burning with fire; to darkness, gloom, and storm;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.19', 'BSB', 'to a trumpet blast or to a voice that made its hearers beg that no further word be spoken.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.20', 'BSB', 'For they could not bear what was commanded: “If even an animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.21', 'BSB', 'The sight was so terrifying that even Moses said, “I am trembling with fear.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.22', 'BSB', 'Instead, you have come to Mount Zion, to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem. You have come to myriads of angels', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.23', 'BSB', 'in joyful assembly, to the congregation of the firstborn, enrolled in heaven. You have come to God the Judge of all, to the spirits of the righteous made perfect,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.24', 'BSB', 'to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the sprinkled blood that speaks a better word than the blood of Abel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.25', 'BSB', 'See to it that you do not refuse Him who speaks. For if the people did not escape when they refused Him who warned them on earth, how much less will we escape if we reject Him who warns us from heaven?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.26', 'BSB', 'At that time His voice shook the earth, but now He has promised, “Once more I will shake not only the earth, but heaven as well.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.27', 'BSB', 'The words “Once more” signify the removal of what can be shaken—that is, created things—so that the unshakable may remain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.28', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since we are receiving an unshakable kingdom, let us be filled with gratitude, and so worship God acceptably with reverence and awe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.12.29', 'BSB', '“For our God is a consuming fire.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.1', 'BSB', 'Continue in brotherly love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.2', 'BSB', 'Do not neglect to show hospitality to strangers, for by so doing some people have entertained angels without knowing it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.3', 'BSB', 'Remember those in prison as if you were bound with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were suffering with them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.4', 'BSB', 'Marriage should be honored by all and the marriage bed kept undefiled, for God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.5', 'BSB', 'Keep your lives free from the love of money and be content with what you have, for God has said: “Never will I leave you, never will I forsake you.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.6', 'BSB', 'So we say with confidence: “The Lord is my helper; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.7', 'BSB', 'Remember your leaders who spoke the word of God to you. Consider the outcome of their way of life and imitate their faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.8', 'BSB', 'Jesus Christ is the same yesterday and today and forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.9', 'BSB', 'Do not be carried away by all kinds of strange teachings, for it is good for the heart to be strengthened by grace and not by foods of no value to those devoted to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.10', 'BSB', 'We have an altar from which those who serve at the tabernacle have no right to eat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.11', 'BSB', 'Although the high priest brings the blood of animals into the Holy Place as a sacrifice for sin, the bodies are burned outside the camp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.12', 'BSB', 'And so Jesus also suffered outside the city gate, to sanctify the people by His own blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore let us go to Him outside the camp, bearing the disgrace He bore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.14', 'BSB', 'For here we do not have a permanent city, but we are looking for the city that is to come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.15', 'BSB', 'Through Jesus, therefore, let us continually offer to God a sacrifice of praise, the fruit of lips that confess His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.16', 'BSB', 'And do not neglect to do good and to share with others, for with such sacrifices God is pleased.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.17', 'BSB', 'Obey your leaders and submit to them, for they watch over your souls as those who must give an account. To this end, allow them to lead with joy and not with grief, for that would be of no advantage to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.18', 'BSB', 'Pray for us; we are convinced that we have a clear conscience and desire to live honorably in every way.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.19', 'BSB', 'And I especially urge you to pray that I may be restored to you soon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.20', 'BSB', 'Now may the God of peace, who through the blood of the eternal covenant brought back from the dead our Lord Jesus, that great Shepherd of the sheep,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.21', 'BSB', 'equip you with every good thing to do His will. And may He accomplish in us what is pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.22', 'BSB', 'I urge you, brothers, to bear with my word of exhortation, for I have only written to you briefly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.23', 'BSB', 'Be aware that our brother Timothy has been released. If he arrives soon, I will come with him to see you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.24', 'BSB', 'Greet all your leaders and all the saints. Those from Italy send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Heb.13.25', 'BSB', 'Grace be with all of you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.1', 'BSB', 'James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, To the twelve tribes of the Dispersion: Greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.2', 'BSB', 'Consider it pure joy, my brothers, when you encounter trials of many kinds,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.3', 'BSB', 'because you know that the testing of your faith develops perseverance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.4', 'BSB', 'Allow perseverance to finish its work, so that you may be mature and complete, not lacking anything.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.5', 'BSB', 'Now if any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask God, who gives generously to all without finding fault, and it will be given to him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.6', 'BSB', 'But he must ask in faith, without doubting, because he who doubts is like a wave of the sea, blown and tossed by the wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.7', 'BSB', 'That man should not expect to receive anything from the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.8', 'BSB', 'He is a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.9', 'BSB', 'The brother in humble circumstances should exult in his high position.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.10', 'BSB', 'But the one who is rich should exult in his low position, because he will pass away like a flower of the field.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.11', 'BSB', 'For the sun rises with scorching heat and withers the plant; its flower falls and its beauty is lost. So too, the rich man will fade away in the midst of his pursuits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.12', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the man who perseveres under trial, because when he has stood the test, he will receive the crown of life that God has promised to those who love Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.13', 'BSB', 'When tempted, no one should say, “God is tempting me.” For God cannot be tempted by evil, nor does He tempt anyone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.14', 'BSB', 'But each one is tempted when by his own evil desires he is lured away and enticed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.15', 'BSB', 'Then after desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.16', 'BSB', 'Do not be deceived, my beloved brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.17', 'BSB', 'Every good and perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of the heavenly lights, with whom there is no change or shifting shadow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.18', 'BSB', 'He chose to give us birth through the word of truth, that we would be a kind of firstfruits of His creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.19', 'BSB', 'My beloved brothers, understand this: Everyone should be quick to listen, slow to speak, and slow to anger,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.20', 'BSB', 'for man’s anger does not bring about the righteousness that God desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.21', 'BSB', 'Therefore, get rid of all moral filth and every expression of evil, and humbly accept the word planted in you, which can save your souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.22', 'BSB', 'Be doers of the word, and not hearers only. Otherwise, you are deceiving yourselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.23', 'BSB', 'For anyone who hears the word but does not carry it out is like a man who looks at his face in a mirror,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.24', 'BSB', 'and after observing himself goes away and immediately forgets what he looks like.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.25', 'BSB', 'But the one who looks intently into the perfect law of freedom, and continues to do so—not being a forgetful hearer, but an effective doer—he will be blessed in what he does.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.26', 'BSB', 'If anyone considers himself religious and yet does not bridle his tongue, he deceives his heart and his religion is worthless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.1.27', 'BSB', 'Pure and undefiled religion before our God and Father is this: to care for orphans and widows in their distress, and to keep oneself from being polluted by the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.1', 'BSB', 'My brothers, as you hold out your faith in our glorious Lord Jesus Christ, do not show favoritism.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.2', 'BSB', 'Suppose a man comes into your meeting wearing a gold ring and fine clothes, and a poor man in shabby clothes also comes in.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.3', 'BSB', 'If you lavish attention on the man in fine clothes and say, “Here is a seat of honor,” but say to the poor man, “You must stand” or “Sit at my feet,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.4', 'BSB', 'have you not discriminated among yourselves and become judges with evil thoughts?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.5', 'BSB', 'Listen, my beloved brothers: Has not God chosen the poor of this world to be rich in faith and to inherit the kingdom He promised those who love Him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.6', 'BSB', 'But you have dishonored the poor. Is it not the rich who oppress you and drag you into court?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.7', 'BSB', 'Are they not the ones who blaspheme the noble name by which you have been called?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.8', 'BSB', 'If you really fulfill the royal law stated in Scripture, “Love your neighbor as yourself,” you are doing well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.9', 'BSB', 'But if you show favoritism, you sin and are convicted by the law as transgressors.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.10', 'BSB', 'Whoever keeps the whole law but stumbles at just one point is guilty of breaking all of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.11', 'BSB', 'For He who said, “Do not commit adultery,” also said, “Do not murder.” If you do not commit adultery, but do commit murder, you have become a lawbreaker.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.12', 'BSB', 'Speak and act as those who are going to be judged by the law that gives freedom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.13', 'BSB', 'For judgment without mercy will be shown to anyone who has not been merciful. Mercy triumphs over judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.14', 'BSB', 'What good is it, my brothers, if someone claims to have faith, but has no deeds? Can such faith save him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.15', 'BSB', 'Suppose a brother or sister is without clothes and daily food.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.16', 'BSB', 'If one of you tells him, “Go in peace; stay warm and well fed,” but does not provide for his physical needs, what good is that?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.17', 'BSB', 'So too, faith by itself, if it does not result in action, is dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.18', 'BSB', 'But someone will say, “You have faith and I have deeds.” Show me your faith without deeds, and I will show you my faith by my deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.19', 'BSB', 'You believe that God is one. Good for you! Even the demons believe that—and shudder.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.20', 'BSB', 'O foolish man, do you want evidence that faith without deeds is worthless?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.21', 'BSB', 'Was not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.22', 'BSB', 'You see that his faith was working with his actions, and his faith was perfected by what he did.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.23', 'BSB', 'And the Scripture was fulfilled that says, “Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness,” and he was called a friend of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.24', 'BSB', 'As you can see, a man is justified by his deeds and not by faith alone.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.25', 'BSB', 'In the same way, was not even Rahab the prostitute justified by her actions when she welcomed the spies and sent them off on another route?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.2.26', 'BSB', 'As the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without deeds is dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.1', 'BSB', 'Not many of you should become teachers, my brothers, because you know that we who teach will be judged more strictly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.2', 'BSB', 'We all stumble in many ways. If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.3', 'BSB', 'When we put bits into the mouths of horses to make them obey us, we can guide the whole animal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.4', 'BSB', 'Consider ships as well. Although they are so large and are driven by strong winds, they are steered by a very small rudder wherever the pilot is inclined.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.5', 'BSB', 'In the same way, the tongue is a small part of the body, but it boasts of great things. Consider how small a spark sets a great forest ablaze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.6', 'BSB', 'The tongue also is a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the body. It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life on fire, and is itself set on fire by hell.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.7', 'BSB', 'All kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and creatures of the sea are being tamed and have been tamed by man,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.8', 'BSB', 'but no man can tame the tongue. It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.9', 'BSB', 'With the tongue we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in God’s likeness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.10', 'BSB', 'Out of the same mouth come blessing and cursing. My brothers, this should not be!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.11', 'BSB', 'Can both fresh water and salt water flow from the same spring?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.12', 'BSB', 'My brothers, can a fig tree grow olives, or a grapevine bear figs? Neither can a salt spring produce fresh water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.13', 'BSB', 'Who is wise and understanding among you? Let him show it by his good conduct, by deeds done in the humility that comes from wisdom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.14', 'BSB', 'But if you harbor bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your hearts, do not boast in it or deny the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.15', 'BSB', 'Such wisdom does not come from above, but is earthly, unspiritual, demonic.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.16', 'BSB', 'For where jealousy and selfish ambition exist, there will be disorder and every evil practice.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.17', 'BSB', 'But the wisdom from above is first of all pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, and sincere.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.3.18', 'BSB', 'Peacemakers who sow in peace reap the fruit of righteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.1', 'BSB', 'What causes conflicts and quarrels among you? Don’t they come from the passions at war within you?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.2', 'BSB', 'You crave what you do not have; you kill and covet, but are unable to obtain it. You quarrel and fight. You do not have, because you do not ask.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.3', 'BSB', 'And when you do ask, you do not receive, because you ask with wrong motives, that you may squander it on your pleasures.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.4', 'BSB', 'You adulteresses! Do you not know that friendship with the world is hostility toward God? Therefore, whoever chooses to be a friend of the world renders himself an enemy of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.5', 'BSB', 'Or do you think the Scripture says without reason that the Spirit He caused to dwell in us yearns with envy?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.6', 'BSB', 'But He gives us more grace. This is why it says: “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.7', 'BSB', 'Submit yourselves, then, to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.8', 'BSB', 'Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you double-minded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.9', 'BSB', 'Grieve, mourn, and weep. Turn your laughter to mourning, and your joy to gloom.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.10', 'BSB', 'Humble yourselves before the Lord, and He will exalt you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.11', 'BSB', 'Brothers, do not slander one another. Anyone who speaks against his brother or judges him speaks against the law and judges it. And if you judge the law, you are not a practitioner of the law, but a judge of it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.12', 'BSB', 'There is only one Lawgiver and Judge, the One who is able to save and destroy. But who are you to judge your neighbor?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.13', 'BSB', 'Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go to this or that city, spend a year there, carry on business, and make a profit.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.14', 'BSB', 'You do not even know what will happen tomorrow! What is your life? You are a mist that appears for a little while and then vanishes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.15', 'BSB', 'Instead, you ought to say, “If the Lord is willing, we will live and do this or that.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.16', 'BSB', 'As it is, you boast in your proud intentions. All such boasting is evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.4.17', 'BSB', 'Anyone, then, who knows the right thing to do, yet fails to do it, is guilty of sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.1', 'BSB', 'Come now, you who are rich, weep and wail over the misery to come upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.2', 'BSB', 'Your riches have rotted and moths have eaten your clothes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.3', 'BSB', 'Your gold and silver are corroded. Their corrosion will testify against you and consume your flesh like fire. You have hoarded treasure in the last days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.4', 'BSB', 'Look, the wages you withheld from the workmen who mowed your fields are crying out against you. The cries of the harvesters have reached the ears of the Lord of Hosts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.5', 'BSB', 'You have lived on earth in luxury and self-indulgence. You have fattened your hearts in the day of slaughter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.6', 'BSB', 'You have condemned and murdered the righteous, who did not resist you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.7', 'BSB', 'Be patient, then, brothers, until the Lord’s coming. See how the farmer awaits the precious fruit of the soil—how patient he is for the fall and spring rains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.8', 'BSB', 'You, too, be patient and strengthen your hearts, because the Lord’s coming is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.9', 'BSB', 'Do not complain about one another, brothers, so that you will not be judged. Look, the Judge is standing at the door!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.10', 'BSB', 'Brothers, as an example of patience in affliction, take the prophets who spoke in the name of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.11', 'BSB', 'See how blessed we consider those who have persevered. You have heard of Job’s perseverance and have seen the outcome from the Lord. The Lord is full of compassion and mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.12', 'BSB', 'Above all, my brothers, do not swear, not by heaven or earth or by any other oath. Simply let your “Yes” be yes, and your “No,” no, so that you will not fall under judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.13', 'BSB', 'Is any one of you suffering? He should pray. Is anyone cheerful? He should sing praises.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.14', 'BSB', 'Is any one of you sick? He should call the elders of the church to pray over him and anoint him with oil in the name of the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.15', 'BSB', 'And the prayer offered in faith will restore the one who is sick. The Lord will raise him up. If he has sinned, he will be forgiven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. The prayer of a righteous man has great power to prevail.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.17', 'BSB', 'Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly that it would not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and a half years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.18', 'BSB', 'Again he prayed, and the heavens gave rain, and the earth yielded its crops.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.19', 'BSB', 'My brothers, if one of you should wander from the truth and someone should bring him back,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jas.5.20', 'BSB', 'consider this: Whoever turns a sinner from the error of his way will save his soul from death and cover over a multitude of sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.1', 'BSB', 'Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, To the elect who are exiles of the Dispersion throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia, chosen', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.2', 'BSB', 'according to the foreknowledge of God the Father and sanctified by the Spirit for obedience to Jesus Christ and sprinkling by His blood: Grace and peace be yours in abundance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.3', 'BSB', 'Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ! By His great mercy He has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.4', 'BSB', 'and into an inheritance that is imperishable, undefiled, and unfading, reserved in heaven for you,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.5', 'BSB', 'who through faith are shielded by God’s power for the salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.6', 'BSB', 'In this you greatly rejoice, though now for a little while you may have had to suffer grief in various trials', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.7', 'BSB', 'so that the proven character of your faith—more precious than gold, which perishes even though refined by fire—may result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.8', 'BSB', 'Though you have not seen Him, you love Him; and though you do not see Him now, you believe in Him and rejoice with an inexpressible and glorious joy,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.9', 'BSB', 'now that you are receiving the goal of your faith, the salvation of your souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.10', 'BSB', 'Concerning this salvation, the prophets who foretold the grace to come to you searched and investigated carefully,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.11', 'BSB', 'trying to determine the time and setting to which the Spirit of Christ in them was pointing when He predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories to follow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.12', 'BSB', 'It was revealed to them that they were not serving themselves, but you, when they foretold the things now announced by those who preached the gospel to you by the Holy Spirit sent from heaven. Even angels long to look into these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.13', 'BSB', 'Therefore prepare your minds for action. Be sober-minded. Set your hope fully on the grace to be given you at the revelation of Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.14', 'BSB', 'As obedient children, do not conform to the passions of your former ignorance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.15', 'BSB', 'But just as He who called you is holy, so be holy in all you do,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.16', 'BSB', 'for it is written: “Be holy, because I am holy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.17', 'BSB', 'Since you call on a Father who judges each one’s work impartially, conduct yourselves in reverent fear during your stay as foreigners.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.18', 'BSB', 'For you know that it was not with perishable things such as silver or gold that you were redeemed from the empty way of life you inherited from your forefathers,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.19', 'BSB', 'but with the precious blood of Christ, a lamb without blemish or spot.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.20', 'BSB', 'He was known before the foundation of the world, but was revealed in the last times for your sake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.21', 'BSB', 'Through Him you believe in God, who raised Him from the dead and glorified Him; and so your faith and hope are in God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.22', 'BSB', 'Since you have purified your souls by obedience to the truth so that you have a genuine love for your brothers, love one another deeply, from a pure heart.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.23', 'BSB', 'For you have been born again, not of perishable seed, but of imperishable, through the living and enduring word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.24', 'BSB', 'For, “All flesh is like grass, and all its glory like the flowers of the field; the grass withers and the flowers fall,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.1.25', 'BSB', 'but the word of the Lord stands forever.” And this is the word that was proclaimed to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.1', 'BSB', 'Rid yourselves, therefore, of all malice, deceit, hypocrisy, envy, and slander.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.2', 'BSB', 'Like newborn babies, crave pure spiritual milk, so that by it you may grow up in your salvation,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.3', 'BSB', 'now that you have tasted that the Lord is good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.4', 'BSB', 'As you come to Him, the living stone, rejected by men but chosen and precious in God’s sight,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.5', 'BSB', 'you also, like living stones, are being built into a spiritual house to be a holy priesthood, offering spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.6', 'BSB', 'For it stands in Scripture: “See, I lay in Zion a stone, a chosen and precious cornerstone; and the one who believes in Him will never be put to shame.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.7', 'BSB', 'To you who believe, then, this stone is precious. But to those who do not believe, “The stone the builders rejected has become the cornerstone,”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.8', 'BSB', 'and, “A stone of stumbling and a rock of offense.” They stumble because they disobey the word—and to this they were appointed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.9', 'BSB', 'But you are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for God’s own possession, to proclaim the virtues of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.10', 'BSB', 'Once you were not a people, but now you are the people of God; once you had not received mercy, but now you have received mercy.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.11', 'BSB', 'Beloved, I urge you, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from the desires of the flesh, which war against your soul.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.12', 'BSB', 'Conduct yourselves with such honor among the Gentiles that, though they slander you as evildoers, they may see your good deeds and glorify God on the day He visits us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.13', 'BSB', 'Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution, whether to the king as the supreme authority,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.14', 'BSB', 'or to governors as those sent by him to punish those who do wrong and to praise those who do right.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.15', 'BSB', 'For it is God’s will that by doing good you should silence the ignorance of foolish men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.16', 'BSB', 'Live in freedom, but do not use your freedom as a cover-up for evil; live as servants of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.17', 'BSB', 'Treat everyone with high regard: Love the brotherhood of believers, fear God, honor the king.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.18', 'BSB', 'Servants, submit yourselves to your masters with all respect, not only to those who are good and gentle, but even to those who are unreasonable.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.19', 'BSB', 'For if anyone endures the pain of unjust suffering because he is conscious of God, this is to be commended.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.20', 'BSB', 'How is it to your credit if you are beaten for doing wrong and you endure it? But if you suffer for doing good and you endure it, this is commendable before God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.21', 'BSB', 'For to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for you, leaving you an example, that you should follow in His footsteps:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.22', 'BSB', '“He committed no sin, and no deceit was found in His mouth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.23', 'BSB', 'When they heaped abuse on Him, He did not retaliate; when He suffered, He made no threats, but entrusted Himself to Him who judges justly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.24', 'BSB', 'He Himself bore our sins in His body on the tree, so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness. “By His stripes you are healed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.2.25', 'BSB', 'For “you were like sheep going astray,” but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.1', 'BSB', 'Wives, in the same way, submit yourselves to your husbands, so that even if they refuse to believe the word, they will be won over without words by the behavior of their wives', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.2', 'BSB', 'when they see your pure and reverent demeanor.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.3', 'BSB', 'Your beauty should not come from outward adornment, such as braided hair or gold jewelry or fine clothes,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.4', 'BSB', 'but from the inner disposition of your heart, the unfading beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in God’s sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.5', 'BSB', 'For this is how the holy women of the past adorned themselves. They put their hope in God and were submissive to their husbands,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.6', 'BSB', 'just as Sarah obeyed Abraham and called him lord. And you are her children if you do what is right and refuse to give way to fear.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.7', 'BSB', 'Husbands, in the same way, treat your wives with consideration as a delicate vessel, and with honor as fellow heirs of the gracious gift of life, so that your prayers will not be hindered.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.8', 'BSB', 'Finally, all of you, be like-minded and sympathetic, love as brothers, be tenderhearted and humble.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.9', 'BSB', 'Do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but with blessing, because to this you were called so that you may inherit a blessing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.10', 'BSB', 'For, “Whoever would love life and see good days must keep his tongue from evil and his lips from deceitful speech.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.11', 'BSB', 'He must turn from evil and do good; he must seek peace and pursue it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.12', 'BSB', 'For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous, and His ears are inclined to their prayer. But the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.13', 'BSB', 'Who can harm you if you are zealous for what is good?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.14', 'BSB', 'But even if you should suffer for what is right, you are blessed. “Do not fear what they fear; do not be shaken.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.15', 'BSB', 'But in your hearts sanctify Christ as Lord. Always be prepared to give a defense to everyone who asks you the reason for the hope that is in you. But respond with gentleness and respect,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.16', 'BSB', 'keeping a clear conscience, so that those who slander you may be put to shame by your good behavior in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.17', 'BSB', 'For it is better, if it is God’s will, to suffer for doing good than for doing evil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.18', 'BSB', 'For Christ also suffered for sins once for all, the righteous for the unrighteous, to bring you to God. He was put to death in the body but made alive in the Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.19', 'BSB', 'in whom He also went and preached to the spirits in prison', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.20', 'BSB', 'who disobeyed long ago when God waited patiently in the days of Noah while the ark was being built. In the ark a few people, only eight souls, were saved through water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.21', 'BSB', 'And this water symbolizes the baptism that now saves you also—not the removal of dirt from the body, but the pledge of a clear conscience toward God—through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.3.22', 'BSB', 'who has gone into heaven and is at the right hand of God, with angels, authorities, and powers subject to Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.1', 'BSB', 'Therefore, since Christ suffered in His body, arm yourselves with the same resolve, because anyone who has suffered in his body is done with sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.2', 'BSB', 'Consequently, he does not live out his remaining time on earth for human passions, but for the will of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.3', 'BSB', 'For you have spent enough time in the past carrying out the same desires as the Gentiles: living in debauchery, lust, drunkenness, orgies, carousing, and detestable idolatry.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.4', 'BSB', 'Because of this, they consider it strange of you not to plunge with them into the same flood of reckless indiscretion, and they heap abuse on you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.5', 'BSB', 'But they will have to give an account to Him who is ready to judge the living and the dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.6', 'BSB', 'That is why the gospel was preached even to those who are now dead, so that they might be judged as men in the flesh, but live according to God in the spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.7', 'BSB', 'The end of all things is near. Therefore be clear-minded and sober, so that you can pray.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.8', 'BSB', 'Above all, love one another deeply, because love covers over a multitude of sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.9', 'BSB', 'Show hospitality to one another without complaining.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.10', 'BSB', 'As good stewards of the manifold grace of God, each of you should use whatever gift he has received to serve one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.11', 'BSB', 'If anyone speaks, he should speak as one conveying the words of God. If anyone serves, he should serve with the strength God provides, so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.12', 'BSB', 'Beloved, do not be surprised at the fiery trial that has come upon you, as though something strange were happening to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.13', 'BSB', 'But rejoice that you share in the sufferings of Christ, so that you may be overjoyed at the revelation of His glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.14', 'BSB', 'If you are insulted for the name of Christ, you are blessed, because the Spirit of glory and of God rests on you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.15', 'BSB', 'Indeed, none of you should suffer as a murderer or thief or wrongdoer, or even as a meddler.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.16', 'BSB', 'But if you suffer as a Christian, do not be ashamed, but glorify God that you bear that name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.17', 'BSB', 'For it is time for judgment to begin with the family of God; and if it begins with us, what will the outcome be for those who disobey the gospel of God?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.18', 'BSB', 'And, “If it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will become of the ungodly and the sinner?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.4.19', 'BSB', 'So then, those who suffer according to God’s will should entrust their souls to their faithful Creator and continue to do good.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.1', 'BSB', 'As a fellow elder, a witness of Christ’s sufferings, and a partaker of the glory to be revealed, I appeal to the elders among you:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.2', 'BSB', 'Be shepherds of God’s flock that is among you, watching over them not out of compulsion, but because it is God’s will; not out of greed, but out of eagerness;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.3', 'BSB', 'not lording it over those entrusted to you, but being examples to the flock.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.4', 'BSB', 'And when the Chief Shepherd appears, you will receive the crown of glory that will never fade away.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.5', 'BSB', 'Young men, in the same way, submit yourselves to your elders. And all of you, clothe yourselves with humility toward one another, because, “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.6', 'BSB', 'Humble yourselves, therefore, under God’s mighty hand, so that in due time He may exalt you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.7', 'BSB', 'Cast all your anxiety on Him, because He cares for you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.8', 'BSB', 'Be sober-minded and alert. Your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, seeking someone to devour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.9', 'BSB', 'Resist him, standing firm in your faith and in the knowledge that your brothers throughout the world are undergoing the same kinds of suffering.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.10', 'BSB', 'And after you have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to His eternal glory in Christ, will Himself restore you, secure you, strengthen you, and establish you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.11', 'BSB', 'To Him be the power forever and ever. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.12', 'BSB', 'Through Silvanus, whom I regard as a faithful brother, I have written to you briefly, encouraging you and testifying that this is the true grace of God. Stand firm in it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.13', 'BSB', 'The church in Babylon, chosen together with you, sends you greetings, as does my son Mark.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1Pet.5.14', 'BSB', 'Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace to all of you who are in Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.1', 'BSB', 'Simon Peter, a servant and apostle of Jesus Christ, To those who through the righteousness of our God and Savior Jesus Christ have received a faith as precious as ours:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.2', 'BSB', 'Grace and peace be multiplied to you through the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.3', 'BSB', 'His divine power has given us everything we need for life and godliness through the knowledge of Him who called us by His own glory and excellence.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.4', 'BSB', 'Through these He has given us His precious and magnificent promises, so that through them you may become partakers of the divine nature, now that you have escaped the corruption in the world caused by evil desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.5', 'BSB', 'For this very reason, make every effort to add to your faith virtue; and to virtue, knowledge;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.6', 'BSB', 'and to knowledge, self-control; and to self-control, perseverance; and to perseverance, godliness;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.7', 'BSB', 'and to godliness, brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness, love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.8', 'BSB', 'For if you possess these qualities and continue to grow in them, they will keep you from being ineffective and unproductive in your knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.9', 'BSB', 'But whoever lacks these traits is nearsighted to the point of blindness, having forgotten that he has been cleansed from his past sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.10', 'BSB', 'Therefore, brothers, strive to make your calling and election sure. For if you practice these things you will never stumble,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.11', 'BSB', 'and you will receive a lavish reception into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore I will always remind you of these things, even though you know them and are established in the truth you now have.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.13', 'BSB', 'I think it is right to refresh your memory as long as I live in the tent of my body,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.14', 'BSB', 'because I know that this tent will soon be laid aside, as our Lord Jesus Christ has made clear to me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.15', 'BSB', 'And I will make every effort to ensure that after my departure, you will be able to recall these things at all times.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.16', 'BSB', 'For we did not follow cleverly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of His majesty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.17', 'BSB', 'For He received honor and glory from God the Father when the voice came to Him from the Majestic Glory, saying, “This is My beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.18', 'BSB', 'And we ourselves heard this voice from heaven when we were with Him on the holy mountain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.19', 'BSB', 'We also have the word of the prophets as confirmed beyond doubt. And you will do well to pay attention to it, as to a lamp shining in a dark place, until the day dawns and the morning star rises in your hearts.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.20', 'BSB', 'Above all, you must understand that no prophecy of Scripture comes from one’s own interpretation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.1.21', 'BSB', 'For no such prophecy was ever brought forth by the will of man, but men spoke from God as they were carried along by the Holy Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.1', 'BSB', 'Now there were also false prophets among the people, just as there will be false teachers among you. They will secretly introduce destructive heresies, even denying the Master who bought them—bringing swift destruction on themselves.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.2', 'BSB', 'Many will follow in their depravity, and because of them the way of truth will be defamed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.3', 'BSB', 'In their greed, these false teachers will exploit you with deceptive words. The longstanding verdict against them remains in force, and their destruction does not sleep.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.4', 'BSB', 'For if God did not spare the angels when they sinned, but cast them deep into hell, placing them in chains of darkness to be held for judgment;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.5', 'BSB', 'if He did not spare the ancient world when He brought the flood on its ungodly people, but preserved Noah, a preacher of righteousness, among the eight;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.6', 'BSB', 'if He condemned the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah to destruction, reducing them to ashes as an example of what is coming on the ungodly;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.7', 'BSB', 'and if He rescued Lot, a righteous man distressed by the depraved conduct of the lawless', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.8', 'BSB', '(for that righteous man, living among them day after day, was tormented in his righteous soul by the lawless deeds he saw and heard)—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.9', 'BSB', 'if all this is so, then the Lord knows how to rescue the godly from trials and to hold the unrighteous for punishment on the day of judgment.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.10', 'BSB', 'Such punishment is specially reserved for those who indulge the corrupt desires of the flesh and despise authority. Bold and self-willed, they are unafraid to slander glorious beings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.11', 'BSB', 'Yet not even angels, though greater in strength and power, dare to bring such slanderous charges against them before the Lord.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.12', 'BSB', 'These men are like irrational animals, creatures of instinct, born to be captured and destroyed. They blaspheme in matters they do not understand, and like such creatures, they too will be destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.13', 'BSB', 'The harm they will suffer is the wages of their wickedness. They consider it a pleasure to carouse in broad daylight. They are blots and blemishes, reveling in their deception as they feast with you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.14', 'BSB', 'Their eyes are full of adultery; their desire for sin is never satisfied; they seduce the unstable. They are accursed children with hearts trained in greed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.15', 'BSB', 'They have left the straight way and wandered off to follow the way of Balaam son of Beor, who loved the wages of wickedness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.16', 'BSB', 'But he was rebuked for his transgression by a donkey, otherwise without speech, that spoke with a man’s voice and restrained the prophet’s madness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.17', 'BSB', 'These men are springs without water and mists driven by a storm. Blackest darkness is reserved for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.18', 'BSB', 'With lofty but empty words, they appeal to the sensual passions of the flesh and entice those who are just escaping from others who live in error.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.19', 'BSB', 'They promise them freedom, while they themselves are slaves to depravity. For a man is a slave to whatever has mastered him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.20', 'BSB', 'If indeed they have escaped the corruption of the world through the knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, only to be entangled and overcome by it again, their final condition is worse than it was at first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.21', 'BSB', 'It would have been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness than to have known it and then to turn away from the holy commandment passed on to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.2.22', 'BSB', 'Of them the proverbs are true: “A dog returns to its vomit,” and, “A sow that is washed goes back to her wallowing in the mud.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.1', 'BSB', 'Beloved, this is now my second letter to you. Both of them are reminders to stir you to wholesome thinking', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.2', 'BSB', 'by recalling what was foretold by the holy prophets and commanded by our Lord and Savior through your apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.3', 'BSB', 'Most importantly, you must understand that in the last days scoffers will come, scoffing and following their own evil desires.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.4', 'BSB', '“Where is the promise of His coming?” they will ask. “Ever since our fathers fell asleep, everything continues as it has from the beginning of creation.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.5', 'BSB', 'But they deliberately overlook the fact that long ago by God’s word the heavens existed and the earth was formed out of water and by water,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.6', 'BSB', 'through which the world of that time perished in the flood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.7', 'BSB', 'And by that same word, the present heavens and earth are reserved for fire, being kept for the day of judgment and destruction of ungodly men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.8', 'BSB', 'Beloved, do not let this one thing escape your notice: With the Lord a day is like a thousand years, and a thousand years are like a day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.9', 'BSB', 'The Lord is not slow in keeping His promise as some understand slowness, but is patient with you, not wanting anyone to perish but everyone to come to repentance.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.10', 'BSB', 'But the Day of the Lord will come like a thief. The heavens will disappear with a roar, the elements will be destroyed by fire, and the earth and its works will be laid bare.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.11', 'BSB', 'Since everything will be destroyed in this way, what kind of people ought you to be? You ought to conduct yourselves in holiness and godliness', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.12', 'BSB', 'as you anticipate and hasten the coming of the day of God, when the heavens will be destroyed by fire and the elements will melt in the heat.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.13', 'BSB', 'But in keeping with God’s promise, we are looking forward to a new heaven and a new earth, where righteousness dwells.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.14', 'BSB', 'Therefore, beloved, as you anticipate these things, make every effort to be found at peace—spotless and blameless in His sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.15', 'BSB', 'Consider also that our Lord’s patience brings salvation, just as our beloved brother Paul also wrote you with the wisdom God gave him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.16', 'BSB', 'He writes this way in all his letters, speaking in them about such matters. Some parts of his letters are hard to understand, which ignorant and unstable people distort, as they do the rest of the Scriptures, to their own destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.17', 'BSB', 'Therefore, beloved, since you already know these things, be on your guard so that you will not be carried away by the error of the lawless and fall from your secure standing.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2Pet.3.18', 'BSB', 'But grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. To Him be the glory both now and to the day of eternity. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.1', 'BSB', 'That which was from the beginning, which we have heard, which we have seen with our own eyes, which we have gazed upon and touched with our own hands—this is the Word of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.2', 'BSB', 'And this is the life that was revealed; we have seen it and testified to it, and we proclaim to you the eternal life that was with the Father and was revealed to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.3', 'BSB', 'We proclaim to you what we have seen and heard, so that you also may have fellowship with us. And this fellowship of ours is with the Father and with His Son, Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.4', 'BSB', 'We write these things so that our joy may be complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.5', 'BSB', 'And this is the message we have heard from Him and announce to you: God is light, and in Him there is no darkness at all.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.6', 'BSB', 'If we say we have fellowship with Him yet walk in the darkness, we lie and do not practice the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.7', 'BSB', 'But if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus His Son cleanses us from all sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.8', 'BSB', 'If we say we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.9', 'BSB', 'If we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.1.10', 'BSB', 'If we say we have not sinned, we make Him out to be a liar, and His word is not in us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.1', 'BSB', 'My little children, I am writing these things to you so that you will not sin. But if anyone does sin, we have an advocate before the Father—Jesus Christ, the Righteous One.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.2', 'BSB', 'He Himself is the atoning sacrifice for our sins, and not only for ours but also for the sins of the whole world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.3', 'BSB', 'By this we can be sure that we have come to know Him: if we keep His commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.4', 'BSB', 'If anyone says, “I know Him,” but does not keep His commandments, he is a liar, and the truth is not in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.5', 'BSB', 'But if anyone keeps His word, the love of God has been truly perfected in him. By this we know that we are in Him:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.6', 'BSB', 'Whoever claims to abide in Him must walk as Jesus walked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.7', 'BSB', 'Beloved, I am not writing to you a new commandment, but an old one, which you have had from the beginning. This commandment is the message you have heard.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.8', 'BSB', 'Then again, I am also writing to you a new commandment, which is true in Him and also in you. For the darkness is fading and the true light is already shining.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.9', 'BSB', 'If anyone claims to be in the light but hates his brother, he is still in the darkness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.10', 'BSB', 'Whoever loves his brother remains in the light, and there is no cause of stumbling in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.11', 'BSB', 'But whoever hates his brother is in the darkness and walks in the darkness. He does not know where he is going, because the darkness has blinded his eyes.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.12', 'BSB', 'I am writing to you, little children, because your sins have been forgiven through His name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.13', 'BSB', 'I am writing to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I am writing to you, young men, because you have overcome the evil one. I have written to you, children, because you know the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.14', 'BSB', 'I have written to you, fathers, because you know Him who is from the beginning. I have written to you, young men, because you are strong, and the word of God abides in you, and you have overcome the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.15', 'BSB', 'Do not love the world or anything in the world. If anyone loves the world, the love of the Father is not in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.16', 'BSB', 'For all that is in the world—the desires of the flesh, the desires of the eyes, and the pride of life—is not from the Father but from the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.17', 'BSB', 'The world is passing away, along with its desires; but whoever does the will of God remains forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.18', 'BSB', 'Children, it is the last hour; and just as you have heard that the antichrist is coming, so now many antichrists have appeared. This is how we know it is the last hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.19', 'BSB', 'They went out from us, but they did not belong to us. For if they had belonged to us, they would have remained with us. But their departure made it clear that none of them belonged to us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.20', 'BSB', 'You, however, have an anointing from the Holy One, and all of you know the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.21', 'BSB', 'I have not written to you because you lack knowledge of the truth, but because you have it, and because no lie comes from the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.22', 'BSB', 'Who is the liar, if it is not the one who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This is the antichrist, who denies the Father and the Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.23', 'BSB', 'Whoever denies the Son does not have the Father, but whoever confesses the Son has the Father as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.24', 'BSB', 'As for you, let what you have heard from the beginning remain in you. If it does, you will also remain in the Son and in the Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.25', 'BSB', 'And this is the promise that He Himself made to us: eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.26', 'BSB', 'I have written these things to you about those who are trying to deceive you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.27', 'BSB', 'And as for you, the anointing you received from Him remains in you, and you do not need anyone to teach you. But just as His true and genuine anointing teaches you about all things, so remain in Him as you have been taught.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.28', 'BSB', 'And now, little children, remain in Christ, so that when He appears, we may be confident and unashamed before Him at His coming.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.2.29', 'BSB', 'If you know that He is righteous, you also know that everyone who practices righteousness has been born of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.1', 'BSB', 'Behold what manner of love the Father has given to us, that we should be called children of God. And that is what we are! The reason the world does not know us is that it did not know Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.2', 'BSB', 'Beloved, we are now children of God, and what we will be has not yet been revealed. We know that when Christ appears, we will be like Him, for we will see Him as He is.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.3', 'BSB', 'And everyone who has this hope in Him purifies himself, just as Christ is pure.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.4', 'BSB', 'Everyone who practices sin practices lawlessness as well. Indeed, sin is lawlessness.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.5', 'BSB', 'But you know that Christ appeared to take away sins, and in Him there is no sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.6', 'BSB', 'No one who remains in Him keeps on sinning. No one who continues to sin has seen Him or known Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.7', 'BSB', 'Little children, let no one deceive you: The one who practices righteousness is righteous, just as Christ is righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.8', 'BSB', 'The one who practices sin is of the devil, because the devil has been sinning from the very start. This is why the Son of God was revealed, to destroy the works of the devil.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.9', 'BSB', 'Anyone born of God refuses to practice sin, because God’s seed abides in him; he cannot go on sinning, because he has been born of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.10', 'BSB', 'By this the children of God are distinguished from the children of the devil: Anyone who does not practice righteousness is not of God, nor is anyone who does not love his brother.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.11', 'BSB', 'This is the message you have heard from the beginning: We should love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.12', 'BSB', 'Do not be like Cain, who belonged to the evil one and murdered his brother. And why did Cain slay him? Because his own deeds were evil, while those of his brother were righteous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.13', 'BSB', 'So do not be surprised, brothers, if the world hates you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.14', 'BSB', 'We know that we have passed from death to life, because we love our brothers. The one who does not love remains in death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.15', 'BSB', 'Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that eternal life does not reside in a murderer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.16', 'BSB', 'By this we know what love is: Jesus laid down His life for us, and we ought to lay down our lives for our brothers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.17', 'BSB', 'If anyone with earthly possessions sees his brother in need, but withholds his compassion from him, how can the love of God abide in him?', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.18', 'BSB', 'Little children, let us love not in word and speech, but in action and truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.19', 'BSB', 'And by this we will know that we belong to the truth, and will assure our hearts in His presence:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.20', 'BSB', 'Even if our hearts condemn us, God is greater than our hearts, and He knows all things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.21', 'BSB', 'Beloved, if our hearts do not condemn us, we have confidence before God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.22', 'BSB', 'and we will receive from Him whatever we ask, because we keep His commandments and do what is pleasing in His sight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.23', 'BSB', 'And this is His commandment: that we should believe in the name of His Son, Jesus Christ, and we should love one another just as He commanded us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.3.24', 'BSB', 'Whoever keeps His commandments remains in God, and God in him. And by this we know that He remains in us: by the Spirit He has given us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.1', 'BSB', 'Beloved, do not believe every spirit, but test the spirits to see whether they are from God. For many false prophets have gone out into the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.2', 'BSB', 'By this you will know the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesses that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is from God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.3', 'BSB', 'and every spirit that does not confess Jesus is not from God. This is the spirit of the antichrist, which you have heard is coming and which is already in the world at this time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.4', 'BSB', 'You, little children, are from God and have overcome them, because greater is He who is in you than he who is in the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.5', 'BSB', 'They are of the world. That is why they speak from the world’s perspective, and the world listens to them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.6', 'BSB', 'We are from God. Whoever knows God listens to us; whoever is not from God does not listen to us. That is how we know the Spirit of truth and the spirit of deception.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.7', 'BSB', 'Beloved, let us love one another, because love comes from God. Everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.8', 'BSB', 'Whoever does not love does not know God, because God is love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.9', 'BSB', 'This is how God’s love was revealed among us: God sent His one and only Son into the world, so that we might live through Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.10', 'BSB', 'And love consists in this: not that we loved God, but that He loved us and sent His Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.11', 'BSB', 'Beloved, if God so loved us, we also ought to love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.12', 'BSB', 'No one has ever seen God; but if we love one another, God remains in us, and His love is perfected in us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.13', 'BSB', 'By this we know that we remain in Him, and He in us: He has given us of His Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.14', 'BSB', 'And we have seen and testify that the Father has sent His Son to be the Savior of the world.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.15', 'BSB', 'If anyone confesses that Jesus is the Son of God, God abides in him, and he in God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.16', 'BSB', 'And we have come to know and believe the love that God has for us. God is love; whoever abides in love abides in God, and God in him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.17', 'BSB', 'In this way, love has been perfected among us, so that we may have confidence on the day of judgment; for in this world we are just like Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.18', 'BSB', 'There is no fear in love, but perfect love drives out fear, because fear involves punishment. The one who fears has not been perfected in love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.19', 'BSB', 'We love because He first loved us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.20', 'BSB', 'If anyone says, “I love God,” but hates his brother, he is a liar. For anyone who does not love his brother, whom he has seen, cannot love God, whom he has not seen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.4.21', 'BSB', 'And we have this commandment from Him: Whoever loves God must love his brother as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.1', 'BSB', 'Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born of God, and everyone who loves the Father also loves those born of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.2', 'BSB', 'By this we know that we love the children of God: when we love God and keep His commandments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.3', 'BSB', 'For this is the love of God, that we keep His commandments. And His commandments are not burdensome,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.4', 'BSB', 'because everyone born of God overcomes the world. And this is the victory that has overcome the world: our faith.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.5', 'BSB', 'Who then overcomes the world? Only he who believes that Jesus is the Son of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.6', 'BSB', 'This is the One who came by water and blood, Jesus Christ—not by water alone, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit who testifies to this, because the Spirit is the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.7', 'BSB', 'For there are three that testify:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.8', 'BSB', 'the Spirit, the water, and the blood—and these three are in agreement.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.9', 'BSB', 'Even if we accept human testimony, the testimony of God is greater. For this is the testimony that God has given about His Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.10', 'BSB', 'Whoever believes in the Son of God has this testimony within him; whoever does not believe God has made Him out to be a liar, because he has not believed in the testimony that God has given about His Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.11', 'BSB', 'And this is that testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.12', 'BSB', 'Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.13', 'BSB', 'I have written these things to you who believe in the name of the Son of God, so that you may know that you have eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.14', 'BSB', 'And this is the confidence that we have before Him: If we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.15', 'BSB', 'And if we know that He hears us in whatever we ask, we know that we already possess what we have asked of Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.16', 'BSB', 'If anyone sees his brother committing a sin not leading to death, he should ask God, who will give life to those who commit this kind of sin. There is a sin that leads to death; I am not saying he should ask regarding that sin.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.17', 'BSB', 'All unrighteousness is sin, yet there is sin that does not lead to death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.18', 'BSB', 'We know that anyone born of God does not keep on sinning; the One who was born of God protects him, and the evil one cannot touch him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.19', 'BSB', 'We know that we are of God, and that the whole world is under the power of the evil one.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.20', 'BSB', 'And we know that the Son of God has come and has given us understanding, so that we may know Him who is true; and we are in Him who is true—in His Son Jesus Christ. He is the true God and eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('1John.5.21', 'BSB', 'Little children, keep yourselves from idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.1', 'BSB', 'The elder, To the chosen lady and her children, whom I love in the truth—and not I alone, but also all who know the truth—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.2', 'BSB', 'because of the truth that abides in us and will be with us forever:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.3', 'BSB', 'Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, will be with us in truth and love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.4', 'BSB', 'I was overjoyed to find some of your children walking in the truth, just as the Father has commanded us.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.5', 'BSB', 'And now I urge you, dear lady—not as a new commandment to you, but one we have had from the beginning—that we love one another.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.6', 'BSB', 'And this is love, that we walk according to His commandments. This is the very commandment you have heard from the beginning, that you must walk in love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.7', 'BSB', 'For many deceivers have gone out into the world, refusing to confess the coming of Jesus Christ in the flesh. Any such person is the deceiver and the antichrist.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.8', 'BSB', 'Watch yourselves, so that you do not lose what we have worked for, but that you may be fully rewarded.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.9', 'BSB', 'Anyone who runs ahead without remaining in the teaching of Christ does not have God. Whoever remains in His teaching has both the Father and the Son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.10', 'BSB', 'If anyone comes to you but does not bring this teaching, do not receive him into your home or even greet him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.11', 'BSB', 'Whoever greets such a person shares in his evil deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.12', 'BSB', 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with paper and ink. Instead, I hope to come and speak with you face to face, so that our joy may be complete.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('2John.1.13', 'BSB', 'The children of your elect sister send you greetings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.1', 'BSB', 'The elder, To the beloved Gaius, whom I love in the truth:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.2', 'BSB', 'Beloved, I pray that in every way you may prosper and enjoy good health, as your soul also prospers.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.3', 'BSB', 'For I was overjoyed when the brothers came and testified about your devotion to the truth, in which you continue to walk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.4', 'BSB', 'I have no greater joy than to hear that my children are walking in the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.5', 'BSB', 'Beloved, you are faithful in what you are doing for the brothers, and especially since they are strangers to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.6', 'BSB', 'They have testified to the church about your love. You will do well to send them on their way in a manner worthy of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.7', 'BSB', 'For they went out on behalf of the Name, accepting nothing from the Gentiles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore we ought to support such men, so that we may be fellow workers for the truth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.9', 'BSB', 'I have written to the church about this, but Diotrephes, who loves to be first, will not accept our instruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.10', 'BSB', 'So if I come, I will call attention to his malicious slander against us. And unsatisfied with that, he refuses to welcome the brothers and forbids those who want to do so, even putting them out of the church.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.11', 'BSB', 'Beloved, do not imitate what is evil, but what is good. The one who does good is of God; the one who does evil has not seen God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.12', 'BSB', 'Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone, and from the truth itself. We also testify for him, and you know that our testimony is true.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.13', 'BSB', 'I have many things to write to you, but I would prefer not to do so with pen and ink.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('3John.1.14', 'BSB', 'Instead, I hope to see you soon and speak with you face to face. Peace to you. The friends here send you greetings. Greet each of our friends there by name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.1', 'BSB', 'Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ and a brother of James, To those who are called, loved by God the Father, and kept in Jesus Christ:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.2', 'BSB', 'Mercy, peace, and love be multiplied to you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.3', 'BSB', 'Beloved, although I made every effort to write to you about the salvation we share, I felt it necessary to write and urge you to contend earnestly for the faith entrusted once for all to the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.4', 'BSB', 'For certain men have crept in among you unnoticed—ungodly ones who were designated long ago for condemnation. They turn the grace of our God into a license for immorality, and they deny our only Master and Lord, Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.5', 'BSB', 'Although you are fully aware of this, I want to remind you that after Jesus had delivered His people out of the land of Egypt, He destroyed those who did not believe.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.6', 'BSB', 'And the angels who did not stay within their own domain but abandoned their proper dwelling—these He has kept in eternal chains under darkness, bound for judgment on that great day.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.7', 'BSB', 'In like manner, Sodom and Gomorrah and the cities around them, who indulged in sexual immorality and pursued strange flesh, are on display as an example of those who sustain the punishment of eternal fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.8', 'BSB', 'Yet in the same way these dreamers defile their bodies, reject authority, and slander glorious beings.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.9', 'BSB', 'But even the archangel Michael, when he disputed with the devil over the body of Moses, did not presume to bring a slanderous charge against him, but said, “The Lord rebuke you!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.10', 'BSB', 'These men, however, slander what they do not understand, and like irrational animals, they will be destroyed by the things they do instinctively.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.11', 'BSB', 'Woe to them! They have traveled the path of Cain; they have rushed headlong into the error of Balaam; they have perished in Korah’s rebellion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.12', 'BSB', 'These men are hidden reefs in your love feasts, shamelessly feasting with you but shepherding only themselves. They are clouds without water, carried along by the wind; fruitless trees in autumn, twice dead after being uprooted.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.13', 'BSB', 'They are wild waves of the sea, foaming up their own shame; wandering stars, for whom blackest darkness has been reserved forever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.14', 'BSB', 'Enoch, the seventh from Adam, also prophesied about them: “Behold, the Lord is coming with myriads of His holy ones', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.15', 'BSB', 'to execute judgment on everyone, and to convict all the ungodly of every ungodly act of wickedness and every harsh word spoken against Him by ungodly sinners.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.16', 'BSB', 'These men are discontented grumblers, following after their own lusts; their mouths spew arrogance; they flatter others for their own advantage.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.17', 'BSB', 'But you, beloved, remember what was foretold by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.18', 'BSB', 'when they said to you, “In the last times there will be scoffers who will follow after their own ungodly desires.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.19', 'BSB', 'These are the ones who cause divisions, who are worldly and devoid of the Spirit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.20', 'BSB', 'But you, beloved, by building yourselves up in your most holy faith and praying in the Holy Spirit,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.21', 'BSB', 'keep yourselves in the love of God as you await the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to bring you eternal life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.22', 'BSB', 'And indeed, have mercy on those who doubt;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.23', 'BSB', 'save others by snatching them from the fire; and to still others show mercy tempered with fear, hating even the clothing stained by the flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.24', 'BSB', 'Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you unblemished in His glorious presence, with great joy—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Jude.1.25', 'BSB', 'to the only God our Savior be glory, majesty, dominion, and authority through Jesus Christ our Lord before all time, and now, and for all eternity. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.1', 'BSB', 'This is the revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave Him to show His servants what must soon come to pass. He made it known by sending His angel to His servant John,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.2', 'BSB', 'who testifies to everything he saw. This is the word of God and the testimony of Jesus Christ.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.3', 'BSB', 'Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of this prophecy, and blessed are those who hear and obey what is written in it, because the time is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.4', 'BSB', 'John, To the seven churches in the province of Asia: Grace and peace to you from Him who is and was and is to come, and from the seven Spirits before His throne,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.5', 'BSB', 'and from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler of the kings of the earth. To Him who loves us and has released us from our sins by His blood,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.6', 'BSB', 'who has made us to be a kingdom, priests to His God and Father—to Him be the glory and power forever and ever! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.7', 'BSB', 'Behold, He is coming with the clouds, and every eye will see Him—even those who pierced Him. And all the tribes of the earth will mourn because of Him. So shall it be! Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.8', 'BSB', '“I am the Alpha and the Omega,” says the Lord God, who is and was and is to come—the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.9', 'BSB', 'I, John, your brother and partner in the tribulation and kingdom and perseverance that are in Jesus, was on the island of Patmos because of the word of God and my testimony about Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.10', 'BSB', 'On the Lord’s day I was in the Spirit, and I heard behind me a loud voice like a trumpet,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.11', 'BSB', 'saying, “Write on a scroll what you see and send it to the seven churches: to Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.12', 'BSB', 'Then I turned to see the voice that was speaking with me. And having turned, I saw seven golden lampstands,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.13', 'BSB', 'and among the lampstands was One like the Son of Man, dressed in a long robe, with a golden sash around His chest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.14', 'BSB', 'The hair of His head was white like wool, as white as snow, and His eyes were like a blazing fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.15', 'BSB', 'His feet were like polished bronze refined in a furnace, and His voice was like the roar of many waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.16', 'BSB', 'He held in His right hand seven stars, and a sharp double-edged sword came from His mouth. His face was like the sun shining at its brightest.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.17', 'BSB', 'When I saw Him, I fell at His feet like a dead man. But He placed His right hand on me and said, “Do not be afraid. I am the First and the Last,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.18', 'BSB', 'the Living One. I was dead, and behold, now I am alive forever and ever! And I hold the keys of Death and of Hades.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.19', 'BSB', 'Therefore write down the things you have seen, and the things that are, and the things that will happen after this.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.1.20', 'BSB', 'This is the mystery of the seven stars you saw in My right hand and of the seven golden lampstands: The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.1', 'BSB', '“To the angel of the church in Ephesus write: These are the words of Him who holds the seven stars in His right hand and walks among the seven golden lampstands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.2', 'BSB', 'I know your deeds, your labor, and your perseverance. I know that you cannot tolerate those who are evil, and you have tested and exposed as liars those who falsely claim to be apostles.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.3', 'BSB', 'Without growing weary, you have persevered and endured many things for the sake of My name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.4', 'BSB', 'But I have this against you: You have abandoned your first love.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.5', 'BSB', 'Therefore, keep in mind how far you have fallen. Repent and perform the deeds you did at first. But if you do not repent, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.6', 'BSB', 'But you have this to your credit: You hate the works of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.7', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to eat from the tree of life in the Paradise of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.8', 'BSB', 'To the angel of the church in Smyrna write: These are the words of the First and the Last, who died and returned to life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.9', 'BSB', 'I know your affliction and your poverty—though you are rich! And I am aware of the slander of those who falsely claim to be Jews, but are in fact a synagogue of Satan.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.10', 'BSB', 'Do not fear what you are about to suffer. Look, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison to test you, and you will suffer tribulation for ten days. Be faithful even unto death, and I will give you the crown of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.11', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. The one who overcomes will not be harmed by the second death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.12', 'BSB', 'To the angel of the church in Pergamum write: These are the words of the One who holds the sharp, double-edged sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.13', 'BSB', 'I know where you live, where the throne of Satan sits. Yet you have held fast to My name and have not denied your faith in Me, even in the day when My faithful witness Antipas was killed among you, where Satan dwells.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.14', 'BSB', 'But I have a few things against you, because some of you hold to the teaching of Balaam, who taught Balak to place a stumbling block before the Israelites so they would eat food sacrificed to idols and commit sexual immorality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.15', 'BSB', 'In the same way, some of you also hold to the teaching of the Nicolaitans.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.16', 'BSB', 'Therefore repent! Otherwise I will come to you shortly and wage war against them with the sword of My mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.17', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches. To the one who overcomes, I will give the hidden manna. I will also give him a white stone inscribed with a new name, known only to the one who receives it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.18', 'BSB', 'To the angel of the church in Thyatira write: These are the words of the Son of God, whose eyes are like a blazing fire and whose feet are like polished bronze.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.19', 'BSB', 'I know your deeds—your love, your faith, your service, your perseverance—and your latter deeds are greater than your first.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.20', 'BSB', 'But I have this against you: You tolerate that woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess. By her teaching she misleads My servants to be sexually immoral and to eat food sacrificed to idols.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.21', 'BSB', 'Even though I have given her time to repent of her immorality, she is unwilling.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.22', 'BSB', 'Behold, I will cast her onto a bed of sickness, and those who commit adultery with her will suffer great tribulation unless they repent of her deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.23', 'BSB', 'Then I will strike her children dead, and all the churches will know that I am the One who searches minds and hearts, and I will repay each of you according to your deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.24', 'BSB', 'But I say to the rest of you in Thyatira, who do not hold to her teaching and have not learned the so-called deep things of Satan: I will place no further burden upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.25', 'BSB', 'Nevertheless, hold fast to what you have until I come.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.26', 'BSB', 'And to the one who overcomes and continues in My work until the end, I will give authority over the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.27', 'BSB', 'He will rule them with an iron scepter and shatter them like pottery —just as I have received authority from My Father.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.28', 'BSB', 'And I will give him the morning star.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.2.29', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.1', 'BSB', '“To the angel of the church in Sardis write: These are the words of the One who holds the seven Spirits of God and the seven stars. I know your deeds; you have a reputation for being alive, yet you are dead.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.2', 'BSB', 'Wake up and strengthen what remains, which was about to die; for I have found your deeds incomplete in the sight of My God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.3', 'BSB', 'Remember, then, what you have received and heard. Keep it and repent. If you do not wake up, I will come like a thief, and you will not know the hour when I will come upon you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.4', 'BSB', 'But you do have a few people in Sardis who have not soiled their garments, and because they are worthy, they will walk with Me in white.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.5', 'BSB', 'Like them, he who overcomes will be dressed in white. And I will never blot out his name from the Book of Life, but I will confess his name before My Father and His angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.6', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.7', 'BSB', 'To the angel of the church in Philadelphia write: These are the words of the One who is holy and true, who holds the key of David. What He opens no one can shut, and what He shuts no one can open.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.8', 'BSB', 'I know your deeds. See, I have placed before you an open door, which no one can shut. For you have only a little strength, yet you have kept My word and have not denied My name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.9', 'BSB', 'Look at those who belong to the synagogue of Satan, who claim to be Jews but are liars instead. I will make them come and bow down at your feet, and they will know that I love you.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.10', 'BSB', 'Because you have kept My command to persevere, I will also keep you from the hour of testing that is about to come upon the whole world, to test those who dwell on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.11', 'BSB', 'I am coming soon. Hold fast to what you have, so that no one will take your crown.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.12', 'BSB', 'The one who overcomes I will make a pillar in the temple of My God, and he will never again leave it. Upon him I will write the name of My God, and the name of the city of My God (the new Jerusalem that comes down out of heaven from My God), and My new name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.13', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.14', 'BSB', 'To the angel of the church in Laodicea write: These are the words of the Amen, the faithful and true Witness, the Originator of God’s creation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.15', 'BSB', 'I know your deeds; you are neither cold nor hot. How I wish you were one or the other!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.16', 'BSB', 'So because you are lukewarm—neither hot nor cold—I am about to vomit you out of My mouth!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.17', 'BSB', 'You say, ‘I am rich; I have grown wealthy and need nothing.’ But you do not realize that you are wretched, pitiful, poor, blind, and naked.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.18', 'BSB', 'I counsel you to buy from Me gold refined by fire so that you may become rich, white garments so that you may be clothed and your shameful nakedness not exposed, and salve to anoint your eyes so that you may see.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.19', 'BSB', 'Those I love, I rebuke and discipline. Therefore be earnest and repent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.20', 'BSB', 'Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will come in and dine with him, and he with Me.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.21', 'BSB', 'To the one who overcomes, I will grant the right to sit with Me on My throne, just as I overcame and sat down with My Father on His throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.3.22', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the churches.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.1', 'BSB', 'After this I looked and saw a door standing open in heaven. And the voice I had previously heard speak to me like a trumpet was saying, “Come up here, and I will show you what must happen after these things.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.2', 'BSB', 'At once I was in the Spirit, and I saw a throne standing in heaven, with someone seated on it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.3', 'BSB', 'The One seated there looked like jasper and carnelian, and a rainbow that gleamed like an emerald encircled the throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.4', 'BSB', 'Surrounding the throne were twenty-four other thrones, and on these thrones sat twenty-four elders dressed in white, with golden crowns on their heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.5', 'BSB', 'From the throne came flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder. Before the throne burned seven torches of fire. These are the seven Spirits of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.6', 'BSB', 'And before the throne was something like a sea of glass, as clear as crystal. In the center, around the throne, were four living creatures, covered with eyes in front and back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.7', 'BSB', 'The first living creature was like a lion, the second like a calf, the third had a face like a man, and the fourth was like an eagle in flight.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.8', 'BSB', 'And each of the four living creatures had six wings and was covered with eyes all around and within. Day and night they never stop saying: “Holy, Holy, Holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.9', 'BSB', 'And whenever the living creatures give glory, honor, and thanks to the One seated on the throne who lives forever and ever,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.10', 'BSB', 'the twenty-four elders fall down before the One seated on the throne, and they worship Him who lives forever and ever. They cast their crowns before the throne, saying:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.4.11', 'BSB', '“Worthy are You, our Lord and God, to receive glory and honor and power, for You created all things; by Your will they exist and came to be.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw a scroll in the right hand of the One seated on the throne. It had writing on both sides and was sealed with seven seals.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.2', 'BSB', 'And I saw a mighty angel proclaiming in a loud voice, “Who is worthy to break the seals and open the scroll?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.3', 'BSB', 'But no one in heaven or on earth or under the earth was able to open the scroll or look inside it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.4', 'BSB', 'And I began to weep bitterly, because no one was found worthy to open the scroll or look inside it.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.5', 'BSB', 'Then one of the elders said to me, “Do not weep! Behold, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has triumphed to open the scroll and its seven seals.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.6', 'BSB', 'Then I saw a Lamb who appeared to have been slain, standing in the center of the throne, encircled by the four living creatures and the elders. The Lamb had seven horns and seven eyes, which represent the seven Spirits of God sent out into all the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.7', 'BSB', 'And He came and took the scroll from the right hand of the One seated on the throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.8', 'BSB', 'When He had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb. Each one had a harp, and they were holding golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.9', 'BSB', 'And they sang a new song: “Worthy are You to take the scroll and open its seals, because You were slain, and by Your blood You purchased for God those from every tribe and tongue and people and nation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.10', 'BSB', 'You have made them to be a kingdom and priests to serve our God, and they will reign upon the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.11', 'BSB', 'Then I looked, and I heard the voices of many angels and living creatures and elders encircling the throne, and their number was myriads of myriads and thousands of thousands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.12', 'BSB', 'In a loud voice they were saying: “Worthy is the Lamb, who was slain, to receive power and riches and wisdom and strength and honor and glory and blessing!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.13', 'BSB', 'And I heard every creature in heaven and on earth and under the earth and in the sea, and all that is in them, saying: “To Him who sits on the throne and to the Lamb be praise and honor and glory and power forever and ever!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.5.14', 'BSB', 'And the four living creatures said, “Amen,” and the elders fell down and worshiped.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.1', 'BSB', 'Then I watched as the Lamb opened one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures say in a thunderous voice, “Come!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.2', 'BSB', 'So I looked and saw a white horse, and its rider held a bow. And he was given a crown, and he rode out to overcome and conquer.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.3', 'BSB', 'And when the Lamb opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature say, “Come!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.4', 'BSB', 'Then another horse went forth. It was bright red, and its rider was granted permission to take away peace from the earth and to make men slay one another. And he was given a great sword.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.5', 'BSB', 'And when the Lamb opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature say, “Come!” Then I looked and saw a black horse, and its rider held in his hand a pair of scales.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.6', 'BSB', 'And I heard what sounded like a voice from among the four living creatures, saying, “A quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius, and do not harm the oil and wine.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.7', 'BSB', 'And when the Lamb opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature say, “Come!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.8', 'BSB', 'Then I looked and saw a pale green horse. Its rider’s name was Death, and Hades followed close behind. And they were given authority over a fourth of the earth, to kill by sword, by famine, by plague, and by the beasts of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.9', 'BSB', 'And when the Lamb opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of those who had been slain for the word of God and for the testimony they had upheld.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.10', 'BSB', 'And they cried out in a loud voice, “How long, O Lord, holy and true, until You avenge our blood and judge those who dwell upon the earth?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.11', 'BSB', 'Then each of them was given a white robe and told to rest a little while longer, until the full number of their fellow servants, their brothers, were killed, just as they had been killed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.12', 'BSB', 'And when I saw the Lamb open the sixth seal, there was a great earthquake, and the sun became black like sackcloth of goat hair, and the whole moon turned blood red,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.13', 'BSB', 'and the stars of the sky fell to the earth like unripe figs dropping from a tree shaken by a great wind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.14', 'BSB', 'The sky receded like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved from its place.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.15', 'BSB', 'Then the kings of the earth, the nobles, the commanders, the rich, the mighty, and every slave and free man hid in the caves and among the rocks of the mountains.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.16', 'BSB', 'And they said to the mountains and the rocks, “Fall on us and hide us from the face of the One seated on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.6.17', 'BSB', 'For the great day of Their wrath has come, and who is able to withstand it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.1', 'BSB', 'After this I saw four angels standing at the four corners of the earth, holding back its four winds so that no wind would blow on land or sea or on any tree.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.2', 'BSB', 'And I saw another angel ascending from the east, with the seal of the living God. And he called out in a loud voice to the four angels who had been given power to harm the land and the sea:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.3', 'BSB', '“Do not harm the land or sea or trees until we have sealed the foreheads of the servants of our God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.4', 'BSB', 'And I heard the number of those who were sealed, 144,000 from all the tribes of Israel:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.5', 'BSB', 'From the tribe of Judah 12,000 were sealed, from the tribe of Reuben 12,000, from the tribe of Gad 12,000,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.6', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Asher 12,000, from the tribe of Naphtali 12,000, from the tribe of Manasseh 12,000,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.7', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Simeon 12,000, from the tribe of Levi 12,000, from the tribe of Issachar 12,000,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.8', 'BSB', 'from the tribe of Zebulun 12,000, from the tribe of Joseph 12,000, and from the tribe of Benjamin 12,000.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.9', 'BSB', 'After this I looked and saw a multitude too large to count, from every nation and tribe and people and tongue, standing before the throne and before the Lamb. They were wearing white robes and holding palm branches in their hands.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.10', 'BSB', 'And they cried out in a loud voice: “Salvation to our God, who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.11', 'BSB', 'And all the angels stood around the throne and around the elders and the four living creatures. And they fell facedown before the throne and worshiped God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.12', 'BSB', 'saying, “Amen! Blessing and glory and wisdom and thanks and honor and power and strength be to our God forever and ever! Amen.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.13', 'BSB', 'Then one of the elders addressed me: “These in white robes,” he asked, “who are they, and where have they come from?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.14', 'BSB', '“Sir,” I answered, “you know.” So he replied, “These are the ones who have come out of the great tribulation; they have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.15', 'BSB', 'For this reason, they are before the throne of God and serve Him day and night in His temple; and the One seated on the throne will spread His tabernacle over them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.16', 'BSB', '‘Never again will they hunger, and never will they thirst; nor will the sun beat down upon them, nor any scorching heat.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.7.17', 'BSB', 'For the Lamb in the center of the throne will be their shepherd. ‘He will lead them to springs of living water,’ and ‘God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.’”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.1', 'BSB', 'When the Lamb opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.2', 'BSB', 'And I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and they were given seven trumpets.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.3', 'BSB', 'Then another angel, who had a golden censer, came and stood at the altar. He was given much incense to offer, along with the prayers of all the saints, on the golden altar before the throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.4', 'BSB', 'And the smoke of the incense, together with the prayers of the saints, rose up before God from the hand of the angel.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.5', 'BSB', 'Then the angel took the censer, filled it with fire from the altar, and hurled it to the earth; and there were peals of thunder, and rumblings, and flashes of lightning, and an earthquake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.6', 'BSB', 'And the seven angels with the seven trumpets prepared to sound them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.7', 'BSB', 'Then the first angel sounded his trumpet, and hail and fire mixed with blood were hurled down upon the earth. A third of the earth was burned up, along with a third of the trees and all the green grass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.8', 'BSB', 'Then the second angel sounded his trumpet, and something like a great mountain burning with fire was thrown into the sea. A third of the sea turned to blood,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.9', 'BSB', 'a third of the living creatures in the sea died, and a third of the ships were destroyed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.10', 'BSB', 'Then the third angel sounded his trumpet, and a great star burning like a torch fell from heaven and landed on a third of the rivers and on the springs of water.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.11', 'BSB', 'The name of the star is Wormwood. A third of the waters turned bitter like wormwood oil, and many people died from the bitter waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.12', 'BSB', 'Then the fourth angel sounded his trumpet, and a third of the sun and moon and stars were struck. A third of the stars were darkened, a third of the day was without light, and a third of the night as well.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.8.13', 'BSB', 'And as I observed, I heard an eagle flying overhead, calling in a loud voice, “Woe! Woe! Woe to those who dwell on the earth, because of the trumpet blasts about to be sounded by the remaining three angels!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.1', 'BSB', 'Then the fifth angel sounded his trumpet, and I saw a star that had fallen from heaven to earth, and it was given the key to the pit of the Abyss.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.2', 'BSB', 'The star opened the pit of the Abyss, and smoke rose out of it like the smoke of a great furnace, and the sun and the air were darkened by the smoke from the pit.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.3', 'BSB', 'And out of the smoke, locusts descended on the earth, and they were given power like that of the scorpions of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.4', 'BSB', 'They were told not to harm the grass of the earth or any plant or tree, but only those who did not have the seal of God on their foreheads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.5', 'BSB', 'The locusts were not given power to kill them, but only to torment them for five months, and their torment was like the stinging of a scorpion.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.6', 'BSB', 'In those days men will seek death and will not find it; they will long to die, but death will escape them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.7', 'BSB', 'And the locusts looked like horses prepared for battle, with something like crowns of gold on their heads, and faces like the faces of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.8', 'BSB', 'They had hair like that of women, and teeth like those of lions.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.9', 'BSB', 'They also had thoraxes like breastplates of iron, and the sound of their wings was like the roar of many horses and chariots rushing into battle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.10', 'BSB', 'They had tails with stingers like scorpions, which had the power to injure people for five months.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.11', 'BSB', 'They were ruled by a king, the angel of the Abyss. His name in Hebrew is Abaddon, and in Greek it is Apollyon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.12', 'BSB', 'The first woe has passed. Behold, two woes are still to follow.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.13', 'BSB', 'Then the sixth angel sounded his trumpet, and I heard a voice from the four horns of the golden altar before God', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.14', 'BSB', 'saying to the sixth angel with the trumpet, “Release the four angels who are bound at the great river Euphrates.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.15', 'BSB', 'So the four angels who had been prepared for this hour and day and month and year were released to kill a third of mankind.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.16', 'BSB', 'And the number of mounted troops was two hundred million; I heard their number.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.17', 'BSB', 'Now the horses and riders in my vision looked like this: The riders had breastplates the colors of fire, sapphire, and sulfur. The heads of the horses were like the heads of lions, and out of their mouths proceeded fire, smoke, and sulfur.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.18', 'BSB', 'A third of mankind was killed by the three plagues of fire, smoke, and sulfur that proceeded from their mouths.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.19', 'BSB', 'For the power of the horses was in their mouths and in their tails; indeed, their tails were like snakes, having heads with which to inflict harm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.20', 'BSB', 'Now the rest of mankind who were not killed by these plagues still did not repent of the works of their hands. They did not stop worshiping demons and idols of gold, silver, bronze, stone, and wood, which cannot see or hear or walk.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.9.21', 'BSB', 'Furthermore, they did not repent of their murder, sorcery, sexual immorality, and theft.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw another mighty angel coming down from heaven, wrapped in a cloud, with a rainbow above his head. His face was like the sun, and his legs were like pillars of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.2', 'BSB', 'He held in his hand a small scroll, which lay open. He placed his right foot on the sea and his left foot on the land.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.3', 'BSB', 'Then he cried out in a loud voice like the roar of a lion. And when he cried out, the seven thunders sounded their voices.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.4', 'BSB', 'When the seven thunders had spoken, I was about to put it in writing. But I heard a voice from heaven saying, “Seal up what the seven thunders have said, and do not write it down.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.5', 'BSB', 'Then the angel I had seen standing on the sea and on the land lifted up his right hand to heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.6', 'BSB', 'And he swore by Him who lives forever and ever, who created heaven and everything in it, the earth and everything in it, and the sea and everything in it: “There will be no more delay!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.7', 'BSB', 'But in the days of the voice of the seventh angel, when he is about to sound his trumpet, the mystery of God will be fulfilled, just as He proclaimed to His servants the prophets.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.8', 'BSB', 'Then the voice that I had heard from heaven spoke to me again, saying, “Go, take the small scroll that lies open in the hand of the angel standing on the sea and on the land.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.9', 'BSB', 'And I went to the angel and said, “Give me the small scroll.” “Take it and eat it,” he said. “It will make your stomach bitter, but in your mouth it will be as sweet as honey.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.10', 'BSB', 'So I took the small scroll from the angel’s hand and ate it; and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth, but when I had eaten it, my stomach turned bitter.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.10.11', 'BSB', 'And they told me, “You must prophesy again about many peoples and nations and tongues and kings.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.1', 'BSB', 'Then I was given a measuring rod like a staff and was told, “Go and measure the temple of God and the altar, and count the number of worshipers there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.2', 'BSB', 'But exclude the courtyard outside the temple. Do not measure it, because it has been given over to the nations, and they will trample the holy city for 42 months.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.3', 'BSB', 'And I will empower my two witnesses, and they will prophesy for 1,260 days, clothed in sackcloth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.4', 'BSB', 'These witnesses are the two olive trees and the two lampstands that stand before the Lord of the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.5', 'BSB', 'If anyone wants to harm them, fire proceeds from their mouths and devours their enemies. In this way, anyone who wants to harm them must be killed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.6', 'BSB', 'These witnesses have power to shut the sky so that no rain will fall during the days of their prophecy, and power to turn the waters into blood and to strike the earth with every kind of plague as often as they wish.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.7', 'BSB', 'When the two witnesses have finished their testimony, the beast that comes up from the Abyss will wage war with them, and will overpower and kill them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.8', 'BSB', 'Their bodies will lie in the street of the great city—figuratively called Sodom and Egypt—where their Lord was also crucified.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.9', 'BSB', 'For three and a half days all peoples and tribes and tongues and nations will view their bodies and will not permit them to be laid in a tomb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.10', 'BSB', 'And those who dwell on the earth will gloat over them, and will celebrate and send one another gifts, because these two prophets had tormented them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.11', 'BSB', 'But after the three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered the two witnesses, and they stood on their feet, and great fear fell upon those who saw them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.12', 'BSB', 'And the witnesses heard a loud voice from heaven saying, “Come up here.” And they went up to heaven in a cloud as their enemies watched them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.13', 'BSB', 'And in that hour there was a great earthquake, and a tenth of the city collapsed. Seven thousand were killed in the quake, and the rest were terrified and gave glory to the God of heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.14', 'BSB', 'The second woe has passed. Behold, the third woe is coming shortly.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.15', 'BSB', 'Then the seventh angel sounded his trumpet, and loud voices called out in heaven: “The kingdom of the world has become the kingdom of our Lord and of His Christ, and He will reign forever and ever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.16', 'BSB', 'And the twenty-four elders who sit on their thrones before God fell on their faces and worshiped God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.17', 'BSB', 'saying: “We give thanks to You, O Lord God Almighty, the One who is and who was, because You have taken Your great power and have begun to reign.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.18', 'BSB', 'The nations were enraged, and Your wrath has come. The time has come to judge the dead and to reward Your servants the prophets, as well as the saints and those who fear Your name, both small and great— and to destroy those who destroy the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.11.19', 'BSB', 'Then the temple of God in heaven was opened, and the ark of His covenant appeared in His temple. And there were flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder, and an earthquake, and a great hailstorm.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.1', 'BSB', 'And a great sign appeared in heaven: a woman clothed in the sun, with the moon under her feet and a crown of twelve stars on her head.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.2', 'BSB', 'She was pregnant and crying out in the pain and agony of giving birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.3', 'BSB', 'Then another sign appeared in heaven: a huge red dragon with seven heads, ten horns, and seven royal crowns on his heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.4', 'BSB', 'His tail swept a third of the stars from the sky, tossing them to the earth. And the dragon stood before the woman who was about to give birth, ready to devour her child as soon as she gave birth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.5', 'BSB', 'And she gave birth to a son, a male child, who will rule all the nations with an iron scepter. And her child was caught up to God and to His throne.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.6', 'BSB', 'And the woman fled into the wilderness, where God had prepared a place for her to be nourished for 1,260 days.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.7', 'BSB', 'Then a war broke out in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon, and the dragon and his angels fought back.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.8', 'BSB', 'But the dragon was not strong enough, and no longer was any place found in heaven for him and his angels.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.9', 'BSB', 'And the great dragon was hurled down—that ancient serpent called the devil and Satan, the deceiver of the whole world. He was hurled to the earth, and his angels with him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.10', 'BSB', 'And I heard a loud voice in heaven saying: “Now have come the salvation and the power and the kingdom of our God, and the authority of His Christ. For the accuser of our brothers has been thrown down— he who accuses them day and night before our God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.11', 'BSB', 'They have conquered him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimony. And they did not love their lives so as to shy away from death.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.12', 'BSB', 'Therefore rejoice, O heavens, and you who dwell in them! But woe to the earth and the sea; with great fury the devil has come down to you, knowing he has only a short time.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.13', 'BSB', 'And when the dragon saw that he had been thrown to the earth, he pursued the woman who had given birth to the male child.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.14', 'BSB', 'But the woman was given two wings of a great eagle to fly from the presence of the serpent to her place in the wilderness, where she was nourished for a time, and times, and half a time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.15', 'BSB', 'Then from the mouth of the serpent spewed water like a river to overtake the woman and sweep her away in the torrent.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.16', 'BSB', 'But the earth helped the woman and opened its mouth to swallow up the river that had poured from the dragon’s mouth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.12.17', 'BSB', 'And the dragon was enraged at the woman, and went to make war with the rest of her children, who keep the commandments of God and hold to the testimony of Jesus. And the dragon stood on the shore of the sea.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw a beast with ten horns and seven heads rising out of the sea. There were ten royal crowns on its horns and blasphemous names on its heads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.2', 'BSB', 'The beast I saw was like a leopard, with the feet of a bear and the mouth of a lion. And the dragon gave the beast his power and his throne and great authority.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.3', 'BSB', 'One of the heads of the beast appeared to be mortally wounded. But the mortal wound was healed, and the whole world marveled and followed the beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.4', 'BSB', 'They worshiped the dragon who had given authority to the beast, and they worshiped the beast, saying, “Who is like the beast, and who can wage war against it?”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.5', 'BSB', 'The beast was given a mouth to speak arrogant and blasphemous words, and authority to act for 42 months.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.6', 'BSB', 'And the beast opened its mouth to speak blasphemies against God and to slander His name and His tabernacle—those who dwell in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.7', 'BSB', 'Then the beast was permitted to wage war against the saints and to conquer them, and it was given authority over every tribe and people and tongue and nation.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.8', 'BSB', 'And all who dwell on the earth will worship the beast—all whose names have not been written from the foundation of the world in the Book of Life belonging to the Lamb who was slain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.9', 'BSB', 'He who has an ear, let him hear:', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.10', 'BSB', '“If anyone is destined for captivity, into captivity he will go; if anyone is to die by the sword, by the sword he must be killed.” Here is a call for the perseverance and faith of the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.11', 'BSB', 'Then I saw another beast rising out of the earth. This beast had two horns like a lamb, but spoke like a dragon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.12', 'BSB', 'And this beast exercised all the authority of the first beast and caused the earth and those who dwell in it to worship the first beast, whose mortal wound had been healed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.13', 'BSB', 'And the second beast performed great signs to cause even fire from heaven to come down to earth in the presence of the people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.14', 'BSB', 'Because of the signs it was given to perform on behalf of the first beast, it deceived those who dwell on the earth, telling them to make an image to the beast that had been wounded by the sword and yet had lived.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.15', 'BSB', 'The second beast was permitted to give breath to the image of the first beast, so that the image could speak and cause all who refused to worship it to be killed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.16', 'BSB', 'And the second beast required all people small and great, rich and poor, free and slave, to receive a mark on their right hand or on their forehead,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.17', 'BSB', 'so that no one could buy or sell unless he had the mark—the name of the beast or the number of its name.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.13.18', 'BSB', 'Here is a call for wisdom: Let the one who has insight calculate the number of the beast, for it is the number of a man, and that number is 666.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.1', 'BSB', 'Then I looked and saw the Lamb standing on Mount Zion, and with Him 144,000 who had His name and His Father’s name written on their foreheads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.2', 'BSB', 'And I heard a sound from heaven like the roar of many waters and the loud rumbling of thunder. And the sound I heard was like harpists strumming their harps.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.3', 'BSB', 'And they sang a new song before the throne and before the four living creatures and the elders. And no one could learn the song except the 144,000 who had been redeemed from the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.4', 'BSB', 'These are the ones who have not been defiled with women, for they are virgins. They follow the Lamb wherever He goes. They have been redeemed from among men as firstfruits to God and to the Lamb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.5', 'BSB', 'And no lie was found in their mouths; they are blameless.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.6', 'BSB', 'Then I saw another angel flying overhead, with the eternal gospel to proclaim to those who dwell on the earth—to every nation and tribe and tongue and people.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.7', 'BSB', 'And he said in a loud voice, “Fear God and give Him glory, because the hour of His judgment has come. Worship the One who made the heavens and the earth and the sea and the springs of waters.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.8', 'BSB', 'Then a second angel followed, saying, “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great, who has made all the nations drink the wine of the passion of her immorality.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.9', 'BSB', 'And a third angel followed them, calling out in a loud voice, “If anyone worships the beast and its image, and receives its mark on his forehead or on his hand,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.10', 'BSB', 'he too will drink the wine of God’s anger, poured undiluted into the cup of His wrath. And he will be tormented in fire and sulfur in the presence of the holy angels and of the Lamb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.11', 'BSB', 'And the smoke of their torment rises forever and ever. Day and night there is no rest for those who worship the beast and its image, or for anyone who receives the mark of its name.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.12', 'BSB', 'Here is a call for the perseverance of the saints who keep the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.13', 'BSB', 'And I heard a voice from heaven telling me to write, “Blessed are the dead—those who die in the Lord from this moment on.” “Yes,” says the Spirit, “they will rest from their labors, for their deeds will follow them.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.14', 'BSB', 'And I looked and saw a white cloud, and seated on the cloud was One like the Son of Man, with a golden crown on His head and a sharp sickle in His hand.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.15', 'BSB', 'Then another angel came out of the temple, crying out in a loud voice to the One seated on the cloud, “Swing Your sickle and reap, because the time has come to harvest; for the crop of the earth is ripe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.16', 'BSB', 'So the One seated on the cloud swung His sickle over the earth, and the earth was harvested.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.17', 'BSB', 'Then another angel came out of the temple in heaven, and he too had a sharp sickle.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.18', 'BSB', 'Still another angel, with authority over the fire, came from the altar and called out in a loud voice to the angel with the sharp sickle, “Swing your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of grapes from the vine of the earth, because its grapes are ripe.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.19', 'BSB', 'So the angel swung his sickle over the earth and gathered the grapes of the earth, and he threw them into the great winepress of God’s wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.14.20', 'BSB', 'And the winepress was trodden outside the city, and the blood that flowed from it rose as high as the bridles of the horses for a distance of 1,600 stadia.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw another great and marvelous sign in heaven: seven angels with the seven final plagues, with which the wrath of God is completed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.2', 'BSB', 'And I saw something like a sea of glass mixed with fire, beside which stood those who had conquered the beast and its image and the number of its name. They were holding harps from God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.3', 'BSB', 'and they sang the song of God’s servant Moses and of the Lamb: “Great and wonderful are Your works, O Lord God Almighty! Just and true are Your ways, O King of the nations!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.4', 'BSB', 'Who will not fear You, O Lord, and glorify Your name? For You alone are holy. All nations will come and worship before You, for Your righteous acts have been revealed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.5', 'BSB', 'After this I looked, and the temple—the tabernacle of the Testimony—was opened in heaven.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.6', 'BSB', 'And out of the temple came the seven angels with the seven plagues, dressed in clean and bright linen and girded with golden sashes around their chests.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.7', 'BSB', 'Then one of the four living creatures gave the seven angels seven golden bowls full of the wrath of God, who lives forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.15.8', 'BSB', 'And the temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God and from His power; and no one could enter the temple until the seven plagues of the seven angels were completed.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.1', 'BSB', 'Then I heard a loud voice from the temple saying to the seven angels, “Go, pour out on the earth the seven bowls of God’s wrath.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.2', 'BSB', 'So the first angel went and poured out his bowl on the earth, and loathsome, malignant sores broke out on those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.3', 'BSB', 'And the second angel poured out his bowl into the sea, and it turned to blood like that of the dead, and every living thing in the sea died.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.4', 'BSB', 'And the third angel poured out his bowl into the rivers and springs of water, and they turned to blood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.5', 'BSB', 'And I heard the angel of the waters say: “Righteous are You, O Holy One, who is and was, because You have brought these judgments.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.6', 'BSB', 'For they have spilled the blood of saints and prophets, and You have given them blood to drink, as they deserve.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.7', 'BSB', 'And I heard the altar reply: “Yes, Lord God Almighty, true and just are Your judgments.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.8', 'BSB', 'Then the fourth angel poured out his bowl on the sun, and it was given power to scorch the people with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.9', 'BSB', 'And the people were scorched by intense heat, and they cursed the name of God, who had authority over these plagues; yet they did not repent and give Him glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.10', 'BSB', 'And the fifth angel poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast, and its kingdom was plunged into darkness, and men began to gnaw their tongues in anguish', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.11', 'BSB', 'and curse the God of heaven for their pains and sores; yet they did not repent of their deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.12', 'BSB', 'And the sixth angel poured out his bowl on the great river Euphrates, and its water was dried up to prepare the way for the kings of the East.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.13', 'BSB', 'And I saw three unclean spirits that looked like frogs coming out of the mouths of the dragon, the beast, and the false prophet.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.14', 'BSB', 'These are demonic spirits that perform signs and go out to all the kings of the earth, to assemble them for battle on the great day of God the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.15', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am coming like a thief. Blessed is the one who remains awake and clothed, so that he will not go naked and let his shame be exposed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.16', 'BSB', 'And they assembled the kings in the place that in Hebrew is called Armageddon.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.17', 'BSB', 'Then the seventh angel poured out his bowl into the air, and a loud voice came from the throne in the temple, saying, “It is done!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.18', 'BSB', 'And there were flashes of lightning, and rumblings, and peals of thunder, and a great earthquake the likes of which had not occurred since men were upon the earth—so mighty was the great quake.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.19', 'BSB', 'The great city was split into three parts, and the cities of the nations collapsed. And God remembered Babylon the great and gave her the cup of the wine of the fury of His wrath.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.20', 'BSB', 'Then every island fled, and no mountain could be found.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.16.21', 'BSB', 'And great hailstones weighing almost a hundred pounds each rained down on them from above. And men cursed God for the plague of hail, because it was so horrendous.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.1', 'BSB', 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the punishment of the great prostitute, who sits on many waters.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.2', 'BSB', 'The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and those who dwell on the earth were intoxicated with the wine of her immorality.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.3', 'BSB', 'And the angel carried me away in the Spirit into a wilderness, where I saw a woman sitting on a scarlet beast that was covered with blasphemous names and had seven heads and ten horns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.4', 'BSB', 'The woman was dressed in purple and scarlet, and adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls. She held in her hand a golden cup full of abominations and the impurities of her sexual immorality.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.5', 'BSB', 'And on her forehead a mysterious name was written: BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF PROSTITUTES AND OF THE ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.6', 'BSB', 'I could see that the woman was drunk with the blood of the saints and witnesses for Jesus. And I was utterly amazed at the sight of her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.7', 'BSB', '“Why are you so amazed?” said the angel. “I will tell you the mystery of the woman and of the beast that carries her, which has the seven heads and ten horns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.8', 'BSB', 'The beast that you saw—it was, and now is no more, but is about to come up out of the Abyss and go to its destruction. And those who dwell on the earth whose names were not written in the Book of Life from the foundation of the world will marvel when they see the beast that was, and is not, and yet will be.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.9', 'BSB', 'This calls for a mind with wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman sits.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.10', 'BSB', 'There are also seven kings. Five have fallen, one is, and the other has not yet come; but when he does come, he must remain for only a little while.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.11', 'BSB', 'The beast that was, and now is not, is an eighth king, who belongs to the other seven and is going into destruction.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.12', 'BSB', 'The ten horns you saw are ten kings who have not yet received a kingdom, but will receive one hour of authority as kings, along with the beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.13', 'BSB', 'These kings have one purpose: to yield their power and authority to the beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.14', 'BSB', 'They will make war against the Lamb, and the Lamb will triumph over them, because He is Lord of lords and King of kings; and He will be accompanied by His called and chosen and faithful ones.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.15', 'BSB', 'Then the angel said to me, “The waters you saw, where the prostitute was seated, are peoples and multitudes and nations and tongues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.16', 'BSB', 'And the ten horns and the beast that you saw will hate the prostitute. They will leave her desolate and naked, and will eat her flesh and burn her with fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.17', 'BSB', 'For God has put it into their hearts to carry out His purpose by uniting to give their kingdom to the beast, until the words of God are fulfilled.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.17.18', 'BSB', 'And the woman you saw is the great city that rules over the kings of the earth.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.1', 'BSB', 'After this I saw another angel descending from heaven with great authority, and the earth was illuminated by his glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.2', 'BSB', 'And he cried out in a mighty voice: “Fallen, fallen is Babylon the great! She has become a lair for demons and a haunt for every unclean spirit, every unclean bird, and every detestable beast.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.3', 'BSB', 'All the nations have drunk the wine of the passion of her immorality. The kings of the earth were immoral with her, and the merchants of the earth have grown wealthy from the extravagance of her luxury.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.4', 'BSB', 'Then I heard another voice from heaven say: “Come out of her, My people, so that you will not share in her sins or contract any of her plagues.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.5', 'BSB', 'For her sins are piled up to heaven, and God has remembered her iniquities.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.6', 'BSB', 'Give back to her as she has done to others; pay her back double for what she has done; mix her a double portion in her own cup.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.7', 'BSB', 'As much as she has glorified herself and lived in luxury, give her the same measure of torment and grief. In her heart she says, ‘I sit as queen; I am not a widow and will never see grief.’', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.8', 'BSB', 'Therefore her plagues will come in one day— death and grief and famine— and she will be consumed by fire, for mighty is the Lord God who judges her.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.9', 'BSB', 'Then the kings of the earth who committed sexual immorality and lived in luxury with her will weep and wail at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.10', 'BSB', 'In fear of her torment, they will stand at a distance and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, the mighty city of Babylon! For in a single hour your judgment has come.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.11', 'BSB', 'And the merchants of the earth will weep and mourn over her, because there is no one left to buy their cargo—', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.12', 'BSB', 'cargo of gold, silver, precious stones, and pearls; of fine linen, purple, silk, and scarlet; of all kinds of citron wood and every article of ivory, precious wood, bronze, iron, and marble;', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.13', 'BSB', 'of cinnamon, spice, incense, myrrh, and frankincense; of wine, olive oil, fine flour, and wheat; of cattle, sheep, horses, and chariots; of slaves and souls of men.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.14', 'BSB', 'And they will say: “The fruit of your soul’s desire has departed from you; all your luxury and splendor have vanished, never to be seen again.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.15', 'BSB', 'The merchants who sold these things and grew their wealth from her will stand at a distance, in fear of her torment. They will weep and mourn,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.16', 'BSB', 'saying: “Woe, woe to the great city, clothed in fine linen and purple and scarlet, adorned with gold and precious stones and pearls!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.17', 'BSB', 'For in a single hour such fabulous wealth has been destroyed!” Every shipmaster, passenger, and sailor, and all who make their living from the sea, will stand at a distance', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.18', 'BSB', 'and cry out at the sight of the smoke rising from the fire that consumes her. “What city was ever like this great city?” they will exclaim.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.19', 'BSB', 'Then they will throw dust on their heads as they weep and mourn and cry out: “Woe, woe to the great city, where all who had ships on the sea were enriched by her wealth! For in a single hour she has been destroyed.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.20', 'BSB', 'Rejoice over her, O heaven, O saints and apostles and prophets, because God has pronounced for you His judgment against her.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.21', 'BSB', 'Then a mighty angel picked up a stone the size of a great millstone and cast it into the sea, saying: “With such violence the great city of Babylon will be cast down, never to be seen again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.22', 'BSB', 'And the sound of harpists and musicians, of flute players and trumpeters, will never ring out in you again. Nor will any craftsmen of any trade be found in you again, nor the sound of a millstone be heard in you again.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.23', 'BSB', 'The light of a lamp will never shine in you again, and the voices of a bride and bridegroom will never call out in you again. For your merchants were the great ones of the earth, because all the nations were deceived by your sorcery.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.18.24', 'BSB', 'And there was found in her the blood of prophets and saints, and of all who had been slain on the earth.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.1', 'BSB', 'After this I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude in heaven, shouting: “Hallelujah! Salvation and glory and power belong to our God!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.2', 'BSB', 'For His judgments are true and just. He has judged the great prostitute who corrupted the earth with her immorality. He has avenged the blood of His servants that was poured out by her hand.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.3', 'BSB', 'And a second time they called out: “Hallelujah! Her smoke rises forever and ever.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.4', 'BSB', 'And the twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fell down and worshiped God who sits on the throne, saying: “Amen, Hallelujah!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.5', 'BSB', 'Then a voice came from the throne, saying: “Praise our God, all you who serve Him, and those who fear Him, small and great alike!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.6', 'BSB', 'And I heard a sound like the roar of a great multitude, like the rushing of many waters, and like a mighty rumbling of thunder, crying out: “Hallelujah! For the Lord our God the Almighty reigns.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.7', 'BSB', 'Let us rejoice and be glad and give Him the glory. For the marriage of the Lamb has come, and His bride has made herself ready.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.8', 'BSB', 'She was given clothing of fine linen, bright and pure.” For the fine linen she wears is the righteous acts of the saints.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.9', 'BSB', 'Then the angel told me to write, “Blessed are those who are invited to the marriage supper of the Lamb.” And he said to me, “These are the true words of God.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.10', 'BSB', 'So I fell at his feet to worship him. But he told me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers who rely on the testimony of Jesus. Worship God! For the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.11', 'BSB', 'Then I saw heaven standing open, and there before me was a white horse. And its rider is called Faithful and True. With righteousness He judges and wages war.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.12', 'BSB', 'He has eyes like blazing fire, and many royal crowns on His head. He has a name written on Him that only He Himself knows.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.13', 'BSB', 'He is dressed in a robe dipped in blood, and His name is The Word of God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.14', 'BSB', 'The armies of heaven, dressed in fine linen, white and pure, follow Him on white horses.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.15', 'BSB', 'And from His mouth proceeds a sharp sword with which to strike down the nations, and He will rule them with an iron scepter. He treads the winepress of the fury of the wrath of God the Almighty.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.16', 'BSB', 'And He has a name written on His robe and on His thigh: KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.17', 'BSB', 'Then I saw an angel standing in the sun, and he cried out in a loud voice to all the birds flying overhead, “Come, gather together for the great supper of God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.18', 'BSB', 'so that you may eat the flesh of kings and commanders and mighty men, of horses and riders, of everyone slave and free, small and great.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.19', 'BSB', 'Then I saw the beast and the kings of the earth with their armies assembled to wage war against the One seated on the horse, and against His army.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.20', 'BSB', 'But the beast was captured along with the false prophet, who on its behalf had performed signs deceiving those who had the mark of the beast and worshiped its image. Both the beast and the false prophet were thrown alive into the fiery lake of burning sulfur.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.19.21', 'BSB', 'And the rest were killed with the sword that proceeded from the mouth of the One seated on the horse. And all the birds gorged themselves on their flesh.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw an angel coming down from heaven with the key to the Abyss, holding in his hand a great chain.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.2', 'BSB', 'He seized the dragon, that ancient serpent who is the devil and Satan, and bound him for a thousand years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.3', 'BSB', 'And he threw him into the Abyss, shut it, and sealed it over him, so that he could not deceive the nations until the thousand years were complete. After that, he must be released for a brief period of time.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.4', 'BSB', 'Then I saw the thrones, and those seated on them had been given authority to judge. And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded for their testimony of Jesus and for the word of God, and those who had not worshiped the beast or its image, and had not received its mark on their foreheads or hands. And they came to life and reigned with Christ for a thousand years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.5', 'BSB', 'The rest of the dead did not come back to life until the thousand years were complete. This is the first resurrection.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.6', 'BSB', 'Blessed and holy are those who share in the first resurrection! The second death has no power over them, but they will be priests of God and of Christ, and will reign with Him for a thousand years.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.7', 'BSB', 'When the thousand years are complete, Satan will be released from his prison,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.8', 'BSB', 'and will go out to deceive the nations in the four corners of the earth—Gog and Magog—to assemble them for battle. Their number is like the sand of the seashore.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.9', 'BSB', 'And they marched across the broad expanse of the earth and surrounded the camp of the saints and the beloved city. But fire came down from heaven and consumed them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.10', 'BSB', 'And the devil who had deceived them was thrown into the lake of fire and sulfur, into which the beast and the false prophet had already been thrown. There they will be tormented day and night forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.11', 'BSB', 'Then I saw a great white throne and the One seated on it. Earth and heaven fled from His presence, and no place was found for them.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.12', 'BSB', 'And I saw the dead, great and small, standing before the throne. And there were open books, and one of them was the Book of Life. And the dead were judged according to their deeds, as recorded in the books.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.13', 'BSB', 'The sea gave up its dead, and Death and Hades gave up their dead, and each one was judged according to his deeds.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.14', 'BSB', 'Then Death and Hades were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death—the lake of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.20.15', 'BSB', 'And if anyone was found whose name was not written in the Book of Life, he was thrown into the lake of fire.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.1', 'BSB', 'Then I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and earth had passed away, and the sea was no more.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.2', 'BSB', 'I saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.3', 'BSB', 'And I heard a loud voice from the throne saying: “Behold, the dwelling place of God is with man, and He will dwell with them. They will be His people, and God Himself will be with them as their God.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.4', 'BSB', '‘He will wipe away every tear from their eyes,’ and there will be no more death or mourning or crying or pain, for the former things have passed away.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.5', 'BSB', 'And the One seated on the throne said, “Behold, I make all things new.” Then He said, “Write this down, for these words are faithful and true.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.6', 'BSB', 'And He told me, “It is done! I am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End. To the thirsty I will give freely from the spring of the water of life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.7', 'BSB', 'The one who overcomes will inherit all things, and I will be his God, and he will be My son.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.8', 'BSB', 'But to the cowardly and unbelieving and abominable and murderers and sexually immoral and sorcerers and idolaters and all liars, their place will be in the lake that burns with fire and sulfur. This is the second death.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.9', 'BSB', 'Then one of the seven angels with the seven bowls full of the seven final plagues came and said to me, “Come, I will show you the bride, the wife of the Lamb.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.10', 'BSB', 'And he carried me away in the Spirit to a mountain great and high, and showed me the holy city of Jerusalem coming down out of heaven from God,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.11', 'BSB', 'shining with the glory of God. Its radiance was like a most precious jewel, like a jasper, as clear as crystal.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.12', 'BSB', 'The city had a great and high wall with twelve gates inscribed with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel, and twelve angels at the gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.13', 'BSB', 'There were three gates on the east, three on the north, three on the south, and three on the west.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.14', 'BSB', 'The wall of the city had twelve foundations bearing the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.15', 'BSB', 'The angel who spoke with me had a golden measuring rod to measure the city and its gates and walls.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.16', 'BSB', 'The city lies foursquare, with its width the same as its length. And he measured the city with the rod, and all its dimensions were equal—12,000 stadia in length and width and height.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.17', 'BSB', 'And he measured its wall to be 144 cubits, by the human measure the angel was using.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.18', 'BSB', 'The wall was made of jasper, and the city itself of pure gold, as pure as glass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.19', 'BSB', 'The foundations of the city walls were adorned with every kind of precious stone: The first foundation was jasper, the second sapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald,', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.20', 'BSB', 'the fifth sardonyx, the sixth carnelian, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and the twelfth amethyst.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.21', 'BSB', 'And the twelve gates were twelve pearls, with each gate consisting of a single pearl. The main street of the city was pure gold, as clear as glass.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.22', 'BSB', 'But I saw no temple in the city, because the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are its temple.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.23', 'BSB', 'And the city has no need of sun or moon to shine on it, because the glory of God illuminates the city, and the Lamb is its lamp.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.24', 'BSB', 'By its light the nations will walk, and into it the kings of the earth will bring their glory.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.25', 'BSB', 'Its gates will never be shut at the end of the day, because there will be no night there.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.26', 'BSB', 'And into the city will be brought the glory and honor of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.21.27', 'BSB', 'But nothing unclean will ever enter it, nor anyone who practices an abomination or a lie, but only those whose names are written in the Lamb’s Book of Life.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.1', 'BSB', 'Then the angel showed me a river of the water of life, as clear as crystal, flowing from the throne of God and of the Lamb', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.2', 'BSB', 'down the middle of the main street of the city. On either side of the river stood a tree of life, bearing twelve kinds of fruit and yielding a fresh crop for each month. And the leaves of the tree are for the healing of the nations.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.3', 'BSB', 'No longer will there be any curse. The throne of God and of the Lamb will be within the city, and His servants will worship Him.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.4', 'BSB', 'They will see His face, and His name will be on their foreheads.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.5', 'BSB', 'There will be no more night in the city, and they will have no need for the light of a lamp or of the sun. For the Lord God will shine on them, and they will reign forever and ever.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.6', 'BSB', 'Then the angel said to me, “These words are faithful and true. The Lord, the God of the spirits of the prophets, has sent His angel to show His servants what must soon take place.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.7', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am coming soon. Blessed is the one who keeps the words of prophecy in this book.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.8', 'BSB', 'And I am John, who heard and saw these things. And when I had heard and seen them, I fell down to worship at the feet of the angel who had shown me these things.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.9', 'BSB', 'But he said to me, “Do not do that! I am a fellow servant with you and your brothers the prophets, and with those who keep the words of this book. Worship God!”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.10', 'BSB', 'Then he told me, “Do not seal up the words of prophecy in this book, because the time is near.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.11', 'BSB', 'Let the unrighteous continue to be unrighteous, and the vile continue to be vile; let the righteous continue to practice righteousness, and the holy continue to be holy.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.12', 'BSB', '“Behold, I am coming soon, and My reward is with Me, to give to each one according to what he has done.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.13', 'BSB', 'I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.14', 'BSB', 'Blessed are those who wash their robes, so that they may have the right to the tree of life and may enter the city by its gates.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.15', 'BSB', 'But outside are the dogs, the sorcerers, the sexually immoral, the murderers, the idolaters, and everyone who loves and practices falsehood.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.16', 'BSB', '“I, Jesus, have sent My angel to give you this testimony for the churches. I am the Root and the Offspring of David, the bright Morning Star.”', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.17', 'BSB', 'The Spirit and the bride say, “Come!” Let the one who hears say, “Come!” And let the one who is thirsty come, and the one who desires the water of life drink freely.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.18', 'BSB', 'I testify to everyone who hears the words of prophecy in this book: If anyone adds to them, God will add to him the plagues described in this book.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.19', 'BSB', 'And if anyone takes away from the words of this book of prophecy, God will take away his share in the tree of life and the holy city, which are described in this book.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.20', 'BSB', 'He who testifies to these things says, “Yes, I am coming soon.” Amen. Come, Lord Jesus!', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
('Rev.22.21', 'BSB', 'The grace of the Lord Jesus be with all the saints. Amen.', 'Public domain', 'Berean Standard Bible (BSB); full notice in bible.translation', 'as imported', NULL),
